nalysis":"動詞形式，強調將某事物（尤其是數據、思想或物質）從更廣泛的整體中分離出來，形成獨立的部分或概念。詞源同上，從 'drawn away' 引申為『抽出』。","definition":"1. to consider something theoretically or separately from something else; 2. to draw out or remove; 3. to make an abstract, summary, or digest of.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It is difficult to abstract meaning from such complex data.\",\n    \"ch\": \"很難從如此複雜的數據中提取出意義。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to abstract the key findings for the report.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要為報告提煉出關鍵發現。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The philosopher tried to abstract principles of morality.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位哲學家試圖歸納出道德原則。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要為報告提煉出關鍵發現。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U41"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5863,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::tackle::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She decided to ____ the difficult project head-on.","expectedAnswer":"tackle","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She decided to ____ the difficult project head-on.","clozeAnswer":"tackle","exampleTranslation":"她決定正面應對這個艱難的項目。","reference":{"eng":"tackle","kk":"ˈtækl","tense":"v.","ch":"[  [    \"處理\"  ],  [    \"應對\"  ],  [    \"解決\"  ],  [    \"阻截\"  ],  [    \"對付\"  ]]","chEntries":["處理","應對","解決","阻截","對付"],"practiceMeaning":"她決定正面應對這個艱難的項目。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 'tæcel' (a snare, noose) 或相關動詞，可能與「抓住」、「纏繞」有關。'Tackle' 的核心語意是「抓住並設法控制或處理」。在體育運動中（如足球、橄欖球），指「阻截」對手，使其無法前進。引申至一般語境，指「主動地面對並試圖解決一個困難的問題或挑戰」。它強調的是一種積極、直接的介入和處理方式。例如，也可指「對付」困難局面。","definition":"1. To make vigorous and determined attempts to deal with (a problem or difficult task).; 2. To (in sports) obstruct (an opponent).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to tackle the issue of climate change.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要著手解決氣候變遷的問題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The defender tackled the forward.\",\n    \"ch\": \"後衛成功阻截了前鋒。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She decided to tackle the difficult project head-on.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她決定正面應對這個艱難的項目。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"How will you tackle this challenge?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你打算如何應對這個挑戰？\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她決定正面應對這個艱難的項目。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5847,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::parallel::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The two buildings have a ____ structure.","expectedAnswer":"parallel","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The two buildings have a ____ structure.","clozeAnswer":"parallel","exampleTranslation":"這兩座建築有著平行的結構。","reference":{"eng":"parallel","kk":"ˈpærəlel","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"平行的\"  ],  [    \"並列的\"  ],  [    \"類似的\"  ],  [    \"同時發生的\"  ]]","chEntries":["平行的","並列的","類似的","同時發生的"],"practiceMeaning":"這兩座建築有著平行的結構。","analysis":"此字源自希臘語 'parallēlos'，由 'para-' (beside) 和 'allos' (other) 構成，意為「相鄰的」或「並行的」。'Parallel' 在幾何學中指永不相交的兩條線。在更廣泛的語境中，它描述的是事物在空間上「並排」或在時間上「同時」發生、或在性質上「類似」的關係。空間上的平行與時間上的同時，以及性質上的類比，都共享了「不交叉」、「不干涉」或「共同前進」的意象。例如，也可指「結構相似的」。","definition":"1. (of lines, planes, or surfaces) side by side and having the same distance continuously between them.; 2. Occurring or existing at the same time.; 3. Having a marked similarity or resemblance.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The two roads run parallel to each other.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這兩條路相互平行。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The events occurred in parallel.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這些事件是同時發生的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His life story has parallel with mine.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的人生經歷與我頗為相似。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The two buildings have a parallel structure.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這兩座建築有著平行的結構。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這兩座建築有著平行的結構。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3198,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::abstract::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Please read the ____ before the full paper.","expectedAnswer":"abstract","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Please read the ____ before the full paper.","clozeAnswer":"abstract","exampleTranslation":"請在閱讀整篇論文前先看摘要。","reference":{"eng":"abstract","kk":"/ˈæbstrækt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['摘要'], ['概要'], ['抽象概念']]","chEntries":["摘要","概要","抽象概念"],"practiceMeaning":"請在閱讀整篇論文前先看摘要。","analysis":"名詞形式，源自形容詞，指將事物的核心或主要觀點獨立出來，形成一個簡要的概述，如同將具體的內容提煉為抽象的重點。也指非具體的概念。","definition":"1. a summary of the contents of a book, article, or speech; 2. a piece of abstract art.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please read the abstract before the full paper.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請在閱讀整篇論文前先看摘要。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The artist's latest work is an abstract.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位藝術家最新的作品是一件抽象畫。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"請在閱讀整篇論文前先看摘要。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U41"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6225,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::exterior::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ walls of the building need painting.","expectedAnswer":"exterior","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ walls of the building need painting.","clozeAnswer":"exterior","exampleTranslation":"建築物的外部牆壁需要粉刷。","reference":{"eng":"exterior","kk":"ɪkˈstɪəriər","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"外部的\"  ],  [    \"外面的\"  ],  [    \"戶外的\"  ],  [    \"外在的\"  ]]","chEntries":["外部的","外面的","戶外的","外在的"],"practiceMeaning":"建築物的外部牆壁需要粉刷。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 exterior，是 externus（外面的）的比較級，意為「更外面的」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作形容詞時，指位於某物或某人的外表、外側或外部。可用於描述物理位置、表面、非實質性方面，或與內部相對。中文翻譯為「外部的；外面的；戶外的；外在的」。","definition":"1. relating to the outside surface or structure of something; 2. happening or done outdoors; 3. relating to a person's outward appearance and behavior rather than their thoughts and feelings.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The exterior walls of the building need painting.\",\n    \"ch\": \"建築物的外部牆壁需要粉刷。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They held the ceremony in the exterior courtyard.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們在戶外的庭院裡舉行了儀式。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Exterior damage to the car was minimal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"汽車的外部損壞很小。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"建築物的外部牆壁需要粉刷。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5571,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::load::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The maximum ____ for this elevator is 1000 kg.","expectedAnswer":"load","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The maximum ____ for this elevator is 1000 kg.","clozeAnswer":"load","exampleTranslation":"這部電梯的最大負荷是 1000 公斤。","reference":{"eng":"load","kk":"loʊd","tense":"n.","ch":"[['負荷'], ['載重'], ['裝載量'], ['負擔']]","chEntries":["負荷","載重","裝載量","負擔"],"practiceMeaning":"這部電梯的最大負荷是 1000 公斤。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 \"lād\"，意為 \"way, journey, cargo\"（路，旅程，貨物），最終可能源自原始印歐語 \\*leith-（to go, to travel，去，旅行）。\"lād\" 最初指「旅程」或「所載的貨物」。\"load\" 作名詞，核心語義是「被攜帶或承受的重量、數量或負擔」。它可以指物理上的「貨物」（cargo）；「機器或車輛所能承受的最大重量」（carrying capacity）；在工程學上指「作用在結構上的力」（force or stress）；在計算機領域指「載入的數據或程式」（data to be loaded）；引申義指「精神上的負擔」（burden）。","definition":"1. A large quantity of goods or people, especially one that is carried or conveyed; 2. The weight of goods put on a vehicle or in a ship, aircraft, etc.; 3. A quantity of something such as ammunition, that is put into a gun; 4. The amount of work or responsibility that someone has.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The maximum load for this elevator is 1000 kg.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這部電梯的最大負荷是 1000 公斤。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The lorry had a heavy load of timber.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這輛貨車載有大量木材。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is carrying a heavy emotional load.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他承受著沉重的精神負擔。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The game's graphics load slowly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"遊戲的畫面載入很慢。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這部電梯的最大負荷是 1000 公斤。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5853,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::patrol::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The guards ____ the grounds day and night.","expectedAnswer":"patrol","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The guards ____ the grounds day and night.","clozeAnswer":"patrol","exampleTranslation":"守衛日夜巡邏園區。","reference":{"eng":"patrol","kk":"pəˈtroʊl","tense":"v.","ch":"[  [    \"巡邏\"  ],  [    \"巡視\"  ],  [    \"守衛\"  ]]","chEntries":["巡邏","巡視","守衛"],"practiceMeaning":"守衛日夜巡邏園區。","analysis":"此動詞形式與名詞形式同源。其核心語意是「進行例行的移動以監控或保護某區域」。'Patrol' 作動詞時，指警察、士兵或安全人員在特定區域進行定期檢查或監視。這通常是為了防止犯罪、確保安全或維持秩序。語源上，與「巡視」、「守衛」的概念相關。例如，也可指「在（某區域）進行巡邏」。","definition":"1. To move around an area in order to keep it under surveillance or guard it.; 2. To act as a guard or watchman.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The guards patrol the grounds day and night.\",\n    \"ch\": \"守衛日夜巡邏園區。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The military began to patrol the border.\",\n    \"ch\": \"軍隊開始巡邏邊境。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She patrolled the aisles of the supermarket.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她巡視著超市的貨架通道。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police patrolled the neighborhood looking for the suspect.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警方在社區巡邏尋找嫌犯。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"守衛日夜巡邏園區。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6240,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::premier::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ announced new policies.","expectedAnswer":"premier","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ announced new policies.","clozeAnswer":"premier","exampleTranslation":"總理宣布了新政策。","reference":{"eng":"premier","kk":"ˈprɛmɪər","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"總理\"  ],  [    \"首相\"  ],  [    \"首映\"  ]]","chEntries":["總理","首相","首映"],"practiceMeaning":"總理宣布了新政策。","analysis":"此字有多個詞源。作「總理；首相」時，源自法語 premier（第一的），指國家的首位官員。作「首映」時，是 premier（首先的）的名詞形式，指首次的公開演出或放映。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。中文翻譯為「總理；首相；首映」。","definition":"1. the leader of the government of a country or region; 2. the first public performance or showing of a film, play, or other work.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The premier announced new policies.\",\n    \"ch\": \"總理宣布了新政策。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The film's premier was held in London.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這部電影的首映會在倫敦舉行。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The premier of Quebec is the head of government.\",\n    \"ch\": \"魁北克省長是政府首腦。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"總理宣布了新政策。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5803,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::resume::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She attached her ____ to the job application.","expectedAnswer":"resume","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She attached her ____ to the job application.","clozeAnswer":"resume","exampleTranslation":"她將她的履歷附在工作申請上。","reference":{"eng":"resume","kk":"ˈrɛzʊmeɪ","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"履歷\"  ],  [    \"簡歷\"  ]]","chEntries":["履歷","簡歷"],"practiceMeaning":"她將她的履歷附在工作申請上。","analysis":"此字為名詞，源自法語résumé，意為「摘要；總結」。法語résumé是動詞résumer（總結）的過去分詞。résumer來自拉丁語resumere（再次拿起；總結）。核心語義是指「個人學經歷、技能和工作經驗的書面總結」，用來申請工作。語意演變上，從「總結」的廣泛概念，具體化為求職用的「個人履歷」。注意：此字名詞發音與動詞不同，且源自法語，常在美式英語中使用，而英式英語更常用CV（Curriculum Vitae）。","definition":"1. a brief summary, especially of something previously written or stated; 2. a document giving a summary of education, qualifications, and previous employment history, sent with a job application.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She attached her resume to the job application.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她將她的履歷附在工作申請上。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The employer asked for a detailed resume.\",\n    \"ch\": \"雇主要求一份詳細的履歷。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He updated his resume with his latest achievements.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他更新了他的履歷，加入了最新的成就。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她將她的履歷附在工作申請上。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3072,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::crack::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The thunder made a loud ____.","expectedAnswer":"crack","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The thunder made a loud ____.","clozeAnswer":"crack","exampleTranslation":"雷聲發出巨大的爆裂聲。","reference":{"eng":"crack","kk":"/kræk/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['裂縫；縫隙'], ['爆裂聲；巨響'], ['（口語）嘗試；機會'], ['（口語）傑作；妙語']]","chEntries":["裂縫","縫隙","爆裂聲","巨響","嘗試","機會","傑作","妙語"],"practiceMeaning":"雷聲發出巨大的爆裂聲。","analysis":"源自古英語 'crac' (a loud noise)，或與動詞 'crack' 同源。指「裂開」的狀態或由此產生的結果。\n1. 裂縫；縫隙：指物體表面或結構上出現的細長開口。\n2. 爆裂聲；巨響：指突然發出的、尖銳或響亮的聲音。\n3. （口語）嘗試；機會：指一次試驗或獲得某事的機會，常帶有一點冒險意味。\n4. （口語）傑作；妙語：指非常出色、令人印象深刻的事情或一句話。","definition":"1. a line on the surface of something along which it has split without breaking apart; 2. a sudden loud noise; 3. an attempt to do something; 4. a very good example of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There is a crack in the wall.\",\n    \"ch\": \"牆上有道裂縫。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The thunder made a loud crack.\",\n    \"ch\": \"雷聲發出巨大的爆裂聲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is your last crack at the problem.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是你解決這個問題的最後一次機會。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"That joke was a real crack!\",\n    \"ch\": \"那個笑話真是太妙了！\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"雷聲發出巨大的爆裂聲。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5849,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::parallel::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His achievements ____ those of his father.","expectedAnswer":"parallel","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His achievements ____ those of his father.","clozeAnswer":"parallel","exampleTranslation":"他的成就與他父親的成就相當。","reference":{"eng":"parallel","kk":"ˈpærəlel","tense":"v.","ch":"[  [    \"與……平行\"  ],  [    \"與……相比\"  ],  [    \"與……同時發生\"  ],  [    \"與……並駕齊驅\"  ]]","chEntries":["與……平行","與……相比","與……同時發生","與……並駕齊驅"],"practiceMeaning":"他的成就與他父親的成就相當。","analysis":"此動詞形式與形容詞、名詞形式同源。其核心語意是「使……與……平行」、「與……相比」、「與……同時發生」。'Parallel' 作動詞時，指使兩條線、兩個事物在空間上保持平行；或使兩個事件、進程同時發生；或在性質上進行類比、對比。它強調將事物置於「並列」或「同步」的關係中。例如，也可指「與……並駕齊驅」，表示發展速度或成就相似。","definition":"1. Be alongside and have the same direction, or be corresponding.; 2. Happen at the same time.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The new highway parallels the old one.\",\n    \"ch\": \"新高速公路與舊公路平行。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His achievements parallel those of his father.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的成就與他父親的成就相當。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The two research projects are paralleling each other.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這兩個研究項目是並行進行的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her career parallels his in many ways.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的事業在許多方面都與他的事業並駕齊驅。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他的成就與他父親的成就相當。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4423,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u9::plenty::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She has ____ of friends.","expectedAnswer":"plenty","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She has ____ of friends.","clozeAnswer":"plenty","exampleTranslation":"她有很多朋友。","reference":{"eng":"plenty","kk":"/ˈplenti/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['足夠的', '大量的']]","chEntries":["足夠的","大量的"],"practiceMeaning":"她有很多朋友。","analysis":"詞源自古法語 'plente'，源自拉丁語 'plenitas' (fullness)。指數量上非常充足，不僅足夠，甚至過剩。","definition":"as much or as much as is needed, or much more than is needed.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There is plenty of food for everyone.\",\n    \"ch\": \"有足夠的食物給每個人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has plenty of friends.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她有很多朋友。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她有很多朋友。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4450,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::rank::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The restaurant is of the highest ____ in the city.","expectedAnswer":"rank","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The restaurant is of the highest ____ in the city.","clozeAnswer":"rank","exampleTranslation":"這家餐廳是城裡等級最高的。","reference":{"eng":"rank","kk":"/ræŋk/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['等級'], ['地位'], ['（軍隊中的）軍階'], ['（受尊敬或重視的）程度'], ['（事物）類別']]","chEntries":["等級","地位","軍階","程度","類別"],"practiceMeaning":"這家餐廳是城裡等級最高的。","analysis":"源自古法語 ranc，意為「隊伍」、「行列」。早期語意指「整齊排列的隊伍」。引申為在隊伍中的位置，即「等級」、「地位」。在軍事中，指軍階。也可引申為事物在某個標準下的位置，例如「受尊敬的程度」。","definition":"1. A position in an organization or society; 2. A level in an organization or society; 3. (often plural) The officers of a particular grade or rank in the armed forces; 4. A high or respected position in a hierarchy or scale.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She achieved the rank of captain in the army.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在軍隊中晉升到上尉軍階。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The restaurant is of the highest rank in the city.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家餐廳是城裡等級最高的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has a high rank among scientists.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在科學家中有很高的地位。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這家餐廳是城裡等級最高的。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5804,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::shed::vt","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She ____ her coat in the warm room.","expectedAnswer":"shed","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She ____ her coat in the warm room.","clozeAnswer":"shed","exampleTranslation":"她在溫暖的房間裡脫掉了外套。","reference":{"eng":"shed","kk":"ʃɛd","tense":"vt.","ch":"[  [    \"脫落\"  ],  [    \"脫去\"  ],  [    \"流（眼淚）\"  ],  [    \"散發（光、熱）\"  ],  [    \"拋棄\"  ]]","chEntries":["脫落","脫去","流","散發","拋棄"],"practiceMeaning":"她在溫暖的房間裡脫掉了外套。","analysis":"此字為及物動詞，源自古英語sceddan，詞源不明，可能與古諾斯語Skeitha（分割；分離）有關。核心語義是「將某物分離、去除」。語意演變上，從「自然脫落」（如蛇蛻皮、樹葉掉落）引申為「主動脫去」衣物，或「流出」眼淚，或「散發」光熱，以及「拋棄」不再需要的事物。","definition":"1. (of an animal) to lose hair, skin, or feathers; 2. to get rid of something unwanted; 3. to let tears fall; 4. to give off a particular light, heat, or sound.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Snakes shed their skin once a year.\",\n    \"ch\": \"蛇每年蛻一次皮。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She shed her coat in the warm room.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在溫暖的房間裡脫掉了外套。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The lamp shed a soft light on the table.\",\n    \"ch\": \"燈在地板上投下柔和的光。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她在溫暖的房間裡脫掉了外套。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6204,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::variable::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He has a ____ temper.","expectedAnswer":"variable","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He has a ____ temper.","clozeAnswer":"variable","exampleTranslation":"他的脾氣很不穩定。","reference":{"eng":"variable","kk":"ˈveriəbl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"變化的\"  ],  [    \"易變的\"  ],  [    \"可變的\"  ],  [    \"不定的\"  ]]","chEntries":["變化的","易變的","可變的","不定的"],"practiceMeaning":"他的脾氣很不穩定。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 variabilis，是動詞 variare「改變」的衍生形容詞。variare 源自 varus「彎曲的、扭曲的」，可能與 varia（斑駁）有關。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 variare「改變」是其核心語意來源。作為形容詞，其核心語義是「能夠或傾向於改變；不穩定的」。詞源中的「改變」概念直接體現了此義。","definition":"1. not always the same; liable to change; 2. able to be changed or adapted.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The weather in this region is very variable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個地區的天氣變化很大。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has a variable temper.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的脾氣很不穩定。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The amount of interest is variable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"利率是可變的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her mood was variable throughout the day.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她一天之間情緒多變。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他的脾氣很不穩定。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5481,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::harvest::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The land yielded a good ____.","expectedAnswer":"harvest","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The land yielded a good ____.","clozeAnswer":"harvest","exampleTranslation":"這片土地收穫頗豐。","reference":{"eng":"harvest","kk":"ˈhɑrvəst","tense":"v.","ch":"[['收割'], ['收穫']]","chEntries":["收割","收穫"],"practiceMeaning":"這片土地收穫頗豐。","analysis":"此字由名詞 'harvest'（收成）派生而來。作為動詞，'harvest' 的意思是「收割、採集農作物」。它直接承襲了名詞的語意，指進行收穫動作的過程。這個動詞強調的是將成熟的作物從土地上採集下來的行為。核心語意是「進行收割」。","definition":"1. Gather (a crop) from the fields.; 2. (Of a crop) yield or give as a harvest.; 3. Gather or reap.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The farmers began to harvest the whea