[  [    \"複數的\"  ],  [    \"多數的\"  ],  [    \"複数\"  ]]","chEntries":["複數的","多數的","複数"],"practiceMeaning":"這家公司有多個股東。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 plūrālis，是 plus（更多）的衍生形容詞，意為「更多的」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 plus「更多」是其核心語意來源。作為形容詞，其核心語義是指「兩個或兩個以上」或「多於一個」的狀態。詞源中的「更多」概念引申出「多數」和「複數」的用法，特別是在語法上指代兩個以上的名詞、代詞或動詞形式。","definition":"1. (of a word or form) denoting more than one; 2. more than one.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The plural of 'cat' is 'cats'.\",\n    \"ch\": \"「cat」的複數是「cats」。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a plural noun.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個複數名詞。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company has plural shareholders.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司有多個股東。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He holds plural positions in the organization.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在該組織中擔任多個職位。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這家公司有多個股東。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6098,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::solo::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The singer's ____ was met with thunderous applause.","expectedAnswer":"solo","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The singer's ____ was met with thunderous applause.","clozeAnswer":"solo","exampleTranslation":"歌手的獨唱贏得了雷鳴般的掌聲。","reference":{"eng":"solo","kk":"ˈsolo","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"獨奏\"  ],  [    \"獨唱\"  ],  [    \"獨自一人\"  ]]","chEntries":["獨奏","獨唱","獨自一人"],"practiceMeaning":"歌手的獨唱贏得了雷鳴般的掌聲。","analysis":"此字源自義大利語 solo（alone）。作為名詞，指「單獨的表演」，如音樂的「獨奏」或「獨唱」。也可以指「獨自的行為」或「獨自一人」。","definition":"1. a thing done alone; 2. a performance by one person, especially in music.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The pianist played a difficult solo.\",\n    \"ch\": \"鋼琴家演奏了一首高難度的獨奏曲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her first solo flight was nerve-wracking.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的第一次單獨飛行令人緊張。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The singer's solo was met with thunderous applause.\",\n    \"ch\": \"歌手的獨唱贏得了雷鳴般的掌聲。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"歌手的獨唱贏得了雷鳴般的掌聲。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6255,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::throne::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The dictator seized the ____ by force.","expectedAnswer":"throne","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The dictator seized the ____ by force.","clozeAnswer":"throne","exampleTranslation":"獨裁者武力奪取了王權。","reference":{"eng":"throne","kk":"θron","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"寶座\"  ],  [    \"王位\"  ],  [    \"王權\"  ],  [    \"（主教等的）座席；高位\"  ]]","chEntries":["寶座","王位","王權","座席","高位"],"practiceMeaning":"獨裁者武力奪取了王權。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 þrōn，後受古法語 trône 影響，最終可追溯至拉丁語 thronus，而拉丁語又源自希臘語 thronos（椅子；寶座）。構詞上，希臘語 thronos 可能與 ethelein（升高）有關，暗示著高高在上的位置。此字沒有可在現代英語中透明拆解的生產性字首或字尾，應視為一個整體詞源演變。核心語義為君主、主教或神祇所坐的特殊椅子，引申為國家或權力的象徵，故可表示王位、王權或至高無上的地位。常見於政治、宗教及文學語境。作為主教的座席，也引申為高位。","definition":"1. a large, stately chair on which a sovereign or other dignitary sits; 2. the office, power, or dignity of a sovereign or bishop; 3. a seat of honor or authority.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The king sat on his ornate throne.\",\n    \"ch\": \"國王坐在他華麗的寶座上。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She ascended the throne at the age of twenty-five.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在二十五歲時繼承了王位。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The dictator seized the throne by force.\",\n    \"ch\": \"獨裁者武力奪取了王權。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The bishop returned to his throne after the synod.\",\n    \"ch\": \"主教在宗教會議後回到了他的座席。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"獨裁者武力奪取了王權。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6250,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::thrust::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The sword ____ was swift and deadly.","expectedAnswer":"thrust","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The sword ____ was swift and deadly.","clozeAnswer":"thrust","exampleTranslation":"劍的刺擊迅速而致命。","reference":{"eng":"thrust","kk":"θrʌst","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"猛推\"  ],  [    \"推進力\"  ],  [    \"刺擊\"  ],  [    \"核心要點\"  ]]","chEntries":["猛推","推進力","刺擊","核心要點"],"practiceMeaning":"劍的刺擊迅速而致命。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 þȳst（用力推，刺）。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。名詞義指猛推、用力推動或刺的動作。也可指推進物體前進的力量（如火箭的推力），或引申為某事物的主要目的、要點或核心。中文翻譯為「猛推；推進力；刺擊；核心要點」。","definition":"1. a strong, pushing movement; 2. the force that propels something forward, especially an aircraft or spacecraft; 3. the main point or purpose of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The engine provided enough thrust to lift the plane.\",\n    \"ch\": \"引擎提供了足夠的推進力使飛機升空。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The thrust of his argument was that the policy was flawed.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他論點的核心要點是這項政策有缺陷。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The sword thrust was swift and deadly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"劍的刺擊迅速而致命。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"劍的刺擊迅速而致命。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6202,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::upgrade::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The hotel provided a complimentary room ____.","expectedAnswer":"upgrade","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The hotel provided a complimentary room ____.","clozeAnswer":"upgrade","exampleTranslation":"這家旅館提供了免費的房間升級。","reference":{"eng":"upgrade","kk":"ˈʌpɡreɪd","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"升級\"  ],  [    \"提升\"  ]]","chEntries":["升級","提升"],"practiceMeaning":"這家旅館提供了免費的房間升級。","analysis":"此字由 up (上) + grade (等級、品質) 構成。此字在現代英語中可視為由 up 和 grade 組合的複合詞。up 表示方向上的「向上」，grade 表示「等級、品質」。作為名詞，其核心語義是由動詞 upgrade「升級」名詞化而來，指「將某物提升到更高等級、標準或性能的行為或結果」。詞源中的「向上」和「等級」概念清晰地體現了此義。","definition":"1. an act of raising something to a higher standard, quality, or level; 2. an improved version of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The recent upgrade of the network improved its speed.\",\n    \"ch\": \"最近的網路升級提高了它的速度。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They are offering a free upgrade to premium.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們提供免費升級到高級版。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The hotel provided a complimentary room upgrade.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家旅館提供了免費的房間升級。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The upgrade to the operating system was successful.\",\n    \"ch\": \"操作系統的升級是成功的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這家旅館提供了免費的房間升級。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6152,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::alien::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The design felt ____ to the rest of the house.","expectedAnswer":"alien","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The design felt ____ to the rest of the house.","clozeAnswer":"alien","exampleTranslation":"這個設計與房子的其他部分顯得格格不入。","reference":{"eng":"alien","kk":"ˈeɪliən","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"外國的\"  ],  [    \"外來的\"  ],  [    \"陌生的\"  ],  [    \"不協調的\"  ],  [    \"不適合的\"  ]]","chEntries":["外國的","外來的","陌生的","不協調的","不適合的"],"practiceMeaning":"這個設計與房子的其他部分顯得格格不入。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 alienus，意為「別人的、外國的、不相干的」。它進入中古英語 via 古法語 alien。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，應視為整體詞源演變。作為形容詞，核心語義是「來自另一國家的」或「與之無關的」。從「外國的」進一步引申出「陌生的、不熟悉的」，再到「不協調的、不適合的」。這些義項都圍繞著「非本地的、不屬於的」概念發展。","definition":"1. belonging to a foreign country or countries; 2. unfamiliar and disturbing; 3. not belonging to a particular place; 4. completely different.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has an alien culture and language.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他有著外來的文化和語言。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The news was alien to him.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這消息對他來說很陌生。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Such behavior is alien to our traditions.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種行為與我們的傳統不符。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The design felt alien to the rest of the house.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個設計與房子的其他部分顯得格格不入。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個設計與房子的其他部分顯得格格不入。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6162,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::collective::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They are part of a writers' ____.","expectedAnswer":"collective","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They are part of a writers' ____.","clozeAnswer":"collective","exampleTranslation":"他們是一個作家團體的成員。","reference":{"eng":"collective","kk":"kəˈlɛktɪv","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"集體\"  ],  [    \"組織\"  ],  [    \"合作社\"  ]]","chEntries":["集體","組織","合作社"],"practiceMeaning":"他們是一個作家團體的成員。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 collectīvus，是動詞 colligere「收集、聚集」的衍生形容詞。colligere 由 com- (together) + legere (to gather) 組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 com-「一起」和 legere「收集」是其核心語意來源。作為名詞，其核心語義是「一個由多個個體組成的團體，共同行動或共享」。詞源中的「一起收集」概念引申為「聚集在一起的群體」。此義項由形容詞「集體的」名詞化而來。","definition":"1. a group of people or things functioning as a single unit; 2. a cooperative association.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The workers formed a collective to improve their conditions.\",\n    \"ch\": \"工人們組成了一個集體來改善他們的處境。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The farm operated as a collective.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個農場作為一個合作社運營。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The artist collective displayed their latest works.\",\n    \"ch\": \"藝術家集體展示了他們最新的作品。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They are part of a writers' collective.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們是一個作家團體的成員。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們是一個作家團體的成員。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3194,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::split::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The tree trunk was ____ by lightning.","expectedAnswer":"split","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The tree trunk was ____ by lightning.","clozeAnswer":"split","exampleTranslation":"樹幹被閃電劈開了。","reference":{"eng":"split","kk":"/splɪt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['分裂；分開'], ['（使）裂開；破裂'], ['分享；分配（尤指不均）']]","chEntries":["分裂","分開","裂開","破裂","分享","分配"],"practiceMeaning":"樹幹被閃電劈開了。","analysis":"詞源來自古諾爾斯語 'splita'，意為「劈開，分裂」。'Split' 的核心是「分離」、「裂開」或「分開」。它可以指物理上的分離，如將物體劈開、裂開，或將一群人分成小組。也可指意見、關係的分歧。在分配財物時，'split' 也常用來表示分享，但有時帶有均勻或不均勻分配的意味。","definition":"1. break or cause to break into pieces; 2. divide into parts or groups; 3. separate from a larger group or body.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The log split easily when I hit it with the axe.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我用斧頭砍下去，木頭很容易就劈開了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The friends decided to split the cost of the meal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"朋友們決定分攤飯錢。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The party split into two factions.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個黨派分裂成兩個派系。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The tree trunk was split by lightning.\",\n    \"ch\": \"樹幹被閃電劈開了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"樹幹被閃電劈開了。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5863,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::tackle::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"How will you ____ this challenge?","expectedAnswer":"tackle","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"How will you ____ this challenge?","clozeAnswer":"tackle","exampleTranslation":"你打算如何應對這個挑戰？","reference":{"eng":"tackle","kk":"ˈtækl","tense":"v.","ch":"[  [    \"處理\"  ],  [    \"應對\"  ],  [    \"解決\"  ],  [    \"阻截\"  ],  [    \"對付\"  ]]","chEntries":["處理","應對","解決","阻截","對付"],"practiceMeaning":"你打算如何應對這個挑戰？","analysis":"此字源自古英語 'tæcel' (a snare, noose) 或相關動詞，可能與「抓住」、「纏繞」有關。'Tackle' 的核心語意是「抓住並設法控制或處理」。在體育運動中（如足球、橄欖球），指「阻截」對手，使其無法前進。引申至一般語境，指「主動地面對並試圖解決一個困難的問題或挑戰」。它強調的是一種積極、直接的介入和處理方式。例如，也可指「對付」困難局面。","definition":"1. To make vigorous and determined attempts to deal with (a problem or difficult task).; 2. To (in sports) obstruct (an opponent).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to tackle the issue of climate change.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要著手解決氣候變遷的問題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The defender tackled the forward.\",\n    \"ch\": \"後衛成功阻截了前鋒。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She decided to tackle the difficult project head-on.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她決定正面應對這個艱難的項目。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"How will you tackle this challenge?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你打算如何應對這個挑戰？\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"你打算如何應對這個挑戰？","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5583,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::classic::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This is a ____ example of her early work.","expectedAnswer":"classic","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This is a ____ example of her early work.","clozeAnswer":"classic","exampleTranslation":"這是她早期作品的一個經典範例。","reference":{"eng":"classic","kk":"ˈklæsɪk","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['經典的'], ['古典的'], ['典型的'], ['一流的']]","chEntries":["經典的","古典的","典型的","一流的"],"practiceMeaning":"這是她早期作品的一個經典範例。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 \"classicus\"，意為 \"of or belonging to the highest class, first-class\"（屬於最高級別的，一流的），來自 \"classis\"（a class, fleet, order，階級，艦隊，秩序）。\"classis\" 最初指「羅馬貴族階層」，後來也指「海軍艦隊」，再引申為「類別」或「等級」。因此，\"classic\" 的核心語義是「屬於最高等級、最經典、最受推崇的」。它可以用來形容「古希臘羅馬時期的」（classical antiquity）；指「代表某一類型最高水準的、永恆的」（exemplary, timeless）；或指「典型的、代表性的」（typical）。","definition":"1. Judged over a period of time to be of the highest quality and significance; timeless; 2. Characteristic of or belonging to a past period, especially of ancient Greece or Rome; 3. Familiarly typical or representative.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a classic example of her early work.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是她早期作品的一個經典範例。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The play is a classic of English literature.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這齣戲是英國文學的經典之作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He drives a classic car.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他開一輛經典老爺車。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was a classic case of misunderstanding.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個典型的誤會案例。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是她早期作品的一個經典範例。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3072,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::crack::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There is a ____ in the wall.","expectedAnswer":"crack","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There is a ____ in the wall.","clozeAnswer":"crack","exampleTranslation":"牆上有道裂縫。","reference":{"eng":"crack","kk":"/kræk/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['裂縫；縫隙'], ['爆裂聲；巨響'], ['（口語）嘗試；機會'], ['（口語）傑作；妙語']]","chEntries":["裂縫","縫隙","爆裂聲","巨響","嘗試","機會","傑作","妙語"],"practiceMeaning":"牆上有道裂縫。","analysis":"源自古英語 'crac' (a loud noise)，或與動詞 'crack' 同源。指「裂開」的狀態或由此產生的結果。\n1. 裂縫；縫隙：指物體表面或結構上出現的細長開口。\n2. 爆裂聲；巨響：指突然發出的、尖銳或響亮的聲音。\n3. （口語）嘗試；機會：指一次試驗或獲得某事的機會，常帶有一點冒險意味。\n4. （口語）傑作；妙語：指非常出色、令人印象深刻的事情或一句話。","definition":"1. a line on the surface of something along which it has split without breaking apart; 2. a sudden loud noise; 3. an attempt to do something; 4. a very good example of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There is a crack in the wall.\",\n    \"ch\": \"牆上有道裂縫。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The thunder made a loud crack.\",\n    \"ch\": \"雷聲發出巨大的爆裂聲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is your last crack at the problem.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是你解決這個問題的最後一次機會。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"That joke was a real crack!\",\n    \"ch\": \"那個笑話真是太妙了！\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"牆上有道裂縫。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4122,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::desert::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The Sahara ____ is the largest hot desert in the world.","expectedAnswer":"Desert","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The Sahara ____ is the largest hot desert in the world.","clozeAnswer":"Desert","exampleTranslation":"撒哈拉沙漠是世界上最大的熱帶沙漠。","reference":{"eng":"desert","kk":"/ˈdɛzərt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['沙漠']]","chEntries":["沙漠"],"practiceMeaning":"撒哈拉沙漠是世界上最大的熱帶沙漠。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 desertum（荒蕪之地），是 desertus（被遺棄的）的中性形式。核心概念是「荒涼」、「無人居住」的地方。引申為極度乾燥、植被稀少的地區。","definition":"a barren or desolate area, especially one with little or no rainfall.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The Sahara Desert is the largest hot desert in the world.\",\n    \"ch\": \"撒哈拉沙漠是世界上最大的熱帶沙漠。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Many desert animals are nocturnal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"許多沙漠動物是夜行性的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They trekked across the desert.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們徒步穿越了沙漠。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"撒哈拉沙漠是世界上最大的熱帶沙漠。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4167,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::living::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The steep rise in ____ costs made it hard to make ends meet.","expectedAnswer":"living","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The steep rise in ____ costs made it hard to make ends meet.","clozeAnswer":"living","exampleTranslation":"生活成本的急劇上漲使得人們難以為繼。","reference":{"eng":"living","kk":"/ˈlɪvɪŋ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['生活', '生計']]","chEntries":["生活","生計"],"practiceMeaning":"生活成本的急劇上漲使得人們難以為繼。","analysis":"由 live（活著，生存）+ -ing（名詞後綴）組成。核心概念是「生存的狀態」或「維持生存所需」。","definition":"1. the state of being alive; 2. a means of supporting oneself financially","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The steep rise in living costs made it hard to make ends meet.\",\n    \"ch\": \"生活成本的急劇上漲使得人們難以為繼。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is working hard to provide a better living for his family.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他正努力工作，為家人提供更好的生活。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The cost of living has gone up.\",\n    \"ch\": \"生活成本上升了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"生活成本的急劇上漲使得人們難以為繼。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6179,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::miniature::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She has a collection of ____ cars.","expectedAnswer":"miniature","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She has a collection of ____ cars.","clozeAnswer":"miniature","exampleTranslation":"她收藏了一批微型汽車。","reference":{"eng":"miniature","kk":"ˈmɪniətʃər","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"小型的\"  ],  [    \"微型的\"  ],  [    \"縮小的\"  ]]","chEntries":["小型的","微型的","縮小的"],"practiceMeaning":"她收藏了一批微型汽車。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 miniatura，與 miniare「塗色」（尤其指手稿中的紅色）有關，可能與 minor「較小的」有關。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，應視為整體詞源演變。作為形容詞，其核心語義是指「非常小的、微小的」。此義項由「小的」概念引申，強調尺寸上的微小。","definition":"1. a thing that is very small in size.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a collection of miniature cars.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她收藏了一批微型汽車。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The artist painted a miniature portrait.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位藝術家畫了一幅微型肖像。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a miniature version of the original building.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是這個建築物的一個縮小版。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He bought a miniature schnauzer puppy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他買了一隻迷你雪納瑞幼犬。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她收藏了一批微型汽車。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3100,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::monitor::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Connect the cable to the computer ____.","expectedAnswer":"monitor","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Connect the cable to the computer ____.","clozeAnswer":"monitor","exampleTranslation":"將電纜連接到電腦顯示器。","reference":{"eng":"monitor","kk":"/ˈmɑːnɪtər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['顯示器；螢幕'], ['（學習、進展等的）監督者；指導者'], ['（飛機、艦船等）監視器']]","chEntries":["顯示器","螢幕","監督者","指導者","監視器"],"practiceMeaning":"將電纜連接到電腦顯示器。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'monitor' (one who warns)，'monere' (to warn, remind)。指「觀察」或「警告」的工具或人。\n1. 顯示器；螢幕：指用於顯示電腦圖像或影片的設備。\n2. （學習、進展等的）監督者；指導者：指負責觀察、指導或評估某人學習或進展的人。\n3. （飛機、艦船等）監視器：指用於監測、觀察或控制特定設備或系統的裝置。","definition":"1. a screen used with a computer; 2. a person who monitors something; 3. a device used to watch or record something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Connect the cable to the computer monitor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"將電纜連接到電腦顯示器。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She was appointed as a monitor for the student council.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她被任命為學生會的監督員。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The ship's monitor tracked the enemy aircraft.\",\n    \"ch\": \"艦船的監視器追蹤了敵機。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"將電纜連接到電腦顯示器。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4418,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u9::opposite::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They hold ____ views on the issue.","expectedAnswer":"opposite","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They hold ____ views on the issue.","clozeAnswer":"opposite","exampleTranslation":"他們在這個問題上持有相反的觀點。","reference":{"eng":"opposite","kk":"/ˈɒpəzɪt/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['相反的', '對立的'], ['對面的', '對著的']]","chEntries":["相反的","對立的","對面的","對著的"],"practiceMeaning":"他們在這個問題上持有相反的觀點。","analysis":"詞源自拉丁語 'oppositus'，'ob-' (against) + 'ponere' (to place)。指位置、性質、順序或觀點上完全不同或相對的。","definition":"in a position facing the other way; in a position across from someone or something; completely different from something else.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They hold opposite views on the issue.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們在這個問題上持有相反的觀點。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The shop is on the opposite side of the street.\",\n    \"ch\": \"商店在街對面。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們在這個問題上持有相反的觀點。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4423,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u9::plenty::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There is ____ of food for everyone.","expectedAnswer":"plenty","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There is ____ of food for everyone.","clozeAnswer":"plenty","exampleTranslation":"有足夠的食物給每個人。","reference":{"eng":"plenty","kk":"/ˈplenti/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['足夠的', '大量的']]","chEntries":["足夠的","大量的"],"practiceMeaning":"有足夠的食物給每個人。","analysis":"詞源自古法語 'plente'，源自拉丁語 'plenitas' (fullness)。指數量上非常充足，不僅足夠，甚至過剩。","definition":"as much or as much as is needed, or much more than is needed.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There is plenty of food for everyone.\",\n    \"ch\": \"有足夠的食物給每個人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has plenty of friends.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她有很多朋友。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"有足夠的食物給每個人。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5804,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::shed::vt","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Snakes ____ their skin once a year.","expectedAnswer":"shed","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Snakes ____ their skin once a year.","clozeAnswer":"shed","exampleTranslation":"蛇每年蛻一次皮。","reference":{"eng":"shed","kk":"ʃɛd","tense":"vt.","ch":"[  [    \"脫落\"  ],  [    \"脫去\"  ],  [    \"流（眼淚）\"  ],  [    \"散發（光、熱）\"  ],  [    \"拋棄\"  ]]","chEntries":["脫落","脫去","流","散發","拋棄"],"practiceMeaning":"蛇每年蛻一次皮。","analysis":"此字為及物動詞，源自古英語sceddan，詞源不明，可能與古諾斯語Skeitha（分割；分離）有關。核心語義是「將某物分離、去除」。語意演變上，從「自然脫落」（如蛇蛻皮、樹葉掉落）引申為「主動脫去」衣物，或「流出」眼淚，或「散發」光熱，以及「拋棄」不再需要的事物。","definition":"1. (of an animal) to lose hair, skin, or feathers; 2. to get rid of something unwanted; 3. to let tears fall; 4. to give off a particular light, heat, or sound.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Snakes shed their skin once a year.\",\n    \"ch\": \"蛇每年蛻一次皮。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She shed her coat in the warm room.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在溫暖的房間裡脫掉了外套。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The lamp shed a soft light on the table.\",\n    \"ch\": \"燈在地板上投下柔和的光。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"蛇每年蛻一次皮。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5568,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::sort::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Please ____ the documents by date.","expectedAnswer":"sort","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Please ____ the documents by date.","clozeAnswer":"sort","exampleTranslation":"請按日期整理這些文件。","reference":{"eng":"sort","kk":"sɔrt","tense":"v.","ch":"[['分類'], ['整理'], ['挑選']]","chEntries":["分類","整理","挑選"],"practiceMeaning":"請按日期整理這些文件。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 \"sortir\"，意為 \"to draw lots, to choose\"（抽籤，選擇），來自拉丁語 \"sortem\"，是 \"sors, sortis\"（lot, fate, share，籤，命運，份額）的賓格形式。 \"sortem\" 引申出「選擇、挑選」的概念。在中古英語中，\"sort\" 的語義發展為「按照某種標準進行挑選或排列」，即「分類」或「整理」。因此，\"sort\" 的核心語義是「根據特定標準將事物分開或排列」。它既可以是物理上的分類（e.g., sorting laundry），也可以是邏輯上的分類（e.g., sorting data）。","definition":"1. Arrange systematically or alphabetically; 2. Classify (something) into different categories; 3. Deal with (a problem or situation) by taking appropriate action.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please sort the documents by date.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請按日期整理這些文件。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is good at sorting out complex problems.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她擅長解決複雜的問題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to sort the apples into different grades.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要將蘋果按等級分類。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"請按日期整理這些文件。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5437,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::spare::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Can you ____ me a moment of your time?","expectedAnswer":"spare","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Can you ____ me a moment of your time?","clozeAnswer":"spare","exampleTranslation":"你能抽一點時間給我嗎？","reference":{"eng":"spare","kk":"sper","tense":"v.","ch":"[['抽出時間'], ['節省'], ['饒恕'], ['免除']]","chEntries":["抽出時間","節省","饒恕","免除"],"practiceMeaning":"你能抽一點時間給我嗎？","analysis":"此字源自古英語 \"spær\"，意為\"節儉的\"、\"稀少的\"。其詞源可能與\"sparse\" (稀疏的) 有聯繫。構詞上沒有明顯的字首、字根或字尾可拆解，應視為一個整體詞源的演變。原始語義是「稀少」、「節省」。作為動詞，它可以表示「節省」資源或時間，即「抽出時間」來做某事；也可以表示「饒恕」某人，即「免除」懲罰或傷害；或「免除」某種不適。","definition":"to refrain from harming or punishing someone; to save someone from harm; to afford to give or give up.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Can you spare me a moment of your time?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你能抽一點時間給我嗎？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The king spared his life.\",\n    \"ch\": \"國王饒恕了他的性命。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We can't spare the resources for such a project.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們無法為這樣一個項目省下資源。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"你能抽一點時間給我嗎？","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4705,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::stomach::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The food was difficult for his ____ to digest.","expectedAnswer":"stomach","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The food was difficult for his ____ to digest.","clozeAnswer":"stomach","exampleTranslation":"這種食物對他的胃來說很難消化。","reference":{"eng":"stomach","kk":"/ˈstʌmək/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['胃'], ['腹部'], ['（非正式）消化能力；容忍力']]","chEntries":["胃","腹部","消化能力","容忍力"],"practiceMeaning":"這種食物對他的胃來說很難消化。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 *stomachus*，來自希臘語 *stómakhos*（食道、胃）。核心是指消化食物的器官。引申至身體的腹部區域，以及非正式地指消化食物的能力，或容忍某種情況的能力。","definition":"1. An organ in the digestive tract where food is mixed with digestive juices. 2. The belly or abdomen. 3. (informal) The capacity to digest food or to tolerate something unpleasant.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The food was difficult for his stomach to digest.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種食物對他的胃來說很難消化。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He clutched his stomach in pain.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他痛苦地捂著肚子。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I don't have the stomach for this kind of violence.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我受不了這種暴力。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這種食物對他的胃來說很難消化。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4551,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::trace::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Scientists are trying to ____ the origin of the disease.","expectedAnswer":"trace","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Scientists are trying to ____ the origin of the disease.","clozeAnswer":"trace","exampleTranslation":"科學家們正試圖追溯這種疾病的起源。","reference":{"eng":"trace","kk":"/treɪs/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['追蹤', '追溯'], ['描繪', '勾勒']]","chEntries":["追蹤","追溯","描繪","勾勒"],"practiceMeaning":"科學家們正試圖追溯這種疾病的起源。","analysis":"動詞用法源自名詞。\n    1. 追蹤、追溯：指通過線索找到某物的起源、經過或下落。\n    2. 描繪、勾勒：指仔細地畫出線條或輪廓，如同追蹤物體的形狀。","definition":"1. follow the course or development of (something).; 2. discover or reveal (something) by a process of investigation or analysis.; 3. copy (a drawing or design) by drawing on a sheet of paper laid over it.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Scientists are trying to trace the origin of the disease.\",\n    \"ch\": \"科學家們正試圖追溯這種疾病的起源。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She traced the outline of the leaf with her finger.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她用手指描繪著葉子的輪廓。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Can you trace the route on this map?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你能在這張地圖上描出路線嗎？\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"科學家們正試圖追溯這種疾病的起源。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6201,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::upgrade::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need to ____ our computer system.","expectedAnswer":"upgrade","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need to ____ our computer system.","clozeAnswer":"upgrade","exampleTranslation":"我們需要升級我們的電腦系統。","reference":{"eng":"upgrade","kk":"ˈʌpɡreɪd","tense":"v.","ch":"[  [    \"升級\"  ],  [    \"提升\"  ],  [    \"改良\"  ]]","chEntries":["升級","提升","改良"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要升級我們的電腦系統。","analysis":"此字由 up (上) + grade (等級、品質) 構成。此字在現代英語中可視為由 up 和 grade 組合的複合詞。up 表示方向上的「向上」，grade 表示「等級、品質」。作為動詞，其核心語義是「將某物提升到更高的等級、標準或性能」。詞源中的「向上」和「等級」概念清晰地體現了此義。","definition":"1. to raise to a higher standard, quality, or level; 2. to replace equipment or machinery with newer, better, or more powerful types.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to upgrade our computer system.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要升級我們的電腦系統。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The airline offered to upgrade their seats to first class.\",\n    \"ch\": \"航空公司主動提出將他們的座位升級到頭等艙。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The software was upgraded to the latest version.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該軟體已升級到最新版本。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They upgraded their house last year.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們去年對他們的房子進行了升級改造。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要升級我們的電腦系統。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3197,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::abstract::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She has a very ____ way of thinking.","expectedAnswer":"abstract","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She has a very ____ way of thinking.","clozeAnswer":"abstract","exampleTranslation":"她的思考方式非常抽象。","reference":{"eng":"abstract","kk":"/ˈæbstrækt/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['抽象的'], ['深奧的'], ['非實體的'], ['理論上的']]","chEntries":["抽象的","深奧的","非實體的","理論上的"],"practiceMeaning":"她的思考方式非常抽象。","analysis":"詞源來自拉丁文 'abstractus'，意為 'drawn away'，即分離、抽出。此字首 'abs-' 意為 'away'，'trahere' 意為 'to draw'。引申為非具體的、概念性的，與具體 'concrete' 相反。","definition":"1. existing in thought or as an idea but not having a physical or concrete existence; 2. relating to or involving general ideas or qualities rather than specific people, events, or things; 3. difficult to understand; abstruse; 4. (of art) not representing reality in a conventional way.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Love is an abstract concept.\",\n    \"ch\": \"愛是一個抽象的概念。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a very abstract way of thinking.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的思考方式非常抽象。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The book deals with abstract philosophical problems.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本書探討抽象的哲學問題。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她的思考方式非常抽象。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U41"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5507,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l5::burst::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She felt a ____ of anger.","expectedAnswer":"burst","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She felt a ____ of anger.","clozeAnswer":"burst","exampleTranslation":"她感到一陣憤怒。","reference":{"eng":"burst","kk":"bɜːrst","tense":"n.","ch":"[['爆炸'], ['迸發'], ['爆發']]","chEntries":["爆炸","迸發","爆發"],"practiceMeaning":"她感到一陣憤怒。","analysis":"此為動詞 'burst' 的名詞形式。作為名詞，它承襲了動詞的核心語義，指「爆炸」的事件或「情感、能量」的突然釋放。無獨立的構詞分析，由動詞轉換而來。語意演變與動詞一致，強調「瞬間的、劇烈的」現象。常用於描述物理爆炸或情感的突然爆發。","definition":"a sudden loud noise made by something bursting; a sudden short period of increased activity or strong emotion.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was a burst of gunfire.\",\n    \"ch\": \"傳來一陣槍響。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She felt a burst of anger.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她感到一陣憤怒。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她感到一陣憤怒。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4185,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::dust::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ the cake with powdered sugar.","expectedAnswer":"Dust","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ the cake with powdered sugar.","clozeAnswer":"Dust","exampleTranslation":"給蛋糕撒上糖粉。","reference":{"eng":"dust","kk":"/dʌst/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['撣去…的灰塵'], ['（灑上）粉末']]","chEntries":["撣去…的灰塵","粉末"],"practiceMeaning":"給蛋糕撒上糖粉。","analysis":"動詞 'dust' 源於名詞 'dust'，表示移除灰塵的動作（'dust off'）。此義項的詞源可追溯至古英語 'dustian'（撣去灰塵）。另一義項是“灑上粉末”，例如 'dust with flour'（用麵粉撒）。這兩個義項都與灰塵或粉末的物理特性相關：一個是清除，一個是覆蓋。","definition":"1. to remove the dust from something by wiping it with a cloth; 2. to sprinkle something with a powder such as flour or sugar.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please dust the shelves regularly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請定期擦拭架子上的灰塵。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Dust the cake with powdered sugar.\",\n    \"ch\": \"給蛋糕撒上糖粉。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He dusted off his old books.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他撣去了舊書上的灰塵。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"給蛋糕撒上糖粉。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6224,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::exterior::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The film was shot on location, with many ____ scenes.","expectedAnswer":"exterior","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The film was shot on location, with many ____ scenes.","clozeAnswer":"exterior","exampleTranslation":"這部電影是在外景地拍攝的，有很多戶外場景。","reference":{"eng":"exterior","kk":"ɪkˈstɪəriər","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"外觀\"  ],  [    \"外景\"  ],  [    \"外部\"  ]]","chEntries":["外觀","外景","外部"],"practiceMeaning":"這部電影是在外景地拍攝的，有很多戶外場景。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 exterior，是 externus（外面的）的比較級，意為「更外面的」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。名詞義指某物或某人的外部表面、外觀或外形，尤指建築物、車輛等的外部特徵。也指拍攝地點在戶外。中文翻譯為「外觀；外景；外部」。","definition":"1. the outer surface or structure of something; 2. a person's outward appearance and behavior; 3. a scene or location filmed outdoors.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The house has a beautiful brick exterior.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座房子有著美麗的磚砌外觀。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The film was shot on location, with many exterior scenes.\",\n    \"c