 the same time as someone or something else; 3. in addition to someone or something else; 4. supporting or cooperating with someone or something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The ship sailed alongside the coast.\",\n    \"ch\": \"船隻沿著海岸航行。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He sat alongside his wife at the wedding.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在婚禮上坐在他妻子旁邊。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We are working alongside our international partners.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們正與我們的國際夥伴一同合作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Alongside his main job, he volunteers at a shelter.\",\n    \"ch\": \"除了他的主要工作之外，他還在收容所做志工。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"船隻沿著海岸航行。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4136,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::appeal::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There was a strong ____ for donations.","expectedAnswer":"appeal","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There was a strong ____ for donations.","clozeAnswer":"appeal","exampleTranslation":"有強烈的捐款呼籲。","reference":{"eng":"appeal","kk":"/əˈpiːl/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['懇求', '請求'], ['吸引力'], ['上訴']]","chEntries":["懇求","請求","吸引力","上訴"],"practiceMeaning":"有強烈的捐款呼籲。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 appellare（向...呼籲，控告）。核心概念是「正式的請求」或「有吸引力的特質」。","definition":"1. an earnest or urgent request; 2. the quality in a person or thing that causes pleasure or satisfaction; 3. an application to a higher court for a decision to be canceled or changed","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was a strong appeal for donations.\",\n    \"ch\": \"有強烈的捐款呼籲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The movie has great appeal for young people.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這部電影對年輕人有很大的吸引力。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The lawyer filed an appeal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"律師提交了上訴。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"有強烈的捐款呼籲。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U5、L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3059,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::associate::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She was asked to ____ with the company's marketing team.","expectedAnswer":"associate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She was asked to ____ with the company's marketing team.","clozeAnswer":"associate","exampleTranslation":"她被要求與公司的行銷團隊合作。","reference":{"eng":"associate","kk":"/əˈsoʊʃieɪt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['使聯繫；與…交往'], ['認為…有關聯；把…視為夥伴'], ['聯合；合作']]","chEntries":["使聯繫","與…交往","認為…有關聯","把…視為夥伴","聯合","合作"],"practiceMeaning":"她被要求與公司的行銷團隊合作。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'associatus'，'ad-' (to, toward) + 'sociatus' (companion)。核心意義是「連結」或「成為夥伴」。\n1. 使聯繫；與…交往：強調人與人之間的連結與互動，常指建立社交或業務關係。\n2. 認為…有關聯；把…視為夥伴：將兩個事物或概念連結在一起，認為它們之間有某種關聯性。\n3. 聯合；合作：指兩個或多個個體或團體共同行動或目標。","definition":"1. join together for a common purpose; unite; connect; 2. consider as connected; link; 3. connect or join; accompany.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She was asked to associate with the company's marketing team.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她被要求與公司的行銷團隊合作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Many people associate wealth with happiness.\",\n    \"ch\": \"許多人將財富與幸福聯繫起來。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was the associate of a known criminal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是個已知罪犯的同夥。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她被要求與公司的行銷團隊合作。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6155,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::beware::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ of the dog.","expectedAnswer":"Beware","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ of the dog.","clozeAnswer":"Beware","exampleTranslation":"小心惡犬。","reference":{"eng":"beware","kk":"bɪˈwɛr","tense":"v.","ch":"[  [    \"警惕\"  ],  [    \"提防\"  ],  [    \"注意\"  ]]","chEntries":["警惕","提防","注意"],"practiceMeaning":"小心惡犬。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 be+ware，意為「注意、警覺」。ware 本身是古英語 wær 的變體，意為「警覺的」。此字通常作為一個獨立的動詞或感嘆詞使用，其核心語義是「對潛在的危險或困難保持警惕」。它的結構由介詞 be- (表示強調或作為動詞前綴) 和形容詞/過去分詞 ware (警覺的) 組成，暗示著一種主動的、持續的警覺狀態。","definition":"1. be careful of (someone or something), especially by avoiding danger or harm.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Beware of the dog.\",\n    \"ch\": \"小心惡犬。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Drivers should beware of icy roads in winter.\",\n    \"ch\": \"司機在冬天應提防結冰的路面。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Beware! He is known for his deceitful tactics.\",\n    \"ch\": \"小心！他以狡猾的策略聞名。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Beware of pickpockets in crowded areas.\",\n    \"ch\": \"在擁擠的地區要小心扒手。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"小心惡犬。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5822,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::blast::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of the explosion was heard for miles.","expectedAnswer":"blast","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of the explosion was heard for miles.","clozeAnswer":"blast","exampleTranslation":"爆炸的巨響遠達數英里。","reference":{"eng":"blast","kk":"blæst","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"爆炸\"  ],  [    \"衝擊波\"  ],  [    \"陣風\"  ],  [    \"巨響\"  ]]","chEntries":["爆炸","衝擊波","陣風","巨響"],"practiceMeaning":"爆炸的巨響遠達數英里。","analysis":"此字詞源不明確，可能與原始日耳曼語 *blastaz（氣息、風）或 *blastōną（吹響）有關，與 'blossom'、'blow' 等詞有關聯。早期用於表示「爆炸」或「衝擊」。字義的演變可能與聲音或空氣的突然釋放有關。一個突發的、強烈的聲音或氣流可以被描述為 'blast'。例如，爆炸的衝擊波，或突然而強烈的風。現代語義擴展至形容音樂的「震耳欲聾」或「強烈的氣流」。例如，也可指「吹奏樂器的響亮聲音」。","definition":"1. An explosion or detonation.; 2. A strong gust of wind.; 3. A loud, short blast of a musical instrument or a siren.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The blast of the explosion was heard for miles.\",\n    \"ch\": \"爆炸的巨響遠達數英里。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A strong blast of wind blew his hat off.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一陣強風吹掉了他的帽子。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The ship's horn gave a loud blast.\",\n    \"ch\": \"船的汽笛發出響亮的鳴響。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The music hit us with a blast of sound.\",\n    \"ch\": \"音樂以震耳欲聾的聲響衝擊著我們。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"爆炸的巨響遠達數英里。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5826,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::bolt::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He tightened the ____ on the door.","expectedAnswer":"bolt","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He tightened the ____ on the door.","clozeAnswer":"bolt","exampleTranslation":"他擰緊了門上的螺栓。","reference":{"eng":"bolt","kk":"boʊlt","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"螺栓\"  ],  [    \"門閂\"  ],  [    \"閃電\"  ],  [    \"閃電般的光\"  ]]","chEntries":["螺栓","門閂","閃電","閃電般的光"],"practiceMeaning":"他擰緊了門上的螺栓。","analysis":"此字有多個同形異源的來源。一來源是表示「門閂」、「槓桿」，來自古英語 'bolta' 或「橫樑」；另一來源是表示「閃電」、「快速跑」，可能與原始日耳曼語 *bult- (to bolt, to build) 或 *baltaz (swift) 有關。當指「門閂」時，其語意與「關閉」、「鎖定」相關。當指「閃電」時，則強調其突然、快速的爆發。另一常見義「螺栓」則是現代引申，借用了「鎖定」或「固定」的意象。還有「快速跑」的動詞義，也與「閃電」的突然性及速度相關。這裡的「閃電般的光」更側重於視覺上的突然出現。","definition":"1. A metal pin used to fasten things together, typically with a nut on the end.; 2. A bar used to fasten a door or gate.; 3. A flash of lightning.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He tightened the bolt on the door.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他擰緊了門上的螺栓。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She slid the bolt across the door.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她拉上門閂。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A bolt of lightning lit up the sky.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一道閃電劃破天空。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A bolt of light shot across the sky.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一道閃光劃過天際。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他擰緊了門上的螺栓。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3067,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::breed::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Many species of birds ____ in this region.","expectedAnswer":"breed","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Many species of birds ____ in this region.","clozeAnswer":"breed","exampleTranslation":"許多鳥類物種在此區域繁殖。","reference":{"eng":"breed","kk":"/briːd/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['繁殖；生育'], ['養育；培養'], ['引起；導致']]","chEntries":["繁殖","生育","養育","培養","引起","導致"],"practiceMeaning":"許多鳥類物種在此區域繁殖。","analysis":"源自古英語 'brēdan' (to nourish, to bring up, to make multiply)，與 'brood' (young of animals) 有關。核心意義是「繁衍」或「養育」。\n1. 繁殖；生育：指動物或植物產生後代的過程。\n2. 養育；培養：指細心照料、教育或發展某人或某物，使其成長。\n3. 引起；導致：指某事物是另一事物發生的原因。","definition":"1. to produce young animals or plants; 2. to keep animals and breed them for a particular purpose; 3. to cause a particular problem or situation to exist.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Many species of birds breed in this region.\",\n    \"ch\": \"許多鳥類物種在此區域繁殖。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was bred to be a doctor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他被培養成醫生。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Poverty can breed crime.\",\n    \"ch\": \"貧困可能導致犯罪。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"許多鳥類物種在此區域繁殖。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5506,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l5::burst::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The balloon ____ with a loud pop.","expectedAnswer":"burst","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The balloon ____ with a loud pop.","clozeAnswer":"burst","exampleTranslation":"氣球砰地一聲爆炸了。","reference":{"eng":"burst","kk":"bɜːrst","tense":"v.","ch":"[['爆炸'], ['迸發'], ['突然出現'], ['衝破'], ['充滿']]","chEntries":["爆炸","迸發","突然出現","衝破","充滿"],"practiceMeaning":"氣球砰地一聲爆炸了。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 'bursten' 或 'bresten'，與古英語 'berstan' 同源，後者可能來自原始日耳曼語 *berstana。其核心語義是「突然破裂」或「爆開」。構詞上，此字無明顯的字首、字根或字尾可供分析，應視為整體詞源演變。原始語義直接指向「破裂」的物理動作。現代英語中，'burst' 擴展為多種意義：指物體突然破裂（爆炸），指情感或能量突然釋放（迸發），指人或物突然出現或離開（衝破），或指充滿某種事物（充滿）。這些引申義都保留了「突然、瞬間」的特徵。","definition":"to break suddenly and unexpectedly; to appear or happen suddenly; to fill with strong emotion.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The balloon burst with a loud pop.\",\n    \"ch\": \"氣球砰地一聲爆炸了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Tears burst from her eyes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"眼淚奪眶而出。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The crowd burst into the stadium.\",\n    \"ch\": \"人群衝進了體育場。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"氣球砰地一聲爆炸了。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5828,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::chubby::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The baby had ____ cheeks.","expectedAnswer":"chubby","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The baby had ____ cheeks.","clozeAnswer":"chubby","exampleTranslation":"那個嬰兒有著圓胖的臉頰。","reference":{"eng":"chubby","kk":"ˈtʃʌbi","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"豐滿的\"  ],  [    \"胖乎乎的\"  ],  [    \"圓胖的\"  ],  [    \"圓潤的\"  ]]","chEntries":["豐滿的","胖乎乎的","圓胖的","圓潤的"],"practiceMeaning":"那個嬰兒有著圓胖的臉頰。","analysis":"此字源於 'chub'，原指一種胖魚（如鯉魚的一種），後來用來形容人或物的圓胖、豐滿。'Chub' 本身來源不明，可能與「腫脹」或「凸起」的語感有關。'-y' 是常見的形容詞字尾，表示「具有……性質的」。'Chubby' 的語意核心是「圓胖、豐滿」，通常帶有可愛、健康的意味，多用於形容嬰兒、兒童或臉頰。它描述的是一種溫和、無攻擊性的肥胖感。例如，也可指「圓潤的」手指或四肢。","definition":"1. (of a person, especially a child) plump; well-rounded.; 2. (of a part of a person's body) rounded and plump.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The baby had chubby cheeks.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那個嬰兒有著圓胖的臉頰。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was a chubby boy with a cheerful smile.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一個胖乎乎但笑容開朗的男孩。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a chubby face.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她有一張豐滿的臉。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The child's chubby fingers reached for the toy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子圓潤的手指伸向了玩具。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"那個嬰兒有著圓胖的臉頰。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5575,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::code::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The programmer wrote the ____ for the new app.","expectedAnswer":"code","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The programmer wrote the ____ for the new app.","clozeAnswer":"code","exampleTranslation":"程式設計師編寫了新應用程式的代碼。","reference":{"eng":"code","kk":"koʊd","tense":"n.","ch":"[['代碼'], ['密碼'], ['編碼'], ['規範'], ['程式碼']]","chEntries":["代碼","密碼","編碼","規範","程式碼"],"practiceMeaning":"程式設計師編寫了新應用程式的代碼。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 \"codex\"，意為 \"book, manuscript, trunk of a tree\"（書本，手稿，樹幹）。\"codex\" 最初是指一種由多張羊皮紙或蠟板黏合而成的書寫形式，與捲軸形式相對。因此，\"code\" 最初指「裝訂好的書冊」或「手稿」。其語義演變包括：指「法律條文的彙編」（a body of laws）；指「一套規則或準則」（a system of rules or principles），例如「行為準則」；在現代，尤其指「用於數據傳輸或儲存的符號系統」（a system of symbols used to transmit or store data），例如「電腦程式碼」、「密碼」或「暗碼」。","definition":"1. A system of words, letters, figures, or symbols used to represent others, especially for the purposes of secrecy; 2. A set of rules or principles, especially one governing the conduct of people or the procedure in a particular activity; 3. A program for a computer written in a particular programming language.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The programmer wrote the code for the new app.\",\n    \"ch\": \"程式設計師編寫了新應用程式的代碼。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This building has strict building codes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這棟建築有嚴格的建築規範。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He used a secret code to send the message.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他使用一種密碼發送了這則訊息。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company has a code of conduct for its employees.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司有員工行為準則。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"程式設計師編寫了新應用程式的代碼。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6212,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::combat::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The soldiers were trained for ____.","expectedAnswer":"combat","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The soldiers were trained for ____.","clozeAnswer":"combat","exampleTranslation":"士兵們接受了戰鬥訓練。","reference":{"eng":"combat","kk":"ˈkɒmbæt","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"戰鬥\"  ],  [    \"戰爭\"  ],  [    \"鬥爭\"  ],  [    \"搏鬥\"  ]]","chEntries":["戰鬥","戰爭","鬥爭","搏鬥"],"practiceMeaning":"士兵們接受了戰鬥訓練。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 combat，由 com-（一起）和 batre（打擊）組成，意為「共同打擊」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。名詞義指軍隊或個人之間進行的激烈對抗、武裝衝突或搏鬥，也引申為任何形式的鬥爭或抗爭。中文翻譯為「戰鬥；戰爭；鬥爭；搏鬥」。","definition":"1. fighting between armed forces; 2. fighting or struggling against something, such as a problem or a disease.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The soldiers were trained for combat.\",\n    \"ch\": \"士兵們接受了戰鬥訓練。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The country has been involved in a protracted combat with rebels.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該國捲入了與叛軍的長期戰鬥。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This organization is dedicated to the combat of poverty.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個組織致力於與貧困作鬥爭。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"士兵們接受了戰鬥訓練。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4341,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::comfort::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She tried to ____ her crying child.","expectedAnswer":"comfort","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She tried to ____ her crying child.","clozeAnswer":"comfort","exampleTranslation":"她試圖安慰她哭泣的孩子。","reference":{"eng":"comfort","kk":"/ˈkʌmfərt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['安慰；慰藉']]","chEntries":["安慰","慰藉"],"practiceMeaning":"她試圖安慰她哭泣的孩子。","analysis":"動詞形式，源自拉丁語 'confortare'，意為『使堅強、使有力』，引申為『使心情舒暢、得到慰藉』。指『安慰』某人，減輕其痛苦、悲傷或焦慮。","definition":"to make someone feel less unhappy, worried, or disappointed","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She tried to comfort her crying child.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她試圖安慰她哭泣的孩子。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was comforted by the thought that he was not alone.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他想到自己並不孤單，心裡得到了一些安慰。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her presence comforted him during his illness.\",\n    \"ch\": \"在她生病期間，她的陪伴讓他感到欣慰。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她試圖安慰她哭泣的孩子。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U8、L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6216,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::commitment::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He made a ____ to finish the project on time.","expectedAnswer":"commitment","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He made a ____ to finish the project on time.","clozeAnswer":"commitment","exampleTranslation":"他承諾按時完成這個項目。","reference":{"eng":"commitment","kk":"kəˈmɪtmənt","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"承諾\"  ],  [    \"保證\"  ],  [    \"投入\"  ],  [    \"奉獻\"  ],  [    \"責任\"  ],  [    \"委身\"  ]]","chEntries":["承諾","保證","投入","奉獻","責任","委身"],"practiceMeaning":"他承諾按時完成這個項目。","analysis":"此字由動詞 commit（承諾；委託；犯罪）加上名詞字尾 -ment（表示狀態、行為、結果）構成。commit 源自拉丁語 committere，意為「交付；委託」。字尾 -ment 將動詞轉為名詞，表示「承諾的行為或狀態」、「盡責的狀態」、「奉獻的狀態」。核心語義是將自己投入某事，或對某事做出堅定的保證。中文翻譯為「承諾；保證；投入；奉獻；責任；委身」。","definition":"1. a promise to do something or to behave in a particular way; 2. the state or quality of being dedicated to a cause, activity, etc.; 3. a long-term obligation or responsibility.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He made a commitment to finish the project on time.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他承諾按時完成這個項目。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her commitment to her work is admirable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對工作的投入令人欽佩。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Marriage is a serious commitment.\",\n    \"ch\": \"婚姻是一項嚴肅的承諾。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They have a strong commitment to environmental protection.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們對環保有堅定的承諾。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他承諾按時完成這個項目。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6164,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::deliberate::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The decision was the result of a ____ choice.","expectedAnswer":"deliberate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The decision was the result of a ____ choice.","clozeAnswer":"deliberate","exampleTranslation":"這個決定是經過深思熟慮的選擇的結果。","reference":{"eng":"deliberate","kk":"dɪˈlɪbərət","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"故意的\"  ],  [    \"蓄意的\"  ],  [    \"審慎的\"  ],  [    \"計畫好的\"  ]]","chEntries":["故意的","蓄意的","審慎的","計畫好的"],"practiceMeaning":"這個決定是經過深思熟慮的選擇的結果。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 dēlīberātus，是 dēlīberāre「仔細考慮、權衡」的過去分詞。dēlīberāre 由 de- (down, completely) + lībra (balance, scale) 組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 de-「完全」和 lībra「秤」是其核心語意來源。作為形容詞，其核心語義是「經過仔細考慮而做出的」。詞源中的「權衡」概念引申出「蓄意的、計畫好的、非偶然的」。","definition":"1. done consciously and intentionally; 2. characterized by careful thought and consideration; 3. slow and careful.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The decision was the result of a deliberate choice.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個決定是經過深思熟慮的選擇的結果。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His remarks were deliberately offensive.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的言論是蓄意冒犯的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She took a deliberate step forward.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她謹慎地向前邁出一步。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The plan was a deliberate attempt to mislead the public.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個計畫是為了誤導公眾而蓄意為之的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個決定是經過深思熟慮的選擇的結果。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5473,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::elaborate::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They wore ____ costumes to the party.","expectedAnswer":"elaborate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They wore ____ costumes to the party.","clozeAnswer":"elaborate","exampleTranslation":"他們穿著精心製作的服裝去參加派對。","reference":{"eng":"elaborate","kk":"iˈlæbərət","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['精緻的'], ['詳盡的'], ['精心製作的']]","chEntries":["精緻的","詳盡的","精心製作的"],"practiceMeaning":"他們穿著精心製作的服裝去參加派對。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'elaboratus'，是動詞 'elaborare'（努力工作、精製）的過去分詞。'Elaborare' 由 'e-'（出、完全）和 'laborare'（工作，來自 'labor'「勞動、工作」）構成。因此，'elaborate' 在形容詞形式下，表示「經過精心製作、詳盡闡述、內容豐富、細節繁多」的狀態。其核心語意是「付出了大量努力和細節」。","definition":"1. Involving many carefully arranged parts or details; detailed and complicated in design and planning.; 2. Developed or executed with great care and thoroughness.; 3. Intricate and richly decorated.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They wore elaborate costumes to the party.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們穿著精心製作的服裝去參加派對。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The report provided an elaborate analysis of the situation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這份報告對情況進行了詳盡的分析。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The architect designed an elaborate building with many ornate features.\",\n    \"ch\": \"建築師設計了一座精緻的建築，有許多華麗的特色。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們穿著精心製作的服裝去參加派對。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5837,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::evolution::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Darwin's theory of ____ revolutionized biology.","expectedAnswer":"evolution","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Darwin's theory of ____ revolutionized biology.","clozeAnswer":"evolution","exampleTranslation":"達爾文的演化論使生物學產生了革命性的變化。","reference":{"eng":"evolution","kk":"ˌɛvəˈluːʃn","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"演化\"  ],  [    \"進化\"  ],  [    \"發展\"  ],  [    \"演變\"  ]]","chEntries":["演化","進化","發展","演變"],"practiceMeaning":"達爾文的演化論使生物學產生了革命性的變化。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'evolutio'，由 'evolvere' (to unfold, to unroll) 構成。'Evolvere' 由 'e-' (out) 和 'volvere' (to roll) 組成。'Evolutio' 的字面意思是「展開」、「展開的過程」。最初用於指「翻書」或「展開捲軸」。後來，其語意引申至生物學，指生物體經過漫長時期，通過自然選擇等機制，發生遺傳變異並適應環境的過程，即「演化」或「進化」。也可用於形容社會、思想、技術等方面的漸進式「發展」或「演變」。","definition":"1. The process by which different kinds of living organism are believed to have developed from earlier forms during the history of the earth.; 2. The gradual development of something, especially from a simple to a more complex form.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Darwin's theory of evolution revolutionized biology.\",\n    \"ch\": \"達爾文的演化論使生物學產生了革命性的變化。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The evolution of language is a fascinating subject.\",\n    \"ch\": \"語言的演變是一個引人入勝的主題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company has undergone significant evolution in recent years.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司近年來經歷了顯著的發展。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The evolution of technology has been rapid.\",\n    \"ch\": \"科技的發展是迅速的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"達爾文的演化論使生物學產生了革命性的變化。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4202,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::exchange::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"I'd like to ____ this shirt for a different size.","expectedAnswer":"exchange","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"I'd like to ____ this shirt for a different size.","clozeAnswer":"exchange","exampleTranslation":"我想把這件襯衫換成別的尺寸。","reference":{"eng":"exchange","kk":"/ɪksˈtʃeɪndʒ/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['交換；兌換'], ['交流；溝通'], ['（在兩國或兩個組織間）交換']]","chEntries":["交換","兌換","交流","溝通"],"practiceMeaning":"我想把這件襯衫換成別的尺寸。","analysis":"源自古法語 escanger，意為“交換”，來自拉丁語 excitangere，'ex-'（出）+ 'tangere'（觸摸，接觸）。核心是“相互接觸並轉移”。1. “交換；兌換”指用一種東西換另一種，或用貨幣換另一種貨幣。2. “交流；溝通”指思想、資訊的相互傳遞。3. “在兩國或兩個組織間交換”是特定領域的應用。","definition":"1. to give one thing and receive another in return; 2. to communicate with someone by giving them information and receiving information from them; 3. to transfer between two countries or two organizations.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I'd like to exchange this shirt for a different size.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我想把這件襯衫換成別的尺寸。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They exchanged ideas on how to improve the project.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們就如何改進項目交換了意見。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The students will exchange with a school in France.\",\n    \"ch\": \"學生們將與一所法國學校進行交換。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我想把這件襯衫換成別的尺寸。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4067,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::experiment::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The scientist conducted an ____ to test his theory.","expectedAnswer":"experiment","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The scientist conducted an ____ to test his theory.","clozeAnswer":"experiment","exampleTranslation":"這位科學家進行了一項實驗來驗證他的理論。","reference":{"eng":"experiment","kk":"/ɪkˈspɛrɪmənt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['實驗']]","chEntries":["實驗"],"practiceMeaning":"這位科學家進行了一項實驗來驗證他的理論。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'experimentum'，由 'experiri' (to try, to test) 構成，'experiri' 又由 'ex-' (out) + 'periri' (to try) 構成。核心是「嘗試」、「測試」。因此，'experiment' 指通過觀察和測試來檢驗某個理論或發現新知識的過程。","definition":"a scientific test done in order to learn how something happens or to check if a particular idea is true","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"這位科學家進行了一項實驗來驗證他的理論。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The scientist conducted an experiment to test his theory.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個危險的實驗。\",\n    \"eng\": \"This is a dangerous experiment.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"實驗結果沒有定論。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The results of the experiment were inconclusive.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這位科學家進行了一項實驗來驗證他的理論。","sourceName":"文華