mand.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The navy deployed a fleet of ships.\",\n    \"ch\": \"海軍部署了一支艦隊。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The airline operates a large fleet of aircraft.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家航空公司運營著龐大的機隊。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A fleet of taxis waited outside the station.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一群計程車在車站外等候。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"海軍部署了一支艦隊。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6173,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::forum::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The internet ____ is a popular place for discussion.","expectedAnswer":"forum","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The internet ____ is a popular place for discussion.","clozeAnswer":"forum","exampleTranslation":"網路論壇是一個受歡迎的討論場所。","reference":{"eng":"forum","kk":"ˈfɔrəm","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"論壇\"  ],  [    \"討論會\"  ],  [    \"廣場\"  ],  [    \"（辯論、討論的）場所\"  ]]","chEntries":["論壇","討論會","廣場","場所"],"practiceMeaning":"網路論壇是一個受歡迎的討論場所。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 forum，意為「公共場所、市場、廣場」。在古羅馬，它是舉行公共集會、辯論和商業活動的中心。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作為名詞，其核心語義是「一個用於公開討論、辯論或交流意見的場所或場合」。此義項由古羅馬時期的「公共廣場」引申出「討論會」和「論壇」的現代用法。","definition":"1. a place, meeting, or medium where ideas and views on a particular issue can be exchanged; 2. a public meeting or lecture, typically held in a university or college, at which invited speakers debate a topic of current interest.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The internet forum is a popular place for discussion.\",\n    \"ch\": \"網路論壇是一個受歡迎的討論場所。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The forum will focus on environmental issues.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這次討論會將聚焦於環境議題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's an open forum for all members to express their views.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是個讓所有成員表達意見的公開論壇。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They held a town hall forum on public safety.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們就公共安全問題舉行了市政廳論壇。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"網路論壇是一個受歡迎的討論場所。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5085,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::foul::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He had to clean the ____ smell from his room.","expectedAnswer":"foul","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He had to clean the ____ smell from his room.","clozeAnswer":"foul","exampleTranslation":"他不得不清除房間裡的惡臭。","reference":{"eng":"foul","kk":"faʊl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['骯髒的'], ['污穢的'], ['惡劣的']]","chEntries":["骯髒的","污穢的","惡劣的"],"practiceMeaning":"他不得不清除房間裡的惡臭。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 'fūl'，與德語 'faul' (rotten) 同源，原始語義為 '腐爛的、惡臭的'。其核心概念是 '不乾淨、不道德或令人不悅的'。這可以指物理上的汙穢，如 'foul water' (髒水)；也可以指道德上的卑劣，如 'foul play' (不正當的手段)；或者指天氣的惡劣，如 'foul weather' (惡劣天氣)。","definition":"1. Very dirty; polluted.; 2. Extremely unpleasant or disagreeable.; 3. (In sports) Against the rules; unfair.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He had to clean the foul smell from his room.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他不得不清除房間裡的惡臭。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The referee called a foul for rough play.\",\n    \"ch\": \"裁判因粗野的犯規判罰了一個犯規。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The weather turned foul during the night.\",\n    \"ch\": \"夜裡天氣變得惡劣。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他不得不清除房間裡的惡臭。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5787,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::grip::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He lost his ____ on the rope and fell.","expectedAnswer":"grip","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He lost his ____ on the rope and fell.","clozeAnswer":"grip","exampleTranslation":"他鬆開了繩索的抓握，掉了下去。","reference":{"eng":"grip","kk":"ɡrɪp","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"緊握\"  ],  [    \"抓牢\"  ],  [    \"控制\"  ],  [    \"吸引力\"  ],  [    \"握把\"  ]]","chEntries":["緊握","抓牢","控制","吸引力","握把"],"practiceMeaning":"他鬆開了繩索的抓握，掉了下去。","analysis":"此字為名詞，與動詞同源，源自中古英語gripen。核心語義是指「用力抓住或握緊的動作或狀態」，或「被抓住的物體」。引申為「控制」、「掌握」，以及「對人產生的強烈吸引力或影響力」。此外，也可指工具或武器上的「握把」。語意演變上，從「抓握」的動作，發展出「控制」、「吸引力」等抽象意義，以及「握把」這類具體名詞。","definition":"1. a firm hold or grasp; 2. control or power over someone or something; 3. the ability to attract and hold people's attention or interest; 4. the part of the handle of a tool or weapon that is held in the hand.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He lost his grip on the rope and fell.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他鬆開了繩索的抓握，掉了下去。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The book has a strong grip on the imagination.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本書對想像力有很強的吸引力。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The pen has a comfortable grip.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這支筆有一個舒適的握把。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他鬆開了繩索的抓握，掉了下去。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5840,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::immune::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Children are often ____ to common colds after exposure.","expectedAnswer":"immune","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Children are often ____ to common colds after exposure.","clozeAnswer":"immune","exampleTranslation":"孩子們在接觸後通常對普通感冒產生免疫。","reference":{"eng":"immune","kk":"ɪˈmjuːn","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"免疫的\"  ],  [    \"不受影響的\"  ],  [    \"免於……的\"  ],  [    \"豁免的\"  ]]","chEntries":["免疫的","不受影響的","免於……的","豁免的"],"practiceMeaning":"孩子們在接觸後通常對普通感冒產生免疫。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'immūnis'，由 'in-' (not) 和 'mūnus' (duty, service, gift) 構成。'Immūnis' 的字面意思是「不受……負擔的」或「免除……義務的」。最初用於指免稅或免於公共服務的人。在醫學上，'immune' 指身體對某種疾病或病原體產生抵抗力，不再容易受到感染。這也與「不受……侵害」的核心意義相符。引申義則指「不受……影響」或「免於……」。例如，也可指「免除……責任的」。","definition":"1. Protected against a particular disease.; 2. Not affected or influenced by something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Children are often immune to common colds after exposure.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子們在接觸後通常對普通感冒產生免疫。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He seems immune to criticism.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他似乎不受批評的影響。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company is immune from prosecution.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司免於起訴。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Diplomats are often immune from local laws.\",\n    \"ch\": \"外交官員通常豁免於當地法律。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"孩子們在接觸後通常對普通感冒產生免疫。","sourceNam