ow::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We walked down a ____ alley.","expectedAnswer":"narrow","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We walked down a ____ alley.","clozeAnswer":"narrow","exampleTranslation":"我們走過一條狹窄的巷子。","reference":{"eng":"narrow","kk":"ˈnæroʊ","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['狹窄的'], ['狹小的'], ['（範圍、機會等）有限的'], ['（視野、思想等）狹隘的'], ['（聲音）尖銳的']]","chEntries":["狹窄的","狹小的","有限的","狹隘的","尖銳的"],"practiceMeaning":"我們走過一條狹窄的巷子。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 narow，可能來自古英語 nearu，意為「窄的」。其詞源與原始日耳曼語 *nauraz（窄）相關，更上溯至原始印歐語 *ner-（左；左邊；在左邊）或 *en-（在內）。此字的核心語義是「空間上的狹窄」，並由此引申出範圍、機會、思想、視野的「有限」或「狹隘」。構詞上，此字為單一詞根，無明顯字首字尾。此處為形容詞用法，描述名詞的空間、範圍、程度或性質。","definition":"limited in width; small in distance from one side to the other; restricted in scope, opportunity, or vision; sharp or high-pitched in sound.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We walked down a narrow alley.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們走過一條狹窄的巷子。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company faces narrow profit margins.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司面臨著狹窄的利潤空間。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has very narrow views on social issues.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在社會議題上有著非常狹隘的觀點。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們走過一條狹窄的巷子。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5671,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l8::negative::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The answer was a clear ____.","expectedAnswer":"negative","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The answer was a clear ____.","clozeAnswer":"negative","exampleTranslation":"答案是明確的否定。","reference":{"eng":"negative","kk":"ˈnɛɡətɪv","tense":"n.","ch":"[['否定'], ['否定詞'], ['負數'], ['（攝影）負片']]","chEntries":["否定","否定詞","負數","負片"],"practiceMeaning":"答案是明確的否定。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 negativus，來自 negare（否認，to deny），其根源為 ne-（不，not）+ -are（動詞字尾）。ne- 來自原始印歐語 *ne-（不）。核心語義為「否認」、「拒絕」或「沒有」。構詞上，ne- 提供「否定」的概念，-gativus 為形容詞後綴，此處轉為名詞用法。此處為名詞用法，指代「否定」、「負面的事物」或「負數」。","definition":"a word or statement that denies or contradicts something; a number less than zero; a photographic image that has reversed light and shade.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The answer was a clear negative.\",\n    \"ch\": \"答案是明確的否定。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The doctor's initial assessment was negative.\",\n    \"ch\": \"醫生的初步評估是陰性的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"答案是明確的否定。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4420,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u9::opposite::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He sat ____ me at the table.","expectedAnswer":"opposite","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He sat ____ me at the table.","clozeAnswer":"opposite","exampleTranslation":"他坐在桌子對面。","reference":{"eng":"opposite","kk":"/ˈɒpəzɪt/","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['在對面']]","chEntries":["在對面"],"practiceMeaning":"他坐在桌子對面。","analysis":"表示位置在相對的一方。","definition":"facing someone or something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He sat opposite me at the table.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他坐在桌子對面。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他坐在桌子對面。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5850,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::partly::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The success was ____ due to luck.","expectedAnswer":"partly","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The success was ____ due to luck.","clozeAnswer":"partly","exampleTranslation":"成功的部分原因在於運氣。","reference":{"eng":"partly","kk":"ˈpɑːrtli","tense":"adv.","ch":"[  [    \"部分地\"  ],  [    \"在某種程度上\"  ],  [    \"多少\"  ]]","chEntries":["部分地","在某種程度上","多少"],"practiceMeaning":"成功的部分原因在於運氣。","analysis":"此字由 'part' (部分) 加上副詞字尾 '-ly' 構成。'Part' 源自拉丁語 'partire' (to divide)。'-ly' 是常見的副詞字尾，將名詞或形容詞轉化為副詞。'Partly' 的核心語意是「不是完全地」、「在一定程度上」，表示某事物僅部分實現或僅部分為真。例如，也可指「有一定程度地」。","definition":"1. To some extent; in part.; 2. Not completely.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The success was partly due to luck.\",\n    \"ch\": \"成功的部分原因在於運氣。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was partly responsible for the accident