r behavior) deliberately and mischievously unconventional and playful; 2. chief; principal.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She gave him an arch look.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她朝他投以一個狡黠的眼神。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was the arch-rival of the champion.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是冠軍的主要對手。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他是冠軍的主要對手。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4523,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::attribute::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Scientists ____ the cause of the disease to a virus.","expectedAnswer":"attribute","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Scientists ____ the cause of the disease to a virus.","clozeAnswer":"attribute","exampleTranslation":"科學家將該疾病的原因歸因於一種病毒。","reference":{"eng":"attribute","kk":"/əˈtrɪbjuːt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['歸因於'], ['認為...是...所特有']]","chEntries":["歸因於","認為...是...所特有"],"practiceMeaning":"科學家將該疾病的原因歸因於一種病毒。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 attribuere，意為「賦予」、「歸於」。ad- (向) + tribuere (給予)。核心語意是「將某物歸於某人或某事」。","definition":"1. Regard something as being caused by (someone or something).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He attributed his success to hard work.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他將自己的成功歸功於勤奮工作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Scientists attribute the cause of the disease to a virus.\",\n    \"ch\": \"科學家將該疾病的原因歸因於一種病毒。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"科學家將該疾病的原因歸因於一種病毒。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、字彙王","unitName":"C3U10、U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3903,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::besides::prep","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ the car, he owns a motorcycle.","expectedAnswer":"Besides","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ the car, he owns a motorcycle.","clozeAnswer":"Besides","exampleTranslation":"除了汽車，他還擁有一輛摩托車。","reference":{"eng":"besides","kk":"/bɪˈsaɪdz/","tense":"prep.","ch":"[['除了…之外（還有）']]","chEntries":["除了…之外"],"practiceMeaning":"除了汽車，他還擁有一輛摩托車。","analysis":"由 'by' (在旁) + 'side' (邊) + '-s' 組成。核心是「在…旁邊」。引申為「除了」，表示在原有事物之外，還有其他的東西，包含被提及的事物。","definition":"in addition to; apart from.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Besides English, she speaks French.\",\n    \"ch\": \"除了英語，她還說法語。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Besides the car, he owns a motorcycle.\",\n    \"ch\": \"除了汽車，他還擁有一輛摩托車。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"除了汽車，他還擁有一輛摩托車。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5821,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::biological::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Genetic engineering has many ____ applications.","expectedAnswer":"biological","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Genetic engineering has many ____ applications.","clozeAnswer":"biological","exampleTranslation":"基因工程有許多生物學上的應用。","reference":{"eng":"biological","kk":"ˌbaɪəˈlɑːdʒɪkl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"生物的\"  ],  [    \"生物學的\"  ],  [    \"生理的\"  ]]","chEntries":["生物的","生物學的","生理的"],"practiceMeaning":"基因工程有許多生物學上的應用。","analysis":"此字由名詞 'biology' 加上形容詞字尾 '-ical' 構成。'Biology' 本身是一個複合詞，來自希臘語 'bios' (life) 和 '-logia' (study of, discourse)。'-logia' 來自 'logos' (word, speech, reason)。因此，'biology' 的字面意思是「生命的學問」。'-ical' 字尾用於將名詞轉化為形容詞，表示「關於……的」、「屬於……的」、「具有……性質的」。所以 'biological' 的意思就是「關於生物的」或「屬於生物學的」。另外，也可指「與生命體正常機能相關的」，即「生理的」。","definition":"1. Relating to or resulting from the functions of living organisms.; 2. Relating to biology.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The research focuses on biological processes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這項研究聚焦於生物過程。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Genetic engineering has many biological applications.\",\n    \"ch\": \"基因工程有許多生物學上的應用。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to consider the biological impact of the pollution.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要考慮污染的生物影響。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The drug has a strong biological effect.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種藥物有強烈的生理效應。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"基因工程有許多生物學上的應用。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5825,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::blur::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His vision began to ____.","expectedAnswer":"blur","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His vision began to ____.","clozeAnswer":"blur","exampleTranslation":"他的視線開始模糊。","reference":{"eng":"blur","kk":"blər","tense":"v.","ch":"[  [    \"使模糊\"  ],  [    \"變得模糊\"  ],  [    \"混淆\"  ]]","chEntries":["使模糊","變得模糊","混淆"],"practiceMeaning":"他的視線開始模糊。","analysis":"此動詞形式與名詞形式同源。其核心語意是「使某物變得不清晰」或「自身變得不清晰」。'Blur' 作動詞時，指通過移動、塗抹、或使之模糊不清，使之難以辨認。這種模糊可能是物理上的（如鏡頭失焦）或概念上的（如混淆界線）。字源上可能與「模糊」的聲音或視覺感受有關，表示一種「失焦」或「混雜」的狀態。也可指「混淆」界線或概念，使其難以區分。","definition":"1. To make or become indistinct or hazy.; 2. To smudge or stain.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The rain blurred the windows.\",\n    \"ch\": \"雨水模糊了窗戶。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His vision began to blur.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的視線開始模糊。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The lines between the two concepts blurred.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這兩個概念之間的界線變得模糊了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Fast movement blurred the image.\",\n    \"ch\": \"快速的移動使影像變得模糊。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他的視線開始模糊。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6160,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::collaboration::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Their ____ resulted in a groundbreaking discovery.","expectedAnswer":"collaboration","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Their ____ resulted in a groundbreaking discovery.","clozeAnswer":"collaboration","exampleTranslation":"他們的協作促成了一項開創性的發現。","reference":{"eng":"collaboration","kk":"kəˌlæbəˈreɪʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"合作\"  ],  [    \"協作\"  ]]","chEntries":["合作","協作"],"practiceMeaning":"他們的協作促成了一項開創性的發現。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 collaboratio，由 collaborare「一起工作」名詞化而來。collaborare 由 com- (together) + laborare (to work) 組成，laborare 又源自 labor (work)。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 com-「一起」和 labor「工作」是其核心語意來源。作為名詞，其核心語義是「兩個或多個個體或團體為達成共同目標而共同工作」。詞源中的「一起工作」清晰地表達了此義。","definition":"1. the action of working with someone to produce or create something; 2. a joint effort.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The project was a successful collaboration between the two departments.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個專案是兩個部門之間成功的合作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Their collaboration resulted in a groundbreaking discovery.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們的協作促成了一項開創性的發現。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Artistic collaboration often leads to innovative results.\",\n    \"ch\": \"藝術上的合作經常帶來創新的成果。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The collaboration lasted for five years.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這次合作持續了五年。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們的協作促成了一項開創性的發現。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6163,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::collector::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The tax ____ visited the household.","expectedAnswer":"collector","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The tax ____ visited the household.","clozeAnswer":"collector","exampleTranslation":"稅吏拜訪了這個家庭。","reference":{"eng":"collector","kk":"kəˈlɛktər","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"收集者\"  ],  [    \"收藏家\"  ],  [    \"稅吏\"  ],  [    \"收賬員\"  ]]","chEntries":["收集者","收藏家","稅吏","收賬員"],"practiceMeaning":"稅吏拜訪了這個家庭。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 collectorem，是動詞 colligere「收集、聚集」的施事者名詞。colligere 由 com- (together) + legere (to gather) 組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 com-「一起」和 legere「收集」是其核心語意來源。作為名詞，其核心語義是「收集某物的人」。詞源中的「一起收集」概念引申為「從眾多事物中聚集、收起」的動作者。除了指收藏家，也用於指負責徵收稅款或債務的人。","definition":"1. a person who collects things of a particular type as a hobby or profession; 2. a person whose job is to collect money that is owed to a company or the government.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is an avid collector of rare stamps.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一位熱情的稀有郵票收藏家。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The tax collector visited the household.\",\n    \"ch\": \"稅吏拜訪了這個家庭。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a collector of antique furniture.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是古董傢俱的收藏家。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The collector ensured all debts were paid.\",\n    \"ch\": \"收賬員確保所有債務都已支付。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"稅吏拜訪了這個家庭。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5832,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::compatible::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They are a ____ couple.","expectedAnswer":"compatible","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They are a ____ couple.","clozeAnswer":"compatible","exampleTranslation":"他們是一對很合適的伴侶。","reference":{"eng":"compatible","kk":"kəmˈpætəbl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"兼容的\"  ],  [    \"相容的\"  ],  [    \"協調的\"  ],  [    \"適合的\"  ]]","chEntries":["兼容的","相容的","協調的","適合的"],"practiceMeaning":"他們是一對很合適的伴侶。","analysis":"此字由拉丁語 'compatibilis' 演變而來，由 'com-' (with) 和 'pati' (to suffer, endure) 構成。'Patibilis' 意為「可承受的」。'Compatibilis' 的字面意思是「可以一起承受」或「可以共存」。在現代英語中，'compatible' 指兩個或多個事物能夠一起良好運作、和諧共處，或在功能上相互適用。這可以是指電腦系統、軟體、硬體之間的「兼容性」，也可以是指人際關係中的「協調」或「適合」。核心概念是「能夠和諧共存或協作」。例如，也可指「性情相投的」。","definition":"1. (of two things) able to exist or occur together without conflict.; 2. (of computer hardware or software) able to be used or run together.; 3. (of a person) having a compatible nature or disposition.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This software is not compatible with older versions.\",\n    \"ch\": \"此軟體與舊版本不兼容。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They are a compatible couple.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們是一對很合適的伴侶。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Ensure the devices are compatible before connecting them.\",\n    \"ch\": \"連接設備前，請確保它們是兼容的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Their personalities were highly compatible.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們的性情非常協調。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們是一對很合適的伴侶。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3131,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::crush::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She had a huge ____ on her history teacher.","expectedAnswer":"crush","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She had a huge ____ on her history teacher.","clozeAnswer":"crush","exampleTranslation":"她對她的歷史老師有強烈的迷戀。","reference":{"eng":"crush","kk":"/krʌʃ/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['壓碎；壓扁'], ['（使）粉碎'], ['（在愛情上）迷戀，暗戀'], ['擊敗；壓制']]","chEntries":["壓碎","壓扁","粉碎","迷戀，暗戀","擊敗","壓制"],"practiceMeaning":"她對她的歷史老師有強烈的迷戀。","analysis":"詞源不明，可能與擬聲有關，模擬「壓碎」的聲音。'Crush' 的核心概念是「用力擠壓，使變形或破碎」。它可以是物理上的壓碎（將堅硬物體弄碎），也可以是使人或物體感到巨大的壓力或無力感。愛情上的「crush」是指強烈的、往往是一時的迷戀，可能帶有「被壓倒」的感受。擊敗或壓制則表示用強大的力量讓對方屈服。","definition":"1. to press something so hard that it is broken or flattened; 2. to defeat or dishearten someone completely; 3. to have a strong romantic feeling for someone, often briefly; 4. to grind or pulp something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The heavy truck crushed the car.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那輛重型卡車壓毀了這輛車。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She had a huge crush on her history teacher.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對她的歷史老師有強烈的迷戀。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The rebellion was brutally crushed.\",\n    \"ch\": \"叛亂被殘酷地鎮壓了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He crushed the empty soda can.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他把空的汽水罐壓扁了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她對她的歷史老師有強烈的迷戀。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6167,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::denial::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She lived in ____ about her illness.","expectedAnswer":"denial","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She lived in ____ about her illness.","clozeAnswer":"denial","exampleTranslation":"她對自己的病情一直處於否認狀態。","reference":{"eng":"denial","kk":"dɪˈnaɪəl","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"否認\"  ],  [    \"否定\"  ],  [    \"拒絕承認\"  ],  [    \"拒絕給予\"  ]]","chEntries":["否認","否定","拒絕承認","拒絕給予"],"practiceMeaning":"她對自己的病情一直處於否認狀態。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 denegare，意為「否認、拒絕」，由 de- (away, negating) + negare (to deny) 組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 de-「否定」和 negare「否認」是其核心語意來源。作為名詞，其核心語義是由動詞 deny「否認」名詞化而來，指「拒絕承認事實或真實性」，也指「拒絕給予某物」。詞源中的「否定」概念是其核心。此義項由「否認」的動作延伸出「拒絕承認」或「拒絕給予」的結果。","definition":"1. the action of declaring something to be untrue; 2. an act of refusing to acknowledge or accept something; 3. an act of refusing to grant or allow something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His denial of the allegations was not convincing.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對這些指控的否認並不可信。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She lived in denial about her illness.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對自己的病情一直處於否認狀態。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The request was met with denial.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個請求被拒絕了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company issued a denial of the rumors.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司發布聲明否認這些謠言。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她對自己的病情一直處於否認狀態。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4122,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::desert::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Many ____ animals are nocturnal.","expectedAnswer":"desert","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Many ____ animals are nocturnal.","clozeAnswer":"desert","exampleTranslation":"許多沙漠動物是夜行性的。","reference":{"eng":"desert","kk":"/ˈdɛzərt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['沙漠']]","chEntries":["沙漠"],"practiceMeaning":"許多沙漠動物是夜行性的。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 desertum（荒蕪之地），是 desertus（被遺棄的）的中性形式。核心概念是「荒涼」、「無人居住」的地方。引申為極度乾燥、植被稀少的地區。","definition":"a barren or desolate area, especially one with little or no rainfall.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The Sahara Desert is the largest hot desert in the world.\",\n    \"ch\": \"撒哈拉沙漠是世界上最大的熱帶沙漠。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Many desert animals are nocturnal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"許多沙漠動物是夜行性的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They trekked across the desert.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們徒步穿越了沙漠。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"許多沙漠動物是夜行性的。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5835,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::dilemma::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company is in a ____ about whether to expand or consolidate.","expectedAnswer":"dilemma","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company is in a ____ about whether to expand or consolidate.","clozeAnswer":"dilemma","exampleTranslation":"公司在是否擴張或整合的問題上陷入了困境。","reference":{"eng":"dilemma","kk":"dɪˈlɛmə","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"困境\"  ],  [    \"兩難\"  ],  [    \"進退兩難\"  ],  [    \"難題\"  ]]","chEntries":["困境","兩難","進退兩難","難題"],"practiceMeaning":"公司在是否擴張或整合的問題上陷入了困境。","analysis":"此字源自希臘語 'dilemma'，由 'di-' (two) 和 'lemma' (premise, assumption, proposition) 構成。原意為「兩項前提」或「兩難的論證」。在邏輯學中，'dilemma' 指一種論證形式，其中兩項可能的選擇都導向不希望的結果。在現代英語中，'dilemma' 指一種需要做出艱難選擇的處境，通常是在兩種或多種相互矛盾的選項之間，且每個選項都有其不利之處。核心語意是「必須在兩個或多個不理想的選項中做出選擇的困境」。例如，也可指「一項難以解決的問題」。","definition":"1. A situation in which a difficult choice has to be made between two or more alternatives, especially equally undesirable ones.; 2. A problem offering no satisfactory solution.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He faced a dilemma: either tell the truth and hurt his friend, or lie and betray his principles.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他面臨兩難：要么說實話傷害朋友，要么撒謊背叛自己的原則。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company is in a dilemma about whether to expand or consolidate.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司在是否擴張或整合的問題上陷入了困境。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's a classic ethical dilemma.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個經典的道德困境。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The scientist faced the dilemma of publishing his findings or keeping them secret.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位科學家面臨著是發表研究結果還是保密的兩難。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"公司在是否擴張或整合的問題上陷入了困境。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5836,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::diminish::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His responsibilities will ____ as he gets older.","expectedAnswer":"diminish","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His responsibilities will ____ as he gets older.","clozeAnswer":"diminish","exampleTranslation":"隨著年齡增長，他的責任將會減少。","reference":{"eng":"diminish","kk":"dɪˈmɪnɪʃ","tense":"v.","ch":"[  [    \"減少\"  ],  [    \"減弱\"  ],  [    \"降低\"  ],  [    \"縮小\"  ]]","chEntries":["減少","減弱","降低","縮小"],"practiceMeaning":"隨著年齡增長，他的責任將會減少。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'diminuere'，由 'di-' (apart, away) 和 'minuere' (to lessen) 構成。'Minuere' 來自 'minus' (less)。'Diminuere' 的字面意思是「使減少」、「使變小」。'-ish' 是常見的動詞字尾，將名詞或形容詞轉化為動詞，表示「使……」或「變得……」。因此，'diminish' 的核心語意是「使之變少、變弱或變小」。它可以指數量、強度、重要性、價值等方面的減少或減弱。例如，也可指「縮小」尺寸或範圍。","definition":"1. To make or become smaller, weaker, or less.; 2. To lessen the authority, dignity, or reputation of.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The threat of war did not diminish.\",\n    \"ch\": \"戰爭的威脅並未減弱。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His responsibilities will diminish as he gets older.\",\n    \"ch\": \"隨著年齡增長，他的責任將會減少。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The drug is used to diminish pain.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種藥物用於減輕疼痛。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The size of the company will diminish after the merger.\",\n    \"ch\": \"合併後公司的規模將會縮小。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"隨著年齡增長，他的責任將會減少。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4698,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::dose::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He was dosed with a healthy ____ of reality about his chances.","expectedAnswer":"dose","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He was dosed with a healthy ____ of reality about his chances.","clozeAnswer":"dose","exampleTranslation":"他被現實好好地潑了一盆冷水，讓他認清了自己的機會。","reference":{"eng":"dose","kk":"/ˈdoʊs/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['給...服藥'], ['（非正式）給予（苦頭、教訓）']]","chEntries":["給...服藥","給予"],"practiceMeaning":"他被現實好好地潑了一盆冷水，讓他認清了自己的機會。","analysis":"動詞形式，指給予特定劑量或一次性的給予。與名詞的非正式用法相對應，指給予某人一次性的教訓或懲罰。","definition":"1. To administer a dose of medicine to someone. 2. (informal) To give someone an unpleasant experience that they have to endure.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The nurse dosed the patient with painkillers.\",\n    \"ch\": \"護士給病人服用了止痛藥。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was dosed with a healthy dose of reality about his chances.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他被現實好好地潑了一盆冷水，讓他認清了自己的機會。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他被現實好好地潑了一盆冷水，讓他認清了自己的機會。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3937,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::downtown::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He works ____.","expectedAnswer":"downtown","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He works ____.","clozeAnswer":"downtown","exampleTranslation":"他在市中心工作。","reference":{"eng":"downtown","kk":"/ˈdaʊntaʊn/","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['在市中心（去）']]","chEntries":["在市中心"],"practiceMeaning":"他在市中心工作。","analysis":"最初指城市中心商業區，由 'down' (副詞，表示向下) 和 'town' (名詞，城市) 組成。表示「在城市的心臟地帶」。","definition":"in or towards the central area of a city or town.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Let's go downtown to buy some clothes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們去市中心買些衣服吧。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He works downtown.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在市中心工作。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他在市中心工作。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3142,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::dread::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Many people ____ going to the dentist.","expectedAnswer":"dread","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Many people ____ going to the dentist.","clozeAnswer":"dread","exampleTranslation":"許多人害怕去看牙醫。","reference":{"eng":"dread","kk":"/drɛd/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['恐懼；害怕'], ['（為某事）感到憂慮；害怕']]","chEntries":["恐懼","害怕","感到憂慮"],"practiceMeaning":"許多人害怕去看牙醫。","analysis":"詞源來自古英語 'drædan'，意為「害怕，敬畏」。'Dread' 強調的是一種強烈的、預期性的恐懼，通常是由於預感到即將發生的不幸、危險或不愉快的事情。這種恐懼往往伴隨著焦慮和不安。它比一般的「fear」程度更深，強調的是對未來的擔憂。","definition":"1. anticipate with great apprehension or fear; 2. regard with great fear or terror.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She dreaded the thought of having to give a speech.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她害怕必須發表演講的想法。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Many people dread going to the dentist.\",\n    \"ch\": \"許多人害怕去看牙醫。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He dreaded the arrival of the bad news.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他預感壞消息的到來，感到非常恐懼。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"許多人害怕去看牙醫。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3280,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::elastic::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company has an ____ work schedule.","expectedAnswer":"elastic","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company has an ____ work schedule.","clozeAnswer":"elastic","exampleTranslation":"這家公司有靈活的工作時間表。","reference":{"eng":"elastic","kk":"/ɪˈlæstɪk/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['有彈性的；彈性的'], ['（價格、需求等）可變的；靈活的']]","chEntries":["有彈性的","彈性的","可變的","靈活的"],"practiceMeaning":"這家公司有靈活的工作時間表。","analysis":"源自希臘語 'elaunein' (打，鞭打) 的過去分詞 'elastos'，意為「可延展的」。指能夠恢復原狀的物質的屬性，引申至非物質領域，表示具備伸縮性或可調節性。","definition":"1. able to stretch and return to its original shape; 2. able to be changed or adapted to meet different circumstances.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This waistband is made of elastic material.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這條褲子的腰帶是彈性材料製成的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company has an elastic work schedule.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司有靈活的工作時間表。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這家公司有靈活的工作時間表。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3984,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u3::flash::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"In a ____, he was gone.","expectedAnswer":"flash","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"In a ____, he was gone.","clozeAnswer":"flash","exampleTranslation":"瞬間，他就消失了。","reference":{"eng":"flash","kk":"/flæʃ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['閃光', '閃光燈'], ['一陣', '瞬間'], ['（新聞）快訊', '（電視）閃報']]","chEntries":["閃光","閃光燈","一陣","瞬間","快訊","閃報"],"practiceMeaning":"瞬間，他就消失了。","analysis":"詞源：同上。名詞指瞬間發生的光或事件。","definition":"1. a sudden brief burst of bright light; 2. a very short period of time; 3. a brief news report.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A flash of lightning lit up the night.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一道閃電照亮了夜晚。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"In a flash, he was gone.\",\n    \"ch\": \"瞬間，他就消失了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We received a flash report on the incident.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們收到了一份關於該事件的快訊。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"瞬間，他就消失了。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5045,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::fluid::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Her movements were ____ and elegant.","expectedAnswer":"fluid","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Her movements were ____ and elegant.","clozeAnswer":"fluid","exampleTranslation":"她的動作流暢而優雅。","reference":{"eng":"fluid","kk":"ˈfluːɪd","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['流動的'], ['流暢的'], ['不穩定的'], ['變化的']]","chEntries":["流動的","流暢的","不穩定的","變化的"],"practiceMeaning":"她的動作流暢而優雅。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語fluidus，是動詞fluere（流動）的形容詞形式。fluere 又來自原始印歐語 *pleu-（流動）。fluid 的核心語意是「能夠流動的，無固定形狀的」。引申為「流暢的、順暢的」（如 fluid movement），或指情況「不穩定的、變化的、彈性的」（如 fluid situation）。OCR 掃描時可能將 'f' 誤判為 'l'。此處修正為 fluid。","definition":"1. able to flow easily; 2. smooth and graceful; 3. (of a situation or plan) changeable; not fixed.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Water is a fluid.\",\n    \"ch\": \"水是流體。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her movements were fluid and elegant.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的動作流暢而優雅。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The political situation remains fluid.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政治局勢仍然不穩定（多變）。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她的動作流暢而優雅。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5785,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::format::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The book's ____ makes it easy to read.","expectedAnswer":"format","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The book's ____ makes it easy to read.","clozeAnswer":"format","exampleTranslation":"這本書的版面設計易於閱讀。","reference":{"eng":"format","kk":"ˈfɔrmæt","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"格式\"  ],  [    \"版面\"  ],  [    \"形式\"  ],  [    \"編排\"  ]]","chEntries":["格式","版面","形式","編排"],"practiceMeaning":"這本書的版面設計易於閱讀。","analysis":"此字為名詞，與動詞同源，源自拉丁語forma（形式；形狀）。format作為名詞，核心語義是指「事物的結構、安排或呈現方式」。可以是文件、磁碟、節目、演講的特定結構或樣式。語意演變上，從「形式」的概念，具體化為「被組織或安排好的樣式」。","definition":"1. the way in which something is arranged or organized; 2. the size, shape, or arrangement of something; 3. a particular way in which something is presented or published.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The report needs to be in a specific format.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這份報告需要採用特定的格式。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The book's format makes it easy to read.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本書的版面設計易於閱讀。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to decide on the format for the presentation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要決定簡報的編排形式。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這本書的版面設計易於閱讀。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5481,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::harvest::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We helped to ____ the apples.","expectedAnswer":"harvest","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We helped to ____ the apples.","clozeAnswer":"harvest","exampleTranslation":"我們幫忙採收蘋果。","reference":{"eng":"harvest","kk":"ˈhɑrvəst","tense":"v.","ch":"[['收割'], ['收穫']]","chEntries":["收割","收穫"],"practiceMeaning":"我們幫忙採收蘋果。","analysis":"此字由名詞 'harvest'（收成）派生而來。作為動詞，'harvest' 的意思是「收割、採集農作物」。它直接承襲了名詞的語意，指進行收穫動作的過程。這個動詞強調的是將成熟的作物從土地上採集下來的行為。核心語意是「進行收割」。","definition":"1. Gather (a crop) from the fields.; 2. (Of a crop) yield or give as a harvest.; 3. Gather or reap.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The farmers began to harvest the wheat.\",\n    \"ch\": \"農民們開始收割小麥。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We helped to harvest the apples.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們幫忙採收蘋果。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The land yielded a good harvest.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這片土地收穫頗豐。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們幫忙採收蘋果。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4178,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::honor::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The bank will ____ the check.","expectedAnswer":"honor","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The bank will ____ the check.","clozeAnswer":"honor","exampleTranslation":"銀行將兌現這張支票。","reference":{"eng":"honor","kk":"/ˈɑːnər/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['尊敬', '敬重'], ['遵守', '履行（諾言、義務）'], ['（銀行）兌現（支票）']]","chEntries":["尊敬","敬重","遵守","履行","兌現"],"practiceMeaning":"銀行將兌現這張支票。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 honor（尊敬、名譽）。核心概念是「給予尊重」或「兌現承諾」。","definition":"1. regard with great respect; 2. fulfill (an obligation) or keep (an agreement); 3. accept and pay (a bill of exchange)","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He always honors his promises.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他總是信守諾言。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The bank will honor the check.\",\n    \"ch\": \"銀行將兌現這張支票。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We must honor our commitments.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們必須履行我們的承諾。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"銀行將兌現這張支票。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4721,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::humor::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The teacher tried to ____ the crying child.","expectedAnswer":"humor","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The teacher tried to ____ the crying child.","clozeAnswer":"humor","exampleTranslation":"老師試圖安撫那個哭泣的孩子。","reference":{"eng":"humor","kk":"/ˈhjumər/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['迎合'], ['遷就']]","chEntries":["迎合","遷就"],"practiceMeaning":"老師試圖安撫那個哭泣的孩子。","analysis":"動詞形式，指為了取悅或避免冒犯某人而遷就或滿足他們。通常用於負面語境，暗示不是真心同意，只是為了保持和諧。","definition":"1. To try to please or satisfy someone, especially by doing or saying what they want.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He always tries to humor his demanding boss.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他總是試圖遷就他那要求嚴苛的老闆。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The teacher tried to humor the crying child.\",\n    \"ch\": \"老師試圖安撫那個哭泣的孩子。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"老師試圖安撫那個哭泣的孩子。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5385,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l2::issue::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The policy will ____ from the ministry.","expectedAnswer":"issue","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The policy will ____ from the ministry.","clozeAnswer":"issue","exampleTranslation":"這項政策將由該部發布。","reference":{"eng":"issue","kk":"ˈɪʃuː","tense":"v.","ch":"[['發行'], ['發布'], ['提出'], ['造成', '引起']]","chEntries":["發行","發布","提出","造成","引起"],"practiceMeaning":"這項政策將由該部發布。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 escuë (出去、發出)，來自拉丁語 exire (出來)。核心語意是「使某物出、發出」。因此，'issue' 作動詞時，可指「正式地發布或發行」（如出版物、貨幣），「提出或討論」（如議題），或「造成、引起」（如問題、狀況）。","definition":"1. supply or distribute (something); 2. originate or stem from; 3. produce or release.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company will issue new shares next month.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司將於下月發行新股。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The policy will issue from the ministry.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這項政策將由該部發布。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這項政策將由該部發布。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4167,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::living::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He is working hard to provide a better ____ for his family.","expectedAnswer":"living","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He is working hard to provide a better ____ for his family.","clozeAnswer":"living","exampleTranslation":"他正努力工作，為家人提供更好的生活。","reference":{"eng":"living","kk":"/ˈlɪvɪŋ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['生活', '生計']]","chEntries":["生活","生計"],"practiceMeaning":"他正努力工作，為家人提供更好的生活。","analysis":"由 live（活著，生存）+ -ing（名詞後綴）組成。核心概念是「生存的狀態」或「維持生存所需」。","definition":"1. the state of being alive; 2. a means of supporting oneself financially","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The steep rise in living costs made it hard to make ends meet.\",\n    \"ch\": \"生活成本的急劇上漲使得人們難以為繼。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is working hard to provide a better living for his family.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他正努力工作，為家人提供更好的生活。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The cost of living has gone up.\",\n    \"ch\": \"生活成本上升了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他正努力工作，為家人提供更好的生活。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5570,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::load::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Please ____ the dishwasher.","expectedAnswer":"load","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Please ____ the dishwasher.","clozeAnswer":"load","exampleTranslation":"請把洗碗機裝滿。","reference":{"eng":"load","kk":"loʊd","tense":"v.","ch":"[['裝載'], ['加載'], ['負荷']]","chEntries":["裝載","加載","負荷"],"practiceMeaning":"請把洗碗機裝滿。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 \"lādan\"，意為 \"to carry, convey, conduct\"（攜帶，運送，引導），最終可能源自原始印歐語 \\*leith-（to go, to travel，去，旅行）。\"lādan\" 的引申義是指「承載、運送」。 \"load\" 作動詞，核心語義是「將某物裝入容器、車輛或系統，使其承擔重量或資訊」。在物理上，指「裝載貨物」；在計算機領域，指「將數據或程式載入記憶體」（load a program）；在數學或工程學上，指「施加負荷」或「承受重量」。","definition":"1. To put a load onto or into; 2. To fill (a vehicle, ship, aircraft, etc.) with goods or passengers; 3. To load data or programs into a computer's memory; 4. To put a heavy burden on.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The truck was loaded with goods.\",\n    \"ch\": \"卡車裝滿了貨物。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please load the dishwasher.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請把洗碗機裝滿。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The system is taking a long time to load the new software.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個系統載入新軟體花費了很長時間。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He felt loaded with responsibility.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他感覺責任重大。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"請把洗碗機裝滿。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3302,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::makeup::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of the committee was diverse.","expectedAnswer":"makeup","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of the committee was diverse.","clozeAnswer":"makeup","exampleTranslation":"委員會的組成很多元化。","reference":{"eng":"makeup","kk":"/ˈmeɪkʌp/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['化妝品'], ['化妝；妝容'], ['組成；構成'], ['（事物的）性質；總體情況'], ['（尤指戲劇、電影中的）化妝，道具']]","chEntries":["化妝品","化妝","妝容","組成","構成","性質","總體情況","化妝，道具"],"practiceMeaning":"委員會的組成很多元化。","analysis":"由 'make' (做) + 'up' (組成) 組成。名詞形式有多種意義：指用於修飾容貌的化妝品；化妝這個動作或結果；事物的組成或性質；以及戲劇中的特殊化妝。這些意義都源於「組成」、「構成」的核心概念。","definition":"1. substances such as lipstick, powder, and mascara that are used to make a person's face look more attractive; 2. the act or process of applying cosmetics; 3. the way in which something is put together or arranged; 4. the nature or character of something; 5. the art of applying cosmetics to an actor's face or body.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She buys a lot of makeup.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她買了很多化妝品。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The makeup of the committee was diverse.\",\n    \"ch\": \"委員會的組成很多元化。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her natural makeup looked very elegant.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的自然妝容看起來非常優雅。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The makeup artist worked quickly before the performance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"化妝師在表演前快速地工作。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"委員會的組成很多元化。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6080,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::massage::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The sports ____ helped relieve his muscle soreness.","expectedAnswer":"massage","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The sports ____ helped relieve his muscle soreness.","clozeAnswer":"massage","exampleTranslation":"運動按摩幫助緩解了他的肌肉痠痛。","reference":{"eng":"massage","kk":"məˈsɑʒ","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"按摩\"  ],  [    \"撫摩\"  ]]","chEntries":["按摩","撫摩"],"practiceMeaning":"運動按摩幫助緩解了他的肌肉痠痛。","analysis":"此字源自法語 massage，本身來自 provencal masa（to knead），追溯至希臘語 massein（to knead）。核心語義是「揉捏」或「按壓」。作為名詞，指一種通過手技（揉、捏、拍打等）來放鬆肌肉、緩解疼痛或促進血液循環的治療或放鬆方法。","definition":"an act of rubbing and kneading the body with the hands, especially to relieve tension or pain.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She found a deep tissue massage very relaxing.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她覺得深層組織按摩非常放鬆。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The sports massage helped relieve his muscle soreness.\",\n    \"ch\": \"運動按摩幫助緩解了他的肌肉痠痛。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A regular massage can improve circulation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"定期的按摩可以改善血液循環。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"運動按摩幫助緩解了他的肌肉痠痛。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3096,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::maximum::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Please do not exceed the ____ speed limit.","expectedAnswer":"maximum","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Please do not exceed the ____ speed limit.","clozeAnswer":"maximum","exampleTranslation":"請勿超過最高限速。","reference":{"eng":"maximum","kk":"/ˈmæksɪməm/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['最大的；最高的']]","chEntries":["最大的","最高的"],"practiceMeaning":"請勿超過最高限速。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'maximus' (greatest)。核心意義是「最大」。\n1. 最大的；最高的：指數量、程度、或尺寸上的最大可能值。","definition":"1. the greatest possible amount or degree; 2. the largest amount or number.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The room has a maximum capacity of 50 people.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這房間的最大容量是50人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please do not exceed the maximum speed limit.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請勿超過最高限速。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"請勿超過最高限速。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39、U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5662,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l8::measure::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need to ____ our progress carefully.","expectedAnswer":"measure","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need to ____ our progress carefully.","clozeAnswer":"measure","exampleTranslation":"我們需要仔細衡量我們的進展。","reference":{"eng":"measure","kk":"ˈmɛʒər","tense":"v.","ch":"[['測量'], ['衡量'], ['評估'], ['（法律、規定等）措施']]","chEntries":["測量","衡量","評估","措施"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要仔細衡量我們的進展。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 mesure，來自古法語 mesure，再追溯至拉丁語 mensura（測量），來自 mensus（測量），是 mētiri（測量，to measure）的過去分詞。mētiri 來自原始印歐語 *meh₁-（測量）。核心語義為「確定尺寸、數量或程度」。構詞上，mētiri 提供「測量」的核心動作，-ure 是常見的名詞字尾，此處轉換為動詞用法。此處為動詞用法，表示「進行測量」、「估算」、「考慮」或「採取措施」。","definition":"to ascertain the size, amount, or degree of something; to assess or evaluate; to take action to achieve a particular aim.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please measure the length of the table.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請測量桌子的長度。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to measure our progress carefully.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要仔細衡量我們的進展。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government has taken measures to control inflation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府已採取措施控制通貨膨脹。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要仔細衡量我們的進展。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4182,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::murder::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Don't ____ the joke by telling it badly.","expectedAnswer":"murder","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Don't ____ the joke by telling it badly.","clozeAnswer":"murder","exampleTranslation":"別把笑話講砸了，那樣會毀了它。","reference":{"eng":"murder","kk":"/ˈmɜːrdər/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['謀殺；殺害'], ['（尤指）殘酷地毀壞；歪曲']]","chEntries":["謀殺","殺害","殘酷地毀壞","歪曲"],"practiceMeaning":"別把笑話講砸了，那樣會毀了它。","analysis":"動詞形式源自名詞 'murder'，表示實施謀殺的行為。核心動詞義是“殺害”。引申義則包括以極其毀滅性的方式對待某物，或惡意地歪曲某事，例如 'murder the language'（歪曲語言）或 'murder the truth'（歪曲事實）。","definition":"1. to kill someone unlawfully; 2. to destroy or spoil something completely; to distort or misrepresent something severely.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was found guilty of murdering his wife.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他被判謀殺其妻有罪。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Don't murder the joke by telling it badly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"別把笑話講砸了，那樣會毀了它。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The artist felt that the changes had murdered his original design.\",\n    \"ch\": \"藝術家覺得這些改動毀了他最初的設計。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"別把笑話講砸了，那樣會毀了它。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U6、L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3190,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::object::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Her main ____ in life is to help others.","expectedAnswer":"object","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Her main ____ in life is to help others.","clozeAnswer":"object","exampleTranslation":"她人生的主要目標是幫助他人。","reference":{"eng":"object","kk":"/ˈɒbdʒɪkt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['物體；物品'], ['（名詞、動詞等的）賓語'], ['目的；目標']]","chEntries":["物體","物品","賓語","目的","目標"],"practiceMeaning":"她人生的主要目標是幫助他人。","analysis":"詞源來自拉丁語 'obiectum'，意為「被提出來的東西」。'Object' 作名詞時，有幾個主要含義：一是物理上可見、可觸摸的「物體」。二是語言學上，句子中承受動作的「賓語」。三是引申義，指某事的「目標」、「目的」或「對象」。這三個意思都圍繞著「被感知、被處理或被指向」的概念。","definition":"1. a material thing that can be seen and touched; 2. a person, thing, or idea that is the subject of an action or feeling; 3. (grammar) a word or phrase naming the person or thing that is affected by the action of a verb.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police found a strange object at the scene of the crime.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警方在犯罪現場發現了一個奇怪的物體。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her main object in life is to help others.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她人生的主要目標是幫助他人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"In the sentence 'He kicked the ball', 'ball' is the direct object.\",\n    \"ch\": \"在句子「他踢了球」中，「球」是直接賓語。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她人生的主要目標是幫助他人。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5845,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::obscure::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He was an ____ poet until his work was rediscovered.","expectedAnswer":"obscure","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He was an ____ poet until his work was rediscovered.","clozeAnswer":"obscure","exampleTranslation":"在作品被重新發現之前，他是一位默默無聞的詩人。","reference":{"eng":"obscure","kk":"əbˈskjʊər","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"晦澀的\"  ],  [    \"模糊的\"  ],  [    \"不起眼的\"  ],  [    \"鮮為人知的\"  ]]","chEntries":["晦澀的","模糊的","不起眼的","鮮為人知的"],"practiceMeaning":"在作品被重新發現之前，他是一位默默無聞的詩人。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'obscurus'，由 'ob-' (over, before) 和 'scurus' (related to 'ceterus' meaning 'other', so implying 'covered') 構成。'Obscurus' 的字面意思是「被覆蓋的」、「隱藏的」。因此，'obscure' 在形容事物時，表示「不清晰的」、「難以理解的」、「不為人知的」或「不顯眼的」。它描述的是缺乏明顯性、缺乏清晰度或缺乏知名度的狀態。例如，也可指「不易辨認的」。","definition":"1. Not discovered or known about; uncertain.; 2. Not clearly expressed or easily understood.; 3. Not important or famous.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The meaning of the poem is obscure.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這首詩的意義很晦澀。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was an obscure poet until his work was rediscovered.\",\n    \"ch\": \"在作品被重新發現之前，他是一位默默無聞的詩人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The small village remained obscure for centuries.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個小村莊幾個世紀以來一直默默無聞。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The entrance to the cave was obscure.\",\n    \"ch\": \"洞穴的入口隱蔽難尋。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"在作品被重新發現之前，他是一位默默無聞的詩人。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5793,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::offering::vt","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company is ____ a new service to its customers.","expectedAnswer":"offering","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company is ____ a new service to its customers.","clozeAnswer":"offering","exampleTranslation":"該公司正在為其客戶提供一項新服務。","reference":{"eng":"offering","kk":"ˈɔfərɪŋ","tense":"vt.","ch":"[  [    \"提供\"  ],  [    \"提出\"  ],  [    \"奉獻\"  ]]","chEntries":["提供","提出","奉獻"],"practiceMeaning":"該公司正在為其客戶提供一項新服務。","analysis":"此處 offering 是動詞offer的現在分詞形式，具動詞義。offer源自古英語offrian，受拉丁語offerre（奉獻；提供）影響。offerre由ob-（朝向；針對）+ferre（帶來；運送）組成。核心語義是用意願將某物呈現給他人，使其可被接受或使用。語意演變上，從「帶來」引申為「主動提出」或「自願給予」。","definition":"1. to present something for acceptance or rejection; 2. to make available for purchase or use; 3. to present or give something as a gift or tribute.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They are offering a discount for early bookings.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們為提前預訂提供折扣。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company is offering a new service to its customers.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司正在為其客戶提供一項新服務。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is offering his help to the community.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他正在向社區提供幫助。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該公司正在為其客戶提供一項新服務。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3236,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::orbit::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The satellite entered its final ____.","expectedAnswer":"orbit","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The satellite entered its final ____.","clozeAnswer":"orbit","exampleTranslation":"衛星進入了它的最終軌道。","reference":{"eng":"orbit","kk":"/ˈɔːrbɪt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['軌道'], ['勢力範圍']]","chEntries":["軌道","勢力範圍"],"practiceMeaning":"衛星進入了它的最終軌道。","analysis":"詞源來自拉丁文 'orbita'，原指『車輪的軌跡』，引申為天體繞著另一個天體運行的路徑。也引申為某人活動的範圍或影響範圍。","definition":"1. the curved path of a celestial object or spacecraft round a star, planet, or moon; 2. the range of action or influence of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The Earth revolves in orbit around the Sun.\",\n    \"ch\": \"地球圍繞太陽運行在軌道上。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The satellite entered its final orbit.\",\n    \"ch\": \"衛星進入了它的最終軌道。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He operates within his own orbit of influence.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他活躍在自己的勢力範圍內。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"衛星進入了它的最終軌道。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U41"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5847,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::parallel::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The events occurred in ____.","expectedAnswer":"parallel","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The events occurred in ____.","clozeAnswer":"parallel","exampleTranslation":"這些事件是同時發生的。","reference":{"eng":"parallel","kk":"ˈpærəlel","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"平行的\"  ],  [    \"並列的\"  ],  [    \"類似的\"  ],  [    \"同時發生的\"  ]]","chEntries":["平行的","並列的","類似的","同時發生的"],"practiceMeaning":"這些事件是同時發生的。","analysis":"此字源自希臘語 'parallēlos'，由 'para-' (beside) 和 'allos' (other) 構成，意為「相鄰的」或「並行的」。'Parallel' 在幾何學中指永不相交的兩條線。在更廣泛的語境中，它描述的是事物在空間上「並排」或在時間上「同時」發生、或在性質上「類似」的關係。空間上的平行與時間上的同時，以及性質上的類比，都共享了「不交叉」、「不干涉」或「共同前進」的意象。例如，也可指「結構相似的」。","definition":"1. (of lines, planes, or surfaces) side by side and having the same distance continuously between them.; 2. Occurring or existing at the same time.; 3. Having a marked similarity or resemblance.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The two roads run parallel to each other.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這兩條路相互平行。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The events occurred in parallel.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這些事件是同時發生的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His life story has parallel with mine.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的人生經歷與我頗為相似。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The two buildings have a parallel structure.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這兩座建築有著平行的結構。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這些事件是同時發生的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5851,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::passionate::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His ____ speech moved the audience.","expectedAnswer":"passionate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His ____ speech moved the audience.","clozeAnswer":"passionate","exampleTranslation":"他充滿激情的演講感動了聽眾。","reference":{"eng":"passionate","kk":"ˈpæʃənət","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"熱情的\"  ],  [    \"激情的\"  ],  [    \"熱烈的\"  ],  [    \"充滿愛意的\"  ]]","chEntries":["熱情的","激情的","熱烈的","充滿愛意的"],"practiceMeaning":"他充滿激情的演講感動了聽眾。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'passio' (suffering, feeling, passion)，由 'pati' (to suffer, endure) 構成。'Passionate' 的核心語意是「充滿強烈情感」，尤其是「熱情」、「激情」或「愛」。它描述的是一種被強烈情感驅動的狀態，無論是正面（如熱愛、激勵）或負面（如憤怒、痛苦）。在現代用法中，通常指對某事物有強烈的興趣、熱情和投入。例如，也可指「充滿愛意的」，用於形容關係。","definition":"1. Showing or caused by strong feelings or a strong belief.; 2. Having or showing strong sexual desire.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is passionate about environmental protection.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對環境保護充滿熱情。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His passionate speech moved the audience.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他充滿激情的演講感動了聽眾。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They have a passionate relationship.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們有一段熱烈的感情。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was passionate in his defense of the proposal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他充滿激情地為該提議辯護。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他充滿激情的演講感動了聽眾。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5530,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l5::sack::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The coach decided to ____ the underperforming player.","expectedAnswer":"sack","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The coach decided to ____ the underperforming player.","clozeAnswer":"sack","exampleTranslation":"教練決定解僱表現不佳的球員。","reference":{"eng":"sack","kk":"sæk","tense":"v.","ch":"[['將……裝入袋中'], ['解僱（美式俚語）'], ['在（美式足球）中擒殺四分衛']]","chEntries":["將……裝入袋中","解僱","在中擒殺四分衛"],"practiceMeaning":"教練決定解僱表現不佳的球員。","analysis":"此為名詞 'sack' 的動詞形式。作為動詞，主要有兩類用法：1. 將物品裝入袋中（源自名詞「麻袋」的動作）；2. 在美式足球中，使對方持球的四分衛喪失前進動力（源自名詞的體育術語，暗示使對方「受困」或「被裝入袋中」）；3. 俚語中指「解僱」（與「被踢出」或「被扔掉」的形象相關）。此處的 OCR 掃描文本暗示的是「裝入袋中」的動作。","definition":"to put something into a sack; to dismiss from employment (slang); to tackle (a quarterback) behind the line of scrimmage.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to sack the grain before storing it.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要將穀物裝袋後再儲存。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The coach decided to sack the underperforming player.\",\n    \"ch\": \"教練決定解僱表現不佳的球員。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"教練決定解僱表現不佳的球員。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5859,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::salon::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ hosted a gathering of artists.","expectedAnswer":"salon","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ hosted a gathering of artists.","clozeAnswer":"salon","exampleTranslation":"這個沙龍舉辦了一場藝術家聚會。","reference":{"eng":"salon","kk":"səˈlɑːn","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"沙龍\"  ],  [    \"美容院\"  ],  [    \"客廳\"  ],  [    \"陳列室\"  ]]","chEntries":["沙龍","美容院","客廳","陳列室"],"practiceMeaning":"這個沙龍舉辦了一場藝術家聚會。","analysis":"此字源自法語 'salon'，原意為「大廳」、「接待室」，由 'salle' (hall) 演變而來，'salle' 源自拉丁語 'sal' (salt)，或有說源自'sala' (room)，表示「主要房間」。'Salon' 在18世紀法國興起，指「名流聚集的客廳」，成為文化交流的場所。現代語義擴展至「美容院」或「髮廊」，指提供美容、美髮服務的專業場所，這些場所也常被設計成舒適、有格調的空間，如同昔日的社交沙龍。例如，也可指「藝術品陳列室」。","definition":"1. A large room in a private house or hotel, especially one used for entertaining guests.; 2. A fashionable beauty salon or hairdressing establishment.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She went to the salon to get her hair done.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她去沙龍做頭髮。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The salon hosted a gathering of artists.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個沙龍舉辦了一場藝術家聚會。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He opened a new beauty salon.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他開了一家新的美容院。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The art salon exhibited works by local painters.\",\n    \"ch\": \"藝術沙龍展出了本地畫家的作品。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個沙龍舉辦了一場藝術家聚會。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6091,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::scrap::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The car was too damaged to repair and was sent for ____.","expectedAnswer":"scrap","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The car was too damaged to repair and was sent for ____.","clozeAnswer":"scrap","exampleTranslation":"這輛車損壞嚴重無法修復，被送去報廢了。","reference":{"eng":"scrap","kk":"skræp","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"碎片\"  ],  [    \"零星的\"  ],  [    \"廢料\"  ],  [    \"報廢品\"  ],  [    \"（信息、數據）片段\"  ]]","chEntries":["碎片","零星的","廢料","報廢品","片段"],"practiceMeaning":"這輛車損壞嚴重無法修復，被送去報廢了。","analysis":"此字的詞源不確定，可能源自古斯堪地那維亞語 skrap，意為「剩餘物」。核心語義是「小的、零散的、無用的部分」。引申為「廢料」、「報廢品」，或「零星的、不完整的片段」。","definition":"1. a small piece or amount of something, especially one that is left over after the greater part has been used or finished; 2. discarded material or refuse.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He found a scrap of paper with a phone number on it.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他找到一張寫著電話號碼的紙條。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The car was too damaged to repair and was sent for scrap.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這輛車損壞嚴重無法修復，被送去報廢了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The report was compiled from various scraps of information.\",\n    \"ch\": \"報告是從各種零散的信息片段匯編而成的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這輛車損壞嚴重無法修復，被送去報廢了。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6248,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::snatch::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He used the brief ____ of silence to escape.","expectedAnswer":"snatch","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He used the brief ____ of silence to escape.","clozeAnswer":"snatch","exampleTranslation":"他利用那短暫的寂靜逃脫了。","reference":{"eng":"snatch","kk":"snætʃ","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"搶奪\"  ],  [    \"奪取\"  ],  [    \"一小段時間\"  ],  [    \"短暫的機會\"  ]]","chEntries":["搶奪","奪取","一小段時間","短暫的機會"],"practiceMeaning":"他利用那短暫的寂靜逃脫了。","analysis":"此字源自擬聲詞，模仿突然抓住的動作。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。名詞義指突然、快速地抓住或拿走某物的行為。也可引申為一段短暫的時間或機會。中文翻譯為「搶奪；奪取；一小段時間；短暫的機會」。","definition":"1. the act of grabbing or taking something quickly; 2. a short period of time or a brief opportunity.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The snatch of the necklace caused panic in the crowd.\",\n    \"ch\": \"項鍊被搶奪引起了人群的恐慌。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He used the brief snatch of silence to escape.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他利用那短暫的寂靜逃脫了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was a desperate snatch for freedom.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那是一次對自由的絕望的奪取。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他利用那短暫的寂靜逃脫了。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5522,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l5::sneak::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The thief was a real ____, always avoiding detection.","expectedAnswer":"sneak","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The thief was a real ____, always avoiding detection.","clozeAnswer":"sneak","exampleTranslation":"那個竊賊是個真正的潛行者，總能避開追蹤。","reference":{"eng":"sneak","kk":"sniːk","tense":"n.","ch":"[['潛行者'], ['鬼鬼祟祟的人'], ['告密者']]","chEntries":["潛行者","鬼鬼祟祟的人","告密者"],"practiceMeaning":"那個竊賊是個真正的潛行者，總能避開追蹤。","analysis":"此為動詞 'sneak' 的名詞形式。作為名詞，它指「偷偷摸摸行動的人」，或引申為「告密者」（指偷偷告密的人）。構詞與語意演變與動詞一致，強調「偷偷地、不被察覺地」的行為者。","definition":"a person who moves stealthily; a person who tells secrets.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was known as a sneak in the classroom.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在教室裡是個以愛告密聞名的人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The thief was a real sneak, always avoiding detection.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那個竊賊是個真正的潛行者，總能避開追蹤。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"那個竊賊是個真正的潛行者，總能避開追蹤。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5569,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::sort::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This ____ of behavior is unacceptable.","expectedAnswer":"sort","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This ____ of behavior is unacceptable.","clozeAnswer":"sort","exampleTranslation":"這種行為是不可接受的。","reference":{"eng":"sort","kk":"sɔrt","tense":"n.","ch":"[['種類'], ['類型'], ['類別'], ['品級']]","chEntries":["種類","類型","類別","品級"],"practiceMeaning":"這種行為是不可接受的。","analysis":"這是 \"sort\" 作動詞的相關名詞形式，源自古法語 \"sortir\"，意為 \"to draw lots, to choose\"（抽籤，選擇），來自拉丁語 \"sors, sortis\"（lot, fate, share，籤，命運，份額）。\"sors\" 最初與「抽籤」或「命運」相關，引申出「一份」、「一部分」的概念，進而演變為「同一類的事物」或「某一類型的東西」。因此，\"sort\" 作為名詞，指「由共同特徵或標準劃分出來的群體或類別」，即「種類」或「類型」。","definition":"1. A category of people or things having common characteristics; 2. A number of people or things that are grouped together because they are similar to each other.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a sort of person who always tries to help.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是那種總是試圖幫忙的人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This sort of behavior is unacceptable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種行為是不可接受的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"What sort of music do you like?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你喜歡哪一類的音樂？\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這種行為是不可接受的。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5436,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::spare::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"I have some ____ time this afternoon.","expectedAnswer":"spare","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"I have some ____ time this afternoon.","clozeAnswer":"spare","exampleTranslation":"我今天下午有些空閒時間。","reference":{"eng":"spare","kk":"sper","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['備用的'], ['多餘的'], ['節省的'], ['空閒的'], ['無事可做的']]","chEntries":["備用的","多餘的","節省的","空閒的","無事可做的"],"practiceMeaning":"我今天下午有些空閒時間。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 \"spær\"，意為\"節儉的\"、\"稀少的\"。其詞源可能與\"sparse\" (稀疏的) 有聯繫。構詞上沒有明顯的字首、字根或字尾可拆解，應視為一個整體詞源的演變。原始語義是「稀少」、「節省」，引申為「不需要的」、「多餘的」，因此可以用作「備用的」；同時也表示「有空閒的」、「可供支配的」。","definition":"not being used or needed at the moment; kept in reserve for future use; not used or spoken; not strictly necessary; not busy; free.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Do you have a spare tire in your car?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你的車上有備胎嗎？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I have some spare time this afternoon.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我今天下午有些空閒時間。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She managed to spare a few dollars for charity.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她設法省下了一些錢捐給慈善機構。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我今天下午有些空閒時間。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3195,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::split::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Let's do a ____ on the bill.","expectedAnswer":"split","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Let's do a ____ on the bill.","clozeAnswer":"split","exampleTranslation":"我們把帳單分攤一下吧。","reference":{"eng":"split","kk":"/splɪt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['分裂；分歧'], ['（尤指兩人或多人之間）分攤；一份'], ['（尤指歌劇、戲劇的）分聲部譜']]","chEntries":["分裂","分歧","分攤","一份","分聲部譜"],"practiceMeaning":"我們把帳單分攤一下吧。","analysis":"名詞用法，源自動詞 'split'。指「分裂」、「分歧」或「裂痕」，常形容意見、團體或關係上的不一致。也可指「分攤」的行為或結果，如分享費用或收益。在音樂領域，'split' 指的是將樂譜分開給不同聲部的樂手。","definition":"1. the act of dividing into parts or groups; 2. a disagreement or division between two or more people or groups; 3. a share of something; 4. (music) printed music for each part of an orchestra or choir.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was a split in the committee over the new proposal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"委員會在新的提案上出現了分歧。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Let's do a split on the bill.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們把帳單分攤一下吧。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The band has experienced several lineup splits.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個樂團經歷了幾次成員的分裂。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們把帳單分攤一下吧。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4705,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::stomach::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He clutched his ____ in pain.","expectedAnswer":"stomach","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He clutched his ____ in pain.","clozeAnswer":"stomach","exampleTranslation":"他痛苦地捂著肚子。","reference":{"eng":"stomach","kk":"/ˈstʌmək/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['胃'], ['腹部'], ['（非正式）消化能力；容忍力']]","chEntries":["胃","腹部","消化能力","容忍力"],"practiceMeaning":"他痛苦地捂著肚子。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 *stomachus*，來自希臘語 *stómakhos*（食道、胃）。核心是指消化食物的器官。引申至身體的腹部區域，以及非正式地指消化食物的能力，或容忍某種情況的能力。","definition":"1. An organ in the digestive tract where food is mixed with digestive juices. 2. The belly or abdomen. 3. (informal) The capacity to digest food or to tolerate something unpleasant.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The food was difficult for his stomach to digest.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種食物對他的胃來說很難消化。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He clutched his stomach in pain.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他痛苦地捂著肚子。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I don't have the stomach for this kind of violence.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我受不了這種暴力。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他痛苦地捂著肚子。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6200,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::threshold::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This event marks a new ____ in our relationship.","expectedAnswer":"threshold","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This event marks a new ____ in our relationship.","clozeAnswer":"threshold","exampleTranslation":"這個事件標誌著我們關係的新開端。","reference":{"eng":"threshold","kk":"ˈθreʃhoʊld","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"門檻\"  ],  [    \"入門\"  ],  [    \"閾值\"  ],  [    \"起始點\"  ]]","chEntries":["門檻","入門","閾值","起始點"],"practiceMeaning":"這個事件標誌著我們關係的新開端。","analysis":"此字是古英語 þrescold 或 þerscold 的演變，由 þres（打穀）和 scold（門檻）組合而成，意為「打穀場的門檻」。此字在現代英語中可視為複合詞，但其詞源的準確性有待考證，通常認為是整體詞源演變。作為名詞，其核心語義是指「進入某個地方的入口處的門檻」，引申為「某事的開始、起始點或進入的關卡」。詞源的「打穀場的門檻」引申出「進入」的物理概念，進而發展出「關鍵的起始點」的抽象概念。","definition":"1. the floor or step at the bottom of a doorway; 2. the point at which something begins; 3. the point at which a stimulus is perceived or a response is initiated; 4. the lower limit of a person's ability to perceive or react to a particular stimulus.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He stepped over the threshold into the house.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他跨過門檻走進屋裡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This event marks a new threshold in our relationship.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個事件標誌著我們關係的新開端。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The pain reached a threshold where she could no longer bear it.\",\n    \"ch\": \"疼痛達到了她無法忍受的閾值。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Crossing the threshold of the ancient temple, they felt a sense of awe.\",\n    \"ch\": \"跨過古老寺廟的門檻，他們感到一陣敬畏。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個事件標誌著我們關係的新開端。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6256,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::throne::vt","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The council members will ____ their leader with great ceremony.","expectedAnswer":"throne","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The council members will ____ their leader with great ceremony.","clozeAnswer":"throne","exampleTranslation":"議會成員將以隆重的儀式確立其領袖的統治地位。","reference":{"eng":"throne","kk":"θron","tense":"vt.","ch":"[  [    \"使坐在寶座上\"  ],  [    \"加冕\"  ],  [    \"確立...的統治地位\"  ]]","chEntries":["使坐在寶座上","加冕","確立...的統治地位"],"practiceMeaning":"議會成員將以隆重的儀式確立其領袖的統治地位。","analysis":"此處 throne 作及物動詞，源自名詞 throne，意指將某人「安置於寶座上」或「授予王位」。核心語義是用權力或儀式確立某人的統治地位。此字沒有可在現代英語中透明拆解的生產性字首或字尾。透過將名詞動詞化，得以表達「給予至高無上的地位」或「確立某人作為領導者的角色」的概念。此用法相對較為正式或文學化，強調權力的授予與穩固。","definition":"1. to place (a sovereign, bishop, or other ruler) on a throne; 2. to enthrone; to seat in state.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The ceremony was held to throne the new king.\",\n    \"ch\": \"舉行了儀式以加冕新國王。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The council members will throne their leader with great ceremony.\",\n    \"ch\": \"議會成員將以隆重的儀式確立其領袖的統治地位。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"議會成員將以隆重的儀式確立其領袖的統治地位。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6250,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::thrust::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of his argument was that the policy was flawed.","expectedAnswer":"thrust","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of his argument was that the policy was flawed.","clozeAnswer":"thrust","exampleTranslation":"他論點的核心要點是這項政策有缺陷。","reference":{"eng":"thrust","kk":"θrʌst","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"猛推\"  ],  [    \"推進力\"  ],  [    \"刺擊\"  ],  [    \"核心要點\"  ]]","chEntries":["猛推","推進力","刺擊","核心要點"],"practiceMeaning":"他論點的核心要點是這項政策有缺陷。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 þȳst（用力推，刺）。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。名詞義指猛推、用力推動或刺的動作。也可指推進物體前進的力量（如火箭的推力），或引申為某事物的主要目的、要點或核心。中文翻譯為「猛推；推進力；刺擊；核心要點」。","definition":"1. a strong, pushing movement; 2. the force that propels something forward, especially an aircraft or spacecraft; 3. the main point or purpose of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The engine provided enough thrust to lift the plane.\",\n    \"ch\": \"引擎提供了足夠的推進力使飛機升空。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The thrust of his argument was that the policy was flawed.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他論點的核心要點是這項政策有缺陷。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The sword thrust was swift and deadly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"劍的刺擊迅速而致命。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他論點的核心要點是這項政策有缺陷。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6251,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::vein::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Geologists searched for a ____ of gold.","expectedAnswer":"vein","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Geologists searched for a ____ of gold.","clozeAnswer":"vein","exampleTranslation":"地質學家們在尋找金礦脈。","reference":{"eng":"vein","kk":"veɪn","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"靜脈\"  ],  [    \"血管\"  ],  [    \"礦脈\"  ],  [    \"紋路\"  ],  [    \"風格\"  ]]","chEntries":["靜脈","血管","礦脈","紋路","風格"],"practiceMeaning":"地質學家們在尋找金礦脈。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 fēn，向上可追溯至拉丁語 vena，意為「血管，水道」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。名詞義指將血液從身體各部位輸送到心臟的血管，也引申指礦藏所在的「礦脈」，物體表面的「紋路」，或人或事物中某種「風格」或「特質」。中文翻譯為「靜脈；血管；礦脈；紋路；風格」。","definition":"1. one of the tubes that carry blood from the body to the heart; 2. a line of mineral ore within a rock; 3. a pattern of lines in something, such as a leaf or a piece of wood; 4. a particular style or manner.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The nurse drew blood from a vein in his arm.\",\n    \"ch\": \"護士從他手臂的一條靜脈抽了血。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Geologists searched for a vein of gold.\",\n    \"ch\": \"地質學家們在尋找金礦脈。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The marble had a beautiful vein pattern.\",\n    \"ch\": \"大理石有著美麗的紋路。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His writing has a sarcastic vein.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的寫作帶有一種諷刺的風格。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"地質學家們在尋找金礦脈。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5348,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l1::worship::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He felt a sense of ____ for his idol.","expectedAnswer":"worship","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He felt a sense of ____ for his idol.","clozeAnswer":"worship","exampleTranslation":"他對他的偶像感到一種崇拜之情。","reference":{"eng":"worship","kk":"ˈwɜːrʃɪp","tense":"n.","ch":"[['崇拜'], ['敬拜'], ['禮拜']]","chEntries":["崇拜","敬拜","禮拜"],"practiceMeaning":"他對他的偶像感到一種崇拜之情。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 weorþscipe，由 weorþ（價值、尊嚴）+ -scipe（狀態、職位，相當於現代的 -ship）組成。原始語意為「價值、尊嚴的狀態」。後演變為「對神祇或崇高事物的尊敬與崇拜」。構詞上，weorþ- 表示「價值、值得」，-scipe 構成抽象名詞。現代語意主要指宗教上的「崇拜、敬拜」。","definition":"adoration and devotion accorded to a deity or to something considered divine or sacred; great love or admiration for someone or something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Religious worship often involves prayer and hymns.\",\n    \"ch\": \"宗教崇拜通常包括祈禱和聖歌。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He felt a sense of worship for his idol.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對他的偶像感到一種崇拜之情。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他對他的偶像感到一種崇拜之情。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3197,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::abstract::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The book deals with ____ philosophical problems.","expectedAnswer":"abstract","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The book deals with ____ philosophical problems.","clozeAnswer":"abstract","exampleTranslation":"這本書探討抽象的哲學問題。","reference":{"eng":"abstract","kk":"/ˈæbstrækt/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['抽象的'], ['深奧的'], ['非實體的'], ['理論上的']]","chEntries":["抽象的","深奧的","非實體的","理論上的"],"practiceMeaning":"這本書探討抽象的哲學問題。","analysis":"詞源來自拉丁文 'abstractus'，意為 'drawn away'，即分離、抽出。此字首 'abs-' 意為 'away'，'trahere' 意為 'to draw'。引申為非具體的、概念性的，與具體 'concrete' 相反。","definition":"1. existing in thought or as an idea but not having a physical or concrete existence; 2. relating to or involving general ideas or qualities rather than specific people, events, or things; 3. difficult to understand; abstruse; 4. (of art) not representing reality in a conventional way.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Love is an abstract concept.\",\n    \"ch\": \"愛是一個抽象的概念。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a very abstract way of thinking.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的思考方式非常抽象。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The book deals with abstract philosophical problems.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本書探討抽象的哲學問題。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這本書探討抽象的哲學問題。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U41"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6153,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::alliance::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of their families was beneficial.","expectedAnswer":"alliance","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of their families was beneficial.","clozeAnswer":"alliance","exampleTranslation":"他們家族之間的結合是有益的。","reference":{"eng":"alliance","kk":"əˈlaɪəns","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"聯盟\"  ],  [    \"聯合\"  ],  [    \"結合\"  ],  [    \"姻親關係\"  ]]","chEntries":["聯盟","聯合","結合","姻親關係"],"practiceMeaning":"他們家族之間的結合是有益的。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 aliance「聯盟」，源自動詞 alier「聯合」，最終可追溯至拉丁語 alligare，意為「綁縛、聯合」，由 ad- (to) + ligare (to bind) 組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 ligare「綁縛」是其核心語意來源。作為名詞，其核心語義是兩個或多個實體（國家、組織、個人）基於共同目標或利益而形成的聯合或結合。詞源中的「綁縛」概念清晰地體現了聯盟的緊密聯繫。此義項由「聯合」的動作延伸出「聯盟」的狀態或組織。","definition":"1. a union or association formed for mutual benefit, especially between countries or organizations; 2. a close connection or relationship, especially one involving shared interests or goals; 3. a relationship by marriage between two families or groups.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The two countries formed a military alliance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"兩國組成了一個軍事聯盟。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This alliance was strategic for both sides.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個聯盟對雙方來說都是戰略性的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The alliance of their families was beneficial.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們家族之間的結合是有益的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A political alliance was formed to contest the election.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一個政治聯盟為了競選而成立。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們家族之間的結合是有益的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4199,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::benefit::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Many people ____ from the public library.","expectedAnswer":"benefit","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Many people ____ from the public library.","clozeAnswer":"benefit","exampleTranslation":"許多人從公共圖書館中獲益。","reference":{"eng":"benefit","kk":"/ˈbenɪfɪt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['使受益；對…有益'], ['從…獲益']]","chEntries":["使受益","對…有益","從…獲益"],"practiceMeaning":"許多人從公共圖書館中獲益。","analysis":"動詞形式源自名詞 'benefit'，表示“給予好處”或“從好處中獲取”。1. “使受益”是被動的語境，表示某事物對他人或他物產生了積極影響。2. “從…獲益”是主動的語境，表示從某事中得到好處。詞源與名詞相同，都與“好”和“做”相關。","definition":"1. to receive an advantage or profit from something; 2. to be useful or helpful to someone.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The new policy will benefit everyone.\",\n    \"ch\": \"新政策將使每個人受益。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He benefited greatly from his teacher's advice.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他從老師的建議中獲益良多。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Many people benefit from the public library.\",\n    \"ch\": \"許多人從公共圖書館中獲益。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"許多人從公共圖書館中獲益。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5622,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l7::bold::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He made a ____ decision to invest in the startup.","expectedAnswer":"bold","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He made a ____ decision to invest in the startup.","clozeAnswer":"bold","exampleTranslation":"他做出了大膽的決定，投資那家初創公司。","reference":{"eng":"bold","kk":"boʊld","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['大膽的'], ['勇敢的'], ['魯莽的'], ['醒目的'], ['粗體的']]","chEntries":["大膽的","勇敢的","魯莽的","醒目的","粗體的"],"practiceMeaning":"他做出了大膽的決定，投資那家初創公司。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 'bāld'，其原始日耳曼語形式為 *balþuz。構詞學上，此字通常被視為一個整體詞，詞源與「強壯」、「大膽」相關。語意核心是「敢於冒險」、「不畏縮」。從「勇敢」、「無畏」引申出「魯莽」的負面含義。在印刷術中，指字體「粗體」，因為這種字體看起來更「醒目」、「強壯」。","definition":"1. Showing an ability to take risks; confident and courageous; 2. (Of a color, design, or shape) having a strong or vivid appearance; 3. (Of print) having the letters thicker and heavier than normal; 4. Showing an impudent lack of respect.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She was bold enough to ask for a raise.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她大膽到足以要求加薪。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The designer used bold colors in the artwork.\",\n    \"ch\": \"設計師在這件藝術品中使用了醒目的顏色。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He made a bold decision to invest in the startup.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他做出了大膽的決定，投資那家初創公司。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please format the headings in bold.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請將標題格式化為粗體。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他做出了大膽的決定，投資那家初創公司。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5829,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::circuit::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They are planning a lecture ____.","expectedAnswer":"circuit","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They are planning a lecture ____.","clozeAnswer":"circuit","exampleTranslation":"他們正在規劃一個演講巡迴路線。","reference":{"eng":"circuit","kk":"ˈsɜːrkɪt","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"電路\"  ],  [    \"迴路\"  ],  [    \"巡迴路線\"  ],  [    \"週期\"  ],  [    \"環形\"  ]]","chEntries":["電路","迴路","巡迴路線","週期","環形"],"practiceMeaning":"他們正在規劃一個演講巡迴路線。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'circuitus'，是 'circuire' (to go around) 的過去分詞，由 'circum' (around) 和 'ire' (to go) 構成。'Circuitus' 的字面意思是「繞行」，引申為「圍繞一圈的路線」或「封閉的循環」。在物理學上，'circuit' 指電流沿著封閉路徑流動的「電路」或「迴路」。在地理或旅行語境中，'circuit' 指「巡迴路線」，如馬戲團或表演團體的巡迴演出路線。它強調的是一種「循環」或「繞行」的概念。例如，也可指「一場比賽的賽道」。","definition":"1. A roughly circular or oval area or path.; 2. A complete electrical path, consisting of wires, components, and a power source.; 3. A route or journey that visits a number of places.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The electrician checked the electrical circuit.\",\n    \"ch\": \"電工檢查了電路。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The race car driver completed another circuit of the track.\",\n    \"ch\": \"賽車手又完成了一圈賽道。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They are planning a lecture circuit.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們正在規劃一個演講巡迴路線。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The Formula 1 circuit is known for its speed.\",\n    \"ch\": \"F1 賽道以其速度聞名。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們正在規劃一個演講巡迴路線。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6158,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::coherent::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The team needs to present a ____ plan.","expectedAnswer":"coherent","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The team needs to present a ____ plan.","clozeAnswer":"coherent","exampleTranslation":"這個團隊需要提出一個前後一致的計畫。","reference":{"eng":"coherent","kk":"koʊˈhɪərənt","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"連貫的\"  ],  [    \"條理清晰的\"  ],  [    \"前後一致的\"  ],  [    \"能理解的\"  ]]","chEntries":["連貫的","條理清晰的","前後一致的","能理解的"],"practiceMeaning":"這個團隊需要提出一個前後一致的計畫。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 cohaerēns，是 cohaerēre「緊密結合、一致」的現在分詞。cohaerēre 由 com- (together) + haerēre (to stick, cling) 組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 com-「一起」和 haerēre「黏合」是其核心語意來源。作為形容詞，其核心語義是「緊密結合，能夠清晰地理解」。從「黏合在一起」引申出「條理清晰、前後一致、易於理解」的語義，特別用於描述論點、計劃或思緒。詞源中的「黏合」概念是其連結性和一致性的基礎。","definition":"1. logical and consistent; 2. able to be understood or believed; 3. forming a whole; 4. (of a group of people) united.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His argument was coherent and well-supported.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的論點連貫且有充分的證據支持。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She found it difficult to make a coherent speech.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她發現很難發表一篇條理清晰的演講。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The team needs to present a coherent plan.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個團隊需要提出一個前後一致的計畫。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"After the accident, he was unable to speak in a coherent manner.\",\n    \"ch\": \"事故發生後，他無法清晰地表達。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個團隊需要提出一個前後一致的計畫。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6162,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::collective::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The artist ____ displayed their latest works.","expectedAnswer":"collective","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The artist ____ displayed their latest works.","clozeAnswer":"collective","exampleTranslation":"藝術家集體展示了他們最新的作品。","reference":{"eng":"collective","kk":"kəˈlɛktɪv","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"集體\"  ],  [    \"組織\"  ],  [    \"合作社\"  ]]","chEntries":["集體","組織","合作社"],"practiceMeaning":"藝術家集體展示了他們最新的作品。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 collectīvus，是動詞 colligere「收集、聚集」的衍生形容詞。colligere 由 com- (together) + legere (to gather) 組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 com-「一起」和 legere「收集」是其核心語意來源。作為名詞，其核心語義是「一個由多個個體組成的團體，共同行動或共享」。詞源中的「一起收集」概念引申為「聚集在一起的群體」。此義項由形容詞「集體的」名詞化而來。","definition":"1. a group of people or things functioning as a single unit; 2. a cooperative association.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The workers formed a collective to improve their conditions.\",\n    \"ch\": \"工人們組成了一個集體來改善他們的處境。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The farm operated as a collective.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個農場作為一個合作社運營。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The artist collective displayed their latest works.\",\n    \"ch\": \"藝術家集體展示了他們最新的作品。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They are part of a writers' collective.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們是一個作家團體的成員。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"藝術家集體展示了他們最新的作品。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3071,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::crack::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The team managed to ____ the code.","expectedAnswer":"crack","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The team managed to ____ the code.","clozeAnswer":"crack","exampleTranslation":"團隊設法破解了密碼。","reference":{"eng":"crack","kk":"/kræk/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['破裂；斷裂'], ['使（聲音）嘶啞'], ['破解；解決（難題）'], ['（尤指戰時）嚴厲批評']]","chEntries":["破裂","斷裂","使嘶啞","破解","解決","嚴厲批評"],"practiceMeaning":"團隊設法破解了密碼。","analysis":"源自古英語 'cracian'，或與斯堪地那維亞語有關。核心意義是「產生縫隙」或「突然斷裂」。\n1. 破裂；斷裂：指物體表面出現裂縫或完全斷開。\n2. 使（聲音）嘶啞：指聲音因壓力、疲勞或情緒而變得不穩定、沙啞。\n3. 破解；解決（難題）：指成功解決複雜的問題或破解密碼。\n4. （尤指戰時）嚴厲批評：指強烈、直接地指出某人的錯誤或缺陷。","definition":"1. to break without dividing into two completely separate pieces; 2. to make a sudden loud noise; 3. to break something into many pieces; 4. to say something in a voice that is not steady because you are sad or angry; 5. to solve a problem or find the answer to something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The ice on the lake began to crack.\",\n    \"ch\": \"湖面上的冰開始破裂。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His voice cracked when he tried to speak.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他試圖說話時聲音變嘶啞了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The team managed to crack the code.\",\n    \"ch\": \"團隊設法破解了密碼。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The newspaper cracked down on the corrupt politician.\",\n    \"ch\": \"報紙嚴厲抨擊了腐敗的政客。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"團隊設法破解了密碼。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4222,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::credit::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She was given ____ for her hard work.","expectedAnswer":"credit","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She was given ____ for her hard work.","clozeAnswer":"credit","exampleTranslation":"她因辛勤工作而受到讚揚。","reference":{"eng":"credit","kk":"/ˈkredɪt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['信用；信譽'], ['（金融機構的）信貸；延期付款'], ['（在帳戶中的）貸方餘額；進帳'], ['功勞；讚揚']]","chEntries":["信用","信譽","信貸","延期付款","貸方餘額","進帳","功勞","讚揚"],"practiceMeaning":"她因辛勤工作而受到讚揚。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 creditum，'credere'（相信，信任）的派生詞。核心是“相信”或“信任”。1. “信用；信譽”指個人或機構的良好聲譽，使人願意相信其承諾。2. “信貸；延期付款”指金融機構基於信任而提供的貸款或允許延期支付。3. “貸方餘額；進帳”指銀行帳戶中的正面餘額。4. “功勞；讚揚”指因某人的貢獻而給予的肯定，基於相信其功績。","definition":"1. the ability of a customer to obtain goods or services before payment, based on the trust that payment will be made in the future; 2. trust in the believe that someone will do what they are expected or supposed to do; 3. an amount of money added to an account; 4. praise or admiration for an achievement.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has good credit and can easily get a loan.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的信用很好，很容易獲得貸款。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"You can buy this item on credit.\",\n    \"ch\": \"你可以賒帳購買這個物品。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She was given credit for her hard work.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她因辛勤工作而受到讚揚。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The deposit will be shown as a credit on your statement.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這筆存款將顯示為您對帳單上的進帳。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她因辛勤工作而受到讚揚。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3076,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::critical::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The patient is in ____ condition.","expectedAnswer":"critical","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The patient is in ____ condition.","clozeAnswer":"critical","exampleTranslation":"病人的情況危急。","reference":{"eng":"critical","kk":"/ˈkrɪtɪkl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['批判性的；挑剔的'], ['關鍵性的；重要的'], ['（情況）危急的；嚴重的'], ['（意見、評論）批評性的；評價性的']]","chEntries":["批判性的","挑剔的","關鍵性的","重要的","危急的","嚴重的","批評性的","評價性的"],"practiceMeaning":"病人的情況危急。","analysis":"源自希臘語 'kritikos' (able to judge)，是 'critic' 的形容詞形式。核心意義是「與判斷或評價相關」。\n1. 批判性的；挑剔的：指對事物進行仔細檢查，並指出其缺點或錯誤的態度。\n2. 關鍵性的；重要的：指對某事物的發展或成功至關重要的。\n3. （情況）危急的；嚴重的：指處於非常重要或危險的關頭，需要緊急處理。\n4. （意見、評論）批評性的；評價性的：指旨在分析和評價某事物優缺點的。","definition":"1. involving careful judgment or discriminating analysis; 2. extremely important or necessary; 3. involving the danger of failure or disaster; 4. expressing adverse or disapproving comments or judgments.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a critical attitude towards any new proposal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對任何新提案都持批判態度。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a critical moment in the negotiations.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是談判中的關鍵時刻。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The patient is in critical condition.\",\n    \"ch\": \"病人的情況危急。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His critical review of the book was widely read.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對這本書的評價性評論被廣泛閱讀。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"病人的情況危急。","sourceName":"字彙王、龍騰課本","unitName":"U39、L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3136,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::curse::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This drought seems to ____ the land.","expectedAnswer":"curse","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This drought seems to ____ the land.","clozeAnswer":"curse","exampleTranslation":"這場乾旱似乎在折磨這片土地。","reference":{"eng":"curse","kk":"/kɜːrs/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['詛咒；咒罵'], ['（使）遭殃；（使）遭受不幸']]","chEntries":["詛咒","咒罵","遭殃","遭受不幸"],"practiceMeaning":"這場乾旱似乎在折磨這片土地。","analysis":"詞源來自拉丁語 'cursus'，意為「跑」，原指「跑來跑去，橫衝直撞」，引申為「災禍，不幸」。'Curse' 作動詞時，可以指祈求或施加超自然的力量造成不幸（詛咒），也可以指使用髒話或冒犯性的語言（咒罵）。更廣泛的用法是指將某事視為不幸的根源，或聲稱某事是災難的起因。","definition":"1. utter imprecations upon, or direct abusive language towards (someone or something); 2. inflict or call down evil or misfortune upon; 3. to cause great harm or suffering to.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The witch cursed the prince to turn into a frog.\",\n    \"ch\": \"女巫詛咒王子變成青蛙。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He cursed loudly when he stubbed his toe.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他踢到腳趾時大聲咒罵。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This drought seems to curse the land.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這場乾旱似乎在折磨這片土地。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這場乾旱似乎在折磨這片土地。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4349,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::decrease::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ in demand led to lower prices.","expectedAnswer":"decrease","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ in demand led to lower prices.","clozeAnswer":"decrease","exampleTranslation":"需求的減少導致價格下跌。","reference":{"eng":"decrease","kk":"/ˈdiːkriːs/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['減少；降低']]","chEntries":["減少","降低"],"practiceMeaning":"需求的減少導致價格下跌。","analysis":"名詞形式，源自動詞 'decrease'，指『減少的數量或程度』，與『增加』相對。","definition":"a reduction in the size, amount, or number of something","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There has been a decrease in violent crime.\",\n    \"ch\": \"暴力犯罪有所減少。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We observed a significant decrease in temperature.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們觀察到氣溫顯著下降。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The decrease in demand led to lower prices.\",\n    \"ch\": \"需求的減少導致價格下跌。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"需求的減少導致價格下跌。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5833,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::descriptive::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He gave a ____ report of the event.","expectedAnswer":"descriptive","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He gave a ____ report of the event.","clozeAnswer":"descriptive","exampleTranslation":"他對這次事件做了一個詳盡的報告。","reference":{"eng":"descriptive","kk":"dɪˈskrɪptɪv","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"描述性的\"  ],  [    \"描寫性的\"  ],  [    \"詳盡的\"  ]]","chEntries":["描述性的","描寫性的","詳盡的"],"practiceMeaning":"他對這次事件做了一個詳盡的報告。","analysis":"此字由名詞 'description' 加上形容詞字尾 '-ive' 構成。'Description' 源自拉丁語 'descriptio'，由 'de-' (down) 和 'scribere' (to write) 構成，字面意思是「寫下」（細節）。'-ive' 是常見的形容詞字尾，表示「具有……性質的」或「傾向於……」。因此，'descriptive' 指「具有描述性質的」或「用來描述的」。它強調的是對事物特徵、細節進行刻畫和描繪的功能。例如，也可指「詳盡的」敘述。","definition":"1. Serving or seeking to describe, especially by giving full, accurate details.; 2. Relating to or characteristic of description.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The author provided a descriptive account of the journey.\",\n    \"ch\": \"作者提供了關於這次旅程的詳細描述。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The book uses descriptive language.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本書使用了描寫性的語言。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He gave a descriptive report of the event.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對這次事件做了一個詳盡的報告。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The teacher asked for a descriptive essay.\",\n    \"ch\": \"老師要求寫一篇描寫性的文章。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他對這次事件做了一個詳盡的報告。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5834,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::destructive::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The wildfire had a ____ impact on the forest.","expectedAnswer":"destructive","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The wildfire had a ____ impact on the forest.","clozeAnswer":"destructive","exampleTranslation":"野火對森林造成了毀滅性的影響。","reference":{"eng":"destructive","kk":"dɪˈstrʌktɪv","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"破壞性的\"  ],  [    \"毀滅性的\"  ],  [    \"有害的\"  ]]","chEntries":["破壞性的","毀滅性的","有害的"],"practiceMeaning":"野火對森林造成了毀滅性的影響。","analysis":"此字由拉丁語 'destructivus' 演變而來，是 'destruere' (to destroy) 的派生詞。'Destruere' 由 'de-' (down) 和 'struere' (to build, to pile up) 構成，字面意思是「拆毀」、「推倒」。'-ive' 是常見的形容詞字尾，表示「具有……性質的」。因此，'destructive' 指「具有破壞性質的」或「傾向於破壞」。它描述的是對事物造成損害、毀滅或瓦解的力量或行為。例如，也可指「對個人身心有害的」。","definition":"1. Causing great damage or destruction.; 2. Tending or likely to destroy.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The hurricane caused destructive winds.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這場颶風帶來了毀滅性的強風。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His criticism was destructive rather than constructive.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的批評具有破壞性而非建設性。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The wildfire had a destructive impact on the forest.\",\n    \"ch\": \"野火對森林造成了毀滅性的影響。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Negative thinking can be destructive.\",\n    \"ch\": \"消極思維可能是有害的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"野火對森林造成了毀滅性的影響。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4184,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::dust::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He sprinkled some flour ____ over the cake.","expectedAnswer":"dust","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He sprinkled some flour ____ over the cake.","clozeAnswer":"dust","exampleTranslation":"他撒了一些麵粉粉末在蛋糕上。","reference":{"eng":"dust","kk":"/dʌst/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['灰塵；塵土'], ['粉末'], ['（植物的）花粉']]","chEntries":["灰塵","塵土","粉末","花粉"],"practiceMeaning":"他撒了一些麵粉粉末在蛋糕上。","analysis":"源自古英語 dust，指“微小的乾燥顆粒”。詞源不詳，可能與印歐語 *dheus-（吹，煙）有關。核心意義是散布在地表或空中的微小顆粒。引申義可用於指任何細小的粉末狀物質，如化妝品、藥粉，或植物的花粉。","definition":"1. fine, dry powder consisting of tiny particles of earth or from other matter; 2. powder, especially that of flour or a cosmetic.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The furniture was covered in dust.\",\n    \"ch\": \"家具上覆蓋著一層灰塵。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She sneezed when the dust tickled her nose.\",\n    \"ch\": \"灰塵癢到她的鼻子，她打了個噴嚏。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He sprinkled some flour dust over the cake.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他撒了一些麵粉粉末在蛋糕上。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他撒了一些麵粉粉末在蛋糕上。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3144,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::dynamic::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Her ____ personality made her popular with everyone.","expectedAnswer":"dynamic","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Her ____ personality made her popular with everyone.","clozeAnswer":"dynamic","exampleTranslation":"她充滿活力的個性讓她深受大家喜愛。","reference":{"eng":"dynamic","kk":"/daɪˈnæmɪk/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['動態的；充滿活力的'], ['（力量、過程）不斷變化的'], ['（人）精力充沛的；活躍的']]","chEntries":["動態的","充滿活力的","不斷變化的","精力充沛的","活躍的"],"practiceMeaning":"她充滿活力的個性讓她深受大家喜愛。","analysis":"源自希臘語 'dynamikos'，意為「有力量的，強大的」，與 'dynamis'（力量）有關。'Dynamic' 強調的是能量、活力、變化和持續的活動。它與「static」（靜態的）相對。語意延伸至形容人、系統、過程或事物，這些都具有不斷變化、發展或活躍的特質。","definition":"1. characterized by constant change, activity, or progress; 2. (of a process or system) characterized by energy and enthusiasm; 3. relating to forces or energy.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company has a very dynamic management team.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司擁有一支極具活力的管理團隊。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The political situation is very dynamic at the moment.\",\n    \"ch\": \"目前的政治局勢變化非常快。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her dynamic personality made her popular with everyone.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她充滿活力的個性讓她深受大家喜愛。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她充滿活力的個性讓她深受大家喜愛。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6224,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::exterior::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Despite his stern ____, he was a kind man.","expectedAnswer":"exterior","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Despite his stern ____, he was a kind man.","clozeAnswer":"exterior","exampleTranslation":"儘管他外表嚴肅，他卻是個善良的人。","reference":{"eng":"exterior","kk":"ɪkˈstɪəriər","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"外觀\"  ],  [    \"外景\"  ],  [    \"外部\"  ]]","chEntries":["外觀","外景","外部"],"practiceMeaning":"儘管他外表嚴肅，他卻是個善良的人。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 exterior，是 externus（外面的）的比較級，意為「更外面的」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。名詞義指某物或某人的外部表面、外觀或外形，尤指建築物、車輛等的外部特徵。也指拍攝地點在戶外。中文翻譯為「外觀；外景；外部」。","definition":"1. the outer surface or structure of something; 2. a person's outward appearance and behavior; 3. a scene or location filmed outdoors.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The house has a beautiful brick exterior.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座房子有著美麗的磚砌外觀。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The film was shot on location, with many exterior scenes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這部電影是在外景地拍攝的，有很多戶外場景。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Despite his stern exterior, he was a kind man.\",\n    \"ch\": \"儘管他外表嚴肅，他卻是個善良的人。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"儘管他外表嚴肅，他卻是個善良的人。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4404,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u9::extreme::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The expedition faced ____ conditions.","expectedAnswer":"extreme","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The expedition faced ____ conditions.","clozeAnswer":"extreme","exampleTranslation":"這次探險面臨極端惡劣的條件。","reference":{"eng":"extreme","kk":"/ɪkˈstriːm/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['極端的', '極大的'], ['極端的', '過激的'], ['極大的', '最大的']]","chEntries":["極端的","極大的","過激的","最大的"],"practiceMeaning":"這次探險面臨極端惡劣的條件。","analysis":"詞源自拉丁語 'extremus'，'ex-' (out) 的最高級。意為「最外面的、最後的」。引申為程度、數量、行為等達到最高或最甚的狀態。","definition":"very great or severe; reaching a high or the highest degree; very different from normal or from each other.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a man of extreme views.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他持有極端的觀點。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The country faced extreme poverty.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該國面臨極度貧困。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The expedition faced extreme conditions.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這次探險面臨極端惡劣的條件。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這次探險面臨極端惡劣的條件。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4321,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::fuel::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His angry words only served to ____ the argument.","expectedAnswer":"fuel","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His angry words only served to ____ the argument.","clozeAnswer":"fuel","exampleTranslation":"他憤怒的話語只是火上澆油，加劇了爭論。","reference":{"eng":"fuel","kk":"/ˈfjuːəl/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['燃料；燃燒物'], ['（助長）動力；食糧']]","chEntries":["燃料","燃燒物","動力","食糧"],"practiceMeaning":"他憤怒的話語只是火上澆油，加劇了爭論。","analysis":"源自古法語 'fouail'，意為 'firewood'，來自拉丁語 'foculus'，意為『壁爐』，最終源自 'focus' (hearth, fire)。最初指用於生火的物質，如木柴。引申為任何可以燃燒產生能量的物質，即『燃料』。另外，它還可以作為比喻，指『提供動力或助長某事（如衝突、爭論）的因素』，相當於『食糧、燃料』。","definition":"a substance such as coal, oil, or gas that is burned to produce heat or energy; something that increases or makes a feeling stronger","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The car runs on unleaded fuel.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這輛車使用無鉛燃料。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Rising energy prices have put a strain on household fuel budgets.\",\n    \"ch\": \"能源價格上漲給家庭燃料預算帶來了壓力。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His angry words only served to fuel the argument.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他憤怒的話語只是火上澆油，加劇了爭論。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他憤怒的話語只是火上澆油，加劇了爭論。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5844,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::masterpiece::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The architect's design was a true ____.","expectedAnswer":"masterpiece","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The architect's design was a true ____.","clozeAnswer":"masterpiece","exampleTranslation":"這位建築師的設計是真正的傑作。","reference":{"eng":"masterpiece","kk":"ˈmæstərpiːs","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"傑作\"  ],  [    \"名作\"  ],  [    \"曠世之作\"  ],  [    \"代表作\"  ]]","chEntries":["傑作","名作","曠世之作","代表作"],"practiceMeaning":"這位建築師的設計是真正的傑作。","analysis":"此字為複合詞，由 'master' (大師) 和 'piece' (作品) 組成。'Master' 源自古英語 'mægester'，來自拉丁語 'magister' (chief, leader, teacher)。'Piece' 源自古法語 'piece'，意為「部分」、「塊」。'Masterpiece' 的字面意思是「大師的作品」，指由一位技藝高超的藝術家或工匠創作的、具有極高藝術價值和技巧的傑出作品。它強調的是作者的「大師級」技藝和作品本身的「非凡」水準。","definition":"1. A work of outstanding artistry, skill, or workmanship.; 2. A person's best piece of work.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The Mona Lisa is a masterpiece by Leonardo da Vinci.\",\n    \"ch\": \"《蒙娜麗莎》是達文西的傑作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This novel is considered his masterpiece.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本小說被認為是他的代表作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The architect's design was a true masterpiece.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位建築師的設計是真正的傑作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The symphony was hailed as a masterpiece.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這首交響樂被譽為傑作。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這位建築師的設計是真正的傑作。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6180,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::miniature::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This is a perfect ____ of the actual castle.","expectedAnswer":"miniature","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This is a perfect ____ of the actual castle.","clozeAnswer":"miniature","exampleTranslation":"這是一個實際城堡的完美縮影。","reference":{"eng":"miniature","kk":"ˈmɪniətʃər","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"縮影\"  ],  [    \"微型模型\"  ],  [    \"微型畫\"  ]]","chEntries":["縮影","微型模型","微型畫"],"practiceMeaning":"這是一個實際城堡的完美縮影。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 miniatura，與 miniare「塗色」有關。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作為名詞，其核心語義是指「一個非常小的複製品或模型」。此義項由形容詞「小型的、微型的」名詞化而來，指代具體的微小事物。","definition":"1. a thing that is very small in size; 2. a very small copy of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He collects miniatures of famous landmarks.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他收藏了著名地標的縮影模型。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The museum has a display of medieval miniatures.\",\n    \"ch\": \"博物館展出了中世紀的微型畫。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a perfect miniature of the actual castle.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個實際城堡的完美縮影。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She bought a miniature of the Eiffel Tower as a souvenir.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她買了一個巴黎鐵塔的縮影作為紀念品。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是一個實際城堡的完美縮影。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3100,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::monitor::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ship's ____ tracked the enemy aircraft.","expectedAnswer":"monitor","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ship's ____ tracked the enemy aircraft.","clozeAnswer":"monitor","exampleTranslation":"艦船的監視器追蹤了敵機。","reference":{"eng":"monitor","kk":"/ˈmɑːnɪtər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['顯示器；螢幕'], ['（學習、進展等的）監督者；指導者'], ['（飛機、艦船等）監視器']]","chEntries":["顯示器","螢幕","監督者","指導者","監視器"],"practiceMeaning":"艦船的監視器追蹤了敵機。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'monitor' (one who warns)，'monere' (to warn, remind)。指「觀察」或「警告」的工具或人。\n1. 顯示器；螢幕：指用於顯示電腦圖像或影片的設備。\n2. （學習、進展等的）監督者；指導者：指負責觀察、指導或評估某人學習或進展的人。\n3. （飛機、艦船等）監視器：指用於監測、觀察或控制特定設備或系統的裝置。","definition":"1. a screen used with a computer; 2. a person who monitors something; 3. a device used to watch or record something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Connect the cable to the computer monitor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"將電纜連接到電腦顯示器。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She was appointed as a monitor for the student council.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她被任命為學生會的監督員。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The ship's monitor tracked the enemy aircraft.\",\n    \"ch\": \"艦船的監視器追蹤了敵機。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"艦船的監視器追蹤了敵機。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4311,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::native::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She has a ____ talent for music.","expectedAnswer":"native","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She has a ____ talent for music.","clozeAnswer":"native","exampleTranslation":"她有音樂方面的天賦。","reference":{"eng":"native","kk":"/ˈneɪtɪv/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['本國的；土生土長的'], ['天生的；固有的']]","chEntries":["本國的","土生土長的","天生的","固有的"],"practiceMeaning":"她有音樂方面的天賦。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'nativus'，意為 'by birth, inborn'，來自 'nasci' (to be born)。這個詞的本義與『出生』直接相關。作為形容詞，它延伸出『出生地固有』、『土生』、『天生具有』等含義。可以指地理上的出生地，也可以指事物固有的、與生俱來的特質。","definition":"belonging to or relating to the place or circumstances in which you were born or that you grew up in; present, existing, or produced naturally in a particular place","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a native speaker of English.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是英語的母語者。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This plant is native to the rainforest.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種植物是雨林的本土植物。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a native talent for music.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她有音樂方面的天賦。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她有音樂方面的天賦。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4505,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::of::prep","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"A group ____ students arrived.","expectedAnswer":"of","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"A group ____ students arrived.","clozeAnswer":"of","exampleTranslation":"一群學生抵達了。","reference":{"eng":"of","kk":"/əv/, /ɒv/","tense":"prep.","ch":"[['...的'], ['關於'], ['屬於'], ['在...之中']]","chEntries":["...的","關於","屬於","在...之中"],"practiceMeaning":"一群學生抵達了。","analysis":"源自古英語 of。是一個極其常見且語意複雜的介詞。核心功能是表示「從...分離」、「來源」或「屬於」。引申義極廣，包括所有格、部分、來源、原因、組成等。","definition":"1. Expressing the relationship between a part and a whole; 2. Expressing the relationship between a ruler and those ruled; 3. Expressing the relationship between a subject and its object; 4. Expressing the relationship between an author and his work; 5. Expressing the origin or cause of something; 6. Denoting belonging or a close connection.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The cover of the book is blue.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本書的封面是藍色的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is afraid of the dark.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他害怕黑暗。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A group of students arrived.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一群學生抵達了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a piece of cake.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一塊蛋糕。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"一群學生抵達了。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4514,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::on::prep","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The concert is ____ Saturday.","expectedAnswer":"on","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The concert is ____ Saturday.","clozeAnswer":"on","exampleTranslation":"音樂會在星期六。","reference":{"eng":"on","kk":"/ɔːn/","tense":"prep.","ch":"[['在...之上'], ['關於'], ['正在進行（演出、廣播等）'], ['附著於'], ['持續（一段時間）']]","chEntries":["在...之上","關於","正在進行","附著於","持續"],"practiceMeaning":"音樂會在星期六。","analysis":"源自古英語 on。是一個表示位置、時間、狀態的多功能介詞。核心語意是「接觸」、「附著」或「覆蓋」。引申義包括「關於」、「處於某種狀態」等。","definition":"1. Physically in contact with and supported by (a surface); 2. Used to indicate the subject or topic of a conversation or piece of writing; 3. Occupying a particular position or place; 4. In the course of being broadcast or performed.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The book is on the table.\",\n    \"ch\": \"書在桌子上。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They are working on a new project.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們正在進行一個新項目。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The concert is on Saturday.\",\n    \"ch\": \"音樂會在星期六。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He lectured on ancient history.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他講授了古代史。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"音樂會在星期六。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3991,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u3::original::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We are looking for ____ ideas for the campaign.","expectedAnswer":"original","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We are looking for ____ ideas for the campaign.","clozeAnswer":"original","exampleTranslation":"我們正在為這次活動尋找原創的點子。","reference":{"eng":"original","kk":"/əˈrɪdʒɪnəl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['原始的', '最初的'], ['獨創的', '新穎的'], ['原創的']]","chEntries":["原始的","最初的","獨創的","新穎的","原創的"],"practiceMeaning":"我們正在為這次活動尋找原創的點子。","analysis":"詞源：拉丁文 'originalis' (最早的)，源自 'origō' (開端、起源)。指事物的開始、來源，或前所未有的、自己創造的。","definition":"1. present or existing from the beginning; first or earliest; 2. new, creative, and inventive; 3. not a copy; first produced.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is the original manuscript of the novel.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是這本小說的原稿。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a very original way of thinking.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她有非常獨創的思考方式。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We are looking for original ideas for the campaign.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們正在為這次活動尋找原創的點子。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們正在為這次活動尋找原創的點子。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6182,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::pledge::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She gave her necklace as a ____.","expectedAnswer":"pledge","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She gave her necklace as a ____.","clozeAnswer":"pledge","exampleTranslation":"她將項鍊作為抵押品。","reference":{"eng":"pledge","kk":"plɛdʒ","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"保證\"  ],  [    \"承諾\"  ],  [    \"誓言\"  ],  [    \"抵押品\"  ]]","chEntries":["保證","承諾","誓言","抵押品"],"practiceMeaning":"她將項鍊作為抵押品。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 plege，意為「保證、抵押品」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作為名詞，其核心語義是由動詞 pledge「保證、承諾、抵押」名詞化而來，指「一個鄭重的承諾或保證」，或「被用作擔保的物品」。詞源中的「抵押品」概念是其核心，引申出「承諾」和「擔保」的意義。","definition":"1. a solemn promise or undertaking; 2. something given as security for a loan or debt.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He made a pledge to donate money.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他承諾捐款。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The pledge was met with skepticism.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個承諾受到了懷疑。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She gave her necklace as a pledge.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她將項鍊作為抵押品。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The candidate made a pledge to lower taxes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位候選人承諾減稅。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她將項鍊作為抵押品。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5472,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::plenty::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She has ____ of talent.","expectedAnswer":"plenty","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She has ____ of talent.","clozeAnswer":"plenty","exampleTranslation":"她有豐富的才能。","reference":{"eng":"plenty","kk":"ˈplɛnti","tense":"n.","ch":"[['充足'], ['豐富'], ['大量']]","chEntries":["充足","豐富","大量"],"practiceMeaning":"她有豐富的才能。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 'plente'，意為「滿足、充足」，來自拉丁語 'plenitas'（充滿），'plenus'（滿的）。最初在中古英語中，'plenty' 既可用作名詞，表示「充足、豐富」，也可作形容詞，表示「充足的」。作為名詞，它強調的是「足夠或超出需求的量」，即「充足、富裕」。它可以指物質上的充足，也可以指抽象意義上的充裕。","definition":"1. A large or sufficient amount or quantity; more than enough.; 2. Abundance.; 3. A state of abundance.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We have plenty of time.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們有充裕的時間。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There is plenty of food for everyone.\",\n    \"ch\": \"每個人都有足夠的食物。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has plenty of talent.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她有豐富的才能。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她有豐富的才能。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6184,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::plural::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of 'mouse' is 'mice'.","expectedAnswer":"plural","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of 'mouse' is 'mice'.","clozeAnswer":"plural","exampleTranslation":"「mouse」的複數是「mice」。","reference":{"eng":"plural","kk":"ˈplʊrəl","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"複數\"  ],  [    \"複數形式\"  ]]","chEntries":["複數","複數形式"],"practiceMeaning":"「mouse」的複數是「mice」。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 plūrālis，是 plus（更多）的衍生形容詞。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作為名詞，其核心語義是由形容詞 plural「複數的」名詞化而來，指「表示兩個或兩個以上數量的形式或狀態」。詞源中的「更多」概念引申出「多數」和「複數」的用法。","definition":"1. the plural form of a word.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"When forming the plural, we often add 's'.\",\n    \"ch\": \"形成複數時，我們經常加 's'。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The word 'children' is the plural of 'child'.\",\n    \"ch\": \"「children」是「child」的複數。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The plural of 'mouse' is 'mice'.\",\n    \"ch\": \"「mouse」的複數是「mice」。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"「mouse」的複數是「mice」。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6239,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::premier::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The film had its ____ last night.","expectedAnswer":"premier","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The film had its ____ last night.","clozeAnswer":"premier","exampleTranslation":"這部電影昨晚首次上映。","reference":{"eng":"premier","kk":"ˈprɛmɪər","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"首先的\"  ],  [    \"最重要的\"  ],  [    \"第一的\"  ]]","chEntries":["首先的","最重要的","第一的"],"practiceMeaning":"這部電影昨晚首次上映。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 primarius，意為「第一的，主要的」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作形容詞時，指在時間、順序或重要性上居於首位，最重要的。中文翻譯為「首先的；最重要的；第一的」。","definition":"1. first in importance, order, or status; 2. most important; 3. first; earliest.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is the premier dancer in the company.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是公司裡最重要的舞者。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The premier issue facing the country is unemployment.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個國家面臨的首要問題是失業。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The film had its premier last night.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這部電影昨晚首次上映。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這部電影昨晚首次上映。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3884,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::process::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The digestion ____ breaks down food.","expectedAnswer":"process","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The digestion ____ breaks down food.","clozeAnswer":"process","exampleTranslation":"消化過程分解食物。","reference":{"eng":"process","kk":"/ˈprɑːsɛs/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['過程', '程序'], ['手續']]","chEntries":["過程","程序","手續"],"practiceMeaning":"消化過程分解食物。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'processus'，'pro-' (forward) + 'cedere' (to go)。核心是「向前進行」。指一系列連續發生的事件、步驟或操作，以達成某種結果。","definition":"a series of actions or steps taken in order to achieve a particular end.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The manufacturing process is complex.\",\n    \"ch\": \"製造過程很複雜。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"What is the process for applying for a visa?\",\n    \"ch\": \"申請簽證的程序是什麼？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The digestion process breaks down food.\",\n    \"ch\": \"消化過程分解食物。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"消化過程分解食物。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5855,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::radical::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This is a ____ solution to the problem.","expectedAnswer":"radical","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This is a ____ solution to the problem.","clozeAnswer":"radical","exampleTranslation":"這是一個解決問題的徹底方案。","reference":{"eng":"radical","kk":"ˈrædɪkl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"激進的\"  ],  [    \"根本的\"  ],  [    \"徹底的\"  ],  [    \"主根的\"  ]]","chEntries":["激進的","根本的","徹底的","主根的"],"practiceMeaning":"這是一個解決問題的徹底方案。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'radicalis'，是 'radix' (root) 的派生詞。'Radix' 指「根」，引申為「基礎」、「起源」。'-al' 是常見的形容詞字尾。'Radical' 的核心語意與「根」相關，指「關於根部的」或「從根源來的」。這引申出「根本的」、「徹底的」意思，表示涉及事物最基本的部分。引申到政治或社會思想，則指追求根本性變革的「激進的」。例如，也可指「極端的」或「全面的」。","definition":"1. Relating to or affecting the fundamental nature of something; far-reaching or thorough.; 2. (of change or action) advocating or based on thorough or complete political or social change.; 3. Relating to the root of a plant or hair follicle.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The proposal calls for radical changes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這項提議要求進行根本性的改變。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is known for his radical political views.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他以其激進的政治觀點而聞名。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a radical solution to the problem.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個解決問題的徹底方案。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The dentist performed a radical surgery to remove the tumor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"牙醫進行了根除性手術以移除腫瘤。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是一個解決問題的徹底方案。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5803,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::resume::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He updated his ____ with his latest achievements.","expectedAnswer":"resume","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He updated his ____ with his latest achievements.","clozeAnswer":"resume","exampleTranslation":"他更新了他的履歷，加入了最新的成就。","reference":{"eng":"resume","kk":"ˈrɛzʊmeɪ","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"履歷\"  ],  [    \"簡歷\"  ]]","chEntries":["履歷","簡歷"],"practiceMeaning":"他更新了他的履歷，加入了最新的成就。","analysis":"此字為名詞，源自法語résumé，意為「摘要；總結」。法語résumé是動詞résumer（總結）的過去分詞。résumer來自拉丁語resumere（再次拿起；總結）。核心語義是指「個人學經歷、技能和工作經驗的書面總結」，用來申請工作。語意演變上，從「總結」的廣泛概念，具體化為求職用的「個人履歷」。注意：此字名詞發音與動詞不同，且源自法語，常在美式英語中使用，而英式英語更常用CV（Curriculum Vitae）。","definition":"1. a brief summary, especially of something previously written or stated; 2. a document giving a summary of education, qualifications, and previous employment history, sent with a job application.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She attached her resume to the job application.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她將她的履歷附在工作申請上。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The employer asked for a detailed resume.\",\n    \"ch\": \"雇主要求一份詳細的履歷。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He updated his resume with his latest achievements.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他更新了他的履歷，加入了最新的成就。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他更新了他的履歷，加入了最新的成就。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5805,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::shed::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They used the ____ as a workshop.","expectedAnswer":"shed","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They used the ____ as a workshop.","clozeAnswer":"shed","exampleTranslation":"他們把棚屋當作工作室。","reference":{"eng":"shed","kk":"ʃɛd","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"小屋\"  ],  [    \"棚屋\"  ],  [    \"簡陋的建築\"  ]]","chEntries":["小屋","棚屋","簡陋的建築"],"practiceMeaning":"他們把棚屋當作工作室。","analysis":"此字為名詞，與動詞同源。核心語義是指「一個簡單、臨時或用於儲存物品的建築物」。通常是獨立的、簡陋的結構，例如工具棚、自行車棚、飼料棚等。語意演變上，從「脫落」或「分離」引申為「與主建築分離的、簡單的附屬建築」。","definition":"1. a simple structure, typically of wood or metal, built for storage or shelter.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He keeps his gardening tools in the shed.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他把園藝工具放在棚屋裡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The old shed was falling apart.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那個舊棚屋快要散架了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They used the shed as a workshop.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們把棚屋當作工作室。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們把棚屋當作工作室。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6190,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::shiver::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"A ____ of disgust crossed his face.","expectedAnswer":"shiver","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"A ____ of disgust crossed his face.","clozeAnswer":"shiver","exampleTranslation":"一絲厭惡的顫抖劃過他的臉。","reference":{"eng":"shiver","kk":"ˈʃɪvər","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"發抖\"  ],  [    \"顫抖\"  ]]","chEntries":["發抖","顫抖"],"practiceMeaning":"一絲厭惡的顫抖劃過他的臉。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 shiveren。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作為名詞，是動詞 shiver「發抖、顫抖」的名詞化。其核心語義是指「由於寒冷、恐懼或興奮而身體不由自主地顫抖的動作」。","definition":"1. an act of shivering.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He gave a shiver and pulled his coat tighter.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他打了一個寒顫，把外套裹得更緊了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She felt a shiver of anticipation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她感到一陣期待的顫抖。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A shiver of disgust crossed his face.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一絲厭惡的顫抖劃過他的臉。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"一絲厭惡的顫抖劃過他的臉。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6192,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::shove::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ sent him off balance.","expectedAnswer":"shove","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ sent him off balance.","clozeAnswer":"shove","exampleTranslation":"那一推讓他失去了平衡。","reference":{"eng":"shove","kk":"ʃʌv","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"推\"  ],  [    \"擠\"  ]]","chEntries":["推","擠"],"practiceMeaning":"那一推讓他失去了平衡。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 shoven。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作為名詞，是動詞 shove「推、擠」的名詞化。其核心語義是指「用力的推動或擠壓的動作」。","definition":"1. an act of shoving.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He gave me a shove and walked past.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他推了我一把就走過去了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A shove from behind sent him stumbling forward.\",\n    \"ch\": \"身後的一推讓他跌跌撞撞地向前。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The shove sent him off balance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那一推讓他失去了平衡。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"那一推讓他失去了平衡。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6198,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::siege::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The prolonged ____ tested the defenders' resolve.","expectedAnswer":"siege","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The prolonged ____ tested the defenders' resolve.","clozeAnswer":"siege","exampleTranslation":"漫長的圍困考驗了守軍的決心。","reference":{"eng":"siege","kk":"siːdʒ","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"圍攻\"  ],  [    \"包圍\"  ],  [    \"圍困\"  ]]","chEntries":["圍攻","包圍","圍困"],"practiceMeaning":"漫長的圍困考驗了守軍的決心。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 siege，意為「座位、場所、圍攻」，最終源自拉丁語 sedes「座位」，與 sedēre「坐」相關。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 sedēre「坐」是其核心語意來源。作為名詞，其核心語義是「軍隊包圍並試圖佔領一個設防城鎮或據點的軍事行動」。詞源中的「座位」引申為「佔據」，進而發展為「圍攻」的意義。","definition":"1. a military blockade of a city or fortress with the intention of capturing it by assault or starvation; 2. a prolonged period of difficulty or hardship.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The city was under siege for months.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座城市被圍攻了數月。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The siege ended with the enemy's surrender.\",\n    \"ch\": \"圍攻在敵軍投降後結束。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The prolonged siege tested the defenders' resolve.\",\n    \"ch\": \"漫長的圍困考驗了守軍的決心。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The castle endured a long siege.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座城堡經受了漫長的圍攻。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"漫長的圍困考驗了守軍的決心。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4567,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::steady::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He remained ____ in the face of danger.","expectedAnswer":"steady","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He remained ____ in the face of danger.","clozeAnswer":"steady","exampleTranslation":"面對危險，他保持鎮定。","reference":{"eng":"steady","kk":"/ˈstɛdi/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['穩定的', '平穩的'], ['持續的', '不變的'], ['鎮定的', '冷靜的']]","chEntries":["穩定的","平穩的","持續的","不變的","鎮定的","冷靜的"],"practiceMeaning":"面對危險，他保持鎮定。","analysis":"源自古法語 'esté'，'ester' (to stand - 站立) 的派生詞。核心概念是「穩固地站著」。\n    1. 穩定的、平穩的：指不搖晃、不顛簸，狀態持續。\n    2. 持續的、不變的：指時間長久，沒有顯著變化。\n    3. 鎮定的、冷靜的：指情緒或反應沉著，不易受影響。","definition":"1. firmly fixed, supported, or balanced; not shaking or moving.; 2. not changing or fluctuating; regular and continuous.; 3. (of a person or their behavior) not showing extreme emotion; calm and sensible.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a steady hand for surgery.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她做手術時手很穩。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company has shown steady growth over the past decade.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司在過去十年中一直保持穩定增長。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He remained steady in the face of danger.\",\n    \"ch\": \"面對危險，他保持鎮定。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"面對危險，他保持鎮定。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5862,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::sustainable::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company aims for ____ growth.","expectedAnswer":"sustainable","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company aims for ____ growth.","clozeAnswer":"sustainable","exampleTranslation":"該公司旨在實現可持續增長。","reference":{"eng":"sustainable","kk":"səˈsteɪnəbl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"可持續的\"  ],  [    \"可維持的\"  ],  [    \"能長久支持的\"  ],  [    \"不會枯竭的\"  ]]","chEntries":["可持續的","可維持的","能長久支持的","不會枯竭的"],"practiceMeaning":"該公司旨在實現可持續增長。","analysis":"此字由動詞 'sustain' 加上形容詞字尾 '-able' 構成。'Sustain' 源自拉丁語 'sustinere' (to hold up, support)。'-able' 字尾表示「能夠……的」。'Sustainable' 的核心語意是「能夠被維持」、「能夠長期存在或進行」。它特別強調在滿足當前需求的同時，不損害後代滿足其自身需求的發展模式，常用於環境、經濟和社會領域。例如，也可指「不會枯竭的」資源。","definition":"1. Able to be maintained at a certain rate or level.; 2. Relating to or being development that meets the needs of the present without compromising the ability of future generations to meet their own needs.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to develop sustainable energy sources.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要發展可持續能源。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This farming method is more sustainable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種耕作方法更具可持續性。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company aims for sustainable growth.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司旨在實現可持續增長。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The renewable resources are sustainable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這些可再生資源是可持續的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該公司旨在實現可持續增長。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4689,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::tag::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We played ____ in the park.","expectedAnswer":"tag","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We played ____ in the park.","clozeAnswer":"tag","exampleTranslation":"我們在公園玩追逐遊戲。","reference":{"eng":"tag","kk":"/ˈtæɡ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['標籤'], ['（非正式）稱號、綽號'], ['（追蹤、定位用的）標識'], ['（兒童遊戲）追逐遊戲']]","chEntries":["標籤","稱號、綽號","標識","追逐遊戲"],"practiceMeaning":"我們在公園玩追逐遊戲。","analysis":"源自斯堪地那維亞語，意為「懸掛物」。核心是附著在物品上用於識別、標示的物品。延伸至非正式的綽號、用於追蹤的電子標識，以及兒童遊戲中的追逐。'tag question' (附加問句) 也是由 'tag' 的附屬、附加的概念衍生。","definition":"1. A label attached to something for the purpose of identification or information. 2. (informal) A nickname. 3. A device attached to something for tracking or identification purposes. 4. A children's game in which one person chases the others.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please remove the price tag before washing the garment.\",\n    \"ch\": \"清洗衣物前請移除價格標籤。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He's known by the tag 'The Professor'.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他被稱為「教授」。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We played tag in the park.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們在公園玩追逐遊戲。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們在公園玩追逐遊戲。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4516,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::to::prep","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"I came ____ help.","expectedAnswer":"to","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"I came ____ help.","clozeAnswer":"to","exampleTranslation":"我來是為了幫忙。","reference":{"eng":"to","kk":"/tu/","tense":"prep.","ch":"[['向'], ['到'], ['對於'], ['以便']]","chEntries":["向","到","對於","以便"],"practiceMeaning":"我來是為了幫忙。","analysis":"源自古英語 tō。是一個極其常見的介詞，用於表示方向、目的地、目的、範圍、程度、時間等。","definition":"1. Expressing motion in the direction of (a particular location); 2. Expressing the recipient of an action or gift; 3. Up to the point in time or the degree specified; 4. In order to achieve or bring about.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He walked to the store.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他走向商店。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Give it to me.\",\n    \"ch\": \"把它給我。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I came to help.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我來是為了幫忙。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is important to me.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這對我來說很重要。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我來是為了幫忙。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4550,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::trace::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He disappeared without a ____.","expectedAnswer":"trace","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He disappeared without a ____.","clozeAnswer":"trace","exampleTranslation":"他消失得無影無蹤。","reference":{"eng":"trace","kk":"/treɪs/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['蹤跡', '痕跡'], ['微量', '少量']]","chEntries":["蹤跡","痕跡","微量","少量"],"practiceMeaning":"他消失得無影無蹤。","analysis":"源自古法語 'tracer'，意為 'to follow a course, track' (跟蹤、追蹤)。\n    1. 蹤跡、痕跡：指過去事件留下的明顯或細微的證據，如 'footprints are traces of someone's passage' (腳印是某人走過的痕跡)。\n    2. 微量、少量：指極其微小的數量，常與 'of' 搭配，如 'a trace of salt' (一點點鹽)。","definition":"1. a mark, object, or other indication of the existence or passing of something.; 2. a very small quantity of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police found no trace of the missing hikers.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警方沒有找到失蹤的登山客的任何蹤跡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was a trace of perfume in the air.\",\n    \"ch\": \"空氣中有一絲香水味。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He disappeared without a trace.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他消失得無影無蹤。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他消失得無影無蹤。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4565,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::trail::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The winning team was followed by a ____ of cheering fans.","expectedAnswer":"trail","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The winning team was followed by a ____ of cheering fans.","clozeAnswer":"trail","exampleTranslation":"獲勝隊伍後面是一群歡呼的粉絲。","reference":{"eng":"trail","kk":"/treɪl/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['蹤跡', '痕跡'], ['小徑', '步道'], ['（一連串）跟隨者', '追隨者'], ['（飄落或拖曳的）蹤跡，軌跡']]","chEntries":["蹤跡","痕跡","小徑","步道","跟隨者","追隨者","蹤跡，軌跡"],"practiceMeaning":"獲勝隊伍後面是一群歡呼的粉絲。","analysis":"源自古法語 'trahiner'，意為 'to drag' (拖曳)。\n    1. 蹤跡、痕跡：指經過留下的可見或不可見的證據。\n    2. 小徑、步道：指在野外或林間供人行走的小路，常是被不斷踩踏形成的。\n    3. 跟隨者：指跟在前面的人或事物後面的隊伍。\n    4. 蹤跡、軌跡：指物體移動後留下的線條或路徑，如 'smoke trail' (煙跡)。","definition":"1. a mark or a series of signs or objects left behind by the passage of someone or something.; 2. a path or track made through a wild or hilly region.; 3. a series of people or things following behind.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The detective followed the faint trail of footprints.\",\n    \"ch\": \"偵探跟蹤著微弱的腳印蹤跡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We hiked along a beautiful mountain trail.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們沿著一條美麗的山間小徑徒步。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The winning team was followed by a trail of cheering fans.\",\n    \"ch\": \"獲勝隊伍後面是一群歡呼的粉絲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A long train of smoke trailed behind the plane.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一長串煙跡在飛機後面拖曳。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"獲勝隊伍後面是一群歡呼的粉絲。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6204,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::variable::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The amount of interest is ____.","expectedAnswer":"variable","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The amount of interest is ____.","clozeAnswer":"variable","exampleTranslation":"利率是可變的。","reference":{"eng":"variable","kk":"ˈveriəbl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"變化的\"  ],  [    \"易變的\"  ],  [    \"可變的\"  ],  [    \"不定的\"  ]]","chEntries":["變化的","易變的","可變的","不定的"],"practiceMeaning":"利率是可變的。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 variabilis，是動詞 variare「改變」的衍生形容詞。variare 源自 varus「彎曲的、扭曲的」，可能與 varia（斑駁）有關。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 variare「改變」是其核心語意來源。作為形容詞，其核心語義是「能夠或傾向於改變；不穩定的」。詞源中的「改變」概念直接體現了此義。","definition":"1. not always the same; liable to change; 2. able to be changed or adapted.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The weather in this region is very variable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個地區的天氣變化很大。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has a variable temper.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的脾氣很不穩定。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The amount of interest is variable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"利率是可變的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her mood was variable throughout the day.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她一天之間情緒多變。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"利率是可變的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5583,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::classic::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It was a ____ case of misunderstanding.","expectedAnswer":"classic","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It was a ____ case of misunderstanding.","clozeAnswer":"classic","exampleTranslation":"這是一個典型的誤會案例。","reference":{"eng":"classic","kk":"ˈklæsɪk","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['經典的'], ['古典的'], ['典型的'], ['一流的']]","chEntries":["經典的","古典的","典型的","一流的"],"practiceMeaning":"這是一個典型的誤會案例。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 \"classicus\"，意為 \"of or belonging to the highest class, first-class\"（屬於最高級別的，一流的），來自 \"classis\"（a class, fleet, order，階級，艦隊，秩序）。\"classis\" 最初指「羅馬貴族階層」，後來也指「海軍艦隊」，再引申為「類別」或「等級」。因此，\"classic\" 的核心語義是「屬於最高等級、最經典、最受推崇的」。它可以用來形容「古希臘羅馬時期的」（classical antiquity）；指「代表某一類型最高水準的、永恆的」（exemplary, timeless）；或指「典型的、代表性的」（typical）。","definition":"1. Judged over a period of time to be of the highest quality and significance; timeless; 2. Characteristic of or belonging to a past period, especially of ancient Greece or Rome; 3. Familiarly typical or representative.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a classic example of her early work.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是她早期作品的一個經典範例。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The play is a classic of English literature.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這齣戲是英國文學的經典之作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He drives a classic car.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他開一輛經典老爺車。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was a classic case of misunderstanding.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個典型的誤會案例。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是一個典型的誤會案例。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6159,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::coincidence::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of their arriving at the same time was surprising.","expectedAnswer":"coincidence","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of their arriving at the same time was surprising.","clozeAnswer":"coincidence","exampleTranslation":"他們同時到達的巧合令人驚訝。","reference":{"eng":"coincidence","kk":"koʊˈɪnsɪdəns","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"巧合\"  ],  [    \"同時發生\"  ]]","chEntries":["巧合","同時發生"],"practiceMeaning":"他們同時到達的巧合令人驚訝。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 coincidentia，是 coincidentem (coincidens)「同時發生、一致」的現在分詞名詞化。coincidentem 由 com- (together) + inciderē (to fall upon, happen) 組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 com-「一起」和 inciderē「發生、落下」是其核心語意來源。作為名詞，核心語義是「兩個或多個事件恰好同時發生，且彼此之間沒有明顯的因果關係」。詞源中的「一起發生」清楚地體現了此義。","definition":"1. the occurrence and development of events in a happy or beneficial way; 2. a situation in which events happen at the same time in a way that has no obvious connection.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was a remarkable coincidence that they met on the same day.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們在同一天見面真是個令人驚嘆的巧合。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Their birthdays falling on the same day is a strange coincidence.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們的生日落在同一天是一個奇怪的巧合。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"What a coincidence! I was just thinking about you.\",\n    \"ch\": \"真是巧合！我剛在想你。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The coincidence of their arriving at the same time was surprising.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們同時到達的巧合令人驚訝。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們同時到達的巧合令人驚訝。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5831,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::commodity::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ price fluctuated greatly.","expectedAnswer":"commodity","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ price fluctuated greatly.","clozeAnswer":"commodity","exampleTranslation":"該商品的價格劇烈波動。","reference":{"eng":"commodity","kk":"kəˈmɑːdəti","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"商品\"  ],  [    \"物品\"  ],  [    \"價值\"  ],  [    \"必需品\"  ]]","chEntries":["商品","物品","價值","必需品"],"practiceMeaning":"該商品的價格劇烈波動。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'commoditas'，意為「便利」、「舒適」、「比例」、「益處」。'Commoditas' 來自 'commodus' (fitting, convenient)，由 'con-' (together) 和 'modus' (measure) 構成，意指「以適當的度量」。在早期中古英語中，'commodity' 意指「便利」或「有益之物」。後來，其語意演變為「有用的物品」或「可供交易的商品」。現代語義中，'commodity' 特指在市場上可買賣的標準化產品，如農產品、礦產或能源，強調其可交易性和價值。例如，也可指「一種商品的價值」。","definition":"1. A raw material or primary agricultural product that can be bought and sold, such as copper or coffee.; 2. A useful or valuable thing.; 3. Convenience; advantage.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Oil is a major global commodity.\",\n    \"ch\": \"石油是主要的全球商品。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to improve the production of this commodity.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要提高這種商品的產量。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Water is a vital commodity.\",\n    \"ch\": \"水是一種至關重要的必需品。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The commodity price fluctuated greatly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該商品的價格劇烈波動。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該商品的價格劇烈波動。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3134,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::crash::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The stock market ____ of 1929 had devastating consequences.","expectedAnswer":"crash","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The stock market ____ of 1929 had devastating consequences.","clozeAnswer":"crash","exampleTranslation":"1929年的股市崩盤帶來了毀滅性的後果。","reference":{"eng":"crash","kk":"/kræʃ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['碰撞；墜毀'], ['（電腦系統等的）故障，崩潰'], ['（價格的）暴跌'], ['（尤指在某種場合，為了尋求某物而）混進去；不請自來']]","chEntries":["碰撞","墜毀","故障，崩潰","暴跌","混進去","不請自來"],"practiceMeaning":"1929年的股市崩盤帶來了毀滅性的後果。","analysis":"名詞用法，源自動詞 'crash'。指「碰撞」或「墜毀」的事件。也指電腦系統或程式的「故障」或「崩潰」，以及金融市場的「暴跌」。'Crash' 也可以指非正式的「混進」某個派對或場合，通常是沒有被邀請的。","definition":"1. a violent impact or collision; 2. a sudden failure of a computer system or program; 3. a sudden and dramatic fall in prices or values; 4. (informal) an act of attending a party or event uninvited.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police are investigating the cause of the car crash.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警方正在調查這起車禍的原因。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A system crash caused the loss of all data.\",\n    \"ch\": \"系統崩潰導致所有數據丟失。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He decided to crash the party since he wasn't invited.\",\n    \"ch\": \"既然沒有被邀請，他決定混進派對。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The stock market crash of 1929 had devastating consequences.\",\n    \"ch\": \"1929年的股市崩盤帶來了毀滅性的後果。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"1929年的股市崩盤帶來了毀滅性的後果。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5839,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::flexibility::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of the material allowed it to be molded into complex shapes.","expectedAnswer":"flexibility","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of the material allowed it to be molded into complex shapes.","clozeAnswer":"flexibility","exampleTranslation":"這種材料的柔韌性使其能夠被塑造成複雜的形狀。","reference":{"eng":"flexibility","kk":"ˌflɛksəˈbɪləti","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"靈活性\"  ],  [    \"彈性\"  ],  [    \"適應性\"  ],  [    \"柔韌性\"  ]]","chEntries":["靈活性","彈性","適應性","柔韌性"],"practiceMeaning":"這種材料的柔韌性使其能夠被塑造成複雜的形狀。","analysis":"此字由形容詞 'flexible' 加上名詞字尾 '-ity' 構成。'Flexible' 源自拉丁語 'flexibilis'，由 'flectere' (to bend) 構成。'-ity' 是常見的名詞字尾，表示「狀態」、「性質」。因此，'flexibility' 指「能夠彎曲」、「容易改變」的性質或狀態。在物理上，指材料的柔韌性；在引申義上，指個人或組織能夠適應變化、靈活應對挑戰的能力。它強調的是一種「可塑性」或「不受拘束」的特質。","definition":"1. The quality of being easily bent or altered.; 2. The ability to adapt or be adapted to new conditions.; 3. Willingness to consider new ideas; open-mindedness.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The job offers flexibility in working hours.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這份工作提供彈性的工作時間。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His flexibility in negotiations was impressive.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在談判中的靈活性令人印象深刻。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to maintain flexibility in our strategy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要在策略上保持彈性。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The flexibility of the material allowed it to be molded into complex shapes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種材料的柔韌性使其能夠被塑造成複雜的形狀。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這種材料的柔韌性使其能夠被塑造成複雜的形狀。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4526,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::for::prep","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They are fighting ____ their freedom.","expectedAnswer":"for","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They are fighting ____ their freedom.","clozeAnswer":"for","exampleTranslation":"他們正在為自由而戰。","reference":{"eng":"for","kk":"/fər/, /fɔːr/","tense":"prep.","ch":"[['為了'], ['給'], ['支持'], ['持續（一段時間）']]","chEntries":["為了","給","支持","持續"],"practiceMeaning":"他們正在為自由而戰。","analysis":"源自古英語 for。是一個極其常見且語意複雜的介詞。核心語意是「目的」、「原因」、「受益者」。引申義廣泛，包括「持續時間」、「代表」、「傾向」等。","definition":"1. Intended to achieve or affect; 2. In order to benefit or be given to; 3. In support of or in agreement with; 4. During (a period of time).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This gift is for you.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這份禮物是給你的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He works for a large company.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在一家大公司工作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She stayed for two weeks.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她待了兩週。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They are fighting for their freedom.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們正在為自由而戰。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們正在為自由而戰。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5843,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::legitimate::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The couple hoped for a ____ heir to the throne.","expectedAnswer":"legitimate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The couple hoped for a ____ heir to the throne.","clozeAnswer":"legitimate","exampleTranslation":"這對夫婦希望有一位合法的王位繼承人。","reference":{"eng":"legitimate","kk":"lɪˈdʒɪtəmət","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"合法的\"  ],  [    \"正當的\"  ],  [    \"合理的\"  ],  [    \"合乎規定的\"  ]]","chEntries":["合法的","正當的","合理的","合乎規定的"],"practiceMeaning":"這對夫婦希望有一位合法的王位繼承人。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'legitimus'，意為「合法的」、「合乎法律的」，由 'lex' (law) 構成。'-ate' 是常見的形容詞或動詞字尾。'Legitimus' 的核心語意是「符合法律」或「基於法律」。在現代英語中，'legitimate' 指符合法律規定、規則、原則或道德標準。它可以指法律上的「合法性」，也可以指行為、要求或理由的「正當性」或「合理性」。例如，也可指「非婚生子女以外的」，即「婚生子女」。","definition":"1. Complying with the law.; 2. Able to be defended with logic or reason.; 3. Genuine, or one regarded as such.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a legitimate business operation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個合法的商業運營。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her concerns are perfectly legitimate.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的擔憂完全是合理的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The court ruled the contract legitimate.\",\n    \"ch\": \"法院裁定該合同合法有效。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The couple hoped for a legitimate heir to the throne.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這對夫婦希望有一位合法的王位繼承人。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這對夫婦希望有一位合法的王位繼承人。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6177,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::migration::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The great ____ of African Americans from the South to the North was a major demographic shift.","expectedAnswer":"migration","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The great ____ of African Americans from the South to the North was a major demographic shift.","clozeAnswer":"migration","exampleTranslation":"非裔美國人從南方大規模遷往北方的運動是人口結構的重大轉變。","reference":{"eng":"migration","kk":"maɪˈɡreɪʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"遷徙\"  ],  [    \"移民\"  ]]","chEntries":["遷徙","移民"],"practiceMeaning":"非裔美國人從南方大規模遷往北方的運動是人口結構的重大轉變。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 migratioinem，是動詞 migrare「遷徙、移居」的名詞化。migrare 的詞源不確定，可能與拉丁語 mīgrāre (to move from one place to another) 或拉丁語 magna (great) 有關，但最常見的說法是源自詞根 *mei- (to go, pass)。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作為名詞，其核心語義是由動詞 migrate「遷徙」名詞化而來，指「為了尋找食物、繁殖地或更好的生存條件而從一個地方移動到另一個地方的行為」。此義項由「移動」的動作延伸出「遷徙」的行為與「移民」的結果。","definition":"1. the movement of persons from one country or locality to another; 2. seasonal movement of animals from one region to another.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Bird migration occurs in the spring and fall.\",\n    \"ch\": \"鳥類遷徙發生在春秋兩季。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The region experienced significant migration of people seeking work.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該地區經歷了大量尋找工作的移民。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Human migration patterns have changed throughout history.\",\n    \"ch\": \"人類的移民模式在歷史上一直變化。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The great migration of African Americans from the South to the North was a major demographic shift.\",\n    \"ch\": \"非裔美國人從南方大規模遷往北方的運動是人口結構的重大轉變。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"非裔美國人從南方大規模遷往北方的運動是人口結構的重大轉變。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6178,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::milestone::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The birth of their first child was a ____ for the couple.","expectedAnswer":"milestone","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The birth of their first child was a ____ for the couple.","clozeAnswer":"milestone","exampleTranslation":"他們第一個孩子的出生對這對夫婦來說是一個重要的里程碑。","reference":{"eng":"milestone","kk":"ˈmaɪlstəʊn","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"里程碑\"  ],  [    \"轉捩點\"  ],  [    \"重要事件\"  ]]","chEntries":["里程碑","轉捩點","重要事件"],"practiceMeaning":"他們第一個孩子的出生對這對夫婦來說是一個重要的里程碑。","analysis":"此字由 mile（英里）和 stone（石頭）兩個名詞組成。在古代，里程碑是用來標示道路距離的石頭。此字在現代英語中可視為複合詞，其語義由兩部分組成。作為名詞，其核心語義是「一個重要的事件或階段，標誌著進步或發展」。詞源中的「標示距離的石頭」引申為「標誌重要進展的事件」。","definition":"1. a significant stage or event in the development of something; 2. a stone or post set up beside a road or path to mark the distance to a place.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company celebrated a major milestone in its history.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司慶祝了其歷史上的重要里程碑。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Graduating from college was a significant milestone for her.\",\n    \"ch\": \"大學畢業對她來說是一個重要的轉捩點。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The signpost marked a milestone of five miles.\",\n    \"ch\": \"路標標示著五英里的里程碑。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The birth of their first child was a milestone for the couple.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們第一個孩子的出生對這對夫婦來說是一個重要的里程碑。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們第一個孩子的出生對這對夫婦來說是一個重要的里程碑。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6187,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::porch::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ swing was comfortable.","expectedAnswer":"porch","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ swing was comfortable.","clozeAnswer":"porch","exampleTranslation":"門廊的吊椅很舒服。","reference":{"eng":"porch","kk":"pɔrtʃ","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"門廊\"  ],  [    \"陽台\"  ],  [    \"走廊\"  ]]","chEntries":["門廊","陽台","走廊"],"practiceMeaning":"門廊的吊椅很舒服。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 porche，最終源自拉丁語 porticus，意為「有柱子的走廊、迴廊」，與 porta「門」相關。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作為名詞，其核心語義是指「房屋入口處有頂的、開放式的區域」。詞源中的「門」和「走廊」概念直接體現了此義。","definition":"1. a covered shelter projecting in front of the entrance of a building; 2. a veranda or balcony.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They sat on the porch watching the rain.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們坐在門廊上看著雨。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The house had a wide front porch.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這房子有一個寬敞的前門廊。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He stood on the porch, waiting for her.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他站在門廊上等她。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The porch swing was comfortable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"門廊的吊椅很舒服。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"門廊的吊椅很舒服。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5856,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::ragged::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The old flag was ____ and torn.","expectedAnswer":"ragged","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The old flag was ____ and torn.","clozeAnswer":"ragged","exampleTranslation":"舊旗幟破舊不堪，撕裂了。","reference":{"eng":"ragged","kk":"ˈræɡɪd","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"破舊的\"  ],  [    \"襤褸的\"  ],  [    \"參差不齊的\"  ],  [    \"沙啞的\"  ]]","chEntries":["破舊的","襤褸的","參差不齊的","沙啞的"],"practiceMeaning":"舊旗幟破舊不堪，撕裂了。","analysis":"此字源於 'rag' (碎布)，'-ed' 是過去分詞字尾，在這裡用作形容詞，表示「像碎布一樣的」。'Rag' 本身來源不明，可能與「撕裂」、「破舊」的語感有關。'Ragged' 的核心語意是「由碎布構成的」、「破舊的」或「邊緣參差不齊的」。它描述的是一種不整齊、不規則、破爛的狀態，可以形容衣物、頭髮、邊緣，甚至聲音。例如，也可指「聲音沙啞的」。","definition":"1. Having rough, torn edges or fringes.; 2. Wearing torn or dirty clothes.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He wore ragged clothes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他穿著襤褸的衣服。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The ragged edge of the cloth needed mending.\",\n    \"ch\": \"布料參差不齊的邊緣需要修補。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The sound of his voice was ragged.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的聲音聽起來沙啞。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The old flag was ragged and torn.\",\n    \"ch\": \"舊旗幟破舊不堪，撕裂了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"舊旗幟破舊不堪，撕裂了。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4466,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::rough::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The sea was ____ today.","expectedAnswer":"rough","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The sea was ____ today.","clozeAnswer":"rough","exampleTranslation":"今天海浪很大。","reference":{"eng":"rough","kk":"/rʌf/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['粗糙的'], ['崎嶇的'], ['劇烈的'], ['嚴酷的'], ['（計劃、概念）大致的'], ['粗暴的'], ['（天氣）惡劣的']]","chEntries":["粗糙的","崎嶇的","劇烈的","嚴酷的","大致的","粗暴的","惡劣的"],"practiceMeaning":"今天海浪很大。","analysis":"源自古英語 rōh，意為「未加工的」、「粗糙的」。核心語意是「表面不光滑」。引申為「不平坦的」（地形），「不細緻的」（計劃、想法），「激烈的」（動作、天氣），「困難的」（經歷），「粗魯的」（人）等。","definition":"1. Having an uneven or irregular surface; not smooth; 2. Not exact or detailed; 3. Violent or severe; 4. Difficult or unpleasant.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The bark of the tree was rough to the touch.\",\n    \"ch\": \"樹皮摸起來很粗糙。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We had a rough journey through the mountains.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們經歷了一趟艱難的山區旅程。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I only have a rough idea of the cost.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我只有對費用的粗略想法。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The sea was rough today.\",\n    \"ch\": \"今天海浪很大。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"今天海浪很大。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U10、L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5857,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::sacred::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ancient temple was considered ____.","expectedAnswer":"sacred","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ancient temple was considered ____.","clozeAnswer":"sacred","exampleTranslation":"這座古老的神廟被認為是神聖的。","reference":{"eng":"sacred","kk":"ˈseɪkrɪd","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"神聖的\"  ],  [    \"聖潔的\"  ],  [    \"宗教的\"  ],  [    \"受尊敬的\"  ]]","chEntries":["神聖的","聖潔的","宗教的","受尊敬的"],"practiceMeaning":"這座古老的神廟被認為是神聖的。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'sacer'，意為「神聖的」、「獻給神的」。'-ed' 是形容詞字尾。'Sacer' 的詞源與印歐語根 *sak- (to make holy) 有關。'Sacred' 的核心語意是指「與宗教、神祇或儀式有關的」，因此被視為「神聖的」、「不可褻瀆的」。引申義則指「極受尊敬的」、「神聖不可侵犯的」，用於形容珍貴的事物或權利。","definition":"1. Connected with God or a god or a religious purpose.; 2. Regarded with great respect and affection.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a sacred site for many religions.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是許多宗教的神聖之地。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They believed the river was sacred.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們相信這條河是神聖的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Freedom of speech is a sacred right.\",\n    \"ch\": \"言論自由是一項神聖的權利。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The ancient temple was considered sacred.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座古老的神廟被認為是神聖的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這座古老的神廟被認為是神聖的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6253,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::verbal::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The professor explained the ____ tenses.","expectedAnswer":"verbal","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The professor explained the ____ tenses.","clozeAnswer":"verbal","exampleTranslation":"教授解釋了動詞的時態。","reference":{"eng":"verbal","kk":"ˈvɜrbəl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"口頭的\"  ],  [    \"言語的\"  ],  [    \"動詞的\"  ]]","chEntries":["口頭的","言語的","動詞的"],"practiceMeaning":"教授解釋了動詞的時態。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 verbalis，意為「關於詞語的」，是 verbum（詞語）的派生詞。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作形容詞時，指通過語言、說話而非書寫傳達的；或與語言、言詞、動詞相關的。中文翻譯為「口頭的；言語的；動詞的」。","definition":"1. relating to or using spoken words; 2. expressed in speech rather than writing; 3. relating to verbs.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They reached a verbal agreement.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們達成了口頭協議。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The verbal contract is binding.\",\n    \"ch\": \"口頭合同具有約束力。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The verbal aspect of communication is crucial.\",\n    \"ch\": \"溝通的言語方面至關重要。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The professor explained the verbal tenses.\",\n    \"ch\": \"教授解釋了動詞的時態。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"教授解釋了動詞的時態。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3925,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::volume::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This is the third ____ of the encyclopedia.","expectedAnswer":"volume","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This is the third ____ of the encyclopedia.","clozeAnswer":"volume","exampleTranslation":"這是百科全書的第三卷。","reference":{"eng":"volume","kk":"/ˈvɒljum/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['音量'], ['體積', '容量'], ['數量', '大量'], ['冊']]","chEntries":["音量","體積","容量","數量","大量","冊"],"practiceMeaning":"這是百科全書的第三卷。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'volumen'，意為「捲、卷軸」，來自 'volvere' (意為「滾動、捲起」)。最初指捲起的紙張，引申為「書本的一卷」；後引申為「物體的體積」；再引申為「聲音的大小」，即「音量」；另引申為「數量、大量」。","definition":"1. the amount of space that a substance or object occupies, or that is enclosed within a container; 2. the loudness of a sound; 3. a quantity of something, especially a large quantity; 4. a single book forming part of a work or series.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please turn down the volume, it's too loud.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請把音量轉小，太吵了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This bottle has a volume of one liter.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個瓶子的容量是一公升。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A large volume of mail arrived today.\",\n    \"ch\": \"今天收到大量的郵件。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is the third volume of the encyclopedia.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是百科全書的第三卷。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是百科全書的第三卷。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U2、L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5502,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::a-fish-out-of-water::idiom","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"As a city person, he felt like ____ on the farm.","expectedAnswer":"a fish out of water","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"As a city person, he felt like ____ on the farm.","clozeAnswer":"a fish out of water","exampleTranslation":"作為一個城市人，他在農場裡感到格格不入。","reference":{"eng":"a fish out of water","kk":"ə fɪʃ aʊt əv ˈwɔtər","tense":"idiom","ch":"[['格格不入'], ['不適應環境'], ['渾身不自在']]","chEntries":["格格不入","不適應環境","渾身不自在"],"practiceMeaning":"作為一個城市人，他在農場裡感到格格不入。","analysis":"這個片語字面意思是「一條離開水的魚」。'Fish' 是魚，'out of water' 指「離開水的」。魚在水中才能生存和自由活動，一旦離開水，牠就會感到極度不適、無法呼吸、行動困難，甚至死亡。因此，'a fish out of water' 用來比喻「處在一個完全陌生、不習慣或不適合的環境中，感到非常不自在、尷尬或無所適從」。核心語意是「在不熟悉或不適合的環境中感到不適」。","definition":"1. A person who is out of place or uncomfortable in a particular situation or environment.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"As a city person, he felt like a fish out of water on the farm.\",\n    \"ch\": \"作為一個城市人，他在農場裡感到格格不入。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She's always been shy, so starting a new job made her feel like a fish out of water.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她一向很害羞，所以開始一份新工作讓她感到渾身不自在。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"During the meeting, I felt like a fish out of water, not understanding any of the technical jargon.\",\n    \"ch\": \"會議期間，我感到很不適應，聽不懂任何專業術語。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"作為一個城市人，他在農場裡感到格格不入。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5116,"wordRef":"字彙王::u62::abrupt::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There was an ____ change in the weather.","expectedAnswer":"abrupt","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There was an ____ change in the weather.","clozeAnswer":"abrupt","exampleTranslation":"天氣突然發生了變化。","reference":{"eng":"abrupt","kk":"əˈbrʌpt","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['突然的'], ['粗魯的'], ['陡峭的']]","chEntries":["突然的","粗魯的","陡峭的"],"practiceMeaning":"天氣突然發生了變化。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 abruptus，是 ab-, abs-（離開、遠離）+ rumpere（弄斷、打破）的過去分詞。rumpere 來自印歐語系 *h₂rem-（停止、休息）或 *reup-（撕裂、拔出）。abruptus 的字面意思是「被弄斷的、被打破的」，引申為「突然發生的、急促的」。由此衍生出「出乎意料的、唐突的、不順暢的」。當用於人際互動時，表示「粗魯、生硬」；當用於地形時，表示「突然中斷、陡峭」。","definition":"sudden and unexpected; brief to the point of rudeness; steep or broken.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was an abrupt change in the weather.\",\n    \"ch\": \"天氣突然發生了變化。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He gave an abrupt answer and walked away.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他唐突地回答了一下就走開了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The road became abrupt at the cliff edge.\",\n    \"ch\": \"道路在懸崖邊變得陡峭。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"天氣突然發生了變化。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U62"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3197,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::abstract::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Love is an ____ concept.","expectedAnswer":"abstract","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Love is an ____ concept.","clozeAnswer":"abstract","exampleTranslation":"愛是一個抽象的概念。","reference":{"eng":"abstract","kk":"/ˈæbstrækt/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['抽象的'], ['深奧的'], ['非實體的'], ['理論上的']]","chEntries":["抽象的","深奧的","非實體的","理論上的"],"practiceMeaning":"愛是一個抽象的概念。","analysis":"詞源來自拉丁文 'abstractus'，意為 'drawn away'，即分離、抽出。此字首 'abs-' 意為 'away'，'trahere' 意為 'to draw'。引申為非具體的、概念性的，與具體 'concrete' 相反。","definition":"1. existing in thought or as an idea but not having a physical or concrete existence; 2. relating to or involving general ideas or qualities rather than specific people, events, or things; 3. difficult to understand; abstruse; 4. (of art) not representing reality in a conventional way.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Love is an abstract concept.\",\n    \"ch\": \"愛是一個抽象的概念。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a very abstract way of thinking.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的思考方式非常抽象。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The book deals with abstract philosophical problems.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本書探討抽象的哲學問題。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"愛是一個抽象的概念。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U41"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3259,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::accent::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She speaks with a strong Southern ____.","expectedAnswer":"accent","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She speaks with a strong Southern ____.","clozeAnswer":"accent","exampleTranslation":"她說話帶著濃重的南方口音。","reference":{"eng":"accent","kk":"/ˈæksənt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['口音；腔調'], ['強調；重音'], ['（尤指演講或寫作中的）標音符號']]","chEntries":["口音","腔調","強調","重音","標音符號"],"practiceMeaning":"她說話帶著濃重的南方口音。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'accentus'，意為「曲調，音調」，由 'ad-'（朝向）+ 'cantus'（歌唱，歌曲）組成。最初指音樂中的音調，後引申至語言中的語音特徵（口音、重音）以及書寫中表示重音的符號。","definition":"1. a distinct way of pronouncing a language, especially one that is characteristic of a particular country, region, or social group; 2. an emphasis given to a particular syllable or word in speech; 3. a mark written above a letter to indicate the pronunciation or stress of a syllable.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She speaks with a strong Southern accent.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她說話帶著濃重的南方口音。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The word 'father' has the accent on the first syllable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"單字 'father' 的重音在第一個音節。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The acute accent (´) is used in some languages.\",\n    \"ch\": \"銳音符號（´）在某些語言中使用。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她說話帶著濃重的南方口音。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3898,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::actually::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"I thought he was joking, but he was ____ serious.","expectedAnswer":"actually","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"I thought he was joking, but he was ____ serious.","clozeAnswer":"actually","exampleTranslation":"我以為他在開玩笑，但他實際上是認真的。","reference":{"eng":"actually","kk":"/ˈæktʃuəli/","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['實際上', '事實上'], ['真的', '確實']]","chEntries":["實際上","事實上","真的","確實"],"practiceMeaning":"我以為他在開玩笑，但他實際上是認真的。","analysis":"由 'actual' (實際的) 加上副詞後綴 '-ly' 組成。核心是「依據事實」。用來強調某事物是真實的，與預期或表面情況不同，或用來引出真實情況。","definition":"1. in fact; in reality. 2. used to emphasize a statement or to correct a misconception.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I thought he was joking, but he was actually serious.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我以為他在開玩笑，但他實際上是認真的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"What actually happened was different.\",\n    \"ch\": \"實際上發生的情況是不同的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's actually quite a simple process.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這實際上是一個相當簡單的過程。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我以為他在開玩笑，但他實際上是認真的。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5460,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::adventure::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He sought ____ in far-off lands.","expectedAnswer":"adventure","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He sought ____ in far-off lands.","clozeAnswer":"adventure","exampleTranslation":"他到遠方尋求冒險。","reference":{"eng":"adventure","kk":"ædvɛnˈtʃɜr","tense":"n.","ch":"[['冒險'], ['奇遇'], ['歷險']]","chEntries":["冒險","奇遇","歷險"],"practiceMeaning":"他到遠方尋求冒險。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 'aventure'，意指「機遇、事件、奇遇」。'Aventure' 又來自拉丁語 'adventura'，字面意思是「將要發生的事」，'ad-' 是「朝向」的意思，'ventura' 是 'venire'（來）的將來分詞。在中古英語中，'adventure' 最初常用來指「意外的事件」或「幸運的機會」，後來逐漸演變成「充滿刺激、危險或新奇的經歷」。核心語意是「未知的、可能充滿挑戰或驚喜的事件或經歷」。","definition":"1. An unusual and exciting or daring experience or activity.; 2. A commercial enterprise undertaken with the hope of succeeding.; 3. A series of exciting or unusual events or experiences.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He sought adventure in far-off lands.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他到遠方尋求冒險。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The novel tells the story of a young explorer's adventure in the jungle.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本小說講述了一位年輕探險家在叢林中的冒險故事。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was an adventure to travel without any plans.\",\n    \"ch\": \"沒有任何計劃的旅行是一場冒險。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他到遠方尋求冒險。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5688,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l9::alcoholic::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He is an ____ and needs professional help.","expectedAnswer":"alcoholic","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He is an ____ and needs professional help.","clozeAnswer":"alcoholic","exampleTranslation":"他是一名酒鬼，需要專業的幫助。","reference":{"eng":"alcoholic","kk":"ˌælkəˈhɒlɪk","tense":"n.","ch":"[['酒鬼'], ['酗酒者'], ['酒精中毒者']]","chEntries":["酒鬼","酗酒者","酒精中毒者"],"practiceMeaning":"他是一名酒鬼，需要專業的幫助。","analysis":"此字由名詞 'alcohol' 加上形容詞化後綴 '-ic'，再轉化為名詞使用，表示「患有酒精相關疾病的人」。'alcohol' 是阿拉伯語 al-kuḥl 的音譯。'-ic' 後綴在此用於形成名詞，指代「患有某種疾病或狀態的人」。其核心語意是「經常過量飲酒的人」或「酒精依賴者」。","definition":"a person who is addicted to alcohol.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is an alcoholic and needs professional help.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一名酒鬼，需要專業的幫助。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他是一名酒鬼，需要專業的幫助。","sourceName":"龍騰課本、字彙王","unitName":"L9、U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6208,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::ally::vi","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The smaller companies decided to ____ against the larger competitor.","expectedAnswer":"ally","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The smaller companies decided to ____ against the larger competitor.","clozeAnswer":"ally","exampleTranslation":"這些小公司決定聯合起來對抗較大的競爭對手。","reference":{"eng":"ally","kk":"əˈlaɪ","tense":"vi.","ch":"[  [    \"結盟\"  ],  [    \"聯合\"  ],  [    \"支持\"  ]]","chEntries":["結盟","聯合","支持"],"practiceMeaning":"這些小公司決定聯合起來對抗較大的競爭對手。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 aleier，意為「結合，聯合」，向上可追溯至拉丁語 alligare，由 ad-（朝向）和 ligare（綁，連結）組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，應視為整體詞源演變。作不及物動詞時，核心語義是與他人或他國建立聯盟、夥伴關係或共同行動，以達成共同目標或互相支持。中文翻譯為「結盟；聯合；支持」。","definition":"1. to join with another person, country, or group in order to achieve something together; 2. to give your support to someone or something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The smaller companies decided to ally against the larger competitor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這些小公司決定聯合起來對抗較大的競爭對手。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She allied herself with the opposition party.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她與反對黨結盟。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They allied to fight the common enemy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們結盟以對抗共同的敵人。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這些小公司決定聯合起來對抗較大的競爭對手。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3124,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::ambiguous::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The politician gave an ____ answer to the reporter's question.","expectedAnswer":"ambiguous","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The politician gave an ____ answer to the reporter's question.","clozeAnswer":"ambiguous","exampleTranslation":"這位政治家對記者的問題給出了模棱兩可的答案。","reference":{"eng":"ambiguous","kk":"/æmˈbɪɡjuəs/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['模棱兩可的；含糊不清的'], ['（意義、動機等）不明確的'], ['（事物）有歧義的']]","chEntries":["模棱兩可的","含糊不清的","不明確的","有歧義的"],"practiceMeaning":"這位政治家對記者的問題給出了模棱兩可的答案。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'ambiguus'，意為「不確定的，變換不定的」。'ambi-'（兩邊，周圍）+ 'agere'（行動，推動）。原意是「可以從兩邊走的」，引申為「不確定的」、「模棱兩可的」。形容詞 'ambiguous' 用來描述語言、指示、行為或情況，其意義不單一，可以有多種解釋，因而造成不確定或混淆。","definition":"1. open to more than one interpretation; having a double meaning; 2. unclear or inexact because a choice between alternative meanings has not been made; 3. (of a situation) not having one obvious meaning or outcome.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The politician gave an ambiguous answer to the reporter's question.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位政治家對記者的問題給出了模棱兩可的答案。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His intentions were ambiguous, making it hard to trust him.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的意圖不明確，讓人難以信任他。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The meaning of the poem is deliberately ambiguous.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這首詩的意義是刻意含糊不清的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這位政治家對記者的問題給出了模棱兩可的答案。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4177,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::apart::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The two buildings are far ____.","expectedAnswer":"apart","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The two buildings are far ____.","clozeAnswer":"apart","exampleTranslation":"這兩棟建築相距甚遠。","reference":{"eng":"apart","kk":"/əˈpɑːrt/","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['分開', '分開地'], ['（差異）懸殊地']]","chEntries":["分開","分開地","懸殊地"],"practiceMeaning":"這兩棟建築相距甚遠。","analysis":"由 a-（介詞）+ part（部分）組成。核心概念是「從整體中分離出來」或「獨立存在」。","definition":"1. separated by a distance; 2. into different pieces or parts; 3. distinct from others","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The two buildings are far apart.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這兩棟建築相距甚遠。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They have to tell A and B apart.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們必須分辨 A 和 B。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The team won the championship, beating their rivals by a wide margin apart.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這支隊伍以巨大的優勢擊敗對手，贏得了冠軍。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這兩棟建築相距甚遠。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5374,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l2::arch::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She gave him an ____ look.","expectedAnswer":"arch","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She gave him an ____ look.","clozeAnswer":"arch","exampleTranslation":"她朝他投以一個狡黠的眼神。","reference":{"eng":"arch","kk":"ɑːrtʃ","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['首要的'], ['主要的'], ['惡作劇的', '淘氣的']]","chEntries":["首要的","主要的","惡作劇的","淘氣的"],"practiceMeaning":"她朝他投以一個狡黠的眼神。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 arche，來自拉丁語 arch-, arcus，最初意為「弓、首領」。此字首 arch- 在後來的法語和英語中，常被用來構成表示「首要的、主要的、主要的」的複合詞，如 archbishop (大主教)、archduke (大公)。同時，在 19 世紀，arch- 也發展出一個非正式的用法，表示「惡作劇的、淘氣的、狡猾的」，與其「首要、領頭」的意義有一種諷刺性的連結，即「領頭做壞事」。","definition":"1. (of a person or their behavior) deliberately and mischievously unconventional and playful; 2. chief; principal.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She gave him an arch look.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她朝他投以一個狡黠的眼神。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was the arch-rival of the champion.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是冠軍的主要對手。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她朝他投以一個狡黠的眼神。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4141,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::aside::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He put the book ____.","expectedAnswer":"aside","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He put the book ____.","clozeAnswer":"aside","exampleTranslation":"他把書放在一旁。","reference":{"eng":"aside","kk":"/əˈsaɪd/","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['在一旁', '到旁邊'], ['（暫時）擱置', '另外']]","chEntries":["在一旁","到旁邊","擱置","另外"],"practiceMeaning":"他把書放在一旁。","analysis":"由 a-（介詞）+ side（邊）組成。核心概念是「在邊緣位置」或「與主要事物分開」。","definition":"1. on or to one side; 2. out of the way; 3. separately, or to one side, from what is being done or considered","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He put the book aside.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他把書放在一旁。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Let's set this problem aside for now.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們暫時把這個問題擱置一邊。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She stepped aside to let him pass.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她往旁邊一讓，讓他通過。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他把書放在一旁。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4509,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::assumption::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We made the ____ that the project would be funded.","expectedAnswer":"assumption","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We made the ____ that the project would be funded.","clozeAnswer":"assumption","exampleTranslation":"我們假設該項目將會獲得資金。","reference":{"eng":"assumption","kk":"/əˈsʌmpʃn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['假設'], ['設想'], ['承擔（責任、職責等）'], ['（態度）傲慢，自以為是']]","chEntries":["假設","設想","承擔","傲慢，自以為是"],"practiceMeaning":"我們假設該項目將會獲得資金。","analysis":"源自 assume (假設、承擔)。加上 -tion (名詞後綴)。核心語意是「假設的行為或狀態」，或「承擔的行為或狀態」。","definition":"1. A thing that is accepted as true or as certain to happen, without proof; 2. The act of taking possession of or taking on something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We made the assumption that the project would be funded.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們假設該項目將會獲得資金。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He rejected the assumption that he was responsible.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他駁斥了他應負責的假設。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The assumption of power by the new leader was widely welcomed.\",\n    \"ch\": \"新領導人掌權的行為受到廣泛歡迎。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們假設該項目將會獲得資金。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4126,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::background::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The photo has a blurry ____.","expectedAnswer":"background","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The photo has a blurry ____.","clozeAnswer":"background","exampleTranslation":"這張照片的背景很模糊。","reference":{"eng":"background","kk":"/ˈbækˌɡraʊnd/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['背景'], ['（人的）出身，經歷'], ['（畫作、照片的）背景']]","chEntries":["背景","出身，經歷"],"practiceMeaning":"這張照片的背景很模糊。","analysis":"由 back（後方）+ ground（地面、背景）組成。核心概念是「後方的景象」或「事物發生的環境」。引申為一個人過去的經歷、社會經濟地位，以及藝術作品中襯托主體的畫面。","definition":"1. the part of a scene, picture, or object against which what is in the foreground stands out; 2. a person's origin, education, and experience; 3. the circumstances in which something happens","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The photo has a blurry background.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這張照片的背景很模糊。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a strong academic background.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她有紮實的學術背景。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His family background made him feel insecure.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的家庭背景使他感到不安。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這張照片的背景很模糊。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4539,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::badly::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He performed ____ in the exam.","expectedAnswer":"badly","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He performed ____ in the exam.","clozeAnswer":"badly","exampleTranslation":"他在考試中表現很差。","reference":{"eng":"badly","kk":"/ˈbædli/","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['糟糕地', '差勁地'], ['嚴重地', '極度地']]","chEntries":["糟糕地","差勁地","嚴重地","極度地"],"practiceMeaning":"他在考試中表現很差。","analysis":"由 'bad' (壞的) 加上副詞字尾 '-ly' 構成。\n    1. 糟糕地、差勁地：指行為、表現或結果不佳。\n    2. 嚴重地、極度地：指程度非常深，常與表示需求、傷害、情況等的詞連用，如 'badly hurt' (嚴重受傷)，'badly needed' (急需)。","definition":"1. in a very bad or poor manner.; 2. severely; extremely.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He performed badly in the exam.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在考試中表現很差。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The car was badly damaged in the accident.\",\n    \"ch\": \"汽車在事故中嚴重損毀。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We are badly in need of funds.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們急需資金。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他在考試中表現很差。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5610,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l7::ban::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There is a ____ on the use of plastic bags.","expectedAnswer":"ban","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There is a ____ on the use of plastic bags.","clozeAnswer":"ban","exampleTranslation":"塑膠袋的使用已被禁止。","reference":{"eng":"ban","kk":"bæn","tense":"n.","ch":"[['禁令'], ['禁止']]","chEntries":["禁令","禁止"],"practiceMeaning":"塑膠袋的使用已被禁止。","analysis":"此字在詞源上較為複雜，可能源自古英語 'bannan'（宣佈、號召），或與古挪威斯語 'banna'（詛咒、禁止）有關，後者與原始日耳曼語 *bannanán（宣佈，禁止）相關。構詞學上，此字通常被視為一個整體詞，現代英語中無明顯字首、字根或字尾。此名詞形式是從動詞 'ban' 派生而來（零轉換）。語意核心是「公開宣佈某事為非法或不被允許」，引申為「禁止令」、「禁令」或「禁止的行為」。","definition":"1. An official or legal prohibition; 2. The prohibition of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There is a ban on the use of plastic bags.\",\n    \"ch\": \"塑膠袋的使用已被禁止。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The organization imposed a temporary ban on new members.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該組織對新成員實施了臨時禁令。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"塑膠袋的使用已被禁止。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3903,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::besides::prep","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ English, she speaks French.","expectedAnswer":"Besides","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ English, she speaks French.","clozeAnswer":"Besides","exampleTranslation":"除了英語，她還說法語。","reference":{"eng":"besides","kk":"/bɪˈsaɪdz/","tense":"prep.","ch":"[['除了…之外（還有）']]","chEntries":["除了…之外"],"practiceMeaning":"除了英語，她還說法語。","analysis":"由 'by' (在旁) + 'side' (邊) + '-s' 組成。核心是「在…旁邊」。引申為「除了」，表示在原有事物之外，還有其他的東西，包含被提及的事物。","definition":"in addition to; apart from.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Besides English, she speaks French.\",\n    \"ch\": \"除了英語，她還說法語。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Besides the car, he owns a motorcycle.\",\n    \"ch\": \"除了汽車，他還擁有一輛摩托車。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"除了英語，她還說法語。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4175,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::between::prep","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There is a significant difference ____ A and B.","expectedAnswer":"between","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There is a significant difference ____ A and B.","clozeAnswer":"between","exampleTranslation":"A 和 B 之間存在顯著的差異。","reference":{"eng":"between","kk":"/bɪˈtwiːn/","tense":"prep.","ch":"[['在...之間']]","chEntries":["在...之間"],"practiceMeaning":"A 和 B 之間存在顯著的差異。","analysis":"源自古英語 betwēonan（在兩者之間）。核心概念是「位於兩個點、區域或事物的中間」。","definition":"1. in or into the space separating (two points, objects, etc.); 2. intermediate to (two points, limits, etc.); 3. in relation to (two or more people or things) considered together","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There is a significant difference between A and B.\",\n    \"ch\": \"A 和 B 之間存在顯著的差異。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She sat between her parents.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她坐在父母之間。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The agreement is between the two countries.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這項協議是在兩國之間達成的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"A 和 B 之間存在顯著的差異。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5821,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::biological::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The research focuses on ____ processes.","expectedAnswer":"biological","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The research focuses on ____ processes.","clozeAnswer":"biological","exampleTranslation":"這項研究聚焦於生物過程。","reference":{"eng":"biological","kk":"ˌbaɪəˈlɑːdʒɪkl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"生物的\"  ],  [    \"生物學的\"  ],  [    \"生理的\"  ]]","chEntries":["生物的","生物學的","生理的"],"practiceMeaning":"這項研究聚焦於生物過程。","analysis":"此字由名詞 'biology' 加上形容詞字尾 '-ical' 構成。'Biology' 本身是一個複合詞，來自希臘語 'bios' (life) 和 '-logia' (study of, discourse)。'-logia' 來自 'logos' (word, speech, reason)。因此，'biology' 的字面意思是「生命的學問」。'-ical' 字尾用於將名詞轉化為形容詞，表示「關於……的」、「屬於……的」、「具有……性質的」。所以 'biological' 的意思就是「關於生物的」或「屬於生物學的」。另外，也可指「與生命體正常機能相關的」，即「生理的」。","definition":"1. Relating to or resulting from the functions of living organisms.; 2. Relating to biology.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The research focuses on biological processes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這項研究聚焦於生物過程。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Genetic engineering has many biological applications.\",\n    \"ch\": \"基因工程有許多生物學上的應用。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to consider the biological impact of the pollution.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要考慮污染的生物影響。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The drug has a strong biological effect.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種藥物有強烈的生理效應。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這項研究聚焦於生物過程。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5622,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l7::bold::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She was ____ enough to ask for a raise.","expectedAnswer":"bold","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She was ____ enough to ask for a raise.","clozeAnswer":"bold","exampleTranslation":"她大膽到足以要求加薪。","reference":{"eng":"bold","kk":"boʊld","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['大膽的'], ['勇敢的'], ['魯莽的'], ['醒目的'], ['粗體的']]","chEntries":["大膽的","勇敢的","魯莽的","醒目的","粗體的"],"practiceMeaning":"她大膽到足以要求加薪。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 'bāld'，其原始日耳曼語形式為 *balþuz。構詞學上，此字通常被視為一個整體詞，詞源與「強壯」、「大膽」相關。語意核心是「敢於冒險」、「不畏縮」。從「勇敢」、「無畏」引申出「魯莽」的負面含義。在印刷術中，指字體「粗體」，因為這種字體看起來更「醒目」、「強壯」。","definition":"1. Showing an ability to take risks; confident and courageous; 2. (Of a color, design, or shape) having a strong or vivid appearance; 3. (Of print) having the letters thicker and heavier than normal; 4. Showing an impudent lack of respect.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She was bold enough to ask for a raise.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她大膽到足以要求加薪。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The designer used bold colors in the artwork.\",\n    \"ch\": \"設計師在這件藝術品中使用了醒目的顏色。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He made a bold decision to invest in the startup.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他做出了大膽的決定，投資那家初創公司。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please format the headings in bold.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請將標題格式化為粗體。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她大膽到足以要求加薪。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5029,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::boost::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The government aims to ____ exports.","expectedAnswer":"boost","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The government aims to ____ exports.","clozeAnswer":"boost","exampleTranslation":"政府旨在提升出口。","reference":{"eng":"boost","kk":"buːst","tense":"v.","ch":"[['提升'], ['促進'], ['鼓勵']]","chEntries":["提升","促進","鼓勵"],"practiceMeaning":"政府旨在提升出口。","analysis":"此字來源不確定，可能與低地德語 bost（隆起）或荷蘭語 botsen（碰撞）有關。動詞 boost 意為「推、頂、抬高」，引申為「促進、增加、鼓勵」。此動詞的核心語意是「使某事物向上或向前移動、增長、變得更好」，強調積極的推動作用。其常見的用法如 boost sales（提升銷售額）或 boost morale（提升士氣）。","definition":"1. help or encourage (someone or something) to increase or improve; 2. push or lift (someone or something) up into the air.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government aims to boost exports.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府旨在提升出口。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His confidence was boosted by the praise.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的信心因讚揚而增強。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"政府旨在提升出口。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5427,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::campaign::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The environmental ____ aims to reduce plastic waste.","expectedAnswer":"campaign","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The environmental ____ aims to reduce plastic waste.","clozeAnswer":"campaign","exampleTranslation":"這個環保運動旨在減少塑膠廢棄物。","reference":{"eng":"campaign","kk":"kæmˈpeɪn","tense":"n.","ch":"[['活動'], ['運動'], ['競選活動'], ['戰役']]","chEntries":["活動","運動","競選活動","戰役"],"practiceMeaning":"這個環保運動旨在減少塑膠廢棄物。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 \"campagne\"，意為\"田野\"、\"平原\"，引申為\"軍隊在田野中作戰\"，即\"戰役\"。其拉丁語詞源為 \"campania\"，意為\"平坦的土地\"，與 \"campus\" ( campo) 意為\"田野\"有關。構詞上，沒有明顯的字首、字根或字尾可拆解，應視為一個整體詞源的演變。原始語義是指在開闊的場地進行軍事行動。後來引申至政治上的「競選活動」，以及為了達成特定目標而組織的、有時限的「活動」或「運動」，如環保運動、公益活動等。","definition":"an organized course of action to achieve a particular goal; a series of coordinated activities designed to achieve a particular objective; a political campaign; a military operation.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The environmental campaign aims to reduce plastic waste.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個環保運動旨在減少塑膠廢棄物。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The presidential campaign will intensify next month.\",\n    \"ch\": \"總統競選活動將於下個月加劇。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The troops prepared for a new campaign in the north.\",\n    \"ch\": \"部隊準備在北方展開新的戰役。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個環保運動旨在減少塑膠廢棄物。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3207,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::cane::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The teacher threatened to ____ the unruly student.","expectedAnswer":"cane","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The teacher threatened to ____ the unruly student.","clozeAnswer":"cane","exampleTranslation":"老師威脅要用藤條鞭打那個不守規矩的學生。","reference":{"eng":"cane","kk":"/keɪn/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['用藤條鞭打']]","chEntries":["用藤條鞭打"],"practiceMeaning":"老師威脅要用藤條鞭打那個不守規矩的學生。","analysis":"源自名詞 'cane'，指用藤條、棍棒等進行懲罰或鞭打。這是名詞意義的延伸，指使用作為工具的『藤條』進行某種行為。","definition":"to beat (someone) with a cane.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The teacher threatened to cane the unruly student.\",\n    \"ch\": \"老師威脅要用藤條鞭打那個不守規矩的學生。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"老師威脅要用藤條鞭打那個不守規矩的學生。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U41"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3880,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::captain::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ steered the ship through the storm.","expectedAnswer":"captain","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ steered the ship through the storm.","clozeAnswer":"captain","exampleTranslation":"船長駕馭著船隻穿越風暴。","reference":{"eng":"captain","kk":"/ˈkæptən/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['船長'], ['隊長'], ['機長'], ['上尉']]","chEntries":["船長","隊長","機長","上尉"],"practiceMeaning":"船長駕馭著船隻穿越風暴。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'capitaneus'，'caput' (head) 的衍生詞。核心是「首領」、「領導者」。最初指船的領導者，後引申為運動隊、飛行器、軍隊等團體的領導人。","definition":"1. the commander of a ship or large boat. 2. the leader of a sports team. 3. the pilot of an aircraft. 4. a rank of officer in the army and air force.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The captain steered the ship through the storm.\",\n    \"ch\": \"船長駕馭著船隻穿越風暴。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was chosen as the captain of the basketball team.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他被選為籃球隊隊長。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The captain of the aircraft announced our descent.\",\n    \"ch\": \"機長宣布了我們的下降。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"船長駕馭著船隻穿越風暴。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3879,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::career::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She had a successful ____ in medicine.","expectedAnswer":"career","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She had a successful ____ in medicine.","clozeAnswer":"career","exampleTranslation":"她在醫學領域擁有成功的職業生涯。","reference":{"eng":"career","kk":"/kəˈrɪr/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['職業生涯', '事業']]","chEntries":["職業生涯","事業"],"practiceMeaning":"她在醫學領域擁有成功的職業生涯。","analysis":"源自法語 'carrière' (road, racecourse)，其根源是拉丁語 'carrum' (cart)。核心是「奔跑的道路」。引申為一個人一生中所從事的職業或事業發展過程。","definition":"an occupation undertaken for a significant period of a person's life and with opportunities for progress.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She had a successful career in medicine.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在醫學領域擁有成功的職業生涯。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is planning his career path.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他正在規劃他的職業道路。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"After college, he pursued a career in finance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"大學畢業後，他追求金融業的事業。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她在醫學領域擁有成功的職業生涯。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3267,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::catalogue::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"I received the new spring collection ____ from the department store.","expectedAnswer":"catalogue","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"I received the new spring collection ____ from the department store.","clozeAnswer":"catalogue","exampleTranslation":"我收到了百貨公司的新春季商品目錄。","reference":{"eng":"catalogue","kk":"/ˈkætəlɔːɡ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['目錄；商品目錄'], ['（圖書館、博物館等的）目錄']]","chEntries":["目錄","商品目錄"],"practiceMeaning":"我收到了百貨公司的新春季商品目錄。","analysis":"源自希臘語 'katalogos'，由 'kata-' (根據) + 'logos' (言論，順序) 組成。原指「列表」，後專指商品目錄、圖書館藏書目錄等。","definition":"a complete list of items, typically one in alphabetical or other systematic order, in particular, a book or leaflet containing a list of goods available for purchase.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I received the new spring collection catalogue from the department store.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我收到了百貨公司的新春季商品目錄。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The library catalogue can be searched online.\",\n    \"ch\": \"圖書館的目錄可以在線上搜尋。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我收到了百貨公司的新春季商品目錄。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4325,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::cattle::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The farmer herds his ____ into the stable.","expectedAnswer":"cattle","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The farmer herds his ____ into the stable.","clozeAnswer":"cattle","exampleTranslation":"農夫將他的牛群趕進牛棚。","reference":{"eng":"cattle","kk":"/ˈkætl/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['牛（總稱，不可數）']]","chEntries":["牛"],"practiceMeaning":"農夫將他的牛群趕進牛棚。","analysis":"源自古英語 'catol'，與古諾爾斯語 'kötull' 同源，但其詞源較不確定。這個詞用於統稱牛，特別是指牛群，無論是公牛、母牛還是小牛。它是一個集合名詞，通常用作不可數名詞，與單數名詞 'cow' 或 'ox' 不同，涵蓋了整個類別。","definition":"cows and bulls, considered together as farm animals","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The farmer herds his cattle into the stable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"農夫將他的牛群趕進牛棚。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There are many heads of cattle on the ranch.\",\n    \"ch\": \"牧場裡有很多頭牛。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The price of cattle has increased.\",\n    \"ch\": \"牛的價格上漲了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"農夫將他的牛群趕進牛棚。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6066,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::civic::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The government launched a new ____ engagement program.","expectedAnswer":"civic","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The government launched a new ____ engagement program.","clozeAnswer":"civic","exampleTranslation":"政府推出了一項新的公民參與計畫。","reference":{"eng":"civic","kk":"ˈsɪvɪk","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"公民的\"  ],  [    \"市民的\"  ],  [    \"市政的\"  ]]","chEntries":["公民的","市民的","市政的"],"practiceMeaning":"政府推出了一項新的公民參與計畫。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 civicus，意為「屬於一個市民的」，來自 civis（citizen）。Civis 最終來源於 proto-Indo-European * (s)kein-「劃分，切割」，引申為「社群、部落」。Civic 作為形容詞，修飾與公民、市民、城市或市政事務相關的事物。核心語義是「與城市或其居民相關的」。","definition":"relating to a town or city, or to the people who live there; relating to the duties or activities of people in a town or city.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government launched a new civic engagement program.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府推出了一項新的公民參與計畫。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They attended a civic ceremony in the town hall.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們參加了市政廳的市民儀式。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Civic duty requires citizens to vote in elections.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公民責任要求市民在選舉中投票。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"政府推出了一項新的公民參與計畫。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5329,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l1::claim::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He made a ____ to the throne.","expectedAnswer":"claim","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He made a ____ to the throne.","clozeAnswer":"claim","exampleTranslation":"他聲稱對王位擁有權利。","reference":{"eng":"claim","kk":"kleɪm","tense":"n.","ch":"[['主張'], ['權利'], ['要求'], ['聲稱']]","chEntries":["主張","權利","要求","聲稱"],"practiceMeaning":"他聲稱對王位擁有權利。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 clamer，來自拉丁語 clamare（喊叫、請求），再追溯至原始印歐語 *kelh₂-（呼喊、召喚）。構詞上，clam- 是字根，表示「呼喊」或「大聲說」。原始語意為「呼喊以求」或「大聲宣告」。現代語意發展為「對某事物提出權利主張」、「要求」或「聲稱擁有」。當名詞使用時，指「聲稱」、「權利」或「要求」的行為或內容。","definition":"an assertion that something is the case, without providing evidence or proof; a right or legal entitlement to have something or to take a particular course of action.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He made a claim to the throne.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他聲稱對王位擁有權利。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The insurance company rejected her claim.\",\n    \"ch\": \"保險公司駁回了她的理賠請求。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他聲稱對王位擁有權利。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6067,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::clarity::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of his explanation was remarkable.","expectedAnswer":"clarity","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of his explanation was remarkable.","clozeAnswer":"clarity","exampleTranslation":"他解釋的清晰度令人矚目。","reference":{"eng":"clarity","kk":"ˈklærəti","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"清晰\"  ],  [    \"清楚\"  ],  [    \"明晰\"  ],  [    \"透明\"  ]]","chEntries":["清晰","清楚","明晰","透明"],"practiceMeaning":"他解釋的清晰度令人矚目。","analysis":"此字由 clear（清晰的）加上名詞後綴 -ity（表示狀態或性質）構成。Clear 源自古法語 cler，來自拉丁語 clarus（clear, bright, famous）。Clarus 最終來源於 proto-Indo-European *kelh₂-「呼喚，聲音」，引申為「響亮的，清晰的」。Clarity 的核心語義是「清晰的狀態或性質」。它可以用來描述聲音、視覺、理解、表達或物質的清晰度。","definition":"1. the quality of being clear and easy to understand; 2. the quality of being easy to see or hear; 3. the quality of being transparent.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The clarity of his explanation was remarkable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他解釋的清晰度令人矚目。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The clarity of the water allowed us to see the fish.\",\n    \"ch\": \"水的清澈度使我們能夠看到魚。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please speak with more clarity.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請講得更清楚些。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他解釋的清晰度令人矚目。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5585,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::classical::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She studied ____ music at university.","expectedAnswer":"classical","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She studied ____ music at university.","clozeAnswer":"classical","exampleTranslation":"她在大學學習古典音樂。","reference":{"eng":"classical","kk":"ˈklæsɪkl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['古典的'], ['經典的'], ['正規的'], ['傳統的']]","chEntries":["古典的","經典的","正規的","傳統的"],"practiceMeaning":"她在大學學習古典音樂。","analysis":"此字是 \"classic\" 的形容詞形式，加上形容詞字尾 \"-al\"。 \"classic\" 源自拉丁語 \"classicus\"，意為 \"of or belonging to the highest class, first-class\"（屬於最高級別的，一流的）。\"-al\" 是常見的形容詞字尾。\"classical\" 主要有兩層核心語義：一是指「古希臘羅馬時期」的，例如 \"classical literature\"、\"classical music\"；二是與 \"classic\" 相似，指「傳統的、正規的、代表性的」，與「現代的」或「非正規的」相對，例如 \"classical economics\"、\"classical ballet\"。","definition":"1. Relating to or belonging to the ancient Greek or Roman tradition, especially in art or literature; 2. Traditionally or typically, rather than modern or experimental; 3. Relating to or characteristic of the formal or artistic traditions of the past.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She studied classical music at university.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在大學學習古典音樂。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Classical physics provides a framework for understanding motion.\",\n    \"ch\": \"古典物理學為理解運動提供了框架。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Classical ballet requires years of rigorous training.\",\n    \"ch\": \"古典芭蕾需要多年的嚴格訓練。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她在大學學習古典音樂。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6114,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::cluster::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"a ____ of stars","expectedAnswer":"cluster","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"a ____ of stars","clozeAnswer":"cluster","exampleTranslation":"一簇星星","reference":{"eng":"cluster","kk":"ˈklʌstər","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"一簇\"  ],  [    \"一叢\"  ],  [    \"一群\"  ],  [    \"集結\"  ]]","chEntries":["一簇","一叢","一群","集結"],"practiceMeaning":"一簇星星","analysis":"此字詞源不確定，可能與古英語 clūst（關閉）或北歐語 klustr（院子）有關，核心語義是「聚集」。此名詞指由許多相似的物體聚集而成的「一簇」或「一叢」，或指人、物的「一群」、「集合」。其語意演變是從具體的「聚集體」到抽象的「群體」。","definition":"1. a group of similar things or people positioned or occurring closely together; 2. a number of things of the same kind growing or occurring together.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"a cluster of stars\",\n    \"ch\": \"一簇星星\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"a cluster of houses\",\n    \"ch\": \"一群房屋\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"a cluster of grapes\",\n    \"ch\": \"一串葡萄\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"一簇星星","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5576,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::code::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need to ____ this data for analysis.","expectedAnswer":"code","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need to ____ this data for analysis.","clozeAnswer":"code","exampleTranslation":"我們需要為這些數據編碼以便分析。","reference":{"eng":"code","kk":"koʊd","tense":"v.","ch":"[['編碼'], ['設定密碼'], ['為……制定規範']]","chEntries":["編碼","設定密碼","為……制定規範"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要為這些數據編碼以便分析。","analysis":"這是 \"code\" 作名詞的動詞形式，源自拉丁語 \"codex\"（book, manuscript，書本，手稿）。\"code\" 作名詞的語義發展包括「一套規則」、「符號系統」等。 \"code\" 作為動詞，核心語義是「將訊息轉換為代碼」或「為某事制定一套規則」。例如，\"to code a message\" 意為「為訊息編碼」；\"to code a building\" 意為「為建築物制定規範」；\"to code software\" 意為「編寫軟體程式碼」。","definition":"1. Write or encode in a particular programming language; 2. Assign a code to (something) for purposes of classification or identification; 3. Formulate a code of rules for (something).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to code this data for analysis.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要為這些數據編碼以便分析。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government is coding new regulations for the industry.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府正在為該行業編訂新的法規。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He spent hours coding the website.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他花了好幾個小時編寫網站的程式碼。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要為這些數據編碼以便分析。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6159,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::coincidence::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It was a remarkable ____ that they met on the same day.","expectedAnswer":"coincidence","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It was a remarkable ____ that they met on the same day.","clozeAnswer":"coincidence","exampleTranslation":"他們在同一天見面真是個令人驚嘆的巧合。","reference":{"eng":"coincidence","kk":"koʊˈɪnsɪdəns","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"巧合\"  ],  [    \"同時發生\"  ]]","chEntries":["巧合","同時發生"],"practiceMeaning":"他們在同一天見面真是個令人驚嘆的巧合。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 coincidentia，是 coincidentem (coincidens)「同時發生、一致」的現在分詞名詞化。coincidentem 由 com- (together) + inciderē (to fall upon, happen) 組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 com-「一起」和 inciderē「發生、落下」是其核心語意來源。作為名詞，核心語義是「兩個或多個事件恰好同時發生，且彼此之間沒有明顯的因果關係」。詞源中的「一起發生」清楚地體現了此義。","definition":"1. the occurrence and development of events in a happy or beneficial way; 2. a situation in which events happen at the same time in a way that has no obvious connection.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was a remarkable coincidence that they met on the same day.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們在同一天見面真是個令人驚嘆的巧合。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Their birthdays falling on the same day is a strange coincidence.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們的生日落在同一天是一個奇怪的巧合。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"What a coincidence! I was just thinking about you.\",\n    \"ch\": \"真是巧合！我剛在想你。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The coincidence of their arriving at the same time was surprising.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們同時到達的巧合令人驚訝。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們在同一天見面真是個令人驚嘆的巧合。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4070,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::collection::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She has a large ____ of stamps.","expectedAnswer":"collection","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She has a large ____ of stamps.","clozeAnswer":"collection","exampleTranslation":"她有很多郵票收藏品。","reference":{"eng":"collection","kk":"/kəˈlɛkʃən/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['收藏品', '蒐集物'], ['集合', '聚集'], ['（稅款、款項的）徵收', '收取']]","chEntries":["收藏品","蒐集物","集合","聚集","徵收","收取"],"practiceMeaning":"她有很多郵票收藏品。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'collectio'，由 'col-' (together) + 'legere' (to gather) 構成，字面意思是「一起收集」。核心是「聚集」、「蒐集」。因此，'collection' 指「蒐集到的物品」（收藏品），「蒐集的行為」，以及「聚集」本身。第四個義項「徵收」則指按規定「收集」款項或稅款。","definition":"1. a group of things that have been collected; 2. the act of collecting things; 3. a number of people or things that are gathered together; 4. the process of gathering money or other items","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"她有很多郵票收藏品。\",\n    \"eng\": \"She has a large collection of stamps.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"博物館展出了一批新的藝術收藏品。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The museum displayed a new collection of art.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"徵收稅款是政府的職責。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The collection of taxes is the responsibility of the government.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她有很多郵票收藏品。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6161,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::collective::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They made a ____ decision to go on strike.","expectedAnswer":"collective","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They made a ____ decision to go on strike.","clozeAnswer":"collective","exampleTranslation":"他們做出了集體罷工的決定。","reference":{"eng":"collective","kk":"kəˈlɛktɪv","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"集體的\"  ],  [    \"共同的\"  ],  [    \"集中的\"  ]]","chEntries":["集體的","共同的","集中的"],"practiceMeaning":"他們做出了集體罷工的決定。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 collectīvus，是動詞 colligere「收集、聚集」的衍生形容詞。colligere 由 com- (together) + legere (to gather) 組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 com-「一起」和 legere「收集」是其核心語意來源。作為形容詞，其核心語義是「屬於、與、或由兩個或多個個體共同組成」。詞源中的「一起收集」概念與「集體的」概念緊密相關。此義項由「聚集」的動作引申為「集體的」狀態或性質。","definition":"1. relating to or affecting all the people or things in a group; 2. done by or involving all the people in a group; 3. formed by the union of several individuals or things into one; 4. relating to or characteristic of a collective or the collective consciousness.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They made a collective decision to go on strike.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們做出了集體罷工的決定。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company has a collective bargaining agreement.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司簽有集體談判協議。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The artist sought to express a collective consciousness.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位藝術家試圖表達集體意識。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The collective effort of the team led to success.\",\n    \"ch\": \"團隊的集體努力帶來了成功。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們做出了集體罷工的決定。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6163,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::collector::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He is an avid ____ of rare stamps.","expectedAnswer":"collector","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He is an avid ____ of rare stamps.","clozeAnswer":"collector","exampleTranslation":"他是一位熱情的稀有郵票收藏家。","reference":{"eng":"collector","kk":"kəˈlɛktər","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"收集者\"  ],  [    \"收藏家\"  ],  [    \"稅吏\"  ],  [    \"收賬員\"  ]]","chEntries":["收集者","收藏家","稅吏","收賬員"],"practiceMeaning":"他是一位熱情的稀有郵票收藏家。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 collectorem，是動詞 colligere「收集、聚集」的施事者名詞。colligere 由 com- (together) + legere (to gather) 組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 com-「一起」和 legere「收集」是其核心語意來源。作為名詞，其核心語義是「收集某物的人」。詞源中的「一起收集」概念引申為「從眾多事物中聚集、收起」的動作者。除了指收藏家，也用於指負責徵收稅款或債務的人。","definition":"1. a person who collects things of a particular type as a hobby or profession; 2. a person whose job is to collect money that is owed to a company or the government.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is an avid collector of rare stamps.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一位熱情的稀有郵票收藏家。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The tax collector visited the household.\",\n    \"ch\": \"稅吏拜訪了這個家庭。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a collector of antique furniture.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是古董傢俱的收藏家。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The collector ensured all debts were paid.\",\n    \"ch\": \"收賬員確保所有債務都已支付。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他是一位熱情的稀有郵票收藏家。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3948,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::colorful::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The market was filled with ____ fruits and vegetables.","expectedAnswer":"colorful","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The market was filled with ____ fruits and vegetables.","clozeAnswer":"colorful","exampleTranslation":"市場裡擺滿了色彩繽紛的水果和蔬菜。","reference":{"eng":"colorful","kk":"/ˈkʌlərfəl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['色彩繽紛的'], ['生動有趣的']]","chEntries":["色彩繽紛的","生動有趣的"],"practiceMeaning":"市場裡擺滿了色彩繽紛的水果和蔬菜。","analysis":"由 'color' (名詞，顏色) 和 '-ful' (形容詞後綴) 組成。指擁有許多鮮豔顏色；也可引申為「生動有趣、豐富多彩」。","definition":"1. having a lot of different colors; 2. interesting or exciting; full of variety.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The market was filled with colorful fruits and vegetables.\",\n    \"ch\": \"市場裡擺滿了色彩繽紛的水果和蔬菜。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a colorful personality.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她擁有一個豐富多彩的個性。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The painting uses bold, colorful strokes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這幅畫使用了大膽、色彩鮮豔的筆觸。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"市場裡擺滿了色彩繽紛的水果和蔬菜。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6211,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::columnist::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The newspaper hired a new political ____.","expectedAnswer":"columnist","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The newspaper hired a new political ____.","clozeAnswer":"columnist","exampleTranslation":"這家報紙聘請了一位新的政治專欄作家。","reference":{"eng":"columnist","kk":"ˈkɒləmɪst","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"專欄作家\"  ],  [    \"專欄作者\"  ]]","chEntries":["專欄作家","專欄作者"],"practiceMeaning":"這家報紙聘請了一位新的政治專欄作家。","analysis":"此字由名詞 column（專欄）加上字尾 -ist（表示人或從事某種職業的人）構成。column 源自拉丁語 columna，意為「柱子，石柱」，引申為報紙或雜誌的「專欄」。字尾 -ist 標示從事該事物的個人。因此，columnist 指在報紙、雜誌或網站上定期撰寫專欄文章的人。中文翻譯為「專欄作家；專欄作者」。","definition":"a person who writes a regular column for a newspaper, magazine, or website.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The newspaper hired a new political columnist.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家報紙聘請了一位新的政治專欄作家。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a renowned food columnist for a popular magazine.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是某本受歡迎雜誌的著名美食專欄作家。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The columnist offered his opinion on the latest event.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位專欄作家就最新事件發表了他的看法。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這家報紙聘請了一位新的政治專欄作家。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5831,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::commodity::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Oil is a major global ____.","expectedAnswer":"commodity","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Oil is a major global ____.","clozeAnswer":"commodity","exampleTranslation":"石油是主要的全球商品。","reference":{"eng":"commodity","kk":"kəˈmɑːdəti","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"商品\"  ],  [    \"物品\"  ],  [    \"價值\"  ],  [    \"必需品\"  ]]","chEntries":["商品","物品","價值","必需品"],"practiceMeaning":"石油是主要的全球商品。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'commoditas'，意為「便利」、「舒適」、「比例」、「益處」。'Commoditas' 來自 'commodus' (fitting, convenient)，由 'con-' (together) 和 'modus' (measure) 構成，意指「以適當的度量」。在早期中古英語中，'commodity' 意指「便利」或「有益之物」。後來，其語意演變為「有用的物品」或「可供交易的商品」。現代語義中，'commodity' 特指在市場上可買賣的標準化產品，如農產品、礦產或能源，強調其可交易性和價值。例如，也可指「一種商品的價值」。","definition":"1. A raw material or primary agricultural product that can be bought and sold, such as copper or coffee.; 2. A useful or valuable thing.; 3. Convenience; advantage.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Oil is a major global commodity.\",\n    \"ch\": \"石油是主要的全球商品。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to improve the production of this commodity.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要提高這種商品的產量。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Water is a vital commodity.\",\n    \"ch\": \"水是一種至關重要的必需品。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The commodity price fluctuated greatly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該商品的價格劇烈波動。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"石油是主要的全球商品。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5038,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::conception::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of democracy has evolved over centuries.","expectedAnswer":"conception","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of democracy has evolved over centuries.","clozeAnswer":"conception","exampleTranslation":"民主的概念已經演變了幾個世紀。","reference":{"eng":"conception","kk":"kənˈsepʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[['概念'], ['構想'], ['設想'], ['懷孕']]","chEntries":["概念","構想","設想","懷孕"],"practiceMeaning":"民主的概念已經演變了幾個世紀。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語conceptio，由 concipere（構想、懷孕）派生而來。con-（一起、完全）+ capere（抓住、拿）。conception 在英語中有多個重要義項：1. 「概念、想法、構想」，指在頭腦中形成的觀念；2. 「懷孕」，指受孕的過程或狀態；3. 「對某事的理解或看法」。這些義項都與其詞源「共同抓住」、「形成」或「包含」的概念相關。OCR 掃描時可能將 'c' 誤判。此處修正為 conception。","definition":"1. the action or capability of forming concepts or ideas; 2. the process of becoming pregnant, involving fertilization or implantation; 3. an idea or understanding of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The conception of democracy has evolved over centuries.\",\n    \"ch\": \"民主的概念已經演變了幾個世紀。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The early stages of conception are critical.\",\n    \"ch\": \"懷孕的早期階段至關重要。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His conception of justice differs from mine.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對正義的看法與我的不同。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"民主的概念已經演變了幾個世紀。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4519,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::concert::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The two departments must ____ their efforts to achieve the goal.","expectedAnswer":"concert","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The two departments must ____ their efforts to achieve the goal.","clozeAnswer":"concert","exampleTranslation":"兩個部門必須協調他們的努力以達成目標。","reference":{"eng":"concert","kk":"/ˈkɒnsərt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['協調']]","chEntries":["協調"],"practiceMeaning":"兩個部門必須協調他們的努力以達成目標。","analysis":"動詞形式，源自名詞 concert。意為「一起行動」、「協調」。","definition":"1. To act together, or in a way that is suitable to the circumstances.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The two departments must concert their efforts to achieve the goal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"兩個部門必須協調他們的努力以達成目標。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"兩個部門必須協調他們的努力以達成目標。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4317,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::conscious::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Are you ____ of the danger?","expectedAnswer":"conscious","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Are you ____ of the danger?","clozeAnswer":"conscious","exampleTranslation":"你意識到危險了嗎？","reference":{"eng":"conscious","kk":"/ˈkɒnʃəs/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['意識到的；察覺到的'], ['有意識的；清醒的'], ['故意的；蓄意的']]","chEntries":["意識到的","察覺到的","有意識的","清醒的","故意的","蓄意的"],"practiceMeaning":"你意識到危險了嗎？","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'conscius'，意為 'sharing knowledge, aware'，由 'con-' (with) 和 'scire' (to know) 構成。字面意思是『一起知道』，引申為『知道某事』、『意識到』。因此，第一個義項是『知道、察覺』。第二個義項是『有知覺、清醒』，與『失去意識』相對。第三個義項是『明知故犯』，強調『有意識地做』。","definition":"aware of something; awake and able to understand what is happening around you; done deliberately","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Are you conscious of the danger?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你意識到危險了嗎？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The patient remained conscious throughout the operation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"病人在手術全程都保持清醒。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was a conscious effort to improve his grades.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是為了提高他成績而付出的有意識的努力。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"你意識到危險了嗎？","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5774,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::considerate::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He was very ____ and helped her with her heavy bags.","expectedAnswer":"considerate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He was very ____ and helped her with her heavy bags.","clozeAnswer":"considerate","exampleTranslation":"他非常體貼，幫她拿沈重的行李。","reference":{"eng":"considerate","kk":"kənˈsɪdərət","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"體貼的\"  ],  [    \"考慮周到的\"  ],  [    \"關懷的\"  ]]","chEntries":["體貼的","考慮周到的","關懷的"],"practiceMeaning":"他非常體貼，幫她拿沈重的行李。","analysis":"此字為形容詞，由consider（考慮）+ -ate（形容詞字尾，表示「具有……特性的」）構成。consider本身源自拉丁語considerare，由con-（一起）+sider-（星星，來自sidus）組成，原意可能與「觀星」、「審視星象」有關，後演變為「仔細思考；考慮」。-ate字尾有時也來自拉丁語-atus。因此，considerate的核心語義是指「經常考慮他人感受或需求的人」，即體貼周到的。語意演變上，從「仔細考慮」的動作，引申為「因考慮他人而表現出的體貼行為」。","definition":"1. showing careful thought for the rights and feelings of others; 2. characterized by careful thought or attention.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was very considerate and helped her with her heavy bags.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他非常體貼，幫她拿沈重的行李。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was considerate of you to bring me soup when I was sick.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我生病時你還帶來湯，真是體貼。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They made a considerate effort to include everyone in the discussion.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們費盡心思，盡力讓每個人都參與討論。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他非常體貼，幫她拿沈重的行李。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4205,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::constant::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The car requires ____ maintenance.","expectedAnswer":"constant","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The car requires ____ maintenance.","clozeAnswer":"constant","exampleTranslation":"這輛車需要持續的維護。","reference":{"eng":"constant","kk":"/ˈkɑːnstənt/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['持續的；不變的'], ['（忠誠、堅持等）堅定的；忠實的']]","chEntries":["持續的","不變的","堅定的","忠實的"],"practiceMeaning":"這輛車需要持續的維護。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 constans，'con-'（一起）+ 'stare'（站立）。字面意思是“一起站立”，引申為“穩定，不變”。1. “持續的；不變的”強調時間或狀態上沒有變化。2. “堅定的；忠實的”強調在情感或關係上的穩定和忠誠。","definition":"1. occurring continuously over a period of time; 2. not changing or varying; 3. faithful and steadfast.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The car requires constant maintenance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這輛車需要持續的維護。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a constant source of inspiration.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是靈感的持續來源。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He remained constant in his loyalty to his friends.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對朋友們的忠誠始終如一。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這輛車需要持續的維護。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5077,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::core::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of the problem is a lack of communication.","expectedAnswer":"core","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of the problem is a lack of communication.","clozeAnswer":"core","exampleTranslation":"問題的核心在於缺乏溝通。","reference":{"eng":"core","kk":"kɔːr","tense":"n.","ch":"[['核心'], ['中心'], ['果核']]","chEntries":["核心","中心","果核"],"practiceMeaning":"問題的核心在於缺乏溝通。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'cor' (heart)。核心概念是事物最內部、最重要、最基本的部分。這可以指一個物體的中心（如蘋果的核心），一個組織的關鍵成員，或一個概念的本質。它引申為事物的基礎、關鍵或主體。","definition":"1. The central or most important part of something.; 2. The hard central part of a fruit, containing the seeds.; 3. The part of the Earth's interior below the mantle.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The core of the problem is a lack of communication.\",\n    \"ch\": \"問題的核心在於缺乏溝通。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She removed the core from the apple.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她取出了蘋果的果核。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is the core business of the company.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是公司的核心業務。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"問題的核心在於缺乏溝通。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3075,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::critic::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He is a well-known ____ of government policy.","expectedAnswer":"critic","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He is a well-known ____ of government policy.","clozeAnswer":"critic","exampleTranslation":"他是政府政策的知名批評者。","reference":{"eng":"critic","kk":"/ˈkrɪtɪk/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['批評者'], ['評論家；評論員'], ['（古希臘）法官；裁判']]","chEntries":["批評者","評論家","評論員","法官","裁判"],"practiceMeaning":"他是政府政策的知名批評者。","analysis":"源自希臘語 'kritēs' (judge)。原意為「裁判」或「判斷者」，後發展為對事物進行評價和判斷的人。\n1. 批評者：指對某人或某事提出批評意見的人。\n2. 評論家；評論員：指在特定領域（如文學、藝術、電影、音樂）進行專業評論的人。\n3. （古希臘）法官；裁判：指在古代希臘負責判斷或裁決事務的人。","definition":"1. a person who expresses an unfavorable opinion of something; 2. a person who is qualified to judge and make comments about the quality of something, especially books, films, or art; 3. a person who expresses a reasoned analysis of the merits and faults of a work of literature or art.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a well-known critic of government policy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是政府政策的知名批評者。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The film critic gave the movie a glowing review.\",\n    \"ch\": \"電影評論家給這部電影寫了極高的評價。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The critic's decision was final.\",\n    \"ch\": \"裁判的決定是最終的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他是政府政策的知名批評者。","sourceName":"字彙王、龍騰課本","unitName":"U39、L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3074,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::criticism::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The new policy has faced a lot of ____.","expectedAnswer":"criticism","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The new policy has faced a lot of ____.","clozeAnswer":"criticism","exampleTranslation":"新政策面臨許多批評。","reference":{"eng":"criticism","kk":"/ˈkrɪtɪsɪzəm/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['批評；評論'], ['（藝術、文學等的）評論；分析'], ['（醫學）診斷']]","chEntries":["批評","評論","分析","診斷"],"practiceMeaning":"新政策面臨許多批評。","analysis":"源自希臘語 'kritēs' (judge)，是 'criticize' 的名詞形式。指「評價」的行為或結果。\n1. 批評；評論：指對某人、某事或某物的評價，通常指出其缺點或錯誤。\n2. （藝術、文學等的）評論；分析：指對作品的風格、內容、結構等進行的專業性評價和分析。\n3. （醫學）診斷：指對病情的判斷。","definition":"1. the act of saying that something is bad or that you disapprove of it; 2. a statement or opinion that expresses disapproval of someone or something; 3. the analysis and judgment of the merits and faults of a literary or artistic work.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The new policy has faced a lot of criticism.\",\n    \"ch\": \"新政策面臨許多批評。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The book received favorable criticism from reviewers.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本書受到了評論家們的好評。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The criticism revealed the underlying disease.\",\n    \"ch\": \"診斷揭示了潛在的疾病。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"新政策面臨許多批評。","sourceName":"字彙王、龍騰課本","unitName":"U39、L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5444,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::crucial::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This decision is ____ for the future of the company.","expectedAnswer":"crucial","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This decision is ____ for the future of the company.","clozeAnswer":"crucial","exampleTranslation":"這個決定對公司的未來至關重要。","reference":{"eng":"crucial","kk":"ˈkruːʃl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['至關重要的'], ['關鍵性的'], ['決定性的']]","chEntries":["至關重要的","關鍵性的","決定性的"],"practiceMeaning":"這個決定對公司的未來至關重要。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 \"crucialis\"，意為\"十字架的\"、\"重要的\"。這個詞與 \"crux\" (關鍵、核心、十字架) 有關，而 \"crux\" 又源自拉丁語 \"crux\"，意為\"十字架\"。構詞上，\"cruc-\" 提供了核心的「十字架」或「關卡」的意象，傳統上十字架是處決或重大事件的象徵，因此引申為「極其重要」或「關鍵」。\"-al\" 是形容詞字尾。 \"Crucial\" 形容某事物「極其重要」到足以決定成敗或結果。","definition":"extremely important or necessary; vital; decisive or critical, especially in the success or failure of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This decision is crucial for the future of the company.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個決定對公司的未來至關重要。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Early diagnosis is crucial for effective treatment.\",\n    \"ch\": \"早期診斷對於有效治療至關重要。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Water is crucial for all forms of life.\",\n    \"ch\": \"水對所有生命形式都至關重要。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個決定對公司的未來至關重要。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3132,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::crush::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The accident resulted in the ____ of the victim's vehicle.","expectedAnswer":"crush","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The accident resulted in the ____ of the victim's vehicle.","clozeAnswer":"crush","exampleTranslation":"事故導致了受害者的車輛被壓毀。","reference":{"eng":"crush","kk":"/krʌʃ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['擠；擠壓；壓碎'], ['（愛情上的）迷戀；傾心'], ['（人群等的）擁擠']]","chEntries":["擠","擠壓","壓碎","迷戀","傾心","擁擠"],"practiceMeaning":"事故導致了受害者的車輛被壓毀。","analysis":"名詞用法，來自動詞 'crush'。指「壓碎」的動作或狀態，或是被壓碎的結果。在愛情語境下，'a crush' 指的是強烈的、短暫的迷戀或傾心。'Crush' 也可以形容人群的擁擠和壓力，與動詞的「擠壓」概念相關聯。","definition":"1. the act or process of crushing or being crushed; 2. a strong but usually temporary romantic infatuation; 3. a crowd of people or things pressing together.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The accident resulted in the crush of the victim's vehicle.\",\n    \"ch\": \"事故導致了受害者的車輛被壓毀。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He admitted he had a crush on his classmate.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他承認他傾心於他的女同學。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was a dangerous crush of fans trying to get close to the singer.\",\n    \"ch\": \"粉絲們為了接近歌手而發生了危險的擁擠。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"事故導致了受害者的車輛被壓毀。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3277,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::cue::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The actor missed his ____ and went on stage too early.","expectedAnswer":"cue","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The actor missed his ____ and went on stage too early.","clozeAnswer":"cue","exampleTranslation":"演員錯過了提示，過早地上台了。","reference":{"eng":"cue","kk":"/kjuː/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['提示；暗示'], ['（演員的）提示；（演奏的）提示'], ['（台球、撞球等的）球棍']]","chEntries":["提示","暗示","球棍"],"practiceMeaning":"演員錯過了提示，過早地上台了。","analysis":"詞源複雜，可能來自希臘字母 'tau' (τ)，用於標記音樂或戲劇中的提示點。引申為任何提供開始行動或回應的信號或提示。","definition":"1. a thing said or done that serves as a signal to a performer to enter or to speak; 2. an action or event that is regarded as a signal for something to happen; 3. a long, slender stick used in billiards and snooker.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The actor missed his cue and went on stage too early.\",\n    \"ch\": \"演員錯過了提示，過早地上台了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her sudden silence was a cue for me to change the subject.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她突然的沉默是個提示，讓我換個話題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He picked up the cue to play billiards.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他拿起球棍打撞球。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"演員錯過了提示，過早地上台了。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3137,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::curse::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ancient artifact was said to carry a powerful ____.","expectedAnswer":"curse","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ancient artifact was said to carry a powerful ____.","clozeAnswer":"curse","exampleTranslation":"據說那個古老的文物帶有強大的詛咒。","reference":{"eng":"curse","kk":"/kɜːrs/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['詛咒；咒語'], ['（罵人的）髒話；穢語'], ['禍根；災難']]","chEntries":["詛咒","咒語","髒話","穢語","禍根","災難"],"practiceMeaning":"據說那個古老的文物帶有強大的詛咒。","analysis":"名詞用法，源自動詞 'curse'。指「詛咒」或「咒語」，即一種超自然的力量或言語，旨在帶來不幸。也指「咒罵」時所說的髒話或侮辱性言語。引申義為「禍根」或「災難」，指某物或某事帶來的持續性不幸或痛苦。","definition":"1. a supernatural power or spell that is thought to cause evil or misfortune; 2. an offensive word or phrase used when someone is angry; 3. the cause of a great deal of trouble or unhappiness.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The ancient artifact was said to carry a powerful curse.\",\n    \"ch\": \"據說那個古老的文物帶有強大的詛咒。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He muttered a curse under his breath.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他壓低聲音嘟囔了一句髒話。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Poverty can be a curse for many families.\",\n    \"ch\": \"貧困對許多家庭來說可能是一場災難。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"據說那個古老的文物帶有強大的詛咒。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4406,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u9::dare::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"How ____ you speak to me like that!","expectedAnswer":"dare","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"How ____ you speak to me like that!","clozeAnswer":"dare","exampleTranslation":"你竟敢這樣對我說話！","reference":{"eng":"dare","kk":"/dɛər/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['敢於', '膽敢']]","chEntries":["敢於","膽敢"],"practiceMeaning":"你竟敢這樣對我說話！","analysis":"詞源自古英語 'darr'，意為「傷害、冒犯」，後來演變為「膽敢、敢於」。常用作情態動詞，後面接原形動詞，尤其是在疑問句和否定句中。","definition":"to have the courage to do something or to do something that is risky or that other people are afraid to do.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"How dare you speak to me like that!\",\n    \"ch\": \"你竟敢這樣對我說話！\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He didn't dare to look.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他不敢看。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"你竟敢這樣對我說話！","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5322,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l1::debate::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The presidential candidates engaged in a heated ____.","expectedAnswer":"debate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The presidential candidates engaged in a heated ____.","clozeAnswer":"debate","exampleTranslation":"總統候選人進行了一場激烈的辯論。","reference":{"eng":"debate","kk":"dɪˈbeɪt","tense":"n.","ch":"[['辯論'], ['爭論'], ['討論']]","chEntries":["辯論","爭論","討論"],"practiceMeaning":"總統候選人進行了一場激烈的辯論。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 dæbætan，意為「辨別、爭論」，後受古法語 debat「爭吵、戰鬥」影響。構詞上，de- 可能為加強語氣的字首，但在此已與原義無關，或來自拉丁語 dis-（分開），-bat 則與古英語 batan（擊打）相關。其核心語意是透過言語較量來釐清問題或立場。現代的「辯論」和「爭論」都源於此，前者常用於正式場合，後者則較為廣泛。亦可作動詞使用。","definition":"an argument or discussion between people in which they express strong disagreement; the activity of arguing about something formally.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The presidential candidates engaged in a heated debate.\",\n    \"ch\": \"總統候選人進行了一場激烈的辯論。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They had a lengthy debate about the best course of action.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們就最佳行動方案進行了冗長的討論。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"總統候選人進行了一場激烈的辯論。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6069,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::deficit::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The country is facing a significant budget ____.","expectedAnswer":"deficit","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The country is facing a significant budget ____.","clozeAnswer":"deficit","exampleTranslation":"該國正面臨嚴重的預算赤字。","reference":{"eng":"deficit","kk":"ˈdɛfɪsɪt","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"赤字\"  ],  [    \"虧損\"  ],  [    \"不足額\"  ],  [    \"缺陷\"  ]]","chEntries":["赤字","虧損","不足額","缺陷"],"practiceMeaning":"該國正面臨嚴重的預算赤字。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 deficit，是 deficere（to be wanting, to fail）的第三人稱單數現在時形式，由 de-（down, away）和 facere（to make, to do）組成。核心語義是「缺少」或「不足」。在經濟和財政領域，deficit 通常指「赤字」，即支出超過收入的金額。它也可以指在其他方面，如人才、資源上的「不足」。","definition":"1. the amount by which something, especially a sum of money, is too small; 2. a shortfall or lack.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The country is facing a significant budget deficit.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該國正面臨嚴重的預算赤字。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There is a deficit of skilled workers in the industry.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個行業缺乏技術工人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company reported a net deficit for the third quarter.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司報告第三季度出現淨虧損。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該國正面臨嚴重的預算赤字。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4206,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::definition::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"What is the ____ of 'onomatopoeia'?","expectedAnswer":"definition","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"What is the ____ of 'onomatopoeia'?","clozeAnswer":"definition","exampleTranslation":"'狀聲詞' 的定義是什麼？","reference":{"eng":"definition","kk":"/ˌdefɪˈnɪʃn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['定義；解釋'], ['清晰度；明確性']]","chEntries":["定義","解釋","清晰度","明確性"],"practiceMeaning":"'狀聲詞' 的定義是什麼？","analysis":"源自拉丁語 definitio，'definire'（確定邊界，定義）的派生詞。'de-'（完全）+ 'finire'（結束，限制）。核心是“確定邊界”或“明確”。1. “定義；解釋”指明確事物的意義或性質。2. “清晰度；明確性”指影像、聲音或想法的清晰程度。","definition":"1. a statement of the exact meaning of a word, especially in a dictionary; 2. the clarity or distinctness of something, such as an image or sound.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"What is the definition of 'onomatopoeia'?\",\n    \"ch\": \"'狀聲詞' 的定義是什麼？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The definition of this photograph is excellent.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這張照片的清晰度非常出色。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The exact definition of the term is still debated.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個術語的確切定義仍在爭論中。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"'狀聲詞' 的定義是什麼？","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4727,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::delay::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There was a significant ____ in the train service.","expectedAnswer":"delay","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There was a significant ____ in the train service.","clozeAnswer":"delay","exampleTranslation":"火車服務出現了顯著的延誤。","reference":{"eng":"delay","kk":"/dɪˈleɪ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['延遲'], ['耽擱']]","chEntries":["延遲","耽擱"],"practiceMeaning":"火車服務出現了顯著的延誤。","analysis":"源自古法語 *deler*，意為「延遲」、「使慢」。核心是使事情發生得比預期晚，或時間上的拖延。","definition":"1. The act of delaying or the state of being delayed.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was a significant delay in the train service.\",\n    \"ch\": \"火車服務出現了顯著的延誤。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We experienced some delays due to unexpected technical issues.\",\n    \"ch\": \"由於意外的技術問題，我們經歷了一些耽擱。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"火車服務出現了顯著的延誤。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6073,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::delegation::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"A large ____ of business leaders visited the country.","expectedAnswer":"delegation","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"A large ____ of business leaders visited the country.","clozeAnswer":"delegation","exampleTranslation":"一個龐大的商業領袖代表團訪問了該國。","reference":{"eng":"delegation","kk":"ˌdɛləˈɡeɪʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"代表團\"  ],  [    \"授權\"  ],  [    \"委派\"  ]]","chEntries":["代表團","授權","委派"],"practiceMeaning":"一個龐大的商業領袖代表團訪問了該國。","analysis":"此字由 delegate（委派）加上名詞後綴 -ion（表示動作或狀態）構成。Delegate 源自拉丁語 delegare，意為「委派」。Delegation 的核心語義是「委派」這個動作或「被委派的人群」。作為名詞，它可以指一個由被委派的代表組成的「代表團」，也可以指「授權」或「委派」本身這個行為。","definition":"1. a group of people sent or authorized to represent others, in particular, government representatives; 2. the action of delegating a task or responsibility.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A large delegation of business leaders visited the country.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一個龐大的商業領袖代表團訪問了該國。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The delegation will meet with government officials tomorrow.\",\n    \"ch\": \"代表團將於明天與政府官員會面。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The process of delegation requires trust and clear communication.\",\n    \"ch\": \"授權過程需要信任和清晰的溝通。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"一個龐大的商業領袖代表團訪問了該國。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6167,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::denial::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His ____ of the allegations was not convincing.","expectedAnswer":"denial","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His ____ of the allegations was not convincing.","clozeAnswer":"denial","exampleTranslation":"他對這些指控的否認並不可信。","reference":{"eng":"denial","kk":"dɪˈnaɪəl","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"否認\"  ],  [    \"否定\"  ],  [    \"拒絕承認\"  ],  [    \"拒絕給予\"  ]]","chEntries":["否認","否定","拒絕承認","拒絕給予"],"practiceMeaning":"他對這些指控的否認並不可信。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 denegare，意為「否認、拒絕」，由 de- (away, negating) + negare (to deny) 組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 de-「否定」和 negare「否認」是其核心語意來源。作為名詞，其核心語義是由動詞 deny「否認」名詞化而來，指「拒絕承認事實或真實性」，也指「拒絕給予某物」。詞源中的「否定」概念是其核心。此義項由「否認」的動作延伸出「拒絕承認」或「拒絕給予」的結果。","definition":"1. the action of declaring something to be untrue; 2. an act of refusing to acknowledge or accept something; 3. an act of refusing to grant or allow something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His denial of the allegations was not convincing.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對這些指控的否認並不可信。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She lived in denial about her illness.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對自己的病情一直處於否認狀態。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The request was met with denial.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個請求被拒絕了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company issued a denial of the rumors.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司發布聲明否認這些謠言。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他對這些指控的否認並不可信。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4121,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::desert::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He would never ____ his family.","expectedAnswer":"desert","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He would never ____ his family.","clozeAnswer":"desert","exampleTranslation":"他絕不會拋棄他的家人。","reference":{"eng":"desert","kk":"/ˈdɛzərt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['拋棄', '遺棄'], ['擅離（職守）', '開小差']]","chEntries":["拋棄","遺棄","擅離","開小差"],"practiceMeaning":"他絕不會拋棄他的家人。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 desertus（被遺棄的），是動詞 deserere（放棄）的過去分詞。核心概念是「離開」、「放棄」某個職責、地點或人。引申為在關鍵時刻離開，給人留下困境。","definition":"1. abandon (a person, cause, or organization) in a way considered disloyal or treacherous; 2. abandon (a place or settlement)","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He would never desert his family.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他絕不會拋棄他的家人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The soldiers were accused of deserting their posts.\",\n    \"ch\": \"士兵們被指控擅離職守。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Don't desert me now!\",\n    \"ch\": \"現在別拋下我！\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他絕不會拋棄他的家人。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4572,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::desirable::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She is a ____ candidate for the job.","expectedAnswer":"desirable","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She is a ____ candidate for the job.","clozeAnswer":"desirable","exampleTranslation":"她是這份工作的理想人選。","reference":{"eng":"desirable","kk":"/dɪˈzaɪərəbəl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['令人渴望的', '合意的'], ['有吸引力的', '值得擁有的']]","chEntries":["令人渴望的","合意的","有吸引力的","值得擁有的"],"practiceMeaning":"她是這份工作的理想人選。","analysis":"由 'desire' (渴望) 加上形容詞字尾 '-able' (表示能夠、值得) 構成。核心概念是「值得渴望」。\n    1. 令人渴望的、合意的：指事物符合人們的願望或需求，非常想要得到。\n    2. 有吸引力的、值得擁有的：指事物在外表、品質或特點上具有吸引力，使人覺得值得追求。","definition":"1. wanted or wished for as a possibility or luxury.; 2. possessing or displaying qualities that give pleasure or satisfaction.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a desirable candidate for the job.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是這份工作的理想人選。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They live in a desirable neighborhood.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們住在一個令人嚮往的社區。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A stable income is a desirable outcome of education.\",\n    \"ch\": \"穩定的收入是教育的一個理想成果。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她是這份工作的理想人選。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5834,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::destructive::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The hurricane caused ____ winds.","expectedAnswer":"destructive","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The hurricane caused ____ winds.","clozeAnswer":"destructive","exampleTranslation":"這場颶風帶來了毀滅性的強風。","reference":{"eng":"destructive","kk":"dɪˈstrʌktɪv","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"破壞性的\"  ],  [    \"毀滅性的\"  ],  [    \"有害的\"  ]]","chEntries":["破壞性的","毀滅性的","有害的"],"practiceMeaning":"這場颶風帶來了毀滅性的強風。","analysis":"此字由拉丁語 'destructivus' 演變而來，是 'destruere' (to destroy) 的派生詞。'Destruere' 由 'de-' (down) 和 'struere' (to build, to pile up) 構成，字面意思是「拆毀」、「推倒」。'-ive' 是常見的形容詞字尾，表示「具有……性質的」。因此，'destructive' 指「具有破壞性質的」或「傾向於破壞」。它描述的是對事物造成損害、毀滅或瓦解的力量或行為。例如，也可指「對個人身心有害的」。","definition":"1. Causing great damage or destruction.; 2. Tending or likely to destroy.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The hurricane caused destructive winds.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這場颶風帶來了毀滅性的強風。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His criticism was destructive rather than constructive.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的批評具有破壞性而非建設性。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The wildfire had a destructive impact on the forest.\",\n    \"ch\": \"野火對森林造成了毀滅性的影響。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Negative thinking can be destructive.\",\n    \"ch\": \"消極思維可能是有害的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這場颶風帶來了毀滅性的強風。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5419,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::development::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of new technologies is essential for economic growth.","expectedAnswer":"development","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of new technologies is essential for economic growth.","clozeAnswer":"development","exampleTranslation":"新技術的發展對經濟增長至關重要。","reference":{"eng":"development","kk":"dɪˈveləpmənt","tense":"n.","ch":"[['發展'], ['開發'], ['進化'], ['成長'], ['事件']]","chEntries":["發展","開發","進化","成長","事件"],"practiceMeaning":"新技術的發展對經濟增長至關重要。","analysis":"此字為派生詞，由動詞 \"develop\" 加上名詞化字尾 \"-ment\" 構成。\"develop\" 源自古法語 \"desveloper\"，意為\"展開\"、\"解開\"。其詞源可能與 \"velop\" (包裹、覆蓋) 有關，表示「解開包裹」的動作。構詞上，\"de-\" 是表示「去除」或「相反」的字首（在此處語意為「展開」），\"velop\" 提供核心的「包裹」語意。字尾 \"-ment\" 將動詞的「展開」或「發展」行為轉化為抽象名詞。\"Development\" 指從一個較不複雜、較不成熟的狀態轉變為更複雜、更成熟狀態的過程或結果，涵蓋物理、社會、經濟、個人成長等多個層面。也可指一系列發生的「事件」。","definition":"the process of developing or being developed; a new stage in a process of change or improvement; a significant event or change; the process of growing or causing something to grow or become bigger or more advanced.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The development of new technologies is essential for economic growth.\",\n    \"ch\": \"新技術的發展對經濟增長至關重要。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We are monitoring the development of the storm.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們正在監測風暴的發展情況。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company announced a new product development.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司宣布了一項新產品開發。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"新技術的發展對經濟增長至關重要。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3139,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::diagram::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Please refer to the ____ on page 10 for instructions.","expectedAnswer":"diagram","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Please refer to the ____ on page 10 for instructions.","clozeAnswer":"diagram","exampleTranslation":"請參考第10頁的圖表以獲得說明。","reference":{"eng":"diagram","kk":"/ˈdaɪəˌɡræm/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['圖表；圖樣'], ['（解剖學、工程學等的）圖解']]","chEntries":["圖表","圖樣","圖解"],"practiceMeaning":"請參考第10頁的圖表以獲得說明。","analysis":"源自希臘語 'diagramma'，意為「圖案，設計」，由 'dia-'（穿過）+ 'graphein'（寫，繪製）組成。'Diagram' 是一種視覺表示，旨在展示事物、結構、原理或過程的組成部分、關係或工作方式。它通常是線條、符號和標籤的組合，用於簡化複雜的概念，使其更易於理解。","definition":"a simplified drawing showing the appearance, structure, or workings of something; a schematic representation.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please refer to the diagram on page 10 for instructions.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請參考第10頁的圖表以獲得說明。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The teacher drew a diagram of the solar system on the blackboard.\",\n    \"ch\": \"老師在黑板上畫了太陽系的圖解。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The manual includes a clear diagram of how to assemble the product.\",\n    \"ch\": \"手冊包含了一個清晰的圖表，說明如何組裝產品。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"請參考第10頁的圖表以獲得說明。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5836,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::diminish::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The threat of war did not ____.","expectedAnswer":"diminish","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The threat of war did not ____.","clozeAnswer":"diminish","exampleTranslation":"戰爭的威脅並未減弱。","reference":{"eng":"diminish","kk":"dɪˈmɪnɪʃ","tense":"v.","ch":"[  [    \"減少\"  ],  [    \"減弱\"  ],  [    \"降低\"  ],  [    \"縮小\"  ]]","chEntries":["減少","減弱","降低","縮小"],"practiceMeaning":"戰爭的威脅並未減弱。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'diminuere'，由 'di-' (apart, away) 和 'minuere' (to lessen) 構成。'Minuere' 來自 'minus' (less)。'Diminuere' 的字面意思是「使減少」、「使變小」。'-ish' 是常見的動詞字尾，將名詞或形容詞轉化為動詞，表示「使……」或「變得……」。因此，'diminish' 的核心語意是「使之變少、變弱或變小」。它可以指數量、強度、重要性、價值等方面的減少或減弱。例如，也可指「縮小」尺寸或範圍。","definition":"1. To make or become smaller, weaker, or less.; 2. To lessen the authority, dignity, or reputation of.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The threat of war did not diminish.\",\n    \"ch\": \"戰爭的威脅並未減弱。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His responsibilities will diminish as he gets older.\",\n    \"ch\": \"隨著年齡增長，他的責任將會減少。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The drug is used to diminish pain.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種藥物用於減輕疼痛。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The size of the company will diminish after the merger.\",\n    \"ch\": \"合併後公司的規模將會縮小。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"戰爭的威脅並未減弱。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5611,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l7::discrimination::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company has a strict policy against ____.","expectedAnswer":"discrimination","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company has a strict policy against ____.","clozeAnswer":"discrimination","exampleTranslation":"該公司有嚴格的反歧視政策。","reference":{"eng":"discrimination","kk":"dɪˌskrɪməˈneɪʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[['歧視'], ['區別對待'], ['識別能力']]","chEntries":["歧視","區別對待","識別能力"],"practiceMeaning":"該公司有嚴格的反歧視政策。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'discriminatio'，意為「區別」，由 'discriminare'（區分）派生，'discriminare' 又由 'dis-'（分開）和 'cernere'（分辨）組成。構詞學上，'dis-' 字首表示「分開」、「分離」，'cernere' 詞根提供「分辨」、「篩選」的核心語意。'-ation' 字尾將動詞轉換為名詞，表示「過程」或「狀態」。原始語意是「將事物分開、區別開來」。引申出兩個主要用法：一是「識別能力」（分辨細微差異的能力），二是「不公平的區別對待」，即「歧視」，特別是在種族、性別、年齡等方面。後者是現代社會語境中較常見的用法。","definition":"1. The unjust or prejudicial treatment of different categories of people, especially on grounds of race, age, or sex; 2. The ability to discern or distinguish between different things; 3. The action of treating a difference between things differently.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company has a strict policy against discrimination.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司有嚴格的反歧視政策。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Children develop the ability for visual discrimination at an early age.\",\n    \"ch\": \"兒童早期就會發展出視覺辨別能力。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Discrimination based on sexual orientation is illegal in many countries.\",\n    \"ch\": \"基於性取向的歧視在許多國家都是非法的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該公司有嚴格的反歧視政策。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5042,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::domain::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Physics is a complex scientific ____.","expectedAnswer":"domain","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Physics is a complex scientific ____.","clozeAnswer":"domain","exampleTranslation":"物理學是一個複雜的科學領域。","reference":{"eng":"domain","kk":"doʊˈmeɪn","tense":"n.","ch":"[['領域'], ['範圍'], ['域名']]","chEntries":["領域","範圍","域名"],"practiceMeaning":"物理學是一個複雜的科學領域。","analysis":"此字源自古法語domaine，本身又來自拉丁語dominium，意為「所有權、領地」，來自 dominus（主人）。原意指「屬於領主的地產」。在英語中，domain 演變出多重語意：1. 「領地、領土」，指某人或某事物所擁有的或控制的範圍；2. 「領域、專業範圍」，指某個學科、知識或活動的專屬範疇；3. 在網路語境中，指「域名」(domain name)。OCR 掃描時可能將 'o' 誤判為 '0'。此處修正為 domain。","definition":"1. an area of territory owned or controlled by a ruler or government; 2. an area of knowledge or activity; 3. a set of possible values for a variable.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Physics is a complex scientific domain.\",\n    \"ch\": \"物理學是一個複雜的科學領域。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company is expanding its domain into new markets.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司正在將其業務範圍擴展到新市場。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"You need to register a domain name for your website.\",\n    \"ch\": \"你需要為你的網站註冊一個域名。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"物理學是一個複雜的科學領域。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4697,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::dose::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The doctor prescribed a daily ____ of vitamins.","expectedAnswer":"dose","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The doctor prescribed a daily ____ of vitamins.","clozeAnswer":"dose","exampleTranslation":"醫生開了每日維生素劑量。","reference":{"eng":"dose","kk":"/ˈdoʊs/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['劑量'], ['（一次的）量'], ['（非正式）（尤指治療性的）一份（苦頭、教訓）']]","chEntries":["劑量","量","一份"],"practiceMeaning":"醫生開了每日維生素劑量。","analysis":"源自希臘語 *dósis*，意為「給予」、「分量」。核心是指定量的藥物或物質。引申至任何一次性的、一次性的給予，包括非正式地指一次需要承受的苦難或教訓。","definition":"1. A quantity of a medicine or drug taken or prescribed at one time. 2. A quantity of something, especially food or drink, taken at one time. 3. (informal) An unpleasant experience that you have to endure.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The doctor prescribed a daily dose of vitamins.\",\n    \"c