 \"The constant paperwork was a drag on our productivity.\",\n    \"ch\": \"不斷的文件工作拖慢了我們的生產力。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The long meeting was a real drag.\",\n    \"ch\": \"冗長的會議真讓人厭煩。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"不斷的文件工作拖慢了我們的生產力。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4189,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::dramatic::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There were ____ changes in the weather.","expectedAnswer":"dramatic","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There were ____ changes in the weather.","clozeAnswer":"dramatic","exampleTranslation":"天氣發生了劇烈的變化。","reference":{"eng":"dramatic","kk":"/drəˈmætɪk/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['戲劇性的；引人注目的'], ['（變化、行動等）突然的；劇烈的'], [' the dramatic arts']]","chEntries":["戲劇性的","引人注目的","突然的","劇烈的","the dramatic arts"],"practiceMeaning":"天氣發生了劇烈的變化。","analysis":"源自希臘語 dramatikos，與 drama（戲劇）相關。'Drama' 來自 'dran'，意為“做”。核心是與戲劇表演相關的特質。1. “戲劇性的”指像戲劇一樣引人注目、情緒強烈。2. “突然的；劇烈的”強調戲劇中常見的轉折和強烈效果，引申為現實生活中顯著的、巨大的變化。3. “戲劇藝術的”直接指與戲劇相關的。","definition":"1. sudden and striking; 2. relating to drama or the performance of plays; 3. exciting and attention-grabbing.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There were dramatic changes in the weather.\",\n    \"ch\": \"天氣發生了劇烈的變化。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The film has a dramatic plot.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這部電影有一個戲劇性的情節。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He made a dramatic entrance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他做了一個引人注目的登場。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"天氣發生了劇烈的變化。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U6、L8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3143,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::dread::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The thought of failing the exam filled him with ____.","expectedAnswer":"dread","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The thought of failing the exam filled him with ____.","clozeAnswer":"dread","exampleTranslation":"考試不及格的想法讓他充滿恐懼。","reference":{"eng":"dread","kk":"/drɛd/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['恐懼；害怕'], ['（預期中的）災禍；禍患']]","chEntries":["恐懼","害怕","災禍","禍患"],"practiceMeaning":"考試不及格的想法讓他充滿恐懼。","analysis":"名詞用法，源自動詞 'dread'。指「強烈的恐懼」、「畏懼」或「恐慌」，特別是對即將發生的不好的事情的預期。它也可以指「災禍」或「禍患」，暗示著一件令人感到恐懼或憂慮的事情。","definition":"1. great fear or apprehension; 2. a cause of great fear or apprehension.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The thought of failing the exam filled him with dread.\",\n    \"ch\": \"考試不及格的想法讓他充滿恐懼。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The dread of war hung over the nation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"戰爭的恐懼籠罩著這個國家。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He lived in constant dread of being discovered.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他生活在被發現的持續恐懼中。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"考試不及格的想法讓他充滿恐懼。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5080,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::dreadful::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The news of the accident was ____.","expectedAnswer":"dreadful","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The news of the accident was ____.","clozeAnswer":"dreadful","exampleTranslation":"事故的消息是可怕的。","reference":{"eng":"dreadful","kk":"ˈdredfl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['可怕的'], ['糟糕的'], ['極度的']]","chEntries":["可怕的","糟糕的","極度的"],"practiceMeaning":"事故的消息是可怕的。","analysis":"此字由 'dread' (恐懼) + '-ful' (形容詞化後綴，表示充滿、具有某種性質) 構成。'-ful' 在此強調充滿了 'dread' 的特質。核心語義是 '引發極度恐懼或憂慮的'。因此，它可以用來形容令人不安、可怕的事物。也可用來表示程度，如 '極度糟糕的'、'非常嚴重的'，強調其負面或強烈的影響。","definition":"1. Causing or involving great suffering, fear, or unhappiness; extremely bad.; 2. Of very low quality; very unpleasant.; 3. Inspiring dread or fear.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The news of the accident was dreadful.\",\n    \"ch\": \"事故的消息是可怕的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The weather was dreadful all week.\",\n    \"ch\": \"整個星期天氣都糟透了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has a dreadful habit of interrupting.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他有打斷別人說話的可怕習慣。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"事故的消息是可怕的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3144,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::dynamic::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company has a very ____ management team.","expectedAnswer":"dynamic","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company has a very ____ management team.","clozeAnswer":"dynamic","exampleTranslation":"這家公司擁有一支極具活力的管理團隊。","reference":{"eng":"dynamic","kk":"/daɪˈnæmɪk/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['動態的；充滿活力的'], ['（力量、過程）不斷變化的'], ['（人）精力充沛的；活躍的']]","chEntries":["動態的","充滿活力的","不斷變化的","精力充沛的","活躍的"],"practiceMeaning":"這家公司擁有一支極具活力的管理團隊。","analysis":"源自希臘語 'dynamikos'，意為「有力量的，強大的」，與 'dynamis'（力量）有關。'Dynamic' 強調的是能量、活力、變化和持續的活動。它與「static」（靜態的）相對。語意延伸至形容人、系統、過程或事物，這些都具有不斷變化、發展或活躍的特質。","definition":"1. characterized by constant change, activity, or progress; 2. (of a process or system) characterized by energy and enthusiasm; 3. relating to forces or energy.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company has a very dynamic management team.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司擁有一支極具活力的管理團隊。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The political situation is very dynamic at the moment.\",\n    \"ch\": \"目前的政治局勢變化非常快。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her dynamic personality made her popular with everyone.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她充滿活力的個性讓她深受大家喜愛。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這家公司擁有一支極具活力的管理團隊。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3982,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u3::easy::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This math problem is too ____ for me.","expectedAnswer":"easy","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This math problem is too ____ for me.","clozeAnswer":"easy","exampleTranslation":"這道數學題對我來說太容易了。","reference":{"eng":"easy","kk":"/ˈiːzi/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['容易的', '輕易的'], ['舒服的', '安逸的'], ['隨和的', '從容的']]","chEntries":["容易的","輕易的","舒服的","安逸的","隨和的","從容的"],"practiceMeaning":"這道數學題對我來說太容易了。","analysis":"詞源：古法語 'aisé' (舒適、方便)，源自拉丁文 'a' (在) 和 'sedes' (座位)。引申為「不費力的」、「無憂無慮的」、「輕鬆自在的」。","definition":"1. achieved without great effort; 2. not difficult to do or understand; 3. comfortable and free from worry.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This math problem is too easy for me.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這道數學題對我來說太容易了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He leads an easy life in retirement.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他退休後過著安逸的生活。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has an easy manner.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她舉止從容。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這道數學題對我來說太容易了。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3281,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::elastic::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ in her skirt had lost its stretch.","expectedAnswer":"elastic","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ in her skirt had lost its stretch.","clozeAnswer":"elastic","exampleTranslation":"她裙子裡的鬆緊帶已經失去彈性了。","reference":{"eng":"elastic","kk":"/ɪˈlæstɪk/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['鬆緊帶；彈性纖維']]","chEntries":["鬆緊帶","彈性纖維"],"practiceMeaning":"她裙子裡的鬆緊帶已經失去彈性了。","analysis":"名詞形式，指用來提供彈性的材料，如製作衣物腰帶或袖口的鬆緊帶。","definition":"a piece of elastic material, used in waistbands, cuffs, etc.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The elastic in her skirt had lost its stretch.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她裙子裡的鬆緊帶已經失去彈性了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She repaired the trousers with a new piece of elastic.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她用一條新的鬆緊帶修好了褲子。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她裙子裡的鬆緊帶已經失去彈性了。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4449,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::electronic::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She bought a new ____ gadget for her kitchen.","expectedAnswer":"electronic","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She bought a new ____ gadget for her kitchen.","clozeAnswer":"electronic","exampleTranslation":"她買了一個新的電子小工具給她的廚房。","reference":{"eng":"electronic","kk":"/ɪˈlɛktrɪk/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['電子的'], ['電腦化的'], ['（尤指）電流通過裝置的']]","chEntries":["電子的","電腦化的","電流通過裝置的"],"practiceMeaning":"她買了一個新的電子小工具給她的廚房。","analysis":"源自 electro- (來自希臘語 ēlektron, 意為琥珀，因其摩擦生電的性質而得名) 加上 -ic (形容詞後綴)。核心概念是與電有關。語意從「與電有關」延伸至「由電力驅動的」、「通過電子元件運作的」，如電子設備 (electronic devices)。","definition":"1. Operated by or using electricity, especially in an advanced or complex way; relating to or using devices that operate by the flow of electrons.; 2. Relating to or concerned with the production and emission of electrons.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She bought a new electronic gadget for her kitchen.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她買了一個新的電子小工具給她的廚房。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Electronic mail has revolutionized communication.\",\n    \"ch\": \"電子郵件徹底改變了通訊方式。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company specializes in electronic components.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司專門生產電子零件。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她買了一個新的電子小工具給她的廚房。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6118,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::eloquent::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He is an ____ speaker.","expectedAnswer":"eloquent","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He is an ____ speaker.","clozeAnswer":"eloquent","exampleTranslation":"他是一位雄辯的演講者。","reference":{"eng":"eloquent","kk":"ˈɛləkwənt","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"雄辯的\"  ],  [    \"口才好的\"  ],  [    \"有說服力的\"  ],  [    \"鮮明的\"  ]]","chEntries":["雄辯的","口才好的","有說服力的","鮮明的"],"practiceMeaning":"他是一位雄辯的演講者。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 ēloquēns，是 ēloquī（說出；流利地說）的現在分詞。構詞上，ē- 是強調字首，loquī 意為「說話」，與 loquor（說）有關。因此，eloquent 的核心語義是「說話有力、流利」。此形容詞用於描述演講、作家、言論或表達方式，強調其具有說服力、感染力和清晰度。其語意演變是從具體的「能說會道」到抽象的「有說服力的、鮮明的」。","definition":"1. fluent or persuasive in speaking or writing; 2. clearly expressing or indicating something; vivid.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is an eloquent speaker.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一位雄辯的演講者。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her eyes were eloquent in their sorrow.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她眼中流露出的悲傷鮮明動人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The book provides an eloquent defense of human rights.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本書有力地捍衛了人權。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他是一位雄辯的演講者。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3146,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::energetic::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The children were ____ and full of fun.","expectedAnswer":"energetic","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The children were ____ and full of fun.","clozeAnswer":"energetic","exampleTranslation":"孩子們精力充沛，充滿樂趣。","reference":{"eng":"energetic","kk":"/ˌɛnərˈdʒɛtɪk/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['精力充沛的；充滿活力的'], ['（行動、過程）需要大量體力的']]","chEntries":["精力充沛的","充滿活力的","需要大量體力的"],"practiceMeaning":"孩子們精力充沛，充滿樂趣。","analysis":"源自名詞 'energy'，意為「能量」。'Energetic' 形容詞表示擁有或顯示出大量的能量、活力和熱情。它強調的是積極、活躍、有幹勁的狀態，常與體力活動或強烈的情緒反應相關。與 'dynamic' 相似，但更側重於個體的活力和行動力。","definition":"1. showing or involving great energy and enthusiasm; 2. requiring a lot of energy.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The children were energetic and full of fun.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子們精力充沛，充滿樂趣。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is an energetic advocate for environmental protection.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是環保運動的積極倡導者。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Renovating the old house was an energetic undertaking.\",\n    \"ch\": \"翻新這座老房子是一項需要大量精力的工程。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"孩子們精力充沛，充滿樂趣。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3887,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::enjoyable::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It was an ____ evening.","expectedAnswer":"enjoyable","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It was an ____ evening.","clozeAnswer":"enjoyable","exampleTranslation":"這是一個愉快的夜晚。","reference":{"eng":"enjoyable","kk":"/ɪnˈdʒɔɪəbl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['愉快的', '令人享受的']]","chEntries":["愉快的","令人享受的"],"practiceMeaning":"這是一個愉快的夜晚。","analysis":"由 'enjoy' (享受) 和 '-able' (形容詞後綴，表示「可…的」) 組成。核心是「可以享受的」。指能帶來樂趣、快樂或滿意的。","definition":"pleasant and giving pleasure.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was an enjoyable evening.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個愉快的夜晚。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We had an enjoyable time at the party.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們在派對上玩得很開心。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The book made for an enjoyable read.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本書提供了愉快的閱讀體驗。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是一個愉快的夜晚。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5587,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::excellent::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"That was an ____ meal!","expectedAnswer":"excellent","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"That was an ____ meal!","clozeAnswer":"excellent","exampleTranslation":"那是一頓極好的餐點！","reference":{"eng":"excellent","kk":"ˈɛksələnt","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['優秀的'], ['卓越的'], ['極好的'], ['出色的']]","chEntries":["優秀的","卓越的","極好的","出色的"],"practiceMeaning":"那是一頓極好的餐點！","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 \"excellēns\"，是 \"excellere\"（to be eminent, surpass, excel，卓越，超越）的現在分詞。\"excellere\" 由 \"ex-\"（out）和 \"cellere\"（to rise, to be eminent，上升，卓越）組成，意為「突出，超越眾人」。因此，\"excellent\" 的核心語義是「非常出色、品質極高、超越一般水準」。它用來形容人、物、表現或情況，表示其達到了極高的標準。","definition":"1. Extremely good; outstanding; 2. Very high in quality or degree.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"That was an excellent meal!\",\n    \"ch\": \"那是一頓極好的餐點！\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He gave an excellent presentation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他做了一個出色的報告。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The team achieved excellent results.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這支隊伍取得了優異的成績。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"那是一頓極好的餐點！","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4203,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::exchange::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of gifts is common at Christmas.","expectedAnswer":"exchange","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of gifts is common at Christmas.","clozeAnswer":"exchange","exampleTranslation":"交換禮物在聖誕節很常見。","reference":{"eng":"exchange","kk":"/ɪksˈtʃeɪndʒ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['交換；兌換'], ['交流；談話'], ['（股票、貨幣等的）交易所']]","chEntries":["交換","兌換","交流","談話","交易所"],"practiceMeaning":"交換禮物在聖誕節很常見。","analysis":"名詞形式源自動詞 'exchange'。1. “交換；兌換”指交換的行為或結果。2. “交流；談話”指思想、資訊的相互傳遞過程。3. “交易所”是特定場所的名稱，指進行金融商品交換的機構。","definition":"1. the act of giving one thing and receiving another in return; 2. conversation; 3. a place where shares or other securities are bought and sold.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The exchange of gifts is common at Christmas.\",\n    \"ch\": \"交換禮物在聖誕節很常見。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We had a brief exchange of views.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們就此交換了簡短的看法。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He works at the stock exchange.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在證券交易所工作。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"交換禮物在聖誕節很常見。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5535,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l5::execution::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of the plan was successful.","expectedAnswer":"execution","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of the plan was successful.","clozeAnswer":"execution","exampleTranslation":"計劃的執行很成功。","reference":{"eng":"execution","kk":"ˌeksɪˈkjuːʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[['執行'], ['處決'], [' تنفيذ'], ['技術']]","chEntries":["執行","處決","تنفيذ","技術"],"practiceMeaning":"計劃的執行很成功。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'executio'，由 'ex-' (out) + 'sequi' (to follow) 構成，意思是「跟隨、執行」。'execute' 是其動詞形式，意為「執行」。構詞上，'ex-' 表示「完成、結束」，'secut-' 是 'sequi' 的詞幹，意為「跟隨」。'execution' 作名詞，指「執行」的動作或過程，包括執行法律判決（處決）、履行職責或完成計劃。在技術或藝術領域，它也指「技藝的熟練程度」或「表現」。多個義項都圍繞著「完成、實施、執行」的核心概念。","definition":"the carrying out of a plan, order, or course of action; the act of putting a condemned person to death; technical skill or performance.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The execution of the plan was successful.\",\n    \"ch\": \"計劃的執行很成功。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The execution of the prisoner took place at dawn.\",\n    \"ch\": \"囚犯的處決於黎明時進行。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her execution of the piano piece was flawless.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她演奏的鋼琴曲無懈可擊。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"計劃的執行很成功。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3149,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::exhausted::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"After the marathon, the runners were completely ____.","expectedAnswer":"exhausted","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"After the marathon, the runners were completely ____.","clozeAnswer":"exhausted","exampleTranslation":"馬拉松賽後，跑者們都筋疲力盡了。","reference":{"eng":"exhausted","kk":"/ɪɡˈzɔːstɪd/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['筋疲力盡的；精疲力竭的'], ['（資源、供應品等）被用盡的']]","chEntries":["筋疲力盡的","精疲力竭的","被用盡的"],"practiceMeaning":"馬拉松賽後，跑者們都筋疲力盡了。","analysis":"動詞 'exhaust' 的過去分詞，用作形容詞。表示處於極度疲憊、精疲力竭的狀態，由於過度的勞動、活動或情緒消耗。也指某種資源、供應或情況已經被完全用完、耗盡。","definition":"1. very tired; 2. having no energy left; 3. completely used up.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"After the marathon, the runners were completely exhausted.\",\n    \"ch\": \"馬拉松賽後，跑者們都筋疲力盡了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The country's oil reserves were nearly exhausted.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該國的石油儲備幾乎被耗盡了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She felt exhausted by the constant worry.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她因持續的擔憂而感到精疲力竭。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"馬拉松賽後，跑者們都筋疲力盡了。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3150,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::exhausting::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Climbing the mountain was an ____ experience.","expectedAnswer":"exhausting","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Climbing the mountain was an ____ experience.","clozeAnswer":"exhausting","exampleTranslation":"攀登這座山是一次令人精疲力竭的經歷。","reference":{"eng":"exhausting","kk":"/ɪɡˈzɔːstɪŋ/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['令人精疲力竭的；使人疲憊不堪的']]","chEntries":["令人精疲力竭的","使人疲憊不堪的"],"practiceMeaning":"攀登這座山是一次令人精疲力竭的經歷。","analysis":"動詞 'exhaust' 的現在分詞，用作形容詞。描述某事物（活動、工作、經歷）能夠導致他人感到極度疲憊、精疲力竭。與 'exhausted'（表示自身狀態）相對，'exhausting' 描述的是原因。","definition":"causing extreme physical or mental tiredness.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Climbing the mountain was an exhausting experience.\",\n    \"ch\": \"攀登這座山是一次令人精疲力竭的經歷。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Dealing with difficult customers can be very exhausting.\",\n    \"ch\": \"應付難纏的顧客會非常累人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The long and exhausting search finally yielded results.\",\n    \"ch\": \"漫長而令人疲憊的搜尋終於有了結果。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"攀登這座山是一次令人精疲力竭的經歷。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6074,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::expedition::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ set out to explore the Amazon rainforest.","expectedAnswer":"expedition","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ set out to explore the Amazon rainforest.","clozeAnswer":"expedition","exampleTranslation":"這次探險隊出發去探索亞馬遜雨林。","reference":{"eng":"expedition","kk":"ˌɛkspəˈdɪʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"遠征\"  ],  [    \"考察\"  ],  [    \"探險\"  ],  [    \"遠足\"  ],  [    \"迅速\"  ]]","chEntries":["遠征","考察","探險","遠足","迅速"],"practiceMeaning":"這次探險隊出發去探索亞馬遜雨林。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 expeditio，是 expédire（to send out, to dispatch）的結果名詞。Expédire 由 ex-（out）和 pes, pedis（foot）組成，字面意思是「派腳出去」，引申為「派遣」，再引申為「迅速完成」、「派出以達成目的」。構詞上，ex- 表「出」，ped- 表「腳」，-ition 是名詞後綴。Expedition 的核心語義是「為特定目的（通常是探索、考察、科學研究或軍事行動）而進行的、有組織的、較長距離的出行」。它也引申為「迅速」這個較少用的意義。","definition":"1. a journey undertaken by a group of people with a particular purpose, especially exploration, scientific research, or war; 2. efficiency and speed in doing something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The expedition set out to explore the Amazon rainforest.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這次探險隊出發去探索亞馬遜雨林。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They prepared for a polar expedition.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們為極地考察做好了準備。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The relief expedition arrived quickly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"救援隊迅速抵達。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這次探險隊出發去探索亞馬遜雨林。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4153,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::experience::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She has ten years of work ____.","expectedAnswer":"experience","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She has ten years of work ____.","clozeAnswer":"experience","exampleTranslation":"她有十年的工作經驗。","reference":{"eng":"experience","kk":"/ɪkˈspɪəriəns/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['經驗'], ['（經歷過的）事情，體驗']]","chEntries":["經驗","事情，體驗"],"practiceMeaning":"她有十年的工作經驗。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 experientia（嘗試，知識），是動詞 experiri（嘗試）的名詞形式。核心概念是「通過嘗試或參與而獲得的知識或技能」。","definition":"1. practical contact with and observation of facts or events; 2. an event or occurrence which leaves an impression on someone","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has ten years of work experience.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她有十年的工作經驗。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was a terrible experience.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那是一次糟糕的經歷。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He gained valuable experience during his internship.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在實習期間獲得了寶貴的經驗。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她有十年的工作經驗。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5783,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::expertise::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The consultant brought considerable ____ to the project.","expectedAnswer":"expertise","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The consultant brought considerable ____ to the project.","clozeAnswer":"expertise","exampleTranslation":"這位顧問為該項目帶來了豐富的專業知識。","reference":{"eng":"expertise","kk":"ˌɛkspərˈtiz","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"專業知識\"  ],  [    \"專長\"  ],  [    \"技能\"  ]]","chEntries":["專業知識","專長","技能"],"practiceMeaning":"這位顧問為該項目帶來了豐富的專業知識。","analysis":"此字為名詞，源自法語expertise，意為「專業知識；專家判斷」。法語expertise本身源自拉丁語expertus（經驗豐富的；證實過的），是expert（專家）的名詞後綴。expert來自拉丁語expertus，由ex-（外面）+pertus（經過；試驗，與parere「生產；經驗」相關）組成，原意是「經過考驗的；有經驗的」。因此，expertise的核心語義是指「由於長時間的學習、訓練或經驗而獲得的深入知識和高超技能」。語意演變上，從「有經驗」的概念，發展為「所擁有的專門知識和技能」。","definition":"1. expert skill or knowledge in a particular field.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The consultant brought considerable expertise to the project.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位顧問為該項目帶來了豐富的專業知識。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her expertise in marketing is invaluable to our team.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在市場營銷方面的專長對我們的團隊來說非常寶貴。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need someone with technical expertise to solve this problem.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要一位具有技術專長的人來解決這個問題。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這位顧問為該項目帶來了豐富的專業知識。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6119,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::explicit::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The instructions were ____.","expectedAnswer":"explicit","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The instructions were ____.","clozeAnswer":"explicit","exampleTranslation":"說明很明確。","reference":{"eng":"explicit","kk":"ɪkˈsplɪsɪt","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"明確的\"  ],  [    \"清晰的\"  ],  [    \"詳盡的\"  ],  [    \"直白的\"  ],  [    \"露骨的\"  ]]","chEntries":["明確的","清晰的","詳盡的","直白的","露骨的"],"practiceMeaning":"說明很明確。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 explicitus，是 explicāre（展開；解釋）的過去分詞。構詞上，ex- 是字首，表示「出；外面」；plicāre 意為「折疊；纏繞」，因此 explicāre 的核心語義是「展開、攤開、解釋清楚」。explicit 的核心語義是「被完全展開、沒有隱藏」。此形容詞表示清晰、無誤、無含糊或隱藏，直接說明。其語意演變是從具體的「被展開、攤開」到抽象的「清晰、明確、直白」。","definition":"1. stated clearly and in detail, leaving no room for confusion or doubt; 2. showing or describing the act of sex, violence, or illegal activity in a very direct way.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The instructions were explicit.\",\n    \"ch\": \"說明很明確。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He made explicit threats.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他做出了明確的威脅。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The film contained explicit scenes of violence.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這部電影包含露骨的暴力場面。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"說明很明確。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6224,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::exterior::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The house has a beautiful brick ____.","expectedAnswer":"exterior","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The house has a beautiful brick ____.","clozeAnswer":"exterior","exampleTranslation":"這座房子有著美麗的磚砌外觀。","reference":{"eng":"exterior","kk":"ɪkˈstɪəriər","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"外觀\"  ],  [    \"外景\"  ],  [    \"外部\"  ]]","chEntries":["外觀","外景","外部"],"practiceMeaning":"這座房子有著美麗的磚砌外觀。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 exterior，是 externus（外面的）的比較級，意為「更外面的」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。名詞義指某物或某人的外部表面、外觀或外形，尤指建築物、車輛等的外部特徵。也指拍攝地點在戶外。中文翻譯為「外觀；外景；外部」。","definition":"1. the outer surface or structure of something; 2. a person's outward appearance and behavior; 3. a scene or location filmed outdoors.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The house has a beautiful brick exterior.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座房子有著美麗的磚砌外觀。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The film was shot on location, with many exterior scenes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這部電影是在外景地拍攝的，有很多戶外場景。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Despite his stern exterior, he was a kind man.\",\n    \"ch\": \"儘管他外表嚴肅，他卻是個善良的人。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這座房子有著美麗的磚砌外觀。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6075,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::faculty::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ met to discuss the new curriculum.","expectedAnswer":"faculty","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ met to discuss the new curriculum.","clozeAnswer":"faculty","exampleTranslation":"全體教職員開會討論新課程。","reference":{"eng":"faculty","kk":"ˈfækəlti","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"系\"  ],  [    \"學院\"  ],  [    \"全體教職員\"  ],  [    \"能力\"  ],  [    \"才能\"  ]]","chEntries":["系","學院","全體教職員","能力","才能"],"practiceMeaning":"全體教職員開會討論新課程。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 facultas，意為「能力，權力，可能性」，來自 facilis（easy），本身由 facere（to make, to do）派生。核心語義是「能力」或「才能」。在學術語境中，faculty 指大學的「教職員」（他們擁有教學和研究的能力），或構成一個學院或學系的「全體教職員」。Also can refer to 'mental or physical power'.","definition":"1. all the teachers at a college or university; 2. a department or group of departments in a university, dealing with a particular subject or range of subjects; 3. an inherent mental or physical power.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The faculty met to discuss the new curriculum.\",\n    \"ch\": \"全體教職員開會討論新課程。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a professor in the Faculty of Arts.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是文學院的教授。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Humans have the faculty of reason.\",\n    \"ch\": \"人類擁有理性思考的能力。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"全體教職員開會討論新課程。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4318,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::fairly::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This book is ____ interesting.","expectedAnswer":"fairly","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This book is ____ interesting.","clozeAnswer":"fairly","exampleTranslation":"這本書相當有趣。","reference":{"eng":"fairly","kk":"/ˈfɛərli/","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['相當地；頗為'], ['公平地；公正地'], ['（路程、時間等）適度地']]","chEntries":["相當地","頗為","公平地","公正地","適度地"],"practiceMeaning":"這本書相當有趣。","analysis":"源自 'fair' (公平的，美麗的)。作為副詞，它繼承了 'fair' 的不同含義。1.『公平地；公正地』：強調判斷或行動的客觀和公正。2.『相當地；頗為』：表示程度，相當於 'quite' 或 'rather'，表示一個中等偏上的程度，有時帶有『還算』的語氣，與『非常』不同，但又比『有點』強。3.『適度地』：指路程、時間等的適中，不遠也不近。","definition":"to a moderate degree; quite; in a fair and honest way","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This book is fairly interesting.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本書相當有趣。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The judge ruled fairly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"法官做出了公平的裁決。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's a fairly long walk to the station.\",\n    \"ch\": \"走到車站的路程相當遠。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這本書相當有趣。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4053,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::faith::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She has great ____ in her doctor's abilities.","expectedAnswer":"faith","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She has great ____ in her doctor's abilities.","clozeAnswer":"faith","exampleTranslation":"她對她醫生的能力深具信心。","reference":{"eng":"faith","kk":"/feɪθ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['信仰', '信念'], ['信任', '信賴'], ['保證', '承諾']]","chEntries":["信仰","信念","信任","信賴","保證","承諾"],"practiceMeaning":"她對她醫生的能力深具信心。","analysis":"源自古法語 'feid'，來自拉丁語 'fides' (faith, trust, belief)，與 'fidelis' (faithful) 同源。核心是「相信」、「信任」。因此，'faith' 可以指宗教上的「信仰」、對某人或某事的「信任」，或是對某事成功或發生的「信念」、「希望」。第四個義項「保證」則是由「信任」引申，表示基於信任而產生的承諾或保證。","definition":"1. strong belief in God or in the doctrines of a religion; 2. complete trust or confidence in someone or something; 3. a strong feeling of trust or confidence","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"她對她醫生的能力深具信心。\",\n    \"eng\": \"She has great faith in her doctor's abilities.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他們對政府已經失去了信心。\",\n    \"eng\": \"They have lost faith in the government.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他對上帝的信仰給予他力量。\",\n    \"eng\": \"His faith in God gives him strength.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她對她醫生的能力深具信心。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5537,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l5::fake::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He was wearing a ____ designer watch.","expectedAnswer":"fake","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He was wearing a ____ designer watch.","clozeAnswer":"fake","exampleTranslation":"他戴著一只仿製的名牌手錶。","reference":{"eng":"fake","kk":"feɪk","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['假的'], ['仿製的'], ['虛假的']]","chEntries":["假的","仿製的","虛假的"],"practiceMeaning":"他戴著一只仿製的名牌手錶。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 'faken'，其詞源不確定，可能與低地德語 'faken' (to deceive) 或北歐語言有關，總體指向「欺騙、偽造」的概念。構詞上無明顯字首、字根、字尾。原始語義與「虛假、欺騙」相關。'fake' 作形容詞時，描述的是「非真實的、仿製的、非本來的」，與「真品、真實」相對立。","definition":"not genuine; imitation or counterfeit.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was wearing a fake designer watch.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他戴著一只仿製的名牌手錶。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The signature on the document looked fake.\",\n    \"ch\": \"文件上的簽名看起來是假的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他戴著一只仿製的名牌手錶。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4075,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::familiar::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He is ____ with the city.","expectedAnswer":"familiar","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He is ____ with the city.","clozeAnswer":"familiar","exampleTranslation":"他熟悉這座城市。","reference":{"eng":"familiar","kk":"/fəˈmɪliər/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['熟悉的', '常見的'], ['親近的', '親密的']]","chEntries":["熟悉的","常見的","親近的","親密的"],"practiceMeaning":"他熟悉這座城市。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'familiaris'，由 'familia' (family) 構成，意為「家庭的」、「屬於家庭的」。核心是與「家」或「親近的人」有關。因此，'familiar' 指「親近的」、「熟悉的」，引申為「常見的」、「容易辨認的」。","definition":"1. well known from long or close contact; 2. closely acquainted; 3. common or ordinary","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他熟悉這座城市。\",\n    \"eng\": \"He is familiar with the city.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"這音樂聽起來很熟悉。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The music sounded familiar.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他們是從小就親近的朋友。\",\n    \"eng\": \"They were familiar friends from childhood.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他熟悉這座城市。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3217,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::farewell::interj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____, my friends! I hope to see you again.","expectedAnswer":"Farewell","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____, my friends! I hope to see you again.","clozeAnswer":"Farewell","exampleTranslation":"朋友們，再會！希望我們能再見面。","reference":{"eng":"farewell","kk":"/ˌfɛrˈwɛl/","tense":"interj.","ch":"[['再會']]","chEntries":["再會"],"practiceMeaning":"朋友們，再會！希望我們能再見面。","analysis":"作為感嘆詞，直接表達『再見』、『祝你旅途平安』的意思，承襲其字面意義『去得好』。","definition":"used when parting from someone.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Farewell, my friends! I hope to see you again.\",\n    \"ch\": \"朋友們，再會！希望我們能再見面。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"朋友們，再會！希望我們能再見面。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U41"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false