anslation":"他為當地隊伍打冰球。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6078,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::honorable::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He is an ____ man known for his integrity.","expectedAnswer":"honorable","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He is an ____ man known for his integrity.","clozeAnswer":"honorable","exampleTranslation":"他是一位以誠信聞名的正直人士。","reference":{"eng":"honorable","kk":"ˈɑnərəbəl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"榮譽的\"  ],  [    \"光榮的\"  ],  [    \"正直的\"  ],  [    \"可敬的\"  ],  [    \"尊稱\"  ]]","chEntries":["榮譽的","光榮的","正直的","可敬的","尊稱"],"practiceMeaning":"他是一位以誠信聞名的正直人士。","analysis":"此字由 honor（榮譽）加上形容詞後綴 -able（能夠……的）構成。Honor 源自拉丁語 honor，意為「尊嚴，尊敬，榮譽」。核心語義是「值得尊敬」、「值得榮譽」或「具有高尚品德」。它可用來形容一個人、行為、事件，或作為一種尊稱（例如 Honorable Mr. President）。","definition":"1. deserving honor and respect; 2. bringing or deserving honor; 3. (used as a title of respect for a judge or certain officials).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is an honorable man known for his integrity.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一位以誠信聞名的正直人士。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was an honorable victory.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一場光榮的勝利。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The judge was addressed as 'Your Honorable'.\",\n    \"ch\": \"法官被尊稱為『閣下』。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他是一位以誠信聞名的正直人士。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4631,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::horrible::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It was a ____ accident.","expectedAnswer":"horrible","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It was a ____ accident.","clozeAnswer":"horrible","exampleTranslation":"那是一場可怕的事故。","reference":{"eng":"horrible","kk":"/ˈhɔːrəbəl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['可怕的'], ['駭人的'], ['糟糕的']]","chEntries":["可怕的","駭人的","糟糕的"],"practiceMeaning":"那是一場可怕的事故。","analysis":"由 'horror' (恐怖) + '-ible' (能夠...的) 組成。此字描述事物引起強烈恐懼、厭惡或不適感，其程度比 'scary' 更深。也可引申形容非常糟糕、令人難受的體驗。","definition":"causing or likely to cause horror; shocking; extremely unpleasant.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was a horrible accident.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那是一場可怕的事故。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The food tasted horrible.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這食物嚐起來糟透了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They heard a horrible scream in the night.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們在夜裡聽到一聲駭人的尖叫。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"那是一場可怕的事故。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4620,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::horror::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The movie was full of ____ and suspense.","expectedAnswer":"horror","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The movie was full of ____ and suspense.","clozeAnswer":"horror","exampleTranslation":"這部電影充滿了恐怖和懸疑。","reference":{"eng":"horror","kk":"/ˈhɔːrər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['恐怖'], ['驚恐'], ['恐懼'], ['（電影、文學作品）恐怖片']]","chEntries":["恐怖","驚恐","恐懼","恐怖片"],"practiceMeaning":"這部電影充滿了恐怖和懸疑。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'horrere' (感到恐懼、戰慄)。核心是強烈的恐懼、厭惡或厭惡感，通常是由於看到或想到可怕、令人不安的事物。其名詞形式 'horror' 指這種感覺本身，也指引起這種感覺的事物，如恐怖電影。","definition":"an intense feeling of fear, shock, or disgust; something that causes such a feeling.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The movie was full of horror and suspense.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這部電影充滿了恐怖和懸疑。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She looked at the scene with horror.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她驚恐地看著眼前的景象。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He's a fan of horror novels.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是恐怖小說迷。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這部電影充滿了恐怖和懸疑。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4720,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::humor::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He has a great sense of ____.","expectedAnswer":"humor","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He has a great sense of ____.","clozeAnswer":"humor","exampleTranslation":"他很有幽默感。","reference":{"eng":"humor","kk":"/ˈhjumər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['幽默感'], ['趣味']]","chEntries":["幽默感","趣味"],"practiceMeaning":"他很有幽默感。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 *humor*，最初指體內的液體（體液學說）。後演變為指人的脾氣、性情，再到指引起笑聲或愉悅感的特質，即幽默感。","definition":"1. The quality of being amusing or comic, especially as expressed in literature or speech. 2. A person's mood or disposition.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has a great sense of humor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他很有幽默感。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The comedian's humor was a bit dark.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位喜劇演員的幽默風格有點暗黑。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他很有幽默感。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4637,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::hunger::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The child cried from ____.","expectedAnswer":"hunger","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The child cried from ____.","clozeAnswer":"hunger","exampleTranslation":"孩子因飢餓而哭泣。","reference":{"eng":"hunger","kk":"/ˈhʌŋɡər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['飢餓'], ['渴望'], ['熱望']]","chEntries":["飢餓","渴望","熱望"],"practiceMeaning":"孩子因飢餓而哭泣。","analysis":"源自古英語 'hungor'，與「飢餓」的生理感受相關。核心是對食物的強烈需求。引申義指對某事物（知識、成功、權力等）的強烈渴望，這種渴望的程度類似於生理上的飢餓。","definition":"a strong desire or craving, especially for food; a strong desire for something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The child cried from hunger.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子因飢餓而哭泣。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has a hunger for knowledge.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對知識有強烈的渴望。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The hunger for power is a dangerous thing.\",\n    \"ch\": \"對權力的渴望是一件危險的事。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"孩子因飢餓而哭泣。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3164,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::ignorance::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ of the law is no excuse.","expectedAnswer":"Ignorance","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ of the law is no excuse.","clozeAnswer":"Ignorance","exampleTranslation":"不知法律是無法作為藉口的。","reference":{"eng":"ignorance","kk":"/ˈɪɡnərəns/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['無知；缺乏知識'], ['（對某事的）不知情；無知']]","chEntries":["無知","缺乏知識","不知情"],"practiceMeaning":"不知法律是無法作為藉口的。","analysis":"名詞，源自形容詞 'ignorant'。'Ignorance' 指的是缺乏知識、信息或理解的狀態。它可以是對廣泛領域的普遍無知，也可以是對特定情況、事實或問題的不知情。這種無知可能是有意為之，也可能是由於缺乏接觸或學習機會。","definition":"1. lack of knowledge or information; 2. a lack of acquaintance with or understanding of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Ignorance of the law is no excuse.\",\n    \"ch\": \"不知法律是無法作為藉口的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His comments revealed his ignorance about the topic.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的評論顯示了他對這個話題的無知。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The project aims to combat ignorance about climate change.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該項目旨在消除人們對氣候變化的無知。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"不知法律是無法作為藉口的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3165,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::ignorant::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He remained ____ of the danger he was in.","expectedAnswer":"ignorant","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He remained ____ of the danger he was in.","clozeAnswer":"ignorant","exampleTranslation":"他對自己身處的危險毫無所知。","reference":{"eng":"ignorant","kk":"/ˈɪɡnərənt/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['無知的；缺乏知識的'], ['（對某事）不知情的']]","chEntries":["無知的","缺乏知識的","不知情的"],"practiceMeaning":"他對自己身處的危險毫無所知。","analysis":"詞源來自拉丁語 'ignorans'，意為「不知道的」，'ignorare'（不知道）。'Ignorant' 形容的是一個人缺乏必要的知識、信息或理解。它可以指普遍缺乏教育，也可以指對某特定情況、事實或問題不了解。有時也帶有不禮貌或粗魯的含義，指未受過良好教育或缺乏禮儀。","definition":"1. lacking knowledge or information; uneducated; 2. not aware of or concerned about something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He remained ignorant of the danger he was in.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對自己身處的危險毫無所知。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Some people are ignorant of the facts.\",\n    \"ch\": \"有些人對事實一無所知。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The teacher warned the students against being ignorant of current events.\",\n    \"ch\": \"老師告誡學生不要對時事無知。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他對自己身處的危險毫無所知。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6174,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::illusion::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The magician created the ____ that he had disappeared.","expectedAnswer":"illusion","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The magician created the ____ that he had disappeared.","clozeAnswer":"illusion","exampleTranslation":"魔術師製造了他消失的幻覺。","reference":{"eng":"illusion","kk":"ɪˈluːʒən","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"幻覺\"  ],  [    \"錯覺\"  ],  [    \"幻想\"  ],  [    \"海市蜃樓\"  ]]","chEntries":["幻覺","錯覺","幻想","海市蜃樓"],"practiceMeaning":"魔術師製造了他消失的幻覺。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 illūsiōnem，是動詞 illudere「欺騙、嘲弄」的名詞化。illudere 由 in- (in, into) + lūdere (to play, mock) 組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 in-「進入」和 lūdere「玩弄、嘲弄」是其核心語意來源。作為名詞，其核心語義是「一種由感官誤解或心理作用產生的虛假感知」，即「幻覺」或「錯覺」。詞源中的「玩弄、嘲弄」引申為「欺騙」，進而產生「虛假的感知」。","definition":"1. a false idea or belief; 2. the state of being deceived; 3. a thing that is or is likely to become or prove false; 4. a deceptive appearance or impression.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The magician created the illusion that he had disappeared.\",\n    \"ch\": \"魔術師製造了他消失的幻覺。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He lives under the illusion that he is rich.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他活在自己是富翁的幻想中。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Mirages are optical illusions.\",\n    \"ch\": \"海市蜃樓是光學錯覺。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company's success was an illusion; they were close to bankruptcy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司的成功是假象；他們離破產不遠了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"魔術師製造了他消失的幻覺。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3932,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::immediate::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need an ____ response to this crisis.","expectedAnswer":"immediate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need an ____ response to this crisis.","clozeAnswer":"immediate","exampleTranslation":"我們需要對這次危機做出立即的回應。","reference":{"eng":"immediate","kk":"/ɪˈmiːdiət/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['立即的', '即刻的'], ['緊鄰的', '直接的']]","chEntries":["立即的","即刻的","緊鄰的","直接的"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要對這次危機做出立即的回應。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'immediatus'，由 'in-' (意為「不」) 和 'mediatus' (意為「中間的」) 組成。原意是「沒有中間步驟的」，引申為「立刻發生的」或「緊鄰的」。","definition":"1. happening or done at once; instant; 2. happening or done right after something else, with no delay; 3. next to or very close to someone or something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need an immediate response to this crisis.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要對這次危機做出立即的回應。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The immediate family gathered at the hospital.\",\n    \"ch\": \"直系親屬聚集在醫院。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was no immediate danger.\",\n    \"ch\": \"沒有立即的危險。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要對這次危機做出立即的回應。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6175,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::implication::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of his words was clear.","expectedAnswer":"implication","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of his words was clear.","clozeAnswer":"implication","exampleTranslation":"他言語的含義很清楚。","reference":{"eng":"implication","kk":"ˌɪmplɪˈkeɪʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"暗示\"  ],  [    \"含義\"  ],  [    \"牽連\"  ],  [    \"牽涉\"  ]]","chEntries":["暗示","含義","牽連","牽涉"],"practiceMeaning":"他言語的含義很清楚。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 implicatiōnem，是動詞 implicare「捲入、包含」的名詞化。implicare 由 in- (in, into) + plicare (to fold) 組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 in-「進入」和 plicare「折疊、捲入」是其核心語意來源。作為名詞，其核心語義是由動詞 implicate「暗示、牽連」名詞化而來，指「間接表達的意義」或「某事所涉及或牽連的範圍」。詞源中的「折疊、捲入」引申為「隱藏、暗示」和「牽連、涉及」。","definition":"1. the conclusion that can be drawn from something, although it is not directly stated; 2. the involvement of someone or something in a crime or other         wrongdoing; 3. a likely consequence or effect of an action or situation.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The implication of his words was clear.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他言語的含義很清楚。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The implication of the new policy on employment is uncertain.\",\n    \"ch\": \"新政策對就業的影響尚不確定。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His implication in the scandal damaged his reputation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在此醜聞中的牽連損害了他的聲譽。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The results have important implications for future research.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這些結果對未來的研究具有重要的含義。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他言語的含義很清楚。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6176,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::incentive::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Higher wages provide a strong ____ for workers.","expectedAnswer":"incentive","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Higher wages provide a strong ____ for workers.","clozeAnswer":"incentive","exampleTranslation":"更高的工資為工人提供了強烈的誘因。","reference":{"eng":"incentive","kk":"ɪnˈsɛntɪv","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"刺激\"  ],  [    \"誘因\"  ],  [    \"動機\"  ]]","chEntries":["刺激","誘因","動機"],"practiceMeaning":"更高的工資為工人提供了強烈的誘因。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 incentivum，是動詞 incendere「點燃、激勵」的中性過去分詞，引申為「激勵因素」。incendere 由 in- (in, into) + candēre (to burn, glow) 組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 in-「進入」和 candēre「燃燒」是其核心語意來源。作為名詞，其核心語義是「促使某人做某事的東西」，即「刺激」或「誘因」。詞源中的「點燃」概念引申為「激發、促使」的動力。","definition":"1. a thing that motivates or encourages one to do something; 2. a payment or other consideration by which one is influenced.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Higher wages provide a strong incentive for workers.\",\n    \"ch\": \"更高的工資為工人提供了強烈的誘因。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government offered tax incentives for new businesses.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府提供了稅收優惠來鼓勵新企業。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"What is your incentive for taking this job?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你從事這份工作的動機是什麼？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The bonus served as an incentive to work harder.\",\n    \"ch\": \"獎金起到了激勵更努力工作的誘因作用。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"更高的工資為工人提供了強烈的誘因。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6228,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::inevitable::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Change is ____ in life.","expectedAnswer":"inevitable","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Change is ____ in life.","clozeAnswer":"inevitable","exampleTranslation":"改變在生活中是不可避免的。","reference":{"eng":"inevitable","kk":"ɪnˈɛvɪtəbl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"不可避免的\"  ],  [    \"必然的\"  ],  [    \"注定的\"  ]]","chEntries":["不可避免的","必然的","注定的"],"practiceMeaning":"改變在生活中是不可避免的。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 inevitabilis，由 in-（否定）和 evadere（逃脫）構成，意為「不能逃脫的」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作形容詞時，指某種情況或結果是無法避免的，必然會發生。中文翻譯為「不可避免的；必然的；注定的」。","definition":"certain to happen; unavoidable.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Change is inevitable in life.\",\n    \"ch\": \"改變在生活中是不可避免的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Given the circumstances, the outcome was inevitable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"鑑於當時的情況，這個結果是必然的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Their success seemed inevitable from the start.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們的成功從一開始似乎就已注定。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"改變在生活中是不可避免的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5088,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::infinite::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The universe is thought to be ____.","expectedAnswer":"infinite","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The universe is thought to be ____.","clozeAnswer":"infinite","exampleTranslation":"宇宙被認為是無限的。","reference":{"eng":"infinite","kk":"ˈɪnfɪnət","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['無限的'], ['無窮的'], ['極大的']]","chEntries":["無限的","無窮的","極大的"],"practiceMeaning":"宇宙被認為是無限的。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'in-' (not) + 'finitus' (bounded, finite)，原意為 '無邊界的、無窮的'。'Infinite' 的核心語義是 '沒有盡頭、沒有限制'。這可以指空間上的無限，時間上的無限，數量的無限，也可以指品質上的極致，如 'infinite patience' (極大的耐心)，強調其程度之深，幾乎沒有極限。","definition":"1. Limitless or endless in space, extent, or size; impossible to measure or calculate.; 2. Extremely large or great, especially in scope or ability.; 3. (Of a mathematical quantity) larger than any assignable quantity or number.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The universe is thought to be infinite.\",\n    \"ch\": \"宇宙被認為是無限的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has infinite patience with the children.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對孩子們有無限的耐心。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The possibilities are infinite.\",\n    \"ch\": \"可能性是無限的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"宇宙被認為是無限的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4164,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::insignificant::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His contribution was ____.","expectedAnswer":"insignificant","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His contribution was ____.","clozeAnswer":"insignificant","exampleTranslation":"他的貢獻微不足道。","reference":{"eng":"insignificant","kk":"/ˌɪnsɪɡˈnɪfɪkənt/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['微不足道的', '無關緊要的']]","chEntries":["微不足道的","無關緊要的"],"practiceMeaning":"他的貢獻微不足道。","analysis":"由 in-（否定前綴）+ significant（重要的）組成。核心概念是「不重要的」、「缺乏意義」。","definition":"1. too small or unimportant to be worth consideration; 2. not significant; trivial","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His contribution was insignificant.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的貢獻微不足道。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The difference between the two amounts is insignificant.\",\n    \"ch\": \"兩個數額之間的差異微乎其微。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We shouldn't waste time on insignificant details.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們不應該在無關緊要的細節上浪費時間。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他的貢獻微不足道。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3174,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::intuition::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She had a strong ____ that something was wrong.","expectedAnswer":"intuition","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She had a strong ____ that something was wrong.","clozeAnswer":"intuition","exampleTranslation":"她強烈的直覺告訴她，有什麼事情不對勁。","reference":{"eng":"intuition","kk":"/ˌɪntuˈɪʃn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['直覺；直覺力']]","chEntries":["直覺","直覺力"],"practiceMeaning":"她強烈的直覺告訴她，有什麼事情不對勁。","analysis":"詞源來自拉丁語 'intueri'，意為「看，觀察」。'Intuition' 指的是一種直接的、非理性或非邏輯的理解或知識，無需經過明顯的推理過程就能獲得。它是一種內在的感知或「預感」，通常基於潛意識的經驗或感受。","definition":"the ability to understand something immediately, without the need for conscious reasoning.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She had a strong intuition that something was wrong.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她強烈的直覺告訴她，有什麼事情不對勁。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Trust your intuition when making important decisions.\",\n    \"ch\": \"做重要決定時，相信你的直覺。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His intuition about the market proved to be correct.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對市場的直覺被證明是正確的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她強烈的直覺告訴她，有什麼事情不對勁。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5385,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l2::issue::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company will ____ new shares next month.","expectedAnswer":"issue","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company will ____ new shares next month.","clozeAnswer":"issue","exampleTranslation":"該公司將於下月發行新股。","reference":{"eng":"issue","kk":"ˈɪʃuː","tense":"v.","ch":"[['發行'], ['發布'], ['提出'], ['造成', '引起']]","chEntries":["發行","發布","提出","造成","引起"],"practiceMeaning":"該公司將於下月發行新股。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 escuë (出去、發出)，來自拉丁語 exire (出來)。核心語意是「使某物出、發出」。因此，'issue' 作動詞時，可指「正式地發布或發行」（如出版物、貨幣），「提出或討論」（如議題），或「造成、引起」（如問題、狀況）。","definition":"1. supply or distribute (something); 2. originate or stem from; 3. produce or release.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company will issue new shares next month.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司將於下月發行新股。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The policy will issue from the ministry.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這項政策將由該部發布。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該公司將於下月發行新股。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4725,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::jazz::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He is a big fan of ____ music.","expectedAnswer":"jazz","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He is a big fan of ____ music.","clozeAnswer":"jazz","exampleTranslation":"他是爵士樂的忠實粉絲。","reference":{"eng":"jazz","kk":"/ˈdʒæz/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['爵士樂'], ['（非正式）胡鬧；大驚小怪'], ['（非正式）狀況；把事情搞砸']]","chEntries":["爵士樂","胡鬧","大驚小怪","狀況","把事情搞砸"],"practiceMeaning":"他是爵士樂的忠實粉絲。","analysis":"詞源不明，可能源於20世紀初美國非裔社群的口語。最初用於指音樂風格，後引申出「弄亂」、「搞砸」或「大驚小怪」的非正式用法。","definition":"1. A genre of music that originated in African-American communities in the United States in the late 19th and early 20th centuries. 2. (informal) Nonsense; fuss. 3. (informal) A situation, especially one that has been spoiled or confused.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a big fan of jazz music.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是爵士樂的忠實粉絲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Don't jazz things up too much; keep it simple.\",\n    \"ch\": \"別把事情搞得太複雜；保持簡單。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He really jazzed up the presentation with visuals.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他用視覺效果把簡報弄得活色生香。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他是爵士樂的忠實粉絲。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4249,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::junior::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He is a ____ partner in the law firm.","expectedAnswer":"junior","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He is a ____ partner in the law firm.","clozeAnswer":"junior","exampleTranslation":"他是這家律師事務所的資淺合夥人。","reference":{"eng":"junior","kk":"/ˈdʒuːnjər/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['資淺的'], ['低年級的'], ['年幼的']]","chEntries":["資淺的","低年級的","年幼的"],"practiceMeaning":"他是這家律師事務所的資淺合夥人。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'iunior'，比較級形式，意為「更年輕的」。'Junior' 在用法上多用於比較，表示在年齡、職位或學業上的較低層級。","definition":"lower in rank or shorter in length of service; younger","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a junior partner in the law firm.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是這家律師事務所的資淺合夥人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The junior high school has students from grades 7 to 9.\",\n    \"ch\": \"初中部有七到九年級的學生。\"\n  }\n]","exam