ue ____ very relaxing.","expectedAnswer":"massage","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She found a deep tissue ____ very relaxing.","clozeAnswer":"massage","exampleTranslation":"她覺得深層組織按摩非常放鬆。","reference":{"eng":"massage","kk":"məˈsɑʒ","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"按摩\"  ],  [    \"撫摩\"  ]]","chEntries":["按摩","撫摩"],"practiceMeaning":"她覺得深層組織按摩非常放鬆。","analysis":"此字源自法語 massage，本身來自 provencal masa（to knead），追溯至希臘語 massein（to knead）。核心語義是「揉捏」或「按壓」。作為名詞，指一種通過手技（揉、捏、拍打等）來放鬆肌肉、緩解疼痛或促進血液循環的治療或放鬆方法。","definition":"an act of rubbing and kneading the body with the hands, especially to relieve tension or pain.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She found a deep tissue massage very relaxing.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她覺得深層組織按摩非常放鬆。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The sports massage helped relieve his muscle soreness.\",\n    \"ch\": \"運動按摩幫助緩解了他的肌肉痠痛。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A regular massage can improve circulation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"定期的按摩可以改善血液循環。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她覺得深層組織按摩非常放鬆。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5573,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::massive::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They live in a ____ house in the countryside.","expectedAnswer":"massive","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They live in a ____ house in the countryside.","clozeAnswer":"massive","exampleTranslation":"他們住在鄉間一棟巨大的房子裡。","reference":{"eng":"massive","kk":"ˈmæsɪv","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['巨大的'], ['大規模的'], ['沉重的'], ['大量的']]","chEntries":["巨大的","大規模的","沉重的","大量的"],"practiceMeaning":"他們住在鄉間一棟巨大的房子裡。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 \"massīvus\"，意為 \"solid, dense\"（固態的，密集的），來自 \"massa\"（mass, lump，團塊，塊狀物）。\"massa\" 的語義是「未經分割的、大塊的物質」。因此，\"massive\" 的核心語義是「像一個大塊物體一樣，巨大、厚重、密集」。它強調的是規模、體積或重量上的龐大。它可以形容物理上的尺寸（e.g., massive building），也可以形容抽象上的數量或影響力（e.g., massive impact）。","definition":"1. Large and heavy or solid; 2. Large in scale or extent; 3. Very large in amount or degree.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They live in a massive house in the countryside.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們住在鄉間一棟巨大的房子裡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The project required massive amounts of funding.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個計畫需要巨額的資金。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company experienced massive layoffs.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司進行了大規模裁員。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們住在鄉間一棟巨大的房子裡。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4158,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::materials::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need to buy building ____.","expectedAnswer":"materials","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need to buy building ____.","clozeAnswer":"materials","exampleTranslation":"我們需要購買建築材料。","reference":{"eng":"materials","kk":"/məˈtɪəriəlz/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['材料', '物資']]","chEntries":["材料","物資"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要購買建築材料。","analysis":"由 material（物質的，材料）的複數形式。來自拉丁語 materialis（物質的）。核心概念是「構成某物的東西」。","definition":"things such as physical objects and substances that are needed for the particular activity or purpose you are referring to","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to buy building materials.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要購買建築材料。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The relief materials included food and medicine.\",\n    \"ch\": \"救濟物資包括食物和藥品。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The artist uses various materials in his work.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位藝術家在他的作品中使用各種材料。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要購買建築材料。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3097,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::maximum::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of the function is 100.","expectedAnswer":"maximum","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of the function is 100.","clozeAnswer":"maximum","exampleTranslation":"該函數的最大值是100。","reference":{"eng":"maximum","kk":"/ˈmæksɪməm/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['最大數量；最大值'], ['最高限度']]","chEntries":["最大數量","最大值","最高限度"],"practiceMeaning":"該函數的最大值是100。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'maximus' (greatest)。是形容詞 'maximum' 的名詞形式。指「最大的數量」或「最高的程度」。\n1. 最大數量；最大值：指某個變數或集合中的最大數值。\n2. 最高限度：指為了達到某種標準或要求所允許的最高條件。","definition":"1. the greatest amount or degree allowed or possible; 2. the highest limit.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The maximum of the function is 100.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該函數的最大值是100。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There is a maximum of two pieces of luggage per person.\",\n    \"ch\": \"每人最多允許攜帶兩件行李。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該函數的最大值是100。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39、U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4606,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::meaningful::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He gave a ____ speech that inspired many.","expectedAnswer":"meaningful","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He gave a ____ speech that inspired many.","clozeAnswer":"meaningful","exampleTranslation":"他做了一場意味深長的演講，激勵了許多人。","reference":{"eng":"meaningful","kk":"/ˈmiːnɪŋfəl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['有意義的'], ['意味深長的'], ['有目的的']]","chEntries":["有意義的","意味深長的","有目的的"],"practiceMeaning":"他做了一場意味深長的演講，激勵了許多人。","analysis":"由 'meaning' (意義) + '-ful' (充滿) 組成。'Meaning' 源自古英語 'mænan' (意指、表達)，與 'mean' (意圖) 同源。'-ful' 是表示「充滿」或「具有」的後綴。此字指事物具有重要的價值、目的或深刻的內涵，能夠引起情感共鳴或啟發思考。","definition":"having or conveying a serious emotion, importance, or purpose.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He gave a meaningful speech that inspired many.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他做了一場意味深長的演講，激勵了許多人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was a meaningful gesture of friendship.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是友誼的充滿意義的表示。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She sought a more meaningful career.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她尋求一份更有意義的職業。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他做了一場意味深長的演講，激勵了許多人。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5662,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l8::measure::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Please ____ the length of the table.","expectedAnswer":"measure","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Please ____ the length of the table.","clozeAnswer":"measure","exampleTranslation":"請測量桌子的長度。","reference":{"eng":"measure","kk":"ˈmɛʒər","tense":"v.","ch":"[['測量'], ['衡量'], ['評估'], ['（法律、規定等）措施']]","chEntries":["測量","衡量","評估","措施"],"practiceMeaning":"請測量桌子的長度。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 mesure，來自古法語 mesure，再追溯至拉丁語 mensura（測量），來自 mensus（測量），是 mētiri（測量，to measure）的過去分詞。mētiri 來自原始印歐語 *meh₁-（測量）。核心語義為「確定尺寸、數量或程度」。構詞上，mētiri 提供「測量」的核心動作，-ure 是常見的名詞字尾，此處轉換為動詞用法。此處為動詞用法，表示「進行測量」、「估算」、「考慮」或「採取措施」。","definition":"to ascertain the size, amount, or degree of something; to assess or evaluate; to take action to achieve a particular aim.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please measure the length of the table.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請測量桌子的長度。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to measure our progress carefully.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要仔細衡量我們的進展。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government has taken measures to control inflation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府已採取措施控制通貨膨脹。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"請測量桌子的長度。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6083,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::mechanism::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of the clock needs to be repaired.","expectedAnswer":"mechanism","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of the clock needs to be repaired.","clozeAnswer":"mechanism","exampleTranslation":"這台鐘表的機械裝置需要修理。","reference":{"eng":"mechanism","kk":"ˈmɛkəˌnɪzəm","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"機制\"  ],  [    \"機械裝置\"  ],  [    \"構造\"  ],  [    \"原理\"  ]]","chEntries":["機制","機械裝置","構造","原理"],"practiceMeaning":"這台鐘表的機械裝置需要修理。","analysis":"此字源自希臘語 mēkhanḗ（machine, device, means），來自 mēkhanos（inventive, clever）。核心語義是「機器」或「裝置」。引申為「機制」，指某事物運作的方式、過程或內部結構，尤其是指一套相互關聯的組成部分如何協同工作以達成某種結果。","definition":"1. a system of parts working together in a machine; 2. a natural or physical process considered in terms of the way in which it operates; 3. a way of achieving something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The mechanism of the clock needs to be repaired.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這台鐘表的機械裝置需要修理。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to understand the mechanism of disease transmission.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要了解疾病傳播的機制。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a simple mechanism to open the bottle.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個開啟瓶子的簡單裝置。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這台鐘表的機械裝置需要修理。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5554,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::merely::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He was ____ trying to help.","expectedAnswer":"merely","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He was ____ trying to help.","clozeAnswer":"merely","exampleTranslation":"他只是想幫忙。","reference":{"eng":"merely","kk":"ˈmɪrli","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['僅僅'], ['只是'], ['不過是']]","chEntries":["僅僅","只是","不過是"],"practiceMeaning":"他只是想幫忙。","analysis":"此字是 \"mere\"（僅僅的）加上副詞字尾 \"-ly\" 構成。\"mere\" 源自古英語 \"mǣre\"，意為 \"boundary, limit, distinguished\"（界線，極限，傑出的），後來語義演變為 \"nothing more than, only\"（僅僅是，不過是），可能與「極小」或「單一」的概念有關。因此，\"merely\" 作為副詞，強調「僅僅」、「只是」的意思，表示所敘述的事物或情況是有限的、微不足道的，或者沒有其他更重要的內容。","definition":"1. Just only; solely; 2. In the smallest degree; only.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was merely trying to help.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他只是想幫忙。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was merely a suggestion, not an order.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這只是一個建議，並非命令。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is not merely a singer, but also a talented actress.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她不只是個歌手，更是一位才華洋溢的演員。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他只是想幫忙。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4679,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::mess::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The room was a complete ____ after the party.","expectedAnswer":"mess","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The room was a complete ____ after the party.","clozeAnswer":"mess","exampleTranslation":"派對結束後，房間一片狼藉。","reference":{"e