ent's vital signs.","expectedAnswer":"monitor","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The nurse will ____ the patient's vital signs.","clozeAnswer":"monitor","exampleTranslation":"護士將監測病人的生命體徵。","reference":{"eng":"monitor","kk":"/ˈmɑːnɪtər/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['監控；監視'], ['（定期）檢查；跟蹤']]","chEntries":["監控","監視","檢查","跟蹤"],"practiceMeaning":"護士將監測病人的生命體徵。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'monitor' (one who warns)，'monere' (to warn, remind)。核心意義是「提醒」或「觀察」。\n1. 監控；監視：指持續觀察、記錄或控制某人或某事的行為或進展。\n2. （定期）檢查；跟蹤：指定期檢查某事物的狀態或進展，以確保其按計劃進行。","definition":"1. to watch and check something or someone over a period of time; 2. to observe and keep a record of the progress or development of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The nurse will monitor the patient's vital signs.\",\n    \"ch\": \"護士將監測病人的生命體徵。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to monitor the situation closely.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要密切關注事態發展。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"護士將監測病人的生命體徵。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5050,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::nasty::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The weather was ____ and cold.","expectedAnswer":"nasty","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The weather was ____ and cold.","clozeAnswer":"nasty","exampleTranslation":"天氣惡劣又寒冷。","reference":{"eng":"nasty","kk":"ˈnæsti","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['惡劣的'], ['討厭的'], ['骯髒的'], ['惡意的'], ['嚴重的（疾病、傷口）']]","chEntries":["惡劣的","討厭的","骯髒的","惡意的","嚴重的"],"practiceMeaning":"天氣惡劣又寒冷。","analysis":"此字源自古英語næhtigr，可能與 neah（靠近）有關，語意演變為「令人厭惡的」。其核心語意是「令人不快、討厭、危險」，可指事物、人、情況或行為。其範圍廣泛，從「骯髒、粗俗」到「惡意的、嚴重的」。OCR 掃描時可能將 'n' 誤判為 'm'。此處修正為 nasty。","definition":"1. very bad or unpleasant; 2. cruel and malicious; 3. (of an illness or injury) severe.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The weather was nasty and cold.\",\n    \"ch\": \"天氣惡劣又寒冷。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He made a nasty remark about her appearance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對她的外貌說了句惡意的話。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a nasty cut on 