」。引申義則指「極受尊敬的」、「神聖不可侵犯的」，用於形容珍貴的事物或權利。","definition":"1. Connected with God or a god or a religious purpose.; 2. Regarded with great respect and affection.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a sacred site for many religions.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是許多宗教的神聖之地。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They believed the river was sacred.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們相信這條河是神聖的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Freedom of speech is a sacred right.\",\n    \"ch\": \"言論自由是一項神聖的權利。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The ancient temple was considered sacred.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座古老的神廟被認為是神聖的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是許多宗教的神聖之地。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4145,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::salary::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Her annual ____ is $50,000.","expectedAnswer":"salary","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Her annual ____ is $50,000.","clozeAnswer":"salary","exampleTranslation":"她的年薪是五萬美元。","reference":{"eng":"salary","kk":"/ˈsæləri/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['薪水', '薪金']]","chEntries":["薪水","薪金"],"practiceMeaning":"她的年薪是五萬美元。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 salarium（羅馬士兵領取的食鹽津貼），後引申為「報酬」。核心概念是「為工作定期支付的固定金錢」。","definition":"a fixed regular payment, typically paid on a monthly or biweekly basis but often expressed as an annual sum, made by an employer to an employee","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her annual salary is $50,000.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的年薪是五萬美元。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company offers a competitive salary.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司提供有競爭力的薪資。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He negotiated a higher salary.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他談判爭取到了更高的薪水。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她的年薪是五萬美元。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U5、L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5859,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::salon::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She went to the ____ to get her hair done.","expectedAnswer":"salon","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She went to the ____ to get her hair done.","clozeAnswer":"salon","exampleTranslation":"她去沙龍做頭髮。","reference":{"eng":"salon","kk":"səˈlɑːn","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"沙龍\"  ],  [    \"美容院\"  ],  [    \"客廳\"  ],  [    \"陳列室\"  ]]","chEntries":["沙龍","美容院","客廳","陳列室"],"practiceMeaning":"她去沙龍做頭髮。","analysis":"此字源自法語 'salon'，原意為「大廳」、「接待室」，由 'salle' (hall) 演變而來，'salle' 源自拉丁語 'sal' (salt)，或有說源自'sala' (room)，表示「主要房間」。'Salon' 在18世紀法國興起，指「名流聚集的客廳」，成為文化交流的場所。現代語義擴展至「美容院」或「髮廊」，指提供美容、美髮服務的專業場所，這些場所也常被設計成舒適、有格調的空間，如同昔日的社交沙龍。例如，也可指「藝術品陳列室」。","definition":"1. A large room in a private house or hotel, especially one used for entertaining guests.; 2. A fashionable beauty salon or hairdressing establishment.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She went to the salon to get her hair done.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她去沙龍做頭髮。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The salon hosted a gathering of artists.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個沙龍舉辦了一場藝術家聚會。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He opened a new beauty salon.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他開了一家新的美容院。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The art salon exhibited works by local painters.\",\n    \"ch\": \"藝術沙龍展出了本地畫家的作品。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她去沙龍做頭髮。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5488,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::sample::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The lab technicians will ____ the water quality.","expectedAnswer":"sample","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The lab technicians will ____ the water quality.","clozeAnswer":"sample","exampleTranslation":"實驗室技術人員將對水質進行採樣。","reference":{"eng":"sample","kk":"ˈsæmpəl","tense":"v.","ch":"[['採樣'], ['試吃'], ['取樣']]","chEntries":["採樣","試吃","取樣"],"practiceMeaning":"實驗室技術人員將對水質進行採樣。","analysis":"此字由名詞 'sample'（樣本）派生。作為動詞，'sample' 的意思是「抽取樣本」、「採集樣本」或「試吃/試用樣本」。它強調的是「獲取一個代表性部分以便進行檢測、展示或品嚐」的行為。核心語意是「以樣本形式獲取」。","definition":"1. Obtain a sample of (a substance, product, or other material) for examination.; 2. Try or taste a sample of.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The lab technicians will sample the water quality.\",\n    \"ch\": \"實驗室技術人員將對水質進行採樣。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We sampled several wines at the vineyard.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們在葡萄園裡品嚐了幾款葡萄酒。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company samples its products to potential customers.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司向潛在客戶提供產品樣品。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"實驗室技術人員將對水質進行採樣。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5579,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::scheme::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They have a ____ to reduce costs.","expectedAnswer":"scheme","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They have a ____ to reduce costs.","clozeAnswer":"scheme","exampleTranslation":"他們有一個削減成本的計畫。","reference":{"eng":"scheme","kk":"skim","tense":"n.","ch":"[['計畫'], ['方案'], ['陰謀'], ['體系']]","chEntries":["計畫","方案","陰謀","體系"],"practiceMeaning":"他們有一個削減成本的計畫。","analysis":"此字源自古希臘語 \"schēma\"（shape, form, appearance, plan，形狀，形式，外觀，計畫），該詞源於 \"echō\"（to have, to hold，擁有，持有）。\"schēma\" 的核心語義是「事物的形式或架構」。在中古英語中，\"scheme\"（原為 \"sceme\"）借用於古法語 \"esqueme\"，繼承了希臘語的「形式、架構」概念。它的語義發展廣泛：指「一個有組織的、事先計畫好的行動藍圖」（a plan or program of action）；指「一個系統或結構」（a system or framework）；也可能帶有負面含義，指「一個秘密的、不誠實的計畫」（a secret plot or conspiracy）。","definition":"1. A plan or program of action; 2. A system of rules, principles, or methods; 3. A secret plan made by a group of people to do something illegal or harmful.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They have a scheme to reduce costs.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們有一個削減成本的計畫。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government introduced a new housing scheme.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府推出了一個新的住房方案。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was involved in a criminal scheme.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他捲入了一個犯罪陰謀。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們有一個削減成本的計畫。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6091,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::scrap::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He found a ____ of paper with a phone number on it.","expectedAnswer":"scrap","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He found a ____ of paper with a phone number on it.","clozeAnswer":"scrap","exampleTranslation":"他找到一張寫著電話號碼的紙條。","reference":{"eng":"scrap","kk":"skræp","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"碎片\"  ],  [    \"零星的\"  ],  [    \"廢料\"  ],  [    \"報廢品\"  ],  [    \"（信息、數據）片段\"  ]]","chEntries":["碎片","零星的","廢料","報廢品","片段"],"practiceMeaning":"他找到一張寫著電話號碼的紙條。","analysis":"此字的詞源不確定，可能源自古斯堪地那維亞語 skrap，意為「剩餘物」。核心語義是「小的、零散的、無用的部分」。引申為「廢料」、「報廢品」，或「零星的、不完整的片段」。","definition":"1. a small piece or amount of something, especially one that is left over after the greater part has been used or finished; 2. discarded material or refuse.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He found a scrap of paper with a phone number on it.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他找到一張寫著電話號碼的紙條。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The car was too damaged to repair and was sent for scrap.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這輛車損壞嚴重無法修復，被送去報廢了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The report was compiled from various scraps of information.\",\n    \"ch\": \"報告是從各種零散的信息片段匯編而成的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他找到一張寫著電話號碼的紙條。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6093,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::script::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The actors rehearsed their lines from the ____.","expectedAnswer":"script","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The actors rehearsed their lines from the ____.","clozeAnswer":"script","exampleTranslation":"演員們根據劇本排練台詞。","reference":{"eng":"script","kk":"skrɪpt","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"劇本\"  ],  [    \"腳本\"  ],  [    \"手稿\"  ],  [    \"（電腦）腳本\"  ],  [    \"字跡\"  ]]","chEntries":["劇本","腳本","手稿","字跡"],"practiceMeaning":"演員們根據劇本排練台詞。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 scriptum（something written），是 scribere（to write）的過去分詞。核心語義是「寫下來的東西」。在戲劇、電影、廣播等領域，script 指演員的「劇本」或「腳本」。在電腦領域，script 指一組用於自動執行任務的指令「腳本」。也可用於指「手稿」或「字跡」。","definition":"1. the written text of a play, film, or broadcast; 2. a set of instructions that a computer can follow; 3. handwriting.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The actors rehearsed their lines from the script.\",\n    \"ch\": \"演員們根據劇本排練台詞。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The web developer wrote a JavaScript script.\",\n    \"ch\": \"網頁開發者寫了一個 JavaScript 腳本。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The manuscript was written in a difficult-to-read script.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這份手稿是用一種難以辨認的字跡寫成的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"演員們根據劇本排練台詞。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6095,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::seminar::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We attended an interesting ____ on climate change.","expectedAnswer":"seminar","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We attended an interesting ____ on climate change.","clozeAnswer":"seminar","exampleTranslation":"我們參加了一個關於氣候變遷的有趣研討會。","reference":{"eng":"seminar","kk":"ˈsɛmɪnɑr","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"研討會\"  ],  [    \"講座\"  ],  [    \"討論會\"  ]]","chEntries":["研討會","講座","討論會"],"practiceMeaning":"我們參加了一個關於氣候變遷的有趣研討會。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 seminarium，意為「種子田」，來自 semen（seed）。核心語義是「播種」，引申為知識、思想的「播種」或傳播之地。在學術語境中，seminar 指一種小型的、通常由專家主持的、參與者進行深入討論或學習的會議。","definition":"a meeting for discussion or exchange of information on a particular subject.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We attended an interesting seminar on climate change.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們參加了一個關於氣候變遷的有趣研討會。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The professor is leading a seminar for graduate students.\",\n    \"ch\": \"教授正在主持一個研究生研討會。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She gave a presentation at the international seminar.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在國際研討會上做了一個報告。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們參加了一個關於氣候變遷的有趣研討會。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4265,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::senior::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He is a ____ engineer with over 20 years of experience.","expectedAnswer":"senior","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He is a ____ engineer with over 20 years of experience.","clozeAnswer":"senior","exampleTranslation":"他是一位擁有超過20年經驗的資深工程師。","reference":{"eng":"senior","kk":"/ˈsiːnjər/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['資深的'], ['高年級的'], ['年長的']]","chEntries":["資深的","高年級的","年長的"],"practiceMeaning":"他是一位擁有超過20年經驗的資深工程師。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'senior'，比較級形式，意為「更年長的」。'Senior' 在用法上多用於比較，表示在年齡、職位或學業上的較高層級。與 'junior' 相對。","definition":"older; having a higher rank or longer period of service.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a senior engineer with over 20 years of experience.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一位擁有超過20年經驗的資深工程師。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The college offers programs for both junior and senior students.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這所大學提供給大學部低年級和高年級學生的課程。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他是一位擁有超過20年經驗的資深工程師。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5860,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::sensation::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The news caused a ____.","expectedAnswer":"sensation","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The news caused a ____.","clozeAnswer":"sensation","exampleTranslation":"這消息引起了轟動。","reference":{"eng":"sensation","kk":"senˈseɪʃn","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"感覺\"  ],  [    \"知覺\"  ],  [    \"轟動\"  ],  [    \"感動\"  ],  [    \"感覺器官\"  ]]","chEntries":["感覺","知覺","轟動","感動","感覺器官"],"practiceMeaning":"這消息引起了轟動。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'sensus' (feeling, sense)，是 'sentire' (to feel) 的名詞形式。'Sensation' 的核心語意是指「通過感官獲得的感覺」或「對刺激的反應」。在更廣泛的語境中，它也可以指「引起強烈興趣或興奮的事件」，即「轟動」或「激動人心的事物」。這種語意轉移是由於強烈的感覺往往伴隨著興奮或情感的波動。例如，也可指「一種感覺器官」。","definition":"1. A physical feeling or perception resulting from a stimulus.; 2. An ability to feel, perceive, or experience objects, quality, and actions through the senses.; 3. An event or situation that causes great public interest and excitement.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The news caused a sensation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這消息引起了轟動。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He lost all sensation in his legs.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他失去雙腿的所有感覺。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The new invention was a sensation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這項新發明引起了轟動。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Touch is one of the five basic sensations.\",\n    \"ch\": \"觸覺是五種基本感覺之一。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這消息引起了轟動。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4700,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::separation::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of the two elements was difficult.","expectedAnswer":"separation","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of the two elements was difficult.","clozeAnswer":"separation","exampleTranslation":"這兩種元素的 the separation 過程很困難。","reference":{"eng":"separation","kk":"/ˌsɛpəˈreɪʃən/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['分離'], ['分居'], ['（科學）分離，（化學）分餾']]","chEntries":["分離","分居","分離，分餾"],"practiceMeaning":"這兩種元素的 the separation 過程很困難。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 *separatio*，由 *separare*（分開）演變而來。核心是將事物或個體分開的狀態或過程。引申至人際關係的分居，以及科學上將不同物質或成分分開的技術。","definition":"1. The state of being separated or divided. 2. The act of ending a marriage or relationship. 3. The process of dividing substances or components.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The separation of the two elements was difficult.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這兩種元素的 the separation 過程很困難。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They have been living in separation for a year.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們已經分居一年了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The separation of milk into cream and skimmed milk is a common process.\",\n    \"ch\": \"牛奶分離成鮮奶油和脫脂牛奶是一個常見的過程。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這兩種元素的 the separation 過程很困難。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5061,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::sequence::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of events was unclear.","expectedAnswer":"sequence","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of events was unclear.","clozeAnswer":"sequence","exampleTranslation":"事件的順序不清楚。","reference":{"eng":"sequence","kk":"ˈsiːkwəns","tense":"n.","ch":"[['序列'], ['順序'], ['連續發生的事情']]","chEntries":["序列","順序","連續發生的事情"],"practiceMeaning":"事件的順序不清楚。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語sequentia，是動詞sequi（跟隨）的派生詞。sequi 又來自原始印歐語 *sekʷ-（跟隨）。sequence 的核心語意是「事物按照特定順序排列或接續」，強調的是「先後關係」或「連續性」。OCR 掃描時可能將 's' 誤判為 '5'，或 'q' 誤判為 'g'。此處修正為 sequence。","definition":"1. a set of related events, movements, or things that follow each other in a particular order; 2. a continuous series of events.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The sequence of events was unclear.\",\n    \"ch\": \"事件的順序不清楚。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He learned the dance steps in sequence.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他按順序學會了舞蹈動作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is the first sequence in the film.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是電影的第一個鏡頭（連續畫面）。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"事件的順序不清楚。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6138,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::server::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The website is down because the ____ is overloaded.","expectedAnswer":"server","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The website is down because the ____ is overloaded.","clozeAnswer":"server","exampleTranslation":"網站無法訪問，因為伺服器過載了。","reference":{"eng":"server","kk":"ˈsɜːrvər","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"伺服器\"  ],  [    \"服務員\"  ],  [    \"侍者\"  ]]","chEntries":["伺服器","服務員","侍者"],"practiceMeaning":"網站無法訪問，因為伺服器過載了。","analysis":"此字由動詞 serve（服務）加上名詞後綴 -er（表示施事者或工具）構成。serve 源自拉丁語 servīre（服務；服從），來自 servus（奴隸）。因此，server 的核心語義是「提供服務者」。在電腦領域，指提供數據、資源或服務的電腦系統（伺服器）。在餐飲業，指提供服務的人（服務員，侍者）。其語意演變是從「服務者」到具體的「伺服器」和「服務員」。","definition":"1. a computer or computer program that manages access to a centralized resource or service; 2. a person who serves food or drinks in a restaurant or bar.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The website is down because the server is overloaded.\",\n    \"ch\": \"網站無法訪問，因為伺服器過載了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The waiter, or server, took our order.\",\n    \"ch\": \"服務員，也就是侍者，為我們點餐。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The database server stores all the user information.\",\n    \"ch\": \"資料庫伺服器儲存了所有使用者資訊。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"網站無法訪問，因為伺服器過載了。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4337,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::shadow::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The tree cast a long ____.","expectedAnswer":"shadow","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The tree cast a long ____.","clozeAnswer":"shadow","exampleTranslation":"這棵樹投下了一道長長的影子。","reference":{"eng":"shadow","kk":"/ˈʃædoʊ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['陰影；影子'], ['（光線被遮擋形成的）暗區'], ['（對某事物的）影響；不安；沮喪'], ['鬼魂；幽靈']]","chEntries":["陰影","影子","暗區","影響","不安","沮喪","鬼魂","幽靈"],"practiceMeaning":"這棵樹投下了一道長長的影子。","analysis":"源自古英語 'sceadwa'，與『遮蔽』、『陰影』相關。1. 光線被物體遮擋而形成的『影子』。2. 物理空間上的『陰影、暗區』。3. 作為比喻，指事物『受到的影響』，可以是負面的，如『不安、沮喪』，或是一個長期存在、難以擺脫的『陰影』。4. 在文學或宗教語境中，指『鬼魂、幽靈』，即沒有實體的影子。","definition":"an area of darkness where light is blocked by an object; a dark area or shape that is produced when an object is between a light source and a surface; an unpleasant feeling that spoils something; the ghost of a dead person","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The tree cast a long shadow.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這棵樹投下了一道長長的影子。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He walked in the shadow of the building.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他走在建築物的陰影裡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The war left a shadow over the country's future.\",\n    \"ch\": \"戰爭給國家的未來蒙上了陰影。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The ghost appeared as a shadowy figure.\",\n    \"ch\": \"鬼魂出現時，像一個模糊的影子。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這棵樹投下了一道長長的影子。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6140,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::sheer::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ joy filled the room.","expectedAnswer":"Sheer","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ joy filled the room.","clozeAnswer":"Sheer","exampleTranslation":"純粹的喜悅充滿了房間。","reference":{"eng":"sheer","kk":"ʃɪr","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"純粹的\"  ],  [    \"徹底的\"  ],  [    \"極度的\"  ],  [    \"陡峭的\"  ],  [    \"透明的\"  ]]","chEntries":["純粹的","徹底的","極度的","陡峭的","透明的"],"practiceMeaning":"純粹的喜悅充滿了房間。","analysis":"此字詞源不確定，可能源自古英語 scīr（純淨的，清澈的）或中古英語 sheer（陡峭的）。modern 用法包含「純粹的、徹底的、極度的」以及「陡峭的、險峻的」。前者語意演變是從「純淨」到「無混雜」，後者則是「垂直的」。","definition":"1. nothing other than; unmitigated; 2. steep or vertical; 3. (of fabric) thin and transparent.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Sheer joy filled the room.\",\n    \"ch\": \"純粹的喜悅充滿了房間。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The cliff was sheer.\",\n    \"ch\": \"懸崖很陡峭。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Sheer determination helped her succeed.\",\n    \"ch\": \"純粹的決心幫助她取得了成功。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"純粹的喜悅充滿了房間。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6096,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::sheriff::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____'s department is responsible for law enforcement in the county.","expectedAnswer":"sheriff","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____'s department is responsible for law enforcement in the county.","clozeAnswer":"sheriff","exampleTranslation":"郡治安官部門負責該縣的執法工作。","reference":{"eng":"sheriff","kk":"ˈʃɛrɪf","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"警長\"  ]]","chEntries":["警長"],"practiceMeaning":"郡治安官部門負責該縣的執法工作。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 scīrgerefa，由 scīr（郡，行政區）和 gerefa（官員）組成。核心語義是「地區官員」，特別是指在英語國家，負責某個郡或縣的執法官員。現代美式英語中，sheriff 通常指由選民選舉產生的、負責一個郡的治安的官員。","definition":"the chief law enforcement officer in a county.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The sheriff's department is responsible for law enforcement in the county.\",\n    \"ch\": \"郡治安官部門負責該縣的執法工作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The sheriff arrived at the scene of the crime.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警長到達了犯罪現場。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was elected sheriff for his third term.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他第三次當