'（行動的）暗示']]","chEntries":["信號","信號燈","標誌","跡象","暗示"],"practiceMeaning":"交通號誌變成了紅色。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'signum' (sign, mark)。核心是「標記」、「記號」。因此，'signal' 可以指用來傳達信息的「信號」（如燈號、聲音），也可以指預示某事的「跡象」或「標誌」，或通過動作傳達的「暗示」。","definition":"1. a gesture, sound, or action that conveys information or instructions; 2. an indication or sign of something; 3. a device that indicates information by visual or auditory means","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"交通號誌變成了紅色。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The traffic signal turned red.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他同意的跡象是一個點頭。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The signal of his agreement was a nod.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他發出了一個啟動引擎的信號。\",\n    \"eng\": \"He gave a signal to start the engine.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"交通號誌變成了紅色。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4475,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::sip::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He took a ____ of his coffee.","expectedAnswer":"sip","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He took a ____ of his coffee.","clozeAnswer":"sip","exampleTranslation":"他喝了一小口咖啡。","reference":{"eng":"sip","kk":"/sɪp/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['一小口']]","chEntries":["一小口"],"practiceMeaning":"他喝了一小口咖啡。","analysis":"名詞形式，源自動詞 sip。意為「小口喝的量」。","definition":"1. A small mouthful of liquid.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He took a sip of his coffee.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他喝了一小口咖啡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Enjoy every sip of your vacation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"享受你假期的每一刻。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他喝了一小口咖啡。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3871,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::situation::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The political ____ is very tense.","expectedAnswer":"situation","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The political ____ is very tense.","clozeAnswer":"situation","exampleTranslation":"政治局勢非常緊張。","reference":{"eng":"situation","kk":"/ˌsɪtʃuˈeɪʃən/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['情況', '局勢'], ['處境'], ['地點', '場所']]","chEntries":["情況","局勢","處境","地點","場所"],"practiceMeaning":"政治局勢非常緊張。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 ' situs' (site, position)，後經由法語 'situation' 傳入。核心是「位置」或「所處的狀態」。可指一個具體情境的實際狀態、一連串事件的發展，或某人所處的困難/有利的境地。較少見的用法指特定地點。","definition":"1. a set of circumstances or conditions; a state of affairs. 2. a person's position or condition at a particular time. 3. a place or location.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The political situation is very tense.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政治局勢非常緊張。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He found himself in a difficult situation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他發現自己處於一個困難的境地。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company is in a good financial situation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司財務狀況良好。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"政治局勢非常緊張。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3950,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::skinny::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He was so ____ after being sick.","expectedAnswer":"skinny","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He was so ____ after being sick.","clozeAnswer":"skinny","exampleTranslation":"病後他變得非常瘦。","reference":{"eng":"skinny","kk":"/ˈskɪni/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['瘦的', '瘠瘦的'], ['薄的', '細的']]","chEntries":["瘦的","瘠瘦的","薄的","細的"],"practiceMeaning":"病後他變得非常瘦。","analysis":"源自古英語 'skinn-', 與 'skin' (皮膚) 有關。指「非常瘦」；也可用於形容物體「薄的、細的」。","definition":"1. unpleasantly thin; 2. very thin and smooth.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was so skinny after being sick.\",\n    \"ch\": \"病後他變得非常瘦。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The skinny jeans are out of fashion.\",\n    \"ch\": \"緊身牛仔褲已經過時了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She ate very little and was quite skinny.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她吃得很少，而且相當瘦。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"病後他變得非常瘦。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5807,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::skull::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ protects the brain.","expectedAnswer":"skull","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ protects the brain.","clozeAnswer":"skull","exampleTranslation":"頭蓋骨保護大腦。","reference":{"eng":"skull","kk":"skʌl","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"頭蓋骨\"  ],  [    \"顱骨\"  ],  [    \"髑髏\"  ]]","chEntries":["頭蓋骨","顱骨","髑髏"],"practiceMeaning":"頭蓋骨保護大腦。","analysis":"此字為名詞，源自古英語scull，可能與古諾斯語skalli（光禿的頭）有關，詞源意義為「頭部」或「頭蓋」。核心語義是指「構成頭部骨骼結構的骨頭」，即頭蓋骨或顱骨。語意演變上，從「頭部」的概念，具體化為保護大腦的「頭骨」。","definition":"1. the bony framework of the head of a person or vertebrate animal, enclosing the brain and supporting the facial structures.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The skull protects the brain.\",\n    \"ch\": \"頭蓋骨保護大腦。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Archaeologists found a human skull at the dig site.\",\n    \"ch\": \"考古學家在挖掘地點發現了一顆人頭骨。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The skull and crossbones is a symbol of danger.\",\n    \"ch\": \"骷髏頭和交叉的骨頭是危險的象徵。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"頭蓋骨保護大腦。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5809,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::slap::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He received a ____ on the back for his achievement.","expectedAnswer":"slap","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He received a ____ on the back for his achievement.","clozeAnswer":"slap","exampleTranslation":"他因成就而得到背部拍打（讚揚）。","reference":{"eng":"slap","kk":"slæp","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"摑（耳光）\"  ],  [    \"拍打\"  ],  [    \"一擊\"  ]]","chEntries":["摑","拍打","一擊"],"practiceMeaning":"他因成就而得到背部拍打（讚揚）。","analysis":"此字為名詞，與動詞同源。核心語義是指「用手掌打擊的動作或聲音」。語意演變上，從具體的「摑耳光」或「拍打」動作，也可用來形容某種突然或有力的接觸，或比喻為一次意外的打擊。","definition":"1. an act of hitting someone or something with the palm of your hand; 2. the sound of a slap; 3. an unpleasant shock or disappointment.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He received a slap on the back for his achievement.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他因成就而得到背部拍打（讚揚）。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The decision was a slap in the face to the workers.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個決定對工人來說是個打擊。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The slap of the waves was loud.\",\n    \"ch\": \"海浪拍打的聲音很大。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他因成就而得到背部拍打（讚揚）。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5101,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::slavery::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The abolition of ____ was a major turning point in history.","expectedAnswer":"slavery","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The abolition of ____ was a major turning point in history.","clozeAnswer":"slavery","exampleTranslation":"廢除奴隸制度是歷史上一個重要的轉捩點。","reference":{"eng":"slavery","kk":"ˈsleɪvəri","tense":"n.","ch":"[['奴隸制度'], ['奴役'], ['被束縛的狀態']]","chEntries":["奴隸制度","奴役","被束縛的狀態"],"practiceMeaning":"廢除奴隸制度是歷史上一個重要的轉捩點。","analysis":"此字由 'slave' (奴隸) + '-ry' (名詞化後綴，表示狀態、職業、集合) 構成。'-ry' 後綴常表示與某事物相關的狀態、職業、地方或集合，如 'bakery' (麵包店)、'bravery' (勇氣)。'Slavery' 的核心語義是 '被視為財產並被迫勞動，且失去自由的狀態'。它既指社會制度，也指個人遭受的 '奴役' 或 '被束縛' 的處境。","definition":"1. The state or condition of being a slave; the practice of owning slaves.; 2. The system whereby people are treated as property and are forced to work.; 3. A state of being controlled by a powerful force or addiction.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The abolition of slavery was a major turning point in history.\",\n    \"ch\": \"廢除奴隸制度是歷史上一個重要的轉捩點。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"For centuries, slavery was practiced in many parts of the world.\",\n    \"ch\": \"數百年來，奴隸制度曾在世界許多地方實行。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He felt in slavery to his ambition.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他覺得自己被野心所奴役。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"廢除奴隸制度是歷史上一個重要的轉捩點。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6245,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::smash::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of glass echoed in the street.","expectedAnswer":"smash","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of glass echoed in the street.","clozeAnswer":"smash","exampleTranslation":"玻璃破碎的聲音迴盪在街上。","reference":{"eng":"smash","kk":"smæʃ","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"破碎\"  ],  [    \"猛撞\"  ],  [    \"粉碎\"  ],  [    \"巨大的成功\"  ]]","chEntries":["破碎","猛撞","粉碎","巨大的成功"],"practiceMeaning":"玻璃破碎的聲音迴盪在街上。","analysis":"此字源自擬聲詞，模仿物體破碎的聲音。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。名詞義指猛烈撞擊、打碎或粉碎的動作及其結果。也可引申為巨大的成功或轟動。中文翻譯為「破碎；猛撞；粉碎；巨大的成功」。","definition":"1. the act of breaking something violently; 2. a loud noise made by something breaking; 3. a great success.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The smash of glass echoed in the street.\",\n    \"ch\": \"玻璃破碎的聲音迴盪在街上。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The car crash resulted in the smash of the windshield.\",\n    \"ch\": \"汽車相撞導致擋風玻璃粉碎。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The band's latest album was a smash hit.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這支樂隊的最新專輯是一次巨大的成功。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"玻璃破碎的聲音迴盪在街上。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6098,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::solo::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The pianist played a difficult ____.","expectedAnswer":"solo","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The pianist played a difficult ____.","clozeAnswer":"solo","exampleTranslation":"鋼琴家演奏了一首高難度的獨奏曲。","reference":{"eng":"solo","kk":"ˈsolo","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"獨奏\"  ],  [    \"獨唱\"  ],  [    \"獨自一人\"  ]]","chEntries":["獨奏","獨唱","獨自一人"],"practiceMeaning":"鋼琴家演奏了一首高難度的獨奏曲。","analysis":"此字源自義大利語 solo（alone）。作為名詞，指「單獨的表演」，如音樂的「獨奏」或「獨唱」。也可以指「獨自的行為」或「獨自一人」。","definition":"1. a thing done alone; 2. a performance by one person, especially in music.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The pianist played a difficult solo.\",\n    \"ch\": \"鋼琴家演奏了一首高難度的獨奏曲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her first solo flight was nerve-wracking.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的第一次單獨飛行令人緊張。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The singer's solo was met with thunderous applause.\",\n    \"ch\": \"歌手的獨唱贏得了雷鳴般的掌聲。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"鋼琴家演奏了一首高難度的獨奏曲。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5478,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::species::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The Amazon rainforest is home to thousands of ____ of plants and animals.","expectedAnswer":"species","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The Amazon rainforest is home to thousands of ____ of plants and animals.","clozeAnswer":"species","exampleTranslation":"亞馬遜雨林是數千種動植物的家園。","reference":{"eng":"species","kk":"ˈspishiz","tense":"n.","ch":"[['物種'], ['種類']]","chEntries":["物種","種類"],"practiceMeaning":"亞馬遜雨林是數千種動植物的家園。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'species'，原意是「樣貌、外觀、形式、種類」，也指「圖像、模型」。在科學分類中，它被用來表示「一個物種」，即生物分類學中的一個基本單位，指一群能夠相互繁殖並產生可育後代的生物。'Species' 是單數與複數同形。其詞源 'specere'（看）表明了「種類」的概念是基於「外觀」的區分。核心語意是「一個具有共同特徵、能夠繁殖的生物分類單元」。","definition":"1. A group of living organisms consisting of similar individuals capable of exchanging genes or interbreeding.; 2. A class or kind of persons or things.; 3. A particular kind of.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The Amazon rainforest is home to thousands of species of plants and animals.\",\n    \"ch\": \"亞馬遜雨林是數千種動植物的家園。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Scientists are trying to protect endangered species.\",\n    \"ch\": \"科學家正努力保護瀕危物種。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a rare species of bird.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是稀有的鳥類物種。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"亞馬遜雨林是數千種動植物的家園。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3301,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::spectacular::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The fireworks display was ____.","expectedAnswer":"spectacular","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The fireworks display was ____.","clozeAnswer":"spectacular","exampleTranslation":"煙火表演非常精彩。","reference":{"eng":"spectacular","kk":"/spɛkˈtækjʊlər/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['壯觀的；引人注目的'], ['精彩的；驚人的']]","chEntries":["壯觀的","引人注目的","精彩的","驚人的"],"practiceMeaning":"煙火表演非常精彩。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'spectaculum' (戲劇表演，景象)，由 'spectare' (觀看) 演變而來。指令人印象深刻、引人注目、極為精彩或壯觀的。","definition":"1. beautiful in a dramatic and eye-catching way; 2. very impressive or remarkable.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The fireworks display was spectacular.\",\n    \"ch\": \"煙火表演非常精彩。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The Grand Canyon offers spectacular views.\",\n    \"ch\": \"大峽谷提供了壯觀的景色。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He made a spectacular recovery from his illness.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他從疾病中奇蹟般地康復了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"煙火表演非常精彩。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3989,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u3::spice::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Cinnamon is a common ____ used in baking.","expectedAnswer":"spice","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Cinnamon is a common ____ used in baking.","clozeAnswer":"spice","exampleTranslation":"肉桂是烘焙中常用的香料。","reference":{"eng":"spice","kk":"/spaɪs/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['香料', '調味料'], ['情趣', '趣味']]","chEntries":["香料","調味料","情趣","趣味"],"practiceMeaning":"肉桂是烘焙中常用的香料。","analysis":"詞源：古法語 'espice' (香料)，來自拉丁文 'species' (種類，這裡指特定的、有價值的物品)。名詞指用於增添食物風味的植物性調味料，引申為能增添生活樂趣或趣味的事物。","definition":"1. a substance obtained from a plant, used to flavor food; 2. a quality that adds interest or excitement.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Cinnamon is a common spice used in baking.\",\n    \"ch\": \"肉桂是烘焙中常用的香料。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A little spice makes life more interesting.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一點情趣能讓生活更有趣。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"肉桂是烘焙中常用的香料。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4570,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::splash::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of water woke him up.","expectedAnswer":"splash","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of water woke him up.","clozeAnswer":"splash","exampleTranslation":"水花濺起的聲音把他吵醒了。","reference":{"eng":"splash","kk":"/splæʃ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['潑濺', '飛濺'], ['（水花）濺起聲'], ['（顏料、墨水等的）一灘', '一抹'], ['（引人注意的）引人注目的事物', '轟動']]","chEntries":["潑濺","飛濺","濺起聲","一灘","一抹","引人注目的事物","轟動"],"practiceMeaning":"水花濺起的聲音把他吵醒了。","analysis":"擬聲詞，模仿水花濺起的聲音。\n    1. 潑濺、飛濺：指液體被拋灑開來的動作或結果。\n    2. 聲音：指水花濺起時發出的聲音。\n    3. 一灘、一抹：指濺灑後在物體表面留下的痕跡。\n    4. 轟動：引申為引起廣泛關注或轟動的事件。","definition":"1. the action or sound of splashing.; 2. a quantity of liquid suddenly or violently dispersed in droplets.; 3. a vivid or striking effect.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The splash of water woke him up.\",\n    \"ch\": \"水花濺起的聲音把他吵醒了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was a splash of ink on the page.\",\n    \"ch\": \"紙上有一灘墨水。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her bold dress made a splash at the party.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她那大膽的洋裝在派對上引起了轟動。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"水花濺起的聲音把他吵醒了。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3195,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::split::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There was a ____ in the committee over the new proposal.","expectedAnswer":"split","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There was a ____ in the committee over the new proposal.","clozeAnswer":"split","exampleTranslation":"委員會在新的提案上出現了分歧。","reference":{"eng":"split","kk":"/splɪt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['分裂；分歧'], ['（尤指兩人或多人之間）分攤；一份'], ['（尤指歌劇、戲劇的）分聲部譜']]","chEntries":["分裂","分歧","分攤","一份","分聲部譜"],"practiceMeaning":"委員會在新的提案上出現了分歧。","analysis":"名詞用法，源自動詞 'split'。指「分裂」、「分歧」或「裂痕」，常形容意見、團體或關係上的不一致。也可指「分攤」的行為或結果，如分享費用或收益。在音樂領域，'split' 指的是將樂譜分開給不同聲部的樂手。","definition":"1. the act of dividing into parts or groups; 2. a disagreement or division between two or more people or groups; 3. a share of something; 4. (music) printed music for each part of an orchestra or choir.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was a split in the committee over the new proposal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"委員會在新的提案上出現了分歧。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Let's do a split on the bill.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們把帳單分攤一下吧。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The band has experienced several lineup splits.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個樂團經歷了幾次成員的分裂。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"委員會在新的提案上出現了分歧。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4003,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u3::staff::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The hotel ____ were very helpful.","expectedAnswer":"staff","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The hotel ____ were very helpful.","clozeAnswer":"staff","exampleTranslation":"酒店員工非常樂於助人。","reference":{"eng":"staff","kk":"/stæf/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['全體員工', '職員'], ['（樂器）棍棒', '（旗幟）旗杆']]","chEntries":["全體員工","職員","棍棒","旗杆"],"practiceMeaning":"酒店員工非常樂於助人。","analysis":"詞源：古英語 'stæf' (權杖、棍子)。最初指權杖或棍棒，引申為武器，再引申為組織中的服務人員，以及用於支撐或懸掛的長條狀物。","definition":"1. a group of people working in a particular organization or department; 2. a long stick used as a support when walking or as a weapon.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The hotel staff were very helpful.\",\n    \"ch\": \"酒店員工非常樂於助人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The wizard carried a magic staff.\",\n    \"ch\": \"巫師拿著一根魔法杖。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"酒店員工非常樂於助人。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3953,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::stand-for::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The letters 'UN' ____ United Nations.","expectedAnswer":"stand for","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The letters 'UN' ____ United Nations.","clozeAnswer":"stand for","exampleTranslation":"字母「UN」代表聯合國。","reference":{"eng":"stand for","kk":"None","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['代表', '象徵'], ['贊成', '支持'], ['容忍']]","chEntries":["代表","象徵","贊成","支持","容忍"],"practiceMeaning":"字母「UN」代表聯合國。","analysis":"此為動詞片語。'stand' (動詞，站立) 加上介詞 'for' (為了)。有多種意義：1. 作為某事的代表或象徵；2. 支持某種觀點或行動；3. 容忍某事（通常用於否定句）。","definition":"1. to be a symbol of something; 2. to support or approve of something; 3. to tolerate something (often used in the negative).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The letters 'UN' stand for United Nations.\",\n    \"ch\": \"字母「UN」代表聯合國。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He will not stand for injustice.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他不會容忍不公。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They stand for equal rights for all.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們主張所有人的平等權利。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"字母「UN」代表聯合國。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4568,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::steady::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The doctor is trying to ____ the patient's heart rate.","expectedAnswer":"steady","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The doctor is trying to ____ the patient's heart rate.","clozeAnswer":"steady","exampleTranslation":"醫生正在努力使病人的心率穩定下來。","reference":{"eng":"steady","kk":"/ˈstɛdi/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['使穩定', '使平穩'], ['使堅定']]","chEntries":["使穩定","使平穩","使堅定"],"practiceMeaning":"醫生正在努力使病人的心率穩定下來。","analysis":"動詞用法源自形容詞，指採取行動使事物變得穩定或平穩。引申為使某人或某事變得更加堅定和有信心。","definition":"1. make or become firm, fixed, or steady.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The doctor is trying to steady the patient's heart rate.\",\n    \"ch\": \"醫生正在努力使病人的心率穩定下來。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He steadied himself against the wall.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他靠著牆站穩。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"醫生正在努力使病人的心率穩定下來。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4148,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::steep::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The path up the mountain was very ____.","expectedAnswer":"steep","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The path up the mountain was very ____.","clozeAnswer":"steep","exampleTranslation":"上山的路非常陡峭。","reference":{"eng":"steep","kk":"/stiːp/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['陡峭的', '險峻的'], ['（價格、增長等）急劇的'], ['（要求、期望）過高的'], ['（學習）艱深的']]","chEntries":["陡峭的","險峻的","急劇的","過高的","艱深的"],"practiceMeaning":"上山的路非常陡峭。","analysis":"源自古英語 steap（高聳的，陡峭的）。核心概念是「極度傾斜」或「高度」。引申為物理上的陡峭、數量上的急劇變化、要求過高，或學習曲線的陡峭。","definition":"1. rising or falling sharply; 2. (of a price or amount) very high; 3. (of a task or idea) demanding or difficult","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The path up the mountain was very steep.\",\n    \"ch\": \"上山的路非常陡峭。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There has been a steep rise in inflation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"通貨膨脹急劇上升。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The tuition fees are very steep.\",\n    \"ch\": \"學費非常高昂。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"上山的路非常陡峭。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4706,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::stomach::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"I can't ____ his arrogance.","expectedAnswer":"stomach","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"I can't ____ his arrogance.","clozeAnswer":"stomach","exampleTranslation":"我無法容忍他的傲慢。","reference":{"eng":"stomach","kk":"/ˈstʌmək/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['容忍'], ['忍受']]","chEntries":["容忍","忍受"],"practiceMeaning":"我無法容忍他的傲慢。","analysis":"動詞形式，取自名詞的非正式用法，指能夠容忍或忍受某事，特別是令人不快的。","definition":"1. To tolerate or endure something unpleasant.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I can't stomach his arrogance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我無法容忍他的傲慢。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She found it hard to stomach the injustice.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她發現很難忍受這種不公。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我無法容忍他的傲慢。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4324,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::stormy::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We had to cancel the picnic due to the ____ weather.","expectedAnswer":"stormy","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We had to cancel the picnic due to the ____ weather.","clozeAnswer":"stormy","exampleTranslation":"由於天氣惡劣，我們不得不取消野餐。","reference":{"eng":"stormy","kk":"/ˈstɔːrmi/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['暴風雨的；有風暴的'], ['（天氣）惡劣的'], ['（局勢、關係等）激烈的；動盪的']]","chEntries":["暴風雨的","有風暴的","惡劣的","激烈的","動盪的"],"practiceMeaning":"由於天氣惡劣，我們不得不取消野餐。","analysis":"源自 'storm' (風暴)。1. 直接指天氣上有『風暴的』。2. 進一步指天氣『惡劣的』。3. 作為比喻，指情況、氣氛、關係等『激烈的、動盪的、充滿衝突的』，如同風暴一樣不平靜。","definition":"characterized by or like a storm; (of weather) very bad with strong winds and rain; full of strong feelings or arguments","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We had to cancel the picnic due to the stormy weather.\",\n    \"ch\": \"由於天氣惡劣，我們不得不取消野餐。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Their marriage was often stormy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們的婚姻經常處於動盪之中。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A stormy argument broke out.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一場激烈的爭論爆發了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"由於天氣惡劣，我們不得不取消野餐。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3987,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u3::structure::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of the novel is complex.","expectedAnswer":"structure","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of the novel is complex.","clozeAnswer":"structure","exampleTranslation":"這本小說的結構很複雜。","reference":{"eng":"structure","kk":"/ˈstrʌktʃər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['結構', '構造'], ['建築物', '建築']]","chEntries":["結構","構造","建築物","建築"],"practiceMeaning":"這本小說的結構很複雜。","analysis":"詞源：拉丁文 'structura' (建造、結構)，源自 'struere' (建造)。核心意義是組成的部分如何組織在一起，引申為由這些部分構成的實體。","definition":"1. the arrangement of and relations between the parts or elements of something complex; 2. a building or other edifice.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The structure of the novel is complex.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本小說的結構很複雜。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The Eiffel Tower is a famous structure in Paris.\",\n    \"ch\": \"艾菲爾鐵塔是巴黎一座著名的建築物。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這本小說的結構很複雜。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4388,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u9::superior::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The soldier must obey his ____.","expectedAnswer":"superior","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The soldier must obey his ____.","clozeAnswer":"superior","exampleTranslation":"士兵必須服從他的長官。","reference":{"eng":"superior","kk":"/suˈpɪəriər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['上級', '長官'], ['（尤指歷史上）最高統治者、權威人士']]","chEntries":["上級","長官","最高統治者、權威人士"],"practiceMeaning":"士兵必須服從他的長官。","analysis":"承襲形容詞的語意，指地位、等級或職位較高的人。","definition":"a person of higher rank or status.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The soldier must obey his superior.\",\n    \"ch\": \"士兵必須服從他的長官。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"士兵必須服從他的長官。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5355,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l1::surrender::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The army was ordered to ____.","expectedAnswer":"surrender","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The army was ordered to ____.","clozeAnswer":"surrender","exampleTranslation":"軍隊接到命令投降。","reference":{"eng":"surrender","kk":"səˈrɛndər","tense":"v.","ch":"[['投降'], ['屈服'], ['交出']]","chEntries":["投降","屈服","交出"],"practiceMeaning":"軍隊接到命令投降。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 surrender，來自 sur-（在……之上）+ render（給予、遞交，來自拉丁語 redere，意為「歸還」）。原始語意為「將某物交還或歸還給他人」，引申為「在壓力下交出控制權」或「投降」。構詞上，sur- 表示「在……之上」或「超過」，render 則意為「給予、交付」。","definition":"to stop resisting an enemy or opponent and submit to their authority; to give up.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The army was ordered to surrender.\",\n    \"ch\": \"軍隊接到命令投降。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He surrendered his weapons to the police.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他向警方交出了武器。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"軍隊接到命令投降。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4315,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::suspect::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The main ____ was arrested last night.","expectedAnswer":"suspect","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The main ____ was arrested last night.","clozeAnswer":"suspect","exampleTranslation":"主要嫌疑犯昨晚被逮捕了。","reference":{"eng":"suspect","kk":"/ˈsʌspɛkt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['嫌疑犯']]","chEntries":["嫌疑犯"],"practiceMeaning":"主要嫌疑犯昨晚被逮捕了。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'suspicere'，意為『懷疑』。在此作為名詞，特指『被懷疑對象』，即在犯罪調查中被認為可能有罪的人，亦即嫌疑犯。與動詞 'suspect' 的『懷疑』含義直接相關。","definition":"a person who is thought to be guilty of a crime","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The main suspect was arrested last night.\",\n    \"ch\": \"主要嫌疑犯昨晚被逮捕了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police questioned several suspects.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警方訊問了幾名嫌疑犯。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"主要嫌疑犯昨晚被逮捕了。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5708,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l9::sway::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Her ____ over the members was immense.","expectedAnswer":"sway","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Her ____ over the members was immense.","clozeAnswer":"sway","exampleTranslation":"她對成員們的影響力是巨大的。","reference":{"eng":"sway","kk":"sweɪ","tense":"n.","ch":"[['搖擺'], ['影響力']]","chEntries":["搖擺","影響力"],"practiceMeaning":"她對成員們的影響力是巨大的。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 swæġe（洪水，溪流，源自原始日耳曼語 \\*swag-），與原始印歐語 \\*swēg-（流動）相關。作為名詞，它指「搖擺的動作」或「影響、左右的能力」。從物理上的「搖擺、搖動」的動作，演變成抽象的「影響力」。","definition":"the power to decide an outcome; the motion of swaying.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her sway over the members was immense.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對成員們的影響力是巨大的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The gentle sway of the boat made him seasick.\",\n    \"ch\": \"船的輕柔搖擺讓他暈船。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她對成員們的影響力是巨大的。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6143,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::theoretical::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"a ____ physicist","expectedAnswer":"theoretical","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"a ____ physicist","clozeAnswer":"theoretical","exampleTranslation":"理論物理學家","reference":{"eng":"theoretical","kk":"ˌθiːəˈrɛtɪkəl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"理論的\"  ],  [    \"學術的\"  ],  [    \"假設的\"  ]]","chEntries":["理論的","學術的","假設的"],"practiceMeaning":"理論物理學家","analysis":"此字由 theory（理論）加上形容詞後綴 -etical 構成。theory 源自希臘語 theōria，意為「觀察；沉思；理論」。因此，theoretical 的核心語義是「與理論相關的」。此形容詞表示基於理論或假說，與實踐相對。其語意演變是從「基於觀察與沉思」到「與理論相關」。","definition":"1. concerned with or constituting theory; 2. based on or concerned with theory rather than practice; hypothetical.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"a theoretical physicist\",\n    \"ch\": \"理論物理學家\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a theoretical model, not a practical solution.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個理論模型，不是實際的解決方案。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The plan is sound in theoretical terms.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個計畫在理論上是可靠的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"理論物理學家","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5107,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::transmission::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of the virus can occur through airborne droplets.","expectedAnswer":"transmission","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of the virus can occur through airborne droplets.","clozeAnswer":"transmission","exampleTranslation":"該病毒可通過空氣飛沫傳播。","reference":{"eng":"transmission","kk":"trænzˈmɪʃn","tense":"n.","ch":"[['傳輸'], ['傳播'], ['變速器']]","chEntries":["傳輸","傳播","變速器"],"practiceMeaning":"該病毒可通過空氣飛沫傳播。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'transmittere'，由 'trans-' (across) + 'mittere' (to send) 構成，原意是 '送過、傳遞'。'Transmission' 的核心語義是 '從一個地方或個體傳遞到另一個地方或個體的過程'。這可以指能量、資訊（如無線電訊號）、疾病（如病毒傳播）、或動力的傳遞（如汽車的變速器）。","definition":"1. The act or process of transmitting something.; 2. The sending of something across places or to people.; 3. (In a vehicle) a system for transmitting mechanical power and torque from the engine to the driven parts.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The transmission of the virus can occur through airborne droplets.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該病毒可通過空氣飛沫傳播。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The radio transmission was clear.\",\n    \"ch\": \"無線電的傳輸很清晰。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He learned how to change the car's 