上。","reference":{"eng":"treasure","kk":"/ˈtrɛʒər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['寶藏；財寶'], ['珍寶；極有價值的人或物'], ['（尤指）儲藏的財富']]","chEntries":["寶藏","財寶","珍寶","極有價值的人或物","儲藏的財富"],"practiceMeaning":"海盜們把他們的寶藏埋在了島上。","analysis":"源自古法語 'tresor'，來自拉丁語 'thesaurus' (寶庫)。指非常珍貴、有價值或被儲存起來的物品，可以是物質的（金銀珠寶）或非物質的（才能、回憶）。","definition":"1. a quantity of valuable things, such as gold, jewels, and coins; 2. a person or thing that is greatly valued or cherished; 3. a collection of valuable objects, especially one that has been carefully collected over a period of time.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Pirates buried their treasure on the island.\",\n    \"ch\": \"海盜們把他們的寶藏埋在了島上。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her children are her greatest treasure.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的孩子是她最大的寶貝。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This old book is a real treasure.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本舊書是真正的珍寶。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"海盜們把他們的寶藏埋在了島上。","sourceName":"字彙王、龍騰課本","unitName":"U42、L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4129,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::tricky::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"That was a ____ question.","expectedAnswer":"tricky","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"That was a ____ question.","clozeAnswer":"tricky","exampleTranslation":"那是一個棘手的問題。","reference":{"eng":"tricky","kk":"/ˈtrɪki/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['棘手的', '難辦的'], ['狡猾的', '奸詐的'], ['需要技巧的', '巧妙的']]","chEntries":["棘手的","難辦的","狡猾的","奸詐的","需要技巧的","巧妙的"],"practiceMeaning":"那是一個棘手的問題。","analysis":"源自 trick（詭計，花招）。核心概念是「需要小心處理」，因為存在隱藏的困難、欺騙或複雜性。引申為難以應付的問題、狡猾的人或需要精細操作的任務。","definition":"1. difficult to deal with or accomplish; 2. cunning or deceitful; 3. requiring skill or dexterity","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"That was a tricky question.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那是一個棘手的問題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He's known for his tricky negotiation tactics.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他以其狡猾的談判策略而聞名。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Learning to juggle can be tricky.\",\n    \"ch\": \"學會玩雜耍可能需要技巧。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"那是一個棘手的問題。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6104,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::unemployment::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The government is trying to reduce ____.","expectedAnswer":"unemployment","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The government is trying to reduce ____.","clozeAnswer":"unemployment","exampleTranslation":"政府正試圖降低失業率。","reference":{"eng":"unemployment","kk":"ˌʌnɪmˈplɔɪmənt","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"失業\"  ],  [    \"失業率\"  ],  [    \"失業狀態\"  ]]","chEntries":["失業","失業率","失業狀態"],"practiceMeaning":"政府正試圖降低失業率。","analysis":"此字由 un-（not）+ employ（僱用）+ -ment（名詞後綴，表示狀態或行為）構成。核心語義是「未被僱用」的狀態。指沒有工作或失業的狀態，以及由此產生的社會現象（失業率）。","definition":"1. the state of being unemployed; 2. the number of people who are unemployed.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government is trying to reduce unemployment.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府正試圖降低失業率。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Unemployment rates have been rising.\",\n    \"ch\": \"失業率一直在上升。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has been facing long-term unemployment.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他一直面臨長期失業。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"政府正試圖降低失業率。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5445,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::urgent::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We have an ____ deadline to meet.","expectedAnswer":"urgent","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We have an ____ deadline to meet.","clozeAnswer":"urgent","exampleTranslation":"我們有一個緊急的截止日期要遵守。","reference":{"eng":"urgent","kk":"ˈɜːrdʒənt","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['緊急的'], ['急迫的'], ['緊迫的']]","chEntries":["緊急的","急迫的","緊迫的"],"practiceMeaning":"我們有一個緊急的截止日期要遵守。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 \"urgens\"，是動詞 \"urgere\" (催促、驅使、緊迫) 的現在分詞。\"urgere\" 的詞源不明確，但與\"torque\" (扭轉、轉動) 有聯繫，可能表示\"被推動\"或\"被施壓\"。構詞上，\"urg-\" 提供了核心的「催促」、「緊迫」語意，\"-ent\" 是形容詞字尾。 \"Urgent\" 形容某事「需要立即關注或處理」，具有「急迫性」或「緊迫性」。","definition":"requiring immediate action or attention; pressing; demanding prompt action.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We have an urgent deadline to meet.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們有一個緊急的截止日期要遵守。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is an urgent matter that requires your immediate attention.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是需要你立即關注的緊急事項。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Emergency services responded to an urgent call.\",\n    \"ch\": \"緊急服務部門響應了一個緊急呼叫。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們有一個緊急的截止日期要遵守。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3928,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::various::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We offer ____ courses to suit your needs.","expectedAnswer":"various","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We offer ____ courses to suit your needs.","clozeAnswer":"various","exampleTranslation":"我們提供各種課程以滿足您的需求。","reference":{"eng":"various","kk":"/ˈveəriəs/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['各種的', '不同的'], ['多樣的']]","chEntries":["各種的","不同的","多樣的"],"practiceMeaning":"我們提供各種課程以滿足您的需求。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'varius' (意為「多樣的、變化的」)。形容事物有多種不同的種類、形式或情況。","definition":"1. different; of different kinds; 2. many and different.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We offer various courses to suit your needs.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們提供各種課程以滿足您的需求。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There are various reasons why this happened.\",\n    \"ch\": \"發生這種事有各種各樣的原因。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The shop sells various kinds of tea.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家店販售各種茶葉。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們提供各種課程以滿足您的需求。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6251,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::vein::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The nurse drew blood from a ____ in his arm.","expectedAnswer":"vein","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The nurse drew blood from a ____ in his arm.","clozeAnswer":"vein","exampleTranslation":"護士從他手臂的一條靜脈抽了血。","reference":{"eng":"vein","kk":"veɪn","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"靜脈\"  ],  [    \"血管\"  ],  [    \"礦脈\"  ],  [    \"紋路\"  ],  [    \"風格\"  ]]","chEntries":["靜脈","血管","礦脈","紋路","風格"],"practiceMeaning":"護士從他手臂的一條靜脈抽了血。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 fēn，向上可追溯至拉丁語 vena，意為「血管，水道」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。名詞義指將血液從身體各部位輸送到心臟的血管，也引申指礦藏所在的「礦脈」，物體表面的「紋路」，或人或事物中某種「風格」或「特質」。中文翻譯為「靜脈；血管；礦脈；紋路；風格」。","definition":"1. one of the tubes that carry blood from the body to the heart; 2. a line of mineral ore within a rock; 3. a pattern of lines in something, such as a leaf or a piece of wood; 4. a particular style or manner.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The nurse drew blood from a vein in his arm.\",\n    \"ch\": \"護士從他手臂的一條靜脈抽了血。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Geologists searched for a vein of gold.\",\n    \"ch\": \"地質學家們在尋找金礦脈。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The marble had a beautiful vein pattern.\",\n    \"ch\": \"大理石有著美麗的紋路。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His writing has a sarcastic vein.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的寫作帶有一種諷刺的風格。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"護士從他手臂的一條靜脈抽了血。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5110,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::viable::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The plan is not ____ in the long term.","expectedAnswer":"viable","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The plan is not ____ in the long term.","clozeAnswer":"viable","exampleTranslation":"這個計劃從長遠來看是不可行的。","reference":{"eng":"viable","kk":"ˈvaɪəbl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['可行的'], ['可持續的'], ['生存的']]","chEntries":["可行的","可持續的","生存的"],"practiceMeaning":"這個計劃從長遠來看是不可行的。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'via' (way)，透過古法語 'viable' (capable of living) 演變而來。其核心語義是 '能夠生存、發展或成功地運作'。這可以指生物的生命力，如 'a viable fetus' (存活的胎兒)，也可以指計劃、項目或商業模式的可行性，強調其在現實條件下能夠實施並產生預期結果的能力。","definition":"1. Capable of working successfully; feasible.; 2. Able to survive or to function successfully.; 3. (Of a newborn infant) able to survive after birth.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The plan is not viable in the long term.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個計劃從長遠來看是不可行的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to find a viable solution.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要找到一個可行的解決方案。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company's business model is no longer viable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司的商業模式已不再可行。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個計劃從長遠來看是不可行的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4201,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::visible::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The stars are ____ tonight.","expectedAnswer":"visible","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The stars are ____ tonight.","clozeAnswer":"visible","exampleTranslation":"今晚星星清晰可見。","reference":{"eng":"visible","kk":"/ˈvɪzəbl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['可見的；看得見的'], ['顯著的；明顯的']]","chEntries":["可見的","看得見的","顯著的","明顯的"],"practiceMeaning":"今晚星星清晰可見。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 visibilis，'videre'（看）+ '-ibilis'（可…的）。字面意思是“可被看見的”。1. “可見的”指客觀上處於可視範圍內。2. “顯著的；明顯的”是抽象意義，指某事物能夠被注意到，其影響或存在是清晰的。","definition":"1. able to be seen; 2. easily seen or noticed; apparent.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The stars are visible tonight.\",\n    \"ch\": \"今晚星星清晰可見。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was a visible increase in their profits.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們的利潤有了顯著的增長。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His relief was visible.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的寬慰顯而易見。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"今晚星星清晰可見。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4131,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::wage::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The country decided to ____ war on terrorism.","expectedAnswer":"wage","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The country decided to ____ war on terrorism.","clozeAnswer":"wage","exampleTranslation":"這個國家決定發動對恐怖主義的戰爭。","reference":{"eng":"wage","kk":"/weɪdʒ/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['發動（戰爭）', '進行（鬥爭）']]","chEntries":["發動","進行"],"practiceMeaning":"這個國家決定發動對恐怖主義的戰爭。","analysis":"源自古英語 wagian（搖動，支付）。此處與名詞 wage（工資）詞源不同，而是與古法語 gaige（抵押品，報酬，從事）有關。核心概念是「積極投入」、「從事」。引申為發動戰爭或進行長期的鬥爭。","definition":"carry on (a war or campaign); engage in","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The country decided to wage war on terrorism.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個國家決定發動對恐怖主義的戰爭。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They waged a relentless campaign for reform.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們進行了不懈的改革鬥爭。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The activists waged a protest against the new law.\",\n    \"ch\": \"活動家們發起了反對新法律的抗議。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個國家決定發動對恐怖主義的戰爭。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4489,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::wisdom::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She offered her ____ and advice.","expectedAnswer":"wisdom","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She offered her ____ and advice.","clozeAnswer":"wisdom","exampleTranslation":"她提供了她的智慧和建議。","reference":{"eng":"wisdom","kk":"/ˈwɪzdəm/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['智慧'], ['明智']]","chEntries":["智慧","明智"],"practiceMeaning":"她提供了她的智慧和建議。","analysis":"源自古英語 wīsdōm，由 wīs (智慧的) 和 -dōm (表示「狀態」、「領域」或「品質」的名詞後綴) 組成。核心語意是「理解深刻事實或情況的能力」，「明辨是非的能力」。","definition":"1. The quality of having experience, knowledge, and good judgment; 2. The quality of being wise.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She offered her wisdom and advice.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她提供了她的智慧和建議。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It takes wisdom to understand complex issues.\",\n    \"ch\": \"理解複雜的問題需要智慧。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is known for his deep wisdom.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他以其深邃的智慧而聞名。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她提供了她的智慧和建議。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U10、L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5591,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::without-a-doubt::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She is ____ the best candidate for the job.","expectedAnswer":"without a doubt","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She is ____ the best candidate for the job.","clozeAnswer":"without a doubt","exampleTranslation":"她毫無疑問是這個職位的最佳人選。","reference":{"eng":"without a doubt","kk":"wɪˈðaʊt ə daʊt","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['無疑地'], ['毫無疑問地']]","chEntries":["無疑地","毫無疑問地"],"practiceMeaning":"她毫無疑問是這個職位的最佳人選。","analysis":"此片語由介詞 \"without\"（沒有），不定冠詞 \"a\"，名詞 \"doubt\"（懷疑）組成。\"without\" 表示「缺乏」。\"doubt\" 表示「懷疑、不確定」。\"without a doubt\" 是一個慣用語，字面意思是「沒有任何懷疑」，引申為「確定地、無疑地」。它用來強調說話者對某件事情的絕對確定性。","definition":"1. Certainly; undoubtedly; 2. Beyond any question or suspicion.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is without a doubt the best candidate for the job.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她毫無疑問是這個職位的最佳人選。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is without a doubt the most beautiful sunset I've ever seen.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這毫無疑問是我見過最美的日落。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He will, without a doubt, succeed in his endeavors.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他肯定會在他的事業上取得成功。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她毫無疑問是這個職位的最佳人選。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5070,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::worthy::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He is a ____ recipient of the award.","expectedAnswer":"worthy","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He is a ____ recipient of the award.","clozeAnswer":"worthy","exampleTranslation":"他是該獎項當之無愧的得主。","reference":{"eng":"worthy","kk":"ˈwɜːrði","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['值得的'], ['有價值的'], ['品格高尚的']]","chEntries":["值得的","有價值的","品格高尚的"],"practiceMeaning":"他是該獎項當之無愧的得主。","analysis":"此字由word（詞）加上字尾-y（形容詞化）構成，但其詞源並非來自word，而是源自古英語wierðe，意為「有價值的、值得的」。其核心語意是「值得尊敬、重視或獲得某事物（如讚揚、關注、獎勵）」。此用法與名詞 worth（價值）相關。OCR 掃描時可能將 'w' 誤判為 'u'，或 'rd' 誤判為 'nd'。此處修正為 worthy。","definition":"1. deserving effort or attention; 2. having or showing the merits or character to deserve attention, honor, or respect.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a worthy recipient of the award.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是該獎項當之無愧的得主。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a cause worthy of our support.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個值得我們支持的事業。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a worthy opponent.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是一位值得尊敬的對手。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他是該獎項當之無愧的得主。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4675,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::wrap::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Please ____ the gift carefully before sending it.","expectedAnswer":"wrap","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Please ____ the gift carefully before sending it.","clozeAnswer":"wrap","exampleTranslation":"請在寄出前仔細包裝禮物。","reference":{"eng":"wrap","kk":"/ˈræp/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['包裹'], ['纏繞'], ['（情緒、思想）沉浸其中']]","chEntries":["包裹","纏繞","沉浸其中"],"practiceMeaning":"請在寄出前仔細包裝禮物。","analysis":"源自古英語 *wrappan*，意為「纏繞」、「覆蓋」。核心是將某物覆蓋或包圍起來。延伸義包括將東西纏繞起來，或將人的心思、注意力完全投入到某事中。","definition":"1. To cover or encase something by folding or rolling something else around it. 2. To wind or coil something around something else. 3. To become completely absorbed or involved in something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please wrap the gift carefully before sending it.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請在寄出前仔細包裝禮物。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She wrapped a scarf around her neck to keep warm.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她圍了一條圍巾在脖子上保暖。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was so wrapped up in his work that he forgot to eat.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他全身心投入工作，以至於忘了吃飯。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"請在寄出前仔細包裝禮物。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5426,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::abundant::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The forest provides ____ opportunities for hiking.","expectedAnswer":"abundant","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The forest provides ____ opportunities for hiking.","clozeAnswer":"abundant","exampleTranslation":"這片森林提供了豐富的健行機會。","reference":{"eng":"abundant","kk":"əˈbʌndənt","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['豐富的'], ['充裕的'], ['大量的'], ['充足的']]","chEntries":["豐富的","充裕的","大量的","充足的"],"practiceMeaning":"這片森林提供了豐富的健行機會。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 \"abundans\"，是動詞 \"abundare\" 的現在分詞，意為\"充溢\"、\"豐富\"。\"abundare\" 由 \"ab-\" (離開、遠離，在此表示\"過多\"或\"溢出\") 和 \"undare\" (波浪般流動) 構成，\"undare\" 又源於 \"unda\" (波浪)。構詞上，\"ab-\" 提供了「過量」的語意，\"undare\" 提供了「流動」的圖像，整體表示「如波浪般湧出、充溢」。\"Abundant\" 作形容詞，描述某物「極其豐富」、「充裕」或「大量存在」，遠超過所需。","definition":"existing or available in large quantities; plentiful; more than enough.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Fresh fruits are abundant in summer.\",\n    \"ch\": \"夏季水果供應充足。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The forest provides abundant opportunities for hiking.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這片森林提供了豐富的健行機會。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Natural gas is abundant in this region.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個地區天然氣儲量豐富。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這片森林提供了豐富的健行機會。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5556,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::accuracy::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The pilot maintained a high level of ____ in navigation.","expectedAnswer":"accuracy","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The pilot maintained a high level of ____ in navigation.","clozeAnswer":"accuracy","exampleTranslation":"飛行員在導航中保持了高度的精確性。","reference":{"eng":"accuracy","kk":"ˈækjərəsi","tense":"n.","ch":"[['精確度'], ['準確性'], ['正確性']]","chEntries":["精確度","準確性","正確性"],"practiceMeaning":"飛行員在導航中保持了高度的精確性。","analysis":"此字由 \"accurate\" 加上名詞化字尾 \"-cy\" 構成。\"accurate\" 源自拉丁語 \"accurrere\"，意為 \"to run to, run up\"（跑到，跑近），由 \"ad-\"（to, toward，向，朝）和 \"currere\"（to run，跑）組成。\"accurrere\" 的引申義是指「達到目標」，因此 \"accurate\" 指「能夠精確地達到目標」或「符合標準」。\"-cy\" 是構成抽象名詞的字尾，表示「狀態、品質」。因此，\"accuracy\" 的核心語義是「達到目標、符合標準的品質或狀態」，即「精確性」或「準確性」。","definition":"1. The condition or quality of being accurate; freedom from error or defect; 2. The degree to which the result of a measurement, calculation, or specification conforms to the correct or a predicted result.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The accuracy of the data is crucial for our research.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這些數據的準確性對我們的研究至關重要。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The pilot maintained a high level of accuracy in navigation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"飛行員在導航中保持了高度的精確性。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to ensure the accuracy of the translation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要確保翻譯的準確性。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"飛行員在導航中保持了高度的精確性。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5604,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l7::addition::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The children are learning basic ____ in school.","expectedAnswer":"addition","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The children are learning basic ____ in school.","clozeAnswer":"addition","exampleTranslation":"孩子們正在學校學習基本的加法。","reference":{"eng":"addition","kk":"əˈdɪʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[['加法'], ['增加'], ['添加物']]","chEntries":["加法","增加","添加物"],"practiceMeaning":"孩子們正在學校學習基本的加法。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'additio'，由動詞 'addere'（添加）派生，'addere' 由 'ad-'（向）和 'dare'（給予）組成。構詞學上，它是由動詞 'add'（添加）加上名詞化後綴 '-tion' 所構成。'-tion' 字尾常將動詞轉換為表示「行動」、「過程」或「結果」的名詞。原始語意是「給予」或「添加」，演變為「加法」（數學上的）、「增加的行為或過程」，以及「被添加的物品」。","definition":"1. The action or process of adding something to something else; 2. The process of adding up numbers; 3. A thing added to something else.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The addition of a new wing significantly increased the museum's exhibition space.\",\n    \"ch\": \"新翼樓的增加顯著擴大了博物館的展覽空間。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The children are learning basic addition in school.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子們正在學校學習基本的加法。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The new feature is a welcome addition to the software.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這項新功能是該軟體一個受歡迎的補充。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"孩子們正在學校學習基本的加法。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6105,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::adverse::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The drug had ____ side effects.","expectedAnswer":"adverse","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The drug had ____ side effects.","clozeAnswer":"adverse","exampleTranslation":"這種藥物有不良副作用。","reference":{"eng":"adverse","kk":"ˈædvɜːrs","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"不利的\"  ],  [    \"有害的\"  ],  [    \"敵對的\"  ],  [    \"相反的\"  ]]","chEntries":["不利的","有害的","敵對的","相反的"],"practiceMeaning":"這種藥物有不良副作用。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 adversus，意為「朝向；反對」。構詞上，ad- 是方向字首，表示「朝向」或「趨向」；versus 則是拉丁語 vertō（轉動）的過去分詞，意為「轉向」。因此，adverse 的核心語義是「轉向相反方向」，引申為「不利的、敵對的、相反的」。此形容詞用於描述條件、影響、結果等，表示對某事造成負面影響或阻礙。其語意演變是從具體的「面對面、反向」到抽象的「不利、有害」。","definition":"1. preventing success or development; harmful; unfavorable; 2. opposing or contrary.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"adverse weather conditions\",\n    \"ch\": \"惡劣的天氣狀況\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The drug had adverse side effects.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種藥物有不良副作用。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He had to overcome adverse circumstances.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他不得不克服不利的環境。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這種藥物有不良副作用。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5504,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l5::agent::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The spy was identified as a foreign ____.","expectedAnswer":"agent","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The spy was identified as a foreign ____.","clozeAnswer":"agent","exampleTranslation":"該間諜被確認為一名外國情報員。","reference":{"eng":"agent","kk":"ˈeɪdʒənt","tense":"n.","ch":"[['代理人'], ['經紀人'], ['特工'], ['情報員'], ['媒介物'], ['動因']]","chEntries":["代理人","經紀人","特工","情報員","媒介物","動因"],"practiceMeaning":"該間諜被確認為一名外國情報員。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'agens' (genitive 'agentis')，意為 'doing' 或 'acting'，是動詞 'agere' (to do, to act) 的現在分詞。構詞上，'ag-' 提供核心動詞語意，'-ent' 是拉丁語主詞字尾，指代執行動作的人或事物。原始語義是「做者」或「行動者」。在現代英語中，'agent' 演變出多個義項：指代代表他人或團體行事的人（代理人、經紀人），在情報領域指從事秘密活動的特工或情報員，在科學或哲學領域指能夠引起變化或產生影響的媒介物或動因。這些義項都圍繞著「採取行動」或「產生影響」的核心概念展開。","definition":"a person who acts or does business for another; a person or thing that has the power to influence or act; a secret agent.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She works as a literary agent for several famous authors.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她擔任幾位著名作家文學經紀人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The spy was identified as a foreign agent.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該間諜被確認為一名外國情報員。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Water is a powerful agent of erosion.\",\n    \"ch\": \"水是侵蝕作用的強大媒介。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該間諜被確認為一名外國情報員。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6150,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::agony::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She was in ____ for days before the diagnosis was made.","expectedAnswer":"agony","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She was in ____ for days before the diagnosis was made.","clozeAnswer":"agony","exampleTranslation":"在做出診斷的前幾天，她一直承受著極度的痛苦。","reference":{"eng":"agony","kk":"ˈæɡəni","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"極度痛苦\"  ],  [    \"煎熬\"  ],  [    \"苦惱\"  ],  [    \"臨死前的掙扎\"  ]]","chEntries":["極度痛苦","煎熬","苦惱","臨死前的掙扎"],"practiceMeaning":"在做出診斷的前幾天，她一直承受著極度的痛苦。","analysis":"此字源自古希臘語 ἀγωνία (agōnia)，意為「掙扎、角鬥、痛苦」，與 ἀγών (agōn)「競技、集會、掙扎」同源。它進入中古英語 via 古法語 agonie。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，應視為整體詞源演變。作為名詞，其核心語義是極度的身體或精神痛苦，常與死亡前的掙扎或嚴重的心理煎熬聯繫。此義項由古希臘語中「掙扎」的含義演變而來。","definition":"1. extreme physical or mental suffering; 2. the pain of childbirth.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He died in agony after the accident.\",\n    \"ch\": \"事故發生後，他痛苦地死去。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She was in agony for days before the diagnosis was made.\",\n    \"ch\": \"在做出診斷的前幾天，她一直承受著極度的痛苦。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The final moments of his life were filled with agony.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他生命的最後時刻充滿了痛苦的掙扎。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"在做出診斷的前幾天，她一直承受著極度的痛苦。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4136,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::appeal::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The movie has great ____ for young people.","expectedAnswer":"appeal","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The movie has great ____ for young people.","clozeAnswer":"appeal","exampleTranslation":"這部電影對年輕人有很大的吸引力。","reference":{"eng":"appeal","kk":"/əˈpiːl/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['懇求', '請求'], ['吸引力'], ['上訴']]","chEntries":["懇求","請求","吸引力","上訴"],"practiceMeaning":"這部電影對年輕人有很大的吸引力。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 appellare（向...呼籲，控告）。核心概念是「正式的請求」或「有吸引力的特質」。","definition":"1. an earnest or urgent request; 2. the quality in a person or thing that causes pleasure or satisfaction; 3. an application to a higher court for a decision to be canceled or changed","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was a strong appeal for donations.\",\n    \"ch\": \"有強烈的捐款呼籲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The movie has great appeal for young people.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這部電影對年輕人有很大的吸引力。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The lawyer filed an appeal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"律師提交了上訴。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這部電影對年輕人有很大的吸引力。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U5、L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3059,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::associate::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Many people ____ wealth with happiness.","expectedAnswer":"associate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Many people ____ wealth with happiness.","clozeAnswer":"associate","exampleTranslation":"許多人將財富與幸福聯繫起來。","reference":{"eng":"associate","kk":"/əˈsoʊʃieɪt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['使聯繫；與…交往'], ['認為…有關聯；把…視為夥伴'], ['聯合；合作']]","chEntries":["使聯繫","與…交往","認為…有關聯","把…視為夥伴","聯合","合作"],"practiceMeaning":"許多人將財富與幸福聯繫起來。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'associatus'，'ad-' (to, toward) + 'sociatus' (companion)。核心意義是「連結」或「成為夥伴」。\n1. 使聯繫；與…交往：強調人與人之間的連結與互動，常指建立社交或業務關係。\n2. 認為…有關聯；把…視為夥伴：將兩個事物或概念連結在一起，認為它們之間有某種關聯性。\n3. 聯合；合作：指兩個或多個個體或團體共同行動或目標。","definition":"1. join together for a common purpose; unite; connect; 2. consider as connected; link; 3. connect or join; accompany.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She was asked to associate with the company's marketing team.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她被要求與公司的行銷團隊合作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Many people associate wealth with happiness.\",\n    \"ch\": \"許多人將財富與幸福聯繫起來。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was the associate of a known criminal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是個已知罪犯的同夥。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"許多人將財富與幸福聯繫起來。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3061,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::association::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The smell of cinnamon has a strong ____ with Christmas for me.","expectedAnswer":"association","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The smell of cinnamon has a strong ____ with Christmas for me.","clozeAnswer":"association","exampleTranslation":"肉桂的味道對我來說強烈地讓人聯想到聖誕節。","reference":{"eng":"association","kk":"/əˌsoʊsiˈeɪʃn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['協會；聯盟'], ['聯想；聯繫'], ['交往；夥伴關係']]","chEntries":["協會","聯盟","聯想","聯繫","交往","夥伴關係"],"practiceMeaning":"肉桂的味道對我來說強烈地讓人聯想到聖誕節。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'associatio'，由 'associatus' (companion) 演變而來，意為「連結」或「連結在一起的群體」。\n1. 協會；聯盟：指為共同目的而組成的團體或組織。\n2. 聯想；聯繫：指思想或觀念之間的連結，或將兩個事物聯繫起來的行為。\n3. 交往；夥伴關係：指與他人建立的聯繫或夥伴關係。","definition":"1. an organization of people with a common purpose; 2. a connection or relationship between things; 3. the process of connecting things or people.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a member of the national writers' association.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是國家作家協會的成員。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The smell of cinnamon has a strong association with Christmas for me.\",\n    \"ch\": \"肉桂的味道對我來說強烈地讓人聯想到聖誕節。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Their association lasted for many years.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們的夥伴關係持續了很多年。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"肉桂的味道對我來說強烈地讓人聯想到聖誕節。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3063,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::assurance::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company offers a money-back ____.","expectedAnswer":"assurance","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company offers a money-back ____.","clozeAnswer":"assurance","exampleTranslation":"該公司提供退款保證。","reference":{"eng":"assurance","kk":"/əˈʃʊərəns/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['保證；信心'], ['擔保；確信'], ['（購買的）保險；保證書']]","chEntries":["保證","信心","擔保","確信","保險","保證書"],"practiceMeaning":"該公司提供退款保證。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'securus' (safe, secure)，經由古法語 'asseurance' 演變而來，是 'assure' 的名詞形式。指「確定」或「使確信」的狀態或行為。\n1. 保證；信心：指說話或行為中表現出的確定感，給予聽者信心。\n2. 擔保；確信：指對某事物的肯定或相信，使其變得確定。\n3. （購買的）保險；保證書：指一種承諾或文件，提供對某種結果的保障。","definition":"1. a statement that something will certainly happen or be true; 2. a feeling of confidence that you can do something well or succeed; 3. a promise or guarantee.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He spoke with great assurance, calming everyone's fears.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他充滿信心地說話，平息了所有人的恐懼。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company offers a money-back assurance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司提供退款保證。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her assurance of success gave him hope.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她成功的保證給了他希望。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該公司提供退款保證。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3065,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::attachment::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She showed a deep ____ to her homeland.","expectedAnswer":"attachment","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She showed a deep ____ to her homeland.","clozeAnswer":"attachment","exampleTranslation":"她對祖國表現出深厚的依戀。","reference":{"eng":"attachment","kk":"/əˈtætʃmənt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['附件；附屬物'], ['情感上的依戀；愛慕'], ['（電腦）附件']]","chEntries":["附件","附屬物","情感上的依戀","愛慕"],"practiceMeaning":"她對祖國表現出深厚的依戀。","analysis":"源自古法語 'atachier' (to fasten, to fix) 的名詞形式。指「附著」的狀態或事物。\n1. 附件；附屬物：指被連接或附屬於主體的事物。\n2. 情感上的依戀；愛慕：指人與人之間或人與物之間產生的深厚情感連結。\n3. （電腦）附件：在電子郵件或其他數位通訊中，與主要訊息一同傳送的文件或檔案。","definition":"1. a document or file sent with an email; 2. a feeling of love or strong connection to someone or something; 3. a device or tool that connects to something else.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The user manual is available as a PDF attachment.\",\n    \"ch\": \"使用者手冊可作為 PDF 附件下載。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She sho