機械的","不自覺的，無意識的"],"practiceMeaning":"她的反應是下意識的。","analysis":"源自希臘語 automatos，意為「自動的」、「自發的」。auto- (自己) + -matos (受驅動的)。核心概念是「自己運作」、「不需要外部持續干預」。引申為行為不受控制或不經思考的。","definition":"1. Working by itself with little or no direct human control; 2. Done or happening without conscious thought or intention.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The car has an automatic transmission.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這輛車有自動變速器。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her response was automatic.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的反應是下意識的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The factory uses automatic machinery to increase production.\",\n    \"ch\": \"工廠使用自動化機器來提高產量。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她的反應是下意識的。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4478,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::awkward::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It was an ____ silence after her comment.","expectedAnswer":"awkward","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It was an ____ silence after her comment.","clozeAnswer":"awkward","exampleTranslation":"她說完後，出現了一段尷尬的沉默。","reference":{"eng":"awkward","kk":"/ˈɔːkwərd/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['笨拙的'], ['尷尬的'], ['難以處理的'], ['不方便的']]","chEntries":["笨拙的","尷尬的","難以處理的","不方便的"],"practiceMeaning":"她說完後，出現了一段尷尬的沉默。","analysis":"源自古挪威語 örvugr，意為「逆向的」、「不順的」。或源自拉丁語 (per) arduum，意為「經過困難」。核心語意是「不順暢」、「不方便」、「難以應對」。引申為行為上的「笨拙」，社交上的「尷尬」，以及處境上的「不方便」或「棘手」。","definition":"1. (of a person) Lacking grace or skill in action, movement, or handling things; 2. (of a situation) Embarrassing, uncomfortable, or inconvenient; 3. Difficult to do or deal with.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He felt awkward when he dropped the vase.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他打翻花瓶時感到很尷尬。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was an awkward silence after her comment.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她說完後，出現了一段尷尬的沉默。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Carrying the heavy box up the stairs was awkward.\",\n    \"ch\": \"把那個沉重的箱子搬上樓梯很費力。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她說完後，出現了一段尷尬的沉默。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3263,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::bankrupt::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He was declared ____ and had to sell all his assets.","expectedAnswer":"bankrupt","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He was declared ____ and had to sell all his assets.","clozeAnswer":"bankrupt","exampleTranslation":"他被宣布破產，不得不出售所有資產。","reference":{"eng":"bankrupt","kk":"/ˈbæŋkrʌpt/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['破產的；倒閉的']]","chEntries":["破產的","倒閉的"],"practiceMeaning":"他被宣布破產，不得不出售所有資產。","analysis":"源自義大利語 'banca rotta'，意為「壞的長凳」。在中世紀，銀行家（banker）若無力償債，其交易的長凳（bench）會被打破，象徵其破產。此詞語意逐漸演變為指財政上的破產。","definition":"declared in law unable to pay one's debts.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company went bankrupt after a year of losses.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司在虧損一年後破產了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was declared bankrupt and had to sell all his assets.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他被宣布破產，不得不出售所有資產。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他被宣布破產，不得不出售所有資產。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3203,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::beg::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"I ____ you to reconsider your decision.","expectedAnswer":"beg","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"I ____ you to reconsider your decision.","clozeAnswer":"beg","exampleTranslation":"我懇求您重新考慮您的決定。","reference":{"eng":"beg","kk":"/bɛɡ/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['乞求'], ['懇求'], ['請求']]","chEntries":["乞求","懇求","請求"],"practiceMeaning":"我懇求您重新考慮您的決定。","analysis":"詞源可能來自古英語 'beggan'，意為 'to pray'，引申為『向他人祈求，尤指金錢或食物』。也可用於比喻，表示極度懇切地請求或期望某事，即使非物質性的。其名詞是 'beggar'。","definition":"1. ask someone earnestly or humbly for something; 2. ask for (something) in order to live; 3. implore or entreat.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He had to beg for food after losing his job.\",\n    \"ch\": \"失業後，他不得不乞求食物。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I beg you to reconsider your decision.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我懇求您重新考慮您的決定。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Don't beg for mercy; you don't deserve it.\",\n    \"ch\": \"不要乞求憐憫；你不配。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我懇求您重新考慮您的決定。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U41"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4198,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::benefit::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She receives unemployment ____.","expectedAnswer":"benefit","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She receives unemployment ____.","clozeAnswer":"benefit","exampleTranslation":"她領取失業救濟金。","reference":{"eng":"benefit","kk":"/ˈbenɪfɪt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['益處；好處'], ['（保險、退休金等的）給付；補助金'], ['（慈善）義演；義賣']]","chEntries":["益處","好處","給付","補助金","義演","義賣"],"practiceMeaning":"她領取失業救濟金。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 benefactum，意為“善行”，'bene-'（好）+ 'facere'（做）。核心是“好的結果”或“好事”。1. “益處；好處”是最廣泛的意義，指任何有利的事物。2. “給付；補助金”是特定領域（金融、福利）的專業用法，指提供的經濟上的好處。3. “義演；義賣”是引申義，指為了獲得“好處”（籌款）而舉行的活動。","definition":"1. an advantage or profit gained from something; 2. a payment made by the state or an insurance scheme to someone who is unable to work or who has lost their job; 3. an event held to raise money for a particular cause.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Regular exercise has many health benefits.\",\n    \"ch\": \"規律運動有很多健康益處。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She receives unemployment benefit.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她領取失業救濟金。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A charity benefit concert was held last night.\",\n    \"ch\": \"昨晚舉行了一場慈善義演音樂會。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她領取失業救濟金。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6110,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::bias::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This report is free from political ____.","expectedAnswer":"bias","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This report is free from political ____.","clozeAnswer":"bias","exampleTranslation":"這份報告沒有政治偏見。","reference":{"eng":"bias","kk":"ˈbaɪəs","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"偏見\"  ],  [    \"偏差\"  ],  [    \"偏心\"  ]]","chEntries":["偏見","偏差","偏心"],"practiceMeaning":"這份報告沒有政治偏見。","analysis":"此字詞源複雜，可能源自古法語 bis、「斜線；斜倚」，或來自義大利語 bias，意為「斜；偏見」。另一說法與骰子不均勻有關。在現代英語中，bias 主要指不公平的傾向、預斷或對某人、某事或某群體的預設偏愛或反感。也可指統計上的偏差。此名詞的語意演變是從具體的「斜向、傾斜」到抽象的「傾向、偏頗」。","definition":"1. prejudice in favor of or against one thing, person, or group compared with another, usually in a way considered to be unfair; 2. the tendency of a statistical sample to over-represent or under-represent some part of the population.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The judge was accused of bias.\",\n    \"ch\": \"法官被指控有偏見。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This report is free from political bias.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這份報告沒有政治偏見。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The experiment was designed to minimize bias.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該實驗的設計旨在將偏差降至最低。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這份報告沒有政治偏見。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5822,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::blast::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"A strong ____ of wind blew his hat off.","expectedAnswer":"blast","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"A strong ____ of wind blew his hat off.","clozeAnswer":"blast","exampleTranslation":"一陣強風吹掉了他的帽子。","reference":{"eng":"blast","kk":"blæst","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"爆炸\"  ],  [    \"衝擊波\"  ],  [    \"陣風\"  ],  [    \"巨響\"  ]]","chEntries":["爆炸","衝擊波","陣風","巨響"],"practiceMeaning":"一陣強風吹掉了他的帽子。","analysis":"此字詞源不明確，可能與原始日耳曼語 *blastaz（氣息、風）或 *blastōną（吹響）有關，與 'blossom'、'blow' 等詞有關聯。早期用於表示「爆炸」或「衝擊」。字義的演變可能與聲音或空氣的突然釋放有關。一個突發的、強烈的聲音或氣流可以被描述為 'blast'。例如，爆炸的衝擊波，或突然而強烈的風。現代語義擴展至形容音樂的「震耳欲聾」或「強烈的氣流」。例如，也可指「吹奏樂器的響亮聲音」。","definition":"1. An explosion or detonation.; 2. A strong gust of wind.; 3. A loud, short blast of a musical instrument or a siren.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The blast of the explosion was heard for miles.\",\n    \"ch\": \"爆炸的巨響遠達數英里。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A strong blast of wind blew his hat off.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一陣強風吹掉了他的帽子。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The ship's horn gave a loud blast.\",\n    \"ch\": \"船的汽笛發出響亮的鳴響。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The music hit us with a blast of sound.\",\n    \"ch\": \"音樂以震耳欲聾的聲響衝擊著我們。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"一陣強風吹掉了他的帽子。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5031,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::bound::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He is ____ to win the championship this year.","expectedAnswer":"bound","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He is ____ to win the championship this year.","clozeAnswer":"bound","exampleTranslation":"他今年註定會贏得錦標賽。","reference":{"eng":"bound","kk":"baʊnd","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['必然會的'], ['註定的']]","chEntries":["必然會的","註定的"],"practiceMeaning":"他今年註定會贏得錦標賽。","analysis":"此字來源於古英語 bunden（被捆綁的），與 bind 同源。在此意義下，bound 演變為「受（法律、道德、命運等）約束或限制」，進而引申為「必然會發生的」、「註定的」。其核心語意是「受到強烈約束或趨勢的引導」。","definition":"certain to happen; inevitable.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This decision is bound to have serious consequences.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個決定必然會產生嚴重後果。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is bound to win the championship this year.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他今年註定會贏得錦標賽。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他今年註定會贏得錦標賽。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5074,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::bruise::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Her harsh words left him with a ____ to his ego.","expectedAnswer":"bruise","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Her harsh words left him with a ____ to his ego.","clozeAnswer":"bruise","exampleTranslation":"她刻薄的話語傷了他的自尊心。","reference":{"eng":"bruise","kk":"bruːz","tense":"n.","ch":"[['瘀傷'], ['擦傷']]","chEntries":["瘀傷","擦傷"],"practiceMeaning":"她刻薄的話語傷了他的自尊心。","analysis":"此字源自古諾爾斯語 'brus'，意為 '腫塊、傷痕'，可能與 'brjosta' (to break) 有關。其核心語義是因撞擊或壓力造成的身體損傷，表現為皮膚下的出血或腫脹。此字不僅指物理上的傷害，也延伸至情感上的傷害，即 '心靈的創傷'。","definition":"1. An injury to a person or animal in which the skin is not broken but blood vessels beneath the skin are damaged, causing a dark area to appear on the skin.; 2. An emotional hurt or wound.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He fell and got a nasty bruise on his leg.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他摔倒了，腿上留下了一塊嚴重的瘀傷。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her harsh words left him with a bruise to his ego.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她刻薄的話語傷了他的自尊心。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她刻薄的話語傷了他的自尊心。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3127,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::brutal::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The winter weather in this region is absolutely ____.","expectedAnswer":"brutal","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The winter weather in this region is absolutely ____.","clozeAnswer":"brutal","exampleTranslation":"這個地區的冬季天氣非常嚴酷。","reference":{"eng":"brutal","kk":"/ˈbrutl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['殘酷的；野蠻的'], ['（天氣、情況等）嚴酷的；嚴重的'], ['（直率、粗魯地）坦率的']]","chEntries":["殘酷的","野蠻的","嚴酷的","嚴重的","坦率的"],"practiceMeaning":"這個地區的冬季天氣非常嚴酷。","analysis":"詞源來自拉丁語 'brutalis'，意為「動物性的，粗野的」，與 'brutus'（笨重的，遲鈍的）有關。最初形容像動物一樣沒有理性、野蠻的行為。'Brutal' 強調的是缺乏人性、殘忍、暴力和極端的嚴酷。其語意延伸至描述極端惡劣的條件或非常直接（甚至令人不舒服）的陳述。","definition":"1. savagely violent; 2. (of a person or their actions) cruel and aggressive; 3. (of weather or other natural phenomena) severe and harsh; 4. (of truth or statements) harsh and direct.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The dictator's regime was known for its brutal treatment of political prisoners.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位獨裁者的政權以其對政治犯的殘酷待遇而聞名。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The winter weather in this region is absolutely brutal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個地區的冬季天氣非常嚴酷。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He delivered the bad news in a brutal, no-nonsense way.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他以一種殘酷、不講情面的方式傳達了壞消息。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個地區的冬季天氣非常嚴酷。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4677,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::bunch::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"A ____ of grapes fell from the table.","expectedAnswer":"bunch","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"A ____ of grapes fell from the table.","clozeAnswer":"bunch","exampleTranslation":"一串葡萄從桌子上掉了下來。","reference":{"eng":"bunch","kk":"/ˈbʌntʃ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['一束'], ['一串'], ['（非正式）一群人']]","chEntries":["一束","一串","一群人"],"practiceMeaning":"一串葡萄從桌子上掉了下來。","analysis":"源自荷蘭語 *bonk*，意為「塊」、「團」，後演變為指將許多相似的物體聚集在一起形成的集合體。引申至一群人，帶有非正式、親切的語氣。","definition":"1. A number of things or people of the same kind growing or fastened together. 2. (informal) A group of people.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She bought a bunch of flowers at the market.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在市場買了一束花。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A bunch of grapes fell from the table.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一串葡萄從桌子上掉了下來。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A bunch of us are going to the concert.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們一群人要去聽演唱會。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"一串葡萄從桌子上掉了下來。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5506,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l5::burst::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Tears ____ from her eyes.","expectedAnswer":"burst","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Tears ____ from her eyes.","clozeAnswer":"burst","exampleTranslation":"眼淚奪眶而出。","reference":{"eng":"burst","kk":"bɜːrst","tense":"v.","ch":"[['爆炸'], ['迸發'], ['突然出現'], ['衝破'], ['充滿']]","chEntries":["爆炸","迸發","突然出現","衝破","充滿"],"practiceMeaning":"眼淚奪眶而出。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 'bursten' 或 'bresten'，與古英語 'berstan' 同源，後者可能來自原始日耳曼語 *berstana。其核心語義是「突然破裂」或「爆開」。構詞上，此字無明顯的字首、字根或字尾可供分析，應視為整體詞源演變。原始語義直接指向「破裂」的物理動作。現代英語中，'burst' 擴展為多種意義：指物體突然破裂（爆炸），指情感或能量突然釋放（迸發），指人或物突然出現或離開（衝破），或指充滿某種事物（充滿）。這些引申義都保留了「突然、瞬間」的特徵。","definition":"to break suddenly and unexpectedly; to appear or happen suddenly; to fill with strong emotion.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The balloon burst with a loud pop.\",\n    \"ch\": \"氣球砰地一聲爆炸了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Tears burst from her eyes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"眼淚奪眶而出。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The crowd burst into the stadium.\",\n    \"ch\": \"人群衝進了體育場。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"眼淚奪眶而出。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4119,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::capable::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He is ____ of handling this task.","expectedAnswer":"capable","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He is ____ of handling this task.","clozeAnswer":"capable","exampleTranslation":"他能夠處理這項任務。","reference":{"eng":"capable","kk":"/ˈkeɪpəbl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['有能力的', '能幹的'], ['能夠（做某事）的']]","chEntries":["有能力的","能幹的","能夠的"],"practiceMeaning":"他能夠處理這項任務。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 capabilis，由 capere（抓住、容納）+ -abilis（能夠）組成。核心概念是「有能力抓住（機會或任務）」或「能容納」。引申為具備某種技能、力量或潛力。","definition":"1. having the ability, fitness, or quality necessary to do or achieve a specified thing; 2. intelligent and quick to understand","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a very capable manager.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是一位非常有能力的經理。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is capable of handling this task.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他能夠處理這項任務。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Are you capable of understanding the seriousness of the situation?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你能夠理解局勢的嚴重性嗎？\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他能夠處理這項任務。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6064,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::chunk::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The report contained a long ____ of technical jargon.","expectedAnswer":"chunk","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The report contained a long ____ of technical jargon.","clozeAnswer":"chunk","exampleTranslation":"報告中包含一大段技術術語。","reference":{"eng":"chunk","kk":"tʃʌŋk","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"大塊\"  ],  [    \"厚片\"  ],  [    \"一段\"  ],  [    \"大量\"  ]]","chEntries":["大塊","厚片","一段","大量"],"practiceMeaning":"報告中包含一大段技術術語。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 chunk，語源不清，可能與「厚」或「大塊」的意象相關。在此作名詞，核心語義是一個「大而厚實的部分」。引申用法包括表示「一段」連續的內容（如一段文本或程式碼），或引申為「大量」的某物，特別是未經處理的材料。構詞上，這是一個單純的詞根詞，沒有顯著的前綴或後綴。","definition":"1. a thick, solid piece of something; 2. a large part or amount of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He ate a large chunk of cake.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他吃了一大塊蛋糕。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The report contained a long chunk of technical jargon.\",\n    \"ch\": \"報告中包含一大段技術術語。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to allocate a big chunk of our budget to marketing.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要將很大一部分預算分配給市場行銷。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"報告中包含一大段技術術語。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5829,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::circuit::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The race car driver completed another ____ of the track.","expectedAnswer":"circuit","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The race car driver completed another ____ of the track.","clozeAnswer":"circuit","exampleTranslation":"賽車手又完成了一圈賽道。","reference":{"eng":"circuit","kk":"ˈsɜːrkɪt","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"電路\"  ],  [    \"迴路\"  ],  [    \"巡迴路線\"  ],  [    \"週期\"  ],  [    \"環形\"  ]]","chEntries":["電路","迴路","巡迴路線","週期","環形"],"practiceMeaning":"賽車手又完成了一圈賽道。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'circuitus'，是 'circuire' (to go around) 的過去分詞，由 'circum' (around) 和 'ire' (to go) 構成。'Circuitus' 的字面意思是「繞行」，引申為「圍繞一圈的路線」或「封閉的循環」。在物理學上，'circuit' 指電流沿著封閉路徑流動的「電路」或「迴路」。在地理或旅行語境中，'circuit' 指「巡迴路線」，如馬戲團或表演團體的巡迴演出路線。它強調的是一種「循環」或「繞行」的概念。例如，也可指「一場比賽的賽道」。","definition":"1. A roughly circular or oval area or path.; 2. A complete electrical path, consisting of wires, components, and a power source.; 3. A route or journey that visits a number of places.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The electrician checked the electrical circuit.\",\n    \"ch\": \"電工檢查了電路。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The race car driver completed another circuit of the track.\",\n    \"ch\": \"賽車手又完成了一圈賽道。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They are planning a lecture circuit.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們正在規劃一個演講巡迴路線。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The Formula 1 circuit is known for its speed.\",\n    \"ch\": \"F1 賽道以其速度聞名。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"賽車手又完成了一圈賽道。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4044,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::civil::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He was always ____ to his neighbors.","expectedAnswer":"civil","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He was always ____ to his neighbors.","clozeAnswer":"civil","exampleTranslation":"他對鄰居總是很有禮貌。","reference":{"eng":"civil","kk":"/ˈsɪvəl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['公民的', '國民的'], ['文明的', '有禮貌的'], ['國內的', '非軍事的']]","chEntries":["公民的","國民的","文明的","有禮貌的","國內的","非軍事的"],"practiceMeaning":"他對鄰居總是很有禮貌。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'civilis'，意為「屬於公民的」、「適合公民的」。'civilis' 又來自 'civis'，意為「市民」、「公民」。核心概念是與「社會」、「國家」或「群體」有關，而非個人或軍事。因此，延伸出「公民的」事務、「文明的」行為（與野蠻相對），以及「國內的」衝突（與戰爭相對）。","definition":"1. relating to a citizen or the state; 2. polite and behaving in a calm and controlled way; 3. relating to the internal affairs of a country, especially in contrast to war or military matters","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"公民權利是民主的基石。\",\n    \"eng\": \"Civil rights are fundamental to democracy.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他對鄰居總是很有禮貌。\",\n    \"eng\": \"He was always civil to his neighbors.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"該國捲入了內戰。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The country has been involved in a civil war.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他對鄰居總是很有禮貌。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5584,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::classic::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This album is a ____ of 1970s rock music.","expectedAnswer":"classic","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This album is a ____ of 1970s rock music.","clozeAnswer":"classic","exampleTranslation":"這張專輯是 70 年代搖滾樂的經典之作。","reference":{"eng":"classic","kk":"ˈklæsɪk","tense":"n.","ch":"[['經典作品'], ['傑作'], ['經典人物']]","chEntries":["經典作品","傑作","經典人物"],"practiceMeaning":"這張專輯是 70 年代搖滾樂的經典之作。","analysis":"這是 \"classic\" 作形容詞的相關名詞形式，源自拉丁語 \"classicus\"，意為 \"of or belonging to the highest class, first-class\"（屬於最高級別的，一流的）。 \"classic\" 作形容詞時，指「屬於最高等級、最經典、最受推崇的」。 \"classic\" 作為名詞，通常指「一部在藝術、文學、音樂等領域被認為具有最高水準、經久不衰的作品」，例如「傑作」。它也可以指「代表某一類型最高水準的人物或事物」。","definition":"1. A work of art of the highest quality, significance, and lasting appeal; 2. A person or thing considered best of its kind.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Shakespeare's plays are considered literary classics.\",\n    \"ch\": \"莎士比亞的戲劇被認為是文學經典。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This album is a classic of 1970s rock music.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這張專輯是 70 年代搖滾樂的經典之作。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這張專輯是 70 年代搖滾樂的經典之作。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6068,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::clause::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This is a subordinate ____.","expectedAnswer":"clause","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This is a subordinate ____.","clozeAnswer":"clause","exampleTranslation":"這是一個從句。","reference":{"eng":"clause","kk":"klɔz","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"條款\"  ],  [    \"子句\"  ],  [    \"從句\"  ]]","chEntries":["條款","子句","從句"],"practiceMeaning":"這是一個從句。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 clausa（closed thing, conclusion），是 claudere（to close）的過去分詞。核心語義是「關閉」或「封閉」，引申為「段落」、「條款」或「獨立的部分」。在法律或契約中，clause 指的是一份文件的「條款」。在語法中，clause 指的是一個包含主語和謂語的「子句」或「從句」。構詞上，-clause 是來自 claudere 的詞幹，沒有顯著的現代前綴或後綴。","definition":"1. a particular statement or condition in a treaty, law, or contract; 2. a group of words containing a subject and a verb, forming part of a sentence.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The contract includes a clause that allows for early termination.\",\n    \"ch\": \"合約包含一條允許提前終止的條款。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a subordinate clause.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個從句。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Each clause in the bill was debated thoroughly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"法案中的每一條都被詳細辯論了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是一個從句。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4320,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::clay::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The children played with modeling ____.","expectedAnswer":"clay","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The children played with modeling ____.","clozeAnswer":"clay","exampleTranslation":"孩子們玩黏土。","reference":{"eng":"clay","kk":"/kleɪ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['黏土；陶土']]","chEntries":["黏土","陶土"],"practiceMeaning":"孩子們玩黏土。","analysis":"源自古英語 'clæg'，與荷蘭語 'klei' 和德語 'Klei' 同源。指的是一種由細小的礦物顆粒組成的泥土，遇水後有黏性，可塑性強，是製作陶器、磚塊等的材料。其核心特徵是『黏性』和『可塑性』。","definition":"earth that is soft and sticky when wet, and becomes hard when it is dry or when it is baked, used for making pots, bricks, etc.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The potter shaped the clay into a beautiful vase.\",\n    \"ch\": \"陶工將黏土塑造成一個美麗的花瓶。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The children played with modeling clay.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子們玩黏土。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Ancient houses were often built of clay bricks.\",\n    \"ch\": \"古代的房屋常由黏土磚建造。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"孩子們玩黏土。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6113,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::clinical::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She has a very ____ approach to her work.","expectedAnswer":"clinical","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She has a very ____ approach to her work.","clozeAnswer":"clinical","exampleTranslation":"她對工作有非常客觀的態度。","reference":{"eng":"clinical","kk":"ˈklɪnɪkəl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"臨床的\"  ],  [    \"診所的\"  ],  [    \"冷淡的\"  ],  [    \"客觀的\"  ],  [    \"嚴謹的\"  ]]","chEntries":["臨床的","診所的","冷淡的","客觀的","嚴謹的"],"practiceMeaning":"她對工作有非常客觀的態度。","analysis":"此字源自希臘語 klinikos，意為「臥室的；床邊的」，與 klinikē（醫術；臨床醫學）有關，而 klinikē 又源自 kline（床）。因此，clinical 的核心語義是與「床邊」或「病床旁」相關，即與直接醫治病人相關。現代用法包括與醫療診斷、治療和研究相關（臨床的），以及引申為冷淡、客觀、不帶感情的（冷淡的；客觀的）。此形容詞的語意演變是從具體的「病床邊」到抽象的「客觀、不帶感情」。","definition":"1. relating to or used in a clinic or the observation and treatment of patients; 2. clinically detached or objective; unemotional.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"clinical trials of the new drug\",\n    \"ch\": \"新藥的臨床試驗\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a very clinical approach to her work.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對工作有非常客觀的態度。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The doctor gave him a clinical examination.\",\n    \"ch\": \"醫生對他進行了臨床檢查。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她對工作有非常客觀的態度。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4506,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::clumsy::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ waiter dropped the tray.","expectedAnswer":"clumsy","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ waiter dropped the tray.","clozeAnswer":"clumsy","exampleTranslation":"那個笨拙的服務員打翻了托盤。","reference":{"eng":"clumsy","kk":"/ˈklʌmzi/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['笨拙的'], ['不靈巧的'], ['（東西）笨重的']]","chEntries":["笨拙的","不靈巧的","笨重的"],"practiceMeaning":"那個笨拙的服務員打翻了托盤。","analysis":"源自古挪威語 klumsa，意為「笨拙」、「無能」。核心語意是「動作不協調」、「不靈巧」。","definition":"1. Awkward in movement or in handling things; 2. (of an object) large, heavy, and awkward to use.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was a clumsy child, always tripping over his own feet.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一個笨拙的孩子，總是絆倒自己的腳。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The clumsy waiter dropped the tray.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那個笨拙的服務員打翻了托盤。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The furniture was old and clumsy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這些傢俱又老又笨重。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"那個笨拙的服務員打翻了托盤。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4076,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::coach::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We took a ____ to London.","expectedAnswer":"coach","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We took a ____ to London.","clozeAnswer":"coach","exampleTranslation":"我們搭乘長途巴士去了倫敦。","reference":{"eng":"coach","kk":"/koʊtʃ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['教練'], ['長途馬車', '巴士'], ['（火車的）頭等車廂']]","chEntries":["教練","長途馬車","巴士","頭等車廂"],"practiceMeaning":"我們搭乘長途巴士去了倫敦。","analysis":"第一個義項「教練」的詞源來自匈牙利語 'kocsi' (a carriage)，最初指15世紀匈牙利科西鎮（Kocs）生產的一種馬車。後來，牛津大學的學生用它來比喻「（能載人順利通過考試的）導師」或「私人教師」。引申到體育領域，即「訓練運動員的教練」。第二個義項「長途馬車」、「巴士」則是直接繼承了馬車的原意。第三個義項「火車車廂」也是由馬車引申而來，指專門的車廂。","definition":"1. a person who trains athletes or sports teams; 2. a large bus used for carrying passengers, especially on long journeys; 3. a private railway carriage","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"教練激勵隊伍取勝。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The coach motivated the team to win.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"我們搭乘長途巴士去了倫敦。\",\n    \"eng\": \"We took a coach to London.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他是籃球隊的主教練。\",\n    \"eng\": \"He is the head coach of the basketball team.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們搭乘長途巴士去了倫敦。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6158,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::coherent::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She found it difficult to make a ____ speech.","expectedAnswer":"coherent","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She found it difficult to make a ____ speech.","clozeAnswer":"coherent","exampleTranslation":"她發現很難發表一篇條理清晰的演講。","reference":{"eng":"coherent","kk":"koʊˈhɪərənt","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"連貫的\"  ],  [    \"條理清晰的\"  ],  [    \"前後一致的\"  ],  [    \"能理解的\"  ]]","chEntries":["連貫的","條理清晰的","前後一致的","能理解的"],"practiceMeaning":"她發現很難發表一篇條理清晰的演講。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 cohaerēns，是 cohaerēre「緊密結合、一致」的現在分詞。cohaerēre 由 com- (together) + haerēre (to stick, cling) 組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 com-「一起」和 haerēre「黏合」是其核心語意來源。作為形容詞，其核心語義是「緊密結合，能夠清晰地理解」。從「黏合在一起」引申出「條理清晰、前後一致、易於理解」的語義，特別用於描述論點、計劃或思緒。詞源中的「黏合」概念是其連結性和一致性的基礎。","definition":"1. logical and consistent; 2. able to be understood or believed; 3. forming a whole; 4. (of a group of people) united.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His argument was coherent and well-supported.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的論點連貫且有充分的證據支持。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She found it difficult to make a coherent speech.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她發現很難發表一篇條理清晰的演講。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The team needs to present a coherent plan.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個團隊需要提出一個前後一致的計畫。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"After the accident, he was unable to speak in a coherent manner.\",\n    \"ch\": \"事故發生後，他無法清晰地表達。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她發現很難發表一篇條理清晰的演講。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6212,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::combat::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The country has been involved in a protracted ____ with rebels.","expectedAnswer":"combat","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The country has been involved in a protracted ____ with rebels.","clozeAnswer":"combat","exampleTranslation":"該國捲入了與叛軍的長期戰鬥。","reference":{"eng":"combat","kk":"ˈkɒmbæt","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"戰鬥\"  ],  [    \"戰爭\"  ],  [    \"鬥爭\"  ],  [    \"搏鬥\"  ]]","chEntries":["戰鬥","戰爭","鬥爭","搏鬥"],"practiceMeaning":"該國捲入了與叛軍的長期戰鬥。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 combat，由 com-（一起）和 batre（打擊）組成，意為「共同打擊」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。名詞義指軍隊或個人之間進行的激烈對抗、武裝衝突或搏鬥，也引申為任何形式的鬥爭或抗爭。中文翻譯為「戰鬥；戰爭；鬥爭；搏鬥」。","definition":"1. fighting between armed forces; 2. fighting or struggling against something, such as a problem or a disease.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The soldiers were trained for combat.\",\n    \"ch\": \"士兵們接受了戰鬥訓練。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The country has been involved in a protracted combat with rebels.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該國捲入了與叛軍的長期戰鬥。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This organization is dedicated to the combat of poverty.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個組織致力於與貧困作鬥爭。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該國捲入了與叛軍的長期戰鬥。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4340,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::comfort::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His words offered ____ to the grieving family.","expectedAnswer":"comfort","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His words offered ____ to the grieving family.","clozeAnswer":"comfort","exampleTranslation":"他的話語給悲傷的家庭帶來了安慰。","reference":{"eng":"comfort","kk":"/ˈkʌmfərt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['舒適；安慰'], ['令人感到舒適的東西或人']]","chEntries":["舒適","安慰","令人感到舒適的東西或人"],"practiceMeaning":"他的話語給悲傷的家庭帶來了安慰。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'confortare'，意為 'to make strong, strengthen'，由 'con-' (with) 和 'fortis' (strong) 構成。最初是『使堅強、使有力』，引申為『使心情舒暢、得到慰藉』，從而產生『舒適』和『安慰』的含義。1. 指身心上的『舒適、安慰』的狀態。2. 指提供這種感受的『人或物』。","definition":"a state of physical ease and freedom from pain or constraint; the relief of a person's feelings of grief or distress","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The warm room provided great comfort.\",\n    \"ch\": \"溫暖的房間帶來極大的舒適。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His words offered comfort to the grieving family.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的話語給悲傷的家庭帶來了安慰。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She found comfort in listening to music.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她從聽音樂中找到了慰藉。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他的話語給悲傷的家庭帶來了安慰。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U8、L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6216,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::commitment::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Her ____ to her work is admirable.","expectedAnswer":"commitment","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Her ____ to her work is admirable.","clozeAnswer":"commitment","exampleTranslation":"她對工作的投入令人欽佩。","reference":{"eng":"commitment","kk":"kəˈmɪtmənt","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"承諾\"  ],  [    \"保證\"  ],  [    \"投入\"  ],  [    \"奉獻\"  ],  [    \"責任\"  ],  [    \"委身\"  ]]","chEntries":["承諾","保證","投入","奉獻","責任","委身"],"practiceMeaning":"她對工作的投入令人欽佩。","analysis":"此字由動詞 commit（承諾；委託；犯罪）加上名詞字尾 -ment（表示狀態、行為、結果）構成。commit 源自拉丁語 committere，意為「交付；委託」。字尾 -ment 將動詞轉為名詞，表示「承諾的行為或狀態」、「盡責的狀態」、「奉獻的狀態」。核心語義是將自己投入某事，或對某事做出堅定的保證。中文翻譯為「承諾；保證；投入；奉獻；責任；委身」。","definition":"1. a promise to do something or to behave in a particular way; 2. the state or quality of being dedicated to a cause, activity, etc.; 3. a long-term obligation or responsibility.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He made a commitment to finish the project on time.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他承諾按時完成這個項目。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her commitment to her work is admirable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對工作的投入令人欽佩。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Marriage is a serious commitment.\",\n    \"ch\": \"婚姻是一項嚴肅的承諾。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They have a strong commitment to environmental protection.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們對環保有堅定的承諾。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她對工作的投入令人欽佩。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4066,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::connect::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It's important to ____ with your colleagues.","expectedAnswer":"connect","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It's important to ____ with your colleagues.","clozeAnswer":"connect","exampleTranslation":"與同事建立良好的聯繫是很重要的。","reference":{"eng":"connect","kk":"/kəˈnɛkt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['連接', '連結'], ['與...取得聯繫', '交往'], ['（思想、事物）聯繫起來']]","chEntries":["連接","連結","與...取得聯繫","交往","聯繫起來"],"practiceMeaning":"與同事建立良好的聯繫是很重要的。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'connectere'，由 'con-' (together) + 'nectere' (to bind, to tie) 構成，字面意思是「一起綁」。核心是「聯合」、「繫在一起」。引申為物理上的「連接」、人際上的「聯繫」，以及觀念上的「連結」或「聯想」。","definition":"1. to join or be joined together; 2. to communicate with someone; 3. to associate one thing with another","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"這些線路將電腦連接到網際網路。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The wires connect the computer to the internet.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"與同事建立良好的聯繫是很重要的。\",\n    \"eng\": \"It's important to connect with your colleagues.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他無法將這些事實聯繫起來。\",\n    \"eng\": \"He can't connect the facts.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"與同事建立良好的聯繫是很重要的。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5773,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::consecutive::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The team had a streak of five ____ victories.","expectedAnswer":"consecutive","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The team had a streak of five ____ victories.","clozeAnswer":"consecutive","exampleTranslation":"這支隊伍取得了五連勝。","reference":{"eng":"consecutive","kk":"kənˈsɛkjʊtɪv","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"連續的\"  ],  [    \"接連的\"  ],  [    \"相繼的\"  ]]","chEntries":["連續的","接連的","相繼的"],"practiceMeaning":"這支隊伍取得了五連勝。","analysis":"此字為形容詞，構詞自con-（全部；一起）+ -secut-（跟隨；繼承，來自拉丁語sequi「跟隨」）+ -ive（形容詞字尾，表示「性質的；傾向的」）。con-源自拉丁語cum，表示「一起」或「加強」。-secut-是sequi的詞幹，sequi的過去分詞是secutus。-ive字尾源自拉丁語-ivus。因此，consecutive的核心語義是「連續跟隨的；一個接一個的」。語意演變上，從「跟隨」的動作引申為「時間或空間上連續不斷」的狀態。","definition":"1. following continuously or without interruption; 2. in unbroken or logical sequence.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She won the award for three consecutive years.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她連續三年贏得該獎項。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The team had a streak of five consecutive victories.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這支隊伍取得了五連勝。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please list the numbers in consecutive order.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請按順序列出數字。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這支隊伍取得了五連勝。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5491,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::consequent::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She made some unwise choices, and the ____ problems were severe.","expectedAnswer":"consequent","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She made some unwise choices, and the ____ problems were severe.","clozeAnswer":"consequent","exampleTranslation":"她做出了一些不明智的選擇，隨之而來的問題也很嚴重。","reference":{"eng":"consequent","kk":"ˈkɑnsəkwɛnt","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['因此而起的'], ['必然的'], ['結果的']]","chEntries":["因此而起的","必然的","結果的"],"practiceMeaning":"她做出了一些不明智的選擇，隨之而來的問題也很嚴重。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'consequens'，是動詞 'consequi'（跟隨、達成）的現在分詞。'Con-'（一起）+ 'sequi'（跟隨）。'Consequent' 作形容詞，意思是「隨之發生的、結果性的」。它用來描述某事是某個原因或事件的直接結果。與 'consequence'（名詞）對應，'consequent' 強調的是「由先前的事件所引發的」這種關聯性。","definition":"1. Happening as a result of something.; 2. Following as a logical or natural result.; 3. Following in order or succession.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The consequent reduction in traffic was noticeable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"隨之而來的交通量減少是顯而易見的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She made some unwise choices, and the consequent problems were severe.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她做出了一些不明智的選擇，隨之而來的問題也很嚴重。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This policy change has many consequent effects.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這項政策變更會產生許多連帶影響。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她做出了一些不明智的選擇，隨之而來的問題也很嚴重。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4491,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::controller::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The thermostat is a temperature ____.","expectedAnswer":"controller","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The thermostat is a temperature ____.","clozeAnswer":"controller","exampleTranslation":"恆溫器是一個溫度控制器。","reference":{"eng":"controller","kk":"/kənˈtroʊlər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['控制者'], ['控制器'], ['（公司）財務主管']]","chEntries":["控制者","控制器","財務主管"],"practiceMeaning":"恆溫器是一個溫度控制器。","analysis":"源自 control (控制)。加上 -er (表示「做某事的人或物」的名詞後綴)。核心語意是「負責控制者」。引申為控制裝置（如飛機的操縱桿），或公司中負責財務管理的人員（財務主管）。","definition":"1. A person or thing that controls or directs something; 2. A device used to control the operation of a machine or system; 3. (in business) A person who manages the finances of a company or organization.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The pilot is the controller of the aircraft.\",\n    \"ch\": \"飛行員是飛機的操控者。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The thermostat is a temperature controller.\",\n    \"ch\": \"恆溫器是一個溫度控制器。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company's controller presented the quarterly financial report.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司的財務主管提出了季度財務報告。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"恆溫器是一個溫度控制器。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5777,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::controversial::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It is a ____ issue with strong opinions on both sides.","expectedAnswer":"controversial","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It is a ____ issue with strong opinions on both sides.","clozeAnswer":"controversial","exampleTranslation":"這是一個有爭議的問題，雙方都有強烈的意見。","reference":{"eng":"controversial","kk":"ˌkɑntrəˈvɜrʃəl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"有爭議的\"  ],  [    \"引起爭議的\"  ]]","chEntries":["有爭議的","引起爭議的"],"practiceMeaning":"這是一個有爭議的問題，雙方都有強烈的意見。","analysis":"此字為形容詞，構詞自controversy（爭議）+ -ial（形容詞字尾，表示「關於……的；具有……性質的」）。-ial與-al同源，都源自拉丁語-alis。controversy本身源自拉丁語controversia，由con-（一起）+vertere（轉動；扭轉）組成，原意為「爭辯；爭論」，即雙方觀點不斷轉變、交鋒。因此，controversial的核心語義是指「容易引起爭論或爭議的」。語意演變上，由「爭論」的概念引申為「具有爭議性的」狀態。","definition":"1. giving rise or likely to give rise to public disagreement.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The politician's statement about immigration was highly controversial.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那位政治人物關於移民的聲明引起了極大的爭議。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It is a controversial issue with strong opinions on both sides.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個有爭議的問題，雙方都有強烈的意見。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The new policy is considered controversial by many.\",\n    \"ch\": \"許多人認為這項新政策是有爭議的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是一個有爭議的問題，雙方都有強烈的意見。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5778,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::controversy::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There is ongoing ____ over the new environmental regulations.","expectedAnswer":"controversy","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There is ongoing ____ over the new environmental regulations.","clozeAnswer":"controversy","exampleTranslation":"關於新的環保條例，持續存在爭議。","reference":{"eng":"controversy","kk":"ˈkɑntrəˌvɜrsi","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"爭議\"  ],  [    \"爭論\"  ]]","chEntries":["爭議","爭論"],"practiceMeaning":"關於新的環保條例，持續存在爭議。","analysis":"此字為名詞，源自拉丁語controversia，由con-（一起）+vertere（轉動；扭轉）組成，原意是「互相扭轉；爭辯；爭論」。字面意思是指雙方觀點不斷交鋒、扭轉的狀態。核心語義是指「公開的、嚴重的爭論或爭議」，通常涉及對某事物的不同意見或衝突。語意演變上，從「爭辯」的動作發展為「爭論」的狀態或議題。","definition":"1. public disagreement about something that many people have strong opinions about; 2. a lengthy dispute or debate.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The recent art exhibition has sparked a lot of controversy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"最近的藝術展覽引發了許多爭議。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There is ongoing controversy over the new environmental regulations.\",\n    \"ch\": \"關於新的環保條例，持續存在爭議。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The film's ending generated considerable controversy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這部電影的結局引起了相當大的爭議。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"關於新的環保條例，持續存在爭議。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3902,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::costly::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Expensive cars can be very ____ to maintain.","expectedAnswer":"costly","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Expensive cars can be very ____ to maintain.","clozeAnswer":"costly","exampleTranslation":"昂貴的汽車可能維護費用很高。","reference":{"eng":"costly","kk":"/ˈkɔːstli/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['昂貴的'], ['代價高昂的']]","chEntries":["昂貴的","代價高昂的"],"practiceMeaning":"昂貴的汽車可能維護費用很高。","analysis":"由 'cost' (成本) 加上形容詞後綴 '-ly' 組成。核心是「有高成本」。指價格高昂，或需要付出巨大代價（不一定是金錢）才能達成或維持。","definition":"1. costing a great deal of money; expensive. 2. involving a great loss or sacrifice.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a costly mistake.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個代價高昂的錯誤。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Expensive cars can be very costly to maintain.\",\n    \"ch\": \"昂貴的汽車可能維護費用很高。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The war proved to be very costly for both sides.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這場戰爭對雙方都 proved to be very costly。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"昂貴的汽車可能維護費用很高。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5608,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l7::council::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The student ____ organized the school fair.","expectedAnswer":"council","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The student ____ organized the school fair.","clozeAnswer":"council","exampleTranslation":"學生會組織了學校的慶典活動。","reference":{"eng":"council","kk":"ˈkaʊnsl","tense":"n.","ch":"[['委員會'], ['理事會'], ['議會']]","chEntries":["委員會","理事會","議會"],"practiceMeaning":"學生會組織了學校的慶典活動。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 'conseil'（建議、會議），它本身源於拉丁語 'consilium'（商議、建議、會議），而 'consilium' 又源於 'consulere'（商議、諮詢）。構詞學上，核心是與「商議」、「建議」相關的詞根，加上名詞化後綴。'-cil' 或 '-cilium' 是常見的拉丁語後綴，表示「地方」或「集合」。因此，'council' 的原始語意是「一個進行商議或提供建議的群體或場所」。現代意義主要指「由選出或任命的人組成的、具有諮詢或決策權的機構」。","definition":"1. An advisory, deliberative, or legislative body of people; 2. A body of people elected or appointed to serve in a local government.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The city council voted on the new zoning laws.\",\n    \"ch\": \"市議會就新的分區法案進行了投票。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The student council organized the school fair.\",\n    \"ch\": \"學生會組織了學校的慶典活動。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The committee serves as an advisory council to the president.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該委員會作為總統的諮詢委員會。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"學生會組織了學校的慶典活動。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3134,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::crash::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"A system ____ caused the loss of all data.","expectedAnswer":"crash","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"A system ____ caused the loss of all data.","clozeAnswer":"crash","exampleTranslation":"系統崩潰導致所有數據丟失。","reference":{"eng":"crash","kk":"/kræʃ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['碰撞；墜毀'], ['（電腦系統等的）故障，崩潰'], ['（價格的）暴跌'], ['（尤指在某種場合，為了尋求某物而）混進去；不請自來']]","chEntries":["碰撞","墜毀","故障，崩潰","暴跌","混進去","不請自來"],"practiceMeaning":"系統崩潰導致所有數據丟失。","analysis":"名詞用法，源自動詞 'crash'。指「碰撞」或「墜毀」的事件。也指電腦系統或程式的「故障」或「崩潰」，以及金融市場的「暴跌」。'Crash' 也可以指非正式的「混進」某個派對或場合，通常是沒有被邀請的。","definition":"1. a violent impact or collision; 2. a sudden failure of a computer system or program; 3. a sudden and dramatic fall in prices or values; 4. (informal) an act of attending a party or event uninvited.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police are investigating the cause of the car crash.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警方正在調查這起車禍的原因。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A system crash caused the loss of all data.\",\n    \"ch\": \"系統崩潰導致所有數據丟失。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He decided to crash the party since he wasn't invited.\",\n    \"ch\": \"既然沒有被邀請，他決定混進派對。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The stock market crash of 1929 had devastating consequences.\",\n    \"ch\": \"1929年的股市崩盤帶來了毀滅性的後果。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"系統崩潰導致所有數據丟失。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3076,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::critical::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This is a ____ moment in the negotiations.","expectedAnswer":"critical","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This is a ____ moment in the negotiations.","clozeAnswer":"critical","exampleTranslation":"這是談判中的關鍵時刻。","reference":{"eng":"critical","kk":"/ˈkrɪtɪkl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['批判性的；挑剔的'], ['關鍵性的；重要的'], ['（情況）危急的；嚴重的'], ['（意見、評論）批評性的；評價性的']]","chEntries":["批判性的","挑剔的","關鍵性的","重要的","危急的","嚴重的","批評性的","評價性的"],"practiceMeaning":"這是談判中的關鍵時刻。","analysis":"源自希臘語 'kritikos' (able to judge)，是 'critic' 的形容詞形式。核心意義是「與判斷或評價相關」。\n1. 批判性的；挑剔的：指對事物進行仔細檢查，並指出其缺點或錯誤的態度。\n2. 關鍵性的；重要的：指對某事物的發展或成功至關重要的。\n3. （情況）危急的；嚴重的：指處於非常重要或危險的關頭，需要緊急處理。\n4. （意見、評論）批評性的；評價性的：指旨在分析和評價某事物優缺點的。","definition":"1. involving careful judgment or discriminating analysis; 2. extremely important or necessary; 3. involving the danger of failure or disaster; 4. expressing adverse or disapproving comments or judgments.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a critical attitude towards any new proposal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對任何新提案都持批判態度。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a critical moment in the negotiations.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是談判中的關鍵時刻。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The patient is in critical condition.\",\n    \"ch\": \"病人的情況危急。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His critical review of the book was widely read.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對這本書的評價性評論被廣泛閱讀。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是談判中的關鍵時刻。","sourceName":"字彙王、龍騰課本","unitName":"U39、L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5079,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::currency::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His ideas gained ____ among young people.","expectedAnswer":"currency","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His ideas gained ____ among young people.","clozeAnswer":"currency","exampleTranslation":"他的想法在年輕人中獲得了通用性。","reference":{"eng":"currency","kk":"ˈkɜːrənsi","tense":"n.","ch":"[['貨幣'], ['通用性'], ['流通']]","chEntries":["貨幣","通用性","流通"],"practiceMeaning":"他的想法在年輕人中獲得了通用性。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'currere' (to run)，透過中古英語 'curraunt' (running, current) 演變而來，與 'current' (當前的，流動的) 同源。其核心語義是 '流通的'。因此，'currency' 指的是在特定地區或國家被廣泛接受並用於交易的 '貨幣'。引申開來，它也指觀念、意見或事物的 '通用性' 或 '流行度'，即它們在當前社會中的 '流通' 程度。","definition":"1. A system of money in general use in a particular country.; 2. The quality or state of being current or generally accepted.; 3. General acceptance or prevalence.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The US dollar is a major international currency.\",\n    \"ch\": \"美元是主要的國際貨幣。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His ideas gained currency among young people.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的想法在年輕人中獲得了通用性。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The currency of this rumor is unknown.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個謠言的流通性（或說來源）不明。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他的想法在年輕人中獲得了通用性。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5291,"wordRef":"字彙王::u63::customs::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ officials inspected his luggage.","expectedAnswer":"customs","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ officials inspected his luggage.","clozeAnswer":"customs","exampleTranslation":"海關官員檢查了他的行李。","reference":{"eng":"customs","kk":"ˈkʌstəmz","tense":"n.","ch":"[['海關'], ['關稅', '進口稅'], ['（個人的）習慣，習俗']]","chEntries":["海關","關稅","進口稅","習慣，習俗"],"practiceMeaning":"海關官員檢查了他的行李。","analysis":"此字是 'custom' 的複數形式，但作為「海關」義時，通常使用複數 'customs'。'custom' 本身源自古法語 'custume'（習慣、稅收），最終來自拉丁語 'consuetudinem'（習慣、慣例）。'customs' 作為「海關」時，是指政府機關負責徵收關稅和管制進出口貨物。其核心語意從「慣例、習慣」引申為「例行徵收的稅款」（關稅），再引申為負責此事務的「海關」機構。","definition":"the place where you go to a country's airport or seaport to check on your luggage and goods, and where officers check if you are carrying anything illegal; taxes paid on goods imported into or exported from a country; the rules or habits that are traditional in a particular society or group.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"You must declare all goods at customs.\",\n    \"ch\": \"您必須在海關申報所有貨物。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The customs officials inspected his luggage.\",\n    \"ch\": \"海關官員檢查了他的行李。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Local customs dictate how guests are treated.\",\n    \"ch\": \"當地的習俗決定了如何對待客人。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"海關官員檢查了他的行李。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U63"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3286,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::deadly::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The situation was ____ serious.","expectedAnswer":"deadly","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The situation was ____ serious.","clozeAnswer":"deadly","exampleTranslation":"情況極其嚴重。","reference":{"eng":"deadly","kk":"/ˈdɛdli/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['致命的；可致死的'], ['極度的；極為的'], ['（尤指）極其安靜的；死一般的']]","chEntries":["致命的","可致死的","極度的","極為的","極其安靜的","死一般的"],"practiceMeaning":"情況極其嚴重。","analysis":"由 'dead' (死的) 加上 '-ly' (形容詞後綴) 構成。直接表示與死亡相關，即可以致人於死地。也可作副詞，形容程度之深，如「極度」。","definition":"1. causing or able to cause death; 2. extreme or very great; 3. very quiet.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The snake's venom is deadly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"蛇的毒液是致命的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The situation was deadly serious.\",\n    \"ch\": \"情況極其嚴重。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The room was deadly silent after the announcement.\",\n    \"ch\": \"宣布後，房間裡一片死寂。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"情況極其嚴重。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4114,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::decade::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The world has changed a lot in the past ____.","expectedAnswer":"decade","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The world has changed a lot in the past ____.","clozeAnswer":"decade","exampleTranslation":"在過去的十年裡，世界發生了巨大的變化。","reference":{"eng":"decade","kk":"/ˈdɛkeɪd/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['十年']]","chEntries":["十年"],"practiceMeaning":"在過去的十年裡，世界發生了巨大的變化。","analysis":"源自希臘語 dekas，意為「十個」。引申為一個持續十年的時間段。","definition":"a period of ten years","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company has been successful for over a decade.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司已經成功經營了十多年。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The world has changed a lot in the past decade.\",\n    \"ch\": \"在過去的十年裡，世界發生了巨大的變化。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He lived abroad for a decade.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在國外住了十年。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"在過去的十年裡，世界發生了巨大的變化。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4348,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::decrease::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The government is trying to ____ unemployment.","expectedAnswer":"decrease","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The government is trying to ____ unemployment.","clozeAnswer":"decrease","exampleTranslation":"政府正試圖減少失業率。","reference":{"eng":"decrease","kk":"/ˈdiːkriːs/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['減少；降低']]","chEntries":["減少","降低"],"practiceMeaning":"政府正試圖減少失業率。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'decrescere'，意為 'to grow less'，由 'de-' (down) 和 'crescere' (to grow) 構成。字面意思是『向下生長』，引申為『變少、降低』。","definition":"to become less or smaller","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The population of the town has decreased in recent years.\",\n    \"ch\": \"近年來，這個鎮的人口有所減少。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government is trying to decrease unemployment.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府正試圖減少失業率。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Sales have decreased by 10% this quarter.\",\n    \"ch\": \"本季銷售額下降了10%。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"政府正試圖減少失業率。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6220,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::deputy::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She is the ____ director of the department.","expectedAnswer":"deputy","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She is the ____ director of the department.","clozeAnswer":"deputy","exampleTranslation":"她是該部門的副主任。","reference":{"eng":"deputy","kk":"ˈdɛpjuti","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"代理人\"  ],  [    \"代表\"  ],  [    \"副手\"  ],  [    \"副官\"  ]]","chEntries":["代理人","代表","副手","副官"],"practiceMeaning":"她是該部門的副主任。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 deputé，意為「被派遣的，代表」，向上可追溯至拉丁語 deputare，由 de-（表示除去，關於）和 putare（認為，估計）組成，意為「認為是，指派」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。名詞義指被正式授權代表他人行事的人，或在特定職位上擔任次要或輔助角色的人，通常是該職位的主要負責人的助手或代理。中文翻譯為「代理人；代表；副手；副官」。","definition":"1. a person who is appointed to act for or replace someone else, especially in a political or official role; 2. a person who is second in command or assists someone in a position of authority.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The sheriff appointed a deputy to help manage the jail.\",\n    \"ch\": \"治安官任命了一名副手來協助管理監獄。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is the deputy director of the department.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是該部門的副主任。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The president's deputy attended the international summit.\",\n    \"ch\": \"總統的代表出席了國際峰會。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她是該部門的副主任。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5702,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l9::despair::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The situation seemed hopeless, filling them with ____.","expectedAnswer":"despair","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The situation seemed hopeless, filling them with ____.","clozeAnswer":"despair","exampleTranslation":"情況看似無望，讓他們充滿絕望。","reference":{"eng":"despair","kk":"dɪˈsper","tense":"n.","ch":"[['絕望'], ['失望']]","chEntries":["絕望","失望"],"practiceMeaning":"情況看似無望，讓他們充滿絕望。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 desespoir，由 de-（表示『否定』或『失去』，來自拉丁語 de-）+ espoir（希望，來自拉丁語 sperare，意為『希望』）構成。構詞上，'de-' 表示『失去』，'espoir' 表示『希望』。核心語意是「失去希望的狀態」。當希望完全喪失時，便產生極度的痛苦和沮喪感，即「絕望」。","definition":"the complete loss or absence of hope.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He sank into despair after failing the exam.\",\n    \"ch\": \"考試失敗後，他陷入了絕望。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The situation seemed hopeless, filling them with despair.\",\n    \"ch\": \"情況看似無望，讓他們充滿絕望。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"情況看似無望，讓他們充滿絕望。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3138,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::dew::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The morning ____ glistened on the spiderweb.","expectedAnswer":"dew","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The morning ____ glistened on the spiderweb.","clozeAnswer":"dew","exampleTranslation":"晨露在蜘蛛網上閃閃發光。","reference":{"eng":"dew","kk":"/djuː/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['露；露水']]","chEntries":["露","露水"],"practiceMeaning":"晨露在蜘蛛網上閃閃發光。","analysis":"詞源來自古英語 'deaw'，與「濕潤」的概念相關。'Dew' 是指夜間或清晨，空氣中的水蒸氣在較冷的物體表面凝結成的小水滴。它是一個自然現象，與清晨、新鮮、濕潤的環境聯繫在一起。其語意通常帶有清新、純潔或短暫的美好意象。","definition":"tiny drops of water that form on cool surfaces at night, when condensation occurs.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The grass was covered in dew when I woke up.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我醒來時，草地上覆蓋著露水。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The morning dew glistened on the spiderweb.\",\n    \"ch\": \"晨露在蜘蛛網上閃閃發光。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A fine dew settled on the leaves.\",\n    \"ch\": \"細密的露水落在葉子上。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"晨露在蜘蛛網上閃閃發光。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4174,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::difference::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"What's the ____ between these two products?","expectedAnswer":"difference","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"What's the ____ between these two products?","clozeAnswer":"difference","exampleTranslation":"這兩款產品有什麼區別？","reference":{"eng":"difference","kk":"/ˈdɪfərəns/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['差異', '區別'], ['（意見的）分歧'], ['重要性']]","chEntries":["差異","區別","分歧","重要性"],"practiceMeaning":"這兩款產品有什麼區別？","analysis":"源自拉丁語 differentia（差異），是動詞 differre（不同，延遲）的名詞形式。核心概念是「事物之間的不相同之處」。","definition":"1. a way in which a person or thing is not the same as another; 2. a disagreement or quarrel; 3. importance or relevance","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There is a significant difference between A and B.\",\n    \"ch\": \"A 和 B 之間存在顯著的差異。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"What's the difference between these two products?\",\n    \"ch\": \"這兩款產品有什麼區別？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His contribution made a real difference.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的貢獻帶來了真正的改變（重要性）。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這兩款產品有什麼區別？","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5040,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::disconnect::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We experienced a brief ____ with the internet.","expectedAnswer":"disconnect","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We experienced a brief ____ with the internet.","clozeAnswer":"disconnect","exampleTranslation":"我們經歷了一次短暫的網路斷線。","reference":{"eng":"disconnect","kk":"ˌdɪskəˈnekt","tense":"n.","ch":"[['斷開'], ['分離'], ['不連貫']]","chEntries":["斷開","分離","不連貫"],"practiceMeaning":"我們經歷了一次短暫的網路斷線。","analysis":"此字由否定前綴 dis-（分離、相反）和名詞 connection（連接）的動詞 connect（連接）派生。dis- 的否定作用與 connect 的「連接」意義結合，構成了「斷開連接、分離」的名詞用法。此名詞指「斷開的狀態」或「不連貫的感覺」，可指物理上的斷開，也可指抽象概念上的「失去聯繫」或「不一致」。","definition":"1. a state of being disconnected; 2. a lack of connection or continuity.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was a disconnect between his words and his actions.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的言行之間存在不一致。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We experienced a brief disconnect with the internet.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們經歷了一次短暫的網路斷線。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們經歷了一次短暫的網路斷線。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3078,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::disorder::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He suffers from a sleep ____.","expectedAnswer":"disorder","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He suffers from a sleep ____.","clozeAnswer":"disorder","exampleTranslation":"他患有睡眠失調症。","reference":{"eng":"disorder","kk":"/dɪsˈɔːrdər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['混亂；無秩序'], ['失調；疾病'], ['（政治、社會）動亂']]","chEntries":["混亂","無秩序","失調","疾病","動亂"],"practiceMeaning":"他患有睡眠失調症。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'dis-' (not) + 'ordo' (order)。核心意義是「缺乏秩序」。\n1. 混亂；無秩序：指缺乏組織、雜亂無章的狀態。\n2. 失調；疾病：指身體或精神功能的不正常、混亂的狀態，通常表現為疾病。\n3. （政治、社會）動亂：指社會秩序的破壞，例如騷亂或暴動。","definition":"1. a state of confusion; 2. a state of not being neat or tidy; 3. an illness or a medical condition that is not normal; 4. a disturbance of the peace.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The room was in a state of complete disorder.\",\n    \"ch\": \"房間裡一片混亂。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He suffers from a sleep disorder.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他患有睡眠失調症。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The protests quickly turned into disorder.\",\n    \"ch\": \"抗議活動很快演變成動亂。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他患有睡眠失調症。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5494,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::disturbance::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We experienced a power ____ during the storm.","expectedAnswer":"disturbance","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We experienced a power ____ during the storm.","clozeAnswer":"disturbance","exampleTranslation":"風暴期間我們經歷了電力中斷（干擾）。","reference":{"eng":"disturbance","kk":"dɪˈstɜrbəns","tense":"n.","ch":"[['干擾'], ['騷動'], ['妨礙']]","chEntries":["干擾","騷動","妨礙"],"practiceMeaning":"風暴期間我們經歷了電力中斷（干擾）。","analysis":"此字由動詞 'disturb'（打擾、干擾）加上名詞字尾 '-ance'（來自拉丁語 '-antia'）構成。'-ance' 用來形成表示「行為、狀態或過程」的名詞。因此，'disturbance' 指的是「打擾、干擾、擾亂」的行為或狀態。它是一個抽象名詞，描述了某種東西打破了原本的平靜、秩序或正常狀態的情況。","definition":"1. The interruption of a settled or peaceful condition.; 2. An act of disturbing.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The loud music caused a disturbance in the neighborhood.\",\n    \"ch\": \"吵鬧的音樂引起了社區的騷動。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We experienced a power disturbance during the storm.\",\n    \"ch\": \"風暴期間我們經歷了電力中斷（干擾）。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police were called to deal with a disturbance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警察被召來處理一起騷亂事件。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"風暴期間我們經歷了電力中斷（干擾）。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4548,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::dock::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The judge asked the prisoner to approach the ____.","expectedAnswer":"dock","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The judge asked the prisoner to approach the ____.","clozeAnswer":"dock","exampleTranslation":"法官請囚犯走近被告席。","reference":{"eng":"dock","kk":"/dɒk/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['碼頭', '泊位'], ['（法院的）被告席']]","chEntries":["碼頭","泊位","被告席"],"practiceMeaning":"法官請囚犯走近被告席。","analysis":"源自荷蘭語 'dok'，可能源自日耳曼語。\n    1. 碼頭、泊位：船隻停泊、裝卸貨物的場所。\n    2. 法院的被告席：專指被告在法庭上站立的地方，引申為被告的身份。","definition":"1. an enclosed area of water in a port where ships may be moored for loading or unloading.; 2. the place in a law court where a prisoner stands or is seated.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The ship is at the dock, unloading its cargo.\",\n    \"ch\": \"船正在碼頭卸貨。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The judge asked the prisoner to approach the dock.\",\n    \"ch\": \"法官請囚犯走近被告席。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"法官請囚犯走近被告席。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4355,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::domestic::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ chores include cooking and cleaning.","expectedAnswer":"Domestic","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ chores include cooking and cleaning.","clozeAnswer":"Domestic","exampleTranslation":"家務包括烹飪和清潔。","reference":{"eng":"domestic","kk":"/dəˈmɛstɪk/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['國內的；本土的'], ['家庭的；家用的'], ['（動物）馴養的']]","chEntries":["國內的","本土的","家庭的","家用的","馴養的"],"practiceMeaning":"家務包括烹飪和清潔。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'domesticus'，意為『家裡的』，來自 'domus' (house)。1. 指發生在國家『國內』的，與『國際』相對。2. 指與『家庭』相關的，如『家庭生活』、『家務』。3. 指被人類馴養的動物，如『家禽』、『家畜』，與『野生的』相對。","definition":"existing or occurring in a country or in domestic policy; relating to the running of a home or to family relations; kept or living at home and not wild","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company focuses on the domestic market.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司專注於國內市場。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Domestic chores include cooking and cleaning.\",\n    \"ch\": \"家務包括烹飪和清潔。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Dogs are domestic animals.\",\n    \"ch\": \"狗是馴養的動物。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"家務包括烹飪和清潔。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U8、L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5081,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::drought::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ has led to crop failures.","expectedAnswer":"drought","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ has led to crop failures.","clozeAnswer":"drought","exampleTranslation":"乾旱導致了農作物歉收。","reference":{"eng":"drought","kk":"draʊt","tense":"n.","ch":"[['乾旱'], ['長期嚴重缺乏']]","chEntries":["乾旱","長期嚴重缺乏"],"practiceMeaning":"乾旱導致了農作物歉收。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 'drūgath'，與 'dry' (乾燥) 同源。其核心語義是 '長期缺乏降水導致的乾燥狀態'。這個物理上的乾旱被廣泛引申為任何重要事物（如水、食物、金錢、靈感）的長期嚴重匱乏。這是一種比喻意義上的 '枯竭'。","definition":"1. A prolonged period of abnormally low rainfall, leading to a shortage of water.; 2. A long period when there is little or no rain.; 3. A long period during which there is a lack of something that is needed.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The region is