j.","ch":"[['效率高的', '功效大的'], ['（人）精幹的', '有能力的']]","chEntries":["效率高的","功效大的","精幹的","有能力的"],"practiceMeaning":"他是一位做事有效的經理。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'efficiens'，'efficere' (to accomplish - 完成、達成) 的現在分詞。核心概念是能夠有效且迅速地達成目標，不浪費資源。\n    1. 效率高的、功效大的：指在生產、工作或運轉時，以最少的投入獲得最大的產出。\n    2. 精幹的、有能力的：指個人在工作方面能夠高效地完成任務。","definition":"1. working or functioning in a way that achieves maximum productivity with minimum wasted effort or expense.; 2. (of a person) competent and capable.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a very efficient method of production.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一種非常高效的生產方法。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is an efficient manager who gets things done.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一位做事有效的經理。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The new system is more efficient than the old one.\",\n    \"ch\": \"新系統比舊系統更有效率。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他是一位做事有效的經理。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U11、L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5473,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::elaborate::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The report provided an ____ analysis of the situation.","expectedAnswer":"elaborate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The report provided an ____ analysis of the situation.","clozeAnswer":"elaborate","exampleTranslation":"這份報告對情況進行了詳盡的分析。","reference":{"eng":"elaborate","kk":"iˈlæbərət","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['精緻的'], ['詳盡的'], ['精心製作的']]","chEntries":["精緻的","詳盡的","精心製作的"],"practiceMeaning":"這份報告對情況進行了詳盡的分析。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'elaboratus'，是動詞 'elaborare'（努力工作、精製）的過去分詞。'Elaborare' 由 'e-'（出、完全）和 'laborare'（工作，來自 'labor'「勞動、工作」）構成。因此，'elaborate' 在形容詞形式下，表示「經過精心製作、詳盡闡述、內容豐富、細節繁多」的狀態。其核心語意是「付出了大量努力和細節」。","definition":"1. Involving many carefully arranged parts or details; detailed and complicated in design and planning.; 2. Developed or executed with great care and thoroughness.; 3. Intricate and richly decorated.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They wore elaborate costumes to the party.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們穿著精心製作的服裝去參加派對。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The report provided an elaborate analysis of the situation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這份報告對情況進行了詳盡的分析。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The architect designed an elaborate building with many ornate features.\",\n    \"ch\": \"建築師設計了一座精緻的建築，有許多華麗的特色。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這份報告對情況進行了詳盡的分析。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3283,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::elegant::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The mathematician found an ____ solution to the problem.","expectedAnswer":"elegant","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The mathematician found an ____ solution to the problem.","clozeAnswer":"elegant","exampleTranslation":"那位數學家找到了一個巧妙的解法來解決這個問題。","reference":{"eng":"elegant","kk":"/ˈɛlɪɡənt/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['優雅的；高雅的'], ['簡潔而有效的；別緻的'], ['（設計、想法等）巧妙的；精緻的']]","chEntries":["優雅的","高雅的","簡潔而有效的","別緻的","巧妙的","精緻的"],"practiceMeaning":"那位數學家找到了一個巧妙的解法來解決這個問題。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'elegans'，意為「有品味的，精緻的」。指具有高雅、精緻、得體的外表、風格或舉止。也可用於描述事物（如解決方案）的巧妙和簡潔。","definition":"1. graceful and stylish in appearance or manner; 2. pleasingly ingenious and simple.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She wore an elegant black dress to the party.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她穿著一襲優雅的黑裙參加派對。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The mathematician found an elegant solution to the problem.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那位數學家找到了一個巧妙的解法來解決這個問題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The hotel lobby was decorated in an elegant style.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家酒店的大廳裝潢風格高雅。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"那位數學家找到了一個巧妙的解法來解決這個問題。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4350,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::element::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Patience is an important ____ of success.","expectedAnswer":"element","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Patience is an important ____ of success.","clozeAnswer":"element","exampleTranslation":"耐心是成功的重要要素。","reference":{"eng":"element","kk":"/ˈɛlɪmənt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['元素（化學）'], ['要素；成分'], ['（惡劣的）天氣；（危險的）環境'], ['（微量的）痕跡']]","chEntries":["元素","要素","成分","天氣","環境","痕跡"],"practiceMeaning":"耐心是成功的重要要素。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'elementum'，意為 'first principle, rudiment, element'。1. 指化學上構成物質的『基本元素』。2. 指構成事物的『基本要素、成分』。3. 指『惡劣的環境、條件』，如風雨、寒冷等，強調其粗獷、基礎的性質。4. 指『微量、痕跡』，如『一絲』、『一點』，強調其是某事物最基礎、最簡單的部分。","definition":"a part of something, especially a system or plan; any of the four basic substances: earth, air, fire, and water; a substance that cannot be broken down into simpler substances by chemical means; a small trace of something","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Oxygen is an element.\",\n    \"ch\": \"氧氣是一種元素。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Patience is an important element of success.\",\n    \"ch\": \"耐心是成功的重要要素。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They were exposed to the elements.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們遭受了風雨的侵襲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was an element of truth in his statement.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的陳述中有一絲真理。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"耐心是成功的重要要素。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4139,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::elevator::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ was out of order.","expectedAnswer":"elevator","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ was out of order.","clozeAnswer":"elevator","exampleTranslation":"電梯故障了。","reference":{"eng":"elevator","kk":"/ˈɛlɪveɪtər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['電梯']]","chEntries":["電梯"],"practiceMeaning":"電梯故障了。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 elevatus，是動詞 elevare（舉起）的過去分詞。核心概念是「使升高」。引申為用來上下移動的裝置。","definition":"a platform or compartment housed in a shaft for raising and lowering people or things to or from various floors or levels","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please take the elevator to the fifth floor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請搭電梯到五樓。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The elevator was out of order.\",\n    \"ch\": \"電梯故障了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He pressed the button for the elevator.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他按了電梯按鈕。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"電梯故障了。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4323,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::emotional::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He is an ____ person who cries easily.","expectedAnswer":"emotional","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He is an ____ person who cries easily.","clozeAnswer":"emotional","exampleTranslation":"他是一個易感傷的人，很容易哭。","reference":{"eng":"emotional","kk":"/ɪˈmoʊʃənəl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['情緒的；感情的'], ['（人）易動情的；激動的'], ['（事件）引起強烈情感的']]","chEntries":["情緒的","感情的","易動情的","激動的","引起強烈情感的"],"practiceMeaning":"他是一個易感傷的人，很容易哭。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'emotio' (a moving, agitation)，來自 'emovere' (to move out, agitate)，由 'e-' (out) 和 'movere' (to move) 構成。核心意為『移出、攪動』，引申為內在情感的湧動。1. 指與『情感、情緒』相關的。2. 形容人『情感豐富、容易激動』。3. 形容事物『能引起強烈情感的』，觸動人心。","definition":"relating to or affecting the emotions; (of a person) having or showing strong feelings; causing strong feelings","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a very emotional response to music.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對音樂有非常感性的回應。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is an emotional person who cries easily.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一個易感傷的人，很容易哭。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The film was an emotional rollercoaster.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這部電影讓人情緒起伏不定。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他是一個易感傷的人，很容易哭。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6223,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::endorsement::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company announced its ____ of the new environmental policy.","expectedAnswer":"endorsement","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company announced its ____ of the new environmental policy.","clozeAnswer":"endorsement","exampleTranslation":"該公司宣布支持新的環保政策。","reference":{"eng":"endorsement","kk":"ɪnˈdɔrsmənt","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"認可\"  ],  [    \"贊同\"  ],  [    \"支持\"  ],  [    \"背書\"  ],  [    \"簽署\"  ]]","chEntries":["認可","贊同","支持","背書","簽署"],"practiceMeaning":"該公司宣布支持新的環保政策。","analysis":"此字由動詞 endorse（認可；背書）加上名詞字尾 -ment（表示行為、狀態、結果）構成。endorse 源自拉丁語 indorare。字尾 -ment 將動詞轉為名詞，表示「認可的行為或聲明」、「贊同的狀態」、「簽署的動作或證明」。核心語義是公開表達支持或認可，或票據背面的簽名。中文翻譯為「認可；贊同；支持；背書；簽署」。","definition":"1. the act of publicly declaring your approval of someone or something; 2. a statement or action that shows you support or approve of someone or something; 3. the act of signing one's name on the back of a check or bill of exchange.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The candidate received the endorsement of several prominent figures.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位候選人獲得了幾位知名人士的背書。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company announced its endorsement of the new environmental policy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司宣布支持新的環保政策。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"An endorsement on the check is required for transfer.\",\n    \"ch\": \"轉讓支票需要進行背書簽署。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該公司宣布支持新的環保政策。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5551,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::enterprise::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Starting a new business is always a risky ____.","expectedAnswer":"enterprise","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Starting a new business is always a risky ____.","clozeAnswer":"enterprise","exampleTranslation":"創辦新事業總是一項充滿風險的冒險。","reference":{"eng":"enterprise","kk":"ˈɛntərˌpraɪz","tense":"n.","ch":"[['企業'], ['事業'], ['公司'], ['進取心'], ['膽量'], ['冒險精神']]","chEntries":["企業","事業","公司","進取心","膽量","冒險精神"],"practiceMeaning":"創辦新事業總是一項充滿風險的冒險。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 \"entreprendre\"，意為 \"to undertake\"（承擔、著手做）。\"entre-\" 意為 \"between, among\"（在……之間），\"prendre\" 則意為 \"to take\"（拿取）。因此，\"enterprise\" 在語源上表示「承擔、著手去做的事情」。早期語義多指「冒險性的、艱鉅的任務」，引申出「膽量、進取心」。隨著商業發展，逐漸演變成指「企業、公司、事業」，尤其指那些有規模、有冒險精神的商業組織。因此，核心語義是「承擔某事」，進而發展出「任務、事業、企業」以及驅動這些事業所需的「進取心」和「膽量」。","definition":"1. A business organization, such as a company or a firm; also, the people who work for it; 2. A project or undertaking, especially one that is difficult, complicated, or requires effort; 3. Resourcefulness and readiness to undertake bold or difficult projects; courage and shrewdness.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company has grown into a large international enterprise.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司已發展成為一家大型的國際企業。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Starting a new business is always a risky enterprise.\",\n    \"ch\": \"創辦新事業總是一項充滿風險的冒險。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She admired his entrepreneurial enterprise and determination.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她讚賞他那創業的膽識與決心。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"創辦新事業總是一項充滿風險的冒險。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5837,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::evolution::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of language is a fascinating subject.","expectedAnswer":"evolution","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of language is a fascinating subject.","clozeAnswer":"evolution","exampleTranslation":"語言的演變是一個引人入勝的主題。","reference":{"eng":"evolution","kk":"ˌɛvəˈluːʃn","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"演化\"  ],  [    \"進化\"  ],  [    \"發展\"  ],  [    \"演變\"  ]]","chEntries":["演化","進化","發展","演變"],"practiceMeaning":"語言的演變是一個引人入勝的主題。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'evolutio'，由 'evolvere' (to unfold, to unroll) 構成。'Evolvere' 由 'e-' (out) 和 'volvere' (to roll) 組成。'Evolutio' 的字面意思是「展開」、「展開的過程」。最初用於指「翻書」或「展開捲軸」。後來，其語意引申至生物學，指生物體經過漫長時期，通過自然選擇等機制，發生遺傳變異並適應環境的過程，即「演化」或「進化」。也可用於形容社會、思想、技術等方面的漸進式「發展」或「演變」。","definition":"1. The process by which different kinds of living organism are believed to have developed from earlier forms during the history of the earth.; 2. The gradual development of something, especially from a simple to a more complex form.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Darwin's theory of evolution revolutionized biology.\",\n    \"ch\": \"達爾文的演化論使生物學產生了革命性的變化。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The evolution of language is a fascinating subject.\",\n    \"ch\": \"語言的演變是一個引人入勝的主題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company has undergone significant evolution in recent years.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司近年來經歷了顯著的發展。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The evolution of technology has been rapid.\",\n    \"ch\": \"科技的發展是迅速的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"語言的演變是一個引人入勝的主題。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5782,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::exotic::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She wore an ____ dress with vibrant colors.","expectedAnswer":"exotic","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She wore an ____ dress with vibrant colors.","clozeAnswer":"exotic","exampleTranslation":"她穿著一件色彩鮮豔的異國風情連衣裙。","reference":{"eng":"exotic","kk":"ɪɡˈzɑtɪk","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"外來的\"  ],  [    \"異國風情的\"  ],  [    \"奇特的\"  ],  [    \"新奇的\"  ]]","chEntries":["外來的","異國風情的","奇特的","新奇的"],"practiceMeaning":"她穿著一件色彩鮮豔的異國風情連衣裙。","analysis":"此字為形容詞，源自中古英語exotique，來自拉丁語exoticus，再追溯至希臘語exōtikos（來自外國的），由exō（在外面）衍生而來。exō本身源自原始印歐語\\\\*eks-（外面）。因此，exotic的核心語義是指「來自外國的」，特別是來自遙遠、不尋常地方的。引申為「奇特的」、「新奇的」或「有異國情調的」。語意演變上，從「來自國外」發展到「與本地不同、奇特、吸引人的」。","definition":"1. originating in or characteristic of a distant foreign country; 2. attractively unusual or different; 3. (of a plant or animal) introduced from another country and not native.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The market was filled with exotic fruits and spices.\",\n    \"ch\": \"市場裡擺滿了各種異國水果和香料。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She wore an exotic dress with vibrant colors.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她穿著一件色彩鮮豔的異國風情連衣裙。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The island is home to many exotic species of birds.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個島嶼是許多奇特鳥類的家園。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她穿著一件色彩鮮豔的異國風情連衣裙。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5083,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::exploration::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company is involved in oil ____.","expectedAnswer":"exploration","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company is involved in oil ____.","clozeAnswer":"exploration","exampleTranslation":"該公司從事石油勘探。","reference":{"eng":"exploration","kk":"ˌekspləˈreɪʃn","tense":"n.","ch":"[['探索'], ['勘探'], ['考察']]","chEntries":["探索","勘探","考察"],"practiceMeaning":"該公司從事石油勘探。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'explorare'，由 'ex-' (out) + 'plorare' (to cry out, to search) 構成，原意是 '喊出以尋找，調查'。'Exploration' 的核心語義是 '對未知或未被充分了解的區域、領域或主題進行深入的調查、發現和研究'。它包含了 '尋找'、'發現' 和 '研究' 的過程，強調的是對新事物的好奇心和求知欲。","definition":"1. The action of exploring an unfamiliar area or subject.; 2. The systematic investigation of a subject or issue.; 3. The activity of traveling around a place to learn about it.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The exploration of space continues to fascinate scientists.\",\n    \"ch\": \"太空探索持續吸引著科學家。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company is involved in oil exploration.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司從事石油勘探。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Their exploration of the Amazon rainforest yielded new discoveries.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們對亞馬遜雨林的考察帶來了新發現。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該公司從事石油勘探。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4404,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u9::extreme::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The country faced ____ poverty.","expectedAnswer":"extreme","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The country faced ____ poverty.","clozeAnswer":"extreme","exampleTranslation":"該國面臨極度貧困。","reference":{"eng":"extreme","kk":"/ɪkˈstriːm/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['極端的', '極大的'], ['極端的', '過激的'], ['極大的', '最大的']]","chEntries":["極端的","極大的","過激的","最大的"],"practiceMeaning":"該國面臨極度貧困。","analysis":"詞源自拉丁語 'extremus'，'ex-' (out) 的最高級。意為「最外面的、最後的」。引申為程度、數量、行為等達到最高或最甚的狀態。","definition":"very great or severe; reaching a high or the highest degree; very different from normal or from each other.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a man of extreme views.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他持有極端的觀點。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The country faced extreme poverty.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該國面臨極度貧困。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The expedition faced extreme conditions.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這次探險面臨極端惡劣的條件。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該國面臨極度貧困。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4155,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::family::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ had dinner together.","expectedAnswer":"family","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ had dinner together.","clozeAnswer":"family","exampleTranslation":"一家人共進晚餐。","reference":{"eng":"family","kk":"/ˈfæməli/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['家庭', '家人'], ['家族']]","chEntries":["家庭","家人","家族"],"practiceMeaning":"一家人共進晚餐。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 familia（家庭，僕人，奴隸），可能是從 famulus（僕人）來的。核心概念是「一起居住並有親屬關係或緊密聯繫的一群人」。","definition":"1. a group consisting of parents and children living together in a household; 2. all the descendants of a common ancestor","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She comes from a large family.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她來自一個大家庭。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The family had dinner together.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一家人共進晚餐。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is very close to his family.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他與家人感情很好。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"一家人共進晚餐。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3151,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::feedback::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Your ____ is important to help us improve.","expectedAnswer":"feedback","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Your ____ is important to help us improve.","clozeAnswer":"feedback","exampleTranslation":"您的意見對我們改進很重要。","reference":{"eng":"feedback","kk":"/ˈfiːdbæk/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['回饋；意見；反應'], ['（電子設備的）反饋，聲嘯']]","chEntries":["回饋","意見","反應","反饋，聲嘯"],"practiceMeaning":"您的意見對我們改進很重要。","analysis":"由 'feed'（饋送）+ 'back'（回）組成。'Feedback' 指將某個過程的結果或輸出作為輸入，以評估、改進或調整該過程。在人際互動中，它是關於某人表現的意見或評價。在技術領域，它可能是系統對其自身輸出的反應，或用戶對產品的反應。核心概念是「回歸」、「反應」或「評估」。","definition":"1. information about the reactions of customers or others to a product, service, or person; 2. the return of output from one stage of a process as input to a later stage; 3. (in electronics) the modification of a signal by passing it back to an earlier stage.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We received a lot of positive feedback on our new product.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們收到了對我們新產品的大量正面回饋。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Your feedback is important to help us improve.\",\n    \"ch\": \"您的意見對我們改進很重要。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The microphone produced an annoying feedback sound.\",\n    \"ch\": \"麥克風發出了一種惱人的聲嘯。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"您的意見對我們改進很重要。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4333,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::fence::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He tripped over the ____.","expectedAnswer":"fence","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He tripped over the ____.","clozeAnswer":"fence","exampleTranslation":"他被籬笆絆倒了。","reference":{"eng":"fence","kk":"/fɛns/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['籬笆；圍欄'], ['（擊劍的）劍']]","chEntries":["籬笆","圍欄","劍"],"practiceMeaning":"他被籬笆絆倒了。","analysis":"源自古法語 'defence' (defence)，最終源自拉丁語 'defendere' (to defend)。1. 指用於分隔、圍繞或保護的『籬笆、圍欄』。2. 在運動領域，指『擊劍的劍』，這是一個同形異義詞，詞源不同，來自法語 'escrime' (fencing, sword)。","definition":"a barrier that incloses an area, typically of posts and wire or boards; a long thin sword used in the sport of fencing","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The garden was surrounded by a wooden fence.\",\n    \"ch\": \"花園被一個木製圍欄環繞。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He tripped over the fence.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他被籬笆絆倒了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She practiced fencing every afternoon.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她每天下午練習擊劍。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他被籬笆絆倒了。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5397,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l2::finance::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The government is responsible for public ____.","expectedAnswer":"finance","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The government is responsible for public ____.","clozeAnswer":"finance","exampleTranslation":"政府負責公共財政。","reference":{"eng":"finance","kk":"ˈfaɪnæns","tense":"n.","ch":"[['財政'], ['金融'], ['（個人或機構的）財務狀況']]","chEntries":["財政","金融","財務狀況"],"practiceMeaning":"政府負責公共財政。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 fin (結束、結算、支付)，最終來自拉丁語 finis (終結)。最初指「支付、結算」，後來引申到「貨幣交易、資金的管理」。核心語意是「關於金錢的運作、管理和流動」。","definition":"1. management of large amounts of money, especially by governments or large companies; 2. the acquisition of control of or influence over a company or institution by a person or another company.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She works in the finance department of the company.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在公司的財務部工作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government is responsible for public finance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府負責公共財政。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"政府負責公共財政。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6121,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::fleet::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The deer were ____ and disappeared into the woods.","expectedAnswer":"fleet","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The deer were ____ and disappeared into the woods.","clozeAnswer":"fleet","exampleTranslation":"鹿跑得飛快，消失在樹林裡。","reference":{"eng":"fleet","kk":"flit","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"快速的\"  ],  [    \"敏捷的\"  ]]","chEntries":["快速的","敏捷的"],"practiceMeaning":"鹿跑得飛快，消失在樹林裡。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 flēot，與 fleet（艦隊）同源，但語義發展不同。原始日耳曼語詞根 *fleutaz- 可能與「流動」或「快速移動」有關。此形容詞描述速度快、行動敏捷。其語意演變是從「流動」引申為「快速」。","definition":"1. swift or speedy; 2. quick and agile in movement.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was too fleet for the pursuers.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對追擊者來說太快了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The deer were fleet and disappeared into the woods.\",\n    \"ch\": \"鹿跑得飛快，消失在樹林裡。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"鹿跑得飛快，消失在樹林裡。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5839,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::flexibility::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His ____ in negotiations was impressive.","expectedAnswer":"flexibility","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His ____ in negotiations was impressive.","clozeAnswer":"flexibility","exampleTranslation":"他在談判中的靈活性令人印象深刻。","reference":{"eng":"flexibility","kk":"ˌflɛksəˈbɪləti","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"靈活性\"  ],  [    \"彈性\"  ],  [    \"適應性\"  ],  [    \"柔韌性\"  ]]","chEntries":["靈活性","彈性","適應性","柔韌性"],"practiceMeaning":"他在談判中的靈活性令人印象深刻。","analysis":"此字由形容詞 'flexible' 加上名詞字尾 '-ity' 構成。'Flexible' 源自拉丁語 'flexibilis'，由 'flectere' (to bend) 構成。'-ity' 是常見的名詞字尾，表示「狀態」、「性質」。因此，'flexibility' 指「能夠彎曲」、「容易改變」的性質或狀態。在物理上，指材料的柔韌性；在引申義上，指個人或組織能夠適應變化、靈活應對挑戰的能力。它強調的是一種「可塑性」或「不受拘束」的特質。","definition":"1. The quality of being easily bent or altered.; 2. The ability to adapt or be adapted to new conditions.; 3. Willingness to consider new ideas; open-mindedness.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The job offers flexibility in working hours.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這份工作提供彈性的工作時間。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His flexibility in negotiations was impressive.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在談判中的靈活性令人印象深刻。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to maintain flexibility in our strategy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要在策略上保持彈性。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The flexibility of the material allowed it to be molded into complex shapes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種材料的柔韌性使其能夠被塑造成複雜的形狀。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他在談判中的靈活性令人印象深刻。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3282,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::flexible::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We offer ____ working hours for our employees.","expectedAnswer":"flexible","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We offer ____ working hours for our employees.","clozeAnswer":"flexible","exampleTranslation":"我們為員工提供彈性工作時間。","reference":{"eng":"flexible","kk":"/ˈflɛksəbl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['靈活的；可彎曲的'], ['易於適應的；適應性強的'], ['（價格、時間等）可協商的']]","chEntries":["靈活的","可彎曲的","易於適應的","適應性強的","可協商的"],"practiceMeaning":"我們為員工提供彈性工作時間。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'flexibilis'，由 'flectere' (彎曲) + '-ibilis' (可) 組成。指能夠輕易彎曲或改變形狀，引申至行為、計劃或安排，表示容易適應變化、不僵化。","definition":"1. able to be easily bent or changed; 2. able to adapt or be adapted to new conditions; 3. open to change or negotiation.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This material is very flexible and easy to work with.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種材料非常柔軟，易於加工。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We offer flexible working hours for our employees.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們為員工提供彈性工作時間。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company has a flexible approach to problem-solving.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司在解決問題方面採取靈活的策略。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們為員工提供彈性工作時間。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4579,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::for-the-sake-of::prep-phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ argument, let's assume you are right.","expectedAnswer":"For the sake of","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ argument, let's assume you are right.","clozeAnswer":"For the sake of","exampleTranslation":"為了辯論起見，我們假設你是對的。","reference":{"eng":"for the sake of","kk":"/fər ðə seɪk əv/","tense":"prep. phrase","ch":"[['為了（某人或某事的）緣故', '為了（某人或某事的）利益']]","chEntries":["為了緣故","為了利益"],"practiceMeaning":"為了辯論起見，我們假設你是對的。","analysis":"此片語由 'for' (為了), 'the' (定冠詞), 'sake' (緣故、利益) 和 'of' (of) 組成。 'sake' 源自古英語 'sacu' (cause, reason)。此片語強調行動的動機是為了某人或某事的益處、目的或緣故。","definition":"1. in the interest of; for the benefit of.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He worked extra hours for the sake of his family.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他加班工作是為了家人的緣故。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"For the sake of argument, let's assume you are right.\",\n    \"ch\": \"為了辯論起見，我們假設你是對的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She compromised for the sake of peace.\",\n    \"ch\": \"為了和平，她做出了讓步。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"為了辯論起見，我們假設你是對的。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6226,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::foster::vt","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need to ____ a sense of community.","expectedAnswer":"foster","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need to ____ a sense of community.","clozeAnswer":"foster","exampleTranslation":"我們需要促進社區意識。","reference":{"eng":"foster","kk":"ˈfɔstər","tense":"vt.","ch":"[  [    \"培養\"  ],  [    \"促進\"  ],  [    \"養育\"  ],  [    \"鼓勵\"  ]]","chEntries":["培養","促進","養育","鼓勵"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要促進社區意識。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 fōster，意為「餵養，養育」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作及物動詞時，核心語義是鼓勵、促進或養育事物的發展，特別是抽象的概念，如成長、進步、關係或情感。也可以指實際養育孩子。此及物動詞義必須接受詞，例如 foster growth、foster understanding、foster children。中文翻譯為「培養；促進；養育；鼓勵」。","definition":"1. to encourage the development or growth of something; 2. to take care of a child, or to provide a home for a child, for a period of time.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The program aims to foster creativity in young children.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該計劃旨在培養幼童的創造力。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to foster a sense of community.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要促進社區意識。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They decided to foster a child from the local orphanage.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們決定領養當地孤兒院的一個孩子。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要促進社區意識。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6227,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::fraction::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He ate only a ____ of his meal.","expectedAnswer":"fraction","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He ate only a ____ of his meal.","clozeAnswer":"fraction","exampleTranslation":"他只吃了一小部分餐點。","reference":{"eng":"fraction","kk":"ˈfrækʃn","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"一小部分\"  ],  [    \"一小塊\"  ],  [    \"零頭\"  ],  [    \"分數\"  ]]","chEntries":["一小部分","一小塊","零頭","分數"],"practiceMeaning":"他只吃了一小部分餐點。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 fractio，意為「打碎，斷裂」，是 frangere（打破，折斷）的派生詞。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。名詞義指某物的一小部分，尤其指由整數除法產生的數學分數。也可泛指非常小的數量、比例或程度。中文翻譯為「一小部分；一小塊；零頭；分數」。","definition":"1. a small part of something, or a small amount; 2. a number that is not a whole number, expressed as one number above another, or as a decimal.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Only a fraction of the students passed the exam.\",\n    \"ch\": \"只有一小部分的學生通過了考試。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He ate only a fraction of his meal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他只吃了一小部分餐點。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Write 3/4 as a fraction.\",\n    \"ch\": \"將 3/4 寫成分數。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他只吃了一小部分餐點。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3154,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::frustration::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The lack of progress led to widespread ____ among the team.","expectedAnswer":"frustration","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The lack of progress led to widespread ____ among the team.","clozeAnswer":"frustration","exampleTranslation":"缺乏進展導致團隊成員普遍感到沮喪。","reference":{"eng":"frustration","kk":"/frʌˈstreɪʃn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['沮喪；挫敗感'], ['阻礙；挫折']]","chEntries":["沮喪","挫敗感","阻礙","挫折"],"practiceMeaning":"缺乏進展導致團隊成員普遍感到沮喪。","analysis":"名詞用法，源自動詞 'frustrate'。指「沮喪」、「挫敗」或「失落」的感覺，通常是由於目標受阻、期望落空或事情不順利而引起。它也可以指「阻礙」或「挫折」本身，即那些導致沮喪情況發生的因素。","definition":"1. the feeling of being upset or annoyed as a result of being unable to change or achieve something; 2. the state of being prevented from achieving a goal.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He slammed his fist on the table in sheer frustration.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他純粹因為沮喪而一拳砸在桌子上。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The lack of progress led to widespread frustration among the team.\",\n    \"ch\": \"缺乏進展導致團隊成員普遍感到沮喪。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Bureaucratic red tape can be a major source of frustration.\",\n    \"ch\": \"官僚主義的繁文縟節是造成挫折的主要原因。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"缺乏進展導致團隊成員普遍感到沮喪。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3086,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::fundamental::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This is a ____ principle of democracy.","expectedAnswer":"fundamental","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This is a ____ principle of democracy.","clozeAnswer":"fundamental","exampleTranslation":"這是民主的一個基本原則。","reference":{"eng":"fundamental","kk":"/ˌfʌndəˈmentl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['根本的；基礎的'], ['根本性的；原則性的'], ['重要的']]","chEntries":["根本的","基礎的","根本性的","原則性的","重要的"],"practiceMeaning":"這是民主的一個基本原則。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'fundamentum' (foundation)。核心意義是「作為基礎」。\n1. 根本的；基礎的：指事物的最基本、最底層的組成部分或原理。\n2. 根本性的；原則性的：指與核心原則或基本結構相關的。\n3. 重要的：指非常重要，是其他一切事物的前提。","definition":"1. forming the most important part of something; 2. relating to the most basic or important ideas or principles; 3. forming a necessary base or core; of central importance.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to address the fundamental issues.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要解決根本問題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a fundamental principle of democracy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是民主的一個基本原則。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It is fundamental to our success.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這對我們的成功至關重要。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是民主的一個基本原則。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3156,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::furious::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ waves crashed against the shore.","expectedAnswer":"furious","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ waves crashed against the shore.","clozeAnswer":"furious","exampleTranslation":"洶湧的海浪拍打著海岸。","reference":{"eng":"furious","kk":"/ˈfjʊəriəs/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['狂怒的；暴怒的'], ['（風、風暴等）猛烈的；狂暴的']]","chEntries":["狂怒的","暴怒的","猛烈的","狂暴的"],"practiceMeaning":"洶湧的海浪拍打著海岸。","analysis":"詞源來自拉丁語 'furiosus'，意為「瘋狂的，狂怒的」，與 'furia'（狂怒，瘋狂）有關。'Furious' 形容的是極度的憤怒，一種失控的情緒狀態。也可用來形容自然現象（如風、海浪）的猛烈和狂暴，這種猛烈程度類似於狂怒的表現。","definition":"1. extremely angry; 2. (of a storm or other natural phenomenon) extremely violent.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was furious when he discovered his car had been stolen.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他發現汽車被偷後勃然大怒。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The furious waves crashed against the shore.\",\n    \"ch\": \"洶湧的海浪拍打著海岸。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She gave a furious look to the person who bumped into her.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她怒視著撞到她的人。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"洶湧的海浪拍打著海岸。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4347,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::garage::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He parks his car in the ____.","expectedAnswer":"garage","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He parks his car in the ____.","clozeAnswer":"garage","exampleTranslation":"他把車停在車庫裡。","reference":{"eng":"garage","kk":"/ɡəˈrɑːʒ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['汽車修理廠；汽車庫'], ['（蘇聯/東歐）集體農莊']]","chEntries":["汽車修理廠","汽車庫","集體農莊"],"practiceMeaning":"他把車停在車庫裡。","analysis":"源自法語 'garage'，意為『車庫』。1. 指存放汽車或修理汽車的地方，即『汽車庫、汽車修理廠』。2. 在蘇聯和東歐，曾指由國家或集體擁有和經營的『農業生產單位』，通常是指集體農莊。","definition":"a building for storing a motor vehicle; a place where cars are repaired","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I need to take my car to the garage for a service.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我需要把車開到修車廠去做保養。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He parks his car in the garage.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他把車停在車庫裡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The garage sale will be held on Saturday.\",\n    \"ch\": \"跳蚤市場將於週六舉行。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他把車停在車庫裡。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3220,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::gear::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We packed all the necessary camping ____.","expectedAnswer":"gear","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We packed all the necessary camping ____.","clozeAnswer":"gear","exampleTranslation