nswer":"grim","exampleTranslation":"他臉上表情嚴肅。","reference":{"eng":"grim","kk":"ɡrɪm","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['嚴肅的'], ['嚴酷的'], ['嚴峻的'], ['令人沮喪的']]","chEntries":["嚴肅的","嚴酷的","嚴峻的","令人沮喪的"],"practiceMeaning":"他臉上表情嚴肅。","analysis":"此字源自古英語grimm，意為「兇猛的、殘酷的」。其核心語意是「令人不安、嚴肅、不愉快」，常帶有嚴酷或嚴峻的色彩。引申為「面容嚴肅」、「情況嚴峻」、「消息令人沮喪」。OCR 掃描時可能將 'g' 誤判為 'l' 或 'c'，或 'i' 誤判為 'l'。此處修正為 grim。","definition":"1. forbidding or uninviting; 2. (of a situation or event) deeply serious; alarming; 3. (of a person's expression) stern and forbidding.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The news of the accident was grim.\",\n    \"ch\": \"事故的消息令人沮喪。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He had a grim expression on his face.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他臉上表情嚴肅。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The future looks grim for the company.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司的未來前景嚴峻。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他臉上表情嚴肅。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3163,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::gulf::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There is a wide ____ between their political views.","expectedAnswer":"gulf","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There is a wide ____ between their political views.","clozeAnswer":"gulf","exampleTranslation":"他們的政治觀點之間存在著巨大的差異。","reference":{"eng":"gulf","kk":"/ɡʌlf/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['（海洋、湖泊的）灣；海灣'], ['（意見、情況等的）巨大差異；鴻溝']]","chEntries":["灣","海灣","巨大差異","鴻溝"],"practiceMeaning":"他們的政治觀點之間存在著巨大的差異。","analysis":"詞源來自希臘語 'kolpos'，意為「灣」。'Gulf' 可以指地理上的地理特徵，即大海或湖泊伸入陸地的寬闊水域。它也可以比喻性地指兩種事物之間（如觀點、情感、地位）的巨大差異、隔閡或鴻溝，這種差異難以跨越。","definition":"1. a deep inlet of the sea almost surrounded by land, with a narrow mouth; 2. a profound difference between people or things.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The ship sailed across the Gulf of Mexico.\",\n    \"ch\": \"船隻航行穿越墨西哥灣。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There is a wide gulf between their political views.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們的政治觀點之間存在著巨大的差異。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The economic gulf between the rich and the poor continues to widen.\",\n    \"ch\": \"貧富之間的經濟鴻溝持續擴大。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們的政治觀點之間存在著巨大的差異。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3222,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::halt::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The police ordered the driver to ____.","expectedAnswer":"halt","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The police ordered the driver to ____.","clozeAnswer":"halt","exampleTranslation":"警察命令司機停車。","reference":{"eng":"halt","kk":"/hɔlt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['停止'], ['中止']]","chEntries":["停止","中止"],"practiceMeaning":"警察命令司機停車。","analysis":"詞源來自古法語 'halta'，意為『暫停』。強調突然或預期的停止，與 'stop' 類似，但常帶有更正式或更突然的語氣。常用於命令或緊急情況。","definition":"to bring or come to an abrupt stop.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The marching band halted in front of the building.\",\n    \"ch\": \"遊行樂隊在建築物前停下了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police ordered the driver to halt.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警察命令司機停車。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Production was halted due to a strike.\",\n    \"ch\": \"由於罷工，生產被中止了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"警察命令司機停車。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U41"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6124,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::icon::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Click on the folder ____ to open it.","expectedAnswer":"icon","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Click on the folder ____ to open it.","clozeAnswer":"icon","exampleTranslation":"點擊文件夾圖標將其打開。","reference":{"eng":"icon","kk":"ˈaɪkɑːn","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"圖像\"  ],  [    \"圖標\"  ],  [    \"偶像\"  ]]","chEntries":["圖像","圖標","偶像"],"practiceMeaning":"點擊文件夾圖標將其打開。","analysis":"此字源自希臘語 eikōn，意為「圖像；肖像」。在早期，主要指宗教畫像，特別是東方教會中用於崇拜的聖像。在 modern English 中，icon 指電腦螢幕上的小圖形符號（圖標），或比喻某個領域中被廣泛崇拜或模仿的傑出人物（偶像）。其語意演變是從「圖像」到「宗教聖像」，再到「電腦圖標」和「現代偶像」。","definition":"1. a person or thing regarded as a representative symbol or as worthy of veneration; 2. a small graphic image or symbol on a computer screen that represents a program, command, or file.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is an icon of the fashion industry.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是時尚界的偶像。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Click on the folder icon to open it.\",\n    \"ch\": \"點擊文件夾圖標將其打開。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The artist became an icon of the youth movement.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位藝術家成為青年運動的標誌性人物。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"點擊文件夾圖標將其打開。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6125,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::ideology::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The novel explores themes of freedom and ____.","expectedAnswer":"ideology","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The novel explores themes of freedom and ____.","clozeAnswer":"ideology","exampleTranslation":"這部小說探討了自由與意識形態的主題。","reference":{"eng":"ideology","kk":"ˌɪdiˈɑːlədʒi","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"意識形態\"  ],  [    \"思想體系\"  ],  [    \"理念\"  ]]","chEntries":["意識形態","思想體系","理念"],"practiceMeaning":"這部小說探討了自由與意識形態的主題。","analysis":"此字源自法語 idéologie，由希臘語 idea（形式；理念；思想）和 -logia（學說；研究）組成。Idea 源自 idea（看；看見）。-logia 來自 logos（詞；言論；學說）。因此，ideology 的核心語義是「關於思想的學說」或「思想體系」。此名詞指一套關於社會、政治或經濟的觀念、信念和價值觀的系統。其語意演變是從「思想的研究」到「一套系統化的思想」。","definition":"A system of ideas and ideals, especially one which forms the basis of economic or political theory and policy.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They shared the same political ideology.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們持有相同的政治意識形態。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The novel explores themes of freedom and ideology.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這部小說探討了自由與意識形態的主題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His actions were driven by a strong ideology.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的行為是由強烈的理念驅動的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這部小說探討了自由與意識形態的主題。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3917,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::imagination::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"You need ____ to be a writer.","expectedAnswer":"imagination","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"You need ____ to be a writer.","clozeAnswer":"imagination","exampleTranslation":"你需要想像力才能成為一名作家。","reference":{"eng":"imagination","kk":"/ɪˌmædʒɪˈneɪʃn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['想像力'], ['幻想', '虛構']]","chEntries":["想像力","幻想","虛構"],"practiceMeaning":"你需要想像力才能成為一名作家。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'imaginatio'，與 'imago' (意為「圖像、影像」) 有關，最終源自 'imagines' (意為「形象」)。指在心中形成圖像、概念的能力，即「想像力」；也可指由此產生的「幻想」或「虛構」。","definition":"1. the faculty or action of forming new ideas, or images or concepts of external objects not present to the senses; 2. the ability of the mind to be creative or resourceful.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Children have a great imagination.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子們有很強的想像力。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"You need imagination to be a writer.\",\n    \"ch\": \"你需要想像力才能成為一名作家。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"That story is pure imagination.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那個故事純粹是虛構的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"你需要想像力才能成為一名作家。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5840,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::immune::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He seems ____ to criticism.","expectedAnswer":"immune","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He seems ____ to criticism.","clozeAnswer":"immune","exampleTranslation":"他似乎不受批評的影響。","reference":{"eng":"immune","kk":"ɪˈmjuːn","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"免疫的\"  ],  [    \"不受影響的\"  ],  [    \"免於……的\"  ],  [    \"豁免的\"  ]]","chEntries":["免疫的","不受影響的","免於……的","豁免的"],"practiceMeaning":"他似乎不受批評的影響。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'immūnis'，由 'in-' (not) 和 'mūnus' (duty, service, gift) 構成。'Immūnis' 的字面意思是「不受……負擔的」或「免除……義務的」。最初用於指免稅或免於公共服務的人。在醫學上，'immune' 指身體對某種疾病或病原體產生抵抗力，不再容易受到感染。這也與「不受……侵害」的核心意義相符。引申義則指「不受……影響」或「免於……」。例如，也可指「免除……責任的」。","definition":"1. Protected against a particular disease.; 2. Not affected or influenced by something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Children are often immune to common colds after exposure.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子們在接觸後通常對普通感冒產生免疫。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He seems immune to criticism.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他似乎不受批評的影響。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company is immune from prosecution.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司免於起訴。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Diplomats are often immune from local laws.\",\n    \"ch\": \"外交官員通常豁免於當地法律。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他似乎不受批評的影響。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5841,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::implement::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need to ____ the changes immediately.","expectedAnswer":"implement","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need to ____ the changes immediately.","clozeAnswer":"implement","exampleTranslation":"我們需要立即執行這些變革。","reference":{"eng":"implement","kk":"ˈɪmplɪmənt","tense":"v.","ch":"[  [    \"執行\"  ],  [    \"實施\"  ],  [    \"實行\"  ],  [    \"完成\"  ]]","chEntries":["執行","實施","實行","完成"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要立即執行這些變革。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'implementum' (filling, completion)，是 'implere' (to fill, to fulfill) 的派生詞。'Implere' 由 'in-' (in) 和 'plere' (to fill) 構成。'Implementum' 的意思是指「填補」、「完成」的工具或手段。作動詞時，'implement' 的核心語意是「將一個計劃、決定、或概念付諸實踐」，即「執行」或「實施」。它強調將抽象的意圖轉化為具體的行動。例如，也可指「完成」一個任務。","definition":"1. To put (a decision, plan, agreement, etc.) into effect.; 2. To carry out.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government will implement new policies next year.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府將在明年實施新政策。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to implement the changes immediately.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要立即執行這些變革。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The committee decided to implement the proposal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"委員會決定實行這項提議。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The workers implemented the new safety procedures.\",\n    \"ch\": \"工人們執行了新的安全程序。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要立即執行這些變革。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4518,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::in::prep","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He lives ____ London.","expectedAnswer":"in","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He lives ____ London.","clozeAnswer":"in","exampleTranslation":"他住在倫敦。","reference":{"eng":"in","kk":"/ɪn/","tense":"prep.","ch":"[['在...裡面'], ['在...之中'], ['在（某個時間、地點、情況）']]","chEntries":["在...裡面","在...之中","在"],"practiceMeaning":"他住在倫敦。","analysis":"源自古英語 in。是一個極其基本且用途廣泛的介詞。核心語意是「在一個封閉的空間或區域內」。引申義涵蓋時間、狀態、方法、組成等。","definition":"1. Expressing the situation of being enclosed or surrounded by something; 2. Expressing location or position within a place or area; 3. Expressing the period of time during which an event occurs.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The keys are in the drawer.\",\n    \"ch\": \"鑰匙在抽屜裡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He lives in London.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他住在倫敦。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She will arrive in an hour.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她將在一小時內到達。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They are involved in the project.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們參與了這個項目。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他住在倫敦。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4578,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::inaccurate::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His memory of the event was ____.","expectedAnswer":"inaccurate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His memory of the event was ____.","clozeAnswer":"inaccurate","exampleTranslation":"他對那次事件的記憶並不準確。","reference":{"eng":"inaccurate","kk":"/ɪnˈækjərət/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['不準確的', '不精確的'], ['錯誤的']]","chEntries":["不準確的","不精確的","錯誤的"],"practiceMeaning":"他對那次事件的記憶並不準確。","analysis":"由否定字首 'in-' (not) 和 'accurate' (準確的) 組成。與 'accurate' 相反，指不準確、不精確或錯誤的。","definition":"1. not correct or precise.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The report contained several inaccurate figures.\",\n    \"ch\": \"報告包含幾個不準確的數字。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His memory of the event was inaccurate.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對那次事件的記憶並不準確。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The map is inaccurate and outdated.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這張地圖既不準確又過時了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他對那次事件的記憶並不準確。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5087,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::index::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The stock market ____ rose today.","expectedAnswer":"index","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The stock market ____ rose today.","clozeAnswer":"index","exampleTranslation":"股市指數今天上漲了。","reference":{"eng":"index","kk":"ˈɪndeks","tense":"n.","ch":"[['索引'], ['指數'], ['指示器']]","chEntries":["索引","指數","指示器"],"practiceMeaning":"股市指數今天上漲了。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'index'，意為 '指示者、標記者'，源於 'indicere' (to proclaim, to announce)。'Index' 最初指 '指示牌' 或 '標記'。在書籍中，它發展成為 '索引'，用於標記和指示內容位置。在經濟學或科學中，'index' 則指 '指數'，用於量化某種趨勢或情況的指標，它指示著變化的方向和幅度。","definition":"1. A list of names, subjects, etc. with references to where they occur, typically found at the end of a book.; 2. A figure or number that indicates the level of something, especially in economics or science.; 3. A sign or indication.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"You can find the topic in the index at the back of the book.\",\n    \"ch\": \"你可以在書後的索引中找到這個主題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The stock market index rose today.\",\n    \"ch\": \"股市指數今天上漲了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The presence of these pollutants is an index of water quality degradation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這些污染物的存在是水質惡化的指標。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"股市指數今天上漲了。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3168,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::indication::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There was no ____ that he was unhappy.","expectedAnswer":"indication","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There was no ____ that he was unhappy.","clozeAnswer":"indication","exampleTranslation":"沒有任何跡象表明他感到不開心。","reference":{"eng":"indication","kk":"/ˌɪndɪˈkeɪʃn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['表示；表明'], ['指示；跡象；徵兆'], ['（醫學）適應症；指徵']]","chEntries":["表示","表明","指示","跡象","徵兆","適應症","指徵"],"practiceMeaning":"沒有任何跡象表明他感到不開心。","analysis":"名詞，源自動詞 'indicate'。'Indication' 指的是某事物顯示、表明或預示的信號或線索。它可以是視覺上的指示（如路標），身體上的症狀（如疾病的跡象），或數據顯示的趨勢。在醫學上，'indication' 指的是某種治療方法適用的情況。","definition":"1. a sign or piece of information that shows something exists or is likely to happen; 2. a sign of a particular situation or condition; 3. (medicine) a sign that a particular treatment or medicine is appropriate for a particular condition.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The dark clouds are an indication of coming rain.\",\n    \"ch\": \"烏雲預示著即將下雨。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was no indication that he was unhappy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"沒有任何跡象表明他感到不開心。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Fever is a common indication of infection.\",\n    \"ch\": \"發燒是感染的常見指徵。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"沒有任何跡象表明他感到不開心。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3188,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::inject::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The new funding will ____ life into the struggling arts program.","expectedAnswer":"inject","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The new funding will ____ life into the struggling arts program.","clozeAnswer":"inject","exampleTranslation":"這筆新資金將為這個陷入困境的藝術項目注入活力。","reference":{"eng":"inject","kk":"/ɪnˈdʒɛkt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['注射；注射給藥'], ['注入；灌輸（尤指想法、情感）']]","chEntries":["注射","注射給藥","注入","灌輸"],"practiceMeaning":"這筆新資金將為這個陷入困境的藝術項目注入活力。","analysis":"詞源來自拉丁語 'injectare'，意為「注入，投擲」，由 'in-'（在...中）+ 'jacere'（扔）組成。'Inject' 的核心是「將某物推入或注入」。最常見的是醫學上的「注射」，將藥物或液體通過針頭注入體內。也可引申為將某物（如想法、情感、資金）注入到某個系統、情況或人身上。","definition":"1. administer (a drug or vaccine) by inserting a needle into a muscle or into a cavity in the body; 2. force (fluid, especially blood) into a vessel or cavity; 3. introduce (a substance) into something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The doctor will inject the vaccine into your arm.\",\n    \"ch\": \"醫生會將疫苗注射到你的手臂。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The new funding will inject life into the struggling arts program.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這筆新資金將為這個陷入困境的藝術項目注入活力。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He needs to inject more confidence into his presentation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他需要在演講中注入更多信心。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這筆新資金將為這個陷入困境的藝術項目注入活力。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4536,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::injury::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The scandal caused a severe ____ to the company's reputation.","expectedAnswer":"injury","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The scandal caused a severe ____ to the company's reputation.","clozeAnswer":"injury","exampleTranslation":"這樁醜聞嚴重損害了公司的聲譽。","reference":{"eng":"injury","kk":"/ˈɪndʒəri/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['傷害', '損傷'], ['（名譽、感情等的）損害']]","chEntries":["傷害","損傷","損害"],"practiceMeaning":"這樁醜聞嚴重損害了公司的聲譽。","analysis":"源自古法語 'injurye'，源於拉丁語 'iniuria'，由 'in-' (not) 和 'ius' (law, right - 法律、權利) 組成。原意為 'wrong, injustice' (錯誤、不公)。引申為對身體造成的傷害（physical injury），以及對名譽、感情、權利等的損害（damage to reputation/feelings/rights）。","definition":"1. physical harm or damage to someone's body.; 2. harm or damage caused to someone's reputation or feelings.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He suffered a serious injury to his knee.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的膝蓋受了重傷。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The scandal caused a severe injury to the company's reputation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這樁醜聞嚴重損害了公司的聲譽。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The injury occurred during training.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這次受傷發生在訓練期間。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這樁醜聞嚴重損害了公司的聲譽。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3170,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::instinct::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"My ____ told me not to trust him.","expectedAnswer":"instinct","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"My ____ told me not to trust him.","clozeAnswer":"instinct","exampleTranslation":"我的直覺告訴我不要相信他。","reference":{"eng":"instinct","kk":"/ˈɪnstɪŋkt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['本能；天性'], ['（對某事的）直覺；天賦']]","chEntries":["本能","天性","直覺","天賦"],"practiceMeaning":"我的直覺告訴我不要相信他。","analysis":"詞源來自拉丁語 'instinctus'，意為「衝動，刺激」，源於 'instinguere'（激勵，驅使）。'Instinct' 指的是一種天生的、非學習而來的行為模式或反應，由生物體的遺傳基因決定，用於應對特定的環境刺激。它也可以引申為對某事的強烈直覺或天賦，一種無需理性思考就能產生的判斷或傾向。","definition":"1. an innate, typically fixed pattern of behavior in animals in response to certain stimuli; 2. a natural or intuitive impulse or tendency.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Birds have an instinct to migrate south for the winter.\",\n    \"ch\": \"鳥類有向南遷徙以度過冬天的本能。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"My instinct told me not to trust him.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我的直覺告訴我不要相信他。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a natural instinct for business.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她有經營生意的天賦。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我的直覺告訴我不要相信他。","sourceName":"字彙王、龍騰課本","unitName":"U40、L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3172,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::insult::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Do not ____ my intelligence by lying to me.","expectedAnswer":"insult","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Do not ____ my intelligence by lying to me.","clozeAnswer":"insult","exampleTranslation":"不要通過對我撒謊來侮辱我的智商。","reference":{"eng":"insult","kk":"/ˈɪnsʌlt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['侮辱；辱罵']]","chEntries":["侮辱","辱罵"],"practiceMeaning":"不要通過對我撒謊來侮辱我的智商。","analysis":"詞源來自拉丁語 'insultare'，意為「跳躍，攻擊」，由 'in-'（在...上）+ 'saltare'（跳躍）組成。'Insult' 指的是用言語或行為冒犯、羞辱或貶低他人。這種行為通常是惡意的，旨在傷害對方的尊嚴或感情。","definition":"1. speak to or treat with great disrespect; insultingly; 2. treat (someone or something) disrespectfully or contemptuously.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He felt insulted by the unfair criticism.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他覺得受到不公平批評的侮辱。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Do not insult my intelligence by lying to me.\",\n    \"ch\": \"不要通過對我撒謊來侮辱我的智商。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The protester insulted the police officer.\",\n    \"ch\": \"抗議者辱罵了那位警官。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"不要通過對我撒謊來侮辱我的智商。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3889,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::invitation::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His ____ was very formal.","expectedAnswer":"invitation","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His ____ was very formal.","clozeAnswer":"invitation","exampleTranslation":"他的邀請非常正式。","reference":{"eng":"invitation","kk":"/ˌɪnvɪˈteɪʃən/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['邀請'], ['邀請函']]","chEntries":["邀請","邀請函"],"practiceMeaning":"他的邀請非常正式。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'invitatio'，'invitare' (to invite) 的名詞形式，意為「邀請」。核心是「呼喚」、「邀請」。指請人參加某事物的請求，或表示這種請求的文件。","definition":"1. a request or order to come somewhere or do something. 2. a written or verbal communication asking someone to attend an event or perform a task.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We received an invitation to the wedding.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們收到了婚禮的邀請。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His invitation was very formal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的邀請非常正式。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Thank you for your kind invitation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"感謝您的盛情邀請。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他的邀請非常正式。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3176,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::isolation::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of the island made it difficult to access.","expectedAnswer":"isolation","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of the island made it difficult to access.","clozeAnswer":"isolation","exampleTranslation":"這個島嶼的地理隔離使得它難以抵達。","reference":{"eng":"isolation","kk":"/ˌaɪsəˈleɪʃn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['孤立；隔離'], ['（與社會的）隔絕']]","chEntries":["孤立","隔離","隔絕"],"practiceMeaning":"這個島嶼的地理隔離使得它難以抵達。","analysis":"名詞，源自動詞 'isolate'。指「孤立」、「隔離」或「隔絕」的狀態或過程。它可以指物理上的分離，如將某人或某物與外界隔離開。也可以指心理或社會上的孤立，即與他人缺乏聯繫，感到孤獨。在醫學上，指隔離傳染病患者的措施。","definition":"1. the process or fact of isolating or being isolated; 2. a state of being alone or removed from others.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The fear of isolation prevented her from speaking out.\",\n    \"ch\": \"對孤立的恐懼阻止了她發聲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The isolation of the island made it difficult to access.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個島嶼的地理隔離使得它難以抵達。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Quarantine is a form of medical isolation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"隔離檢疫是一種醫療隔離形式。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個島嶼的地理隔離使得它難以抵達。","sourceName":"字彙王、龍騰課本","unitName":"U40、L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4723,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::label::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She didn't want to be put in the ____ of 'failure'.","expectedAnswer":"label","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She didn't want to be put in the ____ of 'failure'.","clozeAnswer":"label","exampleTranslation":"她不想被貼上「失敗者」的標籤。","reference":{"eng":"label","kk":"/ˈleɪbəl/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['標籤'], ['標記'], ['（非正式）評價、稱號']]","chEntries":["標籤","標記","評價、稱號"],"practiceMeaning":"她不想被貼上「失敗者」的標籤。","analysis":"源自古法語 *lambel*，指懸掛物，後演變為貼在物品上識別的標籤。引申至對人或事物的一種評價或稱號，通常帶有分類或定性的意味。","definition":"1. A piece of paper or other material fastened by gluing or tying to an object and giving information about it. 2. A descriptive term or designation applied to a person or thing.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Each bottle had a label with the ingredients listed.\",\n    \"ch\": \"每個瓶子都有一個列有成分的標籤。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She didn't want to be put in the label of 'failure'.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她不想被貼上「失敗者」的標籤。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她不想被貼上「失敗者」的標籤。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5790,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::likelihood::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"What is the ____ that the project will be completed on time?","expectedAnswer":"likelihood","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"What is the ____ that the project will be completed on time?","clozeAnswer":"likelihood","exampleTranslation":"這個項目按時完成的可能性有多大？","reference":{"eng":"likelihood","kk":"ˈlaɪkliˌhʊd","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"可能性\"  ],  [    \"概率\"  ]]","chEntries":["可能性","概率"],"practiceMeaning":"這個項目按時完成的可能性有多大？","analysis":"此字為名詞，構詞自likely（可能的；很可能的）+ -hood（名詞字尾，表示「狀態；性質」）。likely本身是形容詞，源自古英語līclīc，由līc（相似的；同樣的）+ -lic（形容詞字尾）組成，līc的原始印歐語詞根是\\\\*līk-（形狀）。-hood字尾源自古英語-hād，與原始日耳曼語\\\\*haiduz（樣式；形式）有關。因此，likelihood的核心語義是指「某事物發生的可能性或概率」。語意演變上，由形容詞「可能的」轉化為表示「可能性」的抽象名詞。","definition":"1. the probability or chance that something will happen or be the case.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There is a high likelihood of rain this afternoon.\",\n    \"ch\": \"今天下午很有可能下雨。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"What is the likelihood that the project will be completed on time?\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個項目按時完成的可能性有多大？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The likelihood of success is quite low.\",\n    \"ch\": \"成功的可能性相當低。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個項目按時完成的可能性有多大？","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4628,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::living::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The documentary presented a ____ history of the village.","expectedAnswer":"living","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The documentary presented a ____ history of the village.","clozeAnswer":"living","exampleTranslation":"這部紀錄片呈現了該村莊的活生生歷史。","reference":{"eng":"living","kk":"/ˈlɪvɪŋ/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['活著的'], ['活生生的']]","chEntries":["活著的","活生生的"],"practiceMeaning":"這部紀錄片呈現了該村莊的活生生歷史。","analysis":"由 'live' (活著) + '-ing' (現在分詞形式，作形容詞用)。指仍然活著的，與「死的」相對。也可用來形容真實、生動的狀態。","definition":"alive; not dead; real or accurate.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The living room was filled with sunlight.\",\n    \"ch\": \"客廳裡陽光充沛。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The documentary presented a living history of the village.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這部紀錄片呈現了該村莊的活生生歷史。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這部紀錄片呈現了該村莊的活生生歷史。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3897,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::majority::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He won the election by a large ____.","expectedAnswer":"majority","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He won the election by a large ____.","clozeAnswer":"majority","exampleTranslation":"他以絕對多數贏得了選舉。","reference":{"eng":"majority","kk":"/məˈdʒɑːrəti/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['大多數', '大部分'], ['（選舉）得票最多者']]","chEntries":["大多數","大部分","得票最多者"],"practiceMeaning":"他以絕對多數贏得了選舉。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'maior' (greater) 的比較級，後演變為名詞 'maioritas'。核心是「更大」、「較多」。指總數中的絕大部分，或在投票中獲得最多票數的一方。","definition":"1. the greater number or part; a number or proportion larger than half the total. 2. the party or side in an election or vote that polls the largest number of votes.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The majority of students passed the exam.\",\n    \"ch\": \"大多數學生通過了考試。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He won the election by a large majority.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他以絕對多數贏得了選舉。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The decision was made by the majority.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個決定是由多數人做出的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他以絕對多數贏得了選舉。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U1、L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5844,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::masterpiece::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This novel is considered his ____.","expectedAnswer":"masterpiece","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This novel is considered his ____.","clozeAnswer":"masterpiece","exampleTranslation":"這本小說被認為是他的代表作。","reference":{"eng":"masterpiece","kk":"ˈmæstərpiːs","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"傑作\"  ],  [    \"名作\"  ],  [    \"曠世之作\"  ],  [    \"代表作\"  ]]","chEntries":["傑作","名作","曠世之作","代表作"],"practiceMeaning":"這本小說被認為是他的代表作。","analysis":"此字為複合詞，由 'master' (大師) 和 'piece' (作品) 組成。'Master' 源自古英語 'mægester'，來自拉丁語 'magister' (chief, leader, teacher)。'Piece' 源自古法語 'piece'，意為「部分」、「塊」。'Masterpiece' 的字面意思是「大師的作品」，指由一位技藝高超的藝術家或工匠創作的、具有極高藝術價值和技巧的傑出作品。它強調的是作者的「大師級」技藝和作品本身的「非凡」水準。","definition":"1. A work of outstanding artistry, skill, or workmanship.; 2. A person's best piece of work.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The Mona Lisa is a masterpiece by Leonardo da Vinci.\",\n    \"ch\": \"《蒙娜麗莎》是達文西的傑作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This novel is considered his masterpiece.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本小說被認為是他的代表作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The architect's design was a true masterpiece.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位建築師的設計是真正的傑作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The symphony was hailed as a masterpiece.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這首交響樂被譽為傑作。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這本小說被認為是他的代表作。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6082,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::meantime::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She's studying abroad for a year. In the ____, her family is taking care of her apartment.","expectedAnswer":"meantime","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She's studying abroad for a year. In the ____, her family is taking care of her apartment.","clozeAnswer":"meantime","exampleTranslation":"她將在國外學習一年。與此同時，她的家人會幫忙照看她的公寓。","reference":{"eng":"meantime","kk":"ˈmintˌaɪm","tense":"adv.","ch":"[  [    \"其間\"  ],  [    \"同時\"  ]]","chEntries":["其間","同時"],"practiceMeaning":"她將在國外學習一年。與此同時，她的家人會幫忙照看她的公寓。","analysis":"此字為複合詞，由 mean（中間的）和 time（時間）組成。核心語義是「在中間的時間裡」或「在兩件事之間的時間裡」。它用來連接兩個事件或時間段，指在第一個事件發生時或之後，到第二個事件發生前的那段時間。","definition":"during the time between two specified times or events.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The train will be here in ten minutes; in the meantime, you can sit down.\",\n    \"ch\": \"火車十分鐘後就到；在此期間，你可以坐下。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She's studying abroad for a year. In the meantime, her family is taking care of her apartment.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她將在國外學習一年。與此同時，她的家人會幫忙照看她的公寓。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We are waiting for the results. Meantime, let's review the previous findings.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們在等待結果。同時，讓我們複習一下之前的發現。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她將在國外學習一年。與此同時，她的家人會幫忙照看她的公寓。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5555,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::mere::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She is a ____ beginner in this field.","expectedAnswer":"mere","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She is a ____ beginner in this field.","clozeAnswer":"mere","exampleTranslation":"她在這個領域只是一個初學者。","reference":{"eng":"mere","kk":"mɪər","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['僅僅的'], ['普通的'], ['渺小的']]","chEntries":["僅僅的","普通的","渺小的"],"practiceMeaning":"她在這個領域只是一個初學者。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 \"mǣre\"，原意為 \"boundary, limit, distinguished\"（界線，極限，傑出的）。其語義演變經歷了從「明確的界線/極限」到「範圍僅限於此」的概念，進而發展出「僅僅是」、「不過是」的含義。另一說法是，它可能與強調「單一」或「微小」的概念有關。現代用法中，\"mere\" 作形容詞，常用來強調事物之少、之小、之普通，或僅僅是某種狀態，與 \"only\" 或 \"just\" 類似，但常帶有一點貶低或不以為然的語氣，強調其不重要性或缺乏其他特質。例如 \"a mere child\"（只是一個小孩），暗示經驗或能力不足。","definition":"1. That is only or no more than what is stated; 2. Small or insignificant.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It took me a mere ten minutes to finish the task.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我只花了短短十分鐘就完成了任務。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a mere beginner in this field.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在這個領域只是一個初學者。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The accident was caused by a mere oversight.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這次意外僅僅是一個疏忽造成的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她在這個領域只是一個初學者。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5791,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::midst::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"In the ____ of the chaos, she remained calm.","expectedAnswer":"midst","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"In the ____ of the chaos, she remained calm.","clozeAnswer":"midst","exampleTranslation":"在混亂之中，她保持了鎮定。","reference":{"eng":"midst","kk":"mɪdst","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"中間\"  ],  [    \"當中\"  ],  [    \"人群中\"  ]]","chEntries":["中間","當中","人群中"],"practiceMeaning":"在混亂之中，她保持了鎮定。","analysis":"此字為名詞，源自古英語middel（中間）+ -est（最高級後綴），是middle的最高級形式。然而，它後來演變為獨立的名詞，表示「中間」或「中央」。其詞源可追溯至原始日耳曼語\\\\*midjilastaz。核心語義是指「某事物或某群人、事物的中心或中間位置」。通常用於固定搭配，如in the midst of。語意演變上，從「最中間」的比較級概念，演變為表示「中間」或「中央」的狀態或位置。","definition":"1. the middle of a place or area; 2. the middle of a group of people or things.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He found himself in the midst of a crowd.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他發現自己身處人群之中。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"In the midst of the chaos, she remained calm.\",\n    \"ch\": \"在混亂之中，她保持了鎮定。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The small village lies in the midst of rolling hills.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個小村莊坐落在連綿起伏的丘陵之間。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"在混亂之中，她保持了鎮定。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6178,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::milestone::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Graduating from college was a significant ____ for her.","expectedAnswer":"milestone","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Graduating from college was a significant ____ for her.","clozeAnswer":"milestone","exampleTranslation":"大學畢業對她來說是一個重要的轉捩點。","reference":{"eng":"milestone","kk":"ˈmaɪlstəʊn","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"里程碑\"  ],  [    \"轉捩點\"  ],  [    \"重要事件\"  ]]","chEntries":["里程碑","轉捩點","重要事件"],"practiceMeaning":"大學畢業對她來說是一個重要的轉捩點。","analysis":"此字由 mile（英里）和 stone（石頭）兩個名詞組成。在古代，里程碑是用來標示道路距離的石頭。此字在現代英語中可視為複合詞，其語義由兩部分組成。作為名詞，其核心語義是「一個重要的事件或階段，標誌著進步或發展」。詞源中的「標示距離的石頭」引申為「標誌重要進展的事件」。","definition":"1. a significant stage or event in the development of something; 2. a stone or post set up beside a road or path to mark the distance to a place.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company celebrated a major milestone in its history.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司慶祝了其歷史上的重要里程碑。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Graduating from college was a significant milestone for her.\",\n    \"ch\": \"大學畢業對她來說是一個重要的轉捩點。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The signpost marked a milestone of five miles.\",\n    \"ch\": \"路標標示著五英里的里程碑。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The birth of their first child was a milestone for the couple.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們第一個孩子的出生對這對夫婦來說是一個重要的里程碑。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"大學畢業對她來說是一個重要的轉捩點。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6231,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::minimal::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need to make ____ changes to the design.","expectedAnswer":"minimal","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need to make ____ changes to the design.","clozeAnswer":"minimal","exampleTranslation":"我們只需要對設計做最低限度的修改。","reference":{"eng":"minimal","kk":"ˈmɪnɪml","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"最小的\"  ],  [    \"極小的\"  ],  [    \"最低限度的\"  ]]","chEntries":["最小的","極小的","最低限度的"],"practiceMeaning":"我們只需要對設計做最低限度的修改。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 minimus，是 parvus（小的）的最高級，意為「最小的」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作形容詞時，指數量、程度或大小極小，是可能的最低水平。中文翻譯為「最小的；極小的；最低限度的」。","definition":"1. the smallest possible amount or degree; 2. very small.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The cost of the repairs was minimal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"維修費用是極小的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to make minimal changes to the design.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們只需要對設計做最低限度的修改。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The artist used a minimal color palette.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位藝術家使用了極簡的調色盤。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們只需要對設計做最低限度的修改。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6232,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::minimize::vt","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company is working to ____ losses.","expectedAnswer":"minimize","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company is working to ____ losses.","clozeAnswer":"minimize","exampleTranslation":"這家公司正努力將損失減到最低。","reference":{"eng":"minimize","kk":"ˈmɪnɪmaɪz","tense":"vt.","ch":"[  [    \"使最小化\"  ],  [    \"減到最低\"  ],  [    \"輕視\"  ],  [    \"低估\"  ]]","chEntries":["使最小化","減到最低","輕視","低估"],"practiceMeaning":"這家公司正努力將損失減到最低。","analysis":"此字由形容詞 minimal（最小的）加上動詞字尾 -ize（使…）構成。minimal 源自拉丁語 minimus。字尾 -ize 將形容詞轉為動詞，表示「使達到最小的程度」。核心語義是將某事物（如成本、損失、影響、風險）減少到可能的最少程度，或低估其重要性。此及物動詞義必須接受詞，例如 minimize costs、minimize risk、minimize damage。中文翻譯為「使最小化；減到最低；輕視；低估」。","definition":"1. to reduce something to the smallest possible amount or degree; 2. to treat or regard something as unimportant.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We should try to minimize our environmental impact.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們應該盡量減少我們的環境影響。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company is working to minimize losses.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司正努力將損失減到最低。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Don't minimize the importance of this issue.\",\n    \"ch\": \"不要輕視這個問題的重要性。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這家公司正努力將損失減到最低。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3095,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::minimum::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company sets a ____ requirement for experience.","expectedAnswer":"minimum","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company sets a ____ requirement for experience.","clozeAnswer":"minimum","exampleTranslation":"公司設定了對經驗的最低要求。","reference":{"eng":"minimum","kk":"/ˈmɪnɪməm/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['最低數量；最小值'], ['最低限度']]","chEntries":["最低數量","最小值","最低限度"],"practiceMeaning":"公司設定了對經驗的最低要求。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'minimus' (smallest)。是形容詞 'minimum' 的名詞形式。指「最小的數量」或「最低的程度」。\n1. 最低數量；最小值：指某個變數或集合中的最小數值。\n2. 最低限度：指為了達到某種標準或要求所必須達到的最低條件。","definition":"1. the smallest amount or number allowed or possible; 2. the least amount or quantity possible.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The minimum for this course is a B grade.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這門課的最低要求是B級。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company sets a minimum requirement for experience.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司設定了對經驗的最低要求。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"公司設定了對經驗的最低要求。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6233,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::mint::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The new coins were minted at the royal ____.","expectedAnswer":"mint","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The new coins were minted at the royal ____.","clozeAnswer":"mint","exampleTranslation":"新硬幣是在皇家造幣廠鑄造的。","reference":{"eng":"mint","kk":"mɪnt","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"薄荷\"  ],  [    \"造幣廠\"  ],  [    \"巨額財富\"  ]]","chEntries":["薄荷","造幣廠","巨額財富"],"practiceMeaning":"新硬幣是在皇家造幣廠鑄造的。","analysis":"此字有多個詞源。作「薄荷」時，源自拉丁語 mentha。作「造幣廠」時，源自拉丁語 moneta（女神名，後指錢幣，鑄幣廠），與 mint（薄荷）的詞源不同，但中古英語時期兩者拼寫合併。作「巨額財富」時，為俚語，來自造幣廠能製造大量金錢的概念。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。名詞義包含植物、製造貨幣的場所，以及引申的「巨額財富」。中文翻譯為「薄荷；造幣廠；巨額財富」。","definition":"1. a type of plant with fragrant leaves that are used to flavor food and in herbal remedies; 2. a place where money is officially made; 3. a very large amount of money (informal).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She put some fresh mint in her tea.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她把一些新鮮薄荷放進茶裡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The new coins were minted at the royal mint.\",\n    \"ch\": \"新硬幣是在皇家造幣廠鑄造的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He made a mint selling software.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他透過銷售軟體賺了一大筆錢。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"新硬幣是在皇家造幣廠鑄造的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3973,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u3::moral::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He has a strong sense of ____.","expectedAnswer":"moral","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He has a strong sense of ____.","clozeAnswer":"moral","exampleTranslation":"他有強烈的道德感。","reference":{"eng":"moral","kk":"/ˈmɔːrəl/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['道德', '品德'], ['寓意']]","chEntries":["道德","品德","寓意"],"practiceMeaning":"他有強烈的道德感。","analysis":"詞源：同上。作為名詞，指一套關於對錯的原則或信念。","definition":"1. a lesson, especially one concerning what is right or prudent, that can be derived from a story, a piece of information, or an experience; 2. a person's standards of behavior or beliefs concerning what is and is not acceptable for them to do.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The moral of the story is to always be kind.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個故事的寓意是永遠都要善良。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has a strong sense of moral.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他有強烈的道德感。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他有強烈的道德感。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3878,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::mostly::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He eats ____ vegetables.","expectedAnswer":"mostly","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He eats ____ vegetables.","clozeAnswer":"mostly","exampleTranslation":"他主要吃蔬菜。","reference":{"eng":"mostly","kk":"/ˈmoʊstli/","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['大部分', '主要'], ['差不多']]","chEntries":["大部分","主要","差不多"],"practiceMeaning":"他主要吃蔬菜。","analysis":"由 'most' (最多) 和 '-ly' (副詞後綴) 組成。核心是「最大程度地」或「佔大部分」。表示在絕大多數情況下、主要地、或涵蓋了絕大部分。","definition":"1. for the most part; mainly; chiefly. 2. in most cases.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The audience was mostly women.\",\n    \"ch\": \"觀眾大部分是女性。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He eats mostly vegetables.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他主要吃蔬菜。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The weather was mostly sunny.\",\n    \"ch\": \"天氣大部分是晴朗的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他主要吃蔬菜。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4132,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::motor::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of the car needs repair.","expectedAnswer":"motor","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of the car needs repair.","clozeAnswer":"motor","exampleTranslation":"汽車的引擎需要修理。","reference":{"eng":"motor","kk":"/ˈməʊtər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['馬達', '電動機'], ['（汽車的）引擎']]","chEntries":["馬達","電動機","引擎"],"practiceMeaning":"汽車的引擎需要修理。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 motor（推動者），是動詞 movere（移動）的名詞形式。核心概念是「產生運動的裝置」。","definition":"1. a machine that produces motion or power for something; 2. an internal combustion engine","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The electric motor is very quiet.\",\n    \"ch\": \"電動馬達非常安靜。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The motor of the car needs repair.\",\n    \"ch\": \"汽車的引擎需要修理。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We heard the sound of the motor starting up.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們聽到了馬達發動的聲音。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"汽車的引擎需要修理。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5466,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::multiple::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She has ____ reasons for her decision.","expectedAnswer":"multiple","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She has ____ reasons for her decision.","clozeAnswer":"multiple","exampleTranslation":"她對她的決定有多重理由。","reference":{"eng":"multiple","kk":"ˈmʌltəpəl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['多個的'], ['多種的'], ['重複的']]","chEntries":["多個的","多種的","重複的"],"practiceMeaning":"她對她的決定有多重理由。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'multiplus'，由 'multus'（許多）和 '-plus'（-倍的）組成。'-plus' 在此類似於「加」或「倍」。'Multus' 意為「多的、許多的」。因此，'multiple' 的核心語意是「由許多部分組成、包含許多事物、或有多個」。它可以用來形容數量、種類或元素的眾多。與 'many' 相比，'multiple' 更強調「由多個獨立部分構成」或「多重性」的概念。","definition":"1. Consisting of, including, or involving more than one individual, element, or part.; 2. Many; numerous.; 3. (Of a number) divisible by another number without a remainder.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The project requires multiple skills.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個專案需要多種技能。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has multiple reasons for her decision.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對她的決定有多重理由。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He suffered multiple injuries in the accident.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在事故中受了多處傷。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她對她的決定有多重理由。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3998,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u3::naked::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ truth is hard to accept.","expectedAnswer":"naked","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ truth is hard to accept.","clozeAnswer":"naked","exampleTranslation":"赤裸的真相很難接受。","reference":{"eng":"naked","kk":"/ˈneɪkɪd/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['裸體的', '赤裸的'], ['沒有掩飾的', '明顯的'], ['（植物）無保護的']]","chEntries":["裸體的","赤裸的","沒有掩飾的","明顯的","無保護的"],"practiceMeaning":"赤裸的真相很難接受。","analysis":"詞源：古英語 'nacod'。指沒有穿衣服的，或沒有任何遮蓋、保護的。","definition":"1. (of a person) not wearing clothes; 2. without any covering or protection; 3. obvious and unconcealed.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was found naked in the street.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他被發現時赤身裸體地躺在街上。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The naked truth is hard to accept.\",\n    \"ch\": \"赤裸的真相很難接受。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The tree was naked in winter.\",\n    \"ch\": \"樹在冬天光禿禿的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"赤裸的真相很難接受。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3179,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::namely::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The report focused on two main issues, ____ budget deficits and unemployment.","expectedAnswer":"namely","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The report focused on two main issues, ____ budget deficits and unemployment.","clozeAnswer":"namely","exampleTranslation":"報告集中討論了兩個主要問題，即預算赤字和失業。","reference":{"eng":"namely","kk":"/ˈneɪmlɪ/","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['即；也就是說']]","chEntries":["即","也就是說"],"practiceMeaning":"報告集中討論了兩個主要問題，即預算赤字和失業。","analysis":"由 'name'（名字）+ 'ly'（副詞後綴）組成，字面意思是「以名字命名」。'Namely' 用於引出對前面所說內容的具體說明、解釋或列舉。它相當於「也就是說」或「即」，用於將一個普遍的陳述細化到具體的項目。","definition":"used when you are going to give more details about something you have just mentioned.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There is one person I want to thank, namely my mother.\",\n    \"ch\": \"有一位我特別想感謝的人，也就是我的母親。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The report focused on two main issues, namely budget deficits and unemployment.\",\n    \"ch\": \"報告集中討論了兩個主要問題，即預算赤字和失業。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We are planning a trip to Europe, namely France and Italy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們正計畫一次歐洲旅行，也就是法國和意大利。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"報告集中討論了兩個主要問題，即預算赤字和失業。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5637,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l8::narrow::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The government is trying to ____ the gap between rich and poor.","expectedAnswer":"narrow","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The government is trying to ____ the gap between rich and poor.","clozeAnswer":"narrow","exampleTranslation":"政府正試圖縮小貧富差距。","reference":{"eng":"narrow","kk":"ˈnæroʊ","tense":"v.","ch":"[['變窄'], ['縮小'], ['限制']]","chEntries":["變窄","縮小","限制"],"practiceMeaning":"政府正試圖縮小貧富差距。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 narow，可能來自古英語 nearu，意為「窄的」。其詞源與原始日耳曼語 *nauraz（窄）相關，更上溯至原始印歐語 *ner-（左；左邊；在左邊）或 *en-（在內）。此字的核心語義是「空間上的狹窄」，並由此引申出範圍、機會、思想、視野的「有限」或「狹隘」。構詞上，此字為單一詞根，無明顯字首字尾。此處為動詞用法，表示主體（寬度、範圍、機會等）「變窄」或「縮小」的動作，或主動「限制」某事物。","definition":"to become less wide; to reduce the width of something; to restrict or limit.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The road narrows considerably ahead.\",\n    \"ch\": \"前方的道路顯著變窄。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government is trying to narrow the gap between rich and poor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府正試圖縮小貧富差距。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"政府正試圖縮小貧富差距。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4311,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::native::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This plant is ____ to the rainforest.","expectedAnswer":"native","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This plant is ____ to the rainforest.","clozeAnswer":"native","exampleTranslation":"這種植物是雨林的本土植物。","reference":{"eng":"native","kk":"/ˈneɪtɪv/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['本國的；土生土長的'], ['天生的；固有的']]","chEntries":["本國的","土生土長的","天生的","固有的"],"practiceMeaning":"這種植物是雨林的本土植物。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'nativus'，意為 'by birth, inborn'，來自 'nasci' (to be born)。這個詞的本義與『出生』直接相關。作為形容詞，它延伸出『出生地固有』、『土生』、『天生具有』等含義。可以指地理上的出生地，也可以指事物固有的、與生俱來的特質。","definition":"belonging to or relating to the place or circumstances in which you were born or that you grew up in; present, existing, or produced naturally in a particular place","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a native speaker of English.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是英語的母語者。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This plant is native to the rainforest.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種植物是雨林的本土植物。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a native talent for music.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她有音樂方面的天賦。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這種植物是雨林的本土植物。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5561,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::network::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The internet is a global computer ____.","expectedAnswer":"network","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The internet is a global computer ____.","clozeAnswer":"network","exampleTranslation":"網際網路是一個全球性的電腦網絡。","reference":{"eng":"network","kk":"ˈnɛtwɜrk","tense":"n.","ch":"[['網絡'], ['網路'], ['網絡系統'], ['人脈']]","chEntries":["網絡","網路","網絡系統","人脈"],"practiceMeaning":"網際網路是一個全球性的電腦網絡。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 \"netwerk\"，由 \"net\"（網）和 \"work\"（工作，結構）組成。\"net\" 源自古英語 \"nett\"，最終可追溯至原始印歐語 \\*ned-（to tie, bind，綁，繫）。\"work\" 源自古英語 \"weorc\"，最終可追溯至原始印歐語 \\*werg-（to do, to work，做，工作）。 \"network\" 最初指「由網狀結構構成的物品」，例如漁網或編織品。隨著科技發展，\"network\" 的語義擴展到「互相連接的系統」，例如電話網絡、電腦網絡。在社會學和商業領域，\"network\" 也指「由人組成的聯繫體系」，即「人脈」或「社交網絡」。核心語義是「由相互連接的元素組成的結構」。","definition":"1. A group of interconnected computers, machines, etc.; 2. A system of roads, railways, etc.; 3. A group of people who know each other and can help each other; 4. A system of connected television or radio stations.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company has an extensive marketing network.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司擁有廣泛的市場網絡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The internet is a global computer network.\",\n    \"ch\": \"網際網路是一個全球性的電腦網絡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Building a strong professional network is important for career advancement.\",\n    \"ch\": \"建立強大的人脈網絡對職業發展很重要。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"網際網路是一個全球性的電腦網絡。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5606,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l7::nursery::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She enrolled her child in a local ____ school.","expectedAnswer":"nursery","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She enrolled her child in a local ____ school.","clozeAnswer":"nursery","exampleTranslation":"她為她的孩子報名了一所當地的托兒所。","reference":{"eng":"nursery","kk":"ˈnɜrsəri","tense":"n.","ch":"[['育嬰室'], ['托兒所'], ['苗圃'], ['（植物）繁殖場']]","chEntries":["育嬰室","托兒所","苗圃","繁殖場"],"practiceMeaning":"她為她的孩子報名了一所當地的托兒所。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 'nursen'（哺乳、照料），而 'nursen' 又源於古法語 'nourrir'（餵養、滋養），最終可追溯至拉丁語 'nutrire'（餵養、滋養）。構詞學上，核心是與「餵養」、「照料」相關的詞根，加上名詞化後綴 '-ery'。'-ery' 字尾常指「地方」、「場所」、「行業」或「收藏」。因此，'nursery' 最初意為「照料嬰兒的地方」，引申為「托兒所」或「育嬰室」。同時，由於「滋養」的概念也適用於植物，故引申出「苗圃」或「繁殖場」的用法。","definition":"1. A room in a house or apartment in which a baby sleeps or plays; 2. A place where children are cared for during the day; 3. A place where young plants are grown for sale.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The baby slept soundly in the nursery.\",\n    \"ch\": \"嬰兒在育嬰室裡睡得很香。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She enrolled her child in a local nursery school.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她為她的孩子報名了一所當地的托兒所。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We bought several saplings from the garden nursery.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們從花園苗圃買了好幾棵樹苗。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她為她的孩子報名了一所當地的托兒所。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5051,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::odds::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ are against us.","expectedAnswer":"odds","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ are against us.","clozeAnswer":"odds","exampleTranslation":"我們勝出的可能性不大。","reference":{"eng":"odds","kk":"ɑːdz","tense":"n.","ch":"[['可能性'], ['機率'], ['（尤指賭博中的）賠率']]","chEntries":["可能性","機率","賠率"],"practiceMeaning":"我們勝出的可能性不大。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語oddes，是 odd（奇數、單獨的）的複數形式。最初可能指「單獨的、不規則的」，引申為「機會、可能性」。其核心語意是「不確定的、難以預測的結果」。在賭博中，odds 指的是「贏的機會與輸的機會的比例」。OCR 掃描時可能將 'o' 誤判為 '0'，或 'd' 誤判為 'cl'。此處修正為 odds，通常以複數形式出現。","definition":"1. the probability of something happening or being the case; 2. the ratio between the amounts staked by parties to a gamble or bet.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"What are the odds of winning the lottery?\",\n    \"ch\": \"中樂透的機率是多少？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The odds are against us.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們勝出的可能性不大。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The odds on the favorite are low.\",\n    \"ch\": \"熱門選手的賠率很低。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們勝出的可能性不大。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5794,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::offering::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company made an initial public ____ of its shares.","expectedAnswer":"offering","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company made an initial public ____ of its shares.","clozeAnswer":"offering","exampleTranslation":"該公司進行了首次公開發行股票。","reference":{"eng":"offering","kk":"ˈɔfərɪŋ","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"供品\"  ],  [    \"祭品\"  ],  [    \"奉獻物\"  ],  [    \"出價\"  ],  [    \"首次公開發行股票（IPO）\"  ]]","chEntries":["供品","祭品","奉獻物","出價","首次公開發行股票"],"practiceMeaning":"該公司進行了首次公開發行股票。","analysis":"此處 offering 作名詞，由動詞offer（提供；奉獻）+ -ing（名詞字尾，表示行為或結果）構成。源自古英語offrian，受拉丁語offerre（奉獻；提供）影響。名詞義可指「自願提供的東西」，特別是宗教上的「供品」或「祭品」。也可指「商業上的出價」或「首次公開發行股票」（IPO），皆為「提供的東西」。語意演變上，由動詞「提供；奉獻」的動作，發展為「被提供的東西」，包括宗教祭品、商業出價，以及金融市場上的「首次公開發行」。","definition":"1. something that is offered, especially a gift or sacrifice to a god; 2. a price offered for something; 3. a company's first offer of stock for sale to the public.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The ancient ritual involved offerings of grain and fruit.\",\n    \"ch\": \"古代儀式涉及穀物和水果的祭品。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company made an initial public offering of its shares.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司進行了首次公開發行股票。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They made a generous offering to the temple.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們向寺廟做出了慷慨的捐獻。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該公司進行了首次公開發行股票。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5590,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::on-time::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Please ensure all deliveries are made ____.","expectedAnswer":"on time","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Please ensure all deliveries are made ____.","clozeAnswer":"on time","exampleTranslation":"請確保所有送貨都準時送達。","reference":{"eng":"on time","kk":"ɒn taɪm","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['準時']]","chEntries":["準時"],"practiceMeaning":"請確保所有送貨都準時送達。","analysis":"此片語由介詞 \"on\" 和名詞 \"time\" 組成。 \"on\" 在這裡表示「基於、根據」的意思，而 \"time\" 指「預定的時間」。 \"on time\" 是一個固定的慣用語，意思是「在預定的或預期的時間內，沒有延遲」。它強調的是準確性，而不是「及時」或「提早」。","definition":"1. Punctually; at the agreed or scheduled time; 2. Not late.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The train arrived on time.\",\n    \"ch\": \"火車準時到達了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please ensure all deliveries are made on time.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請確保所有送貨都準時送達。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is always on time for meetings.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他開會總是準時。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"請確保所有送貨都準時送達。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4418,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u9::opposite::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The shop is on the ____ side of the street.","expectedAnswer":"opposite","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The shop is on the ____ side of the street.","clozeAnswer":"opposite","exampleTranslation":"商店在街對面。","reference":{"eng":"opposite","kk":"/ˈɒpəzɪt/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['相反的', '對立的'], ['對面的', '對著的']]","chEntries":["相反的","對立的","對面的","對著的"],"practiceMeaning":"商店在街對面。","analysis":"詞源自拉丁語 'oppositus'，'ob-' (against) + 'ponere' (to place)。指位置、性質、順序或觀點上完全不同或相對的。","definition":"in a position facing the other way; in a position across from someone or something; completely different from something else.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They hold opposite views on the issue.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們在這個問題上持有相反的觀點。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The shop is on the opposite side of the street.\",\n    \"ch\": \"商店在街對面。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"商店在街對面。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4050,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::oral::adj-n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The patient was prescribed ____ medication.","expectedAnswer":"oral","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The patient was prescribed ____ medication.","clozeAnswer":"oral","exampleTranslation":"患者被開了口服藥。","reference":{"eng":"oral","kk":"/ˈɔrəl/","tense":"adj./n.","ch":"[['口頭的', '口語的 (adj.)'], ['口服的 (adj.)'], ['口試 (n.)']]","chEntries":["口頭的","口語的","口服的","口試"],"practiceMeaning":"患者被開了口服藥。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'oralis'，來自 'os, oris' (mouth)。核心是與「嘴巴」或「口」相關。作為形容詞，指「用嘴說出的」（口頭的、口語的），以及「通過嘴進入體內的」（口服的）。作為名詞，'oral' 常指「口試」，是 'oral examination' 的縮略。","definition":"1. spoken, not written; 2. taken through or relating to the mouth; 3. an examination which is spoken","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"她做了口頭研究報告。\",\n    \"eng\": \"She gave an oral presentation of her research.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"患者被開了口服藥。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The patient was prescribed oral medication.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"期末考是口試。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The final exam is an oral.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"患者被開了口服藥。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3237,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::orbit::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The spacecraft will ____ Mars.","expectedAnswer":"orbit","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The spacecraft will ____ Mars.","clozeAnswer":"orbit","exampleTranslation":"這艘宇宙飛船將繞火星運行。","reference":{"eng":"orbit","kk":"/ˈɔːrbɪt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['繞軌道運行'], ['使繞軌道運行']]","chEntries":["繞軌道運行","使繞軌道運行"],"practiceMeaning":"這艘宇宙飛船將繞火星運行。","analysis":"動詞形式，指天體或其他物體按照軌道移動。強調順應自然或物理規律的運行。與名詞『orbit』的意義一致。","definition":"move in an orbit round (a central star, planet, or moon).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The Moon orbits the Earth.\",\n    \"ch\": \"月球繞地球運行。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The spacecraft will orbit Mars.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這艘宇宙飛船將繞火星運行。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這艘宇宙飛船將繞火星運行。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U41"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5850,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::partly::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He was ____ responsible for the accident.","expectedAnswer":"partly","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He was ____ responsible for the accident.","clozeAnswer":"partly","exampleTranslation":"他對事故負有部分責任。","reference":{"eng":"partly","kk":"ˈpɑːrtli","tense":"adv.","ch":"[  [    \"部分地\"  ],  [    \"在某種程度上\"  ],  [    \"多少\"  ]]","chEntries":["部分地","在某種程度上","多少"],"practiceMeaning":"他對事故負有部分責任。","analysis":"此字由 'part' (部分) 加上副詞字尾 '-ly' 構成。'Part' 源自拉丁語 'partire' (to divide)。'-ly' 是常見的副詞字尾，將名詞或形容詞轉化為副詞。'Partly' 的核心語意是「不是完全地」、「在一定程度上」，表示某事物僅部分實現或僅部分為真。例如，也可指「有一定程度地」。","definition":"1. To some extent; in part.; 2. Not completely.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The success was partly due to luck.\",\n    \"ch\": \"成功的部分原因在於運氣。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was partly responsible for the accident.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對事故負有部分責任。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The room was partly furnished.\",\n    \"ch\": \"房間只部分佈置了家具。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She was partly to blame for the misunderstanding.\",\n    \"ch\": \"誤會的產生她也有一定程度的責任。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他對事故負有部分責任。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4147,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::passage::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Please read the following ____ carefully.","expectedAnswer":"passage","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Please read the following ____ carefully.","clozeAnswer":"passage","exampleTranslation":"請仔細閱讀以下段落。","reference":{"eng":"passage","kk":"/ˈpæsɪdʒ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['通道', '走廊'], ['（書籍、文章等的）段落', '樂句'], ['（時間）流逝'], ['通過', '通行']]","chEntries":["通道","走廊","段落","樂句","流逝","通過","通行"],"practiceMeaning":"請仔細閱讀以下段落。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 passus（步伐），是動詞 pandere（擴展，打開）的過去分詞。核心概念是「前進」或「被打開的路徑」。引申為物理上的通道、時間的流逝、口頭或書面表達的一部分，以及通過的行為。","definition":"1. a narrow area or route that connects one place to another; 2. a portion of a written work or musical composition; 3. the act or process of moving through, under, over, or past something; 4. the continuous passing of time","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The narrow passage led to a hidden room.\",\n    \"ch\": \"狹窄的通道通往一個隱藏的房間。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please read the following passage carefully.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請仔細閱讀以下段落。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"With the passage of time, things will change.\",\n    \"ch\": \"隨著時間的流逝，事情會改變。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They had difficulty in passage through the mountains.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們在穿越山脈時遇到了困難。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"請仔細閱讀以下段落。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3315,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::peculiar::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This custom is ____ to this region.","expectedAnswer":"peculiar","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This custom is ____ to this region.","clozeAnswer":"peculiar","exampleTranslation":"這種習俗是這個地區特有的。","reference":{"eng":"peculiar","kk":"/pɪˈkjuːliər/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['奇怪的；奇特的'], ['（尤指）特有的；獨特的']]","chEntries":["奇怪的","奇特的","特有的","獨特的"],"practiceMeaning":"這種習俗是這個地區特有的。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'peculiaris'，由 'peculium' (私有財產) 演變而來，原意為「屬於某人自己的」，後引申為「特殊的」，再進一步發展為「奇怪的」。","definition":"1. strange or odd; unusual; 2. belonging exclusively to one person, group, or thing.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was a peculiar smell in the room.\",\n    \"ch\": \"房間裡有一種奇怪的氣味。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This custom is peculiar to this region.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種習俗是這個地區特有的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He had a peculiar way of walking.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他走路的方式很奇特。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這種習俗是這個地區特有的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5053,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::pedestrian::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The novel's plot was predictable and ____.","expectedAnswer":"pedestrian","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The novel's plot was predictable and ____.","clozeAnswer":"pedestrian","exampleTranslation":"這本小說的情節可預測且乏味。","reference":{"eng":"pedestrian","kk":"pəˈdɛstriən","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['步行的'], ['（事物）平常的'], ['乏味的'], ['缺乏想像力的']]","chEntries":["步行的","平常的","乏味的","缺乏想像力的"],"practiceMeaning":"這本小說的情節可預測且乏味。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語pedester，意為「步行」。pedester 又來自pes, pedis（腳）。pedestrian 作形容詞，原意是「用腳走的、步行的」。引申指「平凡的、缺乏想像力的、乏味的」，因為步行不像乘車或飛行那樣有速度感或新奇感。其核心語意是「普通的、缺乏特色的」。","definition":"1. of or relating to pedestrians; 2. lacking inspiration or excitement; dull.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He offered some pedestrian observations.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他提出了一些平淡無奇的觀察。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The novel's plot was predictable and pedestrian.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本小說的情節可預測且乏味。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這本小說的情節可預測且乏味。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4162,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::person::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He's a tricky ____ to understand.","expectedAnswer":"person","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He's a tricky ____ to understand.","clozeAnswer":"person","exampleTranslation":"他是一個難以理解的人。","reference":{"eng":"person","kk":"/ˈpɜːrsn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['人']]","chEntries":["人"],"practiceMeaning":"他是一個難以理解的人。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 persona（面具，角色，人）。核心概念是「具有個體意識和行為能力的個體」。","definition":"a human being regarded as an individual","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a very kind person.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是一個非常善良的人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He's a tricky person to understand.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一個難以理解的人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Every person has their own unique qualities.\",\n    \"ch\": \"每個人都有自己獨特的品質。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他是一個難以理解的人。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5、C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6085,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::petition::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The students organized a ____ to protest the tuition increase.","expectedAnswer":"petition","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The students organized a ____ to protest the tuition increase.","clozeAnswer":"petition","exampleTranslation":"學生們組織了一場請願，抗議學費上漲。","reference":{"eng":"petition","kk":"pəˈtɪʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"請願書\"  ],  [    \"請願\"  ],  [    \"申請\"  ]]","chEntries":["請願書","請願","申請"],"practiceMeaning":"學生們組織了一場請願，抗議學費上漲。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 petitio，是 petere（to seek, to ask for, to aim at）的結果名詞。Petere 最終來源於 proto-Indo-European *pet-「to fall, to fly」。核心語義是「尋求」或「請求」。作為名詞，petition 指的是正式的書面請求或懇求，通常簽署有許多人的名字，以表達對某個機構或個人的訴求。","definition":"a formal written request, typically signed by many people, appealing to an authority with respect to a particular cause.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They submitted a petition to the government demanding action.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們向政府提交了一份要求採取行動的請願書。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The students organized a petition to protest the tuition increase.\",\n    \"ch\": \"學生們組織了一場請願，抗議學費上漲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A petition was signed by hundreds of residents.\",\n    \"ch\": \"數百名居民簽署了一份請願書。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"學生們組織了一場請願，抗議學費上漲。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6129,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::pickup::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"I'll give you a ____ on my way home.","expectedAnswer":"pickup","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"I'll give you a ____ on my way home.","clozeAnswer":"pickup","exampleTranslation":"我回家路上會順道載你。","reference":{"eng":"pickup","kk":"ˈpɪkˌʌp","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"皮卡車\"  ],  [    \"接載\"  ],  [    \"撿起\"  ],  [    \"改良\"  ],  [    \"氣氛\"  ],  [    \"搭便車\"  ]]","chEntries":["皮卡車","接載","撿起","改良","氣氛","搭便車"],"practiceMeaning":"我回家路上會順道載你。","analysis":"此字由動詞片語 pick up 構成的名詞。pick 的核心語義是「挑選；選擇」，up 是方向副詞，表示「向上」。pick up 的核心語義是「向上拾起」，引申為「接載；撿起；改良；改善；學會」。此名詞 captures 這些不同的義項。例如，a pickup truck（皮卡車）；give someone a pickup（接載某人）；a pickup in sales（銷售的提升）；a pickup in atmosphere（氣氛的活躍）。因此，此名詞涵蓋了動詞片語的多種義項。","definition":"1. a small truck with low sides and an open back, used for carrying goods; 2. the act of collecting someone or something; 3. a device for picking up sound or signals; 4. an improvement in speed, activity, or mood.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He drove a red pickup truck.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他開了一輛紅色皮卡車。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I'll give you a pickup on my way home.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我回家路上會順道載你。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was a pickup in the stock market.\",\n    \"ch\": \"股市出現了回升。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我回家路上會順道載你。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4251,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::pile::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He has a ____ of work to do.","expectedAnswer":"pile","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He has a ____ of work to do.","clozeAnswer":"pile","exampleTranslation":"他有一大堆工作要做。","reference":{"eng":"pile","kk":"/paɪl/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['堆'], ['一堆'], ['大量']]","chEntries":["堆","一堆","大量"],"practiceMeaning":"他有一大堆工作要做。","analysis":"源自古法語 'pile'，意為「柱子、堆」。'Pile' 的核心意義是「聚集起來的東西」，強調量多或高度。這個概念可以從具體的「堆積物」延伸到抽象的「大量」。","definition":"a heap of things laid or lying one on top of another; a large quantity of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was a large pile of books on the table.\",\n    \"ch\": \"桌子上有一大堆書。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has a pile of work to do.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他有一大堆工作要做。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他有一大堆工作要做。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5471,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::plentiful::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There was a ____ supply of food at the feast.","expectedAnswer":"plentiful","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There was a ____ supply of food at the feast.","clozeAnswer":"plentiful","exampleTranslation":"宴會上有充足的食物供應。","reference":{"eng":"plentiful","kk":"ˈplɛntɪfəl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['豐富的'], ['充裕的'], ['許多的']]","chEntries":["豐富的","充裕的","許多的"],"practiceMeaning":"宴會上有充足的食物供應。","analysis":"此字由名詞 'plenty'（充足）加上形容詞字尾 '-ful'（來自古英語 '-ful'，表示「充滿……的」）構成。'Plenty' 本身源自古法語 'plente'，意為「滿足、充足」，最終來自拉丁語 'plenitas'（充滿），'plenus'（滿的）。因此，'plentiful' 的核心語意是「充滿的、量大的、足夠的」，表示某物非常豐富，有充足的供應，超過了最低需求。","definition":"1. Existing in or yielding great quantities; abundant.; 2. Abundant; ample; copious.; 3. Having plenty of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Fresh fruit is plentiful in the summer.\",\n    \"ch\": \"夏季水果豐富。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was a plentiful supply of food at the feast.\",\n    \"ch\": \"宴會上有充足的食物供應。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Opportunities for graduates are plentiful.\",\n    \"ch\": \"畢業生的機會很多（充裕）。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"宴會上有充足的食物供應。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6184,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::plural::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The word 'children' is the ____ of 'child'.","expectedAnswer":"plural","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The word 'children' is the ____ of 'child'.","clozeAnswer":"plural","exampleTranslation":"「children」是「child」的複數。","reference":{"eng":"plural","kk":"ˈplʊrəl","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"複數\"  ],  [    \"複數形式\"  ]]","chEntries":["複數","複數形式"],"practiceMeaning":"「children」是「child」的複數。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 plūrālis，是 plus（更多）的衍生形容詞。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作為名詞，其核心語義是由形容詞 plural「複數的」名詞化而來，指「表示兩個或兩個以上數量的形式或狀態」。詞源中的「更多」概念引申出「多數」和「複數」的用法。","definition":"1. the plural form of a word.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"When forming the plural, we often add 's'.\",\n    \"ch\": \"形成複數時，我們經常加 's'。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The word 'children' is the plural of 'child'.\",\n    \"ch\": \"「children」是「child」的複數。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The plural of 'mouse' is 'mice'.\",\n    \"ch\": \"「mouse」的複數是「mice」。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"「children」是「child」的複數。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3872,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::political::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He made a ____ speech.","expectedAnswer":"political","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He made a ____ speech.","clozeAnswer":"political","exampleTranslation":"他發表了一篇政治演說。","reference":{"eng":"political","kk":"/pəˈlɪtɪkl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['政治的']]","chEntries":["政治的"],"practiceMeaning":"他發表了一篇政治演說。","analysis":"源自古希臘 'politikos'，意指「關於公民」、「國家」、「政府」等。與政治事務、政府、權力、政策等相關。","definition":"of or relating to the government or public affairs of a country or countries.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The two countries have strong political ties.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這兩個國家有著緊密的政治聯繫。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He made a political speech.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他發表了一篇政治演說。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The decision has significant political implications.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個決定具有重大的政治影響。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他發表了一篇政治演說。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4455,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::poll::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ will be held next Tuesday.","expectedAnswer":"poll","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ will be held next Tuesday.","clozeAnswer":"poll","exampleTranslation":"投票將在下週二舉行。","reference":{"eng":"poll","kk":"/pol/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['民意測驗'], ['投票'], ['（總）票數'], ['（在一處）民意調查']]","chEntries":["民意測驗","投票","票數","民意調查"],"practiceMeaning":"投票將在下週二舉行。","analysis":"源自古英語 pūl，意為「頭」、「頭顱」。後來在16世紀演變成「公眾的意見」或「選舉」。語意從「頭」（代表個人）引申為「許多人的意見總和」，即「民意」。也可以指「投票」的行為或結果。","definition":"1. A survey of public opinion; 2. The process of voting in an election; 3. The total number of votes cast in an election.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The latest poll shows a significant shift in public opinion.\",\n    \"ch\": \"最新的民意測驗顯示公眾意見有顯著轉變。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The poll will be held next Tuesday.\",\n    \"ch\": \"投票將在下週二舉行。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The exit poll indicated who would win the election.\",\n    \"ch\": \"出口民調預示了誰將贏得選舉。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"投票將在下週二舉行。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6237,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::preliminary::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The report contained only ____ findings.","expectedAnswer":"preliminary","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The report contained only ____ findings.","clozeAnswer":"preliminary","exampleTranslation":"該報告只包含初步的調查結果。","reference":{"eng":"preliminary","kk":"prɪˈlɪmɪnɛri","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"初步的\"  ],  [    \"預備的\"  ],  [    \"先行的\"  ]]","chEntries":["初步的","預備的","先行的"],"practiceMeaning":"該報告只包含初步的調查結果。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 præliminarius，由 præ-（在…之前）和 limen（門檻）組成，意為「在門檻之前」，引申為「進入之前，準備階段」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作形容詞時，指發生在主要事件、行動或程序之前，作為準備或預示。中文翻譯為「初步的；預備的；先行的」。","definition":"1. happening before a more important event or activity, especially in order to prepare for it; 2. happening too soon or before the normal time.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They held preliminary talks to discuss the details.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們舉行了初步會談以討論細節。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The report contained only preliminary findings.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該報告只包含初步的調查結果。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is just a preliminary estimate.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這只是一個初步的估計。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該報告只包含初步的調查結果。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5414,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::preservation::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Wildlife ____ efforts have increased.","expectedAnswer":"preservation","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Wildlife ____ efforts have increased.","clozeAnswer":"preservation","exampleTranslation":"野生動物保護的努力已經增加。","reference":{"eng":"preservation","kk":"ˌprezərˈveɪʃn","tense":"n.","ch":"[['保存'], ['保護'], ['維護']]","chEntries":["保存","保護","維護"],"practiceMeaning":"野生動物保護的努力已經增加。","analysis":"此字為派生詞，由動詞 \"preserve\" 加上名詞化字尾 \"-ation\" 構成。\"preserve\" 源自古法語 \"preserver\"，其拉丁語詞源為 \"praeservare\"，意為\"事先保存\"。其中 \"prae-\" 是表示\"事先\"、\"在前面\"的字首，\"servare\" 則是\"保存\"、\"守護\"的意思。構詞上，\"prae-\" 提供了時間上的預防性，\"servare\" 提供了核心的\"保護\"與\"守護\"語意。字尾 \"-ation\" 將動詞轉化為抽象名詞，表示「保存」的行為、狀態或結果。因此，\"preservation\" 指的是為了防止損壞、變質或消失而進行的保護與維護工作，尤其常用於文化遺產、自然環境或食品等方面。","definition":"the act of preserving something; the state of being preserved; the protection of something from harm or destruction; the maintenance of something in its original or existing state.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The preservation of ancient artifacts is crucial.\",\n    \"ch\": \"保存古代文物至關重要。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Wildlife preservation efforts have increased.\",\n    \"ch\": \"野生動物保護的努力已經增加。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The preservation of food through canning is a common method.\",\n    \"ch\": \"通過罐裝保存食物是一種常見的方法。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"野生動物保護的努力已經增加。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5486,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::privacy::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He values his ____ and rarely gives interviews.","expectedAnswer":"privacy","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He values his ____ and rarely gives interviews.","clozeAnswer":"privacy","exampleTranslation":"他重視個人隱私，很少接受採訪。","reference":{"eng":"privacy","kk":"ˈpraɪvəsi","tense":"n.","ch":"[['隱私'], ['私密性'], ['清靜']]","chEntries":["隱私","私密性","清靜"],"practiceMeaning":"他重視個人隱私，很少接受採訪。","analysis":"此字由形容詞 'private'（私人的）加上名詞字尾 '-cy'（來自拉丁語 '-tia' 或 '-cia'）構成。'-cy' 用來形成表示「狀態、品質或條件」的名詞。因此，'privacy' 指的是「私人的狀態、私密的品質，或不受干擾的寧靜」。它強調的是個人空間、資訊和生活不受外部侵擾的權利或狀態。核心語意是「不受干擾或公開的狀態」。","definition":"1. The state of being free from intrusion or disturbance by other people.; 2. The condition of being secluded or secret.; 3. Freedom from publicity or notoriety.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Protecting the privacy of users is crucial.\",\n    \"ch\": \"保護用戶的隱私至關重要。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He values his privacy and rarely gives interviews.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他重視個人隱私，很少接受採訪。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The hotel room offered a sense of privacy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這間飯店房間提供了隱私感。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他重視個人隱私，很少接受採訪。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3942,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::product::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The harvest was a ____ of hard work.","expectedAnswer":"product","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The harvest was a ____ of hard work.","clozeAnswer":"product","exampleTranslation":"這次豐收是辛勤勞動的成果。","reference":{"eng":"product","kk":"/ˈprɒdʌkt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['產品'], ['成果', '結果']]","chEntries":["產品","成果","結果"],"practiceMeaning":"這次豐收是辛勤勞動的成果。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'productum'，是動詞 'producere' (意為「生產、伸展」) 的過去分詞名詞化。指生產出來的物品，或因某事而產生的結果。","definition":"1. a thing that is manufactured or refined for sale; 2. something that is the result of a process.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a new product from our company.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是我們公司的新產品。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The harvest was a product of hard work.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這次豐收是辛勤勞動的成果。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This software is a successful product.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這款軟體是一款成功的產品。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這次豐收是辛勤勞動的成果。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3192,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::project::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She is working on a research ____ for her thesis.","expectedAnswer":"project","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She is working on a research ____ for her thesis.","clozeAnswer":"project","exampleTranslation":"她正在為她的論文進行一個研究項目。","reference":{"eng":"project","kk":"/ˈprɒdʒɛkt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['項目；計畫'], ['（尤指政府或公司的）工程']]","chEntries":["項目","計畫","工程"],"practiceMeaning":"她正在為她的論文進行一個研究項目。","analysis":"名詞用法，源自動詞 'project'。'Project' 指的是一項有特定目標、計劃和時間表的複雜工作或活動，通常需要多個步驟來完成。它可以是個人、公司或政府的計畫。常強調其規模、複雜性和預定的完成時間。","definition":"1. an individual or collaborative enterprise that is carefully planned and designed to achieve a particular aim; 2. a planned piece of work that has a specific purpose.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The construction project is expected to be completed by next year.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個建築項目預計將在明年完工。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is working on a research project for her thesis.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她正在為她的論文進行一個研究項目。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government has launched a new infrastructure project.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府啟動了一個新的基礎設施項目。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她正在為她的論文進行一個研究項目。","sourceName":"字彙王、龍騰課本","unitName":"U40、L2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3873,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::property::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ was inherited from her grandparents.","expectedAnswer":"property","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ was inherited from her grandparents.","clozeAnswer":"property","exampleTranslation":"這份財產是從她祖父母那裡繼承來的。","reference":{"eng":"property","kk":"/ˈprɑːpərti/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['財產', '財物'], ['所有權'], ['特性', '屬性']]","chEntries":["財產","財物","所有權","特性","屬性"],"practiceMeaning":"這份財產是從她祖父母那裡繼承來的。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'proprietas'，意為「所有權」、「特徵」，其根源是 'proprius' (one's own)。核心概念是「屬於某人」的東西。引申為個人擁有的動產或不動產、財產的所有權，以及事物的固有特質或屬性。","definition":"1. things that are owned by a person or company. 2. the exclusive right to own, possess, use, and dispose of something. 3. a quality or characteristic.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He owns a lot of property.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他擁有許多財產。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The property was inherited from her grandparents.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這份財產是從她祖父母那裡繼承來的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Water has the property of expanding when it freezes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"水具有結冰時膨脹的特性。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這份財產是從她祖父母那裡繼承來的。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U1、L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3181,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::prosperous::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The merchant became very ____ through his trading business.","expectedAnswer":"prosperous","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The merchant became very ____ through his trading business.","clozeAnswer":"prosperous","exampleTranslation":"這位商人通過他的貿易生意變得非常富裕。","reference":{"eng":"prosperous","kk":"/ˈprɒspərəs/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['繁榮的；興旺的'], ['富裕的']]","chEntries":["繁榮的","興旺的","富裕的"],"practiceMeaning":"這位商人通過他的貿易生意變得非常富裕。","analysis":"形容詞，源自動詞 'prosper'。表示處於興旺、繁榮、成功或富裕的狀態。可以用來形容國家、城市、企業或個人，指他們在經濟上或整體狀況上取得了良好的發展，通常伴隨著財富和安逸。","definition":"1. successful in material terms; flourishing financially; 2. characterized by success and good fortune.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was a prosperous period for the country.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那是國家的一個繁榮時期。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The merchant became very prosperous through his trading business.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位商人通過他的貿易生意變得非常富裕。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She lives in a prosperous neighborhood.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她住在一處富裕的社區。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這位商人通過他的貿易生意變得非常富裕。","sourceName":"字彙王、龍騰課本","unitName":"U40、L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5142,"wordRef":"字彙王::u62::provision::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The contract includes a ____ for early termination.","expectedAnswer":"provision","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The contract includes a ____ for early termination.","clozeAnswer":"provision","exampleTranslation":"合約包含一項提前終止的規定。","reference":{"eng":"provision","kk":"prəˈvɪʒən","tense":"n.","ch":"[['供應'], ['糧食、補給品'], ['規定、條款'], ['預備']]","chEntries":["供應","糧食、補給品","規定、條款","預備"],"practiceMeaning":"合約包含一項提前終止的規定。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 provisio，來自 providere（預見、準備、供應），由 pro-（向前）+ videre（看見）組成。核心語意是「預見並為未來做準備」。引申為「供應（尤指糧食和物資）」、「為未來做的準備」、「法律或合約中的規定或條款」。","definition":"the action of providing or supplying something for use; an amount of food, drink, or other necessary supplies; a condition or requirement in a legal document.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The army needs adequate provision of food and ammunition.\",\n    \"ch\": \"軍隊需要足夠的糧食和彈藥補給。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The contract includes a provision for early termination.\",\n    \"ch\": \"合約包含一項提前終止的規定。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They made provision for their old age.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們為晚年做好了準備。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"合約包含一項提前終止的規定。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U62"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4558,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::pump::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The water ____ needs to be repaired.","expectedAnswer":"pump","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The water ____ needs to be repaired.","clozeAnswer":"pump","exampleTranslation":"抽水機需要修理。","reference":{"eng":"pump","kk":"/pʌmp/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['泵', '抽水機']]","chEntries":["泵","抽水機"],"practiceMeaning":"抽水機需要修理。","analysis":"源自荷蘭語 'pomp'，可能與 'pump' (to move up and down - 上下移動) 的動作有關。指用來抽吸液體或氣體的裝置。","definition":"1. a mechanical device for moving liquids or gases.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He filled the car with gas at the pump.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在加油機為汽車加油。