allow to escape.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police released the suspect after questioning.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警方在訊問後釋放了嫌疑犯。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company will release its annual report next month.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司將於下月發布年度報告。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Exercise can help release stress.\",\n    \"ch\": \"運動有助於緩解壓力。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"公司將於下月發布年度報告。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3915,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::religious::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She is a very ____ person and attends church every Sunday.","expectedAnswer":"religious","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She is a very ____ person and attends church every Sunday.","clozeAnswer":"religious","exampleTranslation":"她是一個非常虔誠的人，每週日都去教堂。","reference":{"eng":"religious","kk":"/rɪˈlɪdʒəs/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['宗教的', '虔誠的'], ['嚴謹的', '認真的']]","chEntries":["宗教的","虔誠的","嚴謹的","認真的"],"practiceMeaning":"她是一個非常虔誠的人，每週日都去教堂。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'religiosus'，意為「虔誠的」，與 'religio' (意為「宗教、敬畏」) 有關，可能源自 'religare' (意為「綁定、約束」)。最初指與神聖事物相關，引申為「虔誠」；另一層語意則指對某事物的嚴謹態度，類似於「恪守規矩」。","definition":"1. relating to or believing in a particular religion; 2. showing or having strong beliefs about religion; 3. very careful and thorough.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Many people hold strong religious beliefs.\",\n    \"ch\": \"許多人持有堅定的宗教信仰。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a very religious person and attends church every Sunday.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是一個非常虔誠的人，每週日都去教堂。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They have a religious adherence to their daily schedule.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們嚴格遵守他們的日常行程。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她是一個非常虔誠的人，每週日都去教堂。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5656,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l8::rent::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They couldn't afford the ____.","expectedAnswer":"rent","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They couldn't afford the ____.","clozeAnswer":"rent","exampleTranslation":"他們付不起租金。","reference":{"eng":"rent","kk":"rɛnt","tense":"n.","ch":"[['租金'], ['租賃']]","chEntries":["租金","租賃"],"practiceMeaning":"他們付不起租金。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 rent(en)，來自古法語 rente，意為「年貢、收入」，再追溯至拉丁語 reditus，意為「歸還、收入」，是 reddere（歸還，to give back）的動名詞。redd- 來自原始印歐語 *do-（給予）。核心語義為「定期支付的金額」或「歸還的價值」。構詞上，此字直接來自拉丁語中的「歸還」、「收入」概念。此處為名詞用法，指代「租用某物（如房屋、土地）所需的定期付款」。","definition":"a payment made to a landlord for the use of property or land; a period of paying for the use of property.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The rent is due on the first of the month.\",\n    \"ch\": \"租金於每月的第一天到期。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They couldn't afford the rent.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們付不起租金。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們付不起租金。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5658,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l8::rental::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We had to pay a ____ fee for the equipment.","expectedAnswer":"rental","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We had to pay a ____ fee for the equipment.","clozeAnswer":"rental","exampleTranslation":"我們必須支付設備的租賃費。","reference":{"eng":"rental","kk":"ˈrɛntl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['出租的'], ['租用的'], ['關於租賃的']]","chEntries":["出租的","租用的","關於租賃的"],"practiceMeaning":"我們必須支付設備的租賃費。","analysis":"此字由 rent（租金，出租）+ -al（形容詞字尾）構成。rent 源自中古英語 rent(en)，來自古法語 rente，再追溯至拉丁語 reditus（收入，歸還）。-al 是常見的形容詞字尾，表示「與……有關的」。構詞上，rent 提供核心的「租賃」概念，-al 使其成為形容詞。此處為形容詞用法，描述與「租賃」、「出租」相關的事物。","definition":"relating to or available for rent; paid or received as rent.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company offers a wide range of rental cars.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司提供各種各樣的租賃汽車。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We had to pay a rental fee for the equipment.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們必須支付設備的租賃費。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們必須支付設備的租賃費。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5443,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::residence::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The embassy is the ambassador's official ____.","expectedAnswer":"residence","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The embassy is the ambassador's official ____.","clozeAnswer":"residence","exampleTranslation":"大使館是大使的官邸。","reference":{"eng":"residence","kk":"ˈrezɪdəns","tense":"n.","ch":"[['住所'], ['居住地'], ['居住權'], ['官邸']]","chEntries":["住所","居住地","居住權","官邸"],"practiceMeaning":"大使館是大使的官邸。","analysis":"此字為派生詞，由拉丁語 \"residens\" (居住者，來自 \"residere\"，意為\"居住\") 加上名詞化字尾 \"-ce\" (或 \"-cy\") 構成。\"residere\" 由 \"re-\" (回歸、持續) 和 \"sedere\" (坐、居住) 構成。構詞上，\"resid-\" 提供了核心的「居住」語意，\"-ence\" 是名詞字尾，將「居住」的動作或狀態轉化為名詞。因此，\"residence\" 指的是「居住的場所」、「住所」，或是「居住的行為或狀態」，也可能指「居住權」或「官邸」。","definition":"the place where someone lives, especially a house or home; the state of living in a particular place; an official dwelling.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His primary residence is in London.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的主要住所是倫敦。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The embassy is the ambassador's official residence.\",\n    \"ch\": \"大使館是大使的官邸。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Proof of residence is required for the application.\",\n    \"ch\": \"申請需要居住證明。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"大使館是大使的官邸。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3110,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::resignation::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He submitted his ____ today.","expectedAnswer":"resignation","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He submitted his ____ today.","clozeAnswer":"resignation","exampleTranslation":"他今天提交了辭職信。","reference":{"eng":"resignation","kk":"/ˌrezɪɡˈneɪʃn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['辭職；辭職書'], ['順從；聽任']]","chEntries":["辭職","辭職書","順從","聽任"],"practiceMeaning":"他今天提交了辭職信。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'resignare' 的名詞形式。指「放棄」或「接受」的行為或狀態。\n1. 辭職；辭職書：指離開職位的行為，或正式提交的辭職文件。\n2. 順從；聽任：指接受無法改變的事實或情況，帶有平和或無奈的態度。","definition":"1. the act of giving up your job; 2. a formal statement saying that you want to leave your job; 3. the acceptance of something unpleasant that you cannot do anything about.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her resignation surprised everyone.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的辭職令大家感到驚訝。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He submitted his resignation today.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他今天提交了辭職信。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was a sense of resignation in his voice.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的聲音中帶著一絲聽任的語氣。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他今天提交了辭職信。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3111,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::restore::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They are working to ____ the ancient castle.","expectedAnswer":"restore","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They are working to ____ the ancient castle.","clozeAnswer":"restore","exampleTranslation":"他們正在努力修復這座古老的城堡。","reference":{"eng":"restore","kk":"/rɪˈstɔːr/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['恢復；復原'], ['修復；重建'], ['歸還；恢復（權利、地位）']]","chEntries":["恢復","復原","修復","重建","歸還"],"practiceMeaning":"他們正在努力修復這座古老的城堡。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'restaurare'，'re-' (again) + 'staurare' (to set up, to renew)。核心意義是「重新建立」或「恢復」。\n1. 恢復；復原：指使事物回到原來的狀態、健康或功能。\n2. 修復；重建：指修繕破損的建築物、藝術品或其他事物，使其恢復原貌。\n3. 歸還；恢復（權利、地位）：指將先前被剝奪或失去的東西歸還給原主，或恢復其原有的權力或地位。","definition":"1. to bring back a situation or thing to its former condition; 2. to repair something that is old or damaged; 3. to give someone back something that was lost or taken away.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The doctor helped him to restore his health.\",\n    \"ch\": \"醫生幫助他恢復了健康。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They are working to restore the ancient castle.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們正在努力修復這座古老的城堡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government promised to restore public trust.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府承諾恢復公眾的信任。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們正在努力修復這座古老的城堡。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5802,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::resume::vt","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The meeting will ____ at 2 PM.","expectedAnswer":"resume","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The meeting will ____ at 2 PM.","clozeAnswer":"resume","exampleTranslation":"會議將於下午兩點恢復。","reference":{"eng":"resume","kk":"rɪˈzum","tense":"vt.","ch":"[  [    \"恢復（某事）\"  ],  [    \"重新開始\"  ]]","chEntries":["恢復","重新開始"],"practiceMeaning":"會議將於下午兩點恢復。","analysis":"此字為及物動詞，源自拉丁語resumere，由re-（再次）+sumere（拿起；採取）組成。sumere本身來自sub-（在……下面）+emere（拿；購買）。核心語義是「再次拿起」或「重新開始」。語意演變上，從「再次拿取」引申為「恢復中斷的活動或狀態」。","definition":"1. to begin again or continue after a pause or interruption; 2. to take up again.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He decided to resume his studies after a year off.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他決定休學一年後重拾學業。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The meeting will resume at 2 PM.\",\n    \"ch\": \"會議將於下午兩點恢復。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please resume your seat.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請回到您的座位上。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"會議將於下午兩點恢復。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3115,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::retire::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The general decided to ____ after many years of service.","expectedAnswer":"retire","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The general decided to ____ after many years of service.","clozeAnswer":"retire","exampleTranslation":"將軍在服役多年後決定退役。","reference":{"eng":"retire","kk":"/rɪˈtaɪər/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['退休'], ['退役'], ['就寢；休息'], ['退居；隱退']]","chEntries":["退休","退役","就寢","休息","退居","隱退"],"practiceMeaning":"將軍在服役多年後決定退役。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'retirare'，'re-' (back) + 'tendere' (to stretch, to draw)。原意為「退後」，引申為「脫離」或「休息」。\n1. 退休：指停止工作，通常是達到法定年齡或工作年限。\n2. 退役：指軍人或運動員結束其服役或參賽生涯。\n3. 就寢；休息：指準備睡覺或進行休息。\n4. 退居；隱退：指退出公眾事務或活躍的社會生活，過上較為平靜的生活。","definition":"1. to stop working, usually because you have reached an age at which you can stop; 2. to stop being in the army, navy, or air force; 3. to go to bed; 4. to withdraw from public life.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He plans to retire next year.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他計劃明年退休。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The general decided to retire after many years of service.\",\n    \"ch\": \"將軍在服役多年後決定退役。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's time to retire for the night.\",\n    \"ch\": \"是時候去睡覺了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The actor retired from the stage at the height of his career.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位演員在他事業的巔峰時期退出了舞台。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"將軍在服役多年後決定退役。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5572,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::retrace::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Let's ____ the history of this ancient artifact.","expectedAnswer":"retrace","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Let's ____ the history of this ancient artifact.","clozeAnswer":"retrace","exampleTranslation":"讓我們來追溯這件古代文物的歷史。","reference":{"eng":"retrace","kk":"riˈtreɪs","tense":"v.","ch":"[['重走'], ['回溯'], ['追溯']]","chEntries":["重走","回溯","追溯"],"practiceMeaning":"讓我們來追溯這件古代文物的歷史。","analysis":"此字由字首 \"re-\"（again, back，再次，向後）和動詞 \"trace\"（追蹤，描繪）組成。\"trace\" 源自古法語 \"tracer\"，來自拉丁語 \"tractus\"，是 \"trahere\"（to draw, pull，繪製，拉）的過去分詞。\"tractus\" 的語義是「被拉出的線條」或「走過的軌跡」。\"re-\" 加上 \"trace\"，核心語義是「沿著原來的路徑返回」或「重新追溯」。它可以指物理上的「重走」，例如「重走犯罪現場」；也可以指抽象上的「追溯某事的來源、原因或歷史」，例如「追溯某個想法的起源」。","definition":"1. Go back over (a route or journey); 2. Trace back the course or steps of.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police decided to retrace their steps to the scene of the crime.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警方決定重走一遍到犯罪現場的路徑。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Let's retrace the history of this ancient artifact.\",\n    \"ch\": \"讓我們來追溯這件古代文物的歷史。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He tried to retrace his thoughts before the accident.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他試圖回溯事故發生前的思緒。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"讓我們來追溯這件古代文物的歷史。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3255,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::rhyme::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Can you think of a ____ for 'cat'?","expectedAnswer":"rhyme","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Can you think of a ____ for 'cat'?","clozeAnswer":"rhyme","exampleTranslation":"你能想到一個與 'cat' 押韻的詞嗎？","reference":{"eng":"rhyme","kk":"/raɪm/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['押韻'], ['韻腳']]","chEntries":["押韻","韻腳"],"practiceMeaning":"你能想到一個與 'cat' 押韻的詞嗎？","analysis":"詞源來自古希臘文 'rhythmos' (rhythm)。指單詞或詩句結尾的發音相似性。是詩歌和歌曲中常用的結構元素。","definition":"a word that has the same or similar sound as another word.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The poem ends with a couplet that rhymes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這首詩以一對押韻的對句結尾。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Can you think of a rhyme for 'cat'?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你能想到一個與 'cat' 押韻的詞嗎？\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"你能想到一個與 'cat' 押韻的詞嗎？","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U41"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3193,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::rhythm::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of the waves was soothing.","expectedAnswer":"rhythm","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of the waves was soothing.","clozeAnswer":"rhythm","exampleTranslation":"海浪的節奏令人舒緩。","reference":{"eng":"rhythm","kk":"/ˈrɪðəm/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['節奏；韻律'], ['（事物、活動的）規律；週期']]","chEntries":["節奏","韻律","規律","週期"],"practiceMeaning":"海浪的節奏令人舒緩。","analysis":"詞源來自希臘語 'rhythmos'，意為「週期，流動」。'Rhythm' 指的是一種有規律的、重複出現的模式，特別是聲音、運動或事件的模式。在音樂中，它是聲音的高低、長短和強弱的組織。在日常生活中，它可以指一種規律的模式或週期，如工作節奏、生活規律等。","definition":"1. a strong, regular, repeated pattern of movement or sound; 2. a regular pattern of changes or activities.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The music had a catchy rhythm that made people want to dance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這首音樂有著 catchy 的節奏，讓人想跳舞。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The rhythm of the waves was soothing.\",\n    \"ch\": \"海浪的節奏令人舒緩。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He tried to find a rhythm in his writing process.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他試圖在寫作過程中找到一種節奏。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"海浪的節奏令人舒緩。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5098,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::ridiculous::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Wearing a swimsuit in winter is ____.","expectedAnswer":"ridiculous","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Wearing a swimsuit in winter is ____.","clozeAnswer":"ridiculous","exampleTranslation":"冬天穿泳衣是可笑的。","reference":{"eng":"ridiculous","kk":"rɪˈdɪkjələs","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['荒謬的'], ['可笑的'], ['滑稽的']]","chEntries":["荒謬的","可笑的","滑稽的"],"practiceMeaning":"冬天穿泳衣是可笑的。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'ridiculus'，意為 '可笑的'，源於 'ridere' (to laugh)。'Ridiculous' 的核心語義是 '如此愚蠢或不合邏輯，以至於引人發笑'。它強調的是事物與常識、邏輯或合理性之間的巨大差異，導致其顯得荒唐和可笑，通常帶有負面評價。","definition":"1. Deserving or inviting derision or mockery; absurd.; 2. So unreasonable or absurd as to be worthy of mockery.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His suggestion was so ridiculous that no one took it seriously.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的建議太荒謬了，以至於沒人認真對待。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Wearing a swimsuit in winter is ridiculous.\",\n    \"ch\": \"冬天穿泳衣是可笑的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The price they are charging is absolutely ridiculous.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們收取的價格簡直是荒謬的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"冬天穿泳衣是可笑的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5099,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::rigid::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company has ____ rules about punctuality.","expectedAnswer":"rigid","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company has ____ rules about punctuality.","clozeAnswer":"rigid","exampleTranslation":"公司對準時有嚴格的規定。","reference":{"eng":"rigid","kk":"ˈrɪdʒɪd","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['僵化的'], ['堅硬的'], ['嚴格的']]","chEntries":["僵化的","堅硬的","嚴格的"],"practiceMeaning":"公司對準時有嚴格的規定。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'rigidus'，意為 '硬的、僵硬的'，源於 'rigere' (to be stiff)。'Rigid' 的核心語義是 '缺乏彈性、不易彎曲或改變'。這可以指物理上的堅硬，如 'rigid material' (堅硬的材料)；也可以指觀念、規則或體制的僵化，如 'rigid rules' (嚴格的規則) 或 'rigid thinking' (僵化的思維)，強調其不靈活、不變通的特性。","definition":"1. Unable to bend or be deformed.; 2. Stiff and unmoving.; 3. Unable to change or be changed; fixed.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The metal bar was rigid and could not be bent.\",\n    \"ch\": \"金屬棒是堅硬的，無法彎曲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company has rigid rules about punctuality.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司對準時有嚴格的規定。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has a rigid approach to problem-solving.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他解決問題的方法很僵化。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"公司對準時有嚴格的規定。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4166,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::rise::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We witnessed the ____ of the sun.","expectedAnswer":"rise","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We witnessed the ____ of the sun.","clozeAnswer":"rise","exampleTranslation":"我們目睹了太陽的升起。","reference":{"eng":"rise","kk":"/raɪz/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['上漲', '增加'], ['（太陽、月亮等）升起'], ['起義', '反抗']]","chEntries":["上漲","增加","升起","起義","反抗"],"practiceMeaning":"我們目睹了太陽的升起。","analysis":"源自古英語 rīsan（起來，升起）。核心概念是「向上移動」或「增加」。引申為價格、水平的提高，或反抗的行動。","definition":"1. an increase in amount, level, or strength; 2. the act of getting up; 3. an upward movement","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There has been a steep rise in living costs.\",\n    \"ch\": \"生活成本急劇上漲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We witnessed the rise of the sun.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們目睹了太陽的升起。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The rise of the workers led to significant changes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"工人的崛起帶來了重大的變革。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們目睹了太陽的升起。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5858,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::saint::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She is a ____ for putting up with all that trouble.","expectedAnswer":"saint","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She is a ____ for putting up with all that trouble.","clozeAnswer":"saint","exampleTranslation":"她為了忍受所有那些麻煩真是個聖人。","reference":{"eng":"saint","kk":"seɪnt","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"聖人\"  ],  [    \"聖徒\"  ],  [    \"品德高尚的人\"  ],  [    \"極有耐心或善良的人\"  ]]","chEntries":["聖人","聖徒","品德高尚的人","極有耐心或善良的人"],"practiceMeaning":"她為了忍受所有那些麻煩真是個聖人。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'sanctus' (holy, consecrated)，意為「神聖的」。'Sanctus' 是 'sancire' (to make sacred, to hallow) 的過去分詞。'Saint' 在宗教中指被奉為神聖、德行卓著，並常被尊崇崇拜的人，尤其是在基督宗教中。它強調的是「神聖的」、「受人尊敬」和「品德完美」的特質。引申義可用來形容品德極好、行為高尚的人。例如，也可形容「極有耐心或善良的人」。","definition":"1. A person acknowledged as being especially holy or virtuous and as being a representative of God or of a particular religion.; 2. A person of great virtue and goodness.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Saint Peter is one of the apostles.\",\n    \"ch\": \"聖彼得是使徒之一。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a saint for putting up with all that trouble.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她為了忍受所有那些麻煩真是個聖人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Many churches are named after saints.\",\n    \"ch\": \"許多教堂都是以聖徒的名字命名的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He described his neighbor as a saint for helping him move.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他形容他的鄰居像個聖人一樣幫他搬家。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她為了忍受所有那些麻煩真是個聖人。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4117,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::scientific::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company invests heavily in ____ research.","expectedAnswer":"scientific","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company invests heavily in ____ research.","clozeAnswer":"scientific","exampleTranslation":"該公司在科學研究上投入巨資。","reference":{"eng":"scientific","kk":"/ˌsaɪənˈtɪfɪk/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['科學的']]","chEntries":["科學的"],"practiceMeaning":"該公司在科學研究上投入巨資。","analysis":"源自 science（科學），science 源自拉丁語 scientia（知識），由 scire（知道）衍生。scientific 指與科學方法、原理或研究相關的。","definition":"1. relating to or used in science; 2. systematic and methodical","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They conducted a scientific experiment.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們進行了一項科學實驗。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company invests heavily in scientific research.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司在科學研究上投入巨資。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need a scientific approach to solve this problem.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要一個科學的方法來解決這個問題。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該公司在科學研究上投入巨資。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6094,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::sector::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This is a security ____ reform program.","expectedAnswer":"sector","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This is a security ____ reform program.","clozeAnswer":"sector","exampleTranslation":"這是一個安全部門改革計畫。","reference":{"eng":"sector","kk":"ˈsɛktər","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"部門\"  ],  [    \"領域\"  ],  [    \"行業\"  ],  [    \"扇形\"  ]]","chEntries":["部門","領域","行業","扇形"],"practiceMeaning":"這是一個安全部門改革計畫。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 sector（cutter），是 secare（to cut）的結果名詞。核心語義是「被切割的部分」。引申為社會、經濟、地理或數學上的「部分」、「領域」、「部門」或「扇形」。","definition":"1. an area or portion that is distinct from others; 2. a part of the economy or society; 3. (geometry) a part of a circle enclosed by two radii and the arc between them.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The technology sector has grown rapidly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"科技行業發展迅速。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a security sector reform program.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個安全部門改革計畫。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The shaded area is a sector of the circle.\",\n    \"ch\": \"陰影區域是圓的一個扇形。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是一個安全部門改革計畫。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3922,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::semester::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She is taking a leave of absence for one ____.","expectedAnswer":"semester","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She is taking a leave of absence for one ____.","clozeAnswer":"semester","exampleTranslation":"她將休學一個學期。