理。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He reacted with considerable sensitivity to the criticism.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對批評反應相當敏感（不高興）。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"由於其敏感性，這些數據需要小心處理。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4046,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::sexy::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"That was a ____ new sports car.","expectedAnswer":"sexy","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"That was a ____ new sports car.","clozeAnswer":"sexy","exampleTranslation":"那是一輛極具吸引力的新跑車。","reference":{"eng":"sexy","kk":"/ˈsɛksi/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['性感的', '色情的'], ['誘人的', '有魅力的'], ['（使人）興奮的', '刺激的']]","chEntries":["性感的","色情的","誘人的","有魅力的","興奮的","刺激的"],"practiceMeaning":"那是一輛極具吸引力的新跑車。","analysis":"源自 'sex' (性)，加上 '-y' 後綴。直接指與性吸引力有關。引申為「誘人的」、「有魅力的」，不一定僅限於性方面，也可以指事物本身具有吸引力。第三個義項「（使人）興奮的」則強調其能引起強烈興趣或刺激感。","definition":"1. sexually attractive; 2. exciting or interesting; 3. appealing or alluring","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"她穿那件洋裝看起來很性感。\",\n    \"eng\": \"She looked very sexy in that dress.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"那是一輛極具吸引力的新跑車。\",\n    \"eng\": \"That was a sexy new sports car.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"環遊世界的想法很令人興奮。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The idea of traveling the world is a sexy one.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"那是一輛極具吸引力的新跑車。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5805,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::shed::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The old ____ was falling apart.","expectedAnswer":"shed","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The old ____ was falling apart.","clozeAnswer":"shed","exampleTranslation":"那個舊棚屋快要散架了。","reference":{"eng":"shed","kk":"ʃɛd","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"小屋\"  ],  [    \"棚屋\"  ],  [    \"簡陋的建築\"  ]]","chEntries":["小屋","棚屋","簡陋的建築"],"practiceMeaning":"那個舊棚屋快要散架了。","analysis":"此字為名詞，與動詞同源。核心語義是指「一個簡單、臨時或用於儲存物品的建築物」。通常是獨立的、簡陋的結構，例如工具棚、自行車棚、飼料棚等。語意演變上，從「脫落」或「分離」引申為「與主建築分離的、簡單的附屬建築」。","definition":"1. a simple structure, typically of wood or metal, built for storage or shelter.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He keeps his gardening tools in the shed.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他把園藝工具放在棚屋裡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The old shed was falling apart.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那個舊棚屋快要散架了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They used the shed as a workshop.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們把棚屋當作工作室。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"那個舊棚屋快要散架了。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6191,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::shove::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They had to ____ their way through the crowd.","expectedAnswer":"shove","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They had to ____ their way through the crowd.","clozeAnswer":"shove","exampleTranslation":"他們不得不擠過人群。","reference":{"eng":"shove","kk":"ʃʌv","tense":"v.","ch":"[  [    \"推\"  ],  [    \"擠\"  ],  [    \"猛推\"  ]]","chEntries":["推","擠","猛推"],"practiceMeaning":"他們不得不擠過人群。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 shoven，與古英語 scufan「推、刮」同源，可能源自原始日耳曼語 *skūfan。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作為動詞，其核心語義是用力向前或向某方向推動某物或某人。這個動作的語義是其主要構成要素，強調力量和直接性。","definition":"1. push roughly or carelessly; 2. to move or push something with force.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He shoved the door open.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他猛地推開了門。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They had to shove their way through the crowd.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們不得不擠過人群。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Don't shove me!\",\n    \"ch\": \"別推我！\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He shoved the box onto the shelf.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他把箱子塞進了架子。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們不得不擠過人群。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6194,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::shrug::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He gave a ____ and walked away.","expectedAnswer":"shrug","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He gave a ____ and walked away.","clozeAnswer":"shrug","exampleTranslation":"他聳了聳肩就走開了。","reference":{"eng":"shrug","kk":"ʃrʌɡ","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"聳肩\"  ]]","chEntries":["聳肩"],"practiceMeaning":"他聳了聳肩就走開了。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 scrybban。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作為名詞，是動詞 shrug「聳肩」的名詞化。其核心語義是指「聳肩這個動作」，通常用以表達不確定、無知、無所謂或無助。","definition":"1. an act of shrugging the shoulders.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A shrug of indifference was his only reply.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一絲無所謂的聳肩是他的唯一答覆。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He gave a shrug and walked away.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他聳了聳肩就走開了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her shrug conveyed her lack of interest.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的聳肩傳達了她不感興趣。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他聳了聳肩就走開了。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6198,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::siege::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ ended with the enemy's surrender.","expectedAnswer":"siege","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ ended with the enemy's surrender.","clozeAnswer":"siege","exampleTranslation":"圍攻在敵軍投降後結束。","reference":{"eng":"siege","kk":"siːdʒ","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"圍攻\"  ],  [    \"包圍\"  ],  [    \"圍困\"  ]]","chEntries":["圍攻","包圍","圍困"],"practiceMeaning":"圍攻在敵軍投降後結束。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 siege，意為「座位、場所、圍攻」，最終源自拉丁語 sedes「座位」，與 sedēre「坐」相關。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 sedēre「坐」是其核心語意來源。作為名詞，其核心語義是「軍隊包圍並試圖佔領一個設防城鎮或據點的軍事行動」。詞源中的「座位」引申為「佔據」，進而發展為「圍攻」的意義。","definition":"1. a military blockade of a city or fortress with the intention of capturing it by assault or starvation; 2. a prolonged period of difficulty or hardship.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The city was under siege for months.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座城市被圍攻了數月。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The siege ended with the enemy's surrender.\",\n    \"ch\": \"圍攻在敵軍投降後結束。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The prolonged siege tested the defenders' resolve.\",\n    \"ch\": \"漫長的圍困考驗了守軍的決心。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The castle endured a long siege.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座城堡經受了漫長的圍攻。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"圍攻在敵軍投降後結束。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5433,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::situated::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The village is ____ in a remote valley.","expectedAnswer":"situated","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The village is ____ in a remote valley.","clozeAnswer":"situated","exampleTranslation":"這個村莊坐落於一個偏遠的山谷中。","reference":{"eng":"situated","kk":"ˈsɪtʃueɪtɪd","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['位於'], ['坐落於']]","chEntries":["位於","坐落於"],"practiceMeaning":"這個村莊坐落於一個偏遠的山谷中。","analysis":"此字為動詞 \"situate\" 的過去分詞，可作形容詞使用。\"situate\" 源自拉丁語 \"situare\"，意為\"使處於……位置\"，來自 \"situs\" (位置、地點)。構詞上，\"situ-\" 提供了核心的「位置」語意，\"-ate\" 是動詞字尾。 \"Situatd\" 作形容詞，表示某物「被放置在」或「位於」某個特定地點或環境，通常用來描述建築物、城市或地理位置。","definition":"located or positioned in a particular place or position.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The hotel is situated on a hill overlooking the sea.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家酒店坐落於俯瞰大海的山丘上。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The village is situated in a remote valley.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個村莊坐落於一個偏遠的山谷中。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The ancient ruins are situated near the river.\",\n    \"ch\": \"古老的廢墟位於河邊附近。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個村莊坐落於一個偏遠的山谷中。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5806,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::skeleton::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of the building was erected in just a few weeks.","expectedAnswer":"skeleton","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of the building was erected in just a few weeks.","clozeAnswer":"skeleton","exampleTranslation":"這座建築的骨架在短短幾週內就豎立起來了。","reference":{"eng":"skeleton","kk":"ˈskɛlɪtn","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"骨骼\"  ],  [    \"骨架\"  ],  [    \"骨架（結構）\"  ],  [    \"骨架（人或動物）\"  ]]","chEntries":["骨骼","骨架"],"practiceMeaning":"這座建築的骨架在短短幾週內就豎立起來了。","analysis":"此字為名詞，源自中古英語scoleton，來自現代拉丁語Sceletus，後者又源自古希臘語skeletón（乾燥的；枯乾的），來自skelein（弄乾；枯萎）。核心語義是指「支撐身體的骨頭的總體」，即骨骼或骨架。語意演變上，從「乾燥物」的概念，具體化為支撐生物體的「骨架」，再引申為「結構的基本框架」。","definition":"1. all the bones in a person's or animal's body; 2. the basic structure or framework of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The museum displayed a dinosaur skeleton.\",\n    \"ch\": \"博物館展示了恐龍的骨架。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The skeleton of the building was erected in just a few weeks.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座建築的骨架在短短幾週內就豎立起來了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His skeleton was found buried in the garden.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的骸骨被發現埋在花園裡。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這座建築的骨架在短短幾週內就豎立起來了。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4241,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::slave::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He felt like a ____ to his demanding job.","expectedAnswer":"slave","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He felt like a ____ to his demanding job.","clozeAnswer":"slave","exampleTranslation":"他感覺自己像個被苛刻的工作支配的奴隸。","reference":{"eng":"slave","kk":"/sleɪv/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['奴隸'], ['受支配的人']]","chEntries":["奴隸","受支配的人"],"practiceMeaning":"他感覺自己像個被苛刻的工作支配的奴隸。","analysis":"詞源學上，'slave' 的詞源並非直接來自拉丁語 'sclavus'（斯拉夫人），而是通過中世紀晚期法語 'esclave'。'Sclavus' 最初指斯拉夫民族，由於歷史上大量斯拉夫人被虜為奴隸，'sclavus' 逐漸演變成「奴隸」的意思。其核心是「失去自由、被強迫工作的人」。","definition":"a person who is the legal property of another and is forced to obey them.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The ancient Romans relied heavily on slave labor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"古羅馬人嚴重依賴奴隸勞動。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He felt like a slave to his demanding job.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他感覺自己像個被苛刻的工作支配的奴隸。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他感覺自己像個被苛刻的工作支配的奴隸。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6243,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::slot::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The TV program is scheduled for the 8 pm ____.","expectedAnswer":"slot","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The TV program is scheduled 