"exampleTranslation":"這種疾病是該地區特有的。","reference":{"eng":"specific","kk":"/spəˈsɪfɪk/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['特定的', '具體的'], ['明確的', '確切的'], ['（種類）獨特的']]","chEntries":["特定的","具體的","明確的","確切的","獨特的"],"practiceMeaning":"這種疾病是該地區特有的。","analysis":"詞源：拉丁文 'specificus' (區分的、特定的)，源自 'species' (種類、外觀)。指明確界定、不含糊的，或屬於某一特定類別的。","definition":"1. clearly defined or identified; 2. relating to a particular thing, person, or category; 3. precisely indicated or stated.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Do you have any specific instructions for me?\",\n    \"ch\": \"您有任何具體的指示要給我嗎？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This disease is specific to the region.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種疾病是該地區特有的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need more specific details about the project.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要關於這個計畫更具體的細節。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這種疾病是該地區特有的。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5103,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::spine::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The book has a colorful ____.","expectedAnswer":"spine","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The book has a colorful ____.","clozeAnswer":"spine","exampleTranslation":"這本書的書脊色彩鮮豔。","reference":{"eng":"spine","kk":"spaɪn","tense":"n.","ch":"[['脊椎'], ['書脊'], ['勇氣']]","chEntries":["脊椎","書脊","勇氣"],"practiceMeaning":"這本書的書脊色彩鮮豔。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'spina'，意為 '刺、荊棘'，後引申為 '脊骨'，可能因為脊椎像一連串的骨刺。其核心語義是指身體後部的骨骼結構，即 '脊椎'。它也延伸指書籍封面連接的邊緣，即 '書脊'。更比喻地，'spine' 可以指一個人 '堅強的意志' 或 '勇氣'，因為脊椎支撐著身體，給人一種挺直、堅定的形象。","definition":"1. The series of bones forming the backbone of a person or animal.; 2. The back edge of a book, where the pages are bound together.; 3. Courage or determination.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A healthy spine is crucial for good posture.\",\n    \"ch\": \"健康的脊椎對保持良好姿態至關重要。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The book has a colorful spine.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本書的書脊色彩鮮豔。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She found the courage to stand up to her boss, showing real spine.\