:v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The mystery began to ____.","expectedAnswer":"unfold","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The mystery began to ____.","clozeAnswer":"unfold","exampleTranslation":"謎團開始被揭開。","reference":{"eng":"unfold","kk":"ʌnˈfoʊld","tense":"v.","ch":"[  [    \"展開\"  ],  [    \"打開\"  ],  [    \"闡明\"  ],  [    \"發展\"  ]]","chEntries":["展開","打開","闡明","發展"],"practiceMeaning":"謎團開始被揭開。","analysis":"此字由否定字首 un-（不；相反）和動詞 fold（折疊）構成。fold 源自古英語 faldan，意為「摺疊；纏繞」。unfold 的核心語義是「不折疊」，即將折疊的物體打開，使其平展。引申為揭示、闡明事實或情況，或指事件的發展。此處使用 v. 詞性，表示及物與不及物皆可。及物用法如 unfold a map。不及物用法如 the story unfolds。其語意演變是從具體的「打開」到抽象的「揭示；發展」。","definition":"1. to open or spread out something that has been folded; 2. to become clear or revealed; 3. to develop or become clear.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please unfold the map.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請展開地圖。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The mystery began to unfold.\",\n    \"ch\": \"謎團開始被揭開。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"As the events unfold, we will learn more.\",\n    \"ch\": \"隨著事件的發展，我們將了解更多。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"謎團開始被揭開。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3899,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::unique::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This is a ____ opportunity.","expectedAnswer":"unique","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This is a ____ opportunity.","clozeAnswer":"unique","exampleTranslation":"這是一個獨特的機會。","reference":{"eng":"unique","kk":"/juˈniːk/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['獨一無二的', '獨特的'], ['罕見的']]","chEntries":["獨一無二的","獨特的","罕見的"],"practiceMeaning":"這是一個獨特的機會。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'unicus'，'unus' (one) 的衍生詞。核心是「只有一個」。引申為與所有其他事物都不同，因此是獨特的、特別的。","definition":"1. being the only one of its kind; unlike anything else. 2. unusual, special, or rare.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Each snowflake is unique.\",\n    \"ch\": \"每一片雪花都是獨一無二的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a unique opportunity.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個獨特的機會。\"\n  