:urban::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ planning is a complex field.","expectedAnswer":"Urban","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ planning is a complex field.","clozeAnswer":"Urban","exampleTranslation":"都市規劃是一個複雜的領域。","reference":{"eng":"urban","kk":"ˈɜːrbən","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['城市的'], ['都市的']]","chEntries":["城市的","都市的"],"practiceMeaning":"都市規劃是一個複雜的領域。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 \"urbanus\"，意為\"城市的\"、\"屬城市居民的\"，來自 \"urbs\" (城市)。構詞上，\"urban-\" 提供了核心的「城市」語意，\"-us\" 是拉丁語的形容詞字尾。 \"Urban\" 形容與城市相關的事物，包括城市本身、城市的特徵、或城市中的生活方式，與\"rural\" (鄉村的) 形成對比。","definition":"relating to, characteristic of, or found in a city or town; relating to cities rather than rural areas.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The city has a vibrant urban culture.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座城市擁有充滿活力的都市文化。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Urban planning is a complex field.\",\n    \"ch\": \"都市規劃是一個複雜的領域。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Many people move from rural areas to urban centers for work.\",\n    \"ch\": \"許多人為了工作而從鄉村地區遷往城市中心。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"都市規劃是一個複雜的領域。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6203,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::valid::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His argument is ____.","expectedAnswer":"valid","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His argument is ____.","clozeAnswer":"valid","exampleTranslation":"他的論點是有說服力的。","reference":{"eng":"valid","kk":"ˈvælɪd","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"有效的\"  ],  [    \"有法律效力的\"  ],  [    \"合理的\"  ],  [    \"有說服力的\"  ]]","chEntries":["有效的","有法律效力的","合理的","有說服力的"],"practiceMeaning":"他的論點是有說服力的。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 validus，意為「強壯的、有力的」，與 valēre「強壯、有力」相關。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 valēre「強壯、有力」是其核心語意來源。作為形容詞，其核心語義是指「有充分證據或理由支持的、為法律或規章所承認的」。詞源中的「強壯、有力」引申為「有說服力的、有效的」。","definition":"1. legally or officially acceptable; 2. based on known facts and sound reasoning; 3. (of a ticket or other document) allowing the holder to travel or gain admission; 4. 