"exampleTranslation":"我們正在為我們的婚禮招待會尋找一個場所。","reference":{"eng":"venue","kk":"ˈvɛnju","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"場地\"  ],  [    \"地點\"  ],  [    \"場所\"  ]]","chEntries":["場地","地點","場所"],"practiceMeaning":"我們正在為我們的婚禮招待會尋找一個場所。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 venue，意為「到來，地點」，向上可追溯至拉丁語 venire，意為「來」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。名詞義指某事將要發生的地點，特別是活動、演出、會議或運動比賽的場所。中文翻譯為「場地；地點；場所」。","definition":"1. the place where an organized event such as a concert, conference, or sporting event takes place; 2. the place where an action or event happens.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The stadium is a popular venue for concerts.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個體育場是舉辦音樂會的熱門場地。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We are looking for a venue for our wedding reception.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們正在為我們的婚禮招待會尋找一個場所。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The court is the venue for the legal proceedings.\",\n    \"ch\": \"法院是法律訴訟的發生地點。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們正在為我們的婚禮招待會尋找一個場所。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4469,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::violence::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There was a sudden outbreak of ____ in the city.","expectedAnswer":"violence","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There was a sudden outbreak of ____ in the city.","clozeAnswer":"violence","exampleTranslation":"這座城市突然爆發了暴力事件。","reference":{"eng":"violence","kk":"/ˈvaɪələns/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['暴力'], ['猛烈'], ['（行為）不文明']]","chEntries":["暴力","猛烈","不文明"],"practiceMeaning":"這座城市突然爆發了暴力事件。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 violentia，來自 violare，意為「侵犯」、「粗暴對待」。核心語意是「使用武力或力量造成傷害或破壞」。","definition":"1. Behavior involving physical force intended to hurt, damage, or kill someone or something; 2. Intense or uncontrolled force.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The film depicted scenes of extreme violence.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這部電影描繪了極端暴力的場面。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was a sudden outbreak of violence in the city.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座城市突然爆發了暴力事件。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The storm caused considerable violence to the coastline.\",\n    \"ch\": \"風暴對海岸線造成了相當大的破壞。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這座城市突然爆發了暴力事件。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3294,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::virus::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"My computer was infected by a ____.","expectedAnswer":"virus","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"My computer was infected by a ____.","clozeAnswer":"virus","exampleTranslation":"我的電腦被病毒感染了。","reference":{"eng":"virus","kk":"/ˈvaɪərəs/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['病毒'], ['（計算機）病毒'], ['（不良思想、情感等的）傳染性因素；毒害']]","chEntries":["病毒","傳染性因素","毒害"],"practiceMeaning":"我的電腦被病毒感染了。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'virus' (毒液，黏液)。指一種非細胞性的傳染因子，只能在宿主細胞內複製。引申至計算機領域，指惡意代碼。也可用於比喻，指像病毒一樣傳播開來的負面事物。","definition":"1. a submicroscopic infectious agent that replicates only inside the living cells of an organism; 2. a piece of code that is capable of copying itself and spreading from one computer to another, usually causing harm; 3. something that is able to infect and harm others.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The flu is caused by a virus.\",\n    \"ch\": \"流感是由病毒引起的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"My computer was infected by a virus.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我的電腦被病毒感染了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Fear can spread like a virus through a crowd.\",\n    \"ch\": \"恐懼會像病毒一樣在人群中傳播。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我的電腦被病毒感染了。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4048,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::vocabulary::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This book introduces technical ____ for engineers.","expectedAnswer":"vocabulary","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This book introduces technical ____ for engineers.","clozeAnswer":"vocabulary","exampleTranslation":"這本書介紹了工程師的技術術語。","reference":{"eng":"vocabulary","kk":"/voʊˈkæbjəlɛri/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['詞彙', '詞彙量'], ['（某領域的）術語']]","chEntries":["詞彙","詞彙量","術語"],"practiceMeaning":"這本書介紹了工程師的技術術語。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'vocabularium'，意為「詞的列表」，來自 'vocabulum' (a word)，'vocabulum' 又來自 'vocare' (to call)。核心是「被稱為的詞」。引申為個人所知的詞語總匯（詞彙量），以及特定領域或行業使用的專門術語。","definition":"1. all the words that someone knows or uses; 2. all the words that exist in a language; 3. a set of words used in a particular subject or field","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"她的英語詞彙量很大。\",\n    \"eng\": \"She has a large English vocabulary.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"這本書介紹了工程師的技術術語。\",\n    \"eng\": \"This book introduces technical vocabulary for engineers.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"學習新詞彙是語言習得的關鍵。\",\n    \"eng\": \"Learning new vocabulary is essential for language acquisition.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這本書介紹了工程師的技術術語。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3941,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::weakness::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The old man was overcome by ____.","expectedAnswer":"weakness","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The old man was overcome by ____.","clozeAnswer":"weakness","exampleTranslation":"老人因虛弱而倒下。","reference":{"eng":"weakness","kk":"/ˈwiːknəs/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['虛弱', '軟弱'], ['弱點', '缺點']]","chEntries":["虛弱","軟弱","弱點","缺點"],"practiceMeaning":"老人因虛弱而倒下。","analysis":"源自古英語 'wācnes'，由 'wāc' (意為「軟弱的」) 和 '-nes' (名詞後綴，表示「狀態」) 組成。指身體、精神上的虛弱，或指能力、性格上的不足或缺點。","definition":"1. the state of being weak; 2. a fault or failing.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His greatest weakness is his lack of confidence.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他最大的弱點是缺乏自信。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The old man was overcome by weakness.\",\n    \"ch\": \"老人因虛弱而倒下。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company acknowledged its weakness in marketing.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司承認其在行銷方面的弱點。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"老人因虛弱而倒下。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5816,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::whereas::conj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He is very outgoing, ____ his brother is quite shy.","expectedAnswer":"whereas","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He is very outgoing, ____ his brother is quite shy.","clozeAnswer":"whereas","exampleTranslation":"他非常外向，而他的兄弟則相當害羞。","reference":{"eng":"whereas","kk":"ˌwɛərˈæz","tense":"conj.","ch":"[  [    \"然而\"  ],  [    \"比較起來\"  ],  [    \"鑒於\"  ]]","chEntries":["然而","比較起來","鑒於"],"practiceMeaning":"他非常外向，而他的兄弟則相當害羞。","analysis":"此字為連接詞，源自中古英語wheras，由where（在哪裡）+as（如同；和）組成。核心語義是「用來連接兩個對比或比較的子句，表示前者與後者之間的差異」。語意演變上，從「在哪裡……如同……」，演變為表示「對比」或「儘管如此」的連接詞。","definition":"1. in contrast or comparison with; 2. in view of the fact that; because.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Some people like to travel abroad, whereas others prefer to stay home.\",\n    \"ch\": \"有些人喜歡出國旅行，而有些人則偏好待在家裡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is very outgoing, whereas his brother is quite shy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他非常外向，而他的兄弟則相當害羞。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The plan is expensive, whereas the alternative is less effective.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個計劃很昂貴，而另一種選擇效果較差。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他非常外向，而他的兄弟則相當害羞。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5349,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l1::worship::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They gathered to ____ at the church.","expectedAnswer":"worship","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They gathered to ____ at the church.","clozeAnswer":"worship","exampleTranslation":"他們聚集在教堂裡進行禮拜。","reference":{"eng":"worship","kk":"ˈwɜːrʃɪp","tense":"v.","ch":"[['崇拜'], ['敬拜'], ['禮拜']]","chEntries":["崇拜","敬拜","禮拜"],"practiceMeaning":"他們聚集在教堂裡進行禮拜。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 weorþscipe，由 weorþ（價值、尊嚴）+ -scipe（狀態、職位，相當於現代的 -ship）組成。原始語意為「價值、尊嚴的狀態」。後演變為「對神祇或崇高事物的尊敬與崇拜」。構詞上，weorþ- 表示「價值、值得」，-scipe 構成抽象名詞。現代語意主要指宗教上的「崇拜、敬拜」。亦可作名詞使用。","definition":"to show reverence and adoration for (a deity); to honor or revere (an object, idol, or other entity) as a god; to feel or express extreme admiration, love, or reverence for.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Many people worship the sun.\",\n    \"ch\": \"許多人崇拜太陽。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They gathered to worship at the church.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們聚集在教堂裡進行禮拜。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們聚集在教堂裡進行禮拜。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4528,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::about::prep","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The children were playing ____ the room.","expectedAnswer":"about","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The children were playing ____ the room.","clozeAnswer":"about","exampleTranslation":"孩子們在房間裡玩耍。","reference":{"eng":"about","kk":"/əˈbaʊt/","tense":"prep.","ch":"[['關於'], ['大約'], ['在...周圍']]","chEntries":["關於","大約","在...周圍"],"practiceMeaning":"孩子們在房間裡玩耍。","analysis":"源自古英語 on bæftan，意為「在後面」。後來演變成表示「周圍」、「大概」、「關於」。核心語意從「圍繞」引申為「關於」。","definition":"1. On the subject of; concerning; 2. Approximately; 3. On all sides of.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Tell me about your trip.\",\n    \"ch\": \"跟我說說你的旅行。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's about ten o'clock.\",\n    \"ch\": \"大約十點鐘了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The children were playing about the room.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子們在房間裡玩耍。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"孩子們在房間裡玩耍。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5425,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::abundance::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of information online can be overwhelming.","expectedAnswer":"abundance","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of information online can be overwhelming.","clozeAnswer":"abundance","exampleTranslation":"網路上豐富的資訊可能會讓人不知所措。","reference":{"eng":"abundance","kk":"əˈbʌndəns","tense":"n.","ch":"[['豐富'], ['充裕'], ['大量'], ['豐盛']]","chEntries":["豐富","充裕","大量","豐盛"],"practiceMeaning":"網路上豐富的資訊可能會讓人不知所措。","analysis":"此字為派生詞，由形容詞 \"abundant\" 加上名詞化字尾 \"-ance\" 構成。\"abundant\" 源自拉丁語 \"abundans\"，是動詞 \"abundare\" 的現在分詞，意為\"充溢\"、\"豐富\"。\"abundare\" 由 \"ab-\" (離開、遠離，在此表示\"過多\"或\"溢出\") 和 \"undare\" (波浪般流動) 構成，\"undare\" 又源於 \"unda\" (波浪)。構詞上，\"ab-\" 提供了「過量」的語意，\"undare\" 提供了「流動」的圖像，整體表示「如波浪般湧出、充溢」。字尾 \"-ance\" 將形容詞的「充裕」狀態轉化為抽象名詞，表示「豐富」、「充裕」或「大量」的狀態或性質。","definition":"a large quantity of something; a great amount of something; plenty; profusion; more than enough.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The region is known for its abundance of natural resources.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該地區以其豐富的自然資源而聞名。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was an abundance of food at the party.\",\n    \"ch\": \"派對上有豐富的食物。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The abundance of information online can be overwhelming.\",\n    \"ch\": \"網路上豐富的資訊可能會讓人不知所措。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"網路上豐富的資訊可能會讓人不知所措。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4562,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::accurate::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need ____ data to make a decision.","expectedAnswer":"accurate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need ____ data to make a decision.","clozeAnswer":"accurate","exampleTranslation":"我們需要準確的數據來做決定。","reference":{"eng":"accurate","kk":"/ˈækjərət/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['準確的', '精確的'], ['（陳述、測量等）正確的']]","chEntries":["準確的","精確的","正確的"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要準確的數據來做決定。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'accuratus'，'ad-' (to) 和 'cura' (care - 關心、小心) 的組合。核心概念是「非常小心地」進行，從而達到精確。\n    1. 準確的、精確的：指測量、數據、預測等非常接近真實值或目標。\n    2. 正確的：指陳述或判斷符合事實。","definition":"1. (of information, measurements, etc.) precise; exact.; 2. correct in all details; error-free.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The report provided an accurate account of the events.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這份報告提供了對事件的準確敘述。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His estimate of the cost was remarkably accurate.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對費用的估計非常準確。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need accurate data to make a decision.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要準確的數據來做決定。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要準確的數據來做決定。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5459,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::adventurous::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He has an ____ spirit and is always looking for new challenges.","expectedAnswer":"adventurous","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He has an ____ spirit and is always looking for new challenges.","clozeAnswer":"adventurous","exampleTranslation":"他有冒險精神，總是在尋找新的挑戰。","reference":{"eng":"adventurous","kk":"ædvɛnˈtʃɜrəs","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['愛冒險的'], ['大膽的'], ['富於冒險精神的']]","chEntries":["愛冒險的","大膽的","富於冒險精神的"],"practiceMeaning":"他有冒險精神，總是在尋找新的挑戰。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 'æfentyrlic'，由 'adventure'（冒險）加上形容詞字尾 '-ous' 構成，意為「充滿冒險的」。'Adventure' 本身來自古法語 'aventure'，意指「機遇、事件」，源自拉丁語 'adventura'，意為「即將發生的事」。'-ous' 是拉丁語 '-osus' 的英語化形式，用來構成形容詞，表示「充滿……的」或「具有……特性的」。因此，'adventurous' 的核心語意是「喜歡經歷或尋求冒險」，引申為「大膽的、樂於嘗試新事物」。","definition":"1. Eager to take risks or to embark on new, daring ventures; bold; daring; brave; intrepid; courageous; valiant.; 2. Characterized by or involving adventure; exciting; hazardous; risky; dangerous.; 3. Willing to undertake a risky or daring personal project, enterprise, or undertaking.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She was an adventurous child who loved exploring the woods behind her house.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是個熱愛探索屋後森林的冒險兒童。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They planned an adventurous journey through the Amazon rainforest.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們計劃了一次穿越亞馬遜雨林的冒險旅程。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has an adventurous spirit and is always looking for new challenges.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他有冒險精神，總是在尋找新的挑戰。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他有冒險精神，總是在尋找新的挑戰。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5505,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l5::agency::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need to understand the ____ of the virus.","expectedAnswer":"agency","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need to understand the ____ of the virus.","clozeAnswer":"agency","exampleTranslation":"我們需要了解這種病毒的作用。","reference":{"eng":"agency","kk":"ˈeɪdʒənsi","tense":"n.","ch":"[['代理機構'], ['經紀公司'], ['情報機構'], ['作用'], ['效力'], ['媒介']]","chEntries":["代理機構","經紀公司","情報機構","作用","效力","媒介"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要了解這種病毒的作用。","analysis":"此字由 'agent' 加上抽象名詞字尾 '-cy' 構成，表示『代理人的職位、權力或機構』。'-cy' 源自拉丁語 '-tia' 或 '-cia'，用於形成名詞，表示狀態、品質或職位。因此，'agency' 的核心語義是與 'agent' 相關的抽象概念或場所。從「代理權」延伸出「代理機構」（如旅行社、經紀公司），再引申為「情報機構」。此外，它也表示「起作用的能力」或「作用力」，強調的是「執行者」或「媒介物」所展現出的效力。","definition":"a business or organization that provides a particular service; the capacity to act or exert power; an organization that operates on behalf of another.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He signed with a talent agency.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他簽約了一家演藝經紀公司。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The agency reported a significant increase in tourism.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該旅遊局報告稱旅遊業顯著增長。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to understand the agency of the virus.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要了解這種病毒的作用。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要了解這種病毒的作用。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6106,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::agenda::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need to set the ____ for tomorrow's meeting.","expectedAnswer":"agenda","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need to set the ____ for tomorrow's meeting.","clozeAnswer":"agenda","exampleTranslation":"我們需要擬定明天會議的議程。","reference":{"eng":"agenda","kk":"əˈdʒɛndə","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"議程\"  ],  [    \"待辦事項\"  ],  [    \"計劃\"  ],  [    \"潛藏目的\"  ]]","chEntries":["議程","待辦事項","計劃","潛藏目的"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要擬定明天會議的議程。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 agenda，是動詞 agere（做；行動）的女性複數主格形式，意為「該做的事」。原為教務用語，指「應當處理的事項」。在現代英語中，agenda 主要指會議或討論的「議程」，即計劃要討論的事項列表。也可引申為某人或組織隱藏的「計劃」或「目的」，帶有負面含義。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆，應視為整體詞源演變。其語意演變是從「該做的事」到具體的「會議議程」，再到抽象的「計劃、目的」。","definition":"1. a list of things to be done or discussed at a meeting; 2. a set of principles or beliefs that guide someone's actions or a group's behavior; a hidden plan.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The first item on the agenda is the budget report.\",\n    \"ch\": \"議程上的第一項是預算報告。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They have their own political agenda.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們有自己的政治議程。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to set the agenda for tomorrow's meeting.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要擬定明天會議的議程。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要擬定明天會議的議程。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6152,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::alien::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Such behavior is ____ to our traditions.","expectedAnswer":"alien","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Such behavior is ____ to our traditions.","clozeAnswer":"alien","exampleTranslation":"這種行為與我們的傳統不符。","reference":{"eng":"alien","kk":"ˈeɪliən","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"外國的\"  ],  [    \"外來的\"  ],  [    \"陌生的\"  ],  [    \"不協調的\"  ],  [    \"不適合的\"  ]]","chEntries":["外國的","外來的","陌生的","不協調的","不適合的"],"practiceMeaning":"這種行為與我們的傳統不符。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 alienus，意為「別人的、外國的、不相干的」。它進入中古英語 via 古法語 alien。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，應視為整體詞源演變。作為形容詞，核心語義是「來自另一國家的」或「與之無關的」。從「外國的」進一步引申出「陌生的、不熟悉的」，再到「不協調的、不適合的」。這些義項都圍繞著「非本地的、不屬於的」概念發展。","definition":"1. belonging to a foreign country or countries; 2. unfamiliar and disturbing; 3. not belonging to a particular place; 4. completely different.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has an alien culture and language.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他有著外來的文化和語言。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The news was alien to him.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這消息對他來說很陌生。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Such behavior is alien to our traditions.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種行為與我們的傳統不符。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The design felt alien to the rest of the house.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個設計與房子的其他部分顯得格格不入。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這種行為與我們的傳統不符。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4149,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::ambulance::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The injured player was taken to the hospital by ____.","expectedAnswer":"ambulance","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The injured player was taken to the hospital by ____.","clozeAnswer":"ambulance","exampleTranslation":"受傷的運動員被救護車送往醫院。","reference":{"eng":"ambulance","kk":"/ˈæmbjʊləns/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['救護車', ' ambulancia (拉丁文：行走）']]","chEntries":["救護車","ambulancia (拉丁文：行走）"],"practiceMeaning":"受傷的運動員被救護車送往醫院。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 ambulare（行走）。最初指可移動的野戰醫院，後來引申為載運病患的車輛。","definition":"a vehicle equipped for taking sick or injured people to and from the hospital","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The ambulance arrived quickly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"救護車很快就到了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Call an ambulance immediately.\",\n    \"ch\": \"立刻叫救護車。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The injured player was taken to the hospital by ambulance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"受傷的運動員被救護車送往醫院。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"受傷的運動員被救護車送往醫院。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U5、L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4192,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::anyhow::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It's raining, but we'll go out ____.","expectedAnswer":"anyhow","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It's raining, but we'll go out ____.","clozeAnswer":"anyhow","exampleTranslation":"下著雨，但我們還是要出去。","reference":{"eng":"anyhow","kk":"/ˈeniˌhaʊ/","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['不管怎樣；總之'], ['隨便地；雜亂地']]","chEntries":["不管怎樣","總之","隨便地","雜亂地"],"practiceMeaning":"下著雨，但我們還是要出去。","analysis":"複合詞，由 'any' 和 'how' 組成。'Any' 源自古英語 ænig，'how' 源自古英語 hū。'Anyhow' 的核心是“任何方式”，引申為：1. “不管怎樣”，表示儘管有困難或情況，仍然會發生或去做某事。2. “隨便地”，指沒有特殊的方法或秩序，任意而為。","definition":"1. in any way or manner; 2. in any case; nevertheless; 3. carelessly or untidily.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I don't know what to do, but I'll finish it anyhow.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我不知道該怎麼做，但我總之會完成它。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He threw his clothes down anyhow on the chair.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他隨便地把衣服扔在椅子上。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's raining, but we'll go out anyhow.\",\n    \"ch\": \"下著雨，但我們還是要出去。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"下著雨，但我們還是要出去。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5770,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::applause::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We appreciate your ____ and support.","expectedAnswer":"applause","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We appreciate your ____ and support.","clozeAnswer":"applause","exampleTranslation":"我們感謝您的讚賞與支持。","reference":{"eng":"applause","kk":"əˈplɔz","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"掌聲\"  ],  [    \"讚賞\"  ],  [    \"喝采\"  ]]","chEntries":["掌聲","讚賞","喝采"],"practiceMeaning":"我們感謝您的讚賞與支持。","analysis":"此字為名詞，源自中古英語 applaus，由拉丁語 applausus（讚許；喝采）而來，後者是動詞 applaud（鼓掌；讚美）的過去分詞。applaud來自拉丁語applaudere，由ad-（朝向；加強）+ plaudere（鼓掌；拍手）組成。plaudere本身可能與拉丁語plausus（拍擊；鼓掌）及希臘語plosion（爆發；撞擊）有關。因此，applause的核心語義是「因讚賞或喜愛而發出的拍手聲」，引申為「讚賞」或「喝采」。其語意演變是從具體的拍手動作發展到抽象的讚揚和認可。","definition":"1. the act of clapping your hands to show you have enjoyed a performance or someone has done well; 2. enthusiastic approval.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The audience gave the performers a standing ovation and loud applause.\",\n    \"ch\": \"觀眾起立鼓掌，給予表演者熱烈的掌聲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her speech was met with thunderous applause.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的演講獲得了雷鳴般的掌聲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We appreciate your applause and support.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們感謝您的讚賞與支持。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們感謝您的讚賞與支持。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3126,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::assembly::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The general ____ of the United Nations meets annually.","expectedAnswer":"assembly","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The general ____ of the United Nations meets annually.","clozeAnswer":"assembly","exampleTranslation":"聯合國大會每年都會召開。","reference":{"eng":"assembly","kk":"/əˈsɛmblɪ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['集會；集會場所'], ['組裝；裝配'], ['（尤指公司、組織的）大會；議會']]","chEntries":["集會","集會場所","組裝","裝配","大會","議會"],"practiceMeaning":"聯合國大會每年都會召開。","analysis":"名詞，源自動詞 'assemble'。第一個核心意義是「集合」，指一群人為了特定目的聚集在一起，這可以是正式的（如會議、議會）或非正式的。第二個核心意義是「組裝」，指將零件組合起來的過程或結果。'Assembly' 強調的是『聚集』或『組成』的動作或狀態。","definition":"1. a group of people gathered together in one place for a common purpose; 2. the action of assembling a piece of equipment or a machine; 3. a legislative body.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The school holds an assembly every Monday morning.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這所學校每週一早上都會舉行集會。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The final assembly of the aircraft takes several weeks.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這架飛機的最終組裝需要數週時間。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The general assembly of the United Nations meets annually.\",\n    \"ch\": \"聯合國大會每年都會召開。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"聯合國大會每年都會召開。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3064,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::attach::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We ____ great importance to this project.","expectedAnswer":"attach","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We ____ great importance to this project.","clozeAnswer":"attach","exampleTranslation":"我們非常重視這個計畫。","reference":{"eng":"attach","kk":"/əˈtætʃ/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['附上；連接'], ['使依戀；使愛慕'], ['歸因於；認為有']]","chEntries":["附上","連接","使依戀","使愛慕","歸因於","認為有"],"practiceMeaning":"我們非常重視這個計畫。","analysis":"源自古法語 'atachier' (to fasten, to fix)，字源不確定，可能與日耳曼語有關。核心意義是「固定」或「緊密結合」。\n1. 附上；連接：將一個東西連接到另一個東西上，使之固定。\n2. 使依戀；使愛慕：建立情感上的連結，使人對某人或某物產生感情。\n3. 歸因於；認為有：將某種品質、原因或責任與某人或某事連結起來。","definition":"1. to fasten or join one thing to another; 2. to like or love someone or something very much; 3. to consider something to be caused by a particular thing or person.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please attach your resume to the application form.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請將您的履歷附在申請表上。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Children often attach themselves to their parents.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子們常常依戀他們的父母。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We attach great importance to this project.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們非常重視這個計畫。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們非常重視這個計畫。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6109,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::autonomy::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The university has considerable financial ____.","expectedAnswer":"autonomy","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The university has considerable financial ____.","clozeAnswer":"autonomy","exampleTranslation":"這所大學擁有相當大的財務自主性。","reference":{"eng":"autonomy","kk":"ɔːˈtɑːnəmi","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"自治\"  ],  [    \"自主權\"  ],  [    \"自主性\"  ]]","chEntries":["自治","自主權","自主性"],"practiceMeaning":"這所大學擁有相當大的財務自主性。","analysis":"此字源自希臘語 autonomia，由 autos（自己）和 nomos（法則；法律；區域）組成。autos 意為「自己」，nomos 意為「法則」。因此，autonomy 的核心語義是「自己制定法則」或「自行管理」。此名詞表示個人、組織或地區獨立行使權力、自主決策的能力。其語意演變是從「自己統治」到「自我規定」，再到現代的「自主權；自主性」。","definition":"1. the right or condition of self-government; 2. freedom from external control or influence; independence.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The region has a high degree of autonomy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該地區擁有高度的自治權。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Children need to develop a sense of autonomy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子們需要培養自主感。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The university has considerable financial autonomy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這所大學擁有相當大的財務自主性。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這所大學擁有相當大的財務自主性。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4040,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::aware::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He is not ____ of the facts.","expectedAnswer":"aware","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He is not ____ of the facts.","clozeAnswer":"aware","exampleTranslation":"他並不了解事實。","reference":{"eng":"aware","kk":"/əˈwɛr/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['意識到的', '知道的'], ['明白的', '察覺到的']]","chEntries":["意識到的","知道的","明白的","察覺到的"],"practiceMeaning":"他並不了解事實。","analysis":"源自古英語 'gewaer'，由 'ge-' (a past participle prefix) + 'wær' (aware) 構成。'wær' 本身與 'watch' 有關。核心概念是「看到」、「注意」，引申為「意識到」、「知道」或「察覺到」。","definition":"1. knowing or realizing that something is happening or that something exists; 2. having knowledge or understanding","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"你意識到其中存在的危險了嗎？\",\n    \"eng\": \"Are you aware of the dangers involved?\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"她敏銳地察覺到他的不適。\",\n    \"eng\": \"She was keenly aware of his discomfort.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他並不了解事實。\",\n    \"eng\": \"He is not aware of the facts.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他並不了解事實。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3201,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::bald::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He spoke in a ____, direct manner.","expectedAnswer":"bald","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He spoke in a ____, direct manner.","clozeAnswer":"bald","exampleTranslation":"他以一種直率、不加修飾的方式說話。","reference":{"eng":"bald","kk":"/bɔld/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['禿頭的'], ['光禿的'], ['無裝飾的']]","chEntries":["禿頭的","光禿的","無裝飾的"],"practiceMeaning":"他以一種直率、不加修飾的方式說話。","analysis":"詞源可能來自古英語 'balde'，意為 'white, pale'，進而引申為頭髮稀疏或脫落的狀態。也引申至事物缺乏覆蓋物，變得光禿、顯露。","definition":"1. having no hair on the head or a significant amount missing; 2. (of land or a mountain) having little or no vegetation; bare; 3. without adornment or protection.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The old man was completely bald.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那位老人完全禿頭了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The mountain peak was bald and rocky.\",\n    \"ch\": \"山頂光禿禿、多岩石。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He spoke in a bald, direct manner.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他以一種直率、不加修飾的方式說話。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他以一種直率、不加修飾的方式說話。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U41"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6154,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::banner::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She was the ____ of the feminist movement.","expectedAnswer":"banner","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She was the ____ of the feminist movement.","clozeAnswer":"banner","exampleTranslation":"她是女權運動的旗幟人物。","reference":{"eng":"banner","kk":"ˈbænər","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"旗幟\"  ],  [    \"橫幅\"  ],  [    \"標語\"  ],  [    \"冠軍\"  ],  [    \"領袖\"  ]]","chEntries":["旗幟","橫幅","標語","冠軍","領袖"],"practiceMeaning":"她是女權運動的旗幟人物。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 banner、bandiere，意為「旗幟」，其最終詞源可能與日耳曼語系表示「綁帶」的詞根有關，例如古英語 band「綁帶」。在現代英語中，其核心語義是「旗幟」，特別是指用於飄揚、展示或標示的布條。詞源中的「綁帶」概念與旗幟的懸掛方式相關。除了字面上的「旗幟」和「橫幅」，它也引申為「冠軍」的象徵，或用於標示、宣傳的「標語」，以及某個運動或運動的「領袖人物」。","definition":"1. a long strip of cloth bearing a slogan or design, carried in a demonstration or procession or hung in a public place; 2. a large piece of cloth with a name or slogan on it, carried as a symbol; 3. a flag; 4. (often in plural) a person or thing that is a symbol of a particular quality or activity, or that is an outstanding example of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The protestors carried banners calling for peace.\",\n    \"ch\": \"抗議者們舉著呼籲和平的橫幅。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The winning team was awarded a championship banner.\",\n    \"ch\": \"獲勝隊伍被授予了冠軍旗幟。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She was the banner of the feminist movement.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是女權運動的旗幟人物。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The team marched under its banner.\",\n    \"ch\": \"隊伍在他們的旗幟下行進。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她是女權運動的旗幟人物。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4327,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::beneath::prep","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Such behavior is ____ a person of his standing.","expectedAnswer":"beneath","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Such behavior is ____ a person of his standing.","clozeAnswer":"beneath","exampleTranslation":"這樣的行為有損他這樣的身份。","reference":{"eng":"beneath","kk":"/bɪˈniːθ/","tense":"prep.","ch":"[['在…下方；在…下面'], ['（地位、身份）低下於；卑於']]","chEntries":["在…下方","在…下面","低下於","卑於"],"practiceMeaning":"這樣的行為有損他這樣的身份。","analysis":"源自古英語 'beneothan'，由 'bene-' (down) 和 'neath' (near, under) 構成，與 'below' 同源。1. 指物理空間上的『在…下方』。2. 作為比喻，指在社會階層、道德標準或價值觀上的『低於、配不上』，表示不值得、有損身份。","definition":"in or to a lower position than someone or something else; directly under the surface of something; lower than someone or something in rank, status, or quality","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The treasure was buried deep beneath the ground.\",\n    \"ch\": \"寶藏深埋在地下。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She felt a sense of unease beneath her calm exterior.\",\n    \"ch\": \"在她平靜的外表下，她感到一絲不安。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Such behavior is beneath a person of his standing.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這樣的行為有損他這樣的身份。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這樣的行為有損他這樣的身份。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6155,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::beware::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____! He is known for his deceitful tactics.","expectedAnswer":"Beware","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____! He is known for his deceitful tactics.","clozeAnswer":"Beware","exampleTranslation":"小心！他以狡猾的策略聞名。","reference":{"eng":"beware","kk":"bɪˈwɛr","tense":"v.","ch":"[  [    \"警惕\"  ],  [    \"提防\"  ],  [    \"注意\"  ]]","chEntries":["警惕","提防","注意"],"practiceMeaning":"小心！他以狡猾的策略聞名。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 be+ware，意為「注意、警覺」。ware 本身是古英語 wær 的變體，意為「警覺的」。此字通常作為一個獨立的動詞或感嘆詞使用，其核心語義是「對潛在的危險或困難保持警惕」。它的結構由介詞 be- (表示強調或作為動詞前綴) 和形容詞/過去分詞 ware (警覺的) 組成，暗示著一種主動的、持續的警覺狀態。","definition":"1. be careful of (someone or something), especially by avoiding danger or harm.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Beware of the dog.\",\n    \"ch\": \"小心惡犬。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Drivers should beware of icy roads in winter.\",\n    \"ch\": \"司機在冬天應提防結冰的路面。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Beware! He is known for his deceitful tactics.\",\n    \"ch\": \"小心！他以狡猾的策略聞名。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Beware of pickpockets in crowded areas.\",\n    \"ch\": \"在擁擠的地區要小心扒手。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"小心！他以狡猾的策略聞名。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5824,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::blur::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The memory of that day is just a ____.","expectedAnswer":"blur","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The memory of that day is just a ____.","clozeAnswer":"blur","exampleTranslation":"那天的記憶只是一片模糊。","reference":{"eng":"blur","kk":"blər","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"模糊不清\"  ],  [    \"污點\"  ],  [    \"模糊的影像\"  ],  [    \"渾淆不清的狀態\"  ]]","chEntries":["模糊不清","污點","模糊的影像","渾淆不清的狀態"],"practiceMeaning":"那天的記憶只是一片模糊。","analysis":"此字詞源不明，可能與「模糊」的聲音或視覺有關。字義的演變傾向於指代一種不清晰、不確定的視覺或狀態。'Blur' 作名詞時，指一個不清晰的影像、一個模糊的區域，或一種混淆的狀態，使其難以分辨。這種不清晰感可能是由於移動、距離、視覺障礙或概念上的混淆所致。它描述了一種「失去清晰邊界」或「失去準確性」的狀態。例如，有時也指「一種使人興奮或眼花繚亂的迅速變化」。","definition":"1. A thing that is seen or heard indistinctly.; 2. A smudge or stain.; 3. A confused or disordered state.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The city lights were a blur in the distance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"城市燈火在遠方是一片模糊。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Tears made his vision a blur.\",\n    \"ch\": \"淚水使他的視線變得模糊。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The memory of that day is just a blur.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那天的記憶只是一片模糊。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The past few weeks have been a blur of activity.\",\n    \"ch\": \"過去幾周是一段忙碌到眼花繚亂的時期。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"那天的記憶只是一片模糊。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6157,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::blush::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The teacher noticed the student's ____.","expectedAnswer":"blush","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The teacher noticed the student's ____.","clozeAnswer":"blush","exampleTranslation":"老師注意到了學生的臉紅。","reference":{"eng":"blush","kk":"blʌʃ","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"臉紅\"  ],  [    \"羞紅\"  ],  [    \"羞愧\"  ]]","chEntries":["臉紅","羞紅","羞愧"],"practiceMeaning":"老師注意到了學生的臉紅。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 blyscan、blioxidan，意為「發紅、臉紅」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，應視為整體詞源演變。作為名詞，是動詞 blush「臉紅」的衍生物。其核心語義是因害羞、尷尬或羞愧而臉部皮膚變紅的現象或表情。","definition":"1. a reddening of the face, especially from embarrassment or shame.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A slight blush spread across her cheeks.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一抹淡淡的紅暈爬上她的臉頰。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He could not hide his blush.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他無法掩飾自己的臉紅。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The teacher noticed the student's blush.\",\n    \"ch\": \"老師注意到了學生的臉紅。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"老師注意到了學生的臉紅。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6210,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::bonus::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Finding parking was a ____ on such a busy day.","expectedAnswer":"bonus","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Finding parking was a ____ on such a busy day.","clozeAnswer":"bonus","exampleTranslation":"在如此忙碌的一天找到停車位是一份額外的幸運。","reference":{"eng":"bonus","kk":"ˈboʊnəs","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"獎金\"  ],  [    \"紅利\"  ],  [    \"額外津貼\"  ],  [    \"好處\"  ]]","chEntries":["獎金","紅利","額外津貼","好處"],"practiceMeaning":"在如此忙碌的一天找到停車位是一份額外的幸運。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 bonus，意為「好的」，在中古英語和現代英語中演變為「額外的給予，特別的好處」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作名詞時，指在基本工資或報酬之外額外給予的金錢、物品或好處，通常是因為表現良好、公司盈利或特殊節日。中文翻譯為「獎金；紅利；額外津貼；好處」。","definition":"1. an amount of money given to someone in addition to what is usual or expected, especially as a reward for good work; 2. something good that is extra and unexpected.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The employees received a Christmas bonus.\",\n    \"ch\": \"員工們收到了聖誕獎金。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company's excellent performance resulted in a generous bonus for all staff.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司優異的業績為所有員工帶來了豐厚的紅利。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Finding parking was a bonus on such a busy day.\",\n    \"ch\": \"在如此忙碌的一天找到停車位是一份額外的幸運。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"在如此忙碌的一天找到停車位是一份額外的幸運。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4214,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::branch::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Linguistics is a ____ of philology.","expectedAnswer":"branch","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Linguistics is a ____ of philology.","clozeAnswer":"branch","exampleTranslation":"語言學是語文學的一個分支。","reference":{"eng":"branch","kk":"/bræntʃ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['樹枝'], ['分支；分部；分公司'], ['（學科、知識的）分支；分支機構']]","chEntries":["樹枝","分支","分部","分公司","分支機構"],"practiceMeaning":"語言學是語文學的一個分支。","analysis":"源自古法語 branche，意為“樹枝，分支”，來自拉丁語 branca（可能是凱爾特語源）。核心是“分開的部分”。1. “樹枝”是最直接的字面意義。2. “分支；分部”是指一個較大組織的次要部分。3. “分支；分支機構”指一個領域下的次要部分或專業。","definition":"1. a part of a tree that grows out from the trunk or from a bough; 2. a part of a company or organization that is situated away from the main office; 3. a division or sub-category of a subject or field.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A bird was sitting on a branch of the tree.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一隻鳥棲息在樹枝上。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a branch office of our company.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是我們公司的一個分支辦事處。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Linguistics is a branch of philology.\",\n    \"ch\": \"語言學是語文學的一個分支。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"語言學是語文學的一個分支。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3067,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::breed::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Poverty can ____ crime.","expectedAnswer":"breed","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Poverty can ____ crime.","clozeAnswer":"breed","exampleTranslation":"貧困可能導致犯罪。","reference":{"eng":"breed","kk":"/briːd/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['繁殖；生育'], ['養育；培養'], ['引起；導致']]","chEntries":["繁殖","生育","養育","培養","引起","導致"],"practiceMeaning":"貧困可能導致犯罪。","analysis":"源自古英語 'brēdan' (to nourish, to bring up, to make multiply)，與 'brood' (young of animals) 有關。核心意義是「繁衍」或「養育」。\n1. 繁殖；生育：指動物或植物產生後代的過程。\n2. 養育；培養：指細心照料、教育或發展某人或某物，使其成長。\n3. 引起；導致：指某事物是另一事物發生的原因。","definition":"1. to produce young animals or plants; 2. to keep animals and breed them for a particular purpose; 3. to cause a particular problem or situation to exist.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Many species of birds breed in this region.\",\n    \"ch\": \"許多鳥類物種在此區域繁殖。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was bred to be a doctor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他被培養成醫生。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Poverty can breed crime.\",\n    \"ch\": \"貧困可能導致犯罪。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"貧困可能導致犯罪。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4501,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::bulletin::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The news ____ reported on the latest developments.","expectedAnswer":"bulletin","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The news ____ reported on the latest developments.","clozeAnswer":"bulletin","exampleTranslation":"新聞簡報報導了最新的進展。","reference":{"eng":"bulletin","kk":"/ˈbʊlɪtɪn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['公告'], ['簡報'], ['（體育比賽的）即時比分'], ['（天氣）快報']]","chEntries":["公告","簡報","即時比分","快報"],"practiceMeaning":"新聞簡報報導了最新的進展。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 bulla，意為「氣泡」、「印章」。後來指「密封的文件」或「官方聲明」。演變成「正式的公告」或「簡要的報告」。","definition":"1. A short statement or announcement of important news; 2. A periodical publication; 3. A brief report of current events.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The hospital issued a bulletin on the patient's condition.\",\n    \"ch\": \"醫院發布了關於病人情況的公告。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We received a weather bulletin.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們收到了一份天氣快報。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The news bulletin reported on the latest developments.\",\n    \"ch\": \"新聞簡報報導了最新的進展。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"新聞簡報報導了最新的進展。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3204,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::cabinet::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He opened the antique ____ to show the precious vase.","expectedAnswer":"cabinet","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He opened the antique ____ to show the precious vase.","clozeAnswer":"cabinet","exampleTranslation":"他打開古董陳列櫃，展示了那個珍貴的花瓶。","reference":{"eng":"cabinet","kk":"/ˈkæbɪnət/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['內閣'], ['櫥櫃'], ['陳列櫃'], ['（照片）相框']]","chEntries":["內閣","櫥櫃","陳列櫃","相框"],"practiceMeaning":"他打開古董陳列櫃，展示了那個珍貴的花瓶。","analysis":"詞源來自拉丁文 'capanna' (hut) 和 'capa' (head covering)，後演變成中古法語 'cabane' (cabin)。早期指小房間或私人空間，進而引申為存放物品的櫃子，以及政治上聚集重要人物的「小房間」（內閣）。","definition":"1. a group of ministers or other senior government officials; 2. a piece of furniture with shelves or drawers for storing things; 3. a small cupboard or cabinet, especially one used for display.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The president appointed new members to the cabinet.\",\n    \"ch\": \"總統任命了新的內閣成員。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She keeps her china in a glass-fronted cabinet.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她把瓷器放在一個玻璃門櫥櫃裡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He opened the antique cabinet to show the precious vase.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他打開古董陳列櫃，展示了那個珍貴的花瓶。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他打開古董陳列櫃，展示了那個珍貴的花瓶。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U41"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4328,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::chest::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She keeps her old letters in a wooden ____.","expectedAnswer":"chest","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She keeps her old letters in a wooden ____.","clozeAnswer":"chest","exampleTranslation":"她把舊信件放在一個木箱裡。","reference":{"eng":"chest","kk":"/tʃɛst/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['胸部'], ['箱子；櫃子']]","chEntries":["胸部","箱子","櫃子"],"practiceMeaning":"她把舊信件放在一個木箱裡。","analysis":"源自古英語 'cest'，與古希臘語 'kistē' (box) 和拉丁語 'cista' (box, chest) 同源，原意是指『箱子』。1. 指人體或動物身體的『胸部』，這個含義可能是在使用木箱來比喻胸腔的堅固性或容量後發展而來，或是因為胸部常被認為是承載情感的『箱子』。2. 最原始的含義，指『箱子、櫃子』，特別是較大的、用於存放財物的箱子。","definition":"the part of the front of the body between the neck and the stomach; a large strong box with a lid, used for storing things or for travelling","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He suffered a pain in his chest.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他感到胸部疼痛。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The pirate buried his treasure in a chest.\",\n    \"ch\": \"海盜將他的寶藏埋在一個箱子裡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She keeps her old letters in a wooden chest.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她把舊信件放在一個木箱裡。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她把舊信件放在一個木箱裡。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4346,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::cinema::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The history of ____ is fascinating.","expectedAnswer":"cinema","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The history of ____ is fascinating.","clozeAnswer":"cinema","exampleTranslation":"電影的歷史非常迷人。","reference":{"eng":"cinema","kk":"/ˈsɪnəmə/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['電影；電影藝術'], ['電影院']]","chEntries":["電影","電影藝術","電影院"],"practiceMeaning":"電影的歷史非常迷人。","analysis":"源自希臘語 'kinēma' (movement)，來自 'kinein' (to move)。1. 指『電影』作為一種藝術形式或娛樂，即『電影藝術』。2. 指放映電影的場所，即『電影院』。","definition":"the business or activity of making films; the art or technique of making films; a building in which films are shown","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a great admirer of French cinema.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是法國電影藝術的忠實崇拜者。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Let's go to the cinema tonight.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們今晚去看電影吧。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The history of cinema is fascinating.\",\n    \"ch\": \"電影的歷史非常迷人。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"電影的歷史非常迷人。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6065,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::citizenship::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Active ____ is crucial for a healthy democracy.","expectedAnswer":"citizenship","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Active ____ is crucial for a healthy democracy.","clozeAnswer":"citizenship","exampleTranslation":"積極的公民意識對健康的民主至關重要。","reference":{"eng":"citizenship","kk":"ˈsɪtɪzənʃɪp","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"公民權\"  ],  [    \"市民身份\"  ],  [    \"國民身份\"  ],  [    \"公民意識\"  ]]","chEntries":["公民權","市民身份","國民身份","公民意識"],"practiceMeaning":"積極的公民意識對健康的民主至關重要。","analysis":"此字由 citizen（公民）加上名詞後綴 -ship（表示狀態、身份、技能或集合）構成。Citizen 源自古法語 citeien，來自 civitas（city, state），再追溯至 civis（citizen）。Civitas 最終來源於 proto-Indo-European * (s)kein-「劃分，切割」，引申為「部落、社群」。Citizenship 的核心語義是「作為一個公民的身份、權利和義務」，包括法律上的公民權（公民身份），以及更廣泛的「公民責任」或「公民意識」。","definition":"1. the status of being a citizen of a particular country; 2. the rights and duties of a citizen; 3. the quality of behaving well and being useful to your country or community.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He applied for citizenship after living in the country for ten years.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在該國居住了十年後申請了公民權。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Citizenship education teaches people about their rights and responsibilities.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公民教育教導人們了解他們的權利和責任。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Active citizenship is crucial for a healthy democracy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"積極的公民意識對健康的民主至關重要。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"積極的公民意識對健康的民主至關重要。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5456,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::clear-out::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They had to ____ their old apartment before moving.","expectedAnswer":"clear out","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They had to ____ their old apartment before moving.","clozeAnswer":"clear out","exampleTranslation":"他們搬家前必須清空舊公寓。","reference":{"eng":"clear out","kk":"ˈklɪər aʊt","tense":"v.","ch":"[['清理'], ['清除'], ['搬空'], ['離去']]","chEntries":["清理","清除","搬空","離去"],"practiceMeaning":"他們搬家前必須清空舊公寓。","analysis":"此片語由形容詞 \"clear\" (清晰的、乾淨的) 和介詞 \"out\" (出去、外面) 組成。\"clear\" 源自拉丁語 \"clarus\"。在此作為動詞，\"clear out\" 表示「將某處徹底清理乾淨，移走所有不需要的東西」，或是「使某處騰空」，引申為「迅速離開」。","definition":"to remove everything from a place; to make a place empty by removing its contents; to leave a place quickly.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to clear out the garage before winter.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要在冬天來臨前清理車庫。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police told the crowd to clear out.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警方要求人群散開。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They had to clear out their old apartment before moving.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們搬家前必須清空舊公寓。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們搬家前必須清空舊公寓。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3945,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::committee::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ made a decision.","expectedAnswer":"committee","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ made a decision.","clozeAnswer":"committee","exampleTranslation":"委員會做出了決定。","reference":{"eng":"committee","kk":"/kəˈmɪti/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['委員會']]","chEntries":["委員會"],"practiceMeaning":"委員會做出了決定。","analysis":"源自中古英語 'committé' (意為「被託付的人」)，源自拉丁語 'committere' (意為「託付、委託」)。指為特定目的而設立的、由若干人組成的專門小組。","definition":"a group of people appointed for a specific function by a larger group and typically holding regular meetings.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The committee will meet next week to discuss the proposal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"委員會將於下週開會討論該提案。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a member of the planning committee.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是計畫委員會的成員。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The committee made a decision.\",\n    \"ch\": \"委員會做出了決定。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"委員會做出了決定。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3069,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::companion::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He was appointed a ____ of Honour.","expectedAnswer":"Companion","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He was appointed a ____ of Honour.","clozeAnswer":"Companion","exampleTranslation":"他被任命為榮譽會員。","reference":{"eng":"companion","kk":"/kəmˈpænjən/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['同伴；夥伴'], ['陪伴者；伴侶'], ['（用於某些頭銜）同列的']]","chEntries":["同伴","夥伴","陪伴者","伴侶","同列的"],"practiceMeaning":"他被任命為榮譽會員。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'compāniō'，'com-' (with) + 'pānis' (bread)，字面意思是「分享麵包的人」。核心意義是「一起生活或旅行的人」。\n1. 同伴；夥伴：指與某人同行或共同參與某項活動的人。\n2. 陪伴者；伴侶：指經常陪伴某人，提供支持或友誼的人，可以是人或動物。\n3. （用於某些頭銜）同列的：在名稱中表示與另一人或事物並列，例如 'Companion of Honour'。","definition":"1. a person who is with someone else; 2. a person or animal that travels with or lives with someone; 3. a person who is included in a group or order.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She found a loyal companion in her dog.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在她的狗身上找到了忠實的伴侶。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He traveled across Europe with a companion.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他與一位旅伴一同遊歷歐洲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was appointed a Companion of Honour.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他被任命為榮譽會員。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他被任命為榮譽會員。","sourceName":"字彙王、龍騰課本","unitName":"U39、L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5832,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::compatible::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Ensure the devices are ____ before connecting them.","expectedAnswer":"compatible","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Ensure the devices are ____ before connecting them.","clozeAnswer":"compatible","exampleTranslation":"連接設備前，請確保它們是兼容的。","reference":{"eng":"compatible","kk":"kəmˈpætəbl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"兼容的\"  ],  [    \"相容的\"  ],  [    \"協調的\"  ],  [    \"適合的\"  ]]","chEntries":["兼容的","相容的","協調的","適合的"],"practiceMeaning":"連接設備前，請確保它們是兼容的。","analysis":"此字由拉丁語 'compatibilis' 演變而來，由 'com-' (with) 和 'pati' (to suffer, endure) 構成。'Patibilis' 意為「可承受的」。'Compatibilis' 的字面意思是「可以一起承受」或「可以共存」。在現代英語中，'compatible' 指兩個或多個事物能夠一起良好運作、和諧共處，或在功能上相互適用。這可以是指電腦系統、軟體、硬體之間的「兼容性」，也可以是指人際關係中的「協調」或「適合」。核心概念是「能夠和諧共存或協作」。例如，也可指「性情相投的」。","definition":"1. (of two things) able to exist or occur together without conflict.; 2. (of computer hardware or software) able to be used or run together.; 3. (of a person) having a compatible nature or disposition.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This software is not compatible with older versions.\",\n    \"ch\": \"此軟體與舊版本不兼容。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They are a compatible couple.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們是一對很合適的伴侶。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Ensure the devices are compatible before connecting them.\",\n    \"ch\": \"連接設備前，請確保它們是兼容的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Their personalities were highly compatible.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們的性情非常協調。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"連接設備前，請確保它們是兼容的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4055,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::conclusion::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We reached a ____ after a long discussion.","expectedAnswer":"conclusion","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We reached a ____ after a long discussion.","clozeAnswer":"conclusion","exampleTranslation":"經過長時間的討論，我們達成了一個結論。","reference":{"eng":"conclusion","kk":"/kənˈkluʒən/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['結論', '結局'], ['結束']]","chEntries":["結論","結局","結束"],"practiceMeaning":"經過長時間的討論，我們達成了一個結論。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'conclusio'，由 'con-' (together) + 'claudere' (to shut) 構成，字面意思是「關閉在一起」。核心是「結束」、「完結」。因此，'conclusion' 指一個過程或事件的「結束」，也指通過推理或討論得出的「結論」。","definition":"1. the end or final part of something; 2. a judgment or decision reached by reasoning; 3. a final statement or summary","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"你對這個實驗的結論是什麼？\",\n    \"eng\": \"What is your conclusion about the experiment?\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"這部電影有一個出人意料的結局。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The movie had a surprising conclusion.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"經過長時間的討論，我們達成了一個結論。\",\n    \"eng\": \"We reached a conclusion after a long discussion.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"經過長時間的討論，我們達成了一個結論。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U4、L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4069,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::considerable::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This is a ____ achievement.","expectedAnswer":"considerable","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This is a ____ achievement.","clozeAnswer":"considerable","exampleTranslation":"這是一項了不起的成就。","reference":{"eng":"considerable","kk":"/kənˈsɪdərəbəl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['相當大的', '可觀的'], ['值得考慮的', '重要的']]","chEntries":["相當大的","可觀的","值得考慮的","重要的"],"practiceMeaning":"這是一項了不起的成就。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'considerare' (to observe, to examine)，由 'con-' (together) + 'sidus, sideris' (star) 構成，原意是「觀察星辰」，引申為「仔細考慮」、「審視」。因此，'considerable' 指「值得仔細考慮的」、「重要的」，進而延伸為「數量或程度非常大」、「可觀的」。","definition":"1. notably large in size, amount, or extent; 2. large or great enough to be worthy of attention or notice","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"這個項目需要相當多的時間和精力。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The project requires considerable time and effort.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"價格有顯著的增長。\",\n    \"eng\": \"There has been a considerable increase in prices.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"這是一項了不起的成就。\",\n    \"eng\": \"This is a considerable achievement.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是一項了不起的成就。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4168,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::costs::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"What are the associated ____?","expectedAnswer":"costs","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"What are the associated ____?","clozeAnswer":"costs","exampleTranslation":"相關費用有哪些？","reference":{"eng":"costs","kk":"/kɒsts/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['費用', '成本']]","chEntries":["費用","成本"],"practiceMeaning":"相關費用有哪些？","analysis":"由 cost（成本，價值）的複數形式。源自古法語 cost（價值，報酬）。核心概念是「為獲得某物或完成某事所付出的代價」。","definition":"the amount of money needed to buy, produce, or do something","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The steep rise in living costs made it hard to make ends meet.\",\n    \"ch\": \"生活成本的急劇上漲使得人們難以為繼。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to reduce production costs.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要降低生產成本。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"What are the associated costs?\",\n    \"ch\": \"相關費用有哪些？\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"相關費用有哪些？","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5078,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::coverage::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The remote area has poor mobile phone ____.","expectedAnswer":"coverage","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The remote area has poor mobile phone ____.","clozeAnswer":"coverage","exampleTranslation":"那個偏遠地區的手機訊號覆蓋很差。","reference":{"eng":"coverage","kk":"ˈkʌvərɪdʒ","tense":"n.","ch":"[['報導'], ['覆蓋範圍'], ['保險範圍']]","chEntries":["報導","覆蓋範圍","保險範圍"],"practiceMeaning":"那個偏遠地區的手機訊號覆蓋很差。","analysis":"此字由 'cover' (覆蓋) + '-age' (名詞化後綴) 構成。'-age' 常用於形成名詞，表示狀態、行為、總量或集合，如 'storage', 'carriage'。'Coverage' 的核心語義是 '被覆蓋的程度或範圍'。這引申為新聞媒體對事件的 '報導範圍'，保險條款對風險的 '保障範圍'，以及資訊或訊號的 '傳播範圍'。","definition":"1. The extent to which something is covered or protected.; 2. The amount of information about an event or subject that is included in newspapers, television programmes, etc.; 3. The amount of protection that an insurance policy gives you.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The news coverage of the election was extensive.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這次選舉的新聞報導十分廣泛。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"What is the coverage of your car insurance?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你的汽車保險的保險範圍是什麼？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The remote area has poor mobile phone coverage.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那個偏遠地區的手機訊號覆蓋很差。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"那個偏遠地區的手機訊號覆蓋很差。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3072,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::crack::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This is your last ____ at the problem.","expectedAnswer":"crack","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This is your last ____ at the problem.","clozeAnswer":"crack","exampleTranslation":"這是你解決這個問題的最後一次機會。","reference":{"eng":"crack","kk":"/kræk/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['裂縫；縫隙'], ['爆裂聲；巨響'], ['（口語）嘗試；機會'], ['（口語）傑作；妙語']]","chEntries":["裂縫","縫隙","爆裂聲","巨響","嘗試","機會","傑作","妙語"],"practiceMeaning":"這是你解決這個問題的最後一次機會。","analysis":"源自古英語 'crac' (a loud noise)，或與動詞 'crack' 同源。指「裂開」的狀態或由此產生的結果。\n1. 裂縫；縫隙：指物體表面或結構上出現的細長開口。\n2. 爆裂聲；巨響：指突然發出的、尖銳或響亮的聲音。\n3. （口語）嘗試；機會：指一次試驗或獲得某事的機會，常帶有一點冒險意味。\n4. （口語）傑作；妙語：指非常出色、令人印象深刻的事情或一句話。","definition":"1. a line on the surface of something along which it has split without breaking apart; 2. a sudden loud noise; 3. an attempt to do something; 4. a very good example of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There is a crack in the wall.\",\n    \"ch\": \"牆上有道裂縫。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The thunder made a loud crack.\",\n    \"ch\": \"雷聲發出巨大的爆裂聲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is your last crack at the problem.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是你解決這個問題的最後一次機會。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"That joke was a real crack!\",\n    \"ch\": \"那個笑話真是太妙了！\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是你解決這個問題的最後一次機會。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3135,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::cube::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He dropped a sugar ____ into his tea.","expectedAnswer":"cube","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He dropped a sugar ____ into his tea.","clozeAnswer":"cube","exampleTranslation":"他往茶裡丟了一塊方糖。","reference":{"eng":"cube","kk":"/kjuːb/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['立方體；立方塊'], ['（尤指食品）塊；方糖']]","chEntries":["立方體","立方塊","塊","方糖"],"practiceMeaning":"他往茶裡丟了一塊方糖。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'cubus'，再追溯至希臘語 'kybos'，意為「骰子，立方體」。'Cube' 的基本幾何概念是一個三維的、有六個相等正方形面的物體。語意延伸至任何具有立方體或塊狀形狀的物體，特別是切割成規則塊狀的食品，如方糖、冰塊、肉塊等。","definition":"1. a solid body with six equal square sides; 2. a piece of food cut into a cube; 3. a sugar cube.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The magician made the rabbit disappear inside a large cube.\",\n    \"ch\": \"魔術師讓兔子在一個大立方體裡面消失了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please add a cube of butter to the pan.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請在鍋裡加一塊黃油。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He dropped a sugar cube into his tea.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他往茶裡丟了一塊方糖。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他往茶裡丟了一塊方糖。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4591,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::decayed::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The once-grand theater was now ____.","expectedAnswer":"decayed","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The once-grand theater was now ____.","clozeAnswer":"decayed","exampleTranslation":"這座曾經宏偉的劇院如今已衰敗不堪。","reference":{"eng":"decayed","kk":"/dɪˈkeɪd/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['腐爛的', '衰退的']]","chEntries":["腐爛的","衰退的"],"practiceMeaning":"這座曾經宏偉的劇院如今已衰敗不堪。","analysis":"這是動詞 'decay' (腐爛、衰退) 的過去分詞，用作形容詞。 'decay' 源自拉丁語 'decadere'，'de-' (down) 和 'cadere' (to fall - 落下)。\n    1. 腐爛的：指有機物因分解而變得腐敗、發臭。\n    2. 衰退的：指事物（如建築、健康、道德）逐漸惡化、衰敗。","definition":"1. (of organic matter) rot or decompose through the action of bacteria and fungi.; 2. (of something in existence) decline or deteriorate.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The old house looked decayed and abandoned.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座老房子看起來腐朽且被遺棄。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He suffered from decayed teeth.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的牙齒腐爛了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The once-grand theater was now decayed.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座曾經宏偉的劇院如今已衰敗不堪。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這座曾經宏偉的劇院如今已衰敗不堪。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5293,"wordRef":"字彙王::u63::decline::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The Roman Empire began to ____ in the 3rd century.","expectedAnswer":"decline","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The Roman Empire began to ____ in the 3rd century.","clozeAnswer":"decline","exampleTranslation":"羅馬帝國始於三世紀開始衰落。","reference":{"eng":"decline","kk":"dɪˈklaɪn","tense":"v.","ch":"[['拒絕'], ['下降', '減少'], ['衰落', '衰敗']]","chEntries":["拒絕","下降","減少","衰落","衰敗"],"practiceMeaning":"羅馬帝國始於三世紀開始衰落。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'declinare'，由 'de-'（down, away）和 'clinare'（to bend, to lean）組成。'clinare' 又來自印歐語根 '*klei-'（to lean）。構詞上，'de-' 作為方向或程度減弱前綴，'clin-' 為詞根，'-are' 為動詞後綴。原始語義為「向下彎曲、傾斜」。此語義延伸至抽象層面：使事物「向下」或「減少」（經濟、數量），「衰落」（健康、權力），或表示「拒絕」（意願上的「傾斜」或「迴避」）。","definition":"to refuse to accept or consider something; to become smaller, fewer, or less; to fall to a lower level.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She declined the invitation to the party.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她拒絕了派對的邀請。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The birth rate has been declining for years.\",\n    \"ch\": \"出生率多年來一直在下降。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The Roman Empire began to decline in the 3rd century.\",\n    \"ch\": \"羅馬帝國始於三世紀開始衰落。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"羅馬帝國始於三世紀開始衰落。","sourceName":"字彙王、龍騰課本","unitName":"U63、L8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4686,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::deed::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He signed the ____ to the house.","expectedAnswer":"deed","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He signed the ____ to the house.","clozeAnswer":"deed","exampleTranslation":"他簽署了房子的契據。","reference":{"eng":"deed","kk":"/ˈdid/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['行為'], ['事蹟'], ['（法律）契據']]","chEntries":["行為","事蹟","契據"],"practiceMeaning":"他簽署了房子的契據。","analysis":"源自古英語 *dēd*，與 'do'（做）同源。核心是「做出來的事情」。引申至具有重要性或價值的事蹟，以及法律上證明財產權的書面文件。","definition":"1. An action that is done. 2. An act or achievement, especially one that is brave or worthy of admiration. 3. A legal document that transfers ownership of property from one person to another.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His good deed was recognized by the community.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他這個善舉得到了社區的認可。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The heroic deed of the firefighters saved many lives.\",\n    \"ch\": \"消防員的英勇事蹟拯救了許多生命。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He signed the deed to the house.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他簽署了房子的契據。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他簽署了房子的契據。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6164,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::deliberate::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She took a ____ step forward.","expectedAnswer":"deliberate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She took a ____ step forward.","clozeAnswer":"deliberate","exampleTranslation":"她謹慎地向前邁出一步。","reference":{"eng":"deliberate","kk":"dɪˈlɪbərət","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"故意的\"  ],  [    \"蓄意的\"  ],  [    \"審慎的\"  ],  [    \"計畫好的\"  ]]","chEntries":["故意的","蓄意的","審慎的","計畫好的"],"practiceMeaning":"她謹慎地向前邁出一步。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 dēlīberātus，是 dēlīberāre「仔細考慮、權衡」的過去分詞。dēlīberāre 由 de- (down, completely) + lībra (balance, scale) 組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 de-「完全」和 lībra「秤」是其核心語意來源。作為形容詞，其核心語義是「經過仔細考慮而做出的」。詞源中的「權衡」概念引申出「蓄意的、計畫好的、非偶然的」。","definition":"1. done consciously and intentionally; 2. characterized by careful thought and consideration; 3. slow and careful.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The decision was the result of a deliberate choice.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個決定是經過深思熟慮的選擇的結果。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His remarks were deliberately offensive.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的言論是蓄意冒犯的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She took a deliberate step forward.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她謹慎地向前邁出一步。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The plan was a deliberate attempt to mislead the public.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個計畫是為了誤導公眾而蓄意為之的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她謹慎地向前邁出一步。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4143,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::democratic::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He is a staunch supporter of ____ ideals.","expectedAnswer":"democratic","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He is a staunch supporter of ____ ideals.","clozeAnswer":"democratic","exampleTranslation":"他是民主理想的堅定支持者。","reference":{"eng":"democratic","kk":"/ˌdɛməˈkrætɪk/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['民主的']]","chEntries":["民主的"],"practiceMeaning":"他是民主理想的堅定支持者。","analysis":"源自 democracy（民主），democracy 源自希臘語 dēmos（人民）+ kratos（統治）。核心概念是「人民統治」或「支持民主原則」。","definition":"1. relating to or supporting democracy or its principles; 2. (of a country or system of government) controlled by or having elected representatives elected by the people","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They live in a democratic society.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們生活在一個民主社會。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The organization is run on democratic principles.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個組織依照民主原則運作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a staunch supporter of democratic ideals.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是民主理想的堅定支持者。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他是民主理想的堅定支持者。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U5、L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3141,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::dominant::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"In genetics, the ____ allele masks the effect of the recessive allele.","expectedAnswer":"dominant","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"In genetics, the ____ allele masks the effect of the recessive allele.","clozeAnswer":"dominant","exampleTranslation":"在遺傳學中，顯性等位基因會掩蓋隱性等位基因的作用。","reference":{"eng":"dominant","kk":"/ˈdɒmɪnənt/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['占主導地位的；有影響力的'], ['（基因）顯性的'], ['（地理、建築等）顯著的，突出的']]","chEntries":["占主導地位的","有影響力的","顯性的","顯著的，突出的"],"practiceMeaning":"在遺傳學中，顯性等位基因會掩蓋隱性等位基因的作用。","analysis":"形容詞，源自動詞 'dominate'。表示處於權力、控制或影響力的頂峰，是最重要的、最強勢的或最明顯的部分。在生物學中，'dominant gene' 指的是會壓倒另一條基因（隱性基因）並決定性狀的基因。其語意核心是「最重要」、「最強」或「最顯著」。","definition":"1. having power and influence over others; 2. the most important or noticeable; 3. (of a gene) expressing its phenotype readily over a corresponding recessive gene.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She played a dominant role in the negotiations.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在談判中扮演了主導角色。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Red is the dominant color in the painting.\",\n    \"ch\": \"紅色是這幅畫的主導色彩。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"In genetics, the dominant allele masks the effect of the recessive allele.\",\n    \"ch\": \"在遺傳學中，顯性等位基因會掩蓋隱性等位基因的作用。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"在遺傳學中，顯性等位基因會掩蓋隱性等位基因的作用。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4542,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::dumb::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ waiter brought the food up.","expectedAnswer":"dumb","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ waiter brought the food up.","clozeAnswer":"dumb","exampleTranslation":"傳菜電梯把食物送上來了。","reference":{"eng":"dumb","kk":"/dʌm/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['啞的', '無法說話的'], ['愚蠢的', '笨拙的'], ['（機器等）不發聲的，靜止的']]","chEntries":["啞的","無法說話的","愚蠢的","笨拙的","不發聲的，靜止的"],"practiceMeaning":"傳菜電梯把食物送上來了。","analysis":"源自古英語 'dumb'，意為 'mute, silent' (啞的、沉默的)。\n    1. 啞的：指無法說話的能力。\n    2. 愚蠢的：指缺乏智慧或理解力，是比較粗俗的用法。\n    3. 不發聲的、靜止的：指機器或設備沒有發出聲音，或處於靜止狀態，如 'dumb waiter' (傳菜電梯)，'dumb terminal' (啞終端)。","definition":"1. unable to speak.; 2. stupid; foolish.; 3. (of a device or machine) not having or performing the functions of speech or sound.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was born dumb and mute.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他生來就又啞又不能說話。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Don't be dumb; think before you speak.\",\n    \"ch\": \"別那麼笨；說話前先想想。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The dumb waiter brought the food up.\",\n    \"ch\": \"傳菜電梯把食物送上來了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"傳菜電梯把食物送上來了。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5562,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::efficiency::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Her ____ in handling multiple tasks is remarkable.","expectedAnswer":"efficiency","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Her ____ in handling multiple tasks is remarkable.","clozeAnswer":"efficiency","exampleTranslation":"她同時處理多項任務的效率令人稱道。","reference":{"eng":"efficiency","kk":"ɪˈfɪʃənsi","tense":"n.","ch":"[['效率'], ['效能']]","chEntries":["效率","效能"],"practiceMeaning":"她同時處理多項任務的效率令人稱道。","analysis":"此字由 \"efficient\" 加上名詞化字尾 \"-cy\" 構成。\"efficient\" 源自拉丁語 \"efficiēns\"，是 \"efficere\"（to work out, accomplish, produce，完成，達成，生產）的現在分詞。\"efficere\" 由 \"ex-\"（out）和 \"facere\"（to make, to do，製造，做）組成，意為「製造出來，完成」。\"-cy\" 是構成抽象名詞的字尾。因此，\"efficiency\" 的核心語義是「有效完成某事的能力或狀態」，即「效率」或「效能」。它強調的是以最少的資源（時間、精力、金錢）達成最大的產出或目標。","definition":"1. The state or quality of being efficient; 2. The ability to accomplish something with the least amount of wasted time, effort, or resources.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The new system has greatly improved the efficiency of our operations.\",\n    \"ch\": \"新系統大大提高了我們營運的效率。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We are always looking for ways to increase our energy efficiency.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們一直在尋找提高能源效率的方法。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her efficiency in handling multiple tasks is remarkable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她同時處理多項任務的效率令人稱道。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她同時處理多項任務的效率令人稱道。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5447,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::enormous::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The project faced ____ challenges.","expectedAnswer":"enormous","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The project faced ____ challenges.","clozeAnswer":"enormous","exampleTranslation":"這個專案面臨著巨大的挑戰。","reference":{"eng":"enormous","kk":"ɪˈnɔːrməs","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['巨大的'], ['龐大的'], ['極大的']]","chEntries":["巨大的","龐大的","極大的"],"practiceMeaning":"這個專案面臨著巨大的挑戰。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 \"enormis\"，原意為\"不規則的\"、\"畸形的\"、\"巨大的\"。它由 \"e-\" (變體，源於 \"ex-\"，表示\"出\"、\"之外\") 和 \"norma\" (規則、標準、準則) 構成。構詞上，\"e-\" 提供了「超出」的語意，\"norma\" 提供了「標準」或「規則」。因此，\"enormous\" 的原始語義是「超出標準、規則的」，引申為「巨大的」、「龐大的」。","definition":"very large in size, quantity, or extent; extremely large; immense.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company made an enormous profit last year.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司去年獲得了巨額利潤。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They live in an enormous house in the countryside.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們住在鄉村的一棟巨大的房子裡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The project faced enormous challenges.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個專案面臨著巨大的挑戰。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個專案面臨著巨大的挑戰。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5043,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::estate::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Real ____ prices have been rising.","expectedAnswer":"estate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Real ____ prices have been rising.","clozeAnswer":"estate","exampleTranslation":"房地產價格一直在上漲。","reference":{"eng":"estate","kk":"ɪˈsteɪt","tense":"n.","ch":"[['財產'], ['房地產'], ['（尤指大塊的）土地'], ['（某人或某群體的）狀況']]","chEntries":["財產","房地產","土地","狀況"],"practiceMeaning":"房地產價格一直在上漲。","analysis":"此字源自古法語estat，來自拉丁語status，意為「狀態、地位」。最初指「財產」、「財富」。引申為「財產，尤指大片土地及其建築」，如「莊園」(country estate)。在法律語境中，指「遺產」(estate of a deceased person) 或「財產權」(real estate)。其核心語意圍繞著「擁有的財產或地位」。OCR 掃描時可能將 's' 誤判為 '5'。此處修正為 estate。","definition":"1. all the money and property owned by a particular person or company; 2. a large area of land in the country, often with a large house on it; 3. the total property, especially land, owned by someone.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He inherited a large estate from his uncle.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他從叔叔那裡繼承了一大筆財產。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The property is a beautiful country estate.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這處房產是一座美麗的鄉間莊園。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Real estate prices have been rising.\",\n    \"ch\": \"房地產價格一直在上漲。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"房地產價格一直在上漲。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5586,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::excellence::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The award recognizes ____ in scientific research.","expectedAnswer":"excellence","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The award recognizes ____ in scientific research.","clozeAnswer":"excellence","exampleTranslation":"該獎項旨在表彰科學研究的傑出成就。","reference":{"eng":"excellence","kk":"ˈɛksələns","tense":"n.","ch":"[['卓越'], ['優秀'], ['傑出']]","chEntries":["卓越","優秀","傑出"],"practiceMeaning":"該獎項旨在表彰科學研究的傑出成就。","analysis":"此字由 \"excellent\" 加上名詞化字尾 \"-ce\" 構成。\"excellent\" 源自拉丁語 \"excellēns\"，是 \"excellere\"（to be eminent, surpass, excel，卓越，超越）的現在分詞。\"excellere\" 由 \"ex-\"（out）和 \"cellere\"（to rise, to be eminent，上升，卓越）組成，意為「突出，超越眾人」。 \"-ce\" 是構成抽象名詞的字尾。因此，\"excellence\" 的核心語義是「卓越的品質、極高的水準或傑出的表現」。它強調的是在某個領域達到的頂尖水準。","definition":"1. The quality of being outstanding or extremely good; 2. Great and distinguished ability or quality.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The restaurant is known for its culinary excellence.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家餐廳以其卓越的烹飪技藝聞名。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She strives for excellence in everything she does.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她力求在她所做的一切事情上都做到最好。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The award recognizes excellence in scientific research.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該獎項旨在表彰科學研究的傑出成就。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該獎項旨在表彰科學研究的傑出成就。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4067,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::experiment::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The results of the ____ were inconclusive.","expectedAnswer":"experiment","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The results of the ____ were inconclusive.","clozeAnswer":"experiment","exampleTranslation":"實驗結果沒有定論。","reference":{"eng":"experiment","kk":"/ɪkˈspɛrɪmənt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['實驗']]","chEntries":["實驗"],"practiceMeaning":"實驗結果沒有定論。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'experimentum'，由 'experiri' (to try, to test) 構成，'experiri' 又由 'ex-' (out) + 'periri' (to try) 構成。核心是「嘗試」、「測試」。因此，'experiment' 指通過觀察和測試來檢驗某個理論或發現新知識的過程。","definition":"a scientific test done in order to learn how something happens or to check if a particular idea is true","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"這位科學家進行了一項實驗來驗證他的理論。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The scientist conducted an experiment to test his theory.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個危險的實驗。\",\n    \"eng\": \"This is a dangerous experiment.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"實驗結果沒有定論。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The results of the experiment were inconclusive.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"實驗結果沒有定論。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4060,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::expressive::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This music is highly ____.","expectedAnswer":"expressive","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This music is highly ____.","clozeAnswer":"expressive","exampleTranslation":"這音樂極富表現力。","reference":{"eng":"expressive","kk":"/ɪkˈsprɛsɪv/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['富於表情的', '生動的'], ['表達的', '表示的']]","chEntries":["富於表情的","生動的","表達的","表示的"],"practiceMeaning":"這音樂極富表現力。","analysis":"源自 'express' (表達)，加上 '-ive' 後綴。'express' 源自拉丁語 'exprimere'，由 'ex-' (out) + 'premere' (to press) 構成，原意是「壓榨出來」。因此，'expressive' 指「能清晰表達情感或思想的」（富於表情的、生動的），或「用於表達的」、「表示的」。","definition":"1. showing or conveying feelings or thoughts; 2. serving to express or represent","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"她的臉表情非常豐富。\",\n    \"eng\": \"Her face is very expressive.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他發出了一個充滿情感的嘆息。\",\n    \"eng\": \"He gave an expressive sigh.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"這音樂極富表現力。\",\n    \"eng\": \"This music is highly expressive.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這音樂極富表現力。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5638,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l8::extent::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"To what ____ do you agree with him?","expectedAnswer":"extent","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"To what ____ do you agree with him?","clozeAnswer":"extent","exampleTranslation":"你在多大程度上同意他的看法？","reference":{"eng":"extent","kk":"ɪkˈstɛnt","tense":"n.","ch":"[['程度'], ['範圍'], ['面積'], ['廣度']]","chEntries":["程度","範圍","面積","廣度"],"practiceMeaning":"你在多大程度上同意他的看法？","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 extent，意為「測量」。其來自拉丁語 extentus，是 extend（伸展，擴展）的過去分詞。extend 來自拉丁語 extendere，由 ex-（出，out）+ tendere（伸展，to stretch）組成。tendere 來自原始印歐語 *ten-（伸展）。因此，extent 的核心語義是「被伸展或擴展到的範圍或程度」。構詞上，ex- 提供「出」或「向外」的方向，tendere 提供「伸展」的核心動作。此處為名詞用法，指代事物的「程度」、「範圍」、「廣度」或「規模」。","definition":"the degree or scope to which something is the case; the size or amount of something; the area covered by something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The full extent of the damage is not yet known.\",\n    \"ch\": \"損壞的全部程度尚不明確。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The extent of his knowledge is impressive.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他知識的廣度令人印象深刻。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"To what extent do you agree with him?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你在多大程度上同意他的看法？\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"你在多大程度上同意他的看法？","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3171,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::extinct::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The tradition became ____ after the war.","expectedAnswer":"extinct","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The tradition became ____ after the war.","clozeAnswer":"extinct","exampleTranslation":"這個傳統在戰後消失了。","reference":{"eng":"extinct","kk":"/ɪkˈstɪŋkt/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['滅絕的；絕種的'], ['（物種、制度、語言等）已消失的；不復存在的']]","chEntries":["滅絕的","絕種的","已消失的","不復存在的"],"practiceMeaning":"這個傳統在戰後消失了。","analysis":"詞源來自拉丁語 'extinctus'，意為「熄滅，毀滅」，源於 'exstinguere'（熄滅，毀滅）。'Extinct' 指的是某個物種、族群、制度、語言或事物完全消失，不再存在。最常見的用法是形容已滅絕的動物或植物。它強調的是「徹底消失」和「不復存在」的狀態。","definition":"1. (of a species, family, or other larger group) having no living members; 2. no longer in existence; having died out.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Dinosaurs have been extinct for millions of years.\",\n    \"ch\": \"恐龍已經滅絕數百萬年了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The dodo is an example of an extinct bird.\",\n    \"ch\": \"渡渡鳥是一種已滅絕的鳥類。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The tradition became extinct after the war.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個傳統在戰後消失了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個傳統在戰後消失了。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40、U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4534,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::faint::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There was a ____ smell of gas in the air.","expectedAnswer":"faint","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There was a ____ smell of gas in the air.","clozeAnswer":"faint","exampleTranslation":"空氣中有微弱的瓦斯味。","reference":{"eng":"faint","kk":"/feɪnt/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['微弱的', '模糊的'], ['昏眩的', '無力的']]","chEntries":["微弱的","模糊的","昏眩的","無力的"],"practiceMeaning":"空氣中有微弱的瓦斯味。","analysis":"源自古法語 'feint'，意為 'feigned, false, weak' (偽裝的、虛假的、軟弱的)。此字根與 'feign' (假裝) 同源。\n    'adj.' 意義延伸：\n    1. 微弱、模糊：指感官可察覺的程度極低，如 'faint sound' (微弱的聲音)，'faint light' (微弱的光)。\n    2. 虛弱、無力：指身體或精神上的狀態，如 'faint with hunger' (因飢餓而無力)，'faint hope' (渺茫的希望)。","definition":"1. (of a light, sound, smell, or colour) scarcely perceptible; faint.; 2. feeling weak and dizzy and liable to collapse.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She heard a faint cry for help.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她聽到微弱的求救聲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He felt faint and had to sit down.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他感到頭暈，不得不坐下。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was a faint smell of gas in the air.\",\n    \"ch\": \"空氣中有微弱的瓦斯味。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"空氣中有微弱的瓦斯味。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3289,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::feast::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They celebrated the harvest with a ____.","expectedAnswer":"feast","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They celebrated the harvest with a ____.","clozeAnswer":"feast","exampleTranslation":"他們舉辦盛宴慶祝豐收。","reference":{"eng":"feast","kk":"/fiːst/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['盛宴；宴會'], ['（令人高興的）享受；樂事'], ['節日；齋戒日']]","chEntries":["盛宴","宴會","享受","樂事","節日","齋戒日"],"practiceMeaning":"他們舉辦盛宴慶祝豐收。","analysis":"源自古法語 'feste'，來自拉丁語 'festum' (節日，慶祝)。原指宗教節日或慶祝活動，後主要指大規模、豐盛的宴會。","definition":"1. a large meal, typically one to celebrate something; 2. something that provides great pleasure to the senses; 3. a religious festival or anniversary.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The wedding feast lasted all night.\",\n    \"ch\": \"婚宴持續了一整夜。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The mountain scenery was a feast for the eyes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"山景令人賞心悅目。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They celebrated the harvest with a feast.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們舉辦盛宴慶祝豐收。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們舉辦盛宴慶祝豐收。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5449,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::fond::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They are ____ of classical music.","expectedAnswer":"fond","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They are ____ of classical music.","clozeAnswer":"fond","exampleTranslation":"他們喜歡古典音樂。","reference":{"eng":"fond","kk":"fɑːnd","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['喜愛的'], ['深情的'], ['寵愛的'], ['喜歡的']]","chEntries":["喜愛的","深情的","寵愛的","喜歡的"],"practiceMeaning":"他們喜歡古典音樂。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 \"fonned\"，意為\"愚蠢的\"、\"裝模作樣的\"，後來演變成\"喜愛的\"。其詞源與\"fool\" (傻瓜) 可能有關，但語義發生了轉變。構詞上沒有明顯的字首、字根或字尾可拆解，應視為一個整體詞源的演變。原始的「愚蠢」語義可能在某些情境下轉化為「過度的愛」、「溺愛」，進而演變為現代意義上的「喜愛的」、「深情的」。","definition":"having an affection or liking for someone or something; loving or caring deeply for someone or something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is very fond of her grandchildren.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她非常喜愛她的孫子孫女。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has fond memories of his childhood.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對童年有著美好的回憶。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They are fond of classical music.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們喜歡古典音樂。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們喜歡古典音樂。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4526,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::for::prep","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She stayed ____ two weeks.","expectedAnswer":"for","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She stayed ____ two weeks.","clozeAnswer":"for","exampleTranslation":"她待了兩週。","reference":{"eng":"for","kk":"/fər/, /fɔːr/","tense":"prep.","ch":"[['為了'], ['給'], ['支持'], ['持續（一段時間）']]","chEntries":["為了","給","支持","持續"],"practiceMeaning":"她待了兩週。","analysis":"源自古英語 for。是一個極其常見且語意複雜的介詞。核心語意是「目的」、「原因」、「受益者」。引申義廣泛，包括「持續時間」、「代表」、「傾向」等。","definition":"1. Intended to achieve or affect; 2. In order to benefit or be given to; 3. In support of or in agreement with; 4. During (a period of time).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This gift is for you.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這份禮物是給你的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He works for a large company.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在一家大公司工作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She stayed for two weeks.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她待了兩週。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They are fighting for their freedom.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們正在為自由而戰。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她待了兩週。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6172,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::forge::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He learned the art of metalworking in the ____.","expectedAnswer":"forge","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He learned the art of metalworking in the ____.","clozeAnswer":"forge","exampleTranslation":"他在鍛造廠學到了金屬加工的技藝。","reference":{"eng":"forge","kk":"fɔrdʒ","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"鍛造廠\"  ],  [    \"熔爐\"  ]]","chEntries":["鍛造廠","熔爐"],"practiceMeaning":"他在鍛造廠學到了金屬加工的技藝。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 forge，是動詞 forge「鍛造」的名詞化，最終源自拉丁語 fabrica「工廠、製造、工藝」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作為名詞，其核心語義是指「用於鍛造金屬的工廠或設備」。此義項由動詞「鍛造」延伸出動作發生的場所。","definition":"1. a furnace or fire for heating metal; 2. a workshop where metal is forged.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The blacksmith worked in his forge.\",\n    \"ch\": \"鐵匠在他的鍛造廠裡工作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The intense heat of the forge was palpable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"鍛造爐的熾熱讓人觸手可及。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He learned the art of metalworking in the forge.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在鍛造廠學到了金屬加工的技藝。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他在鍛造廠學到了金屬加工的技藝。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6173,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::forum::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It's an open ____ for all members to express their views.","expectedAnswer":"forum","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It's an open ____ for all members to express their views.","clozeAnswer":"forum","exampleTranslation":"這是個讓所有成員表達意見的公開論壇。","reference":{"eng":"forum","kk":"ˈfɔrəm","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"論壇\"  ],  [    \"討論會\"  ],  [    \"廣場\"  ],  [    \"（辯論、討論的）場所\"  ]]","chEntries":["論壇","討論會","廣場","場所"],"practiceMeaning":"這是個讓所有成員表達意見的公開論壇。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 forum，意為「公共場所、市場、廣場」。在古羅馬，它是舉行公共集會、辯論和商業活動的中心。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作為名詞，其核心語義是「一個用於公開討論、辯論或交流意見的場所或場合」。此義項由古羅馬時期的「公共廣場」引申出「討論會」和「論壇」的現代用法。","definition":"1. a place, meeting, or medium where ideas and views on a particular issue can be exchanged; 2. a public meeting or lecture, typically held in a university or college, at which invited speakers debate a topic of current interest.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The internet forum is a popular place for discussion.\",\n    \"ch\": \"網路論壇是一個受歡迎的討論場所。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The forum will focus on environmental issues.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這次討論會將聚焦於環境議題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's an open forum for all members to express their views.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是個讓所有成員表達意見的公開論壇。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They held a town hall forum on public safety.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們就公共安全問題舉行了市政廳論壇。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是個讓所有成員表達意見的公開論壇。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5085,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::foul::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The weather turned ____ during the night.","expectedAnswer":"foul","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The weather turned ____ during the night.","clozeAnswer":"foul","exampleTranslation":"夜裡天氣變得惡劣。","reference":{"eng":"foul","kk":"faʊl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['骯髒的'], ['污穢的'], ['惡劣的']]","chEntries":["骯髒的","污穢的","惡劣的"],"practiceMeaning":"夜裡天氣變得惡劣。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 'fūl'，與德語 'faul' (rotten) 同源，原始語義為 '腐爛的、惡臭的'。其核心概念是 '不乾淨、不道德或令人不悅的'。這可以指物理上的汙穢，如 'foul water' (髒水)；也可以指道德上的卑劣，如 'foul play' (不正當的手段)；或者指天氣的惡劣，如 'foul weather' (惡劣天氣)。","definition":"1. Very dirty; polluted.; 2. Extremely unpleasant or disagreeable.; 3. (In sports) Against the rules; unfair.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He had to clean the foul smell from his room.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他不得不清除房間裡的惡臭。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The referee called a foul for rough play.\",\n    \"ch\": \"裁判因粗野的犯規判罰了一個犯規。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The weather turned foul during the night.\",\n    \"ch\": \"夜裡天氣變得惡劣。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"夜裡天氣變得惡劣。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4610,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::gap::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need to bridge the ____ between the rich and the poor.","expectedAnswer":"gap","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need to bridge the ____ between the rich and the poor.","clozeAnswer":"gap","exampleTranslation":"我們需要縮小貧富之間的差距。","reference":{"eng":"gap","kk":"/ɡæp/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['裂縫'], ['間隙'], ['差距 (意見、年齡、收入等)'], ['缺口']]","chEntries":["裂縫","間隙","差距","缺口"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要縮小貧富之間的差距。","analysis":"源自古挪威語 'gap'，意為「開口、裂縫」。核心概念是兩個事物之間存在的空間或差異。可以是物理上的空間（裂縫、間隙），也可以是抽象的差異（意見、知識、社會經濟地位上的差距）。","definition":"a break or hole in an object or between two things; a difference between two things, especially amounts or qualities.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There is a small gap in the fence.\",\n    \"ch\": \"籬笆上有個小裂縫。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The generation gap is a common issue in families.\",\n    \"ch\": \"世代差距是家庭中常見的問題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to bridge the gap between the rich and the poor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要縮小貧富之間的差距。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要縮小貧富之間的差距。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U16、L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4045,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::governor::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of the central bank announced new policies.","expectedAnswer":"governor","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of the central bank announced new policies.","clozeAnswer":"governor","exampleTranslation":"中央銀行行長宣布了新政策。","reference":{"eng":"governor","kk":"/ˈɡʌvərnər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['州長', '總督'], ['主管', '管理者']]","chEntries":["州長","總督","主管","管理者"],"practiceMeaning":"中央銀行行長宣布了新政策。","analysis":"源自古法語 'governour'，來自拉丁語 'gubernator'，意為「舵手」、「領航員」，進而引申為「管理者」、「統治者」。'gubernator' 本身來自希臘語 'kybernetes' (steersman, governor)。核心是「控制」和「引導」方向。因此，指負責管理或統治一個地區或機構的官員。","definition":"1. the elected head of a U.S. state; 2. a person appointed to govern a colony or province; 3. a person who is in charge of an organization or a part of it","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"州長簽署了新法案，使其成為法律。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The governor signed the new bill into law.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他被任命為新地區的總督。\",\n    \"eng\": \"He was appointed governor of the new territory.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"中央銀行行長宣布了新政策。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The governor of the central bank announced new policies.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"中央銀行行長宣布了新政策。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3160,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::graph::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The bar ____ clearly illustrates the comparison between the two groups.","expectedAnswer":"graph","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The bar ____ clearly illustrates the comparison between the two groups.","clozeAnswer":"graph","exampleTranslation":"長條圖清晰地展示了兩組之間的比較。","reference":{"eng":"graph","kk":"/ɡræf/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['圖；圖表； graf']]","chEntries":["圖","圖表","graf"],"practiceMeaning":"長條圖清晰地展示了兩組之間的比較。","analysis":"源自希臘語 'graphein'，意為「書寫，繪製」。'Graph' 是一種用線條、點或其他符號在平面上表示數據、關係或統計結果的視覺工具。它幫助我們理解數據的趨勢、比較不同的數值或展示變數之間的關係。常見的有折線圖、長條圖、圓形圖等。","definition":"a diagram showing the relation between two or more variables, typically of the form of a curve or a series of points lying on a grid.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The graph shows a steady increase in sales over the past year.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這張圖表顯示了過去一年銷售額的穩定增長。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please plot the data points on the graph.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請將數據點繪製在這張圖上。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The bar graph clearly illustrates the comparison between the two groups.\",\n    \"ch\": \"長條圖清晰地展示了兩組之間的比較。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"長條圖清晰地展示了兩組之間的比較。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5786,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::grip::vt","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The government tried to ____ the economy tighter.","expectedAnswer":"grip","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The government tried to ____ the economy tighter.","clozeAnswer":"grip","exampleTranslation":"政府試圖更嚴格地控制經濟。","reference":{"eng":"grip","kk":"ɡrɪp","tense":"vt.","ch":"[  [    \"緊握\"  ],  [    \"抓牢\"  ],  [    \"控制\"  ],  [    \"吸引（注意力、興趣）\"  ]]","chEntries":["緊握","抓牢","控制","吸引"],"practiceMeaning":"政府試圖更嚴格地控制經濟。","analysis":"此字為及物動詞，源自中古英語gripen，可能與古英語grīpan（抓住）有關，後者源自原始日耳曼語\\\\*grīpanan。核心語義是用手用力抓住或握緊。語意演變上，從具體的「用手抓住」，引申為「控制」、「掌握」，以及「吸引」人的注意力或興趣，使人專注。此字並無明顯的字首、字根或字尾可透明拆解。","definition":"1. to take and hold something firmly; 2. to have a strong effect on someone or something, controlling their feelings or behaviour; 3. to keep someone's attention or interest.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She gripped the steering wheel tightly as she drove.\",\n    \"ch\": \"開車時，她緊緊地握著方向盤。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The story gripped the audience from beginning to end.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個故事從頭到尾都緊緊抓住了觀眾的注意力。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government tried to grip the economy tighter.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府試圖更嚴格地控制經濟。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"政府試圖更嚴格地控制經濟。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5127,"wordRef":"字彙王::u62::gross::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The smell was absolutely ____.","expectedAnswer":"gross","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The smell was absolutely ____.","clozeAnswer":"gross","exampleTranslation":"這氣味真是太噁心了。","reference":{"eng":"gross","kk":"ɡroʊs","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['總的'], ['毛的'], ['嚴重的'], ['令人噁心的']]","chEntries":["總的","毛的","嚴重的","令人噁心的"],"practiceMeaning":"這氣味真是太噁心了。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 gros，意為「大、肥胖、總的」，來自拉丁語 grossus（粗大的）。核心語意是「大的、不精細的」。引申出「總收入」（毛收入，gross income）、「總重量」（毛重，gross weight）等含義。在另一語義發展線上，gross 也引申為「極端的、嚴重的」（gross negligence）以及「令人噁心的、非常討厭的」（gross behavior）。","definition":"without any deductions; total; extremely unpleasant or disgusting; very bad or serious.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company reported a gross profit of $1 million.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司報告了 100 萬美元的毛利。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His gross lack of manners was offensive.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他極其粗魯的無禮行為令人反感。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The smell was absolutely gross.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這氣味真是太噁心了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這氣味真是太噁心了。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U62"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5479,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::harmony::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need to find a way to live in ____ with nature.","expectedAnswer":"harmony","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need to find a way to live in ____ with nature.","clozeAnswer":"harmony","exampleTranslation":"我們需要找到一種與大自然和諧共處的方式。","reference":{"eng":"harmony","kk":"ˈhɑrməni","tense":"n.","ch":"[['和諧'], ['融洽'], ['和聲']]","chEntries":["和諧","融洽","和聲"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要找到一種與大自然和諧共處的方式。","analysis":"此字源自希臘語 'harmonia'（結合、協調、和聲），後來經由拉丁語 'harmonia' 傳入古英語 'harmoie'，再到中古英語 'harmony'。'Harmonia' 本身來自 'harmos'（連接、鎖扣）。在音樂上，它指「不同音高並存時產生的悅耳聲音」。在社會和人際關係上，它引申為「各方之間協調、融洽、沒有衝突的狀態」。核心語意是「各部分組合在一起時產生的協調與一致」。","definition":"1. The quality of forming a pleasing and consistent whole.; 2. Agreement or concord; peaceful relations.; 3. (Music) The combination of notes played or sung simultaneously to produce a pleasing effect.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The two nations lived in harmony for many years.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這兩個國家和諧相處了許多年。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The choir sang in perfect harmony.\",\n    \"ch\": \"合唱團以完美的和聲演唱。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to find a way to live in harmony with nature.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要找到一種與大自然和諧共處的方式。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要找到一種與大自然和諧共處的方式。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5788,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::hence::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This is the main reason; ____, we must act now.","expectedAnswer":"hence","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This is the main reason; ____, we must act now.","clozeAnswer":"hence","exampleTranslation":"這是主要原因；因此，我們必須現在採取行動。","reference":{"eng":"hence","kk":"hɛns","tense":"adv.","ch":"[  [    \"因此\"  ],  [    \"由此\"  ],  [    \"所以\"  ]]","chEntries":["因此","由此","所以"],"practiceMeaning":"這是主要原因；因此，我們必須現在採取行動。","analysis":"此字為副詞，源自古英語hider+efnes，意為「在此處+如同」，後演變為「由此；因此」。其詞源可追溯至原始日耳曼語\\\\*hithran（這裡）+ \\\\*efn-（相等）。它是一個連接詞，用於引出結果或推論。核心語義是用來連接原因與結果，表明後者是前者的必然結果。語意演變上，從「因此處」或「由這點」引申為「基於此原因」。","definition":"1. used to introduce the result of something that has been mentioned; 2. from this time; from now.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The weather forecast predicted rain, hence the event was cancelled.\",\n    \"ch\": \"天氣預報預測有雨，因此活動被取消了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He broke his leg, hence he cannot attend the game.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他摔斷了腿，所以他不能參加比賽。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is the main reason; hence, we must act now.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是主要原因；因此，我們必須現在採取行動。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是主要原因；因此，我們必須現在採取行動。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4120,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::honor::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He always keeps his ____.","expectedAnswer":"honor","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He always keeps his ____.","clozeAnswer":"honor","exampleTranslation":"他始終信守承諾。","reference":{"eng":"honor","kk":"/ˈɑːnər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['榮譽', '光榮'], ['尊敬', '敬意'], ['（尤指女性的）貞節', '名節'], ['（債務的）償還', '履約']]","chEntries":["榮譽","光榮","尊敬","敬意","貞節","名節","償還","履約"],"practiceMeaning":"他始終信守承諾。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 honor（尊敬、名譽）。核心概念是「價值」、「尊嚴」或「受到的高度評價」。引申為社會認可的榮譽、對個人的尊敬、個人品德的貞潔，以及對承諾的履行。","definition":"1. high respect; esteem; 2. privilege; 3. a thing conferred as a mark of respect; an award; 4. good reputation and integrity; 5. the fulfillment of an obligation","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Winning the award brought him great honor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"贏得這個獎項給他帶來了極大的榮譽。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has been honored for her contributions to science.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她因對科學的貢獻而受到表彰。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He always keeps his honor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他始終信守承諾。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The bank will honor the check.\",\n    \"ch\": \"銀行將兌現這張支票。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他始終信守承諾。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3949,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::hopeful::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They are ____ that a solution can be found.","expectedAnswer":"hopeful","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They are ____ that a solution can be found.","clozeAnswer":"hopeful","exampleTranslation":"他們對找到解決方案抱有希望。","reference":{"eng":"hopeful","kk":"/ˈhəʊpfəl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['抱有希望的', '有希望的'], ['充滿希望的']]","chEntries":["抱有希望的","有希望的","充滿希望的"],"practiceMeaning":"他們對找到解決方案抱有希望。","analysis":"由 'hope' (名詞/動詞，希望) 和 '-ful' (形容詞後綴) 組成。指對未來抱有樂觀的期望，或表示有成功的可能。","definition":"1. feeling or inspiring optimism about a future event; 2. having or characterized by hope.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is hopeful about her job prospects.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對自己的工作前景感到樂觀。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's a hopeful sign for the economy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是經濟的一個好兆頭。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They are hopeful that a solution can be found.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們對找到解決方案抱有希望。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們對找到解決方案抱有希望。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6123,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::hypothesis::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This is just a ____, not a proven fact.","expectedAnswer":"hypothesis","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This is just a ____, not a proven fact.","clozeAnswer":"hypothesis","exampleTranslation":"這只是一個假設，不是已證實的事實。","reference":{"eng":"hypothesis","kk":"haɪˈpɑːθəsɪs","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"假設\"  ],  [    \"假說\"  ],  [    \"設想\"  ]]","chEntries":["假設","假說","設想"],"practiceMeaning":"這只是一個假設，不是已證實的事實。","analysis":"此字源自希臘語 hypothesis，由 hypo-（在……下面；次要的）和 thesis（放置；論點；主張）組成。hypo- 意為「在下面」，thesis 意為「放置；主張」。因此，hypothesis 的核心語義是「放在……下面做基礎的主張」，即一個初步的、待驗證的解釋或主張。此名詞常用於科學研究，指對現象的初步解釋，有待實驗驗證。其語意演變是從「放在下面」到「作為基礎的論點」。","definition":"A supposition or proposed explanation made on the basis of limited evidence as a starting point for further investigation.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We formed a hypothesis about the cause of the disease.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們對疾病的成因提出了一個假設。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The scientist tested the hypothesis through experiments.\",\n    \"ch\": \"科學家通過實驗來驗證這個假說。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is just a hypothesis, not a proven fact.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這只是一個假設，不是已證實的事實。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這只是一個假設，不是已證實的事實。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4512,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::idea::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of democracy spread rapidly.","expectedAnswer":"idea","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of democracy spread rapidly.","clozeAnswer":"idea","exampleTranslation":"民主的概念迅速傳播。","reference":{"eng":"idea","kk":"/aɪˈdiːə/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['主意'], ['想法'], ['概念']]","chEntries":["主意","想法","概念"],"practiceMeaning":"民主的概念迅速傳播。","analysis":"源自希臘語 idea，意為「形狀」、「外觀」、「理念」。核心語意是「心智中產生的概念或圖像」。引申為「想法」、「概念」、「意圖」。","definition":"1. A thought or suggestion as to a possible course of action; 2. A conception of or belief about something; 3. A plan or suggestion.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"That's a great idea!\",\n    \"ch\": \"這真是個好主意！\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I have no idea what you are talking about.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我完全不知道你在說什麼。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The idea of democracy spread rapidly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"民主的概念迅速傳播。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"民主的概念迅速傳播。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5418,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::identity::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Cultural ____ plays a big role in shaping our values.","expectedAnswer":"identity","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Cultural ____ plays a big role in shaping our values.","clozeAnswer":"identity","exampleTranslation":"文化認同在塑造我們的價值觀方面扮演著重要角色。","reference":{"eng":"identity","kk":"aɪˈdentəti","tense":"n.","ch":"[['身份'], ['身分'], ['認同'], ['特性'], ['同一性']]","chEntries":["身份","身分","認同","特性","同一性"],"practiceMeaning":"文化認同在塑造我們的價值觀方面扮演著重要角色。","analysis":"此字由形容詞 \"identical\" 加上名詞化字尾 \"-ity\" 構成。\"identical\" 源自拉丁語 \"identicus\"，其詞源為 \"idem\"，意為\"相同\"。構詞上，\"ident-\" 提供了核心的\"相同\"或\"同一\"語意，\"-ical\" 是形容詞字尾，將「相同」的概念描述為一種屬性。而字尾 \"-ity\" 則將形容詞的「相同性」或「同一性」轉化為抽象名詞，形成 \"identity\"。因此，\"identity\" 首先表示「同一性」，即事物是其本身且與其他事物不同；進而引申為「身份」或「身分」，指一個人或物之所以是其自身、其獨特性；也引申為「認同」，即與某人、某群體或某物產生連結感和歸屬感。","definition":"the fact of being who or what a person or thing is; the characteristics and qualities that form who a person is and make them different from others; the state of being the same; the condition of being oneself and not someone else; a sense of self; sameness.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He struggled to find his identity after the accident.\",\n    \"ch\": \"事故後他努力尋找自己的身份認同。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The passport confirms the traveler's identity.\",\n    \"ch\": \"護照證實了旅客的身份。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Cultural identity plays a big role in shaping our values.\",\n    \"ch\": \"文化認同在塑造我們的價值觀方面扮演著重要角色。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"文化認同在塑造我們的價值觀方面扮演著重要角色。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5503,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::in-the-same-boat::idiom","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"With the company facing bankruptcy, all the employees are ____.","expectedAnswer":"in the same boat","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"With the company facing bankruptcy, all the employees are ____.","clozeAnswer":"in the same boat","exampleTranslation":"隨著公司面臨破產，所有員工都處境相同。","reference":{"eng":"in the same boat","kk":"ɪn ðə seɪm boʊt","tense":"idiom","ch":"[['處境相同'], ['同舟共濟'], ['處於同樣的困境']]","chEntries":["處境相同","同舟共濟","處於同樣的困境"],"practiceMeaning":"隨著公司面臨破產，所有員工都處境相同。","analysis":"這個片語字面意思是「在同一條船上」。'In the same boat' 表示「與他人共享相同的處境、情況或命運」。如果一群人都在同一條船上，那麼他們面臨的危險、挑戰或經歷都是相同的。這個片語常用來描述「大家都在同一種困難或不利的處境中」。核心語意是「共享相同的處境」。","definition":"1. In the same difficult or unpleasant situation as someone else.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We're all in the same boat when it comes to saving money.\",\n    \"ch\": \"在省錢這件事上，我們都處境相同。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Don't worry, you're not alone; we're all in the same boat.\",\n    \"ch\": \"別擔心，你不是一個人；我們都處境相同。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"With the company facing bankruptcy, all the employees are in the same boat.\",\n    \"ch\": \"隨著公司面臨破產，所有員工都處境相同。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"隨著公司面臨破產，所有員工都處境相同。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5461,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::indigenous::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company uses ____ materials in its products.","expectedAnswer":"indigenous","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company uses ____ materials in its products.","clozeAnswer":"indigenous","exampleTranslation":"該公司在其產品中使用當地材料。","reference":{"eng":"indigenous","kk":"ɪnˈdɪdʒənəs","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['原住民的'], ['本地的'], ['土生土長的']]","chEntries":["原住民的","本地的","土生土長的"],"practiceMeaning":"該公司在其產品中使用當地材料。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'indigena'，意為「土著、原住民」。'Indigena' 是由 'indi-'（在此處作強調，可能與 'in'「在……裡面」有關）和 'gen-'（出生、產生，來自 'gignere'「產生」）組合而成，直譯為「從內部出生」，引申為「當地出生、本地的、原生的」。'-ous' 是拉丁語 '-osus' 的英語化形式，用於構成形容詞，表示「充滿……的」。因此，'indigenous' 指的是「屬於某地方、某國家或某特定地區的，從該地方發源或產生的」，特別常用來指「原住民」或「當地特有」的動植物、文化等。","definition":"1. Originating or occurring naturally in a particular place; native.; 2. Relating to or characteristic of a particular region or people.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The indigenous people of Australia have a rich cultural heritage.\",\n    \"ch\": \"澳大利亞的原住民擁有豐富的文化遺產。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Eucalyptus is indigenous to Australia.\",\n    \"ch\": \"桉樹是澳大利亞的原生植物。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company uses indigenous materials in its products.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司在其產品中使用當地材料。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該公司在其產品中使用當地材料。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4056,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::information::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He gave me some useful ____.","expectedAnswer":"information","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He gave me some useful ____.","clozeAnswer":"information","exampleTranslation":"他給我了一些有用的消息。","reference":{"eng":"information","kk":"/ˌɪnfərˈmeɪʃən/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['資訊', '情報'], ['消息']]","chEntries":["資訊","情報","消息"],"practiceMeaning":"他給我了一些有用的消息。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'informatio'，由 'informare' (to inform) 構成。核心是「被告知」、「被形成的知識」。因此，'information' 指 facts provided or learned about something or someone; knowledge.","definition":"1. facts provided or learned about something or someone; 2. knowledge or facts obtained about something or someone","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"請提供我們更多資訊。\",\n    \"eng\": \"Please provide us with more information.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"這是對調查很重要的情報。\",\n    \"eng\": \"This is important information for the investigation.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他給我了一些有用的消息。\",\n    \"eng\": \"He gave me some useful information.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他給我了一些有用的消息。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4、C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6229,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::infrastructure::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The internet is an essential part of modern ____.","expectedAnswer":"infrastructure","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The internet is an essential part of modern ____.","clozeAnswer":"infrastructure","exampleTranslation":"網際網路是現代基礎設施的重要組成部分。","reference":{"eng":"infrastructure","kk":"ˈɪnfrəˌstrʌktʃər","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"基礎設施\"  ],  [    \"基礎建設\"  ],  [    \"結構\"  ]]","chEntries":["基礎設施","基礎建設","結構"],"practiceMeaning":"網際網路是現代基礎設施的重要組成部分。","analysis":"此字為複合詞，由 infra-（在…之下）和 structure（結構）構成。infra- 源自拉丁語，意為「下面」。structure 源自拉丁語 structura，意為「建造，構築」。此字在現代英語中可視為由 infra- 和 structure 組合而成。名詞義指支撐一個社會或組織運作的基本設施和系統，包括交通、通訊、能源、公共工程、社會服務等。中文翻譯為「基礎設施；基礎建設；結構」。","definition":"1. the basic physical and organizational structures and facilities (e.g. buildings, roads, power supplies) that a country or organization needs to operate; 2. the basic framework or structure of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government plans to invest heavily in infrastructure.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府計劃大力投資基礎設施。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Poor infrastructure can hinder economic development.\",\n    \"ch\": \"薄弱的基礎建設會阻礙經濟發展。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The internet is an essential part of modern infrastructure.\",\n    \"ch\": \"網際網路是現代基礎設施的重要組成部分。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"網際網路是現代基礎設施的重要組成部分。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6230,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::inherent::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Courage is an ____ quality of a leader.","expectedAnswer":"inherent","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Courage is an ____ quality of a leader.","clozeAnswer":"inherent","exampleTranslation":"勇氣是領導者與生俱來的品質。","reference":{"eng":"inherent","kk":"ɪnˈhɪərənt","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"內在的\"  ],  [    \"固有的\"  ],  [    \"與生俱來的\"  ],  [    \"本質的\"  ]]","chEntries":["內在的","固有的","與生俱來的","本質的"],"practiceMeaning":"勇氣是領導者與生俱來的品質。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 inhærens，是 inhærere（附著在…上）的現在分詞。由 in-（在…裡面）和 hærebere（附著）組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作形容詞時，指某事物與生俱來、屬於其本質的一部分，不可分割。中文翻譯為「內在的；固有的；與生俱來的；本質的」。","definition":"existing in something as a permanent, essential, or characteristic attribute.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There are inherent risks in every investment.\",\n    \"ch\": \"每項投資都存在內在的風險。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The beauty of the natural landscape is inherent.\",\n    \"ch\": \"自然景觀的美是固有的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Courage is an inherent quality of a leader.\",\n    \"ch\": \"勇氣是領導者與生俱來的品質。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"勇氣是領導者與生俱來的品質。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3901,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::jealous::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Be careful, he's ____ of anyone who tries to get close to his wife.","expectedAnswer":"jealous","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Be careful, he's ____ of anyone who tries to get close to his wife.","clozeAnswer":"jealous","exampleTranslation":"小心點，他嫉妒任何試圖接近他妻子的人。","reference":{"eng":"jealous","kk":"/ˈdʒɛləs/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['嫉妒的'], ['羨慕的'], ['提防的']]","chEntries":["嫉妒的","羨慕的","提防的"],"practiceMeaning":"小心點，他嫉妒任何試圖接近他妻子的人。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'zelus'，'zelotypus' (zealous)，意為「熱情的」。其詞源演變較為複雜，但現代意義主要指因擔心失去所愛或所擁有的東西，或因他人擁有自己所沒有的而產生的不滿、敵意或不安。也可指對某事物極為小心、防護的。","definition":"1. feeling or showing envy of someone or their achievements and advantages. 2. feeling or showing suspicion of someone's unfaithfulness to you. 3. fiercely protective or suspicious of (someone or something).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was jealous of his brother's success.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他嫉妒他哥哥的成功。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She felt jealous when her friend got the promotion.\",\n    \"ch\": \"當她的朋友獲得晉升時，她感到嫉妒。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Be careful, he's jealous of anyone who tries to get close to his wife.\",\n    \"ch\": \"小心點，他嫉妒任何試圖接近他妻子的人。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"小心點，他嫉妒任何試圖接近他妻子的人。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3147,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::lively::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She has a ____ personality and is always smiling.","expectedAnswer":"lively","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She has a ____ personality and is always smiling.","clozeAnswer":"lively","exampleTranslation":"她個性活潑，總是面帶笑容。","reference":{"eng":"lively","kk":"/ˈlaɪvlɪ/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['活潑的；生氣勃勃的'], ['（討論、場景等）熱烈的；活躍的'], ['（顏色）鮮豔的；（氣味）濃郁的']]","chEntries":["活潑的","生氣勃勃的","熱烈的","活躍的","鮮豔的","濃郁的"],"practiceMeaning":"她個性活潑，總是面帶笑容。","analysis":"源自古英語 'liflic'，與 'life'（生命）有關。'Lively' 描述的是充滿生命力、活力和興奮的狀態。它可以用來形容人（活潑、精力充沛）、地方（熱鬧、充滿生氣）、活動（熱烈、引人入勝）或事物（鮮豔、濃郁）。'Lively' 的核心概念是「充滿生命力」和「活躍」。","definition":"1. (of a person or their manner) full of energy and enthusiasm; animated; 2. (of a place or event) bustling with activity and excitement; 3. (of a colour or smell) bright and pleasant.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The children were playing a lively game of tag.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子們正在玩一場熱鬧的捉迷藏遊戲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The conversation became quite lively after a few drinks.\",\n    \"ch\": \"喝了幾杯酒後，談話變得相當熱烈。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a lively personality and is always smiling.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她個性活潑，總是面帶笑容。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她個性活潑，總是面帶笑容。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5570,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::load::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The system is taking a long time to ____ the new software.","expectedAnswer":"load","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The system is taking a long time to ____ the new software.","clozeAnswer":"load","exampleTranslation":"這個系統載入新軟體花費了很長時間。","reference":{"eng":"load","kk":"loʊd","tense":"v.","ch":"[['裝載'], ['加載'], ['負荷']]","chEntries":["裝載","加載","負荷"],"practiceMeaning":"這個系統載入新軟體花費了很長時間。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 \"lādan\"，意為 \"to carry, convey, conduct\"（攜帶，運送，引導），最終可能源自原始印歐語 \\*leith-（to go, to travel，去，旅行）。\"lādan\" 的引申義是指「承載、運送」。 \"load\" 作動詞，核心語義是「將某物裝入容器、車輛或系統，使其承擔重量或資訊」。在物理上，指「裝載貨物」；在計算機領域，指「將數據或程式載入記憶體」（load a program）；在數學或工程學上，指「施加負荷」或「承受重量」。","definition":"1. To put a load onto or into; 2. To fill (a vehicle, ship, aircraft, etc.) with goods or passengers; 3. To load data or programs into a computer's memory; 4. To put a heavy burden on.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The truck was loaded with goods.\",\n    \"ch\": \"卡車裝滿了貨物。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please load the dishwasher.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請把洗碗機裝滿。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The system is taking a long time to load the new software.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個系統載入新軟體花費了很長時間。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He felt loaded with responsibility.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他感覺責任重大。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個系統載入新軟體花費了很長時間。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3946,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::magical::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The view from the top of the mountain was ____.","expectedAnswer":"magical","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The view from the top of the mountain was ____.","clozeAnswer":"magical","exampleTranslation":"山頂的景色令人迷醉。","reference":{"eng":"magical","kk":"/ˈmædʒɪkl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['魔法的', '神奇的'], ['迷人的']]","chEntries":["魔法的","神奇的","迷人的"],"practiceMeaning":"山頂的景色令人迷醉。","analysis":"源自 'magic' (名詞，魔法) 加上形容詞後綴 '-al'。指與魔法相關的，或像魔法一樣的，引申為「神奇的、迷人的」。","definition":"1. relating to or resembling magic; 2. having or using the power to produce supernatural effects; 3. very pleasant or attractive.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The story had a magical quality.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個故事有一種神奇的特質。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She performed a magical trick.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她表演了一個魔術把戲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The view from the top of the mountain was magical.\",\n    \"ch\": \"山頂的景色令人迷醉。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"山頂的景色令人迷醉。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3113,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::maintain::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They struggled to ____ their large family.","expectedAnswer":"maintain","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They struggled to ____ their large family.","clozeAnswer":"maintain","exampleTranslation":"他們努力維持著大家庭的生活。","reference":{"eng":"maintain","kk":"/meɪnˈteɪn/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['維持；保持'], ['堅持（觀點）；認為'], ['供給；供養'], ['維修；保養']]","chEntries":["維持","保持","堅持","認為","供給","供養","維修","保養"],"practiceMeaning":"他們努力維持著大家庭的生活。","analysis":"源自古法語 'maintenir'，'main-' (hand) + 'tenir' (to hold)。核心意義是「用手拿著」。\n1. 維持；保持：指使事物處於某種狀態，不使其衰退或改變。\n2. 堅持（觀點）；認為：指不斷主張或信奉某種信念或看法。\n3. 供給；供養：指提供生活所需，支持某人或某物。\n4. 維修；保養：指對設備、建築物等進行必要的修繕和保養，使其正常運作。","definition":"1. to keep something in good condition; 2. to continue to have something; 3. to say something strongly and believe it to be true; 4. to provide someone with the money that they need to live.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It is important to maintain a healthy diet.\",\n    \"ch\": \"保持健康的飲食很重要。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He maintained that he was innocent.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他堅持認為自己是無辜的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They struggled to maintain their large family.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們努力維持著大家庭的生活。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The mechanic will maintain the car regularly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"機械師會定期保養汽車。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們努力維持著大家庭的生活。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4640,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::means::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Calculate the arithmetic ____ of the two sets of data.","expectedAnswer":"means","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Calculate the arithmetic ____ of the two sets of data.","clozeAnswer":"means","exampleTranslation":"計算這兩組數據的算術平均數。","reference":{"eng":"means","kk":"/miːnz/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['方法'], ['手段'], ['財富'], ['（數）平均數']]","chEntries":["方法","手段","財富","平均數"],"practiceMeaning":"計算這兩組數據的算術平均數。","analysis":"源自古英語 'mæġen' (力量、能力)。最初指達成目的的手段或力量。現代用法非常廣泛，可以指到達某個結果的方式（方法、手段），也可以指財富（especially plural \"means\"），在數學中則指平均值。","definition":"a method, course of action, or instrument by which something can be achieved; wealth or financial resources; the average of a set of numbers.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"What is the best means to achieve this goal?\",\n    \"ch\": \"達到這個目標的最佳方法是什麼？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He lives comfortably on his means.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他依靠自己的財富過著舒適的生活。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Calculate the arithmetic means of the two sets of data.\",\n    \"ch\": \"計算這兩組數據的算術平均數。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"計算這兩組數據的算術平均數。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4204,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::mend::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The two countries are trying to ____ their relations.","expectedAnswer":"mend","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The two countries are trying to ____ their relations.","clozeAnswer":"mend","exampleTranslation":"這兩個國家正試圖修復它們的關係。","reference":{"eng":"mend","kk":"/mend/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['修補；縫補'], ['（使）恢復；（使）好轉']]","chEntries":["修補","縫補","恢復","好轉"],"practiceMeaning":"這兩個國家正試圖修復它們的關係。","analysis":"源自古英語 mendan，意為“改善，加強”，後來與法語 demente（破壞）的反義詞 'amender'（改正）混合。核心是“修復，使其回到更好的狀態”。1. “修補”指恢復物體的完整性。2. “恢復；好轉”指恢復健康、關係或狀況。","definition":"1. to repair something that is broken or damaged; 2. to get better or to make something better after a problem or illness.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Can you mend this torn shirt?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你能把這件破了的襯衫補好嗎？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is recovering and will soon mend.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他正在康復，很快就會好起來。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The two countries are trying to mend their relations.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這兩個國家正試圖修復它們的關係。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這兩個國家正試圖修復它們的關係。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6128,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::metropolitan::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ opera","expectedAnswer":"metropolitan","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ opera","clozeAnswer":"metropolitan","exampleTranslation":"大都會歌劇院","reference":{"eng":"metropolitan","kk":"ˌmɛtrəˈpɑːlɪtən","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"都會的\"  ],  [    \"大都會的\"  ],  [    \"首府的\"  ]]","chEntries":["都會的","大都會的","首府的"],"practiceMeaning":"大都會歌劇院","analysis":"此字源自希臘語 mētropolis，由 mētēr（母親）和 polis（城市）組成，意為「母城」，指一個地區的中心城市或首府。構詞上，mētēr 意為「母親」，polis 意為「城市」。因此，metropolitan 的核心語義是「與大城市相關」。此形容詞指與大都市、其區域或居民相關的。其語意演變是從「母城」到「大城市」。","definition":"1. relating to or denoting a metropolis or its inhabitants; 2. the capital or chief city of a country or region.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"metropolitan area\",\n    \"ch\": \"都會區\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The city has a large metropolitan population.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座城市擁有龐大的都會人口。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"metropolitan opera\",\n    \"ch\": \"大都會歌劇院\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"大都會歌劇院","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6177,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::migration::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Human ____ patterns have changed throughout history.","expectedAnswer":"migration","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Human ____ patterns have changed throughout history.","clozeAnswer":"migration","exampleTranslation":"人類的移民模式在歷史上一直變化。","reference":{"eng":"migration","kk":"maɪˈɡreɪʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"遷徙\"  ],  [    \"移民\"  ]]","chEntries":["遷徙","移民"],"practiceMeaning":"人類的移民模式在歷史上一直變化。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 migratioinem，是動詞 migrare「遷徙、移居」的名詞化。migrare 的詞源不確定，可能與拉丁語 mīgrāre (to move from one place to another) 或拉丁語 magna (great) 有關，但最常見的說法是源自詞根 *mei- (to go, pass)。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作為名詞，其核心語義是由動詞 migrate「遷徙」名詞化而來，指「為了尋找食物、繁殖地或更好的生存條件而從一個地方移動到另一個地方的行為」。此義項由「移動」的動作延伸出「遷徙」的行為與「移民」的結果。","definition":"1. the movement of persons from one country or locality to another; 2. seasonal movement of animals from one region to another.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Bird migration occurs in the spring and fall.\",\n    \"ch\": \"鳥類遷徙發生在春秋兩季。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The region experienced significant migration of people seeking work.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該地區經歷了大量尋找工作的移民。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Human migration patterns have changed throughout history.\",\n    \"ch\": \"人類的移民模式在歷史上一直變化。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The great migration of African Americans from the South to the North was a major demographic shift.\",\n    \"ch\": \"非裔美國人從南方大規模遷往北方的運動是人口結構的重大轉變。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"人類的移民模式在歷史上一直變化。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4183,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::missing::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We noticed something ____ from the collection.","expectedAnswer":"missing","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We noticed something ____ from the collection.","clozeAnswer":"missing","exampleTranslation":"我們注意到收藏品中少了些東西。","reference":{"eng":"missing","kk":"/ˈmɪsɪŋ/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['失蹤的；不見的'], ['缺少的；遺漏的']]","chEntries":["失蹤的","不見的","缺少的","遺漏的"],"practiceMeaning":"我們注意到收藏品中少了些東西。","analysis":"來自動詞 'miss' 的現在分詞，原意為“錯過”。'Missing' 作形容詞時，表示某人或某物不在應在的地方，因此找不到。'Miss' 本身源自古諾爾斯語 missa，意為“缺乏，失去”。引申義是指某物本應存在但卻不存在，例如 'missing piece'（缺少的一塊）。","definition":"1. not present in a place or at a time when you would expect it to be; 2. not found or lost.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police are searching for a missing child.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警方正在尋找一個失蹤的兒童。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There is a missing page in this book.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本書缺了一頁。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We noticed something missing from the collection.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們注意到收藏品中少了些東西。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們注意到收藏品中少了些東西。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3994,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u3::mission::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The UN sent a ____ to the conflict zone.","expectedAnswer":"mission","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The UN sent a ____ to the conflict zone.","clozeAnswer":"mission","exampleTranslation":"聯合國派了一個使團前往衝突地區。","reference":{"eng":"mission","kk":"/ˈmɪʃən/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['任務', '使命'], ['（外交）使團'], ['傳教']]","chEntries":["任務","使命","使團","傳教"],"practiceMeaning":"聯合國派了一個使團前往衝突地區。","analysis":"詞源：拉丁文 'missio' (派遣)，源自 'mittere' (派遣)。指被賦予的重要任務或目標，也指被派遣執行某項任務的團體。","definition":"1. an important assignment given to a person or group of people; 2. a body of people sent to a foreign country to act as representatives; 3. an organisation set up to achieve a particular purpose, especially religious or charitable.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The astronauts completed their mission successfully.\",\n    \"ch\": \"太空人成功完成了他們的任務。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She felt a strong sense of mission to help the poor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她覺得自己有幫助窮人的強烈使命感。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The UN sent a mission to the conflict zone.\",\n    \"ch\": \"聯合國派了一個使團前往衝突地區。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"聯合國派了一個使團前往衝突地區。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U3、L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5090,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::monopoly::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This game is about building a real estate ____.","expectedAnswer":"monopoly","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This game is about building a real estate ____.","clozeAnswer":"monopoly","exampleTranslation":"這個遊戲是關於建立房地產壟斷的。","reference":{"eng":"monopoly","kk":"məˈnɒpəli","tense":"n.","ch":"[['壟斷'], ['獨佔'], ['專賣權']]","chEntries":["壟斷","獨佔","專賣權"],"practiceMeaning":"這個遊戲是關於建立房地產壟斷的。","analysis":"此字源自希臘語 'monos' (single) + 'polein' (to sell)。'Monopoly' 指的是一家公司或個人對某種商品或服務擁有 '獨一無二的銷售權'，不受競爭影響。這意味著他們可以控制價格和供應。引申開來，它也可以指對任何事物（如權力、資源）的 '獨佔' 或 '壟斷' 狀態。","definition":"1. The exclusive possession or control of the supply of or trade in a commodity or service.; 2. A company or group having exclusive control of a commodity or service.; 3. Exclusive possession or control.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company has a monopoly on the production of rare minerals.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司獨佔了稀有礦物的生產。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government is trying to break up the monopoly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府正試圖打破壟斷。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This game is about building a real estate monopoly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個遊戲是關於建立房地產壟斷的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個遊戲是關於建立房地產壟斷的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4181,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::murder::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This decision was a ____ of artistic integrity.","expectedAnswer":"murder","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This decision was a ____ of artistic integrity.","clozeAnswer":"murder","exampleTranslation":"這個決定是對藝術完整性的嚴重破壞。","reference":{"eng":"murder","kk":"/ˈmɜːrdər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['謀殺；兇殺案'], ['（尤指）嚴酷的毀滅']]","chEntries":["謀殺","兇殺案","嚴酷的毀滅"],"practiceMeaning":"這個決定是對藝術完整性的嚴重破壞。","analysis":"源自古英語 morthor，意為“謀殺”。詞源學上與古諾爾斯語 morð、古高地德語 mord 相關，最終可追溯至原始印歐語 *mer-，意為“殺死”。其核心概念是蓄意且非法地奪取生命。引申義則是任何極其殘酷的毀滅或傷害，例如 'murder the landscape'（毀壞景觀）。","definition":"1. the unlawful killing of another human being with malice aforethought; 2. a brutal or violent destruction or damage.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police are investigating a brutal murder.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警方正在調查一起殘酷的謀殺案。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They were accused of committing murder.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們被控犯有謀殺罪。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This decision was a murder of artistic integrity.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個決定是對藝術完整性的嚴重破壞。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個決定是對藝術完整性的嚴重破壞。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U6、L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4116,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::neighborhood::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He's a well-respected member of the ____.","expectedAnswer":"neighborhood","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He's a well-respected member of the ____.","clozeAnswer":"neighborhood","exampleTranslation":"他是社區裡備受尊敬的一員。","reference":{"eng":"neighborhood","kk":"/ˈneɪbərˌhʊd/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['鄰近地區', '社區'], ['鄰居關係', '友好的氣氛']]","chEntries":["鄰近地區","社區","鄰居關係","友好的氣氛"],"practiceMeaning":"他是社區裡備受尊敬的一員。","analysis":"由 neighbor（鄰居）+ -hood（名詞後綴，表示狀態、情況、區域）組成。neighbor 源自古英語 nēah（靠近）+ gebūr（居住者）。核心概念是「居住在附近的人或地方」。","definition":"1. a district or area, especially one forming a community or having a particular characteristic; 2. the people living near one another","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We live in a quiet neighborhood.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們住的社區很寧靜。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The children play in the neighborhood.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子們在鄰近地區玩耍。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He's a well-respected member of the neighborhood.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是社區裡備受尊敬的一員。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他是社區裡備受尊敬的一員。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3931,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::normal::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The patient's temperature returned to ____.","expectedAnswer":"normal","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The patient's temperature returned to ____.","clozeAnswer":"normal","exampleTranslation":"病人的體溫恢復正常。","reference":{"eng":"normal","kk":"/ˈnɔːrməl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['正常的'], ['標準的']]","chEntries":["正常的","標準的"],"practiceMeaning":"病人的體溫恢復正常。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'normalis'，由 'norma' (意為「規則、準則」) 演變而來。指符合標準、規則或常規的。","definition":"1. conforming to a standard; usual, typical, or expected; 2. the average or standard condition.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His behavior is not normal for him.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的行為對他來說很不正常。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It is normal to feel tired after a long day.\",\n    \"ch\": \"長日結束後感到疲倦是正常的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The patient's temperature returned to normal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"病人的體溫恢復正常。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"病人的體溫恢復正常。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3886,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::opportunity::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Don't miss this ____ to learn.","expectedAnswer":"opportunity","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Don't miss this ____ to learn.","clozeAnswer":"opportunity","exampleTranslation":"別錯過這個學習的機會。","reference":{"eng":"opportunity","kk":"/ˌɑːpərˈtuːnəti/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['機會']]","chEntries":["機會"],"practiceMeaning":"別錯過這個學習的機會。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'opportunitas'，'opportunus' (favorable, convenient) 的衍生詞，與 'ob-' (towards) + 'portus' (harbor) 有關，指「靠近港口」，因此是「有利的」。引申為有利的時機或條件，可帶來成功或好處的機會。","definition":"a set of circumstances that makes it possible to do something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a great opportunity for us.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這對我們來說是一個絕佳的機會。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He seized the opportunity to study abroad.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他抓住機會出國留學。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Don't miss this opportunity to learn.\",\n    \"ch\": \"別錯過這個學習的機會。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"別錯過這個學習的機會。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U1、L2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered