全的","偏心的","不公平的","偏愛的","對...有好感的"],"practiceMeaning":"他特別喜歡巧克力冰淇淋。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'partialis'，由 'pars' (部分) 演變而來。指事物只佔一部分，而非整體。引申為對待人或事物的態度不公正、不平衡，或只傾向於一方。","definition":"1. not complete; unfinished; 2. favoring one person or side over another; unfair; 3. having a strong liking for.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The report is only partial; the full version will be released next week.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這份報告只是部分的；完整版將於下週發布。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The judge must be partial in his decisions.\",\n    \"ch\": \"法官在判決時必須公正無私。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is partial to chocolate ice cream.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他特別喜歡巧克力冰淇淋。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他特別喜歡巧克力冰淇淋。","sourceName":"字彙王、龍騰課本","unitName":"U42、L8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3316,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::particular::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She has a ____ dislike for loud music.","expectedAnswer":"particular","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She has a ____ dislike for loud music.","clozeAnswer":"particular","exampleTranslation":"她特別討厭吵鬧的音樂。","reference":{"eng":"particular","kk":"/pərˈtɪkjələr/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['特定的；具體的'], ['特別的；過分的；苛求的'], ['堅持己見的；固執的']]","chEntries":["特定的","具體的","特別的","過分的","苛求的","堅持己見的","固執的"],"practiceMeaning":"她特別討厭吵鬧的音樂。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'particularis'，由 'pars' (部分) 演變而來。指單獨的、特定的、非普遍的。也可用於形容對細節要求嚴格、挑剔，或對某事非常堅持。","definition":"1. used to refer to a specific person or thing rather than to all people or things; 2. very fussy or demanding; 3. having a strong opinion about something and refusing to change it.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Do you have any particular reason for asking?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你問這個有什麼特別的原因嗎？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is very particular about his food.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對食物非常講究。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a particular dislike for loud music.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她特別討厭吵鬧的音樂。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她特別討厭吵鬧的音樂。","sourceName":"字彙王、龍騰課本","unitName":"U42、L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5852,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::patrol::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They established a ____ route around the perimeter.","expectedAnswer":"patrol","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They established a ____ route around the perimeter.","clozeAnswer":"patrol","exampleTranslation":"他們在周邊地區設立了巡邏路線。","reference":{"eng":"patrol","kk":"pəˈtroʊl","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"巡邏\"  ],  [    \"巡邏隊\"  ],  [    \"巡邏路線\"  ],  [    \"守衛\"  ]]","chEntries":["巡邏","巡邏隊","巡邏路線","守衛"],"practiceMeaning":"他們在周邊地區設立了巡邏路線。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 'patrouiller' (to wade through mire, to patrol)，其詞源不確定，可能與拉丁語 'pastor' (shepherd) 或 'pala' (spade) 有關，表示「巡視」、「守衛」的概念。'Patrol' 作名詞時，指由軍隊、警察或安全人員進行的例行性巡視，以維護秩序、偵測威脅或確保安全。它強調的是一種「規律性」、「監視性」的移動或隊伍。例如，也可指「輪值守衛」。","definition":"1. The action of moving around as a guard.; 2. A person or group of people or animals who patrol an area.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police patrol car drove by.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警車巡邏經過。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The night patrol is responsible for security.\",\n    \"ch\": \"夜間巡邏隊負責安全。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They established a patrol route around the perimeter.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們在周邊地區設立了巡邏路線。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The patrol spotted a suspicious vehicle.\",\n    \"ch\": \"巡邏隊發現了一輛可疑車輛。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們在周邊地區設立了巡邏路線。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3944,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::performance::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The car has excellent fuel ____.","expectedAnswer":"performance","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The car has excellent fuel ____.","clozeAnswer":"performance","exampleTranslation":"這輛汽車的燃油性能極佳。","reference":{"eng":"performance","kk":"/pərˈfɔːrməns/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['表演', '演出'], ['表現', '績效'], ['性能']]","chEntries":["表演","演出","表現","績效","性能"],"practiceMeaning":"這輛汽車的燃油性能極佳。","analysis":"源自動詞 'perform' (意為「表演、執行」) 加上名詞後綴 '-ance'。指表演、演出；也指執行某項任務的結果，即「表現」或「績效」；在技術領域則指「性能」。","definition":"1. an act of presenting a play, concert, or other event for an audience; 2. how well or badly someone does a job or task; 3. the action of performing a task or function.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The band's performance was electrifying.\",\n    \"ch\": \"樂團的表演令人振奮。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The student's academic performance has improved.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位學生的學術表現有所提高。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The car has excellent fuel performance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這輛汽車的燃油性能極佳。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這輛汽車的燃油性能極佳。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4577,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::permanent::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We are looking for a ____ job, not a temporary one.","expectedAnswer":"permanent","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We are looking for a ____ job, not a temporary one.","clozeAnswer":"permanent","exampleTranslation":"我們在找一份永久性的工作，而不是臨時的。","reference":{"eng":"permanent","kk":"/ˈpɜːrmənənt/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['永久的', '永恆的'], ['（染髮、烙印等）持久的']]","chEntries":["永久的","永恆的","持久的"],"practiceMeaning":"我們在找一份永久性的工作，而不是臨時的。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'permanere'，'per-' (through) 和 'manere' (to remain - 停留)。核心概念是「持續存在」。\n    1. 永久的、永恆的：指不會改變、消失或結束。\n    2. 持久的：指效果或狀態持續很長時間，不易改變，如 'permanent wave' (永久燙髮)。","definition":"1. lasting or intended to last indefinitely or for a long time.; 2. (of a hair-wave or colour) lasting for a long time.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This decision will have permanent consequences.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個決定將會帶來永久性的後果。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He decided to get a permanent tattoo.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他決定紋一個永久性的刺青。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We are looking for a permanent job, not a temporary one.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們在找一份永久性的工作，而不是臨時的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們在找一份永久性的工作，而不是臨時的。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3912,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::permit::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He finally got a ____ to build a house.","expectedAnswer":"permit","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He finally got a ____ to build a house.","clozeAnswer":"permit","exampleTranslation":"他終於獲得了建造房屋的許可證。","reference":{"eng":"permit","kk":"/pərˈmɪt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['允許', '准許'], ['使可能', '使能夠']]","chEntries":["允許","准許","使可能","使能夠"],"practiceMeaning":"他終於獲得了建造房屋的許可證。","analysis":"來自中古英語 'permyten'，意為「允許、放任」，源自拉丁語 'permittere'，由 'per-' (意為「通過、徹底」) 和 'mittere' (意為「派遣、讓…通過」) 組成。字根 'mittere' 也是 send, mission, admit 等字的來源。語意從「讓事情通過，不加以阻止」延伸到「允許、准許」；另一層語意則強調「使某事能夠發生」，即「使可能」。","definition":"1. to allow an activity or behavior to happen, or allow someone to do something; 2. to make something possible or allow it to happen.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Smoking is not permitted in this building.\",\n    \"ch\": \"在這個建築物內禁止吸煙。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The new technology permits us to work more efficiently.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這項新技術使我們能夠更有效率地工作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He finally got a permit to build a house.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他終於獲得了建造房屋的許可證。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他終於獲得了建造房屋的許可證。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6087,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::petty::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The police investigated a ____ theft.","expectedAnswer":"petty","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The police investigated a ____ theft.","clozeAnswer":"petty","exampleTranslation":"警方調查了一起盜竊案。","reference":{"eng":"petty","kk":"ˈpɛti","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"瑣碎的\"  ],  [    \"小氣的\"  ],  [    \"次要的\"  ],  [    \"輕微的\"  ]]","chEntries":["瑣碎的","小氣的","次要的","輕微的"],"practiceMeaning":"警方調查了一起盜竊案。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 petitement（in a small way），來自 petit（small）。核心語義是「小的」。引申為「瑣碎的」、「不重要的」、「次要的」；或形容人「心胸狹窄」、「小氣」；或形容罪行、傷害「輕微的」。","definition":"1. of little importance; trivial; 2. characterized by or showing a lack of tolerance or generosity; mean-spirited; 3. (of a crime or offense) minor.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Don't argue over such petty details.\",\n    \"ch\": \"不要為了這麼瑣碎的細節爭論。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He's too petty to forgive such a small mistake.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他太小氣了，無法原諒這樣一個小錯誤。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police investigated a petty theft.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警方調查了一起盜竊案。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"警方調查了一起盜竊案。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6088,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::phase::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We are going through a difficult ____.","expectedAnswer":"phase","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We are going through a difficult ____.","clozeAnswer":"phase","exampleTranslation":"我們正經歷一段艱難時期。","reference":{"eng":"phase","kk":"feɪz","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"階段\"  ],  [    \"時期\"  ],  [    \"（月亮、行星的）相位\"  ]]","chEntries":["階段","時期","相位"],"practiceMeaning":"我們正經歷一段艱難時期。","analysis":"此字源自希臘語 phasis（appearance, manifestation, phase），來自 phainō（to appear, to show）。核心語義是「出現」或「顯現」。引申為事物發展過程中的一個「階段」或「時期」。在天文學中，指天體可見部分的變化，即「相位」。","definition":"1. a distinct period or stage in a process of change or forming; 2. each of the shapes of the moon or a planet seen from the earth.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The project is in its final phase.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個項目正處於最後階段。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The moon is in its waxing phase.\",\n    \"ch\": \"月亮處於其上弦階段。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We are going through a difficult phase.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們正經歷一段艱難時期。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們正經歷一段艱難時期。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6134,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::placement::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"children's ____ in foster homes","expectedAnswer":"placement","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"children's ____ in foster homes","clozeAnswer":"placement","exampleTranslation":"兒童被安置在寄養家庭","reference":{"eng":"placement","kk":"ˈpleɪsmənt","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"放置\"  ],  [    \"安插\"  ],  [    \"職位安排\"  ],  [    \"安置\"  ]]","chEntries":["放置","安插","職位安排","安置"],"practiceMeaning":"兒童被安置在寄養家庭","analysis":"此字由動詞 place（放置）加上名詞後綴 -ment（表示動作、狀態或結果）構成。place 源自古法語 plaser，意為「地方」，向上可追溯至拉丁語 platea（廣場；街道）。因此，placement 的核心語義是「放置的行為或結果」。此名詞表示將某物放置在特定位置的動作，或指人被安排到某個職位、場所或情況。其語意演變是從具體的「放置」到抽象的「安排、安置」。","definition":"1. the action, process, or result of placing something or someone in a particular position or situation; 2. the arrangement of something in a particular position.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"the placement of the furniture\",\n    \"ch\": \"家具的擺放\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The school helps with job placement.\",\n    \"ch\": \"學校協助學生安排工作職位。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"children's placement in foster homes\",\n    \"ch\": \"兒童被安置在寄養家庭\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"兒童被安置在寄養家庭","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6186,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::poke::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of the stick startled the animal.","expectedAnswer":"poke","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of the stick startled the animal.","clozeAnswer":"poke","exampleTranslation":"那根棍子的戳弄驚嚇到了動物。","reference":{"eng":"poke","kk":"poʊk","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"戳\"  ],  [    \"捅\"  ]]","chEntries":["戳","捅"],"practiceMeaning":"那根棍子的戳弄驚嚇到了動物。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 pokien，可能是擬聲詞。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作為名詞，是動詞 poke「戳、捅」的名詞化。其核心語義是指「用手指或尖物輕輕觸碰、戳或捅的動作」。","definition":"1. an act of poking someone or something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He gave me a poke in the arm.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他戳了我一下手臂。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A quick poke of his finger was all it took.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他手指輕輕一戳就夠了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The poke of the stick startled the animal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那根棍子的戳弄驚嚇到了動物。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"那根棍子的戳弄驚嚇到了動物。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4213,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::police::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ headquarters is located downtown.","expectedAnswer":"police","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ headquarters is located downtown.","clozeAnswer":"police","exampleTranslation":"警察總部設在市中心。","reference":{"eng":"police","kk":"/pəˈliːs/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['警察；警務人員'], ['（尤指）警察部隊；警局']]","chEntries":["警察","警務人員","警察部隊","警局"],"practiceMeaning":"警察總部設在市中心。","analysis":"源自古法語 police，意為“政府，管理，公民事務”，來自拉丁語 politia，'polis'（城市）。原指政府的組織或行政機構。在17世紀，'police' 開始指維持公共秩序的機構，即警察。'Police' 作為集合名詞，指整個警察隊伍。","definition":"The civil force of a state, responsible for the maintenance of public order, the prevention and detection of crime, etc.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police are investigating the crime.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警方正在調查這起罪案。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He reported the incident to the police.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他向警方報告了該事件。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police headquarters is located downtown.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警察總部設在市中心。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"警察總部設在市中心。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6187,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::porch::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He stood on the ____, waiting for her.","expectedAnswer":"porch","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He stood on the ____, waiting for her.","clozeAnswer":"porch","exampleTranslation":"他站在門廊上等她。","reference":{"eng":"porch","kk":"pɔrtʃ","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"門廊\"  ],  [    \"陽台\"  ],  [    \"走廊\"  ]]","chEntries":["門廊","陽台","走廊"],"practiceMeaning":"他站在門廊上等她。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 porche，最終源自拉丁語 porticus，意為「有柱子的走廊、迴廊」，與 porta「門」相關。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作為名詞，其核心語義是指「房屋入口處有頂的、開放式的區域」。詞源中的「門」和「走廊」概念直接體現了此義。","definition":"1. a covered shelter projecting in front of the entrance of a building; 2. a veranda or balcony.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They sat on the porch watching the rain.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們坐在門廊上看著雨。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The house had a wide front porch.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這房子有一個寬敞的前門廊。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He stood on the porch, waiting for her.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他站在門廊上等她。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The porch swing was comfortable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"門廊的吊椅很舒服。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他站在門廊上等她。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4188,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::practically::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It was ____ impossible to get tickets.","expectedAnswer":"practically","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It was ____ impossible to get tickets.","clozeAnswer":"practically","exampleTranslation":"拿到票幾乎是不可能的。","reference":{"eng":"practically","kk":"/ˈpræktɪkli/","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['實際上；差不多'], ['就實際而言']]","chEntries":["實際上","差不多","就實際而言"],"practiceMeaning":"拿到票幾乎是不可能的。","analysis":"由形容詞 'practical' 加上副詞後綴 '-ly' 構成。'Practical' 源自拉丁語 practicus，意為“實踐的”。'Practically' 的核心意思接近於“在實際操作或結果上”。1. “實際上；差不多”表示結果或狀態非常接近真實，幾乎等同。2. “就實際而言”強調從實用或操作的角度來看。","definition":"1. in a way that relates to practice or action rather than theory; 2. in a way that is almost or very nearly the case; virtually.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The job is practically finished.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這份工作實際上已經完成了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Practically speaking, we don't have enough time.\",\n    \"ch\": \"就實際情況而言，我們時間不夠。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was practically impossible to get tickets.\",\n    \"ch\": \"拿到票幾乎是不可能的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"拿到票幾乎是不可能的。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6240,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::premier::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of Quebec is the head of government.","expectedAnswer":"premier","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of Quebec is the head of government.","clozeAnswer":"premier","exampleTranslation":"魁北克省長是政府首腦。","reference":{"eng":"premier","kk":"ˈprɛmɪər","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"總理\"  ],  [    \"首相\"  ],  [    \"首映\"  ]]","chEntries":["總理","首相","首映"],"practiceMeaning":"魁北克省長是政府首腦。","analysis":"此字有多個詞源。作「總理；首相」時，源自法語 premier（第一的），指國家的首位官員。作「首映」時，是 premier（首先的）的名詞形式，指首次的公開演出或放映。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。中文翻譯為「總理；首相；首映」。","definition":"1. the leader of the government of a country or region; 2. the first public performance or showing of a film, play, or other work.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The premier announced new policies.\",\n    \"ch\": \"總理宣布了新政策。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The film's premier was held in London.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這部電影的首映會在倫敦舉行。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The premier of Quebec is the head of government.\",\n    \"ch\": \"魁北克省長是政府首腦。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"魁北克省長是政府首腦。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5799,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::prescription::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There is a ____ against cheating in exams.","expectedAnswer":"prescription","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There is a ____ against cheating in exams.","clozeAnswer":"prescription","exampleTranslation":"考試中禁止作弊的規定。","reference":{"eng":"prescription","kk":"prɪˈskrɪpʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"處方\"  ],  [    \"藥方\"  ],  [    \"規定\"  ],  [    \"指示\"  ]]","chEntries":["處方","藥方","規定","指示"],"practiceMeaning":"考試中禁止作弊的規定。","analysis":"此字為名詞，構詞自prescribe（開處方；規定）+ -ion（名詞字尾，表示行為；結果）。prescribe源自拉丁語praescribere（事先書寫；規定）。因此，prescription的核心語義是指「醫師開出的藥方」或「被規定或指示的事項」。語意演變上，由動詞「開處方；規定」的行為，發展為「處方」這個具體文件，以及「規定」這個抽象概念。","definition":"1. a written instruction from a doctor or dentist for a particular medicine or treatment; 2. a rule or order 