","適中的","不貴的","合乎情理的"],"practiceMeaning":"我們在這件事上必須講道理。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 rationalis，'ratio'（理性，計算）。'Reasonable' 的核心是與“理性”或“道理”相關。1. “合理的；公道的”指基於邏輯、公平和常識。2. “適中的”指價格或數量不過高，符合實際價值。3. “合乎情理的”強調行為、決策的合理性，易於被接受。","definition":"1. fair and sensible; 2. not too expensive; 3. based on or in accordance with good sense or judgment.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"That's a reasonable price for such a good product.\",\n    \"ch\": \"對於這樣好的產品來說，這是個合理的價格。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her request was reasonable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的要求是合情合理的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to be reasonable about this matter.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們在這件事上必須講道理。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們在這件事上必須講道理。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3186,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::rejection::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She experienced feelings of ____ after the breakup.","expectedAnswer":"rejection","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She experienced feelings of ____ after the breakup.","clozeAnswer":"rejection","exampleTranslation":"分手後她經歷了被拒絕的感覺。","reference":{"eng":"rejection","kk":"/rɪˈdʒɛkʃn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['拒絕；駁回'], ['（尤指因求職、求愛等而被）拒絕；被冷落']]","chEntries":["拒絕","駁回","被冷落"],"practiceMeaning":"分手後她經歷了被拒絕的感覺。","analysis":"名詞，源自動詞 'reject'。'Rejection' 指的是拒絕接受、承認或考慮某人或某物。這可以是拒絕提議、請求、申請，或是因為不喜歡、不合適而被拒絕。它常常會帶來失落、沮喪或被排斥的感受。","definition":"1. the act of rejecting or refusing to accept, consider, believe, etc.; 2. the state of being rejected; 3. the dismissive or contemptuous treatment of someone.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He felt devastated by the rejection of his job application.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對工作申請被拒感到非常沮喪。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The rejection of his proposal angered her.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的提議被駁回激怒了她。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She experienced feelings of rejection after the breakup.\",\n    \"ch\": \"分手後她經歷了被拒絕的感覺。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"分手後她經歷了被拒絕的感覺。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5439,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::relieve::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"A fresh pair of eyes can often ____ you of a difficult task.","expectedAnswer":"relieve","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"A fresh pair of eyes can often ____ you of a difficult task.","clozeAnswer":"relieve","exampleTranslation":"換一對新的眼睛來看待，常常能幫你減輕處理艱難任務的壓力。","reference":{"eng":"relieve","kk":"rɪˈliːv","tense":"v.","ch":"[['緩解'], ['減輕'], ['解除'], ['安慰'], ['換班']]","chEntries":["緩解","減輕","解除","安慰","換班"],"practiceMeaning":"換一對新的眼睛來看待，常常能幫你減輕處理艱難任務的壓力。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 \"relever\"，意為\"再次提起\"、\"舉起\"、\"減輕\"。其拉丁語詞源為 \"relevare\"，由 \"re-\" (再次) 和 \"levare\" (減輕，與 \"levis\" 意為\"輕\"有關) 構成。構詞上，\"re-\" 提供了「恢復」或「再次」的語意，\"levare\" 提供了「減輕」或「變輕」的核心語意。因此，\"relieve\" 的核心語義是「使某種負擔、痛苦或壓力變輕」，即「緩解」、「減輕」。引申用法包括「解除」某種義務或憂慮，以及「安慰」某人，使其痛苦減輕，還有「換班」以減輕他人負擔。","definition":"to lessen or remove pain, discomfort, or other suffering; to free someone from a burden or obligation; to provide comfort or reassurance to someone; to take over from someone who has been on duty.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This medicine will relieve your headache.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種藥會緩解你的頭痛。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government is trying to relieve poverty in the region.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府正試圖緩解該地區的貧困問題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A fresh pair of eyes can often relieve you of a difficult task.\",\n    \"ch\": \"換一對新的眼睛來看待，常常能幫你減輕處理艱難任務的壓力。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"換一對新的眼睛來看待，常常能幫你減輕處理艱難任務的壓力。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5423,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::replacement::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of parts is a common maintenance task.","expectedAnswer":"replacement","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of parts is a common maintenance task.","clozeAnswer":"replacement","exampleTranslation":"零件更換是常見的維護工作。","reference":{"eng":"replacement","kk":"rɪˈpleɪsmənt","tense":"n.","ch":"[['取代'], ['替換'], ['替代品'], ['接替者'], ['歸還'], ['放回原處']]","chEntries":["取代","替換","替代品","接替者","歸還","放回原處"],"practiceMeaning":"零件更換是常見的維護工作。","analysis":"此字為派生詞，由動詞 \"replace\" 加上名詞化字尾 \"-ment\" 構成。\"replace\" 由字首 \"re-\" (再次、向後) 和動詞 \"place\" (放置) 構成，原始語義為「再次放置」或「放回原處」，引申為「取代」、「替換」。字尾 \"-ment\" 將動詞的「取代」、「替換」行為轉化為抽象名詞，表示「取代的行為或過程」、「被取代的事物」或「用來取代的事物」。因此，\"replacement\" 指的是將舊的換成新的、用一個事物代替另一個事物的動作、結果，或者指用來替代的物品或人。","definition":"the act of replacing someone or something; something or someone that replaces another; a substitute.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The doctor ordered a replacement for the damaged hip joint.\",\n    \"ch\": \"醫生訂購了一個人工髖關節來替換受損的關節。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We are looking for a suitable replacement for the outgoing employee.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們正在為離職的員工尋找合適的接替人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The replacement of parts is a common maintenance task.\",\n    \"ch\": \"零件更換是常見的維護工作。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"零件更換是常見的維護工作。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3943,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::response::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The body's ____ to the virus was strong.","expectedAnswer":"response","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The body's ____ to the virus was strong.","clozeAnswer":"response","exampleTranslation":"身體對病毒的反應很強烈。","reference":{"eng":"response","kk":"/rɪˈspɒns/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['回應', '答覆'], ['反應']]","chEntries":["回應","答覆","反應"],"practiceMeaning":"身體對病毒的反應很強烈。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'responsum'，是動詞 'respondere' (意為「回答、回應」) 的過去分詞名詞化。指對某事的回應、回答或反應。","definition":"1. an answer or reaction to something; 2. a reply.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We received a positive response to our advertisement.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們對廣告收到了積極的回應。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her response was immediate and helpful.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的回應迅速且有幫助。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The body's 