ense":"n.","ch":"[['革命'], ['變革'], ['（天體）公轉'], ['（循環）']]","chEntries":["革命","變革","公轉"],"practiceMeaning":"地球大約需要 365 天完成一次繞太陽的公轉。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'revolutio'，意為「捲回、翻轉」，由動詞 'revolvere'（捲回）派生，'revolvere' 由 're-'（回、再次）和 'volvere'（捲、轉）組成。構詞學上，'re-' 是表示「回」或「再次」的字首，'vol-' 是「捲」或「轉」的詞根，'-ution' 是表示「過程」或「結果」的名詞化後綴。原始語意是「捲回」或「轉動」。從「重複的轉動」（如天體運行）引申為「徹底的變革」（如社會或政治上的）、「循環」。","definition":"1. A forcible overthrow of a government or other social order in favor of a new system; 2. A fundamental change in the way something is done or thought about; 3. The regular and continuous movement of a celestial body in an orbit around another.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The French Revolution had a profound impact on European history.\",\n    \"ch\": \"法國大革命對歐洲歷史產生了深遠的影響。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The discovery of penicillin was a revolution in medicine.\",\n    \"ch\": \"盤尼西林的發現是醫學上的一場革命。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The Earth completes one revolution around the Sun in approximately 365 days.\",\n    \"ch\": \"地球大約需要 365 天完成一次繞太陽的公轉。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"地球大約需要 365 天完成一次繞太陽的公轉。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5100,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::rim::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She wore glasses with a thin metal ____.","expectedAnswer":"rim","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She wore glasses with a thin metal ____.","clozeAnswer":"rim","exampleTranslation":"她戴著一副細金屬框眼鏡。","reference":{"eng":"rim","kk":"rɪm","tense":"n.","ch":"[['邊緣'], ['輪緣'], ['框']]","chEntries":["邊緣","輪緣","框"],"practiceMeaning":"她戴著一副細金屬框眼鏡。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 'rim'，意為 '邊緣'，可能與 'rein' (bridle rein) 有關。其核心語義是指一個物體的外圍邊緣，特別是圓形或環狀物體的頂部邊緣。例如，輪胎的輪緣、杯子的邊緣、眼鏡的鏡框。它代表的是物體的外部界限。","definition":"1. The outer, typically circular or oval, edge of something.; 2. The wheel of a motor vehicle or bicycle.; 3. A border or margin.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He dropped his keys over the rim of the well.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他把鑰匙掉進了井緣裡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The bicycle rim was bent.\",\n    \"ch\": \"自行車的輪緣彎了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She wore glasses with a thin metal rim.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她戴著一副細金屬框眼鏡。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她戴著一副細金屬框眼鏡。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4466,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::rough::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"I only have a ____ idea of the cost.","expectedAnswer":"rough","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"I only have a ____ idea of the cost.","clozeAnswer":"rough","exampleTranslation":"我只有對費用的粗略想法。","reference":{"eng":"rough","kk":"/rʌf/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['粗糙的'], ['崎嶇的'], ['劇烈的'], ['嚴酷的'], ['（計劃、概念）大致的'], ['粗暴的'], ['（天氣）惡劣的']]","chEntries":["粗糙的","崎嶇的","劇烈的","嚴酷的","大致的","粗暴的","惡劣的"],"practiceMeaning":"我只有對費用的粗略想法。","analysis":"源自古英語 rōh，意為「未加工的」、「粗糙的」。核心語意是「表面不光滑」。引申為「不平坦的」（地形），「不細緻的」（計劃、想法），「激烈的」（動作、天氣），「困難的」（經歷），「粗魯的」（人）等。","definition":"1. Having an uneven or irregular surface; not smooth; 2. Not exact or detailed; 3. Violent or severe; 4. Difficult or unpleasant.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The bark of the tree was rough to the touch.\",\n    \"ch\": \"樹皮摸起來很粗糙。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We had a rough journey through the mountains.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們經歷了一趟艱難的山區旅程。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I only have a rough idea of the cost.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我只有對費用的粗略想法。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The sea was rough today.\",\n    \"ch\": \"今天海浪很大。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我只有對費用的粗略想法。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U10、L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5564,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::roughly::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The box was ____ made.","expectedAnswer":"roughly","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The box was ____ made.","clozeAnswer":"roughly","exampleTranslation":"這個盒子做得很粗糙。","reference":{"eng":"roughly","kk":"ˈrʌfli","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['大致上'], ['粗略地'], ['約略地']]","chEntries":["大致上","粗略地","約略地"],"practiceMeaning":"這個盒子做得很粗糙。","analysis":"此字由形容詞 \"rough\" 加上副詞字尾 \"-ly\" 構成。\"rough\" 的詞源較複雜，可能源自古諾爾斯語 \"hruggr\"（rough, coarse，粗糙的），或與原始日耳曼語 \\*ruhhaz（rough，粗糙的）有關。其原始語義與「粗糙、不平滑」有關。因此，\"roughly\" 作為副詞，主要有兩層語義：一是形容「以粗糙、不精確的方式」進行，例如 \"roughly handled\"（被粗魯地對待）；二是形容「不精確、大致的程度」，例如 \"roughly 100 people\"（大約 100 人）。這種語義上的演變是從「物理上的不平滑、不精細」延伸到「抽象上的不精確、不詳細」。","definition":"1. In a way that is approximate or not exact; 2. In a way that is harsh or violent.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There were roughly 50 people at the meeting.\",\n    \"ch\": \"會議上大約有 50 人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He explained the plan roughly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他粗略地解釋了計畫。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The box was roughly made.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個盒子做得很粗糙。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個盒子做得很粗糙。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4553,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::satisfactory::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We are pleased with the ____ progress made so far.","expectedAnswer":"satisfactory","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We are pleased with the ____ progress made so far.","clozeAnswer":"satisfactory","exampleTranslation":"我們對迄今為止令人滿意的進展感到高興。","reference":{"eng":"satisfactory","kk":"/ˌsætɪsˈfæktəri/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['滿意的', '令人滿意的'], ['合格的', '令人滿意的']]","chEntries":["滿意的","令人滿意的","合格的"],"practiceMeaning":"我們對迄今為止令人滿意的進展感到高興。","analysis":"由 'satisfy' (使滿意) 加上形容詞字尾 '-ory' (表示具有某種性質或傾向) 構成。核心概念是能滿足需求或期望。\n    1. 滿意的、令人滿意的：指結果、表現等達到了期望或要求，讓人感到高興或認可。\n    2. 合格的、令人滿意的：指事物達到了基本的標準，雖然不一定突出，但足以接受。","definition":"1. fulfilling expectations or needs adequately.; 2. acceptable and meeting the required standards.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The results of the experiment were satisfactory.\",\n    \"ch\": \"實驗結果是令人滿意的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her performance in the exam was satisfactory.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在考試中的表現尚可。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We are pleased with the satisfactory progress made so far.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們對迄今為止令人滿意的進展感到高興。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們對迄今為止令人滿意的進展感到高興。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4059,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::scary::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He told a ____ story about ghosts.","expectedAnswer":"scary","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He told a ____ story about ghosts.","clozeAnswer":"scary","exampleTranslation":"他講了一個關於鬼的恐怖故事。","reference":{"eng":"scary","kk":"/ˈskɛri/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['嚇人的', '可怕的']]","chEntries":["嚇人的","可怕的"],"practiceMeaning":"他講了一個關於鬼的恐怖故事。","analysis":"源自動詞 'scare' (害怕，驚嚇)，加上 '-y' 後綴。'scare' 的詞源可能與北歐語言有關，意為「驚嚇」。核心是引起恐懼。因此，'scary' 指「使人感到害怕的」。","definition":"frightening or causing fear","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"那是一部嚇人的電影！\",\n    \"eng\": \"That was a scary movie!\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"突然的聲音相當可怕。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The sudden noise was quite scary.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他講了一個關於鬼的恐怖故事。\",\n    \"eng\": \"He told a scary story about ghosts.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他講了一個關於鬼的恐怖故事。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5313,"wordRef":"字彙王::u63::scope::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The microscope has a wide-field ____.","expectedAnswer":"scope","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The microscope has a wide-field ____.","clozeAnswer":"scope","exampleTranslation":"這顯微鏡有一個廣視場的目鏡筒。","reference":{"eng":"scope","kk":"skoʊp","tense":"n.","ch":"[['範圍', '幅度'], ['（能力、影響等的）範圍', '餘地'], ['（望遠鏡、顯微鏡等的）鏡筒']]","chEntries":["範圍","幅度","餘地","鏡筒"],"practiceMeaning":"這顯微鏡有一個廣視場的目鏡筒。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'scopus'（目標，目的），來自希臘語 'skopos' (σκοπός)，意為「觀察者、目標、目的」。構詞上，'scop-' 為詞根，'-us' 為名詞後綴。原始語意為「看」、「觀察」或「目標」。此語意引申為「觀察的範圍」、「理解的範圍」、「活動的範圍」或「影響的範圍」。","definition":"the extent of the area or subject matter that something deals with; the opportunity for doing something; the part of a telescope or microscope that contains the lenses.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The scope of the research was limited.\",\n    \"ch\": \"研究的範圍是有限的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This decision is beyond the scope of my authority.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個決定超出了我的權限範圍。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The microscope has a wide-field scope.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這顯微鏡有一個廣視場的目鏡筒。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這顯微鏡有一個廣視場的目鏡筒。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U63"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6137,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::sentimental::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It was a ____ journey down memory lane.","expectedAnswer":"sentimental","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It was a ____ journey down memory lane.","clozeAnswer":"sentimental","exampleTranslation":"這是一次回憶往昔的感傷之旅。","reference":{"eng":"sentimental","kk":"ˌsɛntɪˈmɛntl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"感傷的\"  ],  [    \"情感的\"  ],  [    \"多愁善感的\"  ],  [    \"情意的\"  ]]","chEntries":["感傷的","情感的","多愁善感的","情意的"],"practiceMeaning":"這是一次回憶往昔的感傷之旅。","analysis":"此字由 sentiment（情感）加上形容詞後綴 -al 構成。sentiment 源自拉丁語 sentimentum（感覺；思想）。因此，sentimental 的核心語義是「與情感相關的」。此形容詞描述傾向於表達或受到強烈情感（尤其是感傷、溫情）影響的。其語意演變是從「情感的」到「過於感傷的」或「充滿溫情的」。","definition":"1. of or prompted by sentiment or emotion; 2. of or relating to feelings of tenderness, sadness, or nostalgia; 3. characterized by or showing excessive tenderness, sadness, or nostalgia.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"a sentimental song\",\n    \"ch\": \"一首感傷的歌\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is sentimental about his childhood.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對童年充滿感傷。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was a sentimental journey down memory lane.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一次回憶往昔的感傷之旅。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是一次回憶往昔的感傷之旅。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5062,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::session::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The training ____ lasted for three hours.","expectedAnswer":"session","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The training ____ lasted for three hours.","clozeAnswer":"session","exampleTranslation":"這次培訓持續了三個小時。","reference":{"eng":"session","kk":"ˈseʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[['會議'], ['會議期間'], ['（活動或課程的）一次（時間段）']]","chEntries":["會議","會議期間","一次"],"practiceMeaning":"這次培訓持續了三個小時。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語sessio，是動詞sedere（坐）的派生詞。sedere 又來自原始印歐語 *sed-（坐）。session 的核心語意是「人們聚集在一起進行某項活動（如開會、上課、治療）的一段時間」。它強調的是活動的持續時間和集體性。OCR 掃描時可能將 's' 誤判為 '5'，或 'o' 誤判為 '0'。此處修正為 session。","definition":"1. a period devoted to a particular activity or meeting; 2. a period of time during which a court, legislature, or other body is assembled.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The parliament will convene for a special session next week.\",\n    \"ch\": \"議會將於下週召開特別會議。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a therapy session every Tuesday.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她每週二都有一次治療時間。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The training session lasted for three hours.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這次培訓持續了三個小時。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這次培訓持續了三個小時。","sourceName":"字彙王、龍騰課本","unitName":"U59、L2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5477,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::shallow::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She found his interest in fashion to be rather ____.","expectedAnswer":"shallow","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She found his interest in fashion to be rather ____.","clozeAnswer":"shallow","exampleTranslation":"她覺得他對時尚的興趣相當膚淺。","reference":{"eng":"shallow","kk":"ˈʃæloʊ","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['淺的'], ['淺薄的'], ['膚淺的']]","chEntries":["淺的","淺薄的","膚淺的"],"practiceMeaning":"她覺得他對時尚的興趣相當膚淺。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 'schalowe'，可能與古英語 'sceald'（淺水）有關，詞源不太確定，但與「淺」的概念緊密聯繫。'Shallow' 作形容詞，最基本的意思是指「水、容器等深度不大」，與 'deep'（深的）相對。引申義則用於形容「思想、情感、性格等缺乏深度」，即「膚淺的、淺薄的」，這是一種比喻用法，將「水淺」的物理概念類比到「思想不深」的抽象概念。","definition":"1. (Of a body of water or the landscape beneath it)<bos> of little depth.; 2. Not showing any intellectual or emotional depth.; 3. Superficial.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The children played in the shallow end of the pool.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子們在泳池的淺水區玩耍。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His arguments were shallow and lacked evidence.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的論點很膚淺，缺乏證據。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She found his interest in fashion to be rather shallow.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她覺得他對時尚的興趣相當膚淺。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她覺得他對時尚的興趣相當膚淺。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6196,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::shuttle::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The airport ____ was convenient.","expectedAnswer":"shuttle","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The airport ____ was convenient.","clozeAnswer":"shuttle","exampleTranslation":"機場接駁車很方便。","reference":{"eng":"shuttle","kk":"ˈʃʌtl","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"梭子\"  ],  [    \"接駁車\"  ],  [    \"穿梭班機\"  ]]","chEntries":["梭子","接駁車","穿梭班機"],"practiceMeaning":"機場接駁車很方便。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 shuttle，原意指紡織機上的「梭子」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作為名詞，其核心語義是指「用於紡織機上來回移動的梭子」，引申為「短程來回運輸的車輛或飛機」。詞源中的「梭子」象徵著來回移動的特徵。","definition":"1. a large shuttlecock used in badminton; 2. a device for weaving that moves back and forth between the threads of a warp; 3. a bus, train, or aircraft that travels regularly between two places.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The shuttle runs every hour from the hotel to the airport.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這班接駁車每小時一班，從旅館到機場。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She hit the shuttlecock hard in the game.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在比賽中用力擊打羽毛球。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The airport shuttle was convenient.\",\n    \"ch\": \"機場接駁車很方便。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The shuttle service operates between the terminal and the parking lot.\",\n    \"ch\": \"接駁車服務在航站樓和停車場之間運營。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"機場接駁車很方便。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4144,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::significant::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Her contribution played a ____ role in the project's success.","expectedAnswer":"significant","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Her contribution played a ____ role in the project's success.","clozeAnswer":"significant","exampleTranslation":"她的貢獻在項目的成功中起到了重要作用。","reference":{"eng":"significant","kk":"/sɪɡˈnɪfɪkənt/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['顯著的', '重要的'], ['（數量）相當大的'], ['意味深長的']]","chEntries":["顯著的","重要的","相當大的","意味深長的"],"practiceMeaning":"她的貢獻在項目的成功中起到了重要作用。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 significare（意指，表示），由 signum（標誌）+ facere（製造）組成。核心概念是「有重要意義」或「值得注意」。引申為數量上的重大、影響力的強大，或內涵的豐富。","definition":"1. sufficiently great or important to be worthy of attention; noteworthy; 2. having a particular meaning; indicative; 3. large or noticeable","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There has been a significant increase in sales.\",\n    \"ch\": \"銷售額有了顯著增長。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a significant development in the field.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是該領域的一項重要發展。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her contribution played a significant role in the project's success.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的貢獻在項目的成功中起到了重要作用。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她的貢獻在項目的成功中起到了重要作用。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3936,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::skillful::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He made a ____ escape from the building.","expectedAnswer":"skillful","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He made a ____ escape from the building.","clozeAnswer":"skillful","exampleTranslation":"他巧妙地逃離了建築物。","reference":{"eng":"skillful","kk":"/ˈskɪlfəl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['熟練的', '靈巧的'], ['技術精湛的']]","chEntries":["熟練的","靈巧的","技術精湛的"],"practiceMeaning":"他巧妙地逃離了建築物。","analysis":"源自古英語 'scille' (意為「有能力、有技巧」) 和 '-ful' (形容詞後綴)。指擁有技巧、能力或熟練掌握某種技能。","definition":"1. having or showing skill; expert; 2. done or made with skill.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a very skillful negotiator.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是一位非常熟練的談判專家。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The chef prepared a skillful meal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位廚師準備了一頓烹調精湛的餐點。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He made a skillful escape from the building.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他巧妙地逃離了建築物。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他巧妙地逃離了建築物。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6248,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::snatch::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It was a desperate ____ for freedom.","expectedAnswer":"snatch","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It was a desperate ____ for freedom.","clozeAnswer":"snatch","exampleTranslation":"那是一次對自由的絕望的奪取。","reference":{"eng":"snatch","kk":"snætʃ","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"搶奪\"  ],  [    \"奪取\"  ],  [    \"一小段時間\"  ],  [    \"短暫的機會\"  ]]","chEntries":["搶奪","奪取","一小段時間","短暫的機會"],"practiceMeaning":"那是一次對自由的絕望的奪取。","analysis":"此字源自擬聲詞，模仿突然抓住的動作。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。名詞義指突然、快速地抓住或拿走某物的行為。也可引申為一段短暫的時間或機會。中文翻譯為「搶奪；奪取；一小段時間；短暫的機會」。","definition":"1. the act of grabbing or taking something quickly; 2. a short period of time or a brief opportunity.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The snatch of the necklace caused panic in the crowd.\",\n    \"ch\": \"項鍊被搶奪引起了人群的恐慌。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He used the brief snatch of silence to escape.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他利用那短暫的寂靜逃脫了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was a desperate snatch for freedom.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那是一次對自由的絕望的奪取。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"那是一次對自由的絕望的奪取。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5568,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::sort::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need to ____ the apples into different grades.","expectedAnswer":"sort","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need to ____ the apples into different grades.","clozeAnswer":"sort","exampleTranslation":"我們需要將蘋果按等級分類。","reference":{"eng":"sort","kk":"sɔrt","tense":"v.","ch":"[['分類'], ['整理'], ['挑選']]","chEntries":["分類","整理","挑選"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要將蘋果按等級分類。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 \"sortir\"，意為 \"to draw lots, to choose\"（抽籤，選擇），來自拉丁語 \"sortem\"，是 \"sors, sortis\"（lot, fate, share，籤，命運，份額）的賓格形式。 \"sortem\" 引申出「選擇、挑選」的概念。在中古英語中，\"sort\" 的語義發展為「按照某種標準進行挑選或排列」，即「分類」或「整理」。因此，\"sort\" 的核心語義是「根據特定標準將事物分開或排列」。它既可以是物理上的分類（e.g., sorting laundry），也可以是邏輯上的分類（e.g., sorting data）。","definition":"1. Arrange systematically or alphabetically; 2. Classify (something) into different categories; 3. Deal with (a problem or situation) by taking appropriate action.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please sort the documents by date.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請按日期整理這些文件。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is good at sorting out complex problems.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她擅長解決複雜的問題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to sort the apples into different grades.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要將蘋果按等級分類。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要將蘋果按等級分類。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5464,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::span::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of their control was limited.","expectedAnswer":"span","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of their control was limited.","clozeAnswer":"span","exampleTranslation":"他們控制的範圍有限。","reference":{"eng":"span","kk":"spæn","tense":"n.","ch":"[['跨度'], ['期間'], ['範圍']]","chEntries":["跨度","期間","範圍"],"practiceMeaning":"他們控制的範圍有限。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 'spanne'，最初指「兩端之間的距離」，特別是張開拇指和中指（或小指）所能測量的長度，大約是九英寸。這個詞與古諾爾斯語 'spann'（跨度、尺度）以及荷蘭語 'span'（跨度）有關。隨著時間推移，'span' 的語意從具體的物理長度擴展到抽象的「時間長度」或「範圍」。核心語意是「兩個點之間的最大距離或持續時間」。","definition":"1. The full extent of something from end to end; the length, breadth, or width of a space or object.; 2. The period of time between the beginning and the end of something, especially a life, an event, or a period of activity.; 3. The distance between the two points of support of a bridge or other structure.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The bridge has a span of over 500 meters.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座橋的跨度超過 500 公尺。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her career spanned four decades.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的職業生涯橫跨了四十年。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The span of their control was limited.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們控制的範圍有限。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們控制的範圍有限。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5437,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::spare::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We can't ____ the resources for such a project.","expectedAnswer":"spare","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We can't ____ the resources for such a project.","clozeAnswer":"spare","exampleTranslation":"我們無法為這樣一個項目省下資源。","reference":{"eng":"spare","kk":"sper","tense":"v.","ch":"[['抽出時間'], ['節省'], ['饒恕'], ['免除']]","chEntries":["抽出時間","節省","饒恕","免除"],"practiceMeaning":"我們無法為這樣一個項目省下資源。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 \"spær\"，意為\"節儉的\"、\"稀少的\"。其詞源可能與\"sparse\" (稀疏的) 有聯繫。構詞上沒有明顯的字首、字根或字尾可拆解，應視為一個整體詞源的演變。原始語義是「稀少」、「節省」。作為動詞，它可以表示「節省」資源或時間，即「抽出時間」來做某事；也可以表示「饒恕」某人，即「免除」懲罰或傷害；或「免除」某種不適。","definition":"to refrain from harming or punishing someone; to save someone from harm; to afford to give or give up.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Can you spare me a moment of your time?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你能抽一點時間給我嗎？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The king spared his life.\",\n    \"ch\": \"國王饒恕了他的性命。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We can't spare the resources for such a project.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們無法為這樣一個項目省下資源。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們無法為這樣一個項目省下資源。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4540,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::stale::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Open the window to let in some fresh air; the room is ____.","expectedAnswer":"stale","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Open the window to let in some fresh air; the room is ____.","clozeAnswer":"stale","exampleTranslation":"打開窗戶讓新鮮空氣進來；房間裡的空氣不流通。","reference":{"eng":"stale","kk":"/steɪl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['不新鮮的', '變質的'], ['陳舊的', '乏味的'], ['（空氣）不流通的']]","chEntries":["不新鮮的","變質的","陳舊的","乏味的","不流通的"],"practiceMeaning":"打開窗戶讓新鮮空氣進來；房間裡的空氣不流通。","analysis":"源自古法語 'estale'，意為 'stale, immovable' (陳舊的、不動的)。\n    1. 不新鮮、變質：指食物失去新鮮度，如 'stale bread' (不新鮮的麵包)。\n    2. 陳舊、乏味：指事物缺乏新意、吸引力，如 'stale jokes' (陳舊的笑話)。\n    3. 空氣不流通：指室內空氣因缺乏流通而變得污濁。 'go stale' 指變質或變得乏味。","definition":"1. no longer fresh and therefore unpleasant to eat or smell.; 2. lacking in originality or freshness; dull.; 3. (of air) no longer fresh and pleasant; stagnant.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The bread had gone stale.\",\n    \"ch\": \"麵包已經不新鮮了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The conversation became stale after a while.\",\n    \"ch\": \"談話過了一會兒就變得乏味了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Open the window to let in some fresh air; the room is stale.\",\n    \"ch\": \"打開窗戶讓新鮮空氣進來；房間裡的空氣不流通。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"打開窗戶讓新鮮空氣進來；房間裡的空氣不流通。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4487,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::stir::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Don't ____ from your seat.","expectedAnswer":"stir","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Don't ____ from your seat.","clozeAnswer":"stir","exampleTranslation":"別從座位上移動。","reference":{"eng":"stir","kk":"/stɜːr/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['攪拌'], ['移動'], ['激發'], ['引起（感情、興趣等）']]","chEntries":["攪拌","移動","激發","引起"],"practiceMeaning":"別從座位上移動。","analysis":"源自古英語 styrian，意為「移動」、「激動」。核心語意是「引起移動」。引申為「攪拌」液體，使之混合或活躍；「引起」注意、興趣或情感。也可指「使開始行動」。","definition":"1. To move or cause to move slightly; 2. To mix (a substance) by moving it around with a spoon or similar object; 3. To rouse or incite; 4. To arouse or inspire (a feeling or quality).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Stir the soup gently.\",\n    \"ch\": \"輕輕攪拌湯。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The news of his success stirred excitement among his friends.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他成功的消息激起了他朋友們的興奮。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Don't stir from your seat.\",\n    \"ch\": \"別從座位上移動。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"別從座位上移動。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5621,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l7::strict::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The measurement must be ____.","expectedAnswer":"strict","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The measurement must be ____.","clozeAnswer":"strict","exampleTranslation":"測量必須精確。","reference":{"eng":"strict","kk":"strɪkt","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['嚴格的'], ['嚴厲的'], ['精確的'], ['嚴謹的']]","chEntries":["嚴格的","嚴厲的","精確的","嚴謹的"],"practiceMeaning":"測量必須精確。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'strictus'，是動詞 'stringere'（拉緊、緊束、約束）的過去分詞。構詞學上，'strin-'/'strict-' 是「拉緊」、「緊密」的詞根，'-us' 是過去分詞後綴。原始語意是「被拉緊的」、「被約束的」。從「緊繃」、「不受鬆懈」引申出「嚴格的」、「嚴厲的」（指規則、紀律、對待方式）以及「精確的」、「嚴謹的」（指方法、定義）。","definition":"1. (Of a rule or discipline) demanding exact compliance; 2. (Of a person or their manner) severe and unsparing in the giving or exacting of discipline, conditions, or the like; 3. Precisely accurate; exact.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The teacher has strict rules about homework.\",\n    \"ch\": \"老師對家庭作業有嚴格的規定。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is very strict with his children.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對他的孩子要求很嚴厲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The measurement must be strict.\",\n    \"ch\": \"測量必須精確。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"測量必須精確。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4470,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::survey::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"A recent ____ revealed that most people prefer to work from home.","expectedAnswer":"survey","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"A recent ____ revealed that most people prefer to work from home.","clozeAnswer":"survey","exampleTranslation":"最近的一項調查顯示，大多數人更願意在家工作。","reference":{"eng":"survey","kk":"/ˈsɜːrveɪ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['調查'], ['勘測']]","chEntries":["調查","勘測"],"practiceMeaning":"最近的一項調查顯示，大多數人更願意在家工作。","analysis":"源自古法語 surveoir，意為「看」、「檢查」。sur- (上) + voir (看)。核心語意是「仔細地觀看」、「檢查」。引申為對情況、意見或土地進行整體性的「調查」或「勘測」。","definition":"1. A general view, examination, or description of something; 2. An investigation of the opinions or experience of a group of people, based on a series of questions; 3. An act of measuring the position, slopes, or dimensions of an area of land.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company conducted a survey of customer satisfaction.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司進行了一項客戶滿意度調查。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The surveyor took measurements for the new building.\",\n    \"ch\": \"測量員為新建築進行了測量。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A recent survey revealed that most people prefer to work from home.\",\n    \"ch\": \"最近的一項調查顯示，大多數人更願意在家工作。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"最近的一項調查顯示，大多數人更願意在家工作。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5566,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::swiftly::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The rescue team worked ____ to save the stranded hikers.","expectedAnswer":"swiftly","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The rescue team worked ____ to save the stranded hikers.","clozeAnswer":"swiftly","exampleTranslation":"救援隊迅速行動，營救了受困的登山者。","reference":{"eng":"swiftly","kk":"ˈswɪftli","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['迅速地'], ['快速地']]","chEntries":["迅速地","快速地"],"practiceMeaning":"救援隊迅速行動，營救了受困的登山者。","analysis":"此字由形容詞 \"swift\" 加上副詞字尾 \"-ly\" 構成。\"swift\" 源自古英語 \"swift\"，與荷蘭語 \"swift\"、德語 \"sch(w)ift\" 同源，最終可追溯至原始印歐語 \\*swep-（to go, to flow，去，流動）。其核心語義是「快速、敏捷」。因此，\"swiftly\" 作為副詞，用來描述動作或事件發生的速度非常快，強調其敏捷性、即時性，沒有延遲。","definition":"1. At a great speed; very quickly; 2. Without delay; promptly.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The news spread swiftly through the town.\",\n    \"ch\": \"消息迅速傳遍了整個城鎮。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She replied swiftly to his question.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她迅速回答了他的問題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The 