"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5652,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l8::thoughtful::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It was ____ of you to help me.","expectedAnswer":"thoughtful","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It was ____ of you to help me.","clozeAnswer":"thoughtful","exampleTranslation":"你幫助我真是考慮周到。","reference":{"eng":"thoughtful","kk":"ˈθɔːtfəl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['體貼的'], ['考慮周到的'], ['深思熟慮的'], ['引人深思的']]","chEntries":["體貼的","考慮周到的","深思熟慮的","引人深思的"],"practiceMeaning":"你幫助我真是考慮周到。","analysis":"此字由 thought（思想，思考）+ -ful（充滿，-ful）構成。thought 是源自古英語 þōht，來自原始日耳曼語 *þancō（思想）。-ful 是常見的形容詞字尾，表示「充滿……」、「具有……」，常加在名詞後面。構詞上，thought 提供核心的「思考」概念，-ful 表示「充滿」或「具有」。因此，thoughtful 的核心語義為「充滿思考」或「具有深思」。此處為形容詞用法，描述行為、言語或人「周密考慮」、「體貼他人」或「引人深思」。","definition":"showing consideration for the needs or feelings of others; characterized by careful thought; causing one to think deeply.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"That was a very thoughtful gift.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那是一份很體貼的禮物。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She gave him a thoughtful look.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她給了他一個若有所思的眼神。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was thoughtful of you to help me.\",\n    \"ch\": \"你幫助我真是考慮周到。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"你幫助我真是考慮周到。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4630,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::thread::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There was a ____ of hope in her voice.","expectedAnswer":"thread","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There was a ____ of hope in her voice.","clozeAnswer":"thread","exampleTranslation":"她的聲音中透著一線希望。","reference":{"eng":"thread","kk":"/θred/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['線'], ['絲線'], ['（故事、談話等的）線索'], ['（思想、情緒等的）一絲']]","chEntries":["線","絲線","線索","一絲"],"practiceMeaning":"她的聲音中透著一線希望。","analysis":"源自古英語 'þræd'，與「紡織」相關。核心概念是一根細長、柔軟且連續的物質，可用於縫紉、編織。引申義指貫穿整個敘事、討論或情感的連貫性，是理解或追蹤的關鍵。","definition":"a long, thin strand of cotton, nylon, or other fibres used in sewing or weaving; a continuous element or theme running through a narrative, speech, or series of events.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She sewed the button back on with a strong thread.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她用結實的線把鈕扣縫了回去。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He lost the thread of the conversation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他聽不明白談話的內容了（失去了談話的線索）。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was a thread of hope in her voice.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的聲音中透著一線希望。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她的聲音中透著一線希望。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5675,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l8::throw-up::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They managed to ____ a temporary shelter.","expectedAnswer":"throw up","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They managed to ____ a temporary shelter.","clozeAnswer":"throw up","exampleTranslation":"他們設法迅速搭建了一個臨時住所。","reference":{"eng":"throw up","kk":"θroʊ ʌp","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['嘔吐'], ['（突然）放棄'], ['（建築物）建造']]","chEntries":["嘔吐","放棄","建造"],"practiceMeaning":"他們設法迅速搭建了一個臨時住所。","analysis":"此為一個常見的片語動詞。throw（扔，擲）的過去式 threw，up（向上）。字面意思為「向上扔」，引申為「嘔吐」。另一義為「突然放棄」或「終止」，例如 throw up a job。第三義為「建造」或「建造起來」，例如 throw up a wall。核心語義圍繞「扔」、「拋」的概念，引申出嘔吐（將食物向上排出）、放棄（像丟掉東西一樣）、建造（快速建起）。此處應考慮上下文，OCR 文本未提供具體上下文，但此片語有多個常見義。這裡提供最常見的「嘔吐」和「放棄」。","definition":"to vomit; to abandon or give up suddenly; to construct quickly.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He ate too much and had to throw up.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他吃得太多，不得不嘔吐。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She decided to throw up her job.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她決定辭掉工作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They managed to throw up a temporary shelter.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們設法迅速搭建了一個臨時住所。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們設法迅速搭建了一個臨時住所。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4161,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::time::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"With the passage of ____, old memories fade.","expectedAnswer":"time","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"With the passage of ____, old memories fade.","clozeAnswer":"time","exampleTranslation":"隨著時間的流逝，舊的記憶會逐漸淡忘。","reference":{"eng":"time","kk":"/taɪm/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['時間'], ['次數'], ['時代', '時期']]","chEntries":["時間","次數","時代","時期"],"practiceMeaning":"隨著時間的流逝，舊的記憶會逐漸淡忘。","analysis":"源自古英語 tīma（時間，時期）。核心概念是「連續的事件」，是事物發生、發展、變化的基本度量。","definition":"1. the indefinite continued progress of existence and events; 2. a particular occasion when something happens; 3. a period considered as a distinct entity","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"How much time do we have?\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們有多少時間？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is the third time he has called.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是他打來的第三次電話。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"With the passage of time, old memories fade.\",\n    \"ch\": \"隨著時間的流逝，舊的記憶會逐漸淡忘。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"隨著時間的流逝，舊的記憶會逐漸淡忘。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5501,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::to-come::idiom","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She wants to make a difference in the world ____.","expectedAnswer":"to come","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She wants to make a difference in the world ____.","clozeAnswer":"to come","exampleTranslation":"她想在即將到來的世界裡有所作為。","reference":{"eng":"to come","kk":"tu kʌm","tense":"idiom","ch":"[['即將到來的'], ['將來']]","chEntries":["即將到來的","將來"],"practiceMeaning":"她想在即將到來的世界裡有所作為。","analysis":"這個短語由不定詞 'to come' 構成。'To come' 作不定詞，表示「來」這個動作。當用作形容詞或修飾名詞時，'to come' 通常表示「即將到來的」、「未來的」。例如 'the years to come'（未來幾年）。它強調的是「尚未發生但即將發生」的狀態。核心語意是「即將發生」。","definition":"1. Future; to be expected in the future.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We are looking forward to the years to come.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們期待著未來。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The problems to come may be even greater.\",\n    \"ch\": \"即將到來的問題可能更大。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She wants to make a difference in the world to come.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她想在即將到來的世界裡有所作為。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她想在即將到來的世界裡有所作為。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5463,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::tribal::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The conflict was fueled by ____ rivalries.","expectedAnswer":"tribal","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The conflict was fueled by ____ rivalries.","clozeAnswer":"tribal","exampleTranslation":"衝突是由部落之間的對立所加劇的。","reference":{"eng":"tribal","kk":"ˈtraɪbəl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['部落的'], ['部族的']]","chEntries":["部落的","部族的"],"practiceMeaning":"衝突是由部落之間的對立所加劇的。","analysis":"此字由名詞 'tribe'（部落）加上形容詞字尾 '-al' 構成。'-al' 是來自拉丁語 '-alis' 的變體，用於構成形容詞，表示「……的、關於……的」。因此，'tribal' 的意思是「屬於部落的、與部落有關的」，用來形容與部落社會結構、文化、習俗或組織相關的事物。","definition":"1. Relating to or characteristic of a tribe or tribes.; 2. Organized according to a tribe.; 3. Belonging to or characteristic of a tribal society.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They have a rich tribal history and traditions.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們擁有豐富的部落歷史和傳統。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The artist painted a scene of tribal life.\",\n    \"ch\": \"藝術家描繪了一幅部落生活的景象。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The conflict was fueled by tribal rivalries.\",\n    \"ch\": \"衝突是由部落之間的對立所加劇的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"衝突是由部落之間的對立所加劇的。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5446,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::urgency::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The organization stressed the ____ of climate action.","expectedAnswer":"urgency","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The organization stressed the ____ of climate action.","clozeAnswer":"urgency","exampleTranslation":"該組織強調了氣候行動的緊迫性。","reference":{"eng":"urgency","kk":"ˈɜːrdʒənsi","tense":"n.","ch":"[['緊急'], ['急迫'], ['緊迫']]","chEntries":["緊急","急迫","緊迫"],"practiceMeaning":"該組織強調了氣候行動的緊迫性。","analysis":"此字為派生詞，由形容詞 \"urgent\" (緊急的) 加上名詞化字尾 \"-cy\" (或 \"-cy\") 構成。\"urgent\" 源自拉丁語 \"urgens\" (催促、緊迫)，是動詞 \"urgere\" 的現在分詞。構詞上，\"urg-\" 提供了核心的「催促」、「緊迫」語意，\"-ency\" 是常見的名詞字尾，表示「狀態」、「品質」或「情況」。因此，\"urgency\" 指的是「需要立即關注或處理的緊急、急迫或緊迫的狀態」。","definition":"an important and urgent need or demand; the quality or state of being urgent.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The urgency of the situation became clear immediately.\",\n    \"ch\": \"局勢的緊急性立即可見。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There is a sense of urgency in their voices.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們的語氣中帶著一種急迫感。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The organization stressed the urgency of climate action.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該組織強調了氣候行動的緊迫性。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該組織強調了氣候行動的緊迫性。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6253,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::verbal::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ aspect of communication is crucial.","expectedAnswer":"verbal","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ aspect of communication is crucial.","clozeAnswer":"verbal","exampleTranslation":"溝通的言語方面至關重要。","reference":{"eng":"verbal","kk":"ˈvɜrbəl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"口頭的\"  ],  [    \"言語的\"  ],  [    \"動詞的\"  ]]","chEntries":["口頭的","言語的","動詞的"],"practiceMeaning":"溝通的言語方面至關重要。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 verbalis，意為「關於詞語的」，是 verbum（詞語）的派生詞。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作形容詞時，指通過語言、說話而非書寫傳達的；或與語言、言詞、動詞相關的。中文翻譯為「口頭的；言語的；動詞的」。","definition":"1. relating to or using spoken words; 2. expressed in speech rather than writing; 3. relating to verbs.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They reached a verbal agreement.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們達成了口頭協議。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The verbal contract is binding.\",\n    \"ch\": \"口頭合同具有約束力。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The verbal aspect of communication is crucial.\",\n    \"ch\": \"溝通的言語方面至關重要。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The professor explained the verbal tenses.\",\n    \"ch\": \"教授解釋了動詞的時態。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"溝通的言語方面至關重要。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4507,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::versatile::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She is a ____ actress, equally adept at comedy and drama.","expectedAnswer":"versatile","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She is a ____ actress, equally adept at comedy and drama.","clozeAnswer":"versatile","exampleTranslation":"她是一位多才多藝的女演員，擅長喜劇和戲劇。","reference":{"eng":"versatile","kk":"/ˈvɜːrsətl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['多才多藝的'], ['多用途的'], ['適應性強的']]","chEntries":["多才多藝的","多用途的","適應性強的"],"practiceMeaning":"她是一位多才多藝的女演員，擅長喜劇和戲劇。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 versatilis，意為「可旋轉的」、「多變的」。vertere (轉動)。核心語意是「能轉向」、「能適應不同方向」。引申為「能做多種事情」（人才），「能用於多種目的」（物品）。","definition":"1. Able to adapt or be adapted to many different functions or activities; 2. Having or showing ability in many different skills.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a versatile athlete, skilled in many sports.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一位多才多藝的運動員，擅長多種運動。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a versatile tool that can be used for various tasks.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個多功能的工具，可用於各種任務。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a versatile actress, equally adept at comedy and drama.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是一位多才多藝的女演員，擅長喜劇和戲劇。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她是一位多才多藝的女演員，擅長喜劇和戲劇。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4186,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::vision::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The entrepreneur's ____ revolutionized the industry.","expectedAnswer":"vision","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The entrepreneur's ____ revolutionized the industry.","clozeAnswer":"vision","exampleTranslation":"這位企業家的遠見徹底改變了這個行業。","reference":{"eng":"vision","kk":"/ˈvɪʒn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['視力；視覺'], ['想像；幻想'], ['遠見；洞察力'], ['（對未來的）設想；規劃']]","chEntries":["視力","視覺","想像","幻想","遠見","洞察力","設想","規劃"],"practiceMeaning":"這位企業家的遠見徹底改變了這個行業。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 visio，意為“看，看見，景象”。'Visio' 來自 'videre'，意為“看”。核心是“看”的能力和所見的景象。引申至抽象概念：1. 抽象化的“看”即“想像”或“幻想”；2. 預見未來、有遠見的“看”即“遠見”或“洞察力”；3. 具體規劃的“看”即對未來的“設想”或“規劃”。","definition":"1. the ability to see; sight; 2. the ability to imagine or think about the future with imagination or wisdom; 3. a mental image or picture of what the future could be like.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has poor vision in his left eye.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他左眼的視力很差。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She had a vision of a better future for her country.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對國家有了一個更美好未來的設想。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The entrepreneur's vision revolutionized the industry.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位企業家的遠見徹底改變了這個行業。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He described his vision in vivid detail.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他生動地描述了他的幻想。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這位企業家的遠見徹底改變了這個行業。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5111,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::vocal::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ music is an important part of the concert.","expectedAnswer":"Vocal","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ music is an important part of the concert.","clozeAnswer":"Vocal","exampleTranslation":"聲樂是音樂會的重要組成部分。","reference":{"eng":"vocal","kk":"ˈvoʊkl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['聲音的'], ['發聲的'], ['直言不諱的']]","chEntries":["聲音的","發聲的","直言不諱的"],"practiceMeaning":"聲樂是音樂會的重要組成部分。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'vocalis'，意為 '與聲音有關的'，源於 'vox, vocis' (voice)。'Vocal' 的核心語義是指 '與聲音相關的'，如 'vocal cords' (聲帶)。引申開來，'vocal' 也指 '能夠發聲的'。更進一步，它形容一個人 '直言不諱'，能夠清晰、公開地表達自己的意見，尤其是在表達不滿或批評時，這意味著他們的聲音被清晰地 '聽見'。","definition":"1. Relating to or produced by the voice.; 2. Able to speak or utter sounds.; 3. Expressing opinions or feelings strongly and openly.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a strong vocal presence.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她有很強的聲音表現力。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is very vocal in his opposition to the plan.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對這項計劃的Opposition非常直言不諱。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Vocal music is an important part of the concert.\",\n    \"ch\": \"聲樂是音樂會的重要組成部分。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"聲樂是音樂會的重要組成部分。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3925,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::volume::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"A large ____ of mail arrived today.","expectedAnswer":"volume","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"A large ____ of mail arrived today.","clozeAnswer":"volume","exampleTranslation":"今天收到大量的郵件。","reference":{"eng":"volume","kk":"/ˈvɒljum/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['音量'], ['體積', '容量'], ['數量', '大量'], ['冊']]","chEntries":["音量","體積","容量","數量","大量","冊"],"practiceMeaning":"今天收到大量的郵件。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'volumen'，意為「捲、卷軸」，來自 'volvere' (意為「滾動、捲起」)。最初指捲起的紙張，引申為「書本的一卷」；後引申為「物體的體積」；再引申為「聲音的大小」，即「音量」；另引申為「數量、大量」。","definition":"1. the amount of space that a substance or object occupies, or that is enclosed within a container; 2. the loudness of a sound; 3. a quantity of something, especially a large quantity; 4. a single book forming part of a work or series.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please turn down the volume, it's too loud.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請把音量轉小，太吵了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This bottle has a volume of one liter.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個瓶子的容量是一公升。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A large volume of mail arrived today.\",\n    \"ch\": \"今天收到大量的郵件。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is the third volume of the encyclopedia.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是百科全書的第三卷。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"今天收到大量的郵件。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U2、L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4218,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::warning::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ signs were ignored.","expectedAnswer":"warning","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ signs were ignored.","clozeAnswer":"warning","exampleTranslation":"警告標誌被忽略了。","reference":{"eng":"warning","kk":"/ˈwɔːrnɪŋ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['警告；預警'], ['（對危險等的）告誡']]","chEntries":["警告","預警","告誡"],"practiceMeaning":"警告標誌被忽略了。","analysis":"由動詞 'warn'（警告）加上名詞後綴 '-ing' 構成。'Warn' 源自古英語 warnian，意為“警告，告誡”。核心是預先告知某人潛在的危險或不利後果，以使其採取預防措施。","definition":"A statement or event that indicates a possible or impending danger, problem, or unpleasant situation.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The alarm is a warning of fire.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警報是火災的預警。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He received a stern warning from his boss.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他接到了老闆嚴厲的警告。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The warning signs were ignored.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警告標誌被忽略了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"警告標誌被忽略了。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4520,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::with::prep","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This is a problem ____ the software.","expectedAnswer":"with","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This is a problem ____ the software.","clozeAnswer":"with","exampleTranslation":"這是軟體的一個問題。","reference":{"eng":"with","kk":"/wɪð/","tense":"prep.","ch":"[['和...一起'], ['帶著'], ['使用'], ['關於']]","chEntries":["和...一起","帶著","使用","關於"],"practiceMeaning":"這是軟體的一個問題。","analysis":"源自古英語 wið。是一個表示陪伴、工具、原因、方式等的多功能介詞。核心語意是「一起」、「伴隨」。","definition":"1. Accompanied by (another person or people); 2. Indicating the instrument or agent used to perform an action; 3. In the company of or in addition to; 4. Having or possessing (a particular quality or characteristic).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is talking with her friend.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她正在和她的朋友說話。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He cut the cake with a knife.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他用刀切蛋糕。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a problem with the software.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是軟體的一個問題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a man with great courage.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一個有巨大勇氣的人。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是軟體的一個問題。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6062,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::acute::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She suffers from ____ appendicitis.","expectedAnswer":"acute","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She suffers from ____ appendicitis.","clozeAnswer":"acute","exampleTranslation":"她患有急性闌尾炎。","reference":{"eng":"acute","kk":"əˈkjut","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"尖銳的\"  ],  [    \"敏銳的\"  ],  [    \"嚴重的\"  ],  [    \"急性的\"  ]]","chEntries":["尖銳的","敏銳的","嚴重的","急性的"],"practiceMeaning":"她患有急性闌尾炎。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 acutus，意為「尖的，銳利的」，是動詞 acuere（to sharpen）的過去分詞。構詞上，ac- 來自 acu-，意為「尖、銳利」，-ute 是形容詞後綴。此字的核心語義與「尖銳」相關，引申出多種含義：物理上的「尖銳」形狀；感知上的「敏銳」；情況上的「嚴重」或「劇烈」；醫學上的「急性」發作。這些義項都體現了「程度極高」或「非常明顯」的特點。","definition":"1. sharp or penetrating, especially in intellect, perception, or physical appearance (e.g., an acute angle); 2. (of a bad situation or feeling) intense; severe; 3. (of a disease or condition) of sudden onset, sharp rise, and short course.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The triangle has an acute angle.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個三角形有一個銳角。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has an acute sense of smell.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他有靈敏的嗅覺。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The situation is becoming increasingly acute.\",\n    \"ch\": \"局勢正變得日益嚴峻。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She suffers from acute appendicitis.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她患有急性闌尾炎。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她患有急性闌尾炎。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6153,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::alliance::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"A political ____ was formed to contest the election.","expectedAnswer":"alliance","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"A political ____ was formed to contest the election.","clozeAnswer":"alliance","exampleTranslation":"一個政治聯盟為了競選而成立。","reference":{"eng":"alliance","kk":"əˈlaɪəns","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"聯盟\"  ],  [    \"聯合\"  ],  [    \"結合\"  ],  [    \"姻親關係\"  ]]","chEntries":["聯盟","聯合","結合","姻親關係"],"practiceMeaning":"一個政治聯盟為了競選而成立。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 aliance「聯盟」，源自動詞 alier「聯合」，最終可追溯至拉丁語 alligare，意為「綁縛、聯合」，由 ad- (to) + ligare (to bind) 組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 ligare「綁縛」是其核心語意來源。作為名詞，其核心語義是兩個或多個實體（國家、組織、個人）基於共同目標或利益而形成的聯合或結合。詞源中的「綁縛」概念清晰地體現了聯盟的緊密聯繫。此義項由「聯合」的動作延伸出「聯盟」的狀態或組織。","definition":"1. a union or association formed for mutual benefit, especially between countries or organizations; 2. a close connection or relationship, especially one involving shared interests or goals; 3. a relationship by marriage between two families or groups.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The two countries formed a military alliance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"兩國組成了一個軍事聯盟。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This alliance was strategic for both sides.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個聯盟對雙方來說都是戰略性的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The alliance of their families was beneficial.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們家族之間的結合是有益的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A political alliance was formed to contest the election.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一個政治聯盟為了競選而成立。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"一個政治聯盟為了競選而成立。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6209,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::alongside::prep","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ his main job, he volunteers at a shelter.","expectedAnswer":"Alongside","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ his main job, he volunteers at a shelter.","clozeAnswer":"Alongside","exampleTranslation":"除了他的主要工作之外，他還在收容所做志工。","reference":{"eng":"alongside","kk":"əˈlɔŋˈsaɪd","tense":"prep.","ch":"[  [    \"在…旁邊\"  ],  [    \"與…並排\"  ],  [    \"與…同時\"  ],  [    \"除了…之外\"  ]]","chEntries":["在…旁邊","與…並排","與…同時","除了…之外"],"practiceMeaning":"除了他的主要工作之外，他還在收容所做志工。","analysis":"此片語由介詞 along 和名詞 side 組成。along 源自古英語，意為「 along（沿著）」，side 源自古英語 sīde，意為「邊緣，側面」。此字在現代英語中可視為固定搭配，不需拆解。作介詞時，表示空間上的「在…旁邊；與…並排」，或表示時間、行動上的「與…同時；與…一起」，以及表示比較或支持的「與…相比；支持…」。","definition":"1. next to someone or something; 2. at the same time as someone or something else; 3. in addition to someone or something else; 4. supporting or cooperating with someone or something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The ship sailed alongside the coast.\",\n    \"ch\": \"船隻沿著海岸航行。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He sat alongside his wife at the wedding.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在婚禮上坐在他妻子旁邊。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We are working alongside our international partners.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們正與我們的國際夥伴一同合作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Alongside his main job, he volunteers at a shelter.\",\n    \"ch\": \"除了他的主要工作之外，他還在收容所做志工。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"除了他的主要工作之外，他還在收容所做志工。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5820,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::attribute::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Intelligence is a valuable ____.","expectedAnswer":"attribute","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Intelligence is a valuable ____.","clozeAnswer":"attribute","exampleTranslation":"智慧是一種寶貴的特質。","reference":{"eng":"attribute","kk":"ˈætrɪbjuːt","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"特質\"  ],  [    \"屬性\"  ],  [    \"特徵\"  ],  [    \"特性\"  ]]","chEntries":["特質","屬性","特徵","特性"],"practiceMeaning":"智慧是一種寶貴的特質。","analysis":"此名詞形式的 'attribute' 源自拉丁語 'attributum' (something bestowed or assigned)，是 'attribuere' 的過去分詞中性形式。其核心語意為「被分配或賦予給某物的一項」。在構詞上，'ad-' (to) + 'tribuere' (to assign)。作為名詞，'attribute' 指的是屬於某人或某物的特質、品質、性質或特徵，這些都是被「賦予」或「歸屬於」主體的。它與動詞形式的「歸因於」密切相關，因為特質（名詞）就是被認為是某事物「歸因於」的那個東西。例如，也可指「一項特殊能力或才能」。","definition":"1. A quality or feature regarded as a characteristic or inherent part of someone or something.; 2. A thing regarded as a property of a person or thing.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Patience is an important attribute for a teacher.\",\n    \"ch\": \"耐心是老師重要的特質。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The book is rich in historical attributes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本書富含歷史特徵。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Honesty is a key attribute of his character.\",\n    \"ch\": \"誠實是他性格的關鍵屬性。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Intelligence is a valuable attribute.\",\n    \"ch\": \"智慧是一種寶貴的特質。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"智慧是一種寶貴的特質。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3066,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::authority::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need to check the ____ of this source.","expectedAnswer":"authority","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need to check the ____ of this source.","clozeAnswer":"authority","exampleTranslation":"我們需要核實這個來源的權威性。","reference":{"eng":"authority","kk":"/əˈθɔːrəti/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['權威；權力'], ['當局；權力機構'], ['權威人士；專家'], ['（學術）權威；準確性']]","chEntries":["權威","權力","當局","權力機構","權威人士","專家","準確性"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要核實這個來源的權威性。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'auctoritas'，'auctor' (originator, author) 的衍生詞。最初意為「影響力」、「權威」，後來發展出多重含義。\n1. 權威；權力：指被承認的發布命令、做出決定的權力。\n2. 當局；權力機構：指擁有合法權力的政府機構或組織。\n3. 權威人士；專家：指在某個領域具有知識、技能和影響力的人。\n4. （學術）權威；準確性：指資訊來源的可靠性和學術上的重要性。","definition":"1. the power or right to give orders, make decisions, and enforce obedience; 2. the people or organizations that have the power to make decisions and enforce laws; 3. a person or organization that has power or control in a particular area; 4. an expert on a subject.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police have the authority to arrest criminals.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警方有權逮捕罪犯。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Local authorities are responsible for public services.\",\n    \"ch\": \"地方當局負責公共服務。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is an authority on ancient Roman history.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是古羅馬歷史方面的權威。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to check the authority of this source.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要核實這個來源的權威性。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要核實這個來源的權威性。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5826,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::bolt::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"A ____ of light shot across the sky.","expectedAnswer":"bolt","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"A ____ of light shot across the sky.","clozeAnswer":"bolt","exampleTranslation":"一道閃光劃過天際。","reference":{"eng":"bolt","kk":"boʊlt","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"螺栓\"  ],  [    \"門閂\"  ],  [    \"閃電\"  ],  [    \"閃電般的光\"  ]]","chEntries":["螺栓","門閂","閃電","閃電般的光"],"practiceMeaning":"一道閃光劃過天際。","analysis":"此字有多個同形異源的來源。一來源是表示「門閂」、「槓桿」，來自古英語 'bolta' 或「橫樑」；另一來源是表示「閃電」、「快速跑」，可能與原始日耳曼語 *bult- (to bolt, to build) 或 *baltaz (swift) 有關。當指「門閂」時，其語意與「關閉」、「鎖定」相關。當指「閃電」時，則強調其突然、快速的爆發。另一常見義「螺栓」則是現代引申，借用了「鎖定」或「固定」的意象。還有「快速跑」的動詞義，也與「閃電」的突然性及速度相關。這裡的「閃電般的光」更側重於視覺上的突然出現。","definition":"1. A metal pin used to fasten things together, typically with a nut on the end.; 2. A bar used to fasten a door or gate.; 3. A flash of lightning.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He tightened the bolt on the door.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他擰緊了門上的螺栓。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She slid the bolt across the door.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她拉上門閂。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A bolt of lightning lit up the sky.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一道閃電劃破天空。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A bolt of light shot across the sky.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一道閃光劃過天際。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"一道閃光劃過天際。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5828,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::chubby::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The child's ____ fingers reached for the toy.","expectedAnswer":"chubby","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The child's ____ fingers reached for the toy.","clozeAnswer":"chubby","exampleTranslation":"孩子圓潤的手指伸向了玩具。","reference":{"eng":"chubby","kk":"ˈtʃʌbi","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"豐滿的\"  ],  [    \"胖乎乎的\"  ],  [    \"圓胖的\"  ],  [    \"圓潤的\"  ]]","chEntries":["豐滿的","胖乎乎的","圓胖的","圓潤的"],"practiceMeaning":"孩子圓潤的手指伸向了玩具。","analysis":"此字源於 'chub'，原指一種胖魚（如鯉魚的一種），後來用來形容人或物的圓胖、豐滿。'Chub' 本身來源不明，可能與「腫脹」或「凸起」的語感有關。'-y' 是常見的形容詞字尾，表示「具有……性質的」。'Chubby' 的語意核心是「圓胖、豐滿」，通常帶有可愛、健康的意味，多用於形容嬰兒、兒童或臉頰。它描述的是一種溫和、無攻擊性的肥胖感。例如，也可指「圓潤的」手指或四肢。","definition":"1. (of a person, especially a child) plump; well-rounded.; 2. (of a part of a person's body) rounded and plump.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The baby had chubby cheeks.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那個嬰兒有著圓胖的臉頰。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was a chubby boy with a cheerful smile.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一個胖乎乎但笑容開朗的男孩。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a chubby face.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她有一張豐滿的臉。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The child's chubby fingers reached for the toy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子圓潤的手指伸向了玩具。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"孩子圓潤的手指伸向了玩具。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6160,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::collaboration::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ lasted for five years.","expectedAnswer":"collaboration","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ lasted for five years.","clozeAnswer":"collaboration","exampleTranslation":"這次合作持續了五年。","reference":{"eng":"collaboration","kk":"kəˌlæbəˈreɪʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"合作\"  ],  [    \"協作\"  ]]","chEntries":["合作","協作"],"practiceMeaning":"這次合作持續了五年。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 collaboratio，由 collaborare「一起工作」名詞化而來。collaborare 由 com- (together) + laborare (to work) 組成，laborare 又源自 labor (work)。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 com-「一起」和 labor「工作」是其核心語意來源。作為名詞，其核心語義是「兩個或多個個體或團體為達成共同目標而共同工作」。詞源中的「一起工作」清晰地表達了此義。","definition":"1. the action of working with someone to produce or create something; 2. a joint effort.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The project was a successful collaboration between the two departments.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個專案是兩個部門之間成功的合作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Their collaboration resulted in a groundbreaking discovery.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們的協作促成了一項開創性的發現。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Artistic collaboration often leads to innovative results.\",\n    \"ch\": \"藝術上的合作經常帶來創新的成果。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The collaboration lasted for five years.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這次合作持續了五年。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這次合作持續了五年。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4222,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::credit::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The deposit will be shown as a ____ on your statement.","expectedAnswer":"credit","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The deposit will be shown as a ____ on your statement.","clozeAnswer":"credit","exampleTranslation":"這筆存款將顯示為您對帳單上的進帳。","reference":{"eng":"credit","kk":"/ˈkredɪt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['信用；信譽'], ['（金融機構的）信貸；延期付款'], ['（在帳戶中的）貸方餘額；進帳'], ['功勞；讚揚']]","chEntries":["信用","信譽","信貸","延期付款","貸方餘額","進帳","功勞","讚揚"],"practiceMeaning":"這筆存款將顯示為您對帳單上的進帳。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 creditum，'credere'（相信，信任）的派生詞。核心是“相信”或“信任”。1. “信用；信譽”指個人或機構的良好聲譽，使人願意相信其承諾。2. “信貸；延期付款”指金融機構基於信任而提供的貸款或允許延期支付。3. “貸方餘額；進帳”指銀行帳戶中的正面餘額。4. “功勞；讚揚”指因某人的貢獻而給予的肯定，基於相信其功績。","definition":"1. the ability of a customer to obtain goods or services before payment, based on the trust that payment will be made in the future; 2. trust in the believe that someone will do what they are expected or supposed to do; 3. an amount of money added to an account; 4. praise or admiration for an achievement.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has good credit and can easily get a loan.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的信用很好，很容易獲得貸款。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"You can buy this item on credit.\",\n    \"ch\": \"你可以賒帳購買這個物品。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She was given credit for her hard work.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她因辛勤工作而受到讚揚。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The deposit will be shown as a credit on your statement.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這筆存款將顯示為您對帳單上的進帳。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這筆存款將顯示為您對帳單上的進帳。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5833,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::descriptive::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The teacher asked for a ____ essay.","expectedAnswer":"descriptive","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The teacher asked for a ____ essay.","clozeAnswer":"descriptive","exampleTranslation":"老師要求寫一篇描寫性的文章。","reference":{"eng":"descriptive","kk":"dɪˈskrɪptɪv","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"描述性的\"  ],  [    \"描寫性的\"  ],  [    \"詳盡的\"  ]]","chEntries":["描述性的","描寫性的","詳盡的"],"practiceMeaning":"老師要求寫一篇描寫性的文章。","analysis":"此字由名詞 'description' 加上形容詞字尾 '-ive' 構成。'Description' 源自拉丁語 'descriptio'，由 'de-' (down) 和 'scribere' (to write) 構成，字面意思是「寫下」（細節）。'-ive' 是常見的形容詞字尾，表示「具有……性質的」或「傾向於……」。因此，'descriptive' 指「具有描述性質的」或「用來描述的」。它強調的是對事物特徵、細節進行刻畫和描繪的功能。例如，也可指「詳盡的」敘述。","definition":"1. Serving or seeking to describe, especially by giving full, accurate details.; 2. Relating to or characteristic of description.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The author provided a descriptive account of the journey.\",\n    \"ch\": \"作者提供了關於這次旅程的詳細描述。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The book uses descriptive language.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本書使用了描寫性的語言。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He gave a descriptive report of the event.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對這次事件做了一個詳盡的報告。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The teacher asked for a descriptive essay.\",\n    \"ch\": \"老師要求寫一篇描寫性的文章。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"老師要求寫一篇描寫性的文章。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5835,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::dilemma::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The scientist faced the ____ of publishing his findings or keeping them secret.","expectedAnswer":"dilemma","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The scientist faced the ____ of publishing his findings or keeping them secret.","clozeAnswer":"dilemma","exampleTranslation":"這位科學家面臨著是發表研究結果還是保密的兩難。","reference":{"eng":"dilemma","kk":"dɪˈlɛmə","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"困境\"  ],  [    \"兩難\"  ],  [    \"進退兩難\"  ],  [    \"難題\"  ]]","chEntries":["困境","兩難","進退兩難","難題"],"practiceMeaning":"這位科學家面臨著是發表研究結果還是保密的兩難。","analysis":"此字源自希臘語 'dilemma'，由 'di-' (two) 和 'lemma' (premise, assumption, proposition) 構成。原意為「兩項前提」或「兩難的論證」。在邏輯學中，'dilemma' 指一種論證形式，其中兩項可能的選擇都導向不希望的結果。在現代英語中，'dilemma' 指一種需要做出艱難選擇的處境，通常是在兩種或多種相互矛盾的選項之間，且每個選項都有其不利之處。核心語意是「必須在兩個或多個不理想的選項中做出選擇的困境」。例如，也可指「一項難以解決的問題」。","definition":"1. A situation in which a difficult choice has to be made between two or more alternatives, especially equally undesirable ones.; 2. A problem offering no satisfactory solution.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He faced a dilemma: either tell the truth and hurt his friend, or lie and betray his principles.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他面臨兩難：要么說實話傷害朋友，要么撒謊背叛自己的原則。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company is in a dilemma about whether to expand or consolidate.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司在是否擴張或整合的問題上陷入了困境。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's a classic ethical dilemma.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個經典的道德困境。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The scientist faced the dilemma of publishing his findings or keeping them secret.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位科學家面臨著是發表研究結果還是保密的兩難。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這位科學家面臨著是發表研究結果還是保密的兩難。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5574,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::handle::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He refused to ____ the delicate negotiations.","expectedAnswer":"handle","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He refused to ____ the delicate negotiations.","clozeAnswer":"handle","exampleTranslation":"他拒絕處理這些敏感的談判。","reference":{"eng":"handle","kk":"ˈhændl","tense":"v.","ch":"[['處理'], ['應付'], ['操作'], ['觸摸'], ['交易']]","chEntries":["處理","應付","操作","觸摸","交易"],"practiceMeaning":"他拒絕處理這些敏感的談判。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 \"handlian\"，意為 \"to touch with the hands, to manage\"（用手觸摸，管理），來自 \"hand\"（手）。\"handlian\" 的原始語義是「用手進行的動作」。因此，\"handle\" 的核心語義是「用手接觸、操作或控制」。引申義則非常廣泛：指「處理、應付」（manage or deal with），例如「處理問題」；指「經營、交易」（deal in），例如「處理商品」；指「對待」（treat），例如「小心處理易碎品」；也可用於指「觸摸」或「拿取」。","definition":"1. To touch, hold, or move (something) with the hands; 2. To deal with or manage (a situation or problem); 3. To buy and sell (goods); 4. To treat or behave towards (a person or thing) in a certain way.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She can handle the pressure very well.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她能很好地應付壓力。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please handle the fragile items with care.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請小心處理易碎物品。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The shop handles a wide range of products.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家店經營各式各樣的產品。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He refused to handle the delicate negotiations.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他拒絕處理這些敏感的談判。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他拒絕處理這些敏感的談判。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6180,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::miniature::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She bought a ____ of the Eiffel Tower as a souvenir.","expectedAnswer":"miniature","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She bought a ____ of the Eiffel Tower as a souvenir.","clozeAnswer":"miniature","exampleTranslation":"她買了一個巴黎鐵塔的縮影作為紀念品。","reference":{"eng":"miniature","kk":"ˈmɪniətʃər","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"縮影\"  ],  [    \"微型模型\"  ],  [    \"微型畫\"  ]]","chEntries":["縮影","微型模型","微型畫"],"practiceMeaning":"她買了一個巴黎鐵塔的縮影作為紀念品。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 miniatura，與 miniare「塗色」有關。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作為名詞，其核心語義是指「一個非常小的複製品或模型」。此義項由形容詞「小型的、微型的」名詞化而來，指代具體的微小事物。","definition":"1. a thing that is very small in size; 2. a very small copy of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He collects miniatures of famous landmarks.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他收藏了著名地標的縮影模型。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The museum has a display of medieval miniatures.\",\n    \"ch\": \"博物館展出了中世紀的微型畫。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a perfect miniature of the actual castle.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個實際城堡的完美縮影。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She bought a miniature of the Eiffel Tower as a souvenir.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她買了一個巴黎鐵塔的縮影作為紀念品。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她買了一個巴黎鐵塔的縮影作為紀念品。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4505,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::of::prep","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This is a piece ____ cake.","expectedAnswer":"of","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This is a piece ____ cake.","clozeAnswer":"of","exampleTranslation":"這是一塊蛋糕。","reference":{"eng":"of","kk":"/əv/, /ɒv/","tense":"prep.","ch":"[['...的'], ['關於'], ['屬於'], ['在...之中']]","chEntries":["...的","關於","屬於","在...之中"],"practiceMeaning":"這是一塊蛋糕。","analysis":"源自古英語 of。是一個極其常見且語意複雜的介詞。核心功能是表示「從...分離」、「來源」或「屬於」。引申義極廣，包括所有格、部分、來源、原因、組成等。","definition":"1. Expressing the relationship between a part and a whole; 2. Expressing the relationship between a ruler and those ruled; 3. Expressing the relationship between a subject and its object; 4. Expressing the relationship between an author and his work; 5. Expressing the origin or cause of something; 6. Denoting belonging or a close connection.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The cover of the book is blue.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本書的封面是藍色的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is afraid of the dark.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他害怕黑暗。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A group of students arrived.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一群學生抵達了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a piece of cake.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一塊蛋糕。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是一塊蛋糕。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4514,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::on::prep","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He lectured ____ ancient history.","expectedAnswer":"on","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He lectured ____ ancient history.","clozeAnswer":"on","exampleTranslation":"他講授了古代史。","reference":{"eng":"on","kk":"/ɔːn/","tense":"prep.","ch":"[['在...之上'], ['關於'], ['正在進行（演出、廣播等）'], ['附著於'], ['持續（一段時間）']]","chEntries":["在...之上","關於","正在進行","附著於","持續"],"practiceMeaning":"他講授了古代史。","analysis":"源自古英語 on。是一個表示位置、時間、狀態的多功能介詞。核心語意是「接觸」、「附著」或「覆蓋」。引申義包括「關於」、「處於某種狀態」等。","definition":"1. Physically in contact with and supported by (a surface); 2. Used to indicate the subject or topic of a conversation or piece of writing; 3. Occupying a particular position or place; 4. In the course of being broadcast or performed.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The book is on the table.\",\n    \"ch\": \"書在桌子上。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They are working on a new project.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們正在進行一個新項目。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The concert is on Saturday.\",\n    \"ch\": \"音樂會在星期六。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He lectured on ancient history.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他講授了古代史。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他講授了古代史。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4336,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::pure::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It was ____ luck that he found the keys.","expectedAnswer":"pure","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It was ____ luck that he found the keys.","clozeAnswer":"pure","exampleTranslation":"他找到鑰匙純粹是運氣。","reference":{"eng":"pure","kk":"/pjʊər/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['純粹的；純淨的'], ['（品質、味道等）完全的；不含雜質的'], ['（人）純潔的；無辜的'], ['（僅僅）純粹的；絕對的']]","chEntries":["純粹的","純淨的","完全的","不含雜質的","純潔的","無辜的","絕對的"],"practiceMeaning":"他找到鑰匙純粹是運氣。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'purus'，意為 'clean, pure'。核心意為『沒有混合物』、『沒有污染』。1. 指物質『沒有雜質』，純淨。2. 指『品質、味道』等是原來的、未被稀釋或改變的。3. 指道德上『純潔、無辜』，未受污染。4. 作為副詞的用法（較少見），表示『僅僅、完全』，強調『純粹』的某種狀態。","definition":"not mixed with any other substances or chemicals and therefore not contaminated or polluted; having no negative qualities; without any bad or unwanted elements","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is pure gold.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是純金。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a pure heart.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她有一顆純潔的心。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The artist insisted on using pure colors.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位藝術家堅持使用純色。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was pure luck that he found the keys.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他找到鑰匙純粹是運氣。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他找到鑰匙純粹是運氣。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4115,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::relief::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The statue featured intricate ____ work.","expectedAnswer":"relief","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The statue featured intricate ____ work.","clozeAnswer":"relief","exampleTranslation":"這座雕像以精緻的浮雕工藝為特色。","reference":{"eng":"relief","kk":"/rɪˈliːf/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['緩解', '減輕'], ['救濟', '援助'], ['解脫', '安慰'], ['（雕塑、繪畫等的）浮雕']]","chEntries":["緩解","減輕","救濟","援助","解脫","安慰","浮雕"],"practiceMeaning":"這座雕像以精緻的浮雕工藝為特色。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 relevare，由 re-（再次）+ levare（舉起、減輕）組成。核心概念是「減輕負擔」或「解除痛苦」。引申為疾病的緩解、災難的援助、壓力的釋放，甚至藝術中的凸顯效果。","definition":"1. a feeling of reassurance and relaxation following release from anxiety or distress; 2. assistance to people in a sudden emergency or disaster; 3. the easing or alleviation of a pain or symptom; 4. (in art) the projection of a figure or design from its background","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The medicine provided some relief from her pain.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種藥物減輕了她的疼痛。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"International relief efforts were mobilized after the earthquake.\",\n    \"ch\": \"地震發生後，國際救濟行動被迅速調動起來。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was a great relief to hear that he was safe.\",\n    \"ch\": \"聽到他安然無恙，我感到鬆了一口氣。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The statue featured intricate relief work.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座雕像以精緻的浮雕工藝為特色。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這座雕像以精緻的浮雕工藝為特色。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U5、L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4563,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::reserve::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He spoke with great ____.","expectedAnswer":"reserve","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He spoke with great ____.","clozeAnswer":"reserve","exampleTranslation":"他講話時非常矜持。","reference":{"eng":"reserve","kk":"/rɪˈzɜːrv/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['儲備', '貯備'], ['保留', '預訂'], ['（土地、森林等的）保護區', '禁區'], ['矜持', '拘謹']]","chEntries":["儲備","貯備","保留","預訂","保護區","禁區","矜持","拘謹"],"practiceMeaning":"他講話時非常矜持。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'reservare'，'re-' (back) 和 'servare' (keep - 保留)。核心意思是「留下來」。\n    1. 儲備：為將來需要而保存的東西，如 'food reserves' (食物儲備)。\n    2. 保留、預訂：指將某物為某人或某事留出，如 'a seat reservation' (座位預訂)。\n    3. 保護區：指為保護自然或特定目的而保留的土地，如 'wildlife reserve' (野生動物保護區)。\n    4. 矜持、拘謹：指在言行舉止上的克制和不輕易表露情感，如 'she has a reserve' (她很矜持)。","definition":"1. a supply of something kept ready for use when needed.; 2. an arrangement by which something is kept available for a particular person or purpose.; 3. an area of land set aside for a particular purpose.; 4. self-restraint in the expression of emotion or enthusiasm.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The country has large oil reserves.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該國擁有大量的石油儲備。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I made a reservation for a table at 7 PM.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我預訂了晚上七點的桌子。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This area is a nature reserve.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個地區是一個自然保護區。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He spoke with great reserve.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他講話時非常矜持。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他講話時非常矜持。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4342,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::scale::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company is trying to move up the ____ of quality.","expectedAnswer":"scale","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company is trying to move up the ____ of quality.","clozeAnswer":"scale","exampleTranslation":"公司正試圖提升品質等級。","reference":{"eng":"scale","kk":"/skeɪl/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['規模；尺度'], ['（測量儀器的）刻度'], ['（魚、爬蟲等的）鱗'], ['級別；等級']]","chEntries":["規模","尺度","刻度","鱗","級別","等級"],"practiceMeaning":"公司正試圖提升品質等級。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'scala'，意為 'ladder, staircase, scale'。1. 指事物的『大小、範圍』，即『規模、尺度』。2. 指測量儀器上的『刻度、標尺』。3. 指魚類、爬行動物體表的『鱗片』。4. 指事物系統化的『等級、級別』。","definition":"the size or extent of something; a series of marks or lines at fixed distances on a ruler, thermometer, etc., showing measurements; one of the small, flat plates that cover the skin of fish and reptiles; a system of measuring the size or amount of something","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The project was carried out on a large scale.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個專案是以大規模進行的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The thermometer has a scale from 0 to 100 degrees.\",\n    \"ch\": \"溫度計的刻度從0到100度。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The fish's scales shimmered in the light.\",\n    \"ch\": \"魚鱗在燈光下閃閃發光。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company is trying to move up the scale of quality.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司正試圖提升品質等級。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"公司正試圖提升品質等級。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4701,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::seal::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The rubber ____ around the door was worn out.","expectedAnswer":"seal","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The rubber ____ around the door was worn out.","clozeAnswer":"seal","exampleTranslation":"門周圍的橡膠密封圈已經磨損了。","reference":{"eng":"seal","kk":"/ˈsil/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['印章'], ['封條'], ['（海豹）'], ['密封物']]","chEntries":["印章","封條","密封物"],"practiceMeaning":"門周圍的橡膠密封圈已經磨損了。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 *sigillum*（小標記），與 'sign'（標誌）同源。第一義指用於壓印圖案或文字的工具，常代表權威或認證。第二義指用於封閉或保護的材料。第三義指一種海洋哺乳動物。第四義指用於防止滲漏的裝置。","definition":"1. A stamp or device used to impress a mark or design, typically for authentication or security. 2. A piece of wax or other material used to fasten or secure something. 3. A marine mammal of the order Pinnipedia. 4. A device or material used to prevent the passage of liquid or gas.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The document bore the official seal of the king.\",\n    \"ch\": \"文件蓋有國王的官方印章。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The package was secured with a tamper-proof seal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"包裹用了一個防損封條固定。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We saw seals basking on the rocks.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們看到海豹在岩石上曬太陽。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The rubber seal around the door was worn out.\",\n    \"ch\": \"門周圍的橡膠密封圈已經磨損了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"門周圍的橡膠密封圈已經磨損了。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U17、L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4330,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::substance::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His argument has a lot of ____.","expectedAnswer":"substance","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His argument has a lot of ____.","clozeAnswer":"substance","exampleTranslation":"他的論點很有分量。","reference":{"eng":"substance","kk":"/ˈsʌbstəns/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['物質；材料'], ['實質；要旨'], ['（論點、計畫等的）重要性；意義'], ['（非法）藥物']]","chEntries":["物質","材料","實質","要旨","重要性","意義","藥物"],"practiceMeaning":"他的論點很有分量。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'substantia'，意為 'being, essence, material'，來自 'subsistere' (to stand under, to exist)，由 'sub-' (under) 和 'sistere' (to stand) 構成。核心意為『立足於下』、『存在』。1. 指『物質、材料』，有形的、構成事物的東西。2. 指事物的『實質、要旨』，內在的內容而非形式。3. 指『重要性、意義』，有實質內容，有價值。4. 指具有精神作用的『藥物』，強調其作為一種『物質』對人的影響。","definition":"a type of solid liquid, or gas that is made of a particular combination of atoms and that makes up all matter; the most important part of something; importance or value","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Water is a chemical substance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"水是一種化學物質。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The report lacks substance and is full of vague statements.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這份報告缺乏實質內容，充滿了含糊不清的陳述。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He had a substance abuse problem.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他有藥物濫用問題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His argument has a lot of substance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的論點很有分量。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他的論點很有分量。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5862,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::sustainable::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The renewable resources are ____.","expectedAnswer":"sustainable","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The renewable resources are ____.","clozeAnswer":"sustainable","exampleTranslation":"這些可再生資源是可持續的。","reference":{"eng":"sustainable","kk":"səˈsteɪnəbl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"可持續的\"  ],  [    \"可維持的\"  ],  [    \"能長久支持的\"  ],  [    \"不會枯竭的\"  ]]","chEntries":["可持續的","可維持的","能長久支持的","不會枯竭的"],"practiceMeaning":"這些可再生資源是可持續的。","analysis":"此字由動詞 'sustain' 加上形容詞字尾 '-able' 構成。'Sustain' 源自拉丁語 'sustinere' (to hold up, support)。'-able' 字尾表示「能夠……的」。'Sustainable' 的核心語意是「能夠被維持」、「能夠長期存在或進行」。它特別強調在滿足當前需求的同時，不損害後代滿足其自身需求的發展模式，常用於環境、經濟和社會領域。例如，也可指「不會枯竭的」資源。","definition":"1. Able to be maintained at a certain rate or level.; 2. Relating to or being development that meets the needs of the present without compromising the ability of future generations to meet their own needs.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to develop sustainable energy sources.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要發展可持續能源。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This farming method is more sustainable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種耕作方法更具可持續性。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company aims for sustainable growth.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司旨在實現可持續增長。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The renewable resources are sustainable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這些可再生資源是可持續的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這些可再生資源是可持續的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6200,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::threshold::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Crossing the ____ of the ancient temple, they felt a sense of awe.","expectedAnswer":"threshold","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Crossing the ____ of the ancient temple, they felt a sense of awe.","clozeAnswer":"threshold","exampleTranslation":"跨過古老寺廟的門檻，他們感到一陣敬畏。","reference":{"eng":"threshold","kk":"ˈθreʃhoʊld","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"門檻\"  ],  [    \"入門\"  ],  [    \"閾值\"  ],  [    \"起始點\"  ]]","chEntries":["門檻","入門","閾值","起始點"],"practiceMeaning":"跨過古老寺廟的門檻，他們感到一陣敬畏。","analysis":"此字是古英語 þrescold 或 þerscold 的演變，由 þres（打穀）和 scold（門檻）組合而成，意為「打穀場的門檻」。此字在現代英語中可視為複合詞，但其詞源的準確性有待考證，通常認為是整體詞源演變。作為名詞，其核心語義是指「進入某個地方的入口處的門檻」，引申為「某事的開始、起始點或進入的關卡」。詞源的「打穀場的門檻」引申出「進入」的物理概念，進而發展出「關鍵的起始點」的抽象概念。","definition":"1. the floor or step at the bottom of a doorway; 2. the point at which something begins; 3. the point at which a stimulus is perceived or a response is initiated; 4. the lower limit of a person's ability to perceive or react to a particular stimulus.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He stepped over the threshold into the house.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他跨過門檻走進屋裡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This event marks a new threshold in our relationship.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個事件標誌著我們關係的新開端。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The pain reached a threshold where she could no longer bear it.\",\n    \"ch\": \"疼痛達到了她無法忍受的閾值。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Crossing the threshold of the ancient temple, they felt a sense of awe.\",\n    \"ch\": \"跨過古老寺廟的門檻，他們感到一陣敬畏。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"跨過古老寺廟的門檻，他們感到一陣敬畏。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6255,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::throne::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The bishop returned to his ____ after the synod.","expectedAnswer":"throne","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The bishop returned to his ____ after the synod.","clozeAnswer":"throne","exampleTranslation":"主教在宗教會議後回到了他的座席。","reference":{"eng":"throne","kk":"θron","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"寶座\"  ],  [    \"王位\"  ],  [    \"王權\"  ],  [    \"（主教等的）座席；高位\"  ]]","chEntries":["寶座","王位","王權","座席","高位"],"practiceMeaning":"主教在宗教會議後回到了他的座席。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 þrōn，後受古法語 trône 影響，最終可追溯至拉丁語 thronus，而拉丁語又源自希臘語 thronos（椅子；寶座）。構詞上，希臘語 thronos 可能與 ethelein（升高）有關，暗示著高高在上的位置。此字沒有可在現代英語中透明拆解的生產性字首或字尾，應視為一個整體詞源演變。核心語義為君主、主教或神祇所坐的特殊椅子，引申為國家或權力的象徵，故可表示王位、王權或至高無上的地位。常見於政治、宗教及文學語境。作為主教的座席，也引申為高位。","definition":"1. a large, stately chair on which a sovereign or other dignitary sits; 2. the office, power, or dignity of a sovereign or bishop; 3. a seat of honor or authority.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The king sat on his ornate throne.\",\n    \"ch\": \"國王坐在他華麗的寶座上。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She ascended the throne at the age of twenty-five.\",\n    \