results.","expectedAnswer":"variation","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We observed a slight ____ in the results.","clozeAnswer":"variation","exampleTranslation":"我們觀察到結果有輕微的差異。","reference":{"eng":"variation","kk":"ˌveəriˈeɪʃn","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"變化\"  ],  [    \"差異\"  ],  [    \"變異\"  ],  [    \"變奏\"  ]]","chEntries":["變化","差異","變異","變奏"],"practiceMeaning":"我們觀察到結果有輕微的差異。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'variatio'，是 'variare' (to change, alter) 的名詞形式。'Variare' 來自 'varius' (various, diverse)。'-ion' 是常見的名詞字尾，表示「過程」、「狀態」或「結果」。'Variation' 的核心語意是指「改變」、「差異」或「一種與標準不同的形式」。它可以指事物在數量、程度、形式或性質上的不同，也可以指物種的遺傳變異，或音樂中的主題變奏。例如，也可指「一種變奏形式」。","definition":"1. A change or difference between two or more similar things.; 2. The process or result of varying.; 3. A deviation from a standard or norm.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There are noticeable variations in temperature.\",\n    \"ch\": \"溫度存在明顯的差異。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Genetic variation is essential for evolution.\",\n    \"ch\": \"遺傳變異對演化至關重要。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The orchestra performed a variation on the theme.\",\n    \"ch\": \"樂團演奏了該主題的變奏曲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We observed a slight variation in the results.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們觀察到結果有輕微的差異。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們觀察到結果有輕微的差異。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4511,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::a::art","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"I saw ____ dog in the park.","expectedAnswer":"a","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"I saw ____ dog in the park.","clozeAnswer":"a","exampleTranslation":"我在公園裡看到了一隻狗。","reference":{"eng":"a","kk":"/ə/, /eɪ/","tense":"art.","ch":"[['一個']]","chEntries":["一個"],"practiceMeaning":"我在公園裡看到了一隻狗。","analysis":"不定冠詞，源自古英語 ān，意為「一」。用於單數可數名詞前，表示「一個」、「某個」、「任何一個」。","definition":"1. Used before singular countable nouns to refer to a non-specific or non-particular member of a group or category; 2. Used when mentioning something for the first time.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I saw a dog in the park.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我在公園裡看到了一隻狗。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a doctor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是一位醫生。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我在公園裡看到了一隻狗。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4285,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::a-narrow-alley::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He walked down ____, looking for the restaurant.","expectedAnswer":"a narrow alley","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He walked down ____, looking for the restaurant.","clozeAnswer":"a narrow alley","exampleTranslation":"他沿著一條狹窄的小巷走，尋找那家餐廳。","reference":{"eng":"a narrow alley","kk":"/ə ˈnɛroʊ ˈæli/","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['一條狹窄的小巷']]","chEntries":["一條狹窄的小巷"],"practiceMeaning":"他沿著一條狹窄的小巷走，尋找那家餐廳。","analysis":"由不定冠詞 'a'、形容詞 'narrow'（狹窄的）和名詞 'alley'（小巷）組成。'A narrow alley' 描述的是一個「狹窄的、兩側有建築物的小通道」，強調其空間的侷促。","definition":"a small, narrow passage between buildings.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He walked down a narrow alley, looking for the restaurant.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他沿著一條狹窄的小巷走，尋找那家餐廳。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The team found a hidden entrance in a narrow alley.\",\n    \"ch\": \"隊伍在一個狹窄的小巷裡發現了一個隱藏的入口。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他沿著一條狹窄的小巷走，尋找那家餐廳。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4297,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::a-pile-of::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She found ____ old letters in the attic.","expectedAnswer":"a pile of","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She found ____ old letters in the attic.","clozeAnswer":"a pile of","exampleTranslation":"她在閣樓裡找到一堆舊信件。","reference":{"eng":"a pile of","kk":"/ə paɪl əv/","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['一堆...'], ['許多...']]","chEntries":["一堆...","許多..."],"practiceMeaning":"她在閣樓裡找到一堆舊信件。","analysis":"由不定冠詞 'a'、名詞 'pile'（堆）和介詞 'of'（的）組成。'A pile of' 用於指代「許多、大量的某物，堆積在一起」或「許多不整齊的某物」。","definition":"a heap of things laid or lying one on top of another; a large quantity of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She found a pile of old letters in the attic.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在閣樓裡找到一堆舊信件。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He had a pile of work to complete before the deadline.\",\n    \"ch\": \"截止日期前他有一大堆工作要完成。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她在閣樓裡找到一堆舊信件。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4648,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::a-ray-of-sun::idiom","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ broke through the clouds.","expectedAnswer":"A ray of sun","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ broke through the clouds.","clozeAnswer":"A ray of sun","exampleTranslation":"一線陽光穿破雲層。","reference":{"eng":"a ray of sun","kk":"/ə reɪ əv sʌn/","tense":"idiom","ch":"[['一線陽光']]","chEntries":["一線陽光"],"practiceMeaning":"一線陽光穿破雲層。","analysis":"此為固定片語。'Ray' (射線、光線) 是指從光源發出的直線光束。'Sun' (太陽) 是光源。整個片語描繪了陽光穿透雲層或陰影，照射下來的微小光束，常被用來比喻微弱的希望或光明。","definition":"a thin line of light from the sun.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A ray of sun broke through the clouds.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一線陽光穿破雲層。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"In the darkness, a ray of sun offered some hope.\",\n    \"ch\": \"在黑暗中，一線陽光帶來了一絲希望。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"一線陽光穿破雲層。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4286,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::a-shopping-paradise::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Dubai is often described as ____ for luxury goods.","expectedAnswer":"a shopping paradise","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Dubai is often described as ____ for luxury goods.","clozeAnswer":"a shopping paradise","exampleTranslation":"杜拜常被形容為奢侈品的購物天堂。","reference":{"eng":"a shopping paradise","kk":"/ə ˈʃɑːpɪŋ ˈpærədaɪs/","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['購物天堂']]","chEntries":["購物天堂"],"practiceMeaning":"杜拜常被形容為奢侈品的購物天堂。","analysis":"結合了動名詞 'shopping'（購物）和名詞 'paradise'（天堂、樂園）。'A shopping paradise' 指一個「提供極多樣化、高品質商品，且購物體驗極佳的地方」，讓熱愛購物的人感到非常滿足。","definition":"a place where people can buy a very wide range of goods, or enjoy shopping very much.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Dubai is often described as a shopping paradise for luxury goods.\",\n    \"ch\": \"杜拜常被形容為奢侈品的購物天堂。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"With its numerous boutiques, the city is a shopping paradise for fashion lovers.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座城市擁有眾多精品店，是時尚愛好者的購物天堂。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"杜拜常被形容為奢侈品的購物天堂。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4351,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::a-stormy-argument::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They had ____ about the division of property.","expectedAnswer":"a stormy argument","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They had ____ about the division of property.","clozeAnswer":"a stormy argument","exampleTranslation":"他們為了財產分割而進行了一場激烈的爭吵。","reference":{"eng":"a stormy argument","kk":"None","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['一場激烈的爭吵']]","chEntries":["一場激烈的爭吵"],"practiceMeaning":"他們為了財產分割而進行了一場激烈的爭吵。","analysis":"此為片語分析。'stormy' (adj.) 源自 'storm' (n.)，意為『暴風雨的』，比喻『激烈的、動盪的』。'argument' (n.) 源自拉丁語 'argumentum'，指『爭論、辯論』。兩者結合，形容一場充滿激烈情緒、口角、衝突的爭吵。","definition":"an argument that is very angry and full of strong feelings or disagreements","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They had a stormy argument about the division of property.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們為了財產分割而進行了一場激烈的爭吵。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The committee meeting ended with a stormy argument.\",\n    \"ch\": \"委員會會議以一場激烈的爭論結束。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們為了財產分割而進行了一場激烈的爭吵。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4583,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::a-wildlife-reserve::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They visited ____ to see elephants and lions.","expectedAnswer":"a wildlife reserve","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They visited ____ to see elephants and lions.","clozeAnswer":"a wildlife reserve","exampleTranslation":"他們參觀了一個野生動物保護區，看到了大象和獅子。","reference":{"eng":"a wildlife reserve","kk":"/ə ˈwaɪldlaɪf rɪˈzɜːrv/","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['野生動物保護區']]","chEntries":["野生動物保護區"],"practiceMeaning":"他們參觀了一個野生動物保護區，看到了大象和獅子。","analysis":"此片語由 'a' (不定冠詞), 'wildlife' (野生動物) 和 'reserve' (保護區) 組成。 'reserve' 源自拉丁語 'reservare' (to keep back - 留存)，在此指為特定目的（保護野生動植物）而保留的土地。 'wildlife' 指未經馴化的動植物。","definition":"1. an area of land where animals and plants are protected.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They visited a wildlife reserve to see elephants and lions.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們參觀了一個野生動物保護區，看到了大象和獅子。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government established a wildlife reserve to protect endangered species.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府設立了一個野生動物保護區來保護瀕危物種。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們參觀了一個野生動物保護區，看到了大象和獅子。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5353,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l1::abandon::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They had to ____ their car in the snow.","expectedAnswer":"abandon","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They had to ____ their car in the snow.","clozeAnswer":"abandon","exampleTranslation":"他們不得不把車子丟在雪中。","reference":{"eng":"abandon","kk":"əˈbændən","tense":"v.","ch":"[['拋棄'], ['放棄'], ['離棄']]","chEntries":["拋棄","放棄","離棄"],"practiceMeaning":"他們不得不把車子丟在雪中。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 abandonner，來自 an-（在……情況下）+ bandon（法語的控制權、禁止）。原始概念為「脫離控制」、「在沒有保護的情況下」。構詞上，a- 是加強語氣或表示「給予」的字首，bandon- 來自 banna（命令、禁止）。核心語意是「將某物置於無人管轄、無人保護的狀態」，引申為「拋棄」、「放棄」或「離棄」。","definition":"to give up completely a course of action, a practice, or a way of thinking; to cease to support or look after (someone); desert.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They had to abandon their car in the snow.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們不得不把車子丟在雪中。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He decided to abandon his dreams of becoming a musician.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他決定放棄成為音樂家的夢想。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們不得不把車子丟在雪中。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5114,"wordRef":"字彙王::u62::abnormal::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His behavior was ____ for a child his age.","expectedAnswer":"abnormal","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His behavior was ____ for a child his age.","clozeAnswer":"abnormal","exampleTranslation":"他的行為對他這個年紀的孩子來說很不尋常。","reference":{"eng":"abnormal","kk":"æbˈnɔːrməl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['反常的'], ['變態的'], ['不規則的']]","chEntries":["反常的","變態的","不規則的"],"practiceMeaning":"他的行為對他這個年紀的孩子來說很不尋常。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 abnormalis，由 ab-（離開、遠離）+ norma（規則、標準）+ -al（形容詞字尾）組成。ab- 來自印歐語系 *apo-，意為「離開、遠離」。norma 來自拉丁語，意為「角尺、規範、標準」，可能與 *ǵnō-（知道、辨認）有關。-al 是常見的拉丁形容詞字尾，用於將名詞轉為形容詞。核心語意為「偏離標準」或「不符合規則」，由此引申出「反常的、不尋常的、變態的」等義。","definition":"deviating from what is normal or usual; unusual; irregular; pathological.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His behavior was abnormal for a child his age.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的行為對他這個年紀的孩子來說很不尋常。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The test results showed some abnormal readings.\",\n    \"ch\": \"檢測結果顯示了一些異常讀數。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他的行為對他這個年紀的孩子來說很不尋常。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U62"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3199,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::abstract::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It is difficult to ____ meaning from such complex data.","expectedAnswer":"abstract","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It is difficult to ____ meaning from such complex data.","clozeAnswer":"abstract","exampleTranslation":"很難從如此複雜的數據中提取出意義。","reference":{"eng":"abstract","kk":"/æbˈstrækt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['提取'], ['抽取出'], ['摘要'], ['使抽象化']]","chEntries":["提取","抽取出","摘要","使抽象化"],"practiceMeaning":"很難從如此複雜的數據中提取出意義。","analysis":"動詞形式，強調將某事物（尤其是數據、思想或物質）從更廣泛的整體中分離出來，形成獨立的部分或概念。詞源同上，從 'drawn away' 引申為『抽出』。","definition":"1. to consider something theoretically or separately from something else; 2. to draw out or remove; 3. to make an abstract, summary, or digest of.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It is difficult to abstract meaning from such complex data.\",\n    \"ch\": \"很難從如此複雜的數據中提取出意義。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to abstract the key findings for the report.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要為報告提煉出關鍵發現。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The philosopher tried to abstract principles of morality.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位哲學家試圖歸納出道德原則。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"很難從如此複雜的數據中提取出意義。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U41"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5425,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::abundance::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The region is known for its ____ of natural resources.","expectedAnswer":"abundance","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The region is known for its ____ of natural resources.","clozeAnswer":"abundance","exampleTranslation":"該地區以其豐富的自然資源而聞名。","reference":{"eng":"abundance","kk":"əˈbʌndəns","tense":"n.","ch":"[['豐富'], ['充裕'], ['大量'], ['豐盛']]","chEntries":["豐富","充裕","大量","豐盛"],"practiceMeaning":"該地區以其豐富的自然資源而聞名。","analysis":"此字為派生詞，由形容詞 \"abundant\" 加上名詞化字尾 \"-ance\" 構成。\"abundant\" 源自拉丁語 \"abundans\"，是動詞 \"abundare\" 的現在分詞，意為\"充溢\"、\"豐富\"。\"abundare\" 由 \"ab-\" (離開、遠離，在此表示\"過多\"或\"溢出\") 和 \"undare\" (波浪般流動) 構成，\"undare\" 又源於 \"unda\" (波浪)。構詞上，\"ab-\" 提供了「過量」的語意，\"undare\" 提供了「流動」的圖像，整體表示「如波浪般湧出、充溢」。字尾 \"-ance\" 將形容詞的「充裕」狀態轉化為抽象名詞，表示「豐富」、「充裕」或「大量」的狀態或性質。","definition":"a large quantity of something; a great amount of something; plenty; profusion; more than enough.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The region is known for its abundance of natural resources.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該地區以其豐富的自然資源而聞名。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was an abundance of food at the party.\",\n    \"ch\": \"派對上有豐富的食物。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The abundance of information online can be overwhelming.\",\n    \"ch\": \"網路上豐富的資訊可能會讓人不知所措。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該地區以其豐富的自然資源而聞名。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4616,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::acceptable::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The proposal is ____ to all parties.","expectedAnswer":"acceptable","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The proposal is ____ to all parties.","clozeAnswer":"acceptable","exampleTranslation":"這項提議對所有相關方來說都是可以接受的。","reference":{"eng":"acceptable","kk":"/əkˈseptəbəl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['可接受的'], ['令人滿意的'], ['尚可的']]","chEntries":["可接受的","令人滿意的","尚可的"],"practiceMeaning":"這項提議對所有相關方來說都是可以接受的。","analysis":"由 'accept' (接受) + '-able' (能夠...的) 組成。'Accept' 源自拉丁語 'accipere' (接受、拿到)。此字指事物達到某種最低標準，雖然不一定完美，但足以被容忍、接受或認為可以。","definition":"satisfactory or good enough; able to be accepted.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The proposal is acceptable to all parties.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這項提議對所有相關方來說都是可以接受的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His performance was acceptable, but not outstanding.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的表現尚可，但並不突出。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這項提議對所有相關方來說都是可以接受的。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3261,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::accountant::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"I need to hire an ____ to help with my taxes.","expectedAnswer":"accountant","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"I need to hire an ____ to help with my taxes.","clozeAnswer":"accountant","exampleTranslation":"我需要聘請一位會計師來幫我處理稅務。","reference":{"eng":"accountant","kk":"/əˈkaʊntənt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['會計師']]","chEntries":["會計師"],"practiceMeaning":"我需要聘請一位會計師來幫我處理稅務。","analysis":"源自 'account' (帳目，敘述)，加上 '-ant'（從事某事的人）後綴。指專門負責管理和審核帳目的人。","definition":"a person whose job is to keep the financial accounts of a business and to check them.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I need to hire an accountant to help with my taxes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我需要聘請一位會計師來幫我處理稅務。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company's accountant discovered a discrepancy in the records.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司的會計師發現記錄中有出入。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我需要聘請一位會計師來幫我處理稅務。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5556,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::accuracy::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of the data is crucial for our research.","expectedAnswer":"accuracy","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of the data is crucial for our research.","clozeAnswer":"accuracy","exampleTranslation":"這些數據的準確性對我們的研究至關重要。","reference":{"eng":"accuracy","kk":"ˈækjərəsi","tense":"n.","ch":"[['精確度'], ['準確性'], ['正確性']]","chEntries":["精確度","準確性","正確性"],"practiceMeaning":"這些數據的準確性對我們的研究至關重要。","analysis":"此字由 \"accurate\" 加上名詞化字尾 \"-cy\" 構成。\"accurate\" 源自拉丁語 \"accurrere\"，意為 \"to run to, run up\"（跑到，跑近），由 \"ad-\"（to, toward，向，朝）和 \"currere\"（to run，跑）組成。\"accurrere\" 的引申義是指「達到目標」，因此 \"accurate\" 指「能夠精確地達到目標」或「符合標準」。\"-cy\" 是構成抽象名詞的字尾，表示「狀態、品質」。因此，\"accuracy\" 的核心語義是「達到目標、符合標準的品質或狀態」，即「精確性」或「準確性」。","definition":"1. The condition or quality of being accurate; freedom from error or defect; 2. The degree to which the result of a measurement, calculation, or specification conforms to the correct or a predicted result.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The accuracy of the data is crucial for our research.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這些數據的準確性對我們的研究至關重要。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The pilot maintained a high level of accuracy in navigation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"飛行員在導航中保持了高度的精確性。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to ensure the accuracy of the translation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要確保翻譯的準確性。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這些數據的準確性對我們的研究至關重要。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4562,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::accurate::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The report provided an ____ account of the events.","expectedAnswer":"accurate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The report provided an ____ account of the events.","clozeAnswer":"accurate","exampleTranslation":"這份報告提供了對事件的準確敘述。","reference":{"eng":"accurate","kk":"/ˈækjərət/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['準確的', '精確的'], ['（陳述、測量等）正確的']]","chEntries":["準確的","精確的","正確的"],"practiceMeaning":"這份報告提供了對事件的準確敘述。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'accuratus'，'ad-' (to) 和 'cura' (care - 關心、小心) 的組合。核心概念是「非常小心地」進行，從而達到精確。\n    1. 準確的、精確的：指測量、數據、預測等非常接近真實值或目標。\n    2. 正確的：指陳述或判斷符合事實。","definition":"1. (of information, measurements, etc.) precise; exact.; 2. correct in all details; error-free.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The report provided an accurate account of the events.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這份報告提供了對事件的準確敘述。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His estimate of the cost was remarkably accurate.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對費用的估計非常準確。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need accurate data to make a decision.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要準確的數據來做決定。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這份報告提供了對事件的準確敘述。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5337,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l1::acquire::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He managed to ____ a valuable collection of stamps.","expectedAnswer":"acquire","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He managed to ____ a valuable collection of stamps.","clozeAnswer":"acquire","exampleTranslation":"他設法獲得了大量珍貴的郵票收藏。","reference":{"eng":"acquire","kk":"əˈkwaɪər","tense":"v.","ch":"[['獲得'], ['學到'], ['購得']]","chEntries":["獲得","學到","購得"],"practiceMeaning":"他設法獲得了大量珍貴的郵票收藏。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 aquerre，來自拉丁語 adquirere，由 ad-（朝向、加上）+ quirere（尋找、獲得）組成， quirere 為 quaerere（尋找、詢問）的變體。構詞上，ad- 表示「朝向」，quir- 是字根，表示「尋找、獲得」。原始語意為「主動尋找並獲得」。現代語意涵蓋「透過努力或購買獲得」、「學到（知識、技能）」等。","definition":"to gain something by purchase or by birth, or by effort, skill, or the like; to learn or develop a skill or habit.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He managed to acquire a valuable collection of stamps.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他設法