形容詞，表示「充滿……的」或「具有……特性的」。因此，'adventurous' 的核心語意是「喜歡經歷或尋求冒險」，引申為「大膽的、樂於嘗試新事物」。","definition":"1. Eager to take risks or to embark on new, daring ventures; bold; daring; brave; intrepid; courageous; valiant.; 2. Characterized by or involving adventure; exciting; hazardous; risky; dangerous.; 3. Willing to undertake a risky or daring personal project, enterprise, or undertaking.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She was an adventurous child who loved exploring the woods behind her house.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是個熱愛探索屋後森林的冒險兒童。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They planned an adventurous journey through the Amazon rainforest.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們計劃了一次穿越亞馬遜雨林的冒險旅程。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has an adventurous spirit and is always looking for new challenges.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他有冒險精神，總是在尋找新的挑戰。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她是個熱愛探索屋後森林的冒險兒童。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6105,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::adverse::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ weather conditions","expectedAnswer":"adverse","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ weather conditions","clozeAnswer":"adverse","exampleTranslation":"惡劣的天氣狀況","reference":{"eng":"adverse","kk":"ˈædvɜːrs","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"不利的\"  ],  [    \"有害的\"  ],  [    \"敵對的\"  ],  [    \"相反的\"  ]]","chEntries":["不利的","有害的","敵對的","相反的"],"practiceMeaning":"惡劣的天氣狀況","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 adversus，意為「朝向；反對」。構詞上，ad- 是方向字首，表示「朝向」或「趨向」；versus 則是拉丁語 vertō（轉動）的過去分詞，意為「轉向」。因此，adverse 的核心語義是「轉向相反方向」，引申為「不利的、敵對的、相反的」。此形容詞用於描述條件、影響、結果等，表示對某事造成負面影響或阻礙。其語意演變是從具體的「面對面、反向」到抽象的「不利、有害」。","definition":"1. preventing success or development; harmful; unfavorable; 2. opposing or contrary.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"adverse weather conditions\",\n    \"ch\": \"惡劣的天氣狀況\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The drug had adverse side effects.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種藥物有不良副作用。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He had to overcome adverse circumstances.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他不得不