出（時間、精力、金錢）而造成困難。","definition":"1. to have enough money to pay for something; 2. to provide or supply (something, esp. an opportunity or advantage); 3. to be able to bear or endure (the cost, strain, etc.).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We cannot afford to buy a new car.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們買不起新車。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This policy affords protection to citizens.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這項政策為公民提供了保護。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Can you afford to take a week off?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你承受得起請一週假嗎？\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們買不起新車。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4508,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::after::prep","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The meeting will be held ____ lunch.","expectedAnswer":"after","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The meeting will be held ____ lunch.","clozeAnswer":"after","exampleTranslation":"會議將在午餐後舉行。","reference":{"eng":"after","kk":"/ˈæftər/","tense":"prep.","ch":"[['在...之後'], ['跟隨']]","chEntries":["在...之後","跟隨"],"practiceMeaning":"會議將在午餐後舉行。","analysis":"源自古英語 æfter。是一個表示時間、順序或位置的介詞。核心語意是「緊隨其後」。","definition":"1. At a time subsequent to (a particular event or time); 2. Following behind in order or position.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The meeting will be held after lunch.\",\n    \"ch\": \"會議將在午餐後舉行。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He arrived shortly after.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他不久後就到了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She always follows in her mother's footsteps.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她總是追隨她母親的腳步。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"會議將在午餐後舉行。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5505,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l5::agency::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He signed with a talent ____.","expectedAnswer":"agency","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He signed with a talent ____.","clozeAnswer":"agency","exampleTranslation":"他簽約了一家演藝經紀公司。","reference":{"eng":"agency","kk":"ˈeɪdʒənsi","tense":"n.","ch":"[['代理機構'], ['經紀公司'], ['情報機構'], ['作用'], ['效力'], ['媒介']]","chEntries":["代理機構","經紀公司","情報機構","作用","效力","媒介"],"practiceMeaning":"他簽約了一家演藝經紀公司。","analysis":"此字由 'agent' 加上抽象名詞字尾 '-cy' 構成，表示『代理人的職位、權力或機構』。'-cy' 源自拉丁語 '-tia' 或 '-cia'，用於形成名詞，表示狀態、品質或職位。因此，'agency' 的核心語義是與 'agent' 相關的抽象概念或場所。從「代理權」延伸出「代理機構」（如旅行社、經紀公司），再引申為「情報機構」。此外，它也表示「起作用的能力」或「作用力」，強調的是「執行者」或「媒介物」所展現出的效力。","definition":"a business or organization that provides a particular service; the capacity to act or exert power; an organization that operates on behalf of another.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He signed with a talent agency.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他簽約了一家演藝經紀公司。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The agency reported a significant increase in tourism.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該旅遊局報告稱旅遊業顯著增長。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to understand the agency of the virus.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要了解這種病毒的作用。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他簽約了一家演藝經紀公司。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6106,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::agenda::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The first item on the ____ is the budget report.","expectedAnswer":"agenda","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The first item on the ____ is the budget report.","clozeAnswer":"agenda","exampleTranslation":"議程上的第一項是預算報告。","reference":{"eng":"agenda","kk":"əˈdʒɛndə","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"議程\"  ],  [    \"待辦事項\"  ],  [    \"計劃\"  ],  [    \"潛藏目的\"  ]]","chEntries":["議程","待辦事項","計劃","潛藏目的"],"practiceMeaning":"議程上的第一項是預算報告。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 agenda，是動詞 agere（做；行動）的女性複數主格形式，意為「該做的事」。原為教務用語，指「應當處理的事項」。在現代英語中，agenda 主要指會議或討論的「議程」，即計劃要討論的事項列表。也可引申為某人或組織隱藏的「計劃」或「目的」，帶有負面含義。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆，應視為整體詞源演變。其語意演變是從「該做的事」到具體的「會議議程」，再到抽象的「計劃、目的」。","definition":"1. a list of things to be done or discussed at a meeting; 2. a set of principles or beliefs that guide someone's actions or a group's behavior; a hidden plan.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The first item on the agenda is the budget report.\",\n    \"ch\": \"議程上的第一項是預算報告。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They have their own political agenda.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們有自己的政治議程。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to set the agenda for tomorrow's meeting.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要擬定明天會議的議程。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"議程上的第一項是預算報告。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6107,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::aggression::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The country was accused of unprovoked ____.","expectedAnswer":"aggression","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The country was accused of unprovoked ____.","clozeAnswer":"aggression","exampleTranslation":"該國被指控發動無端侵略。","reference":{"eng":"aggression","kk":"əˈɡrɛʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"侵略\"  ],  [    \"攻擊性\"  ],  [    \"敵意\"  ],  [    \"侵犯\"  ]]","chEntries":["侵略","攻擊性","敵意","侵犯"],"practiceMeaning":"該國被指控發動無端侵略。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 aggressiō，由動詞 adgredī（接近；攻擊）演變而來。構詞上，ad- 是方向字首，表示「朝向」；gredī 來自 gradī（行走，前進），與 gradus（步；等級）有關。因此，aggression 的核心語義是「朝向某物前進並發動攻擊」。此名詞表示行為上的主動攻擊、侵略，或態度上的敵意、攻擊性。語意演變是從具體的「走上前去攻擊」到抽象的「侵略性行為或態度」。","definition":"1. hostile or violent behavior or attitudes toward another, especially in readiness or shown willingness to attack; 2. the act of attacking or invading.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The country was accused of unprovoked aggression.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該國被指控發動無端侵略。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His aggressive behavior was a result of insecurity.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他具攻擊性的行為源於不安全感。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The team displayed great aggression on the field.\",\n    \"ch\": \"球隊在場上展現了極大的拼勁。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該國被指控發動無端侵略。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6150,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::agony::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He died in ____ after the accident.","expectedAnswer":"agony","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He died in ____ after the accident.","clozeAnswer":"agony","exampleTranslation":"事故發生後，他痛苦地死去。","reference":{"eng":"agony","kk":"ˈæɡəni","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"極度痛苦\"  ],  [    \"煎熬\"  ],  [    \"苦惱\"  ],  [    \"臨死前的掙扎\"  ]]","chEntries":["極度痛苦","煎熬","苦惱","臨死前的掙扎"],"practiceMeaning":"事故發生後，他痛苦地死去。","analysis":"此字源自古希臘語 ἀγωνία (agōnia)，意為「掙扎、角鬥、痛苦」，與 ἀγών (agōn)「競技、集會、掙扎」同源。它進入中古英語 via 古法語 agonie。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，應視為整體詞源演變。作為名詞，其核心語義是極度的身體或精神痛苦，常與死亡前的掙扎或嚴重的心理煎熬聯繫。此義項由古希臘語中「掙扎」的含義演變而來。","definition":"1. extreme physical or mental suffering; 2. the pain of childbirth.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He died in agony after the accident.\",\n    \"ch\": \"事故發生後，他痛苦地死去。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She was in agony for days before the diagnosis was made.\",\n    \"ch\": \"在做出診斷的前幾天，她一直承受著極度的痛苦。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The final moments of his life were filled with agony.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他生命的最後時刻充滿了痛苦的掙扎。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"事故發生後，他痛苦地死去。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5686,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l9::alcohol::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The drink contained a high percentage of ____.","expectedAnswer":"alcohol","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The drink contained a high percentage of ____.","clozeAnswer":"alcohol","exampleTranslation":"這杯飲料含有高比例的酒精。","reference":{"eng":"alcohol","kk":"ˈælkəhɒl","tense":"n.","ch":"[['酒精'], ['酒']]","chEntries":["酒精","酒"],"practiceMeaning":"這杯飲料含有高比例的酒精。","analysis":"此字源自阿拉伯語 al-kuḥl，最初指一種細粉狀的化妝品（如眼影粉），後來指「純淨物」或「蒸餾物」，最終用於指代「乙醇」。'al-' 是阿拉伯語定冠詞「the」。'kuḥl' 源自古希臘語 kôlon，指「膽汁」，也可能與「蒸餾」過程相關。構詞上，此字是一個直接借詞，語意演變從「精細粉末」到「蒸餾物」，再專指「乙醇」。","definition":"a colorless volatile flammable liquid which is produced by the normal fermentation of sugars and is the intoxicating constituent of wine, beer, spirits and other drinks; an intoxicating liquor.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The drink contained a high percentage of alcohol.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這杯飲料含有高比例的酒精。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Excessive consumption of alcohol can be harmful.\",\n    \"ch\": \"過量飲酒會對身體有害。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這杯飲料含有高比例的酒精。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5687,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l9::alcoholic::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He has an ____ problem.","expectedAnswer":"alcoholic","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He has an ____ problem.","clozeAnswer":"alcoholic","exampleTranslation":"他有酗酒的問題。","reference":{"eng":"alcoholic","kk":"ˌælkəˈhɒlɪk","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['酒精的'], ['患酒精中毒的'], ['酗酒的']]","chEntries":["酒精的","患酒精中毒的","酗酒的"],"practiceMeaning":"他有酗酒的問題。","analysis":"此字由名詞 'alcohol' 加上形容詞化後綴 '-ic' 構成。'alcohol' 是阿拉伯語 al-kuḥl 的音譯。'-ic' 後綴用於將名詞轉化為形容詞，表示「與……有關的」或「具有……特性的」。因此，'alcoholic' 主要指「與酒精有關的」，包括「由酒精引起的」（如酒精中毒）或「與過量飲酒有關的」（如酗酒的）。","definition":"relating to or caused by alcohol; suffering from alcoholism.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has an alcoholic problem.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他有酗酒的問題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The effects of alcoholic beverages are well-known.\",\n    \"ch\": \"酒精飲料的影響是眾所周知的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他有酗酒的問題。","sourceName":"龍騰課本、字彙王","unitName":"L9、U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6152,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::alien::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He has an ____ culture and language.","expectedAnswer":"alien","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He has an ____ culture and language.","clozeAnswer":"alien","exampleTranslation":"他有著外來的文化和語言。","reference":{"eng":"alien","kk":"ˈeɪliən","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"外國的\"  ],  [    \"外來的\"  ],  [    \"陌生的\"  ],  [    \"不協調的\"  ],  [    \"不適合的\"  ]]","chEntries":["外國的","外來的","陌生的","不協調的","不適合的"],"practiceMeaning":"他有著外來的文化和語言。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 alienus，意為「別人的、外國的、不相干的」。它進入中古英語 via 古法語 alien。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，應視為整體詞源演變。作為形容詞，核心語義是「來自另一國家的」或「與之無關的」。從「外國的」進一步引申出「陌生的、不熟悉的」，再到「不協調的、不適合的」。這些義項都圍繞著「非本地的、不屬於的」概念發展。","definition":"1. belonging to a foreign country or countries; 2. unfamiliar and disturbing; 3. not belonging to a particular place; 4. completely different.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has an alien culture and language.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他有著外來的文化和語言。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The news was alien to him.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這消息對他來說很陌生。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Such behavior is alien to our traditions.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種行為與我們的傳統不符。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The design felt alien to the rest of the house.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個設計與房子的其他部分顯得格格不入。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他有著外來的文化和語言。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5454,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::all-in-all::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____, it was a successful event.","expectedAnswer":"All in all","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____, it was a successful event.","clozeAnswer":"All in all","exampleTranslation":"總而言之，這是一次成功的活動。","reference":{"eng":"all in all","kk":"ɔːl ɪn ɔːl","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['總而言之'], ['總體來說']]","chEntries":["總而言之","總體來說"],"practiceMeaning":"總而言之，這是一次成功的活動。","analysis":"此片語是一個慣用語，由不定代名詞 \"all\"，介系詞 \"in\"，以及不定代名詞 \"all\" 重複構成。其含義是考慮了所有相關因素後，對整體情況做出總結或判斷，與 \"as a whole\" 和 \"in conclusion\" 類似。","definition":"considering everything; taking everything into account.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"All in all, it was a successful event.\",\n    \"ch\": \"總而言之，這是一次成功的活動。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The food was a bit expensive, but all in all, we had a good time.\",\n    \"ch\": \"食物有點貴，但總體來說，我們玩得很開心。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"總而言之，這是一次成功的活動。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4238,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::alley::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The children played hide-and-seek in the narrow ____ behind the shops.","expectedAnswer":"alley","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The children played hide-and-seek in the narrow ____ behind the shops.","clozeAnswer":"alley","exampleTranslation":"孩子們躲在商店後面的狹窄小巷裡玩捉迷藏。","reference":{"eng":"alley","kk":"/ˈæli/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['小巷'], ['弄']]","chEntries":["小巷","弄"],"practiceMeaning":"孩子們躲在商店後面的狹窄小巷裡玩捉迷藏。","analysis":"源自古法語 'ale', 'allee'，意為「走道、通道」。最初指「經過或走到某處的通道」，後來演變成狹窄的後街或小巷。詞源與「行走」的動作有關。","definition":"a narrow passage between buildings or houses","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The children played hide-and-seek in the narrow alley behind the shops.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子們躲在商店後面的狹窄小巷裡玩捉迷藏。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He emerged from the dark alley.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他從黑暗的小巷裡走出來。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"孩子們躲在商店後面的狹窄小巷裡玩捉迷藏。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6153,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::alliance::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The two countries formed a military ____.","expectedAnswer":"alliance","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The two countries formed a military ____.","clozeAnswer":"alliance","exampleTranslation":"兩國組成了一個軍事聯盟。","reference":{"eng":"alliance","kk":"əˈlaɪəns","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"聯盟\"  ],  [    \"聯合\"  ],  [    \"結合\"  ],  [    \"姻親關係\"  ]]","chEntries":["聯盟","聯合","結合","姻親關係"],"practiceMeaning":"兩國組成了一個軍事聯盟。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 aliance「聯盟」，源自動詞 alier「聯合」，最終可追溯至拉丁語 alligare，意為「綁縛、聯合」，由 ad- (to) + ligare (to bind) 組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 ligare「綁縛」是其核心語意來源。作為名詞，其核心語義是兩個或多個實體（國家、組織、個人）基於共同目標或利益而形成的聯合或結合。詞源中的「綁縛」概念清晰地體現了聯盟的緊密聯繫。此義項由「聯合」的動作延伸出「聯盟」的狀態或組織。","definition":"1. a union or association formed for mutual benefit, especially between countries or organizations; 2. a close connection or relationship, especially one involving shared interests or goals; 3. a relationship by marriage between two families or groups.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The two countries formed a military alliance.\",\n    \