tionType":"typing","prompt":"Can you recite the English ____?","expectedAnswer":"alphabet","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Can you recite the English ____?","clozeAnswer":"alphabet","exampleTranslation":"你能背誦英文字母表嗎？","reference":{"eng":"alphabet","kk":"/ˈælfəˌbɛt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['字母表']]","chEntries":["字母表"],"practiceMeaning":"你能背誦英文字母表嗎？","analysis":"源自希臘語 'alphabētos'，由希臘字母表的前兩個字母 'alpha' (α) 和 'beta' (β) 組成。指一套用於書寫某種語言的符號系統。","definition":"1. a set of letters or symbols in a fixed order, used to represent the basic sounds of a language.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Can you recite the English alphabet?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你能背誦英文字母表嗎？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is still learning his alphabet.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他還在學習字母表。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"你能背誦英文字母表嗎？","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4093,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::an-elective-course::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She decided to take ____ in art history.","expectedAnswer":"an elective course","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She decided to take ____ in art history.","clozeAnswer":"an elective course","exampleTranslation":"她決定選修一門藝術史課程。","reference":{"eng":"an elective course","kk":"/ən ɪˈlɛktɪv kɔrs/","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['選修課程']]","chEntries":["選修課程"],"practiceMeaning":"她決定選修一門藝術史課程。","analysis":"'Elective' (選修的) 源自拉丁語 'electus' (chosen)，是 'elect' 的形容詞形式，指「可供選擇的」。'Course' (課程) 源自拉丁語 'cursus' (course, race)。'An elective course' 指學生可以自由選擇是否要學習的課程。","definition":"a course that a student can choose to study but is not required","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"她決定選修一門藝術史課程。\",\n    \"eng\": \"She decided to take an elective course in art history.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"這是為對電影製作感興趣的學生開設的選修課程。\",\n    \"eng\": \"This is an elective course for students interested in filmmaking.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她決定選修一門藝術史課程。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3960,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::an-immediate-response::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need ____ to the customer's complaint.","expectedAnswer":"an immediate response","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need ____ to the customer's complaint.","clozeAnswer":"an immediate response","exampleTranslation":"我們需要立即回應顧客的投訴。","reference":{"eng":"an immediate response","kk":"None","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['立即的回應']]","chEntries":["立即的回應"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要立即回應顧客的投訴。","analysis":"不定冠詞 'an' 加上形容詞 'immediate' (立即的) 和名詞 'response' (回應)。表示迅速、毫不延遲的回應。","definition":"a reply or reaction that is given without any delay.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need an immediate response to the customer's complaint.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要立即回應顧客的投訴。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government promised an immediate response to the disaster.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府承諾對災難做出緊急回應。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要立即回應顧客的投訴。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5615,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l7::anniversary::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Today is their wedding ____.","expectedAnswer":"anniversary","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Today is their wedding ____.","clozeAnswer":"anniversary","exampleTranslation":"今天是他們的結婚週年紀念日。","reference":{"eng":"anniversary","kk":"ˌænəˈvɜrsəri","tense":"n.","ch":"[['週年紀念日'], ['紀念日']]","chEntries":["週年紀念日","紀念日"],"practiceMeaning":"今天是他們的結婚週年紀念日。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'anniversarius'，意為「一年一度的」，由 'annus'（年）和 'vertere'（轉動）組成，再加上形容詞化後綴 '-arius'。構詞學上，'ann-' 是「年」的詞根，'vers-'（來自 'vertere'）是「轉動」的詞根，'-ary' 是形容詞化後綴。組合起來意為「每年都會轉動的」或「一年輪迴一次的」。原始語意是「一年一度的事件」，引申為「週年紀念日」，指每年一次、紀念特定事件的日子。","definition":"1. The date on which an event took place in a previous year, or the celebration of this; 2. The yearly recurrence of a date marking a notable event.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Today is their wedding anniversary.\",\n    \"ch\": \"今天是他們的結婚週年紀念日。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company is celebrating its 50th anniversary.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司正在慶祝其成立五十週年。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"今天是他們的結婚週年紀念日。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4012,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u3::anxious::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She was ____ about her upcoming exam.","expectedAnswer":"anxious","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She was ____ about her upcoming exam.","clozeAnswer":"anxious","exampleTranslation":"她對即將到來的考試感到焦慮。","reference":{"eng":"anxious","kk":"/ˈæŋkʃəs/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['焦慮的', '不安的'], ['渴望的', '急切的']]","chEntries":["焦慮的","不安的","渴望的","急切的"],"practiceMeaning":"她對即將到來的考試感到焦慮。","analysis":"詞源：拉丁文 'anxius' (擔憂的)，源自 'angere' (使痛苦)。指因擔憂未來或未知情況而產生的不安感，也指對某事極度渴望。","definition":"1. feeling or showing worry about what may happen; 2. eager or desirous to do something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She was anxious about her upcoming exam.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對即將到來的考試感到焦慮。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was anxious to start his new job.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他急切地想開始他的新工作。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她對即將到來的考試感到焦慮。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5770,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::applause::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The audience gave the performers a standing ovation and loud ____.","expectedAnswer":"applause","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The audience gave the performers a standing ovation and loud ____.","clozeAnswer":"applause","exampleTranslation":"觀眾起立鼓掌，給予表演者熱烈的掌聲。","reference":{"eng":"applause","kk":"əˈplɔz","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"掌聲\"  ],  [    \"讚賞\"  ],  [    \"喝采\"  ]]","chEntries":["掌聲","讚賞","喝采"],"practiceMeaning":"觀眾起立鼓掌，給予表演者熱烈的掌聲。","analysis":"此字為名詞，源自中古英語 applaus，由拉丁語 applausus（讚許；喝采）而來，後者是動詞 applaud（鼓掌；讚美）的過去分詞。applaud來自拉丁語applaudere，由ad-（朝向；加強）+ plaudere（鼓掌；拍手）組成。plaudere本身可能與拉丁語plausus（拍擊；鼓掌）及希臘語plosion（爆發；撞擊）有關。因此，applause的核心語義是「因讚賞或喜愛而發出的拍手聲」，引申為「讚賞」或「喝采」。其語意演變是從具體的拍手動作發展到抽象的讚揚和認可。","definition":"1. the act of clapping your hands to show you have enjoyed a performance or someone has done well; 2. enthusiastic approval.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The audience gave the performers a standing ovation and loud applause.\",\n    \"ch\": \"觀眾起立鼓掌，給予表演者熱烈的掌聲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her speech was met with thunderous applause.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的演講獲得了雷鳴般的掌聲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We appreciate your applause and support.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們感謝您的讚賞與支持。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"觀眾起立鼓掌，給予表演者熱烈的掌聲。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5682,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l9::appointment::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Her ____ as CEO was controversial.","expectedAnswer":"appointment","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Her ____ as CEO was controversial.","clozeAnswer":"appointment","exampleTranslation":"她被任命為執行長的決定備受爭議。","reference":{"eng":"appointment","kk":"əˈpɔɪntmənt","tense":"n.","ch":"[['任命'], ['委派'], ['職位'], ['約會'], ['預約']]","chEntries":["任命","委派","職位","約會","預約"],"practiceMeaning":"她被任命為執行長的決定備受爭議。","analysis":"此字由動詞 'appoint' 加上名詞化後綴 '-ment' 構成。'appoint' 源自古法語 apointier（來自拉丁語 pungere，意為『刺，戳，使之明確』），核心語意是「明確指定」。'-ment' 後綴用於將動詞轉化為名詞，表示動作、狀態、結果或所產生的事物。因此，'appointment' 可以指「被任命的動作或結果」（任命、委派、職位），也可以指「被約定的動作或結果」（約會、預約）。語意上的區別體現在「對人」的指定（任命）與「對事」的指定（約會）上。","definition":"the act of appointing someone to a job or position; an arrangement to meet someone at a particular time and place; a job or position to which someone is appointed.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her appointment as CEO was controversial.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她被任命為執行長的決定備受爭議。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I have an appointment with the dentist at 3 PM.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我下午三點有一個牙醫的預約。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她被任命為執行長的決定備受爭議。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5369,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l2::appropriate::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This is not the ____ time to discuss such matters.","expectedAnswer":"appropriate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This is not the ____ time to discuss such matters.","clozeAnswer":"appropriate","exampleTranslation":"這不是討論這類事情的適當時機。","reference":{"eng":"appropriate","kk":"əˈproʊpriɪt","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['適當的'], ['恰當的'], ['合適的']]","chEntries":["適當的","恰當的","合適的"],"practiceMeaning":"這不是討論這類事情的適當時機。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 appropriat，來自拉丁語 appropriatus，是動詞 'appropriare' (使屬於某人，佔有) 的過去分詞。'appropriare' 由 ad- (to) + proprius (one's own) 構成。核心概念是「屬於某人、符合某人所有」。因此，引申為「符合某目的、場合或標準」，即「適當的、恰當的」。","definition":"Suitable or proper in the circumstances.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is not the appropriate time to discuss such matters.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這不是討論這類事情的適當時機。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please wear appropriate attire for the formal event.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請穿著適合正式場合的服裝。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這不是討論這類事情的適當時機。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5373,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l2::arch::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The old church had a beautiful stone ____.","expectedAnswer":"arch","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The old church had a beautiful stone ____.","clozeAnswer":"arch","exampleTranslation":"這座古老的教堂有一個美麗的石拱門。","reference":{"eng":"arch","kk":"ɑːrtʃ","tense":"n.","ch":"[['拱門'], ['拱形'], ['拱狀結構']]","chEntries":["拱門","拱形","拱狀結構"],"practiceMeaning":"這座古老的教堂有一個美麗的石拱門。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 arche，最終來自拉丁語 arcus，意為「弓、拱」。核心語意是「一種彎曲的結構，通常用於支撐上方重量或形成開口」。在建築中，拱門是最常見的應用。引申語意包括「拱形」本身，或任何類似拱形的結構。","definition":"1. a curved symmetrical structure spanning an opening and typically supporting the weight of a bridge, roof, or wall; 2. a structure like an arch, especially one that frames a doorway or opening.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The old church had a beautiful stone arch.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座古老的教堂有一個美麗的石拱門。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The rainbow formed a perfect arch in the sky.\",\n    \"ch\": \"彩虹在天上形成了一個完美的拱形。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這座古老的教堂有一個美麗的石拱門。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5372,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l2::arched::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The bridge had a series of ____ spans.","expectedAnswer":"arched","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The bridge had a series of ____ spans.","clozeAnswer":"arched","exampleTranslation":"這座橋有一系列的拱形跨度。","reference":{"eng":"arched","kk":"ɑːrtʃt","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['拱形的'], ['有拱門的']]","chEntries":["拱形的","有拱門的"],"practiceMeaning":"這座橋有一系列的拱形跨度。","analysis":"此字是名詞 'arch' (拱門) 的過去分詞 'arched' 用作形容詞。'arch' 源自古法語 arche，來自拉丁語 arcus，意為「弓、拱」。核心語意是「彎曲的線條，形成一個向上或向外的弧形」。因此，'arched' 形容事物「呈現拱形」的狀態。","definition":"Having the form of an arch.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The bridge had a series of arched spans.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座橋有一系列的拱形跨度。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her eyebrows were neatly arched.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的眉毛被整齊地畫成了弓形。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這座橋有一系列的拱形跨度。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5453,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::as-a-whole::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____, the team performed well.","expectedAnswer":"As a whole","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____, the team performed well.","clozeAnswer":"As a whole","exampleTranslation":"總體而言，這支隊伍表現不錯。","reference":{"eng":"as a whole","kk":"æz ə hoʊl","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['總體而言'], ['整體來說']]","chEntries":["總體而言","整體來說"],"practiceMeaning":"總體而言，這支隊伍表現不錯。","analysis":"此片語由介系詞 \"as\" (如同)，不定冠詞 \"a\"，以及形容詞 \"whole\" (整個的) 組成。\"whole\" 源自古英語 \"hāl\"。此片語意指將事物視為一個單一、不可分割的整體來考量，強調其整體性而非個別部分。","definition":"considering everything or everyone as a single unit; on the whole.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"As a whole, the team performed well.\",\n    \"ch\": \"總體而言，這支隊伍表現不錯。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The country, as a whole, is experiencing economic recovery.\",\n    \"ch\": \"整個國家正在經歷經濟復甦。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"總體而言，這支隊伍表現不錯。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3125,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::assemble::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need to ____ all the furniture before the guests arrive.","expectedAnswer":"assemble","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need to ____ all the furniture before the guests arrive.","clozeAnswer":"assemble","exampleTranslation":"我們需要在客人到達前組裝好所有家具。","reference":{"eng":"assemble","kk":"/əˈsɛmbl/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['組裝；裝配'], ['集合；聚集']]","chEntries":["組裝","裝配","集合","聚集"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要在客人到達前組裝好所有家具。","analysis":"詞源來自古法語 'assembler'，意為「聚集，集合」，由 'as-'（朝向）+ 'sembler'（聚集，類似）。'sembler' 又來自拉丁語 'simulare'（模仿，使其相似），最終源於 'similis'（相似的）。最初指將相似或相關的事物聚集在一起，引申為將零件組裝成一個整體，或將人聚集在一起。動詞 'assemble' 涵蓋了將分散的部分變成一個完整單位的概念，無論是物理上的組裝還是人員的聚集。","definition":"1. to bring together or come together in one place for a common purpose; 2. to fit together the separate component parts of (a machine or other object).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to assemble all the furniture before the guests arrive.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要在客人到達前組裝好所有家具。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The students will assemble in the auditorium for the assembly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"學生們將在禮堂集合參加集會。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The engineers assembled the prototype car in just two weeks.\",\n    \"ch\": \"工程師們僅用了兩週就組裝好了原型車。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要在客人到達前組裝好所有家具。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3126,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::assembly::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The school holds an ____ every Monday morning.","expectedAnswer":"assembly","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The school holds an ____ every Monday morning.","clozeAnswer":"assembly","exampleTranslation":"這所學校每週一早上都會舉行集會。","reference":{"eng":"assembly","kk":"/əˈsɛmblɪ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['集會；集會場所'], ['組裝；裝配'], ['（尤指公司、組織的）大會；議會']]","chEntries":["集會","集會場所","組裝","裝配","大會","議會"],"practiceMeaning":"這所學校每週一早上都會舉行集會。","analysis":"名詞，源自動詞 'assemble'。第一個核心意義是「集合」，指一群人為了特定目的聚集在一起，這可以是正式的（如會議、議會）或非正式的。第二個核心意義是「組裝」，指將零件組合起來的過程或結果。'Assembly' 強調的是『聚集』或『組成』的動作或狀態。","definition":"1. a group of people gathered together in one place for a common purpose; 2. the action of assembling a piece of equipment or a machine; 3. a legislative body.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The school holds an assembly every Monday morning.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這所學校每週一早上都會舉行集會。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The final assembly of the aircraft takes several weeks.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這架飛機的最終組裝需要數週時間。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The general assembly of the United Nations meets annually.\",\n    \"ch\": \"聯合國大會每年都會召開。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這所學校每週一早上都會舉行集會。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3060,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::associate::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She is an ____ professor at the university.","expectedAnswer":"associate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She is an ____ professor at the university.","clozeAnswer":"associate","exampleTranslation":"她是大學的副教授。","reference":{"eng":"associate","kk":"/əˈsoʊʃiət/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['同事；夥伴'], ['副手；助理']]","chEntries":["同事","夥伴","副手","助理"],"practiceMeaning":"她是大學的副教授。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'associatus'，'ad-' (to, toward) + 'sociatus' (companion)。指與某人或組織有連結、合作關係的人。\n1. 同事；夥伴：指在同一公司、組織或共同目標下工作的人。\n2. 副手；助理：在特定職位上，協助較高級別人員工作的人。","definition":"1. a person who works with or is connected with someone else in a profession or business; 2. a person who is on the same team, in the same group, or in partnership with someone.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is an associate professor at the university.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是大學的副教授。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He started his career as a junior associate in a law firm.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他最初是一家律師事務所的初級助理。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她是大學的副教授。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3063,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::assurance::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He spoke with great ____, calming everyone's fears.","expectedAnswer":"assurance","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He spoke with great ____, calming everyone's fears.","clozeAnswer":"assurance","exampleTranslation":"他充滿信心地說話，平息了所有人的恐懼。","reference":{"eng":"assurance","kk":"/əˈʃʊərəns/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['保證；信心'], ['擔保；確信'], ['（購買的）保險；保證書']]","chEntries":["保證","信心","擔保","確信","保險","保證書"],"practiceMeaning":"他充滿信心地說話，平息了所有人的恐懼。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'securus' (safe, secure)，經由古法語 'asseurance' 演變而來，是 'assure' 的名詞形式。指「確定」或「使確信」的狀態或行為。\n1. 保證；信心：指說話或行為中表現出的確定感，給予聽者信心。\n2. 擔保；確信：指對某事物的肯定或相信，使其變得確定。\n3. （購買的）保險；保證書：指一種承諾或文件，提供對某種結果的保障。","definition":"1. a statement that something will certainly happen or be true; 2. a feeling of confidence that you can do something well or succeed; 3. a promise or guarantee.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He spoke with great assurance, calming everyone's fears.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他充滿信心地說話，平息了所有人的恐懼。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company offers a money-back assurance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司提供退款保證。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her assurance of success gave him hope.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她成功的保證給了他希望。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他充滿信心地說話，平息了所有人的恐懼。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4291,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::at-first-glance::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____, the task seemed impossible.","expectedAnswer":"At first glance","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____, the task seemed impossible.","clozeAnswer":"At first glance","exampleTranslation":"乍一看，這項任務似乎是不可能的。","reference":{"eng":"at first glance","kk":"/æt fɜːrst ˈɡlæns/","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['乍一看'], ['第一眼看去']]","chEntries":["乍一看","第一眼看去"],"practiceMeaning":"乍一看，這項任務似乎是不可能的。","analysis":"由介詞 'at'、名詞 'first'（第一）和名詞 'glance'（一瞥）組成。'At first glance' 意為「僅僅從第一次、簡短的觀察來看」，強調初步印象，可能與實際情況有所不同。","definition":"from the first look; seemingly.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"At first glance, the task seemed impossible.\",\n    \"ch\": \"乍一看，這項任務似乎是不可能的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The house looked ordinary at first glance, but it had many hidden features.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這棟房子乍一看很普通，但它有很多隱藏的特色。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"乍一看，這項任務似乎是不可能的。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4237,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::attractive::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She found the candidate's proposals very ____.","expectedAnswer":"attractive","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She found the candidate's proposals very ____.","clozeAnswer":"attractive","exampleTranslation":"她覺得該候選人的提議非常有吸引力。","reference":{"eng":"attractive","kk":"/əˈtræktɪv/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['吸引人的'], ['有魅力的']]","chEntries":["吸引人的","有魅力的"],"practiceMeaning":"她覺得該候選人的提議非常有吸引力。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'attrahere'（吸引），由 'ad-'（朝向）+ 'trahere'（拉）組成。'Attractive' 意指能夠吸引人注意或喜愛。此詞語根 'tract' 意為「拉、拖」，延伸出「吸引」的意義。","definition":"pleasing or appealing to the senses; having the power to attract","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She found the candidate's proposals very attractive.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她覺得該候選人的提議非常有吸引力。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The new marketing campaign is designed to be attractive to young consumers.\",\n    \"ch\": \"新的行銷活動旨在吸引年輕消費者。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她覺得該候選人的提議非常有吸引力。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5820,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::attribute::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Patience is an important ____ for a teacher.","expectedAnswer":"attribute","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Patience is an important ____ for a teacher.","clozeAnswer":"attribute","exampleTranslation":"耐心是老師重要的特質。","reference":{"eng":"attribute","kk":"ˈætrɪbjuːt","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"特質\"  ],  [    \"屬性\"  ],  [    \"特徵\"  ],  [    \"特性\"  ]]","chEntries":["特質","屬性","特徵","特性"],"practiceMeaning":"耐心是老師重要的特質。","analysis":"此名詞形式的 'attribute' 源自拉丁語 'attributum' (something bestowed or assigned)，是 'attribuere' 的過去分詞中性形式。其核心語意為「被分配或賦予給某物的一項」。在構詞上，'ad-' (to) + 'tribuere' (to assign)。作為名詞，'attribute' 指的是屬於某人或某物的特質、品質、性質或特徵，這些都是被「賦予」或「歸屬於」主體的。它與動詞形式的「歸因於」密切相關，因為特質（名詞）就是被認為是某事物「歸因於」的那個東西。例如，也可指「一項特殊能力或才能」。","definition":"1. A quality or feature regarded as a characteristic or inherent part of someone or something.; 2. A thing regarded as a property of a person or thing.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Patience is an important attribute for a teacher.\",\n    \"ch\": \"耐心是老師重要的特質。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The book is rich in historical attributes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本書富含歷史特徵。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Honesty is a key attribute of his character.\",\n    \"ch\": \"誠實是他性格的關鍵屬性。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Intelligence is a valuable attribute.\",\n    \"ch\": \"智慧是一種寶貴的特質。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"耐心是老師重要的特質。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4001,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u3::audience::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ applauded enthusiastically.","expectedAnswer":"audience","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ applauded enthusiastically.","clozeAnswer":"audience","exampleTranslation":"觀眾熱烈鼓掌。","reference":{"eng":"audience","kk":"/ˈɔːdiəns/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['聽眾', '觀眾'], ['（謁見）謁見']]","chEntries":["聽眾","觀眾","謁見"],"practiceMeaning":"觀眾熱烈鼓掌。","analysis":"詞源：拉丁文 'audientia' (聽)，源自 'audire' (聽)。指聽眾或觀眾，也指覲見權貴的場合。","definition":"1. the assembled spectators or listeners at a public event, such as a play, concert, or meeting; 2. an interview given by a person in authority.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The audience applauded enthusiastically.\",\n    \"ch\": \"觀眾熱烈鼓掌。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He had a private audience with the Pope.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他有機會私下謁見教宗。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"觀眾熱烈鼓掌。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4040,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::aware::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Are you ____ of the dangers involved?","expectedAnswer":"aware","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Are you ____ of the dangers involved?","clozeAnswer":"aware","exampleTranslation":"你意識到其中存在的危險了嗎？","reference":{"eng":"aware","kk":"/əˈwɛr/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['意識到的', '知道的'], ['明白的', '察覺到的']]","chEntries":["意識到的","知道的","明白的","察覺到的"],"practiceMeaning":"你意識到其中存在的危險了嗎？","analysis":"源自古英語 'gewaer'，由 'ge-' (a past participle prefix) + 'wær' (aware) 構成。'wær' 本身與 'watch' 有關。核心概念是「看到」、「注意」，引申為「意識到」、「知道」或「察覺到」。","definition":"1. knowing or realizing that something is happening or that something exists; 2. having knowledge or understanding","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"你意識到其中存在的危險了嗎？\",\n    \"eng\": \"Are you aware of the dangers involved?\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"她敏銳地察覺到他的不適。\",\n    \"eng\": \"She was keenly aware of his discomfort.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他並不了解事實。\",\n    \"eng\": \"He is not aware of the facts.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"你意識到其中存在的危險了嗎？","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5024,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::awe::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The vastness of the desert filled him with ____.","expectedAnswer":"awe","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The vastness of the desert filled him with ____.","clozeAnswer":"awe","exampleTranslation":"沙漠的廣袤讓他充滿敬畏。","reference":{"eng":"awe","kk":"ɔː","tense":"n.","ch":"[['敬畏'], ['驚嘆'], ['敬畏感']]","chEntries":["敬畏","驚嘆","敬畏感"],"practiceMeaning":"沙漠的廣袤讓他充滿敬畏。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 ege，意為「恐懼、敬畏」。與現代德語 Ehrfurcht（敬畏）同源。其語意核心為一種強烈的、帶有恐懼感的驚嘆，通常是對超乎尋常、強大或神聖的事物產生的反應。在現代英語中，awe 仍然保留了這種「既敬又畏」的語意，但恐懼成分有所減弱，更多強調「驚嘆、崇敬」。","definition":"a feeling of reverential respect mixed with fear or wonder.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The vastness of the desert filled him with awe.\",\n    \"ch\": \"沙漠的廣袤讓他充滿敬畏。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We looked in awe at the magnificent view.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們驚嘆地看著壯麗的景色。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"沙漠的廣袤讓他充滿敬畏。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5359,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l1::back-and-forth::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The pendulum swung ____.","expectedAnswer":"back and forth","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The pendulum swung ____.","clozeAnswer":"back and forth","exampleTranslation":"鐘擺來回擺動。","reference":{"eng":"back and forth","kk":"ˌbæk ən ˈfɔːrθ","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['來來回回'], ['來回地'], ['前後地']]","chEntries":["來來回回","來回地","前後地"],"practiceMeaning":"鐘擺來回擺動。","analysis":"此片語由 back（後退）和 forth（往前）組合而成，直接描述了來回移動或方向的變換。back- 和 forth- 都是副詞，共同強調了在兩個方向之間的持續運動。常用來形容物體或人的移動方式，或抽象概念的拉鋸。","definition":"moving from one place to another and in again; repeatedly in opposite directions.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The pendulum swung back and forth.\",\n    \"ch\": \"鐘擺來回擺動。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They argued back and forth for hours.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們爭論了好幾個小時。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"鐘擺來回擺動。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3293,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::bacteria::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Some ____ are beneficial to human health.","expectedAnswer":"bacteria","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Some ____ are beneficial to human health.","clozeAnswer":"bacteria","exampleTranslation":"有些細菌對人體健康有益。","reference":{"eng":"bacteria","kk":"/bækˈtɪəriə/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['細菌（複數）']]","chEntries":["細菌"],"practiceMeaning":"有些細菌對人體健康有益。","analysis":"來自拉丁語 'bacterium' 的複數形式。指一類單細胞微生物，其中一些是病原體，另一些則對生態系統至關重要。","definition":"microscopic single-celled organisms that lack a nucleus and reproduce by fission.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Some bacteria are beneficial to human health.\",\n    \"ch\": \"有些細菌對人體健康有益。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The lab is studying the growth of bacteria in different conditions.\",\n    \"ch\": \"實驗室正在研究細菌在不同條件下的生長情況。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"有些細菌對人體健康有益。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3262,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::ballet::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She has been studying ____ since she was a child.","expectedAnswer":"ballet","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She has been studying ____ since she was a child.","clozeAnswer":"ballet","exampleTranslation":"她從小就開始學習芭蕾舞。","reference":{"eng":"ballet","kk":"/ˈbæleɪ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['芭蕾舞'], ['芭蕾舞劇']]","chEntries":["芭蕾舞","芭蕾舞劇"],"practiceMeaning":"她從小就開始學習芭蕾舞。","analysis":"源自義大利語 'balletto'，是 'ballo'（舞蹈）的小型詞。最初指一種宮廷娛樂，後來發展為一種專業的戲劇性舞蹈。","definition":"a type of dancing in which you move your body in a graceful way, usually to music, often telling a story; a performance of this type of dancing.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has been studying ballet since she was a child.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她從小就開始學習芭蕾舞。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The Bolshoi Ballet is famous worldwide.\",\n    \"ch\": \"莫斯科大劇院芭蕾舞團舉世聞名。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她從小就開始學習芭蕾舞。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5118,"wordRef":"字彙王::u62::ballot::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Each voter received a ____ paper.","expectedAnswe