":"boost","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The new policy provided a ____ to the economy.","clozeAnswer":"boost","exampleTranslation":"新政策為經濟提供了促進。","reference":{"eng":"boost","kk":"buːst","tense":"n.","ch":"[['提升'], ['促進'], ['推動（尤指一次性的）']]","chEntries":["提升","促進","推動"],"practiceMeaning":"新政策為經濟提供了促進。","analysis":"此字來源不確定，可能與低地德語 bost（隆起）或荷蘭語 botsen（碰撞）有關。現代意義的 boost，尤其是在 18 世紀後期出現，意為「推、頂、抬高」，引申為「促進、增加」。此名詞用法表示「一次顯著的提升或促進」，強調的是其積極的作用。OCR 掃描時可能將 'o' 誤判為 '0'，或將 'st' 誤判。此處修正為 boost，其語意為「一次性的促進或提升」。","definition":"1. a rise or increase, typically one that is significant or dramatic; 2. an act of helping or encouraging someone or something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The new policy provided a boost to the economy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"新政策為經濟提供了促進。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a real boost for our team's morale.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這對我們隊伍的士氣是個真正的鼓舞。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"新政策為經濟提供了促進。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5032,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::bound::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The river forms the northern ____ of the property.","expectedAnswer":"bound","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The river forms the northern ____ of the property.","clozeAnswer":"bound","exampleTranslation":"河流構成了該房產的北部界限。","reference":{"eng":"bound","kk":"baʊnd","tense":"n.","ch":"[['界限'], ['範圍'], ['限制']]","chEntries":["界限","範圍","限制"],"practiceMeaning":"河流構成了該房產的北部界限。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 bondir（跳躍），引申為「界限」，與表示「跳躍」的動詞 bound 同源，但語意發展不同。其核心語意是「事物發展的邊界或範圍」，通常是人為或自然的限制。在現代英語中，此用法常與複數形式 bounds 一起出現。","definition":"1. a limit or boundary; 2. the limits of a person's endurance or tolerance.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The river forms the northern bound of the property.\",\n    \"ch\": \"河流構成了該房產的北部界限。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His behavior was beyond all bounds.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的行為超出了所有界限。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"河流構成了該房產的北部界限。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"lea