h\": \"他在大學主修化學。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was an instant chemistry between the two actors.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這兩位演員之間有立即的來電。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他在大學主修化學。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3128,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::chorus::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The audience joined in to sing the ____.","expectedAnswer":"chorus","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The audience joined in to sing the ____.","clozeAnswer":"chorus","exampleTranslation":"觀眾們加入進來一起唱副歌。","reference":{"eng":"chorus","kk":"/ˈkɔːrəs/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['合唱；合唱團'], ['（歌曲的）副歌；（戲劇的）合唱隊'], ['（眾人的）齊聲發言；呼聲']]","chEntries":["合唱","合唱團","副歌","合唱隊","齊聲發言","呼聲"],"practiceMeaning":"觀眾們加入進來一起唱副歌。","analysis":"詞源來自希臘語 'khoros'，原指「跳舞的地方」，後來指「一隊跳舞或歌唱的人」，再演變為「合唱」。'Chorus' 的核心概念是「集合的聲音」或「共同的聲音」。它可以指一群人一起唱歌（合唱團、合唱），也可以指歌曲或詩歌中重複出現的部分（副歌），或者是一群人同時表達的共同意見或呼聲。","definition":"1. a part of a song that is repeated after each verse; 2. a group of people or animals singing or speaking together; 3. a large choir or choir of singers.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The audience joined in to sing the chorus.\",\n    \"ch\": \"觀眾們加入進來一起唱副歌。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The church choir practiced for the Sunday service.\",\n    \"ch\": \"教堂的合唱團為週日禮拜進行練習。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A chorus of disapproval met the proposal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"對這項提議響起了一片反對的呼聲。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"觀眾們加入進來一起唱副歌。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6064,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::chunk::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He ate a large ____ of cake.","expectedAnswer":"chunk","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He ate a large ____ of cake.","clozeAnswer":"chunk","exampleTranslation":"他吃了一大塊蛋糕。","reference":{"eng":"chunk","kk":"tʃʌŋk","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"大塊\"  ],  [    \"厚片\"  ],  [    \"一段\"  ],  [    \"大量\"  ]]","chEntries":["大塊","厚片","一段","大量"],"practiceMeaning":"他吃了一大塊蛋糕。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 chunk，語源不清，可能與「厚」或「大塊」的意象相關。在此作名詞，核心語義是一個「大而厚實的部分」。引申用法包括表示「一段」連續的內容（如一段文本或程式碼），或引申為「大量」的某物，特別是未經處理的材料。構詞上，這是一個單純的詞根詞，沒有顯著的前綴或後綴。","definition":"1. a thick, solid piece of something; 2. a large part or amount of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He ate a large chunk of cake.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他吃了一大塊蛋糕。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The report contained a long chunk of technical jargon.\",\n    \"ch\": \"報告中包含一大段技術術語。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to allocate a big chunk of our budget to marketing.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要將很大一部分預算分配給市場行銷。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他吃了一大塊蛋糕。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4091,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::civil-rights::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The movement fought for ____ for all people.","expectedAnswer":"civil rights","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The movement fought for ____ for all people.","clozeAnswer":"civil rights","exampleTranslation":"該運動為所有人爭取公民權利。","reference":{"eng":"civil rights","kk":"/ˈsɪvəl raɪts/","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['公民權利']]","chEntries":["公民權利"],"practiceMeaning":"該運動為所有人爭取公民權利。","analysis":"'Civil' (公民的) 源自拉丁語 'civilis' (of a citizen)。'Rights' (權利) 源自古法語 'droiture' (justice, right)。'Civil rights' 指公民在法律上應享有的基本權利，例如不受歧視和壓迫的權利。","definition":"the rights that citizens are entitled to by law, especially the right to be treated equally","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"該運動為所有人爭取公民權利。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The movement fought for civil rights for all people.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"保護公民權利是政府的職責。\",\n    \"eng\": \"Protecting civil rights is a government's duty.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該運動為所有人爭取公民權利。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6068,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::clause::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The contract includes a ____ that allows for early termination.","expectedAnswer":"clause","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The contract includes a ____ that allows for early termination.","clozeAnswer":"clause","exampleTranslation":"合約包含一條允許提前終止的條款。","reference":{"eng":"clause","kk":"klɔz","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"條款\"  ],  [    \"子句\"  ],  [    \"從句\"  ]]","chEntries":["條款","子句","從句"],"practiceMeaning":"合約包含一條允許提前終止的條款。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 clausa（closed thing, conclusion），是 claudere（to close）的過去分詞。核心語義是「關閉」或「封閉」，引申為「段落」、「條款」或「獨立的部分」。在法律或契約中，clause 指的是一份文件的「條款」。在語法中，clause 指的是一個包含主語和謂語的「子句」或「從句」。構詞上，-clause 是來自 claudere 的詞幹，沒有顯著的現代前綴或後綴。","definition":"1. a particular statement or condition in a treaty, law, or contract; 2. a group of words containing a subject and a verb, forming part of a sentence.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The contract includes a clause that allows for early termination.\",\n    \"ch\": \"合約包含一條允許提前終止的條款。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a subordinate clause.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個從句。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Each clause in the bill was debated thoroughly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"法案中的每一條都被詳細辯論了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"合約包含一條允許提前終止的條款。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4320,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::clay::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The potter shaped the ____ into a beautiful vase.","expectedAnswer":"clay","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The potter shaped the ____ into a beautiful vase.","clozeAnswer":"clay","exampleTranslation":"陶工將黏土塑造成一個美麗的花瓶。","reference":{"eng":"clay","kk":"/kleɪ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['黏土；陶土']]","chEntries":["黏土","陶土"],"practiceMeaning":"陶工將黏土塑造成一個美麗的花瓶。","analysis":"源自古英語 'clæg'，與荷蘭語 'klei' 和德語 'Klei' 同源。指的是一種由細小的礦物顆粒組成的泥土，遇水後有黏性，可塑性強，是製作陶器、磚塊等的材料。其核心特徵是『黏性』和『可塑性』。","definition":"earth that is soft and sticky when wet, and becomes hard when it is dry or when it is baked, used for making pots, bricks, etc.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The potter shaped the clay into a beautiful vase.\",\n    \"ch\": \"陶工將黏土塑造成一個美麗的花瓶。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The children played with modeling clay.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子們玩黏土。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Ancient houses were often built of clay bricks.\",\n    \"ch\": \"古代的房屋常由黏土磚建造。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"陶工將黏土塑造成一個美麗的花瓶。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5456,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::clear-out::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need to ____ the garage before winter.","expectedAnswer":"clear out","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need to ____ the garage before winter.","clozeAnswer":"clear out","exampleTranslation":"我們需要在冬天來臨前清理車庫。","reference":{"eng":"clear out","kk":"ˈklɪər aʊt","tense":"v.","ch":"[['清理'], ['清除'], ['搬空'], ['離去']]","chEntries":["清理","清除","搬空","離去"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要在冬天來臨前清理車庫。","analysis":"此片語由形容詞 \"clear\" (清晰的、乾淨的) 和介詞 \"out\" (出去、外面) 組成。\"clear\" 源自拉丁語 \"clarus\"。在此作為動詞，\"clear out\" 表示「將某處徹底清理乾淨，移走所有不需要的東西」，或是「使某處騰空」，引申為「迅速離開」。","definition":"to remove everything from a place; to make a place empty by removing its contents; to leave a place quickly.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to clear out the garage before winter.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要在冬天來臨前清理車庫。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police told the crowd to clear out.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警方要求人群散開。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They had to clear out their old apartment before moving.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們搬家前必須清空舊公寓。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要在冬天來臨前清理車庫。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6113,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::clinical::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ trials of the new drug","expectedAnswer":"clinical","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ trials of the new drug","clozeAnswer":"clinical","exampleTranslation":"新藥的臨床試驗","reference":{"eng":"clinical","kk":"ˈklɪnɪkəl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"臨床的\"  ],  [    \"診所的\"  ],  [    \"冷淡的\"  ],  [    \"客觀的\"  ],  [    \"嚴謹的\"  ]]","chEntries":["臨床的","診所的","冷淡的","客觀的","嚴謹的"],"practiceMeaning":"新藥的臨床試驗","analysis":"此字源自希臘語 klinikos，意為「臥室的；床邊的」，與 klinikē（醫術；臨床醫學）有關，而 klinikē 又源自 kline（床）。因此，clinical 的核心語義是與「床邊」或「病床旁」相關，即與直接醫治病人相關。現代用法包括與醫療診斷、治療和研究相關（臨床的），以及引申為冷淡、客觀、不帶感情的（冷淡的；客觀的）。此形容詞的語意演變是從具體的「病床邊」到抽象的「客觀、不帶感情」。","definition":"1. relating to or used in a clinic or the observation and treatment of patients; 2. clinically detached or objective; unemotional.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"clinical trials of the new drug\",\n    \"ch\": \"新藥的臨床試驗\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a very clinical approach to her work.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對工作有非常客觀的態度。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The doctor gave him a clinical examination.\",\n    \"ch\": \"醫生對他進行了臨床檢查。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"新藥的臨床試驗","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6116,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::cocaine::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The smugglers were caught with a large amount of ____.","expectedAnswer":"cocaine","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The smugglers were caught with a large amount of ____.","clozeAnswer":"cocaine","exampleTranslation":"走私者被抓到時攜帶了大量古柯鹼。","reference":{"eng":"cocaine","kk":"koʊˈkeɪn","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"古柯鹼\"  ],  [    \"可卡因\"  ]]","chEntries":["古柯鹼","可卡因"],"practiceMeaning":"走私者被抓到時攜帶了大量古柯鹼。","analysis":"此字源自西班牙語 coca，指南美洲的一種植物，加上後綴 -ine，用以表示化學物質。Coca 源自蓋丘亞語 kuka。Cocaine 是從古柯樹葉提取的一種興奮劑和局部麻醉劑。此名詞指這種特定的化學物質。其語意演變是從植物名到從植物中提取的物質名。","definition":"A powerful illegal stimulant drug, derived from the coca plant.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The smugglers were caught with a large amount of cocaine.\",\n    \"ch\": \"走私者被抓到時攜帶了大量古柯鹼。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Cocaine addiction is a serious problem.\",\n    \"ch\": \"古柯鹼成癮是一個嚴重的問題。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"走私者被抓到時攜帶了大量古柯鹼。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6158,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::coherent::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His argument was ____ and well-supported.","expectedAnswer":"coherent","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His argument was ____ and well-supported.","clozeAnswer":"coherent","exampleTranslation":"他的論點連貫且有充分的證據支持。","reference":{"eng":"coherent","kk":"koʊˈhɪərənt","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"連貫的\"  ],  [    \"條理清晰的\"  ],  [    \"前後一致的\"  ],  [    \"能理解的\"  ]]","chEntries":["連貫的","條理清晰的","前後一致的","能理解的"],"practiceMeaning":"他的論點連貫且有充分的證據支持。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 cohaerēns，是 cohaerēre「緊密結合、一致」的現在分詞。cohaerēre 由 com- (together) + haerēre (to stick, cling) 組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 com-「一起」和 haerēre「黏合」是其核心語意來源。作為形容詞，其核心語義是「緊密結合，能夠清晰地理解」。從「黏合在一起」引申出「條理清晰、前後一致、易於理解」的語義，特別用於描述論點、計劃或思緒。詞源中的「黏合」概念是其連結性和一致性的基礎。","definition":"1. logical and consistent; 2. able to be understood or believed; 3. forming a whole; 4. (of a group of people) united.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His argument was coherent and well-supported.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的論點連貫且有充分的證據支持。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She found it difficult to make a coherent speech.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她發現很難發表一篇條理清晰的演講。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The team needs to present a coherent plan.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個團隊需要提出一個前後一致的計畫。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"After the accident, he was unable to speak in a coherent manner.\",\n    \"ch\": \"事故發生後，他無法清晰地表達。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他的論點連貫且有充分的證據支持。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6160,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::collaboration::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The project was a successful ____ between the two departments.","expectedAnswer":"collaboration","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The project was a successful ____ between the two departments.","clozeAnswer":"collaboration","exampleTranslation":"這個專案是兩個部門之間成功的合作。","reference":{"eng":"collaboration","kk":"kəˌlæbəˈreɪʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"合作\"  ],  [    \"協作\"  ]]","chEntries":["合作","協作"],"practiceMeaning":"這個專案是兩個部門之間成功的合作。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 collaboratio，由 collaborare「一起工作」名詞化而來。collaborare 由 com- (together) + laborare (to work) 組成，laborare 又源自 labor (work)。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 com-「一起」和 labor「工作」是其核心語意來源。作為名詞，其核心語義是「兩個或多個個體或團體為達成共同目標而共同工作」。詞源中的「一起工作」清晰地表達了此義。","definition":"1. the action of working with someone to produce or create something; 2. a joint effort.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The project was a successful collaboration between the two departments.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個專案是兩個部門之間成功的合作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Their collaboration resulted in a groundbreaking discovery.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們的協作促成了一項開創性的發現。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Artistic collaboration often leads to innovative results.\",\n    \"ch\": \"藝術上的合作經常帶來創新的成果。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The collaboration lasted for five years.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這次合作持續了五年。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個專案是兩個部門之間成功的合作。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4555,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::colony::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"India was once a British ____.","expectedAnswer":"colony","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"India was once a British ____.","clozeAnswer":"colony","exampleTranslation":"印度曾是英國的殖民地。","reference":{"eng":"colony","kk":"/ˈkɒləni/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['殖民地'], ['（細菌、細胞等的）菌落，培養物'], ['（植物、動物的）群落，棲息地']]","chEntries":["殖民地","菌落，培養物","群落，棲息地"],"practiceMeaning":"印度曾是英國的殖民地。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'colonia'，意為 'settlement, possession' (定居點、領地)。\n    1. 殖民地：指由一國人民在異國建立並由其管轄的地區。\n    2. 菌落、培養物：指在培養基上生長繁殖的一群微生物。\n    3. 群落、棲息地：指一群同種動植物聚集在一起的生活區域。","definition":"1. a country or area under the full or partial political control of another country, typically a distant one, and occupied by settlers from that country.; 2. a group of people of one nationality or ethnic group living in a particular country or city.; 3. a mass of microorganisms, such as bacteria or yeast, grown in or on a solid culture medium.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"India was once a British colony.\",\n    \"ch\": \"印度曾是英國的殖民地。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The petri dish contained a colony of bacteria.\",\n    \"ch\": \"培養皿裡有一團細菌菌落。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Penguins live in large colonies on the coast.\",\n    \"ch\": \"企鵝棲息在海岸的大群落中。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"印度曾是英國的殖民地。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5830,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::comedian::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ told a series of hilarious jokes.","expectedAnswer":"comedian","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ told a series of hilarious jokes.","clozeAnswer":"comedian","exampleTranslation":"這位喜劇演員講了一系列搞笑的笑話。","reference":{"eng":"comedian","kk":"kəˈmiːdiən","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"喜劇演員\"  ],  [    \"演員\"  ],  [    \"喜劇演員\"  ]]","chEntries":["喜劇演員","演員"],"practiceMeaning":"這位喜劇演員講了一系列搞笑的笑話。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'comoedus' (actor in comedy)，該字又源自希臘語 'kōmōidos' (comic actor)，由 'kōmos' (revel, merry procession) 和 'aeidein' (to sing) 構成。'Kōmos' 最初指古代希臘酒神祭祀中的遊行隊伍，後來演變成「喜劇」。'-ian' 是常見的職業或身分字尾，表示「從事……的人」。因此，'comedian' 指「從事喜劇表演的人」，即「喜劇演員」。","definition":"1. A person who tells jokes and makes people laugh as a profession.; 2. An actor in a comedy.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The comedian told a series of hilarious jokes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位喜劇演員講了一系列搞笑的笑話。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He dreams of becoming a famous comedian.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他夢想成為一位著名的喜劇演員。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The show featured several popular comedians.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該節目邀請了幾位受歡迎的喜劇演員。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這位喜劇演員講了一系列搞笑的笑話。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4340,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::comfort::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The warm room provided great ____.","expectedAnswer":"comfort","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The warm room provided great ____.","clozeAnswer":"comfort","exampleTranslation":"溫暖的房間帶來極大的舒適。","reference":{"eng":"comfort","kk":"/ˈkʌmfərt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['舒適；安慰'], ['令人感到舒適的東西或人']]","chEntries":["舒適","安慰","令人感到舒適的東西或人"],"practiceMeaning":"溫暖的房間帶來極大的舒適。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'confortare'，意為 'to make strong, strengthen'，由 'con-' (with) 和 'fortis' (strong) 構成。最初是『使堅強、使有力』，引申為『使心情舒暢、得到慰藉』，從而產生『舒適』和『安慰』的含義。1. 指身心上的『舒適、安慰』的狀態。2. 指提供這種感受的『人或物』。","definition":"a state of physical ease and freedom from pain or constraint; the relief of a person's feelings of grief or distress","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The warm room provided great comfort.\",\n    \"ch\": \"溫暖的房間帶來極大的舒適。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His words offered comfort to the grieving family.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的話語給悲傷的家庭帶來了安慰。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She found comfort in listening to music.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她從聽音樂中找到了慰藉。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"溫暖的房間帶來極大的舒適。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U8、L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6214,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::commentary::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The book includes extensive ____ on Shakespeare's plays.","expectedAnswer":"commentary","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The book includes extensive ____ on Shakespeare's plays.","clozeAnswer":"commentary","exampleTranslation":"這本書包含對莎士比亞劇作的詳盡評論。","reference":{"eng":"commentary","kk":"ˈkɒmənˌtɛri","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"評論\"  ],  [    \"註釋\"  ],  [    \"旁白\"  ],  [    \"講評\"  ]]","chEntries":["評論","註釋","旁白","講評"],"practiceMeaning":"這本書包含對莎士比亞劇作的詳盡評論。","analysis":"此字由名詞 comment（評論）加上字尾 -ary（表示與…相關的；集合的；地方）構成。comment 源自拉丁語 commentum，意為「思想，解釋」，後來演變為「意見，評論」。字尾 -ary 在此表示「與評論相關的」或「評論的集合」。因此，commentary 指對某事物的解釋、評論、分析，或在體育賽事、新聞節目中的旁白或講評。中文翻譯為「評論；註釋；旁白；講評」。","definition":"1. an explanation or discussion of something, especially a written one in a book or article; 2. a set of remarks on an event or situation, especially by an expert; 3. spoken descriptions of an event, especially a sports event, that are broadcast on television or radio.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The book includes extensive commentary on Shakespeare's plays.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本書包含對莎士比亞劇作的詳盡評論。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The sports commentator provided expert analysis during the game.\",\n    \"ch\": \"體育節目講評員在比賽期間提供了專業分析。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her commentary on the political situation was insightful.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對政治局勢的評論頗具見地。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這本書包含對莎士比亞劇作的詳盡評論。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4607,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::communicate::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It's important to ____ your feelings openly.","expectedAnswer":"communicate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It's important to ____ your feelings openly.","clozeAnswer":"communicate","exampleTranslation":"坦誠地傳達你的感受是很重要的。","reference":{"eng":"communicate","kk":"/kəˈmjuːnɪkeɪt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['溝通'], ['傳達'], ['交流']]","chEntries":["溝通","傳達","交流"],"practiceMeaning":"坦誠地傳達你的感受是很重要的。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'communicare'，意為「分享、交換、使共有」。'Communis' (共同的) 是其詞根。此字的核心在於建立或維持一種連結，透過語言、符號、行動等方式交換訊息、思想或情感，達成彼此理解。","definition":"to share or exchange information, news, or ideas; to convey or impart.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's important to communicate your feelings openly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"坦誠地傳達你的感受是很重要的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They communicated through letters for many years.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們多年來透過書信交流。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The software allows us to communicate instantly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這款軟體讓我們能夠即時溝通。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"坦誠地傳達你的感受是很重要的。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4316,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::comparison::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"A ____ of the two plans shows that the second is cheaper.","expectedAnswer":"comparison","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"A ____ of the two plans shows that the second is cheaper.","clozeAnswer":"comparison","exampleTranslation":"比較這兩個計畫顯示，第二個比較便宜。","reference":{"eng":"comparison","kk":"/kəmˈpærɪsən/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['比較；對照'], ['比似；比喻']]","chEntries":["比較","對照","比似","比喻"],"practiceMeaning":"比較這兩個計畫顯示，第二個比較便宜。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'comparare'，意為 'to liken, to compare'，由 'com-' (together) 和 'par' (equal) 構成。字面意思是『使相等』、『使並列』，引申為『放在一起看』，從而產生『比較』、『對照』的含義。也可指事物之間的相似性，即『比似』或在修辭上用作『比喻』。","definition":"the act of comparing two or more people or things; a statement or discussion of how different people or things are similar or different","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A comparison of the two plans shows that the second is cheaper.\",\n    \"ch\": \"比較這兩個計畫顯示，第二個比較便宜。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The book uses vivid comparisons to describe the scenery.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本書使用生動的比喻來描寫風景。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There is no comparison between their skills.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們的技能無法相比。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"比較這兩個計畫顯示，第二個比較便宜。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5512,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l5::compassionate::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He was a kind and ____ leader.","expectedAnswer":"compassionate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He was a kind and ____ leader.","clozeAnswer":"compassionate","exampleTranslation":"他是一位善良且富有同情心的領導者。","reference":{"eng":"compassionate","kk":"kəmˈpæʃənət","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['富同情心的'], ['憐憫的'], ['慈悲的']]","chEntries":["富同情心的","憐憫的","慈悲的"],"practiceMeaning":"他是一位善良且富有同情心的領導者。","analysis":"此字由名詞 'compassion' 加上形容詞字尾 '-ate' 構成。'-ate' 是拉丁語來源的字尾，常用於形成形容詞，表示『具有……性質』。'compassion' 源自拉丁語 'compassio'，由 'com-' (together) + 'passio' (suffering) 構成，意為「共同感受痛苦」。因此，'compassionate' 的構詞結構清晰地表明其核心語意為「具有共同感受痛苦的能力」，即「富同情心的」。語意上，它描述了一種能體諒他人苦難並願意施予幫助的情感特質。","definition":"feeling or showing sympathy and concern for others.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was a kind and compassionate leader.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一位善良且富有同情心的領導者。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The nurse offered compassionate care to the patients.\",\n    \"ch\": \"護士對病患提供了充滿關懷的照顧。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他是一位善良且富有同情心的領導者。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4490,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::compete::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The two companies ____ for market share.","expectedAnswer":"compete","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The two companies ____ for market share.","clozeAnswer":"compete","exampleTranslation":"這兩家公司爭奪市場份額。","reference":{"eng":"compete","kk":"/kəmˈpiːt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['競爭'], ['比賽'], ['爭奪']]","chEntries":["競爭","比賽","爭奪"],"practiceMeaning":"這兩家公司爭奪市場份額。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 competere，意為「共同尋求」、「達到」。com- (一起) + petere (尋求)。核心語意是「一起尋求某樣東西（通常是勝利或領先）」。引申為「競爭」、「比賽」。","definition":"1. To strive to win by being the best or by doing better than others; 2. To take part in a contest or competition.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The two companies compete for market share.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這兩家公司爭奪市場份額。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She will compete in the Olympic Games.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她將參加奧運會比賽。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這兩家公司爭奪市場份額。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5034,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::competent::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He is a ____ programmer.","expectedAnswer":"competent","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He is a ____ programmer.","clozeAnswer":"competent","exampleTranslation":"他是一位稱職的程式設計師。","reference":{"eng":"competent","kk":"ˈkɑːmpɪtənt","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['有能力的'], ['稱職的'], ['勝任的']]","chEntries":["有能力的","稱職的","勝任的"],"practiceMeaning":"他是一位稱職的程式設計師。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語competentem（有資格的、夠格的），是動詞 competere 的現在分詞。competere 由 com-（共同、一起）+ petere（尋求、爭取、達到）組成，原意為「共同努力以達成目標」、「相等、適合」。competent 形容詞意指「有足夠能力或資格做某事」，強調的是具備完成任務所需的技能、知識和素質。此形容詞與名詞 competence 緊密相關。","definition":"1. having the necessary ability, knowledge, or skill to do something successfully; 2. sufficient; adequate.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a competent programmer.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一位稱職的程式設計師。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The team produced a competent performance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該團隊的表現稱職。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他是一位稱職的程式設計師。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5649,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l8::complaint::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"I have a ____ about the service.","expectedAnswer":"complaint","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"I have a ____ about the service.","clozeAnswer":"complaint","exampleTranslation":"我對這項服務有一個投訴。","reference":{"eng":"complaint","kk":"kəmˈpleɪnt","tense":"n.","ch":"[['抱怨'], ['投訴'], ['（身體）不適'], ['申訴']]","chEntries":["抱怨","投訴","不適","申訴"],"practiceMeaning":"我對這項服務有一個投訴。","analysis":"此字由 complain（抱怨）+ -t（名詞字尾）構成。complain 源自中古英語 complainen，來自古法語 complaindre，再追溯至拉丁語 complangere，由 com-（完全，together）+ plangere（哀悼，to lament, to beat one's breast）組成。plangere 來自原始印歐語 *pleh₂g-（打擊）。核心語義為「表達不滿或哀悼」。構詞上，com- 加強語氣，plangere 提供「表達痛苦」或「哀傷」的核心動作，-t 將其名詞化。此處為名詞用法，指代「抱怨」、「投訴」的行為或內容。","definition":"a statement that something is unsatisfactory or unacceptable; an expression of dissatisfaction or discontent; a physical ailment or symptom.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I have a complaint about the service.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我對這項服務有一個投訴。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He made numerous complaints about the noise.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對噪音發出了許多抱怨。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The most common complaint is headache.\",\n    \"ch\": \"最常見的身體不適是頭痛。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我對這項服務有一個投訴。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4066,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::connect::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The wires ____ the computer to the internet.","expectedAnswer":"connect","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The wires ____ the computer to the internet.","clozeAnswer":"connect","exampleTranslation":"這些線路將電腦連接到網際網路。","reference":{"eng":"connect","kk":"/kəˈnɛkt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['連接', '連結'], ['與...取得聯繫', '交往'], ['（思想、事物）聯繫起來']]","chEntries":["連接","連結","與...取得聯繫","交往","聯繫起來"],"practiceMeaning":"這些線路將電腦連接到網際網路。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'connectere'，由 'con-' (together) + 'nectere' (to bind, to tie) 構成，字面意思是「一起綁」。核心是「聯合」、「繫在一起」。引申為物理上的「連接」、人際上的「聯繫」，以及觀念上的「連結」或「聯想」。","definition":"1. to join or be joined together; 2. to communicate with someone; 3. to associate one thing with another","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"這些線路將電腦連接到網際網路。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The wires connect the computer to the internet.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"與同事建立良好的聯繫是很重要的。\",\n    \"eng\": \"It's important to connect with your colleagues.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他無法將這些事實聯繫起來。\",\n    \"eng\": \"He can't connect the facts.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這些線路將電腦連接到網際網路。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5773,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::consecutive::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She won the award for three ____ years.","expectedAnswer":"consecutive","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She won the award for three ____ years.","clozeAnswer":"consecutive","exampleTranslation":"她連續三年贏得該獎項。","reference":{"eng":"consecutive","kk":"kənˈsɛkjʊtɪv","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"連續的\"  ],  [    \"接連的\"  ],  [    \"相繼的\"  ]]","chEntries":["連續的","接連的","相繼的"],"practiceMeaning":"她連續三年贏得該獎項。","analysis":"此字為形容詞，構詞自con-（全部；一起）+ -secut-（跟隨；繼承，來自拉丁語sequi「跟隨」）+ -ive（形容詞字尾，表示「性質的；傾向的」）。con-源自拉丁語cum，表示「一起」或「加強」。-secut-是sequi的詞幹，sequi的過去分詞是secutus。-ive字尾源自拉丁語-ivus。因此，consecutive的核心語義是「連續跟隨的；一個接一個的」。語意演變上，從「跟隨」的動作引申為「時間或空間上連續不斷」的狀態。","definition":"1. following continuously or without interruption; 2. in unbroken or logical sequence.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She won the award for three consecutive years.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她連續三年贏得該獎項。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The team had a streak of five consecutive victories.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這支隊伍取得了五連勝。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please list the numbers in consecutive order.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請按順序列出數字。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她連續三年贏得該獎項。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5777,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::controversial::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The politician's statement about immigration was highly ____.","expectedAnswer":"controversial","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The politician's statement about immigration was highly ____.","clozeAnswer":"controversial","exampleTranslation":"那位政治人物關於移民的聲明引起了極大的爭議。","reference":{"eng":"controversial","kk":"ˌkɑntrəˈvɜrʃəl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"有爭議的\"  ],  [    \"引起爭議的\"  ]]","chEntries":["有爭議的","引起爭議的"],"practiceMeaning":"那位政治人物關於移民的聲明引起了極大的爭議。","analysis":"此字為形容詞，構詞自controversy（爭議）+ -ial（形容詞字尾，表示「關於……的；具有……性質的」）。-ial與-al同源，都源自拉丁語-alis。controversy本身源自拉丁語controversia，由con-（一起）+vertere（轉動；扭轉）組成，原意為「爭辯；爭論」，即雙方觀點不斷轉變、交鋒。因此，controversial的核心語義是指「容易引起爭論或爭議的」。語意演變上，由「爭論」的概念引申為「具有爭議性的」狀態。","definition":"1. giving rise or likely to give rise to public disagreement.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The politician's statement about immigration was highly controversial.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那位政治人物關於移民的聲明引起了極大的爭議。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It is a controversial issue with strong opinions on both sides.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個有爭議的問題，雙方都有強烈的意見。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The new policy is considered controversial by many.\",\n    \"ch\": \"許多人認為這項新政策是有爭議的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"那位政治人物關於移民的聲明引起了極大的爭議。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5778,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::controversy::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The recent art exhibition has sparked a lot of ____.","expectedAnswer":"controversy","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The recent art exhibition has sparked a lot of ____.","clozeAnswer":"controversy","exampleTranslation":"最近的藝術展覽引發了許多爭議。","reference":{"eng":"controversy","kk":"ˈkɑntrəˌvɜrsi","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"爭議\"  ],  [    \"爭論\"  ]]","chEntries":["爭議","爭論"],"practiceMeaning":"最近的藝術展覽引發了許多爭議。","analysis":"此字為名詞，源自拉丁語controversia，由con-（一起）+vertere（轉動；扭轉）組成，原意是「互相扭轉；爭辯；爭論」。字面意思是指雙方觀點不斷交鋒、扭轉的狀態。核心語義是指「公開的、嚴重的爭論或爭議」，通常涉及對某事物的不同意見或衝突。語意演變上，從「爭辯」的動作發展為「爭論」的狀態或議題。","definition":"1. public disagreement about something that many people have strong opinions about; 2. a lengthy dispute or debate.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The recent art exhibition has sparked a lot of controversy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"最近的藝術展覽引發了許多爭議。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There is ongoing controversy over the new environmental regulations.\",\n    \"ch\": \"關於新的環保條例，持續存在爭議。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The film's ending generated considerable controversy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這部電影的結局引起了相當大的爭議。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"最近的藝術展覽引發了許多爭議。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5527,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l5::convince::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He tried to ____ her that he was telling the truth.","expectedAnswer":"convince","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He tried to ____ her that he was telling the truth.","clozeAnswer":"convince","exampleTranslation":"他試圖說服她他所說的是實話。","reference":{"eng":"convince","kk":"kənˈvɪns","tense":"v.","ch":"[['說服'], ['使信服']]","chEntries":["說服","使信服"],"practiceMeaning":"他試圖說服她他所說的是實話。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'convincere'，由 'com-' (together, with) + 'vincere' (to conquer, to overcome) 構成。原始語義是「徹底克服」或「征服」，引申為「通過論證使對方信服」。構詞上，'com-' 表示「徹底地」或「共同」，'vinc-' 是 'vincere' 的詞幹，意為「克服、戰勝」。'convince' 的核心語意是「通過說理或證據，使人相信某事或某觀點」。它強調的是說服的過程和使對方產生認知上的轉變。","definition":"to cause (someone) to believe firmly in the truth of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He tried to convince her that he was telling the truth.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他試圖說服她他所說的是實話。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The evidence was enough to convince the jury.\",\n    \"ch\": \"證據足以讓陪審團信服。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他試圖說服她他所說的是實話。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5076,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::coordinate::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need to ____ our efforts to finish the project on time.","expectedAnswer":"coordinate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need to ____ our efforts to finish the project on time.","clozeAnswer":"coordinate","exampleTranslation":"我們需要協調我們的努力，以便按時完成專案。","reference":{"eng":"coordinate","kk":"koʊˈɔːrdnət","tense":"v.","ch":"[['協調'], ['協同工作'], ['使同步']]","chEntries":["協調","協同工作","使同步"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要協調我們的努力，以便按時完成專案。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'con-' (together) + 'ordinare' (to put in order)，原意是 '共同使之有序'。其核心概念是將獨立的元素、行動或系統安排在一起，使其和諧地共同運作，達到預期目標。這涉及時間、空間、功能上的整合，以避免衝突並提高效率。","definition":"1. To bring the different elements of (a group or organization) into a harmonious or efficient relationship.; 2. To work together efficiently.; 3. To cause two or more things to happen or move at the same time or in the same way.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to coordinate our efforts to finish the project on time.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要協調我們的努力，以便按時完成專案。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The dancers coordinated their movements perfectly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"舞者們完美地協調了他們的動作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The organization works to coordinate aid to disaster areas.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該組織致力於協調對災