"],"practiceMeaning":"他是一名出色的板球運動員。","analysis":"1. 指一種流行的英國球類運動，『板球』。2. 指一種昆蟲，『蟋蟀』，因其發出的鳴叫聲而得名，可能與其聲音的擬聲詞有關。","definition":"a game played with a bat and ball between two teams of eleven players; a small jumping insect that makes a high-pitched sound","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a great cricket player.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一名出色的板球運動員。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The sound of crickets filled the summer night.\",\n    \"ch\": \"蟋蟀的叫聲充滿了夏夜。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They went to watch a cricket match.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們去看了一場板球比賽。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他是一名出色的板球運動員。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4277,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::crop::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The farmer surveyed his healthy wheat ____.","expectedAnswer":"crop","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The farmer surveyed his healthy wheat ____.","clozeAnswer":"crop","exampleTranslation":"農夫檢查他健康的小麥收成。","reference":{"eng":"crop","kk":"/krɑːp/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['農作物'], ['收成'], ['（短髮）齊髮尾的']]","chEntries":["農作物","收成","齊髮尾的"],"practiceMeaning":"農夫檢查他健康的小麥收成。","analysis":"源自古英語 'crop'，意為「莖、嫩芽」。'Crop' 指「一年生長的植物，尤指穀物」，也可以指「一次收成的總量」。引申為「短髮齊髮尾的」樣式，可能與植物被一次性收割的形象相似。","definition":"a cultivated plant that is grown on a large scale to provide food, animal fodder, or other products; the amount of a plant that is gathered.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The farmer surveyed his healthy wheat crop.\",\n    \"ch\": \"農夫檢查他健康的小麥收成。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This year's crop of strawberries is excellent.\",\n    \"ch\": \"今年的草莓收成非常好。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"農夫檢查他健康的小麥收成。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3135,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::cube::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The magician made the rabbit disappear inside a large ____.","expectedAnswer":"cube","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The magician made the rabbit disappear inside a large ____.","clozeAnswer":"cube","exampleTranslation":"魔術師讓兔子在一個大立方體裡面消失了。","reference":{"eng":"cube","kk":"/kjuːb/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['立方體；立方塊'], ['（尤指食品）塊；方糖']]","chEntries":["立方體","立方塊","塊","方糖"],"practiceMeaning":"魔術師讓兔子在一個大立方體裡面消失了。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'cubus'，再追溯至希臘語 'kybos'，意為「骰子，立方體」。'Cube' 的基本幾何概念是一個三維的、有六個相等正方形面的物體。語意延伸至任何具有立方體或塊狀形狀的物體，特別是切割成規則塊狀的食品，如方糖、冰塊、肉塊等。","definition":"1. a solid body with six equal square sides; 2. a piece of food cut into a cube; 3. a sugar cube.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The magician made the rabbit disappear inside a large cube.\",\n    \"ch\": \"魔術師讓兔子在一個大立方體裡面消失了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please add a cube of butter to the pan.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請在鍋裡加一塊黃油。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He dropped a sugar cube into his tea.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他往茶裡丟了一塊方糖。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"魔術師讓兔子在一個大立方體裡面消失了。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5079,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::currency::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The US dollar is a major international ____.","expectedAnswer":"currency","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The US dollar is a major international ____.","clozeAnswer":"currency","exampleTranslation":"美元是主要的國際貨幣。","reference":{"eng":"currency","kk":"ˈkɜːrənsi","tense":"n.","ch":"[['貨幣'], ['通用性'], ['流通']]","chEntries":["貨幣","通用性","流通"],"practiceMeaning":"美元是主要的國際貨幣。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'currere' (to run)，透過中古英語 'curraunt' (running, current) 演變而來，與 'current' (當前的，流動的) 同源。其核心語義是 '流通的'。因此，'currency' 指的是在特定地區或國家被廣泛接受並用於交易的 '貨幣'。引申開來，它也指觀念、意見或事物的 '通用性' 或 '流行度'，即它們在當前社會中的 '流通' 程度。","definition":"1. A system of money in general use in a particular country.; 2. The quality or state of being current or generally accepted.; 3. General acceptance or prevalence.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The US dollar is a major international currency.\",\n    \"ch\": \"美元是主要的國際貨幣。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His ideas gained currency among young people.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的想法在年輕人中獲得了通用性。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The currency of this rumor is unknown.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個謠言的流通性（或說來源）不明。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"美元是主要的國際貨幣。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5291,"wordRef":"字彙王::u63::customs::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"You must declare all goods at ____.","expectedAnswer":"customs","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"You must declare all goods at ____.","clozeAnswer":"customs","exampleTranslation":"您必須在海關申報所有貨物。","reference":{"eng":"customs","kk":"ˈkʌstəmz","tense":"n.","ch":"[['海關'], ['關稅', '進口稅'], ['（個人的）習慣，習俗']]","chEntries":["海關","關稅","進口稅","習慣，習俗"],"practiceMeaning":"您必須在海關申報所有貨物。","analysis":"此字是 'custom' 的複數形式，但作為「海關」義時，通常使用複數 'customs'。'custom' 本身源自古法語 'custume'（習慣、稅收），最終來自拉丁語 'consuetudinem'（習慣、慣例）。'customs' 作為「海關」時，是指政府機關負責徵收關稅和管制進出口貨物。其核心語意從「慣例、習慣」引申為「例行徵收的稅款」（關稅），再引申為負責此事務的「海關」機構。","definition":"the place where you go to a country's airport or seaport to check on your luggage and goods, and where officers check if you are carrying anything illegal; taxes paid on goods imported into or exported from a country; the rules or habits that are traditional in a particular society or group.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"You must declare all goods at customs.\",\n    \"ch\": \"您必須在海關申報所有貨物。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The customs officials inspected his luggage.\",\n    \"ch\": \"海關官員檢查了他的行李。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Local customs dictate how guests are treated.\",\n    \"ch\": \"當地的習俗決定了如何對待客人。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"您必須在海關申報所有貨物。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U63"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3212,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::damp::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The clothes are still ____ after washing.","expectedAnswer":"damp","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The clothes are still ____ after washing.","clozeAnswer":"damp","exampleTranslation":"衣服洗過後還是潮濕的。","reference":{"eng":"damp","kk":"/dæmp/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['潮濕的'], ['微濕的']]","chEntries":["潮濕的","微濕的"],"practiceMeaning":"衣服洗過後還是潮濕的。","analysis":"詞源來自古荷蘭語 'damp'，意為 'moisture, vapor'。指輕微的濕潤，通常是由於水汽或滲入的水分，與『dry』（乾燥）相對。","definition":"slightly wet.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The clothes are still damp after washing.\",\n    \"ch\": \"衣服洗過後還是潮濕的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The air in the basement was cold and damp.\",\n    \"ch\": \"地下室的空氣又冷又潮濕。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"衣服洗過後還是潮濕的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U41"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3279,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::deadline::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ for submitting the proposal is Friday.","expectedAnswer":"deadline","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ for submitting the proposal is Friday.","clozeAnswer":"deadline","exampleTranslation":"提交提案的截止日期是週五。","reference":{"eng":"deadline","kk":"/ˈdɛdlaɪn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['截止日期；最後期限']]","chEntries":["截止日期","最後期限"],"practiceMeaning":"提交提案的截止日期是週五。","analysis":"最初指戰俘營中劃定的、越過則會被射殺的線（dead line）。後來引申為任何工作的最後限期。","definition":"the time by which something must be finished or submitted.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The deadline for submitting the proposal is Friday.\",\n    \"ch\": \"提交提案的截止日期是週五。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I'm working hard to meet the deadline.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我正努力趕上最後期限。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"提交提案的截止日期是週五。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5125,"wordRef":"字彙王::u62::debut::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The young actress made her ____ on Broadway.","expectedAnswer":"debut","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The young actress made her ____ on Broadway.","clozeAnswer":"debut","exampleTranslation":"這位年輕女演員在百老匯首次亮相。","reference":{"eng":"debut","kk":"ˈdeɪbjuː","tense":"n.","ch":"[['首次亮相'], ['初次登場'], ['首次演出']]","chEntries":["首次亮相","初次登場","首次演出"],"practiceMeaning":"這位年輕女演員在百老匯首次亮相。","analysis":"此字源自法語 début，意為「開始、開端」，來自 débuter（開始、首次登場）。débuter 本身是法語中表示「開始」的動詞。核心語意是「第一次公開露面或表演」，常用於演藝界、體育界或時尚界。","definition":"a person's first appearance or performance in public, in a particular role or capacity; the first of a series of performances of a show.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The young actress made her debut on Broadway.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位年輕女演員在百老匯首次亮相。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The band's debut album was a huge success.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該樂團的首張專輯取得了巨大成功。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這位年輕女演員在百老匯首次亮相。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U62"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5292,"wordRef":"字彙王::u63::deceive::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He tried to ____ the public with false promises.","expectedAnswer":"deceive","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He tried to ____ the public with false promises.","clozeAnswer":"deceive","exampleTranslation":"他試圖用虛假的承諾來欺騙公眾。","reference":{"eng":"deceive","kk":"dɪˈsiːv","tense":"v.","ch":"[['欺騙', '騙取']]","chEntries":["欺騙","騙取"],"practiceMeaning":"他試圖用虛假的承諾來欺騙公眾。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'decipere'，由 'de-'（down, away）和 'capere'（to take）組成。構詞上，'de-' 作為否定或錯誤前綴，'capere' 是詞根，'-ere' 是動詞後綴。原始語義為「向下拿取」，引申為「欺騙、使受騙」。'deceive' 強調通過虛假信息或行為來誤導他人，使其相信不真實的事物。","definition":"to deliberately cause someone to believe something that is not true, especially for the gain of the deceiver.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He tried to deceive the public with false promises.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他試圖用虛假的承諾來欺騙公眾。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Don't let them deceive you.\",\n    \"ch\": \"別讓他們欺騙了你。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他試圖用虛假的承諾來欺騙公眾。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U63"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5640,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l8::decline::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We observed a sharp ____ in sales.","expectedAnswer":"decline","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We observed a sharp ____ in sales.","clozeAnswer":"decline","exampleTranslation":"我們觀察到銷售額急劇下降。","reference":{"eng":"decline","kk":"dɪˈklaɪn","tense":"n.","ch":"[['下降'], ['衰退'], ['減少']]","chEntries":["下降","衰退","減少"],"practiceMeaning":"我們觀察到銷售額急劇下降。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 declinen，來自拉丁語 declinare，由 de-（向下，away）+ clinare（彎曲，to bend）組成。clinare 來自原始印歐語 *klei-（傾斜；依偎）。因此，decline 的核心語義是「向下彎曲」或「轉向」。從物理的「向下」延伸至抽象的「減少」、「衰退」。此處為名詞用法，指代「下降」、「衰退」或「減少」的現象或趨勢。構詞上，de- 表達「向下」或「遠離」，clinare 提供「彎曲」或「傾斜」的核心動作。","definition":"a downward movement or trend; a decrease in quantity or quality; a deterioration.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We observed a sharp decline in sales.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們觀察到銷售額急劇下降。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The country experienced an economic decline.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個國家經歷了經濟衰退。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們觀察到銷售額急劇下降。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4349,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::decrease::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There has been a ____ in violent crime.","expectedAnswer":"decrease","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There has been a ____ in violent crime.","clozeAnswer":"decrease","exampleTranslation":"暴力犯罪有所減少。","reference":{"eng":"decrease","kk":"/ˈdiːkriːs/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['減少；降低']]","chEntries":["減少","降低"],"practiceMeaning":"暴力犯罪有所減少。","analysis":"名詞形式，源自動詞 'decrease'，指『減少的數量或程度』，與『增加』相對。","definition":"a reduction in the size, amount, or number of something","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There has been a decrease in violent crime.\",\n    \"ch\": \"暴力犯罪有所減少。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We observed a significant decrease in temperature.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們觀察到氣溫顯著下降。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The decrease in demand led to lower prices.\",\n    \"ch\": \"需求的減少導致價格下跌。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"暴力犯罪有所減少。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4686,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::deed::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His good ____ was recognized by the community.","expectedAnswer":"deed","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His good ____ was recognized by the community.","clozeAnswer":"deed","exampleTranslation":"他這個善舉得到了社區的認可。","reference":{"eng":"deed","kk":"/ˈdid/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['行為'], ['事蹟'], ['（法律）契據']]","chEntries":["行為","事蹟","契據"],"practiceMeaning":"他這個善舉得到了社區的認可。","analysis":"源自古英語 *dēd*，與 'do'（做）同源。核心是「做出來的事情」。引申至具有重要性或價值的事蹟，以及法律上證明財產權的書面文件。","definition":"1. An action that is done. 2. An act or achievement, especially one that is brave or worthy of admiration. 3. A legal document that transfers ownership of property from one person to another.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His good deed was recognized by the community.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他這個善舉得到了社區的認可。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The heroic deed of the firefighters saved many lives.\",\n    \"ch\": \"消防員的英勇事蹟拯救了許多生命。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He signed the deed to the house.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他簽署了房子的契據。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他這個善舉得到了社區的認可。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5614,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l7::democracy::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Many countries around the world strive for ____.","expectedAnswer":"democracy","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Many countries around the world strive for ____.","clozeAnswer":"democracy","exampleTranslation":"世界各國許多國家都在努力爭取民主。","reference":{"eng":"democracy","kk":"dəˈmɑkrəsi","tense":"n.","ch":"[['民主'], ['民主制度'], ['民主國家']]","chEntries":["民主","民主制度","民主國家"],"practiceMeaning":"世界各國許多國家都在努力爭取民主。","analysis":"此字源自希臘語 'dēmokratía' (δημοκρατία)，意為「人民統治」，由 'dēmos'（人民）和 'kratos'（權力、統治）組成，加上名詞化後綴 '-ia'。構詞學上，'dēmo-' 是「人民」的詞根，'-krat-' 是「權力」或「統治」的詞根，'-cy'（來自 '-ia'）是表示「狀態」、「政府」或「制度」的名詞化後綴。原始語意是「人民的統治」。現代意義指一種由人民透過直接或間接方式掌握政治權力的政府形式或社會制度。","definition":"1. Government by the people, especially rule of the majority, either directly or through elected representatives; 2. A state or society characterized by such government.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Many countries around the world strive for democracy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"世界各國許多國家都在努力爭取民主。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The transition to democracy was difficult but ultimately successful.\",\n    \"ch\": \"向民主制度的轉變雖然艱難，但最終是成功的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"世界各國許多國家都在努力爭取民主。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4143,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::democratic::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They live in a ____ society.","expectedAnswer":"democratic","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They live in a ____ society.","clozeAnswer":"democratic","exampleTranslation":"他們生活在一個民主社會。","reference":{"eng":"democratic","kk":"/ˌdɛməˈkrætɪk/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['民主的']]","chEntries":["民主的"],"practiceMeaning":"他們生活在一個民主社會。","analysis":"源自 democracy（民主），democracy 源自希臘語 dēmos（人民）+ kratos（統治）。核心概念是「人民統治」或「支持民主原則」。","definition":"1. relating to or supporting democracy or its principles; 2. (of a country or system of government) controlled by or having elected representatives elected by the people","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They live in a democratic society.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們生活在一個民主社會。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The organization is run on democratic principles.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個組織依照民主原則運作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a staunch supporter of democratic ideals.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是民主理想的堅定支持者。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們生活在一個民主社會。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U5、L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6220,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::deputy::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The sheriff appointed a ____ to help manage the jail.","expectedAnswer":"deputy","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The sheriff appointed a ____ to help manage the jail.","clozeAnswer":"deputy","exampleTranslation":"治安官任命了一名副手來協助管理監獄。","reference":{"eng":"deputy","kk":"ˈdɛpjuti","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"代理人\"  ],  [    \"代表\"  ],  [    \"副手\"  ],  [    \"副官\"  ]]","chEntries":["代理人","代表","副手","副官"],"practiceMeaning":"治安官任命了一名副手來協助管理監獄。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 deputé，意為「被派遣的，代表」，向上可追溯至拉丁語 deputare，由 de-（表示除去，關於）和 putare（認為，估計）組成，意為「認為是，指派」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。名詞義指被正式授權代表他人行事的人，或在特定職位上擔任次要或輔助角色的人，通常是該職位的主要負責人的助手或代理。中文翻譯為「代理人；代表；副手；副官」。","definition":"1. a person who is appointed to act for or replace someone else, especially in a political or official role; 2. a person who is second in command or assists someone in a position of authority.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The sheriff appointed a deputy to help manage the jail.\",\n    \"ch\": \"治安官任命了一名副手來協助管理監獄。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is the deputy director of the department.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是該部門的副主任。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The president's deputy attended the international summit.\",\n    \"ch\": \"總統的代表出席了國際峰會。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"治安官任命了一名副手來協助管理監獄。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6221,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::derive::vt","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Many people ____ great pleasure from reading.","expectedAnswer":"derive","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Many people ____ great pleasure from reading.","clozeAnswer":"derive","exampleTranslation":"許多人從閱讀中獲得極大的樂趣。","reference":{"eng":"derive","kk":"dɪˈraɪv","tense":"vt.","ch":"[  [    \"獲得\"  ],  [    \"得到\"  ],  [    \"源自\"  ],  [    \"源於\"  ],  [    \"推導出\"  ]]","chEntries":["獲得","得到","源自","源於","推導出"],"practiceMeaning":"許多人從閱讀中獲得極大的樂趣。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 deriver，由 de-（表示源自，關於）和 river（河流）組成，意為「從…流出」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作及物動詞時，核心語義是從某個來源獲得、得到某物，特別是利益、知識、名稱或從某個源頭演變而來。在數學或邏輯上，也指從已知前提推導出結論。此及物動詞義必須接受詞，例如 derive income、derive pleasure、derive from sth.。中文翻譯為「獲得；得到；源自；源於；推導出」。","definition":"1. to get something, especially an advantage or pleasure, from something; 2. to come from or be descended from a particular person, place, or thing; 3. to reach a conclusion or an answer by reasoning.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Many people derive great pleasure from reading.\",\n    \"ch\": \"許多人從閱讀中獲得極大的樂趣。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This word is derived from Latin.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個詞源自拉丁語。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company derives its revenue from online sales.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司的收入來自於線上銷售。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We can derive the formula from the given principles.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們可以從給定的原理推導出這個公式。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"許多人從閱讀中獲得極大的樂趣。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5703,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l9::despair::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Don't ____; things will get better.","expectedAnswer":"despair","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Don't ____; things will get better.","clozeAnswer":"despair","exampleTranslation":"別絕望；事情會好轉的。","reference":{"eng":"despair","kk":"dɪˈsper","tense":"v.","ch":"[['絕望'], ['失望']]","chEntries":["絕望","失望"],"practiceMeaning":"別絕望；事情會好轉的。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 desespoir，由 de-（來自拉丁語 de-，表示『否定』或『失去』）+ espoir（來自拉丁語 sperare，意為『希望』）構成。作為動詞，其核心語意是「失去希望」，或者「感到非常失望，以至於認為沒有希望」。","definition":"to lose all hope.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Don't despair; things will get better.\",\n    \"ch\": \"別絕望；事情會好轉的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She despaired of ever finding a job.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對能找到工作感到絕望。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"別絕望；事情會好轉的。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3138,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::dew::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The grass was covered in ____ when I woke up.","expectedAnswer":"dew","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The grass was covered in ____ when I woke up.","clozeAnswer":"dew","exampleTranslation":"我醒來時，草地上覆蓋著露水。","reference":{"eng":"dew","kk":"/djuː/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['露；露水']]","chEntries":["露","露水"],"practiceMeaning":"我醒來時，草地上覆蓋著露水。","analysis":"詞源來自古英語 'deaw'，與「濕潤」的概念相關。'Dew' 是指夜間或清晨，空氣中的水蒸氣在較冷的物體表面凝結成的小水滴。它是一個自然現象，與清晨、新鮮、濕潤的環境聯繫在一起。其語意通常帶有清新、純潔或短暫的美好意象。","definition":"tiny drops of water that form on cool surfaces at night, when condensation occurs.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The grass was covered in dew when I woke up.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我醒來時，草地上覆蓋著露水。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The morning dew glistened on the spiderweb.\",\n    \"ch\": \"晨露在蜘蛛網上閃閃發光。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A fine dew settled on the leaves.\",\n    \"ch\": \"細密的露水落在葉子上。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我醒來時，草地上覆蓋著露水。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4174,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::difference::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There is a significant ____ between A and B.","expectedAnswer":"difference","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There is a significant ____ between A and B.","clozeAnswer":"difference","exampleTranslation":"A 和 B 之間存在顯著的差異。","reference":{"eng":"difference","kk":"/ˈdɪfərəns/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['差異', '區別'], ['（意見的）分歧'], ['重要性']]","chEntries":["差異","區別","分歧","重要性"],"practiceMeaning":"A 和 B 之間存在顯著的差異。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 differentia（差異），是動詞 differre（不同，延遲）的名詞形式。核心概念是「事物之間的不相同之處」。","definition":"1. a way in which a person or thing is not the same as another; 2. a disagreement or quarrel; 3. importance or relevance","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There is a significant difference between A and B.\",\n    \"ch\": \"A 和 B 之間存在顯著的差異。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"What's the difference between these two products?\",\n    \"ch\": \"這兩款產品有什麼區別？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His contribution made a real difference.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的貢獻帶來了真正的改變（重要性）。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"A 和 B 之間存在顯著的差異。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5039,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::disconnect::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Please ____ the power cord before cleaning.","expectedAnswer":"disconnect","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Please ____ the power cord before cleaning.","clozeAnswer":"disconnect","exampleTranslation":"清潔前請斷開電源線。","reference":{"eng":"disconnect","kk":"ˌdɪskəˈnekt","tense":"v.","ch":"[['斷開'], ['分離'], ['使失去聯繫']]","chEntries":["斷開","分離","使失去聯繫"],"practiceMeaning":"清潔前請斷開電源線。","analysis":"此字由否定前綴 dis-（分離、相反）和動詞 connect（連接）組合而成。dis- 的否定作用與 connect 的「連接」意義結合，構成了「斷開連接、分離」的核心語意。此動詞可指物理上的斷開，也可指抽象概念上的「失去聯繫」或「不一致」。OCR 掃描時可能將 'c' 誤判為 'l'，或單字黏合。此處修正為 disconnect，其語意清晰。","definition":"1. to break the connection between two or more things; 2. to separate or detach.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please disconnect the power cord before cleaning.\",\n    \"ch\": \"清潔前請斷開電源線。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The team felt disconnected from management.\",\n    \"ch\": \"團隊感覺與管理層失去了聯繫。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"清潔前請斷開電源線。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5612,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l7::discriminate::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It is important not to ____ against any job applicants.","expectedAnswer":"discriminate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It is important not to ____ against any job applicants.","clozeAnswer":"discriminate","exampleTranslation":"重要的是不要歧視任何求職者。","reference":{"eng":"discriminate","kk":"dɪˈskrɪmɪneɪt","tense":"v.","ch":"[['歧視'], ['區別對待'], ['辨別']]","chEntries":["歧視","區別對待","辨別"],"practiceMeaning":"重要的是不要歧視任何求職者。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'discriminare'，意為「區分」，由 'dis-'（分開）和 'cernere'（分辨）組成。構詞學上，'dis-' 字首表示「分開」、「分離」，'cernere' 詞根提供「分辨」、「篩選」的核心語意。'-ate' 是常見的動詞化字尾。原始語意是「將事物分開、區別開來」。引申出兩個主要用法：一是「分辨、辨別」（distinguish），即識別細微差異的能力；二是「不公平地對待、區別對待」，即「歧視」。","definition":"1. Make an unjust or prejudicial distinction in the treatment of different categories of people or things, especially on the grounds of race, sex, or age; 2. Recognize or afford indication of the difference between.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It is important not to discriminate against any job applicants.\",\n    \"ch\": \"重要的是不要歧視任何求職者。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Babies can discriminate between familiar and unfamiliar faces.\",\n    \"ch\": \"嬰兒可以辨別熟悉的和不熟悉的臉孔。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The law prohibits employers from discriminating on the basis of age.\",\n    \"ch\": \"法律禁止雇主基於年齡進行歧視。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"重要的是不要歧視任何求職者。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3078,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::disorder::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The room was in a state of complete ____.","expectedAnswer":"disorder","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The room was in a state of complete ____.","clozeAnswer":"disorder","exampleTranslation":"房間裡一片混亂。","reference":{"eng":"disorder","kk":"/dɪsˈɔːrdər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['混亂；無秩序'], ['失調；疾病'], ['（政治、社會）動亂']]","chEntries":["混亂","無秩序","失調","疾病","動亂"],"practiceMeaning":"房間裡一片混亂。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'dis-' (not) + 'ordo' (order)。核心意義是「缺乏秩序」。\n1. 混亂；無秩序：指缺乏組織、雜亂無章的狀態。\n2. 失調；疾病：指身體或精神功能的不正常、混亂的狀態，通常表現為疾病。\n3. （政治、社會）動亂：指社會秩序的破壞，例如騷亂或暴動。","definition":"1. a state of confusion; 2. a state of not being neat or tidy; 3. an illness or a medical condition that is not normal; 4. a disturbance of the peace.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The room was in a state of complete disorder.\",\n    \"ch\": \"房間裡一片混亂。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He suffers from a sleep disorder.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他患有睡眠失調症。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The protests quickly turned into disorder.\",\n    \"ch\": \"抗議活動很快演變成動亂。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"房間裡一片混亂。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4011,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u3::dizzy::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The roller coaster ride made me feel ____.","expectedAnswer":"dizzy","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The roller coaster ride made me feel ____.","clozeAnswer":"dizzy","exampleTranslation":"坐雲霄飛車讓我感到頭暈。","reference":{"eng":"dizzy","kk":"/ˈdɪzi/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['頭暈的', '暈眩的'], ['眼花繚亂的']]","chEntries":["頭暈的","暈眩的","眼花繚亂的"],"practiceMeaning":"坐雲霄飛車讓我感到頭暈。","analysis":"詞源：來自 'daze' (使發呆)。指頭部失去平衡感，感覺天旋地轉。","definition":"1. having or causing a sensation of spinning around and losing one's balance; 2. bewildered or confused.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The roller coaster ride made me feel dizzy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"坐雲霄飛車讓我感到頭暈。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The sheer number of choices made her dizzy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"琳瑯滿目的選擇讓她眼花繚亂。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"坐雲霄飛車讓我感到頭暈。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4548,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::dock::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ship is at the ____, unloading its cargo.","expectedAnswer":"dock","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ship is at the ____, unloading its cargo.","clozeAnswer":"dock","exampleTranslation":"船正在碼頭卸貨。","reference":{"eng":"dock","kk":"/dɒk/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['碼頭', '泊位'], ['（法院的）被告席']]","chEntries":["碼頭","泊位","被告席"],"practiceMeaning":"船正在碼頭卸貨。","analysis":"源自荷蘭語 'dok'，可能源自日耳曼語。\n    1. 碼頭、泊位：船隻停泊、裝卸貨物的場所。\n    2. 法院的被告席：專指被告在法庭上站立的地方，引申為被告的身份。","definition":"1. an enclosed area of water in a port where ships may be moored for loading or unloading.; 2. the place in a law court where a prisoner stands or is seated.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The ship is at the dock, unloading its cargo.\",\n    \"ch\": \"船正在碼頭卸貨。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The judge asked the prisoner to approach the dock.\",\n    \"ch\": \"法官請囚犯走近被告席。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"船正在碼頭卸貨。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3141,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::dominant::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She played a ____ role in the negotiations.","expectedAnswer":"dominant","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She played a ____ role in the negotiations.","clozeAnswer":"dominant","exampleTranslation":"她在談判中扮演了主導角色。","reference":{"eng":"dominant","kk":"/ˈdɒmɪnənt/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['占主導地位的；有影響力的'], ['（基因）顯性的'], ['（地理、建築等）顯著的，突出的']]","chEntries":["占主導地位的","有影響力的","顯性的","顯著的，突出的"],"practiceMeaning":"她在談判中扮演了主導角色。","analysis":"形容詞，源自動詞 'dominate'。表示處於權力、控制或影響力的頂峰，是最重要的、最強勢的或最明顯的部分。在生物學中，'dominant gene' 指的是會壓倒另一條基因（隱性基因）並決定性狀的基因。其語意核心是「最重要」、「最強」或「最顯著」。","definition":"1. having power and influence over others; 2. the most important or noticeable; 3. (of a gene) expressing its phenotype readily over a corresponding recessive gene.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She played a dominant role in the negotiations.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在談判中扮演了主導角色。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Red is the dominant color in the painting.\",\n    \"ch\": \"紅色是這幅畫的主導色彩。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"In genetics, the dominant allele masks the effect of the recessive allele.\",\n    \"ch\": \"在遺傳學中，顯性等位基因會掩蓋隱性等位基因的作用。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她在談判中扮演了主導角色。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5779,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::donate::vt","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Many people decided to ____ blood after the earthquake.","expectedAnswer":"donate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Many people decided to ____ blood after the earthquake.","clozeAnswer":"donate","exampleTranslation":"許多人在地震後決定捐血。","reference":{"eng":"donate","kk":"ˈdoʊneɪt","tense":"vt.","ch":"[  [    \"捐贈\"  ],  [    \"捐獻\"  ],  [    \"贈送\"  ]]","chEntries":["捐贈","捐獻","贈送"],"practiceMeaning":"許多人在地震後決定捐血。","analysis":"此字為及物動詞，源自拉丁語donare，意為「給予；捐贈」。donare又來自donum（禮物），donum則源自donare（給予），其詞根是do（給予）。-ate是拉丁語動詞字尾。因此，donate的核心語義是「將物品或金錢自願地給予他人或機構」。語意演變上，從「給予」的廣泛概念，具體化為「出於慈善或支持目的而捐贈」。","definition":"1. to give money, food, or help to a charitable organization or to someone in need; 2. to give blood or organs for medical use.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Many people decided to donate blood after the earthquake.\",\n    \"ch\": \"許多人在地震後決定捐血。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She donates a portion of her salary to charity each month.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她每月將一部分薪水捐給慈善機構。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company will donate computers to local schools.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司將向當地學校捐贈電腦。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"許多人在地震後決定捐血。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3937,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::downtown::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Let's go ____ to buy some clothes.","expectedAnswer":"downtown","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Let's go ____ to buy some clothes.","clozeAnswer":"downtown","exampleTranslation":"我們去市中心買些衣服吧。","reference":{"eng":"downtown","kk":"/ˈdaʊntaʊn/","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['在市中心（去）']]","chEntries":["在市中心"],"practiceMeaning":"我們去市中心買些衣服吧。","analysis":"最初指城市中心商業區，由 'down' (副詞，表示向下) 和 'town' (名詞，城市) 組成。表示「在城市的心臟地帶」。","definition":"in or towards the central area of a city or town.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Let's go downtown to buy some clothes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們去市中心買些衣服吧。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He works downtown.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在市中心工作。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們去市中心買些衣服吧。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5641,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l8::dramatically::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The stock market fell ____.","expectedAnswer":"dramatically","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The stock market fell ____.","clozeAnswer":"dramatically","exampleTranslation":"股市劇烈下跌。","reference":{"eng":"dramatically","kk":"drəˈmætɪkli","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['戲劇性地'], ['引人注目地'], ['劇烈地']]","chEntries":["戲劇性地","引人注目地","劇烈地"],"practiceMeaning":"股市劇烈下跌。","analysis":"此字為 dramatic（戲劇性的）的副詞形式，由 dramatic + -ally（副詞字尾）構成。dramatic 源自拉丁語 dramaticus，來自希臘語 dramatikos，意為「戲劇的」，其根源為 drama（戲劇），來自希臘語 dromos（奔跑，賽跑），再追溯至動詞 δρα- (dran) / δράω (draō)（做，行動）。核心語義與「戲劇」相關，引申為「誇張的」、「引人注目的」、「激烈的」。-ally 是常見的副詞字尾，由 -al + -ly 構成，將形容詞轉為副詞，表示「以……的方式」。構詞上，drama 是核心，-tic 表「相關的」，-ally 表「方式」。","definition":"in a very noticeable and striking way; to a very great extent; suddenly and to a surprising degree.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The stock market fell dramatically.\",\n    \"ch\": \"股市劇烈下跌。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her life changed dramatically after winning the lottery.\",\n    \"ch\": \"贏得樂透後，她的生活發生了戲劇性的變化。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"股市劇烈下跌。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5081,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::drought::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The region is suffering from a severe ____.","expectedAnswer":"drought","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The region is suffering from a severe ____.","clozeAnswer":"drought","exampleTranslation":"該地區正遭受嚴重乾旱。","reference":{"eng":"drought","kk":"draʊt","tense":"n.","ch":"[['乾旱'], ['長期嚴重缺乏']]","chEntries":["乾旱","長期嚴重缺乏"],"practiceMeaning":"該地區正遭受嚴重乾旱。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 'drūgath'，與 'dry' (乾燥) 同源。其核心語義是 '長期缺乏降水導致的乾燥狀態'。這個物理上的乾旱被廣泛引申為任何重要事物（如水、食物、金錢、靈感）的長期嚴重匱乏。這是一種比喻意義上的 '枯竭'。","definition":"1. A prolonged period of abnormally low rainfall, leading to a shortage of water.; 2. A long period when there is little or no rain.; 3. A long period during which there is a lack of something that is needed.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The region is suffering from a severe drought.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該地區正遭受嚴重乾旱。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The drought has led to crop failures.\",\n    \"ch\": \"乾旱導致了農作物歉收。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was a drought of new ideas in the company.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司裡新點子匱乏。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該地區正遭受嚴重乾旱。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3079,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::durable::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This material is very ____ and resistant to wear.","expectedAnswer":"durable","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This material is very ____ and resistant to wear.","clozeAnswer":"durable","exampleTranslation":"這種材料非常耐用，抗磨損。","reference":{"eng":"durable","kk":"/ˈdʊrəbl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['耐用的；持久的'], ['堅固的；強韌的']]","chEntries":["耐用的","持久的","堅固的","強韌的"],"practiceMeaning":"這種材料非常耐用，抗磨損。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'durare' (to last, to endure)。核心意義是「能夠長時間存在或使用」。\n1. 耐用的；持久的：指能夠承受長時間的使用或磨損而不損壞。\n2. 堅固的；強韌的：形容物質材料或結構的穩固和強壯。","definition":"1. able to last for a long time without being damaged; 2. strong and not easily damaged.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This material is very durable and resistant to wear.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種材料非常耐用，抗磨損。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They are looking for durable solutions to environmental problems.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們正在尋找持久的環境問題解決方案。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這種材料非常耐用，抗磨損。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4184,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::dust::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The furniture was covered in ____.","expectedAnswer":"dust","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The furniture was covered in ____.","clozeAnswer":"dust","exampleTranslation":"家具上覆蓋著一層灰塵。","reference":{"eng":"dust","kk":"/dʌst/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['灰塵；塵土'], ['粉末'], ['（植物的）花粉']]","chEntries":["灰塵","塵土","粉末","花粉"],"practiceMeaning":"家具上覆蓋著一層灰塵。","analysis":"源自古英語 dust，指“微小的乾燥顆粒”。詞源不詳，可能與印歐語 *dheus-（吹，煙）有關。核心意義是散布在地表或空中的微小顆粒。引申義可用於指任何細小的粉末狀物質，如化妝品、藥粉，或植物的花粉。","definition":"1. fine, dry powder consisting of tiny particles of earth or from other matter; 2. powder, 