furious","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He was ____ when he discovered his car had been stolen.","clozeAnswer":"furious","exampleTranslation":"他發現汽車被偷後勃然大怒。","reference":{"eng":"furious","kk":"/ˈfjʊəriəs/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['狂怒的；暴怒的'], ['（風、風暴等）猛烈的；狂暴的']]","chEntries":["狂怒的","暴怒的","猛烈的","狂暴的"],"practiceMeaning":"他發現汽車被偷後勃然大怒。","analysis":"詞源來自拉丁語 'furiosus'，意為「瘋狂的，狂怒的」，與 'furia'（狂怒，瘋狂）有關。'Furious' 形容的是極度的憤怒，一種失控的情緒狀態。也可用來形容自然現象（如風、海浪）的猛烈和狂暴，這種猛烈程度類似於狂怒的表現。","definition":"1. extremely angry; 2. (of a storm or other natural phenomenon) extremely violent.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was furious when he discovered his car had been stolen.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他發現汽車被偷後勃然大怒。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The furious waves crashed against the shore.\",\n    \"ch\": \"洶湧的海浪拍打著海岸。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She gave a furious look to the person who bumped into her.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她怒視著撞到她的人。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他發現汽車被偷後勃然大怒。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4347,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::garage::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"I need to take my car to the ____ for a service.","expectedAnswer":"garage","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"I need to take my car to the ____ for a service.","clozeAnswer":"garage","exampleTranslation":"我需要把車開到修車廠去做保養。","reference":{"eng":"garage","kk":"/ɡəˈrɑːʒ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['汽車修理廠；汽車庫'], ['（蘇聯/東歐）集體農莊']]","chEntries":["汽車修理廠","汽車庫","集體農莊"],"practiceMeaning":"我需要把車開到修車廠去做保養。","analysis":"源自法語 'garage'，意為『車庫』。1. 指存放汽車或修理汽車的地方，即『汽車庫、汽車修理廠』。2. 在蘇聯和東歐，曾指由國家或集體擁有和經營的『農業生產單位』，通常是指集體農莊。","definition":"a building for storing a motor vehicle; a place where cars are repaired","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I need to take my car to the garage for a service.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我需要把車開到修車廠去做保養。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He parks his car in the garage.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他把車停在車庫裡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The garage sale will be held on Saturday.\",\n    \"ch\": \"跳蚤市場將於週六舉行。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我需要把車開到修車廠去做保養。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3219,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::gaze::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Her ____ was fixed on the horizon.","expectedAnswer":"gaze","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Her ____ was fixed on the horizon.","clozeAnswer":"gaze","exampleTranslation":"她的目光固定在地平線上。","reference":{"eng":"gaze","kk":"/ɡeɪz/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['凝視'], ['注視']]","chEntries":["凝視","注視"],"practiceMeaning":"她的目光固定在地平線上。","analysis":"名詞形式，指『凝視』或『注視』的行為。由動詞 'gaze' 衍生。","definition":"a steady look.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her gaze was fixed on the horizon.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的目光固定在地平線上。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He gave her a long, lingering gaze.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他給了她一個長久、流連的凝視。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她的目光固定在地平線上。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U41"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5402,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l2::geography::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She excelled in ____ and history at school.","expectedAnswer":"geography","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She excelled in ____ and history at school.","clozeAnswer":"geography","exampleTranslation":"她在學校的地理和歷史科目上表現優異。","reference":{"eng":"geography","kk":"dʒiˈɒɡrəfi","tense":"n.","ch":"[['地理'], ['地理學']]","chEntries":["地理","地理學"],"practiceMeaning":"她在學校的地理和歷史科目上表現優異。","analysis":"此字源自希臘語 geōgraphia，由 'gē' (earth) + 'graphein' (to write) 組成，原意是「地球的描寫」。核心語意是「對地球表面及其現象的學術研究和描述」。","definition":"1. the study of the physical features of the earth's surface, including landforms, climate, population distribution, etc.; 2. the physical features of an area.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She excelled in geography and history at school.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在學校的地理和歷史科目上表現優異。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Understanding the geography of the region is crucial for trade.\",\n    \"ch\": \"了解該地區的地理對於貿易至關重要。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她在學校的地理和歷史科目上表現優異。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5416,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::glimpse::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"I caught a ____ of her as she left the room.","expectedAnswer":"glimpse","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"I caught a ____ of her as she left the room.","clozeAnswer":"glimpse","exampleTranslation":"她離開房間時我瞥見了她一眼。","reference":{"eng":"glimpse","kk":"ɡlɪmps","tense":"n.","ch":"[['一瞥'], ['瞥見'], ['短暫的觀察']]","chEntries":["一瞥","瞥見","短暫的觀察"],"practiceMeaning":"她離開房間時我瞥見了她一眼。","analysis":"此字詞源尚不明確，可能與中古英語 \"glim\" (微弱的光) 或 \"glint\" (閃爍) 有關，或是擬聲詞。其核心語意圍繞著「短暫的」、「模糊的」或「不完整的」視覺體驗。構詞上沒有明顯的字首、字根或字尾可拆解，應視為一個整體詞源的發展。原始語義可能與微弱或快速的光線有關，引申為「短暫的看見」或「看到一小部分」的動作或結果。","definition":"a momentary or brief look; a quick sight; a slight suggestion or indication.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I caught a glimpse of her as she left the room.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她離開房間時我瞥見了她一眼。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The documentary offered a glimpse into the lives of the villagers.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這部紀錄片讓我們得以一窺村民的生活。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We only had a glimpse of the magnificent mountain range.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們僅能窺見壯麗的山脈一角。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她離開房間時我瞥見了她一眼。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4557,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::global::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ warming is a serious environmental issue.","expectedAnswer":"Global","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ warming is a serious environmental issue.","clozeAnswer":"Global","exampleTranslation":"全球暖化是一個嚴重的環境問題。","reference":{"eng":"global","kk":"/ˈɡloʊbəl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['全球的', '全世界的'], ['整體的', '全面的']]","chEntries":["全球的","全世界的","整體的","全面的"],"practiceMeaning":"全球暖化是一個嚴重的環境問題。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'globus'，意為 'ball, sphere' (球體)。核心概念是指像球體一樣涵蓋整個地球。\n    1. 全球的、全世界的：指涉及整個地球或全世界範圍的。\n    2. 整體的、全面的：指涵蓋所有部分或方面，不局限於局部。","definition":"1. relating to or affecting the whole world.; 2. encompassing or covering the whole of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Global warming is a serious environmental issue.\",\n    \"ch\": \"全球暖化是一個嚴重的環境問題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company has a global presence.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司業務遍及全球。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need a global approach to solve this crisis.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要一個整體的辦法來解決這次危機。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"全球暖化是一個嚴重的環境問題。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4592,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::global-warming::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Scientists are concerned about the effects of ____.","expectedAnswer":"global warming","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Scientists are concerned about the effects of ____.","clozeAnswer":"global warming","exampleTranslation":"科學家們對全球暖化的影響感到擔憂。","reference":{"eng":"global warming","kk":"/ˈɡloʊbəl ˈwɔːrmɪŋ/","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['全球暖化']]","chEntries":["全球暖化"],"practiceMeaning":"科學家們對全球暖化的影響感到擔憂。","analysis":"此片語由 'global' (全球的) 和 'warming' (暖化) 組成。 'global' 源自拉丁語 'globus' (ball)，指涉及整個地球。 'warming' 是動詞 'warm' (變暖) 的現在分詞形式。此片語專指由於人類活動（主要是燃燒化石燃料）導致大氣中溫室氣體濃度增加，進而引起的地球表面平均溫度上升的現象。","definition":"1. the gradual heating of Earth's surface, oceans, and atmosphere, primarily caused by human activities, such as the burning of fossil fuels, that increase the level of greenhouse gases in the atmosphere.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Scientists are concerned about the effects of global warming.\",\n    \"ch\": \"科學家們對全球暖化的影響感到擔憂。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Reducing carbon emissions is crucial to combat global warming.\",\n    \"ch\": \"減少碳排放對於應對全球暖化至關重要。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"科學家們對全球暖化的影響感到擔憂。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4590,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::go-stale::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The bread will ____ if you don't eat it soon.","expectedAnswer":"go stale","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The bread will ____ if you don't eat it soon.","clozeAnswer":"go stale","exampleTranslation":"如果你不快點吃，麵包就會變不新鮮。","reference":{"eng":"go stale","kk":"/ɡoʊ steɪl/","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['（食物）變質', '不新鮮'], ['（想法、興趣等）變得陳舊', '乏味']]","chEntries":["變質","不新鮮","變得陳舊","乏味"],"practiceMeaning":"如果你不快點吃，麵包就會變不新鮮。","analysis":"此片語由 'go' (變得) 和 'stale' (不新鮮的、陳舊的) 組成。 'stale' 源自古法語 'estale' (old)。\n    1. （食物）變質、不新鮮：指食物失去原有的新鮮度和風味，不再適合食用。\n    2. （想法、興趣等）變得陳舊、乏味：指事物失去新意或吸引力，變得單調無聊。","definition":"1. become no longer fresh or appealing; become old-fashioned or boring.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The bread will go stale if you don't eat it soon.\",\n    \"ch\": \"如果你不快點吃，麵包就會變不新鮮。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"After a while, the conversation began to go stale.\",\n    \"ch\": \"過了一會兒，談話開始變得乏味了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"如果你不快點吃，麵包就會變不新鮮。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4062,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::golf::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He plays ____ every weekend.","expectedAnswer":"golf","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He plays ____ every weekend.","clozeAnswer":"golf","exampleTranslation":"他每個週末都打高爾夫球。","reference":{"eng":"golf","kk":"/ɡɔlf/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['高爾夫球運動']]","chEntries":["高爾夫球運動"],"practiceMeaning":"他每個週末都打高爾夫球。","analysis":"詞源有爭議，但普遍認為源自荷蘭語 'kolf' 或 'kolve'，意為「球棒」。此詞在16世紀從荷蘭傳入蘇格蘭，演變成 'golf'。核心是使用球桿擊球的運動。","definition":"a game played by hitting a small ball into a series of holes on a course, using clubs","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他每個週末都打高爾夫球。\",\n    \"eng\": \"He plays golf every weekend.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個很有挑戰性的高爾夫球場。\",\n    \"eng\": \"This is a difficult golf course