es":[],"clozeSentence":"The survey results ____ a growing trend.","clozeAnswer":"indicate","exampleTranslation":"調查結果顯示出一個增長的趨勢。","reference":{"eng":"indicate","kk":"/ˈɪndɪkeɪt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['表明；顯示'], ['指示；指向'], ['（醫學）適宜於']]","chEntries":["表明","顯示","指示","指向","適宜於"],"practiceMeaning":"調查結果顯示出一個增長的趨勢。","analysis":"詞源來自拉丁語 'indicare'，意為「指出，宣告」，由 'in-'（在...上）+ 'dicare'（宣告，指示）組成。'Indicate' 的核心是「指出」或「顯示」。它可以指用語言或行動表明某事，預示某種情況，或用手指、箭頭等指向某個方向。在醫學上，它用於說明某種治療方法是否適合某種疾病。","definition":"1. point out or show; 2. suggest as a desirable or necessary course of action; 3. (of a fact or event) serve as a sign or symptom of.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The survey results indicate a growing trend.\",\n    \"ch\": \"調查結果顯示出一個增長的趨勢。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He indicated the correct way to his students.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他向他的學生們指出了正確的方法。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"High blood pressure may indicate underlying health problems.\",\n    \"ch\": \"高血壓可能表明存在潛在的健康問題。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"調查結果顯示出一個增長的趨勢。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3168,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::indication::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The dark clouds are an ____ of coming rain.","expectedAnswer":"indication","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The dark clouds are an ____ of coming rain.","clozeAnswer":"indication","exampleTranslation":"烏雲預示著即將下雨。","reference":{"eng":"indication","kk":"/ˌɪndɪˈkeɪʃn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['表示；表明'], ['指示；跡象；徵兆'], ['（醫學）適應症；指徵']]","chEntries":["表示","表明","指示","跡象","徵兆","適應症","指徵"],"practiceMeaning":"烏雲預示著即將下雨。","analysis":"名詞，源自動詞 'indicate'。'Indication' 指的是某事物顯示、表明或預示的信號或線索。它可以是視覺上的指示（如路標），身體上的症狀（如疾病的跡象），或數據顯示的趨勢。在醫學上，'indication' 指的是某種治療方法適用的情況。","definition":"1. a sign or piece of information that shows something exists or is likely to happen; 2. a sign of a particular situation or condition; 3. (medicine) a sign that a particular treatment or medicine is appropriate for a particular condition.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The dark clouds are an indication of coming rain.\",\n    \"ch\": \"烏雲預示著即將下雨。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was no indication that he was unhappy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"沒有任何跡象表明他感到不開心。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Fever is a common indication of infection.\",\n    \"ch\": \"發燒是感染的常見指徵。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"烏雲預示著即將下雨。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4042,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::inform::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Please ____ us of any changes in your address.","expectedAnswer":"inform","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Please ____ us of any changes in your address.","clozeAnswer":"inform","exampleTranslation":"請通知我們您住址的任何變更。","reference":{"eng":"inform","kk":"/ɪnˈfɔrm/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['通知', '告知'], ['使...有所了解', '給...情報']]","chEntries":["通知","告知","使...有所了解","給...情報"],"practiceMeaning":"請通知我們您住址的任何變更。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'informare'，由 'in-' (into) + 'formare' (to form, to shape) 構成，原意是「賦予形狀」、「塑造」，引申為「告知」、「使（人）形成概念」。因此，它的核心意義是「傳達信息」，讓人知道某事。","definition":"1. to tell someone about something; 2. to give someone information","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"請通知我們您住址的任何變更。\",\n    \"eng\": \"Please inform us of any changes in your address.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"警方向家屬告知了事故情況。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The police informed the family of the accident.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"這本書會讓你了解羅馬的歷史。\",\n    \"eng\": \"This book will inform you about the history of Rome.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"請通知我們您住址的任何變更。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4056,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::information::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Please provide us with more ____.","expectedAnswer":"information","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Please provide us with more ____.","clozeAnswer":"information","exampleTranslation":"請提供我們更多資訊。","reference":{"eng":"information","kk":"/ˌɪnfərˈmeɪʃən/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['資訊', '情報'], ['消息']]","chEntries":["資訊","情報","消息"],"practiceMeaning":"請提供我們更多資訊。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'informatio'，由 'informare' (to inform) 構成。核心是「被告知」、「被形成的知識」。因此，'information' 指 facts provided or learned about something or someone; knowledge.","definition":"1. facts provided or learned about something or someone; 2. knowledge or facts obtained about something or someone","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"請提供我們更多資訊。\",\n    \"eng\": \"Please provide us with more information.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"這是對調查很重要的情報。\",\n    \"eng\": \"This is important information for the investigation.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他給我了一些有用的消息。\",\n    \"eng\": \"He gave me some useful information.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"請提供我們更多資訊。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4、C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5497,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::inhabit::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Many species ____ the deep ocean.","expectedAnswer":"inhabit","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Many species ____ the deep ocean.","clozeAnswer":"inhabit","exampleTranslation":"許多物種棲息在深海。","reference":{"eng":"inhabit","kk":"ɪnˈhæbɪt","tense":"v.","ch":"[['居住'], ['棲息'], ['佔據']]","chEntries":["居住","棲息","佔據"],"practiceMeaning":"許多物種棲息在深海。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'inhabitatare'，由 'in-'（在……裡面）和 'habitatare'（居住，來自 'habitare'）構成。'Habitare' 源於 'habere'（擁有）。因此，'inhabit' 的基本語意是「居住在某個地方」，特別是指「在某個地方建立家園或生活」。它可以指人，也可以指動植物。核心語意是「在某處生活或棲息」。","definition":"1. Live in or occupy (a place or environment).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Many species inhabit the deep ocean.\",\n    \"ch\": \"許多物種棲息在深海。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They plan to inhabit the newly built houses.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們計劃入住新蓋的房子。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This cave was inhabited by bats.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個洞穴曾由蝙蝠居住。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"許多物種棲息在深海。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6230,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::inherent::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There are ____ risks in every investment.","expectedAnswer":"inherent","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There are ____ risks in every investment.","clozeAnswer":"inherent","exampleTranslation":"每項投資都存在內在的風險。","reference":{"eng":"inherent","kk":"ɪnˈhɪərənt","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"內在的\"  ],  [    \"固有的\"  ],  [    \"與生俱來的\"  ],  [    \"本質的\"  ]]","chEntries":["內在的","固有的","與生俱來的","本質的"],"practiceMeaning":"每項投資都存在內在的風險。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 inhærens，是 inhærere（附著在…上）的現在分詞。由 in-（在…裡面）和 hærebere（附著）組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作形容詞時，指某事物與生俱來、屬於其本質的一部分，不可分割。中文翻譯為「內在的；固有的；與生俱來的；本質的」。","definition":"existing in something as a permanent, essential, or characteristic attribute.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There are inherent risks in every investment.\",\n    \"ch\": \"每項投資都存在內在的風險。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The beauty of the natural landscape is inherent.\",\n    \"ch\": \"自然景觀的美是固有的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Courage is an inherent quality of a leader.\",\n    \"ch\": \"勇氣是領導者與生俱來的品質。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"每項投資都存在內在的風險。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4536,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::injury::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He suffered a serious ____ to his knee.","expectedAnswer":"injury","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He suffered a serious ____ to his knee.","clozeAnswer":"injury","exampleTranslation":"他的膝蓋受了重傷。","reference":{"eng":"injury","kk":"/ˈɪndʒəri/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['傷害', '損傷'], ['（名譽、感情等的）損害']]","chEntries":["傷害","損傷","損害"],"practiceMeaning":"他的膝蓋受了重傷。","analysis":"源自古法語 'injurye'，源於拉丁語 'iniuria'，由 'in-' (not) 和 'ius' (law, right - 法律、權利) 組成。原意為 'wrong, injustice' (錯誤、不公)。引申為對身體造成的傷害（physical injury），以及對名譽、感情、權利等的損害（damage to reputation/feelings/rights）。","definition":"1. physical harm or damage to someone's body.; 2. harm or damage caused to someone's reputation or feelings.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He suffered a serious injury to his knee.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的膝蓋受了重傷。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The scandal caused a severe injury to the company's reputation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這樁醜聞嚴重損害了公司的聲譽。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The injury occurred during training.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這次受傷發生在訓練期間。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他的膝蓋受了重傷。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4289,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::inner-beauty::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"True happiness comes from ____, not just looks.","expectedAnswer":"inner beauty","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"True happiness comes from ____, not just looks.","clozeAnswer":"inner beauty","exampleTranslation":"真正的幸福來自內在美，而不僅僅是外表。","reference":{"eng":"inner beauty","kk":"/ˈɪnər ˈbjuːti/","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['內在美']]","chEntries":["內在美"],"practiceMeaning":"真正的幸福來自內在美，而不僅僅是外表。","analysis":"結合了形容詞 'inner'（內部的、內在的）和名詞 'beauty'（美）。'Inner beauty' 指「一個人的品格、個性、精神特質等非外在的、來自內心的美」，與外表美相對。","definition":"the attractive qualities of a person's character or personality, rather than their physical appearance.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"True happiness comes from inner beauty, not just looks.\",\n    \"ch\": \"真正的幸福來自內在美，而不僅僅是外表。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her kindness and compassion are examples of her inner beauty.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的善良和同情心是她內在美的體現。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"真正的幸福來自內在美，而不僅僅是外表。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5698,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l9::instinctively::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She ____ knew that something was wrong.","expectedAnswer":"instinctively","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She ____ knew that something was wrong.","clozeAnswer":"instinctively","exampleTranslation":"她憑本能就知道有些事不對勁。","reference":{"eng":"instinctively","kk":"ɪnˈstɪŋktɪvli","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['憑本能地'], ['直覺地'], ['本能地']]","chEntries":["憑本能地","直覺地","本能地"],"practiceMeaning":"她憑本能就知道有些事不對勁。","analysis":"此字由名詞 'instinct' 加上形容詞化後綴 '-ive'，再接副詞化後綴 '-ly' 構成。'instinct' 源自拉丁語 instinctus（驅使，激勵），由 instinguere（驅使，激勵）演變而來。'-ive' 後綴使名詞轉化為形容詞，表示「具有……的特性的」。'-ly' 後綴將形容詞轉化為副詞，表示「以……的方式」。核心語意是「與本能、內在驅動力相關的」，因此「instinctively」表示「以一種不受意識思考控制、而是由內在驅動或本能反應的方式進行」。","definition":"in a way that is automatic and unthinking; by natural impulse or inclination.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She instinctively knew that something was wrong.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她憑本能就知道有些事不對勁。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He instinctively dodged the ball.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他本能地躲開了球。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她憑本能就知道有些事不對勁。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5352,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l1::intentional::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The damage to the car was ____.","expectedAnswer":"intentional","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The damage to the car was ____.","clozeAnswer":"intentional","exampleTranslation":"汽車的損壞是故意的。","reference":{"eng":"intentional","kk":"ɪnˈtɛnʃənəl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['故意的'], ['蓄意的'], ['有意的']]","chEntries":["故意的","蓄意的","有意的"],"practiceMeaning":"汽車的損壞是故意的。","analysis":"此字由名詞 intention 加上形容詞字尾 -al 構成。intention 源自拉丁語 intentio（意圖、打算）。-al 是常見的形容詞字尾，表示「關於……的」。因此，intentional 的核心語意為「關於意圖的」，引申為「故意的、蓄意的」，與 accidental（意外的）相對。","definition":"done on purpose; deliberate.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The damage to the car was intentional.\",\n    \"ch\": \"汽車的損壞是故意的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She gave him an intentional smile.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對他露出了一個意味深長的微笑。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"汽車的損壞是故意的。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3175,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::isolate::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The government decided to ____ the affected region to prevent the spread of the virus.","expectedAnswer":"isolate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The government decided to ____ the affected region to prevent the spread of the virus.","clozeAnswer":"isolate","exampleTranslation":"政府決定隔離受影響地區以防止病毒傳播。","reference":{"eng":"isolate","kk":"/ˈaɪsəleɪt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['孤立；使隔離'], ['（使）隔離，（使）隔絕']]","chEntries":["孤立","使隔離","隔離，隔絕"],"practiceMeaning":"政府決定隔離受影響地區以防止病毒傳播。","analysis":"詞源來自意大利語 'isola'，意為「島嶼」。'Isolate' 的核心是「使分離」、「使獨處」。它可以指將人或物體從其他群體中分開，使其單獨存在。在醫學上，常用於指隔離病人以防止疾病傳播。也可指將某事物從其周圍環境中分離出來進行研究或分析。","definition":"1. cause (a person or place) to be or remain alone or apart from others; 2. set apart, disconnect, or remove from all others.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government decided to isolate the affected region to prevent the spread of the virus.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府決定隔離受影響地區以防止病毒傳播。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He felt isolated after moving to a new city.\",\n    \"ch\": \"搬到新城市後，他感到孤獨。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Scientists isolate the active compound from the plant.\",\n    \"ch\": \"科學家們從植物中分離出活性化合物。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"政府決定隔離受影響地區以防止病毒傳播。","sourceName":"字彙王、龍騰課本","unitName":"U40、L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3176,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::isolation::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The fear of ____ prevented her from speaking out.","expectedAnswer":"isolation","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The fear of ____ prevented her from speaking out.","clozeAnswer":"isolation","exampleTranslation":"對孤立的恐懼阻止了她發聲。","reference":{"eng":"isolation","kk":"/ˌaɪsəˈleɪʃn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['孤立；隔離'], ['（與社會的）隔絕']]","chEntries":["孤立","隔離","隔絕"],"practiceMeaning":"對孤立的恐懼阻止了她發聲。","analysis":"名詞，源自動詞 'isolate'。指「孤立」、「隔離」或「隔絕」的狀態或過程。它可以指物理上的分離，如將某人或某物與外界隔離開。也可以指心理或社會上的孤立，即與他人缺乏聯繫，感到孤獨。在醫學上，指隔離傳染病患者的措施。","definition":"1. the process or fact of isolating or being isolated; 2. a state of being alone or removed from others.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The fear of isolation prevented her from speaking out.\",\n    \"ch\": \"對孤立的恐懼阻止了她發聲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The isolation of the island made it difficult to access.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個島嶼的地理隔離使得它難以抵達。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Quarantine is a form of medical isolation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"隔離檢疫是一種醫療隔離形式。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"對孤立的恐懼阻止了她發聲。","sourceName":"字彙王、龍騰課本","unitName":"U40、L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4361,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::it-is-fairly-difficult-to::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ understand his accent.","expectedAnswer":"It is fairly difficult to","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ understand his accent.","clozeAnswer":"It is fairly difficult to","exampleTranslation":"要聽懂他的口音相當困難。","reference":{"eng":"it is fairly difficult to","kk":"None","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['這相當難以…']]","chEntries":["這相當難以…"],"practiceMeaning":"要聽懂他的口音相當困難。","analysis":"此為片語分析。'it is' (pronoun + verb) 指『這是』。'fairly' (adv.) 源自 'fair'，意為『相當地，頗為』。'difficult' (adj.) 源自拉丁語 'difficilis'，意為『困難的』。'to' (prep.) 帶出不定詞。整個片語表示『做某事相當困難』，『其難度在中等偏上』。","definition":"it is quite hard or challenging to do something","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It is fairly difficult to understand his accent.\",\n    \"ch\": \"要聽懂他的口音相當困難。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It is fairly difficult to finish the project on time.\",\n    \"ch\": \"要在期限內完成這個項目相當困難。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"要聽懂他的口音相當困難。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4250,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::junior::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She is the ____ in their department.","expectedAnswer":"junior","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She is the ____ in their department.","clozeAnswer":"junior","exampleTranslation":"她是他們部門裡較年輕的（或資淺的）。","reference":{"eng":"junior","kk":"/ˈdʒuːnjər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['晚輩'], ['學長姐（指較年輕或資淺者）'], ['低年級學生']]","chEntries":["晚輩","學長姐","低年級學生"],"practiceMeaning":"她是他們部門裡較年輕的（或資淺的）。","analysis":"由形容詞 'junior' 衍生而來，用作名詞時，指代比自己年輕、職位較低或年級較低的個人。與 'senior' 相對。","definition":"a person who is younger than another person, or who has a lower rank or position.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is the junior in their department.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是他們部門裡較年輕的（或資淺的）。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The coach gave advice to the juniors.\",\n    \"ch\": \"教練給了學弟學妹們一些建議。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她是他們部門裡較年輕的（或資淺的）。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3298,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::kettle::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Please put the ____ on, I'd like some tea.","expectedAnswer":"kettle","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Please put the ____ on, I'd like some tea.","clozeAnswer":"kettle","exampleTranslation":"請燒壺水，我想喝點茶。","reference":{"eng":"kettle","kk":"/ˈkɛtl/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['水壺；茶壺（燒水用的）']]","chEntries":["水壺","茶壺"],"practiceMeaning":"請燒壺水，我想喝點茶。","analysis":"源自古法語 'ketel'，來自拉丁語 'cattos'，意為「鍋」。專指用來煮水或燒水的器具，通常帶有壺嘴和把手。","definition":"a container, typically with a lid, handle, and spout, used for boiling water.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please put the kettle on, I'd like some tea.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請燒壺水，我想喝點茶。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The kettle whistled when the water was boiling.\",\n    \"ch\": \"水燒開時，水壺發出了嘯叫聲。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"請燒壺水，我想喝點茶。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4080,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::kindergarten::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"My son started ____ this year.","expectedAnswer":"kindergarten","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"My son started ____ this year.","clozeAnswer":"kindergarten","exampleTranslation":"我兒子今年開始上幼稚園。","reference":{"eng":"ki