需要駕照才能開車。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 licence，來自古法語 licence，再追溯至拉丁語 licentia，意為「自由」，來自 licēre（被允許，to be permitted）。licēre 來自原始印歐語 *legʰ-（允許）。核心語義為「被允許」或「給予自由」。構詞上，licēre 提供「允許」的核心概念，-entia 是拉丁語名詞字尾，-ia 演變為中古英語的 -ce。此處為名詞用法，指代「官方許可」或「允許的自由」。","definition":"a permit from an official authority to own or use something, do a particular activity, or carry on a trade; freedom to behave as one wishes.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"You need a license to drive a car.\",\n    \"ch\": \"你需要駕照才能開車。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The artist was granted a license to practice.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該藝術家獲得了執業許可。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The story took liberties with historical facts.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個故事對史實有所歪曲（利用了虛構的自由）。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"你需要駕照才能開車。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5790,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::likelihood::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There is a high ____ of rain this afternoon.","expectedAnswer":"likelihood","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There is a high ____ of rain this afternoon.","clozeAnswer":"likelihood","exampleTranslation":"今天下午很有可能下雨。","reference":{"eng":"likelihood","kk":"ˈlaɪkliˌhʊd","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"可能性\"  ],  [    \"概率\"  ]]","chEntries":["可能性","概率"],"practiceMeaning":"今天下午很有可能下雨。","analysis":"此字為名詞，構詞自likely（可能的；很可能的）+ -hood（名詞字尾，表示「狀態；性質」）。likely本身是形容詞，源自古英語līclīc，由līc（相似的；同樣的）+ -lic（形容詞字尾）組成，līc的原始印歐語詞根是\\\\*līk-（形狀）。-hood字尾源自古英語-hād，與原始日耳曼語\\\\*haiduz（樣式；形式）有關。因此，likelihood的核心語義是指「某事物發生的可能性或概率」。語意演變上，由形容詞「可能的」轉化為表示「可能性」的抽象名詞。","definition":"1. the probability or chance that something will happen or be the case.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There is a high likelihood of rain this afternoon.\",\n    \"ch\": \"今天下午很有可能下雨。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"What is the likelihood that the project will be completed on time?\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個項目按時完成的可能性有多大？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The likelihood of success is quite low.\",\n 