授身上找到了一位很棒的導師。","reference":{"eng":"mentor","kk":"ˈmɛntɔːr","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"導師\"  ],  [    \"顧問\"  ],  [    \"良師益友\"  ]]","chEntries":["導師","顧問","良師益友"],"practiceMeaning":"她在教授身上找到了一位很棒的導師。","analysis":"此字源自古希臘神話人物 Mentor，他是奧德修斯的朋友，負責教導和保護奧德修斯的兒子 Telemachus。在 modern English 中，mentor 指經驗豐富、提供建議和指導的顧問或導師。此名詞的語意直接來自於歷史人物名稱。因此，它是一個專有名詞演變而來的普通名詞。","definition":"An experienced and trusted advisor.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She found a great mentor in her professor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在教授身上找到了一位很棒的導師。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The program pairs young entrepreneurs with experienced mentors.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該計畫為年輕企業家配備了經驗豐富的導師。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He served as a mentor to many aspiring writers.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他曾是許多有抱負的作家的人生導師。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她在教授身上找到了一位很棒的導師。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6127,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::merge::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The two companies decided to ____.","expectedAnswer":"merge","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The two companies decided to ____.","clozeAnswer":"merge","exampleTranslation":"兩家公司決定合併。","reference":{"eng":"merge","kk":"mɜːrdʒ","tense":"v.","ch":"[  [    \"合併\"  ],  [    \"融合\"  ],  [    \"併入\"  ]]","chEntries":["合併","融合","併入"],"practiceMeaning":"兩家公司決定合併。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 mergere，意為「淹沒；沉浸」。構詞上，mergere 的核心語義是「浸入」或「沉入」。此動詞表示兩個或更多個事物結合、合併，形成一個單一的整體。常用於商業、法律或抽象概念。此處使用 v. 詞性，表示及物與不及物皆可。當作及物動詞時，表示「合併」，例如 merge two companies。當作不及物動詞時，表示「合併」，例如 the two companies merge。其語意演變是從「沉浸、淹沒」到「結合、融合」。","definition":"1. to combine or cause to combine to form a single entity; 2. to become absorbed or integrated into something else.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The two companies decided to merge.\",\n    \"ch\": \"兩家公司決定合併。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The small stream merges into the river.\",\n    \"ch\": \"小溪匯入河流。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The firm will merge with its competitor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司將與其競爭對手合併。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"兩家公司決定合併。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6177,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::migration::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Bird ____ occurs in the spring and fall.","expectedAnswer":"migration","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Bird ____ occurs in the spring and fall.","clozeAnswer":"migration","exampleTranslation":"鳥類遷徙發生在春秋兩季。","reference":{"eng":"migration","kk":"maɪˈɡreɪʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"遷徙\"  ],  [    \"移民\"  ]]","chEntries":["遷徙","移民"],"practiceMeaning":"鳥類遷徙發生在春秋兩季。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 migratioinem，是動詞 migrare「遷徙、移居」的名詞化。migrare 的詞源不確定，可能與拉丁語 mīgrāre (to move from one place to another) 或拉丁語 magna (great) 有關，但最常見的說法是源自詞根 *mei- (to go, pass)。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作為名詞，其核心語義是由動詞 migrate「遷徙」名詞化而來，指「為了尋找食物、繁殖地或更好的生存條件而從一個地方移動到另一個地方的行為」。此義項由「移動」的動作延伸出「遷徙」的行為與「移民」的結果。","definition":"1. the movement of persons from one country or locality to another; 2. seasonal movement of animals from one region to another.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Bird migration occurs in the spring and fall.\",\n    \"ch\": \"鳥類遷徙發生在春秋兩季。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The region experienced significant migration of people seeking work.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該地區經歷了大量尋找工作的移民。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Human migration patterns have changed throughout history.\",\n    \"ch\": \"人類的移民模式在歷史上一直變化。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The great migration of African Americans from the South to the North was a major demographic shift.\",\n    \"ch\": \"非裔美國人從南方大規模遷往北方的運動是人口結構的重大轉變。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"鳥類遷徙發生在春秋兩季。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6178,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::milestone::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company celebrated a major ____ in its history.","expectedAnswer":"milestone","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company celebrated a major ____ in its history.","clozeAnswer":"milestone","exampleTranslation":"這家公司慶祝了其歷史上的重要里程碑。","reference":{"eng":"milestone","kk":"ˈmaɪlstəʊn","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"里程碑\"  ],  [    \"轉捩點\"  ],  [    \"重要事件\"  ]]","chEntries":["里程碑","轉捩點","重要事件"],"practiceMeaning":"這家公司慶祝了其歷史上的重要里程碑。","analysis":"此字由 mile（英里）和 stone（石頭）兩個名詞組成。在古代，里程碑是用來標示道路距離的石頭。此字在現代英語中可視為複合詞，其語義由兩部分組成。作為名詞，其核心語義是「一個重要的事件或階段，標誌著進步或發展」。詞源中的「標示距離的石頭」引申為「標誌重要進展的事件」。","definition":"1. a significant stage or event in the development of something; 2. a stone or post set up beside a road or path to mark the distance to a place.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company celebrated a major milestone in its history.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司慶祝了其歷史上的重要里程碑。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Graduating from college was a significant milestone for her.\",\n    \"ch\": \"大學畢業對她來說是一個重要的轉捩點。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The signpost marked a milestone of five miles.\",\n    \"ch\": \"路標標示著五英里的里程碑。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The birth of their first child was a milestone for the couple.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們第一個孩子的出生對這對夫婦來說是一個重要的里程碑。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這家公司慶祝了其歷史上的重要里程碑。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6233,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::mint::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She put some fresh ____ in her tea.","expectedAnswer":"mint","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She put some fresh ____ in her tea.","clozeAnswer":"mint","exampleTranslation":"她把一些新鮮薄荷放進茶裡。","reference":{"eng":"mint","kk":"mɪnt","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"薄荷\"  ],  [    \"造幣廠\"  ],  [    \"巨額財富\"  ]]","chEntries":["薄荷","造幣廠","巨額財富"],"practiceMeaning":"她把一些新鮮薄荷放進茶裡。","analysis":"此字有多個詞源。作「薄荷」時，源自拉丁語 mentha。作「造幣廠」時，源自拉丁語 moneta（女神名，後指錢幣，鑄幣廠），與 mint（薄荷）的詞源不同，但中古英語時期兩者拼寫合併。作「巨額財富」時，為俚語，來自造幣廠能製造大量金錢的概念。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。名詞義包含植物、製造貨幣的場所，以及引申的「巨額財富」。中文翻譯為「薄荷；造幣廠；巨額財富」。","definition":"1. a type of plant with fragrant leaves that are 