ntries":["失蹤的","不見的","缺少的","遺漏的"],"practiceMeaning":"警方正在尋找一個失蹤的兒童。","analysis":"來自動詞 'miss' 的現在分詞，原意為“錯過”。'Missing' 作形容詞時，表示某人或某物不在應在的地方，因此找不到。'Miss' 本身源自古諾爾斯語 missa，意為“缺乏，失去”。引申義是指某物本應存在但卻不存在，例如 'missing piece'（缺少的一塊）。","definition":"1. not present in a place or at a time when you would expect it to be; 2. not found or lost.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police are searching for a missing child.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警方正在尋找一個失蹤的兒童。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There is a missing page in this book.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本書缺了一頁。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We noticed something missing from the collection.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們注意到收藏品中少了些東西。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"警方正在尋找一個失蹤的兒童。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3994,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u3::mission::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The astronauts completed their ____ successfully.","expectedAnswer":"mission","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The astronauts completed their ____ successfully.","clozeAnswer":"mission","exampleTranslation":"太空人成功完成了他們的任務。","reference":{"eng":"mission","kk":"/ˈmɪʃən/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['任務', '使命'], ['（外交）使團'], ['傳教']]","chEntries":["任務","使命","使團","傳教"],"practiceMeaning":"太空人成功完成了他們的任務。","analysis":"詞源：拉丁文 'missio' (派遣)，源自 'mittere' (派遣)。指被賦予的重要任務或目標，也指被派遣執行某項任務的團體。","definition":"1. an important assignment given to a person or group of people; 2. a body of people sent to a foreign country to act as representatives; 3. an organisation set up to achieve a particular purpose, especially religious or charitable.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The astronauts completed their mission successfully.\",\n    \"ch\": \"太空人成功完成了他們的任務。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She felt a strong sense of mission to help the poor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她覺得自己有幫助窮人的強烈使命感。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The UN sent a mission to the conflict zone.\",\n    \"ch\": \"聯合國派了一個使團前往衝突地區。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTra