mpleTranslation":"白金漢宮是英國君主的官邸。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3241,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::panel::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The pilot checked the control ____.","expectedAnswer":"panel","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The pilot checked the control ____.","clozeAnswer":"panel","exampleTranslation":"飛行員檢查了儀表板。","reference":{"eng":"panel","kk":"/ˈpænl/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['儀表板'], ['鑲板'], ['面板'], ['陪審團']]","chEntries":["儀表板","鑲板","面板","陪審團"],"practiceMeaning":"飛行員檢查了儀表板。","analysis":"詞源來自古法語 'pan' (piece of cloth)。最初指鑲嵌在牆壁或門上的裝飾性板塊。引申為各種具有平坦表面的板狀物，如汽車的儀表板、電腦的顯示面板。也指由選定人員組成的『專家組』或『陪審團』。","definition":"1. a flat or curved piece of wood or other hard material, used as a part of a door, wall, or screen; 2. a flat surface containing a group of instruments or controls; 3. a group of people chosen to hear evidence and make a decision.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The pilot checked the control panel.\",\n    \"ch\": \"飛行員檢查了儀表板。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The room had wooden panels on the walls.\",\n    \"ch\": \"房間的牆壁有木質鑲板。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A panel of judges will decide the winner.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一個由法官組成的陪審團將決定獲勝者。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"飛行員檢查了儀表板。","sourceName":"字彙王、龍騰課本","unitName":"U41、L2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4270,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::paradise::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The tropical island was a ____ for sunbathers.","expectedAnswer":"paradise","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The tropical island was a ____ for sunbathers.","clozeAnswer":"paradise","exampleTranslation":"這座熱帶島嶼是日光浴愛好者的天堂。","reference":{"eng":"paradise","kk":"/ˈpærədaɪs/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['天堂'], ['樂園'], ['極樂之地']]","chEntries":["天堂","樂園","極樂之地"],"practiceMeaning":"這座熱帶島嶼是日光浴愛好者的天堂。","analysis":"源自古波斯語 'pairidaēza'，意為「圍場、花園」。經過希臘語 'paradeisos'，最終進入英語。'Paradise' 最初指「伊甸園」，後來演變成「極樂之地」、「天堂」或任何令人極度愉悅、完美的地方。","definition":"an ideal or perfect place or state of happiness; heaven.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The tropical island was a paradise for sunbathers.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座熱帶島嶼是日光浴愛好者的天堂。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He dreamt of reaching paradise after death.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他夢想死後能到達天堂。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這座熱帶島嶼是日光浴愛好者的天堂。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5847,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::parallel::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The two roads run ____ to each other.","expectedAnswer":"parallel","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The two roads run ____ to each other.","clozeAnswer":"parallel","exampleTranslation":"這兩條路相互平行。","reference":{"eng":"parallel","kk":"ˈpærəlel","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"平行的\"  ],  [    \"並列的\"  ],  [    \"類似的\"  ],  [    \"同時發生的\"  ]]","chEntries":["平行的","並列的","類似的","同時發生的"],"practiceMeaning":"這兩條路相互平行。","analysis":"此字源自希臘語 'parallēlos'，由 'para-' (beside) 和 'allos' (other) 構成，意為「相鄰的」或「並行的」。'Parallel' 在幾何學中指永不相交的兩條線。在更廣泛的語境中，它描述的是事物在空間上「並排」或在時間上「同時」發生、或在性質上「類似」的關係。空間上的平行與時間上的同時，以及性質上的類比，都共享了「不交叉」、「不干涉」或「共同前進」的意象。例如，也可指「結構相似的」。","definition":"1. (of lines, planes, or surfaces) side by side and having the same distance continuously between them.; 2. Occurring or existing at the same time.; 3. Having a marked similarity or resemblance.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The two roads run parallel to each other.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這兩條路相互平行。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The events occurred in parallel.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這些事件是同時發生的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His life story has parallel with mine.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的人生經歷與我頗為相似。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The two buildings have a parallel structure.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這兩座建築有著平行的結構。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這兩條路相互平行。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3314,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::partnership::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They formed a business ____ to open a restaurant.","expectedAnswer":"partnership","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They formed a business ____ to open a restaurant.","clozeAnswer":"partnership","exampleTranslation":"他們成立了商業夥伴關係，開了一家餐廳。","reference":{"eng":"partnership","kk":"/ˈpɑːrtnərʃɪp/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['夥伴關係；合夥'], ['（兩國、兩組織等的）合作關係']]","chEntries":["夥伴關係","合夥","合作關係"],"practiceMeaning":"他們成立了商業夥伴關係，開了一家餐廳。","analysis":"由 'partner' (夥伴) 加上 '-ship' (狀態，關係) 後綴構成。指兩人或多人共同經營事業的關係，或廣泛意義上的合作關係。","definition":"1. the state of being partners; 2. an association of two or more people to conduct business, in which the profits and losses are shared.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They formed a business partnership to open a restaurant.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們成立了商業夥伴關係，開了一家餐廳。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The partnership between the two companies was successful.\",\n    \"ch\": \"兩家公司之間的合作夥伴關係很成功。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們成立了商業夥伴關係，開了一家餐廳。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5307,"wordRef":"字彙王::u63::patron::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He is a wealthy ____ of the arts.","expectedAnswer":"patron","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He is a wealthy ____ of the arts.","clozeAnswer":"patron","exampleTranslation":"他是一位富有的藝術贊助人。","reference":{"eng":"patron","kk":"ˈpeɪtrən","tense":"n.","ch":"[['贊助人', '保護人'], ['顧客', '常客'], ['（聖徒）守護神']]","chEntries":["贊助人","保護人","顧客","常客","守護神"],"practiceMeaning":"他是一位富有的藝術贊助人。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'patronus'，意為「保護者、贊助人」，來自 'pater'（father）。構詞上，'patr-' 為詞根，'-on' 為名詞後綴。原始語意為「像父親一樣保護者」。此字有多重語意發展：在古代羅馬，'patronus' 指保護自由民或奴隸的貴族；引申為藝術、文學的「贊助人」；在商業語境中，指商店的「顧客」或「常客」；在宗教語境中，指教堂的「守護神」。","definition":"a person who gives financial or other support to a person, organization, cause, or activity; a regular customer of a shop or restaurant; a person or spirit regarded as a special protector.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a wealthy patron of the arts.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一位富有的藝術贊助人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We are regulars at this restaurant, we are loyal patrons.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們是這家餐廳的常客，是忠實的顧客。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"St. Patrick is the patron saint of Ireland.\",\n    \"ch\": \"聖派崔克是愛爾蘭的守護神。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他是一位富有的藝術贊助人。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U63"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4647,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::peak::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The climber stood at the ____ of the mountain.","expectedAnswer":"peak","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The climber stood at the ____ of the mountain.","clozeAnswer":"peak","exampleTranslation":"登山者站在山峰之巔。","reference":{"eng":"peak","kk":"/piːk/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['山頂'], ['頂峰'], ['最高點'], ['達到頂峰']]","chEntries":["山頂","頂峰","最高點","達到頂峰"],"practiceMeaning":"登山者站在山峰之巔。","analysis":"源自古英語 'pician' (尖、頂)，與「尖銳」有關。指山峰的頂端，或任何事物發展的最高點。引申義也可指達到某種狀態的最高水平。","definition":"the pointed top of a mountain; the highest point or level of something; to reach the highest level or point.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The climber stood at the peak of the mountain.\",\n    \"ch\": \"登山者站在山峰之巔。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Sales are expected to peak next quarter.\",\n    \"ch\": \"預計下個季度銷售額將達到頂峰。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"登山者站在山峰之巔。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3315,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::peculiar::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There was a ____ smell in the room.","expectedAnswer":"peculiar","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There was a ____ smell in the room.","clozeAnswer":"peculiar","exampleTranslation":"房間裡有一種奇怪的氣味。","reference":{"eng":"peculiar","kk":"/pɪˈkjuːliər/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['奇怪的；奇特的'], ['（尤指）特有的；獨特的']]","chEntries":["奇怪的","奇特的","特有的","獨特的"],"practiceMeaning":"房間裡有一種奇怪的氣味。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'peculiaris'，由 'peculium' (私有財產) 演變而來，原意為「屬於某人自己的」，後引申為「特殊的」，再進一步發展為「奇怪的」。","definition":"1. strange or odd; unusual; 2. belonging exclusively to one person, group, or thing.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was a peculiar smell in the room.\",\n    \"ch\": \"房間裡有一種奇怪的氣味。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This custom is peculiar to this region.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種習俗是這個地區特有的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He had a peculiar way of walking.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他走路的方式很奇特。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"房間裡有一種奇怪的氣味。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5053,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::pedestrian::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He offered some ____ observations.","expectedAnswer":"pedestrian","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He offered some ____ observations.","clozeAnswer":"pedestrian","exampleTranslation":"他提出了一些平淡無奇的觀察。","reference":{"eng":"pedestrian","kk":"pəˈdɛstriən","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['步行的'], ['（事物）平常的'], ['乏味的'], ['缺乏想像力的']]","chEntries":["步行的","平常的","乏味的","缺乏想像力的"],"practiceMeaning":"他提出了一些平淡無奇的觀察。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語pedester，意為「步行」。pedester 又來自pes, pedis（腳）。pedestrian 作形容詞，原意是「用腳走的、步行的」。引申指「平凡的、缺乏想像力的、乏味的」，因為步行不像乘車或飛行那樣有速度感或新奇感。其核心語意是「普通的、缺乏特色的」。","definition":"1. of or relating to pedestrians; 2. lacking inspiration or excitement; dull.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He offered some pedestrian observations.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他提出了一些平淡無奇的觀察。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The novel's plot was predictable and pedestrian.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本小說的情節可預測且乏味。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他提出了一些平淡無奇的觀察。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4162,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::person::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She is a very kind ____.","expectedAnswer":"person","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She is a very kind ____.","clozeAnswer":"person","exampleTranslation":"她是一個非常善良的人。","reference":{"eng":"person","kk":"/ˈpɜːrsn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['人']]","chEntries":["人"],"practiceMeaning":"她是一個非常善良的人。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 persona（面具，角色，人）。核心概念是「具有個體意識和行為能力的個體」。","definition":"a human being regarded as an individual","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a very kind person.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是一個非常善良的人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He's a tricky person to understand.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一個難以理解的人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Every person has their own unique qualities.\",\n    \"ch\": \"每個人都有自己獨特的品質。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她是一個非常善良的人。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5、C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6087,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::petty::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Don't argue over such ____ details.","expectedAnswer":"petty","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Don't argue over such ____ details.","clozeAnswer":"petty","exampleTranslation":"不要為了這麼瑣碎的細節爭論。","reference":{"eng":"petty","kk":"ˈpɛti","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"瑣碎的\"  ],  [    \"小氣的\"  ],  [    \"次要的\"  ],  [    \"輕微的\"  ]]","chEntries":["瑣碎的","小氣的","次要的","輕微的"],"practiceMeaning":"不要為了這麼瑣碎的細節爭論。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 petitement（in a small way），來自 petit（small）。核心語義是「小的」。引申為「瑣碎的」、「不重要的」、「次要的」；或形容人「心胸狹窄」、「小氣」；或形容罪行、傷害「輕微的」。","definition":"1. of little importance; trivial; 2. characterized by or showing a lack of tolerance or generosity; mean-spirited; 3. (of a crime or offense) minor.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Don't argue over such petty details.\",\n    \"ch\": \"不要為了這麼瑣碎的細節爭論。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He's too petty to forgive such a small mistake.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他太小氣了，無法原諒這樣一個小錯誤。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police investigated a petty theft.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警方調查了一起盜竊案。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"不要為了這麼瑣碎的細節爭論。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4251,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::pile::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There was a large ____ of books on the table.","expectedAnswer":"pile","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There was a large ____ of books on the table.","clozeAnswer":"pile","exampleTranslation":"桌子上有一大堆書。","reference":{"eng":"pile","kk":"/paɪl/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['堆'], ['一堆'], ['大量']]","chEntries":["堆","一堆","大量"],"practiceMeaning":"桌子上有一大堆書。","analysis":"源自古法語 'pile'，意為「柱子、堆」。'Pile' 的核心意義是「聚集起來的東西」，強調量多或高度。這個概念可以從具體的「堆積物」延伸到抽象的「大量」。","definition":"a heap of things laid or lying one on top of another; a large quantity of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was a large pile of books on the table.\",\n    \"ch\": \"桌子上有一大堆書。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has a pile of work to do.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他有一大堆工作要做。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"桌子上有一大堆書。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5471,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::plentiful::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Fresh fruit is ____ in the summer.","expectedAnswer":"plentiful","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Fresh fruit is ____ in the summer.","clozeAnswer":"plentiful","exampleTranslation":"夏季水果豐富。","reference":{"eng":"plentiful","kk":"ˈplɛntɪfəl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['豐富的'], ['充裕的'], ['許多的']]","chEntries":["豐富的","充裕的","許多的"],"practiceMeaning":"夏季水果豐富。","analysis":"此字由名詞 'plenty'（充足）加上形容詞字尾 '-ful'（來自古英語 '-ful'，表示「充滿……的」）構成。'Plenty' 本身源自古法語 'plente'，意為「滿足、充足」，最終來自拉丁語 'plenitas'（充滿），'plenus'（滿的）。因此，'plentiful' 的核心語意是「充滿的、量大的、足夠的」，表示某物非常豐富，有充足的供應，超過了最低需求。","definition":"1. Existing in or yielding great quantities; abundant.; 2. Abundant; ample; copious.; 3. Having plenty of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Fresh fruit is plentiful in the summer.\",\n    \"ch\": \"夏季水果豐富。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was a plentiful supply of food at the feast.\",\n    \"ch\": \"宴會上有充足的食物供應。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Opportunities for graduates are plentiful.\",\n    \"ch\": \"畢業生的機會很多（充裕）。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"夏季水果豐富。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4424,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u9::plenty::pron","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ were invited, but few came.","expectedAnswer":"Plenty","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ were invited, but few came.","clozeAnswer":"Plenty","exampleTranslation":"受邀的人很多，但來的人很少。","reference":{"eng":"plenty","kk":"/ˈplenti/","tense":"pron.","ch":"[['充足', '大量']]","chEntries":["充足","大量"],"practiceMeaning":"受邀的人很多，但來的人很少。","analysis":"指數量上的充足。","definition":"a large amount or number; more than enough.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Plenty were invited, but few came.\",\n    \"ch\": \"受邀的人很多，但來的人很少。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"受邀的人很多，但來的人很少。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4685,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::plug::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Could you ____ in the lamp?","expectedAnswer":"plug","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Could you ____ in the lamp?","clozeAnswer":"plug","exampleTranslation":"你能插上檯燈的插頭嗎？","reference":{"eng":"plug","kk":"/ˈplʌɡ/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['插入'], ['堵塞'], ['（非正式）推銷']]","chEntries":["插入","堵塞","推銷"],"practiceMeaning":"你能插上檯燈的插頭嗎？","analysis":"動詞形式，與名詞意義對應。第一義指將插頭插入；第二義指用塞子或其他物體堵住；第三義指大力推銷或宣傳。","definition":"1. To connect something to an electrical device or power supply by inserting a plug. 2. To stop up or block a hole or opening. 3. (informal) To promote or advertise something vigorously.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Could you plug in the lamp?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你能插上檯燈的插頭嗎？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The plumber plugged the drain.\",\n    \"ch\": \"水管工堵住了排水管。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The band's new album is being plugged everywhere.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這支樂團的新專輯正在到處被大力推銷。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"你能插上檯燈的插頭嗎？","sourceN