ll 源自古英語 pūl，意為「頭」、「頭顱」，引申為「公眾意見」、「投票」。動詞 poll 意為「對（某人）進行民意調查」或「投票」。","definition":"1. Questioned to obtain opinions; 2. Voted in an election.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The senator was polled about his stance on the issue.\",\n    \"ch\": \"參議員被就他對該問題的立場進行了民意調查。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The residents were polled on their preferred building materials.\",\n    \"ch\": \"居民們被就他們偏好的建築材料進行了投票。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"參議員被就他對該問題的立場進行了民意調查。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5140,"wordRef":"字彙王::u62::portfolio::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The artist showed her ____ to the gallery owner.","expectedAnswer":"portfolio","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The artist showed her ____ to the gallery owner.","clozeAnswer":"portfolio","exampleTranslation":"這位藝術家向畫廊老闆展示了她的作品集。","reference":{"eng":"portfolio","kk":"pɔːrtˈfoʊlioʊ","tense":"n.","ch":"[['投資組合'], ['作品集'], ['公事包']]","chEntries":["投資組合","作品集","公事包"],"practiceMeaning":"這位藝術家向畫廊老闆展示了她的作品集。","analysis":"此字為拉丁語複合詞，由 portare（攜帶）+ folium（葉子、紙張）組成。Folium 在此引申為「文件」。核心語意是「攜帶文件的夾子或本子」。引申為「藝術家或設計師的作品集」，以及「投資人持有的所有證券的總稱」。","definition":"a set of drawings, photographs, or other documents put inside a large stiff envelope or book; a collection of investments, especially stocks and shares, held by a person or company.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The artist showed her portfolio to the gallery owner.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位藝術家向畫廊老闆展示了她的作品集。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He manages a diversified investment portfolio.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他管理著一個多元化的投資組合。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這位藝術家向畫廊老闆展示了她的作品集。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U62"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4345,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::pour::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Please ____ me a cup of tea.","expectedAnswer":"pour","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Please ____ me a cup of tea.","clozeAnswer":"pour","exampleTranslation":"請倒一杯茶給我。","reference":{"eng":"pour","kk":"/pɔːr/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['傾倒；倒（液體）'], ['（雨、雪等）傾瀉；（人、物）湧現']]","chEntries":["傾倒","倒","傾瀉","湧現"],"practiceMeaning":"請倒一杯茶給我。","analysis":"源自古法語 'porer'，意為 'to let flow, to pour'，可能來自拉丁語 'perponere' (to set through)，或直接與『流動』相關。1. 指將液體從一個容器轉移到另一個容器，『傾倒』。2. 形容雨雪等『大量、迅速地落下』，或形容人、物『大量地、不斷地湧入』。","definition":"to flow rapidly in a steady stream; to flow rapidly and in large quantities","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please pour me a cup of tea.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請倒一杯茶給我。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It started to pour rain heavily.\",\n    \"ch\": \"大雨傾盆而下。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The crowds poured into the stadium.\",\n    \"ch\": \"人群湧入體育場。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He poured the milk into the bowl.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他把牛奶倒進碗裡。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"請倒一杯茶給我。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6236,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::prejudice::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ against women is still a problem in some parts of the world.","expectedAnswer":"Prejudice","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ against women is still a problem in some parts of the world.","clozeAnswer":"Prejudice","exampleTranslation":"對女性的偏見在世界某些地區仍然是一個問題。","reference":{"eng":"prejudice","kk":"ˈprɛdʒədɪs","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"偏見\"  ],  [    \"歧視\"  ],  [    \"成見\"  ]]","chEntries":["偏見","歧視","成見"],"practiceMeaning":"對女性的偏見在世界某些地區仍然是一個問題。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 præjudicium，意為「先前的判斷」，由 præ-（先）和 judicare（判斷）構成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。名詞義指對某人或某群人基於其所屬群體（如種族、性別、宗教）而產生的不公平的、預先形成的負面看法或態度，通常缺乏理性根據，並可能導致歧視。中文翻譯為「偏見；歧視；成見」。","definition":"1. a preconceived opinion that is not based on reason or actual experience; 2. the tendency to pre-judge or form an opinion before obtaining adequate information; 3. unreasonable feelings, opinions, or attitudes, especially of hostility, toward an ethnic, racial, sex, or national group.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Prejudice against women is still a problem in some parts of the world.\",\n    \"ch\": \"對女性的偏見在世界某些地區仍然是一個問題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We must overcome our own prejudices.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們必須克服自身的偏見。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The judge must be free from prejudice.\",\n    \"ch\": \"法官必須不受偏見影響。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"對女性的偏見在世界某些地區仍然是一個問題。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6237,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::preliminary::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They held ____ talks to discuss the details.","expectedAnswer":"preliminary","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They held ____ talks to discuss the details.","clozeAnswer":"preliminary","exampleTranslation":"他們舉行了初步會談以討論細節。","reference":{"eng":"preliminary","kk":"prɪˈlɪmɪnɛri","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"初步的\"  ],  [    \"預備的\"  ],  [    \"先行的\"  ]]","chEntries":["初步的","預備的","先行的"],"practiceMeaning":"他們舉行了初步會談以討論細節。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 præliminarius，由 præ-（在…之前）和 limen（門檻）組成，意為「在門檻之前」，引申為「進入之前，準備階段」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作形容詞時，指發生在主要事件、行動或程序之前，作為準備或預示。中文翻譯為「初步的；預備的；先行的」。","definition":"1. happening before a more important event or activity, especially in order to prepare for it; 2. happening too soon or before the normal time.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They held preliminary talks to discuss the details.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們舉行了初步會談以討論細節。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The report contained only preliminary findings.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該報告只包含初步的調查結果。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is just a preliminary estimate.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這只是一個初步的估計。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們舉行了初步會談以討論細節。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6239,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::premier::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She is the ____ dancer in the company.","expectedAnswer":"premier","choices"