sis":"此字由 rent（租金，出租）+ -al（名詞字尾）構成。rent 源自中古英語 rent(en)，來自古法語 rente，再追溯至拉丁語 reditus（收入，歸還）。-al 是常見的名詞字尾，可將形容詞轉為名詞，表示「與……相關的事物」。構詞上，rent 提供核心的「租賃」概念，-al 使其成為名詞。此處為名詞用法，指代「租金」、「租賃的物品」或「出租的行為」。","definition":"an amount of money that you pay to rent something; property or goods that are available to be rented.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The monthly rental for the apartment is high.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這間公寓的月租金很高。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We made the booking for the rental online.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們在網上預訂了租賃事宜。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這間公寓的月租金很高。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3110,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::resignation::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Her ____ surprised everyone.","expectedAnswer":"resignation","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Her ____ surprised everyone.","clozeAnswer":"resignation","exampleTranslation":"她的辭職令大家感到驚訝。","reference":{"eng":"resignation","kk":"/ˌrezɪɡˈneɪʃn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['辭職；辭職書'], ['順從；聽任']]","chEntries":["辭職","辭職書","順從","聽任"],"practiceMeaning":"她的辭職令大家感到驚訝。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'resignare' 的名詞形式。指「放棄」或「接受」的行為或狀態。\n1. 辭職；辭職書：指離開職位的行為，或正式提交的辭職文件。\n2. 順從；聽任：指接受無法改變的事實或情況，帶有平和或無奈的態度。","definition":"1. the act of giving up your job; 2. a formal statement saying that you want to leave your job; 3. the acceptance of something unpleasant that you cannot do anything about.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her resignation surprised everyone.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的辭職令大家感到驚訝。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He submitted his resignation today.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他今天提交了辭職信。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was a sense of resignation in his voice.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的聲音中帶著一絲聽任的語氣。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她的辭職令大家感到驚訝。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4118,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::resource::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Water is a vital natural ____.","expectedAnswer":"resource","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Water is a vital natural ____.","clozeAnswer":"resource","exampleTranslation":"水是重要的自然資源。","reference":{"eng":"resource","kk":"/ˈriːsɔːrs/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['資源'], ['財力', '物力'], ['應變的能力', '辦法']]","chEntries":["資源","財力","物力","應變的能力","辦法"],"practiceMeaning":"水是重要的自然資源。","analysis":"源自古法語 ressource，意為「重新振作、恢復」。最初指一種應急的手段或支持。引申為可供利用的來源，包括自然資源、人力資源、財政資源，以及個人解決問題的能力。","definition":"1. a stock or supply of money, materials, staff, and other assets that can be drawn on by a person or organization in order to function effectively; 2. a natural wealth of a country, such as land, forests, water, or minerals; 3. the ability to cope with difficult situations","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Water is a vital natural resource.\",\n    \"ch\": \"水是重要的自然資源。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The project requires significant financial resources.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個項目需要大量的財政資源。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a lot of resource when it comes to solving problems.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在解決問題方面很有辦法。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"水是重要的自然資源。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3943,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::response::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We received a positive ____ to our advertisement.","expectedAnswer":"response","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We received a positive ____ to our advertisement.","clozeAnswer":"response","exampleTranslation":"我們對廣告收到了積極的回應。","reference":{"eng":"response","kk":"/rɪˈspɒns/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['回應', '答覆'], ['反應']]","chEntries":["回應","答覆","反應"],"practiceMeaning":"我們對廣告收到了積極的回應。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'responsum'，是動詞 'respondere' (意為「回答、回應」) 的過去分詞名詞化。指對某事的回應、回答或反應。","definition":"1. an answer or reaction to something; 2. a reply.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We received a positive response to our advertisement.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們對廣告收到了積極的回應。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her response was immediate and helpful.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的回應迅速且有幫助。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The body's response to the virus was strong.\",\n    \"ch\": \"身體對病毒的反應很強烈。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們對廣告收到了積極的回應。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3918,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::responsibility::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Taking care of a pet is a big ____.","expectedAnswer":"responsibility","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Taking care of a pet is a big ____.","clozeAnswer":"responsibility","exampleTranslation":"照顧寵物是一項重大的責任。","reference":{"eng":"responsibility","kk":"/rɪˌspɒnsəˈbɪləti/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['責任', '職責'], ['負責的能力'], ['應負的責任']]","chEntries":["責任","職責","負責的能力","應負的責任"],"practiceMeaning":"照顧寵物是一項重大的責任。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'responsus' (動詞 'respondere' 的過去分詞，意為「回答、承擔」)。're-' (意為「再次」) + 'spondere' (意為「承諾、保證」)。原指「承諾」或「回答」，後演變為「應負的責任」或「擔任責任的能力」。","definition":"1. the state or fact of having a duty to deal with something or of having control over someone; 2. the state or fact of being accountable or to blame for something; 3. the opportunity or ability to do something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Taking care of a pet is a big responsibility.\",\n    \"ch\": \"照顧寵物是一項重大的責任。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He resigned from his position due to personal responsibility.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他因個人責任辭去了職務。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a strong sense of responsibility.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她有強烈的責任感。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"照顧寵物是一項重大的責任。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3112,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::retain::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She managed to ____ her composure during the crisis.","expectedAnswer":"retain","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She managed to ____ her composure during the crisis.","clozeAnswer":"retain","exampleTranslation":"她在危機中設法保持了鎮定。","reference":{"eng":"retain","kk":"/rɪˈteɪn/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['保留；保持'], ['（在記憶中）記住'], ['聘請（律師等）']]","chEntries":["保留","保持","記住","聘請"],"practiceMeaning":"她在危機中設法保持了鎮定。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'retinere'，'re-' (back) + 'tenere' (to hold)。核心意義是「再次抓住」或「保持」。\n1. 保留；保持：指繼續擁有、持有或維持某物。\n2. （在記憶中）記住：指能夠記住信息或知識。\n3. 聘請（律師等）：指為獲得某人的專業服務而預付費用，使其隨時待命。","definition":"1. to keep something or continue to have something; 2. to remember information; 3. to keep someone employed by paying them a fee.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She managed to retain her composure during the crisis.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在危機中設法保持了鎮定。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This law will retain its importance for years to come.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這項法律在未來幾年仍將保持其重要性。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was retained by the company as a legal advisor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他被公司聘為法律顧問。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她在危機中設法保持了鎮定。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3115,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::retire::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He plans to ____ next year.","expectedAnswer":"retire","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He plans to ____ next year.","clozeAnswer":"retire","exampleTranslation":"他計劃明年退休。","reference":{"eng":"retire","kk":"/rɪˈtaɪər/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['退休'], ['退役'], ['就寢；休息'], ['退居；隱退']]","chEntries":["退休","退役","就寢","休息","退居","隱退"],"practiceMeaning":"他計劃明年退休。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'retirare'，'re-' (back) + 'tendere' (to stretch, to draw)。原意為「退後」，引申為「脫離」或「休息」。\n1. 退休：指停止工作，通常是達到法定年齡或工作年限。\n2. 退役：指軍人或運動員結束其服役或參賽生涯。\n3. 就寢；休息：指準備睡覺或進行休息。\n4. 退居；隱退：指退出公眾事務或活躍的社會生活，過上較為平靜的生活。","definition":"1. to stop working, usually because you have reached an age at which you can stop; 2. to stop being in the army, navy, or air force; 3. to go to bed; 4. to withdraw from public life.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He plans to retire next year.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他計劃明年退休。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The general decided to retire after many years of service.\",\n    \"ch\": \"將軍在服役多年後決定退役。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's time to retire for the night.\",\n    \"ch\": \"是時候去睡覺了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The actor retired from the stage at the height of his career.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位演員在他事業的巔峰時期退出了舞台。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他計劃明年退休。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3116,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::retirement::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She is looking forward to her ____.","expectedAnswer":"retirement","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She is looking forward to her ____.","clozeAnswer":"retirement","exampleTranslation":"她期待著她的退休生活。","reference":{"eng":"retirement","kk":"/rɪˈtaɪərmənt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['退休'], ['退休生活']]","chEntries":["退休","退休生活"],"practiceMeaning":"她期待著她的退休生活。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'retirare' 的名詞形式。指「停止工作」的狀態或過程。\n1. 退休：指停止工作的行為或時期。\n2. 退休生活：指退休後的生活狀態，通常是較為悠閒和放鬆的。","definition":"1. the state of no longer having a job, usually because you have reached an age at which you can stop working; 2. the period of time after you have stopped working.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is looking forward to her retirement.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她期待著她的退休生活。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company offers a good retirement plan.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司提供良好的退休金計劃。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她期待著她的退休生活。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5572,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::retrace::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The police decided to ____ their steps to the scene of the crime.","expectedAnswer":"retrace","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The police decided to ____ their steps to the scene of the crime.","clozeAnswer":"retrace","exampleTranslation":"警方決定重走一遍到犯罪現場的路徑。","reference":{"eng":"retrace","kk":"riˈtreɪs","tense":"v.","ch":"[['重走'], ['回溯'], ['追溯']]","chEntries":["重走","回溯","追溯"],"practiceMeaning":"警方決定重走一遍到犯罪現場的路徑。","analysis":"此字由字首 \"re-\"（again, back，再次，向後）和動詞 \"trace\"（追蹤，描繪）組成。\"trace\" 源自古法語 \"tracer\"，來自拉丁語 \"tractus\"，是 \"trahere\"（to draw, pull，繪製，拉）的過去分詞。\"tractus\" 的語義是「被拉出的線條」或「走過的軌跡」。\"re-\" 加上 \"trace\"，核心語義是「沿著原來的路徑返回」或「重新追溯」。它可以指物理上的「重走」，例如「重走犯罪現場」；也可以指抽象上的「追溯某事的來源、原因或歷史」，例如「追溯某個想法的起源」。","definition":"1. Go back over (a route or journey); 2. Trace back the course or steps of.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police decided to retrace their steps to the scene of the crime.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警方決定重走一遍到犯罪現場的路徑。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Let's retrace the history of this ancient artifact.\",\n    \"ch\": \"讓我們來追溯這件古代文物的歷史。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He tried to retrace his thoughts before the accident.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他試圖回溯事故發生前的思緒。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"警方決定重走一遍到犯罪現場的路徑。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5619,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l7::revolution::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The French ____ had a profound impact on European history.","expectedAnswer":"Revolution","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The French ____ had a profound impact on European history.","clozeAnswer":"Revolution","exampleTranslation":"法國大革命對歐洲歷史產生了深遠的影響。","reference":{"eng":"revolution","kk":"ˌrɛvəˈluʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[['革命'], ['變革'], ['（天體）公轉'], ['（循環）']]","chEntries":["革命","變革","公轉"],"practiceMeaning":"法國大革命對歐洲歷史產生了深遠的影響。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'revolutio'，意為「捲回、翻轉」，由動詞 'revolvere'（捲回）派生，'revolvere' 由 're-'（回、再次）和 'volvere'（捲、轉）組成。構詞學上，'re-' 是表示「回」或「再次」的字首，'vol-' 是「捲」或「轉」的詞根，'-ution' 是表示「過程」或「結果」的名詞化後綴。原始語意是「捲回」或「轉動」。從「重複的轉動」（如天體運行）引申為「徹底的變革」（如社會或政治上的）、「循環」。","definition":"1. A forcible overthrow of a government or other social order in favor of a new system; 2. A fundamental change in the way something is done or thought about; 3. The regular and continuous movement of a celestial body in an orbit around another.","example":"[\