ozeSentence":"He adjusted the ____ before riding the horse.","clozeAnswer":"saddle","exampleTranslation":"騎馬前他調整了馬鞍。","reference":{"eng":"saddle","kk":"ˈsædl","tense":"n.","ch":"[['馬鞍'], ['（自行車、摩托車等的）鞍座']]","chEntries":["馬鞍","鞍座"],"practiceMeaning":"騎馬前他調整了馬鞍。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 'sadol'，可能與原始日耳曼語 '*sadulaz' 或原始印歐語根 '*sed-'（to sit）有關。核心語意為「用於騎乘的座位」。最初用於馬匹，現也用於自行車、摩托車等。","definition":"a seat for a rider on the back of a horse or other animal; a seat on a bicycle or motorcycle.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He adjusted the saddle before riding the horse.\",\n    \"ch\": \"騎馬前他調整了馬鞍。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The saddle on my bike is uncomfortable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我自行車的鞍座很不舒服。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"騎馬前他調整了馬鞍。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U63"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5858,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::saint::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ Peter is one of the apostles.","expectedAnswer":"Saint","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ Peter is one of the apostles.","clozeAnswer":"Saint","exampleTranslation":"聖彼得是使徒之一。","reference":{"eng":"saint","kk":"seɪnt","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"聖人\"  ],  [    \"聖徒\"  ],  [    \"品德高尚的人\"  ],  [    \"極有耐心或善良的人\"  ]]","chEntries":["聖人","聖徒","品德高尚的人","極有耐心或善良的人"],"practiceMeaning":"聖彼得是使徒之一。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'sanctus' (holy, consecrated)，意為「神聖的」。'Sanctus' 是 'sancire' (to make sacred, to hallow) 的過去分詞。'Saint' 在宗教中指被奉為神聖、德行卓著，並常被尊崇崇拜的人，尤其是在基督宗教中。它強調的是「神聖的」、「受人尊敬」和「品德完美」的特質。引申義可用來形容品德極好、行為高尚的人。例如，也可形容「極有耐心或善良的人」。","definition":"1. A person acknowledged as being especially holy or virtuous and as being a representative of God or of a particular religion.; 2. A person of great virtue and goodness.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Saint Peter is one of the apostles.\",\n    \"ch\": \"聖彼得是使徒之一。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a saint for putting up with all that trouble.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她為了忍受所有那些麻煩真是個聖人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Many churches are named after saints.\",\n    \"ch\": \"許多教堂都是以聖徒的名字命名的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He described his neighbor as a saint for helping him move.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他形容他的鄰居像個聖人一樣幫他搬家。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"聖彼得是使徒之一。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4531,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::sake::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"For goodness ____, stop that noise!","expectedAnswer":"sake","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"For goodness ____, stop that noise!","clozeAnswer":"sake","exampleTranslation":"看在上帝的份上，停止那噪音！","reference":{"eng":"sake","kk":"/seɪk/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['緣故', '理由'], ['（為了）...的利益']]","chEntries":["緣故","理由","...的利益"],"practiceMeaning":"看在上帝的份上，停止那噪音！","analysis":"源自古英語 'sacu'，意為 'cause, reason, lawsuit' (原因、理由、訴訟)。在現代英文中，'sake' 尤其常用於介詞片語 'for the sake of' (為了...的緣故/利益)，強調為了某人或某事的利益而行動。","definition":"1. benefit or advantage; well-being.; 2. the purpose of; the reason for.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"For goodness sake, stop that noise!\",\n    \"ch\": \"看在上帝的份上，停止那噪音！\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He sacrificed his career for the sake of his family.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他為了家庭犧牲了自己的事業。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"看在上帝的份上，停止那噪音！","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5310,"wordRef":"字彙王::u63::salmon::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We had grilled ____ for dinner.","expectedAnswer":"salmon","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We had grilled ____ for dinner.","clozeAnswer":"salmon","exampleTranslation":"我們晚餐吃了烤鮭魚。","reference":{"eng":"salmon","kk":"ˈsæmən","tense":"n.","ch":"[['鮭魚', '三文魚'], ['（鮭魚的）淡粉紅色']]","chEntries":["鮭魚","三文魚","淡粉紅色"],"practiceMeaning":"我們晚餐吃了烤鮭魚。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 'saumon'，來自拉丁語 'salamo'，最終可能與拉丁語 'salire'（to leap）有關，指鮭魚跳躍的習性。在英語中，'l' 在此處不發音。核心語意為一種特定的魚類——鮭魚。也可用於描述其獨特的粉紅色。","definition":"a large edible fish that is the<bos>-coloured member of the cod family; a pinkish orange colour.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We had grilled salmon for dinner.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們晚餐吃了烤鮭魚。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her favorite color is salmon pink.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她最喜歡的顏色是鮭魚粉色。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們晚餐吃了烤鮭魚。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U63"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5312,"wordRef":"字彙王::u63::scenario::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"What is the worst-case ____?","expectedAnswer":"scenario","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"What is the worst-case ____?","clozeAnswer":"scenario","exampleTranslation":"最壞的情況是怎樣的？","reference":{"eng":"scenario","kk":"səˈnɑːrioʊ","tense":"n.","ch":"[['情況', '局面'], ['（電影、戲劇等的）劇本', '情節'], ['設想的場景、方案']]","chEntries":["情況","局面","劇本","情節","設想的場景、方案"],"practiceMeaning":"最壞的情況是怎樣的？","analysis":"此字源自義大利語 'scenario'（情節、劇本），可能源自 'scena'（場景，來自拉丁語 'scena'，希臘語 'skēnē'），或與「下雨」有關（指農作物的情境）。最初指戲劇的「劇本」或「情節」。在現代英語中，'scenario' 廣泛指代對未來可能發生的「情況」、「局面」或「一系列事件」的設想或描述，常用於規劃、風險評估等。","definition":"a postulated sequence or development of events; a written list of scenes and dialogue for a play or film; an imagined situation or sequence of events.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"What is the worst-case scenario?\",\n    \"ch\": \"最壞的情況是怎樣的？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The film's scenario was praised for its originality.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這部電影的情節因其原創性而受到讚揚。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"最壞的情況是怎樣的？","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U63"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4391,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u9::scholarship::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She received a ____ to study abroad.","expectedAnswer":"scholarship","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She received a ____ to study abroad.","clozeAnswer":"scholarship","exampleTranslation":"她獲得獎學金出國留學。","reference":{"eng":"scholarship","kk":"/ˈskɒləʃɪp/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['獎學金'], ['學術成就', '學識']]","chEntries":["獎學金","學術成就","學識"],"practiceMeaning":"她獲得獎學金出國留學。","analysis":"詞源自 'scholar'（學者）， '-ship' 是表示狀態、技能或職位的後綴。原意是學者應具備的學識或品質。現今最常見的用法是指學校或機構提供的，用於資助學生學習的經濟援助，即獎學金。","definition":"an amount of money given by a school, university, or other organization to a student to help pay for their education; the studies and achievements of a scholar.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She received a scholarship to study abroad.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她獲得獎學金出國留學。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His scholarship in ancient history is well-known.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在古代史方面的學術造詣眾所周知。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她獲得獎學金出國留學。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4079,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::scissors::n-plural","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Can you pass me the ____?","expectedAnswer":"scissors","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Can you pass me the ____?","clozeAnswer":"scissors","exampleTranslation":"你能把剪刀遞給我嗎？","reference":{"eng":"scissors","kk":"/ˈsɪzərz/","tense":"n. (plural)","ch":"[['剪刀']]","chEntries":["剪刀"],"practiceMeaning":"你能把剪刀遞給我嗎？","analysis":"源自古法語 'cisour'，來自拉丁語 'caesorius'，意為「切割的」。'scissors' 在語法上始終為複數形式，因為它指由兩片刀刃組成的工具。","definition":"a tool for cutting cloth, paper, and other light materials, consisting of two blades joined at one end that move against each other","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"你能把剪刀遞給我嗎？\",\n    \"eng\": \"Can you pass me the scissors?\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"她用剪刀剪了紙。\",\n    \"eng\": \"She cut the paper with scissors.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"你能把剪刀遞給我嗎？","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5313,"wordRef":"字彙王::u63::scope::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of the research was limited.","expectedAnswer":"scope","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of the research was limited.","clozeAnswer":"scope","exampleTranslation":"研究的範圍是有限的。","reference":{"eng":"scope","kk":"skoʊp","tense":"n.","ch":"[['範圍', '幅度'], ['（能力、影響等的）範圍', '餘地'], ['（望遠鏡、顯微鏡等的）鏡筒']]","chEntries":["範圍","幅度","餘地","鏡筒"],"practiceMeaning":"研究的範圍是有限的。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'scopus'（目標，目的），來自希臘語 'skopos' (σκοπός)，意為「觀察者、目標、目的」。構詞上，'scop-' 為詞根，'-us' 為名詞後綴。原始語意為「看」、「觀察」或「目標」。此語意引申為「觀察的範圍」、「理解的範圍」、「活動的範圍」或「影響的範圍」。","definition":"the extent of the area or subject matter that something deals with; the opportunity for doing something; the part of a telescope or microscope that contains the lenses.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The scope of the research was limited.\",\n    \"ch\": \"研究的範圍是有限的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This decision is beyond the scope of my authority.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個決定超出了我的權限範圍。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The microscope has a wide-field scope.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這顯微鏡有一個廣視場的目鏡筒。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"研究的範圍是有限的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U63"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4260,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::sensible::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It's ____ to save money for emergencies.","expectedAnswer":"sensible","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It's ____ to save money for emergencies.","clozeAnswer":"sensible","exampleTranslation":"為應急情況存錢是很明智的。","reference":{"eng":"sensible","kk":"/ˈsɛnsəbəl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['明智的'], ['理性的'], ['切實可行的'], ['（指衣物、顏色等）實用的']]","chEntries":["明智的","理性的","切實可行的","實用的"],"practiceMeaning":"為應急情況存錢是很明智的。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'sensibilis'（有感覺的、可感覺到的），與 'sentire'（感覺、思考）有關。'Sensible' 指「基於理性、判斷力或常識的」，能夠做出好的、明智的決策。它強調一種務實和理性的態度。","definition":"having or showing good judgment; practical and reasonable; aware of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's sensible to save money for emergencies.\",\n    \"ch\": \"為應急情況存錢是很明智的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She wore sensible shoes for the hike.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她為徒步旅行穿了實用的鞋子。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"為應急情況存錢是很明智的。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U7、L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5060,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::sensitivity::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She has great ____ to the needs of others.","expectedAnswer":"sensitivity","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She has great ____ to the needs of others.","clozeAnswer":"sensitivity","exampleTranslation":"她對他人的需求有很強的敏感性（體貼）。","reference":{"eng":"sensitivity","kk":"ˌsensəˈtɪvəti","tense":"n.","ch":"[['敏感性'], ['敏感度'], ['體貼'], ['（對批評或指責的）不高興']]","chEntries":["敏感性","敏感度","體貼","不高興"],"practiceMeaning":"她對他人的需求有很強的敏感性（體貼）。","analysis":"此字由形容詞 sensitive（敏感的）加上名詞化字尾 -ity（表示狀態或性質）構成。sensitive 源自拉丁語sensibilis，是動詞sentire（感覺）的派生詞。sensitivity 指「容易受到影響、感覺或傷害的性質或程度」，可指生理上（對刺激）、情感上（對他人感受）或智力上（對細微差別）的敏感。OCR 掃描時可能將 's' 誤判為 '5'，或 't' 誤判為 'l'。此處修正為 sensitivity。","definition":"1. the quality or state of being sensitive; 2. the ability to detect or respond to physical stimuli; 3. a quick and sympathetic awareness of the feelings of others.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has great sensitivity to the needs of others.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對他人的需求有很強的敏感性（體貼）。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The data requires careful handling due to its sensitivity.\",\n    \"ch\": \"由於其敏感性，這些數據需要小心處理。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He reacted with considerable sensitivity to the criticism.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對批評反應相當敏感（不高興）。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她對他人的需求有很強的敏感性（體貼）。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6137,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::sentimental::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"a ____ song","expectedAnswer":"sentimental","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"a ____ song","clozeAnswer":"sentimental","exampleTranslation":"一首感傷的歌","reference":{"eng":"sentimental","kk":"ˌsɛntɪˈmɛntl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"感傷的\"  ],  [    \"情感的\"  ],  [    \"多愁善感的\"  ],  [    \"情意的\"  ]]","chEntries":["感傷的","情感的","多愁善感的","情意的"],"practiceMeaning":"一首感傷的歌","analysis":"此字由 sentiment（情感）加上形容詞後綴 -al 構成。sentiment 源自拉丁語 sentimentum（感覺；思想）。因此，sentimental 的核心語義是「與情感相關的」。此形容詞描述傾向於表達或受到強烈情感（尤其是感傷、溫情）影響的。其語意演變是從「情感的」到「過於感傷的」或「充滿溫情的」。","definition":"1. of or prompted by sentiment or emotion; 2. of or relating to feelings of tenderness, sadness, or nostalgia; 3. characterized by or showing excessive tenderness, sadness, or nostalgia.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"a sentimental song\",\n    \"ch\": \"一首感傷的歌\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is sentimental about his childhood.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對童年充滿感傷。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was a sentimental journey down memory lane.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一次回憶往昔的感傷之旅。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"一首感傷的歌","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5062,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::session::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The parliament will convene for a special ____ next week.","expectedAnswer":"session","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The parliament will convene for a special ____ next week.","clozeAnswer":"session","exampleTranslation":"議會將於下週召開特別會議。","reference":{"eng":"session","kk":"ˈseʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[['會議'], ['會議期間'], ['（活動或課程的）一次（時間段）']]","chEntries":["會議","會議期間","一次"],"practiceMeaning":"議會將於下週召開特別會議。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語sessio，是動詞sedere（坐）的派生詞。sedere 又來自原始印歐語 *sed-（坐）。session 的核心語意是「人們聚集在一起進行某項活動（如開會、上課、治療）的一段時間」。它強調的是活動的持續時間和集體性。OCR 掃描時可能將 's' 誤判為 '5'，或 'o' 誤判為 '0'。此處修正為 session。","definition":"1. a period devoted to a particular activity or meeting; 2. a period of time during which a court, legislature, or other body is assembled.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The parliament will convene for a special session next week.\",\n    \"ch\": \"議會將於下週召開特別會議。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a therapy session every Tuesday.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她每週二都有一次治療時間。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The training session lasted for three hours.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這次培訓持續了三個小時。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation"