ound the courage to stand up to her boss, showing real spine.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她鼓起勇氣反抗老闆，展現了真正的勇氣。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"健康的脊椎對保持良好姿態至關重要。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3194,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::split::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The log ____ easily when I hit it with the axe.","expectedAnswer":"split","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The log ____ easily when I hit it with the axe.","clozeAnswer":"split","exampleTranslation":"我用斧頭砍下去，木頭很容易就劈開了。","reference":{"eng":"split","kk":"/splɪt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['分裂；分開'], ['（使）裂開；破裂'], ['分享；分配（尤指不均）']]","chEntries":["分裂","分開","裂開","破裂","分享","分配"],"practiceMeaning":"我用斧頭砍下去，木頭很容易就劈開了。","analysis":"詞源來自古諾爾斯語 'splita'，意為「劈開，分裂」。'Split' 的核心是「分離」、「裂開」或「分開」。它可以指物理上的分離，如將物體劈開、裂開，或將一群人分成小組。也可指意見、關係的分歧。在分配財物時，'split' 也常用來表示分享，但有時帶有均勻或不均勻分配的意味。","definition":"1. break or cause to break into pieces; 2. divide into parts or groups; 3. separate from a larger group or body.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The log split easily when I hit it with the axe.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我用斧頭砍下去，木頭很容易就劈開了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The friends decided to split the cost of the meal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"朋友們決定分攤飯錢。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The party split into two factions.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個黨派分裂成兩個派系。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The tree trunk was split by lightning.\",\n    \"ch\": \"樹幹被閃電劈開了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我用斧頭砍下去，木頭很容易就劈開了。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4004,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u3::staff::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company is looking to ____ a new branch.","expectedAnswer":"staff","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company is looking to ____ a new branch.","clozeAnswer":"staff","exampleTranslation":"公司正在為新分部招聘員工。","reference":{"eng":"staff","kk":"/stæf/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['為...配備人員', '僱用']]","chEntries":["為...配備人員","僱用"],"practiceMeaning":"公司正在為新分部招聘員工。","analysis":"詞源：同上。動詞形式，指為某個組織或部門配備工作人員。","definition":"to supply with staff; to recruit employees for.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company is looking to staff a new branch.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司正在為新分部招聘員工。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"公司正在為新分部招聘員工。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4540,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::stale::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The bread had gone ____.","expectedAnswer":"stale","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The bread had gone ____.","clozeAnswer":"stale","exampleTranslation":"麵包已經不新鮮了。","reference":{"eng":"stale","kk":"/steɪl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['不新鮮的', '變質的'], ['陳舊的', '乏味的'], ['（空氣）不流通的']]","chEntries":["不新鮮的","變質的","陳舊的","乏味的","不流通的"],"practiceMeaning":"麵包已經不新鮮了。","analysis":"源自古法語 'estale'，意為 'stale, immovable' (陳舊的、不動的)。\n    1. 不新鮮、變質：指食物失去新鮮度，如 'stale bread' (不新鮮的麵包)。\n    2. 陳舊、乏味：指事物缺乏新意、吸引力，如 'stale jokes' (陳舊的笑話)。\n    3. 空氣不流通：指室內空氣因缺乏流通而變得污濁。 'go stale' 指變質或變得乏味。","definition":"1. no longer fresh and therefore unpleasant to eat or smell.; 2. lacking in originality or freshness; dull.; 3. (of air) no longer fresh and pleasant; stagnant.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The bread had gone stale.\",\n    \"ch\": \"麵包已經不新鮮了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The conversation became stale after a while.\",\n    \"ch\": \"談話過了一會兒就變得乏味了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Open the window to let in some fresh air; the room is stale.\",\n    \"ch\": \"打開窗戶讓新鮮空氣進來；房間裡的空氣不流通。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"麵包已經不新鮮了。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4567,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::steady::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She has a ____ hand for surgery.","expectedAnswer":"steady","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She has a ____ hand for surgery.","clozeAnswer":"steady","exampleTranslation":"她做手術時手很穩。","reference":{"eng":"steady","kk":"/ˈstɛdi/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['穩定的', '平穩的'], ['持續的', '不變的'], ['鎮定的', '冷靜的']]","chEntries":["穩定的","平穩的","持續的","不變的","鎮定的","冷靜的"],"practiceMeaning":"她做手術時手很穩。","analysis":"源自古法語 'esté'，'ester' (to stand - 站立) 的派生詞。核心概念是「穩固地站著」。\n    1. 穩定的、平穩的：指不搖晃、不顛簸，狀態持續。\n    2. 持續的、不變的：指時間長久，沒有顯著變化。\n    3. 鎮定的、冷靜的：指情緒或反應沉著，不易受影響。","definition":"1. firmly fixed, supported, or balanced; not shaking or moving.; 2. not changing or fluctuating; regular and continuous.; 3. (of a person or their behavior) not showing extreme emotion; calm and sensible.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a steady hand for surgery.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她做手術時手很穩。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company has shown steady growth over the past decade.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司在過去十年中一直保持穩定增長。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He remained steady in the face of danger.\",\n    \"ch\": \"面對危險，他保持鎮定。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她做手術時手很穩。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5450,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::strike-a-balance::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It's important to ____ between work and personal life.","expectedAnswer":"strike a balance","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It's important to ____ between work and personal life.","clozeAnswer":"strike a balance","exampleTranslation":"在工作和個人生活之間取得平衡是很重要的。","reference":{"eng":"strike a balance","kk":"ˈstraɪk ə ˈbælən(t)s","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['達成平衡'], ['取得平衡']]","chEntries":["達成平衡","取得平衡"],"practiceMeaning":"在工作和個人生活之間取得平衡是很重要的。","analysis":"此片語由動詞 \"strike\" (在此意為「達成」、「取得」) 和名詞 \"balance\" (平衡) 組成。\"strike\" 在此是比喻用法，指成功地達到某個點或狀態。\"balance\" 源自拉丁語 \"bilancia\"，意為\"天平\"，引申為\"平衡\"。此片語意指在兩種對立或不同的事物之間找到一個適當的、中庸的點，使其既能實現一方面的需求，又不犧牲另一方面的利益。","definition":"to achieve a situation where two opposite things exist together in a reasonable or acceptable way.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"e