lysis":"'Substitute' 源自拉丁語 'substituere' (to put under, to place instead of)，由 'sub-' (under) + 'stituere' (to place) 構成，意為「代替」。'Teacher' 是「老師」。'Substitute teacher' 指「代替正式老師上課的老師」。","definition":"a person who takes the place of a regular teacher who is absent","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"一位代課老師上了今天的課。\",\n    \"eng\": \"A substitute teacher led today's class.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"原來的老師生病了，所以我們有了一位代課老師。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The regular teacher was sick, so we had a substitute teacher.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"一位代課老師上了今天的課。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5149,"wordRef":"字彙王::u62::subtle::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There was a ____ change in her attitude.","expectedAnswer":"subtle","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There was a ____ change in her attitude.","clozeAnswer":"subtle","exampleTranslation":"她的態度有了微妙的轉變。","reference":{"eng":"subtle","kk":"ˈsʌtl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['微妙的'], ['精細的'], ['不易察覺的'], ['狡猾的']]","chEntries":["微妙的","精細的","不易察覺的","狡猾的"],"practiceMeaning":"她的態度有了微妙的轉變。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 sotil，意為「精細、纖細、巧妙」，來自拉丁語 subtilis，由 sub-（在…下面）+ tĭla（紡織品、結構，來自 texere「編織」）組成。原意是「編織得非常細密」。引申為「不易察覺的、微妙的、精細的」。可指氣味、味道、變化、或人的心思。","definition":"so delicate or precise as not to be obvious; slight and gradual; (of a person or their manner) making use of clever indirect methods; artful.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was a subtle change in her attitude.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的態度有了微妙的轉變。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has a subtle sense of humor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他有著一種含蓄的幽默感。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The wine had a subtle hint of oak.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這款酒帶有一絲淡淡的橡木味。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她的態度有了微妙的轉變。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U62"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4576,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::subtract::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"You need to ____ five from ten.","expectedAnswer":"subtract","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"You need to ____ five from ten.","clozeAnswer":"subtract","exampleTranslation":"你需要從十中減去五。","reference":{"eng":"subtract","kk":"/səbˈtrækt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['減去', '扣除']]","chEntries":["減去","扣除"],"practiceMeaning":"你需要從十中減去五。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'subtractum'，'sub-' (under) 和 'trahere' (to draw - 牽引)。核心概念是「從下面抽出」或「從總數中移走」。\n    1. 減去、扣除：在數學上表示從一個數中減去另一個數；在實際應用中，指從總額中扣除一部分。","definition":"1. take away (a number or amount) from another.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"You need to subtract five from ten.\",\n    \"ch\": \"你需要從十中減去五。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Taxes are subtracted from your salary before you receive it.\",\n    \"ch\": \"稅金在你收到薪水前會被扣除。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Subtract the costs from the revenue to find the profit.\",\n    \"ch\": \"從收入中減去成本來找出利潤。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"你需要從十中減去五。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4296,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::sufficient-food::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The supply ship brought ____ for the entire expedition.","expectedAnswer":"sufficient food","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The supply ship brought ____ for the entire expedition.","clozeAnswer":"sufficient food","exampleTranslation":"補給船帶來了足夠整個探險隊的食物。","reference":{"eng":"sufficient food","kk":"/səˈfɪʃənt fuːd/","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['足夠的食物']]","chEntries":["足夠的食物"],"practiceMeaning":"補給船帶來了足夠整個探險隊的食物。","analysis":"由形容詞 'sufficient'（足夠的）和名詞 'food'（食物）組成。'Sufficient food' 指「量、種類或質量能滿足需求的食物」，強調其滿足感和足夠性。","definition":"enough food for a particular purpose or need.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The supply ship brought sufficient food for the entire expedition.\",\n    \"ch\": \"補給船帶來了足夠整個探險隊的食物。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Make sure you pack sufficient food and water for the hike.\",\n    \"ch\": \"確保你為徒步旅行打包了足夠的食物和水。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"補給