choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He secured his promotion, ____ earning a higher salary.","clozeAnswer":"thereby","exampleTranslation":"他獲得了晉升，從而獲得了更高的薪水。","reference":{"eng":"thereby","kk":"ˌðɛərˈbaɪ","tense":"adv.","ch":"[  [    \"藉此\"  ],  [    \"因此\"  ],  [    \"從而\"  ]]","chEntries":["藉此","因此","從而"],"practiceMeaning":"他獲得了晉升，從而獲得了更高的薪水。","analysis":"此字為合成詞，由 there（在那裡；因此）和 by（藉著；通過）構成。there 來自古英語 þær（在那裡）。by 來自古英語 bī（在……旁邊；通過）。因此，thereby 的核心語義是「藉著那個」或「因此」。此副詞用於連接兩個子句，表示通過前一個子句的動作或情況，而達到了後一個子句的結果。其語意演變是從「通過那個」到「因此；從而」。","definition":"By that means; as a result of that.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He secured his promotion, thereby earning a higher salary.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他獲得了晉升，從而獲得了更高的薪水。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company increased its investment, thereby boosting its market share.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司增加了投資，藉此提升了其市場份額。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She mastered the technique, thereby impressing her instructor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她掌握了這項技術，因此給了她的指導員一個深刻的印象。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他獲得了晉升，從而獲得了更高的薪水。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5810,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::thigh::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He had a deep cut on his ____.","expectedAnswer":"thigh","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He had a deep cut on his ____.","clozeAnswer":"thigh","exampleTranslation":"他的大腿上有一個很深的傷口。","reference":{"eng":"thigh","kk":"θaɪ","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"大腿\"  ]]","chEntries":["大腿"],"practiceMeaning":"他的大腿上有一個很深的傷口。","analysis":"此字為名詞，源自古英語þēoh，詞源不明。核心語義是指人或動物腿部從臀部到膝蓋的部分，即大腿。此字沒有明顯的字首、字根或字尾可透明拆解。","definition":"1. the part of the human leg between the hip and the knee.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He had a deep cut on his thigh.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的大腿上有一個很深的傷口。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The horse galloped, its powerful thighs propelling it forward.\",\n    \"ch\": \"馬匹奔馳，牠強壯的大腿推動牠前進。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She rested her arm on her thigh.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她把手臂放在大腿上。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他的大腿上有一個很深的傷口。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5668,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l8::thorough::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We conducted a ____ investigation.","expectedAnswer":"thorough","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We conducted a ____ investigation.","clozeAnswer":"thorough","exampleTranslation":"我們進行了一項徹底的調查。","reference":{"eng":"thorough","kk":"ˈθɜːroʊ","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['徹底的'], ['全面的'], ['詳盡的'], ['仔細的']]","chEntries":["徹底的","全面的","詳盡的","仔細的"],"practiceMeaning":"我們進行了一項徹底的調查。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 þurh，意為「通過」，與 through 同源。其詞源追溯至原始日耳曼語 *thurz（通過）。核心語義為「穿過」、「完全」。構詞上，此字為單一詞根，無明顯字首字尾，其意義由詞根本身演變而來。此處為形容詞用法，描述事物「完全」、「仔細」、「不遺漏任何細節」。","definition":"complete with regard to every detail; not overlooking any part or point; performed with great care and completeness.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We conducted a thorough investigation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們進行了一項徹底的調查。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He gave the car a thorough cleaning.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他把汽車徹底地清洗了一遍。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們進行了一項徹底的調查。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6200,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::threshold::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He stepped over the ____ into the house.","expectedAnswer":"threshold","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He stepped over the ____ into the house.","clozeAnswer":"threshold","exampleTranslation":"他跨過門檻走進屋裡。","reference":{"eng":"threshold","kk":"ˈθreʃhoʊld","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"門檻\"  ],  [    \"入門\"  ],  [    \"閾值\"  ],  [    \"起始點\"  ]]","chEntries":["門檻","入門","閾值","起始點"],"practiceMeaning":"他跨過門檻走進屋裡。","analysis":"此字是古英語 þrescold 或 þerscold 的演變，由 þres（打穀）和 scold（門檻）組合而成，意為「打穀場的門檻」。此字在現代英語中可視為複合詞，但其詞源的準確性有待考證，通常認為是整體詞源演變。作為名詞，其核心語義是指「進入某個地方的入口處的門檻」，引申為「某事的開始、起始點或進入的關卡」。詞源的「打穀場的門檻」引申出「進入」的物理概念，進而發展出「關鍵的起始點」的抽象概念。","definition":"1. the floor or step at the bottom of a doorway; 2. the point at which something begins; 3. the point at which a stimulus is perceived or a response is initiated; 4. the lower limit of a person's ability to perceive or react to a particular stimulus.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He stepped over the threshold into the house.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他跨過門檻走進屋裡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This event marks a new threshold in our relationship.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個事件標誌著我們關係的新開端。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The pain reached a threshold where she could no longer bear it.\",\n    \"ch\": \"疼痛達到了她無法忍受的閾值。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Crossing the threshold of the ancient temple, they felt a sense of awe.\",\n    \"ch\": \"跨過古老寺廟的門檻，他們感到一陣敬畏。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他跨過門檻走進屋裡。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5812,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::thrill::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ski jump gave her a real ____.","expectedAnswer":"thrill","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ski jump gave her a real ____.","clozeAnswer":"thrill","exampleTranslation":"滑雪跳躍讓她感到真正的興奮。","reference":{"eng":"thrill","kk":"θrɪl","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"興奮\"  ],  [    \"激動\"  ],  [    \"戰慄\"  ],  [    \"驚險刺激\"  ]]","chEntries":["興奮","激動","戰慄","驚險刺激"],"practiceMeaning":"滑雪跳躍讓她感到真正的興奮。","analysis":"此字為名詞，與動詞同源。核心語義是指「強烈的興奮、激動或恐懼的感覺」。語意演變上，從「顫抖」的生理反應，引申為「強烈的情感衝擊」，包括愉悅的興奮，也包括因恐懼而產生的戰慄。也可用來指「驚險刺激的體驗」。","definition":"1. a sudden feeling of excitement and pleasure; 2. a feeling of fear or excitement; 3. an experience that gives you a strong feeling of excitement.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The ski jump gave her a real thrill.\",\n    \"ch\": \"滑雪跳躍讓她感到真正的興奮。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There's a thrill in exploring the unknown.\",\n    \"ch\": \"探索未知充滿了驚險刺激。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He experienced the thrill of victory.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他體驗了勝利的激動。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"滑雪跳躍讓她感到真正的興奮。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6255,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::throne::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The king sat on his ornate ____.","expectedAnswer":"throne","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The king sat on his ornate ____.","clozeAnswer":"throne","exampleTranslation":"國王坐在他華麗的寶座上。","reference":{"eng":"throne","kk":"θron","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"寶座\"  ],  [    \"王位\"  ],  [    \"王權\"  ],  [    \"（主教等的）座席；高位\"  ]]","chEntries":["寶座","王位","王權","座席","高位"],"practiceMeaning":"國王坐在他華麗的寶座上。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 þrōn，後受古法語 trône 影響，最終可追溯至拉丁語 thronus，而拉丁語又源自希臘語 thronos（椅子；寶座）。構詞上，希臘語 thronos 可能與 ethelein（升高）有關，暗示著高高在上的位置。此字沒有可在現代英語中透明拆解的生產性字首或字尾，應視為一個整體詞源演變。核心語義為君主、主教或神祇所坐的特殊椅子，引申為國家或權力的象徵，故可表示王位、王權或至高無上的地位。常見於政治、宗教及文學語境。作為主教的座席，也引申為高位。","definition":"1. a large, stately chair on which a sovereign or other dignitary sits; 2. the office, power, or dignity of a sovereign or bishop; 3. a seat of honor or authority.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The king sat on his ornate throne.\",\n    \"ch\": \"國王坐在他華麗的寶座上。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She ascended the throne at the age of twenty-five.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在二十五歲時繼承了王位。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The dictator seized the throne by force.\",\n    \"ch\": \"獨裁者武力奪取了王權。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The bishop returned to his throne after the synod.\",\n    \"ch\": \"主教在宗教會議後回到了他的座席。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"國王坐在他華麗的寶座上。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6249,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::thrust::vt","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He ____ his hands into his pockets.","expectedAnswer":"thrust","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He ____ his hands into his pockets.","clozeAnswer":"thrust","exampleTranslation":"他把手插進口袋裡。","reference":{"eng":"thrust","kk":"θrʌst","tense":"vt.","ch":"[  [    \"插入\"  ],  [    \"刺\"  ],  [    \"猛推\"  ],  [    \"推進\"  ]]","chEntries":["插入","刺","猛推","推進"],"practiceMeaning":"他把手插進口袋裡。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 þȳst（用力推，刺）。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作及物動詞時，核心語義是用力將某物向前、向上或向某方向推動或刺入。也可指突然將某人或某物推入某個地方。此及物動詞義必須接受詞，例如 thrust a sword、thrust a hand、thrust someone into a room。中文翻譯為「插入；刺；猛推；推進」。","definition":"1. to push something or someone with force; 2. to put something somewhere with a sudden, forceful movement; 3. to push something forward or into something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He thrust his hands into his pockets.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他把手插進口袋裡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The bull thrust its horns at the matador.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公牛用角刺向鬥牛士。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The engine thrust the boat forward.\",\n    \"ch\": \"引擎推動船向前行駛。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他把手插進口袋裡。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4161,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::time::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"How much ____ do we have?","expectedAnswer":"time","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"How much ____ do we have?","clozeAnswer":"time","exampleTranslation":"我們有多少時間？","reference":{"eng":"time","kk":"/taɪm/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['時間'], ['次數'], ['時代', '時期']]","chEntries":["時間","次數","時代","時期"],"practiceMeaning":"我們有多少時間？","analysis":"源自古英語 tīma（時間，時期）。核心概念是「連續的事件」，是事物發生、發展、變化的基本度量。","definition":"1. the indefinite continued progress of existence and events; 2. a particular occasion when something happens; 3. a period considered as a distinct entity","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"How much time do we have?\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們有多少時間？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is the third time he has called.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是他打來的第三次電話。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"With the passage of time, old memories fade.\",\n    \"ch\": \"隨著時間的流逝，舊的記憶會逐漸淡忘。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們有多少時間？","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4217,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::timely::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ warning saved many lives.","expectedAnswer":"timely","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ warning saved many lives.","clozeAnswer":"timely","exampleTranslation":"及時的警告拯救了許多生命。","reference":{"eng":"timely","kk":"/ˈtaɪmli/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['及時的；適時的']]","chEntries":["及時的","適時的"],"practiceMeaning":"及時的警告拯救了許多生命。","analysis":"由 'time'（時間）和後綴 '-ly'（形容詞化）構成。核心是與“時間”相關。表示行動、事件發生在最合適、最有益或最需要的時候。","definition":"Done or occurring at a favorable or useful time; opportune.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The timely warning saved many lives.\",\n    \"ch\": \"及時的警告拯救了許多生命。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Your advice was very timely.\",\n    \"ch\": \"你的建議非常及時。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"及時的警告拯救了許多生命。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4516,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::to::prep","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He walked ____ the store.","expectedAnswer":"to","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He walked ____ the store.","clozeAnswer":"to","exampleTranslation":"他走向商店。","reference":{"eng":"to","kk":"/tu/","tense":"prep.","ch":"[['向'], ['到'], ['對於'], ['以便']]","chEntries":["向","到","對於","以便"],"practiceMeaning":"他走向商店。","analysis":"源自古英語 tō。是一個極其常見的介詞，用於表示方向、目的地、目的、範圍、程度、時間等。","definition":"1. Expressing motion in the direction of (a particular location); 2. Expressing the recipient of an action or gift; 3. Up to the point in time or the degree specified; 4. In order to achieve or bring about.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He walked to the store.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他走向商店。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Give it to me.\",\n    \"ch\": \"把它給我。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I came to help.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我來是為了幫忙。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is important to me.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這對我來說很重要。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他走向商店。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5673,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l8::to-such-an-extent-that::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He was tired ____ he fell asleep standing up.","expectedAnswer":"to such an extent that","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He was tired ____ he fell asleep standing up.","clozeAnswer":"to such an extent that","exampleTranslation":"他疲倦到了站著都能睡著的程度。","reference":{"eng":"to such an extent that","kk":"tuː sʌtʃ ən ɪkˈstɛnt ðæt","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['到了……的程度'], ['以至於']]","chEntries":["到了……的程度","以至於"],"practiceMeaning":"他疲倦到了站著都能睡著的程度。","analysis":"此片語由介詞 to + 程度不定詞 such + 名詞 extent（程度）+ 連接詞 that 構成。extent 源自拉丁語 extentus（伸展，擴展）。such an extent 指「如此大的程度」，that 則引出結果。整體表達「程度之大，以至於發生……」。此為一個固定的表示程度和結果的連接片語，應視為整體處理，不可拆解為個別字詞的詞彙分析。","definition":"to a degree so great that something else happens.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was tired to such an extent that he fell asleep standing up.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他疲倦到了站著都能睡著的程度。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The damage was to such an extent that the building had to be demolished.\",\n    \"ch\": \"損壞的程度如此之大，以至於這棟建築物必須拆除。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他疲倦到了站著都能睡著的程度。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5550,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l5::to-this-day::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"I still remember that day ____.","expectedAnswer":"to this day","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"I still remember that day ____.","clozeAnswer":"to this day","exampleTranslation":"我至今仍然記得那天。","reference":{"eng":"to this day","kk":"tə ðɪs deɪ","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['至今'], ['直到今天']]","chEntries":["至今","直到今天"],"practiceMeaning":"我至今仍然記得那天。","analysis":"此為固定片語，由介詞 'to'，指示詞 'this'，名詞 'day' 構成。'this day' 指「今天、此刻」。'to this day' 表示「從過去的某個時間點一直持續到今天」，強調某事物（事件、狀態、信念等）的延續性或持續影響力。它常與過去發生的事情連結，說明該事件的影響力延續至今。此片語用來強調時間的連續性。","definition":"until the present time; up to now.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I still remember that day to this day.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我至今仍然記得那天。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The mystery remains unsolved to this day.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個謎團至今仍未解開。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我至今仍然記得那天。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4658,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::tragedy::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Shakespeare's Hamlet is a famous ____.","expectedAnswer":"tragedy","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Shakespeare's Hamlet is a famous ____.","clozeAnswer":"tragedy","exampleTranslation":"莎士比亞的《哈姆雷特》是一部著名的悲劇。","reference":{"eng":"tragedy","kk":"/ˈtrædʒədi/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['悲劇'], ['悲劇作品'], ['災難']]","chEntries":["悲劇","悲劇作品","災難"],"practiceMeaning":"莎士比亞的《哈姆雷特》是一部著名的悲劇。","analysis":"源自希臘語 'tragoidia'，意為「悲劇」。指以悲慘結局為特點的戲劇、電影或文學作品。引申義指非常不幸的事件或災難。","definition":"a genre of drama in which the main character(s) suffer disaster or misfortune; an event causing great suffering, destruction, and distress.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Shakespeare's Hamlet is a famous tragedy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"莎士比亞的《哈姆雷特》是一部著名的悲劇。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The earthquake was a terrible tragedy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那場地震是一場可怕的災難。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"莎士比亞的《哈姆雷特》是一部著名的悲劇。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4565,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::trail::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The detective followed the faint ____ of footprints.","expectedAnswer":"trail","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The detective followed the faint ____ of footprints.","clozeAnswer":"trail","exampleTranslation":"偵探跟蹤著微弱的腳印蹤跡。","reference":{"eng":"trail","kk":"/treɪl/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['蹤跡', '痕跡'], ['小徑', '步道'], ['（一連串）跟隨者', '追隨者'], ['（飄落或拖曳的）蹤跡，軌跡']]","chEntries":["蹤跡","痕跡","小徑","步道","跟隨者","追隨者","蹤跡，軌跡"],"practiceMeaning":"偵探跟蹤著微弱的腳印蹤跡。","analysis":"源自古法語 'trahiner'，意為 'to drag' (拖曳)。\n    1. 蹤跡、痕跡：指經過留下的可見或不可見的證據。\n    2. 小徑、步道：指在野外或林間供人行走的小路，常是被不斷踩踏形成的。\n    3. 跟隨者：指跟在前面的人或事物後面的隊伍。\n    4. 蹤跡、軌跡：指物體移動後留下的線條或路徑，如 'smoke trail' (煙跡)。","definition":"1. a mark or a series of signs or objects left behind by the passage of someone or something.; 2. a path or track made through a wild or hilly region.; 3. a series of people or things following behind.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The detective followed the faint trail of footprints.\",\n    \"ch\": \"偵探跟蹤著微弱的腳印蹤跡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We hiked along a beautiful mountain trail.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們沿著一條美麗的山間小徑徒步。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The winning team was followed by a trail of cheering fans.\",\n    \"ch\": \"獲勝隊伍後面是一群歡呼的粉絲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A long train of smoke trailed behind the plane.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一長串煙跡在飛機後面拖曳。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"偵探跟蹤著微弱的腳印蹤跡。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5463,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::tribal::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They have a rich ____ history and traditions.","expectedAnswer":"tribal","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They have a rich ____ history and traditions.","clozeAnswer":"tribal","exampleTranslation":"他們擁有豐富的部落歷史和傳統。","reference":{"eng":"tribal","kk":"ˈtraɪbəl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['部落的'], ['部族的']]","chEntries":["部落的","部族的"],"practiceMeaning":"他們擁有豐富的部落歷史和傳統。","analysis":"此字由名詞 'tribe'（部落）加上形容詞字尾 '-al' 構成。'-al' 是來自拉丁語 '-alis' 的變體，用於構成形容詞，表示「……的、關於……的」。因此，'tribal' 的意思是「屬於部落的、與部落有關的」，用來形容與部落社會結構、文化、習俗或組織相關的事物。","definition":"1. Relating to or characteristic of a tribe or tribes.; 2. Organized according to a tribe.; 3. Belonging to or characteristic of a tribal society.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They have a rich tribal history and traditions.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們擁有豐富的部落歷史和傳統。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The artist painted a scene of tribal life.\",\n    \"ch\": \"藝術家描繪了一幅部落生活的景象。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The conflict was fueled by tribal rivalries.\",\n    \"ch\": \"衝突是由部落之間的對立所加劇的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們擁有豐富的部落歷史和傳統。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5151,"wordRef":"字彙王::u62::trivial::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Don't worry about such ____ matters.","expectedAnswer":"trivial","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Don't worry about such ____ matters.","clozeAnswer":"trivial","exampleTranslation":"別擔心那些瑣碎的小事。","reference":{"eng":"trivial","kk":"ˈtrɪviəl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['瑣碎的'], ['微不足道的'], ['不重要的']]","chEntries":["瑣碎的","微不足道的","不重要的"],"practiceMeaning":"別擔心那些瑣碎的小事。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 trivialis，由 tri-（三）+ via（道路）組成。原意是「位於三條道路交匯處的，隨處可見的、普通的」。引申為「平凡的、不值一提的」。","definition":"of little value or importance; insignificant.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Don't worry about such trivial matters.\",\n    \"ch\": \"別擔心那些瑣碎的小事。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The argument was over something trivial.\",\n    \"ch\": \"爭吵是為了某件微不足道的事情。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"別擔心那些瑣碎的小事。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U62"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4329,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::troop::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"A ____ of soldiers marched into the town.","expectedAnswer":"troop","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"A ____ of soldiers marched into the town.","clozeAnswer":"troop","exampleTranslation":"一支部隊開進了鎮上。","reference":{"eng":"troop","kk":"/truːp/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['部隊；軍隊'], ['（表演、遊行等的）群；組']]","chEntries":["部隊","軍隊","群","組"],"practiceMeaning":"一支部隊開進了鎮上。","analysis":"源自法語 'troupe'，意為『一夥人』，來自拉丁語 'troppus' (flock, herd)。1. 特指軍事單位，如『部隊』、『軍隊』。2. 指一群一起行動的人，如『（馬戲團的）一隊演員』、『（童子軍的）小隊』等，強調『一群』的概念。","definition":"a group of soldiers, especially an armoured or airborne unit; a group of performers or dancers","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A troop of soldiers marched into the town.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一支部隊開進了鎮上。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The circus featured a troop of acrobats.\",\n    \"ch\": \"馬戲團有一個雜技演員團。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Scout troops often go camping at weekends.\",\n    \"ch\": \"童子軍小隊週末經常去露營。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"一支部隊開進了鎮上。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5317,"wordRef":"字彙王::u63::trophy::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The team proudly displayed their championship ____.","expectedAnswer":"trophy","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The team proudly displayed their championship ____.","clozeAnswer":"trophy","exampleTranslation":"這支隊伍自豪地展示了他們的冠軍獎杯。","reference":{"eng":"trophy","kk":"ˈtroʊfi","tense":"n.","ch":"[['獎杯'], ['戰利品'], ['（狩獵的）戰利品']]","chEntries":["獎杯","戰利品"],"practiceMeaning":"這支隊伍自豪地展示了他們的冠軍獎杯。","analysis":"此字源自希臘語 'tropaion' ( τρόπαιον)，意為「勝利的標誌」，來自 'trepein' (τρέπ╓ν)，意為「轉動、擊退」。在古希臘，'tropaion' 是為了紀念戰勝敵軍而設立的紀念物。構詞上，'troph-' 為詞根，'-y' 為名詞後綴。核心語意為「勝利的象徵」。引申為體育競賽的「獎杯」，以及戰爭中的「戰利品」。","definition":"a prize for winning a competition or race; a spoil taken from an enemy, especially in battle; a symbol of victory or achievement.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The team proudly displayed their championship trophy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這支隊伍自豪地展示了他們的冠軍獎杯。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He brought back a trophy from his African safari.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他從非洲狩獵之旅帶回了一件戰利品。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這支隊伍自豪地展示了他們的冠軍獎杯。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U63"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4525,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::trouble::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He got into ____ with the law.","expectedAnswer":"trouble","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He got into ____ with the law.","clozeAnswer":"trouble","exampleTranslation":"他捲入了法律麻煩。","reference":{"eng":"trouble","kk":"/ˈtrʌbl/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['麻煩'], ['困難'], ['憂慮'], ['（健康）病痛']]","chEntries":["麻煩","困難","憂慮","病痛"],"practiceMeaning":"他捲入了法律麻煩。","analysis":"源自古法語 troble，來自拉丁語 turba，意為「混亂」、「人群」。核心語意是「混亂、干擾」。引申為「困難」、「麻煩」、「憂慮」、「疾病」等。","definition":"1. Difficulty or problems; 2. Worry or anxiety; 3. A state of commotion or disturbance.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He got into trouble with the law.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他捲入了法律麻煩。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I don't want to cause you any trouble.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我不想給你帶來任何麻煩。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is having trouble sleeping.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她睡眠方面有些困難。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他捲入了法律麻煩。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5318,"wordRef":"字彙王::u63::tuition::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ fees for this year have increased.","expectedAnswer":"tuition","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ fees for this year have increased.","clozeAnswer":"tuition","exampleTranslation":"今年的學費上漲了。","reference":{"eng":"tuition","kk":"tuˈɪʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[['學費'], ['教學', '指導']]","chEntries":["學費","教學","指導"],"practiceMeaning":"今年的學費上漲了。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'tutio'（保護，守衛），'tutor'（保護者，導師）。構詞上，'tuit-' 為詞根，'-ion' 為名詞後綴。原始語意為「保護」或「指導」。此語意引申為「教學、指導」，以及由此產生的費用，即「學費」。","definition":"money that you pay for teaching, especially at a college or university; instruction or teaching.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The tuition fees for this year have increased.\",\n    \"ch\": \"今年的學費上漲了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She received private tuition in mathematics.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她接受了數學的私人指導。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"今年的學費上漲了。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U63"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6145,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::tumor::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The doctor diagnosed a benign ____.","expectedAnswer":"tumor","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The doctor diagnosed a benign ____.","clozeAnswer":"tumor","exampleTranslation":"醫生診斷出一個良性腫瘤。","reference":{"eng":"tumor","kk":"ˈtuːmər","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"腫瘤\"  ],  [    \"腫塊\"  ]]","chEntries":["腫瘤","腫塊"],"practiceMeaning":"醫生診斷出一個良性腫瘤。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 tumor，意為「腫脹；鼓起」，來自 tumēre（腫脹）。原始印歐語詞根 *tu- 可能與「鼓起；腫起」有關。此名詞指身體上異常的腫塊，通常是由異常細胞增殖而成。其語意演變是從「腫脹」到「病理性的腫塊」。","definition":"A swelling of a part of the body, generally without pain or fever, caused by an abnormal growth of tissue.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The doctor diagnosed a benign tumor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"醫生診斷出一個良性腫瘤。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Surgery was required to remove the tumor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"手術是為了移除腫瘤。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Early detection of the tumor is crucial.\",\n    \"ch\": \"早期發現腫瘤至關重要。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"醫生診斷出一個良性腫瘤。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3947,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::underlying::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need to address the ____ causes of the problem.","expectedAnswer":"underlying","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need to address the ____ causes of the problem.","clozeAnswer":"underlying","exampleTranslation":"我們需要解決問題的根本原因。","reference":{"eng":"underlying","kk":"/ˌʌndərˈlaɪɪŋ/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['潛在的', '根本的'], ['在下面的']]","chEntries":["潛在的","根本的","在下面的"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要解決問題的根本原因。","analysis":"由 'under' (介詞，在…下面) 和 'lying' (動詞 'lie' 的現在分詞) 組成。指位於表面之下，但對事物有重要影響的，即「潛在的、根本的」；也可以指實際位於物理下方的位置。","definition":"1. fundamental; basic; 2. located below.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to address the underlying causes of the problem.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要解決問題的根本原因。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There are underlying tensions in the community.\",\n    \"ch\": \"社區中存在潛在的緊張關係。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The underlying layer of soil is rich in nutrients.\",\n    \"ch\": \"下面的土壤層富含營養。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要解決問題的根本原因。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered