譯本","改編","敘述","說法"],"practiceMeaning":"這是最新版本的軟體。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 version（翻譯，來自拉丁語 versio，意為『轉動，轉變，翻譯』），由 vertere（轉動，轉變）+ -io（名詞化後綴）構成。構詞上，'vertere' 提供核心語意「轉變」，'-io' 則形成名詞。核心語意是「從一種形式或狀態轉變到另一種形式或狀態」。這直接體現在「翻譯」（將一種語言轉化為另一種語言）、書籍或電影的「版本」（同一作品的不同呈現方式）、以及個人對事件的「敘述」或「說法」（基於個人視角轉變的呈現）。","definition":"a particular form of something that differs in certain respects from other forms of the same type or from a more basic type; an account given by one who has witnessed or experienced an event.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is the latest version of the software.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是最新版本的軟體。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She gave her version of the story.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她說了她對這件事的說法。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是最新版本的軟體。","sourceName":"龍騰課本、字彙王","unitName":"L9、U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5710,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l9::victory::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The team celebrated their hard-won ____.","expectedAnswer":"victory","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The team celebrated their hard-won ____.","clozeAnswer":"victory","exampleTranslation":"隊伍慶祝他們來之不易的勝利。","reference":{"eng":"victory","kk":"ˈvɪktəri","tense":"n.","ch":"[['勝利'], ['成功']]","chEntries":["勝利","成功"],"practiceMeaning":"隊伍慶祝他們來之不易的勝利。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 victoire，來自拉丁語 victoria（勝利），由 vincere（征服，獲勝）+ -ia（名詞化後綴）構成。構詞上，'vincere' 提供核心語意「征服」，'-ia' 則形成抽象名詞。核心語意是「在競爭、衝突或鬥爭中獲得的成功」，即「勝利」。","definition":"an act of defeating an enemy or opponent in a battle, game, or other competition; success in a struggle or endeavor.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The team celebrated their hard-won victory.\",\n    \"ch\": \"隊伍慶祝他們來之不易的勝利。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was a major victory for the civil rights movement.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是民權運動的一項重大勝利。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"隊伍慶祝他們來之不易的勝利。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4469,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::violence::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The film depicted scenes of extreme ____.","expectedAnswer":"violence","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The film depicted scenes of extreme ____.","clozeAnswer":"violence","exampleTranslation":"這部電影描繪了極端暴力的場面。","reference":{"eng":"violence","kk":"/ˈvaɪələns/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['暴力'], ['猛烈'], ['（行為）不文明']]","chEntries":["暴力","猛烈","不文明"],"practiceMeaning":"這部電影描繪了極端暴力的場面。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 violentia，來自 violare，意為「侵犯」、「粗暴對待」。核心語意是「使用武力或力量造成傷害或破壞」。","definition":"1. Behavior involving physical force intended to hurt, damage, or kill someone or something; 2. Intense or uncontrolled force.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The film depicted scenes of extreme violence.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這部電影描繪了極端暴力的場面。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was a sudden outbreak of violence in the city.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座城市突然爆發了暴力事件。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The storm caused considerable violence to the coastline.\",\n    \"ch\": \"風暴對海岸線造成了相當大的破壞。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這部電影描繪了極端暴力的場面。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4499,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::violently::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He objected ____ to the proposal.","expectedAnswer":"violently","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He objected ____ to the proposal.","clozeAnswer":"violently","exampleTranslation":"他強烈反對這項提議。","reference":{"eng":"violently","kk":"/ˈvaɪələntli/","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['猛烈地'], ['粗暴地']]","chEntries":["猛烈地","粗暴地"],"practiceMeaning":"他強烈反對這項提議。","analysis":"源自 violence (暴力)。加上 -ly (副詞後綴)。意為「以暴力的方式」、「強烈地」。","definition":"1. In a way that involves physical force intended to hurt, damage, or kill; 2. With great force; intensely.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He objected violently to the proposal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他強烈反對這項提議。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The storm raged violently.\",\n    \"ch\": \"風暴猛烈地肆虐。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他強烈反對這項提議。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5153,"wordRef":"字彙王::u62::virtual::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Although not officially president, he was the ____ leader of the country.","expectedAnswer":"virtual","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Although not officially president, he was the ____ leader of the country.","clozeAnswer":"virtual","exampleTranslation":"雖然他不是正式的總統，但他實際上是國家的領導人。","reference":{"eng":"virtual","kk":"ˈvɜːrtʃuəl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['實質上的'], ['虛擬的']]","chEntries":["實質上的","虛擬的"],"practiceMeaning":"雖然他不是正式的總統，但他實際上是國家的領導人。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 virtus，意為「力量、德行、本質」。virtus 本身來自 vir（男人、美德）。核心語意是「具有某種性質或力量，但可能在形式上不同」。引申為「實質上的、幾乎是」（in effect, though not in fact），以及在電腦科技中的「虛擬的」（relating to or being a computer-generated environment that can be interacted with in a seemingly real or physical way）。","definition":"almost or nearly as described, but not completely or according to strict definition; (of a computer environment) simulated by computer software.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Although not officially president, he was the virtual leader of the country.\",\n    \"ch\": \"雖然他不是正式的總統，但他實際上是國家的領導人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Virtual reality allows users to experience simulated environments.\",\n    \"ch\": \"虛擬實境讓使用者體驗模擬的環境。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"雖然他不是正式的總統，但他實際上是國家的領導人。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U62"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3294,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::virus::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The flu is caused by a ____.","expectedAnswer":"virus","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The flu is caused by a ____.","clozeAnswer":"virus","exampleTranslation":"流感是由病毒引起的。","reference":{"eng":"virus","kk":"/ˈvaɪərəs/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['病毒'], ['（計算機）病毒'], ['（不良思想、情感等的）傳染性因素；毒害']]","chEntries":["病毒","傳染性因素","毒害"],"practiceMeaning":"流感是由病毒引起的。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'virus' (毒液，黏液)。指一種非細胞性的傳染因子，只能在宿主細胞內複製。引申至計算機領域，指惡意代碼。也可用於比喻，指像病毒一樣傳播開來的負面事物。","definition":"1. a submicroscopic infectious agent that replicates only inside the living cells of an organism; 2. a piece of code that is capable of copying itself and spreading from one computer to another, usually causing harm; 3. something that is able to infect and harm others.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The flu is caused by a virus.\",\n    \"ch\": \"流感是由病毒引起的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"My computer was infected by a virus.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我的電腦被病毒感染了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Fear can spread like a virus through a crowd.\",\n    \"ch\": \"恐懼會像病毒一樣在人群中傳播。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"流感是由病毒引起的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4048,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::vocabulary::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She has a large English ____.","expectedAnswer":"vocabulary","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She has a large English ____.","clozeAnswer":"vocabulary","exampleTranslation":"她的英語詞彙量很大。","reference":{"eng":"vocabulary","kk":"/voʊˈkæbjəlɛri/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['詞彙', '詞彙量'], ['（某領域的）術語']]","chEntries":["詞彙","詞彙量","術語"],"practiceMeaning":"她的英語詞彙量很大。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'vocabularium'，意為「詞的列表」，來自 'vocabulum' (a word)，'vocabulum' 又來自 'vocare' (to call)。核心是「被稱為的詞」。引申為個人所知的詞語總匯（詞彙量），以及特定領域或行業使用的專門術語。","definition":"1. all the words that someone knows or uses; 2. all the words that exist in a language; 3. a set of words used in a particular subject or field","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"她的英語詞彙量很大。\",\n    \"eng\": \"She has a large English vocabulary.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"這本書介紹了工程師的技術術語。\",\n    \"eng\": \"This book introduces technical vocabulary for engineers.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"學習新詞彙是語言習得的關鍵。\",\n    \"eng\": \"Learning new vocabulary is essential for language acquisition.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她的英語詞彙量很大。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5111,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::vocal::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She has a strong ____ presence.","expectedAnswer":"vocal","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She has a strong ____ presence.","clozeAnswer":"vocal","exampleTranslation":"她有很強的聲音表現力。","reference":{"eng":"vocal","kk":"ˈvoʊkl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['聲音的'], ['發聲的'], ['直言不諱的']]","chEntries":["聲音的","發聲的","直言不諱的"],"practiceMeaning":"她有很強的聲音表現力。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'vocalis'，意為 '與聲音有關的'，源於 'vox, vocis' (voice)。'Vocal' 的核心語義是指 '與聲音相關的'，如 'vocal cords' (聲帶)。引申開來，'vocal' 也指 '能夠發聲的'。更進一步，它形容一個人 '直言不諱'，能夠清晰、公開地表達自己的意見，尤其是在表達不滿或批評時，這意味著他們的聲音被清晰地 '聽見'。","definition":"1. Relating to or produced by the voice.; 2. Able to speak or utter sounds.; 3. Expressing opinions or feelings strongly and openly.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a strong vocal presence.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她有很強的聲音表現力。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is very vocal in his opposition to the plan.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對這項計劃的Opposition非常直言不諱。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Vocal music is an important part of the concert.\",\n    \"ch\": \"聲樂是音樂會的重要組成部分。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她有很強的聲音表現力。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3925,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::volume::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Please turn down the ____, it's too loud.","expectedAnswer":"volume","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Please turn down the ____, it's too loud.","clozeAnswer":"volume","exampleTranslation":"請把音量轉小，太吵了。","reference":{"eng":"volume","kk":"/ˈvɒljum/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['音量'], ['體積', '容量'], ['數量', '大量'], ['冊']]","chEntries":["音量","體積","容量","數量","大量","冊"],"practiceMeaning":"請把音量轉小，太吵了。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'volumen'，意為「捲、卷軸」，來自 'volvere' (意為「滾動、捲起」)。最初指捲起的紙張，引申為「書本的一卷」；後引申為「物體的體積」；再引申為「聲音的大小」，即「音量」；另引申為「數量、大量」。","definition":"1. the amount of space that a substance or object occupies, or that is enclosed within a container; 2. the loudness of a sound; 3. a quantity of something, especially a large quantity; 4. a single book forming part of a work or series.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please turn down the volume, it's too loud.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請把音量轉小，太吵了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This bottle has a volume of one liter.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個瓶子的容量是一公升。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A large volume of mail arrived today.\",\n    \"ch\": \"今天收到大量的郵件。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is the third volume of the encyclopedia.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是百科全書的第三卷。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"請把音量轉小，太吵了。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U2、L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4130,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::wage::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The minimum ____ has increased.","expectedAnswer":"wage","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The minimum ____ has increased.","clozeAnswer":"wage","exampleTranslation":"最低工資有所提高。","reference":{"eng":"wage","kk":"/weɪdʒ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['工資', '薪水']]","chEntries":["工資","薪水"],"practiceMeaning":"最低工資有所提高。","analysis":"源自古英語 wæcce（警衛），後引申為「報酬」，尤其是為勞動或服務支付的。核心概念是「為工作付出的代價」。","definition":"a fixed regular payment, typically paid on a daily or weekly basis, made by an employer to an employee","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The minimum wage has increased.\",\n    \"ch\": \"最低工資有所提高。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She earns a decent wage.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的收入不錯。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They are fighting for higher wages.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們正在爭取更高的工資。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"最低工資有所提高。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4390,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u9::wagon::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The farmer loaded hay onto the ____.","expectedAnswer":"wagon","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The farmer loaded hay onto the ____.","clozeAnswer":"wagon","exampleTranslation":"農夫將乾草裝上貨車。","reference":{"eng":"wagon","kk":"/ˈwæɡən/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['（四輪）貨車', '馬車'], ['（兒童玩的）拖車、手推車']]","chEntries":["貨車","馬車","拖車、手推車"],"practiceMeaning":"農夫將乾草裝上貨車。","analysis":"詞源來自古法語 'wagoun'，最終可追溯至日耳曼語。指一種有輪子、用於運輸貨物或乘客的車輛。","definition":"a vehicle with four wheels, pulled by horses or an ox, used for transporting goods or people; a small cart for a baby or for carrying things.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The farmer loaded hay onto the wagon.\",\n    \"ch\": \"農夫將乾草裝上貨車。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The children pulled their toys in a little wagon.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子們拖著他們的玩具小車。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"農夫將乾草裝上貨車。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4218,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::warning::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The alarm is a ____ of fire.","expectedAnswer":"warning","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The alarm is a ____ of fire.","clozeAnswer":"warning","exampleTranslation":"警報是火災的預警。","reference":{"eng":"warning","kk":"/ˈwɔːrnɪŋ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['警告；預警'], ['（對危險等的）告誡']]","chEntries":["警告","預警","告誡"],"practiceMeaning":"警報是火災的預警。","analysis":"由動詞 'warn'（警告）加上名詞後綴 '-ing' 構成。'Warn' 源自古英語 warnian，意為“警告，告誡”。核心是預先告知某人潛在的危險或不利後果，以使其採取預防措施。","definition":"A statement or event that indicates a possible or impending danger, problem, or unpleasant situation.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The alarm is a warning of fire.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警報是火災的預警。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He received a stern warning from his boss.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他接到了老闆嚴厲的警告。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The warning signs were ignored.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警告標誌被忽略了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"警報是火災的預警。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4279,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::weaken::v","mode":"cloze_en","quest