ysis":"由 a-（介詞）+ part（部分）組成。核心概念是「從整體中分離出來」或「獨立存在」。","definition":"1. separated by a distance; 2. into different pieces or parts; 3. distinct from others","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The two buildings are far apart.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這兩棟建築相距甚遠。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They have to tell A and B apart.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們必須分辨 A 和 B。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The team won the championship, beating their rivals by a wide margin apart.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這支隊伍以巨大的優勢擊敗對手，贏得了冠軍。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們必須分辨 A 和 B。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3200,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::aquarium::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He has a small ____ with several goldfish.","expectedAnswer":"aquarium","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He has a small ____ with several goldfish.","clozeAnswer":"aquarium","exampleTranslation":"他有一個小型養魚缸，裡面有幾條金魚。","reference":{"eng":"aquarium","kk":"/əˈkwɛəriəm/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['水族館'], ['養魚缸']]","chEntries":["水族館","養魚缸"],"practiceMeaning":"他有一個小型養魚缸，裡面有幾條金魚。","analysis":"詞源來自拉丁文 'aquarium'，意為 'water-vessel'，來自 'aqua' (water)。最初指盛水的容器，後來引申為展示水生生物的場所。","definition":"1. a transparent tank of water in which fish and other water creatures are kept; 2. a building or establishment where aquatic animals are exhibited.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We visited the city aquarium last weekend.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們上週末參觀了市裡的水族館。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has a small aquarium with several goldfish.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他有一個小型養魚缸，裡面有幾條金魚。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他有一個小型養魚缸，裡面有幾條金魚。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U41"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5361,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l1::around-the-clock::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The factory operates ____.","expectedAnswer":"around the clock","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The factory operates ____.","clozeAnswer":"around the clock","exampleTranslation":"這家工廠全天候運營。","reference":{"eng":"around the clock","kk":"əˈraʊnd ðə ˈklɑːk","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['日以繼夜地'], ['全天候地']]","chEntries":["日以繼夜地","全天候地"],"practiceMeaning":"這家工廠全天候運營。","analysis":"此片語直譯為「繞著時鐘」。時鐘以 12 小時或 24 小時計，繞一圈代表一整天的時間。因此，around the clock 的意思就是「一天 24 小時不間斷地」，強調時間上的連續性與不停止。常用來描述工作、活動或監控的持續時間。","definition":"all day and all night; continuously.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The rescue team worked around the clock to find the missing hikers.\",\n    \"ch\": \"救援隊日以繼夜地工作，以尋找失蹤的登山者。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The factory operates around the clock.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家工廠全天候運營。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這家工廠全天候運營。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5071,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::array::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She presented an impressive ____ of arguments.","expectedAnswer":"array","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She presented an impressive ____ of arguments.","clozeAnswer":"array","exampleTranslation":"她提出了一系列令人印象深刻的論點。","reference":{"eng":"array","kk":"əˈreɪ","tense":"n.","ch":"[['陣列'], ['一系列'], ['隊伍']]","chEntries":["陣列","一系列","隊伍"],"practiceMeaning":"她提出了一系列令人印象深刻的論點。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'array'，意為 '排列、部署'。在數學與電腦科學中，它特指一種線性數據結構，其中元素以索引順序存儲。這個概念從早期的軍事部署、列隊訓練延伸到現代計算機科學中的組織化數據集合，強調了其結構化和有序性。","definition":"1. An ordered series or arrangement of things; a collection of items arranged in a particular order.; 2. (Computing) A data structure that stores a collection of elements of the same type, typically in contiguous memory locations, and can be accessed using an index.; 3. A formation of troops or ships drawn up in order of battle.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The data was stored in a two-dimensional array.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這些數據被儲存在一個二維陣列中。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She presented an impressive array of arguments.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她提出了一系列令人印象深刻的論點。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她提出了一系列令人印象深刻的論點。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5685,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l9::assault::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The politician launched a fierce ____ on the government's policy.","expectedAnswer":"assault","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The politician launched a fierce ____ on the government's policy.","clozeAnswer":"assault","exampleTranslation":"這位政治家對政府的政策發動了猛烈抨擊。","reference":{"eng":"assault","kk":"əˈsɔːlt","tense":"v.","ch":"[['攻擊'], ['襲擊'], ['猛烈批評']]","chEntries":["攻擊","襲擊","猛烈批評"],"practiceMeaning":"這位政治家對政府的政策發動了猛烈抨擊。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 assaut（攻擊，衝擊），由 a-（來自拉丁語 ad-，表示『向……』）+ salt（跳，來自拉丁語 saltus，意為『跳躍』）構成。構詞上，'a-' 表示方向，'salt' 則強調『跳躍』或『衝擊』的動作。核心語意是「突然的、猛烈的攻擊或衝擊」。語意演變路徑為：從『跳躍、衝擊』到『身體上的攻擊』，再引申到『語言上的猛烈批評』。","definition":"to make a physical attack on someone; to criticize someone or something forcefully.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The suspect was arrested for assault.\",\n    \"ch\": \"嫌疑人因襲擊罪被逮捕。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The politician launched a fierce assault on the government's policy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位政治家對政府的政策發動了猛烈抨擊。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這位政治家對政府的政策發動了猛烈抨擊。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4509,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::assumption::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He rejected the ____ that he was responsible.","expectedAnswer":"assumption","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He rejected the ____ that he was responsible.","clozeAnswer":"assumption","exampleTranslation":"他駁斥了他應負責的假設。","reference":{"eng":"assumption","kk":"/əˈsʌmpʃn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['假設'], ['設想'], ['承擔（責任、職責等）'], ['（態度）傲慢，自以為是']]","chEntries":["假設","設想","承擔","傲慢，自以為是"],"practiceMeaning":"他駁斥了他應負責的假設。","analysis":"源自 assume (假設、承擔)。加上 -tion (名詞後綴)。核心語意是「假設的行為或狀態」，或「承擔的行為或狀態」。","definition":"1. A thing that is accepted as true or as certain to happen, without proof; 2. The act of taking possession of or taking on something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We made the assumption that the project would be funded.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們假設該項目將會獲得資金。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He rejected the assumption that he was responsible.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他駁斥了他應負責的假設。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The assumption of power by the new leader was widely welcomed.\",\n    \"ch\": \"新領導人掌權的行為受到廣泛歡迎。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他駁斥了他應負責的假設。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3062,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::assure::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The government must ____ the safety of its citizens.","expectedAnswer":"assure","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The government must ____ the safety of its citizens.","clozeAnswer":"assure","exampleTranslation":"政府必須確保其公民的安全。","reference":{"eng":"assure","kk":"/əˈʃʊər/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['向…保證；使…確信'], ['確保；保證（某事發生）']]","chEntries":["向…保證","使…確信","確保","保證"],"practiceMeaning":"政府必須確保其公民的安全。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'securus' (safe, secure)，經由古法語 'asseurer' 演變而來。核心意為「使安全」或「使確定」。\n1. 向…保證；使…確信：透過言語或行動，讓某人放下疑慮，相信某事會發生或為真。\n2. 確保；保證（某事發生）：採取行動以確保某個結果的實現，使其變得確定。","definition":"1. to tell someone that something will definitely happen or is true, so that they stop worrying; 2. to make certain that something will happen or be done.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I can assure you that the package will arrive on time.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我可以向您保證包裹會準時送達。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government must assure the safety of its citizens.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府必須確保其公民的安全。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"政府必須確保其公民的安全。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4638,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::astonished::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She looked at him, ____.","expectedAnswer":"astonished","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She looked at him, ____.","clozeAnsw