age.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他把他的汽車停在車庫裡。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他把他的汽車停在車庫裡。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6109,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::autonomy::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Children need to develop a sense of ____.","expectedAnswer":"autonomy","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Children need to develop a sense of ____.","clozeAnswer":"autonomy","exampleTranslation":"孩子們需要培養自主感。","reference":{"eng":"autonomy","kk":"ɔːˈtɑːnəmi","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"自治\"  ],  [    \"自主權\"  ],  [    \"自主性\"  ]]","chEntries":["自治","自主權","自主性"],"practiceMeaning":"孩子們需要培養自主感。","analysis":"此字源自希臘語 autonomia，由 autos（自己）和 nomos（法則；法律；區域）組成。autos 意為「自己」，nomos 意為「法則」。因此，autonomy 的核心語義是「自己制定法則」或「自行管理」。此名詞表示個人、組織或地區獨立行使權力、自主決策的能力。其語意演變是從「自己統治」到「自我規定」，再到現代的「自主權；自主性」。","definition":"1. the right or condition of self-government; 2. freedom from external control or influence; independence.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The region has a high degree of autonomy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該地區擁有高度的自治權。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Children need to develop a sense of autonomy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子們需要培養自主感。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The university has considerable financial autonomy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這所大學擁有相當大的財務自主性。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"孩子們需要培養自主感。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4269,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::avenue::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need to explore every ____ to solve this crisis.","expectedAnswer":"avenue","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need to explore every ____ to solve this crisis.","clozeAnswer":"avenue","exampleTranslation":"我們需要探索所有途徑來解決這次危機。","reference":{"eng":"avenue","kk":"/ˈævənuː/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['大道'], ['（通往某處的）林蔭道'], ['途徑'], ['方法']]","chEntries":["大道","林蔭道","途徑","方法"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要探索所有途徑來解決這次危機。","analysis":"源自古法語 'avenue'，意為「到來、進入」。最初指「道路」，特別是通往莊園或城堡的林蔭大道。後來引申為「途徑」或「方法」，指達成某事的各種可能性或途徑。","definition":"a wide street, especially one lined with trees; a way of approaching a problem or making a progress.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The main avenue was closed for the parade.\",\n    \"ch\": \"主大道因遊行而關閉。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to explore every avenue to solve this crisis.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要探索所有途徑來解決這次危機。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要探索所有途徑來解決這次危機。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3201,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::bald::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The mountain peak was ____ and rocky.","expectedAnswer":"bald","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The mountain peak was ____ and rocky.","clozeAnswer":"bald","exampleTranslation":"山頂光禿禿、多岩石。","reference":{"eng":"bald","kk":"/bɔld/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['禿頭的'], ['光禿的'], ['無裝飾的']]","chEntries":["禿頭的","光禿的","無裝飾的"],"practiceMeaning":"山頂光禿禿、多岩石。","analysis":"詞源可能來自古英語 'balde'，意為 'white, pale'，進而引申為頭髮稀疏或脫落的狀態。也引申至事物缺乏覆蓋物，變得光禿、顯露。","definition":"1. having no hair on the head or a significant amount missing; 2. (of land or a mountain) having little or no vegetation; bare; 3. without adornment or protection.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The old man was completely bald.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那位老人完全禿頭了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The mountain peak was bald and rocky.\",\n    \"ch\": \"山頂光禿禿、多岩石。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He spoke in a bald, direct manner.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他以一種直率、不加修飾的方式說話。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"山頂光禿禿、多岩石。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U41"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4247,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::bamboo::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Pandas eat a lot of ____.","expectedAnswer":"bamboo","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Pandas eat a lot of ____.","clozeAnswer":"bamboo","exampleTranslation":"熊貓吃很多竹子。","reference":{"eng":"bamboo","kk":"/bæmˈbuː/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['竹子'], ['竹製品']]","chEntries":["竹子","竹製品"],"practiceMeaning":"熊貓吃很多竹子。","analysis":"詞源有爭議，可能源自馬來語 'bambu' 或荷蘭語 'bamboe'。'Bamboo' 指一種生長迅速的禾本科植物，其莖部堅韌中空，用途廣泛。","definition":"a tall, hard, shiny, hollow stem of a tropical plant, used for making furniture and other things.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The furniture was made from sustainable bamboo.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這些家具是用可持續的竹子製成的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Pandas eat a lot of bamboo.\",\n    \"ch\": \"熊貓吃很多竹子。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"熊貓吃很多竹子。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5610,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l7::ban::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The organization imposed a temporary ____ on new members.","expectedAnswer":"ban","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The organization imposed a temporary ____ on new members.","clozeAnswer":"ban","exampleTranslation":"該組織對新成員實施了臨時禁令。","reference":{"eng":"ban","kk":"bæn","tense":"n.","ch":"[['禁令'], ['禁止']]","chEntries":["禁令","禁止"],"practiceMeaning":"該組織對新成員實施了臨時禁令。","analysis":"此字在詞源上較為複雜，可能源自古英語 'bannan'（宣佈、號召），或與古挪威斯語 'banna'（詛咒、禁止）有關，後者與原始日耳曼語 *bannanán（宣佈，禁止）相關。構詞學上，此字通常被視為一個整體詞，現代英語中無明顯字首、字根或字尾。此名詞形式是從動詞 'ban' 派生而來（零轉換）。語意核心是「公開宣佈某事為非法或不被允許」，引申為「禁止令」、「禁令」或「禁止的行為」。","definition":"1. An official or legal prohibition; 2. The prohibition of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There is a ban on the use of plastic bags.\",\n    \"ch\": \"塑膠袋的使用已被禁止。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The organization imposed a temporary ban on new members.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該組織對新成員實施了臨時禁令。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該組織對新成員實施了臨時禁令。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4383,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u9::bang::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The car went ____ as it hit the wall.","expectedAnswer":"bang","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The car went ____ as it hit the wall.","clozeAnswer":"bang","exampleTranslation":"汽車撞到牆上時發出巨大的砰聲。","reference":{"eng":"bang","kk":"/bæŋ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['巨響', '爆炸聲'], ['猛擊', '撞擊']]","chEntries":["巨響","爆炸聲","猛擊","撞擊"],"practiceMeaning":"汽車撞到牆上時發出巨大的砰聲。","analysis":"語源來自擬聲詞，模擬突然的巨大聲響。常用於形容爆炸聲或強烈的撞擊聲。","definition":"a sudden loud noise; a sudden hard hit.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The fireworks went off with a loud bang.\",\n    \"ch\": \"煙火以一聲巨響爆炸。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The car went bang as it hit the wall.\",\n    \"ch\": \"汽車撞到牆上時發出巨大的砰聲。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"汽車撞到牆上時發出巨大的砰聲。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6154,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::banner::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The winning team was awarded a championship ____.","expectedAnswer":"banner","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The winning team was awarded a championship ____.","clozeAnswer":"banner","exampleTranslation":"獲勝隊伍被授予了冠軍旗幟。","reference":{"eng":"banner","kk":"ˈbænər","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"旗幟\"  ],  [    \"橫幅\"  ],  [    \"標語\"  ],  [    \"冠軍\"  ],  [    \"領袖\"  ]]","chEntries":["旗幟","橫幅","標語","冠軍","領袖"],"practiceMeaning":"獲勝隊伍被授予了冠軍旗幟。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 banner、bandiere，意為「旗幟」，其最終詞源可能與日耳曼語系表示「綁帶」的詞根有關，例如古英語 band「綁帶」。在現代英語中，其核心語義是「旗幟」，特別是指用於飄揚、展示或標示的布條。詞源中的「綁帶」概念與旗幟的懸掛方式相關。除了字面上的「旗幟」和「橫幅」，它也引申為「冠軍」的象徵，或用於標示、宣傳的「標語」，以及某個運動或運動的「領袖人物」。","definition":"1. a long strip of cloth bearing a slogan or design, carried in a demonstration or procession or hung in a public place; 2. a large piece of cloth with a name or slogan on it, carried as a symbol; 3. a flag; 4. (often in plural) a person or thing that is a symbol of a particular quality or activity, or that is an outstanding example of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The protestors carried banners calling for peace.\",\n    \"ch\": \"抗議者們舉著呼籲和平的橫幅。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The winning team was awarded a championship banner.\",\n    \"ch\": \"獲勝隊伍被授予了冠軍旗幟。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She was the banner of the feminist movement.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是女權運動的旗幟人物。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The team marched under its banner.\",\n    \"ch\": \"隊伍在他們的旗幟下行進。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"獲勝隊伍被授予了冠軍旗幟。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5403,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l2::barrier::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Lack of communication can be a ____ to understanding.","expectedAnswer":"barrier","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Lack of communication can be a ____ to understanding.","clozeAnswer":"barrier","exampleTranslation":"缺乏溝通可能成為理解的障礙。","reference":{"eng":"barrier","kk":"ˈbæriər","tense":"n.","ch":"[['障礙物'], ['障礙'], ['隔閡'], ['界線']]","chEntries":["障礙物","障礙","隔閡","界線"],"practiceMeaning":"缺乏溝通可能成為理解的障礙。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 barriere，意為「柵欄、籬笆、障礙」。其詞源可能與 bar (槓、條) 或 barrer (阻擋) 有關。核心語意是「任何阻止前進、阻礙或分隔的事物」。這可以是物理上的障礙物，也可以是抽象的隔閡（如語言障礙、心理障礙）。","definition":"1. a fence or other obstacle that prevents movement across or past something; 2. a circumstance that prevents an agreement or cooperation from being reached.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A high barrier was built to prevent illegal crossings.\",\n    \"ch\": \"築起了一道高牆以阻止非法越境。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Lack of communication can be a barrier to understanding.\",\n    \"ch\": \"缺乏溝通可能成為理解的障礙。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"缺乏溝通可能成為理解的障礙。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4230,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::be-reasonable-about::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The teacher asked the students to ____ their complaints.","expectedAnswer":"be reasonable about","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The teacher asked the students to ____ their complaints.","clozeAnswer":"be reasonable about","exampleTranslation":"老師要求學生們對他們的抱怨要合乎情理。","reference":{"eng":"be reasonable about","kk":"/ˈriːznəbl əˈbaʊt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['對…講道理；對…持通情達理的態度']]","chEntries":["對…講道理","對…持通情達理的態度"],"practiceMeaning":"老師要求學生們對他們的抱怨要合乎情理。","analysis":"這是一個短語動詞，由形容詞 'reasonable'（合理的，情理之中的）和介詞 'about'（關於）構成。核心含義是“採取理性的、合乎情理的態度來對待某事或某人”。它強調在溝通或決策時，應基於事實、邏輯和公平。","definition":"To act or think in a sensible, fair, and logical way regarding a particular matter or person.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"You need to be reasonable about the amount of time you spend playing games.\",\n    \"ch\": \"你需要在玩遊戲的時間上有所節制，講道理。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The teacher asked the students to be reasonable about their complaints.\",\n    \"ch\": \"老師要求學生們對他們的抱怨要合乎情理。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"老師要求學生們對他們的抱怨要合乎情理。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3202,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::beggar::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The story of the ____ who became king is a classic.","expectedAnswer":"beggar","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The story of the ____ who became king is a classic.","clozeAnswer":"beggar","exampleTranslation":"乞丐變成國王的故事是經典。","reference":{"eng":"beggar","kk":"/ˈbɛɡər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['乞丐']]","chEntries":["乞丐"],"practiceMeaning":"乞丐變成國王的故事是經典。","analysis":"源自動詞 'beg'，意為 'to ask for alms'。詞根 'beg' 據信來自古英語 'beggan'，意為 'to pray'，後引申為『懇求、乞求』。'beggar' 則是執行此行為的人。","definition":"a person, especially one who is poor, who asks for money or food from other people.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The beggar sat by the roadside, asking for money.\",\n    \"ch\": \"乞丐坐在路邊，乞討錢財。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The story of the beggar who became king is a classic.\",\n    \"ch\": \"乞丐變成國王的故事是經典。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"乞丐變成國王的故事是經典。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U41"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4327,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::beneath::prep","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She felt a sense of unease ____ her calm exterior.","expectedAnswer":"beneath","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She felt a sense of unease ____ her calm exterior.","clozeAnswer":"beneath","exampleTranslation":"在她平靜的外表下，她感到一絲不安。","reference":{"eng":"beneath","kk":"/bɪˈniːθ/","tense":"prep.","ch":"[['在…下方；在…下面'], ['（地位、身份）低下於；卑於']]","chEntries":["在…下方","在…下面","低下於","卑於"],"practiceMeaning":"在她平靜的外表下，她感到一絲不安。","analysis":"源自古英語 'beneothan'，由 'bene-' (down) 和 'neath' (near, under) 構成，與 'below' 同源。1. 指物理空間上的『在…下方』。2. 作為比喻，指在社會階層、道德標準或價值觀上的『低於、配不上』，表示不值得、有損身份。","definition":"in or to a lower position than someone or something else; directly under the surface of something; lower than someone or something in rank, status, or quality","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The treasure was buried deep beneath the ground.\",\n    \"ch\": \"寶藏深埋在地下。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She felt a sense of unease beneath her calm exterior.\",\n    \"ch\": \"在她平靜的外表下，她感到一絲不安。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Such behavior is beneath a person of his standing.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這樣的行為有損他這樣的身份。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"在她平靜的外表下，她感到一絲不安。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3904,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::besides::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"I don't want to go. ____, I'm too tired.","expectedAnswer":"Besides","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"I don't want to go. ____, I'm too tired.","clozeAnswer":"Besides","exampleTranslation":"我不想去。再說，我太累了。","reference":{"eng":"besides","kk":"/bɪˈsaɪdz/","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['而且', '此外'], ['再說']]","chEntries":["而且","此外","再說"],"practiceMeaning":"我不想去。再說，我太累了。","analysis":"由 'by' (在旁) + 'side' (邊) + '-s' 組成。核心是「在…旁邊」。引申為「此外」，表示在已提出的論點之外，還有更多補充的理由或事實。","definition":"in addition; moreover.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The hotel is too expensive. Besides, it's too far from the city center.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家飯店太貴了。而且，它離市中心太遠了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I don't want to go. Besides, I'm too tired.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我不想去。再說，我太累了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我不想去。再說，我太累了。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6155,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::beware::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Drivers should ____ of icy roads in winter.","expectedAnswer":"beware","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Drivers should ____ of icy roads in winter.","clozeAnswer":"beware","exampleTranslation":"司機在冬天應提防結冰的路面。","reference":{"eng":"beware","kk":"bɪˈwɛr","tense":"v.","ch":"[  [    \"警惕\"  ],  [    \"提防\"  ],  [    \"注意\"  ]]","chEntries":["警惕","提防","注意"],"practiceMeaning":"司機在冬天應提防結冰的路面。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 be+ware，意為「注意、警覺」。ware 本身是古英語 wær 的變體，意為「警覺的」。此字通常作為一個獨立的動詞或感嘆詞使用，其核心語義是「對潛在的危險或困難保持警惕」。它的結構由介詞 be- (表示強調或作為動詞前綴) 和形容詞/過去分詞 ware (警覺的) 組成，暗示著一種主動的、持續的警覺狀態。","definition":"1. be careful of (someone or something), especially by avoiding danger or harm.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Beware of the dog.\",\n    \"ch\": \"小心惡犬。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Drivers should beware of icy roads in winter.\",\n    \"ch\": \"司機在冬天應提防結冰的路面。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Beware! He is known for his deceitful tactics.\",\n    \"ch\": \"小心！他以狡猾的策略聞名。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Beware of pickpockets in crowded areas.\",\n    \"ch\": \"在擁擠的地區要小心扒手。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"司機在冬天應提防結冰的路面。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4656,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::blockbuster::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Her latest novel became a literary ____.","expectedAnswer":"blockbuster","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Her latest novel became a literary ____.","clozeAnswer":"blockbuster","exampleTranslation":"她最新的小說成了一部文學巨製。","reference":{"eng":"blockbuster","kk":"/ˈblɒkˌbʌstər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['轟動一時的電影/作品'], ['巨製']]","chEntries":["轟動一時的電影/作品","巨製"],"practiceMeaning":"她最新的小說成了一部文學巨製。","analysis":"此為固定片語。'Block' (街區) + 'buster' (打破者)。原指巨型炸彈。現代用法指非常成功、票房極佳或引起廣泛關注的電影、書籍或表演，通常是大規模製作。","definition":"a film that is very popular and successful; a very large or successful product or enterprise.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The new superhero movie is expected to be a blockbuster.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這部新的超級英雄電影預計將成為一部轟動大片。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her latest novel became a literary blockbuster.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她最新的小說成了一部文學巨製。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她最新的小說成了一部文學巨製。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5622,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l7::bold::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The designer used ____ colors in the artwork.","expectedAnswer":"bold","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The designer used ____ colors in the artwork.","clozeAnswer":"bold","exampleTranslation":"設計師在這件藝術品中使用了醒目的顏色。","reference":{"eng":"bold","kk":"boʊld","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['大膽的'], ['勇敢的'], ['魯莽的'], ['醒目的'], ['粗體的']]","chEntries":["大膽的","勇敢的","魯莽的","醒目的","粗體的"],"practiceMeaning":"設計師在這件藝術品中使用了醒目的顏色。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 'bāld'，其原始日耳曼語形式為 *balþuz。構詞學上，此字通常被視為一個整體詞，詞源與「強壯」、「大膽」相關。語意核心是「敢於冒險」、「不畏縮」。從「勇敢」、「無畏」引申出「魯莽」的負面含義。在印刷術中，指字體「粗體」，因為這種字體看起來更「醒目」、「強壯」。","definition":"1. Showing an ability to take risks; confident and courageous; 2. (Of a color, design, or shape) having a strong or vivid appearance; 3. (Of print) having the letters thicker and heavier than normal; 4. Showing an impudent lack of respect.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She was bold enough to ask for a raise.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她大膽到足以要求加薪。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The designer used bold colors in the artwork.\",\n    \"ch\": \"設計師在這件藝術品中使用了醒目的顏色。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He made a bold decision to invest in the startup.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他做出了大膽的決定，投資那家初創公司。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please format the headings in bold.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請將標題格式化為粗體。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"設計師在這件藝術品中使用了醒目的顏色。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5826,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::bolt::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She slid the ____ across the door.","expectedAnswer":"bolt","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She slid the ____ across the door.","clozeAnswer":"bolt","exampleTranslation":"她拉上門閂。","reference":{"eng":"bolt","kk":"boʊlt","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"螺栓\"  ],  [    \"門閂\"  ],  [    \"閃電\"  ],  [    \"閃電般的光\"  ]]","chEntries":["螺栓","門閂","閃電","閃電般的光"],"practiceMeaning":"她拉上門閂。","analysis":"此字有多個同形異源的來源。一來源是表示「門閂」、「槓桿」，來自古英語 'bolta' 或「橫樑」；另一來源是表示「閃電」、「快速跑」，可能與原始日耳曼語 *bult- (to bolt, to build) 或 *baltaz (swift) 有關。當指「門閂」時，其語意與「關閉」、「鎖定」相關。當指「閃電」時，則強調其突然、快速的爆發。另一常見義「螺栓」則是現代引申，借用了「鎖定」或「固定」的意象。還有「快速跑」的動詞義，也與「閃電」的突然性及速度相關。這裡的「閃電般的光」更側重於視覺上的突然出現。","definition":"1. A metal pin used to fasten things together, typically with a nut on the end.; 2. A bar used to fasten a door or gate.; 3. A flash of lightning.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He tightened the bolt on the door.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他擰緊了門上的螺栓。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She slid the bolt across the door.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她拉上門閂。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A bolt of lightning lit up the sky.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一道閃電劃破天空。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A bolt of light shot across the sky.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一道閃光劃過天際。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她拉上門閂。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6210,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::bonus::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company's excellent performance resulted in a generous ____ for all staff.","expectedAnswer":"bonus","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company's excellent performance resulted in a generous ____ for all staff.","clozeAnswer":"bonus","exampleTranslation":"公司優異的業績為所有員工帶來了豐厚的紅利。","reference":{"eng":"bonus","kk":"ˈboʊnəs","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"獎金\"  ],  [    \"紅利\"  ],  [    \"額外津貼\"  ],  [    \"好處\"  ]]","chEntries":["獎金","紅利","額外津貼","好處"],"practiceMeaning":"公司優異的業績為所有員工帶來了豐厚的紅利。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 bonus，意為「好的」，在中古英語和現代英語中演變為「額外的給予，特別的好處」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作名詞時，指在基本工資或報酬之外額外給予的金錢、物品或好處，通常是因為表現良好、公司盈利或特殊節日。中文翻譯為「獎金；紅利；額外津貼；好處」。","definition":"1. an amount of money given to someone in addition to what is usual or expected, especially as a reward for good work; 2. something good that is extra and unexpected.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The employees received a Christmas bonus.\",\n    \"ch\": \"員工們收到了聖誕獎金。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company's excellent performance resulted in a generous bonus for all staff.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司優異的業績為所有員工帶來了豐厚的紅利。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Finding parking was a bonus on such a busy day.\",\n    \"ch\": \"在如此忙碌的一天找到停車位是一份額外的幸運。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"公司優異的業績為所有員工帶來了豐厚的紅利。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5026,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::boom::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The dot-com ____ was a period of rapid growth in internet companies.","expectedAnswer":"boom","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The dot-com ____ was a period of rapid growth in internet companies.","clozeAnswer":"boom","exampleTranslation":"網路泡沫（科技公司）的繁榮時期是網際網路公司快速發展的階段。","reference":{"eng":"boom","kk":"buːm","tense":"n.","ch":"[['轟鳴聲'], ['繁榮（時期）'], ['低沉響亮的聲音']]","chEntries":["轟鳴聲","繁榮","低沉響亮的聲音"],"practiceMeaning":"網路泡沫（科技公司）的繁榮時期是網際網路公司快速發展的階段。","analysis":"此字可能源自擬聲詞，模仿低沉、響亮的聲音，如連續的槍聲、雷聲或鐘聲。其語意核心是「一種低沉、響亮且持續的聲音」。引申意義包括經濟或商業上的「繁榮、蓬勃發展」，此處的「繁榮」可理解為一種「強勁、廣泛」的影響，類似於聲音的擴散。OCR 掃描時可能將 'o' 誤判為 '0'，或單字切開、黏合。此處修正為 boom，具備廣泛的語意。","definition":"1. a deep, resonant sound; 2. a period of rapid economic growth or success; 3. a loud, deep, sustained sound.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The boom of the cannons echoed across the valley.\",\n    \"ch\": \"砲聲在山谷間迴盪。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The dot-com boom was a period of rapid growth in internet companies.\",\n    \"ch\": \"網路泡沫（科技公司）的繁榮時期是網際網路公司快速發展的階段。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"網路泡沫（科技公司）的繁榮時期是網際網路公司快速發展的階段。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5772,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::boxer::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He became a professional ____ at a young age.","expectedAnswer":"boxer","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He became a professional ____ at a young age.","clozeAnswer":"boxer","exampleTranslation":"他在年輕時成為了一名職業拳擊手。","reference":{"eng":"boxer","kk":"ˈbɑksər","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"拳擊手\"  ],  [    \"拳擊運動員\"  ]]","chEntries":["拳擊手","拳擊運動員"],"practiceMeaning":"他在年輕時成為了一名職業拳擊手。","analysis":"此字為名詞，由box（拳擊；拳擊比賽）+ -er（名詞字尾，表示「從事某種活動的人」）構成。box作為拳擊比賽的用語，其詞源較為複雜，可能與古法語bouts「圍繞」或與拳頭擊打動作發音有關。-er字尾源自日耳曼語系（如古英語-ere），常用於指代執行某動作或從事某職業的人。因此，boxer的核心語義是指「從事拳擊運動的人」，即拳擊手。此字沒有其他常見的、由box轉品而來的詞義。","definition":"1. a person who fights professionally in the sport of boxing.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The boxer trained rigorously for the upcoming championship.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位拳擊手為即將到來的錦標賽進行了嚴格的訓練。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He became a professional boxer at a young age.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在年輕時成為了一名職業拳擊手。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他在年輕時成為了一名職業拳擊手。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3068,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::breed::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He comes from a good ____.","expectedAnswer":"breed","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He comes from a good ____.","clozeAnswer":"breed","exampleTranslation":"他出身名門（好血統）。","reference":{"eng":"breed","kk":"/briːd/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['品種；種類'], ['（人、動物的）家系；血統']]","chEntries":["品種","種類","家系","血統"],"practiceMeaning":"他出身名門（好血統）。","analysis":"源自古英語 'brēdan' (to nourish, to bring up, to make multiply)。指由繁殖而產生的特定類型或家系。\n1. 品種；種類：指由於特定特徵而區分的動植物類別。\n2. （人、動物的）家系；血統：指同一家族或血緣關係的成員，或其遺傳特質。","definition":"1. a particular type of animal or plant, especially one that has been developed by people; 2. a type of person or thing.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a rare breed of dog.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是稀有的犬種。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He comes from a good breed.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他出身名門（好血統）。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他出身名門（好血統）。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4496,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::bulletproof::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His alibi was ____.","expectedAnswer":"bulletproof","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His alibi was ____.","clozeAnswer":"bulletproof","exampleTranslation":"他的不在場證明無懈可擊。","reference":{"eng":"bulletproof","kk":"/ˈbʊlɪtˌpruːf/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['防彈的'], ['（計劃、論點等）無懈可擊的']]","chEntries":["防彈的","無懈可擊的"],"practiceMeaning":"他的不在場證明無懈可擊。","analysis":"由 bullet (子彈) 和 proof (防護) 組成。核心語意是「能抵擋子彈的」。引申為「絕對可靠」、「無懈可擊」的計劃、理論等。","definition":"1. Impervious to bullets; 2. Impossible to disprove or contradict.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The limousine was equipped with bulletproof glass.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這輛轎車配備了防彈玻璃。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His alibi was bulletproof.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的不在場證明無懈可擊。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他的不在場證明無懈可擊。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3206,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::cane::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The chair was made of woven ____.","expectedAnswer":"cane","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The chair was made of woven ____.","clozeAnswer":"cane","exampleTranslation":"這把椅子是用編織的藤條製成的。","reference":{"eng":"cane","kk":"/keɪn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['手杖'], ['藤條'], ['蘆葦']]","chEntries":["手杖","藤條","蘆葦"],"practiceMeaning":"這把椅子是用編織的藤條製成的。","analysis":"詞源來自希臘文 'kanna'，經拉丁文 'canna' 傳入。原指中空的植物莖，如蘆葦。引申為由這種莖製作的物品，如藤條、竹竿，以及用於支撐身體的「手杖」。","definition":"1. a walking stick made of wood or metal; 2. the hollow 