"ch":"[['魅力'], ['吸引力'], ['護身符']]","chEntries":["魅力","吸引力","護身符"],"practiceMeaning":"考試時他戴著一個幸運護身符。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'carminare' (唱歌、咒語)。最初指能帶來好運的護身符或咒語。引申義指個人身上散發出的吸引人的氣質、風度或魔力，讓人產生好感。","definition":"the power to attract or delight; a small object worn as a token of good luck or as a reminder.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a natural charm that makes people like her.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她天生具有一種魅力，讓人喜歡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He wore a lucky charm for the exam.\",\n    \"ch\": \"考試時他戴著一個幸運護身符。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"考試時他戴著一個幸運護身符。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4328,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::chest::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The pirate buried his treasure in a ____.","expectedAnswer":"chest","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The pirate buried his treasure in a ____.","clozeAnswer":"chest","exampleTranslation":"海盜將他的寶藏埋在一個箱子裡。","reference":{"eng":"chest","kk":"/tʃɛst/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['胸部'], ['箱子；櫃子']]","chEntries":["胸部","箱子","櫃子"],"practiceMeaning":"海盜將他的寶藏埋在一個箱子裡。","analysis":"源自古英語 'cest'，與古希臘語 'kistē' (box) 和拉丁語 'cista' (box, chest) 同源，原意是指『箱子』。1. 指人體或動物身體的『胸部』，這個含義可能是在使用木箱來比喻胸腔的堅固性或容量後發展而來，或是因為胸部常被認為是承載情感的『箱子』。2. 最原始的含義，指『箱子、櫃子』，特別是較大的、用於存放財物的箱子。","definition":"the part of the front of the body between the neck and the stomach; a large strong box with a lid, used for storing things or for travelling","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He suffered a pain in his chest.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他感到胸部疼痛。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The pirate buried his treasure in a chest.\",\n    \"ch\": \"海盜將他的寶藏埋在一個箱子裡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She keeps her old letters in a wooden chest.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她把舊信件放在一個木箱裡。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"海盜將他的寶藏埋在一個箱子裡。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5289,"wordRef":"字彙王::u63::chord::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"A ____ connects two points on the circumference of a circle.","expectedAnswer":"chord","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"A ____ connects two points on the circumference of a circle.","clozeAnswer":"chord","exampleTranslation":"弦連接圓周上的兩個點。","reference":{"eng":"chord","kk":"kɔːrd","tense":"n.","ch":"[['和弦'], ['（幾何學）弦'], ['（尤指電線）纜線，線']]","chEntries":["和弦","弦","纜線，線"],"practiceMeaning":"弦連接圓周上的兩個點。","analysis":"此字有兩個主要詞源。一是來自古希臘語 'chordē' (χορδή)，意為「腸線、弦」。這個詞源導向了音樂中的「和弦」和幾何學中的「弦」。二是來自古法語 'corde'（繩索、線），源自拉丁語 'chorda'，與希臘語 'chordē' 同源，均指「腸線、弦、繩索」。在現代英語中，'chord' 作名詞時，最常見的意義是音樂中的「和弦」，幾何學中的「弦」，以及表示「線」或「纜線」時，儘管 'cord' 更常用於此意。","definition":"a group of three or more notes sounded together in harmony; a straight line or curve connecting two points on a curve or circle; a flexible insulated electrical cable.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The pianist played a beautiful chord.\",\n    \"ch\": \"鋼琴師彈奏了一個優美的和弦。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A chord connects two points on the circumference of a circle.\",\n    \"ch\": \"弦連接圓周上的兩個點。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"弦連接圓周上的兩個點。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U63"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5828,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::chubby::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He was a ____ boy with a cheerful smile.","expectedAnswer":"chubby","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He was a ____ boy with a cheerful smile.","clozeAnswer":"chubby","exampleTranslation":"他是一個胖乎乎但笑容開朗的男孩。","reference":{"eng":"chubby","kk":"ˈtʃʌbi","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"豐滿的\"  ],  [    \"胖乎乎的\"  ],  [    \"圓胖的\"  ],  [    \"圓潤的\"  ]]","chEntries":["豐滿的","胖乎乎的","圓胖的","圓潤的"],"practiceMeaning":"他是一個胖乎乎但笑容開朗的男孩。","analysis":"此字源於 'chub'，原指一種胖魚（如鯉魚的一種），後來用來形容人或物的圓胖、豐滿。'Chub' 本身來源不明，可能與「腫脹」或「凸起」的語感有關。'-y' 是常見的形容詞字尾，表示「具有……性質的」。'Chubby' 的語意核心是「圓胖、豐滿」，通常帶有可愛、健康的意味，多用於形容嬰兒、兒童或臉頰。它描述的是一種溫和、無攻擊性的肥胖感。例如，也可指「圓潤的」手指或四肢。","definition":"1. (of a person, especially a child) plump; well-rounded.; 2. (of a part of a person's body) rounded and plump.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The baby had chubby cheeks.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那個嬰兒有著圓胖的臉頰。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was a chubby boy with a cheerful smile.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一個胖乎乎但笑容開朗的男孩。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a chubby face.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她有一張豐滿的臉。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The child's chubby fingers reached for the toy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子圓潤的手指伸向了玩具。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他是一個胖乎乎但笑容開朗的男孩。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4346,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::cinema::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Let's go to the ____ tonight.","expectedAnswer":"cinema","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Let's go to the ____ tonight.","clozeAnswer":"cinema","exampleTranslation":"我們今晚去看電影吧。","reference":{"eng":"cinema","kk":"/ˈsɪnəmə/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['電影；電影藝術'], ['電影院']]","chEntries":["電影","電影藝術","電影院"],"practiceMeaning":"我們今晚去看電影吧。","analysis":"源自希臘語 'kinēma' (movement)，來自 'kinein' (to move)。1. 指『電影』作為一種藝術形式或娛樂，即『電影藝術』。2. 指放映電影的場所，即『電影院』。","definition":"the business or activity of making films; the art or technique of making films; a building in which films are shown","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a great admirer of French cinema.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是法國電影藝術的忠實崇拜者。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Let's go to the cinema tonight.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們今晚去看電影吧。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The history of cinema is fascinating.\",\n    \"ch\": \"電影的歷史非常迷人。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們今晚去看電影吧。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4626,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::citizen::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She has been a proud ____ of this country for twenty years.","expectedAnswer":"citizen","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She has been a proud ____ of this country for twenty years.","clozeAnswer":"citizen","exampleTranslation":"她做這個國家的自豪公民已經二十年了。","reference":{"eng":"citizen","kk":"/ˈsɪtɪzən/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['公民'], ['市民']]","chEntries":["公民","市民"],"practiceMeaning":"她做這個國家的自豪公民已經二十年了。","analysis":"源自古法語 'citeien'，拉丁語 'civis' (城市居民)。指一個國家或地區的合法成員，享有權利並負有義務。可指國家公民，也可指城市居民。","definition":"a legally recognized subject or national of a state or commonwealth, either native or naturalized; an inhabitant of a city or town.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Every citizen has the right to vote.\",\n    \"ch\": \"每個公民都有投票權。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has been a proud citizen of this country for twenty years.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她做這個國家的自豪公民已經二十年了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她做這個國家的自豪公民已經二十年了。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6065,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::citizenship::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ education teaches people about their rights and responsibilities.","expectedAnswer":"Citizenship","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ education teaches people about their rights and responsibilities.","clozeAnswer":"Citizenship","exampleTranslation":"公民教育教導人們了解他們的權利和責任。","reference":{"eng":"citizenship","kk":"ˈsɪtɪzənʃɪp","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"公民權\"  ],  [    \"市民身份\"  ],  [    \"國民身份\"  ],  [    \"公民意識\"  ]]","chEntries":["公民權","市民身份","國民身份","公民意識"],"practiceMeaning":"公民教育教導人們了解他們的權利和責任。","analysis":"此字由 citizen（公民）加上名詞後綴 -ship（表示狀態、身份、技能或集合）構成。Citizen 源自古法語 citeien，來自 civitas（city, state），再追溯至 civis（citizen）。Civitas 最終來源於 proto-Indo-European * (s)kein-「劃分，切割」，引申為「部落、社群」。Citizenship 的核心語義是「作為一個公民的身份、權利和義務」，包括法律上的公民權（公民身份），以及更廣泛的「公民責任」或「公民意識」。","definition":"1. the status of being a citizen of a particular country; 2. the rights and duties of a citizen; 3. the quality of behaving well and being useful to your country or community.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He applied for citizenship after living in the country for ten years.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在該國居住了十年後申請了公民權。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Citizenship education teaches people about their rights and responsibilities.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公民教育教導人們了解他們的權利和責任。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Active citizenship is crucial for a healthy democracy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"積極的公民意識對健康的民主至關重要。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"公民教育教導人們了解他們的權利和責任。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6066,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::civic::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They attended a ____ ceremony in the town hall.","expectedAnswer":"civic","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They attended a ____ ceremony in the town hall.","clozeAnswer":"civic","exampleTranslation":"他們參加了市政廳的市民儀式。","reference":{"eng":"civic","kk":"ˈsɪvɪk","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"公民的\"  ],  [    \"市民的\"  ],  [    \"市政的\"  ]]","chEntries":["公民的","市民的","市政的"],"practiceMeaning":"他們參加了市政廳的市民儀式。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 civicus，意為「屬於一個市民的」，來自 civis（citizen）。Civis 最終來源於 proto-Indo-European * (s)kein-「劃分，切割」，引申為「社群、部落」。Civic 作為形容詞，修飾與公民、市民、城市或市政事務相關的事物。核心語義是「與城市或其居民相關的」。","definition":"relating to a town or city, or to the people who live there; relating to the duties or activities of people in a town or city.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government launched a new civic engagement program.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府推出了一項新的公民參與計畫。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They attended a civic ceremony in the town hall.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們參加了市政廳的市民儀式。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Civic duty requires citizens to vote in elections.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公民責任要求市民在選舉中投票。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們參加了市政廳的市民儀式。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5329,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l1::claim::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The insurance company rejected her ____.","expectedAnswer":"claim","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The insurance company rejected her ____.","clozeAnswer":"claim","exampleTranslation":"保險公司駁回了她的理賠請求。","reference":{"eng":"claim","kk":"kleɪm","tense":"n.","ch":"[['主張'], ['權利'], ['要求'], ['聲稱']]","chEntries":["主張","權利","要求","聲稱"],"practiceMeaning":"保險公司駁回了她的理賠請求。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 clamer，來自拉丁語 clamare（喊叫、請求），再追溯至原始印歐語 *kelh₂-（呼喊、召喚）。構詞上，clam- 是字根，表示「呼喊」或「大聲說」。原始語意為「呼喊以求」或「大聲宣告」。現代語意發展為「對某事物提出權利主張」、「要求」或「聲稱擁有」。當名詞使用時，指「聲稱」、「權利」或「要求」的行為或內容。","definition":"an assertion that something is the case, without providing evidence or proof; a right or legal entitlement to have something or to take a particular course of action.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He made a claim to the throne.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他聲稱對王位擁有權利。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The insurance company rejected her claim.\",\n    \"ch\": \"保險公司駁回了她的理賠請求。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"保險公司駁回了她的理賠請求。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5583,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::classic::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The play is a ____ of English literature.","expectedAnswer":"classic","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The play is a ____ of English literature.","clozeAnswer":"classic","exampleTranslation":"這齣戲是英國文學的經典之作。","reference":{"eng":"classic","kk":"ˈklæsɪk","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['經典的'], ['古典的'], ['典型的'], ['一流的']]","chEntries":["經典的","古典的","典型的","一流的"],"practiceMeaning":"這齣戲是英國文學的經典之作。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 \"classicus\"，意為 \"of or belonging to the highest class, first-class\"（屬於最高級別的，一流的），來自 \"classis\"（a class, fleet, order，階級，艦隊，秩序）。\"classis\" 最初指「羅馬貴族階層」，後來也指「海軍艦隊」，再引申為「類別」或「等級」。因此，\"classic\" 的核心語義是「屬於最高等級、最經典、最受推崇的」。它可以用來形容「古希臘羅馬時期的」（classical antiquity）；指「代表某一類型最高水準的、永恆的」（exemplary, timeless）；或指「典型的、代表性的」（typical）。","definition":"1. Judged over a period of time to be of the highest quality and significance; timeless; 2. Characteristic of or belonging to a past period, especially of ancient Greece or Rome; 3. Familiarly typical or representative.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a classic example of her early work.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是她早期作品的一個經典範例。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The play is a classic of English literature.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這齣戲是英國文學的經典之作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He drives a classic car.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他開一輛經典老爺車。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was a classic case of misunderstanding.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個典型的誤會案例。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這齣戲是英國文學的經典之作。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6114,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::cluster::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"a ____ of houses","expectedAnswer":"cluster","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"a ____ of houses","clozeAnswer":"cluster","exampleTranslation":"一群房屋","reference":{"eng":"cluster","kk":"ˈklʌstər","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"一簇\"  ],  [    \"一叢\"  ],  [    \"一群\"  ],  [    \"集結\"  ]]","chEntries":["一簇","一叢","一群","集結"],"practiceMeaning":"一群房屋","analysis":"此字詞源不確定，可能與古英語 clūst（關閉）或北歐語 klustr（院子）有關，核心語義是「聚集」。此名詞指由許多相似的物體聚集而成的「一簇」或「一叢」，或指人、物的「一群」、「集合」。其語意演變是從具體的「聚集體」到抽象的「群體」。","definition":"1. a group of similar things or people positioned or occurring closely together; 2. a number of things of the same kind growing or occurring together.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"a cluster of stars\",\n    \"ch\": \"一簇星星\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"a cluster of houses\",\n    \"ch\": \"一群房屋\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"a cluster of grapes\",\n    \"ch\": \"一串葡萄\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"一群房屋","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6117,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::coffin::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They lowered the ____ into the grave.","expectedAnswer":"coffin","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They lowered the ____ into the grave.","clozeAnswer":"coffin","exampleTranslation":"他們將棺材下葬。","reference":{"eng":"coffin","kk":"ˈkɔːfɪn","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"棺材\"  ],  [    \"靈柩\"  ]]","chEntries":["棺材","靈柩"],"practiceMeaning":"他們將棺材下葬。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 cofin，意為「盒子」，來自拉丁語 cophinus，來自希臘語 kophinos，意為「籃子」。因此，coffin 的核心語義是「一種容器」。在 modern English 中，它特指用於存放死者遺體的「棺材」。其語意演變是從「籃子」到「盒子」，再到「棺材」。","definition":"A box-like container for a dead body.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The coffin was made of dark wood.\",\n    \"ch\": \"棺材是由深色木材製成的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They lowered the coffin into the grave.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們將棺材下葬。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們將棺材下葬。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6159,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::coincidence::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Their birthdays falling on the same day is a strange ____.","expectedAnswer":"coincidence","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Their birthdays falling on the same day is a strange ____.","clozeAnswer":"coincidence","exampleTranslation":"他們的生日落在同一天是一個奇怪的巧合。","reference":{"eng":"coincidence","kk":"koʊˈɪnsɪdəns","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"巧合\"  ],  [    \"同時發生\"  ]]","chEntries":["巧合","同時發生"],"practiceMeaning":"他們的生日落在同一天是一個奇怪的巧合。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 coincidentia，是 coincidentem (coincidens)「同時發生、一致」的現在分詞名詞化。coincidentem 由 com- (together) + inciderē (to fall upon, happen) 組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 com-「一起」和 inciderē「發生、落下」是其核心語意來源。作為名詞，核心語義是「兩個或多個事件恰好同時發生，且彼此之間沒有明顯的因果關係」。詞源中的「一起發生」清楚地體現了此義。","definition":"1. the occurrence and development of events in a happy or beneficial way; 2. a situation in which events happen at the same time in a way that has no obvious connection.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was a remarkable coincidence that they met on the same day.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們在同一天見面真是個令人驚嘆的巧合。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Their birthdays falling on the same day is a strange coincidence.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們的生日落在同一天是一個奇怪的巧合。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"What a coincidence! I was just thinking about you.\",\n    \"ch\": \"真是巧合！我剛在想你。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The coincidence of their arriving at the same time was surprising.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們同時到達的巧合令人驚訝。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們的生日落在同一天是一個奇怪的巧合。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4070,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::collection::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The museum displayed a new ____ of art.","expectedAnswer":"collection","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The museum displayed a new ____ of art.","clozeAnswer":"collection","exampleTranslation":"博物館展出了一批新的藝術收藏品。","reference":{"eng":"collection","kk":"/kəˈlɛkʃən/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['收藏品', '蒐集物'], ['集合', '聚集'], ['（稅款、款項的）徵收', '收取']]","chEntries":["收藏品","蒐集物","集合","聚集","徵收","收取"],"practiceMeaning":"博物館展出了一批新的藝術收藏品。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'collectio'，由 'col-' (together) + 'legere' (to gather) 構成，字面意思是「一起收集」。核心是「聚集」、「蒐集」。因此，'collection' 指「蒐集到的物品」（收藏品），「蒐集的行為」，以及「聚集」本身。第四個義項「徵收」則指按規定「收集」款項或稅款。","definition":"1. a group of things that have been collected; 2. the act of collecting things; 3. a number of people or things that are gathered together; 4. the process of gathering money or other items","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"她有很多郵票收藏品。\",\n    \"eng\": \"She has a large collection of stamps.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"博物館展出了一批新的藝術收藏品。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The museum displayed a new collection of art.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"徵收稅款是政府的職責。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The collection of taxes is the responsibility of the government.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"博物館展出了一批新的藝術收藏品。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6161,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::collective::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company has a ____ bargaining agreement.","expectedAnswer":"collective","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company has a ____ bargaining agreement.","clozeAnswer":"collective","exampleTranslation":"這家公司簽有集體談判協議。","reference":{"eng":"collective","kk":"kəˈlɛktɪv","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"集體的\"  ],  [    \"共同的\"  ],  [    \"集中的\"  ]]","chEntries":["集體的","共同的","集中的"],"practiceMeaning":"這家公司簽有集體談判協議。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 collectīvus，是動詞 colligere「收集、聚集」的衍生形容詞。colligere 由 com- (together) + legere (to gather) 組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 com-「一起」和 legere「收集」是其核心語意來源。作為形容詞，其核心語義是「屬於、與、或由兩個或多個個體共同組成」。詞源中的「一起收集」概念與「集體的」概念緊密相關。此義項由「聚集」的動作引申為「集體的」狀態或性質。","definition":"1. relating to or affecting all the people or things in a group; 2. done by or involving all the people in a group; 3. formed by the union of several individuals or things into one; 4. relating to or characteristic of a collective or the collective consciousness.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They made a collective decision to go on strike.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們做出了集體罷工的決定。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company has a collective bargaining agreement.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司簽有集體談判協議。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The artist sought to express a collective consciousness.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位藝術家試圖表達集體意識。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The collective effort of the team led to success.\",\n    \"ch\": \"團隊的集體努力帶來了成功。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這家公司簽有集體談判協議。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3948,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::colorful::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She has a ____ personality.","expectedAnswer":"colorful","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She has a ____ personality.","clozeAnswer":"colorful","exampleTranslation":"她擁有一個豐富多彩的個性。","reference":{"eng":"colorful","kk":"/ˈkʌlərfəl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['色彩繽紛的'], ['生動有趣的']]","chEntries":["色彩繽紛的","生動有趣的"],"practiceMeaning":"她擁有一個豐富多彩的個性。","analysis":"由 'color' (名詞，顏色) 和 '-ful' (形容詞後綴) 組成。指擁有許多鮮豔顏色；也可引申為「生動有趣、豐富多彩」。","definition":"1. having a lot of different colors; 2. interesting or exciting; full of variety.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The market was filled with colorful fruits and vegetables.\",\n    \"ch\": \"市場裡擺滿了色彩繽紛的水果和蔬菜。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a colorful personality.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她擁有一個豐富多彩的個性。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The painting uses bold, colorful strokes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這幅畫使用了大膽、色彩鮮豔的筆觸。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她擁有一個豐富多彩的個性。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6213,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::combat::vt","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Scientists are working to ____ the spread of the virus.","expectedAnswer":"combat","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Scientists are working to ____ the spread of the virus.","clozeAnswer":"combat","exampleTranslation":"科學家們正在努力對抗病毒的傳播。","reference":{"eng":"combat","kk":"kəmˈbæt","tense":"vt.","ch":"[  [    \"戰鬥\"  ],  [    \"與…搏鬥\"  ],  [    \"對抗\"  ],  [    \"反對\"  ]]","chEntries":["戰鬥","與…搏鬥","對抗","反對"],"practiceMeaning":"科學家們正在努力對抗病毒的傳播。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 combat，由 com-（一起）和 batre（打擊）組成，意為「共同打擊」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作及物動詞時，核心語義是用武力與敵人交戰，或與某種難題、問題、疾病等進行激烈鬥爭。此及物動詞義必須接受詞，例如 combat the enemy、combat disease、combat poverty。中文翻譯為「戰鬥；與…搏鬥；對抗；反對」。","definition":"1. to fight against an enemy or opponent in order to win control of something; 2. to try to stop something bad from happening or to stop someone from doing something bad.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The army successfully combatted the invasion.\",\n    \"ch\": \"軍隊成功擊退了入侵。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Scientists are working to combat the spread of the virus.\",\n    \"ch\": \"科學家們正在努力對抗病毒的傳播。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We must combat all forms of discrimination.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們必須反對一切形式的歧視。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"科學家們正在努力對抗病毒的傳播。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4657,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::comedy::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His stand-up routine was a great ____.","expectedAnswer":"comedy","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His stand-up routine was a great ____.","clozeAnswer":"comedy","exampleTranslation":"他的單口相聲表演非常搞笑。","reference":{"eng":"comedy","kk":"/ˈkɒmədi/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['喜劇'], ['喜劇作品']]","chEntries":["喜劇","喜劇作品"],"practiceMeaning":"他的單口相聲表演非常搞笑。","analysis":"源自希臘語 'komoidia'，意為「喜劇」。指以引人發笑為目的的戲劇、電影、文學作品或表演。其特點通常是幽默、諷刺、誇張或滑稽的情節和人物。","definition":"a genre of film or theatre in which the primary purpose is to amuse and entertain the audience, often through humor.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They went to see a comedy last night.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們昨晚去看了一部喜劇。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His stand-up routine was a great comedy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的單口相聲表演非常搞笑。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他的單口相聲表演非常搞笑。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3945,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::committee::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She is a member of the planning ____.","expectedAnswer":"committee","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She is a member of the planning ____.","clozeAnswer":"committee","exampleTranslation":"她是計畫委員會的成員。","reference":{"eng":"committee","kk":"/kəˈmɪti/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['委員會']]","chEntries":["委員會"],"practiceMeaning":"她是計畫委員會的成員。","analysis":"源自中古英語 'committé' (意為「被託付的人」)，源自拉丁語 'committere' (意為「託付、委託」)。指為特定目的而設立的、由若干人組成的專門小組。","definition":"a group of people appointed for a specific function by a larger group and typically holding regular meetings.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The committee will meet next week to discuss the proposal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"委員會將於下週開會討論該提案。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a member of the planning committee.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是計畫委員會的成員。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The committee made a decision.\",\n    \"ch\": \"委員會做出了決定。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她是計畫委員會的成員。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5831,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::commodity::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need to improve the production of this ____.","expectedAnswer":"commodity","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need to improve the production of this ____.","clozeAnswer":"commodity","exampleTranslation":"我們需要提高這種商品的產量。","reference":{"eng":"commodity","kk":"kəˈmɑːdəti","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"商品\"  ],  [    \"物品\"  ],  [    \"價值\"  ],  [    \"必需品\"  ]]","chEntries":["商品","物品","價值","必需品"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要提高這種商品的產量。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'commoditas'，意為「便利」、「舒適」、「比例」、「益處」。'Commoditas' 來自 'commodus' (fitting, convenient)，由 'con-' (together) 和 'modus' (measure) 構成，意指「以適當的度量」。在早期中古英語中，'commodity' 意指「便利」或「有益之物」。後來，其語意演變為「有用的物品」或「可供交易的商品」。現代語義中，'commodity' 特指在市場上可買賣的標準化產品，如農產品、礦產或能源，強調其可交易性和價值。例如，也可指「一種商品的價值」。","definition":"1. A raw material or primary agricultural product that can be bought and sold, such as copper or coffee.; 2. A useful or valuable thing.; 3. Convenience; advantage.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Oil is a major global commodity.\",\n    \"ch\": \"石油是主要的全球商品。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to improve the production of this commodity.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要提高這種商品的產量。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Water is a vital commodity.\",\n    \"ch\": \"水是一種至關重要的必需品。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The commodity price fluctuated greatly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該商品的價格劇烈波動。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要提高這種商品的產量。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5559,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::commute::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He complained about the long ____.","expectedAnswer":"commute","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He complained about the long ____.","clozeAnswer":"commute","exampleTranslation":"他抱怨通勤時間太長。","reference":{"eng":"commute","kk":"kəˈmjuːt","tense":"n.","ch":"[['通勤']]","chEntries":["通勤"],"practiceMeaning":"他抱怨通勤時間太長。","analysis":"這是 \"commute\" 作動詞的相關名詞形式，源自拉丁語 \"commūtāre\"（to exchange, change，交換，改變）。\"com-\"（together, with，一起）和 \"mūtāre\"（to change，改變）。\"commūtāre\" 的語義演變是指「改變居住地與工作地之間的距離，透過往返移動來完成」。因此，\"commute\" 作為名詞，指「每天從家往返工作地點或學校的行為」，也就是「通勤」。此名詞形式主要與其動詞形式的「通勤」義相關聯。","definition":"1. The act or instance of commuting; 2. The journey made when one commutes.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"My daily commute takes about an hour each way.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我每天的通勤單程大約要一個小時。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He complained about the long commute.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他抱怨通勤時間太長。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他抱怨通勤時間太長。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3069,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::companion::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He traveled across Europe with a ____.","expectedAnswer":"companion","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He traveled across Europe with a ____.","clozeAnswer":"companion","exampleTranslation":"他與一位旅伴一同遊歷歐洲。","reference":{"eng":"companion","kk":"/kəmˈpænjən/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['同伴；夥伴'], ['陪伴者；伴侶'], ['（用於某些頭銜）同列的']]","chEntries":["同伴","夥伴","陪伴者","伴侶","同列的"],"practiceMeaning":"他與一位旅伴一同遊歷歐洲。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'compāniō'，'com-' (with) + 'pānis' (bread)，字面意思是「分享麵包的人」。核心意義是「一起生活或旅行的人」。\n1. 同伴；夥伴：指與某人同行或共同參與某項活動的人。\n2. 陪伴者；伴侶：指經常陪伴某人，提供支持或友誼的人，可以是人或動物。\n3. （用於某些頭銜）同列的：在名稱中表示與另一人或事物並列，例如 'Companion of Honour'。","definition":"1. a person who is with someone else; 2. a person or animal that travels with or lives with someone; 3. a person who is included in a group or order.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She found a loyal companion in her dog.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在她的狗身上找到了忠實的伴侶。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He traveled across Europe with a companion.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他與一位旅伴一同遊歷歐洲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was appointed a Companion of Honour.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他被任命為榮譽會員。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他與一位旅伴一同遊歷歐洲。","sourceName":"字彙王、龍騰課本","unitName":"U39、L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5513,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l5::compassion::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The organization works to alleviate suffering and promote ____.","expectedAnswer":"compassion","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The organization works to alleviate suffering and promote ____.","clozeAnswer":"compassion","exampleTranslation":"該組織致力於減輕痛苦並推廣慈悲。","reference":{"eng":"compassion","kk":"kəmˈpæʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[['同情心'], ['憐憫'], ['慈悲']]","chEntries":["同情心","憐憫","慈悲"],"practiceMeaning":"該組織致力於減輕痛苦並推廣慈悲。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'compassio'，由 'com-' (together) + 'passio' (suffering) 構成，意為「共同感受痛苦」。'passio' 本身來自 'patior' (to suffer)。構詞上，'com-' 強調「一同、共同」，'passio' 提供了「痛苦、苦難」的核心語意。原始語義是「與他人一同承受痛苦」。引申為一種感同身受的能力，並因此產生關懷與幫助他人的動機。這是一種強調情感共鳴和互助精神的抽象概念。","definition":"sympathetic pity and concern for the sufferings or misfortunes of others.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She felt great compassion for the refugees.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對難民們感到非常同情。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The organization works to alleviate suffering and promote compassion.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該組織致力於減輕痛苦並推廣慈悲。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該組織致力於減輕痛苦並推廣慈悲。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5033,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::competence::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company has proven its ____ in software development.","expectedAnswer":"competence","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company has proven its ____ in software development.","clozeAnswer":"competence","exampleTranslation":"該公司已證明了其在軟體開發方面的能力。","reference":{"eng":"competence","kk":"ˈkɑːmpɪtəns","tense":"n.","ch":"[['能力'], ['勝任'], ['才幹']]","chEntries":["能力","勝任","才幹"],"practiceMeaning":"該公司已證明了其在軟體開發方面的能力。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語competentem（有資格的、夠格的），是動詞 competere 的現在分詞。competere 由 com-（共同、一起）+ petere（尋求、爭取、達到）組成，原意為「共同努力以達成目標」、「相等、適合」。competence 意指「有能力完成某事的能力或資格」，強調的是具備完成任務所需的技能、知識和素質。","definition":"1. the ability to do something successfully or efficiently; 2. the ability to meet the needs of a situation.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her competence in financial management is outstanding.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在財務管理方面的能力非常傑出。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company has proven its competence in software development.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司已證明了其在軟體開發方面的能力。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該公司已證明了其在軟體開發方面的能力。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5038,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::conception::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The early stages of ____ are critical.","expectedAnswer":"conception","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The early stages of ____ are critical.","clozeAnswer":"conception","exampleTranslation":"懷孕的早期階段至關重要。","reference":{"eng":"conception","kk":"kənˈsepʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[['概念'], ['構想'], ['設想'], ['懷孕']]","chEntries":["概念","構想","設想","懷孕"],"practiceMeaning":"懷孕的早期階段至關重要。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語conceptio，由 concipere（構想、懷孕）派生而來。con-（一起、完全）+ capere（抓住、拿）。conception 在英語中有多個重要義項：1. 「概念、想法、構想」，指在頭腦中形成的觀念；2. 「懷孕」，指受孕的過程或狀態；3. 「對某事的理解或看法」。這些義項都與其詞源「共同抓住」、「形成」或「包含」的概念相關。OCR 掃描時可能將 'c' 誤判。此處修正為 conception。","definition":"1. the action or capability of forming concepts or ideas; 2. the process of becoming pregnant, involving fertilization or implantation; 3. an idea or understanding of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The conception of democracy has evolved over centuries.\",\n    \"ch\": \"民主的概念已經演變了幾個世紀。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The early stages of conception are critical.\",\n    \"ch\": \"懷孕的早期階段至關重要。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His conception of justice differs from mine.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對正義的看法與我的不同。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"懷孕的早期階段至關重要。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4484,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::concert::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The two companies worked in ____ to develop the new product.","expectedAnswer":"concert","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The two companies worked in ____ to develop the new product.","clozeAnswer":"concert","exampleTranslation":"兩家公司協同合作開發新產品。","reference":{"eng":"concert","kk":"/ˈkɒnsərt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['音樂會'], ['（尤指）演奏會'], ['（群體或個人之間的）協同，一致']]","chEntries":["音樂會","演奏會","協同，一致"],"practiceMeaning":"兩家公司協同合作開發新產品。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 concertare，意為「競爭」、「爭論」，後來在義大利語中演變成「協調」、「協同」。核心語意從「一起行動」引申為「（音樂）合奏」、「音樂會」。也保留了「協調一致」的語意。","definition":"1. A musical performance for an audience; 2. An agreement or concord; harmony.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We went to a classical music concert last night.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們昨晚去聽了一場古典音樂會。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The two companies worked in concert to develop the new product.\",\n    \"ch\": \"兩家公司協同合作開發新產品。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"兩家公司協同合作開發新產品。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4055,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::conclusion::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The movie had a surprising ____.","expectedAnswer":"conclusion","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The movie had a surprising ____.","clozeAnswer":"conclusion","exampleTranslation":"這部電影有一個出人意料的結局。","reference":{"eng":"conclusion","kk":"/kənˈkluʒən/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['結論', '結局'], ['結束']]","chEntries":["結論","結局","結束"],"practiceMeaning":"這部電影有一個出人意料的結局。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'conclusio'，由 'con-' (together) + 'claudere' (to shut) 構成，字面意思是「關閉在一起」。核心是「結束」、「完結」。因此，'conclusion' 指一個過程或事件的「結束」，也指通過推理或討論得出的「結論」。","definition":"1. the end or final part of something; 2. a judgment or decision reached by reasoning; 3. a final statement or summary","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"你對這個實驗的結論是什麼？\",\n    \"eng\": \"What is your conclusion about the experiment?\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"這部電影有一個出人意料的結局。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The movie had a surprising conclusion.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"經過長時間的討論，我們達成了一個結論。\",\n    \"eng\": \"We reached a conclusion after a long discussion.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這部電影有一個出人意料的結局。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U4、L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3070,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::conference::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The Lakers won the Western ____ championship.","expectedAnswer":"Conference","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The Lakers won the Western ____ championship.","clozeAnswer":"Conference","exampleTranslation":"湖人隊贏得了西區聯盟的冠軍。","reference":{"eng":"conference","kk":"/ˈkɑːnfərəns/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['會議；討論會'], ['（體育）聯盟；賽區']]","chEntries":["會議","討論會","聯盟","賽區"],"practiceMeaning":"湖人隊贏得了西區聯盟的冠軍。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'conferentia'，'con-' (together) + 'ferre' (to bring)。核心意義是「將事物帶到一起討論」。\n1. 會議；討論會：指為特定目的聚集一群人進行討論、交流或決策的正式場合。\n2. （體育）聯盟；賽區：指在體育比賽中，由多支隊伍組成的聯合體。","definition":"1. a formal meeting for discussion; 2. a large meeting where people with the same interests or profession come together to share ideas and information; 3. a group of teams in sports that compete against each other.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The annual conference on artificial intelligence will be held next month.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一年一度的人工智慧會議將於下個月舉行。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The Lakers won the Western Conference championship.\",\n    \"ch\": \"湖人隊贏得了西區聯盟的冠軍。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"湖人隊贏得了西區聯盟的冠軍。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4069,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::considerable::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There has been a ____ increase in prices.","expectedAnswer":"considerable","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There has been a ____ increase in prices.","clozeAnswer":"considerable","exampleTranslation":"價格有顯著的增長。","reference":{"eng":"considerable","kk":"/kənˈsɪdərəbəl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['相當大的', '可觀的'], ['值得考慮的', '重要的']]","chEntries":["相當大的","可觀的","值得考慮的","重要的"],"practiceMeaning":"價格有顯著的增長。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'considerare' (to observe, to examine)，由 'con-' (together) + 'sidus, sideris' (star) 構成，原意是「觀察星辰」，引申為「仔細考慮」、「審視」。因此，'considerable' 指「值得仔細考慮的」、「重要的」，進而延伸為「數量或程度非常大」、「可觀的」。","definition":"1. notably large in size, amount, or extent; 2. large or great enough to be worthy of attention or notice","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"這個項目需要相當多的時間和精力。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The project requires considerable time and effort.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"價格有顯著的增長。\",\n    \"eng\": \"There has been a considerable increase in prices.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"這是一項了不起的成就。\",\n    \"eng\": \"This is a considerable achievement.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"價格有顯著的增長。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5774,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::considerate::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It was ____ of you to bring me soup when I was sick.","expectedAnswer":"considerate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It was ____ of you to bring me soup when I was sick.","clozeAnswer":"considerate","exampleTranslation":"我生病時你還帶來湯，真是體貼。","reference":{"eng":"considerate","kk":"kənˈsɪdərət","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"體貼的\"  ],  [    \"考慮周到的\"  ],  [    \"關懷的\"  ]]","chEntries":["體貼的","考慮周到的","關懷的"],"practiceMeaning":"我生病時你還帶來湯，真是體貼。","analysis":"此字為形容詞，由consider（考慮）+ -ate（形容詞字尾，表示「具有……特性的」）構成。consider本身源自拉丁語considerare，由con-（一起）+sider-（星星，來自sidus）組成，原意可能與「觀星」、「審視星象」有關，後演變為「仔細思考；考慮」。-ate字尾有時也來自拉丁語-atus。因此，considerate的核心語義是指「經常考慮他人感受或需求的人」，即體貼周到的。語意演變上，從「仔細考慮」的動作，引申為「因考慮他人而表現出的體貼行為」。","definition":"1. showing careful thought for the rights and feelings of others; 2. characterized by careful thought or attention.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was very considerate and helped her with her heavy bags.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他非常體貼，幫她拿沈重的行李。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was considerate of you to bring me soup when I was sick.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我生病時你還帶來湯，真是體貼。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They made a considerate effort to include everyone in the discussion.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們費盡心思，盡力讓每個人都參與討論。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我生病時你還帶來湯，真是體貼。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4205,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::constant::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She is a ____ source of inspiration.","expectedAnswer":"constant","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She is a ____ source of inspiration.","clozeAnswer":"constant","exampleTranslation":"她是靈感的持續來源。","reference":{"eng":"constant","kk":"/ˈkɑːnstənt/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['持續的；不變的'], ['（忠誠、堅持等）堅定的；忠實的']]","chEntries":["持續的","不變的","堅定的","忠實的"],"practiceMeaning":"她是靈感的持續來源。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 constans，'con-'（一起）+ 'stare'（站立）。字面意思是“一起站立”，引申為“穩定，不變”。1. “持續的；不變的”強調時間或狀態上沒有變化。2. “堅定的；忠實的”強調在情感或關係上的穩定和忠誠。","definition":"1. occurring continuously over a period of time; 2. not changing or varying; 3. faithful and steadfast.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The car requires constant maintenance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這輛車需要持續的維護。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a constant source of inspiration.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是靈感的持續來源。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He remained constant in his loyalty to his friends.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對朋友們的忠誠始終如一。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她是靈感的持續來源。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5776,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::contend::vi","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She had to ____ with a lot of opposition.","expectedAnswer":"contend","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She had to ____ with a lot of opposition.","clozeAnswer":"contend","exampleTranslation":"她必須面對許多反對的聲音。","reference":{"eng":"contend","kk":"kənˈtɛnd","tense":"vi.","ch":"[  [    \"競爭\"  ],  [    \"爭奪\"  ],  [    \"奮鬥\"  ],  [    \"認為（某事）是真的\"  ]]","chEntries":["競爭","爭奪","奮鬥","認為是真的"],"practiceMeaning":"她必須面對許多反對的聲音。","analysis":"此字為不及物動詞，源自拉丁語contendere，由con-（一起；加強）+ tendere（伸展；努力）組成。tendere的原始印歐語詞根是\\\\*ten-（伸展）。因此，contend的核心語義是「一起努力；爭取」。語意演變上，從「一起伸展爭取」引申出「競爭」、「爭奪」，以及在辯論或論證中的「主張」或「認為」。此字作為vi.時，常接with（與……競爭/抗爭）或for（爭奪……）。","definition":"1. to try hard to deal with a difficult situation; 2. to compete with someone in order to win something; 3. to state something as a fact; compete or argue vigorously.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The two companies will contend for the leading market share.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這兩家公司將爭奪市場領導地位。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She had to contend with a lot of opposition.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她必須面對許多反對的聲音。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He contended that the evidence was insufficient.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他認為證據不足。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她必須面對許多反對的聲音。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5077,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::core::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She removed the ____ from the apple.","expectedAnswer":"core","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She removed the ____ from the apple.","clozeAnswer":"core","exampleTranslation":"她取出了蘋果的果核。","reference":{"eng":"core","kk":"kɔːr","tense":"n.","ch":"[['核心'], ['中心'], ['果核']]","chEntries":["核心","中心","果核"],"practiceMeaning":"她取出了蘋果的果核。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'cor' (heart)。核心概念是事物最內部、最重要、最基本的部分。這可以指一個物體的中心（如蘋果的核心），一個組織的關鍵成員，或一個概念的本質。它引申為事物的基礎、關鍵或主體。","definition":"1. The central or most important part of something.; 2. The hard central part of a fruit, containing the seeds.; 3. The part of the Earth's interior below the mantle.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The core of the problem is a lack of communication.\",\n    \"ch\": \"問題的核心在於缺乏溝通。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She removed the core from the apple.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她取出了蘋果的果核。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is the core business of the company.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是公司的核心業務。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她取出了蘋果的果核。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4168,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::costs::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need to reduce production ____.","expectedAnswer":"costs","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need to reduce production ____.","clozeAnswer":"costs","exampleTranslation":"我們需要降低生產成本。","reference":{"eng":"costs","kk":"/kɒsts/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['費用', '成本']]","chEntries":["費用","成本"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要降低生產成本。","analysis":"由 cost（成本，價值）的複數形式。源自古法語 cost（價值，報酬）。核心概念是「為獲得某物或完成某事所付出的代價」。","definition":"the amount of money needed to buy, produce, or do something","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The steep rise in living costs made it hard to make ends meet.\",\n    \"ch\": \"生活成本的急劇上漲使得人們難以為繼。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to reduce production costs.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要降低生產成本。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"What are the associated costs?\",\n    \"ch\": \"相關費用有哪些？\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要降低生產成本。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4541,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::crab::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Don't be such a ____; try to be more positive.","expectedAnswer":"crab","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Don't be such a ____; try to be more positive.","clozeAnswer":"crab","exampleTranslation":"別那麼愛抱怨；試著積極一點。","reference":{"eng":"crab","kk":"/kræb/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['螃蟹'], ['（用於指責或抱怨的）抱怨者，批評者']]","chEntries":["螃蟹","抱怨者，批評者"],"practiceMeaning":"別那麼愛抱怨；試著積極一點。","analysis":"源自古英語 'crabba'，與斯堪地那維亞語系語言中的同類詞有關。\n    1. 螃蟹：指甲殼類動物。\n    2. 抱怨者、批評者：此用法較為俚語化，指那些習慣性抱怨或挑剔的人，可能與螃蟹橫行的移動方式或其鉗子的攻擊性有關。","definition":"1. a decapod crustacean with a broad, flat body, stalked eyes, and five pairs of limbs, the first pair of which are modified as large, strong pincers.; 2. a person who is always complaining or finding fault.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He caught a large crab at the beach.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在海灘抓到一隻大螃蟹。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Don't be such a crab; try to be more positive.\",\n    \"ch\": \"別那麼愛抱怨；試著積極一點。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"別那麼愛抱怨；試著積極一點。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4222,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::credit::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"You can buy this item on ____.","expectedAnswer":"credit","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"You can buy this item on ____.","clozeAnswer":"credit","exampleTranslation":"你可以賒帳購買這個物品。","reference":{"eng":"credit","kk":"/ˈkredɪt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['信用；信譽'], ['（金融機構的）信貸；延期付款'], ['（在帳戶中的）貸方餘額；進帳'], ['功勞；讚揚']]","chEntries":["信用","信譽","信貸","延期付款","貸方餘額","進帳","功勞","讚揚"],"practiceMeaning":"你可以賒帳購買這個物品。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 creditum，'credere'（相信，信任）的派生詞。核心是“相信”或“信任”。1. “信用；信譽”指個人或機構的良好聲譽，使人願意相信其承諾。2. “信貸；延期付款”指金融機構基於信任而提供的貸款或允許延期支付。3. “貸方餘額；進帳”指銀行帳戶中的正面餘額。4. “功勞；讚揚”指因某人的貢獻而給予的肯定，基於相信其功績。","definition":"1. the ability of a customer to obtain goods or services before payment, based on the trust that payment will be made in the future; 2. trust in the believe that someone will do what they are expected or supposed to do; 3. an amount of money added to an account; 4. praise or admiration for an achievement.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has good credit and can easily get a loan.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的信用很好，很容易獲得貸款。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"You can buy this item on credit.\",\n    \"ch\": \"你可以賒帳購買這個物品。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She was given credit for her hard work.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她因辛勤工作而受到讚揚。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The deposit will be shown as a credit on your statement.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這筆存款將顯示為您對帳單上的進帳。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"你可以賒帳購買這個物品。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4245,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::crispy::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The fried chicken was perfectly ____.","expectedAnswer":"crispy","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The fried chicken was perfectly ____.","clozeAnswer":"crispy","exampleTranslation":"炸雞炸得非常酥脆。","reference":{"eng":"crispy","kk":"/ˈkrɪspi/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['酥脆的'], ['脆的']]","chEntries":["酥脆的","脆的"],"practiceMeaning":"炸雞炸得非常酥脆。","analysis":"源自中古英語 'crisp'（捲曲、有彈性的），與古法語 'crespe'（捲曲）有關。'Crispy' 最初指物體的質地，後來引申為食品的「酥脆」口感，強調其斷裂時的聲音和質地。此詞的語意從「捲曲」延伸到「易碎、有聲響的斷裂」。","definition":"firm enough to break with a snapping sound; pleasantly hard and dry","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I love the crispy crust of the freshly baked bread.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我喜歡剛烤好的麵包酥脆的表皮。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The fried chicken was perfectly crispy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"炸雞炸得非常酥脆。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"炸雞炸得非常酥脆。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3074,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::criticism::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The book received favorable ____ from reviewers.","expectedAnswer":"criticism","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The book received favorable ____ from reviewers.","clozeAnswer":"criticism","exampleTranslation":"這本書受到了評論家們的好評。","reference":{"eng":"criticism","kk":"/ˈkrɪtɪsɪzəm/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['批評；評論'], ['（藝術、文學等的）評論；分析'], ['（醫學）診斷']]","chEntries":["批評","評論","分析","診斷"],"practiceMeaning":"這本書受到了評論家們的好評。","analysis":"源自希臘語 'kritēs' (judge)，是 'criticize' 的名詞形式。指「評價」的行為或結果。\n1. 批評；評論：指對某人、某事或某物的評價，通常指出其缺點或錯誤。\n2. （藝術、文學等的）評論；分析：指對作品的風格、內容、結構等進行的專業性評價和分析。\n3. （醫學）診斷：指對病情的判斷。","definition":"1. the act of saying that something is bad or that you disapprove of it; 2. a statement or opinion that expresses disapproval of someone or something; 3. the analysis and judgment of the merits and faults of a literary or artistic work.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The new policy has faced a lot of criticism.\",\n    \"ch\": \"新政策面臨許多批評。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The book received favorable criticism from reviewers.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本書受到了評論家們的好評。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The criticism revealed the underlying disease.\",\n    \"ch\": \"診斷揭示了潛在的疾病。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這本書受到了評論家們的好評。","sourceName":"字彙王、龍騰課本","unitName":"U39、L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5444,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::crucial::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Early diagnosis is ____ for effective treatment.","expectedAnswer":"crucial","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Early diagnosis is ____ for effective treatment.","clozeAnswer":"crucial","exampleTranslation":"早期診斷對於有效治療至關重要。","reference":{"eng":"crucial","kk":"ˈkruːʃl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['至關重要的'], ['關鍵性的'], ['決定性的']]","chEntries":["至關重要的","關鍵性的","決定性的"],"practiceMeaning":"早期診斷對於有效治療至關重要。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 \"crucialis\"，意為\"十字架的\"、\"重要的\"。這個詞與 \"crux\" (關鍵、核心、十字架) 有關，而 \"crux\" 又源自拉丁語 \"crux\"，意為\"十字架\"。構詞上，\"cruc-\" 提供了核心的「十字架」或「關卡」的意象，傳統上十字架是處決或重大事件的象徵，因此引申為「極其重要」或「關鍵」。\"-al\" 是形容詞字尾。 \"Crucial\" 形容某事物「極其重要」到足以決定成敗或結果。","definition":"extremely important or necessary; vital; decisive or critical, especially in the success or failure of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This decision is crucial for the future of the company.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個決定對公司的未來至關重要。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Early diagnosis is crucial for effective treatment.\",\n    \"ch\": \"早期診斷對於有效治療至關重要。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Water is crucial for all forms of life.\",\n    \"ch\": \"水對所有生命形式都至關重要。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"早期診斷對於有效治療至關重要。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3137,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::curse::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He muttered a ____ under his breath.","expectedAnswer":"curse","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He muttered a ____ under his breath.","clozeAnswer":"curse","exampleTranslation":"他壓低聲音嘟囔了一句髒話。","reference":{"eng":"curse","kk":"/kɜːrs/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['詛咒；咒語'], ['（罵人的）髒話；穢語'], ['禍根；災難']]","chEntries":["詛咒","咒語","髒話","穢語","禍根","災難"],"practiceMeaning":"他壓低聲音嘟囔了一句髒話。","analysis":"名詞用法，源自動詞 'curse'。指「詛咒」或「咒語」，即一種超自然的力量或言語，旨在帶來不幸。也指「咒罵」時所說的髒話或侮辱性言語。引申義為「禍根」或「災難」，指某物或某事帶來的持續性不幸或痛苦。","definition":"1. a supernatural power or spell that is thought to cause evil or misfortune; 2. an offensive word or phrase used when someone is angry; 3. the cause of a great deal of trouble or unhappiness.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The ancient artifact was said to carry a powerful curse.\",\n    \"ch\": \"據說那個古老的文物帶有強大的詛咒。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He muttered a curse under his breath.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他壓低聲音嘟囔了一句髒話。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Poverty can be a curse for many families.\",\n    \"ch\": \"貧困對許多家庭來說可能是一場災難。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他壓低聲音嘟囔了一句髒話。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5123,"wordRef":"字彙王::u62::custody::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The police took him into ____ for questioning.","expectedAnswer":"custody","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The police took him into ____ for questioning.","clozeAnswer":"custody","exampleTranslation":"警方將他拘留以進行訊問。","reference":{"eng":"custody","kk":"ˈkʌstədi","tense":"n.","ch":"[['監護權'], ['拘留'], ['保管']]","chEntries":["監護權","拘留","保管"],"practiceMeaning":"警方將他拘留以進行訊問。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 custodia，意為「看守、保護」，來自 custos（守衛者、保護者）。custos 可能來自古拉丁語 *cos-tos，與 *kes-（切、削減）或 *kew-（守護）有關。核心語意是「被看管、被保護的狀態」。在法律語境中，引申為「對子女的監護權」或「對嫌疑人的拘留」。","definition":"the care and control of a child; the state of being kept in prison or in police detention; protection or safekeeping.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The court granted her sole custody of the children.\",\n    \"ch\": \"法院授予她對孩子們的單獨監護權。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police took him into custody for questioning.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警方將他拘留以進行訊問。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"警方將他拘留以進行訊問。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U62"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4406,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u9::dare::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He didn't ____ to look.","expectedAnswer":"dare","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He didn't ____ to look.","clozeAnswer":"dare","exampleTranslation":"他不敢看。","reference":{"eng":"dare","kk":"/dɛər/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['敢於', '膽敢']]","chEntries":["敢於","膽敢"],"practiceMeaning":"他不敢看。","analysis":"詞源自古英語 'darr'，意為「傷害、冒犯」，後來演變為「膽敢、敢於」。常用作情態動詞，後面接原形動詞，尤其是在疑問句和否定句中。","definition":"to have the courage to do something or to do something that is risky or that other people are afraid to do.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"How dare you speak to me like that!\",\n    \"ch\": \"你竟敢這樣對我說話！\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He didn't dare to look.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他不敢看。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他不敢看。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5627,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l7::day-off::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It's been a long week; I'm looking forward to my ____.","expectedAnswer":"day off","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It's been a long week; I'm looking forward to my ____.","clozeAnswer":"day off","exampleTranslation":"這週很漫長；我很期待我的休假日。","reference":{"eng":"day off","kk":"deɪ ɔf","tense":"n.","ch":"[['休假日'], ['休息日']]","chEntries":["休假日","休息日"],"practiceMeaning":"這週很漫長；我很期待我的休假日。","analysis":"此片語由 'day'（天）和 'off'（離開、關閉）組成。'day' 源自古英語 'dæg'，意為「一天」；'off' 源自古英語 'off'，表示「離開、遠離」。構詞學上，這是一個固定的片語，'off' 在此作為一個表示「暫停」、「停止」或「不工作」狀態的副詞或介詞，與 'day' 結合，表示「停止工作的一天」或「不工作的日子」。語意上，它代表一天無需工作、可以休息或做其他事情的時間。","definition":"A day on which one does not have to work.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I'm taking a day off next Friday to go to the dentist.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我下週五要請一天假去看牙醫。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's been a long week; I'm looking forward to my day off.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這週很漫長；我很期待我的休假日。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這週很漫長；我很期待我的休假日。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4552,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::dealer::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The police arrested a major drug ____.","expectedAnswer":"dealer","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The police arrested a major drug ____.","clozeAnswer":"dealer","exampleTranslation":"警方逮捕了一名主要的毒品販子。","reference":{"eng":"dealer","kk":"/ˈdilər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['經銷商', '代理商'], ['（毒品、贓物等的）販子']]","chEntries":["經銷商","代理商","販子"],"practiceMeaning":"警方逮捕了一名主要的毒品販子。","analysis":"由 'deal' (交易、買賣) 加上名詞字尾 '-er' (表示從事某種職業或活動的人) 構成。\n    1. 經銷商、代理商：指合法買賣商品或服務的人。\n    2. 販子：指從事非法交易的人，如毒品販子 'drug dealer'。","definition":"1. a person or company whose occupation is trading in a specified commodity.; 2. a person who sells illicit drugs.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a reputable car dealer.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一位信譽良好的汽車經銷商。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police arrested a major drug dealer.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警方逮捕了一名主要的毒品販子。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"警方逮捕了一名主要的毒品販子。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5323,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l1::debate::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She likes to ____ with her colleagues.","expectedAnswer":"debate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She likes to ____ with her colleagues.","clozeAnswer":"debate","exampleTranslation":"她喜歡與同事爭論。","reference":{"eng":"debate","kk":"dɪˈbeɪt","tense":"v.","ch":"[['辯論'], ['爭論']]","chEntries":["辯論","爭論"],"practiceMeaning":"她喜歡與同事爭論。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 dæbætan，意為「辨別、爭論」，後受古法語 debat「爭吵、戰鬥」影響。構詞上，de- 可能為加強語氣的字首，但在此已與原義無關，或來自拉丁語 dis-（分開），-bat 則與古英語 batan（擊打）相關。其核心語意是透過言語較量來釐清問題或立場。現代的「辯論」和「爭論」都源於此，前者常用於正式場合，後者則較為廣泛。亦可作名詞使用。","definition":"to argue about something, especially in a formal speech or discussion; to argue about an important subject with people who have a different opinion.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We debated the pros and cons of the new policy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們辯論了這項新政策的利弊。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She likes to debate with her colleagues.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她喜歡與同事爭論。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她喜歡與同事爭論。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5124,"wordRef":"字彙王::u62::debris::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The explosion left a trail of ____.","expectedAnswer":"debris","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The explosion left a trail of ____.","clozeAnswer":"debris","exampleTranslation":"爆炸留下了碎片痕跡。","reference":{"eng":"debris","kk":"ˈdeɪbriː","tense":"n.","ch":"[['碎片'], ['殘骸'], ['瓦礫']]","chEntries":["碎片","殘骸","瓦礫"],"practiceMeaning":"爆炸留下了碎片痕跡。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 debriser，意為「打碎、破壞」，由 de-（否定、徹底）+ briser（打碎）組成。briser 來自拉丁語 brisare（打碎），可能是來自 *brevianis（短暫的）。核心語意是「被打破、被破壞後留下的零散物」。","definition":"scattered pieces of something left after it has been destroyed or broken; rubble.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Rescuers searched through the debris for survivors.\",\n    \"ch\": \"救援人員在瓦礫中搜尋倖存者。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The explosion left a trail of debris.\",\n    \"ch\": \"爆炸留下了碎片痕跡。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"爆炸留下了碎片痕跡。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U62"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4591,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::decayed::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He suffered from ____ teeth.","expectedAnswer":"decayed","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He suffered from ____ teeth.","clozeAnswer":"decayed","exampleTranslation":"他的牙齒腐爛了。","reference":{"eng":"decayed","kk":"/dɪˈkeɪd/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['腐爛的', '衰退的']]","chEntries":["腐爛的","衰退的"],"practiceMeaning":"他的牙齒腐爛了。","analysis":"這是動詞 'decay' (腐爛、衰退) 的過去分詞，用作形容詞。 'decay' 源自拉丁語 'decadere'，'de-' (down) 和 'cadere' (to fall - 落下)。\n    1. 腐爛的：指有機物因分解而變得腐敗、發臭。\n    2. 衰退的：指事物（如建築、健康、道德）逐漸惡化、衰敗。","definition":"1. (of organic matter) rot or decompose through the action of bacteria and fungi.; 2. (of something in existence) decline or deteriorate.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The old house looked decayed and abandoned.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座老房子看起來腐朽且被遺棄。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He suffered from decayed teeth.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的牙齒腐爛了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The once-grand theater was now decayed.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座曾經宏偉的劇院如今已衰敗不堪。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他的牙齒腐爛了。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5713,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l9::definite::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There is no ____ proof of his involvement.","expectedAnswer":"definite","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There is no ____ proof of his involvement.","clozeAnswer":"definite","exampleTranslation":"沒有確鑿的證據證明他參與其中。","reference":{"eng":"definite","kk":"ˈdefɪnɪt","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['明確的'], ['確定的'], ['清晰的'], ['一定的']]","chEntries":["明確的","確定的","清晰的","一定的"],"practiceMeaning":"沒有確鑿的證據證明他參與其中。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 definitus（被限定的，明確的），是 definire（定義，限定，闡明）的過去分詞。構詞上，'de-'（向下，完全）+ 'finire'（限定，來自 finis，邊界，結束）。核心語意是「完全被限定、明確，沒有模糊之處」。它描述的是事物界限清楚、意義明確、無可懷疑的狀態。","definition":"clearly stated or explained; able to be seen, heard, or understood clearly; not vague or doubtful; clearly defined or determined.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need a definite answer by Friday.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們週五前需要一個確切的答覆。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There is no definite proof of his involvement.\",\n    \"ch\": \"沒有確鑿的證據證明他參與其中。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"沒有確鑿的證據證明他參與其中。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5712,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l9::definitely::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She ____ knows the answer.","expectedAnswer":"definitely","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She ____ knows the answer.","clozeAnswer":"definitely","exampleTranslation":"她肯定知道答案。","reference":{"eng":"definitely","kk":"ˈdefɪnətli","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['肯定地'], ['無疑地'], ['確實地']]","chEntries":["肯定地","無疑地","確實地"],"practiceMeaning":"她肯定知道答案。","analysis":"此字由形容詞 'definite' 加上副詞化後綴 '-ly' 構成。'definite' 源自拉丁語 definitus（被限定的，明確的），是 definire（定義，限定，闡明）的過去分詞。構詞上，'de-'（向下，完全）+ 'finire'（限定，來自 finis，邊界，結束）。核心語意是「完全被限定、明確」。'-ly' 後綴使形容詞轉化為副詞，表示「以……的方式」。因此，'definitely' 的核心語意是「以一種明確、無疑、毫無疑問的方式」。","definition":"in a way that is clearly defined and clearly stated; without doubt; certainly.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I will definitely be there on time.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我肯定會準時到那裡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She definitely knows the answer.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她肯定知道答案。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她肯定知道答案。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4206,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::definition::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of this photograph is excellent.","expectedAnswer":"definition","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of this photograph is excellent.","clozeAnswer":"definition","exampleTranslation":"這張照片的清晰度非常出色。","reference":{"eng":"definition","kk":"/ˌdefɪˈnɪʃn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['定義；解釋'], ['清晰度；明確性']]","chEntries":["定義","解釋","清晰度","明確性"],"practiceMeaning":"這張照片的清晰度非常出色。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 definitio，'definire'（確定邊界，定義）的派生詞。'de-'（完全）+ 'finire'（結束，限制）。核心是“確定邊界”或“明確”。1. “定義；解釋”指明確事物的意義或性質。2. “清晰度；明確性”指影像、聲音或想法的清晰程度。","definition":"1. a statement of the exact meaning of a word, especially in a dictionary; 2. the clarity or distinctness of something, such as an image or sound.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"What is the definition of 'onomatopoeia'?\",\n    \"ch\": \"'狀聲詞' 的定義是什麼？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The definition of this photograph is excellent.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這張照片的清晰度非常出色。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The exact definition of the term is still debated.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個術語的確切定義仍在爭論中。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這張照片的清晰度非常出色。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4728,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::delay::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Don't ____ your visit to the doctor.","expectedAnswer":"delay","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Don't ____ your visit to the doctor.","clozeAnswer":"delay","exampleTranslation":"不要延遲看醫生的時間。","reference":{"eng":"delay","kk":"/dɪˈleɪ/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['延遲'], ['耽擱']]","chEntries":["延遲","耽擱"],"practiceMeaning":"不要延遲看醫生的時間。","analysis":"動詞形式，指使某事發生得比預期晚，或使某人耽擱。","definition":"1. To make something happen later than expected. 2. To cause someone or something to be late or slow.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The bad weather will delay the construction project.\",\n    \"ch\": \"惡劣的天氣將會延遲這個建築專案。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Don't delay your visit to the doctor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"不要延遲看醫生的時間。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"不要延遲看醫生的時間。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6166,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::democrat::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The senator is a prominent ____.","expectedAnswer":"democrat","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The senator is a prominent ____.","clozeAnswer":"democrat","exampleTranslation":"這位參議員是一位著名的民主黨員。","reference":{"eng":"democrat","kk":"ˈdɛməkræt","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"民主主義者\"  ],  [    \"民主黨員\"  ]]","chEntries":["民主主義者","民主黨員"],"practiceMeaning":"這位參議員是一位著名的民主黨員。","analysis":"此字源自希臘語 dēmokratēs，意為「民主的支持者」，由 dēmos (people) + kratos (power, rule) 組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 dēmos「人民」和 kratos「權力、統治」是其核心語意來源。作為名詞，其核心語義是指信奉或支持民主政治制度的人。在美國，通常特指美國民主黨黨員。","definition":"1. a person who believes in or supports democracy; 2. a member of the Democratic Party.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a lifelong democrat who believes in equality.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一位畢生信奉民主、相信平等的民主主義者。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The senator is 