language.","clozeAnswer":"descriptive","exampleTranslation":"這本書使用了描寫性的語言。","reference":{"eng":"descriptive","kk":"dɪˈskrɪptɪv","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"描述性的\"  ],  [    \"描寫性的\"  ],  [    \"詳盡的\"  ]]","chEntries":["描述性的","描寫性的","詳盡的"],"practiceMeaning":"這本書使用了描寫性的語言。","analysis":"此字由名詞 'description' 加上形容詞字尾 '-ive' 構成。'Description' 源自拉丁語 'descriptio'，由 'de-' (down) 和 'scribere' (to write) 構成，字面意思是「寫下」（細節）。'-ive' 是常見的形容詞字尾，表示「具有……性質的」或「傾向於……」。因此，'descriptive' 指「具有描述性質的」或「用來描述的」。它強調的是對事物特徵、細節進行刻畫和描繪的功能。例如，也可指「詳盡的」敘述。","definition":"1. Serving or seeking to describe, especially by giving full, accurate details.; 2. Relating to or characteristic of description.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The author provided a descriptive account of the journey.\",\n    \"ch\": \"作者提供了關於這次旅程的詳細描述。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The book uses descriptive language.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本書使用了描寫性的語言。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He gave a descriptive report of the event.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對這次事件做了一個詳盡的報告。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The teacher asked for a descriptive essay.\",\n    \"ch\": \"老師要求寫一篇描寫性的文章。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這本書使用了描寫性的語言。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4572,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::desirable::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They live in a ____ neighborhood.","expectedAnswer":"desirable","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They live in a ____ neighborhood.","clozeAnswer":"desirable","exampleTranslation":"他們住在一個令人嚮往的社區。","reference":{"eng":"desirable","kk":"/dɪˈzaɪərəbəl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['令人渴望的', '合意的'], ['有吸引力的', '值得擁有的']]","chEntries":["令人渴望的","合意的","有吸引力的","值得擁有的"],"practiceMeaning":"他們住在一個令人嚮往的社區。","analysis":"由 'desire' (渴望) 加上形容詞字尾 '-able' (表示能夠、值得) 構成。核心概念是「值得渴望」。\n    1. 令人渴望的、合意的：指事物符合人們的願望或需求，非常想要得到。\n    2. 有吸引力的、值得擁有的：指事物在外表、品質或特點上具有吸引力，使人覺得值得追求。","definition":"1. wanted or wished for as a possibility or luxury.; 2. possessing or displaying qualities that give pleasure or satisfaction.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a desirable candidate for the job.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是這份工作的理想人選。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They live in a desirable neighborhood.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們住在一個令人嚮往的社區。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A stable income is a desirable outcome of education.\",\n    \"ch\": \"穩定的收入是教育的一個理想成果。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們住在一個令人嚮往的社區。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5834,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::destructive::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His criticism was ____ rather than constructive.","expectedAnswer":"destructive","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His criticism was ____ rather than constructive.","clozeAnswer":"destructive","exampleTranslation":"他的批評具有破壞性而非建設性。","reference":{"eng":"destructive","kk":"dɪˈstrʌktɪv","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"破壞性的\"  ],  [    \"毀滅性的\"  ],  [    \"有害的\"  ]]","chEntries":["破壞性的","毀滅性的","有害的"],"practiceMeaning":"他的批評具有破壞性而非建設性。","analysis":"此字由拉丁語 'destructivus' 演變而來，是 'destruere' (to destroy) 的派生詞。'Destruere' 由 'de-' (down) 和 'struere' (to build, to pile up) 構成，字面意思是「拆毀」、「推倒」。'-ive' 是常見的形容詞字尾，表示「具有……性質的」。因此，'destructive' 指「具有破壞性質的」或「傾向於破壞」。它描述的是對事物造成損害、毀滅或瓦解的力量或行為。例如，也可指「對個人身心有害的」。","definition":"1. Causing great damage or destruction.; 2. Tending or likely to destroy.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The hurricane caused destructive winds.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這場颶風帶來了毀滅性的強風。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His criticism was destructive rather than constructive.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的批評具有破壞性而非建設性。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The wildfire had a destructive impact on the forest.\",\n    \"ch\": \"野火對森林造成了毀滅性的影響。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Negative thinking can be destructive.\",\n    \"ch\": \"消極思維可能是有害的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他的批評具有破壞性而非建設性。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5419,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::development::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We are monitoring the ____ of the storm.","expectedAnswer":"development","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We are monitoring the ____ of the storm.","clozeAnswer":"development","exampleTranslation":"我們正在監測風暴的發展情況。","reference":{"eng":"development","kk":"dɪˈveləpmənt","tense":"n.","ch":"[['發展'], ['開發'], ['進化'], ['成長'], ['事件']]","chEntries":["發展","開發","進化","成長","事件"],"practiceMeaning":"我們正在監測風暴的發展情況。","analysis":"此字為派生詞，由動詞 \"develop\" 加上名詞化字尾 \"-ment\" 構成。\"develop\" 源自古法語 \"desveloper\"，意為\"展開\"、\"解開\"。其詞源可能與 \"velop\" (包裹、覆蓋) 有關，表示「解開包裹」的動作。構詞上，\"de-\" 是表示「去除」或「相反」的字首（在此處語意為「展開」），\"velop\" 提供核心的「包裹」語意。字尾 \"-ment\" 將動詞的「展開」或「發展」行為轉化為抽象名詞。\"Development\" 指從一個較不複雜、較不成熟的狀態轉變為更複雜、更成熟狀態的過程或結果，涵蓋物理、社會、經濟、個人成長等多個層面。也可指一系列發生的「事件」。","definition":"the process of developing or being developed; a new stage in a process of change or improvement; a significant event or change; the process of growing or causing something to grow or become bigger or more advanced.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The development of new technologies is essential for economic growth.\",\n    \"ch\": \"新技術的發展對經濟增長至關重要。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We are monitoring the development of the storm.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們正在監測風暴的發展情況。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company announced a new product development.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司宣布了一項新產品開發。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們正在監測風暴的發展情況。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3139,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::diagram::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The teacher drew a ____ of the solar system on the blackboard.","expectedAnswer":"diagram","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The teacher drew a ____ of the solar system on the blackboard.","clozeAnswer":"diagram","exampleTranslation":"老師在黑板上畫了太陽系的圖解。","reference":{"eng":"diagram","kk":"/ˈdaɪəˌɡræm/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['圖表；圖樣'], ['（解剖學、工程學等的）圖解']]","chEntries":["圖表","圖樣","圖解"],"practiceMeaning":"老師在黑板上畫了太陽系的圖解。","analysis":"源自希臘語 'diagramma'，意為「圖案，設計」，由 'dia-'（穿過）+ 'graphein'（寫，繪製）組成。'Diagram' 是一種視覺表示，旨在展示事物、結構、原理或過程的組成部分、關係或工作方式。它通常是線條、符號和標籤的組合，用於簡化複雜的概念，使其更易於理解。","definition":"a simplified drawing showing the appearance, structure, or workings of something; a schematic representation.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please refer to the diagram on page 10 for instructions.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請參考第10頁的圖表以獲得說明。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The teacher drew a diagram of the solar system on the blackboard.\",\n    \"ch\": \"老師在黑板上畫了太陽系的圖解。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The manual includes a clear diagram of how to assemble the product.\",\n    \"ch\": \"手冊包含了一個清晰的圖表，說明如何組裝產品。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"老師在黑板上畫了太陽系的圖解。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5345,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l1::disgust::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Her actions were met with ____ by the public.","expectedAnswer":"disgust","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Her actions were met with ____ by the public.","clozeAnswer":"disgust","exampleTranslation":"她的行為引起了公眾的反感。","reference":{"eng":"disgust","kk":"dɪsˈɡʌst","tense":"n.","ch":"[['厭惡'], ['反感']]","chEntries":["厭惡","反感"],"practiceMeaning":"她的行為引起了公眾的反感。","analysis":"此字源自法語 dégoût，由 dé-（否定、反對）+ goût（味道、喜好）組成。原始概念是「失去對某事物的喜好」或「味道不對」。構詞上，dis- 在此是加強語氣的否定字首，表示「徹底地」，gust- 來自 gustus（味道，來自拉丁語 gustare「品嚐」）。核心語意為「極度的不喜歡或厭煩」，通常是對令人不快的事物產生的強烈反感。","definition":"a feeling of revulsion or strong disapproval aroused by something unpleasant or offensive.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The sight of the decaying food filled him with disgust.\",\n    \"ch\": \"腐爛食物的景象讓他感到厭惡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her actions were met with disgust by the public.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的行為引起了公眾的反感。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她的行為引起了公眾的反感。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5041,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::distract::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Loud noises can ____ students during an exam.","expectedAnswer":"distract","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Loud noises can ____ students during an exam.","clozeAnswer":"distract","exampleTranslation":"嘈雜的聲音可能會在考試期間分散學生的注意力。","reference":{"eng":"distract","kk":"dɪˈstrækt","tense":"v.","ch":"[['使分心'], ['分散（注意力）'], ['干擾']]","chEntries":["使分心","分散","干擾"],"practiceMeaning":"嘈雜的聲音可能會在考試期間分散學生的注意力。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語distrahere，由 dis-（分離）+ trahere（拖曳、拉）組成，原意為「將事物拉開、分散」。在英語中，distract 意為「分散某人的注意力，使其無法集中於某事」，語意上直接體現了「將注意力從一處拉開」的詞源含義。OCR 掃描時可能將 's' 誤判為 '5' 或 'f'，或 't' 誤判為 'l'。此處修正為 distract。","definition":"1. to prevent someone from giving their full attention to something; 2. to divert the attention of (someone) from something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Don't distract the driver while he is operating the vehicle.\",\n    \"ch\": \"開車時不要讓司機分心。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Loud noises can distract students during an exam.\",\n    \"ch\": \"嘈雜的聲音可能會在考試期間分散學生的注意力。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"嘈雜的聲音可能會在考試期間分散學生的注意力。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4697,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::dose::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He took a large ____ of medicine.","expectedAnswer":"dose","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He took a large ____ of medicine.","clozeAnswer":"dose","exampleTranslation":"他服用了大劑量的藥物。","reference":{"eng":"dose","kk":"/ˈdoʊs/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['劑量'], ['（一次的）量'], ['（非正式）（尤指治療性的）一份（苦頭、教訓）']]","chEntries":["劑量","量","一份"],"practiceMeaning":"他服用了大劑量的藥物。","analysis":"源自希臘語 *dósis*，意為「給予」、「分量」。核心是指定量的藥物或物質。引申至任何一次性的、一次性的給予，包括非正式地指一次需要承受的苦難或教訓。","definition":"1. A quantity of a medicine or drug taken or prescribed at one time. 2. A quantity of something, especially food or drink, taken at one time. 3. (informal) An unpleasant experience that you have to endure.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The doctor prescribed a daily dose of vitamins.\",\n    \"ch\": \"醫生開了每日維生素劑量。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He took a large dose of medicine.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他服用了大劑量的藥物。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She got her dose of criticism for being late.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她因為遲到而挨了一頓批評。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他服用了大劑量的藥物。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4010,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u3::drag::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The long meeting was a real ____.","expectedAnswer":"drag","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The long meeting was a real ____.","clozeAnswer":"drag","exampleTranslation":"冗長的會議真讓人厭煩。","reference":{"eng":"drag","kk":"/dræɡ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['拖累', '阻礙'], ['（活動、事件）乏味漫長的過程']]","chEntries":["拖累","阻礙","乏味漫長的過程"],"practiceMeaning":"冗長的會議真讓人厭煩。","analysis":"詞源：同上。名詞形式，指拖曳的動作，引申為阻礙，或令人厭煩、緩慢的過程。","definition":"1. something that impedes progress; a hindrance; 2. a tedious or boring process.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The constant paperwork was a drag on our productivity.\",\n    \"ch\": \"不斷的文件工作拖慢了我們的生產力。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The long meeting was a real drag.\",\n    \"ch\": \"冗長的會議真讓人厭煩。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"冗長的會議真讓人厭煩。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4189,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::dramatic::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The film has a ____ plot.","expectedAnswer":"dramatic","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The film has a ____ plot.","clozeAnswer":"dramatic","exampleTranslation":"這部電影有一個戲劇性的情節。","reference":{"eng":"dramatic","kk":"/drəˈmætɪk/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['戲劇性的；引人注目的'], ['（變化、行動等）突然的；劇烈的'], [' the dramatic arts']]","chEntries":["戲劇性的","引人注目的","突然的","劇烈的","the dramatic arts"],"practiceMeaning":"這部電影有一個戲劇性的情節。","analysis":"源自希臘語 dramatikos，與 drama（戲劇）相關。'Drama' 來自 'dran'，意為“做”。核心是與戲劇表演相關的特質。1. “戲劇性的”指像戲劇一樣引人注目、情緒強烈。2. “突然的；劇烈的”強調戲劇中常見的轉折和強烈效果，引申為現實生活中顯著的、巨大的變化。3. “戲劇藝術的”直接指與戲劇相關的。","definition":"1. sudden and striking; 2. relating to drama or the performance of plays; 3. exciting and attention-grabbing.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There were dramatic changes in the weather.\",\n    \"ch\": \"天氣發生了劇烈的變化。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The film has a dramatic plot.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這部電影有一個戲劇性的情節。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He made a dramatic entrance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他做了一個引人注目的登場。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這部電影有一個戲劇性的情節。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U6、L8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4542,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::dumb::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Don't be ____; think before you speak.","expectedAnswer":"dumb","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Don't be ____; think before you speak.","clozeAnswer":"dumb","exampleTranslation":"別那麼笨；說話前先想想。","reference":{"eng":"dumb","kk":"/dʌm/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['啞的', '無法說話的'], ['愚蠢的', '笨拙的'], ['（機器等）不發聲的，靜止的']]","chEntries":["啞的","無法說話的","愚蠢的","笨拙的","不發聲的，靜止的"],"practiceMeaning":"別那麼笨；說話前先想想。","analysis":"源自古英語 'dumb'，意為 'mute, silent' (啞的、沉默的)。\n    1. 啞的：指無法說話的能力。\n    2. 愚蠢的：指缺乏智慧或理解力，是比較粗俗的用法。\n    3. 不發聲的、靜止的：指機器或設備沒有發出聲音，或處於靜止狀態，如 'dumb waiter' (傳菜電梯)，'dumb terminal' (啞終端)。","definition":"1. unable to speak.; 2. stupid; foolish.; 3. (of a device or machine) not having or performing the functions of speech or sound.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was born dumb and mute.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他生來就又啞又不能說話。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Don't be dumb; think before you speak.\",\n    \"ch\": \"別那麼笨；說話前先想想。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The dumb waiter brought the food up.\",\n    \"ch\": \"傳菜電梯把食物送上來了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"別那麼笨；說話前先想想。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3144,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::dynamic::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The political situation is very ____ at the moment.","expectedAnswer":"dynamic","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The political situation is very ____ at the moment.","clozeAnswer":"dynamic","exampleTranslation":"目前的政治局勢變化非常快。","reference":{"eng":"dynamic","kk":"/daɪˈnæmɪk/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['動態的；充滿活力的'], ['（力量、過程）不斷變化的'], ['（人）精力充沛的；活躍的']]","chEntries":["動態的","充滿活力的","不斷變化的","精力充沛的","活躍的"],"practiceMeaning":"目前的政治局勢變化非常快。","analysis":"源自希臘語 'dynamikos'，意為「有力量的，強大的」，與 'dynamis'（力量）有關。'Dynamic' 強調的是能量、活力、變化和持續的活動。它與「static」（靜態的）相對。語意延伸至形容人、系統、過程或事物，這些都具有不斷變化、發展或活躍的特質。","definition":"1. characterized by constant change, activity, or progress; 2. (of a process or system) characterized by energy and enthusiasm; 3. relating to forces or energy.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company has a very dynamic management team.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司擁有一支極具活力的管理團隊。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The political situation is very dynamic at the moment.\",\n    \"ch\": \"目前的政治局勢變化非常快。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her dynamic personality made her popular with everyone.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她充滿活力的個性讓她深受大家喜愛。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"目前的政治局勢變化非常快。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3080,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::dynasty::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The family built a business ____ that lasted for generations.","expectedAnswer":"dynasty","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The family built a business ____ that lasted for generations.","clozeAnswer":"dynasty","exampleTranslation":"這個家族建立了一個延續了幾代的商業王朝。","reference":{"eng":"dynasty","kk":"/ˈdaɪnəsti/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['王朝；朝代'], ['（某一家族或團體的）長時期統治；一系列']]","chEntries":["王朝","朝代","長時期統治","一系列"],"practiceMeaning":"這個家族建立了一個延續了幾代的商業王朝。","analysis":"源自希臘語 'dynasteia' (power, dominion)，'dynastēs' (ruler)。核心意義是「統治」或「權力」。\n1. 王朝；朝代：指由同一家族在一個國家中連續執政的時期。\n2. （某一家族或團體的）長時期統治；一系列：指在某個領域（如商業、政治）由同一家族或團體長期佔據主導地位，或一系列連續發生的事物。","definition":"1. a series of rulers or leaders of the same family; 2. a period of time in which one family rules a country; 3. a succession of rulers from the same family or line.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The Ming Dynasty was known for its porcelain.\",\n    \"ch\": \"明朝以其瓷器聞名。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The family built a business dynasty that lasted for generations.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個家族建立了一個延續了幾代的商業王朝。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個家族建立了一個延續了幾代的商業王朝。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3982,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u3::easy::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He leads an ____ life in retirement.","expectedAnswer":"easy","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He leads an ____ life in retirement.","clozeAnswer":"easy","exampleTranslation":"他退休後過著安逸的生活。","reference":{"eng":"easy","kk":"/ˈiːzi/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['容易的', '輕易的'], ['舒服的', '安逸的'], ['隨和的', '從容的']]","chEntries":["容易的","輕易的","舒服的","安逸的","隨和的","從容的"],"practiceMeaning":"他退休後過著安逸的生活。","analysis":"詞源：古法語 'aisé' (舒適、方便)，源自拉丁文 'a' (在) 和 'sedes' (座位)。引申為「不費力的」、「無憂無慮的」、「輕鬆自在的」。","definition":"1. achieved without great effort; 2. not difficult to do or understand; 3. comfortable and free from worry.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This math problem is too easy for me.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這道數學題對我來說太容易了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He leads an easy life in retirement.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他退休後過著安逸的生活。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has an easy manner.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她舉止從容。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他退休後過著安逸的生活。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3281,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::elastic::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She repaired the trousers with a new piece of ____.","expectedAnswer":"elastic","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She repaired the trousers with a new piece of ____.","clozeAnswer":"elastic","exampleTranslation":"她用一條新的鬆緊帶修好了褲子。","reference":{"eng":"elastic","kk":"/ɪˈlæstɪk/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['鬆緊帶；彈性纖維']]","chEntries":["鬆緊帶","彈性纖維"],"practiceMeaning":"她用一條新的鬆緊帶修好了褲子。","analysis":"名詞形式，指用來提供彈性的材料，如製作衣物腰帶或袖口的鬆緊帶。","definition":"a piece of elastic material, used in waistbands, cuffs, etc.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The elastic in her skirt had lost its stretch.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她裙子裡的鬆緊帶已經失去彈性了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She repaired the trousers with a new piece of elastic.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她用一條新的鬆緊帶修好了褲子。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她用一條新的鬆緊帶修好了褲子。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4043,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::election::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He won the ____ by a landslide.","expectedAnswer":"election","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He won the ____ by a landslide.","clozeAnswer":"election","exampleTranslation":"他在這次選舉中以壓倒性優勢獲勝。","reference":{"eng":"election","kk":"/ɪˈlɛkʃən/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['選舉', '競選']]","chEntries":["選舉","競選"],"practiceMeaning":"他在這次選舉中以壓倒性優勢獲勝。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'electio'，由 'eligere' (to choose, to select) 演變而來。'eligere' 又由 'e-' (out) + 'legere' (to gather, to choose) 構成。核心是「選擇」或「挑選」。因此，'election' 指的是通過投票等方式選出代表或領導人的過程。","definition":"the process of choosing someone for a public office by voting","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"選舉將於下個月舉行。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The election will be held next month.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他在這次選舉中以壓倒性優勢獲勝。\",\n    \"eng\": \"He won the election by a landslide.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他在這次選舉中以壓倒性優勢獲勝。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3284,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::elegance::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of the design impressed everyone.","expectedAnswer":"elegance","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of the design impressed everyone.","clozeAnswer":"elegance","exampleTranslation":"設計的巧妙讓每個人都印象深刻。","reference":{"eng":"elegance","kk":"/ˈɛlɪɡəns/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['優雅；高雅'], ['巧妙；別緻']]","chEntries":["優雅","高雅","巧妙","別緻"],"practiceMeaning":"設計的巧妙讓每個人都印象深刻。","analysis":"由 'elegant' 加上 '-ce' (名詞後綴) 構成。指優雅、高貴、精緻的品質或狀態。也指事物（如設計、解決方案）的巧妙和簡潔。","definition":"the quality of being graceful and stylish in appearance or manner; a pleasingly ingenious and simple quality.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her elegance on the dance floor was captivating.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在舞池中的優雅令人著迷。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The elegance of the design impressed everyone.\",\n    \"ch\": \"設計的巧妙讓每個人都印象深刻。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"設計的巧妙讓每個人都印象深刻。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4367,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::emotional-quotient::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Developing your ____ can improve your relationships.","expectedAnswer":"emotional quotient","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Developing your ____ can improve your relationships.","clozeAnswer":"emotional quotient","exampleTranslation":"培養你的情商可以改善你的人際關係。","reference":{"eng":"emotional quotient","kk":"None","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['情商']]","chEntries":["情商"],"practiceMeaning":"培養你的情商可以改善你的人際關係。","analysis":"此為片語分析。'emotional' (adj.) 源自拉丁語 'emotio'，指『情緒的，感情的』。'quotient' (n.) 源自拉丁語 'quotiens'，意為『多少次』，在此指『指數、測量值』。結合起來，指衡量一個人『情緒管理、自我認知、同理心等能力』的指標，即『情商』（EQ）。","definition":"a measure of a person's ability to be aware of and to control their own emotions, and to understand and deal with the emotions of others","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"High emotional quotient is crucial for leadership.\",\n    \"ch\": \"高情商對於領導力至關重要。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Developing your emotional quotient can improve your relationships.\",\n    \"ch\": \"培養你的情商可以改善你的人際關係。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"培養你的情商可以改善你的人際關係。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4674,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::emperor::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ decreed a new law for his subjects.","expectedAnswer":"emperor","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ decreed a new law for his subjects.","clozeAnswer":"emperor","exampleTranslation":"皇帝為他的臣民頒布了一項新法律。","reference":{"eng":"emperor","kk":"/ˈɛmpərər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['皇帝']]","chEntries":["皇帝"],"practiceMeaning":"皇帝為他的臣民頒布了一項新法律。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 *imperator*，意為「指揮官」、「統帥」，最初指羅馬共和時期擁有絕對權力的軍事首長。後來演變為帝國最高統治者的稱號，具有至高無上的權力。","definition":"1. The ruler of an empire.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The Roman emperor ruled with absolute power.\",\n    \"ch\": \"羅馬皇帝擁有絕對的統治權。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The emperor decreed a new law for his subjects.\",\n    \"ch\": \"皇帝為他的臣民頒布了一項新法律。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"皇帝為他的臣民頒布了一項新法律。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6222,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::endorse::vt","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Many celebrities ____ products in commercials.","expectedAnswer":"endorse","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Many celebrities ____ products in commercials.","clozeAnswer":"endorse","exampleTranslation":"許多名人在廣告中代言產品。","reference":{"eng":"endorse","kk":"ɪnˈdɔrs","tense":"vt.","ch":"[  [    \"認可\"  ],  [    \"贊同\"  ],  [    \"背書\"  ],  [    \"簽署\"  ]]","chEntries":["認可","贊同","背書","簽署"],"practiceMeaning":"許多名人在廣告中代言產品。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 indorare，由 in-（在…上）和 dorare（給予）組成，意為「在背面簽名」。在中古英語演變為 to write on the back，後來引申為「支持；贊同」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作及物動詞時，核心語義是公開表示支持、贊同或認可某人、某事或某產品。在商業和金融領域，也指在票據背面簽字以表示轉讓或擔保。此及物動詞義必須接受詞，例如 endorse a candidate、endorse a product、endorse a check。中文翻譯為「認可；贊同；背書；簽署」。","definition":"1. to declare your public approval of someone or something; 2. to sign your name on the back of a check, bill of exchange, or other document in order to transfer it to someone else or to authorize payment; 3. to recommend a product or service publicly.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The politician was endorsed by the union.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位政治家得到了工會的認可。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Many celebrities endorse products in commercials.\",\n    \"ch\": \"許多名人在廣告中代言產品。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please endorse the check before depositing it.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請在存入支票前簽名背書。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"許多名人在廣告中代言產品。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5447,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::enormous::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They live in an ____ house in the countryside.","expectedAnswer":"enormous","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They live in an ____ house in the countryside.","clozeAnswer":"enormous","exampleTranslation":"他們住在鄉村的一棟巨大的房子裡。","reference":{"eng":"enormous","kk":"ɪˈnɔːrməs","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['巨大的'], ['龐大的'], ['極大的']]","chEntries":["巨大的","龐大的","極大的"],"practiceMeaning":"他們住在鄉村的一棟巨大的房子裡。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 \"enormis\"，原意為\"不規則的\"、\"畸形的\"、\"巨大的\"。它由 \"e-\" (變體，源於 \"ex-\"，表示\"出\"、\"之外\") 和 \"norma\" (規則、標準、準則) 構成。構詞上，\"e-\" 提供了「超出」的語意，\"norma\" 提供了「標準」或「規則」。因此，\"enormous\" 的原始語義是「超出標準、規則的」，引申為「巨大的」、「龐大的」。","definition":"very large in size, quantity, or extent; extremely large; immense.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company made an enormous profit last year.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司去年獲得了巨額利潤。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They live in an enormous house in the countryside.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們住在鄉村的一棟巨大的房子裡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The project faced enormous challenges.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個專案面臨著巨大的挑戰。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們住在鄉村的一棟巨大的房子裡。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3254,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::entertainment::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They offer live ____ every weekend.","expectedAnswer":"entertainment","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They offer live ____ every weekend.","clozeAnswer":"entertainment","exampleTranslation":"他們每週末都提供現場演出。","reference":{"eng":"entertainment","kk":"/ˌɛntərˈteɪnmənt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['娛樂'], ['款待'], ['演出']]","chEntries":["娛樂","款待","演出"],"practiceMeaning":"他們每週末都提供現場演出。","analysis":"源自 'entertain'，指『使人愉快』、『款待』。指提供令人愉悅的活動、表演或內容，以供人們消遣和娛樂。","definition":"the action of providing or being provided with amusement or enjoyment.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The concert was a great source of entertainment.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這場音樂會是極好的娛樂來源。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They offer live entertainment every weekend.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們每週末都提供現場演出。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們每週末都提供現場演出。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U41"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5044,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::exaggeration::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Avoid ____ when describing your skills.","expectedAnswer":"exaggeration","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Avoid ____ when describing your skills.","clozeAnswer":"exaggeration","exampleTranslation":"描述你的技能時，要避免誇張。","reference":{"eng":"exaggeration","kk":"ɪɡˌzædʒəˈreɪʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[['誇張'], ['言過其實']]","chEntries":["誇張","言過其實"],"practiceMeaning":"描述你的技能時，要避免誇張。","analysis":"此字由動詞 exaggerate（誇大）的名詞化而來。exaggerate 源自拉丁語exaggerare，由 ex-（出、極度）+ aggerare（堆積）組成，原意為「堆積起來」。引申為「極度誇大、渲染」。exaggeration 指「誇大事物的行為或結果」，強調將事物描述得比實際情況更嚴重、更重要或更大。OCR 掃描時可能將 'g' 誤判為 'l' 或 'c'，或 'a' 誤判為 'e'。此處修正為 exaggeration。","definition":"the action of representing something as being larger, greater, or more important than it really is.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His account of the event was a clear exaggeration.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對事件的描述明顯是誇大的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Avoid exaggeration when describing your skills.\",\n    \"ch\": \"描述你的技能時，要避免誇張。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"描述你的技能時，要避免誇張。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5586,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::excellence::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She strives for ____ in everything she does.","expectedAnswer":"excellence","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She strives for ____ in everything she does.","clozeAnswer":"excellence","exampleTranslation":"她力求在她所做的一切事情上都做到最好。","reference":{"eng":"excellence","kk":"ˈɛksələns","tense":"n.","ch":"[['卓越'], ['優秀'], ['傑出']]","chEntries":["卓越","優秀","傑出"],"practiceMeaning":"她力求在她所做的一切事情上都做到最好。","analysis":"此字由 \"excellent\" 加上名詞化字尾 \"-ce\" 構成。\"excellent\" 源自拉丁語 \"excellēns\"，是 \"excellere\"（to be eminent, surpass, excel，卓越，超越）的現在分詞。\"excellere\" 由 \"ex-\"（out）和 \"cellere\"（to rise, to be eminent，上升，卓越）組成，意為「突出，超越眾人」。 \"-ce\" 是構成抽象名詞的字尾。因此，\"excellence\" 的核心語義是「卓越的品質、極高的水準或傑出的表現」。它強調的是在某個領域達到的頂尖水準。","definition":"1. The quality of being outstanding or extremely good; 2. Great and distinguished ability or quality.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The restaurant is known for its culinary excellence.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家餐廳以其卓越的烹飪技藝聞名。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She strives for excellence in everything she does.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她力求在她所做的一切事情上都做到最好。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The award recognizes excellence in scientific research.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該獎項旨在表彰科學研究的傑出成就。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她力求在她所做的一切事情上都做到最好。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5536,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l5::execute::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The commander ordered his troops to ____ the attack.","expectedAnswer":"execute","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The commander ordered his troops to ____ the attack.","clozeAnswer":"execute","exampleTranslation":"指揮官命令他的部隊執行攻擊任務。","reference":{"eng":"execute","kk":"ˈeksɪkjuːt","tense":"v.","ch":"[['執行'], ['處決'], [' تنفيذ'], ['實施']]","chEntries":["執行","處決","تنفيذ","實施"],"practiceMeaning":"指揮官命令他的部隊執行攻擊任務。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'exsequi'，由 'ex-' (out) + 'sequi' (to follow) 構成，意為「跟隨到底，執行」。'exsequi' 的本意是「跟隨（送葬隊伍）」，引申為「完成、執行」。構詞上，'ex-' 表「完成」，'secut-' 是 'sequi' 的詞幹，意為「跟隨」。'execute' 的核心語義是「將計劃、命令或判決付諸實施」。這包括法律上的「處決」，以及一般意義上的「執行」某項任務、計劃或程序。在計算機領域，它還指「運行（程式）」。","definition":"to carry out or put into effect (a plan, order, or course of action); to carry out a sentence of death on (a legally condemned person).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government decided to execute the new policy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府決定執行這項新政策。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The commander ordered his troops to execute the attack.\",\n    \"ch\": \"指揮官命令他的部隊執行攻擊任務。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The court ruled that the death penalty would be executed.\",\n    \"ch\": \"法院裁定將執行死刑。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"指揮官命令他的部隊執行攻擊任務。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4397,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u9::exhibition::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The new products will be on ____ next month.","expectedAnswer":"exhibition","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The new products will be on ____ next month.","clozeAnswer":"exhibition","exampleTranslation":"新產品將於下個月展出。","reference":{"eng":"exhibition","kk":"/ˌeksɪˈbɪʃn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['展覽會', '陳列']]","chEntries":["展覽會","陳列"],"practiceMeaning":"新產品將於下個月展出。","analysis":"詞源自拉丁語 'exhibere'，'ex-' (out) + 'habere' (to hold, have)。原意是「展示、呈現」。指公開展示藝術品、商品或資訊的活動。","definition":"an event at which objects of interest are displayed, e.g. works of art or items of antiquarian value; a public display of works of art or items of interest.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The museum is holding an exhibition of Impressionist paintings.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家博物館正在舉辦印象派畫作展。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The new products will be on exhibition next month.\",\n    \"ch\": \"新產品將於下個月展出。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"新產品將於下個月展出。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5295,"wordRef":"字彙王::u63::exile::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He lived in ____ for twenty years.","expectedAnswer":"exile","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He lived in ____ for twenty years.","clozeAnswer":"exile","exampleTranslation":"他流亡了二十年。","reference":{"eng":"exile","kk":"ˈɛkˌsaɪl","tense":"n.","ch":"[['流亡者', '被放逐者'], ['流亡', '放逐']]","chEntries":["流亡者","被放逐者","流亡","放逐"],"practiceMeaning":"他流亡了二十年。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'exilium'（放逐），'exsul'（被放逐者）。'exsul' 本身由 'ex-'（out）和 'sule'（to wander）構成。構詞上，'ex-' 為前綴，'sul-' 為詞根。原始語義為「被逐出家園、四處流浪」。'exile' 作為名詞，指代被放逐的人或被放逐的狀態。作動詞時，表示「迫使某人離開家園」。","definition":"the state of being barred from one's native country, typically for political or punitive reasons; a person who lives in exile.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The political leader became an exile after the revolution.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那位政治領袖在革命後成為了流亡者。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He lived in exile for twenty years.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他流亡了二十年。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他流亡了二十年。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U63"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4153,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::experience::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It was a terrible ____.","expectedAnswer":"experience","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It was a terrible ____.","clozeAnswer":"experience","exampleTranslation":"那是一次糟糕的經歷。","reference":{"eng":"experience","kk":"/ɪkˈspɪəriəns/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['經驗'], ['（經歷過的）事情，體驗']]","chEntries":["經驗","事情，體驗"],"practiceMeaning":"那是一次糟糕的經歷。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 experientia（嘗試，知識），是動詞 experiri（嘗試）的名詞形式。核心概念是「通過嘗試或參與而獲得的知識或技能」。","definition":"1. practical contact with and observation of facts or events; 2. an event or occurrence which leaves an impression on someone","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has ten years of work experience.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她有十年的工作經驗。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was a terrible experience.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那是一次糟糕的經歷。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He gained valuable experience during his internship.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在實習期間獲得了寶貴的經驗。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"那是一次糟糕的經歷。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4068,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::experiment::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Don't ____ with dangerous chemicals.","expectedAnswer":"experiment","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Don't ____ with dangerous chemicals.","clozeAnswer":"experiment","exampleTranslation":"不要實驗危險的化學品。","reference":{"eng":"experiment","kk":"/ɪkˈspɛrɪmɛnt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['進行實驗', '實驗']]","chEntries":["進行實驗","實驗"],"practiceMeaning":"不要實驗危險的化學品。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'experimentum'，由 'experiri' (to try, to test) 構成。作為動詞，指「進行實驗」以求證某事或發現新事物。","definition":"to try out new ideas or methods in order to discover or prove something","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"科學家們正在實驗新藥。\",\n    \"eng\": \"Scientists are experimenting with new drugs.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"不要實驗危險的化學品。\",\n    \"eng\": \"Don't experiment with dangerous chemicals.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"不要實驗危險的化學品。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5783,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::expertise::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Her ____ in marketing is invaluable to our team.","expectedAnswer":"expertise","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Her ____ in marketing is invaluable to our team.","clozeAnswer":"expertise","exampleTranslation":"她在市場營銷方面的專長對我們的團隊來說非常寶貴。","reference":{"eng":"expertise","kk":"ˌɛkspərˈtiz","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"專業知識\"  ],  [    \"專長\"  ],  [    \"技能\"  ]]","chEntries":["專業知識","專長","技能"],"practiceMeaning":"她在市場營銷方面的專長對我們的團隊來說非常寶貴。","analysis":"此字為名詞，源自法語expertise，意為「專業知識；專家判斷」。法語expertise本身源自拉丁語expertus（經驗豐富的；證實過的），是expert（專家）的名詞後綴。expert來自拉丁語expertus，由ex-（外面）+pertus（經過；試驗，與parere「生產；經驗」相關）組成，原意是「經過考驗的；有經驗的」。因此，expertise的核心語義是指「由於長時間的學習、訓練或經驗而獲得的深入知識和高超技能」。語意演變上，從「有經驗」的概念，發展為「所擁有的專門知識和技能」。","definition":"1. expert skill or knowledge in a particular field.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The consultant brought considerable expertise to the project.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位顧問為該項目帶來了豐富的專業知識。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her expertise in marketing is invaluable to our team.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在市場營銷方面的專長對我們的團隊來說非常寶貴。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need someone with technical expertise to solve this problem.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要一位具有技術專長的人來解決這個問題。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她在市場營銷方面的專長對我們的團隊來說非常寶貴。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3082,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::explanation::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He offered no ____ for his absence.","expectedAnswer":"explanation","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He offered no ____ for his absence.","clozeAnswer":"explanation","exampleTranslation":"他沒有對自己的缺席給出任何解釋。","reference":{"eng":"explanation","kk":"/ˌɛkspləˈneɪʃn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['解釋；說明'], ['闡明；辯解']]","chEntries":["解釋","說明","闡明","辯解"],"practiceMeaning":"他沒有對自己的缺席給出任何解釋。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'explanatio'，'explanare' (to make plain, to explain)。是 'explain' 的名詞形式。指「使事物變得清楚」的過程或結果。\n1. 解釋；說明：指對事物的原因、性質、意義等進行闡述，使其易於理解。\n2. 闡明；辯解：指對自己的行為、決定等進行的辯護或說明。","definition":"1. a statement or account that makes something clear; 2. the reasons given for something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The teacher gave a clear explanation of the difficult concept.\",\n    \"ch\": \"老師對這個難懂的概念給出了清晰的解釋。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He offered no explanation for his absence.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他沒有對自己的缺席給出任何解釋。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他沒有對自己的缺席給出任何解釋。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6119,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::explicit::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He made ____ threats.","expectedAnswer":"explicit","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He made ____ threats.","clozeAnswer":"explicit","exampleTranslation":"他做出了明確的威脅。","reference":{"eng":"explicit","kk":"ɪkˈsplɪsɪt","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"明確的\"  ],  [    \"清晰的\"  ],  [    \"詳盡的\"  ],  [    \"直白的\"  ],  [    \"露骨的\"  ]]","chEntries":["明確的","清晰的","詳盡的","直白的","露骨的"],"practiceMeaning":"他做出了明確的威脅。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 explicitus，是 explicāre（展開；解釋）的過去分詞。構詞上，ex- 是字首，表示「出；外面」；plicāre 意為「折疊；纏繞」，因此 explicāre 的核心語義是「展開、攤開、解釋清楚」。explicit 的核心語義是「被完全展開、沒有隱藏」。此形容詞表示清晰、無誤、無含糊或隱藏，直接說明。其語意演變是從具體的「被展開、攤開」到抽象的「清晰、明確、直白」。","definition":"1. stated clearly and in detail, leaving no room for confusion or doubt; 2. showing or describing the act of sex, violence, or illegal activity in a very direct way.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The instructions were explicit.\",\n    \"ch\": \"說明很明確。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He made explicit threats.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他做出了明確的威脅。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The film contained explicit scenes of violence.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這部電影包含露骨的暴力場面。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他做出了明確的威脅。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6169,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::exploit::vt","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need to ____ these new opportunities.","expectedAnswer":"exploit","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need to ____ these new opportunities.","clozeAnswer":"exploit","exampleTranslation":"我們需要利用這些新的機會。","reference":{"eng":"exploit","kk":"ɪkˈsplɔɪt","tense":"vt.","ch":"[  [    \"剝削\"  ],  [    \"利用\"  ],  [    \"開發\"  ],  [    \"發揮\"  ]]","chEntries":["剝削","利用","開發","發揮"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要利用這些新的機會。","analysis":"此字源自法語 exploiter，最終源自拉丁語 explicare「展開、闡明」，後來意義轉變為「利用、發揮」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但其詞源演變是關鍵。作為及物動詞，其核心語義有兩方面：一是指「開發或利用（資源、潛力）」，這部分語義帶有積極或中性的意味；二是指「剝削、不正當地利用（人）」，這部分語義帶有負面含義。詞源的「展開」引申出「發揮」和「利用」的用法，而後者又發展出「剝削」的負面意義。","definition":"1. to make full use of and derive benefit from (a resource); 2. to treat (a person or situation) unfairly in order to benefit from them; 3. to develop or make use of (a resource).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company was accused of exploiting its workers.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司被指控剝削其工人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to exploit these new opportunities.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要利用這些新的機會。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The region's natural resources are being fully exploited.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該地區的自然資源正在被充分開發。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She knows how to exploit every advantage.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她知道如何利用一切優勢。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要利用這些新的機會。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4060,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::expressive::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He gave an ____ sigh.","expectedAnswer":"expressive","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He gave an ____ sigh.","clozeAnswer":"expressive","exampleTranslation":"他發出了一個充滿情感的嘆息。","reference":{"eng":"expressive","kk":"/ɪkˈsprɛsɪv/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['富於表情的', '生動的'], ['表達的', '表示的']]","chEntries":["富於表情的","生動的","表達的","表示的"],"practiceMeaning":"他發出了一個充滿情感的嘆息。","analysis":"源自 'express' (表達)，加上 '-ive' 後綴。'express' 源自拉丁語 'exprimere'，由 'ex-' (out) + 'premere' (to press) 構成，原意是「壓榨出來」。因此，'expressive' 指「能清晰表達情感或思想的」（富於表情的、生動的），或「用於表達的」、「表示的」。","definition":"1. showing or conveying feelings or thoughts; 2. serving to express or represent","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"她的臉表情非常豐富。\",\n    \"eng\": \"Her face is very expressive.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他發出了一個充滿情感的嘆息。\",\n    \"eng\": \"He gave an expressive sigh.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"這音樂極富表現力。\",\n    \"eng\": \"This music is highly expressive.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他發出了一個充滿情感的嘆息。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4096,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::extensive-reading::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He enjoys ____ on various topics.","expectedAnswer":"extensive reading","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He enjoys ____ on various topics.","clozeAnswer":"extensive reading","exampleTranslation":"他喜歡就各種主題進行廣泛閱讀。","reference":{"eng":"extensive reading","kk":"/ɪkˈstɛnsɪv ˈridɪŋ/","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['廣泛閱讀']]","chEntries":["廣泛閱讀"],"practiceMeaning":"他喜歡就各種主題進行廣泛閱讀。","analysis":"'Extensive' (廣泛的) 源自拉丁語 'extensus' (stretched out)，是 'extend' 的過去分詞。'Reading' (閱讀) 是動名詞。'Extensive reading' 指閱讀大量不同主題或類型的材料，以擴展知識和詞彙量。","definition":"reading a large amount of material, often for pleasure or general knowledge, rather than for detailed study","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"廣泛閱讀對於提高語言流暢度至關重要。\",\n    \"eng\": \"Extensive reading is crucial for improving language fluency.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他喜歡就各種主題進行廣泛閱讀。\",\n    \"eng\": \"He enjoys extensive reading on various topics.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他喜歡就各種主題進行廣泛閱讀。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6225,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::exterior::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They held the ceremony in the ____ courtyard.","expectedAnswer":"exterior","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They held the ceremony in the ____ courtyard.","clozeAnswer":"exterior","exampleTranslation":"他們在戶外的庭院裡舉行了儀式。","reference":{"eng":"exterior","kk":"ɪkˈstɪəriər","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"外部的\"  ],  [    \"外面的\"  ],  [    \"戶外的\"  ],  [    \"外在的\"  ]]","chEntries":["外部的","外面的","戶外的","外在的"],"practiceMeaning":"他們在戶外的庭院裡舉行了儀式。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 exterior，是 externus（外面的）的比較級，意為「更外面的」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作形容詞時，指位於某物或某人的外表、外側或外部。可用於描述物理位置、表面、非實質性方面，或與內部相對。中文翻譯為「外部的；外面的；戶外的；外在的」。","definition":"1. relating to the outside surface or structure of something; 2. happening or done outdoors; 3. relating to a person's outward appearance and behavior rather than their thoughts and feelings.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The exterior walls of the building need painting.\",\n    \"ch\": \"建築物的外部牆壁需要粉刷。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They held the ceremony in the exterior courtyard.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們在戶外的庭院裡舉行了儀式。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Exterior damage to the car was minimal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"汽車的外部損壞很小。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們在戶外的庭院裡舉行了儀式。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4440,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u9::extremes::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They lived in ____ of wealth and poverty.","expectedAnswer":"extremes","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They lived in ____ of wealth and poverty.","clozeAnswer":"extremes","exampleTranslation":"他們經歷著極端的貧富差距。","reference":{"eng":"extremes","kk":"/ɪkˈstriːmz/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['極端', '極度']]","chEntries":["極端","極度"],"practiceMeaning":"他們經歷著極端的貧富差距。","analysis":"名詞 'extreme' 的複數形式。指事物的最高或最低程度，或不尋常的、不極端的狀態。","definition":"the greatest or highest degree of something; things that are very different from each other or from what is considered normal.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He always goes to extremes in his opinions.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在觀點上總是走極端。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They lived in extremes of wealth and poverty.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們經歷著極端的貧富差距。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們經歷著極端的貧富差距。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5296,"wordRef":"字彙王::u63::fabulous::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It's a ____ story about a magical kingdom.","expectedAnswer":"fabulous","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It's a ____ story about a magical kingdom.","clozeAnswer":"fabulous","exampleTranslation":"這是一個關於魔法王國的奇幻故事。","reference":{"eng":"fabulous","kk":"ˈfæbjələs","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['極好的', '絕妙的'], ['傳說中的', '虛構的'], ['難以置信的', '驚人的']]","chEntries":["極好的","絕妙的","傳說中的","虛構的","難以置信的","驚人的"],"practiceMeaning":"這是一個關於魔法王國的奇幻故事。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'fabulosus'，意為「傳說中的，寓言式的」，來自 'fabula'（故事，演講，來自 'fari'，意為「說話」）。構詞上，'fabul-' 為詞根，'-ous' 為形容詞後綴。原始語義為「與故事相關的」，引申為「虛構的」、「傳說中的」。在現代英語中，'fabulous' 常用來表示「極好的」、「令人驚嘆的」，這是一種語意上的擴張和褒義化，形容事物好到像傳說中一樣不可思議。","definition":"extraordinarily good or attractive; very pleasing; of or relating to a fable; legendary or mythical.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She looked fabulous in her new dress.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她穿著新洋裝看起來棒極了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's a fabulous story about a magical kingdom.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個關於魔法王國的奇幻故事。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是一個關於魔法王國的奇幻故事。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U63"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3084,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::facial::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"A ____ massage can help relax the skin.","expectedAnswer":"facial","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"A ____ massage can help relax the skin.","clozeAnswer":"facial","exampleTranslation":"臉部按摩有助於放鬆皮膚。","reference":{"eng":"facial","kk":"/ˈfeɪʃl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['臉部的；面部的']]","chEntries":["臉部的","面部的"],"practiceMeaning":"臉部按摩有助於放鬆皮膚。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'facies' (face)。核心意義是「與臉有關」。\n1. 臉部的；面部的：指與臉部相關的、發生在臉上的、或用於臉部的。","definition":"1. relating to the face; 2. on or for the face.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has beautiful facial features.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她有美麗的面部特徵。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A facial massage can help relax the skin.\",\n    \"ch\": \"臉部按摩有助於放鬆皮膚。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"臉部按摩有助於放鬆皮膚。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6075,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::faculty::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She is a professor in the ____ of Arts.","expectedAnswer":"Faculty","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She is a professor in the ____ of Arts.","clozeAnswer":"Faculty","exampleTranslation":"她是文學院的教授。","reference":{"eng":"faculty","kk":"ˈfækəlti","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"系\"  ],  [    \"學院\"  ],  [    \"全體教職員\