tom'（底部）構成。原始語義是指「從最高處到最低處」，描述一個垂直的空間範圍。隨著語意發展，它引申為「徹底地」、「全面地」、「從根本上」的意思，強調檢查、清潔或改變的範圍涵蓋整個對象，不留死角。此處的 OCR 掃描文本可能暗示的是「徹底地」進行某事，例如檢查或清潔。","definition":"completely and thoroughly; from the highest part to the lowest part.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The house was cleaned from top to bottom.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這房子被徹底打掃了一遍。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The inspector examined the engine from top to bottom.\",\n    \"ch\": \"檢查員從上到下檢查了引擎。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"檢查員從上到下檢查了引擎。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4321,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::fuel::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Rising energy prices have put a strain on household ____ budgets.","expectedAnswer":"fuel","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Rising energy prices have put a strain on household ____ budgets.","clozeAnswer":"fuel","exampleTranslation":"能源價格上漲給家庭燃料預算帶來了壓力。","reference":{"eng":"fuel","kk":"/ˈfjuːəl/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['燃料；燃燒物'], ['（助長）動力；食糧']]","chEntries":["燃料","燃燒物","動力","食糧"],"practiceMeaning":"能源價格上漲給家庭燃料預算帶來了壓力。","analysis":"源自古法語 'fouail'，意為 'firewood'，來自拉丁語 'foculus'，意為『壁爐』，最終源自 'focus' (hearth, fire)。最初指用於生火的物質，如木柴。引申為任何可以燃燒產生能量的物質，即『燃料』。另外，它還可以作為比喻，指『提供動力或助長某事（如衝突、爭論）的因素』，相當於『食糧、燃料』。","definition":"a substance such as coal, oil, or gas that is burned to produce heat or energy; something that increases or makes a feeling stronger","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The car runs on unleaded fuel.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這輛車使用無鉛燃料。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Rising energy prices have put a strain on household fuel budgets.\",\n    \"ch\": \"能源價格上漲給家庭燃料預算帶來了壓力。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His angry words only served to fuel the argument.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他憤怒的話語只是火上澆油，加劇了爭論。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"能源價格上漲給家庭燃料預算帶來了壓力。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4610,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::gap::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The generation ____ is a common issue in families.","expectedAnswer":"gap","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The generation ____ is a common issue in families.","clozeAnswer":"gap","exampleTranslation":"世代差距是家庭中常見的問題。","reference":{"eng":"gap","kk":"/ɡæp/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['裂縫'], ['間隙'], ['差距 (意見、年齡、收入等)'], ['缺口']]","chEntries":["裂縫","間隙","差距","缺口"],"practiceMeaning":"世代差距是家庭中常見的問題。","analysis":"源自古挪威語 'gap'，意為「開口、裂縫」。核心概念是兩個事物之間存在的空間或差異。可以是物理上的空間（裂縫、間隙），也可以是抽象的差異（意見、知識、社會經濟地位上的差距）。","definition":"a break or hole in an object or between two things; a difference between two things, especially amounts or qualities.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There is a small gap in the fence.\",\n    \"ch\": \"籬笆上有個小裂縫。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The generation gap is a common issue in families.\",\n    \"ch\": \"世代差距是家庭中常見的問題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to bridge the gap between the rich and the poor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要縮小貧富之間的差距。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"世代差距是家庭中常見的問題。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U16、L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3221,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::gear::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need to ____ our strategy to the current market.","expectedAnswer":"gear","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need to ____ our strategy to the current market.","clozeAnswer":"gear","exampleTranslation":"我們需要使我們的策略適應當前市場。","reference":{"eng":"gear","kk":"/ɡɪər/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['使適應'], ['使適合']]","chEntries":["使適應","使適合"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要使我們的策略適應當前市場。","analysis":"動詞形式，源自名詞『gear』的『設備』、『裝備』意義，引申為『為某目的做好準備』或『使事物與特定情況相匹配』。","definition":"to make or become suitable for a particular purpose or situation.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company is gearing up for the new product launch.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司正在為新產品發布做準備。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to gear our strategy to the current market.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要使我們的策略適應當前市場。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要使我們的策略適應當前市場。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U41"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5592,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l7::gender::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ roles can vary significantly across different cultures.","expectedAnswer":"Gender","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ roles can vary significantly across different cultures.","clozeAnswer":"Gender","exampleTranslation":"社會性別角色在不同文化間可能存在顯著差異。","reference":{"eng":"gender","kk":"ˈdʒɛndər","tense":"n.","ch":"[['性別'], ['社會性別']]","chEntries":["性別","社會性別"],"practiceMeaning":"社會性別角色在不同文化間可能存在顯著差異。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'genus'（種類、血統），經由古法語 'gendre' 傳入英語。在構詞學上，'gender' 主要是作為一個整體詞，但其詞源與表示「種類」或「出生」的概念相關。原始語意指向生物學上的性別，後來在社會科學領域，特別是女性主義和性別研究中，延伸出 '社會性別' (social gender) 的概念，用以區分生理性別 (sex) 與個人或社會建構的性別角色、行為和認同。這種區分是為了強調性別並非全然由生物學決定，而是受到社會文化因素的深刻影響。","definition":"1. The state of being male or female or, in some contexts, neither or both, as determined by biology or social or cultural factors; 2. The classification of nouns and pronouns in some languages as masculine, feminine, or neuter; 3. A social or cultural construct relating to aspects of personality and identity.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The study examined the influence of gender on career choices.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這項研究檢視了性別對職涯選擇的影響。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Gender roles can vary significantly across different cultures.\",\n    \"ch\": \"社會性別角色在不同文化間可能存在顯著差異。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"社會性別角色在不同文化間可能存在顯著差異。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4659,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::generation-gap::idiom","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They discussed the challenges of the ____.","expectedAnswer":"generation gap","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They discussed the challenges of the ____.","clozeAnswer":"generation gap","exampleTranslation":"他們討論了代溝帶來的挑戰。","reference":{"eng":"generation gap","kk":"/ˌdʒenəˈreɪʃən ɡæp/","tense":"idiom","ch":"[['代溝']]","chEntries":["代溝"],"practiceMeaning":"他們討論了代溝帶來的挑戰。","analysis":"此為固定片語。'Generation' (世代) + 'gap' (差距)。指不同世代之間在觀念、價值觀、生活方式、興趣等方面存在的顯著差異和隔閡。","definition":"a difference in attitudes or understanding between older and younger generations.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The generation gap can lead to misunderstandings between parents and children.\",\n    \"ch\": \"代溝可能導致父母與子女之間的誤解。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They discussed the challenges of the generation gap.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們討論了代溝帶來的挑戰。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們討論了代溝帶來的挑戰。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3158,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::generous::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The restaurant served ____ portions of food.","expectedAnswer":"generous","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The restaurant served ____ portions of food.","clozeAnswer":"generous","exampleTranslation":"這家餐廳提供的份量很豐富。","reference":{"eng":"generous","kk":"/ˈdʒɛnərəs/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['慷慨的；大方的'], ['（尺寸、數量等）豐富的，寬大的'], ['（思想、氣度等）寬宏的']]","chEntries":["慷慨的","大方的","豐富的，寬大的","寬宏的"],"practiceMeaning":"這家餐廳提供的份量很豐富。","analysis":"詞源來自拉丁語 'generosus'，意為「出身高貴的，慷慨的」。'Generous' 形容的是一個人樂於給予、分享，並且不吝嗇。其語意也延伸至描述尺寸、份量或提供的東西非常豐富、充足，或是一種寬宏大量、不計較的態度。","definition":"1. showing a readiness to give more of something, especially money, than is strictly necessary or expected; 2. (of a thing) larger or more plentiful than is usual or necessary; 3. showing kindness and openness of mind.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a generous donor to many charities.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是許多慈善機構的慷慨捐助者。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The restaurant served generous portions of food.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家餐廳提供的份量很豐富。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a generous spirit and always tries to help others.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她有著寬宏的 spirit，總是試圖幫助他人。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這家餐廳提供的份量很豐富。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5401,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l2::geographical::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We studied the ____ distribution of the species.","expectedAnswer":"geographical","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We studied the ____ distribution of the species.","clozeAnswer":"geographical","exampleTranslation":"我們研究了該物種的地理分佈。","reference":{"eng":"geographical","kk":"ˌdʒiːəˈɡræfɪkl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['地理的'], ['地理學的']]","chEntries":["地理的","地理學的"],"practiceMeaning":"我們研究了該物種的地理分佈。","analysis":"此字源自名詞 'geography' (地理學)。'-ical' 是常見的形容詞字尾，表示「與……有關的」。'geography' 源自希臘語 geōgraphia，由 'gē' (earth) + 'graphein' (to write) 組成，意為「描寫地球」。核心語意是「與地球的表面、地形、氣候、人口等相關的」。","definition":"1. relating to the physical features of the earth's surface; 2. relating to the study of geography.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The region has unique geographical characteristics.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該地區具有獨特的地理特徵。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We studied the geographical distribution of the species.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們研究了該物種的地理分佈。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們研究了該物種的地理分佈。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4072,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::gesture::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Her ____ of kindness was much appreciated.","expectedAnswer":"gesture","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Her ____ of kindness was much appreciated.","clozeAnswer":"gesture","exampleTranslation":"她善意的姿態非常受讚賞。","reference":{"eng":"gesture","kk":"/ˈdʒɛstʃər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['手勢', '姿態'], ['表示', '姿態（尤指善意的）']]","chEntries":["手勢","姿態","表示"],"practiceMeaning":"她善意的姿態非常受讚賞。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'gestus'，是 'gerere' (to carry, to bear, to do) 的過去分詞。核心是「做」、「執行」。因此，'gesture' 指通過身體動作（尤其是手和頭）來表達意思的「手勢」或「姿態」，也指為了表示某種情感或意圖而做的「表示」或「姿態」。","definition":"1. a movement of your hand or body to express an idea or meaning; 2. an action that you take in order to show your feelings or intentions","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他做了一個歡迎的手勢。\",\n    \"eng\": \"He made a welcoming gesture.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"她善意的姿態非常受讚賞。\",\n    \"eng\": \"Her gesture of kindness was much appreciated.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他舉起手，表示投降。\",\n    \"eng\": \"He raised his hand in a gesture of surrender.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她善意的姿態非常受讚賞。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3295,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::gifted::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The program supports ____ children in their education.","expectedAnswer":"gifted","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The program supports ____ children in their education.","clozeAnswer":"gifted","exampleTranslation":"該計畫支持資優兒童的教育。","reference":{"eng":"gifted","kk":"/ˈɡɪftɪd/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['有天賦的；才華橫溢的']]","chEntries":["有天賦的","才華橫溢的"],"practiceMeaning":"該計畫支持資優兒童的教育。","analysis":"由 'gift' (天賦) 加上過去分詞形式的 '-ed' 後綴構成，表示「被賦予了天賦」。指在某方面擁有特別才能或技能的人。","definition":"having or showing exceptional talent or natural ability.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a gifted musician at a young age.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是一位年紀輕輕就有天賦的音樂家。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The program supports gifted children in their education.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該計畫支持資優兒童的教育。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該計畫支持資優兒童的教育。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4045,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::governor::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He was appointed ____ of the new territory.","expectedAnswer":"governor","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He was appointed ____ of the new territory.","clozeAnswer":"governor","exampleTranslation":"他被任命為新地區的總督。","reference":{"eng":"governor","kk":"/ˈɡʌvərnər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['州長', '總督'], ['主管', '管理者']]","chEntries":["州長","總督","主管","管理者"],"practiceMeaning":"他被任命為新地區的總督。","analysis":"源自古法語 'governour'，來自拉丁語 'gubernator'，意為「舵手」、「領航員」，進而引申為「管理者」、「統治者」。'gubernator' 本身來自希臘語 'kybernetes' (steersman, governor)。核心是「控制」和「引導」方向。因此，指負責管理或統治一個地區或機構的官員。","definition":"1. the elected head of a U.S. state; 2. a person appointed to govern a colony or province; 3. a person who is in charge of an organization or a part of it","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"州長簽署了新法案，使其成為法律。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The governor signed the new bill into law.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他被任命為新地區的總督。\",\n    \"eng\": \"He was appointed governor of the new territory.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"中央銀行行長宣布了新政策。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The governor of the central bank announced new policies.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他被任命為新地區的總督。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3088,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::graceful::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She has a ____ way of speaking.","expectedAnswer":"graceful","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She has a ____ way of speaking.","clozeAnswer":"graceful","exampleTranslation":"她的說話方式很優雅。","reference":{"eng":"graceful","kk":"/ˈɡreɪsfl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['優雅的；雅緻的'], ['（動作、姿態）好看的；得體的']]","chEntries":["優雅的","雅緻的","好看的","得體的"],"practiceMeaning":"她的說話方式很優雅。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'gratia' (grace, favor)，經由古法語 'grace' 演變而來。核心意義是「優美」、「迷人」。\n1. 優雅的；雅緻的：指姿態、舉止、風格等方面具有美感，令人賞心悅目。\n2. （動作、姿態）好看的；得體的：形容動作自然、協調，給人以美感和得體之感。","definition":"1. elegant and stylish in form or movement; 2. pleasing and attractive.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The ballerina performed a graceful dance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位芭蕾舞演員跳了一支優雅的舞蹈。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a graceful way of speaking.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的說話方式很優雅。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她的說話方式很優雅。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3160,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::graph::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Please plot the data points on the ____.","expectedAnswer":"graph","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Please plot the data points on the ____.","clozeAnswer":"graph","exampleTranslation":"請將數據點繪製在這張圖上。","reference":{"eng":"graph","kk":"/ɡræf/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['圖；圖表； graf']]","chEntries":["圖","圖表","graf"],"practiceMeaning":"請將數據點繪製在這張圖上。","analysis":"源自希臘語 'graphein'，意為「書寫，繪製」。'Graph' 是一種用線條、點或其他符號在平面上表示數據、關係或統計結果的視覺工具。它幫助我們理解數據的趨勢、比較不同的數值或展示變數之間的關係。常見的有折線圖、長條圖、圓形圖等。","definition":"a diagram showing the relation between two or more variables, typically of the form of a curve or a series of points lying on a grid.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The graph shows a steady increase in sales over the past year.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這張圖表顯示了過去一年銷售額的穩定增長。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please plot the data points on the graph.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請將數據點繪製在這張圖上。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The bar graph clearly illustrates the comparison between the two groups.\",\n    \"ch\": \"長條圖清晰地展示了兩組之間的比較。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"請將數據點繪製在這張圖上。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5787,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::grip::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The book has a strong ____ on the imagination.","expectedAnswer":"grip","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The book has a strong ____ on the imagination.","clozeAnswer":"grip","exampleTranslation":"這本書對想像力有很強的吸引力。","reference":{"eng":"grip","kk":"ɡrɪp","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"緊握\"  ],  [    \"抓牢\"  ],  [    \"控制\"  ],  [    \"吸引力\"  ],  [    \"握把\"  ]]","chEntries":["緊握","抓牢","控制","吸引力","握把"],"practiceMeaning":"這本書對想像力有很強的吸引力。","analysis":"此字為名詞，與動詞同源，源自中古英語gripen。核心語義是指「用力抓住或握緊的動作或狀態」，或「被抓住的物體」。引申為「控制」、「掌握」，以及「對人產生的強烈吸引力或影響力」。此外，也可指工具或武器上的「握把」。語意演變上，從「抓握」的動作，發展出「控制」、「吸引力」等抽象意義，以及「握把」這類具體名詞。","definition":"1. a firm hold or grasp; 2. control or power over someone or something; 3. the ability to attract and hold people's attention or interest; 4. the part of the handle of a tool or weapon that is held in the hand.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He lost his grip on the rope and fell.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他鬆開了繩索的抓握，掉了下去。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The book has a strong grip on the imagination.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本書對想像力有很強的吸引力。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The pen has a comfortable grip.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這支筆有一個舒適的握把。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這本書對想像力有很強的吸引力。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5127,"wordRef":"字彙王::u62::gross::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His ____ lack of manners was offensive.","expectedAnswer":"gross","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His ____ lack of manners was offensive.","clozeAnswer":"gross","exampleTranslation":"他極其粗魯的無禮行為令人反感。","reference":{"eng":"gross","kk":"ɡroʊs","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['總的'], ['毛的'], ['嚴重的'], ['令人噁心的']]","chEntries":["總的","毛的","嚴重的","令人噁心的"],"practiceMeaning":"他極其粗魯的無禮行為令人反感。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 gros，意為「大、肥胖、總的」，來自拉丁語 grossus（粗大的）。核心語意是「大的、不精細的」。引申出「總收入」（毛收入，gross income）、「總重量」（毛重，gross weight）等含義。在另一語義發展線上，gross 也引申為「極端的、嚴重的」（gross negligence）以及「令人噁心的、非常討厭的」（gross behavior）。","definition":"without any deductions; total; extremely unpleasant or disgusting; very bad or serious.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company reported a gross profit of $1 million.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司報告了 100 萬美元的毛利。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His gross lack of manners was offensive.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他極其粗魯的無禮行為令人反感。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The smell was absolutely gross.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這氣味真是太噁心了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他極其粗魯的無禮行為令人反感。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U62"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5356,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l1::guilt::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The evidence confirmed his ____.","expectedAnswer":"guilt","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The evidence confirmed his ____.","clozeAnswer":"guilt","exampleTranslation":"證據證實了他的罪責。","reference":{"eng":"guilt","kk":"ɡɪlt","tense":"n.","ch":"[['罪惡感'], ['內疚'], ['罪責']]","chEntries":["罪惡感","內疚","罪責"],"practiceMeaning":"證據證實了他的罪責。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 gylt，來自原始日耳曼語 *gulthiz，可能與原始印歐語 *ghel-（獎賞、償還）有關，但語意演變複雜。核心概念是「欠下的債」或「應受的懲罰」。構詞上，gult- 是字根，表示「債務、應受」。原始語意指向「因行為不當而應受的懲罰或責任」。現代語意主要指「犯罪的行為」或「知道自己做錯事而產生的內疚感」。","definition":"the fact of having committed a specified offence or crime; a feeling of having done something wrong or failed to do something that one can properly be blamed for.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He felt a deep sense of guilt for his actions.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對自己的行為感到深深的內疚。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The evidence confirmed his guilt.\",\n    \"ch\": \"證據證實了他的罪責。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"證據證實了他的罪責。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5357,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l1::guilty::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He looked ____ when the teacher asked him who broke the window.","expectedAnswer":"guilty","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He looked ____ when the teacher asked him who broke the window.","clozeAnswer":"guilty","exampleTranslation":"當老師問是誰打破窗戶時，他顯得很內疚。","reference":{"eng":"guilty","kk":"ˈɡɪlti","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['有罪的'], ['內疚的'], ['罪惡的']]","chEntries":["有罪的","內疚的","罪惡的"],"practiceMeaning":"當老師問是誰打破窗戶時，他顯得很內疚。","analysis":"此字由名詞 guilt 加上形容詞字尾 -y 構成。guilt 源自古英語 gylt，意為「罪惡感、罪責」。-y 是常見的形容詞字尾，表示「充滿……的」。因此，guilty 的核心語意為「充滿罪惡感或罪責的」，引申為「已被判定有罪」或「感覺自己做錯事」。","definition":"responsible for or legally liable for a criminal offense; feeling or showing guilt.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The jury found the defendant guilty.\",\n    \"ch\": \"陪審團裁定被告有罪。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He looked guilty when the teacher asked him who broke the window.\",\n    \"ch\": \"當老師問是誰打破窗戶時，他顯得很內疚。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"當老師問是誰打破窗戶時，他顯得很內疚。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4150,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::handkerchief::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She blew her nose with a ____.","expectedAnswer":"handkerchief","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She blew her nose with a ____.","clozeAnswer":"handkerchief","exampleTranslation":"她用紙巾擤了鼻涕。","reference":{"eng":"handkerchief","kk":"/ˈhæŋkərtʃɪf/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['手帕']]","chEntries":["手帕"],"practiceMeaning":"她用紙巾擤了鼻涕。","analysis":"由 hand（手）+ kerchief（頭巾，源自古法語 couvrechef，意為「遮蓋頭部」）組成。最初指放在手裡或頭上的布，後來特指擦拭用的小方巾。","definition":"a piece of cloth for wiping the nose or tears or used by women to cover the head","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He took out a handkerchief to wipe his brow.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他拿出了一塊手帕擦了擦額頭。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She blew her nose with a handkerchief.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她用紙巾擤了鼻涕。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她用紙巾擤了鼻涕。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5718,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l9::have-high-hopes::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The parents ____ for their child's future.","expectedAnswer":"have high hopes","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The parents ____ for their child's future.","clozeAnswer":"have high hopes","exampleTranslation":"父母對他們孩子的未來抱有很高的期望。","reference":{"eng":"have high hopes","kk":"hæv haɪ hoʊps","tense":"v.","ch":"[['寄予厚望'], ['抱有很高期望']]","chEntries":["寄予厚望","抱有很高期望"],"practiceMeaning":"父母對他們孩子的未來抱有很高的期望。","analysis":"這是一個固定片語。'have' 源自古英語 habban（擁有）。'high' 源自古英語 hēah（高的）。'hopes' 源自古英語 hopa（希望）。字面意思是「擁有高的希望」。引申為「對某人或某事抱有非常積極的預期，期望會成功或取得好結果」。核心語意是「對未來有非常樂觀的預測」。","definition":"to expect that something good will happen; to have great expectations.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We have high hopes for the success of this project.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們對這個計畫的成功寄予厚望。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The parents have high hopes for their child's future.\",\n    \"ch\": \"父母對他們孩子的未來抱有很高的期望。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"父母對他們孩子的未來抱有很高的期望。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5299,"wordRef":"字彙王::u63::hazard::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The icy roads created a traffic ____.","expectedAnswer":"hazard","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The icy roads created a traffic ____.","clozeAnswer":"hazard","exampleTranslation":"結冰的路面造成了交通危險。","reference":{"eng":"hazard","kk":"ˈhæzərd","tense":"n.","ch":"[['危險', '風險'], ['（可能造成危害的）危險因素', '威脅']]","chEntries":["危險","風險","危險因素","威脅"],"practiceMeaning":"結冰的路面造成了交通危險。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 'hasart'（賭注，尤其指骰子遊戲中的風險），可能與阿拉伯語 'al-zahr'（骰子）有關。最初意為「偶然發生的事，風險」，尤其是在遊戲中。核心語意是「不可預測的、可能帶來損失或傷害的事物」。在現代英語中，'hazard' 廣泛指代任何可能造成傷害、損失或不良後果的潛在危險。作動詞時，意為「冒險」，但較少用。","definition":"a danger or risk; a source of danger.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Smoking is a health hazard.\",\n    \"ch\": \"吸煙對健康是一種危險。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The icy roads created a traffic hazard.\",\n    \"ch\": \"結冰的路面造成了交通危險。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"結冰的路面造成了交通危險。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U63"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5788,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::hence::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He broke his leg, ____ he cannot attend the game.","expectedAnswer":"hence","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He broke his leg, ____ he cannot attend the game.","clozeAnswer":"hence","exampleTranslation":"他摔斷了腿，所以他不能參加比賽。","reference":{"eng":"hence","kk":"hɛns","tense":"adv.","ch":"[  [    \"因此\"  ],  [    \"由此\"  ],  [    \"所以\"  ]]","chEntries":["因此","由此","所以"],"practiceMeaning":"他摔斷了腿，所以他不能參加比賽。","analysis":"此字為副詞，源自古英語hider+efnes，意為「在此處+如同」，後演變為「由此；因此」。其詞源可追溯至原始日耳曼語\\\\*hithran（這裡）+ \\\\*efn-（相等）。它是一個連接詞，用於引出結果或推論。核心語義是用來連接原因與結果，表明後者是前者的必然結果。語意演變上，從「因此處」或「由這點」引申為「基於此原因」。","definition":"1. used to introduce the result of something that has been mentioned; 2. from this time; from now.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The weather forecast predicted rain, hence the event was cancelled.\",\n    \"ch\": \"天氣預報預測有雨，因此活動被取消了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He broke his leg, hence he cannot attend the game.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他摔斷了腿，所以他不能參加比賽。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is the main reason; hence, we must act now.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是主要原因；因此，我們必須現在採取行動。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他摔斷了腿，所以他不能參加比賽。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6077,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::hockey::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Field ____ is a popular sport in many countries.","expectedAnswer":"hockey","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Field ____ is a popular sport in many countries.","clozeAnswer":"hockey","exampleTranslation":"曲棍球在許多國家是一種受歡迎的運動。","reference":{"eng":"hockey","kk":"ˈhɔki","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"曲棍球\"  ]]","chEntries":["曲棍球"],"practiceMeaning":"曲棍球在許多國家是一種受歡迎的運動。","analysis":"此字的詞源不確定，可能源自古法語 hoquet（牧羊杖），或與某種詞頭相關，表示「棍棒」。核心語義是指一種使用棍棒擊球的運動。最常見的是指冰球（ice hockey）或草地曲棍球（field hockey）。","definition":"a game played on ice or a grass field between two teams of players who try to score points by hitting a puck or ball into the opponents' goal with a stick.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He plays ice hockey for the local team.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他為當地隊伍打冰球。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Field hockey is a popular sport in many countries.\",\n    \"ch\": \"曲棍球在許多國家是一種受歡迎的運動。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The children were playing hockey in the park.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子們正在公園裡玩曲棍球。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"曲棍球在許多國家是一種受歡迎的運動。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4240,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::hollow::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He felt a ____ ache in his chest.","expectedAnswer":"hollow","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He felt a ____ ache in his chest.","clozeAnswer":"hollow","exampleTranslation":"他感到胸中有一種空虛的疼痛。","reference":{"eng":"hollow","kk":"/ˈhɑːloʊ/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['中空的'], ['空心的']]","chEntries":["中空的","空心的"],"practiceMeaning":"他感到胸中有一種空虛的疼痛。","analysis":"源自古英語 'holh'，意為「洞、孔」。與「空」的物理狀態緊密相關。此詞的基本概念是「內部有空間」。","definition":"having a hole or empty space inside","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The tree trunk was hollow and provided shelter for birds.\",\n    \"ch\": \"樹幹是中空的，為鳥類提供了庇護所。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He felt a hollow ache in his chest.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他感到胸中有一種空虛的疼痛。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他感到胸中有一種空虛的疼痛。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3876,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::homesick::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The child was ____ and wanted to go back home.","expectedAnswer":"homesick","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The child was ____ and wanted to go back home.","clozeAnswer":"homesick","exampleTranslation":"孩子想家了，想要回家。","reference":{"eng":"homesick","kk":"/ˈhoʊmˌsɪk/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['想家的', '思鄉的']]","chEntries":["想家的","思鄉的"],"practiceMeaning":"孩子想家了，想要回家。","analysis":"由 'home' (家) 和 'sick' (生病的) 組成。核心是「因思念家而感到不適」。形容因離家太久而產生的鄉愁或思念之情。","definition":"suffering from depression caused by longing for one's home.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"After a month abroad, she started to feel homesick.\",\n    \"ch\": \"在國外一個月後，她開始感到想家。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The child was homesick and wanted to go back home.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子想家了，想要回家。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"孩子想家了，想要回家。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6079,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::hormone::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Adrenaline is a ____ that is released in response to stress.","expectedAnswer":"hormone","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Adrenaline is a ____ that is released in response to stress.","clozeAnswer":"hormone","exampleTranslation":"腎上腺素是一種壓力荷爾蒙。","reference":{"eng":"hormone","kk":"ˈhɔrmon","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"荷爾蒙\"  ],  [    \"激素\"  ]]","chEntries":["荷爾蒙","激素"],"practiceMeaning":"腎上腺素是一種壓力荷爾蒙。","analysis":"此字源自希臘語 horman，意為「激動，刺激，使……開始」，由 hormē（衝動，推動）演變而來。Hormone 指的是由生物體內的內分泌腺體分泌，並通過血液輸送到身體其他部位，對身體功能產生調節作用的化學物質。核心語義是「引發生理反應的化學信號」。","definition":"a regulatory substance produced in an organism and transported in the blood or other fluid to distant cells or organs to regulate physiology or behavior.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The doctor explained the role of hormones in the body.\",\n    \"ch\": \"醫生解釋了荷爾蒙在人體中的作用。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Adrenaline is a hormone that is released in response to stress.\",\n    \"ch\": \"腎上腺素是一種壓力荷爾蒙。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Hormone levels can fluctuate during different life stages.\",\n    \"ch\": \"荷爾蒙水平在不同生命階段可能會波動。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"腎上腺素是一種壓力荷爾蒙。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4620,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::horror::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She looked at the scene with ____.","expectedAnswer":"horror","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She looked at the scene with ____.","clozeAnswer":"horror","exampleTranslation":"她驚恐地看著眼前的景象。","reference":{"eng":"horror","kk":"/ˈhɔːrər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['恐怖'], ['驚恐'], ['恐懼'], ['（電影、文學作品）恐怖片']]","chEntries":["恐怖","驚恐","恐懼","恐怖片"],"practiceMeaning":"她驚恐地看著眼前的景象。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'horrere' (感到恐懼、戰慄)。核心是強烈的恐懼、厭惡或厭惡感，通常是由於看到或想到可怕、令人不安的事物。其名詞形式 'horror' 指這種感覺本身，也指引起這種感覺的事物，如恐怖電影。","definition":"an intense feeling of fear, shock, or disgust; something that causes such a feeling.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The movie was full of horror and suspense.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這部電影充滿了恐怖和懸疑。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She looked at the scene with horror.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她驚恐地看著眼前的景象。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He's a fan of horror novels.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是恐怖小說迷。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她驚恐地看著眼前的景象。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4720,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::humor::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The comedian's ____ was a bit dark.","expectedAnswer":"humor","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The comedian's ____ was a bit dark.","clozeAnswer":"humor","exampleTranslation":"這位喜劇演員的幽默風格有點暗黑。","reference":{"eng":"humor","kk":"/ˈhjumər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['幽默感'], ['趣味']]","chEntries":["幽默感","趣味"],"practiceMeaning":"這位喜劇演員的幽默風格有點暗黑。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 *humor*，最初指體內的液體（體液學說）。後演變為指人的脾氣、性情，再到指引起笑聲或愉悅感的特質，即幽默感。","definition":"1. The quality of being amusing or comic, especially as expressed in literature or speech. 2. A person's mood or disposition.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has a great sense of humor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他很有幽默感。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The comedian's humor was a bit dark.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位喜劇演員的幽默風格有點暗黑。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這位喜劇演員的幽默風格有點暗黑。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5388,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l2::hygiene::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Food ____ standards must be strictly followed.","expectedAnswer":"hygiene","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Food ____ standards must be strictly followed.","clozeAnswer":"hygiene","exampleTranslation":"食品衛生標準必須嚴格遵守。","reference":{"eng":"hygiene","kk":"ˈhaɪdʒiːn","tense":"n.","ch":"[['衛生'], ['（個人）清潔']]","chEntries":["衛生","清潔"],"practiceMeaning":"食品衛生標準必須嚴格遵守。","analysis":"此字源自希臘語 Hygieia (健康女神的名字)，引申出 'hygienic' (衛生的)。'-e' 是名詞結尾。核心語意是「與健康和清潔相關的狀態或實踐」。'Hygiene' 指維持健康和預防疾病所需的衛生習慣和條件，包括個人清潔、環境清潔等。","definition":"Conditions or practices conducive to maintaining health and preventing disease, especially through cleanliness.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Good personal hygiene is important to prevent the spread of germs.\",\n    \"ch\": \"良好的個人衛生對於防止細菌傳播很重要。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Food hygiene standards must be strictly followed.\",\n    \"ch\": \"食品衛生標準必須嚴格遵守。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"食品衛生標準必須嚴格遵守。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4512,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::idea::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"I have no ____ what you are talking about.","expectedAnswer":"idea","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"I have no ____ what you are talking about.","clozeAnswer":"idea","exampleTranslation":"我完全不知道你在說什麼。","reference":{"eng":"idea","kk":"/aɪˈdiːə/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['主意'], ['想法'], ['概念']]","chEntries":["主意","想法","概念"],"practiceMeaning":"我完全不知道你在說什麼。","analysis":"源自希臘語 idea，意為「形狀」、「外觀」、「理念」。核心語意是「心智中產生的概念或圖像」。引申為「想法」、「概念」、「意圖」。","definition":"1. A thought or suggestion as to a possible course of action; 2. A conception of or belief about something; 3. A plan or suggestion.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"That's a great idea!\",\n    \"ch\": \"這真是個好主意！\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I have no idea what you are talking about.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我完全不知道你在說什麼。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The idea of democracy spread rapidly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"民主的概念迅速傳播。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我完全不知道你在說什麼。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5418,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::identity::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The passport confirms the traveler's ____.","expectedAnswer":"identity","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The passport confirms the traveler's ____.","clozeAnswer":"identity","exampleTranslation":"護照證實了旅客的身份。","reference":{"eng":"identity","kk":"aɪˈdentəti","tense":"n.","ch":"[['身份'], ['身分'], ['認同'], ['特性'], ['同一性']]","chEntries":["身份","身分","認同","特性","同一性"],"practiceMeaning":"護照證實了旅客的身份。","analysis":"此字由形容詞 \"identical\" 加上名詞化字尾 \"-ity\" 構成。\"identical\" 源自拉丁語 \"identicus\"，其詞源為 \"idem\"，意為\"相同\"。構詞上，\"ident-\" 提供了核心的\"相同\"或\"同一\"語意，\"-ical\" 是形容詞字尾，將「相同」的概念描述為一種屬性。而字尾 \"-ity\" 則將形容詞的「相同性」或「同一性」轉化為抽象名詞，形成 \"identity\"。因此，\"identity\" 首先表示「同一性」，即事物是其本身且與其他事物不同；進而引申為「身份」或「身分」，指一個人或物之所以是其自身、其獨特性；也引申為「認同」，即與某人、某群體或某物產生連結感和歸屬感。","definition":"the fact of being who or what a person or thing is; the characteristics and qualities that form who a person is and make them different from others; the state of being the same; the condition of being oneself and not someone else; a sense of self; sameness.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He struggled to find his identity after the accident.\",\n    \"ch\": \"事故後他努力尋找自己的身份認同。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The passport confirms the traveler's identity.\",\n    \"ch\": \"護照證實了旅客的身份。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Cultural identity plays a big role in shaping our values.\",\n    \"ch\": \"文化認同在塑造我們的價值觀方面扮演著重要角色。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"護照證實了旅客的身份。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3311,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::impartial::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"A good teacher should be ____ to all students.","expectedAnswer":"impartial","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"A good teacher should be ____ to all students.","clozeAnswer":"impartial","exampleTranslation":"一個好老師應該對所有學生都一視同仁。","reference":{"eng":"impartial","kk":"/ɪmˈpɑːrʃl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['公正的；不偏不倚的'], ['無私的']]","chEntries":["公正的","不偏不倚的","無私的"],"practiceMeaning":"一個好老師應該對所有學生都一視同仁。","analysis":"由 'im-' (否定前綴) + 'partial' (偏心的) 組成。與 'partial' 相反，指不偏向任何一方，公平地對待。","definition":"treating all rivals or disputants equally; fair and just.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The jury must remain impartial throughout the trial.\",\n    \"ch\": \"陪審團在整個審判過程中必須保持公正。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A good teacher should be impartial to all students.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一個好老師應該對所有學生都一視同仁。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"一個好老師應該對所有學生都一視同仁。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5325,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l1::imprisonment::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The court ordered his ____.","expectedAnswer":"imprisonment","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The court ordered his ____.","clozeAnswer":"imprisonment","exampleTranslation":"法院判處他監禁。","reference":{"eng":"imprisonment","kk":"ɪmˈprɪzənmənt","tense":"n.","ch":"[['監禁'], ['囚禁']]","chEntries":["監禁","囚禁"],"practiceMeaning":"法院判處他監禁。","analysis":"此字由動詞 imprison 加上名詞字尾 -ment 構成。imprison 源自古法語 enprisoner，由 in-（進入）+ pris（被抓、被捕，來自拉丁語 prehendere「抓住」）+ -on（動詞字尾）組成，字面意思為「使被捕、被關入」。-ment 是常見的名詞化字尾，表示狀態、動作或結果。因此，imprisonment 的核心語意是「被監禁的狀態或行為」。","definition":"the state of being imprisoned; the action of imprisoning someone.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He served five years of imprisonment for his crimes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他因罪行服刑五年監禁。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The court ordered his imprisonment.\",\n    \"ch\": \"法院判處他監禁。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"法院判處他監禁。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5588,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::in-large-part::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____, the changes were driven by new technology.","expectedAnswer":"In large part","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____, the changes were driven by new technology.","clozeAnswer":"In large part","exampleTranslation":"這些改變主要由新技術推動。","reference":{"eng":"in large part","kk":"ɪn lɑrdʒ pɑrt","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['在很大程度上'], ['主要地']]","chEntries":["在很大程度上","主要地"],"practiceMeaning":"這些改變主要由新技術推動。","analysis":"此片語由介詞 \"in\"，形容詞 \"large\"（大的），名詞 \"part\"（部分）組成。\"in large part\" 是一個慣用語，意思是指「由於大部分的原因」或「在很大程度上」。\"large\" 形容 \"part\"，強調「比例的巨大」。 \"in\" 則表示「在……範圍內」。因此，整個片語表示「原因或影響是佔據了主要部分的」。","definition":"1. To a great extent; largely; 2. For the most part.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The success of the project was in large part due to her efforts.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個專案的成功在很大程度上歸功於她的努力。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"In large part, the changes were driven by new technology.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這些改變主要由新技術推動。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這些改變主要由新技術推動。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5452,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::in-need-of::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Many elderly people are ____ assistance with daily tasks.","expectedAnswer":"in need of","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Many elderly people are ____ assistance with daily tasks.","clozeAnswer":"in need of","exampleTranslation":"許多老年人需要日常事務的協助。","reference":{"eng":"in need of","kk":"ɪn niːd ɒv","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['需要'], ['有所需求']]","chEntries":["需要","有所需求"],"practiceMeaning":"許多老年人需要日常事務的協助。","analysis":"此片語由介系詞 \"in\"，名詞 \"need\" (需求)，以及介系詞 \"of\" 組成。\"need\" 源自古英語 \"nēod\"。此片語表示「處於需要……的狀態」，強調對某物或某種幫助的匱乏感。","definition":"requiring something that you do not have.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The organization provides aid to those in need of food and shelter.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該組織為那些需要食物和住所的人提供援助。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Many elderly people are in need of assistance with daily tasks.\",\n    \"ch\": \"許多老年人需要日常事務的協助。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"許多老年人需要日常事務的協助。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3966,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::in-response-to::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company increased its advertising ____ falling sales.","expectedAnswer":"in response to","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company increased its advertising ____ falling sales.","clozeAnswer":"in response to","exampleTranslation":"由於銷量下滑，該公司增加了廣告投放。","reference":{"eng":"in response to","kk":"None","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['回應', '作為對…的回應']]","chEntries":["回應","作為對…的回應"],"practiceMeaning":"由於銷量下滑，該公司增加了廣告投放。","analysis":"介詞片語，表示某個行動是為了回應或針對某事而發生的。","definition":"as an answer or reaction to something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He acted in response to the urgent request.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他根據緊急請求採取了行動。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company increased its advertising in response to falling sales.\",\n    \"ch\": \"由於銷量下滑，該公司增加了廣告投放。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"由於銷量下滑，該公司增加了廣告投放。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5451,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::in-the-end::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It was a difficult situation, but ____, everything worked out.","expectedAnswer":"in the end","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It was a difficult situation, but ____, everything worked out.","clozeAnswer":"in the end","exampleTranslation":"那是一個困難的局面，但最終，一切都解決了。","reference":{"eng":"in the end","kk":"ɪn ði ˈend","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['最終'], ['最後']]","chEntries":["最終","最後"],"practiceMeaning":"那是一個困難的局面，但最終，一切都解決了。","analysis":"此片語由介系詞 \"in\"，定冠詞 \"the\"，以及名詞 \"end\" (結尾、結束) 組成。\"end\" 源自古英語 \"ende\"。此片語表示事物發展到最後的階段或結果，相當於 \"finally\" 或 \"at last\"。","definition":"finally; at last.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"In the end, they decided to get married.\",\n    \"ch\": \"最後，他們決定結婚。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was a difficult situation, but in the end, everything worked out.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那是一個困難的局面，但最終，一切都解決了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"那是一個困難的局面，但最終，一切都解決了。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5789,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::incorporate::vt","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company decided to ____ overseas branches into its main structure.","expectedAnswer":"incorporate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company decided to ____ overseas branches into its main structure.","clozeAnswer":"incorporate","exampleTranslation":"這家公司決定將海外分支機構納入其主體結構。","reference":{"eng":"incorporate","kk":"ɪnˈkɔrpəreɪt","tense":"vt.","ch":"[  [    \"包含\"  ],  [    \"納入\"  ],  [    \"吸收\"  ],  [    \"使公司法人化\"  ]]","chEntries":["包含","納入","吸收","使公司法人化"],"practiceMeaning":"這家公司決定將海外分支機構納入其主體結構。","analysis":"此字為及物動詞，源自拉丁語incorporare，由in-（進入；在……之中）+corpus（身體；身體，來自原始印歐語\\\\*korpus-）組成。corpus是拉丁語。因此，incorporate的核心語義是「將某物納入一個整體中，使其成為整體的一部分」，如同將東西「化為身體」一樣。語意演變上，從「使成一體」的概念，引申出「包含」、「納入」、「吸收」，以及法律上「使一個組織法人化」的特定用法。","definition":"1. to include something as part of a group, system, or plan; 2. to form a company or organization legally so that it becomes a separate legal entity.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The new design incorporates feedback from customers.\",\n    \"ch\": \"新設計納入了客戶的意見。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company decided to incorporate overseas branches into its main structure.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司決定將海外分支機構納入其主體結構。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They chose to incorporate their business as a limited liability company.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們選擇將他們的業務註冊為有限責任公司（使公司法人化）。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這家公司決定將海外分支機構納入其主體結構。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5404,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l2::indeed::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He is a very talented musician, ____.","expectedAnswer":"indeed","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He is a very talented musician, ____.","clozeAnswer":"indeed","exampleTranslation":"他確實是一位非常有才華的音樂家。","reference":{"eng":"indeed","kk":"ɪnˈdiːd","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['確實'], ['的確'], ['實在']]","chEntries":["確實","的確","實在"],"practiceMeaning":"他確實是一位非常有才華的音樂家。","analysis":"此字是中古英語 in dede 的組合，意為「在事實中」。'in' (in) + 'dede' (deed, deed)。核心語意是「強調事實或真實性」。'Indeed' 用來加強語氣，表示肯定、確認，或用於引出更具體的解釋、進一步的資訊，或者表示同意。","definition":"1. used to emphasize a statement or response; truly; certainly; 2. used to express polite disbelief, surprise, or incredulity.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was indeed a beautiful day.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這確實是個美好的一天。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a very talented musician, indeed.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他確實是一位非常有才華的音樂家。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他確實是一位非常有才華的音樂家。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5461,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::indigenous::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Eucalyptus is ____ to Australia.","expectedAnswer":"indigenous","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Eucalyptus is ____ to Australia.","clozeAnswer":"indigenous","exampleTranslation":"桉樹是澳大利亞的原生植物。","reference":{"eng":"indigenous","kk":"ɪnˈdɪdʒənəs","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['原住民的'], ['本地的'], ['土生土長的']]","chEntries":["原住民的","本地的","土生土長的"],"practiceMeaning":"桉樹是澳大利亞的原生植物。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'indigena'，意為「土著、原住民」。'Indigena' 是由 'indi-'（在此處作強調，可能與 'in'「在……裡面」有關）和 'gen-'（出生、產生，來自 'gignere'「產生」）組合而成，直譯為「從內部出生」，引申為「當地出生、本地的、原生的」。'-ous' 是拉丁語 '-osus' 的英語化形式，用於構成形容詞，表示「充滿……的」。因此，'indigenous' 指的是「屬於某地方、某國家或某特定地區的，從該地方發源或產生的」，特別常用來指「原住民」或「當地特有」的動植物、文化等。","definition":"1. Originating or occurring naturally in a particular place; native.; 2. Relating to or characteristic of a particular region or people.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The indigenous people of Australia have a rich cultural heritage.\",\n    \"ch\": \"澳大利亞的原住民擁有豐富的文化遺產。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Eucalyptus is indigenous to Australia.\",\n    \"ch\": \"桉樹是澳大利亞的原生植物。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company uses indigenous materials in its products.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司在其產品中使用當地材料。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"桉樹是澳大利亞的原生植物。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6229,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::infrastructure::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Poor ____ can hinder economic development.","expectedAnswer":"infrastructure","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Poor ____ can hinder economic development.","clozeAnswer":"infrastructure","exampleTranslation":"薄弱的基礎建設會阻礙經濟發展。","reference":{"eng":"infrastructure","kk":"ˈɪnfrəˌstrʌktʃər","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"基礎設施\"  ],  [    \"基礎建設\"  ],  [    \"結構\"  ]]","chEntries":["基礎設施","基礎建設","結構"],"practiceMeaning":"薄弱的基礎建設會阻礙經濟發展。","analysis":"此字為複合詞，由 infra-（在…之下）和 structure（結構）構成。infra- 源自拉丁語，意為「下面」。structure 源自拉丁語 structura，意為「建造，構築」。此字在現代英語中可視為由 infra- 和 structure 組合而成。名詞義指支撐一個社會或組織運作的基本設施和系統，包括交通、通訊、能源、公共工程、社會服務等。中文翻譯為「基礎設施；基礎建設；結構」。","definition":"1. the basic physical and organizational structures and facilities (e.g. buildings, roads, power supplies) that a country or organization needs to operate; 2. the basic framework or structure of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government plans to invest heavily in infrastructure.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府計劃大力投資基礎設施。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Poor infrastructure can hinder economic development.\",\n    \"ch\": \"薄弱的基礎建設會阻礙經濟發展。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The internet is an essential part of modern infrastructure.\",\n    \"ch\": \"網際網路是現代基礎設施的重要組成部分。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"薄弱的基礎建設會阻礙經濟發展。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5597,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l7::injustice::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She dedicated her life to fighting against ____.","expectedAnswer":"injustice","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She dedicated her life to fighting against ____.","clozeAnswer":"injustice","exampleTranslation":"她畢生致力於反對不公。","reference":{"eng":"injustice","kk":"ɪnˈdʒʌstɪs","tense":"n.","ch":"[['不公'], ['不義'], ['不公之事']]","chEntries":["不公","不義","不公之事"],"practiceMeaning":"她畢生致力於反對不公。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'injustitia'，由否定字首 'in-'（不）加上 'justitia'（正義）組成。'-ia' 字尾表示狀態或品質。'justitia' 本身源自 'justus'（公正的、合法的），而 'justus' 又源於 'jus'（法律、權利）。構詞學上，'in-' 字首的加入直接否定了「正義」的概念，形成「不正義」或「不公」的狀態。原始語意是「缺乏正義」，演變為指「不公平的行為、待遇或情況」。","definition":"1. Lack of fairness or justice; 2. An unjust act or occurrence.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The report highlighted cases of systemic injustice.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這份報告強調了系統性不公的案例。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She dedicated her life to fighting against injustice.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她畢生致力於反對不公。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她畢生致力於反對不公。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4731,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::inn::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ offered hearty meals and local ale.","expectedAnswer":"inn","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ offered hearty meals and local ale.","clozeAnswer":"inn","exampleTranslation":"這家客棧提供豐盛的餐點和當地啤酒。","reference":{"eng":"inn","kk":"/ˈɪn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['小旅館'], ['客棧']]","chEntries":["小旅館","客棧"],"practiceMeaning":"這家客棧提供豐盛的餐點和當地啤酒。","analysis":"源自古英語 *inne*，指「內部」。原指房屋內部，後演變為提供食宿的小型公共場所，特別是鄉村或公路旁的地方。與 'hotel' 相比，規模較小，通常更傳統。","definition":"1. A small hotel or lodging house, typically in the country.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They stayed at a charming old inn in the countryside.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們住在鄉村一家迷人的老客棧。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The inn offered hearty meals and local ale.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家客棧提供豐盛的餐點和當地啤酒。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這家客棧提供豐盛的餐點和當地啤酒。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4256,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::inner::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ workings of the machine were complex.","expectedAnswer":"inner","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ workings of the machine were complex.","clozeAnswer":"inner","exampleTranslation":"機器的內部運作非常複雜。","reference":{"eng":"inner","kk":"/ˈɪnər/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['內部的'], ['內在的'], ['隱藏的']]","chEntries":["內部的","內在的","隱藏的"],"practiceMeaning":"機器的內部運作非常複雜。","analysis":"比較級形式，源自古英語 'in'（內）。'Inner' 指的是「在裡面」，與「外面」相對。它可以指物理上的內部，也可以指抽象的、情感或精神層面的內部。","definition":"situated on or toward the inside; internal; relating to the mind or spirit.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She possessed great inner strength.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她擁有巨大的內在力量。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The inner workings of the machine were complex.\",\n    \"ch\": \"機器的內部運作非常複雜。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"機器的內部運作非常複雜。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4164,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::insignificant::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The difference between the two amounts is ____.","expectedAnswer":"insignificant","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The difference between the two amounts is ____.","clozeAnswer":"insignificant","exampleTranslation":"兩個數額之間的差異微乎其微。","reference":{"eng":"insignificant","kk":"/ˌɪnsɪɡˈnɪfɪkənt/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['微不足道的', '無關緊要的']]","chEntries":["微不足道的","無關緊要的"],"practiceMeaning":"兩個數額之間的差異微乎其微。","analysis":"由 in-（否定前綴）+ significant（重要的）組成。核心概念是「不重要的」、「缺乏意義」。","definition":"1. too small or unimportant to be worth consideration; 2. not significant; trivial","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His contribution was insignificant.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的貢獻微不足道。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The difference between the two amounts is insignificant.\",\n    \"ch\": \"兩個數額之間的差異微乎其微。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We shouldn't waste time on insignificant details.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們不應該在無關緊要的細節上浪費時間。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"兩個數額之間的差異微乎其微。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5699,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l9::instinctive::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His reaction was ____, not deliberate.","expectedAnswer":"instinctive","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His reaction was ____, not deliberate.","clozeAnswer":"instinctive","exampleTranslation":"他的反應是本能的，而非刻意的。","reference":{"eng":"instinctive","kk":"ɪnˈstɪŋktɪv","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['憑本能的'], ['直覺的'], ['本能的']]","chEntries":["憑本能的","直覺的","本能的"],"practiceMeaning":"他的反應是本能的，而非刻意的。","analysis":"此字由名詞 'instinct' 加上形容詞化後綴 '-ive' 構成。'instinct' 源自拉丁語 instinctus（驅使，激勵），由 instinguere（驅使，激勵）演變而來。'-ive' 後綴使名詞轉化為形容詞，表示「具有……的特性的」。因此，'instinctive' 的核心語意是「與本能、天性或內在驅動力相關的，而非學習或思考的結果」。它描述的是一種發生在意識層面之下的、自動的反應或行為。","definition":"based on or resulting from a natural feeling or urge that is not conscious; natural; not learned.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Babies have an instinctive need to be held.\",\n    \"ch\": \"嬰兒有一種被擁抱的本能需求。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His reaction was instinctive, not deliberate.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的反應是本能的，而非刻意的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他的反應是本能的，而非刻意的。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3173,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::insult::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She refused to tolerate such an ____.","expectedAnswer":"insult","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She refused to tolerate such an ____.","clozeAnswer":"insult","exampleTranslation":"她拒絕容忍這樣的侮辱。","reference":{"eng":"insult","kk":"/ˈɪnsʌlt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['侮辱；辱罵；冒犯']]","chEntries":["侮辱","辱罵","冒犯"],"practiceMeaning":"她拒絕容忍這樣的侮辱。","analysis":"名詞用法，源自動詞 'insult'。指「侮辱」、「辱罵」或「冒犯」的行為或言論，通常是故意用來貶低、傷害或激怒他人。它是一種對他人尊嚴或感情的攻擊。","definition":"1. a disrespectful or scornfully abusive remark or action; 2. an act or statement that shows disrespect or offends.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His comments were a direct insult to her intelligence.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的評論是對她智慧的直接侮辱。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She refused to tolerate such an insult.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她拒絕容忍這樣的侮辱。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The public reaction was seen as an insult to the nation's heroes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公眾的反應被視為對國家英雄的侮辱。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她拒絕容忍這樣的侮辱。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5351,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l1::intend::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They ____ to get married next year.","expectedAnswer":"intend","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They ____ to get married next year.","clozeAnswer":"intend","exampleTranslation":"他們打算明年結婚。","reference":{"eng":"intend","kk":"ɪnˈtɛnd","tense":"v.","ch":"[['打算'], ['意欲'], ['意圖']]","chEntries":["打算","意欲","意圖"],"practiceMeaning":"他們打算明年結婚。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 intendere，由 in-（朝向）+ tendere（伸展）組成。構詞上，in- 表示「朝向」，tend- 是字根，表示「伸展、拉緊」。原始語意為「朝著某方向伸展」，引申為「心理上朝著某目標努力」，即「意圖、打算」。","definition":"to plan to do something; to have as one's purpose or aim.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I intend to finish this book by tonight.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我打算今晚讀完這本書。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They intend to get married next year.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們打算明年結婚。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們打算明年結婚。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3093,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::interfere::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Loud noises can ____ with sleep.","expectedAnswer":"interfere","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Loud noises can ____ with sleep.","clozeAnswer":"interfere","exampleTranslation":"嘈雜的噪音會妨礙睡眠。","reference":{"eng":"interfere","kk":"/ˌɪntərˈfɪr/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['干涉；干預'], ['妨礙；阻礙']]","chEntries":["干涉","干預","妨礙","阻礙"],"practiceMeaning":"嘈雜的噪音會妨礙睡眠。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'inter-' (between) + 'ferire' (to strike)。核心意義是「在兩者之間插入」，引申為「干涉」。\n1. 干涉；干預：指未經允許介入他人的事務，試圖控制或影響。\n2. 妨礙；阻礙：指阻礙事物的正常進行或發展。","definition":"1. to get involved in a situation in order to influence the outcome; 2. to prevent something from continuing or being able to do something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please don't interfere in my personal matters.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請不要干涉我的個人事務。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Loud noises can interfere with sleep.\",\n    \"ch\": \"嘈雜的噪音會妨礙睡眠。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"嘈雜的噪音會妨礙睡眠。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3174,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::intuition::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Trust your ____ when making important decisions.","expectedAnswer":"intuition","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Trust your ____ when making important decisions.","clozeAnswer":"intuition","exampleTranslation":"做重要決定時，相信你的直覺。","reference":{"eng":"intuition","kk":"/ˌɪntuˈɪʃn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['直覺；直覺力']]","chEntries":["直覺","直覺力"],"practiceMeaning":"做重要決定時，相信你的直覺。","analysis":"詞源來自拉丁語 'intueri'，意為「看，觀察」。'Intuition' 指的是一種直接的、非理性或非邏輯的理解或知識，無需經過明顯的推理過程就能獲得。它是一種內在的感知或「預感」，通常基於潛意識的經驗或感受。","definition":"the ability to understand something immediately, without the need for conscious reasoning.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She had a strong intuition that something was wrong.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她強烈的直覺告訴她，有什麼事情不對勁。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Trust your intuition when making important decisions.\",\n    \"ch\": \"做重要決定時，相信你的直覺。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His intuition about the market proved to be correct.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對市場的直覺被證明是正確的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"做重要決定時，相信你的直覺。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5647,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l8::invasion::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The city experienced an ____ of tourists during the summer.","expectedAnswer":"invasion","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The city experienced an ____ of tourists during the summer.","clozeAnswer":"invasion","exampleTranslation":"這座城市在夏季湧入了大量的遊客。","reference":{"eng":"invasion","kk":"ɪnˈveɪʒən","tense":"n.","ch":"[['入侵'], ['侵略'], ['湧入'], ['（意見、要求等）干擾']]","chEntries":["入侵","侵略","湧入","干擾"],"practiceMeaning":"這座城市在夏季湧入了大量的遊客。","analysis":"此字由 invade（入侵）+ -sion（名詞字尾）構成。invade 源自拉丁語 invadere，由 in-（進入，into）+ vadere（行走，to go）組成。vadere 來自原始印歐語 *gwem-（行走，to come）。-sion 是常見的名詞字尾，用於將動詞轉為名詞，表示「動作」、「狀態」或「結果」。構詞上，in- 表示「進入」，vadere 提供「行走」或「進入」的核心動作，-sion 將其名詞化。核心語義為「進入」某地，尤指帶有敵意或強制性地。","definition":"an act or instance of invading a country or region with an armed force; an encroachment or intrusion; a sudden rush or influx.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The invasion of the enemy forces was swift.\",\n    \"ch\": \"敵軍的入侵行動迅速。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The city experienced an invasion of tourists during the summer.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座城市在夏季湧入了大量的遊客。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這座城市在夏季湧入了大量的遊客。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5523,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l5::isolated::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He felt ____ after his friends moved away.","expectedAnswer":"isolated","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He felt ____ after his friends moved away.","clozeAnswer":"isolated","exampleTranslation":"朋友們搬走後，他感到孤立無援。","reference":{"eng":"isolated","kk":"ˈaɪsəleɪtɪd","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['孤立的'], ['偏僻的'], ['隔絕的']]","chEntries":["孤立的","偏僻的","隔絕的"],"practiceMeaning":"朋友們搬走後，他感到孤立無援。","analysis":"此字是動詞 'isolate' 的過去分詞，用作形容詞。'isolate' 源自西班牙語 'isla' (island)，透過意語 'isola' 傳入，意為「島嶼」。構詞上，'island' + '-ate'（動詞化字尾）。語意上，'isolate' 指「使成為孤島」，即「使隔絕、使孤立」。因此，'isolated' 作形容詞時，描述的是「被隔離開來、處於孤獨或偏僻狀態」的。它涵蓋了地理上的「偏僻」和社交上的「孤立」兩種情境。","definition":"far away from other places, buildings, or people; remote; forming a separate unit or units.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The village is isolated in the mountains.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個村莊孤立在山區。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He felt isolated after his friends moved away.\",\n    \"ch\": \"朋友們搬走後，他感到孤立無援。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"朋友們搬走後，他感到孤立無援。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5384,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l2::issue::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This is the latest ____ of the magazine.","expectedAnswer":"issue","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This is the latest ____ of the magazine.","clozeAnswer":"issue","exampleTranslation":"這是最新一期的雜誌。","reference":{"eng":"issue","kk":"ˈɪʃuː","tense":"n.","ch":"[['問題'], ['議題'], ['爭議'], ['（報刊）期'], ['（小孩、動物的）後代'], ['發行']]","chEntries":["問題","議題","爭議","期","後代","發行"],"practiceMeaning":"這是最新一期的雜誌。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 escuë (出去、發出)，來自拉丁語 exire (出來)。核心語意是「從某處出來、出現」。因此，'issue' 作名詞時，可以指「一個出現或引起關注的事件或情況」（問題、議題），「報刊的某一期」（出版物從發行源出來），或「子女」（從父母那裡出現）等。","definition":"1. an important topic or problem for debate or discussion; 2. a regular weekly or monthly magazine or newspaper; 3. the act of supplying or distributing something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Climate change is a major global issue.\",\n    \"ch\": \"氣候變遷是一個主要的全球性議題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is the latest issue of the magazine.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是最新一期的雜誌。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是最新一期的雜誌。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4363,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::it-s-pouring-now::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Look outside – ____.","expectedAnswer":"it’s pouring now","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Look outside – ____.","clozeAnswer":"it’s pouring now","exampleTranslation":"看看外面——現在正在下大雨。","reference":{"eng":"it’s pouring now","kk":"None","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['現在正在下大雨']]","chEntries":["現在正在下大雨"],"practiceMeaning":"看看外面——現在正在下大雨。","analysis":"此為片語分析。'it's' (it is) 指『這是』。'pouring' (v. present participle) 源自 'pour' (v.)，意為『傾倒』，在此引申為『（雨）傾瀉』。'now' (adv.) 指『現在』。整個片語表示『現在雨下得非常大』。","definition":"it is raining very heavily at the present time","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We can't go out, it’s pouring now!\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們不能出去，現在正在下大雨！\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Look outside – it’s pouring now.\",\n    \"ch\": \"看看外面——現在正在下大雨。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"看看外面——現在正在下大雨。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4725,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::jazz::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Don't ____ things up too much; keep it simple.","expectedAnswer":"jazz","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Don't ____ things up too much; keep it simple.","clozeAnswer":"jazz","exampleTranslation":"別把事情搞得太複雜；保持簡單。","reference":{"eng":"jazz","kk":"/ˈdʒæz/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['爵士樂'], ['（非正式）胡鬧；大驚小怪'], ['（非正式）狀況；把事情搞砸']]","chEntries":["爵士樂","胡鬧","大驚小怪","狀況","把事情搞砸"],"practiceMeaning":"別把事情搞得太複雜；保持簡單。","analysis":"詞源不明，可能源於20世紀初美國非裔社群的口語。最初用於指音樂風格，後引申出「弄亂」、「搞砸」或「大驚小怪」的非正式用法。","definition":"1. A genre of music that originated in African-American communities in the United States in the late 19th and early 20th centuries. 2. (informal) Nonsense; fuss. 3. (informal) A situation, especially one that has been spoiled or confused.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a big fan of jazz music.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是爵士樂的忠實粉絲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Don't jazz things up too much; keep it simple.\",\n    \"ch\": \"別把事情搞得太複雜；保持簡單。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He really jazzed up the presentation with visuals.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他用視覺效果把簡報弄得活色生香。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"別把事情搞得太複雜；保持簡單。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3901,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::jealous::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She felt ____ when her friend got the promotion.","expectedAnswer":"jealous","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She felt ____ when her friend got the promotion.","clozeAnswer":"jealous","exampleTranslation":"當她的朋友獲得晉升時，她感到嫉妒。","reference":{"eng":"jealous","kk":"/ˈdʒɛləs/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['嫉妒的'], ['羨慕的'], ['提防的']]","chEntries":["嫉妒的","羨慕的","提防的"],"practiceMeaning":"當她的朋友獲得晉升時，她感到嫉妒。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'zelus'，'zelotypus' (zealous)，意為「熱情的」。其詞源演變較為複雜，但現代意義主要指因擔心失去所愛或所擁有的東西，或因他人擁有自己所沒有的而產生的不滿、敵意或不安。也可指對某事物極為小心、防護的。","definition":"1. feeling or showing envy of someone or their achievements and advantages. 2. feeling or showing suspicion of someone's unfaithfulness to you. 3. fiercely protective or suspicious of (someone or something).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was jealous of his brother's success.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他嫉妒他哥哥的成功。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She felt jealous when her friend got the promotion.\",\n    \"ch\": \"當她的朋友獲得晉升時，她感到嫉妒。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Be careful, he's jealous of anyone who tries to get close to his wife.\",\n    \"ch\": \"小心點，他嫉妒任何試圖接近他妻子的人。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"當她的朋友獲得晉升時，她感到嫉妒。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4691,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::jeep::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ was equipped for all kinds of weather.","expectedAnswer":"jeep","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ was equipped for all kinds of weather.","clozeAnswer":"jeep","exampleTranslation":"這輛吉普車配備了應對各種天氣的設備。","reference":{"eng":"jeep","kk":"/ˈdʒip/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['吉普車（越野車）']]","chEntries":["吉普車"],"practiceMeaning":"這輛吉普車配備了應對各種天氣的設備。","analysis":"原為第二次世界大戰時期軍用車輛的通用名稱，據信源自 GP（General Purpose，通用）的縮寫，或是由士兵口語發音演變而成。後成為一種註冊商標，但廣泛用於指代多功能、輕便的越野車。","definition":"1. A robust, four-wheel-drive vehicle, typically with an open top and removable hood, designed for off-road use.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They hired a jeep to explore the rugged terrain.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們租了一輛吉普車來探索崎嶇的地形。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The jeep was equipped for all kinds of weather.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這輛吉普車配備了應對各種天氣的設備。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這輛吉普車配備了應對各種天氣的設備。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5701,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l9::jury::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He was acquitted by the ____.","expectedAnswer":"jury","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He was acquitted by the ____.","clozeAnswer":"jury","exampleTranslation":"他被陪審團判無罪。","reference":{"eng":"jury","kk":"ˈdʒʊəri","tense":"n.","ch":"[['陪審團']]","chEntries":["陪審團"],"practiceMeaning":"他被陪審團判無罪。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 juree（宣誓，陪審員），來自拉丁語 iurare（發誓），源自 ius（法律）。構詞上，此字表示「一群被召喚來聽取證據並做出裁決的人」。其核心語意與「發誓」和「法律」緊密相關，指代在法庭上，由一群普通公民組成的、負責判斷事實真相的組織。","definition":"a group of people, typically twelve in number, who together consider the case of a defendant in a trial, and reach a verdict.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The jury reached a unanimous verdict.\",\n    \"ch\": \"陪審團達成了一致的裁決。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was acquitted by the jury.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他被陪審團判無罪。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他被陪審團判無罪。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3312,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::just::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He believes that everyone deserves a ____ punishment.","expectedAnswer":"just","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He believes that everyone deserves a ____ punishment.","clozeAnswer":"just","exampleTranslation":"他認為每個人都應該受到應有的懲罰。","reference":{"eng":"just","kk":"/dʒʌst/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['公正的；合乎正義的'], ['應得的；理所應當的']]","chEntries":["公正的","合乎正義的","應得的","理所應當的"],"practiceMeaning":"他認為每個人都應該受到應有的懲罰。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'justus'，由 'jus' (法律，權利) 演變而來。指符合道德、法律或公平原則，沒有偏倚，理應如此。","definition":"1. based on or behaving according to what is morally right and fair; 2. based on or behaving according to what is morally right and fair; deserved.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The judge made a just decision.\",\n    \"ch\": \"法官做出了公正的判決。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He believes that everyone deserves a just punishment.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他認為每個人都應該受到應有的懲罰。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他認為每個人都應該受到應有的懲罰。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5549,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l5::keep-a-record::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It's important to ____ of your expenses.","expectedAnswer":"keep a record","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It's important to ____ of your expenses.","clozeAnswer":"keep a record","exampleTranslation":"記錄下你的開銷很重要。","reference":{"eng":"keep a record","kk":"kiːp ə ˈrekərd","tense":"v.","ch":"[['記錄下來'], ['保持記錄']]","chEntries":["記錄下來","保持記錄"],"practiceMeaning":"記錄下你的開銷很重要。","analysis":"此為固定搭配。'keep' (保持、持有) + 'a record' (一份記錄)。'record' 源自拉丁語 'recordari' (to remember)，意為「記憶、記錄」。'keep a record' 的意思是指「為了將來查閱而保存某事物的信息」，通常是以書面、電子或其他形式。它強調的是「持續地保存」和「完整的資訊」。","definition":"to write down information so that it can be used or referred to in the future.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company keeps detailed records of all its transactions.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司對所有交易都保持詳細記錄。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's important to keep a record of your expenses.\",\n    \"ch\": \"記錄下你的開銷很重要。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"記錄下你的開銷很重要。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3965,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::lack-variety::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Life in the small town could ____ for some people.","expectedAnswer":"lack variety","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Life in the small town could ____ for some people.","clozeAnswer":"lack variety","exampleTranslation":"對於一些人來說，小鎮的生活可能缺乏多樣性。","reference":{"eng":"lack variety","kk":"None","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['缺乏多樣性', '缺乏變化']]","chEntries":["缺乏多樣性","缺乏變化"],"practiceMeaning":"對於一些人來說，小鎮的生活可能缺乏多樣性。","analysis":"動詞 'lack' (缺乏) 加上名詞 'variety' (多樣性)。表示事物種類不多，單調或缺乏變化。","definition":"to not have enough different types of things; to be monotonous.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The menu tends to lack variety.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這份菜單似乎缺乏變化。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Life in the small town could lack variety for some people.\",\n    \"ch\": \"對於一些人來說，小鎮的生活可能缺乏多樣性。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"對於一些人來說，小鎮的生活可能缺乏多樣性。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4703,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::ladder::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She is determined to climb the corporate ____.","expectedAnswer":"ladder","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She is determined to climb the corporate ____.","clozeAnswer":"ladder","exampleTranslation":"她決心在企業界逐步晉升。","reference":{"eng":"ladder","kk":"/ˈlædər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['梯子'], ['（事業、組織等的）等級、階梯']]","chEntries":["梯子","等級、階梯"],"practiceMeaning":"她決心在企業界逐步晉升。","analysis":"源自古英語 *lǣder*，可能與古諾斯語 *þröstr*（梯子）同源。核心是向上或向下攀爬的結構。引申至事業、社會地位等逐步晉升的等級或過程。","definition":"1. A piece of equipment consisting of two long side-pieces joined by rungs, used for climbing up or down something. 2. A series of levels or steps in a hierarchy or career.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He climbed the ladder to reach the roof.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他爬上梯子到達屋頂。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is determined to climb the corporate ladder.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她決心在企業界逐步晉升。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她決心在企業界逐步晉升。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3891,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::lately::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"What have you been doing ____?","expectedAnswer":"lately","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"What have you been doing ____?","clozeAnswer":"lately","exampleTranslation":"你最近在忙什麼？","reference":{"eng":"lately","kk":"/ˈleɪtli/","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['最近', '近來']]","chEntries":["最近","近來"],"practiceMeaning":"你最近在忙什麼？","analysis":"由 'late' (晚的) 加上副詞後綴 '-ly' 構成。核心是「晚近的」。指在不久的過去，相對於現在的時間點而言。","definition":"recently; in the recent past.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I haven't seen him lately.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我最近沒見到他。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"What have you been doing lately?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你最近在忙什麼？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The weather has been strange lately.\",\n    \"ch\": \"最近天氣很奇怪。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"你最近在忙什麼？","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4219,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::launch::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company will ____ a new advertising campaign.","expectedAnswer":"launch","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company will ____ a new advertising campaign.","clozeAnswer":"launch","exampleTranslation":"公司將啟動一個新的廣告活動。","reference":{"eng":"launch","kk":"/lɔːntʃ/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['發射（導彈、火箭等）'], ['推出（新產品）；發動（活動）'], ['使（船）下水']]","chEntries":["發射","推出","發動","使下水"],"practiceMeaning":"公司將啟動一個新的廣告活動。","analysis":"源自古法語 lancier，意為“投擲，揮動”，來自拉丁語 lancea（長矛）。核心是“向前投擲”或“推動”。1. “發射”是將武器或飛行器向目標或空間推動。2. “推出；發動”是將新事物或活動投入市場或執行。3. “使下水”是將船隻移入水中。","definition":"1. to set in motion by pushing or thrusting; 2. to start or set in motion; 3. to introduce (a new product or service) to the market.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They plan to launch a new missile next month.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們計劃下個月發射一枚新導彈。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company will launch a new advertising campaign.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司將啟動一個新的廣告活動。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The ship was launched yesterday.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這艘船昨天被下水了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"公司將啟動一個新的廣告活動。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5843,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::legitimate::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Her concerns are perfectly ____.","expectedAnswer":"legitimate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Her concerns are perfectly ____.","clozeAnswer":"legitimate","exampleTranslation":"她的擔憂完全是合理的。","reference":{"eng":"legitimate","kk":"lɪˈdʒɪtəmət","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"合法的\"  ],  [    \"正當的\"  ],  [    \"合理的\"  ],  [    \"合乎規定的\"  ]]","chEntries":["合法的","正當的","合理的","合乎規定的"],"practiceMeaning":"她的擔憂完全是合理的。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'legitimus'，意為「合法的」、「合乎法律的」，由 'lex' (law) 構成。'-ate' 是常見的形容詞或動詞字尾。'Legitimus' 的核心語意是「符合法律」或「基於法律」。在現代英語中，'legitimate' 指符合法律規定、規則、原則或道德標準。它可以指法律上的「合法性」，也可以指行為、要求或理由的「正當性」或「合理性」。例如，也可指「非婚生子女以外的」，即「婚生子女」。","definition":"1. Complying with the law.; 2. Able to be defended with logic or reason.; 3. Genuine, or one regarded as such.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a legitimate business operation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個合法的商業運營。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her concerns are perfectly legitimate.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的擔憂完全是合理的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The court ruled the contract legitimate.\",\n    \"ch\": \"法院裁定該合同合法有效。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The couple hoped for a legitimate heir to the throne.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這對夫婦希望有一位合法的王位繼承人。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她的擔憂完全是合理的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4664,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::let-out-a-sigh::idiom","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She ____ of disappointment.","expectedAnswer":"let out a sigh","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She ____ of disappointment.","clozeAnswer":"let out a sigh","exampleTranslation":"她失望地嘆了口氣。","reference":{"eng":"let out a sigh","kk":"/lɛt aʊt ə saɪ/","tense":"idiom","ch":"[['嘆了口氣']]","chEntries":["嘆了口氣"],"practiceMeaning":"她失望地嘆了口氣。","analysis":"此為固定片語。'Let out' (放出、發出) + 'a sigh' (一次嘆息)。描述一個人深長地呼氣，通常表示疲倦、寬慰、失望或滿足等情緒。","definition":"to breathe out audibly, typically to express an emotion such as relief, sadness, or tiredness.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He let out a sigh of relief when he saw the results.\",\n    \"ch\": \"看到結果時，他如釋重負地嘆了口氣。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She let out a sigh of disappointment.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她失望地嘆了口氣。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她失望地嘆了口氣。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4246,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::lettuce::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ is a common ingredient in sandwiches.","expectedAnswer":"Lettuce","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ is a common ingredient in sandwiches.","clozeAnswer":"Lettuce","exampleTranslation":"生菜是三明治的常見配料。","reference":{"eng":"lettuce","kk":"/ˈlɛtɪs/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['生菜'], ['萵苣']]","chEntries":["生菜","萵苣"],"practiceMeaning":"生菜是三明治的常見配料。","analysis":"源自古法語 'laitue'，來自拉丁語 'lactuca'，意為「乳狀的、奶狀的」，因為其莖部含有乳白色汁液。'Lettuce' 是指一種常見的葉菜。","definition":"a plant with crisp, green leaves that are eaten as a vegetable, usually in salads.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The salad contained fresh lettuce, tomatoes, and cucumbers.\",\n    \"ch\": \"沙拉裡有新鮮的生菜、番茄和黃瓜。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Lettuce is a common ingredient in sandwiches.\",\n    \"ch\": \"生菜是三明治的常見配料。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"生菜是三明治的常見配料。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5571,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::load::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The lorry had a heavy ____ of timber.","expectedAnswer":"load","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The lorry had a heavy ____ of timber.","clozeAnswer":"load","exampleTranslation":"這輛貨車載有大量木材。","reference":{"eng":"load","kk":"loʊd","tense":"n.","ch":"[['負荷'], ['載重'], ['裝載量'], ['負擔']]","chEntries":["負荷","載重","裝載量","負擔"],"practiceMeaning":"這輛貨車載有大量木材。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 \"lād\"，意為 \"way, journey, cargo\"（路，旅程，貨物），最終可能源自原始印歐語 \\*leith-（to go, to travel，去，旅行）。\"lād\" 最初指「旅程」或「所載的貨物」。\"load\" 作名詞，核心語義是「被攜帶或承受的重量、數量或負擔」。它可以指物理上的「貨物」（cargo）；「機器或車輛所能承受的最大重量」（carrying capacity）；在工程學上指「作用在結構上的力」（force or stress）；在計算機領域指「載入的數據或程式」（data to be loaded）；引申義指「精神上的負擔」（burden）。","definition":"1. A large quantity of goods or people, especially one that is carried or conveyed; 2. The weight of goods put on a vehicle or in a ship, aircraft, etc.; 3. A quantity of something such as ammunition, that is put into a gun; 4. The amount of work or responsibility that someone has.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The maximum load for this elevator is 1000 kg.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這部電梯的最大負荷是 1000 公斤。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The lorry had a heavy load of timber.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這輛貨車載有大量木材。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is carrying a heavy emotional load.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他承受著沉重的精神負擔。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The game's graphics load slowly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"遊戲的畫面載入很慢。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這輛貨車載有大量木材。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4000,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u3::look::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The new ____ for the season is all about bright colors.","expectedAnswer":"look","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The new ____ for the season is all about bright colors.","clozeAnswer":"look","exampleTranslation":"這一季的新造型是關於鮮豔的色彩。","reference":{"eng":"look","kk":"/lʊk/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['外觀', '樣子'], ['神情', '表情'], ['（時尚）潮流']]","chEntries":["外觀","樣子","神情","表情","潮流"],"practiceMeaning":"這一季的新造型是關於鮮豔的色彩。","analysis":"詞源：同上。名詞形式，指外表、給人印象的樣子，或流行風格。","definition":"1. the outward appearance or visible aspect of a person or thing; 2. a particular facial expression; 3. a style or fashion.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her look of surprise was evident.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她驚訝的神情很明顯。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The new look for the season is all about bright colors.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這一季的新造型是關於鮮豔的色彩。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這一季的新造型是關於鮮豔的色彩。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3120,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::lunar::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The astronauts collected ____ samples.","expectedAnswer":"lunar","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The astronauts collected ____ samples.","clozeAnswer":"lunar","exampleTranslation":"太空人收集了月球樣本。","reference":{"eng":"lunar","kk":"/ˈluːnər/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['月亮的；月球的']]","chEntries":["月亮的","月球的"],"practiceMeaning":"太空人收集了月球樣本。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'lunaris'，'luna' (moon)。核心意義是「與月亮有關」。\n1. 月亮的；月球的：指與月亮、月球有關的。","definition":"1. relating to the moon; 2. of or resembling the moon.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The lunar surface is covered in craters.\",\n    \"ch\": \"月球表面布滿了隕石坑。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The astronauts collected lunar samples.\",\n    \"ch\": \"太空人收集了月球樣本。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTransla