":4681,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::panic::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The sudden news caused widespread ____ among the investors.","expectedAnswer":"panic","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The sudden news caused widespread ____ among the investors.","clozeAnswer":"panic","exampleTranslation":"這突如其來的消息在投資者中引起了廣泛的恐慌。","reference":{"eng":"panic","kk":"/ˈpænɪk/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['恐慌'], ['驚慌失措']]","chEntries":["恐慌","驚慌失措"],"practiceMeaning":"這突如其來的消息在投資者中引起了廣泛的恐慌。","analysis":"源自希臘神話中的牧神 Pan，據說他的嘶喊能引起無端的恐懼。核心概念是突然、強烈的、非理性的恐懼。此恐懼感常常導致行動失控。","definition":"1. A sudden uncontrollable fear or anxiety, often causing wildly unthinking behavior.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was a moment of panic when the fire alarm went off.\",\n    \"ch\": \"火警響起時，曾有一刻的恐慌。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The sudden news caused widespread panic among the investors.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這突如其來的消息在投資者中引起了廣泛的恐慌。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這突如其來的消息在投資者中引起了廣泛的恐慌。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4227,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::parrot::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"A ____ is known for its ability to mimic.","expectedAnswer":"parrot","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"A ____ is known for its ability to mimic.","clozeAnswer":"parrot","exampleTranslation":"鸚鵡以其模仿能力而聞名。","reference":{"eng":"parrot","kk":"/ˈpærət/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['鸚鵡']]","chEntries":["鸚鵡"],"practiceMeaning":"鸚鵡以其模仿能力而聞名。","analysis":"詞源不確定，可能來自西班牙語 papagayo 或葡萄牙語 papagaio。鸚鵡是一種通常色彩鮮豔、能模仿人語的熱帶鳥類。該詞主要指這種鳥類，沒有廣泛的引申義。","definition":"A brightly colored tropical bird with a strong curved beak, known for its ability to mimic sounds and human speech.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The parrot repeated everything the child said.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那隻鸚鵡重複了孩子說的每一句話。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A parrot is known for its ability to mimic.\",\n    \"ch\": \"鸚鵡以其模仿能力而聞名。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslatio