],"practiceMeaning":"房子後面有一小塊花園。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 'pach'，意為「縫補、修補」，可能與低地德語 'patsken'（輕拍、修補）有關。核心語意為「用於修補的塊狀物」或「修補後的小區域」。廣泛用於衣物上的補丁、土地上的一小塊區域、或軟體上的修正檔。","definition":"a piece of material used to cover a hole or mend a tear; a small area of something that is different from the rest of it; a piece of software code designed to fix bugs or improve performance.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He put a patch on his torn trousers.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他給他破了的褲子打了一個補丁。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There's a small patch of garden behind the house.\",\n    \"ch\": \"房子後面有一小塊花園。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The software update includes several security patches.\",\n    \"ch\": \"軟體更新包含幾個安全補丁。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"房子後面有一小塊花園。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U63"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5306,"wordRef":"字彙王::u63::pathetic::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His attempt to apologize was ____.","expectedAnswer":"pathetic","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His attempt to apologize was ____.","clozeAnswer":"pathetic","exampleTranslation":"他試圖道歉的樣子真可笑。","reference":{"eng":"pathetic","kk":"pəˈθɛtɪk","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['可憐的', '悲哀的'], ['令人同情的', '惹人憐愛的'], ['（令人）不滿的，遜的，可笑的']]","chEntries":["可憐的","悲哀的","令人同情的","惹人憐愛的","不滿的，遜的，可笑的"],"practiceMeaning":"他試圖道歉的樣子真可笑。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'patheticus'，來自希臘語 'pathētikos' (παθητικός)，意為「感受到的，情感的」，來自 'pathos' (πάθος)，意為「苦難，情感」。構詞上，'path-' 為詞根，'-etikos' 為形容詞後綴。原始語意與「情感」或「痛苦」有關。現代英語中的 'pathetic' 涵蓋了「引起同情、可憐」的意思，但更常用來形容「令人同情到覺得可笑、遜」的情況，帶有輕蔑意味。","definition":"arousing pity, especially through vulnerability or sadness; miserably weak or inadequate.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The lost dog looked pathetic.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那隻走失的狗看起來很可憐。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His attempt to apologize was pathetic.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他試圖道歉的樣子真可笑。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他試圖道歉的樣子真可笑。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U63"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5852,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::patrol::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The night ____ is responsible for security.","expectedAnswer":"patrol","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The night ____ is responsible for security.","clozeAnswer":"patrol","exampleTranslation":"夜間巡邏隊負責安全。","reference":{"eng":"patrol","kk":"pəˈtroʊl","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"巡邏\"  ],  [    \"巡邏隊\"  ],  [    \"巡邏路線\"  ],  [    \"守衛\"  ]]","chEntries":["巡邏","巡邏隊","巡邏路線","守衛"],"practiceMeaning":"夜間巡邏隊負責安全。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 'patrouiller' (to wade through mire, to patrol)，其詞源不確定，可能與拉丁語 'pastor' (shepherd) 或 'pala' (spade) 有關，表示「巡視」、「守衛」的概念。'Patrol' 作名詞時，指由軍隊、警察或安全人員進行的例行性巡視，以維護秩序、偵測威脅或確保安全。它強調的是一種「規律性」、「監視性」的移動或隊伍。例如，也可指「輪值守衛」。","definition":"1. The action of moving around as a guard.; 2. A person or group of people or animals who patrol an area.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police patrol car drove by.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警車巡邏經過。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The night patrol is responsible for security.\",\n    \"ch\": \"夜間巡邏隊負責安全。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They established a patrol route around the perimeter.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們在周邊地區設立了巡邏路線。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The patrol spotted a suspicious vehicle.\",\n    \"ch\": \"巡邏隊發現了一輛可疑車輛。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"夜間巡邏隊負責安全。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5324,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l1::penalty::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The team was given a ____ for a foul.","expectedAnswer":"penalty","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The team was given a ____ for a foul.","clozeAnswer":"penalty","exampleTranslation":"該隊因犯規受到懲罰。","reference":{"eng":"penalty","kk":"ˈpɛnəlti","tense":"n.","ch":"[['懲罰'], ['罰款'], ['處罰']]","chEntries":["懲罰","罰款","處罰"],"practiceMeaning":"該隊因犯規受到懲罰。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 penalité，來自拉丁語 poenalitas，意為「罪、懲罰」，根源於拉丁語 poena（痛苦、懲罰）。構詞上，poen-（來自拉丁語 poena）是字根，-al 是形容詞字尾，-ity 是名詞字尾，原意為「受懲罰的狀態」。現代語義從「因犯罪而應受的處罰」擴展到體育競賽中的「犯規罰則」，以及法律上的「罰款」。","definition":"a punishment imposed for breaking a law, rule, or contract; a disadvantage imposed on a competitor in a sport for breaking a rule.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The penalty for speeding is a fine.\",\n    \"ch\": \"超速的罰款是罰金。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The team was given a penalty for a foul.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該隊因犯規受到懲罰。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該隊因犯規受到懲罰。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5308,"wordRef":"字彙王::u63::pension::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The government plans to increase the state ____.","expectedAnswer":"pension","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The government plans to increase the state ____.","clozeAnswer":"pension","exampleTranslation":"政府計劃增加國家養老金。","reference":{"eng":"pension","kk":"ˈpɛnʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[['養老金', '退休金'], ['（政府給予的）津貼、補助金']]","chEntries":["養老金","退休金","津貼、補助金"],"practiceMeaning":"政府計劃增加國家養老金。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'pensio'（支付，稱重），來自 'pendere'（to hang, to weigh, to pay）。構詞上，'pens-' 為詞根，'-ion' 為名詞後綴。原始語意為「支付」。此語意引申為定期支付的款項，尤其是指退休後從雇主或政府處獲得的「養老金」。","definition":"a regular payment made during a person's retirement from a former employer or the state; a sum paid regularly to a person.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She receives a modest pension from her former employer.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她從前雇主那裡領取一筆不多的退休金。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government plans to increase the state pension.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府計劃增加國家養老金。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"政府計劃增加國家養老金。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U63"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3934,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::pepper::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She likes her food very spicy, with lots of ____.","expectedAnswer":"pepper","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She likes her food very spicy, with lots of ____.","clozeAnswer":"pepper","exampleTranslation":"她喜歡她的食物非常辣，要加很多辣椒。","reference":{"eng":"pepper","kk":"/ˈpepər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['胡椒'], ['辣椒'], ['胡椒粉']]","chEntries":["胡椒","辣椒","胡椒粉"],"practiceMeaning":"她喜歡她的食物非常辣，要加很多辣椒。","analysis":"源自古英語 'pipor'，經由拉丁語 'piper'，最終源自梵語 'pippala' (意為「長胡椒」)。最初指胡椒，後泛指各種辛辣的香料，包括辣椒。","definition":"1. a hot-tasting powder made from dried, ground berries, used in cooking; 2. a hollow green, red, or yellow vegetable that is sweet when cooked and can be eaten raw; 3. a red or black powder used to give food a hot taste.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please add some pepper to the soup.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請在湯裡加點胡椒粉。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She likes her food very spicy, with lots of pepper.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她喜歡她的食物非常辣，要加很多辣椒。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Black pepper is a common spice.\",\n    \"ch\": \"黑胡椒是一種常見的香料。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她喜歡她的食物非常辣，要加很多辣椒。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3944,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::performance::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The student's academic ____ has improved.","expectedAnswer":"performance","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The student's academic ____ has improved.","clozeAnswer":"performance","exampleTranslation":"這位學生的學術表現有所提高。","reference":{"eng":"performance","kk":"/pərˈfɔːrməns/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['表演', '演出'], ['表現', '績效'], ['性能']]","chEntries":["表演","演出","表現","績效","性能"],"practiceMeaning":"這位學生的學術表現有所提高。","analysis":"源自動詞 'perform' (意為「表演、執行」) 加上名詞後綴 '-ance'。指表演、演出；也指執行某項任務的結果，即「表現」或「績效」；在技術領域則指「性能」。","definition":"1. an act of presenting a play, concert, or other event for an audience; 2. how well or badly someone does a job or task; 3. the action of performing a task or function.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The band's performance was electrifying.\",\n    \"ch\": \"樂團的表演令人振奮。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The student's academic performance has improved.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位學生的學術表現有所提高。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The car has excellent fuel performance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這輛汽車的燃油性能極佳。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這位學生的學術表現有所提高。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4577,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::permanent::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He decided to get a ____ tattoo.","expectedAnswer":"permanent","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He decided to get a ____ tattoo.","clozeAnswer":"permanent","exampleTranslation":"他決定紋一個永久性的刺青。","reference":{"eng":"permanent","kk":"/ˈpɜːrmənənt/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['永久的', '永恆的'], ['（染髮、烙印等）持久的']]","chEntries":["永久的","永恆的","持久的"],"practiceMeaning":"他決定紋一個永久性的刺青。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'permanere'，'per-' (through) 和 'manere' (to remain - 停留)。核心概念是「持續存在」。\n    1. 永久的、永恆的：指不會改變、消失或結束。\n    2. 持久的：指效果或狀態持續很長時間，不易改變，如 'permanent wave' (永久燙髮)。","definition":"1. lasting or intended to last indefinitely or for a long time.; 2. (of a hair-wave or colour) lasting for a long time.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This decision will have permanent consequences.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個決定將會帶來永久性的後果。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He decided to get a permanent tattoo.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他決定紋一個永久性的刺青。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We are looking for a permanent job, not a temporary one.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們在找一份永久性的工作，而不是臨時的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他決定紋一個永久性的刺青。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3913,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::permit::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The construction ____ was approved yesterday.","expectedAnswer":"permit","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The construction ____ was approved yesterday.","clozeAnswer":"permit","exampleTranslation":"建築許可證昨天已獲批准。","reference":{"eng":"permit","kk":"/ˈpɜːrmɪt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['許可證', '執照']]","chEntries":["許可證","執照"],"practiceMeaning":"建築許可證昨天已獲批准。","analysis":"此為名