sis":"此字為形容詞，構詞自poet（詩人）+ -ic（形容詞字尾，表示「關於……的；具有……性質的」）。poet源自古希臘語poiētēs（創作者，詩人），來自poiein（製作；創造）。-ic字尾源自拉丁語-icus。因此，poetic的核心語義是指「與詩歌有關的」，或「具有詩歌的特質」，例如優美、富有想像力、富含情感等。語意演變上，從「詩歌的」具體意義，擴展到「富含詩意」的抽象描述。","definition":"1. relating to or characteristic of poets or poetry; 2. having an appropriate quality or style for poetry; 3. having an imaginative or expressive quality.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The sunset cast a poetic glow over the landscape.\",\n    \"ch\": \"夕陽為大地投下詩意的光輝。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She wrote a poetic description of her childhood.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她寫了一段詩意般地描述她的童年。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The poem uses simple language but has a powerful poetic effect.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這首詩語言樸素，卻有強烈的詩意效果。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她寫了一段詩意般地描述她的童年。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4213,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::police::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He reported the incident to the ____.","expectedAnswer":"police","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He reported the incident to the ____.","clozeAnswer":"police","exampleTranslation":"他向警方報告了該事件。","reference":{"eng":"police","kk":"/pəˈliːs/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['警察；警務人員'], ['（尤指）警察部隊；警局']]","chEntries":["警察","警務人員","警察部隊","警局"],"practiceMeaning":"他向警方報告了該事件。","analysis":"源自古法語 police，意為“政府，管理，公民事務”，來自拉丁語 politia，'polis'（城市）。原指政府的組織或行政機構。在17世紀，'police' 開始指維持公共秩序的機構，即警察。'Police' 作為集合名詞，指整個警察隊伍。","definition":"The civil force of a state, responsible for the maintenance of public order, the prevention and detection of crime, etc.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police are investigating the crime.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警方正在調查這起罪案。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He reported the incident to the police.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他向警方報告了該事件。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police headquarters is located downtown.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警察總部設在市中心。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他向警方報告了該事件。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3909,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::politics::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The election results will have a significant impact on the country's ____.","expectedAnswer":"politics","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The election results will have a significant impact on the country's ____.","clozeAnswer":"politics","exampleTranslation":"選舉結果將對國家的政治產生重大影響。","reference":{"eng":"politics","kk":"/ˈpɑːlɪtɪks/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['政治']]","chEntries":["政治"],"practiceMeaning":"選舉結果將對國家的政治產生重大影響。","analysis":"源自古希臘 'politika'，'polis' (city, state) 的複數形式。指關於政府、國家、權力、政策等事務的學問或活動。","definition":"the activities associated with the governance of a country or other area, especially the debate or conflict among individuals or parties having or hoping to achieve power.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is very interested in politics.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對政治很感興趣。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The election results will have a significant impact on the country's politics.\",\n    \"ch\": \"選舉結果將對國家的政治產生重大影響。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"選舉結果將對國家的政治產生重大影響。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5594,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l7::population::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The survey aims to gather data on the entire adult ____.","expectedAnswer":"population","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The survey aims to gather data on the entire adult ____.","clozeAnswer":"population","exampleTranslation":"這項調查旨在收集有關所有成年居民的數據。","reference":{"eng":"population","kk":"ˌpɑpjəˈleɪʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[['人口'], ['居民'], ['（特定區域的）總數']]","chEntries":["人口","居民","總數"],"practiceMeaning":"這項調查旨在收集有關所有成年居民的數據。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'populus'（人民），經由古法語 'pople' 進入中古英語。構詞上，'population' 是由詞根 'popul-'（人民）加上名詞化字尾 '-ation' 所組成。'-ation' 字尾通常將動詞轉換為名詞，表示狀態、過程或結果。在此字中，它表示「人民的總體」或「人口的狀態」。原始語意指向「人民」，後來演變為指「居住在特定地區的所有居民的總數」。","definition":"1. All the inhabitants of a particular place; 2. The action or process of forming or being formed into a group, body, or community.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The population of the city has grown rapidly in recent years.\",\n    \"ch\": \"近年來，這座城市的人口快速增長。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The survey aims to gather data on the entire adult population.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這項調查旨在收集有關所有成年居民的數據。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這項調查旨在收集有關所有成年居民的數據。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6187,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::porch::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The house had a wide front ____.","expectedAnswer":"porch","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The house had a wide front ____.","clozeAnswer":"porch","exampleTranslation":"這房子有一個寬敞的前門廊。","reference":{"eng":"porch","kk":"pɔrtʃ","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"門廊\"  ],  [    \"陽台\"  ],  [    \"走廊\"  ]]","chEntries":["門廊","陽台","走廊"],"practiceMeaning":"這房子有一個寬敞的前門廊。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 porche，最終源自拉丁語 porticus，意為「有柱子的走廊、迴廊」，與 porta「門」相關。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作為名詞，其核心語義是指「房屋入口處有頂的、開放式的區域」。詞源中的「門」和「走廊」概念直接體現了此義。","definition":"1. a covered shelter projecting in front of the entrance of a building; 2. a veranda or balcony.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They sat on the porch watching the rain.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們坐在門廊上看著雨。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The house had a wide front porch.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這房子有一個寬敞的前門廊。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He stood on the porch, waiting for her.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他站在門廊上等她。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The porch swing was comfortable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"門廊的吊椅很舒服。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這房子有一個寬敞的前門廊。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4188,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::practically::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ speaking, we don't have enough time.","expectedAnswer":"Practically","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ speaking, we don't have enough time.","clozeAnswer":"Practically","exampleTranslation":"就實際情況而言，我們時間不夠。","reference":{"eng":"practically","kk":"/ˈpræktɪkli/","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['實際上；差不多'], ['就實際而言']]","chEntries":["實際上","差不多","就實際而言"],"practiceMeaning":"就實際情況而言，我們時間不夠。","analysis":"由形容詞 'practical' 加上副詞後綴 '-ly' 構成。'Practical' 源自拉丁語 practicus，意為“實踐的”。'Practically' 的核心意思接近於“在實際操作或結果上”。1. “實際上；差不多”表示結果或狀態非常接近真實，幾乎等同。2. “就實際而言”強調從實用或操作的角度來看。","definition":"1. in a way that relates to practice or action rather than theory; 2. in a way that is almost or very nearly the case; virtually.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The job is practically finished.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這份工作實際上已經完成了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Practically speaking, we don't have enough time.\",\n    \"ch\": \"就實際情況而言，我們時間不夠。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was practically impossible to get tickets.\",\n    \"ch\": \"拿到票幾乎是不可能的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"就實際情況而言，我們時間不夠。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4113,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::previous::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This is the ____ owner's phone number.","expectedAnswer":"previous","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This is the ____ owner's phone number.","clozeAnswer":"previous","exampleTranslation":"這是前任主人的電話號碼。","reference":{"eng":"previous","kk":"/ˈpriːviəs/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['先前的', '以前的'], ['（順序、時間或地位）前面的']]","chEntries":["先前的","以前的","前面的"],"practiceMeaning":"這是前任主人的電話號碼。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 praevius，由 prae-（在...之前）+ via（道路）組成，原意為「走在前面的」。引申為在時間、順序或重要性上「先於」某事或某物。","definition":"1. existing or happening before the present time or in the past; 2. coming before something else in order or importance","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has no previous experience in this field.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在這個領域沒有先前經驗。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is the previous owner's phone number.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是前任主人的電話號碼。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We discussed this issue in the previous meeting.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們在上次會議中討論了這個問題。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是前任主人的電話號碼。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4210,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::price::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He learned the hard way the ____ of dishonesty.","expectedAnswer":"price","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He learned the hard way the ____ of dishonesty.","clozeAnswer":"price","exampleTranslation":"他通過慘痛的教訓明白了不誠實的代價。","reference":{"eng":"price","kk":"/praɪs/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['價格'], ['（為獲得某物所付出的）代價']]","chEntries":["價格","代價"],"practiceMeaning":"他通過慘痛的教訓明白了不誠實的代價。","analysis":"源自古法語 pris，意為“獎勵，價值”，來自拉丁語 pretium（價格，價值）。核心是某物或某事的價值評估。1. “價格”是指商品或服務的貨幣價值。2. “代價”是抽象意義，指為了達成某事而必須付出的努力、犧牲或其他成本。","definition":"1. the amount of money expected, required, or given in payment for something; 2. the cost, especially in terms of effort or sacrifice, incurred in achieving or obtaining something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"What is the price of this book?\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本書的價格是多少？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He learned the hard way the price of dishonesty.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他通過慘痛的教訓明白了不誠實的代價。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The price of success is hard work.\",\n    \"ch\": \"成功的代價是辛勤的工作。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他通過慘痛的教訓明白了不誠實的代價。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5327,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l1::prison::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ was overcrowded.","expectedAnswer":"prison","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ was overcrowded.","clozeAnswer":"prison","exampleTranslation":"這座監獄過於擁擠。","reference":{"eng":"prison","kk":"ˈprɪzən","tense":"n.","ch":"[['監獄'], ['牢房'], ['拘留所']]","chEntries":["監獄","牢房","拘留所"],"practiceMeaning":"這座監獄過於擁擠。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 prisun，來自拉丁語 prensio（一種被抓住的狀態、捕獲），進一步來自拉丁語 prehendere（抓住）。構詞上，prehend- 是字根，表示「抓住、握住」，-sion 是拉丁語的抽象名詞字尾，表示「狀態或行為」。原始語意為「被抓住的地方」或「被捕的狀態」。現代語意為「關押犯人的機構」，即監獄。亦可作動詞使用。","definition":"a building where people are legally kept as a punishment for a crime they have committed or while they are waiting to be judged for a crime; a place where people are kept if they are guilty of a crime.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was sent to prison for ten years.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他被判入獄十年。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The prison was overcrowded.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座監獄過於擁擠。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這座監獄過於擁擠。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3894,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::probable::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ cause of the accident is mechanical failure.","expectedAnswer":"probable","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ cause of the accident is mechanical failure.","clozeAnswer":"probable","exampleTranslation":"事故的可能原因是機械故障。","reference":{"eng":"probable","kk":"/ˈprɑːbəbl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['可能的', '很可能的']]","chEntries":["可能的","很可能的"],"practiceMeaning":"事故的可能原因是機械故障。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'probabilis'，'probare' (to approve, to test) 的衍生詞。核心是「可驗證的」、「可信的」。引申為有很大可能性發生的，或可以推斷為真的。","definition":"likely to happen or be true.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It is probable that it will rain tomorrow.\",\n    \"ch\": \"明天很可能會下雨。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The probable cause of the accident is mechanical failure.\",\n    \"ch\": \"事故的可能原因是機械故障。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A probable outcome is that prices will increase.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一個可能結果是價格會上漲。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"事故的可能原因是機械故障。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3884,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::process::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"What is the ____ for applying for a visa?","expectedAnswer":"process","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"What is the ____ for applying for a visa?","clozeAnswer":"process","exampleTranslation":"申請簽證的程序是什麼？","reference":{"eng":"process","kk":"/ˈprɑːsɛs/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['過程', '程序'], ['手續']]","chEntries":["過程","程序","手續"],"practiceMeaning":"申請簽證的程序是什麼？","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'processus'，'pro-' (forward) + 'cedere' (to go)。核心是「向前進行」。指一系列連續發生的事件、步驟或操作，以達成某種結果。","definition":"a series of actions or steps taken in order to achieve a particular end.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The manufacturing process is complex.\",\n    \"ch\": \"製造過程很複雜。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"What is the process for applying for a visa?\",\n    \"ch\": \"申請簽證的程序是什麼？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The digestion process breaks down food.\",\n    \"ch\": \"消化過程分解食物。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"申請簽證的程序是什麼？","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4212,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::profit::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It's in our best interest to maximize ____.","expectedAnswer":"profit","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It's in our best interest to maximize ____.","clozeAnswer":"profit","exampleTranslation":"我們的最大利益在於將利潤最大化。","reference":{"eng":"profit","kk":"/ˈprɒfɪt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['利潤；收益'], ['好處；益處']]","chEntries":["利潤","收益","好處","益處"],"practiceMeaning":"我們的最大利益在於將利潤最大化。","analysis":"源自古法語 profit，意為“好處，進步”，來自拉丁語 profectus，'pro-'（向前）+ 'facere'（做）。字面意思是“向前做”，引申為“進步，成就，好處”。1. “利潤”是商業和金融領域的核心含義。2. “好處；益處”是更廣泛的意義，指任何有益的結果。","definition":"1. a financial gain, especially the difference between the amount earned and the amount spent in buying, operating, or producing something; 2. an advantage or benefit gained from something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company made a large profit last year.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司去年盈利頗豐。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's in our best interest to maximize profit.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們的最大利益在於將利潤最大化。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He found great profit in studying history.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在研究歷史中發現了很多益處。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們的最大利益在於將利潤最大化。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5339,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l1::profound::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He is a scholar of ____ learning.","expectedAnswer":"profound","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He is a scholar of ____ learning.","clozeAnswer":"profound","exampleTranslation":"他是一位學識淵博的學者。","reference":{"eng":"profound","kk":"prəˈfaʊnd","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['深刻的'], ['深遠的'], ['巨大的'], ['淵博的']]","chEntries":["深刻的","深遠的","巨大的","淵博的"],"practiceMeaning":"他是一位學識淵博的學者。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 profundus，意為「深的」，來自 pro-（往前）+ fundus（底部）。構詞上，pro- 表示「往前」，fund- 是字根，來自 fundus（底部、深處）。原始語意為「從底部往下很深」。現代語意上，用於形容「深刻的思想、情感、影響」或「淵博的知識」，強調其深度與廣度，如同深海一樣。","definition":"very great or intense; having or showing great knowledge or insight.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The book made a profound impact on her thinking.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本書對她的思考產生了深刻的影響。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a scholar of profound learning.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一位學識淵博的學者。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他是一位學識淵博的學者。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5141,"wordRef":"字彙王::u62::prolong::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They tried to ____ the discussion.","expectedAnswer":"prolong","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They tried to ____ the discussion.","clozeAnswer":"prolong","exampleTranslation":"他們試圖延長討論的時間。","reference":{"eng":"prolong","kk":"prəˈlɔːŋ","tense":"v.","ch":"[['延長'], ['拖延']]","chEntries":["延長","拖延"],"practiceMeaning":"他們試圖延長討論的時間。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 prolongare，由 pro-（向前、提前）+ longus（長）組成。核心語意是「使變得更長」或「向前延伸」。引申為「延長時間、延續」。","definition":"extend the duration of (something); lengthen.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The delay will prolong the construction period.\",\n    \"ch\": \"延誤將延長建設