n    \"ch\": \"他用一根長桿釣魚。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The king carried a royal rod.\",\n    \"ch\": \"國王手持權杖。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"國王手持權杖。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U62"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4172,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::role::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The internet plays a vital ____ in our lives.","expectedAnswer":"role","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The internet plays a vital ____ in our lives.","clozeAnswer":"role","exampleTranslation":"網際網路在我們的生活中扮演著至關重要的作用。","reference":{"eng":"role","kk":"/roʊl/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['角色'], ['作用', '職責']]","chEntries":["角色","作用","職責"],"practiceMeaning":"網際網路在我們的生活中扮演著至關重要的作用。","analysis":"源自古法語 rolle（捲軸，列表，記錄），後引申為戲劇中的演員角色，再擴展到任何職責或功能。","definition":"1. the function assumed or part played by a person or thing in a particular situation or activity; 2. a part played by an actor or actress","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She plays a significant role in the company.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在公司中扮演著重要的角色。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The internet plays a vital role in our lives.\",\n    \"ch\": \"網際網路在我們的生活中扮演著至關重要的作用。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has the lead role in the play.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在戲劇中擔任主角。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"網際網路在我們的生活中扮演著至關重要的作用。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5564,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::roughly::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He explained the plan ____.","expectedAnswer":"roughly","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He explained the plan ____.","clozeAnswer":"roughly","exampleTranslation":"他粗略地解釋了計畫。","reference":{"eng":"roughly","kk":"ˈrʌfli","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['大致上'], ['粗略地'], ['約略地']]","chEntries":["大致上","粗略地","約略地"],"practiceMeaning":"他粗略地解釋了計畫。","analysis":"此字由形容詞 \"rough\" 加上副詞字尾 \"-ly\" 構成。\"rough\" 的詞源較複雜，可能源自古諾爾斯語 \"hruggr\"（rough, coarse，粗糙的），或與原始日耳曼語 \\*ruhhaz（rough，粗糙的）有關。其原始語義與「粗糙、不平滑」有關。因此，\"roughly\" 作為副詞，主要有兩層語義：一是形容「以粗糙、不精確的方式」進行，例如 \"roughly handled\"（被粗魯地對待）；二是形容「不精確、大致的程度」，例如 \"roughly 100 people\"（大約 100 人）。這種語義上的演變是從「物理上的不平滑、不精細」延伸到「抽象上的不精確、不詳細」。","definition":"1. In a way that is approximate or not exact; 2. In a way that is harsh or violent.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There were roughly 50 people at the meeting.\",\n    \"ch\": \"會議上大約有 50 人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He explained the plan roughly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他粗略地解釋了計畫。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The box was roughly made.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個盒子做得很粗糙。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他粗略地解釋了計畫。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5358,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l1::rumor::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Don't believe every ____ you hear.","expectedAnswer":"rumor","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Don't believe every ____ you hear.","clozeAnswer":"rumor","exampleTranslation":"不要相信你聽到的每一個謠言。","reference":{"eng":"rumor","kk":"ˈruːmər","tense":"n.","ch":"[['謠言'], ['傳聞']]","chEntries":["謠言","傳聞"],"practiceMeaning":"不要相信你聽到的每一個謠言。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 rumour，來自拉丁語 rumor，意為「喧囂、叫喊、傳聞」。原始語意為「人群的嘈雜聲」，引申為「未經證實的、廣泛流傳的消息」。構詞上，rum- 是字根，表示「叫喊、喧鬧」。","definition":"a piece of information that is spread from person to person without any source or evidence of its truth; a current story or report of uncertain origin.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There's a rumor that the company will be sold.\",\n    \"ch\": \"有傳言說公司將被出售。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Don't believe every rumor you hear.\",\n    \"ch\": \"不要相信你聽到的每一個謠言。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"不要相信你聽到的每一個謠言。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4145,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::salary::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company offers a competitive ____.","expectedAnswer":"salary","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company offers a competitive ____.","clozeAnswer":"salary","exampleTranslation":"這家公司提供有競爭力的薪資。","reference":{"eng":"salary","kk":"/ˈsæləri/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['薪水', '薪金']]","chEntries":["薪水","薪金"],"practiceMeaning":"這家公司提供有競爭力的薪資。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 salarium（羅馬士兵領取的食鹽津貼），後引申為「報酬」。核心概念是「為工作定期支付的固定金錢」。","definition":"a fixed regular payment, typically paid on a monthly or biweekly basis but often expressed as an annual sum, made by an employer to an employee","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her annual salary is $50,000.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的年薪是五萬美元。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company offers a competitive salary.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司提供有競爭力的薪資。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He negotiated a higher salary.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他談判爭取到了更高的薪水。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這家公司提供有競爭力的薪資。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U5、L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5487,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::sample::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The scientist took a blood ____ for analysis.","expectedAnswer":"sample","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The scientist took a blood ____ for analysis.","clozeAnswer":"sample","exampleTranslation":"科學家抽取了血液樣本進行分析。","reference":{"eng":"sample","kk":"ˈsæmpəl","tense":"n.","ch":"[['樣本'], ['樣品'], ['範例']]","chEntries":["樣本","樣品","範例"],"practiceMeaning":"科學家抽取了血液樣本進行分析。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 'essample'，意為「範例、例子」，來自拉丁語 'exemplum'（例子、範本）。'Exemplum' 是由 'ex-'（出）和 'templum'（樣板、模型）構成。在中古英語中，'sample' 是一個非標準形式，後來演變成現代的 'sample'。'Sample' 作名詞，指「為了代表整體而取出的部分」，用於檢驗、展示或研究。核心語意是「代表整體的一部分」。","definition":"1. A small part or quantity intended to show what the whole is like.; 2. A specimen or example.; 3. A representative part or a single item from a larger whole.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Would you like to try a sample of our new cheese?\",\n    \"ch\": \"您想嚐嚐我們的起司樣本嗎？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The scientist took a blood sample for analysis.\",\n    \"ch\": \"科學家抽取了血液樣本進行分析。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is just a sample of his work.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這只是他作品的一個範例。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"科學家抽取了血液樣本進行分析。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4553,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::satisfactory::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Her performance in the exam was ____.","expectedAnswer":"satisfactory","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Her performance in the exam was ____.","clozeAnswer":"satisfactory","exampleTranslation":"她在考試中的表現尚可。","reference":{"eng":"satisfactory","kk":"/ˌsætɪsˈfæktəri/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['滿意的', '令人滿意的'], ['合格的', '令人滿意的']]","chEntries":["滿意的","令人滿意的","合格的"],"practiceMeaning":"她在考試中的表現尚可。","analysis":"由 'satisfy' (使滿意) 加上形容詞字尾 '-ory' (表示具有某種性質或傾向) 構成。核心概念是能滿足需求或期望。\n    1. 滿意的、令人滿意的：指結果、表現等達到了期望或要求，讓人感到高興或認可。\n    2. 合格的、令人滿意的：指事物達到了基本的標準，雖然不一定突出，但足以接受。","definition":"1. fulfilling expectations or needs adequately.; 2. acceptable and meeting the required standards.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The results of the experiment were satisfactory.\",\n    \"ch\": \"實驗結果是令人滿意的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her performance in the exam was satisfactory.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在考試中的表現尚可。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We are pleased with the satisfactory progress made so far.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們對迄今為止令人滿意的進展感到高興。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她在考試中的表現尚可。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4342,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::scale::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The thermometer has a ____ from 0 to 100 degrees.","expectedAnswer":"scale","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The thermometer has a ____ from 0 to 100 degrees.","clozeAnswer":"scale","exampleTranslation":"溫度計的刻度從0到100度。","reference":{"eng":"scale","kk":"/skeɪl/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['規模；尺度'], ['（測量儀器的）刻度'], ['（魚、爬蟲等的）鱗'], ['級別；等級']]","chEntries":["規模","尺度","刻度","鱗","級別","等級"],"practiceMeaning":"溫度計的刻度從0到100度。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'scala'，意為 'ladder, staircase, scale'。1. 指事物的『大小、範圍』，即『規模、尺度』。2. 指測量儀器上的『刻度、標尺』。3. 指魚類、爬行動物體表的『鱗片』。4. 指事物系統化的『等級、級別』。","definition":"the size or extent of something; a series of marks or lines at fixed distances on a ruler, thermometer, etc., showing measurements; one of the small, flat plates that cover the skin of fish and reptiles; a system of measuring the size or amount of something","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The project was carried out on a large scale.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個專案是以大規模進行的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The thermometer has a scale from 0 to 100 degrees.\",\n    \"ch\": \"溫度計的刻度從0到100度。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The fish's scales shimmered in the light.\",\n    \"ch\": \"魚鱗在燈光下閃閃發光。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company is trying to move up the scale of quality.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司正試圖提升品質等級。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"溫度計的刻度從0到100度。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5311,"wordRef":"字彙王::u63::scar::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The war left a deep ____ on the nation's psyche.","expectedAnswer":"scar","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The war left a deep ____ on the nation's psyche.","clozeAnswer":"scar","exampleTranslation":"戰爭在國家心理上留下了深刻的創傷。","reference":{"eng":"scar","kk":"skɑːr","tense":"n.","ch":"[['疤痕'], ['（過去經歷留下的）創傷、傷痕']]","chEntries":["疤痕","創傷、傷痕"],"practiceMeaning":"戰爭在國家心理上留下了深刻的創傷。","analysis":"此字源自古諾爾斯語 'skor'（切痕，傷疤），或與古英語 'scar'（傷疤）同源，最終可能與原始印歐語根 '*sker-'（to cut）有關。核心語意是「皮膚因創傷癒合後留下的痕跡」。此語意可引申為精神上的創傷或難以磨滅的印記。","definition":"a mark left on the skin or in the tissue of a wound or injury; a lasting mark or trace.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has a scar on his forehead from a childhood accident.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他額頭上有童年事故留下的疤痕。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The war left a deep scar on the nation's psyche.\",\n    \"ch\": \"戰爭在國家心理上留下了深刻的創傷。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"戰爭在國家心理上留下了深刻的創傷。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U63"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4059,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::scary::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The sudden noise was quite ____.","expectedAnswer":"scary","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The sudden noise was quite ____.","clozeAnswer":"scary","exampleTranslation":"突然的聲音相當可怕。","reference":{"eng":"scary","kk":"/ˈskɛri/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['嚇人的', '可怕的']]","chEntries":["嚇人的","可怕的"],"practiceMeaning":"突然的聲音相當可怕。","analysis":"源自動詞 'scare' (害怕，驚嚇)，加上 '-y' 後綴。'scare' 的詞源可能與北歐語言有關，意為「驚嚇」。核心是引起恐懼。因此，'scary' 指「使人感到害怕的」。","definition":"frightening or causing fear","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"那是一部嚇人的電影！\",\n    \"eng\": \"That was a scary movie!\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"突然的聲音相當可怕。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The sudden noise was quite scary.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他講了一個關於鬼的恐怖故事。\",\n    \"eng\": \"He told a scary story about ghosts.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"突然的聲音相當可怕。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5579,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::scheme::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The government introduced a new housing ____.","expectedAnswer":"scheme","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The government introduced a new housing ____.","clozeAnswer":"scheme","exampleTranslation":"政府推出了一個新的住房方案。","reference":{"eng":"scheme","kk":"skim","tense":"n.","ch":"[['計畫'], ['方案'], ['陰謀'], ['體系']]","chEntries":["計畫","方案","陰謀","體系"],"practiceMeaning":"政府推出了一個新的住房方案。","analysis":"此字源自古希臘語 \"schēma\"（shape, form, appearance, plan，形狀，形式，外觀，計畫），該詞源於 \"echō\"（to have, to hold，擁有，持有）。\"schēma\" 的核心語義是「事物的形式或架構」。在中古英語中，\"scheme\"（原為 \"sceme\"）借用於古法語 \"esqueme\"，繼承了希臘語的「形式、架構」概念。它的語義發展廣泛：指「一個有組織的、事先計畫好的行動藍圖」（a plan or program of action）；指「一個系統或結構」（a system or framework）；也可能帶有負面含義，指「一個秘密的、不誠實的計畫」（a secret plot or conspiracy）。","definition":"1. A plan or program of action; 2. A system of rules, principles, or methods; 3. A secret plan made by a group of people to do something illegal or harmful.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They have a scheme to reduce costs.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們有一個削減成本的計畫。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government introduced a new housing scheme.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府推出了一個新的住房方案。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was involved in a criminal scheme.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他捲入了一個犯罪陰謀。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"政府推出了一個新的住房方案。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4426,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u9::scholar::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He was a brilliant ____ who won a scholarship to Oxford.","expectedAnswer":"scholar","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He was a brilliant ____ who won a scholarship to Oxford.","clozeAnswer":"scholar","exampleTranslation":"他是一位傑出的學者，獲得獎學金進入牛津大學。","reference":{"eng":"scholar","kk":"/ˈskɒlər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['學者'], ['獎學金獲得者']]","chEntries":["學者","獎學金獲得者"],"practiceMeaning":"他是一位傑出的學者，獲得獎學金進入牛津大學。","analysis":"詞源自古英語 'scolere'，意為「學生」，源自拉丁語 'schola' (school, lecture)。指在某一學科領域有深入研究並有權威的專家，也指獲得獎學金的學生。","definition":"a specialist in a particular subject, especially one who conducts academic research; a person who studies at a school or college, especially a university, who receives a scholarship.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The book is written by a renowned scholar of ancient languages.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本書由一位著名的古代語言學者撰寫。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was a brilliant scholar who won a scholarship to Oxford.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一位傑出的學者，獲得獎學金進入牛津大學。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他是一位傑出的學者，獲得獎學金進入牛津大學。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6092,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::scrap::vt","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The government decided to ____ the controversial policy.","expectedAnswer":"scrap","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The government decided to ____ the controversial policy.","clozeAnswer":"scrap","exampleTranslation":"政府決定取消這項有爭議的政策。","reference":{"eng":"scrap","kk":"skræp","tense":"vt.","ch":"[  [    \"報廢\"  ],  [    \"廢棄\"  ],  [    \"捨棄\"  ],  [    \"（尤指）取消（計畫）\"  ]]","chEntries":["報廢","廢棄","捨棄","取消"],"practiceMeaning":"政府決定取消這項有爭議的政策。","analysis":"此字源自 scrap 的名詞用法，意為「零碎的、無用的部分」。作為及物動詞，核心語義是「將……視為廢棄物，從而處理掉」。引申為「捨棄」、「廢棄」，或尤其指「取消（計畫、協議）」。","definition":"1. discard or get rid of (something no longer useful or wanted); 2. abandon or cancel (a plan, policy, or agreement).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The old factory was eventually scrapped.\",\n    \"ch\": \"舊工廠最終被廢棄了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government decided to scrap the controversial policy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府決定取消這項有爭議的政策。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They had to scrap their holiday plans due to the storm.\",\n    \"ch\": \"由於風暴，他們不得不取消了假期計畫。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"政府決定取消這項有爭議的政策。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4701,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::seal::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The package was secured with a tamper-proof ____.","expectedAnswer":"seal","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The package was secured with a tamper-proof ____.","clozeAnswer":"seal","exampleTranslation":"包裹用了一個防損封條固定。","reference":{"eng":"seal","kk":"/ˈsil/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['印章'], ['封條'], ['（海豹）'], ['密封物']]","chEntries":["印章","封條","密封物"],"practiceMeaning":"包裹用了一個防損封條固定。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 *sigillum*（小標記），與 'sign'（標誌）同源。第一義指用於壓印圖案或文字的工具，常代表權威或認證。第二義指用於封閉或保護的材料。第三義指一種海洋哺乳動物。第四義指用於防止滲漏的裝置。","definition":"1. A stamp or device used to impress a mark or design, typically for authentication or security. 2. A piece of wax or other material used to fasten or secure something. 3. A marine mammal of the order Pinnipedia. 4. A device or material used to prevent the passage of liquid or gas.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The document bore the official seal of the king.\",\n    \"ch\": \"文件蓋有國王的官方印章。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The package was secured with a tamper-proof seal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"包裹用了一個防損封條固定。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We saw seals basking on the rocks.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們看到海豹在岩石上曬太陽。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The rubber seal around the door was worn out.\",\n    \"ch\": \"門周圍的橡膠密封圈已經磨損了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"包裹用了一個防損封條固定。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U17、L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4054,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::security::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need to ensure the ____ of our data.","expectedAnswer":"security","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need to ensure the ____ of our data.","clozeAnswer":"security","exampleTranslation":"我們需要確保我們數據的安全。","reference":{"eng":"security","kk":"/sɪˈkjʊrəti/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['安全', '保安'], ['保障', '保證'], ['證券', '股票']]","chEntries":["安全","保安","保障","保證","證券","股票"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要確保我們數據的安全。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'securitas'，由 'se-' (without) + 'cura' (care, anxiety) 構成，字面意思是「沒有憂慮」。核心是「安全」、「沒有危險」。因此，'security' 指「安全」的狀態，也指「保障」和「安全措施」。第四個義項「證券」則是由「保障」、「保證」延伸而來，指能提供價值保障的財產證明，如股票、債券。","definition":"1. the state of being safe and protected from harm or danger; 2. measures taken to ensure safety; 3. the confidence that something is safe or certain; 4. a person or thing that provides safety or protection; 5. a document showing that a person has a right to claim a sum of money or property","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"這家旅館為客人提供優良的保安服務。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The hotel provides excellent security for its guests.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要確保我們數據的安全。\",\n    \"eng\": \"We need to ensure the security of our data.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他投資了股票和證券。\",\n    \"eng\": \"He invested in stocks and securities.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要確保我們數據的安全。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5542,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l5::selfless::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The volunteer performed ____ acts of kindness.","expectedAnswer":"selfless","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The volunteer performed ____ acts of kindness.","clozeAnswer":"selfless","exampleTranslation":"這位志願者做出了忘我的善舉。","reference":{"eng":"selfless","kk":"ˈselfles","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['無私的'], ['忘我的']]","chEntries":["無私的","忘我的"],"practiceMeaning":"這位志願者做出了忘我的善舉。","analysis":"此字由 'self' (自己) 加上否定字尾 '-less' 構成。'-less' 源自古英語，表示「沒有……」。'self' 是指「自我、個人」。因此，'selfless' 的構詞結構清晰地表明其含義是「沒有自我意識的」、「不考慮自己的」。語意上，它描述了一種將他人福祉置於自己利益之上的品質，強調利他主義和忘我精神。","definition":"not thinking of yourself first; unselfish.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her selfless dedication to the cause inspired many.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對事業的無私奉獻激勵了許多人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The volunteer performed selfless acts of kindness.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位志願者做出了忘我的善舉。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這位志願者做出了忘我的善舉。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5314,"wordRef":"字彙王::u63::senator::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She was elected as a ____.","expectedAnswer":"senator","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She was elected as a ____.","clozeAnswer":"senator","exampleTranslation":"她被選為參議員。","reference":{"eng":"senator","kk":"ˈsɛnətər","tense":"n.","ch":"[['參議員']]","chEntries":["參議員"],"practiceMeaning":"她被選為參議員。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'senator'（參議員），來自 'senex'（老的，長者）。構詞上，'sen-' 為詞根，'-ator' 為表示「人」的後綴。核心語意指「長者」，引申為在古代羅馬元老院或現代議會中的「參議員」，因其通常是較有經驗或地位較高的人士。","definition":"a member of a senate, especially the upper house of the United States Congress.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The senator gave a speech on national security.\",\n    \"ch\": \"參議員就國家安全發表了演講。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She was elected as a senator.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她被選為參議員。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她被選為參議員。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U63"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4266,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::senior::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She graduated as a ____ from the university.","expectedAnswer":"senior","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She graduated as a ____ from the university.","clozeAnswer":"senior","exampleTranslation":"她從大學畢業時是一名高年級生。","reference":{"eng":"senior","kk":"/ˈsiːnjər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['長者'], ['前輩'], ['（大學）高年級學生'], ['（公司）資深員工']]","chEntries":["長者","前輩","高年級學生","資深員工"],"practiceMeaning":"她從大學畢業時是一名高年級生。","analysis":"由形容詞 'senior' 衍生而來，用作名詞時，指代比自己年長、職位較高或年級較高的個人。與 'junior' 相對。","definition":"a person who is older than another person, or who has a higher rank or position.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The seniors in the club are expected to mentor the juniors.\",\n    \"ch\": \"俱樂部的前輩們被期望指導晚輩。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She graduated as a senior from the university.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她從大學畢業時是一名高年級生。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她從大學畢業時是一名高年級生。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5860,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::sensation::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He lost all ____ in his legs.","expectedAnswer":"sensation","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He lost all ____ in his legs.","clozeAnswer":"sensation","exampleTranslation":"他失去雙腿的所有感覺。","reference":{"eng":"sensation","kk":"senˈseɪʃn","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"感覺\"  ],  [    \"知覺\"  ],  [    \"轟動\"  ],  [    \"感動\"  ],  [    \"感覺器官\"  ]]","chEntries":["感覺","知覺","轟動","感動","感覺器官"],"practiceMeaning":"他失去雙腿的所有感覺。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'sensus' (feeling, sense)，是 'sentire' (to feel) 的名詞形式。'Sensation' 的核心語意是指「通過感官獲得的感覺」或「對刺激的反應」。在更廣泛的語境中，它也可以指「引起強烈興趣或興奮的事件」，即「轟動」或「激動人心的事物」。這種語意轉移是由於強烈的感覺往往伴隨著興奮或情感的波動。例如，也可指「一種感覺器官」。","definition":"1. A physical feeling or perception resulting from a stimulus.; 2. An ability to feel, perceive, or experience objects, quality, and actions through the senses.; 3. An event or situation that causes great public interest and excitement.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The news caused a sensation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這消息引起了轟動。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He lost all sensation in his legs.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他失去雙腿的所有感覺。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The new invention was a sensation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這項新發明引起了轟動。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Touch is one of the five basic sensations.\",\n    \"ch\": \"觸覺是五種基本感覺之一。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他失去雙腿的所有感覺。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5406,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l2::severe::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company faced ____ criticism for its environmental policies.","expectedAnswer":"severe","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company faced ____ criticism for its environmental policies.","clozeAnswer":"severe","exampleTranslation":"該公司因其環境政策而面臨嚴厲批評。","reference":{"eng":"severe","kk":"sɪˈvɪər","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['嚴重的'], ['嚴峻的'], ['劇烈的'], ['嚴格的']]","chEntries":["嚴重的","嚴峻的","劇烈的","嚴格的"],"practiceMeaning":"該公司因其環境政策而面臨嚴厲批評。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 severus，意為「嚴肅的、嚴格的、嚴厲的」。核心語意是「程度極高，超出一般標準，令人難以承受」。因此，'severe' 用於描述天氣、疾病、損害、懲罰、批評等，表示其程度非常嚴重，可能造成重大影響。","definition":"1. (of something bad or unpleasant) intense or serious; 2. (of a person or their manner) strict or harsh.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The patient is suffering from a severe infection.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這名病人正在遭受嚴重的感染。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company faced severe criticism for its environmental policies.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司因其環境政策而面臨嚴厲批評。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該公司因其環境政策而面臨嚴厲批評。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4087,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::sexual-discrimination::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She has experienced ____ in the workplace.","expectedAnswer":"sexual discrimination","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She has experienced ____ in the workplace.","clozeAnswer":"sexual discrimination","exampleTranslation":"她在工作場所經歷過性別歧視。","reference":{"eng":"sexual discrimination","kk":"/ˈsɛkʃuəl dɪˌskrɪmɪˈneɪʃən/","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['性別歧視']]","chEntries":["性別歧視"],"practiceMeaning":"她在工作場所經歷過性別歧視。","analysis":"'Sexual' (性別的) 源自拉丁語 'sexus' (sex)。'Discrimination' (歧視) 源自拉丁語 'discriminare' (to distinguish, to separate)，意為「區別對待」。'Sexual discrimination' 指基於性別而產生的不公平對待。","definition":"unfair treatment of someone based on their sex or gender","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"性別歧視在許多國家都是非法的。\",\n    \"eng\": \"Sexual discrimination is illegal in many countries.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"她在工作場所經歷過性別歧視。\",\n    \"eng\": \"She has experienced sexual discrimination in the workplace.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她在工作場所經歷過性別歧視。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4088,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::sexual-harassment::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She reported the incident of ____.","expectedAnswer":"sexual harassment","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She reported the incident of ____.","clozeAnswer":"sexual harassment","exampleTranslation":"她舉報了性騷擾事件。","reference":{"eng":"sexual harassment","kk":"/ˈsɛkʃuəl həˈræsmənt/","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['性騷擾']]","chEntries":["性騷擾"],"practiceMeaning":"她舉報了性騷擾事件。","analysis":"'Sexual' (性別的) 源自拉丁語 'sexus' (sex)。'Harassment' (騷擾) 源自古法語 'haras' (a stud farm)，後來引申為「煩擾」、「侵擾」。'Sexual harassment' 指任何不受歡迎的、與性有關的行為，會冒犯或侮辱他人。","definition":"unwelcome sexual advances, requests for sexual favors, and other verbal or physical conduct of a sexual nature","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"公司有嚴格的反性騷擾政策。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The company has a strict policy against sexual harassment.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"她舉報了性騷擾事件。\",\n    \"eng\": \"She reported the incident of sexual harassment.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她舉報了性騷擾事件。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5477,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::shallow::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His arguments were ____ and lacked evidence.","expectedAnswer":"shallow","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His arguments were ____ and lacked evidence.","clozeAnswer":"shallow","exampleTranslation":"他的論點很膚淺，缺乏證據。","reference":{"eng":"shallow","kk":"ˈʃæloʊ","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['淺的'], ['淺薄的'], ['膚淺的']]","chEntries":["淺的","淺薄的","膚淺的"],"practiceMeaning":"他的論點很膚淺，缺乏證據。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 'schalowe'，可能與古英語 'sceald'（淺水）有關，詞源不太確定，但與「淺」的概念緊密聯繫。'Shallow' 作形容詞，最基本的意思是指「水、容器等深度不大」，與 'deep'（深的）相對。引申義則用於形容「思想、情感、性格等缺乏深度」，即「膚淺的、淺薄的」，這是一種比喻用法，將「水淺」的物理概念類比到「思想不深」的抽象概念。","definition":"1. (Of a body of water or the landscape beneath it)<bos> of little depth.; 2. Not showing any intellectual or emotional depth.; 3. Superficial.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The children played in the shallow end of the pool.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子們在泳池的淺水區玩耍。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His arguments were shallow and lacked evidence.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的論點很膚淺，缺乏證據。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She found his interest in fashion to be rather shallow.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她覺得他對時尚的興趣相當膚淺。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他的論點很膚淺，缺乏證據。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6096,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::sheriff::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ arrived at the scene of the crime.","expectedAnswer":"sheriff","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ arrived at the scene of the crime.","clozeAnswer":"sheriff","exampleTranslation":"警長到達了犯罪現場。","reference":{"eng":"sheriff","kk":"ˈʃɛrɪf","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"警長\"  ]]","chEntries":["警長"],"practiceMeaning":"警長到達了犯罪現場。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 scīrgerefa，由 scīr（郡，行政區）和 gerefa（官員）組成。核心語義是「地區官員」，特別是指在英語國家，負責某個郡或縣的執法官員。現代美式英語中，sheriff 通常指由選民選舉產生的、負責一個郡的治安的官員。","definition":"the chief law enforcement officer in a county.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The sheriff's department is responsible for law enforcement in the county.\",\n    \"ch\": \"郡治安官部門負責該縣的執法工作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The sheriff arrived at the scene of the crime.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警長到達了犯罪現場。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was elected sheriff for his third term.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他第三次當選為警長。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"警長到達了犯罪現場。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4465,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::shiny::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She had ____, dark hair.","expectedAnswer":"shiny","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She had ____, dark hair.","clozeAnswer":"shiny","exampleTranslation":"她有著烏黑光澤的頭髮。","reference":{"eng":"shiny","kk":"/ˈʃaɪni/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['閃亮的'], ['光澤的']]","chEntries":["閃亮的","光澤的"],"practiceMeaning":"她有著烏黑光澤的頭髮。","analysis":"源自 shine (發光)。加上 -y (形容詞後綴)。核心語意是「發出光線」、「有光澤的」。","definition":"1. Giving out or reflecting much light; 2. Bright and polished.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The car was parked in the sun, its surface shiny.\",\n    \"ch\": \"汽車停在陽光下，車身閃閃發光。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She had shiny, dark hair.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她有著烏黑光澤的頭髮。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她有著烏黑光澤的頭髮。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4081,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::shrimp::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He's just a ____ compared to his older brother.","expectedAnswer":"shrimp","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He's just a ____ compared to his older brother.","clozeAnswer":"shrimp","exampleTranslation":"跟他哥哥比起來，他只是個小矮子。","reference":{"eng":"shrimp","kk":"/ʃrɪmp/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['蝦'], ['矮子', '瘦小的人']]","chEntries":["蝦","矮子","瘦小的人"],"practiceMeaning":"跟他哥哥比起來，他只是個小矮子。","analysis":"第一個義項「蝦」的詞源有爭議，可能與斯堪地那維亞語有關，指一種小的水生動物。第二個義項「矮子」、「瘦小的人」則是比喻用法，形容身材矮小、瘦弱，類似蝦的體型。","definition":"1. a small sea creature with ten legs and a shell, that has a long body and tail and is eaten as food; 2. a small or thin person","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"我點了一盤烤蝦。\",\n    \"eng\": \"I ordered a plate of grilled shrimp.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"跟他哥哥比起來，他只是個小矮子。\",\n    \"eng\": \"He's just a shrimp compared to his older brother.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"跟他哥哥比起來，他只是個小矮子。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5511,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l5::sigh::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Her ____ conveyed her disappointment.","expectedAnswer":"sigh","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Her ____ conveyed her disappointment.","clozeAnswer":"sigh","exampleTranslation":"她的嘆息傳達了她的失望。","reference":{"eng":"sigh","kk":"saɪ","tense":"n.","ch":"[['嘆息'], ['嘆氣聲']]","chEntries":["嘆息","嘆氣聲"],"practiceMeaning":"她的嘆息傳達了她的失望。","analysis":"此為動詞 'sigh' 的名詞形式。作為名詞，它指「嘆氣」這個動作或由此發出的聲音。構詞與語意演變與動詞一致，承襲了「表達情緒的呼氣」的概念。","definition":"an audible exhalation expressing sadness, relief, tiredness, or similar emotion.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He let out a long sigh.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他發出了一聲長長的嘆息。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her sigh conveyed her disappointment.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的嘆息傳達了她的失望。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她的嘆息傳達了她的失望。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4144,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::significant::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This is a ____ development in the field.","expectedAnswer":"significant","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This is a ____ development in the field.","clozeAnswer":"significant","exampleTranslation":"這是該領域的一項重要發展。","reference":{"eng":"significant","kk":"/sɪɡˈnɪfɪkənt/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['顯著的', '重要的'], ['（數量）相當大的'], ['意味深長的']]","chEntries":["顯著的","重要的","相當大的","意味深長的"],"practiceMeaning":"這是該領域的一項重要發展。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 significare（意指，表示），由 signum（標誌）+ facere（製造）組成。核心概念是「有重要意義」或「值得注意」。引申為數量上的重大、影響力的強大，或內涵的豐富。","definition":"1. sufficiently great or important to be worthy of attention; noteworthy; 2. having a particular meaning; indicative; 3. large or noticeable","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There has been a significant increase in sales.\",\n    \"ch\": \"銷售額有了顯著增長。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a significant development in the field.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是該領域的一項重要發展。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her contribution played a significant role in the project's success.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的貢獻在項目的成功中起到了重要作用。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是該領域的一項重要發展。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4458,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::similarity::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of their voices made it difficult to tell them apart.","expectedAnswer":"similarity","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of their voices made it difficult to tell them apart.","clozeAnswer":"similarity","exampleTranslation":"他們聲音的相似之處使得很難分辨出彼此。","reference":{"eng":"similarity","kk":"/ˌsɪməˈlæriti/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['相似']]","chEntries":["相似"],"practiceMeaning":"他們聲音的相似之處使得很難分辨出彼此。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 similis，意為「相似的」。加上 -ity (名詞後綴)。核心語意是「兩個或多個事物之間共同的特徵或性質」。","definition":"1. The state or fact of being similar; 2. A point or feature that is shared by two or more things.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There is a striking similarity between the two paintings.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這兩幅畫之間有著驚人的相似之處。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The similarity of their voices made it difficult to tell them apart.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們聲音的相似之處使得很難分辨出彼此。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們聲音的相似之處使得很難分辨出彼此。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4482,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::sin::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Greed is considered a deadly ____.","expectedAnswer":"sin","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Greed is considered a deadly ____.","clozeAnswer":"sin","exampleTranslation":"貪婪被認為是致命的罪惡。","reference":{"eng":"sin","kk":"/sɪn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['罪'], ['罪惡'], ['（行為）過失']]","chEntries":["罪","罪惡","過失"],"practiceMeaning":"貪婪被認為是致命的罪惡。","analysis":"源自古英語 synn。核心語意是「違反道德或宗教準則的行為」。","definition":"1. An act that is regarded in Judaism and Christianity as a transgression of the divine law; 2. An immoral act,SACTION, or thought.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He confessed his sins to the priest.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他向牧師懺悔了自己的罪過。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Greed is considered a deadly sin.\",\n    \"ch\": \"貪婪被認為是致命的罪惡。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"貪婪被認為是致命的罪惡。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U10、L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4475,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::sip::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Enjoy every ____ of your vacation.","expectedAnswer":"sip","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Enjoy every ____ of your vacation.","clozeAnswer":"sip","exampleTranslation":"享受你假期的每一刻。","reference":{"eng":"sip","kk":"/sɪp/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['一小口']]","chEntries":["一小口"],"practiceMeaning":"享受你假期的每一刻。","analysis":"名詞形式，源自動詞 sip。意為「小口喝的量」。","definition":"1. A small mouthful of liquid.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He took a sip of his coffee.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他喝了一小口咖啡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Enjoy every sip of your vacation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"享受你假期的每一刻。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"享受你假期的每一刻。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3871,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::situation::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He found himself in a difficult ____.","expectedAnswer":"situation","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He found himself in a difficult ____.","clozeAnswer":"situation","exampleTranslation":"他發現自己處於一個困難的境地。","reference":{"eng":"situation","kk":"/ˌsɪtʃuˈeɪʃən/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['情況', '局勢'], ['處境'], ['地點', '場所']]","chEntries":["情況","局勢","處境","地點","場所"],"practiceMeaning":"他發現自己處於一個困難的境地。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 ' situs' (site, position)，後經由法語 'situation' 傳入。核心是「位置」或「所處的狀態」。可指一個具體情境的實際狀態、一連串事件的發展，或某人所處的困難/有利的境地。較少見的用法指特定地點。","definition":"1. a set of circumstances or conditions; a state of affairs. 2. a person's position or condition at a particular time. 3. a place or location.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The political situation is very tense.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政治局勢非常緊張。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He found himself in a difficult situation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他發現自己處於一個困難的境地。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company is in a good financial situation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司財務狀況良好。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他發現自己處於一個困難的境地。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5532,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l5::smuggler::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He made a fortune as a diamond ____.","expectedAnswer":"smuggler","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He made a fortune as a diamond ____.","clozeAnswer":"smuggler","exampleTranslation":"他作為鑽石走私者賺了大錢。","reference":{"eng":"smuggler","kk":"ˈsmʌɡlər","tense":"n.","ch":"[['走私者']]","chEntries":["走私者"],"practiceMeaning":"他作為鑽石走私者賺了大錢。","analysis":"此字由動詞 'smuggle' 加上執行者字尾 '-er' 構成。'-er' 是常見的字尾，源自古英語，用於將動詞轉化為指代執行該動作的人或事物。'smuggle' 源自低地德語 'smuggeln'。因此，'smuggler' 的構詞結構清晰地表明其含義是「從事走私活動的人」。語意上，它指進行非法運輸商品或人員活動的人。","definition":"a person who smuggles goods.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The smuggler was arrested at the border.\",\n    \"ch\": \"走私者在邊境被捕。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He made a fortune as a diamond smuggler.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他作為鑽石走私者賺了大錢。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他作為鑽石走私者賺了大錢。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6247,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::snatch::vt","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He managed to ____ a victory in the final seconds.","expectedAnswer":"snatch","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He managed to ____ a victory in the final seconds.","clozeAnswer":"snatch","exampleTranslation":"他在最後幾秒鐘設法贏得了勝利。","reference":{"eng":"snatch","kk":"snætʃ","tense":"vt.","ch":"[  [    \"搶奪\"  ],  [    \"奪取\"  ],  [    \"猛抓住\"  ],  [    \"急忙拿到\"  ]]","chEntries":["搶奪","奪取","猛抓住","急忙拿到"],"practiceMeaning":"他在最後幾秒鐘設法贏得了勝利。","analysis":"此字源自擬聲詞，模仿突然抓住的動作。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作及物動詞時，核心語義是突然、快速地抓住或拿走某物，通常帶有欺騙、暴力或急迫性。也可引申為搶到寶貴的機會或時間。此及物動詞義必須接受詞，例如 snatch a purse、snatch an opportunity、snatch a moment。中文翻譯為「搶奪；奪取；猛抓住；急忙拿到」。","definition":"1. to quickly take something or someone away from a place or person, often by force or trickery; 2. to catch or get something, especially a chance, quickly.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The thief snatched her bag and ran away.\",\n    \"ch\": \"小偷搶走了她的包就跑了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He managed to snatch a victory in the final seconds.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在最後幾秒鐘設法贏得了勝利。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She snatched a quick look at her watch.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她匆忙瞥了一眼手錶。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他在最後幾秒鐘設法贏得了勝利。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3118,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::software::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He is developing new ____ for graphic design.","expectedAnswer":"software","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He is developing new ____ for graphic design.","clozeAnswer":"software","exampleTranslation":"他正在開發用於平面設計的新軟體。","reference":{"eng":"software","kk":"/ˈsɔːftwɛər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['軟體；軟件']]","chEntries":["軟體","軟件"],"practiceMeaning":"他正在開發用於平面設計的新軟體。","analysis":"由 'soft' (soft) + 'ware' (suffix for manufactured goods) 組成。與 'hardware' (硬體) 相對，指非實體的計算機程序。\n1. 軟體；軟件：指計算機系統中用於執行特定任務的程序、數據和指令。","definition":"1. the programs, data, etc. 