t yet known or stated; for some reason.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Somehow, I always manage to find my keys.\",\n    \"ch\": \"不知何故，我總是能找到我的鑰匙。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She will arrive here somehow.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她會以某種方式抵達這裡。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她會以某種方式抵達這裡。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5478,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::species::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Scientists are trying to protect endangered ____.","expectedAnswer":"species","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Scientists are trying to protect endangered ____.","clozeAnswer":"species","exampleTranslation":"科學家正努力保護瀕危物種。","reference":{"eng":"species","kk":"ˈspishiz","tense":"n.","ch":"[['物種'], ['種類']]","chEntries":["物種","種類"],"practiceMeaning":"科學家正努力保護瀕危物種。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'species'，原意是「樣貌、外觀、形式、種類」，也指「圖像、模型」。在科學分類中，它被用來表示「一個物種」，即生物分類學中的一個基本單位，指一群能夠相互繁殖並產生可育後代的生物。'Species' 是單數與複數同形。其詞源 'specere'（看）表明了「種類」的概念是基於「外觀」的區分。核心語意是「一個具有共同特徵、能夠繁殖的生物分類單元」。","definition":"1. A group of living organisms consisting of similar individuals capable of exchanging genes or interbreeding.; 2. A class or kind of persons or things.; 3. A particular kind of.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The Amazon rainforest is home to thousands of species of plants and animals.\",\n    \"ch\": \"亞馬遜雨林是數千種動植物的家園。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Scientists are trying to protect endangered species.\",\n    \"ch\": \"科學家正努力保護瀕危物種。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a rare species of bird.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是稀有的鳥類物種。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"科學家正努力保護瀕危物種。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3301,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::spectacular::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The Grand Canyon offers ____ views.","expectedAnswer":"spectacular","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The Grand Canyon offers ____ views.","clozeAnswer":"spectacular","exampleTranslation":"大峽谷提供了壯觀的景色。","reference":{"eng":"spectacular","kk":"/spɛkˈtækjʊlər/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['壯觀的；引人注目的'], ['精彩的；驚人的']]","chEntries":["壯觀的","引人注目的","精彩的","驚人的"],"practiceMeaning":"大峽谷提供了壯觀的景色。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'spectaculum' (戲劇表演，景象)，由 'spectare' (觀看) 演變而來。指令人印象深刻、引人注目、極為精彩或壯觀的。","definition":"1. beautiful in a dramatic and eye-catching way; 2. very impressive or remarkable.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The fireworks display was spectacular.\",\n    \"ch\": \"煙火表演非常精彩。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The Grand Canyon offers spectacular views.\",\n    \"ch\": \"大峽谷提供了壯觀的景色。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He made a spectacular recovery from his illness.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他從疾病中奇蹟般地康復了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"大峽谷提供了壯觀的景色。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3990,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u3::spice::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He decided to ____ up his routine with a new hobby.","expectedAnswer":"spice","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He decided to ____ up his routine with a new hobby.","clozeAnswer":"spice","exampleTranslation":"他決定用一個新愛好來增加他生活的趣味。","reference":{"eng":"spice","kk":"/spaɪs/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['為...調味'], ['增加...的情趣', '使...更刺激']]","chEntries":["為...調味","增加...的情趣","使...更刺激"],"practiceMeaning":"他決定用一個新愛好來增加他生活的趣味。","analysis":"詞源：同上。動詞形式，指添加香料，或引申為添加趣味、刺激。","definition":"1. flavor with spice; 2. add excitement, interest, or variety to.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She spiced the soup with herbs and spices.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她用香草和香料為湯調味。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He decided to spice up his routine with a new hobby.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他決定用一個新愛好來增加他生活的趣味。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他決定用一個新愛好來增加他生活的趣味。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4570,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::splash::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There was a ____ of ink on the page.","expectedAnswer":"splash","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There was a ____ of ink on the page.","clozeAnswer":"splash","exampleTranslation":"紙上有一灘墨水。","reference":{"eng":"splash","kk":"/splæʃ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['潑濺', '飛濺'], ['（水花）濺起聲'], ['（顏料、墨水等的）一灘', '一抹'], ['（引人注意的）引人注目的事物', '轟動']]","chEntries":["潑濺","飛濺","濺起聲","一灘","一抹","引人注目的事物","轟動"],"practiceMeaning":"紙上有一灘墨水。","analysis":"擬聲詞，模仿水花濺起的聲音。\n    1. 潑濺、飛濺：指液體被拋灑開來的動作或結果。\n    2. 聲音：指水花濺起時發出的聲音。\n    3. 一灘、一抹：指濺灑後在物體表面留下的痕跡。\n    4. 轟動：引申為引起廣泛關注或轟動的事件。","definition":"1. the action or sound of splashing.; 2. a quantity of liquid suddenly or violently dispersed in droplets.; 3. a vivid or striking effect.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The splash of water woke him up.\",\n    \"ch\": \"水花濺起的聲音把他吵醒了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was a splash of ink on the page.\",\n    \"ch\": \"紙上有一灘墨水。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her bold dress made a splash at the party.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她那大膽的洋裝在派對上引起了轟動。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"紙上有一灘墨水。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4193,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::squirrel::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"I saw a ____ burying nuts in the garden.","expectedAnswer":"squirrel","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"I saw a ____ burying nuts in the garden.","clozeAnswer":"squirrel","exampleTranslation":"我看見一隻松鼠在花園裡埋堅果。","reference":{"eng":"squirrel","kk":"/ˈskwɜːrəl/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['松鼠']]","chEntries":["松鼠"],"practiceMeaning":"我看見一隻松鼠在花園裡埋堅果。","analysis":"源自古希臘語 skiouros，意為“影子尾巴”。'skia'（影子）+ 'oura'（尾巴）。此名來自松鼠常將尾巴搭在背上的習性。該詞在14世紀經由古法語 écureuil 進入英語。是一個典型的動物名稱，沒有明顯的引申義，主要指這種哺乳動物。","definition":"A gnawing mammal that typically has a bushy tail and lives in trees.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The squirrel quickly climbed up the tree.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那隻松鼠迅速爬上了樹。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I saw a squirrel burying nuts