"kk":"/ˈsuːəˌsaɪd/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['自殺']]","chEntries":["自殺"],"practiceMeaning":"警方正在調查疑似自殺的案件。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 *suicidium*，由 *suus*（自己）和 *caedere*（殺死）構成。字面意思是「殺死自己」。指故意結束自己生命的行為。","definition":"1. The act or an instance of killing oneself intentionally.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was suffering from severe depression and eventually committed suicide.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他患有嚴重憂鬱症，最終自殺了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police are investigating the suspected suicide.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警方正在調查疑似自殺的案件。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"警方正在調查疑似自殺的案件。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5528,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l5::suitcase::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Please check in your ____ at the counter.","expectedAnswer":"suitcase","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Please check in your ____ at the counter.","clozeAnswer":"suitcase","exampleTranslation":"請在櫃檯托運行李箱。","reference":{"eng":"suitcase","kk":"ˈsuːtkeɪs","tense":"n.","ch":"[['行李箱']]","chEntries":["行李箱"],"practiceMeaning":"請在櫃檯托運行李箱。","analysis":"此字為複合詞，由 'suit' (適合、套裝) + 'case' (箱子) 構成。'suit' 源自古法語 'suite' (following, retinue)，引申為「成套的服裝」。'case' 源自拉丁語 'capsa' (box)。'suitcase' 的原始語義是指「用來裝旅行時的套裝（suit）的箱子」。隨著時代發展，其意義擴展到泛指所有用於裝載旅行用品的箱子。構詞上，兩個獨立詞素結合，共同形成一個新的名詞，描述一種特定用途的容器。","definition":"a rectangular piece of luggage with a handle, used for carrying clothes and personal belongings when travelling.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She packed her clothes into a large suitcase.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她把衣服裝進了一個大行李箱。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please check in your suitcase at the counter.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請在櫃檯托運行李箱。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"請在櫃檯托運行李箱。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4387,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u9::superior::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This new model is far ____ to the old one.","expectedAnswer":"superior","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This new model is far ____ to the old one.","clozeAnswer":"superior","exampleTranslation":"這個新模型比舊型號好得多。","reference":{"eng":"superior","kk":"/suˈpɪəriər/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['上級的', '優越的'], ['（地位、職位）更高的'], ['（品質）優良的', '卓越的']]","chEntries":["上級的","優越的","更高的","優良的","卓越的"],"practiceMeaning":"這個新模型比舊型號好得多。","analysis":"詞源自拉丁語 'superior'，意為「較高的」，是 'super'（在...之上）的比較級。核心概念是「位置或等級的更高」，由此延伸出品質、能力等方面的優越。與 'inferior'（較低的）相對。","definition":"higher in rank, status, or quality; better than average or most people/things.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a superior officer.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一位上級軍官。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This new model is far superior to the old one.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個新模型比舊型號好得多。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個新模型比舊型號好得多。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4314,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::suspect::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"I ____ it will rain later.","expectedAnswer":"suspect","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"I ____ it will rain later.","clozeAnswer":"suspect","exampleTranslation":"我猜待會可能會下雨。","reference":{"eng":"suspect","kk":"/səˈspɛkt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['懷疑；不信任'], ['認為…可能是；猜想']]","chEntries":["懷疑","不信任","認為…可能是","猜想"],"practiceMeaning":"我猜待會可能會下雨。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'suspicere'，意為 'look up at, distrust, surmise'，由 'sub-' (under) 和 'specere' (to look) 構成。字面意思是『從下方仰望』，引申為『偷偷看』，進而產生『猜疑』、『懷疑』、『覺得有問題』的意思。也可表示『猜測』某事為真，但證據不確鑿。","definition":"to think that someone is guilty of a crime or that something bad has happened or is going to happen; to believe that something is probably true","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police suspect him of theft.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警方懷疑他犯了竊盜罪。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I suspect it will rain later.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我猜待會可能會下雨。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She suspected that he was not telling the truth.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她懷疑他沒有說實話。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我猜待會可能會下雨。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5862,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::sustainable::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This farming method is more ____.","expectedAnswer":"sustainable","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This farming method is more ____.","clozeAnswer":"sustainable","exampleTranslation":"這種耕作方法更具可持續性。","reference":{"eng":"sustainable","kk":"səˈsteɪnəbl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"可持續的\"  ],  [    \"可維持的\"  ],  [    \"能長久支持的\"  ],  [    \"不會枯竭的\"  ]]","chEntries":["可持續的","可維持的","能長久支持的","不會枯竭的"],"practiceMeaning":"這種耕作方法更具可持續性。","analysis":"此字由動詞 'sustain' 加上形容詞字尾 '-able' 構成。'Sustain' 源自拉丁語 'sustinere' (to hold up, support)。'-able' 字尾表示「能夠……的」。'Sustainable' 的核心語意是「能夠被維持」、「能夠長期存在或進行」。它特別強調在滿足當前需求的同時，不損害後代滿足其自身需求的發展模式，常用於環境、經濟和社會領域。例如，也可指「不會枯竭的」資源。","definition":"1. Able to be maintained at a certain rate or level.; 2. Relating to or being development that meets the needs of the present without compromising the ability of future generations to meet their own needs.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to develop sustainable energy sources.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要發展可持續能源。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This farming method is more sustainable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種耕作方法更具可持續性。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company aims for sustainable growth.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司旨在實現可持續增長。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The renewable resources are sustainable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這些可再生資源是可持續的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這種耕作方法更具可持續性。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5707,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l9::sway::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His opinions often ____ the crowd.","expectedAnswer":"sway","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His opinions often ____ the crowd.","clozeAnswer":"sway","exampleTranslation":"他的意見常常左右著群眾。","reference":{"eng":"sway","kk":"sweɪ","tense":"v.","ch":"[['搖擺'], ['搖動'], ['影響'], ['擺佈']]","chEntries":["搖擺","搖動","影響","擺佈"],"practiceMeaning":"他的意見常常左右著群眾。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 swæġe（洪水，溪流，源自原始日耳曼語 \\*swag-），與原始印歐語 \\*swēg-（流動）相關。核心語意是「流動、移動」。從物理上的「搖擺、搖動」引申出「影響、擺佈」的抽象意義，即「左右某人的思想、行為或決定」。語意演變路徑：從『流動』到『擺動、搖晃』，再到『左右、影響』。","definition":"to move slowly or rhythmically back and forth or from side to side; to control or influence (a person or course of action).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The trees swayed in the wind.\",\n    \"ch\": \"樹木在風中搖曳。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His opinions often sway the crowd.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的意見常常左右著群眾。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他的意見常常左右著群眾。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4618,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::swell::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The sound of the music began to ____.","expectedAnswer":"swell","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The sound of the music began to ____.","clozeAnswer":"swell","exampleTranslation":"音樂的聲響開始變大。","reference":{"eng":"swell","kk":"/swɛl/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['腫脹'], ['膨脹'], ['（水位、聲量）上漲、增大'], ['（情緒）高漲、激動']]","chEntries":["腫脹","膨脹","上漲、增大","高漲、激動"],"practiceMeaning":"音樂的聲響開始變大。","analysis":"源自古英語 'swellan'，意為「膨脹、腫起」。核心概念是體積、尺寸或強度的增加，通常是由於內部壓力、液體積聚或情感的擴張。可以是物理上的，也可以是抽象的（如驕傲、波浪）。","definition":"to become larger or rounder in size, often because of pressure from inside or an accumulation of fluid; to increase in size, volume, or intensity; to become more extreme in strength or emotion.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His ankle started to swell after the injury.\",\n    \"ch\": \"受傷後，他的腳踝開始腫脹。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The sound of the music began to swell.\",\n    \"ch\": \"音樂的聲響開始變大。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her heart swelled with pride at his achievement.\",\n    \"ch\": \"看到他的成就，她的心充滿了驕傲。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"音樂的聲響開始變大。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5566,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::swiftly::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She replied ____ to his question.","expectedAnswer":"swiftly","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She replied ____ to his question.","clozeAnswer":"swiftly","exampleTranslation":"她迅速回答了他的問題。","reference":{"eng":"swiftly","kk":"ˈswɪftli","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['迅速地'], ['快速地']]","chEntries":["迅速地","快速地"],"practiceMeaning":"她迅速回答了他的問題。","analysis":"此字由形容詞 \"swift\" 加上副詞字尾 \"-ly\" 構成。\"swift\" 源自古英語 \"swift\"，與荷蘭語 \"swift\"、德語 \"sch(w)ift\" 同源，最終可追溯至原始印歐語 \\*swep-（to go, to flow，去，流動）。其核心語義是「快速、敏捷」。因此，\"swiftly\" 作為副詞，用來描述動作或事件發生的速度非常快，強調其敏捷性、即時性，沒有延遲。","definition":"1. At a great speed; very quickly; 2. Without delay; promptly.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The news spread swiftly through the town.\",\n    \"ch\": \"消息迅速傳遍了整個城鎮。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She replied swiftly to his question.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她迅速回答了他的問題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The rescue team worked swiftly to save the stranded hikers.\",\n    \"ch\": \"救援隊迅速行動，營救了受困的登山者。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她迅速回答了他的問題。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5580,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::tactic::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company adopted a new marketing ____.","expectedAnswer":"tactic","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company adopted a new marketing ____.","clozeAnswer":"tactic","exampleTranslation":"該公司採用了一種新的市場行銷策略。","reference":{"eng":"tactic","kk":"ˈtæktɪk","tense":"n.","ch":"[['策略'], ['戰術']]","chEntries":["策略","戰術"],"practiceMeaning":"該公司採用了一種新的市場行銷策略。","analysis":"此字源自希臘語 \"tak tikos\"（relating to arrangement or order，與安排或秩序有關），來自 \"tassein\"（to arrange, put in order，安排，排序）。\"tassein\" 引申為「戰術上的安排」。\"tactic\"（單數）和 \"tactics\"（複數）都可以指「為達成特定目標而採取的具體行動或策略」。 \"tactics\"（複數）更常指「軍事上的戰術」，而 \"tactic\"（單數）則更傾向於指「在特定情境下的一種應對方式或策略」。核心語義是「為了實現某個較大目標而採取的具體步驟或方法」。","definition":"1. An action or tactic used to achieve a particular aim; 2. A plan for achieving a particular goal; a strategy.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His tactic was to divide and conquer.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的策略是分而治之。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company adopted a new marketing tactic.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司採用了一種新的市場行銷策略。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"What is your tactic for dealing with difficult customers?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你處理難纏客戶的策略是什麼？\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該公司採用了一種新的市場行銷策略。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3299,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::teapot::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ was made of fine porcelain.","expectedAnswer":"teapot","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ was made of fine porcelain.","clozeAnswer":"teapot","exampleTranslation":"這茶壺是用精緻的瓷器製成的。","reference":{"eng":"teapot","kk":"/ˈtiːpɒt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['茶壺']]","chEntries":["茶壺"],"practiceMeaning":"這茶壺是用精緻的瓷器製成的。","analysis":"由 'tea' (茶) + 'pot' (壺) 組成。專指用於泡茶、倒茶的器具。","definition":"a pot with a lid, handle, and spout, used for making and serving tea.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She poured tea from the teapot into the cups.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她從茶壺裡倒茶到杯子裡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The teapot was made of fine porcelain.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這茶壺是用精緻的瓷器製成的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這茶壺是用精緻的瓷器製成的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4655,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::tearjerker::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It's a touching story, a real ____.","expectedAnswer":"tearjerker","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It's a touching story, a real ____.","clozeAnswer":"tearjerker","exampleTranslation":"這是一個感人的故事，真是一部催淚片。","reference":{"eng":"tearjerker","kk":"/ˈtɪərdʒɜːrkər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['催淚片'], ['令人感動或悲傷的故事/電影']]","chEntries":["催淚片","令人感動或悲傷的故事/電影"],"practiceMeaning":"這是一個感人的故事，真是一部催淚片。","analysis"