the painting.","expectedAnswer":"theft","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The police are investigating the ____ of the painting.","clozeAnswer":"theft","exampleTranslation":"警方正在調查這幅畫的盜竊案。","reference":{"eng":"theft","kk":"θɛft","tense":"n.","ch":"[['盜竊'], ['偷竊（的行為）'], ['被盜物品']]","chEntries":["盜竊","偷竊","被盜物品"],"practiceMeaning":"警方正在調查這幅畫的盜竊案。","analysis":"此字源自古英語þeofþ，是þēof（小偷）的名詞化。þēof又來自原始日耳曼語\\*theubaz（小偷）。theft 的核心語意是「非法獲取他人財物的行為」。此名詞通常指盜竊的總稱或行為本身，而不是指單一的被盜物品（除非上下文另有說明）。OCR 掃描時可能將 'th' 誤判為 'f'，或 'f' 誤判為 't'。此處修正為 theft。","definition":"the action or crime of stealing.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The shop reported a significant increase in theft.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該商店報告盜竊行為顯著增加。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police are investigating the theft of the painting.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警方正在調查這幅畫的盜竊案。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"警方正在調查這幅畫的盜竊案。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5066,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::therapist::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The physical ____ helped him regain movement in his leg.","expectedAnswer":"therapist","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The physical ____ helped him regain movement in his leg.","clozeAnswer":"therapist","exampleTranslation":"物理治療師幫助他恢復了腿部的活動能力。","reference":{"eng":"therapist","kk":"ˈθɛrəpɪst","tense":"n.","ch":"[['治療師'], ['理療師']]","chEntries":["治療師","理療師"],"practiceMeaning":"物理治療師幫助他恢復了腿部的活動能力。","analysis":"此字源自希臘語therapeutēs，意為「服侍者、治療者」。therapeutēs 又來自therapeuein（治療、醫治）。therapy（治療）是其詞根。therapist 指「從事治療專業的人」，涵蓋範圍廣泛，包括心理治療師、物理治療師、職能治療師等。OCR 掃描時可能將 'th' 誤判為 'f'，或 'p' 誤判為 'r'。此處修正為 therapist。","definition":"a person qualified to treat mental or physical illness.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She started seeing a therapist to deal with her anxiety.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她開始看心理治療師來處理焦慮。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The physical therapist helped him regain movement in his leg.\",\n    \"ch\": \"物理治療師幫助他恢復了腿部的活動能力。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"物理治療師幫助他恢復了腿部的活動能力。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5067,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::therapy::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Cognitive behavioral ____ is a common form of psychotherapy.","expectedAnswer":"therapy","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Cognitive behavioral ____ is a common form of psychotherapy.","clozeAnswer":"therapy","exampleTranslation":"認知行為療法是一種常見的心理治療形式。","reference":{"eng":"therapy","kk":"ˈθɛrəpi","tense":"n.","ch":"[['治療'], ['療法'], ['（心理）諮詢']]","chEntries":["治療","療法","諮詢"],"practiceMeaning":"認知行為療法是一種常見的心理治療形式。","analysis":"此字源自希臘語therapeia，意為「治療、醫治」，來自therapeuein（治療、醫治）。therapy 指「用於治癒疾病或減輕疼痛、痛苦的一種方法或過程」。涵蓋範圍廣泛，包括醫學治療、心理治療（如諮詢）、物理治療等。OCR 掃描時可能將 'th' 誤判為 'f'，或 'p' 誤判為 'r'。此處修正為 therapy。","definition":"1. the treatment of disease or disorders by physical, chemical, or psychological means; 2. a course of treatment designed to help a person recover from illness or injury.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is undergoing radiation therapy for cancer.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他正在接受癌症放射治療。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Cognitive behavioral therapy is a common form of psychotherapy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"認知行為療法是一種常見的心理治療形式。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"認知行為療法是一種常見的心理治療形式。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6199,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::thesis::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His ____ argued for the importance of early childhood education.","expectedAnswer":"thesis","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His ____ argued for the importance of early childhood education.","clozeAnswer":"thesis","exampleTranslation":"他的論文主張了早期兒童教育的重要性。","reference":{"eng":"thesis","kk":"ˈθiːsɪs","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"論文\"  ],  [    \"論點\"  ],  [    \"學說\"  ]]","chEntries":["論文","論點","學說"],"practiceMeaning":"他的論文主張了早期兒童教育的重要性。","analysis":"此字源自古希臘語 θέσις (thesis)，意為「放置、安排、主張」，與 θεῖναι (theinai)「放置」同源。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作為名詞，其核心語義是指「為學術目的而寫的一篇長篇文章」，通常是大學學位的要求。詞源中的「放置、安排、主張」概念引申為「提出的論點」和「學術性的主張」。","definition":"1. a long essay or dissertation involving personal research, written as part of a course of study for a degree; 2. a statement or theory that is put forward as a premise to be maintained or proved.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is writing her doctoral thesis on artificial intelligence.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她正在撰寫關於人工智能的博士論文。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His thesis argued for the importance of early childhood education.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的論文主張了早期兒童教育的重要性。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This paper presents a novel thesis.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這篇論文提出了一個新穎的論點。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The thesis defended the author's position.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這篇論點為作者的立場辯護。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他的論文主張了早期兒童教育的重要性。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5652,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l8::thoughtful::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She gave him a ____ look.","expectedAnswer":"thoughtful","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She gave him a ____ look.","clozeAnswer":"thoughtful","exampleTranslation":"她給了他一個若有所思的眼神。","reference":{"eng":"thoughtful","kk":"ˈθɔːtfəl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['體貼的'], ['考慮周到的'], ['深思熟慮的'], ['引人深思的']]","chEntries":["體貼的","考慮周到的","深思熟慮的","引人深思的"],"practiceMeaning":"她給了他一個若有所思的眼神。","analysis":"此字由 thought（思想，思考）+ -ful（充滿，-ful）構成。thought 是源自古英語 þōht，來自原始日耳曼語 *þancō（思想）。-ful 是常見的形容詞字尾，表示「充滿……」、「具有……」，常加在名詞後面。構詞上，thought 提供核心的「思考」概念，-ful 表示「充滿」或「具有」。因此，thoughtful 的核心語義為「充滿思考」或「具有深思」。此處為形容詞用法，描述行為、言語或人「周密考慮」、「體貼他人」或「引人深思」。","definition":"showing consideration for the needs or feelings of others; characterized by careful thought; causing one to think deeply.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"That was a very thoughtful gift.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那是一份很體貼的禮物。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She gave him a thoughtful look.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她給了他一個若有所思的眼神。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was thoughtful of you to help me.\",\n    \"ch\": \"你幫助我真是考慮周到。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她給了他一個若有所思的眼神。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5651,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l8::thoughtless::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His ____ remarks upset everyone.","expectedAnswer":"thoughtless","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His ____ remarks upset everyone.","clozeAnswer":"thoughtless","exampleTranslation":"他無心的言論惹惱了所有人。","reference":{"eng":"thoughtless","kk":"ˈθɔːtləs","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['欠考慮的'], ['不體貼的'], ['魯莽的'], ['未經思考的']]","chEntries":["欠考慮的","不體貼的","魯莽的","未經思考的"],"practiceMeaning":"他無心的言論惹惱了所有人。","analysis":"此字由 thought（思想，思考）+ -less（無，-less）構成。thought 是源自古英語 þōht，來自原始日耳曼語 *þancō（思想）。-less 是常見的形容詞字尾，表示「沒有……」、「缺少……」，常加在名詞後面。構詞上，thought 提供核心的「思考」概念，-less 表示「缺少」或「沒有」。因此，thoughtless 的核心語義為「缺少思考」或「沒有考慮」。此處為形容詞用法，描述行為、言語或人「未經深思熟慮」、「不考慮他人感受」或「魯莽」。","definition":"without consideration for others; showing no thought for the consequences of one's actions; careless or unthinking.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was thoughtless of him to forget her birthday.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他忘了她的生日，真是欠考慮。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His thoughtless remarks upset everyone.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他無心的言論惹惱了所有人。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他無心的言論惹惱了所有人。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4630,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::thread::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He lost the ____ of the conversation.","expectedAnswer":"thread","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He lost the ____ of the conversation.","clozeAnswer":"thread","exampleTranslation":"他聽不明白談話的內容了（失去了談話的線索）。","reference":{"eng":"thread","kk":"/θred/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['線'], ['絲線'], ['（故事、談話等的）線索'], ['（思想、情緒等的）一絲']]","chEntries":["線","絲線","線索","一絲"],"practiceMeaning":"他聽不明白談話的內容了（失去了談話的線索）。","analysis":"源自古英語 'þræd'，與「紡織」相關。核心