xpectedAnswer":"throw up","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She decided to ____ her job.","clozeAnswer":"throw up","exampleTranslation":"她決定辭掉工作。","reference":{"eng":"throw up","kk":"θroʊ ʌp","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['嘔吐'], ['（突然）放棄'], ['（建築物）建造']]","chEntries":["嘔吐","放棄","建造"],"practiceMeaning":"她決定辭掉工作。","analysis":"此為一個常見的片語動詞。throw（扔，擲）的過去式 threw，up（向上）。字面意思為「向上扔」，引申為「嘔吐」。另一義為「突然放棄」或「終止」，例如 throw up a job。第三義為「建造」或「建造起來」，例如 throw up a wall。核心語義圍繞「扔」、「拋」的概念，引申出嘔吐（將食物向上排出）、放棄（像丟掉東西一樣）、建造（快速建起）。此處應考慮上下文，OCR 文本未提供具體上下文，但此片語有多個常見義。這裡提供最常見的「嘔吐」和「放棄」。","definition":"to vomit; to abandon or give up suddenly; to construct quickly.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He ate too much and had to throw up.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他吃得太多，不得不嘔吐。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She decided to throw up her job.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她決定辭掉工作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They managed to throw up a temporary shelter.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們設法迅速搭建了一個臨時住所。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她決定辭掉工作。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4253,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::tide::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of public opinion was turning against the policy.","expectedAnswer":"tide","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of public opinion was turning against the policy.","clozeAnswer":"tide","exampleTranslation":"公眾輿論的潮流正轉向反對該政策。","reference":{"eng":"tide","kk":"/taɪd/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['潮汐'], ['潮流'], ['趨勢']]","chEntries":["潮汐","潮流","趨勢"],"practiceMeaning":"公眾輿論的潮流正轉向反對該政策。","analysis":"源自古英語 'tīd'，最初意為「時間、時刻」。後來演變成「潮汐」，可能因為潮汐的漲落與時間的週期性變化相關。進一步延伸，'tide' 可指「趨勢」或「潮流」，即事物發展的總體方向，類似於「trend」。","definition":"the rise and fall of the sea, caused by the pull of the moon and sun; a general tendency or direction.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We went to the beach during low tide.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們在低潮時去了海灘。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The tide of public opinion was turning against the policy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公眾輿論的潮流正轉向反對該政策。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"公眾輿論的潮流正轉向反對該政策。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5501,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::to-come::idiom","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The problems ____ may be even greater.","expectedAnswer":"to come","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The problems ____ may be even greater.","clozeAnswer":"to come","exampleTranslation":"即將到來的問題可能更大。","reference":{"eng":"to come","kk":"tu kʌm","tense":"idiom","ch":"[['即將到來的'], ['將來']]","chEntries":["即將到來的","將來"],"practiceMeaning":"即將到來的問題可能更大。","analysis":"這個短語由不定詞 'to come' 構成。'To come' 作不定詞，表示「來」這個動作。當用作形容詞或修飾名詞時，'to come' 通常表示「即將到來的」、「未來的」。例如 'the years to come'（未來幾年）。它強調的是「尚未發生但即將發生」的狀態。核心語意是「即將發生」。","definition":"1. Future; to be expected in the future.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We are looking forward to the years to come.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們期待著未來。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The problems to come may be even greater.\",\n    \"ch\": \"即將到來的問題可能更大。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She wants to make a difference in the world to come.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她想在即將到來的世界裡有所作為。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"即將到來的問題可能更大。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5107,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::transmission::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The radio ____ was clear.","expectedAnswer":"transmission","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The radio ____ was clear.","clozeAnswer":"transmission","exampleTranslation":"無線電的傳輸很清晰。","reference":{"eng":"transmission","kk":"trænzˈmɪʃn","tense":"n.","ch":"[['傳輸'], ['傳播'], ['變速器']]","chEntries":["傳輸","傳播","變速器"],"practiceMeaning":"無線電的傳輸很清晰。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'transmittere'，由 'trans-' (across) + 'mittere' (to send) 構成，原意是 '送過、傳遞'。'Transmission' 的核心語義是 '從一個地方或個體傳遞到另一個地方或個體的過程'。這可以指能量、資訊（如無線電訊號）、疾病（如病毒傳播）、或動力的傳遞（如汽車的變速器）。","definition":"1. The act or process of transmitting something.; 2. The sending of something across places or to people.; 3. (In a vehicle) a system for transmitting mechanical power and torque from the engine to the driven parts.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The transmission of the virus can occur through airborne droplets.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該病毒可通過空氣飛沫傳播。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The radio transmission was clear.\",\n    \"ch\": \"無線電的傳輸很清晰。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He learned how to change the car's transmission.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他學會了如何更換汽車的變速器。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"無線電的傳輸很清晰。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5432,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::transportation::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The cost of ____ has increased significantly.","expectedAnswer":"transportation","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The cost of ____ has increased significantly.","clozeAnswer":"transportation","exampleTranslation":"運輸成本已顯著增加。","reference":{"eng":"transportation","kk":"ˌtrænspɔːrˈteɪʃn","tense":"n.","ch":"[['運輸'], ['交通'], ['運輸工具'], ['放逐']]","chEntries":["運輸","交通","運輸工具","放逐"],"practiceMeaning":"運輸成本已顯著增加。","analysis":"此字為派生詞，由動詞 \"transport\" 加上名詞化字尾 \"-ation\" 構成。\"transport\" 源自拉丁語 \"transportare\"，意為\"搬運\"、\"運送\"，由 \"trans-\" (跨越) 和 \"portare\" (攜帶) 組成。構詞上，\"trans-\" 提供了移動的「方向」或「跨越」的語意，\"portare\" 提供了核心的「攜帶」動作。字尾 \"-ation\" 將動詞的「運輸」行為轉化為抽象名詞。因此，\"transportation\" 指的是「運輸」的系統、過程、行業，或是「交通」方式。也可指「運輸工具」或「放逐」的行為。","definition":"the action of transporting someone or something or the process of being transported; the system or means of carrying passengers or goods from place to place.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Public transportation in the city is efficient.\",\n    \"ch\": \"市區的公共交通系統很有效率。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The cost of transportation has increased significantly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"運輸成本已顯著增加。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The country relies heavily on air transportation for international trade.\",\n    \"ch\": \