.","expectedAnswer":"undo","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The king decided to ____ the decree.","clozeAnswer":"undo","exampleTranslation":"國王決定撤銷那項法令。","reference":{"eng":"undo","kk":"ʌnˈdu","tense":"vt.","ch":"[  [    \"解開\"  ],  [    \"撤銷\"  ],  [    \"取消\"  ],  [    \"毀掉\"  ]]","chEntries":["解開","撤銷","取消","毀掉"],"practiceMeaning":"國王決定撤銷那項法令。","analysis":"此字由 un-（not, the opposite of）和 do（做）構成。核心語義是「與『做』相反的動作」，即「撤銷」、「取消」或「恢復到未做之前的狀態」。可指物理上的解開（如解開釦子），或抽象上的取消（如撤銷決定）。","definition":"1. unfasten or loosen (something that is tied, fastened, or wrapped); 2. cancel or reverse the effect or consequence of (an action or event); 3. spoil or destroy (a positive result or achievement).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please undo the knots in the rope.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請解開繩子上的結。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The king decided to undo the decree.\",\n    \"ch\": \"國王決定撤銷那項法令。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His mistake undid all his hard work.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的錯誤毀掉了他所有的辛勤工作。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"國王決定撤銷那項法令。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5109,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::undoubtedly::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The project was ____ a success.","expectedAnswer":"undoubtedly","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The project was ____ a success.","clozeAnswer":"undoubtedly","exampleTranslation":"這個專案無疑是成功的。","reference":{"eng":"undoubtedly","kk":"ʌnˈdaʊtɪdli","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['毫無疑問地'], ['確定地']]","chEntries":["毫無疑問地","確定地"],"practiceMeaning":"這個專案無疑是成功的。","analysis":"此字由 'un-' (not) + 'doubt' (懷疑) + '-ed' (過去分詞或形容詞後綴) + '-ly' (副詞化後綴) 構成。'Doubt' 源自古英語 'dūfan' (to dive, to sink)，引申為 '懷疑'。'Undoubtedly' 的核心語義是 '沒有任何懷疑的餘地'，強調某事是確鑿的、無可置疑的。它用來加強語氣，表明說話者對所述內容的高度確定性。","definition":"1. Without doubt; certainly.; 2. Beyond doubt; unquestionably.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is undoubtedly the best candidate for the job.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她無疑是這份工作最好的候選人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The project was undoubtedly a success.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個專案無疑是成功的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個專案無疑是成功的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5446,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::urgency::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There is a sense of ____ in their voices.","expectedAnswer":"urgency","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There is a sense of ____ in their voices.","clozeAnswer":"urgency","exampleTranslation":"他們的語氣中帶著一種急迫感。","reference":{"eng":"urgency","kk":"ˈɜːrdʒənsi","tense":"n.","ch":"[['緊急'], ['急迫'], ['緊迫']]","chEntries":["緊急","急迫","緊迫"],"practiceMeaning":"他們的語氣中帶著一種急迫感。","analysis":"此字為派生詞，由形容詞 \"urgent\" (緊急的) 加上名詞化字尾 \"-cy\" (或 \"-cy\") 構成。\"urgent\" 源自拉丁語 \"urgens\" (催促、緊迫)，是動詞 \"urgere\" 的現在分詞。構詞上，\"urg-\" 提供了核心的「催促」、「緊迫」語意，\"-ency\" 是常見的名詞字尾，表示「狀態」、「品質」或「情況」。因此，\"urgency\" 指的是「需要立即關注或處理的緊急、急迫或緊迫的狀態」。","definition":"an important and urgent need or demand; the quality or state of being urgent.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The urgency of the situation became clear immediately.\",\n    \"ch\": \"局勢的緊急性立即可見。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There is a sense of urgency in their voices.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們的語氣中帶著一種急迫感。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The organization stressed the urgency of climate action.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該組織強調了氣候行動的緊迫性。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們的語氣中帶著一種急迫感。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5445,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::urgent::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This is an ____ matter that requires your immediate attention.","expectedAnswer":"urgent","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This is an ____ matter that requires your immediate attention.","clozeAnswer":"urgent","exampleTranslation":"這是需要你立即關注的緊急事項。","reference":{"eng":"urgent","kk":"ˈɜːrdʒənt","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['緊急的'], ['急迫的'], ['緊迫的']]","chEntries":["緊急的","急迫的","緊迫的"],"practiceMeaning":"這是需要你立即關注的緊急事項。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 \"urgens\"，是動詞 \"urgere\" (催促、驅使、緊迫) 的現在分詞。\"urgere\" 的詞源不明確，但與\"torque\" (扭轉、轉動) 有聯繫，可能表示\"被推動\"或\"被施壓\"。構詞上，\"urg-\" 提供了核心的「催促」、「緊迫」語意，\"-ent\" 是形容詞字尾。 \"Urgent\" 形容某事「需要立即關注或處理」，具有「急迫性」或「緊迫性」。","definition":"requiring immediate action or attention; pressing; demanding prompt action.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We have an urgent deadline to meet.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們有一個緊急的截止日期要遵守。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is an urgent matter that requires your immediate attention.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是需要你立即關注的緊急事項。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Emergency services responded to an urgent call.\",\n    \"ch\": \"緊急服務部門響應了一個緊急呼叫。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是需要你立即關注的緊急事項。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5152,"wordRef":"字彙王::u62::utility::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We pay our ____ bills every month.","expectedAnswer":"utility","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We pay our ____ bills every month.","clozeAnswer":"utility","exampleTranslation":"我們每月支付公共事業的帳單。","reference":{"eng":"utility","kk":"juːˈtɪləti","tense":"n.","ch":"[['效用'], ['功用'], ['公共事業（水、電、煤氣等）']]","chEntries":["效用","功用","公共事業"],"practiceMeaning":"我們每月支付公共事業的帳單。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 utilitas，意為「有用性、好處」，來自 utilis（有用的），而 utilis 來自 uti（使用）。核心語意是「有用性、功能性」。引申為「能滿足人類需求的服務」（如水、電、瓦斯等公共事業），以及「具有實用價值的東西」。","definition":"the state or quality of being useful; usefulness; an organization or company that provides a basic service, such as electricity, water, or gas, to the public.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The utility of this tool is immense.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個工具的效用是巨大的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We pay our utility bills every month.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們每月支付公共事業的帳單。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們每月支付公共事業的帳單。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U62"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5866,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::variation::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Genetic ____ is essential for evolution.","expectedAnswer":"variation","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Genetic ____ is essential for evolution.","clozeAnswer":"variation","exampleTranslation":"遺傳變異對演化至關重要。","reference":{"eng":"variation","kk":"ˌveəriˈeɪʃn","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"變化\"  ],  [    \"差異\"  ],  [    \"變異\"  ],  [    \"變奏\"  ]]","chEntries":["變化","差異","變異","變奏"],"practiceMeaning":"遺傳變異對演化至關重要。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'variatio'，是 'variare' (to change, alter) 的名詞形式。'Variare' 來自 'varius' (various, diverse)。'-ion' 是常見的名詞字尾，表示「過程」、「狀態」或「結果」。'Variation' 的核心語意是指「改變」、「差異」或「一種與標準不同的形式」。它可以指事物在數量、程度、形式或性質上的不同，也可以指物種的遺傳變異，或音樂中的主題變奏。例如，也可指「一種變奏形式」。","definition":"1. A change or difference between two or more similar things.; 2. The process or result of varying.; 3. A deviation from a standard or norm.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There are noticeable variations in temperature.\",\n    \"ch\": \"溫度存在明顯的差異。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Genetic variation is essential for evolution.\",\n    \"ch\": \"遺傳變異對演化至關重要。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The orchestra performed a variation on the theme.\",\n    \"ch\": \"樂團演奏了該主題的變奏曲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We observed a slight variation in the results.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們觀察到結果有輕微的差異。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"遺傳變異對演化至關重要。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3928,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::various::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There are ____ reasons why this happened.","expectedAnswer":"various","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There are ____ reasons why this happened.","clozeAnswer":"various","exampleTranslation":"發生這種事有各種各樣的原因。","reference":{"eng":"various","kk":"/ˈveəriəs/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['各種的', '不同的'], ['多樣的']]","chEntries":["各種的","不同的","多樣的"],"practiceMeaning":"發生這種事有各種各樣的原因。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'varius' (意為「多樣的、變化的」)。形容事物有多種不同的種類、形式或情況。","definition":"1. different; of different kinds; 2. many and different.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We offer various courses to suit your needs.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們提供各種課程以滿足您的需求。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There are various reasons why this happened.\",\n    \"ch\": \"發生這種事有各種各樣的原因。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The shop sells various kinds of tea.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家店販售各種茶葉。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"發生這種事有各種各樣的原因。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6253,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::verbal::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ contract is binding.","expectedAnswer":"verbal","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ contract is binding.","clozeAnswer":"verbal","exampleTranslation":"口頭合同具有約束力。","reference":{"eng":"verbal","kk":"ˈvɜrbəl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"口頭的\"  ],  [    \"言語的\"  ],  [    \"動詞的\"  ]]","chEntries":["口頭的","言語的","動詞的"],"practiceMeaning":"口頭合同具有約束力。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 verbalis，意為「關於詞語的」，是 verbum（詞語）的派生詞。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作形容詞時，指通過語言、說話而非書寫傳達的；或與語言、言詞、動詞相關的。中文翻譯為「口頭的；言語的；動詞的」。","definition":"1. relating to or using spoken words; 2. expressed in speech rather than writing; 3. relating to verbs.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They reached a verbal agreement.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們達成了口頭協議。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The verbal contract is binding.\",\n    \"ch\": \"口頭合同具有約束力。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The verbal aspect of communication is crucial.\",\n    \"ch\": \"溝通的言語方面至關重要。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The professor explained the verbal tenses.\",\n    \"ch\": \"教授解釋了動詞的時態。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"口頭合同具有約束力。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5709,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l9::verdict::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The critics gave their ____ on the new play.","expectedAnswer":"verdict","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The critics gave their ____ on the new play.","clozeAnswer":"verdict","exampleTranslation":"評論家們對這部新劇做出了他們的定論。","reference":{"eng":"verdict","kk":"ˈvɜːrdɪkt","tense":"n.","ch":"[['判決'], ['裁決'], ['定論']]","chEntries":["判決","裁決","定論"],"practiceMeaning":"評論家們對這部新劇做出了他們的定論。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 veredictus，由 ver（真實，來自拉丁語 verus）+ dict（言論，來自拉丁語 dictus，是 dicere 的過去分詞，意為『說』）複合而成。構詞上，'ver' 表示『真實』，'dict' 表示『言論』。核心語意是「關於真實情況的陳述或判斷」。在法律語境中，特指陪審團根據事實做出的「真實的裁決」，即「判決」或「裁決」。","definition":"an opinion or decision reached after consideration; the decision of a jury in a trial.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The jury returned a guilty verdict.\",\n    \"ch\": \"陪審團裁定有罪。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The critics gave their verdict on the new play.\",\n    \"ch\": \"評論家們對這部新劇做出了他們的定論。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"評論家們對這部新劇做出了他們的定論。","sourceName":"龍騰課本、字彙王","unitName":"L9、U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5711,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l9::victor::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He was declared the ____ of the race.","expectedAnswer":"victor","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He was declared the ____ of the race.","clozeAnswer":"victor","exampleTranslation":"他被宣佈為這場比賽的獲勝者。","reference":{"eng":"victor","kk":"ˈvɪktər","tense":"n.","ch":"[['勝利者'], ['獲勝者']]","chEntries":["勝利者","獲勝者"],"practiceMeaning":"他被宣佈為這場比賽的獲勝者。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 victore，來自拉丁語 victor（征服者，獲勝者），由 vincere（征服，獲勝）+ -or（表示『人』的名詞化後綴）構成。構詞上，'vincere' 提供核心語意「征服」，'-or' 則指代「執行此動作的人」。核心語意是「在衝突或競爭中取得成功的人」，即「勝利者」。","definition":"a winner in a contest or struggle; a conqueror.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The victor was carried on the shoulders of his supporters.\",\n    \"ch\": \"勝利者被他的支持者們扛在肩上。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was declared the victor of the race.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他被宣佈為這場比賽的獲勝者。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他被宣佈為這場比賽的獲勝者。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4201,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::visible::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There was a ____ increase in their profits.","expectedAnswer":"visible","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There was a ____ increase in their profits.","clozeAnswer":"visible","exampleTranslation":"他們的利潤有了顯著的增長。","reference":{"eng":"visible","kk":"/ˈvɪzəbl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['可見的；看得見的'], ['顯著的；明顯的']]","chEntries":["可見的","看得見的","顯著的","明顯的"],"practiceMeaning":"他們的利潤有了顯著的增長。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 visibilis，'videre'（看）+ '-ibilis'（可…的）。字面意思是“可被看見的”。1. “可見的”指客觀上處於可視範圍內。2. “顯著的；明顯的”是抽象意義，指某事物能夠被注意到，其影響或存在是清晰的。","definition":"1. able to be seen; 2. easily seen or noticed; apparent.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The stars are visible tonight.\",\n    \"ch\": \"今晚星星清晰可見。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was a visible increase in their profits.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們的利潤有了顯著的增長。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His relief was visible.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的寬慰顯而易見。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們的利潤有了顯著的增長。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4186,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::vision::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She had a ____ of a better future for her country.","expectedAnswer":"vision","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She had a ____ of a better future for her country.","clozeAnswer":"vision","exampleTranslation":"她對國家有了一個更美好未來的設想。","reference":{"eng":"vision","kk":"/ˈvɪʒn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['視力；視覺'], ['想像；幻想'], ['遠見；洞察力'], ['（對未來的）設想；規劃']]","chEntries":["視力","視覺","想像","幻想","遠見","洞察力","設想","規劃"],"practiceMeaning":"她對國家有了一個更美好未來的設想。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 visio，意為“看，看見，景象”。'Visio' 來自 'videre'，意為“看”。核心是“看”的能力和所見的景象。引申至抽象概念：1. 抽象化的“看”即“想像”或“幻想”；2. 預見未來、有遠見的“看”即“遠見”或“洞察力”；3. 具體規劃的“看”即對未來的“設想”或“規劃”。","definition":"1. the ability to see; sight; 2. the ability to imagine or think about the future with imagination or wisdom; 3. a mental image or picture of what the future could be like.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has poor vision in his left eye.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他左眼的視力很差。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She had a vision of a better future for her country.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對國家有了一個更美好未來的設想。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The entrepreneur's vision revolutionized the industry.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位企業家的遠見徹底改變了這個行業。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He described his vision in vivid detail.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他生動地描述了他的幻想。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她對國家有了一個更美好未來的設想。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4078,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::volleyball::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She is a professional ____ player.","expectedAnswer":"volleyball","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She is a professional ____ player.","clozeAnswer":"volleyball","exampleTranslation":"她是一名職業排球運動員。","reference":{"eng":"volleyball","kk":"/ˈvɑlɪbɔl/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['排球運動']]","chEntries":["排球運動"],"practiceMeaning":"她是一名職業排球運動員。","analysis":"由 'volley' (擊球，使球在空中飛) + 'ball' (球) 組合而成。'volley' 源自法語 'volée' (flight, volley)，意為「飛翔」。'volleyball' 指一種在網上用手擊球的運動。","definition":"a game played by two teams of six people on a court divided by a net, in which each team tries to make the ball hit the ground on the other team's side","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他們在沙灘上打排球。\",\n    \"eng\": \"They played volleyball on the beach.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"她是一名職業排球運動員。\",\n    \"eng\": \"She is a professional volleyball player.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她是一名職業排球運動員。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4497,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::waterproof::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She bought ____ mascara.","expectedAnswer":"waterproof","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She bought ____ mascara.","clozeAnswer":"waterproof","exampleTranslation":"她買了防水睫毛膏。","reference":{"eng":"waterproof","kk":"/ˈwɔːtərˌpruːf/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['防水的'], ['防水的']]","chEntries":["防水的"],"practiceMeaning":"她買了防水睫毛膏。","analysis":"由 water (水) 和 proof (防護) 組成。核心語意是「能抵抗水滲透的」。","definition":"1. Impervious to water.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This jacket is waterproof and windproof.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這件夾克防水防風。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She bought waterproof mascara.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她買了防水睫毛膏。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她買了防水睫毛膏。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4476,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::wheat::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Bread is made from ____ flour.","expectedAnswer":"wheat","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Bread is made from ____ flour.","clozeAnswer":"wheat","exampleTranslation":"麵包是用小麥麵粉製成的。","reference":{"eng":"wheat","kk":"/wit/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['小麥']]","chEntries":["小麥"],"practiceMeaning":"麵包是用小麥麵粉製成的。","analysis":"源自古英語 hwǣte。是一種重要的穀物，用於製作麵包、麵食等。語意專指這種穀物。","definition":"1. A cereal plant that yields grain, used for making flour.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The fields were covered with golden wheat.\",\n    \"ch\": \"田野覆蓋著金黃色的小麥。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Bread is made from wheat flour.\",\n    \"ch\": \"麵包是用小麥麵粉製成的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"麵包是用小麥麵粉製成的。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5069,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::whereabouts::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"What are the ____ of the missing documents?","expectedAnswer":"whereabouts","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"What are the ____ of the missing documents?","clozeAnswer":"whereabouts","exampleTranslation":"遺失文件的所在何處？","reference":{"eng":"whereabouts","kk":"ˈwɛrəˌbaʊts","tense":"n.","ch":"[['下落'], ['行蹤'], ['（某事物的）所在地']]","chEntries":["下落","行蹤","所在地"],"practiceMeaning":"遺失文件的所在何處？","analysis":"此字是由where（哪裡）加上複數字尾-abouts（圍繞、附近）構成的複合詞。其核心語意是「某人或某物所在的具體位置」。通常用於詢問或討論某人或某物的「下落」或「行蹤」。OCR 掃描時可能將 'w' 誤判為 'u'，或 'b' 誤判為 'd'。此處修正為 whereabouts，通常以複數形式出現，但視為單數名詞。","definition":"1. the place where a person or thing is located; 2. the general position or location of someone or something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police are trying to discover the suspect's whereabouts.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警方正試圖找出嫌疑人的下落。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"What are the whereabouts of the missing documents?\",\n    \"ch\": \"遺失文件的所在何處？\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"遺失文件的所在何處？","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5591,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::without-a-doubt::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This is ____ the most beautiful sunset I've ever seen.","expectedAnswer":"without a doubt","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This is ____ the most beautiful sunset I've ever seen.","clozeAnswer":"without a doubt","exampleTranslation":"這毫無疑問是我見過最美的日落。","reference":{"eng":"without a doubt","kk":"wɪˈðaʊt ə daʊt","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['無疑地'], ['毫無疑問地']]","chEntries":["無疑地","毫無疑問地"],"practiceMeaning":"這毫無疑問是我見過最美的日落。","analysis":"此片語由介詞 \"without\"（沒有），不定冠詞 \"a\"，名詞 \"doubt\"（懷疑）組成。\"without\" 表示「缺乏」。\"doubt\" 表示「懷疑、不確定」。\"without a doubt\" 是一個慣用語，字面意思是「沒有任何懷疑」，引申為「確定地、無疑地」。它用來強調說話者對某件事情的絕對確定性。","definition":"1. Certainly; undoubtedly; 2. Beyond any question or suspicion.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is without a doubt the best candidate for the job.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她毫無疑問是這個職位的最佳人選。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is without a doubt the most beautiful sunset I've ever seen.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這毫無疑問是我見過最美的日落。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He will, without a doubt, succeed in his endeavors.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他肯定會在他的事業上取得成功。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這毫無疑問是我見過最美的日落。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4517,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::work::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The new strategy is starting to ____.","expectedAnswer":"work","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The new strategy is starting to ____.","clozeAnswer":"work","exampleTranslation":"新的策略開始奏效了。","reference":{"eng":"work","kk":"/wɜːrk/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['工作'], ['起作用'], ['奏效'], ['（機器）運行']]","chEntries":["工作","起作用","奏效","運行"],"practiceMeaning":"新的策略開始奏效了。","analysis":"源自古英語 weorc，意為「勞動」、「工作」。核心語意是「進行有目的的活動以生產成果」。引申為「機器運行」、「計劃奏效」等。","definition":"1. To perform work or tasks; 2. To function or operate properly; 3. To achieve a desired result.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She works in a hospital.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在一家醫院工作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The new strategy is starting to work.\",\n    \"ch\": \"新的策略開始奏效了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"My car doesn't work anymore.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我的車不能開了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"新的策略開始奏效了。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4676,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::wrap::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"I ordered a chicken ____ for lunch.","expectedAnswer":"wrap","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"I ordered a chicken ____ for lunch.","clozeAnswer":"wrap","exampleTranslation":"我午餐點了一個雞肉捲餅。","reference":{"eng":"wrap","kk":"/ˈræp/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['包裹物'], ['（食物）捲餅']]","chEntries":["包裹物","捲餅"],"practiceMeaning":"我午餐點了一個雞肉捲餅。","analysis":"名詞形式，指動詞 wrap 的結果，即被包裹起來的東西。可以是禮物、文件等，也專指用薄餅包裹餡料的食物。","definition":"1. An outer covering or wrapping. 2. A large flatbread folded around a filling.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The present had a beautiful gift wrap.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這份禮物有著美麗的包裝紙。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I ordered a chicken wrap for lunch.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我午餐點了一個雞肉捲餅。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我午餐點了一個雞肉捲餅。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5502,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::a-fish-out-of-water::idiom","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"During the meeting, I felt like ____, not understanding any of the technical jargon.","expectedAnswer":"a fish out of water","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"During the meeting, I felt like ____, not understanding any of the technical jargon.","clozeAnswer":"a fish out of water","exampleTranslation":"會議期間，我感到很不適應，聽不懂任何專業術語。","reference":{"eng":"a fish out of water","kk":"ə fɪʃ aʊt əv ˈwɔtər","tense":"idiom","ch":"[['格格不入'], ['不適應環境'], ['渾身不自在']]","chEntries":["格格不入","不適應環境","渾身不自在"],"practiceMeaning":"會議期間，我感到很不適應，聽不懂任何專業術語。","analysis":"這個片語字面意思是「一條離開水的魚」。'Fish' 是魚，'out of water' 指「離開水的」。魚在水中才能生存和自由活動，一旦離開水，牠就會感到極度不適、無法呼吸、行動困難，甚至死亡。因此，'a fish out of water' 用來比喻「處在一個完全陌生、不習慣或不適合的環境中，感到非常不自在、尷尬或無所適從」。核心語意是「在不熟悉或不適合的環境中感到不適」。","definition":"1. A person who is out of place or uncomfortable in a particular situation or environment.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"As a city person, he felt like a fish out of water on the farm.\",\n    \"ch\": \"作為一個城市人，他在農場裡感到格格不入。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She's always been shy, so starting a new job made her feel like a fish out of water.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她一向很害羞，所以開始一份新工作讓她感到渾身不自在。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"During the meeting, I felt like a fish out of water, not understanding any of the technical jargon.\",\n    \"ch\": \"會議期間，我感到很不適應，聽不懂任何專業術語。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"會議期間，我感到很不適應，聽不懂任何專業術語。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5426,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::abundant::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Natural gas is ____ in this region.","expectedAnswer":"abundant","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Natural gas is ____ in this region.","clozeAnswer":"abundant","exampleTranslation":"這個地區天然氣儲量豐富。","reference":{"eng":"abundant","kk":"əˈbʌndənt","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['豐富的'], ['充裕的'], ['大量的'], ['充足的']]","chEntries":["豐富的","充裕的","大量的","充足的"],"practiceMeaning":"這個地區天然氣儲量豐富。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 \"abundans\"，是動詞 \"abundare\" 的現在分詞，意為\"充溢\"、\"豐富\"。\"abundare\" 由 \"ab-\" (離開、遠離，在此表示\"過多\"或\"溢出\") 和 \"undare\" (波浪般流動) 構成，\"undare\" 又源於 \"unda\" (波浪)。構詞上，\"ab-\" 提供了「過量」的語意，\"undare\" 提供了「流動」的圖像，整體表示「如波浪般湧出、充溢」。\"Abundant\" 作形容詞，描述某物「極其豐富」、「充裕」或「大量存在」，遠超過所需。","definition":"existing or available in large quantities; plentiful; more than enough.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Fresh fruits are abundant in summer.\",\n    \"ch\": \"夏季水果供應充足。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The forest provides abundant opportunities for hiking.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這片森林提供了豐富的健行機會。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Natural gas is abundant in this region.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個地區天然氣儲量豐富。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個地區天然氣儲量豐富。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3259,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::accent::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The acute ____ (´) is used in some languages.","expectedAnswer":"accent","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The acute ____ (´) is used in some languages.","clozeAnswer":"accent","exampleTranslation":"銳音符號（´）在某些語言中使用。","reference":{"eng":"accent","kk":"/ˈæksənt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['口音；腔調'], ['強調；重音'], ['（尤指演講或寫作中的）標音符號']]","chEntries":["口音","腔調","強調","重音","標音符號"],"practiceMeaning":"銳音符號（´）在某些語言中使用。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'accentus'，意為「曲調，音調」，由 'ad-'（朝向）+ 'cantus'（歌唱，歌曲）組成。最初指音樂中的音調，後引申至語言中的語音特徵（口音、重音）以及書寫中表示重音的符號。","definition":"1. a distinct way of pronouncing a language, especially one that is characteristic of a particular country, region, or social group; 2. an emphasis given to a particular syllable or word in speech; 3. a mark written above a letter to indicate the pronunciation or stress of a syllable.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She speaks with a strong Southern accent.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她說話帶著濃重的南方口音。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The word 'father' has the accent on the first syllable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"單字 'father' 的重音在第一個音節。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The acute accent (´) is used in some languages.\",\n    \"ch\": \"銳音符號（´）在某些語言中使用。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"銳音符號（´）在某些語言中使用。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6061,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::activist::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He became a peace ____ after the war.","expectedAnswer":"activist","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He became a peace ____ after the war.","clozeAnswer":"activist","exampleTranslation":"戰後他成為了一名和平主義者。","reference":{"eng":"activist","kk":"ˈæktəvɪst","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"行動主義者\"  ],  [    \"活動家\"  ],  [    \"積極分子\"  ]]","chEntries":["行動主義者","活動家","積極分子"],"practiceMeaning":"戰後他成為了一名和平主義者。","analysis":"此字由 active（活躍的）加上名詞後綴 -ist（從事某種活動或信仰的人）構成。Active 源自拉丁語 activus，意為「活動的，活躍的」，本身來自 act-（to do, to act）。Activist 指的是一個積極參與某項政治或社會事業，並採取實際行動來推動變革的人。核心語義是「積極採取行動去倡導或反對某事的人」。","definition":"a person who campaigns to bring about political or social change, especially through direct action.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a well-known environmental activist.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是一位知名的環保活動家。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The group of activists staged a protest.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那群活動家發起了抗議。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He became a peace activist after the war.\",\n    \"ch\": \"戰後他成為了一名和平主義者。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"戰後他成為了一名和平主義者。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3898,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::actually::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It's ____ quite a simple process.","expectedAnswer":"actually","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It's ____ quite a simple process.","clozeAnswer":"actually","exampleTranslation":"這實際上是一個相當簡單的過程。","reference":{"eng":"actually","kk":"/ˈæktʃuəli/","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['實際上', '事實上'], ['真的', '確實']]","chEntries":["實際上","事實上","真的","確實"],"practiceMeaning":"這實際上是一個相當簡單的過程。","analysis":"由 'actual' (實際的) 加上副詞後綴 '-ly' 組成。核心是「依據事實」。用來強調某事物是真實的，與預期或表面情況不同，或用來引出真實情況。","definition":"1. in fact; in reality. 2. used to emphasize a statement or to correct a misconception.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I thought he was joking, but he was actually serious.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我以為他在開玩笑，但他實際上是認真的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"What actually happened was different.\",\n    \"ch\": \"實際上發生的情況是不同的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's actually quite a simple process.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這實際上是一個相當簡單的過程。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這實際上是一個相當簡單的過程。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5460,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::adventure::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It was an ____ to travel without any plans.","expectedAnswer":"adventure","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It was an ____ to travel without any plans.","clozeAnswer":"adventure","exampleTranslation":"沒有任何計劃的旅行是一場冒險。","reference":{"eng":"adventure","kk":"ædvɛnˈtʃɜr","tense":"n.","ch":"[['冒險'], ['奇遇'], ['歷險']]","chEntries":["冒險","奇遇","歷險"],"practiceMeaning":"沒有任何計劃的旅行是一場冒險。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 'aventure'，意指「機遇、事件、奇遇」。'Aventure' 又來自拉丁語 'adventura'，字面意思是「將要發生的事」，'ad-' 是「朝向」的意思，'ventura' 是 'venire'（來）的將來分詞。在中古英語中，'adventure' 最初常用來指「意外的事件」或「幸運的機會」，後來逐漸演變成「充滿刺激、危險或新奇的經歷」。核心語意是「未知的、可能充滿挑戰或驚喜的事件或經歷」。","definition":"1. An unusual and exciting or daring experience or activity.; 2. A commercial enterprise undertaken with the hope of succeeding.; 3. A series of exciting or unusual events or experiences.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He sought adventure in far-off lands.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他到遠方尋求冒險。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The novel tells the story of a young explorer's adventure in the jungle.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本小說講述了一位年輕探險家在叢林中的冒險故事。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was an adventure to travel without any plans.\",\n    \"ch\": \"沒有任何計劃的旅行是一場冒險。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"沒有任何計劃的旅行是一場冒險。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5504,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l5::agent::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Water is a powerful ____ of erosion.","expectedAnswer":"agent","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Water is a powerful ____ of erosion.","clozeAnswer":"agent","exampleTranslation":"水是侵蝕作用的強大媒介。","reference":{"eng":"agent","kk":"ˈeɪdʒənt","tense":"n.","ch":"[['代理人'], ['經紀人'], ['特工'], ['情報員'], ['媒介物'], ['動因']]","chEntries":["代理人","經紀人","特工","情報員","媒介物","動因"],"practiceMeaning":"水是侵蝕作用的強大媒介。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'agens' (genitive 'agentis')，意為 'doing' 或 'acting'，是動詞 'agere' (to do, to act) 的現在分詞。構詞上，'ag-' 提供核心動詞語意，'-ent' 是拉丁語主詞字尾，指代執行動作的人或事物。原始語義是「做者」或「行動者」。在現代英語中，'agent' 演變出多個義項：指代代表他人或團體行事的人（代理人、經紀人），在情報領域指從事秘密活動的特工或情報員，在科學或哲學領域指能夠引起變化或產生影響的媒介物或動因。這些義項都圍繞著「採取行動」或「產生影響」的核心概念展開。","definition":"a person who acts or does business for another; a person or thing that has the power to influence or act; a secret agent.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She works as a literary agent for several famous authors.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她擔任幾位著名作家文學經紀人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The spy was identified as a foreign agent.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該間諜被確認為一名外國情報員。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Water is a powerful agent of erosion.\",\n    \"ch\": \"水是侵蝕作用的強大媒介。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"水是侵蝕作用的強大媒介。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3124,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::ambiguous::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The meaning of the poem is deliberately ____.","expectedAnswer":"ambiguous","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The meaning of the poem is deliberately ____.","clozeAnswer":"ambiguous","exampleTranslation":"這首詩的意義是刻意含糊不清的。","reference":{"eng":"ambiguous","kk":"/æmˈbɪɡjuəs/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['模棱兩可的；含糊不清的'], ['（意義、動機等）不明確的'], ['（事物）有歧義的']]","chEntries":["模棱兩可的","含糊不清的","不明確的","有歧義的"],"practiceMeaning":"這首詩的意義是刻意含糊不清的。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'ambiguus'，意為「不確定的，變換不定的」。'ambi-'（兩邊，周圍）+ 'agere'（行動，推動）。原意是「可以從兩邊走的」，引申為「不確定的」、「模棱兩可的」。形容詞 'ambiguous' 用來描述語言、指示、行為或情況，其意義不單一，可以有多種解釋，因而造成不確定或混淆。","definition":"1. open to more than one interpretation; having a double meaning; 2. unclear or inexact because a choice between alternative meanings has not been made; 3. (of a situation) not having one obvious meaning or outcome.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The politician gave an ambiguous answer to the reporter's question.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位政治家對記者的問題給出了模棱兩可的答案。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His intentions were ambiguous, making it hard to trust him.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的意圖不明確，讓人難以信任他。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The meaning of the poem is deliberately ambiguous.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這首詩的意義是刻意含糊不清的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這首詩的意義是刻意含糊不清的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4135,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::appeal::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He decided to ____ the court's decision.","expectedAnswer":"appeal","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He decided to ____ the court's decision.","clozeAnswer":"appeal","exampleTranslation":"他決定就法院的判決提出上訴。","reference":{"eng":"appeal","kk":"/əˈpiːl/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['懇求', '呼籲'], ['（使）有吸引力', '對...有魅力'], ['上訴']]","chEntries":["懇求","呼籲","有吸引力","對...有魅力","上訴"],"practiceMeaning":"他決定就法院的判決提出上訴。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 appellare（向...呼籲，控告）。核心概念是「正式向某人請求」或「引起某人的興趣」。引申為向法院請求，或對某人產生吸引力。","definition":"1. make a serious or urgent or heartfelt request; 2. be attractive or interesting to; 3. take an application or request to a higher court for review","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police appealed for witnesses.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警方呼籲目擊者出面。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This music doesn't appeal to me.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種音樂對我沒有吸引力。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He decided to appeal the court's decision.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他決定就法院的判決提出上訴。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他決定就法院的判決提出上訴。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U5、L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4141,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::aside::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She stepped ____ to let him pass.","expectedAnswer":"aside","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She stepped ____ to let him pass.","clozeAnswer":"aside","exampleTranslation":"她往旁邊一讓，讓他通過。","reference":{"eng":"aside","kk":"/əˈsaɪd/","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['在一旁', '到旁邊'], ['（暫時）擱置', '另外']]","chEntries":["在一旁","到旁邊","擱置","另外"],"practiceMeaning":"她往旁邊一讓，讓他通過。","analysis":"由 a-（介詞）+ side（邊）組成。核心概念是「在邊緣位置」或「與主要事物分開」。","definition":"1. on or to one side; 2. out of the way; 3. separately, or to one side, from what is being done or considered","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He put the book aside.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他把書放在一旁。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Let's set this problem aside for now.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們暫時把這個問題擱置一邊。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She stepped aside to let him pass.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她往旁邊一讓，讓他通過。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她往旁邊一讓，讓他通過。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3061,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::association::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Their ____ lasted for many years.","expectedAnswer":"association","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Their ____ lasted for many years.","clozeAnswer":"association","exampleTranslation":"他們的夥伴關係持續了很多年。","reference":{"eng":"association","kk":"/əˌsoʊsiˈeɪʃn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['協會；聯盟'], ['聯想；聯繫'], ['交往；夥伴關係']]","chEntries":["協會","聯盟","聯想","聯繫","交往","夥伴關係"],"practiceMeaning":"他們的夥伴關係持續了很多年。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'associatio'，由 'associatus' (companion) 演變而來，意為「連結」或「連結在一起的群體」。\n1. 協會；聯盟：指為共同目的而組成的團體或組織。\n2. 聯想；聯繫：指思想或觀念之間的連結，或將兩個事物聯繫起來的行為。\n3. 交往；夥伴關係：指與他人建立的聯繫或夥伴關係。","definition":"1. an organization of people with a common purpose; 2. a connection or relationship between things; 3. the process of connecting things or people.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a member of the national writers' association.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是國家作家協會的成員。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The smell of cinnamon has a strong association with Christmas for me.\",\n    \"ch\": \"肉桂的味道對我來說強烈地讓人聯想到聖誕節。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Their association lasted for many years.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們的夥伴關係持續了很多年。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們的夥伴關係持續了很多年。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3065,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::attachment::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The printer is an ____ to the main computer.","expectedAnswer":"attachment","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The printer is an ____ to the main computer.","clozeAnswer":"attachment","exampleTranslation":"印表機是主電腦的一個附屬設備。","reference":{"eng":"attachment","kk":"/əˈtætʃmənt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['附件；附屬物'], ['情感上的依戀；愛慕'], ['（電腦）附件']]","chEntries":["附件","附屬物","情感上的依戀","愛慕"],"practiceMeaning":"印表機是主電腦的一個附屬設備。","analysis":"源自古法語 'atachier' (to fasten, to fix) 的名詞形式。指「附著」的狀態或事物。\n1. 附件；附屬物：指被連接或附屬於主體的事物。\n2. 情感上的依戀；愛慕：指人與人之間或人與物之間產生的深厚情感連結。\n3. （電腦）附件：在電子郵件或其他數位通訊中，與主要訊息一同傳送的文件或檔案。","definition":"1. a document or file sent with an email; 2. a feeling of love or strong connection to someone or something; 3. a device or tool that connects to something else.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The user manual is available as a PDF attachment.\",\n    \"ch\": \"使用者手冊可作為 PDF 附件下載。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She showed a deep attachment to her homeland.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對祖國表現出深厚的依戀。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The printer is an attachment to the main computer.\",\n    \"ch\": \"印表機是主電腦的一個附屬設備。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"印表機是主電腦的一個附屬設備。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3914,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::attitude::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The dancer struck a dramatic ____.","expectedAnswer":"attitude","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The dancer struck a dramatic ____.","clozeAnswer":"attitude","exampleTranslation":"舞者擺出了一個戲劇性的姿態。","reference":{"eng":"attitude","kk":"/ˈætɪtuːd/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['態度', '看法'], ['姿態']]","chEntries":["態度","看法","姿態"],"practiceMeaning":"舞者擺出了一個戲劇性的姿態。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'attitudo'，意為「姿態、位置」，由 'aptus' (意為「合適的、準備好的」) 演變而來。最初指身體的姿態，後延伸至心理、情緒上的「態度」或「看法」。","definition":"1. a settled way of thinking or feeling about someone or something, typically one that is reflected in a person's behavior or that inspires one to act in a certain way; 2. a person's way of standing or holding their body.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her positive attitude helped her overcome the challenges.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她積極的態度幫助她克服了挑戰。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has a bad attitude towards work.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對工作有不良的態度。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The dancer struck a dramatic attitude.\",\n    \"ch\": \"舞者擺出了一個戲劇性的姿態。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"舞者擺出了一個戲劇性的姿態。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3066,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::authority::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She is an ____ on ancient Roman history.","expectedAnswer":"authority","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She is an ____ on ancient Roman history.","clozeAnswer":"authority","exampleTranslation":"她是古羅馬歷史方面的權威。","reference":{"eng":"authority","kk":"/əˈθɔːrəti/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['權威；權力'], ['當局；權力機構'], ['權威人士；專家'], ['（學術）權威；準確性']]","chEntries":["權威","權力","當局","權力機構","權威人士","專家","準確性"],"practiceMeaning":"她是古羅馬歷史方面的權威。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'auctoritas'，'auctor' (originator, author) 的衍生詞。最初意為「影響力」、「權威」，後來發展出多重含義。\n1. 權威；權力：指被承認的發布命令、做出決定的權力。\n2. 當局；權力機構：指擁有合法權力的政府機構或組織。\n3. 權威人士；專家：指在某個領域具有知識、技能和影響力的人。\n4. （學術）權威；準確性：指資訊來源的可靠性和學術上的重要性。","definition":"1. the power or right to give orders, make decisions, and enforce obedience; 2. the people or organizations that have the power to make decisions and enforce laws; 3. a person or organization that has power or control in a particular area; 4. an expert on a subject.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police have the authority to arrest criminals.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警方有權逮捕罪犯。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Local authorities are responsible for public services.\",\n    \"ch\": \"地方當局負責公共服務。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is an authority on ancient Roman history.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是古羅馬歷史方面的權威。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to check the authority of this source.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要核實這個來源的權威性。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她是古羅馬歷史方面的權威。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4457,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::automatic::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The factory uses ____ machinery to increase production.","expectedAnswer":"automatic","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The factory uses ____ machinery to increase production.","clozeAnswer":"automatic","exampleTranslation":"工廠使用自動化機器來提高產量。","reference":{"eng":"automatic","kk":"/ˌɔːtəˈmætɪk/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['自動的'], ['機械的'], ['（行為）不自覺的，無意識的']]","chEntries":["自動的","機械的","不自覺的，無意識的"],"practiceMeaning":"工廠使用自動化機器來提高產量。","analysis":"源自希臘語 automatos，意為「自動的」、「自發的」。auto- (自己) + -matos (受驅動的)。核心概念是「自己運作」、「不需要外部持續干預」。引申為行為不受控制或不經思考的。","definition":"1. Working by itself with little or no direct human control; 2. Done or happening without conscious thought or intention.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The car has an automatic transmission.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這輛車有自動變速器。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her response was automatic.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的反應是下意識的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The factory uses automatic machinery to increase production.\",\n    \"ch\": \"工廠使用自動化機器來提高產量。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"工廠使用自動化機器來提高產量。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4478,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::awkward::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Carrying the heavy box up the stairs was ____.","expectedAnswer":"awkward","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Carrying the heavy box up the stairs was ____.","clozeAnswer":"awkward","exampleTranslation":"把那個沉重的箱子搬上樓梯很費力。","reference":{"eng":"awkward","kk":"/ˈɔːkwərd/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['笨拙的'], ['尷尬的'], ['難以處理的'], ['不方便的']]","chEntries":["笨拙的","尷尬的","難以處理的","不方便的"],"practiceMeaning":"把那個沉重的箱子搬上樓梯很費力。","analysis":"源自古挪威語 örvugr，意為「逆向的」、「不順的」。或源自拉丁語 (per) arduum，意為「經過困難」。核心語意是「不順暢」、「不方便」、「難以應對」。引申為行為上的「笨拙」，社交上的「尷尬」，以及處境上的「不方便」或「棘手」。","definition":"1. (of a person) Lacking grace or skill in action, movement, or handling things; 2. (of a situation) Embarrassing, uncomfortable, or inconvenient; 3. Difficult to do or deal with.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He felt awkward when he dropped the vase.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他打翻花瓶時感到很尷尬。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was an awkward silence after her comment.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她說完後，出現了一段尷尬的沉默。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Carrying the heavy box up the stairs was awkward.\",\n    \"ch\": \"把那個沉重的箱子搬上樓梯很費力。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"把那個沉重的箱子搬上樓梯很費力。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4126,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::background::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His family ____ made him feel insecure.","expectedAnswer":"background","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His family ____ made him feel insecure.","clozeAnswer":"background","exampleTranslation":"他的家庭背景使他感到不安。","reference":{"eng":"background","kk":"/ˈbækˌɡraʊnd/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['背景'], ['（人的）出身，經歷'], ['（畫作、照片的）背景']]","chEntries":["背景","出身，經歷"],"practiceMeaning":"他的家庭背景使他感到不安。","analysis":"由 back（後方）+ ground（地面、背景）組成。核心概念是「後方的景象」或「事物發生的環境」。引申為一個人過去的經歷、社會經濟地位，以及藝術作品中襯托主體的畫面。","definition":"1. the part of a scene, picture, or object against which what is in the foreground stands out; 2. a person's origin, education, and experience; 3. the circumstances in which something happens","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The photo has a blurry background.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這張照片的背景很模糊。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a strong academic background.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她有紮實的學術背景。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His family background made him feel insecure.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的家庭背景使他感到不安。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他的家庭背景使他感到不安。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4539,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::badly::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We are ____ in need of funds.","expectedAnswer":"badly","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We are ____ in need of funds.","clozeAnswer":"badly","exampleTranslation":"我們急需資金。","reference":{"eng":"badly","kk":"/ˈbædli/","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['糟糕地', '差勁地'], ['嚴重地', '極度地']]","chEntries":["糟糕地","差勁地","嚴重地","極度地"],"practiceMeaning":"我們急需資金。","analysis":"由 'bad' (壞的) 加上副詞字尾 '-ly' 構成。\n    1. 糟糕地、差勁地：指行為、表現或結果不佳。\n    2. 嚴重地、極度地：指程度非常深，常與表示需求、傷害、情況等的詞連用，如 'badly hurt' (嚴重受傷)，'badly needed' (急需)。","definition":"1. in a very bad or poor manner.; 2. severely; extremely.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He performed badly in the exam.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在考試中表現很差。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The car was badly damaged in the accident.\",\n    \"ch\": \"汽車在事故中嚴重損毀。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We are badly in need of funds.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們急需資金。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們急需資金。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4198,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::benefit::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"A charity ____ concert was held last night.","expectedAnswer":"benefit","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"A charity ____ concert was held last night.","clozeAnswer":"benefit","exampleTranslation":"昨晚舉行了一場慈善義演音樂會。","reference":{"eng":"benefit","kk":"/ˈbenɪfɪt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['益處；好處'], ['（保險、退休金等的）給付；補助金'], ['（慈善）義演；義賣']]","chEntries":["益處","好處","給付","補助金","義演","義賣"],"practiceMeaning":"昨晚舉行了一場慈善義演音樂會。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 benefactum，意為“善行”，'bene-'（好）+ 'facere'（做）。核心是“好的結果”或“好事”。1. “益處；好處”是最廣泛的意義，指任何有利的事物。2. “給付；補助金”是特定領域（金融、福利）的專業用法，指提供的經濟上的好處。3. “義演；義賣”是引申義，指為了獲得“好處”（籌款）而舉行的活動。","definition":"1. an advantage or profit gained from something; 2. a payment made by the state or an insurance scheme to someone who is unable to work or who has lost their job; 3. an event held to raise money for a particular cause.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Regular exercise has many health benefits.\",\n    \"ch\": \"規律運動有很多健康益處。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She receives unemployment benefit.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她領取失業救濟金。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A charity benefit concert was held last night.\",\n    \"ch\": \"昨晚舉行了一場慈善義演音樂會。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"昨晚舉行了一場慈善義演音樂會。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4175,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::between::prep","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The agreement is ____ the two countries.","expectedAnswer":"between","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The agreement is ____ the two countries.","clozeAnswer":"between","exampleTranslation":"這項協議是在兩國之間達成的。","reference":{"eng":"between","kk":"/bɪˈtwiːn/","tense":"prep.","ch":"[['在...之間']]","chEntries":["在...之間"],"practiceMeaning":"這項協議是在兩國之間達成的。","analysis":"源自古英語 betwēonan（在兩者之間）。核心概念是「位於兩個點、區域或事物的中間」。","definition":"1. in or into the space separating (two points, objects, etc.); 2. intermediate to (two points, limits, etc.); 3. in relation to (two or more people or things) considered together","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There is a significant difference between A and B.\",\n    \"ch\": \"A 和 B 之間存在顯著的差異。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She sat between her parents.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她坐在父母之間。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The agreement is between the two countries.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這項協議是在兩國之間達成的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這項協議是在兩國之間達成的。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5821,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::biological::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need to consider the ____ impact of the pollution.","expectedAnswer":"biological","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need to consider the ____ impact of the pollution.","clozeAnswer":"biological","exampleTranslation":"我們需要考慮污染的生物影響。","reference":{"eng":"biological","kk":"ˌbaɪəˈlɑːdʒɪkl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"生物的\"  ],  [    \"生物學的\"  ],  [    \"生理的\"  ]]","chEntries":["生物的","生物學的","生理的"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要考慮污染的生物影響。","analysis":"此字由名詞 'biology' 加上形容詞字尾 '-ical' 構成。'Biology' 本身是一個複合詞，來自希臘語 'bios' (life) 和 '-logia' (study of, discourse)。'-logia' 來自 'logos' (word, speech, reason)。因此，'biology' 的字面意思是「生命的學問」。'-ical' 字尾用於將名詞轉化為形容詞，表示「關於……的」、「屬於……的」、「具有……性質的」。所以 'biological' 的意思就是「關於生物的」或「屬於生物學的」。另外，也可指「與生命體正常機能相關的」，即「生理的」。","definition":"1. Relating to or resulting from the functions of living organisms.; 2. Relating to biology.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The research focuses on biological processes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這項研究聚焦於生物過程。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Genetic engineering has many biological applications.\",\n    \"ch\": \"基因工程有許多生物學上的應用。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to consider the biological impact of the pollution.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要考慮污染的生物影響。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The drug has a strong biological effect.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種藥物有強烈的生理效應。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要考慮污染的生物影響。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5822,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::blast::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ship's horn gave a loud ____.","expectedAnswer":"blast","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ship's horn gave a loud ____.","clozeAnswer":"blast","exampleTranslation":"船的汽笛發出響亮的鳴響。","reference":{"eng":"blast","kk":"blæst","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"爆炸\"  ],  [    \"衝擊波\"  ],  [    \"陣風\"  ],  [    \"巨響\"  ]]","chEntries":["爆炸","衝擊波","陣風","巨響"],"practiceMeaning":"船的汽笛發出響亮的鳴響。","analysis":"此字詞源不明確，可能與原始日耳曼語 *blastaz（氣息、風）或 *blastōną（吹響）有關，與 'blossom'、'blow' 等詞有關聯。早期用於表示「爆炸」或「衝擊」。字義的演變可能與聲音或空氣的突然釋放有關。一個突發的、強烈的聲音或氣流可以被描述為 'blast'。例如，爆炸的衝擊波，或突然而強烈的風。現代語義擴展至形容音樂的「震耳欲聾」或「強烈的氣流」。例如，也可指「吹奏樂器的響亮聲音」。","definition":"1. An explosion or detonation.; 2. A strong gust of wind.; 3. A loud, short blast of a musical instrument or a siren.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The blast of the explosion was heard for miles.\",\n    \"ch\": \"爆炸的巨響遠達數英里。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A strong blast of wind blew his hat off.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一陣強風吹掉了他的帽子。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The ship's horn gave a loud blast.\",\n    \"ch\": \"船的汽笛發出響亮的鳴響。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The music hit us with a blast of sound.\",\n    \"ch\": \"音樂以震耳欲聾的聲響衝擊著我們。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"船的汽笛發出響亮的鳴響。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3127,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::brutal::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He delivered the bad news in a ____, no-nonsense way.","expectedAnswer":"brutal","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He delivered the bad news in a ____, no-nonsense way.","clozeAnswer":"brutal","exampleTranslation":"他以一種殘酷、不講情面的方式傳達了壞消息。","reference":{"eng":"brutal","kk":"/ˈbrutl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['殘酷的；野蠻的'], ['（天氣、情況等）嚴酷的；嚴重的'], ['（直率、粗魯地）坦率的']]","chEntries":["殘酷的","野蠻的","嚴酷的","嚴重的","坦率的"],"practiceMeaning":"他以一種殘酷、不講情面的方式傳達了壞消息。","analysis":"詞源來自拉丁語 'brutalis'，意為「動物性的，粗野的」，與 'brutus'（笨重的，遲鈍的）有關。最初形容像動物一樣沒有理性、野蠻的行為。'Brutal' 強調的是缺乏人性、殘忍、暴力和極端的嚴酷。其語意延伸至描述極端惡劣的條件或非常直接（甚至令人不舒服）的陳述。","definition":"1. savagely violent; 2. (of a person or their actions) cruel and aggressive; 3. (of weather or other natural phenomena) severe and harsh; 4. (of truth or statements) harsh and direct.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The dictator's regime was known for its brutal treatment of political prisoners.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位獨裁者的政權以其對政治犯的殘酷待遇而聞名。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The winter weather in this region is absolutely brutal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個地區的冬季天氣非常嚴酷。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He delivered the bad news in a brutal, no-nonsense way.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他以一種殘酷、不講情面的方式傳達了壞消息。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他以一種殘酷、不講情面的方式傳達了壞消息。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5506,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l5::burst::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The crowd ____ into the stadium.","expectedAnswer":"burst","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The crowd ____ into the stadium.","clozeAnswer":"burst","exampleTranslation":"人群衝進了體育場。","reference":{"eng":"burst","kk":"bɜːrst","tense":"v.","ch":"[['爆炸'], ['迸發'], ['突然出現'], ['衝破'], ['充滿']]","chEntries":["爆炸","迸發","突然出現","衝破","充滿"],"practiceMeaning":"人群衝進了體育場。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 'bursten' 或 'bresten'，與古英語 'berstan' 同源，後者可能來自原始日耳曼語 *berstana。其核心語義是「突然破裂」或「爆開」。構詞上，此字無明顯的字首、字根或字尾可供分析，應視為整體詞源演變。原始語義直接指向「破裂」的物理動作。現代英語中，'burst' 擴展為多種意義：指物體突然破裂（爆炸），指情感或能量突然釋放（迸發），指人或物突然出現或離開（衝破），或指充滿某種事物（充滿）。這些引申義都保留了「突然、瞬間」的特徵。","definition":"to break suddenly and unexpectedly; to appear or happen suddenly; to fill with strong emotion.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The balloon burst with a loud pop.\",\n    \"ch\": \"氣球砰地一聲爆炸了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Tears burst from her eyes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"眼淚奪眶而出。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The crowd burst into the stadium.\",\n    \"ch\": \"人群衝進了體育場。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"人群衝進了體育場。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5427,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::campaign::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The troops prepared for a new ____ in the north.","expectedAnswer":"campaign","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The troops prepared for a new ____ in the north.","clozeAnswer":"campaign","exampleTranslation":"部隊準備在北方展開新的戰役。","reference":{"eng":"campaign","kk":"kæmˈpeɪn","tense":"n.","ch":"[['活動'], ['運動'], ['競選活動'], ['戰役']]","chEntries":["活動","運動","競選活動","戰役"],"practiceMeaning":"部隊準備在北方展開新的戰役。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 \"campagne\"，意為\"田野\"、\"平原\"，引申為\"軍隊在田野中作戰\"，即\"戰役\"。其拉丁語詞源為 \"campania\"，意為\"平坦的土地\"，與 \"campus\" ( campo) 意為\"田野\"有關。構詞上，沒有明顯的字首、字根或字尾可拆解，應視為一個整體詞源的演變。原始語義是指在開闊的場地進行軍事行動。後來引申至政治上的「競選活動」，以及為了達成特定目標而組織的、有時限的「活動」或「運動」，如環保運動、公益活動等。","definition":"an organized course of action to achieve a particular goal; a series of coordinated activities designed to achieve a particular objective; a political campaign; a military operation.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The environmental campaign aims to reduce plastic waste.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個環保運動旨在減少塑膠廢棄物。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The presidential campaign will intensify next month.\",\n    \"ch\": \"總統競選活動將於下個月加劇。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The troops prepared for a new campaign in the north.\",\n    \"ch\": \"部隊準備在北方展開新的戰役。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"部隊準備在北方展開新的戰役。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4119,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::capable::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Are you ____ of understanding the seriousness of the situation?","expectedAnswer":"capable","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Are you ____ of understanding the seriousness of the situation?","clozeAnswer":"capable","exampleTranslation":"你能夠理解局勢的嚴重性嗎？","reference":{"eng":"capable","kk":"/ˈkeɪpəbl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['有能力的', '能幹的'], ['能夠（做某事）的']]","chEntries":["有能力的","能幹的","能夠的"],"practiceMeaning":"你能夠理解局勢的嚴重性嗎？","analysis":"源自拉丁語 capabilis，由 capere（抓住、容納）+ -abilis（能夠）組成。核心概念是「有能力抓住（機會或任務）」或「能容納」。引申為具備某種技能、力量或潛力。","definition":"1. having the ability, fitness, or quality necessary to do or achieve a specified thing; 2. intelligent and quick to understand","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a very capable manager.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是一位非常有能力的經理。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is capable of handling this task.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他能夠處理這項任務。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Are you capable of understanding the seriousness of the situation?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你能夠理解局勢的嚴重性嗎？\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"你能夠理解局勢的嚴重性嗎？","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3211,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::carry::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This vaccine can ____ antibodies.","expectedAnswer":"carry","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This vaccine can ____ antibodies.","clozeAnswer":"carry","exampleTranslation":"這種疫苗可以攜帶抗體。","reference":{"eng":"carry","kk":"/ˈkæri/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['攜帶'], ['搬運'], ['運輸'], ['傳播'], ['承受']]","chEntries":["攜帶","搬運","運輸","傳播","承受"],"practiceMeaning":"這種疫苗可以攜帶抗體。","analysis":"詞源來自古法語 'cariere'，意為 'cart, wagon'，源自拉丁文 'carrum' (cart)。核心意義是『移動某物從一地到另一地』。此意義延伸至物理上的搬運、傳送，以及抽象的傳遞（信息、疾病）、承擔（責任、重量）。","definition":"1. to support and move (someone or something) from one place to another; 2. to convey or transmit (information, news, etc.); 3. to have or produce (a particular quality or result); 4. to be sold in a particular shop.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please carry this bag for me.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請幫我提這個包。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The news spread quickly, carried by word of mouth.\",\n    \"ch\": \"消息迅速傳開，靠口耳相傳。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This vaccine can carry antibodies.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種疫苗可以攜帶抗體。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He carried the team to victory.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他帶領隊伍贏得了勝利。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這種疫苗可以攜帶抗體。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U41"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4325,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::cattle::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The price of ____ has increased.","expectedAnswer":"cattle","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The price of ____ has increased.","clozeAnswer":"cattle","exampleTranslation":"牛的價格上漲了。","reference":{"eng":"cattle","kk":"/ˈkætl/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['牛（總稱，不可數）']]","chEntries":["牛"],"practiceMeaning":"牛的價格上漲了。","analysis":"源自古英語 'catol'，與古諾爾斯語 'kötull' 同源，但其詞源較不確定。這個詞用於統稱牛，特別是指牛群，無論是公牛、母牛還是小牛。它是一個集合名詞，通常用作不可數名詞，與單數名詞 'cow' 或 'ox' 不同，涵蓋了整個類別。","definition":"cows and bulls, considered together as farm animals","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The farmer herds his cattle into the stable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"農夫將他的牛群趕進牛棚。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There are many heads of cattle on the ranch.\",\n    \"ch\": \"牧場裡有很多頭牛。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The price of cattle has increased.\",\n    \"ch\": \"牛的價格上漲了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"牛的價格上漲了。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4226,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::change::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We made a ____ to the original plan.","expectedAnswer":"change","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We made a ____ to the original plan.","clozeAnswer":"change","exampleTranslation":"我們對原計劃進行了修改。","reference":{"eng":"change","kk":"/tʃeɪndʒ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['變化；變更'], ['零錢'], ['（一次）交換']]","chEntries":["變化","變更","零錢","交換"],"practiceMeaning":"我們對原計劃進行了修改。","analysis":"源自古法語 changier，意為“改變”，來自拉丁語 cambiare（交換，改變）。核心是“從一種狀態轉變為另一種狀態”。1. “變化；變更”指事物狀態、性質、形式等的改變。2. “零錢”是指貨幣面額較小的部分。3. “交換”指兩方之間互換物品或資訊。","definition":"1. the act or instance of making or becoming different; 2. coins, as opposed to banknotes; 3. an act of giving one thing and receiving another in return.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There have been dramatic changes in technology.\",\n    \"ch\": \"科技發生了戲劇性的變化。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Do you have change for a dollar?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你有零錢換一美元嗎？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We made a change to the original plan.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們對原計劃進行了修改。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們對原計劃進行了修改。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4044,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::civil::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The country has been involved in a ____ war.","expectedAnswer":"civil","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The country has been involved in a ____ war.","clozeAnswer":"civil","exampleTranslation":"該國捲入了內戰。","reference":{"eng":"civil","kk":"/ˈsɪvəl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['公民的', '國民的'], ['文明的', '有禮貌的'], ['國內的', '非軍事的']]","chEntries":["公民的","國民的","文明的","有禮貌的","國內的","非軍事的"],"practiceMeaning":"該國捲入了內戰。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'civilis'，意為「屬於公民的」、「適合公民的」。'civilis' 又來自 'civis'，意為「市民」、「公民」。核心概念是與「社會」、「國家」或「群體」有關，而非個人或軍事。因此，延伸出「公民的」事務、「文明的」行為（與野蠻相對），以及「國內的」衝突（與戰爭相對）。","definition":"1. relating to a citizen or the state; 2. polite and behaving in a calm and controlled way; 3. relating to the internal affairs of a country, especially in contrast to war or military matters","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"公民權利是民主的基石。\",\n    \"eng\": \"Civil rights are fundamental to democracy.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他對鄰居總是很有禮貌。\",\n    \"eng\": \"He was always civil to his neighbors.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"該國捲入了內戰。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The country has been involved in a civil war.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該國捲入了內戰。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6067,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::clarity::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Please speak with more ____.","expectedAnswer":"clarity","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Please speak with more ____.","clozeAnswer":"clarity","exampleTranslation":"請講得更清楚些。","reference":{"eng":"clarity","kk":"ˈklærəti","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"清晰\"  ],  [    \"清楚\"  ],  [    \"明晰\"  ],  [    \"透明\"  ]]","chEntries":["清晰","清楚","明晰","透明"],"practiceMeaning":"請講得更清楚些。","analysis":"此字由 clear（清晰的）加上名詞後綴 -ity（表示狀態或性質）構成。Clear 源自古法語 cler，來自拉丁語 clarus（clear, bright, famous）。Clarus 最終來源於 proto-Indo-European *kelh₂-「呼喚，聲音」，引申為「響亮的，清晰的」。Clarity 的核心語義是「清晰的狀態或性質」。它可以用來描述聲音、視覺、理解、表達或物質的清晰度。","definition":"1. the quality of being clear and easy to understand; 2. the quality of being easy to see or hear; 3. the quality of being transparent.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The clarity of his explanation was remarkable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他解釋的清晰度令人矚目。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The clarity of the water allowed us to see the fish.\",\n    \"ch\": \"水的清澈度使我們能夠看到魚。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please speak with more clarity.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請講得更清楚些。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"請講得更清楚些。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5585,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::classical::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ ballet requires years of rigorous training.","expectedAnswer":"Classical","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ ballet requires years of rigorous training.","clozeAnswer":"Classical","exampleTranslation":"古典芭蕾需要多年的嚴格訓練。","reference":{"eng":"classical","kk":"ˈklæsɪkl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['古典的'], ['經典的'], ['正規的'], ['傳統的']]","chEntries":["古典的","經典的","正規的","傳統的"],"practiceMeaning":"古典芭蕾需要多年的嚴格訓練。","analysis":"此字是 \"classic\" 的形容詞形式，加上形容詞字尾 \"-al\"。 \"classic\" 源自拉丁語 \"classicus\"，意為 \"of or belonging to the highest class, first-class\"（屬於最高級別的，一流的）。\"-al\" 是常見的形容詞字尾。\"classical\" 主要有兩層核心語義：一是指「古希臘羅馬時期」的，例如 \"classical literature\"、\"classical music\"；二是與 \"classic\" 相似，指「傳統的、正規的、代表性的」，與「現代的」或「非正規的」相對，例如 \"classical economics\"、\"classical ballet\"。","definition":"1. Relating to or belonging to the ancient Greek or Roman tradition, especially in art or literature; 2. Traditionally or typically, rather than modern or experimental; 3. Relating to or characteristic of the formal or artistic traditions of the past.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She studied classical music at university.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在大學學習古典音樂。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Classical physics provides a framework for understanding motion.\",\n    \"ch\": \"古典物理學為理解運動提供了框架。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Classical ballet requires years of rigorous training.\",\n    \"ch\": \"古典芭蕾需要多年的嚴格訓練。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"古典芭蕾需要多年的嚴格訓練。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3129,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::claw::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He accidentally scratched his arm with the crab's ____.","expectedAnswer":"claw","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He accidentally scratched his arm with the crab's ____.","clozeAnswer":"claw","exampleTranslation":"他不小心被螃蟹的鉗子劃傷了手臂。","reference":{"eng":"claw","kk":"/klɔː/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['爪；（動物的）爪子'], ['（螃蟹、龍蝦等的）鉗'], ['（鳥類的）腳爪']]","chEntries":["爪","爪子","鉗","腳爪"],"practiceMeaning":"他不小心被螃蟹的鉗子劃傷了手臂。","analysis":"詞源來自古英語 'clawu'，與「抓」、「刮」有關。'Claw' 指的是動物（鳥類、爬行動物、部分哺乳動物）腳趾末端尖銳、堅硬的角質結構，用於抓、爬、撕或防禦。它也可以指甲殼類動物的鉗子。'Claw' 的特點是其彎曲、尖銳的形狀，以及用於抓握或挖掘的功能。","definition":"1. (in an animal) each of the hornyকুটtipped digits on the feet of birds, reptiles, and some mammals; 2. a sharp, hooked nail on the foot of a bird or mammal; 3. a pincer-like limb of a crab or lobster.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The cat sharpened its claws on the scratching post.\",\n    \"ch\": \"貓在貓抓板上磨牠的爪子。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The eagle's powerful claws could easily carry off its prey.\",\n    \"ch\": \"老鷹強有力的爪子可以輕易地叼走牠的獵物。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He accidentally scratched his arm with the crab's claw.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他不小心被螃蟹的鉗子劃傷了手臂。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他不小心被螃蟹的鉗子劃傷了手臂。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4506,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::clumsy::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The furniture was old and ____.","expectedAnswer":"clumsy","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The furniture was old and ____.","clozeAnswer":"clumsy","exampleTranslation":"這些傢俱又老又笨重。","reference":{"eng":"clumsy","kk":"/ˈklʌmzi/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['笨拙的'], ['不靈巧的'], ['（東西）笨重的']]","chEntries":["笨拙的","不靈巧的","笨重的"],"practiceMeaning":"這些傢俱又老又笨重。","analysis":"源自古挪威語 klumsa，意為「笨拙」、「無能」。核心語意是「動作不協調」、「不靈巧」。","definition":"1. Awkward in movement or in handling things; 2. (of an object) large, heavy, and awkward to use.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was a clumsy child, always tripping over his own feet.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一個笨拙的孩子，總是絆倒自己的腳。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The clumsy waiter dropped the tray.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那個笨拙的服務員打翻了托盤。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The furniture was old and clumsy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這些傢俱又老又笨重。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這些傢俱又老又笨重。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4076,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::coach::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He is the head ____ of the basketball team.","expectedAnswer":"coach","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He is the head ____ of the basketball team.","clozeAnswer":"coach","exampleTranslation":"他是籃球隊的主教練。","reference":{"eng":"coach","kk":"/koʊtʃ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['教練'], ['長途馬車', '巴士'], ['（火車的）頭等車廂']]","chEntries":["教練","長途馬車","巴士","頭等車廂"],"practiceMeaning":"他是籃球隊的主教練。","analysis":"第一個義項「教練」的詞源來自匈牙利語 'kocsi' (a carriage)，最初指15世紀匈牙利科西鎮（Kocs）生產的一種馬車。後來，牛津大學的學生用它來比喻「（能載人順利通過考試的）導師」或「私人教師」。引申到體育領域，即「訓練運動員的教練」。第二個義項「長途馬車」、「巴士」則是直接繼承了馬車的原意。第三個義項「火車車廂」也是由馬車引申而來，指專門的車廂。","definition":"1. a person who trains athletes or sports teams; 2. a large bus used for carrying passengers, especially on long journeys; 3. a private railway carriage","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"教練激勵隊伍取勝。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The coach motivated the team to win.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"我們搭乘長途巴士去了倫敦。\",\n    \"eng\": \"We took a coach to London.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他是籃球隊的主教練。\",\n    \"eng\": \"He is the head coach of the basketball team.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他是籃球隊的主教練。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3979,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u3::column::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Please enter your name in the first ____.","expectedAnswer":"column","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Please enter your name in the first ____.","clozeAnswer":"column","exampleTranslation":"請在第一欄輸入您的名字。","reference":{"eng":"column","kk":"/ˈkɒləm/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['圓柱', '柱子'], ['專欄'], ['（隊伍、行列中的）縱隊', '一欄']]","chEntries":["圓柱","柱子","專欄","縱隊","一欄"],"practiceMeaning":"請在第一欄輸入您的名字。","analysis":"詞源：拉丁文 'columna' (柱子)。核心意義是垂直的、支撐結構。引申為報紙或雜誌中固定由一人撰寫的定期文章 (專欄)，以及表格或列表中的垂直部分 (一欄)。","definition":"1. a vertical architectural support of stone, typically cylindrical or rectangular in cross section; 2. a regular feature in a newspaper or magazine, typically one expressing the writer's opinions or discussing a particular subject; 3. a vertical section of a table or spreadsheet.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The ancient temple had many marble columns.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座古廟有許多大理石柱子。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He writes a weekly column on finance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他寫一篇關於金融的每週專欄。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please enter your name in the first column.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請在第一欄輸入您的名字。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"請在第一欄輸入您的名字。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6211,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::columnist::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ offered his opinion on the latest event.","expectedAnswer":"columnist","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ offered his opinion on the latest event.","clozeAnswer":"columnist","exampleTranslation":"這位專欄作家就最新事件發表了他的看法。","reference":{"eng":"columnist","kk":"ˈkɒləmɪst","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"專欄作家\"  ],  [    \"專欄作者\"  ]]","chEntries":["專欄作家","專欄作者"],"practiceMeaning":"這位專欄作家就最新事件發表了他的看法。","analysis":"此字由名詞 column（專欄）加上字尾 -ist（表示人或從事某種職業的人）構成。column 源自拉丁語 columna，意為「柱子，石柱」，引申為報紙或雜誌的「專欄」。字尾 -ist 標示從事該事物的個人。因此，columnist 指在報紙、雜誌或網站上定期撰寫專欄文章的人。中文翻譯為「專欄作家；專欄作者」。","definition":"a person who writes a regular column for a newspaper, magazine, or website.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The newspaper hired a new political columnist.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家報紙聘請了一位新的政治專欄作家。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a renowned food columnist for a popular magazine.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是某本受歡迎雜誌的著名美食專欄作家。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The columnist offered his opinion on the latest event.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位專欄作家就最新事件發表了他的看法。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這位專欄作家就最新事件發表了他的看法。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6215,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::commentator::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She is a respected cultural ____.","expectedAnswer":"commentator","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She is a respected cultural ____.","clozeAnswer":"commentator","exampleTranslation":"她是一位受尊敬的文化評論員。","reference":{"eng":"commentator","kk":"ˈkɒmənˌteɪtər","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"評論員\"  ],  [    \"講評員\"  ],  [    \"註釋者\"  ]]","chEntries":["評論員","講評員","註釋者"],"practiceMeaning":"她是一位受尊敬的文化評論員。","analysis":"此字由名詞 commentary（評論）加上字尾 -or（表示人，從事某種職業者）構成。commentary 源自拉丁語 commentum。字尾 -or 標示從事評論或提供講評的人。因此，commentator 指撰寫或發表評論、講評或分析的人，特別是在新聞、體育、政治等領域。中文翻譯為「評論員；講評員；註釋者」。","definition":"1. a person who explains or discusses something, especially in a newspaper or magazine; 2. a person who describes a sports event or other public event on the radio or television.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a well-known political commentator.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一位知名的政治評論員。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The football match was broadcast with live commentary.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這場足球賽事有現場講評播出。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a respected cultural commentator.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是一位受尊敬的文化評論員。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她是一位受尊敬的文化評論員。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5037,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::conceive::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The couple hoped to ____ a child.","expectedAnswer":"conceive","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The couple hoped to ____ a child.","clozeAnswer":"conceive","exampleTranslation":"這對夫婦希望懷孕生子。","reference":{"eng":"conceive","kk":"kənˈsiːv","tense":"v.","ch":"[['構想'], ['設想'], ['懷孕']]","chEntries":["構想","設想","懷孕"],"practiceMeaning":"這對夫婦希望懷孕生子。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語concipere，由 con-（一起、完全）+ capere（抓住、拿）組成，原意為「共同抓住」、「理解」或「懷孕」。在英語中，conceive 演變出多重語意：1. 「在心中形成概念、構想」，強調思維的創造性；2. 「懷孕」，指女性受孕；3. 「理解、認為」，表示對某事的看法。OCR 掃描時可能將 'c' 誤判為 'l' 或 'e' 誤判為 'c'。此處修正為 conceive，其多樣語意都圍繞著「形成」或「包含」的核心概念。","definition":"1. to form or have a mental concept or plan; 2. to become pregnant; 3. to form or devise (a plan or idea).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's difficult to conceive of a world without the internet.\",\n    \"ch\": \"很難想像一個沒有網際網路的世界。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She conceived a plan for the new project.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她為新專案構想了一個計畫。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The couple hoped to conceive a child.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這對夫婦希望懷孕生子。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這對夫婦希望懷孕生子。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4317,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::conscious::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It was a ____ effort to improve his grades.","expectedAnswer":"conscious","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It was a ____ effort to improve his grades.","clozeAnswer":"conscious","exampleTranslation":"這是為了提高他成績而付出的有意識的努力。","reference":{"eng":"conscious","kk":"/ˈkɒnʃəs/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['意識到的；察覺到的'], ['有意識的；清醒的'], ['故意的；蓄意的']]","chEntries":["意識到的","察覺到的","有意識的","清醒的","故意的","蓄意的"],"practiceMeaning":"這是為了提高他成績而付出的有意識的努力。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'conscius'，意為 'sharing knowledge, aware'，由 'con-' (with) 和 'scire' (to know) 構成。字面意思是『一起知道』，引申為『知道某事』、『意識到』。因此，第一個義項是『知道、察覺』。第二個義項是『有知覺、清醒』，與『失去意識』相對。第三個義項是『明知故犯』，強調『有意識地做』。","definition":"aware of something; awake and able to understand what is happening around you; done deliberately","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Are you conscious of the danger?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你意識到危險了嗎？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The patient remained conscious throughout the operation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"病人在手術全程都保持清醒。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was a conscious effort to improve his grades.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是為了提高他成績而付出的有意識的努力。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是為了提高他成績而付出的有意識的努力。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5491,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::consequent::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This policy change has many ____ effects.","expectedAnswer":"consequent","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This policy change has many ____ effects.","clozeAnswer":"consequent","exampleTranslation":"這項政策變更會產生許多連帶影響。","reference":{"eng":"consequent","kk":"ˈkɑnsəkwɛnt","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['因此而起的'], ['必然的'], ['結果的']]","chEntries":["因此而起的","必然的","結果的"],"practiceMeaning":"這項政策變更會產生許多連帶影響。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'consequens'，是動詞 'consequi'（跟隨、達成）的現在分詞。'Con-'（一起）+ 'sequi'（跟隨）。'Consequent' 作形容詞，意思是「隨之發生的、結果性的」。它用來描述某事是某個原因或事件的直接結果。與 'consequence'（名詞）對應，'consequent' 強調的是「由先前的事件所引發的」這種關聯性。","definition":"1. Happening as a result of something.; 2. Following as a logical or natural result.; 3. Following in order or succession.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The consequent reduction in traffic was noticeable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"隨之而來的交通量減少是顯而易見的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She made some unwise choices, and the consequent problems were severe.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她做出了一些不明智的選擇，隨之而來的問題也很嚴重。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This policy change has many consequent effects.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這項政策變更會產生許多連帶影響。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這項政策變更會產生許多連帶影響。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4491,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::controller::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company's ____ presented the quarterly financial report.","expectedAnswer":"controller","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company's ____ presented the quarterly financial report.","clozeAnswer":"controller","exampleTranslation":"該公司的財務主管提出了季度財務報告。","reference":{"eng":"controller","kk":"/kənˈtroʊlər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['控制者'], ['控制器'], ['（公司）財務主管']]","chEntries":["控制者","控制器","財務主管"],"practiceMeaning":"該公司的財務主管提出了季度財務報告。","analysis":"源自 control (控制)。加上 -er (表示「做某事的人或物」的名詞後綴)。核心語意是「負責控制者」。引申為控制裝置（如飛機的操縱桿），或公司中負責財務管理的人員（財務主管）。","definition":"1. A person or thing that controls or directs something; 2. A device used to control the operation of a machine or system; 3. (in business) A person who manages the finances of a company or organization.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The pilot is the controller of the aircraft.\",\n    \"ch\": \"飛行員是飛機的操控者。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The thermostat is a temperature controller.\",\n    \"ch\": \"恆溫器是一個溫度控制器。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company's controller presented the quarterly financial report.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司的財務主管提出了季度財務報告。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該公司的財務主管提出了季度財務報告。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3902,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::costly::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The war proved to be very ____ for both sides.","expectedAnswer":"costly","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The war proved to be very ____ for both sides.","clozeAnswer":"costly","exampleTranslation":"這場戰爭對雙方都 proved to be very costly。","reference":{"eng":"costly","kk":"/ˈkɔːstli/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['昂貴的'], ['代價高昂的']]","chEntries":["昂貴的","代價高昂的"],"practiceMeaning":"這場戰爭對雙方都 proved to be very costly。","analysis":"由 'cost' (成本) 加上形容詞後綴 '-ly' 組成。核心是「有高成本」。指價格高昂，或需要付出巨大代價（不一定是金錢）才能達成或維持。","definition":"1. costing a great deal of money; expensive. 2. involving a great loss or sacrifice.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a costly mistake.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個代價高昂的錯誤。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Expensive cars can be very costly to maintain.\",\n    \"ch\": \"昂貴的汽車可能維護費用很高。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The war proved to be very costly for both sides.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這場戰爭對雙方都 proved to be very costly。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這場戰爭對雙方都 proved to be very costly。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6218,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::cripple::vt","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The new regulations could ____ the industry.","expectedAnswer":"cripple","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The new regulations could ____ the industry.","clozeAnswer":"cripple","exampleTranslation":"新的規定可能會癱瘓這個行業。","reference":{"eng":"cripple","kk":"ˈkrɪpl","tense":"vt.","ch":"[  [    \"使殘疾\"  ],  [    \"嚴重損害\"  ],  [    \"削弱\"  ],  [    \"癱瘓\"  ]]","chEntries":["使殘疾","嚴重損害","削弱","癱瘓"],"practiceMeaning":"新的規定可能會癱瘓這個行業。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 crypel，意為「跛的，殘疾的」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作及物動詞時，核心語義是使某人身體殘疾、行動不便，或嚴重損害、削弱某事物的能力、功能或發展。此及物動詞義必須接受詞，例如 cripple a person、cripple an economy、cripple a company。中文翻譯為「使殘疾；嚴重損害；削弱；癱瘓」。","definition":"1. to cause someone to be unable to walk or move properly; 2. to damage something so severely that it cannot function properly; 3. to weaken or destroy the ability of someone or something to do something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The accident crippled him for life.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那場事故使他終身殘疾。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The economic recession crippled many businesses.\",\n    \"ch\": \"經濟衰退嚴重損害了許多企業。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The new regulations could cripple the industry.\",\n    \"ch\": \"新的規定可能會癱瘓這個行業。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"新的規定可能會癱瘓這個行業。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3075,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::critic::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____'s decision was final.","expectedAnswer":"critic","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____'s decision was final.","clozeAnswer":"critic","exampleTranslation":"裁判的決定是最終的。","reference":{"eng":"critic","kk":"/ˈkrɪtɪk/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['批評者'], ['評論家；評論員'], ['（古希臘）法官；裁判']]","chEntries":["批評者","評論家","評論員","法官","裁判"],"practiceMeaning":"裁判的決定是最終的。","analysis":"源自希臘語 'kritēs' (judge)。原意為「裁判」或「判斷者」，後發展為對事物進行評價和判斷的人。\n1. 批評者：指對某人或某事提出批評意見的人。\n2. 評論家；評論員：指在特定領域（如文學、藝術、電影、音樂）進行專業評論的人。\n3. （古希臘）法官；裁判：指在古代希臘負責判斷或裁決事務的人。","definition":"1. a person who expresses an unfavorable opinion of something; 2. a person who is qualified to judge and make comments about the quality of something, especially books, films, or art; 3. a person who expresses a reasoned analysis of the merits and faults of a work of literature or art.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a well-known critic of government policy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是政府政策的知名批評者。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The film critic gave the movie a glowing review.\",\n    \"ch\": \"電影評論家給這部電影寫了極高的評價。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The critic's decision was final.\",\n    \"ch\": \"裁判的決定是最終的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"裁判的決定是最終的。","sourceName":"字彙王、龍騰課本","unitName":"U39、L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3132,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::crush::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There was a dangerous ____ of fans trying to get close to the singer.","expectedAnswer":"crush","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There was a dangerous ____ of fans trying to get close to the singer.","clozeAnswer":"crush","exampleTranslation":"粉絲們為了接近歌手而發生了危險的擁擠。","reference":{"eng":"crush","kk":"/krʌʃ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['擠；擠壓；壓碎'], ['（愛情上的）迷戀；傾心'], ['（人群等的）擁擠']]","chEntries":["擠","擠壓","壓碎","迷戀","傾心","擁擠"],"practiceMeaning":"粉絲們為了接近歌手而發生了危險的擁擠。","analysis":"名詞用法，來自動詞 'crush'。指「壓碎」的動作或狀態，或是被壓碎的結果。在愛情語境下，'a crush' 指的是強烈的、短暫的迷戀或傾心。'Crush' 也可以形容人群的擁擠和壓力，與動詞的「擠壓」概念相關聯。","definition":"1. the act or process of crushing or being crushed; 2. a strong but usually temporary romantic infatuation; 3. a crowd of people or things pressing together.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The accident resulted in the crush of the victim's vehicle.\",\n    \"ch\": \"事故導致了受害者的車輛被壓毀。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He admitted he had a crush on his classmate.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他承認他傾心於他的女同學。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was a dangerous crush of fans trying to get close to the singer.\",\n    \"ch\": \"粉絲們為了接近歌手而發生了危險的擁擠。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"粉絲們為了接近歌手而發生了危險的擁擠。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3277,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::cue::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He picked up the ____ to play billiards.","expectedAnswer":"cue","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He picked up the ____ to play billiards.","clozeAnswer":"cue","exampleTranslation":"他拿起球棍打撞球。","reference":{"eng":"cue","kk":"/kjuː/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['提示；暗示'], ['（演員的）提示；（演奏的）提示'], ['（台球、撞球等的）球棍']]","chEntries":["提示","暗示","球棍"],"practiceMeaning":"他拿起球棍打撞球。","analysis":"詞源複雜，可能來自希臘字母 'tau' (τ)，用於標記音樂或戲劇中的提示點。引申為任何提供開始行動或回應的信號或提示。","definition":"1. a thing said or done that serves as a signal to a performer to enter or to speak; 2. an action or event that is regarded as a signal for something to happen; 3. a long, slender stick used in billiards and snooker.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The actor missed his cue and went on stage too early.\",\n    \"ch\": \"演員錯過了提示，過早地上台了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her sudden silence was a cue for me to change the subject.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她突然的沉默是個提示，讓我換個話題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He picked up the cue to play billiards.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他拿起球棍打撞球。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他拿起球棍打撞球。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3286,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::deadly::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The room was ____ silent after the announcement.","expectedAnswer":"deadly","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The room was ____ silent after the announcement.","clozeAnswer":"deadly","exampleTranslation":"宣布後，房間裡一片死寂。","reference":{"eng":"deadly","kk":"/ˈdɛdli/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['致命的；可致死的'], ['極度的；極為的'], ['（尤指）極其安靜的；死一般的']]","chEntries":["致命的","可致死的","極度的","極為的","極其安靜的","死一般的"],"practiceMeaning":"宣布後，房間裡一片死寂。","analysis":"由 'dead' (死的) 加上 '-ly' (形容詞後綴) 構成。直接表示與死亡相關，即可以致人於死地。也可作副詞，形容程度之深，如「極度」。","definition":"1. causing or able to cause death; 2. extreme or very great; 3. very quiet.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The snake's venom is deadly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"蛇的毒液是致命的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The situation was deadly serious.\",\n    \"ch\": \"情況極其嚴重。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The room was deadly silent after the announcement.\",\n    \"ch\": \"宣布後，房間裡一片死寂。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"宣布後，房間裡一片死寂。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4114,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::decade::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He lived abroad for a ____.","expectedAnswer":"decade","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He lived abroad for a ____.","clozeAnswer":"decade","exampleTranslation":"他在國外住了十年。","reference":{"eng":"decade","kk":"/ˈdɛkeɪd/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['十年']]","chEntries":["十年"],"practiceMeaning":"他在國外住了十年。","analysis":"源自希臘語 dekas，意為「十個」。引申為一個持續十年的時間段。","definition":"a period of ten years","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company has been successful for over a decade.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司已經成功經營了十多年。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The world has changed a lot in the past decade.\",\n    \"ch\": \"在過去的十年裡，世界發生了巨大的變化。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He lived abroad for a decade.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在國外住了十年。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他在國外住了十年。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6069,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::deficit::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company reported a net ____ for the third quarter.","expectedAnswer":"deficit","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company reported a net ____ for the third quarter.","clozeAnswer":"deficit","exampleTranslation":"公司報告第三季度出現淨虧損。","reference":{"eng":"deficit","kk":"ˈdɛfɪsɪt","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"赤字\"  ],  [    \"虧損\"  ],  [    \"不足額\"  ],  [    \"缺陷\"  ]]","chEntries":["赤字","虧損","不足額","缺陷"],"practiceMeaning":"公司報告第三季度出現淨虧損。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 deficit，是 deficere（to be wanting, to fail）的第三人稱單數現在時形式，由 de-（down, away）和 facere（to make, to do）組成。核心語義是「缺少」或「不足」。在經濟和財政領域，deficit 通常指「赤字」，即支出超過收入的金額。它也可以指在其他方面，如人才、資源上的「不足」。","definition":"1. the amount by which something, especially a sum of money, is too small; 2. a shortfall or lack.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The country is facing a significant budget deficit.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該國正面臨嚴重的預算赤字。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There is a deficit of skilled workers in the industry.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個行業缺乏技術工人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company reported a net deficit for the third quarter.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司報告第三季度出現淨虧損。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"公司報告第三季度出現淨虧損。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6071,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::delegate::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She served as a ____ at the political convention.","expectedAnswer":"delegate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She served as a ____ at the political convention.","clozeAnswer":"delegate","exampleTranslation":"她在大會上擔任了代表。","reference":{"eng":"delegate","kk":"ˈdɛləɡət","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"代表\"  ],  [    \"委員\"  ]]","chEntries":["代表","委員"],"practiceMeaning":"她在大會上擔任了代表。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 delegatus，是 deligare（to send, to entrust）的過去分詞。構詞上，de-（away）和 ligare（to bind）。核心語義是「被委派」或「被託付」的人。作為名詞，delegate 指的是被授權代表他人或組織參加會議、進行談判或履行職責的人。","definition":"a person sent or authorized to represent others, in particular, an elected representative sent to a conference.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Each country sent three delegates to the summit.\",\n    \"ch\": \"每個國家都派了三名代表參加峰會。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The delegates debated the new proposal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"代表們辯論了這項新提案。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She served as a delegate at the political convention.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在大會上擔任了代表。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她在大會上擔任了代表。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6073,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::delegation::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The process of ____ requires trust and clear communication.","expectedAnswer":"delegation","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The process of ____ requires trust and clear communication.","clozeAnswer":"delegation","exampleTranslation":"授權過程需要信任和清晰的溝通。","reference":{"eng":"delegation","kk":"ˌdɛləˈɡeɪʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"代表團\"  ],  [    \"授權\"  ],  [    \"委派\"  ]]","chEntries":["代表團","授權","委派"],"practiceMeaning":"授權過程需要信任和清晰的溝通。","analysis":"此字由 delegate（委派）加上名詞後綴 -ion（表示動作或狀態）構成。Delegate 源自拉丁語 delegare，意為「委派」。Delegation 的核心語義是「委派」這個動作或「被委派的人群」。作為名詞，它可以指一個由被委派的代表組成的「代表團」，也可以指「授權」或「委派」本身這個行為。","definition":"1. a group of people sent or authorized to represent others, in particular, government representatives; 2. the action of delegating a task or responsibility.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A large delegation of business leaders visited the country.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一個龐大的商業領袖代表團訪問了該國。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The delegation will meet with government officials tomorrow.\",\n    \"ch\": \"代表團將於明天與政府官員會面。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The process of delegation requires trust and clear communication.\",\n    \"ch\": \"授權過程需要信任和清晰的溝通。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"授權過程需要信任和清晰的溝通。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6167,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::denial::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The request was met with ____.","expectedAnswer":"denial","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The request was met with ____.","clozeAnswer":"denial","exampleTranslation":"這個請求被拒絕了。","reference":{"eng":"denial","kk":"dɪˈnaɪəl","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"否認\"  ],  [    \"否定\"  ],  [    \"拒絕承認\"  ],  [    \"拒絕給予\"  ]]","chEntries":["否認","否定","拒絕承認","拒絕給予"],"practiceMeaning":"這個請求被拒絕了。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 denegare，意為「否認、拒絕」，由 de- (away, negating) + negare (to deny) 組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 de-「否定」和 negare「否認」是其核心語意來源。作為名詞，其核心語義是由動詞 deny「否認」名詞化而來，指「拒絕承認事實或真實性」，也指「拒絕給予某物」。詞源中的「否定」概念是其核心。此義項由「否認」的動作延伸出「拒絕承認」或「拒絕給予」的結果。","definition":"1. the action of declaring something to be untrue; 2. an act of refusing to acknowledge or accept something; 3. an act of refusing to grant or allow something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His denial of the allegations was not convincing.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對這些指控的否認並不可信。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She lived in denial about her illness.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對自己的病情一直處於否認狀態。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The request was met with denial.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個請求被拒絕了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company issued a denial of the rumors.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司發布聲明否認這些謠言。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個請求被拒絕了。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5458,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::depend-on::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We can ____ him to finish the job.","expectedAnswer":"depend on","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We can ____ him to finish the job.","clozeAnswer":"depend on","exampleTranslation":"我們可以信賴他完成這項工作。","reference":{"eng":"depend on","kk":"dɪˈpend ɒn","tense":"v.","ch":"[['依賴'], ['依靠'], ['取決於']]","chEntries":["依賴","依靠","取決於"],"practiceMeaning":"我們可以信賴他完成這項工作。","analysis":"此片語由動詞 \"depend\" (依賴) 和介系詞 \"on\" 組成。\"depend\" 源自拉丁語 \"dependere\"，由 \"de-\" (來自、向下) 和 \"pendere\" (懸掛、稱重) 構成，原始語義是「懸掛在……之下」，引申為「依賴」、「取決於」。\"on\" 在此處表示依附或關聯。因此，\"depend on\" 表示「將……視為支持或基礎」，「需要……才能存在或發生」。","definition":"to rely on or trust someone or something; to be determined by or contingent on something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The success of the project depends on your cooperation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個項目的成功取決於你的合作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Children often depend on their parents for support.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子們經常依靠父母的支持。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We can depend on him to finish the job.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們可以信賴他完成這項工作。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們可以信賴他完成這項工作。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4122,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::desert::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They trekked across the ____.","expectedAnswer":"desert","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They trekked across the ____.","clozeAnswer":"desert","exampleTranslation":"他們徒步穿越了沙漠。","reference":{"eng":"desert","kk":"/ˈdɛzərt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['沙漠']]","chEntries":["沙漠"],"practiceMeaning":"他們徒步穿越了沙漠。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 desertum（荒蕪之地），是 desertus（被遺棄的）的中性形式。核心概念是「荒涼」、「無人居住」的地方。引申為極度乾燥、植被稀少的地區。","definition":"a barren or desolate area, especially one with little or no rainfall.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The Sahara Desert is the largest hot desert in the world.\",\n    \"ch\": \"撒哈拉沙漠是世界上最大的熱帶沙漠。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Many desert animals are nocturnal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"許多沙漠動物是夜行性的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They trekked across the desert.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們徒步穿越了沙漠。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們徒步穿越了沙漠。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5835,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::dilemma::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It's a classic ethical ____.","expectedAnswer":"dilemma","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It's a classic ethical ____.","clozeAnswer":"dilemma","exampleTranslation":"這是一個經典的道德困境。","reference":{"eng":"dilemma","kk":"dɪˈlɛmə","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"困境\"  ],  [    \"兩難\"  ],  [    \"進退兩難\"  ],  [    \"難題\"  ]]","chEntries":["困境","兩難","進退兩難","難題"],"practiceMeaning":"這是一個經典的道德困境。","analysis":"此字源自希臘語 'dilemma'，由 'di-' (two) 和 'lemma' (premise, assumption, proposition) 構成。原意為「兩項前提」或「兩難的論證」。在邏輯學中，'dilemma' 指一種論證形式，其中兩項可能的選擇都導向不希望的結果。在現代英語中，'dilemma' 指一種需要做出艱難選擇的處境，通常是在兩種或多種相互矛盾的選項之間，且每個選項都有其不利之處。核心語意是「必須在兩個或多個不理想的選項中做出選擇的困境」。例如，也可指「一項難以解決的問題」。","definition":"1. A situation in which a difficult choice has to be made between two or more alternatives, especially equally undesirable ones.; 2. A problem offering no satisfactory solution.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He faced a dilemma: either tell the truth and hurt his friend, or lie and betray his principles.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他面臨兩難：要么說實話傷害朋友，要么撒謊背叛自己的原則。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company is in a dilemma about whether to expand or consolidate.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司在是否擴張或整合的問題上陷入了困境。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's a classic ethical dilemma.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個經典的道德困境。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The scientist faced the dilemma of publishing his findings or keeping them secret.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位科學家面臨著是發表研究結果還是保密的兩難。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是一個經典的道德困境。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5611,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l7::discrimination::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ based on sexual orientation is illegal in many countries.","expectedAnswer":"Discrimination","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ based on sexual orientation is illegal in many countries.","clozeAnswer":"Discrimination","exampleTranslation":"基於性取向的歧視在許多國家都是非法的。","reference":{"eng":"discrimination","kk":"dɪˌskrɪməˈneɪʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[['歧視'], ['區別對待'], ['識別能力']]","chEntries":["歧視","區別對待","識別能力"],"practiceMeaning":"基於性取向的歧視在許多國家都是非法的。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'discriminatio'，意為「區別」，由 'discriminare'（區分）派生，'discriminare' 又由 'dis-'（分開）和 'cernere'（分辨）組成。構詞學上，'dis-' 字首表示「分開」、「分離」，'cernere' 詞根提供「分辨」、「篩選」的核心語意。'-ation' 字尾將動詞轉換為名詞，表示「過程」或「狀態」。原始語意是「將事物分開、區別開來」。引申出兩個主要用法：一是「識別能力」（分辨細微差異的能力），二是「不公平的區別對待」，即「歧視」，特別是在種族、性別、年齡等方面。後者是現代社會語境中較常見的用法。","definition":"1. The unjust or prejudicial treatment of different categories of people, especially on grounds of race, age, or sex; 2. The ability to discern or distinguish between different things; 3. The action of treating a difference between things differently.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company has a strict policy against discrimination.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司有嚴格的反歧視政策。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Children develop the ability for visual discrimination at an early age.\",\n    \"ch\": \"兒童早期就會發展出視覺辨別能力。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Discrimination based on sexual orientation is illegal in many countries.\",\n    \"ch\": \"基於性取向的歧視在許多國家都是非法的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"基於性取向的歧視在許多國家都是非法的。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5494,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::disturbance::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The police were called to deal with a ____.","expectedAnswer":"disturbance","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The police were called to deal with a ____.","clozeAnswer":"disturbance","exampleTranslation":"警察被召來處理一起騷亂事件。","reference":{"eng":"disturbance","kk":"dɪˈstɜrbəns","tense":"n.","ch":"[['干擾'], ['騷動'], ['妨礙']]","chEntries":["干擾","騷動","妨礙"],"practiceMeaning":"警察被召來處理一起騷亂事件。","analysis":"此字由動詞 'disturb'（打擾、干擾）加上名詞字尾 '-ance'（來自拉丁語 '-antia'）構成。'-ance' 用來形成表示「行為、狀態或過程」的名詞。因此，'disturbance' 指的是「打擾、干擾、擾亂」的行為或狀態。它是一個抽象名詞，描述了某種東西打破了原本的平靜、秩序或正常狀態的情況。","definition":"1. The interruption of a settled or peaceful condition.; 2. An act of disturbing.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The loud music caused a disturbance in the neighborhood.\",\n    \"ch\": \"吵鬧的音樂引起了社區的騷動。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We experienced a power disturbance during the storm.\",\n    \"ch\": \"風暴期間我們經歷了電力中斷（干擾）。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police were called to deal with a disturbance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警察被召來處理一起騷亂事件。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"警察被召來處理一起騷亂事件。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5042,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::domain::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"You need to register a ____ name for your website.","expectedAnswer":"domain","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"You need to register a ____ name for your website.","clozeAnswer":"domain","exampleTranslation":"你需要為你的網站註冊一個域名。","reference":{"eng":"domain","kk":"doʊˈmeɪn","tense":"n.","ch":"[['領域'], ['範圍'], ['域名']]","chEntries":["領域","範圍","域名"],"practiceMeaning":"你需要為你的網站註冊一個域名。","analysis":"此字源自古法語domaine，本身又來自拉丁語dominium，意為「所有權、領地」，來自 dominus（主人）。原意指「屬於領主的地產」。在英語中，domain 演變出多重語意：1. 「領地、領土」，指某人或某事物所擁有的或控制的範圍；2. 「領域、專業範圍」，指某個學科、知識或活動的專屬範疇；3. 在網路語境中，指「域名」(domain name)。OCR 掃描時可能將 'o' 誤判為 '0'。此處修正為 domain。","definition":"1. an area of territory owned or controlled by a ruler or government; 2. an area of knowledge or activity; 3. a set of possible values for a variable.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Physics is a complex scientific domain.\",\n    \"ch\": \"物理學是一個複雜的科學領域。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company is expanding its domain into new markets.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司正在將其業務範圍擴展到新市場。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"You need to register a domain name for your website.\",\n    \"ch\": \"你需要為你的網站註冊一個域名。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"你需要為你的網站註冊一個域名。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4355,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::domestic::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Dogs are ____ animals.","expectedAnswer":"domestic","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Dogs are ____ animals.","clozeAnswer":"domestic","exampleTranslation":"狗是馴養的動物。","reference":{"eng":"domestic","kk":"/dəˈmɛstɪk/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['國內的；本土的'], ['家庭的；家用的'], ['（動物）馴養的']]","chEntries":["國內的","本土的","家庭的","家用的","馴養的"],"practiceMeaning":"狗是馴養的動物。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'domesticus'，意為『家裡的』，來自 'domus' (house)。1. 指發生在國家『國內』的，與『國際』相對。2. 指與『家庭』相關的，如『家庭生活』、『家務』。3. 指被人類馴養的動物，如『家禽』、『家畜』，與『野生的』相對。","definition":"existing or occurring in a country or in domestic policy; relating to the running of a home or to family relations; kept or living at home and not wild","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company focuses on the domestic market.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司專注於國內市場。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Domestic chores include cooking and cleaning.\",\n    \"ch\": \"家務包括烹飪和清潔。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Dogs are domestic animals.\",\n    \"ch\": \"狗是馴養的動物。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"狗是馴養的動物。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U8、L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5780,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::donation::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Your ____ will make a real difference.","expectedAnswer":"donation","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Your ____ will make a real difference.","clozeAnswer":"donation","exampleTranslation":"您的捐贈將帶來真正的改變。","reference":{"eng":"donation","kk":"doʊˈneɪʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"捐贈\"  ],  [    \"捐款\"  ],  [    \"捐獻物\"  ]]","chEntries":["捐贈","捐款","捐獻物"],"practiceMeaning":"您的捐贈將帶來真正的改變。","analysis":"此字為名詞，構詞自donate（捐贈）+ -ion（名詞字尾，表示「行為；狀態；結果」）。-ion字尾源自拉丁語-io。donate源自拉丁語donare（給予；捐贈）。因此，donation的核心語義是指「捐贈的行為」或「被捐贈的物品或金錢」。語意演變上，由動詞「捐贈」的動作，發展為抽象的「捐贈行為」和具體的「捐贈物」。","definition":"1. money or goods given to help a charity or other organization; 2. the act of giving something, especially to a charity.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We received a generous donation from a local business.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們收到了一家本地企業的大筆捐款。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The hospital relies on donations to fund its research.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家醫院依靠捐款來資助其研究。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Your donation will make a real difference.\",\n    \"ch\": \"您的捐贈將帶來真正的改變。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"您的捐贈將帶來真正的改變。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3143,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::dread::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He lived in constant ____ of being discovered.","expectedAnswer":"dread","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He lived in constant ____ of being discovered.","clozeAnswer":"dread","exampleTranslation":"他生活在被發現的持續恐懼中。","reference":{"eng":"dread","kk":"/drɛd/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['恐懼；害怕'], ['（預期中的）災禍；禍患']]","chEntries":["恐懼","害怕","災禍","禍患"],"practiceMeaning":"他生活在被發現的持續恐懼中。","analysis":"名詞用法，源自動詞 'dread'。指「強烈的恐懼」、「畏懼」或「恐慌」，特別是對即將發生的不好的事情的預期。它也可以指「災禍」或「禍患」，暗示著一件令人感到恐懼或憂慮的事情。","definition":"1. great fear or apprehension; 2. a cause of great fear or apprehension.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The thought of failing the exam filled him with dread.\",\n    \"ch\": \"考試不及格的想法讓他充滿恐懼。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The dread of war hung over the nation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"戰爭的恐懼籠罩著這個國家。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He lived in constant dread of being discovered.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他生活在被發現的持續恐懼中。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他生活在被發現的持續恐懼中。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5080,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::dreadful::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He has a ____ habit of interrupting.","expectedAnswer":"dreadful","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He has a ____ habit of interrupting.","clozeAnswer":"dreadful","exampleTranslation":"他有打斷別人說話的可怕習慣。","reference":{"eng":"dreadful","kk":"ˈdredfl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['可怕的'], ['糟糕的'], ['極度的']]","chEntries":["可怕的","糟糕的","極度的"],"practiceMeaning":"他有打斷別人說話的可怕習慣。","analysis":"此字由 'dread' (恐懼) + '-ful' (形容詞化後綴，表示充滿、具有某種性質) 構成。'-ful' 在此強調充滿了 'dread' 的特質。核心語義是 '引發極度恐懼或憂慮的'。因此，它可以用來形容令人不安、可怕的事物。也可用來表示程度，如 '極度糟糕的'、'非常嚴重的'，強調其負面或強烈的影響。","definition":"1. Causing or involving great suffering, fear, or unhappiness; extremely bad.; 2. Of very low quality; very unpleasant.; 3. Inspiring dread or fear.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The news of the accident was dreadful.\",\n    \"ch\": \"事故的消息是可怕的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The weather was dreadful all week.\",\n    \"ch\": \"整個星期天氣都糟透了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has a dreadful habit of interrupting.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他有打斷別人說話的可怕習慣。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他有打斷別人說話的可怕習慣。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4191,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::educate::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need to ____ the public about the risks.","expectedAnswer":"educate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need to ____ the public about the risks.","clozeAnswer":"educate","exampleTranslation":"我們需要向公眾灌輸有關風險的知識。","reference":{"eng":"educate","kk":"/ˈedʒukeɪt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['教育；培養'], ['訓練；教授'], ['（用特定觀點）教育，教導（使有某種觀念）']]","chEntries":["教育","培養","訓練","教授","教育，教導"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要向公眾灌輸有關風險的知識。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 educare，意為“引導出來，培養”，來自 ēdūcere（引導，提出）。'ē-'（出）+ 'dūcere'（引導）。核心意義是“引導，培養”。1. “教育；培養”是最普遍的意義，指傳授知識和技能。2. “訓練；教授”更側重於具體的技能傳授。3. “教導（使有某種觀念）”則指通過教育來塑造人的思想和價值觀。","definition":"1. to teach or train someone, especially at a school or university; 2. to provide knowledge and understanding; 3. to provide with a particular set of ideas or beliefs.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The school aims to educate children from diverse backgrounds.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這所學校旨在教育來自不同背景的兒童。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was educated in England.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在英國接受教育。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to educate the public about the risks.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要向公眾灌輸有關風險的知識。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要向公眾灌輸有關風險的知識。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4449,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::electronic::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company specializes in ____ components.","expectedAnswer":"electronic","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company specializes in ____ components.","clozeAnswer":"electronic","exampleTranslation":"該公司專門生產電子零件。","reference":{"eng":"electronic","kk":"/ɪˈlɛktrɪk/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['電子的'], ['電腦化的'], ['（尤指）電流通過裝置的']]","chEntries":["電子的","電腦化的","電流通過裝置的"],"practiceMeaning":"該公司專門生產電子零件。","analysis":"源自 electro- (來自希臘語 ēlektron, 意為琥珀，因其摩擦生電的性質而得名) 加上 -ic (形容詞後綴)。核心概念是與電有關。語意從「與電有關」延伸至「由電力驅動的」、「通過電子元件運作的」，如電子設備 (electronic devices)。","definition":"1. Operated by or using electricity, especially in an advanced or complex way; relating to or using devices that operate by the flow of electrons.; 2. Relating to or concerned with the production and emission of electrons.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She bought a new electronic gadget for her kitchen.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她買了一個新的電子小工具給她的廚房。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Electronic mail has revolutionized communication.\",\n    \"ch\": \"電子郵件徹底改變了通訊方式。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company specializes in electronic components.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司專門生產電子零件。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該公司專門生產電子零件。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5623,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l7::eliminate::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This diet plan helps to ____ unhealthy cravings.","expectedAnswer":"eliminate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This diet plan helps to ____ unhealthy cravings.","clozeAnswer":"eliminate","exampleTranslation":"這個飲食計畫有助於消除不健康的渴望。","reference":{"eng":"eliminate","kk":"ɪˈlɪmɪneɪt","tense":"v.","ch":"[['消除'], ['排除'], ['淘汰']]","chEntries":["消除","排除","淘汰"],"practiceMeaning":"這個飲食計畫有助於消除不健康的渴望。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'eliminare'，意為「移出門外」、「排除」，由 'e-'（出）和 'limen'（門檻）組成。構詞學上，'e-' 是表示「出」或「離開」的字首，'limen' 是「門檻」的核心詞根，'-ate' 是動詞化字尾。原始語意是「將某物移出門檻之外」，引申為「清除」、「排除」、「消除」或「淘汰」。","definition":"1. Remove or get rid of (something unwanted); 2. Completely destroy or put an end to; 3. Exclude or expel from a contest or place.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to eliminate waste from the production process.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要從生產過程中消除浪費。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The team was eliminated in the semi-finals.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該隊在半決賽中被淘汰了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This diet plan helps to eliminate unhealthy cravings.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個飲食計畫有助於消除不健康的渴望。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個飲食計畫有助於消除不健康的渴望。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6118,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::eloquent::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The book provides an ____ defense of human rights.","expectedAnswer":"eloquent","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The book provides an ____ defense of human rights.","clozeAnswer":"eloquent","exampleTranslation":"這本書有力地捍衛了人權。","reference":{"eng":"eloquent","kk":"ˈɛləkwənt","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"雄辯的\"  ],  [    \"口才好的\"  ],  [    \"有說服力的\"  ],  [    \"鮮明的\"  ]]","chEntries":["雄辯的","口才好的","有說服力的","鮮明的"],"practiceMeaning":"這本書有力地捍衛了人權。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 ēloquēns，是 ēloquī（說出；流利地說）的現在分詞。構詞上，ē- 是強調字首，loquī 意為「說話」，與 loquor（說）有關。因此，eloquent 的核心語義是「說話有力、流利」。此形容詞用於描述演講、作家、言論或表達方式，強調其具有說服力、感染力和清晰度。其語意演變是從具體的「能說會道」到抽象的「有說服力的、鮮明的」。","definition":"1. fluent or persuasive in speaking or writing; 2. clearly expressing or indicating something; vivid.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is an eloquent speaker.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一位雄辯的演講者。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her eyes were eloquent in their sorrow.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她眼中流露出的悲傷鮮明動人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The book provides an eloquent defense of human rights.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本書有力地捍衛了人權。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這本書有力地捍衛了人權。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3146,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::energetic::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Renovating the old house was an ____ undertaking.","expectedAnswer":"energetic","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Renovating the old house was an ____ undertaking.","clozeAnswer":"energetic","exampleTranslation":"翻新這座老房子是一項需要大量精力的工程。","reference":{"eng":"energetic","kk":"/ˌɛnərˈdʒɛtɪk/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['精力充沛的；充滿活力的'], ['（行動、過程）需要大量體力的']]","chEntries":["精力充沛的","充滿活力的","需要大量體力的"],"practiceMeaning":"翻新這座老房子是一項需要大量精力的工程。","analysis":"源自名詞 'energy'，意為「能量」。'Energetic' 形容詞表示擁有或顯示出大量的能量、活力和熱情。它強調的是積極、活躍、有幹勁的狀態，常與體力活動或強烈的情緒反應相關。與 'dynamic' 相似，但更側重於個體的活力和行動力。","definition":"1. showing or involving great energy and enthusiasm; 2. requiring a lot of energy.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The children were energetic and full of fun.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子們精力充沛，充滿樂趣。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is an energetic advocate for environmental protection.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是環保運動的積極倡導者。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Renovating the old house was an energetic undertaking.\",\n    \"ch\": \"翻新這座老房子是一項需要大量精力的工程。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"翻新這座老房子是一項需要大量精力的工程。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4146,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::engage::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The gears failed to ____.","expectedAnswer":"engage","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The gears failed to ____.","clozeAnswer":"engage","exampleTranslation":"齒輪未能嚙合。","reference":{"eng":"engage","kk":"/ɪnˈɡeɪdʒ/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['從事', '參與'], ['僱用', '聘請'], ['吸引（注意力、興趣）'], ['（機器）嚙合', '結合'], ['訂婚']]","chEntries":["從事","參與","僱用","聘請","吸引","嚙合","結合","訂婚"],"practiceMeaning":"齒輪未能嚙合。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 angere（引誘，捆綁）。核心概念是「被牽連」或「投入」。引申為積極參與、吸引他人注意、機器部件的咬合，以及婚姻的承諾（訂婚）。","definition":"1. occupy, attract, or involve (someone's interest or attention); 2. enter into conflict with (an enemy); 3. employ or hire someone; 4. (of gears) mesh or interlock; 5. lodge or carry on (a war); 6. promise to marry","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The teacher tried to engage the students' interest.\",\n    \"ch\": \"老師試圖吸引學生的興趣。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company engages in international trade.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司從事國際貿易。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The gears failed to engage.\",\n    \"ch\": \"齒輪未能嚙合。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They became engaged last year.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們去年訂婚了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"齒輪未能嚙合。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3887,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::enjoyable::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The book made for an ____ read.","expectedAnswer":"enjoyable","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The book made for an ____ read.","clozeAnswer":"enjoyable","exampleTranslation":"這本書提供了愉快的閱讀體驗。","reference":{"eng":"enjoyable","kk":"/ɪnˈdʒɔɪəbl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['愉快的', '令人享受的']]","chEntries":["愉快的","令人享受的"],"practiceMeaning":"這本書提供了愉快的閱讀體驗。","analysis":"由 'enjoy' (享受) 和 '-able' (形容詞後綴，表示「可…的」) 組成。核心是「可以享受的」。指能帶來樂趣、快樂或滿意的。","definition":"pleasant and giving pleasure.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was an enjoyable evening.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個愉快的夜晚。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We had an enjoyable time at the party.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們在派對上玩得很開心。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The book made for an enjoyable read.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本書提供了愉快的閱讀體驗。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這本書提供了愉快的閱讀體驗。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5551,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::enterprise::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She admired his entrepreneurial ____ and determination.","expectedAnswer":"enterprise","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She admired his entrepreneurial ____ and determination.","clozeAnswer":"enterprise","exampleTranslation":"她讚賞他那創業的膽識與決心。","reference":{"eng":"enterprise","kk":"ˈɛntərˌpraɪz","tense":"n.","ch":"[['企業'], ['事業'], ['公司'], ['進取心'], ['膽量'], ['冒險精神']]","chEntries":["企業","事業","公司","進取心","膽量","冒險精神"],"practiceMeaning":"她讚賞他那創業的膽識與決心。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 \"entreprendre\"，意為 \"to undertake\"（承擔、著手做）。\"entre-\" 意為 \"between, among\"（在……之間），\"prendre\" 則意為 \"to take\"（拿取）。因此，\"enterprise\" 在語源上表示「承擔、著手去做的事情」。早期語義多指「冒險性的、艱鉅的任務」，引申出「膽量、進取心」。隨著商業發展，逐漸演變成指「企業、公司、事業」，尤其指那些有規模、有冒險精神的商業組織。因此，核心語義是「承擔某事」，進而發展出「任務、事業、企業」以及驅動這些事業所需的「進取心」和「膽量」。","definition":"1. A business organization, such as a company or a firm; also, the people who work for it; 2. A project or undertaking, especially one that is difficult, complicated, or requires effort; 3. Resourcefulness and readiness to undertake bold or difficult projects; courage and shrewdness.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company has grown into a large international enterprise.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司已發展成為一家大型的國際企業。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Starting a new business is always a risky enterprise.\",\n    \"ch\": \"創辦新事業總是一項充滿風險的冒險。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She admired his entrepreneurial enterprise and determination.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她讚賞他那創業的膽識與決心。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她讚賞他那創業的膽識與決心。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4481,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::entry::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ fee for the exhibition is $10.","expectedAnswer":"entry","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ fee for the exhibition is $10.","clozeAnswer":"entry","exampleTranslation":"這次展覽的入場費是10美元。","reference":{"eng":"entry","kk":"/ˈɛntri/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['入口'], ['進入'], ['（書籍、名單等的）條目'], ['（參賽）報名']]","chEntries":["入口","進入","條目","報名"],"practiceMeaning":"這次展覽的入場費是10美元。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 intrare，意為「進入」。通過古法語 entree，演變成英語的 entry。核心語意是「進入的行為或地點」。引申為「進入某個領域或列表中的一個項目」，以及「登記參加某個活動」。","definition":"1. An act of going or coming in; 2. A way into or up to a place; 3. A word or statement in a dictionary or encyclopedia, or an item in a list; 4. An act of signing up for a competition or event.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The main entrance to the building is on the north side.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這棟建築的主要入口在北面。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her name was an entry in the Guinness Book of Records.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的名字是健力士世界紀錄中的一項記錄。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The entry fee for the exhibition is $10.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這次展覽的入場費是10美元。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"All entries must be submitted by Friday.\",\n    \"ch\": \"所有報名者必須在週五前提交。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這次展覽的入場費是10美元。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5587,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::excellent::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The team achieved ____ results.","expectedAnswer":"excellent","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The team achieved ____ results.","clozeAnswer":"excellent","exampleTranslation":"這支隊伍取得了優異的成績。","reference":{"eng":"excellent","kk":"ˈɛksələnt","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['優秀的'], ['卓越的'], ['極好的'], ['出色的']]","chEntries":["優秀的","卓越的","極好的","出色的"],"practiceMeaning":"這支隊伍取得了優異的成績。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 \"excellēns\"，是 \"excellere\"（to be eminent, surpass, excel，卓越，超越）的現在分詞。\"excellere\" 由 \"ex-\"（out）和 \"cellere\"（to rise, to be eminent，上升，卓越）組成，意為「突出，超越眾人」。因此，\"excellent\" 的核心語義是「非常出色、品質極高、超越一般水準」。它用來形容人、物、表現或情況，表示其達到了極高的標準。","definition":"1. Extremely good; outstanding; 2. Very high in quality or degree.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"That was an excellent meal!\",\n    \"ch\": \"那是一頓極好的餐點！\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He gave an excellent presentation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他做了一個出色的報告。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The team achieved excellent results.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這支隊伍取得了優異的成績。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這支隊伍取得了優異的成績。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4202,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::exchange::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The students will ____ with a school in France.","expectedAnswer":"exchange","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The students will ____ with a school in France.","clozeAnswer":"exchange","exampleTranslation":"學生們將與一所法國學校進行交換。","reference":{"eng":"exchange","kk":"/ɪksˈtʃeɪndʒ/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['交換；兌換'], ['交流；溝通'], ['（在兩國或兩個組織間）交換']]","chEntries":["交換","兌換","交流","溝通"],"practiceMeaning":"學生們將與一所法國學校進行交換。","analysis":"源自古法語 escanger，意為“交換”，來自拉丁語 excitangere，'ex-'（出）+ 'tangere'（觸摸，接觸）。核心是“相互接觸並轉移”。1. “交換；兌換”指用一種東西換另一種，或用貨幣換另一種貨幣。2. “交流；溝通”指思想、資訊的相互傳遞。3. “在兩國或兩個組織間交換”是特定領域的應用。","definition":"1. to give one thing and receive another in return; 2. to communicate with someone by giving them information and receiving information from them; 3. to transfer between two countries or two organizations.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I'd like to exchange this shirt for a different size.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我想把這件襯衫換成別的尺寸。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They exchanged ideas on how to improve the project.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們就如何改進項目交換了意見。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The students will exchange with a school in France.\",\n    \"ch\": \"學生們將與一所法國學校進行交換。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"學生們將與一所法國學校進行交換。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5535,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l5::execution::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Her ____ of the piano piece was flawless.","expectedAnswer":"execution","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Her ____ of the piano piece was flawless.","clozeAnswer":"execution","exampleTranslation":"她演奏的鋼琴曲無懈可擊。","reference":{"eng":"execution","kk":"ˌeksɪˈkjuːʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[['執行'], ['處決'], [' تنفيذ'], ['技術']]","chEntries":["執行","處決","تنفيذ","技術"],"practiceMeaning":"她演奏的鋼琴曲無懈可擊。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'executio'，由 'ex-' (out) + 'sequi' (to follow) 構成，意思是「跟隨、執行」。'execute' 是其動詞形式，意為「執行」。構詞上，'ex-' 表示「完成、結束」，'secut-' 是 'sequi' 的詞幹，意為「跟隨」。'execution' 作名詞，指「執行」的動作或過程，包括執行法律判決（處決）、履行職責或完成計劃。在技術或藝術領域，它也指「技藝的熟練程度」或「表現」。多個義項都圍繞著「完成、實施、執行」的核心概念。","definition":"the carrying out of a plan, order, or course of action; the act of putting a condemned person to death; technical skill or performance.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The execution of the plan was successful.\",\n    \"ch\": \"計劃的執行很成功。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The execution of the prisoner took place at dawn.\",\n    \"ch\": \"囚犯的處決於黎明時進行。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her execution of the piano piece was flawless.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她演奏的鋼琴曲無懈可擊。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她演奏的鋼琴曲無懈可擊。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3149,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::exhausted::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She felt ____ by the constant worry.","expectedAnswer":"exhausted","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She felt ____ by the constant worry.","clozeAnswer":"exhausted","exampleTranslation":"她因持續的擔憂而感到精疲力竭。","reference":{"eng":"exhausted","kk":"/ɪɡˈzɔːstɪd/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['筋疲力盡的；精疲力竭的'], ['（資源、供應品等）被用盡的']]","chEntries":["筋疲力盡的","精疲力竭的","被用盡的"],"practiceMeaning":"她因持續的擔憂而感到精疲力竭。","analysis":"動詞 'exhaust' 的過去分詞，用作形容詞。表示處於極度疲憊、精疲力竭的狀態，由於過度的勞動、活動或情緒消耗。也指某種資源、供應或情況已經被完全用完、耗盡。","definition":"1. very tired; 2. having no energy left; 3. completely used up.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"After the marathon, the runners were completely exhausted.\",\n    \"ch\": \"馬拉松賽後，跑者們都筋疲力盡了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The country's oil reserves were nearly exhausted.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該國的石油儲備幾乎被耗盡了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She felt exhausted by the constant worry.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她因持續的擔憂而感到精疲力竭。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她因持續的擔憂而感到精疲力竭。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3150,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::exhausting::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The long and ____ search finally yielded results.","expectedAnswer":"exhausting","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The long and ____ search finally yielded results.","clozeAnswer":"exhausting","exampleTranslation":"漫長而令人疲憊的搜尋終於有了結果。","reference":{"eng":"exhausting","kk":"/ɪɡˈzɔːstɪŋ/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['令人精疲力竭的；使人疲憊不堪的']]","chEntries":["令人精疲力竭的","使人疲憊不堪的"],"practiceMeaning":"漫長而令人疲憊的搜尋終於有了結果。","analysis":"動詞 'exhaust' 的現在分詞，用作形容詞。描述某事物（活動、工作、經歷）能夠導致他人感到極度疲憊、精疲力竭。與 'exhausted'（表示自身狀態）相對，'exhausting' 描述的是原因。","definition":"causing extreme physical or mental tiredness.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Climbing the mountain was an exhausting experience.\",\n    \"ch\": \"攀登這座山是一次令人精疲力竭的經歷。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Dealing with difficult customers can be very exhausting.\",\n    \"ch\": \"應付難纏的顧客會非常累人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The long and exhausting search finally yielded results.\",\n    \"ch\": \"漫長而令人疲憊的搜尋終於有了結果。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"漫長而令人疲憊的搜尋終於有了結果。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6074,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::expedition::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The relief ____ arrived quickly.","expectedAnswer":"expedition","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The relief ____ arrived quickly.","clozeAnswer":"expedition","exampleTranslation":"救援隊迅速抵達。","reference":{"eng":"expedition","kk":"ˌɛkspəˈdɪʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"遠征\"  ],  [    \"考察\"  ],  [    \"探險\"  ],  [    \"遠足\"  ],  [    \"迅速\"  ]]","chEntries":["遠征","考察","探險","遠足","迅速"],"practiceMeaning":"救援隊迅速抵達。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 expeditio，是 expédire（to send out, to dispatch）的結果名詞。Expédire 由 ex-（out）和 pes, pedis（foot）組成，字面意思是「派腳出去」，引申為「派遣」，再引申為「迅速完成」、「派出以達成目的」。構詞上，ex- 表「出」，ped- 表「腳」，-ition 是名詞後綴。Expedition 的核心語義是「為特定目的（通常是探索、考察、科學研究或軍事行動）而進行的、有組織的、較長距離的出行」。它也引申為「迅速」這個較少用的意義。","definition":"1. a journey undertaken by a group of people with a particular purpose, especially exploration, scientific research, or war; 2. efficiency and speed in doing something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The expedition set out to explore the Amazon rainforest.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這次探險隊出發去探索亞馬遜雨林。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They prepared for a polar expedition.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們為極地考察做好了準備。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The relief expedition arrived quickly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"救援隊迅速抵達。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"救援隊迅速抵達。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4053,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::faith::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His ____ in God gives him strength.","expectedAnswer":"faith","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His ____ in God gives him strength.","clozeAnswer":"faith","exampleTranslation":"他對上帝的信仰給予他力量。","reference":{"eng":"faith","kk":"/feɪθ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['信仰', '信念'], ['信任', '信賴'], ['保證', '承諾']]","chEntries":["信仰","信念","信任","信賴","保證","承諾"],"practiceMeaning":"他對上帝的信仰給予他力量。","analysis":"源自古法語 'feid'，來自拉丁語 'fides' (faith, trust, belief)，與 'fidelis' (faithful) 同源。核心是「相信」、「信任」。因此，'faith' 可以指宗教上的「信仰」、對某人或某事的「信任」，或是對某事成功或發生的「信念」、「希望」。第四個義項「保證」則是由「信任」引申，表示基於信任而產生的承諾或保證。","definition":"1. strong belief in God or in the doctrines of a religion; 2. complete trust or confidence in someone or something; 3. a strong feeling of trust or confidence","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"她對她醫生的能力深具信心。\",\n    \"eng\": \"She has great faith in her doctor's abilities.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他們對政府已經失去了信心。\",\n    \"eng\": \"They have lost faith in the government.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他對上帝的信仰給予他力量。\",\n    \"eng\": \"His faith in God gives him strength.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他對上帝的信仰給予他力量。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4155,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::family::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He is very close to his ____.","expectedAnswer":"family","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He is very close to his ____.","clozeAnswer":"family","exampleTranslation":"他與家人感情很好。","reference":{"eng":"family","kk":"/ˈfæməli/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['家庭', '家人'], ['家族']]","chEntries":["家庭","家人","家族"],"practiceMeaning":"他與家人感情很好。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 familia（家庭，僕人，奴隸），可能是從 famulus（僕人）來的。核心概念是「一起居住並有親屬關係或緊密聯繫的一群人」。","definition":"1. a group consisting of parents and children living together in a household; 2. all the descendants of a common ancestor","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She comes from a large family.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她來自一個大家庭。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The family had dinner together.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一家人共進晚餐。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is very close to his family.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他與家人感情很好。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他與家人感情很好。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3923,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::fearful::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She gave a ____ glance at the approaching storm.","expectedAnswer":"fearful","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She gave a ____ glance at the approaching storm.","clozeAnswer":"fearful","exampleTranslation":"她對逼近的風暴投以恐懼的一瞥。","reference":{"eng":"fearful","kk":"/ˈfɪərfəl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['害怕的', '恐懼的'], ['令人害怕的']]","chEntries":["害怕的","恐懼的","令人害怕的"],"practiceMeaning":"她對逼近的風暴投以恐懼的一瞥。","analysis":"源自古英語 'fēarlīc'，由 'fēar' (意為「恐懼」) 和 '-ful' (形容詞後綴) 組成。有兩層意思：一是指「感到恐懼」，二是指「引起恐懼」。","definition":"1. feeling fear or anxiety; frightened; 2. feeling or showing fear; 3. causing fear.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was fearful of the dark.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他害怕黑暗。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The fearful news spread quickly through the town.\",\n    \"ch\": \"令人恐懼的消息迅速傳遍了整個城鎮。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She gave a fearful glance at the approaching storm.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對逼近的風暴投以恐懼的一瞥。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她對逼近的風暴投以恐懼的一瞥。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4334,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::fence::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need to ____ the new plot of land.","expectedAnswer":"fence","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need to ____ the new plot of land.","clozeAnswer":"fence","exampleTranslation":"我們需要為這塊新地塊圍上籬笆。","reference":{"eng":"fence","kk":"/fɛns/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['用籬笆圍起來'], ['（擊劍）做劍術擊擋']]","chEntries":["用籬笆圍起來","做劍術擊擋"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要為這塊新地塊圍上籬笆。","analysis":"動詞形式，根據其名詞含義發展：1. 指用『圍欄』將某地『圍起來』。2. 在擊劍運動中，指用劍進行『格擋』或『擊擋』的動作。","definition":"to enclose with a fence; to fight with swords, trying to hit each other","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They decided to fence their backyard.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們決定圍起自家的後院。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The fencer expertly fenced off his opponent's attack.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這名劍客巧妙地擋住了對手的攻擊。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to fence the new plot of land.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要為這塊新地塊圍上籬笆。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要為這塊新地塊圍上籬笆。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3152,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::flatter::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Compliments can sometimes ____, but genuine praise is always welcome.","expectedAnswer":"flatter","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Compliments can sometimes ____, but genuine praise is always welcome.","clozeAnswer":"flatter","exampleTranslation":"讚美有時可能帶有諂媚，但真誠的讚揚總是受歡迎的。","reference":{"eng":"flatter","kk":"/ˈflætər/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['奉承；諂媚'], ['使（某人）感到高興；取悅'], ['（光線、表面等）使顯得更好看']]","chEntries":["奉承","諂媚","使感到高興","取悅","使顯得更好看"],"practiceMeaning":"讚美有時可能帶有諂媚，但真誠的讚揚總是受歡迎的。","analysis":"詞源來自古法語 'flater'，意為「吹噓，奉承」，可能與拉丁語 'flare'（吹）有關。'Flatter' 有兩個主要語意：一是通過說好聽的話或做討好的事來取悅或奉承他人，通常帶有不真誠的意味；二是通過光線、角度或修飾使人或物體顯得更漂亮、更有吸引力。","definition":"1. praise (someone) importunately and insincerely; 2. praise highly; 3. make (someone) feel pleased or attractive; 4. make (something) appear more attractive than it really is.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He tried to flatter the boss into giving him a raise.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他試圖奉承老闆以獲得加薪。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The flattering portrait made her look younger and slimmer.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這幅討人喜歡的肖像使她看起來更年輕、更苗條。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Compliments can sometimes flatter, but genuine praise is always welcome.\",\n    \"ch\": \"讚美有時可能帶有諂媚，但真誠的讚揚總是受歡迎的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"讚美有時可能帶有諂媚，但真誠的讚揚總是受歡迎的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6120,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::fleet::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"A ____ of taxis waited outside the station.","expectedAnswer":"fleet","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"A ____ of taxis waited outside the station.","clozeAnswer":"fleet","exampleTranslation":"一群計程車在車站外等候。","reference":{"eng":"fleet","kk":"flit","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"艦隊\"  ],  [    \"船隊\"  ],  [    \"機隊\"  ],  [    \"車隊\"  ]]","chEntries":["艦隊","船隊","機隊","車隊"],"practiceMeaning":"一群計程車在車站外等候。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 flēot，意為「船；船隻」，與 flēotan（漂浮；航行）有關。其原始日耳曼語詞根 *fleutaz- 可能與「流動」有關。此名詞指由許多船隻、飛機或其他交通工具組成的「船隊」、「機隊」或「車隊」。其語意演變是從單一的「船」到一群船或交通工具。","definition":"A group of ships or other vessels sailing or travelling together, under the same command.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The navy deployed a fleet of ships.\",\n    \"ch\": \"海軍部署了一支艦隊。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The airline operates a large fleet of aircraft.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家航空公司運營著龐大的機隊。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A fleet of taxis waited outside the station.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一群計程車在車站外等候。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"一群計程車在車站外等候。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6122,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::fluency::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of the river's flow.","expectedAnswer":"fluency","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of the river's flow.","clozeAnswer":"fluency","exampleTranslation":"河流順暢的流動。","reference":{"eng":"fluency","kk":"ˈfluːənsi","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"流利\"  ],  [    \"流暢\"  ],  [    \"流利性\"  ]]","chEntries":["流利","流暢","流利性"],"practiceMeaning":"河流順暢的流動。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 fluēns，是 fluere（流動）的現在分詞。構詞上，fluere 的核心語義是「流動」。此名詞表示說話或寫作時的流利、順暢，沒有停頓或困難。也可指事物或過程的流暢性。其語意演變是從具體的「流動」到抽象的「說話順暢」。","definition":"1. the ability to speak or write a language easily, smoothly, and expressively; 2. the quality of flowing easily or smoothly.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She speaks English with great fluency.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她能流利地說英語。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His fluency in Spanish impressed the interviewers.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他西班牙語的流暢度給面試官留下了深刻印象。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The fluency of the river's flow.\",\n    \"ch\": \"河流順暢的流動。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"河流順暢的流動。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6227,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::fraction::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Write 3/4 as a ____.","expectedAnswer":"fraction","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Write 3/4 as a ____.","clozeAnswer":"fraction","exampleTranslation":"將 3/4 寫成分數。","reference":{"eng":"fraction","kk":"ˈfrækʃn","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"一小部分\"  ],  [    \"一小塊\"  ],  [    \"零頭\"  ],  [    \"分數\"  ]]","chEntries":["一小部分","一小塊","零頭","分數"],"practiceMeaning":"將 3/4 寫成分數。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 fractio，意為「打碎，斷裂」，是 frangere（打破，折斷）的派生詞。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。名詞義指某物的一小部分，尤其指由整數除法產生的數學分數。也可泛指非常小的數量、比例或程度。中文翻譯為「一小部分；一小塊；零頭；分數」。","definition":"1. a small part of something, or a small amount; 2. a number that is not a whole number, expressed as one number above another, or as a decimal.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Only a fraction of the students passed the exam.\",\n    \"ch\": \"只有一小部分的學生通過了考試。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He ate only a fraction of his meal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他只吃了一小部分餐點。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Write 3/4 as a fraction.\",\n    \"ch\": \"將 3/4 寫成分數。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"將 3/4 寫成分數。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3086,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::fundamental::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It is ____ to our success.","expectedAnswer":"fundamental","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It is ____ to our success.","clozeAnswer":"fundamental","exampleTranslation":"這對我們的成功至關重要。","reference":{"eng":"fundamental","kk":"/ˌfʌndəˈmentl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['根本的；基礎的'], ['根本性的；原則性的'], ['重要的']]","chEntries":["根本的","基礎的","根本性的","原則性的","重要的"],"practiceMeaning":"這對我們的成功至關重要。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'fundamentum' (foundation)。核心意義是「作為基礎」。\n1. 根本的；基礎的：指事物的最基本、最底層的組成部分或原理。\n2. 根本性的；原則性的：指與核心原則或基本結構相關的。\n3. 重要的：指非常重要，是其他一切事物的前提。","definition":"1. forming the most important part of something; 2. relating to the most basic or important ideas or principles; 3. forming a necessary base or core; of central importance.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to address the fundamental issues.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要解決根本問題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a fundamental principle of democracy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是民主的一個基本原則。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It is fundamental to our success.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這對我們的成功至關重要。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這對我們的成功至關重要。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3155,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::funeral::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She wore black to the ____ as a sign of mourning.","expectedAnswer":"funeral","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She wore black to the ____ as a sign of mourning.","clozeAnswer":"funeral","exampleTranslation":"她穿著黑色的衣服參加葬禮，以示哀悼。","reference":{"eng":"funeral","kk":"/ˈfjuːnərəl/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['葬禮；喪禮']]","chEntries":["葬禮","喪禮"],"practiceMeaning":"她穿著黑色的衣服參加葬禮，以示哀悼。","analysis":"詞源來自拉丁語 'funus'，意為「喪禮，屍體」。'Funeral' 指的是為死者舉行的儀式，通常包括告別、埋葬或火化等環節。它是一個與死亡、哀悼和紀念相關的莊重儀式。","definition":"a ceremony for burying or cremating a dead person.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We attended the funeral of our close friend.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們參加了我們摯友的葬禮。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The funeral procession moved slowly through the town.\",\n    \"ch\": \"送葬隊伍緩慢地穿過城鎮。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She wore black to the funeral as a sign of mourning.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她穿著黑色的衣服參加葬禮，以示哀悼。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她穿著黑色的衣服參加葬禮，以示哀悼。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3157,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::generosity::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of spirit shown by the community was inspiring.","expectedAnswer":"generosity","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of spirit shown by the community was inspiring.","clozeAnswer":"generosity","exampleTranslation":"社區所展現的精神上的慷慨鼓舞人心。","reference":{"eng":"generosity","kk":"/ˌdʒɛnəˈrɒsɪtɪ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['慷慨；大方'], ['（尤指對窮人）慷慨的捐贈']]","chEntries":["慷慨","大方","慷慨的捐贈"],"practiceMeaning":"社區所展現的精神上的慷慨鼓舞人心。","analysis":"名詞，源自形容詞 'generous'。'Generosity' 是指樂於給予、分享或幫助他人的品質，特別是慷慨地付出金錢、時間或情感，且不求回報。它強調的是一種寬宏大量、無私的品格。","definition":"the quality of being kind and generous; the quality of being willing to give more of something, especially money, than is expected or needed.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her generosity in helping the homeless was admirable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她幫助無家可歸者的慷慨令人欽佩。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We were touched by the generosity of the donors.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們對捐助者的慷慨深受感動。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The generosity of spirit shown by the community was inspiring.\",\n    \"ch\": \"社區所展現的精神上的慷慨鼓舞人心。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"社區所展現的精神上的慷慨鼓舞人心。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3159,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::genuine::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He showed ____ concern for her well-being.","expectedAnswer":"genuine","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He showed ____ concern for her well-being.","clozeAnswer":"genuine","exampleTranslation":"他對她的健康表現出真誠的關心。","reference":{"eng":"genuine","kk":"/ˈdʒɛnjuɪn/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['真誠的；真實的'], ['（物品）名副其實的；正宗的']]","chEntries":["真誠的","真實的","名副其實的","正宗的"],"practiceMeaning":"他對她的健康表現出真誠的關心。","analysis":"詞源來自拉丁語 'genuinus'，意為「天然的，固有的」，與 'genus'（種類，出生）有關，原意是「屬於某個家族的」。'Genuine' 強調的是真實性、純正性，不存在虛假、偽造或模仿。用於描述情感、意圖或人時，指真誠、沒有虛偽。用於描述物品時，指正宗、非仿冒品。","definition":"1. truly what something is said to be; authentic; 2. sincere and honest; 3. (of a person) not trying to deceive anyone.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her apology seemed genuine.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的道歉似乎是真誠的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a genuine antique vase.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個真正的古董花瓶。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He showed genuine concern for her well-being.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對她的健康表現出真誠的關心。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他對她的健康表現出真誠的關心。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3161,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::grief::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The death of his pet was a great ____ to him.","expectedAnswer":"grief","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The death of his pet was a great ____ to him.","clozeAnswer":"grief","exampleTranslation":"他的寵物去世給他帶來了巨大的悲傷。","reference":{"eng":"grief","kk":"/ɡriːf/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['（尤指因親人死亡而引起的）悲痛；哀傷'], ['（使人）悲痛的事']]","chEntries":["悲痛","哀傷","悲痛的事"],"practiceMeaning":"他的寵物去世給他帶來了巨大的悲傷。","analysis":"詞源來自古法語 'grief'，意為「悲傷，痛苦」，與拉丁語 'gravis'（沉重的）有關。'Grief' 指的是一種極其深沉、痛苦的情感反應，通常是由於失去親人、重大損失或創傷性事件而引起的。它是一種強烈的悲傷、哀痛和失落感。","definition":"1. deep sorrow, especially that caused by someone's death; 2. a cause of such sorrow.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is still in deep grief over the loss of her husband.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她因丈夫的離世仍在深切的悲痛之中。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The community shared in the family's grief.\",\n    \"ch\": \"社區分擔了這個家庭的悲痛。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The death of his pet was a great grief to him.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的寵物去世給他帶來了巨大的悲傷。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他的寵物去世給他帶來了巨大的悲傷。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5047,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::grim::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The future looks ____ for the company.","expectedAnswer":"grim","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The future looks ____ for the company.","clozeAnswer":"grim","exampleTranslation":"公司的未來前景嚴峻。","reference":{"eng":"grim","kk":"ɡrɪm","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['嚴肅的'], ['嚴酷的'], ['嚴峻的'], ['令人沮喪的']]","chEntries":["嚴肅的","嚴酷的","嚴峻的","令人沮喪的"],"practiceMeaning":"公司的未來前景嚴峻。","analysis":"此字源自古英語grimm，意為「兇猛的、殘酷的」。其核心語意是「令人不安、嚴肅、不愉快」，常帶有嚴酷或嚴峻的色彩。引申為「面容嚴肅」、「情況嚴峻」、「消息令人沮喪」。OCR 掃描時可能將 'g' 誤判為 'l' 或 'c'，或 'i' 誤判為 'l'。此處修正為 grim。","definition":"1. forbidding or uninviting; 2. (of a situation or event) deeply serious; alarming; 3. (of a person's expression) stern and forbidding.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The news of the accident was grim.\",\n    \"ch\": \"事故的消息令人沮喪。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He had a grim expression on his face.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他臉上表情嚴肅。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The future looks grim for the company.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司的未來前景嚴峻。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"公司的未來前景嚴峻。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4546,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::guidance::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need clear ____ on this matter.","expectedAnswer":"guidance","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need clear ____ on this matter.","clozeAnswer":"guidance","exampleTranslation":"我們需要關於這件事的明確指導。","reference":{"eng":"guidance","kk":"/ˈɡaɪdəns/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['指導', '引導'], ['建議', '意見']]","chEntries":["指導","引導","建議","意見"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要關於這件事的明確指導。","analysis":"由 'guide' (指導) 加上名詞字尾 '-ance' (表示狀態、行為) 構成。 'guide' 源自古法語 'guider'，最終源自日耳曼語，意為 'to show the way' (指引方向)。 'guidance' 指提供方向、建議或幫助的行為或過程。","definition":"1. advice or information aimed at resolving a problem or difficulty.; 2. the process of showing or telling someone the way to a place or destination.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She received excellent guidance from her mentor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她從導師那裡得到了極好的指導。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The teacher provided guidance on how to write the essay.\",\n    \"ch\": \"老師就如何寫論文提供了指導。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need clear guidance on this matter.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要關於這件事的明確指導。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要關於這件事的明確指導。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3163,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::gulf::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The economic ____ between the rich and the poor continues to widen.","expectedAnswer":"gulf","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The economic ____ between the rich and the poor continues to widen.","clozeAnswer":"gulf","exampleTranslation":"貧富之間的經濟鴻溝持續擴大。","reference":{"eng":"gulf","kk":"/ɡʌlf/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['（海洋、湖泊的）灣；海灣'], ['（意見、情況等的）巨大差異；鴻溝']]","chEntries":["灣","海灣","巨大差異","鴻溝"],"practiceMeaning":"貧富之間的經濟鴻溝持續擴大。","analysis":"詞源來自希臘語 'kolpos'，意為「灣」。'Gulf' 可以指地理上的地理特徵，即大海或湖泊伸入陸地的寬闊水域。它也可以比喻性地指兩種事物之間（如觀點、情感、地位）的巨大差異、隔閡或鴻溝，這種差異難以跨越。","definition":"1. a deep inlet of the sea almost surrounded by land, with a narrow mouth; 2. a profound difference between people or things.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The ship sailed across the Gulf of Mexico.\",\n    \"ch\": \"船隻航行穿越墨西哥灣。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There is a wide gulf between their political views.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們的政治觀點之間存在著巨大的差異。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The economic gulf between the rich and 