好、或過於嚴苛。\n2. 刺耳的；粗糙的：指聲音不悅耳，或觸感粗糙，令人不適。\n3. 嚴酷的（天氣、條件）：指天氣惡劣，環境艱難，難以忍受。","definition":"1. unpleasantly rough or shocking to the senses; 2. severe or cruel; 3. (of a sound or voice) unpleasantly harsh or grating.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The teacher gave him harsh criticism.\",\n    \"ch\": \"老師對他進行了嚴厲的批評。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The desert climate is harsh.\",\n    \"ch\": \"沙漠氣候十分嚴酷。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The noise was harsh and loud.\",\n    \"ch\": \"噪音刺耳而響亮。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"噪音刺耳而響亮。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3935,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::hateful::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She felt ____ towards her former boss.","expectedAnswer":"hateful","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She felt ____ towards her former boss.","clozeAnswer":"hateful","exampleTranslation":"她對她以前的老闆充滿了仇恨。","reference":{"eng":"hateful","kk":"/ˈheɪtfəl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['可恨的', '討厭的'], ['充滿仇恨的']]","chEntries":["可恨的","討厭的","充滿仇恨的"],"practiceMeaning":"她對她以前的老闆充滿了仇恨。","analysis":"源自古英語 'hætelīc'，由 'hate' (意為「憎恨」) 和 '-ful' (形容詞後綴) 組成。指「充滿憎恨的」或「引起憎恨的、可憎的」。","definition":"1. full of or showing hatred; 2. deserving hatred; detestable.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He made a hateful remark about her.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對她說了句可恨的話。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The dictator was known for his hateful policies.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那位獨裁者以其令人憎惡的政策而聞名。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She felt hateful towards her former boss.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對她以前的老闆充滿了仇恨。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她對她以前的老闆充滿了仇恨。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3900,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::hire::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They are looking to ____ a qualified manager.","expectedAnswer":"hire","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They are looking to ____ a qualified manager.","clozeAnswer":"hire","exampleTranslation":"他們正在尋找一位合格的經理來聘用。","reference":{"eng":"hire","kk":"/ˈhaɪər/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['僱用', '聘請'], ['租用']]","chEntries":["僱用","聘請","租用"],"practiceMeaning":"他們正在尋找一位合格的經理來聘用。","analysis":"源自古英語 'hyrian'，意為「僱用」。核心是「給予報酬以使用某人或某物」。引申為支付工資僱用員工，或支付租金使用物品。","definition":"1. to pay someone for their services. 2. to pay for the use of something for a period of time.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company decided to hire new staff.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司決定僱用新員工。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We hired a car for our trip.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們為了這次旅行租了一輛車。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They are looking to hire a qualified manager.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們正在尋找一位合格的經理來聘用。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們正在尋找一位合格的經理來聘用。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6078,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::honorable::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The judge was addressed as 'Your ____'.","expectedAnswer":"Honorable","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The judge was addressed as 'Your ____'.","clozeAnswer":"Honorable","exampleTranslation":"法官被尊稱為『閣下』。","reference":{"eng":"honorable","kk":"ˈɑnərəbəl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"榮譽的\"  ],  [    \"光榮的\"  ],  [    \"正直的\"  ],  [    \"可敬的\"  ],  [    \"尊稱\"  ]]","chEntries":["榮譽的","光榮的","正直的","可敬的","尊稱"],"practiceMeaning":"法官被尊稱為『閣下』。","analysis":"此字由 honor（榮譽）加上形容詞後綴 -able（能夠……的）構成。Honor 源自拉丁語 honor，意為「尊嚴，尊敬，榮譽」。核心語義是「值得尊敬」、「值得榮譽」或「具有高尚品德」。它可用來形容一個人、行為、事件，或作為一種尊稱（例如 Honorable Mr. President）。","definition":"1. deserving honor and respect; 2. bringing or deserving honor; 3. (used as a title of respect for a judge or certain officials).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is an honorable man known for his integrity.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一位以誠信聞名的正直人士。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was an honorable victory.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一場光榮的勝利。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The judge was addressed as 'Your Honorable'.\",\n    \"ch\": \"法官被尊稱為『閣下』。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"法官被尊稱為『閣下』。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4631,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::horrible::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They heard a ____ scream in the night.","expectedAnswer":"horrible","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They heard a ____ scream in the night.","clozeAnswer":"horrible","exampleTranslation":"他們在夜裡聽到一聲駭人的尖叫。","reference":{"eng":"horrible","kk":"/ˈhɔːrəbəl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['可怕的'], ['駭人的'], ['糟糕的']]","chEntries":["可怕的","駭人的","糟糕的"],"practiceMeaning":"他們在夜裡聽到一聲駭人的尖叫。","analysis":"由 'horror' (恐怖) + '-ible' (能夠...的) 組成。此字描述事物引起強烈恐懼、厭惡或不適感，其程度比 'scary' 更深。也可引申形容非常糟糕、令人難受的體驗。","definition":"causing or likely to cause horror; shocking; extremely unpleasant.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was a horrible accident.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那是一場可怕的事故。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The food tasted horrible.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這食物嚐起來糟透了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They heard a horrible scream in the night.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們在夜裡聽到一聲駭人的尖叫。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們在夜裡聽到一聲駭人的尖叫。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4637,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::hunger::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ for power is a dangerous thing.","expectedAnswer":"hunger","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ for power is a dangerous thing.","clozeAnswer":"hunger","exampleTranslation":"對權力的渴望是一件危險的事。","reference":{"eng":"hunger","kk":"/ˈhʌŋɡər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['飢餓'], ['渴望'], ['熱望']]","chEntries":["飢餓","渴望","熱望"],"practiceMeaning":"對權力的渴望是一件危險的事。","analysis":"源自古英語 'hungor'，與「飢餓」的生理感受相關。核心是對食物的強烈需求。引申義指對某事物（知識、成功、權力等）的強烈渴望，這種渴望的程度類似於生理上的飢餓。","definition":"a strong desire or craving, especially for food; a strong desire for something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The child cried from hunger.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子因飢餓而哭泣。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has a hunger for knowledge.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對知識有強烈的渴望。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The hunger for power is a dangerous thing.\",\n    \"ch\": \"對權力的渴望是一件危險的事。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"對權力的渴望是一件危險的事。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6125,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::ideology::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His actions were driven by a strong ____.","expectedAnswer":"ideology","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His actions were driven by a strong ____.","clozeAnswer":"ideology","exampleTranslation":"他的行為是由強烈的理念驅動的。","reference":{"eng":"ideology","kk":"ˌɪdiˈɑːlədʒi","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"意識形態\"  ],  [    \"思想體系\"  ],  [    \"理念\"  ]]","chEntries":["意識形態","思想體系","理念"],"practiceMeaning":"他的行為是由強烈的理念驅動的。","analysis":"此字源自法語 idéologie，由希臘語 idea（形式；理念；思想）和 -logia（學說；研究）組成。Idea 源自 idea（看；看見）。-logia 來自 logos（詞；言論；學說）。因此，ideology 的核心語義是「關於思想的學說」或「思想體系」。此名詞指一套關於社會、政治或經濟的觀念、信念和價值觀的系統。其語意演變是從「思想的研究」到「一套系統化的思想」。","definition":"A system of ideas and ideals, especially one which forms the basis of economic or political theory and policy.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They shared the same political ideology.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們持有相同的政治意識形態。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The novel explores themes of freedom and ideology.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這部小說探討了自由與意識形態的主題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His actions were driven by a strong ideology.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的行為是由強烈的理念驅動的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他的行為是由強烈的理念驅動的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3164,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::ignorance::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The project aims to combat ____ about climate change.","expectedAnswer":"ignorance","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The project aims to combat ____ about climate change.","clozeAnswer":"ignorance","exampleTranslation":"該項目旨在消除人們對氣候變化的無知。","reference":{"eng":"ignorance","kk":"/ˈɪɡnərəns/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['無知；缺乏知識'], ['（對某事的）不知情；無知']]","chEntries":["無知","缺乏知識","不知情"],"practiceMeaning":"該項目旨在消除人們對氣候變化的無知。","analysis":"名詞，源自形容詞 'ignorant'。'Ignorance' 指的是缺乏知識、信息或理解的狀態。它可以是對廣泛領域的普遍無知，也可以是對特定情況、事實或問題的不知情。這種無知可能是有意為之，也可能是由於缺乏接觸或學習機會。","definition":"1. lack of knowledge or information; 2. a lack of acquaintance with or understanding of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Ignorance of the law is no excuse.\",\n    \"ch\": \"不知法律是無法作為藉口的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His comments revealed his ignorance about the topic.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的評論顯示了他對這個話題的無知。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The project aims to combat ignorance about climate change.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該項目旨在消除人們對氣候變化的無知。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該項目旨在消除人們對氣候變化的無知。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3165,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::ignorant::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The teacher warned the students against being ____ of current events.","expectedAnswer":"ignorant","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The teacher warned the students against being ____ of current events.","clozeAnswer":"ignorant","exampleTranslation":"老師告誡學生不要對時事無知。","reference":{"eng":"ignorant","kk":"/ˈɪɡnərənt/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['無知的；缺乏知識的'], ['（對某事）不知情的']]","chEntries":["無知的","缺乏知識的","不知情的"],"practiceMeaning":"老師告誡學生不要對時事無知。","analysis":"詞源來自拉丁語 'ignorans'，意為「不知道的」，'ignorare'（不知道）。'Ignorant' 形容的是一個人缺乏必要的知識、信息或理解。它可以指普遍缺乏教育，也可以指對某特定情況、事實或問題不了解。有時也帶有不禮貌或粗魯的含義，指未受過良好教育或缺乏禮儀。","definition":"1. lacking knowledge or information; uneducated; 2. not aware of or concerned about something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He remained ignorant of the danger he was in.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對自己身處的危險毫無所知。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Some people are ignorant of the facts.\",\n    \"ch\": \"有些人對事實一無所知。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The teacher warned the students against being ignorant of current events.\",\n    \"ch\": \"老師告誡學生不要對時事無知。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"老師告誡學生不要對時事無知。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3917,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::imagination::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"That story is pure ____.","expectedAnswer":"imagination","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"That story is pure ____.","clozeAnswer":"imagination","exampleTranslation":"那個故事純粹是虛構的。","reference":{"eng":"imagination","kk":"/ɪˌmædʒɪˈneɪʃn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['想像力'], ['幻想', '虛構']]","chEntries":["想像力","幻想","虛構"],"practiceMeaning":"那個故事純粹是虛構的。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'imaginatio'，與 'imago' (意為「圖像、影像」) 有關，最終源自 'imagines' (意為「形象」)。指在心中形成圖像、概念的能力，即「想像力」；也可指由此產生的「幻想」或「虛構」。","definition":"1. the faculty or action of forming new ideas, or images or concepts of external objects not present to the senses; 2. the ability of the mind to be creative or resourceful.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Children have a great imagination.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子們有很強的想像力。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"You need imagination to be a writer.\",\n    \"ch\": \"你需要想像力才能成為一名作家。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"That story is pure imagination.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那個故事純粹是虛構的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"那個故事純粹是虛構的。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3932,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::immediate::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There was no ____ danger.","expectedAnswer":"immediate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There was no ____ danger.","clozeAnswer":"immediate","exampleTranslation":"沒有立即的危險。","reference":{"eng":"immediate","kk":"/ɪˈmiːdiət/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['立即的', '即刻的'], ['緊鄰的', '直接的']]","chEntries":["立即的","即刻的","緊鄰的","直接的"],"practiceMeaning":"沒有立即的危險。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'immediatus'，由 'in-' (意為「不」) 和 'mediatus' (意為「中間的」) 組成。原意是「沒有中間步驟的」，引申為「立刻發生的」或「緊鄰的」。","definition":"1. happening or done at once; instant; 2. happening or done right after something else, with no delay; 3. next to or very close to someone or something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need an immediate response to this crisis.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要對這次危機做出立即的回應。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The immediate family gathered at the hospital.\",\n    \"ch\": \"直系親屬聚集在醫院。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was no immediate danger.\",\n    \"ch\": \"沒有立即的危險。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"沒有立即的危險。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5841,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::implement::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The committee decided to ____ the proposal.","expectedAnswer":"implement","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The committee decided to ____ the proposal.","clozeAnswer":"implement","exampleTranslation":"委員會決定實行這項提議。","reference":{"eng":"implement","kk":"ˈɪmplɪmənt","tense":"v.","ch":"[  [    \"執行\"  ],  [    \"實施\"  ],  [    \"實行\"  ],  [    \"完成\"  ]]","chEntries":["執行","實施","實行","完成"],"practiceMeaning":"委員會決定實行這項提議。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'implementum' (filling, completion)，是 'implere' (to fill, to fulfill) 的派生詞。'Implere' 由 'in-' (in) 和 'plere' (to fill) 構成。'Implementum' 的意思是指「填補」、「完成」的工具或手段。作動詞時，'implement' 的核心語意是「將一個計劃、決定、或概念付諸實踐」，即「執行」或「實施」。它強調將抽象的意圖轉化為具體的行動。例如，也可指「完成」一個任務。","definition":"1. To put (a decision, plan, agreement, etc.) into effect.; 2. To carry out.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government will implement new policies next year.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府將在明年實施新政策。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to implement the changes immediately.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要立即執行這些變革。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The committee decided to implement the proposal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"委員會決定實行這項提議。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The workers implemented the new safety procedures.\",\n    \"ch\": \"工人們執行了新的安全程序。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"委員會決定實行這項提議。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6175,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::implication::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His ____ in the scandal damaged his reputation.","expectedAnswer":"implication","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His ____ in the scandal damaged his reputation.","clozeAnswer":"implication","exampleTranslation":"他在此醜聞中的牽連損害了他的聲譽。","reference":{"eng":"implication","kk":"ˌɪmplɪˈkeɪʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"暗示\"  ],  [    \"含義\"  ],  [    \"牽連\"  ],  [    \"牽涉\"  ]]","chEntries":["暗示","含義","牽連","牽涉"],"practiceMeaning":"他在此醜聞中的牽連損害了他的聲譽。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 implicatiōnem，是動詞 implicare「捲入、包含」的名詞化。implicare 由 in- (in, into) + plicare (to fold) 組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 in-「進入」和 plicare「折疊、捲入」是其核心語意來源。作為名詞，其核心語義是由動詞 implicate「暗示、牽連」名詞化而來，指「間接表達的意義」或「某事所涉及或牽連的範圍」。詞源中的「折疊、捲入」引申為「隱藏、暗示」和「牽連、涉及」。","definition":"1. the conclusion that can be drawn from something, although it is not directly stated; 2. the involvement of someone or something in a crime or other         wrongdoing; 3. a likely consequence or effect of an action or situation.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The implication of his words was clear.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他言語的含義很清楚。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The implication of the new policy on employment is uncertain.\",\n    \"ch\": \"新政策對就業的影響尚不確定。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His implication in the scandal damaged his reputation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在此醜聞中的牽連損害了他的聲譽。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The results have important implications for future research.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這些結果對未來的研究具有重要的含義。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他在此醜聞中的牽連損害了他的聲譽。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4518,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::in::prep","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She will arrive ____ an hour.","expectedAnswer":"in","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She will arrive ____ an hour.","clozeAnswer":"in","exampleTranslation":"她將在一小時內到達。","reference":{"eng":"in","kk":"/ɪn/","tense":"prep.","ch":"[['在...裡面'], ['在...之中'], ['在（某個時間、地點、情況）']]","chEntries":["在...裡面","在...之中","在"],"practiceMeaning":"她將在一小時內到達。","analysis":"源自古英語 in。是一個極其基本且用途廣泛的介詞。核心語意是「在一個封閉的空間或區域內」。引申義涵蓋時間、狀態、方法、組成等。","definition":"1. Expressing the situation of being enclosed or surrounded by something; 2. Expressing location or position within a place or area; 3. Expressing the period of time during which an event occurs.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The keys are in the drawer.\",\n    \"ch\": \"鑰匙在抽屜裡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He lives in London.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他住在倫敦。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She will arrive in an hour.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她將在一小時內到達。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They are involved in the project.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們參與了這個項目。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她將在一小時內到達。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4578,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::inaccurate::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The map is ____ and outdated.","expectedAnswer":"inaccurate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The map is ____ and outdated.","clozeAnswer":"inaccurate","exampleTranslation":"這張地圖既不準確又過時了。","reference":{"eng":"inaccurate","kk":"/ɪnˈækjərət/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['不準確的', '不精確的'], ['錯誤的']]","chEntries":["不準確的","不精確的","錯誤的"],"practiceMeaning":"這張地圖既不準確又過時了。","analysis":"由否定字首 'in-' (not) 和 'accurate' (準確的) 組成。與 'accurate' 相反，指不準確、不精確或錯誤的。","definition":"1. not correct or precise.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The report contained several inaccurate figures.\",\n    \"ch\": \"報告包含幾個不準確的數字。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His memory of the event was inaccurate.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對那次事件的記憶並不準確。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The map is inaccurate and outdated.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這張地圖既不準確又過時了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這張地圖既不準確又過時了。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6176,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::incentive::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"What is your ____ for taking this job?","expectedAnswer":"incentive","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"What is your ____ for taking this job?","clozeAnswer":"incentive","exampleTranslation":"你從事這份工作的動機是什麼？","reference":{"eng":"incentive","kk":"ɪnˈsɛntɪv","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"刺激\"  ],  [    \"誘因\"  ],  [    \"動機\"  ]]","chEntries":["刺激","誘因","動機"],"practiceMeaning":"你從事這份工作的動機是什麼？","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 incentivum，是動詞 incendere「點燃、激勵」的中性過去分詞，引申為「激勵因素」。incendere 由 in- (in, into) + candēre (to burn, glow) 組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 in-「進入」和 candēre「燃燒」是其核心語意來源。作為名詞，其核心語義是「促使某人做某事的東西」，即「刺激」或「誘因」。詞源中的「點燃」概念引申為「激發、促使」的動力。","definition":"1. a thing that motivates or encourages one to do something; 2. a payment or other consideration by which one is influenced.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Higher wages provide a strong incentive for workers.\",\n    \"ch\": \"更高的工資為工人提供了強烈的誘因。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government offered tax incentives for new businesses.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府提供了稅收優惠來鼓勵新企業。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"What is your incentive for taking this job?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你從事這份工作的動機是什麼？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The bonus served as an incentive to work harder.\",\n    \"ch\": \"獎金起到了激勵更努力工作的誘因作用。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"你從事這份工作的動機是什麼？","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6228,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::inevitable::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Their success seemed ____ from the start.","expectedAnswer":"inevitable","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Their success seemed ____ from the start.","clozeAnswer":"inevitable","exampleTranslation":"他們的成功從一開始似乎就已注定。","reference":{"eng":"inevitable","kk":"ɪnˈɛvɪtəbl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"不可避免的\"  ],  [    \"必然的\"  ],  [    \"注定的\"  ]]","chEntries":["不可避免的","必然的","注定的"],"practiceMeaning":"他們的成功從一開始似乎就已注定。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 inevitabilis，由 in-（否定）和 evadere（逃脫）構成，意為「不能逃脫的」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作形容詞時，指某種情況或結果是無法避免的，必然會發生。中文翻譯為「不可避免的；必然的；注定的」。","definition":"certain to happen; unavoidable.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Change is inevitable in life.\",\n    \"ch\": \"改變在生活中是不可避免的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Given the circumstances, the outcome was inevitable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"鑑於當時的情況，這個結果是必然的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Their success seemed inevitable from the start.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們的成功從一開始似乎就已注定。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們的成功從一開始似乎就已注定。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5088,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::infinite::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The possibilities are ____.","expectedAnswer":"infinite","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The possibilities are ____.","clozeAnswer":"infinite","exampleTranslation":"可能性是無限的。","reference":{"eng":"infinite","kk":"ˈɪnfɪnət","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['無限的'], ['無窮的'], ['極大的']]","chEntries":["無限的","無窮的","極大的"],"practiceMeaning":"可能性是無限的。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'in-' (not) + 'finitus' (bounded, finite)，原意為 '無邊界的、無窮的'。'Infinite' 的核心語義是 '沒有盡頭、沒有限制'。這可以指空間上的無限，時間上的無限，數量的無限，也可以指品質上的極致，如 'infinite patience' (極大的耐心)，強調其程度之深，幾乎沒有極限。","definition":"1. Limitless or endless in space, extent, or size; impossible to measure or calculate.; 2. Extremely large or great, especially in scope or ability.; 3. (Of a mathematical quantity) larger than any assignable quantity or number.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The universe is thought to be infinite.\",\n    \"ch\": \"宇宙被認為是無限的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has infinite patience with the children.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對孩子們有無限的耐心。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The possibilities are infinite.\",\n    \"ch\": \"可能性是無限的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"可能性是無限的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3188,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::inject::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He needs to ____ more confidence into his presentation.","expectedAnswer":"inject","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He needs to ____ more confidence into his presentation.","clozeAnswer":"inject","exampleTranslation":"他需要在演講中注入更多信心。","reference":{"eng":"inject","kk":"/ɪnˈdʒɛkt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['注射；注射給藥'], ['注入；灌輸（尤指想法、情感）']]","chEntries":["注射","注射給藥","注入","灌輸"],"practiceMeaning":"他需要在演講中注入更多信心。","analysis":"詞源來自拉丁語 'injectare'，意為「注入，投擲」，由 'in-'（在...中）+ 'jacere'（扔）組成。'Inject' 的核心是「將某物推入或注入」。最常見的是醫學上的「注射」，將藥物或液體通過針頭注入體內。也可引申為將某物（如想法、情感、資金）注入到某個系統、情況或人身上。","definition":"1. administer (a drug or vaccine) by inserting a needle into a muscle or into a cavity in the body; 2. force (fluid, especially blood) into a vessel or cavity; 3. introduce (a substance) into something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The doctor will inject the vaccine into your arm.\",\n    \"ch\": \"醫生會將疫苗注射到你的手臂。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The new funding will inject life into the struggling arts program.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這筆新資金將為這個陷入困境的藝術項目注入活力。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He needs to inject more confidence into his presentation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他需要在演講中注入更多信心。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他需要在演講中注入更多信心。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3170,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::instinct::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She has a natural ____ for business.","expectedAnswer":"instinct","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She has a natural ____ for business.","clozeAnswer":"instinct","exampleTranslation":"她有經營生意的天賦。","reference":{"eng":"instinct","kk":"/ˈɪnstɪŋkt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['本能；天性'], ['（對某事的）直覺；天賦']]","chEntries":["本能","天性","直覺","天賦"],"practiceMeaning":"她有經營生意的天賦。","analysis":"詞源來自拉丁語 'instinctus'，意為「衝動，刺激」，源於 'instinguere'（激勵，驅使）。'Instinct' 指的是一種天生的、非學習而來的行為模式或反應，由生物體的遺傳基因決定，用於應對特定的環境刺激。它也可以引申為對某事的強烈直覺或天賦，一種無需理性思考就能產生的判斷或傾向。","definition":"1. an innate, typically fixed pattern of behavior in animals in response to certain stimuli; 2. a natural or intuitive impulse or tendency.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Birds have an instinct to migrate south for the winter.\",\n    \"ch\": \"鳥類有向南遷徙以度過冬天的本能。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"My instinct told me not to trust him.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我的直覺告訴我不要相信他。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a natural instinct for business.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她有經營生意的天賦。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她有經營生意的天賦。","sourceName":"字彙王、龍騰課本","unitName":"U40、L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3889,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::invitation::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Thank you for your kind ____.","expectedAnswer":"invitation","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Thank you for your kind ____.","clozeAnswer":"invitation","exampleTranslation":"感謝您的盛情邀請。","reference":{"eng":"invitation","kk":"/ˌɪnvɪˈteɪʃən/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['邀請'], ['邀請函']]","chEntries":["邀請","邀請函"],"practiceMeaning":"感謝您的盛情邀請。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'invitatio'，'invitare' (to invite) 的名詞形式，意為「邀請」。核心是「呼喚」、「邀請」。指請人參加某事物的請求，或表示這種請求的文件。","definition":"1. a request or order to come somewhere or do something. 2. a written or verbal communication asking someone to attend an event or perform a task.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We received an invitation to the wedding.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們收到了婚禮的邀請。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His invitation was very formal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的邀請非常正式。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Thank you for your kind invitation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"感謝您的盛情邀請。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"感謝您的盛情邀請。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5598,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l7::justice::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He believed that true ____ could only be achieved through reform.","expectedAnswer":"justice","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He believed that true ____ could only be achieved through reform.","clozeAnswer":"justice","exampleTranslation":"他相信真正的公正只能透過改革實現。","reference":{"eng":"justice","kk":"ˈdʒʌstɪs","tense":"n.","ch":"[['正義'], ['公正'], ['司法'], ['審判']]","chEntries":["正義","公正","司法","審判"],"practiceMeaning":"他相信真正的公正只能透過改革實現。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'justitia'（正義、公正），它本身由 'justus'（正確的、合法的）和 '-itia'（名詞化後綴，表示狀態或品質）構成，而 'justus' 又源於 'jus'（法律、權利）。構詞學上，核心是 'jus'（法律、權利）加上形容詞化及名詞化後綴。原始語意是「合乎法律」或「符合權利」，演變為指「公平與正義的原則」、「公正的待遇」以及「司法的系統或權威」。多個義項之間的核心關聯在於「正確性」、「公平性」和「依循規則」。","definition":"1. The quality of being fair and reasonable; 2. The administration of the law or authority in maintaining this; 3. A judge or the authority to administer justice.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The pursuit of justice is a fundamental principle of law.\",\n    \"ch\": \"追求正義是法律的基本原則。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The court system aims to deliver justice to all citizens.\",\n    \"ch\": \"法院系統旨在為所有公民伸張正義。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He believed that true justice could only be achieved through reform.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他相信真正的公正只能透過改革實現。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他相信真正的公正只能透過改革實現。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4326,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::liberty::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He took the ____ of borrowing my car without asking.","expectedAnswer":"liberty","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He took the ____ of borrowing my car without asking.","clozeAnswer":"liberty","exampleTranslation":"他擅自借了我的車，沒有經過我的允許。","reference":{"eng":"liberty","kk":"/ˈlɪbərti/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['自由'], ['（對規則、禮節等的）失禮；過分鹵莽']]","chEntries":["自由","失禮","過分鹵莽"],"practiceMeaning":"他擅自借了我的車，沒有經過我的允許。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'libertas' (freedom)，來自 'liber' (free)。核心是『自由』的概念。1. 指享有政治、社會、個人不受約束的權利和狀態，即『自由』。2. 指過度行使自由，不受約束，導致『失禮』或『鹵莽』的行為，超過了應有的界限。","definition":"the state of being free to make your own choices and decisions and to live as you want to live; freedom to behave or act in a way you choose","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Millions of people fought for their liberty.\",\n    \"ch\": \"數百萬人為他們的自由而戰。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Students were given more liberty in choosing their courses.\",\n    \"ch\": \"學生們在選擇課程方面被賦予了更多的自由。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He took the liberty of borrowing my car without asking.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他擅自借了我的車，沒有經過我的允許。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他擅自借了我的車，沒有經過我的允許。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4167,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::living::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The cost of ____ has gone up.","expectedAnswer":"living","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The cost of ____ has gone up.","clozeAnswer":"living","exampleTranslation":"生活成本上升了。","reference":{"eng":"living","kk":"/ˈlɪvɪŋ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['生活', '生計']]","chEntries":["生活","生計"],"practiceMeaning":"生活成本上升了。","analysis":"由 live（活著，生存）+ -ing（名詞後綴）組成。核心概念是「生存的狀態」或「維持生存所需」。","definition":"1. the state of being alive; 2. a means of supporting oneself financially","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The steep rise in living costs made it hard to make ends meet.\",\n    \"ch\": \"生活成本的急劇上漲使得人們難以為繼。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is working hard to provide a better living for his family.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他正努力工作，為家人提供更好的生活。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The cost of living has gone up.\",\n    \"ch\": \"生活成本上升了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"生活成本上升了。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3890,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::locate::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Can you ____ the source of the problem?","expectedAnswer":"locate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Can you ____ the source of the problem?","clozeAnswer":"locate","exampleTranslation":"你能找出問題的根源嗎？","reference":{"eng":"locate","kk":"/ˈloʊkeɪt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['定位', '找出'], ['設置', '坐落於']]","chEntries":["定位","找出","設置","坐落於"],"practiceMeaning":"你能找出問題的根源嗎？","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'locus' (place)。核心是「標示位置」。引申為找出某物的確切位置，或將某物安置在某個特定地點。","definition":"1. to discover the exact position of. 2. to situate or place in a particular position.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police are trying to locate the missing child.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警方正試圖找到失蹤的孩子。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The new office will be located downtown.\",\n    \"ch\": \"新辦公室將設在市中心。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Can you locate the source of the problem?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你能找出問題的根源嗎？\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"你能找出問題的根源嗎？","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4427,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u9::loose::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The dog is ____.","expectedAnswer":"loose","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The dog is ____.","clozeAnswer":"loose","exampleTranslation":"狗跑出來了。","reference":{"eng":"loose","kk":"/luːs/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['鬆的', '不緊的'], ['不精確的', '寬鬆的'], ['（道德、紀律）鬆懈的'], ['（不受約束的）自由的']]","chEntries":["鬆的","不緊的","不精確的","寬鬆的","鬆懈的","自由的"],"practiceMeaning":"狗跑出來了。","analysis":"詞源自古挪威語 'lauss'。核心概念是「未被固定、束縛或限制」。引申到物理上的不緊、概念上的不明確，以及行為上的不受約束。","definition":"not firmly fixed or attached; not tight; not precise or exact; not strict.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The button on my shirt is loose.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我襯衫上的鈕扣鬆了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He gave a loose description of the suspect.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對嫌疑犯的描述很含糊。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The dog is loose.\",\n    \"ch\": \"狗跑出來了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"狗跑出來了。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4140,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::lover::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She is a secret ____ of chocolate.","expectedAnswer":"lover","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She is a secret ____ of chocolate.","clozeAnswer":"lover","exampleTranslation":"她是巧克力的忠實擁趸。","reference":{"eng":"lover","kk":"/ˈlʌvər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['戀人', '愛人'], ['愛好者', '愛好者（從事某事的人）']]","chEntries":["戀人","愛人","愛好者"],"practiceMeaning":"她是巧克力的忠實擁趸。","analysis":"源自 love（愛）+ -er（名詞後綴）。核心概念是「充滿愛意的人」。引申為浪漫關係中的伴侶，或指對某事有強烈興趣或熱愛的人。","definition":"1. a person who loves another; 2. a person who enjoys or is fond of something","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They are lovers who have been together for years.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們是在一起多年的戀人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a lover of classical music.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是古典音樂的愛好者。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a secret lover of chocolate.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是巧克力的忠實擁趸。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她是巧克力的忠實擁趸。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5573,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::massive::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company experienced ____ layoffs.","expectedAnswer":"massive","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company experienced ____ layoffs.","clozeAnswer":"massive","exampleTranslation":"公司進行了大規模裁員。","reference":{"eng":"massive","kk":"ˈmæsɪv","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['巨大的'], ['大規模的'], ['沉重的'], ['大量的']]","chEntries":["巨大的","大規模的","沉重的","大量的"],"practiceMeaning":"公司進行了大規模裁員。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 \"massīvus\"，意為 \"solid, dense\"（固態的，密集的），來自 \"massa\"（mass, lump，團塊，塊狀物）。\"massa\" 的語義是「未經分割的、大塊的物質」。因此，\"massive\" 的核心語義是「像一個大塊物體一樣，巨大、厚重、密集」。它強調的是規模、體積或重量上的龐大。它可以形容物理上的尺寸（e.g., massive building），也可以形容抽象上的數量或影響力（e.g., massive impact）。","definition":"1. Large and heavy or solid; 2. Large in scale or extent; 3. Very large in amount or degree.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They live in a massive house in the countryside.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們住在鄉間一棟巨大的房子裡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The project required massive amounts of funding.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個計畫需要巨額的資金。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company experienced massive layoffs.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司進行了大規模裁員。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"公司進行了大規模裁員。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4158,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::materials::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The artist uses various ____ in his work.","expectedAnswer":"materials","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The artist uses various ____ in his work.","clozeAnswer":"materials","exampleTranslation":"這位藝術家在他的作品中使用各種材料。","reference":{"eng":"materials","kk":"/məˈtɪəriəlz/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['材料', '物資']]","chEntries":["材料","物資"],"practiceMeaning":"這位藝術家在他的作品中使用各種材料。","analysis":"由 material（物質的，材料）的複數形式。來自拉丁語 materialis（物質的）。核心概念是「構成某物的東西」。","definition":"things such as physical objects and substances that are needed for the particular activity or purpose you are referring to","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to buy building materials.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要購買建築材料。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The relief materials included food and medicine.\",\n    \"ch\": \"救濟物資包括食物和藥品。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The artist uses various materials in his work.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位藝術家在他的作品中使用各種材料。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這位藝術家在他的作品中使用各種材料。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4694,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::mathematical::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Her daily routine was ____.","expectedAnswer":"mathematical","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Her daily routine was ____.","clozeAnswer":"mathematical","exampleTranslation":"她日常的作息非常規律。","reference":{"eng":"mathematical","kk":"/ˌmæθəˈmætɪkəl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['數學的'], ['精確的'], ['（非正式）按部就班的，有規律的']]","chEntries":["數學的","精確的","按部就班的，有規律的"],"practiceMeaning":"她日常的作息非常規律。","analysis":"源自希臘語 *mathēmatikós*，意為「學習的」、「學術的」，後指與數學相關的。核心是關於數字、數量、空間、結構和變化的科學。引申為精確、有條理，如同數學公式般規律。","definition":"1. Relating to or concerned with mathematics. 2. Precise or exact. 3. (informal) Methodical; systematic.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has a strong mathematical aptitude.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他有很強的數學天賦。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The results were mathematically proven.\",\n    \"ch\": \"結果已經數學上證明了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her daily routine was mathematical.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她日常的作息非常規律。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她日常的作息非常規律。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4606,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::meaningful::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She sought a more ____ career.","expectedAnswer":"meaningful","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She sought a more ____ career.","clozeAnswer":"meaningful","exampleTranslation":"她尋求一份更有意義的職業。","reference":{"eng":"meaningful","kk":"/ˈmiːnɪŋfəl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['有意義的'], ['意味深長的'], ['有目的的']]","chEntries":["有意義的","意味深長的","有目的的"],"practiceMeaning":"她尋求一份更有意義的職業。","analysis":"由 'meaning' (意義) + '-ful' (充滿) 組成。'Meaning' 源自古英語 'mænan' (意指、表達)，與 'mean' (意圖) 同源。'-ful' 是表示「充滿」或「具有」的後綴。此字指事物具有重要的價值、目的或深刻的內涵，能夠引起情感共鳴或啟發思考。","definition":"having or conveying a serious emotion, importance, or purpose.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He gave a meaningful speech that inspired many.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他做了一場意味深長的演講，激勵了許多人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was a meaningful gesture of friendship.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是友誼的充滿意義的表示。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She sought a more meaningful career.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她尋求一份更有意義的職業。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她尋求一份更有意義的職業。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5555,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::mere::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The accident was caused by a ____ oversight.","expectedAnswer":"mere","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The accident was caused by a ____ oversight.","clozeAnswer":"mere","exampleTranslation":"這次意外僅僅是一個疏忽造成的。","reference":{"eng":"mere","kk":"mɪər","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['僅僅的'], ['普通的'], ['渺小的']]","chEntries":["僅僅的","普通的","渺小的"],"practiceMeaning":"這次意外僅僅是一個疏忽造成的。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 \"mǣre\"，原意為 \"boundary, limit, distinguished\"（界線，極限，傑出的）。其語義演變經歷了從「明確的界線/極限」到「範圍僅限於此」的概念，進而發展出「僅僅是」、「不過是」的含義。另一說法是，它可能與強調「單一」或「微小」的概念有關。現代用法中，\"mere\" 作形容詞，常用來強調事物之少、之小、之普通，或僅僅是某種狀態，與 \"only\" 或 \"just\" 類似，但常帶有一點貶低或不以為然的語氣，強調其不重要性或缺乏其他特質。例如 \"a mere child\"（只是一個小孩），暗示經驗或能力不足。","definition":"1. That is only or no more than what is stated; 2. Small or insignificant.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It took me a mere ten minutes to finish the task.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我只花了短短十分鐘就完成了任務。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a mere beginner in this field.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在這個領域只是一個初學者。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The accident was caused by a mere oversight.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這次意外僅僅是一個疏忽造成的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這次意外僅僅是一個疏忽造成的。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4679,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::mess::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There was a ____ of papers on his desk.","expectedAnswer":"mess","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There was a ____ of papers on his desk.","clozeAnswer":"mess","exampleTranslation":"他的桌上有一大堆文件。","reference":{"eng":"mess","kk":"/ˈmɛs/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['混亂'], ['髒亂'], ['（令人不快的）處境'], ['（非正式）相當數量']]","chEntries":["混亂","髒亂","處境","相當數量"],"practiceMeaning":"他的桌上有一大堆文件。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 *missus*（投擲），與 *mittere*（發送）有關，可能指「被丟棄、攪亂的東西」。核心概念是無序、不整潔的狀態。延伸至令人不快的困境，或非正式地指「相當多」的某物。","definition":"1. A situation or state of untidiness or disorder. 2. A situation that is confused, difficult, or unpleasant. 3. (informal) A large amount or number of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The room was a complete mess after the party.\",\n    \"ch\": \"派對結束後，房間一片狼藉。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He got himself into a terrible mess with his finances.\",\n    \