he was safe.","expectedAnswer":"relief","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It was a great ____ to hear that he was safe.","clozeAnswer":"relief","exampleTranslation":"聽到他安然無恙，我感到鬆了一口氣。","reference":{"eng":"relief","kk":"/rɪˈliːf/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['緩解', '減輕'], ['救濟', '援助'], ['解脫', '安慰'], ['（雕塑、繪畫等的）浮雕']]","chEntries":["緩解","減輕","救濟","援助","解脫","安慰","浮雕"],"practiceMeaning":"聽到他安然無恙，我感到鬆了一口氣。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 relevare，由 re-（再次）+ levare（舉起、減輕）組成。核心概念是「減輕負擔」或「解除痛苦」。引申為疾病的緩解、災難的援助、壓力的釋放，甚至藝術中的凸顯效果。","definition":"1. a feeling of reassurance and relaxation following release from anxiety or distress; 2. assistance to people in a sudden emergency or disaster; 3. the easing or alleviation of a pain or symptom; 4. (in art) the projection of a figure or design from its background","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The medicine provided some relief from her pain.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種藥物減輕了她的疼痛。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"International relief efforts were mobilized after the earthquake.\",\n    \"ch\": \"地震發生後，國際救濟行動被迅速調動起來。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was a great relief to hear that he was safe.\",\n    \"ch\": \"聽到他安然無恙，我感到鬆了一口氣。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The statue featured intricate relief work.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座雕像以精緻的浮雕工藝為特色。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"聽到他安然無恙，我感到鬆了一口氣。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U5、L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4041,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::replace::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Can you ____ the lid on this jar?","expectedAnswer":"replace","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Can you ____ the lid on this jar?","clozeAnswer":"replace","exampleTranslation":"你能把這個罐子的蓋子蓋回去嗎？","reference":{"eng":"replace","kk":"/rɪˈpleɪs/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['取代', '替換'], ['歸還', '放回原處']]","chEntries":["取代","替換","歸還","放回原處"],"practiceMeaning":"你能把這個罐子的蓋子蓋回去嗎？","analysis":"源自古法語 'replacer'，由 're-' (back) + 'placer' (to place) 構成。核心意思是「再次放置」。第一個義項「取代」、「替換」是指用新的東西放到原來的東西所在的位置，或讓一個人或物接替另一個。第二個義項「歸還」、「放回原處」則強調將某物放回它原本的位置，是一種特殊的「替換」情境，即將其「放回」原位。","definition":"1. to take the place of something or someone; 2. to put something back in the place where it was before","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要用一個新的電池來替換舊電池。\",\n    \"eng\": \"We need to replace the old battery with a new one.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"她把書放回書架上。\",\n    \"eng\": \"She replaced the book on the shelf.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"你能把這個罐子的蓋子蓋回去嗎？\",\n    \"eng\": \"Can you replace the lid on this jar?\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"你能把這個罐子的蓋子蓋回去嗎？","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U4、L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5443,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::residence::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Proof of ____ is required for the application.","expectedAnswer":"residence","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Proof of ____ is required for the application.","clozeAnswer":"residence","exampleTranslation":"申請需要居住證明。","reference":{"eng":"residence","kk":"ˈrezɪdəns","tense":"n.","ch":"[['住所'], ['居住地'], ['居住權'], ['官邸']]","chEntries":["住所","居住地","居住權","官邸"],"practiceMeaning":"申請需要居住證明。","analysis":"此字為派生詞，由拉丁語 \"residens\" (居住者，來自 \"residere\"，意為\"居住\") 加上名詞化字尾 \"-ce\" (或 \"-cy\") 構成。\"residere\" 由 \"re-\" (回歸、持續) 和 \"sedere\" (坐、居住) 構成。構詞上，\"resid-\" 提供了核心的「居住」語意，\"-ence\" 是名詞字尾，將「居住」的動作或狀態轉化為名詞。因此，\"residence\" 指的是「居住的場所」、「住所」，或是「居住的行為或狀態」，也可能指「居住權」或「官邸」。","definition":"the place where someone lives, especially a house or home; the state of living in a particular place; an official dwelling.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His primary residence is in London.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的主要住所是倫敦。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The embassy is the ambassador's official residence.\",\n    \"ch\": \"大使館是大使的官邸。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Proof of residence is required for the application.\",\n    \"ch\": \"申請需要居住證明。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"申請需要居住證明。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3111,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::restore::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The government promised to ____ public trust.","expectedAnswer":"restore","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The government promised to ____ public trust.","clozeAnswer":"restore","exampleTranslation":"政府承諾恢復公眾的信任。","reference":{"eng":"restore","kk":"/rɪˈstɔːr/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['恢復；復原'], ['修復；重建'], ['歸還；恢復（權利、地位）']]","chEntries":["恢復","復原","修復","重建","歸還"],"practiceMeaning":"政府承諾恢復公眾的信任。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'restaurare'，'re-' (again) + 'staurare' (to set up, to renew)。核心意義是「重新建立」或「恢復」。\n1. 恢復；復原：指使事物回到原來的狀態、健康或功能。\n2. 修復；重建：指修繕破損的建築物、藝術品或其他事物，使其恢復原貌。\n3. 歸還；恢復（權利、地位）：指將先前被剝奪或失去的東西歸還給原主，或恢復其原有的權力或地位。","definition":"1. to bring back a situation or thing to its former condition; 2. to repair something that is old or damaged; 3. to give someone back something that was lost or taken away.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The doctor helped him to restore his health.\",\n    \"ch\": \"醫生幫助他恢復了健康。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They are working to restore the ancient castle.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們正在努力修復這座古老的城堡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government promised to restore public trust.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府承諾恢復公眾的信任。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"政府承諾恢復公眾的信任。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3193,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::rhythm::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He tried to find a ____ in his writing process.","expectedAnswer":"rhythm","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He tried to find a ____ in his writing process.","clozeAnswer":"rhythm","exampleTranslation":"他試圖在寫作過程中找到一種節奏。","reference":{"eng":"rhythm","kk":"/ˈrɪðəm/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['節奏；韻律'], ['（事物、活動的）規律；週期']]","chEntries":["節奏","韻律","規律","週期"],"practiceMeaning":"他試圖在寫作過程中找到一種節奏。","analysis":"詞源來自希臘語 'rhythmos'，意為「週期，流動」。'Rhythm' 指的是一種有規律的、重複出現的模式，特別是聲音、運動或事件的模式。在音樂中，它是聲音的高低、長短和強弱的組織。在日常生活中，它可以指一種規律的模式或週期，如工作節奏、生活規律等。","definition":"1. a strong, regular, repeated pattern of movement or sound; 2. a regular pattern of changes or activities.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The music had a catchy rhythm that made people want to dance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這首音樂有著 catchy 的節奏，讓人想跳舞。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The rhythm of the waves was soothing.\",\n    \"ch\": \"海浪的節奏令人舒緩。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He tried to find a rhythm in his writing process.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他試圖在寫作過程中找到一種節奏。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他試圖在寫作過程中找到一種節奏。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5099,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::rigid::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He has a ____ approach to problem-solving.","expectedAnswer":"rigid","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He has a ____ approach to problem-solving.","clozeAnswer":"rigid","exampleTranslation":"他解決問題的方法很僵化。","reference":{"eng":"rigid","kk":"ˈrɪdʒɪd","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['僵化的'], ['堅硬的'], ['嚴格的']]","chEntries":["僵化的","堅硬的","嚴格的"],"practiceMeaning":"他解決問題的方法很僵化。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'rigidus'，意為 '硬的、僵硬的'，源於 'rigere' (to be stiff)。'Rigid' 的核心語義是 '缺乏彈性、不易彎曲或改變'。這可以指物理上的堅硬，如 'rigid material' (堅硬的材料)；也可以指觀念、規則或體制的僵化，如 'rigid rules' (嚴格的規則) 或 'rigid thinking' (僵化的思維)，強調其不靈活、不變通的特性。","definition":"1. Unable to bend or be deformed.; 2. Stiff and unmoving.; 3. Unable to change or be changed; fixed.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The metal bar was rigid and could not be bent.\",\n    \"ch\": \"金屬棒是堅硬的，無法彎曲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company has rigid rules about punctuality.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司對準時有嚴格的規定。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has a rigid approach to problem-solving.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他解決問題的方法很僵化。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他解決問題的方法很僵化。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5857,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::sacred::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Freedom of speech is a ____ right.","expectedAnswer":"sacred","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Freedom of speech is a ____ right.","clozeAnswer":"sacred","exampleTranslation":"言論自由是一項神聖的權利。","reference":{"eng":"sacred","kk":"ˈseɪkrɪd","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"神聖的\"  ],  [    \"聖潔的\"  ],  [    \"宗教的\"  ],  [    \"受尊敬的\"  ]]","chEntries":["神聖的","聖潔的","宗教的","受尊敬的"],"practiceMeaning":"言論自由是一項神聖的權利。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'sacer'，意為「神聖的」、「獻給神的」。'-ed' 是形容詞字尾。'Sacer' 的詞源與印歐語根 *sak- (to make holy) 有關。'Sacred' 的核心語意是指「與宗教、神祇或儀式有關的」，因此被視為「神聖的」、「不可褻瀆的」。引申義則指「極受尊敬的」、「神聖不可侵犯的」，用於形容珍貴的事物或權利。","definition":"1. Connected with God or a god or a religious purpose.; 2. Regarded with great respect and affection.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a sacred site for many religions.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是許多宗教的神聖之地。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They believed the river was sacred.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們相信這條河是神聖的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Freedom of speech is a sacred right.\",\n    \"ch\": \"言論自由是一項神聖的權利。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The ancient temple was considered sacred.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座古老的神廟被認為是神聖的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"言論自由是一項神聖的權利。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5859,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::salon::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He opened a new beauty ____.","expectedAnswer":"salon","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He opened a new beauty ____.","clozeAnswer":"salon","exampleTranslation":"他開了一家新的美容院。","reference":{"eng":"salon","kk":"səˈlɑːn","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"沙龍\"  ],  [    \"美容院\"  ],  [    \"客廳\"  ],  [    \"陳列室\"  ]]","chEntries":["沙龍","美容院","客廳","陳列室"],"practiceMeaning":"他開了一家新的美容院。","analysis":"此字源自法語 'salon'，原意為「大廳」、「接待室」，由 'salle' (hall) 演變而來，'salle' 源自拉丁語 'sal' (salt)，或有說源自'sala' (room)，表示「主要房間」。'Salon' 在18世紀法國興起，指「名流聚集的客廳」，成為文化交流的場所。現代語義擴展至「美容院」或「髮廊」，指提供美容、美髮服務的專業場所，這些場所也常被設計成舒適、有格調的空間，如同昔日的社交沙龍。例如，也可指「藝術品陳列室」。","definition":"1. A large room in a private house or hotel, especially one used for entertaining guests.; 2. A fashionable beauty salon or hairdressing establishment.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She went to the salon to get her hair done.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她去沙龍做頭髮。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The salon hosted a gathering of artists.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個沙龍舉辦了一場藝術家聚會。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He opened a new beauty salon.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他開了一家新的美容院。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The art salon exhibited works by local painters.\",\n    \"ch\": \"藝術沙龍展出了本地畫家的作品。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他開了一家新的美容院。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4117,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::scientific::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need a ____ approach to solve this problem.","expectedAnswer":"scientific","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need a ____ approach to solve this problem.","clozeAnswer":"scientific","exampleTranslation":"我們需要一個科學的方法來解決這個問題。","reference":{"eng":"scientific","kk":"/ˌsaɪənˈtɪfɪk/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['科學的']]","chEntries":["科學的"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要一個科學的方法來解決這個問題。","analysis":"源自 science（科學），science 源自拉丁語 scientia（知識），由 scire（知道）衍生。scientific 指與科學方法、原理或研究相關的。","definition":"1. relating to or used in science; 2. systematic and methodical","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They conducted a scientific experiment.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們進行了一項科學實驗。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company invests heavily in scientific research.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司在科學研究上投入巨資。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need a scientific approach to solve this problem.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要一個科學的方法來解決這個問題。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要一個科學的方法來解決這個問題。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6093,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::script::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The manuscript was written in a difficult-to-read ____.","expectedAnswer":"script","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The manuscript was written in a difficult-to-read ____.","clozeAnswer":"script","exampleTranslation":"這份手稿是用一種難以辨認的字跡寫成的。","reference":{"eng":"script","kk":"skrɪpt","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"劇本\"  ],  [    \"腳本\"  ],  [    \"手稿\"  ],  [    \"（電腦）腳本\"  ],  [    \"字跡\"  ]]","chEntries":["劇本","腳本","手稿","字跡"],"practiceMeaning":"這份手稿是用一種難以辨認的字跡寫成的。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 scriptum（something written），是 scribere（to write）的過去分詞。核心語義是「寫下來的東西」。在戲劇、電影、廣播等領域，script 指演員的「劇本」或「腳本」。在電腦領域，script 指一組用於自動執行任務的指令「腳本」。也可用於指「手稿」或「字跡」。","definition":"1. the written text of a play, film, or broadcast; 2. a set of instructions that a computer can follow; 3. handwriting.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The actors rehearsed their lines from the script.\",\n    \"ch\": \"演員們根據劇本排練台詞。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The web developer wrote a JavaScript script.\",\n    \"ch\": \"網頁開發者寫了一個 JavaScript 腳本。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The manuscript was written in a difficult-to-read script.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這份手稿是用一種難以辨認的字跡寫成的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這份手稿是用一種難以辨認的字跡寫成的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6094,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::sector::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The shaded area is a ____ of the circle.","expectedAnswer":"sector","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The shaded area is a ____ of the circle.","clozeAnswer":"sector","exampleTranslation":"陰影區域是圓的一個扇形。","reference":{"eng":"sector","kk":"ˈsɛktər","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"部門\"  ],  [    \"領域\"  ],  [    \"行業\"  ],  [    \"扇形\"  ]]","chEntries":["部門","領域","行業","扇形"],"practiceMeaning":"陰影區域是圓的一個扇形。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 sector（cutter），是 secare（to cut）的結果名詞。核心語義是「被切割的部分」。引申為社會、經濟、地理或數學上的「部分」、「領域」、「部門」或「扇形」。","definition":"1. an area or portion that is distinct from others; 2. a part of the economy or society; 3. (geometry) a part of a circle enclosed by two radii and the arc between them.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The technology sector has grown rapidly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"科技行業發展迅速。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a security sector reform program.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個安全部門改革計畫。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The shaded area is a sector of the circle.\",\n    \"ch\": \"陰影區域是圓的一個扇形。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"陰影區域是圓的一個扇形。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3922,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::semester::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Final exams will be held at the end of the ____.","expectedAnswer":"semester","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Final exams will be held at the end of the ____.","clozeAnswer":"semester","exampleTranslation":"期末考試將在學期末舉行。","reference":{"eng":"semester","kk":"/səˈmestər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['學期']]","chEntries":["學期"],"practiceMeaning":"期末考試將在學期末舉行。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'semestris'，由 'sex' (意為「六」) 和 'mensis' (意為「月」) 組成，意為「六個月」。最初指六個月的時期，後特指學術機構中的一個學期。","definition":"either of the two periods of time in a school year, at the end of which there are holidays.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The fall semester begins in September.\",\n    \"ch\": \"秋季學期於九月開始。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is taking a leave of absence for one semester.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她將休學一個學期。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Final exams will be held at the end of the semester.\",\n    \"ch\": \"期末考試將在學期末舉行。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"期末考試將在學期末舉行。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6095,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::seminar::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She gave a presentation at the international ____.","expectedAnswer":"seminar","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She gave a presentation at the international ____.","clozeAnswer":"seminar","exampleTranslation":"她在國際研討會上做了一個報告。","reference":{"eng":"seminar","kk":"ˈsɛmɪnɑr","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"研討會\"  ],  [    \"講座\"  ],  [    \"討論會\"  ]]","chEntries":["研討會","講座","討論會"],"practiceMeaning":"她在國際研討會上做了一個報告。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 seminarium，意為「種子田」，來自 semen（seed）。核心語義是「播種」，引申為知識、思想的「播種」或傳播之地。在學術語境中，seminar 指一種小型的、通常由專家主持的、參與者進行深入討論或學習的會議。","definition":"a meeting for discussion or exchange of information on a particular subject.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We attended an interesting seminar on climate change.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們參加了一個關於氣候變遷的有趣研討會。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The professor is leading a seminar for graduate students.\",\n    \"ch\": \"教授正在主持一個研究生研討會。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She gave a presentation at the international seminar.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在國際研討會上做了一個報告。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她在國際研討會上做了一個報告。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6135,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::sensor::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The motion ____ activated the alarm.","expectedAnswer":"sensor","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The motion ____ activated the alarm.","clozeAnswer":"sensor","exampleTranslation":"運動感測器啟動了警報。","reference":{"eng":"sensor","kk":"ˈsɛnsər","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"感測器\"  ],  [    \"探測器\"  ],  [    \"感應器\"  ]]","chEntries":["感測器","探測器","感應器"],"practiceMeaning":"運動感測器啟動了警報。","analysis":"此字由動詞 sense（感覺；感知）加上名詞後綴 -or（表示施事者或工具）構成。sense 源自拉丁語 sensus，意為「感覺；知覺」，來自 sentire（感覺）。因此，sensor 的核心語義是「感知或偵測的工具」。此名詞指能夠偵測物理現象（如光、熱、運動、濕度、壓力等）並將其轉化為電信號的裝置。其語意演變是從「感知者」到「偵測裝置」。","definition":"A device that detects and responds to some type of input from the physical environment.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The car is equipped with several sensors.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這輛車配備了多個感測器。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A smoke sensor detected the fire.\",\n    \"ch\": \"煙霧感測器偵測到了火災。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The motion sensor activated the alarm.\",\n    \"ch\": \"運動感測器啟動了警報。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"運動感測器啟動了警報。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4700,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::separation::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of milk into cream and skimmed milk is a common process.","expectedAnswer":"separation","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of milk into cream and skimmed milk is a common process.","clozeAnswer":"separation","exampleTranslation":"牛奶分離成鮮奶油和脫脂牛奶是一個常見的過程。","reference":{"eng":"separation","kk":"/ˌsɛpəˈreɪʃən/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['分離'], ['分居'], ['（科學）分離，（化學）分餾']]","chEntries":["分離","分居","分離，分餾"],"practiceMeaning":"牛奶分離成鮮奶油和脫脂牛奶是一個常見的過程。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 *separatio*，由 *separare*（分開）演變而來。核心是將事物或個體分開的狀態或過程。引申至人際關係的分居，以及科學上將不同物質或成分分開的技術。","definition":"1. The state of being separated or divided. 2. The act of ending a marriage or relationship. 3. The process of dividing substances or components.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The separation of the two elements was difficult.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這兩種元素的 the separation 過程很困難。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They have been living in separation for a year.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們已經分居一年了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The separation of milk into cream and skimmed milk is a common process.\",\n    \"ch\": \"牛奶分離成鮮奶油和脫脂牛奶是一個常見的過程。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"牛奶分離成鮮奶油和脫脂牛奶是一個常見的過程。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5061,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::sequence::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This is the first ____ in the film.","expectedAnswer":"sequence","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This is the first ____ in the film.","clozeAnswer":"sequence","exampleTranslation":"這是電影的第一個鏡頭（連續畫面）。","reference":{"eng":"sequence","kk":"ˈsiːkwəns","tense":"n.","ch":"[['序列'], ['順序'], ['連續發生的事情']]","chEntries":["序列","順序","連續發生的事情"],"practiceMeaning":"這是電影的第一個鏡頭（連續畫面）。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語sequentia，是動詞sequi（跟隨）的派生詞。sequi 又來自原始印歐語 *sekʷ-（跟隨）。sequence 的核心語意是「事物按照特定順序排列或接續」，強調的是「先後關係」或「連續性」。OCR 掃描時可能將 's' 誤判為 '5'，或 'q' 誤判為 'g'。此處修正為 sequence。","definition":"1. a set of related events, movements, or things that follow each other in a particular order; 2. a continuous series of events.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The sequence of events was unclear.\",\n    \"ch\": \"事件的順序不清楚。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He learned the dance steps in sequence.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他按順序學會了舞蹈動作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is the first sequence in the film.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是電影的第一個鏡頭（連續畫面）。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是電影的第一個鏡頭（連續畫面）。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6138,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::server::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The database ____ stores all the user information.","expectedAnswer":"server","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The database ____ stores all the user information.","clozeAnswer":"server","exampleTranslation":"資料庫伺服器儲存了所有使用者資訊。","reference":{"eng":"server","kk":"ˈsɜːrvər","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"伺服器\"  ],  [    \"服務員\"  ],  [    \"侍者\"  ]]","chEntries":["伺服器","服務員","侍者"],"practiceMeaning":"資料庫伺服器儲存了所有使用者資訊。","analysis":"此字由動詞 serve（服務）加上名詞後綴 -er（表示施事者或工具）構成。serve 源自拉丁語 servīre（服務；服從），來自 servus（奴隸）。因此，server 的核心語義是「提供服務者」。在電腦領域，指提供數據、資源或服務的電腦系統（伺服器）。在餐飲業，指提供服務的人（服務員，侍者）。其語意演變是從「服務者」到具體的「伺服器」和「服務員」。","definition":"1. a computer or computer program that manages access to a centralized resource or service; 2. a person who serves food or drinks in a restaurant or bar.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The website is down because the server is overloaded.\",\n    \"ch\": \"網站無法訪問，因為伺服器過載了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The waiter, or server, took our order.\",\n    \"ch\": \"服務員，也就是侍者，為我們點餐。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The database server stores all the user information.\",\n    \"ch\": \"資料庫伺服器儲存了所有使用者資訊。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"資料庫伺服器儲存了所有使用者資訊。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4337,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::shadow::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The war left a ____ over the country's future.","expectedAnswer":"shadow","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The war left a ____ over the country's future.","clozeAnswer":"shadow","exampleTranslation":"戰爭給國家的未來蒙上了陰影。","reference":{"eng":"shadow","kk":"/ˈʃædoʊ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['陰影；影子'], ['（光線被遮擋形成的）暗區'], ['（對某事物的）影響；不安；沮喪'], ['鬼魂；幽靈']]","chEntries":["陰影","影子","暗區","影響","不安","沮喪","鬼魂","幽靈"],"practiceMeaning":"戰爭給國家的未來蒙上了陰影。","analysis":"源自古英語 'sceadwa'，與『遮蔽』、『陰影』相關。1. 光線被物體遮擋而形成的『影子』。2. 物理空間上的『陰影、暗區』。3. 作為比喻，指事物『受到的影響』，可以是負面的，如『不安、沮喪』，或是一個長期存在、難以擺脫的『陰影』。4. 在文學或宗教語境中，指『鬼魂、幽靈』，即沒有實體的影子。","definition":"an area of darkness where light is blocked by an object; a dark area or shape that is produced when an object is between a light source and a surface; an unpleasant feeling that spoils something; the ghost of a dead person","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The tree cast a long shadow.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這棵樹投下了一道長長的影子。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He walked in the shadow of the building.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他走在建築物的陰影裡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The war left a shadow over the country's future.\",\n    \"ch\": \"戰爭給國家的未來蒙上了陰影。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The ghost appeared as a shadowy figure.\",\n    \"ch\": \"鬼魂出現時，像一個模糊的影子。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"戰爭給國家的未來蒙上了陰影。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5804,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::shed::vt","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The lamp ____ a soft light on the table.","expectedAnswer":"shed","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The lamp ____ a soft light on the table.","clozeAnswer":"shed","exampleTranslation":"燈在地板上投下柔和的光。","reference":{"eng":"shed","kk":"ʃɛd","tense":"vt.","ch":"[  [    \"脫落\"  ],  [    \"脫去\"  ],  [    \"流（眼淚）\"  ],  [    \"散發（光、熱）\"  ],  [    \"拋棄\"  ]]","chEntries":["脫落","脫去","流","散發","拋棄"],"practiceMeaning":"燈在地板上投下柔和的光。","analysis":"此字為及物動詞，源自古英語sceddan，詞源不明，可能與古諾斯語Skeitha（分割；分離）有關。核心語義是「將某物分離、去除」。語意演變上，從「自然脫落」（如蛇蛻皮、樹葉掉落）引申為「主動脫去」衣物，或「流出」眼淚，或「散發」光熱，以及「拋棄」不再需要的事物。","definition":"1. (of an animal) to lose hair, skin, or feathers; 2. to get rid of something unwanted; 3. to let tears fall; 4. to give off a particular light, heat, or sound.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Snakes shed their skin once a year.\",\n    \"ch\": \"蛇每年蛻一次皮。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She shed her coat in the warm room.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在溫暖的房間裡脫掉了外套。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The lamp shed a soft light on the table.\",\n    \"ch\": \"燈在地板上投下柔和的光。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"燈在地板上投下柔和的光。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6140,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::sheer::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ determination helped her succeed.","expectedAnswer":"Sheer","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ determination helped her succeed.","clozeAnswer":"Sheer","exampleTranslation":"純粹的決心幫助她取得了成功。","reference":{"eng":"sheer","kk":"ʃɪr","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"純粹的\"  ],  [    \"徹底的\"  ],  [    \"極度的\"  ],  [    \"陡峭的\"  ],  [    \"透明的\"  ]]","chEntries":["純粹的","徹底的","極度的","陡峭的","透明的"],"practiceMeaning":"純粹的決心幫助她取得了成功。","analysis":"此字詞源不確定，可能源自古英語 scīr（純淨的，清澈的）或中古英語 sheer（陡峭的）。modern 用法包含「純粹的、徹底的、極度的」以及「陡峭的、險峻的」。前者語意演變是從「純淨」到「無混雜」，後者則是「垂直的」。","definition":"1. nothing other than; unmitigated; 2. steep or vertical; 3. (of fabric) thin and transparent.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Sheer joy filled the room.\",\n    \"ch\": \"純粹的喜悅充滿了房間。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The cliff was sheer.\",\n    \"ch\": \"懸崖很陡峭。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Sheer determination helped her succeed.\",\n    \"ch\": \"純粹的決心幫助她取得了成功。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"純粹的決心幫助她取得了成功。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}