:"[['瘦的', '瘠瘦的'], ['薄的', '細的']]","chEntries":["瘦的","瘠瘦的","薄的","細的"],"practiceMeaning":"她吃得很少，而且相當瘦。","analysis":"源自古英語 'skinn-', 與 'skin' (皮膚) 有關。指「非常瘦」；也可用於形容物體「薄的、細的」。","definition":"1. unpleasantly thin; 2. very thin and smooth.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was so skinny after being sick.\",\n    \"ch\": \"病後他變得非常瘦。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The skinny jeans are out of fashion.\",\n    \"ch\": \"緊身牛仔褲已經過時了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She ate very little and was quite skinny.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她吃得很少，而且相當瘦。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她吃得很少，而且相當瘦。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5807,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::skull::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ and crossbones is a symbol of danger.","expectedAnswer":"skull","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ and crossbones is a symbol of danger.","clozeAnswer":"skull","exampleTranslation":"骷髏頭和交叉的骨頭是危險的象徵。","reference":{"eng":"skull","kk":"skʌl","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"頭蓋骨\"  ],  [    \"顱骨\"  ],  [    \"髑髏\"  ]]","chEntries":["頭蓋骨","顱骨","髑髏"],"practiceMeaning":"骷髏頭和交叉的骨頭是危險的象徵。","analysis":"此字為名詞，源自古英語scull，可能與古諾斯語skalli（光禿的頭）有關，詞源意義為「頭部」或「頭蓋」。核心語義是指「構成頭部骨骼結構的骨頭」，即頭蓋骨或顱骨。語意演變上，從「頭部」的概念，具體化為保護大腦的「頭骨」。","definition":"1. the bony framework of the head of a person or vertebrate animal, enclosing the brain and supporting the facial structures.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The skull protects the brain.\",\n    \"ch\": \"頭蓋骨保護大腦。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Archaeologists found a human skull at the dig site.\",\n    \"ch\": \"考古學家在挖掘地點發現了一顆人頭骨。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The skull and crossbones is a symbol of danger.\",\n    \"ch\": \"骷髏頭和交叉的骨頭是危險的象徵。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"骷髏頭和交叉的骨頭是危險的象徵。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5809,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::slap::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of the waves was loud.","expectedAnswer":"slap","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of the waves was loud.","clozeAnswer":"slap","exampleTranslation":"海浪拍打的聲音很大。","reference":{"eng":"slap","kk":"slæp","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"摑（耳光）\"  ],  [    \"拍打\"  ],  [    \"一擊\"  ]]","chEntries":["摑","拍打","一擊"],"practiceMeaning":"海浪拍打的聲音很大。","analysis":"此字為名詞，與動詞同源。核心語義是指「用手掌打擊的動作或聲音」。語意演變上，從具體的「摑耳光」或「拍打」動作，也可用來形容某種突然或有力的接觸，或比喻為一次意外的打擊。","definition":"1. an act of hitting someone or something with the palm of your hand; 2. the sound of a slap; 3. an unpleasant shock or disappointment.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He received a slap on the back for his achievement.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他因成就而得到背部拍打（讚揚）。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The decision was a slap in the face to the workers.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個決定對工人來說是個打擊。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The slap of the waves was loud.\",\n    \"ch\": \"海浪拍打的聲音很大。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"海浪拍打的聲音很大。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5101,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::slavery::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He felt in ____ to his ambition.","expectedAnswer":"slavery","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He felt in ____ to his ambition.","clozeAnswer":"slavery","exampleTranslation":"他覺得自己被野心所奴役。","reference":{"eng":"slavery","kk":"ˈsleɪvəri","tense":"n.","ch":"[['奴隸制度'], ['奴役'], ['被束縛的狀態']]","chEntries":["奴隸制度","奴役","被束縛的狀態"],"practiceMeaning":"他覺得自己被野心所奴役。","analysis":"此字由 'slave' (奴隸) + '-ry' (名詞化後綴，表示狀態、職業、集合) 構成。'-ry' 後綴常表示與某事物相關的狀態、職業、地方或集合，如 'bakery' (麵包店)、'bravery' (勇氣)。'Slavery' 的核心語義是 '被視為財產並被迫勞動，且失去自由的狀態'。它既指社會制度，也指個人遭受的 '奴役' 或 '被束縛' 的處境。","definition":"1. The state or condition of being a slave; the practice of owning slaves.; 2. The system whereby people are treated as property and are forced to work.; 3. A state of being controlled by a powerful force or addiction.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The abolition of 