支樂隊的最新專輯是一次巨大的成功。","reference":{"eng":"smash","kk":"smæʃ","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"破碎\"  ],  [    \"猛撞\"  ],  [    \"粉碎\"  ],  [    \"巨大的成功\"  ]]","chEntries":["破碎","猛撞","粉碎","巨大的成功"],"practiceMeaning":"這支樂隊的最新專輯是一次巨大的成功。","analysis":"此字源自擬聲詞，模仿物體破碎的聲音。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。名詞義指猛烈撞擊、打碎或粉碎的動作及其結果。也可引申為巨大的成功或轟動。中文翻譯為「破碎；猛撞；粉碎；巨大的成功」。","definition":"1. the act of breaking something violently; 2. a loud noise made by something breaking; 3. a great success.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The smash of glass echoed in the street.\",\n    \"ch\": \"玻璃破碎的聲音迴盪在街上。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The car crash resulted in the smash of the windshield.\",\n    \"ch\": \"汽車相撞導致擋風玻璃粉碎。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The band's latest album was a smash hit.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這支樂隊的最新專輯是一次巨大的成功。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這支樂隊的最新專輯是一次巨大的成功。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6246,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::smog::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ alert was issued due to high pollution levels.","expectedAnswer":"smog","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ alert was issued due to high pollution levels.","clozeAnswer":"smog","exampleTranslation":"由於污染水平很高，發布了霧霾警報。","reference":{"eng":"smog","kk":"smɔɡ","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"煙霧\"  ],  [    \"霧霾\"  ]]","chEntries":["煙霧","霧霾"],"practiceMeaning":"由於污染水平很高，發布了霧霾警報。","analysis":"此字為合成詞，由 smoke（煙）和 fog（霧）組成。此字在現代英語中是常見的合成詞，由兩個獨立的詞合併而成。名詞義指由煙霧和霧氣混合而成的污染空氣。中文翻譯為「煙霧；霧霾」。","definition":"fog mixed with smoke and pollution.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The city was covered in a thick layer of smog.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座城市籠罩在厚厚的煙霧中。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Smog can cause respiratory problems.\",\n    \"ch\": \"霧霾會引起呼吸系統問題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The smog alert was issued due to high pollution levels.\",\n    \"ch\": \"由於污染水平很高，發布了霧霾警報。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"由於污染水平很高，發布了霧霾警報。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6097,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::solo::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The violinist played a beautiful ____.","expectedAnswer":"solo","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The violinist played a beautiful ____.","clozeAnswer":"solo","exampleTranslation":"小提琴家演奏了一曲優美的獨奏。","reference":{"eng":"solo","kk":"ˈsolo","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"單獨的\"  ],  [    \"獨奏的\"  ],  [    \"獨唱的\"  ]]","chEntries":["單獨的","獨奏的","獨唱的"],"practiceMeaning":"小提琴家演奏了一曲優美的獨奏。","analysis":"此字源自義大利語 solo，意為「單獨的」，最終來源於拉丁語 solus（alone）。核心語義是「獨自一人」。可以用來形容表演（獨奏、獨唱）或行為（獨自完成）。","definition":"1. performed alone; 2. done or being performed by a person without help.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She performed a solo dance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她表演了一段獨舞。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He achieved his goals through solo effort.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他通過單獨努力達成了目標。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The violinist played a beautiful solo.\",\n    \"ch\": \"小提琴家演奏了一曲優美的獨奏。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"小提琴家演奏了一曲優美的獨奏。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5569,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::sort::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"What ____ of music do you like?","expectedAnswer":"sort","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"What ____ of music do you like?","clozeAnswer":"sort","exampleTranslation":"你喜歡哪一類的音樂？","reference":{"eng":"sort","kk":"sɔrt","tense":"n.","ch":"[['種類'], ['類型'], ['類別'], ['品級']]","chEntries":["種類","類型","類別","品級"],"practiceMeaning":"你喜歡哪一類的音樂？","analysis":"這是 \"sort\" 作動詞的相關名詞形式，源自古法語 \"sortir\"，意為 \"to draw lots, to choose\"（抽籤，選擇），來自拉丁語 \"sors, sortis\"（lot, fate, share，籤，命運，份額）。\"sors\" 最初與「抽籤」或「命運」相關，引申出「一份」、「一部分」的概念，進而演變為「同一類的事物」或「某一類型的東西」。因此，\"sort\" 作為名詞，指「由共同特徵或標準劃分出來的群體或類別」，即「種類」或「類型」。","definition":"1. A category of people or things having common characteristics; 2. A number of people or things that are grouped together because they are similar to each other.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a sort of person who always tries to help.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是那種總是試圖幫忙的人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This sort of behavior is unacceptable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種行為是不可接受的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"What sort of music do you like?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你喜歡哪一類的音樂？\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"你喜歡哪一類的音樂？","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5104,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::stereotype::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He refused to be defined by such a narrow ____.","expectedAnswer":"stereotype","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He refused to be defined by such a narrow ____.","clozeAnswer":"stereotype","exampleTranslation":"他拒絕被如此狹隘的刻板印象所定義。","reference":{"eng":"stereotype","kk":"ˈsteriəˌtaɪp","tense":"n.","ch":"[['刻板印象'], ['成見'], ['標準化模式']]","chEntries":["刻板印象","成見","標準化模式"],"practiceMeaning":"他拒絕被如此狹隘的刻板印象所定義。","analysis":"此字源自希臘語 'stereos' (solid) + 'typos' (impression, mark)，原意是 '堅固的印模'。在印刷業中，它指 '鑄版'，即製作一個標準化的、可重複使用的印刷模具。引申至社會學和心理學，'stereotype' 指的是一種 '固定化、過度簡化且通常不準確的對某類人或群體的看法'，這種看法像一個 '印模'，將所有個體都歸入同一類別，缺乏個別差異的考量，容易造成偏見。","definition":"1. A widely held but fixed and oversimplified image or idea of a particular type of person or thing.; 2. A set of printed characters that can be used as a mold for casting metal type.; 3. An act of stereotyping someone or something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We must challenge stereotypes about women in leadership roles.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們必須挑戰關於女性領導者的刻板印象。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The media often perpetuates harmful stereotypes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"媒體經常延續有害的刻板印象。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He refused to be defined by such a narrow stereotype.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他拒絕被如此狹隘的刻板印象所定義。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他拒絕被如此狹隘的刻板印象所定義。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6143,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::theoretical::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The plan is sound in ____ terms.","expectedAnswer":"theoretical","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The plan is sound in ____ terms.","clozeAnswer":"theoretical","exampleTranslation":"這個計畫在理論上是可靠的。","reference":{"eng":"theoretical","kk":"ˌθiːəˈrɛtɪkəl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"理論的\"  ],  [    \"學術的\"  ],  [    \"假設的\"  ]]","chEntries":["理論的","學術的","假設的"],"practiceMeaning":"這個計畫在理論上是可靠的。","analysis":"此字由 theory（理論）加上形容詞後綴 -etical 構成。theory 源自希臘語 theōria，意為「觀察；沉思；理論」。因此，theoretical 的核心語義是「與理論相關的」。此形容詞表示基於理論或假說，與實踐相對。其語意演變是從「基於觀察與沉思」到「與理論相關」。","definition":"1. concerned with or constituting theory; 2. based on or concerned with theory rather than practice; hypothetical.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"a theoretical physicist\",\n    \"ch\": \"理論物理學家\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a theoretical model, not a practical solution.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個理論模型，不是實際的解決方案。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The plan is sound in theoretical terms.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個計畫在理論上是可靠的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個計畫在理論上是可靠的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5813,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::thriller::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The adventure was a real ____ for the participants.","expectedAnswer":"thriller","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The adventure was a real ____ for the participants.","clozeAnswer":"thriller","exampleTranslation":"這次冒險對參與者來說是一次真正的刺激體驗。","reference":{"eng":"thriller","kk":"ˈθrɪlər","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"驚悚片\"  ],  [    \"驚悚小說\"  ],  [    \"令人興奮的事物\"  ]]","chEntries":["驚悚片","驚悚小說","令人興奮的事物"],"practiceMeaning":"這次冒險對參與者來說是一次真正的刺激體驗。","analysis":"此字為名詞，構詞自thrill（使興奮；使激動）+ -er（名詞字尾，表示「事物」或「人」）。thrill源自中古英語。因此，thriller的核心語義是指「能夠引起強烈興奮、激動或恐懼的事物」，特別是用於指「驚悚電影」或「驚悚小說」，這類作品旨在提供強烈的感官刺激和緊張感。語意演變上，由形容「令人興奮的」轉化為指代「能製造這種興奮體驗的媒介（電影、書籍）」。","definition":"1. a novel, play, or film that has an exciting or frightening plot; 2. a person or thing that causes excitement.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She enjoys reading thrillers before bed.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她喜歡睡前閱讀驚悚小說。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The movie was a political thriller with a lot of suspense.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這部電影是一部充滿懸念的政治驚悚片。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The adventure was a real thriller for the participants.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這次冒險對參與者來說是一次真正的刺激體驗。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這次冒險對參與者來說是一次真正的刺激體驗。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4636,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::tight::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We have a ____ schedule for the project.","expectedAnswer":"tight","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We have a ____ schedule for the project.","clozeAnswer":"tight","exampleTranslation":"我們這個專案的時間表很緊。","reference":{"eng":"tight","kk":"/taɪt/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['緊的'], ['牢固的'], ['（空間）狹窄的'], ['（供應）緊張的'], ['（時間）緊迫的']]","chEntries":["緊的","牢固的","狹窄的","緊張的","緊迫的"],"practiceMeaning":"我們這個專案的時間表很緊。","analysis":"源自古英語 'tiht' (緊湊、快速)，與 'tie' (綁) 同源。核心概念是緊密、不易移動或變形。可以是物理上的緊縛，也可以是抽象上的限制，如空間、時間或供應的緊縮。","definition":"fixed firmly in place; not loose; not having much space; limited in supply or time.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The knot was very tight.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個結打得很緊。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The city streets are very tight and narrow.\",\n    \"ch\": \"市區的街道非常狹窄。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We have a tight schedule for the project.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們這個專案的時間表很緊。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The money supply is tight.\",\n    \"ch\": \"資金供應緊張。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們這個專案的時間表很緊。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4551,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::trace::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Can you ____ the route on this map?","expectedAnswer":"trace","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Can you ____ the route on this map?","clozeAnswer":"trace","exampleTranslation":"你能在這張地圖上描出路線嗎？","reference":{"eng":"trace","kk":"/treɪs/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['追蹤', '追溯'], ['描繪', '勾勒']]","chEntries":["追蹤","追溯","描繪","勾勒"],"practiceMeaning":"你能在這張地圖上描出路線嗎？","analysis":"動詞用法源自名詞。\n    1. 追蹤、追溯：指通過線索找到某物的起源、經過或下落。\n    2. 描繪、勾勒：指仔細地畫出線條或輪廓，如同追蹤物體的形狀。","definition":"1. follow the course or development of (something).; 2. discover or reveal (something) by a process of investigation or analysis.; 3. copy (a drawing or design) by drawing on a sheet of paper laid over it.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Scientists are trying to trace the origin of the disease.\",\n    \"ch\": \"科學家們正試圖追溯這種疾病的起源。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She traced the outline of the leaf with her finger.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她用手指描繪著葉子的輪廓。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Can you trace the route on this map?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你能在這張地圖上描出路線嗎？\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"你能在這張地圖上描出路線嗎？","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5462,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::tribe::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They lived in a small village belonging to the ____.","expectedAnswer":"tribe","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They lived in a small village belonging to the ____.","clozeAnswer":"tribe","exampleTranslation":"他們住在一屬於該部落的小村莊裡。","reference":{"eng":"tribe","kk":"traɪb","tense":"n.","ch":"[['部落'], ['部族'], ['（某些動物的）族']]","chEntries":["部落","部族","族"],"practiceMeaning":"他們住在一屬於該部落的小村莊裡。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'tribus'，原意指古羅馬的「三個部落」，是羅馬社會的基本組成單位。在羅馬共和國後期，'tribus' 演變為行政區劃單位。後來，這個詞被借用到古英語和中古英語中，尤其是在描述社會組織形式時。在人類學和社會學中，'tribe' 指的是一個由共同血緣、語言、文化或地域聯繫起來的社會群體，通常具有較為簡單的政治組織。核心語意是「一個具有共同特徵和組織結構的群體」。","definition":"1. A social group consisting of families or clans with a common kinship, culture, and dialect, typically having a recognized leader.; 2. A group of people of common lineage, often a clan or federation of clans.; 3. A social group that shares a common culture, leadership, and territory.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The Amazon basin is home to many indigenous tribes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"亞馬遜盆地是許多原住民部落的家園。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The members of the tribe were known for their hunting skills.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個部落的成員以他們的狩獵技巧而聞名。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They lived in a small village belonging to the tribe.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們住在一屬於該部落的小村莊裡。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們住在一屬於該部落的小村莊裡。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4129,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::tricky::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Learning to juggle can be ____.","expectedAnswer":"tricky","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Learning to juggle can be ____.","clozeAnswer":"tricky","exampleTranslation":"學會玩雜耍可能需要技巧。","reference":{"eng":"tricky","kk":"/ˈtrɪki/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['棘手的', '難辦的'], ['狡猾的', '奸詐的'], ['需要技巧的', '巧妙的']]","chEntries":["棘手的","難辦的","狡猾的","奸詐的","需要技巧的","巧妙的"],"practiceMeaning":"學會玩雜耍可能需要技巧。","analysis":"源自 trick（詭計，花招）。核心概念是「需要小心處理」，因為存在隱藏的困難、欺騙或複雜性。引申為難以應付的問題、狡猾的人或需要精細操作的任務。","definition":"1. difficult to deal with or accomplish; 2. cunning or deceitful; 3. requiring skill or dexterity","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"That was a tricky question.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那是一個棘手的問題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He's known for his tricky negotiation tactics.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他以其狡猾的談判策略而聞名。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Learning to juggle can be tricky.\",\n    \"ch\": \"學會玩雜耍可能需要技巧。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"學會玩雜耍可能需要技巧。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6146,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::tuna::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The fisherman caught a giant ____.","expectedAnswer":"tuna","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The fisherman caught a giant ____.","clozeAnswer":"tuna","exampleTranslation":"漁夫捕獲了一條巨大的鮪魚。","reference":{"eng":"tuna","kk":"ˈtuːnə","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"鮪魚\"  ],  [    \"金槍魚\"  ]]","chEntries":["鮪魚","金槍魚"],"practiceMeaning":"漁夫捕獲了一條巨大的鮪魚。","analysis":"此字詞源可能來自西班牙語或葡萄牙語 atún，來自阿拉伯語 al-tūn，最後可能追溯至拉丁語 thynnus，希臘語 thynnos，意為「快速的魚」，可能與 thynō（衝刺；快速移動）有關。此名詞指一種大型的海洋魚類，如鮪魚或金槍魚。其語意演變是從「快速的魚」到具體的魚類名稱。","definition":"A large, active, predatory fish of the sea, typically having a streamlined body and being of commercial importance as food.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I had tuna salad for lunch.\",\n    \"ch\": \"午餐我吃了鮪魚沙拉。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Canned tuna is a popular source of protein.\",\n    \"ch\": \"罐頭鮪魚是受歡迎的蛋白質來源。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The fisherman caught a giant tuna.\",\n    \"ch\": \"漁夫捕獲了一條巨大的鮪魚。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"漁夫捕獲了一條巨大的鮪魚。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6104,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::unemployment::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He has been facing long-term ____.","expectedAnswer":"unemployment","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He has been facing long-term ____.","clozeAnswer":"unemployment","exampleTranslation":"他一直面臨長期失業。","reference":{"eng":"unemployment","kk":"ˌʌnɪmˈplɔɪmənt","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"失業\"  ],  [    \"失業率\"  ],  [    \"失業狀態\"  ]]","chEntries":["失業","失業率","失業狀態"],"practiceMeaning":"他一直面臨長期失業。","analysis":"此字由 un-（not）+ employ（僱用）+ -ment（名詞後綴，表示狀態或行為）構成。核心語義是「未被僱用」的狀態。指沒有工作或失業的狀態，以及由此產生的社會現象（失業率）。","definition":"1. the state of being unemployed; 2. the number of people who are unemployed.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government is trying to reduce unemployment.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府正試圖降低失業率。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Unemployment rates have been rising.\",\n    \"ch\": \"失業率一直在上升。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has been facing long-term unemployment.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他一直面臨長期失業。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他一直面臨長期失業。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6147,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::unfold::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"As the events ____, we will learn more.","expectedAnswer":"unfold","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"As the events ____, we will learn more.","clozeAnswer":"unfold","exampleTranslation":"隨著事件的發展，我們將了解更多。","reference":{"eng":"unfold","kk":"ʌnˈfoʊld","tense":"v.","ch":"[  [    \"展開\"  ],  [    \"打開\"  ],  [    \"闡明\"  ],  [    \"發展\"  ]]","chEntries":["展開","打開","闡明","發展"],"practiceMeaning":"隨著事件的發展，我們將了解更多。","analysis":"此字由否定字首 un-（不；相反）和動詞 fold（折疊）構成。fold 源自古英語 faldan，意為「摺疊；纏繞」。unfold 的核心語義是「不折疊」，即將折疊的物體打開，使其平展。引申為揭示、闡明事實或情況，或指事件的發展。此處使用 v. 詞性，表示及物與不及物皆可。及物用法如 unfold a map。不及物用法如 the story unfolds。其語意演變是從具體的「打開」到抽象的「揭示；發展」。","definition":"1. to open or spread out something that has been folded; 2. to become clear or revealed; 3. to develop or become clear.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please unfold the map.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請展開地圖。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The mystery began to unfold.\",\n    \"ch\": \"謎團開始被揭開。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"As the events unfold, we will learn more.\",\n    \"ch\": \"隨著事件的發展，我們將了解更多。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"隨著事件的發展，我們將了解更多。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6148,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::unlock::vt","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ your phone with a passcode.","expectedAnswer":"Unlock","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ your phone with a passcode.","clozeAnswer":"Unlock","exampleTranslation":"用密碼解鎖你的手機。","reference":{"eng":"unlock","kk":"ʌnˈlɑːk","tense":"vt.","ch":"[  [    \"解鎖\"  ],  [    \"打開\"  ],  [    \"揭示\"  ]]","chEntries":["解鎖","打開","揭示"],"practiceMeaning":"用密碼解鎖你的手機。","analysis":"此字由否定字首 un-（不；相反）和動詞 lock（鎖）構成。lock 源自古英語 loca，意為「鎖；閂」。unlock 的核心語義是「解除鎖定」，即打開鎖著的東西。引申為揭示秘密、答案或潛在的可能性。此及物動詞表示打開被鎖住的門、盒子、密碼等，或揭示隱藏的信息。其語意演變是從具體的「開鎖」到抽象的「揭示」。","definition":"1. to open (a door, window, or container) by unlocking it; 2. to make something accessible or available; to reveal.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He used the key to unlock the door.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他用鑰匙解鎖了門。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The discovery unlocked the secrets of the ancient civilization.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這項發現揭開了古代文明的秘密。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Unlock your phone with a passcode.\",\n    \"ch\": \"用密碼解鎖你的手機。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"用密碼解鎖你的手機。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4524,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::up::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It's time to clean ____.","expectedAnswer":"up","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It's time to clean ____.","clozeAnswer":"up","exampleTranslation":"該打掃了。","reference":{"eng":"up","kk":"/ʌp/","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['向上'], ['起來'], ['在...上面'], ['完成']]","chEntries":["向上","起來","在...上面","完成"],"practiceMeaning":"該打掃了。","analysis":"源自古英語 up。是一個表示方向、位置、狀態或完成的副詞。核心語意是「朝上」、「向上」。引申義廣泛，包括「停止」、「完成」、「在場」等。","definition":"1. Towards a higher place or position; 2. Completely or entirely; 3. Out of bed; 4. In progress.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Look up!\",\n    \"ch\": \"向上看！\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He got up early.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他早早地起床了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's time to clean up.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該打掃了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The meeting is all wrapped up.\",\n    \"ch\": \"會議已經全部結束了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該打掃了。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6203,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::valid::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Please ensure your passport is ____.","expectedAnswer":"valid","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Please ensure your passport is ____.","clozeAnswer":"valid","exampleTranslation":"請確保您的護照有效。","reference":{"eng":"valid","kk":"ˈvælɪd","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"有效的\"  ],  [    \"有法律效力的\"  ],  [    \"合理的\"  ],  [    \"有說服力的\"  ]]","chEntries":["有效的","有法律效力的","合理的","有說服力的"],"practiceMeaning":"請確保您的護照有效。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 validus，意為「強壯的、有力的」，與 valēre「強壯、有力」相關。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 valēre「強壯、有力」是其核心語意來源。作為形容詞，其核心語義是指「有充分證據或理由支持的、為法律或規章所承認的」。詞源中的「強壯、有力」引申為「有說服力的、有效的」。","definition":"1. legally or officially acceptable; 2. based on known facts and sound reasoning; 3. (of a ticket or other document) allowing the holder to travel or gain admission; 4. (of an argument or point) having a sound basis in logic or fact.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This ticket is valid for one year.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這張票一年內有效。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His argument is valid.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的論點是有說服力的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please ensure your passport is valid.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請確保您的護照有效。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The contract is valid from today.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該合同從今天起生效。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"請確保您的護照有效。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5110,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::viable::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company's business model is no longer ____.","expectedAnswer":"viable","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company's business model is no longer ____.","clozeAnswer":"viable","exampleTranslation":"這家公司的商業模式已不再可行。","reference":{"eng":"viable","kk":"ˈvaɪəbl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['可行的'], ['可持續的'], ['生存的']]","chEntries":["可行的","可持續的","生存的"],"practiceMeaning":"這家公司的商業模式已不再可行。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'via' (way)，透過古法語 'viable' (capable of living) 演變而來。其核心語義是 '能夠生存、發展或成功地運作'。這可以指生物的生命力，如 'a viable fetus' (存活的胎兒)，也可以指計劃、項目或商業模式的可行性，強調其在現實條件下能夠實施並產生預期結果的能力。","definition":"1. Capable of working successfully; feasible.; 2. Able to survive or to function successfully.; 3. (Of a newborn infant) able to survive after birth.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The plan is not viable in the long term.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個計劃從長遠來看是不可行的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to find a viable solution.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要找到一個可行的解決方案。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company's business model is no longer viable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司的商業模式已不再可行。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這家公司的商業模式已不再可行。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4489,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::wisdom::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He is known for his deep ____.","expectedAnswer":"wisdom","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He is known for his deep ____.","clozeAnswer":"wisdom","exampleTranslation":"他以其深邃的智慧而聞名。","reference":{"eng":"wisdom","kk":"/ˈwɪzdəm/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['智慧'], ['明智']]","chEntries":["智慧","明智"],"practiceMeaning":"他以其深邃的智慧而聞名。","analysis":"源自古英語 wīsdōm，由 wīs (智慧的) 和 -dōm (表示「狀態」、「領域」或「品質」的名詞後綴) 組成。核心語意是「理解深刻事實或情況的能力」，「明辨是非的能力」。","definition":"1. The quality of having experience, knowledge, and good judgment; 2. The quality of being wise.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She offered her wisdom and advice.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她提供了她的智慧和建議。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It takes wisdom to understand complex issues.\",\n    \"ch\": \"理解複雜的問題需要智慧。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is known for his deep wisdom.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他以其深邃的智慧而聞名。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他以其深邃的智慧而聞名。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U10、L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5070,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::worthy::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She is a ____ opponent.","expectedAnswer":"worthy","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She is a ____ opponent.","clozeAnswer":"worthy","exampleTranslation":"她是一位值得尊敬的對手。","reference":{"eng":"worthy","kk":"ˈwɜːrði","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['值得的'], ['有價值的'], ['品格高尚的']]","chEntries":["值得的","有價值的","品格高尚的"],"practiceMeaning":"她是一位值得尊敬的對手。","analysis":"此字由word（詞）加上字尾-y（形容詞化）構成，但其詞源並非來自word，而是源自古英語wierðe，意為「有價值的、值得的」。其核心語意是「值得尊敬、重視或獲得某事物（如讚揚、關注、獎勵）」。此用法與名詞 worth（價值）相關。OCR 掃描時可能將 'w' 誤判為 'u'，或 'rd' 誤判為 'nd'。此處修正為 worthy。","definition":"1. deserving effort or attention; 2. having or showing the merits or character to deserve attention, honor, or respect.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a worthy recipient of the award.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是該獎項當之無愧的得主。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a cause worthy of our support.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個值得我們支持的事業。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a worthy opponent.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是一位值得尊敬的對手。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她是一位值得尊敬的對手。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5829,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::circuit::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The Formula 1 ____ is known for its speed.","expectedAnswer":"circuit","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The Formula 1 ____ is known for its speed.","clozeAnswer":"circuit","exampleTranslation":"F1 賽道以其速度聞名。","reference":{"eng":"circuit","kk":"ˈsɜːrkɪt","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"電路\"  ],  [    \"迴路\"  ],  [    \"巡迴路線\"  ],  [    \"週期\"  ],  [    \"環形\"  ]]","chEntries":["電路","迴路","巡迴路線","週期","環形"],"practiceMeaning":"F1 賽道以其速度聞名。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'circuitus'，是 'circuire' (to go around) 的過去分詞，由 'circum' (around) 和 'ire' (to go) 構成。'Circuitus' 的字面意思是「繞行」，引申為「圍繞一圈的路線」或「封閉的循環」。在物理學上，'circuit' 指電流沿著封閉路徑流動的「電路」或「迴路」。在地理或旅行語境中，'circuit' 指「巡迴路線」，如馬戲團或表演團體的巡迴演出路線。它強調的是一種「循環」或「繞行」的概念。例如，也可指「一場比賽的賽道」。","definition":"1. A roughly circular or oval area or path.; 2. A complete electrical path, consisting of wires, components, and a power source.; 3. A route or journey that visits a number of places.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The electrician checked the electrical circuit.\",\n    \"ch\": \"電工檢查了電路。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The race car driver completed another circuit of the track.\",\n    \"ch\": \"賽車手又完成了一圈賽道。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They are planning a lecture circuit.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們正在規劃一個演講巡迴路線。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The Formula 1 circuit is known for its speed.\",\n    \"ch\": \"F1 賽道以其速度聞名。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"F1 賽道以其速度聞名。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5575,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::code::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company has a ____ of conduct for its employees.","expectedAnswer":"code","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company has a ____ of conduct for its employees.","clozeAnswer":"code","exampleTranslation":"這家公司有員工行為準則。","reference":{"eng":"code","kk":"koʊd","tense":"n.","ch":"[['代碼'], ['密碼'], ['編碼'], ['規範'], ['程式碼']]","chEntries":["代碼","密碼","編碼","規範","程式碼"],"practiceMeaning":"這家公司有員工行為準則。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 \"codex\"，意為 \"book, manuscript, trunk of a tree\"（書本，手稿，樹幹）。\"codex\" 最初是指一種由多張羊皮紙或蠟板黏合而成的書寫形式，與捲軸形式相對。因此，\"code\" 最初指「裝訂好的書冊」或「手稿」。其語義演變包括：指「法律條文的彙編」（a body of laws）；指「一套規則或準則」（a system of rules or principles），例如「行為準則」；在現代，尤其指「用於數據傳輸或儲存的符號系統」（a system of symbols used to transmit or store data），例如「電腦程式碼」、「密碼」或「暗碼」。","definition":"1. A system of words, letters, figures, or symbols used to represent others, especially for the purposes of secrecy; 2. A set of rules or principles, especially one governing the conduct of people or the procedure in a particular activity; 3. A program for a computer written in a particular programming language.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The programmer wrote the code for the new app.\",\n    \"ch\": \"程式設計師編寫了新應用程式的代碼。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This building has strict building codes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這棟建築有嚴格的建築規範。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He used a secret code to send the message.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他使用一種密碼發送了這則訊息。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company has a code of conduct for its employees.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司有員工行為準則。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這家公司有員工行為準則。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6163,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::collector::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ ensured all debts were paid.","expectedAnswer":"collector","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ ensured all debts were paid.","clozeAnswer":"collector","exampleTranslation":"收賬員確保所有債務都已支付。","reference":{"eng":"collector","kk":"kəˈlɛktər","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"收集者\"  ],  [    \"收藏家\"  ],  [    \"稅吏\"  ],  [    \"收賬員\"  ]]","chEntries":["收集者","收藏家","稅吏","收賬員"],"practiceMeaning":"收賬員確保所有債務都已支付。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 collectorem，是動詞 colligere「收集、聚集」的施事者名詞。colligere 由 com- (together) + legere (to gather) 組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 com-「一起」和 legere「收集」是其核心語意來源。作為名詞，其核心語義是「收集某物的人」。詞源中的「一起收集」概念引申為「從眾多事物中聚集、收起」的動作者。除了指收藏家，也用於指負責徵收稅款或債務的人。","definition":"1. a person who collects things of a particular type as a hobby or profession; 2. a person whose job is to collect money that is owed to a company or the government.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is an avid collector of rare stamps.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一位熱情的稀有郵票收藏家。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The tax collector visited the household.\",\n    \"ch\": \"稅吏拜訪了這個家庭。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a collector of antique furniture.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是古董傢俱的收藏家。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The collector ensured all debts were paid.\",\n    \"ch\": \"收賬員確保所有債務都已支付。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"收賬員確保所有債務都已支付。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6216,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::commitment::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They have a strong ____ to environmental protection.","expectedAnswer":"commitment","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They have a strong ____ to environmental protection.","clozeAnswer":"commitment","exampleTranslation":"他們對環保有堅定的承諾。","reference":{"eng":"commitment","kk":"kəˈmɪtmənt","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"承諾\"  ],  [    \"保證\"  ],  [    \"投入\"  ],  [    \"奉獻\"  ],  [    \"責任\"  ],  [    \"委身\"  ]]","chEntries":["承諾","保證","投入","奉獻","責任","委身"],"practiceMeaning":"他們對環保有堅定的承諾。","analysis":"此字由動詞 commit（承諾；委託；犯罪）加上名詞字尾 -ment（表示狀態、行為、結果）構成。commit 源自拉丁語 committere，意為「交付；委託」。字尾 -ment 將動詞轉為名詞，表示「承諾的行為或狀態」、「盡責的狀態」、「奉獻的狀態」。核心語義是將自己投入某事，或對某事做出堅定的保證。中文翻譯為「承諾；保證；投入；奉獻；責任；委身」。","definition":"1. a promise to do something or to behave in a particular way; 2. the state or quality of being dedicated to a cause, activity, etc.; 3. a long-term obligation or responsibility.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He made a commitment to finish the project on time.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他承諾按時完成這個項目。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her commitment to her work is admirable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對工作的投入令人欽佩。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Marriage is a serious commitment.\",\n    \"ch\": \"婚姻是一項嚴肅的承諾。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They have a strong commitment to environmental protection.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們對環保有堅定的承諾。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們對環保有堅定的承諾。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5832,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::compatible::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Their personalities were highly ____.","expectedAnswer":"compatible","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Their personalities were highly ____.","clozeAnswer":"compatible","exampleTranslation":"他們的性情非常協調。","reference":{"eng":"compatible","kk":"kəmˈpætəbl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"兼容的\"  ],  [    \"相容的\"  ],  [    \"協調的\"  ],  [    \"適合的\"  ]]","chEntries":["兼容的","相容的","協調的","適合的"],"practiceMeaning":"他們的性情非常協調。","analysis":"此字由拉丁語 'compatibilis' 演變而來，由 'com-' (with) 和 'pati' (to suffer, endure) 構成。'Patibilis' 意為「可承受的」。'Compatibilis' 的字面意思是「可以一起承受」或「可以共存」。在現代英語中，'compatible' 指兩個或多個事物能夠一起良好運作、和諧共處，或在功能上相互適用。這可以是指電腦系統、軟體、硬體之間的「兼容性」，也可以是指人際關係中的「協調」或「適合」。核心概念是「能夠和諧共存或協作」。例如，也可指「性情相投的」。","definition":"1. (of two things) able to exist or occur together without conflict.; 2. (of computer hardware or software) able to be used or run together.; 3. (of a person) having a compatible nature or disposition.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This software is not compatible with older versions.\",\n    \"ch\": \"此軟體與舊版本不兼容。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They are a compatible couple.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們是一對很合適的伴侶。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Ensure the devices are compatible before connecting them.\",\n    \"ch\": \"連接設備前，請確保它們是兼容的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Their personalities were highly compatible.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們的性情非常協調。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們的性情非常協調。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3076,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::critical::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His ____ review of the book was widely read.","expectedAnswer":"critical","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His ____ review of the book was widely read.","clozeAnswer":"critical","exampleTranslation":"他對這本書的評價性評論被廣泛閱讀。","reference":{"eng":"critical","kk":"/ˈkrɪtɪkl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['批判性的；挑剔的'], ['關鍵性的；重要的'], ['（情況）危急的；嚴重的'], ['（意見、評論）批評性的；評價性的']]","chEntries":["批判性的","挑剔的","關鍵性的","重要的","危急的","嚴重的","批評性的","評價性的"],"practiceMeaning":"他對這本書的評價性評論被廣泛閱讀。","analysis":"源自希臘語 'kritikos' (able to judge)，是 'critic' 的形容詞形式。核心意義是「與判斷或評價相關」。\n1. 批判性的；挑剔的：指對事物進行仔細檢查，並指出其缺點或錯誤的態度。\n2. 關鍵性的；重要的：指對某事物的發展或成功至關重要的。\n3. （情況）危急的；嚴重的：指處於非常重要或危險的關頭，需要緊急處理。\n4. （意見、評論）批評性的；評價性的：指旨在分析和評價某事物優缺點的。","definition":"1. involving careful judgment or discriminating analysis; 2. extremely important or necessary; 3. involving the danger of failure or disaster; 4. expressing adverse or disapproving comments or judgments.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a critical attitude towards any new proposal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對任何新提案都持批判態度。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a critical moment in the negotiations.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是談判中的關鍵時刻。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The patient is in critical condition.\",\n    \"ch\": \"病人的情況危急。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His critical review of the book was widely read.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對這本書的評價性評論被廣泛閱讀。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他對這本書的評價性評論被廣泛閱讀。","sourceName":"字彙王、龍騰課本","unitName":"U39、L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6164,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::deliberate::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The plan was a ____ attempt to mislead the public.","expectedAnswer":"deliberate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The plan was a ____ attempt to mislead the public.","clozeAnswer":"deliberate","exampleTranslation":"這個計畫是為了誤導公眾而蓄意為之的。","reference":{"eng":"deliberate","kk":"dɪˈlɪbərət","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"故意的\"  ],  [    \"蓄意的\"  ],  [    \"審慎的\"  ],  [    \"計畫好的\"  ]]","chEntries":["故意的","蓄意的","審慎的","計畫好的"],"practiceMeaning":"這個計畫是為了誤導公眾而蓄意為之的。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 dēlīberātus，是 dēlīberāre「仔細考慮、權衡」的過去分詞。dēlīberāre 由 de- (down, completely) + lībra (balance, scale) 組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 de-「完全」和 lībra「秤」是其核心語意來源。作為形容詞，其核心語義是「經過仔細考慮而做出的」。詞源中的「權衡」概念引申出「蓄意的、計畫好的、非偶然的」。","definition":"1. done consciously and intentionally; 2. characterized by careful thought and consideration; 3. slow and careful.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The decision was the result of a deliberate choice.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個決定是經過深思熟慮的選擇的結果。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His remarks were deliberately offensive.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的言論是蓄意冒犯的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She took a deliberate step forward.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她謹慎地向前邁出一步。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The plan was a deliberate attempt to mislead the public.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個計畫是為了誤導公眾而蓄意為之的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個計畫是為了誤導公眾而蓄意為之的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5836,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::diminish::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The size of the company will ____ after the merger.","expectedAnswer":"diminish","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The size of the company will ____ after the merger.","clozeAnswer":"diminish","exampleTranslation":"合併後公司的規模將會縮小。","reference":{"eng":"diminish","kk":"dɪˈmɪnɪʃ","tense":"v.","ch":"[  [    \"減少\"  ],  [    \"減弱\"  ],  [    \"降低\"  ],  [    \"縮小\"  ]]","chEntries":["減少","減弱","降低","縮小"],"practiceMeaning":"合併後公司的規模將會縮小。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'diminuere'，由 'di-' (apart, away) 和 'minuere' (to lessen) 構成。'Minuere' 來自 'minus' (less)。'Diminuere' 的字面意思是「使減少」、「使變小」。'-ish' 是常見的動詞字尾，將名詞或形容詞轉化為動詞，表示「使……」或「變得……」。因此，'diminish' 的核心語意是「使之變少、變弱或變小」。它可以指數量、強度、重要性、價值等方面的減少或減弱。例如，也可指「縮小」尺寸或範圍。","definition":"1. To make or become smaller, weaker, or less.; 2. To lessen the authority, dignity, or reputation of.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The threat of war did not diminish.\",\n    \"ch\": \"戰爭的威脅並未減弱。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His responsibilities will diminish as he gets older.\",\n    \"ch\": \"隨著年齡增長，他的責任將會減少。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The drug is used to diminish pain.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種藥物用於減輕疼痛。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The size of the company will diminish after the merger.\",\n    \"ch\": \"合併後公司的規模將會縮小。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"合併後公司的規模將會縮小。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5837,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::evolution::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of technology has been rapid.","expectedAnswer":"evolution","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of technology has been rapid.","clozeAnswer":"evolution","exampleTranslation":"科技的發展是迅速的。","reference":{"eng":"evolution","kk":"ˌɛvəˈluːʃn","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"演化\"  ],  [    \"進化\"  ],  [    \"發展\"  ],  [    \"演變\"  ]]","chEntries":["演化","進化","發展","演變"],"practiceMeaning":"科技的發展是迅速的。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'evolutio'，由 'evolvere' (to unfold, to unroll) 構成。'Evolvere' 由 'e-' (out) 和 'volvere' (to roll) 組成。'Evolutio' 的字面意思是「展開」、「展開的過程」。最初用於指「翻書」或「展開捲軸」。後來，其語意引申至生物學，指生物體經過漫長時期，通過自然選擇等機制，發生遺傳變異並適應環境的過程，即「演化」或「進化」。也可用於形容社會、思想、技術等方面的漸進式「發展」或「演變」。","definition":"1. The process by which different kinds of living organism are believed to have developed from earlier forms during the history of the earth.; 2. The gradual development of something, especially from a simple to a more complex form.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Darwin's theory of evolution revolutionized biology.\",\n    \"ch\": \"達爾文的演化論使生物學產生了革命性的變化。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The evolution of language is a fascinating subject.\",\n    \"ch\": \"語言的演變是一個引人入勝的主題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company has undergone significant evolution in recent years.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司近年來經歷了顯著的發展。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The evolution of technology has been rapid.\",\n    \"ch\": \"科技的發展是迅速的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"科技的發展是迅速的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4120,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::honor::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The bank will ____ the check.","expectedAnswer":"honor","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The bank will ____ the check.","clozeAnswer":"honor","exampleTranslation":"銀行將兌現這張支票。","reference":{"eng":"honor","kk":"/ˈɑːnər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['榮譽', '光榮'], ['尊敬', '敬意'], ['（尤指女性的）貞節', '名節'], ['（債務的）償還', '履約']]","chEntries":["榮譽","光榮","尊敬","敬意","貞節","名節","償還","履約"],"practiceMeaning":"銀行將兌現這張支票。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 honor（尊敬、名譽）。核心概念是「價值」、「尊嚴」或「受到的高度評價」。引申為社會認可的榮譽、對個人的尊敬、個人品德的貞潔，以及對承諾的履行。","definition":"1. high respect; esteem; 2. privilege; 3. a thing conferred as a mark of respect; an award; 4. good reputation and integrity; 5. the fulfillment of an obligation","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Winning the award brought him great honor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"贏得這個獎項給他帶來了極大的榮譽。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has been honored for her contributions to science.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她因對科學的貢獻而受到表彰。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He always keeps his honor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他始終信守承諾。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The bank will honor the check.\",\n    \"ch\": \"銀行將兌現這張支票。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"銀行將兌現這張支票。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6174,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::illusion::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company's success was an ____; they were close to bankruptcy.","expectedAnswer":"illusion","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company's success was an ____; they were close to bankruptcy.","clozeAnswer":"illusion","exampleTranslation":"公司的成功是假象；他們離破產不遠了。","reference":{"eng":"illusion","kk":"ɪˈluːʒən","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"幻覺\"  ],  [    \"錯覺\"  ],  [    \"幻想\"  ],  [    \"海市蜃樓\"  ]]","chEntries":["幻覺","錯覺","幻想","海市蜃樓"],"practiceMeaning":"公司的成功是假象；他們離破產不遠了。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 illūsiōnem，是動詞 illudere「欺騙、嘲弄」的名詞化。illudere 由 in- (in, into) + lūdere (to play, mock) 組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 in-「進入」和 lūdere「玩弄、嘲弄」是其核心語意來源。作為名詞，其核心語義是「一種由感官誤解或心理作用產生的虛假感知」，即「幻覺」或「錯覺」。詞源中的「玩弄、嘲弄」引申為「欺騙」，進而產生「虛假的感知」。","definition":"1. a false idea or belief; 2. the state of being deceived; 3. a thing that is or is likely to become or prove false; 4. a deceptive appearance or impression.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The magician created the illusion that he had disappeared.\",\n    \"ch\": \"魔術師製造了他消失的幻覺。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He lives under the illusion that he is rich.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他活在自己是富翁的幻想中。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Mirages are optical illusions.\",\n    \"ch\": \"海市蜃樓是光學錯覺。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company's success was an illusion; they were close to bankruptcy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司的成功是假象；他們離破產不遠了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"公司的成功是假象；他們離破產不遠了。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5840,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::immune::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Diplomats are often ____ from local laws.","expectedAnswer":"immune","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Diplomats are often ____ from local laws.","clozeAnswer":"immune","exampleTranslation":"外交官員通常豁免於當地法律。","reference":{"eng":"immune","kk":"ɪˈmjuːn","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"免疫的\"  ],  [    \"不受影響的\"  ],  [    \"免於……的\"  ],  [    \"豁免的\"  ]]","chEntries":["免疫的","不受影響的","免於……的","豁免的"],"practiceMeaning":"外交官員通常豁免於當地法律。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'immūnis'，由 'in-' (not) 和 'mūnus' (duty, service, gift) 構成。'Immūnis' 的字面意思是「不受……負擔的」或「免除……義務的」。最初用於指免稅或免於公共服務的人。在醫學上，'immune' 指身體對某種疾病或病原體產生抵抗力，不再容易受到感染。這也與「不受……侵害」的核心意義相符。引申義則指「不受……影響」或「免於……」。例如，也可指「免除……責任的」。","definition":"1. Protected against a particular disease.; 2. Not affected or influenced by something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Children are often immune to common colds after exposure.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子們在接觸後通常對普通感冒產生免疫。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He seems immune to criticism.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他似乎不受批評的影響。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company is immune from prosecution.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司免於起訴。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Diplomats are often immune from local laws.\",\n    \"ch\": \"外交官員通常豁免於當地法律。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"外交官員通常豁免於當地法律。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3302,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::makeup::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ artist worked quickly before the performance.","expectedAnswer":"makeup","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ artist worked quickly before the performance.","clozeAnswer":"makeup","exampleTranslation":"化妝師在表演前快速地工作。","reference":{"eng":"makeup","kk":"/ˈmeɪkʌp/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['化妝品'], ['化妝；妝容'], ['組成；構成'], ['（事物的）性質；總體情況'], ['（尤指戲劇、電影中的）化妝，道具']]","chEntries":["化妝品","化妝","妝容","組成","構成","性質","總體情況","化妝，道具"],"practiceMeaning":"化妝師在表演前快速地工作。","analysis":"由 'make' (做) + 'up' (組成) 組成。名詞形式有多種意義：指用於修飾容貌的化妝品；化妝這個動作或結果；事物的組成或性質；以及戲劇中的特殊化妝。這些意義都源於「組成」、「構成」的核心概念。","definition":"1. substances such as lipstick, powder, and mascara that are used to make a person's face look more attractive; 2. the act or process of applying cosmetics; 3. the way in which something is put together or arranged; 4. the nature or character of something; 5. the art of applying cosmetics to an actor's face or body.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She buys a lot of makeup.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她買了很多化妝品。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The makeup of the committee was diverse.\",\n    \"ch\": \"委員會的組成很多元化。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her natural makeup looked very elegant.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的自然妝容看起來非常優雅。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The makeup artist worked quickly before the performance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"化妝師在表演前快速地工作。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"化妝師在表演前快速地工作。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5844,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::masterpiece::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The symphony was hailed as a ____.","expectedAnswer":"masterpiece","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The symphony was hailed as a ____.","clozeAnswer":"masterpiece","exampleTranslation":"這首交響樂被譽為傑作。","reference":{"eng":"masterpiece","kk":"ˈmæstərpiːs","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"傑作\"  ],  [    \"名作\"  ],  [    \"曠世之作\"  ],  [    \"代表作\"  ]]","chEntries":["傑作","名作","曠世之作","代表作"],"practiceMeaning":"這首交響樂被譽為傑作。","analysis":"此字為複合詞，由 'master' (大師) 和 'piece' (作品) 組成。'Master' 源自古英語 'mægester'，來自拉丁語 'magister' (chief, leader, teacher)。'Piece' 源自古法語 'piece'，意為「部分」、「塊」。'Masterpiece' 的字面意思是「大師的作品」，指由一位技藝高超的藝術家或工匠創作的、具有極高藝術價值和技巧的傑出作品。它強調的是作者的「大師級」技藝和作品本身的「非凡」水準。","definition":"1. A work of outstanding artistry, skill, or workmanship.; 2. A person's best piece of work.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The Mona Lisa is a masterpiece by Leonardo da Vinci.\",\n    \"ch\": \"《蒙娜麗莎》是達文西的傑作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This novel is considered his masterpiece.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本小說被認為是他的代表作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The architect's design was a true masterpiece.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位建築師的設計是真正的傑作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The symphony was hailed as a masterpiece.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這首交響樂被譽為傑作。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這首交響樂被譽為傑作。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5845,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::obscure::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The entrance to the cave was ____.","expectedAnswer":"obscure","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The entrance to the cave was ____.","clozeAnswer":"obscure","exampleTranslation":"洞穴的入口隱蔽難尋。","reference":{"eng":"obscure","kk":"əbˈskjʊər","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"晦澀的\"  ],  [    \"模糊的\"  ],  [    \"不起眼的\"  ],  [    \"鮮為人知的\"  ]]","chEntries":["晦澀的","模糊的","不起眼的","鮮為人知的"],"practiceMeaning":"洞穴的入口隱蔽難尋。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'obscurus'，由 'ob-' (over, before) 和 'scurus' (related to 'ceterus' meaning 'other', so implying 'covered') 構成。'Obscurus' 的字面意思是「被覆蓋的」、「隱藏的」。因此，'obscure' 在形容事物時，表示「不清晰的」、「難以理解的」、「不為人知的」或「不顯眼的」。它描述的是缺乏明顯性、缺乏清晰度或缺乏知名度的狀態。例如，也可指「不易辨認的」。","definition":"1. Not discovered or known about; uncertain.; 2. Not clearly expressed or easily understood.; 3. Not important or famous.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The meaning of the poem is obscure.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這首詩的意義很晦澀。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was an obscure poet until his work was rediscovered.\",\n    \"ch\": \"在作品被重新發現之前，他是一位默默無聞的詩人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The small village remained obscure for centuries.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個小村莊幾個世紀以來一直默默無聞。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The entrance to the cave was obscure.\",\n    \"ch\": \"洞穴的入口隱蔽難尋。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"洞穴的入口隱蔽難尋。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5850,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::partly::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She was ____ to blame for the misunderstanding.","expectedAnswer":"partly","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She was ____ to blame for the misunderstanding.","clozeAnswer":"partly","exampleTranslation":"誤會的產生她也有一定程度的責任。","reference":{"eng":"partly","kk":"ˈpɑːrtli","tense":"adv.","ch":"[  [    \"部分地\"  ],  [    \"在某種程度上\"  ],  [    \"多少\"  ]]","chEntries":["部分地","在某種程度上","多少"],"practiceMeaning":"誤會的產生她也有一定程度的責任。","analysis":"此字由 'part' (部分) 加上副詞字尾 '-ly' 構成。'Part' 源自拉丁語 'partire' (to divide)。'-ly' 是常見的副詞字尾，將名詞或形容詞轉化為副詞。'Partly' 的核心語意是「不是完全地」、「在一定程度上」，表示某事物僅部分實現或僅部分為真。例如，也可指「有一定程度地」。","definition":"1. To some extent; in part.; 2. Not completely.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The success was partly due to luck.\",\n    \"ch\": \"成功的部分原因在於運氣。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was partly responsible for the accident.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對事故負有部分責任。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The room was partly furnished.\",\n    \"ch\": \"房間只部分佈置了家具。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She was partly to blame for the misunderstanding.\",\n    \"ch\": \"誤會的產生她也有一定程度的責任。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"誤會的產生她也有一定程度的責任。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5851,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::passionate::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He was ____ in his defense of the proposal.","expectedAnswer":"passionate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He was ____ in his defense of the proposal.","clozeAnswer":"passionate","exampleTranslation":"他充滿激情地為該提議辯護。","reference":{"eng":"passionate","kk":"ˈpæʃənət","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"熱情的\"  ],  [    \"激情的\"  ],  [    \"熱烈的\"  ],  [    \"充滿愛意的\"  ]]","chEntries":["熱情的","激情的","熱烈的","充滿愛意的"],"practiceMeaning":"他充滿激情地為該提議辯護。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'passio' (suffering, feeling, passion)，由 'pati' (to suffer, endure) 構成。'Passionate' 的核心語意是「充滿強烈情感」，尤其是「熱情」、「激情」或「愛」。它描述的是一種被強烈情感驅動的狀態，無論是正面（如熱愛、激勵）或負面（如憤怒、痛苦）。在現代用法中，通常指對某事物有強烈的興趣、熱情和投入。例如，也可指「充滿愛意的」，用於形容關係。","definition":"1. Showing or caused by strong feelings or a strong belief.; 2. Having or showing strong sexual desire.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is passionate about environmental protection.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對環境保護充滿熱情。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His passionate speech moved the audience.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他充滿激情的演講感動了聽眾。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They have a passionate relationship.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們有一段熱烈的感情。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was passionate in his defense of the proposal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他充滿激情地為該提議辯護。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他充滿激情地為該提議辯護。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6189,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::shiver::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"A cold ____ ran down his spine.","expectedAnswer":"shiver","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"A cold ____ ran down his spine.","clozeAnswer":"shiver","exampleTranslation":"一陣寒意沿著他的脊椎爬過。","reference":{"eng":"shiver","kk":"ˈʃɪvər","tense":"v.","ch":"[  [    \"發抖\"  ],  [    \"顫抖\"  ]]","chEntries":["發抖","顫抖"],"practiceMeaning":"一陣寒意沿著他的脊椎爬過。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 shiveren，可能是擬聲詞，模仿寒冷或恐懼時的顫抖聲。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，應視為整體詞源演變。作為動詞，其核心語義是「由於寒冷、恐懼或興奮而身體不由自主地顫抖」。此生理反應的語義是其主要構成要素。","definition":"1. tremble, typically as a result of fear, excitement, or cold.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He shivered in the cold wind.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在寒風中發抖。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She shivered with fear when she heard the noise.\",\n    \"ch\": \"聽到噪音時，她因為害怕而顫抖。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The music made her shiver with delight.\",\n    \"ch\": \"音樂讓她高興得渾身顫抖。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A cold shiver ran down his spine.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一陣寒意沿著他的脊椎爬過。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"一陣寒意沿著他的脊椎爬過。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6198,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::siege::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The castle endured a long ____.","expectedAnswer":"siege","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The castle endured a long ____.","clozeAnswer":"siege","exampleTranslation":"這座城堡經受了漫長的圍攻。","reference":{"eng":"siege","kk":"siːdʒ","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"圍攻\"  ],  [    \"包圍\"  ],  [    \"圍困\"  ]]","chEntries":["圍攻","包圍","圍困"],"practiceMeaning":"這座城堡經受了漫長的圍攻。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 siege，意為「座位、場所、圍攻」，最終源自拉丁語 sedes「座位」，與 sedēre「坐」相關。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 sedēre「坐」是其核心語意來源。作為名詞，其核心語義是「軍隊包圍並試圖佔領一個設防城鎮或據點的軍事行動」。詞源中的「座位」引申為「佔據」，進而發展為「圍攻」的意義。","definition":"1. a military blockade of a city or fortress with the intention of capturing it by assault or starvation; 2. a prolonged period of difficulty or hardship.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The city was under siege for months.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座城市被圍攻了數月。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The siege ended with the enemy's surrender.\",\n    \"ch\": \"圍攻在敵軍投降後結束。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The prolonged siege tested the defenders' resolve.\",\n    \"ch\": \"漫長的圍困考驗了守軍的決心。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The castle endured a long siege.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座城堡經受了漫長的圍攻。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這座城堡經受了漫長的圍攻。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4128,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::solid::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The team's performance was ____ throughout the season.","expectedAnswer":"solid","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The team's performance was ____ throughout the season.","clozeAnswer":"solid","exampleTranslation":"整個賽季球隊的表現都很穩定。","reference":{"eng":"solid","kk":"/ˈsɒlɪd/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['固體的'], ['結實的', '穩固的'], ['可靠的', '實在的'], ['一致的', '無異議的']]","chEntries":["固體的","結實的","穩固的","可靠的","實在的","一致的","無異議的"],"practiceMeaning":"整個賽季球隊的表現都很穩定。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 solidus（堅實的，完整的）。核心概念是「穩定」、「不流動」、「堅固」。引申為物理狀態（固體），結構的穩固，證據的確鑿，或意見的一致性。","definition":"1. firmly packed or condensed; 2. (of a substance) having a definite shape and volume; 3. strong and reliable; 4. showing firm agreement or support","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Ice is the solid form of water.\",\n    \"ch\": \"冰是水的固體形態。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The building is made of solid stone.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座建築是用實心石頭建造的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We have solid evidence to prove his guilt.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們有確鑿的證據證明他的罪行。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The team's performance was solid throughout the season.\",\n    \"ch\": \"整個賽季球隊的表現都很穩定。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"整個賽季球隊的表現都很穩定。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3927,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::strength::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of the argument was undeniable.","expectedAnswer":"strength","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of the argument was undeniable.","clozeAnswer":"strength","exampleTranslation":"這個論點的說服力是無可否認的。","reference":{"eng":"strength","kk":"/streŋkθ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['力量', '力氣'], ['強度'], ['優勢'], ['效力']]","chEntries":["力量","力氣","強度","優勢","效力"],"practiceMeaning":"這個論點的說服力是無可否認的。","analysis":"源自古英語 'strengþu'，由 'streng' (意為「強壯的」) 和 '-þu' (名詞後綴，表示「狀態」) 組成。指物理上的力量、堅固的程度、精神上的毅力、能力或優勢。","definition":"1. the quality or state of being physically strong; 2. the capacity to withstand great force or pressure; 3. the degree to which something is powerful or effective; 4. an advantage or good quality.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has great physical strength.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他擁有強大的體力。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The strength of the fabric is impressive.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這塊布料的強度令人印象深刻。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her biggest strength is her determination.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她最大的優勢是她的決心。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The strength of the argument was undeniable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個論點的說服力是無可否認的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個論點的說服力是無可否認的。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5864,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::tackle::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ box contained various lures and hooks.","expectedAnswer":"tackle","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ box contained various lures and hooks.","clozeAnswer":"tackle","exampleTranslation":"漁具箱裡裝有各種釣餌和魚鉤。","reference":{"eng":"tackle","kk":"ˈtækl","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"處理\"  ],  [    \"阻截\"  ],  [    \"裝備\"  ],  [    \"漁具\"  ],  [    \"工具\"  ]]","chEntries":["處理","阻截","裝備","漁具","工具"],"practiceMeaning":"漁具箱裡裝有各種釣餌和魚鉤。","analysis":"此名詞形式與動詞形式同源。當指「處理」或「阻截」時，是從動詞派生而來，表示「處理」或「阻截」的行為。在體育語境中，指「阻截」的動作。另一常見義是指「設備」或「工具」，特別是「釣魚用具」或「運動裝備」。此義的來源可能與「抓住」的原始概念有關，因為這些工具都是用來「抓住」或「操控」對象的。例如，也可指「釣魚的工具」。","definition":"1. The action of tackling in sports.; 2. Equipment used for a particular sport or activity, especially fishing.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The tackle was successful.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那次阻截很成功。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He bought new fishing tackle.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他買了新的釣魚裝備。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The football player made a great tackle.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那位足球運動員做出了一個精彩的阻截。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The tackle box contained various lures and hooks.\",\n    \"ch\": \"漁具箱裡裝有各種釣餌和魚鉤。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"漁具箱裡裝有各種釣餌和魚鉤。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4504,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::take::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Do you ____ sugar in your coffee?","expectedAnswer":"take","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Do you ____ sugar in your coffee?","clozeAnswer":"take","exampleTranslation":"你的咖啡加糖嗎？","reference":{"eng":"take","kk":"/teɪk/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['拿'], ['取得'], ['接受'], ['花費（時間、金錢）'], ['考慮'], ['採取（行動、措施）']]","chEntries":["拿","取得","接受","花費","考慮","採取"],"practiceMeaning":"你的咖啡加糖嗎？","analysis":"源自古英語 tacan，意為「抓住」、「獲得」。是一個非常核心且用途廣泛的動詞。其語意極其豐富，涵蓋了從具體的「獲取」、「攜帶」到抽象的「接受」、「考慮」、「採取」等。","definition":"1. To lay hold of (something) with one's hands; 2. To obtain possession of; 3. To accept or receive; 4. To spend or require (time or effort); 5. To consider or regard in a particular way; 6. To carry out or perform (an action or undertaking).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please take this book.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請拿這本書。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It will take an hour to finish.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這需要一個小時才能完成。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to take action immediately.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們必須立即採取行動。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Do you take sugar in your coffee?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你的咖啡加糖嗎？\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"你的咖啡加糖嗎？","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3888,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::tough::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The police were ____ on the criminals.","expectedAnswer":"tough","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The police were ____ on the criminals.","clozeAnswer":"tough","exampleTranslation":"警方對罪犯採取了嚴厲的措施。","reference":{"eng":"tough","kk":"/tʌf/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['困難的', '艱難的'], ['堅強的', '頑固的'], ['嚴厲的'], ['強韌的', '堅韌的']]","chEntries":["困難的","艱難的","堅強的","頑固的","嚴厲的","強韌的","堅韌的"],"practiceMeaning":"警方對罪犯採取了嚴厲的措施。","analysis":"源自古英語 'tōh'，意為「韌性的」。核心是「難以處理」或「不易被改變」。可指事情的難度、人的堅韌或頑固、物質的堅固或不易破損。","definition":"1. difficult to overcome or deal with. 2. strong and resilient; not easily broken or cut. 3. able to endure hardship or adversity. 4. severe or harsh.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was a tough decision to make.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個艱難的決定。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He's a tough negotiator.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一位強硬的談判者。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Leather is a tough material.\",\n    \"ch\": \"皮革是一種堅韌的材料。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police were tough on the criminals.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警方對罪犯採取了嚴厲的措施。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"警方對罪犯採取了嚴厲的措施。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U1、L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6202,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::upgrade::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ to the operating system was successful.","expectedAnswer":"upgrade","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ to the operating system was successful.","clozeAnswer":"upgrade","exampleTranslation":"操作系統的升級是成功的。","reference":{"eng":"upgrade","kk":"ˈʌpɡreɪd","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"升級\"  ],  [    \"提升\"  ]]","chEntries":["升級","提升"],"practiceMeaning":"操作系統的升級是成功的。","analysis":"此字由 up (上) + grade (等級、品質) 構成。此字在現代英語中可視為由 up 和 grade 組合的複合詞。up 表示方向上的「向上」，grade 表示「等級、品質」。作為名詞，其核心語義是由動詞 upgrade「升級」名詞化而來，指「將某物提升到更高等級、標準或性能的行為或結果」。詞源中的「向上」和「等級」概念清晰地體現了此義。","definition":"1. an act of raising something to a higher standard, quality, or level; 2. an improved version of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The recent upgrade of the network improved its speed.\",\n    \"ch\": \"最近的網路升級提高了它的速度。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They are offering a free upgrade to premium.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們提供免費升級到高級版。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The hotel provided a complimentary room upgrade.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家旅館提供了免費的房間升級。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The upgrade to the operating system was successful.\",\n    \"ch\": \"操作系統的升級是成功的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"操作系統的升級是成功的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6204,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::variable::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Her mood was ____ throughout the day.","expectedAnswer":"variable","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Her mood was ____ throughout the day.","clozeAnswer":"variable","exampleTranslation":"她一天之間情緒多變。","reference":{"eng":"variable","kk":"ˈveriəbl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"變化的\"  ],  [    \"易變的\"  ],  [    \"可變的\"  ],  [    \"不定的\"  ]]","chEntries":["變化的","易變的","可變的","不定的"],"practiceMeaning":"她一天之間情緒多變。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 variabilis，是動詞 variare「改變」的衍生形容詞。variare 源自 varus「彎曲的、扭曲的」，可能與 varia（斑駁）有關。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 variare「改變」是其核心語意來源。作為形容詞，其核心語義是「能夠或傾向於改變；不穩定的」。詞源中的「改變」概念直接體現了此義。","definition":"1. not always the same; liable to change; 2. able to be changed or adapted.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The weather in this region is very variable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個地區的天氣變化很大。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has a variable temper.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的脾氣很不穩定。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The amount of interest is variable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"利率是可變的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her mood was variable throughout the day.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她一天之間情緒多變。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她一天之間情緒多變。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6251,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::vein::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His writing has a sarcastic ____.","expectedAnswer":"vein","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His writing has a sarcastic ____.","clozeAnswer":"vein","exampleTranslation":"他的寫作帶有一種諷刺的風格。","reference":{"eng":"vein","kk":"veɪn","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"靜脈\"  ],  [    \"血管\"  ],  [    \"礦脈\"  ],  [    \"紋路\"  ],  [    \"風格\"  ]]","chEntries":["靜脈","血管","礦脈","紋路","風格"],"practiceMeaning":"他的寫作帶有一種諷刺的風格。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 fēn，向上可追溯至拉丁語 vena，意為「血管，水道」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。名詞義指將血液從身體各部位輸送到心臟的血管，也引申指礦藏所在的「礦脈」，物體表面的「紋路」，或人或事物中某種「風格」或「特質」。中文翻譯為「靜脈；血管；礦脈；紋路；風格」。","definition":"1. one of the tubes that carry blood from the body to the heart; 2. a line of mineral ore within a rock; 3. a pattern of lines in something, such as a leaf or a piece of wood; 4. a particular style or manner.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The nurse drew blood from a vein in his arm.\",\n    \"ch\": \"護士從他手臂的一條靜脈抽了血。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Geologists searched for a vein of gold.\",\n    \"ch\": \"地質學家們在尋找金礦脈。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The marble had a beautiful vein pattern.\",\n    \"ch\": \"大理石有著美麗的紋路。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His writing has a sarcastic vein.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的寫作帶有一種諷刺的風格。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他的寫作帶有一種諷刺的風格。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4520,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::with::prep","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He is a man ____ great courage.","expectedAnswer":"with","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He is a man ____ great courage.","clozeAnswer":"with","exampleTranslation":"他是一個有巨大勇氣的人。","reference":{"eng":"with","kk":"/wɪð/","tense":"prep.","ch":"[['和...一起'], ['帶著'], ['使用'], ['關於']]","chEntries":["和...一起","帶著","使用","關於"],"practiceMeaning":"他是一個有巨大勇氣的人。","analysis":"源自古英語 wið。是一個表示陪伴、工具、原因、方式等的多功能介詞。核心語意是「一起」、「伴隨」。","definition":"1. Accompanied by (another person or people); 2. Indicating the instrument or agent used to perform an action; 3. In the company of or in addition to; 4. Having or possessing (a particular quality or characteristic).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is talking with her friend.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她正在和她的朋友說話。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He cut the cake with a knife.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他用刀切蛋糕。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a problem with the software.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是軟體的一個問題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a man with great courage.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一個有巨大勇氣的人。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他是一個有巨大勇氣的人。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4649,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::a-beam-of-light::idiom","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ shone through the window.","expectedAnswer":"A beam of light","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ shone through the window.","clozeAnswer":"A beam of light","exampleTranslation":"一道光線透過窗戶照進來。","reference":{"eng":"a beam of light","kk":"/ə biːm əv laɪt/","tense":"idiom","ch":"[['一道光'], ['光束']]","chEntries":["一道光","光束"],"practiceMeaning":"一道光線透過窗戶照進來。","analysis":"此為固定片語。'Beam' (光束、樑) 指從光源發出的直線光束。'Light' (光) 是基礎。與 'ray of sun' 類似，但 'beam' 有時暗示比 'ray' 更強或更集中的光線。","definition":"a ray of light.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A beam of light shone through the window.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一道光線透過窗戶照進來。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The lighthouse sent out a powerful beam of light.\",\n    \"ch\": \"燈塔發出強烈的光束。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"一道光線透過窗戶照進來。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4589,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::a-big-melting-pot::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"New York City is often described as ____ of cultures.","expectedAnswer":"a big melting pot","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"New York City is often described as ____ of cultures.","clozeAnswer":"a big melting pot","exampleTranslation":"紐約市常被形容為一個文化大熔爐。","reference":{"eng":"a big melting pot","kk":"/ə bɪɡ ˈmɛltɪŋ ˌpɒt/","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['一個大熔爐（指文化、民族等融合之地）']]","chEntries":["一個大熔爐"],"practiceMeaning":"紐約市常被形容為一個文化大熔爐。","analysis":"此片語由 'a big' (一個大的) 和 'melting pot' (熔爐) 組成。 'melting pot' 比喻一個地方，其中不同的文化、種族、思想等相互融合，形成新的整體。這個概念常用來形容像美國這樣移民眾多的國家，各種文化在此匯聚並相互影響。","definition":"1. a place or situation in which people or cultures of different kinds come together and are mixed.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"New York City is often described as a big melting pot of cultures.\",\n    \"ch\": \"紐約市常被形容為一個文化大熔爐。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The classroom was a melting pot of students from various countries.\",\n    \"ch\": \"教室裡來自不同國家的學生匯聚在一起，形成一個小小的熔爐。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"紐約市常被形容為一個文化大熔爐。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4031,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u3::a-charity-fund::n-phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They donated to ____ for disaster relief.","expectedAnswer":"a charity fund","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They donated to ____ for disaster relief.","clozeAnswer":"a charity fund","exampleTranslation":"他們捐款給了一個用於救災的慈善基金。","reference":{"eng":"a charity fund","kk":"/ə ˈtʃærəti fʌnd/","tense":"n. phrase","ch":"[['慈善基金']]","chEntries":["慈善基金"],"practiceMeaning":"他們捐款給了一個用於救災的慈善基金。","analysis":"結合冠詞 'a', 名詞 'charity' (慈善) 和 'fund' (基金)。指為慈善目的而設立或募集的資金。","definition":"a sum of money collected or available for a charitable purpose.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They