":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She is studying ____ at university.","expectedAnswer":"accounting","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She is studying ____ at university.","clozeAnswer":"accounting","exampleTranslation":"她正在大學學習會計學。","reference":{"eng":"accounting","kk":"əˈkaʊntɪŋ","tense":"n.","ch":"[['會計學'], ['會計工作', '帳務處理']]","chEntries":["會計學","會計工作","帳務處理"],"practiceMeaning":"她正在大學學習會計學。","analysis":"此字由動詞 'account' 加上名詞化後綴 '-ing' 構成。'account' 本身源自古法語 'aconter'（計算、敘述），由 'a-'（to）和 'conte'（計算，來自拉丁語 'computare'）組成。'accounting' 作為名詞，指代記錄、分類、匯總和解釋財務交易的系統或實踐。其核心語意是「計算」和「報告」，引申為「會計學」或「會計工作」。","definition":"the systematic recording, reporting, and analysis of the financial transactions of a business or organization; the profession or work of an accountant.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is studying accounting at university.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她正在大學學習會計學。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company hired a new accountant to handle their accounting.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司僱用了一位新會計師來處理他們的帳務。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她正在大學學習會計學。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U63"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5684,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l9::accusation::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ was never proven.","expectedAnswer":"accusation","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ was never proven.","clozeAnswer":"accusation","exampleTranslation":"這項指控從未被證實。","reference":{"eng":"accusation","kk":"ˌækjuˈzeɪʃn","tense":"n.","ch":"[['指控'], ['控告'], ['指責']]","chEntries":["指控","控告","指責"],"practiceMeaning":"這項指控從未被證實。","analysis":"此字由動詞 'accuse' 加上名詞化後綴 '-ation' 構成。'accuse' 源自古法語 acuser（來自拉丁語 causari，意為『爭論，引起訴訟』）。'-ation' 後綴用於將動詞轉化為名詞，表示動作、過程、狀態或結果。因此，'accusation' 指的就是「被指控的動作或陳述」，即「指控、控告」。核心語意是「提出某人有罪或有過失的言論」。","definition":"a charge or claim that someone has done something illegal or wrong; the act of accusing someone.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The accusation was never proven.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這項指控從未被證實。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He faced a serious accusation of fraud.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他面臨嚴重的欺詐指控。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這項指控從未被證實。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3920,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::achieve::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She worked hard to ____ her goals.","expectedAnswer":"achieve","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She worked hard to ____ her goals.","clozeAnswer":"achieve","exampleTranslation":"她努力工作以實現她的目標。","reference":{"eng":"achieve","kk":"/əˈtʃiːv/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['達成', '實現'], ['獲得']]","chEntries":["達成","實現","獲得"],"practiceMeaning":"她努力工作以實現她的目標。","analysis":"源自古法語 'achever' (意為「完成、達到頂點」)，來自 'a-' (意為「到」) + 'chef' (意為「頭、頂」)。最初的意思是「達到頂峰」，引申為「完成、實現、達成目標」。","definition":"1. to succeed in doing or achieving something; 2. to obtain something, especially by effort.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She worked hard to achieve her goals.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她努力工作以實現她的目標。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The team achieved a remarkable victory.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這支隊伍取得了一場了不起的勝利。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He finally achieved fame in his field.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他終於在他的領域獲得了名聲。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她努力工作以實現她的目標。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5817,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::acknowledge::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He has to ____ his mistakes.","expectedAnswer":"acknowledge","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He has to ____ his mistakes.","clozeAnswer":"acknowledge","exampleTranslation":"他必須承認他的錯誤。","reference":{"eng":"acknowledge","kk":"əkˈnɑlɪdʒ","tense":"v.","ch":"[  [    \"承認\"  ],  [    \"認可\"  ],  [    \"告知\"  ],  [    \"表示收到\"  ]]","chEntries":["承認","認可","告知","表示收到"],"practiceMeaning":"他必須承認他的錯誤。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 acknown（知道）加上ledge（承認），結合了「知道」與「承認」兩層含義。acknowledge 的核心構詞可追溯至古英語 'cnāwan'（知道）和 'lecgan'（放置、使……），意指「確認某事物已知」。詞源上，'a-' 是加強前綴，'know' 來自原始日耳曼語 *kannaną (to know)，'ledge' 則來自古英語 'lecgan' (to lay down, to cause to lie down)，與'lay' 同源。在語言演變中，'a-' 前綴加強了動詞的語意，'ledge' 演變成與承認、確認相關的意義。最初的語義是「確認某事已知的狀態」，進而引申出「承認」或「認可」某事實、聲明或權威。此外，'acknowledge' 也可用來表示「告知」收件人已收到訊息，這源於確認訊息已「被知道」的概念。更進一步，也可指「表示對某人的存在或地位的認可」，例如在社交場合。","definition":"1. To accept or admit the existence or truth of; to recognize the fact or importance of.; 2. To express recognition or appreciation of.; 3. To inform (someone) of the receipt of (a letter, message, etc.).; 4. To recognize the existence, presence, or fact of.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has to acknowledge his mistakes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他必須承認他的錯誤。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We acknowledge receipt of your order.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們謹此告知已收到您的訂單。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She acknowledged his efforts with a smile.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她以微笑認可了他的努力。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The guard acknowledged the visitor with a nod.\",\n    \"ch\": \"守衛點頭表示認可訪客。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他必須承認他的錯誤。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5284,"wordRef":"字彙王::u63::acquaint::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"I need to ____ myself with the new procedures.","expectedAnswer":"acquaint","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"I need to ____ myself with the new procedures.","clozeAnswer":"acquaint","exampleTranslation":"我需要熟悉新的流程。","reference":{"eng":"acquaint","kk":"əˈkweɪnt","tense":"v.","ch":"[['使認識', '使熟悉', '告知']]","chEntries":["使認識","使熟悉","告知"],"practiceMeaning":"我需要熟悉新的流程。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 'acointier'，由 'a-'（to）和 'cointer'（使認識，可能來自中古拉丁語 'accognitare'，意為「變得熟悉」）。構詞上，'a-' 作為加強或使動前綴，'cointer' 為詞根。其原始語義為「使某人與某事或某人變得熟悉」。現代英語中的 'acquaint' 常與介詞 'with' 連用，表示「使熟悉某事物」或「告知某事」。","definition":"to make someone aware of or familiar with something; to introduce to someone.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I need to acquaint myself with the new procedures.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我需要熟悉新的流程。\"\n  },\n  {\n  