gs.","expectedAnswer":"barrier","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"A high ____ was built to prevent illegal crossings.","clozeAnswer":"barrier","exampleTranslation":"築起了一道高牆以阻止非法越境。","reference":{"eng":"barrier","kk":"ˈbæriər","tense":"n.","ch":"[['障礙物'], ['障礙'], ['隔閡'], ['界線']]","chEntries":["障礙物","障礙","隔閡","界線"],"practiceMeaning":"築起了一道高牆以阻止非法越境。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 barriere，意為「柵欄、籬笆、障礙」。其詞源可能與 bar (槓、條) 或 barrer (阻擋) 有關。核心語意是「任何阻止前進、阻礙或分隔的事物」。這可以是物理上的障礙物，也可以是抽象的隔閡（如語言障礙、心理障礙）。","definition":"1. a fence or other obstacle that prevents movement across or past something; 2. a circumstance that prevents an agreement or cooperation from being reached.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A high barrier was built to prevent illegal crossings.\",\n    \"ch\": \"築起了一道高牆以阻止非法越境。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Lack of communication can be a barrier to understanding.\",\n    \"ch\": \"缺乏溝通可能成為理解的障礙。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"築起了一道高牆以阻止非法越境。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5285,"wordRef":"字彙王::u63::batch::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"I baked a ____ of cookies.","expectedAnswer":"batch","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"I baked a ____ of cookies.","clozeAnswer":"batch","exampleTranslation":"我烤了一批餅乾。","reference":{"eng":"batch","kk":"bætʃ","tense":"n.","ch":"[['一批', '一組', '一組（東西）'], ['（烘焙的）一爐']]","chEntries":["一批","一組","一爐"],"practiceMeaning":"我烤了一批餅乾。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 'bache'，指「烤麵包的量」。其詞源不甚清晰，可能與古法語 'bata'（一捆）或 'batcher'（製造）有關。核心語意是「一群或一批一起處理的物品」。在現代英語中，'batch' 可以指生產過程中的一批產品（如烘焙食品、藥品、製造品），也可以指電腦處理中的一批數據，或任何具有共同特徵的一組事物。在烘焙業中，'batch' 特指一次烘烤的量。","definition":"a number of things, or a group of people or things, that are dealt with as a group; a quantity baked or cooked at one time.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I baked a batch of cookies.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我烤了一批餅乾。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The system processes data in batches.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該系統以批次方式處理數據。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我烤了一批餅乾。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U63"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4230,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::be-reasonable-about::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"You need to ____ the amount of time you spend playing games.","expectedAnswer":"be reasonable about","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"You need to ____ the amount of time you spend playing games.","clozeAnswer":"be reasonable about","exampleTranslation":"你需要在玩遊戲的時間上有所節制，講道理。","reference":{"eng":"be reasonable about","kk":"/ˈriːznəbl əˈbaʊt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['對…講道理；對…持通情達理的態度']]","chEntries":["對…講道理","對…持通情達理的態度"],"practiceMeaning":"你需要在玩遊戲的時間上有所節制，講道理。","analysis":"這是一個短語動詞，由形容詞 'reasonable'（合理的，情理之中的）和介詞 'about'（關於）構成。核心含義是“採取理性的、合乎情理的態度來對待某事或某人”。它強調在溝通或決策時，應基於事實、邏輯和公平。","definition":"To act or think in a sensible, fair, and logical way regarding a particular matter or person.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"You need to be reasonable about the amount of time you spend playing games.\",\n    \"ch\": \"你需要在玩遊戲的時間上有所節制，講道理。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The teacher asked the students to be reasonable about their complaints.\",\n    \"ch\": \"老師要求學生們對他們的抱怨要合乎情理。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"你需要在玩遊戲的時間上有所節制，講道理。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4307,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::be-sufficient-for::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This amount of money will ____ our trip.","expectedAnswer":"be sufficient for","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This amount of money will ____ our trip.","clozeAnswer":"be sufficient for","exampleTranslation":"這筆錢足夠我們這次旅行使用。","reference":{"eng":"be sufficient for","kk":"/bi səˈfɪʃənt fɔːr/","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['對...足夠']]","chEntries":["對...足夠"],"practiceMeaning":"這筆錢足夠我們這次旅行使用。","analysis":"結合了動詞 'be'（是）、形容詞 'sufficient'（足夠的）和介詞 'for'（為了）。'Be sufficient for' 指「某事物在數量、程度或能力上足夠滿足某個特定目