 'buster' (打破者)。原指巨型炸彈。現代用法指非常成功、票房極佳或引起廣泛關注的電影、書籍或表演，通常是大規模製作。","definition":"a film that is very popular and successful; a very large or successful product or enterprise.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The new superhero movie is expected to be a blockbuster.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這部新的超級英雄電影預計將成為一部轟動大片。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her latest novel became a literary blockbuster.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她最新的小說成了一部文學巨製。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這部新的超級英雄電影預計將成為一部轟動大片。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3997,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u3::bone::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The dog is happily gnawing on a ____.","expectedAnswer":"bone","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The dog is happily gnawing on a ____.","clozeAnswer":"bone","exampleTranslation":"這隻狗正高興地啃著骨頭。","reference":{"eng":"bone","kk":"/boʊn/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['（狗等）啃骨頭'], ['（人）仔細研究', '斟酌']]","chEntries":["啃骨頭","仔細研究","斟酌"],"practiceMeaning":"這隻狗正高興地啃著骨頭。","analysis":"詞源：同上。動詞形式，原指動物啃食骨頭，引申為人仔細地、深入地探究某事。","definition":"1. (of a dog or other animal) gnaw or chew on.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The dog is happily gnawing on a bone.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這隻狗正高興地啃著骨頭。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這隻狗正高興地啃著骨頭。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6210,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::bonus::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The employees received a Christmas ____.","expectedAnswer":"bonus","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The employees received a Christmas ____.","clozeAnswer":"bonus","exampleTranslation":"員工們收到了聖誕獎金。","reference":{"eng":"bonus","kk":"ˈboʊnəs","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"獎金\"  ],  [    \"紅利\"  ],  [    \"額外津貼\"  ],  [    \"好處\"  ]]","chEntries":["獎金","紅利","額外津貼","好處"],"practiceMeaning":"員工們收到了聖誕獎金。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 bonus，意為「好的」，在中古英語和現代英語中演變為「額外的給予，特別的好處」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作名詞時，指在基本工資或報酬之外額外給予的金錢、物品或好處，通常是因為表現良好、公司盈利或特殊節日。中文翻譯為「獎金；紅利；額外津貼；好處」。","definition":"1. an amount of money given to someone in addition to what is usual or expected, especially as a reward for good work; 2. something good that is extra and unexpected.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The employees received a Christmas bonus.\",\n    \"ch\": \"員工們收到了聖誕獎金。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company's excellent performance resulted in a generous bonus for all staff.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司優異的業績為所有員工帶來了豐厚的紅利。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Finding parking was a bonus on such a busy day.\",\n    \"ch\": \"在如此忙碌的一天找到停車位是一份額外的幸運。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"員工們收到了聖誕獎金。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5026,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::boom::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of the cannons echoed across the valley.","expectedAnswer":"boom","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of the cannons echoed across the valley.","clozeAnswer":"boom","exampleTranslation":"砲聲在山谷間迴盪。","reference":{"eng":"boom","kk":"buːm","tense":"n.","ch":"[['轟鳴聲'], ['繁榮（時期）'], ['低沉響亮的聲音']]","chEntries":["轟鳴聲","繁榮","低沉響亮的聲音"],"practiceMeaning":"砲聲在山谷間迴盪。","analysis":"此字可能源自擬聲詞，模仿低沉、響亮的聲音，如連續的槍聲、雷聲或鐘聲。其語意核心是「一種低沉、響亮且持續的聲音」。引申意義包括經濟或商業上的「繁榮、蓬勃發展」，此處的「繁榮」可理解為一種「強勁、廣泛」的影響，類似於聲音的擴散。OCR 掃描時可能將 'o' 誤判為 '0'，或單字切開、黏合。此處修正為 boom，具備廣泛的語意。","definition":"1. a deep, resonant sound; 2. a period of rapid economic growth or success; 3. a loud, deep, sustained sound.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The boom of the cannons echoed across the valley.\",\n    \"ch\": \"砲聲在山谷間迴盪。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The dot-com boom was a period of rapid growth in internet companies.\",\n    \"ch\": \"網路泡沫（科技公司）的繁榮時期是網際網路公司快速發展的階段。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"砲聲在山谷間迴盪。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5031,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::bound::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This decision is ____ to have serious consequences.","expectedAnswer":"bound","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This decision is ____ to have serious consequences.","clozeAnswer":"bound","exampleTranslation":"這個決定必然會產生嚴重後果。","reference":{"eng":"bound","kk":"baʊnd","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['必然會的'], ['註定的']]","chEntries":["必然會的","註定的"],"practiceMeaning":"這個決定必然會產生嚴重後果。","analysis":"此字來源於古英語 bunden（被捆綁的），與 bind 同源。在此意義下，bound 演變為「受（法律、道德、命運等）約束或限制」，進而引申為「必然會發生的」、「註定的」。其核心語意是「受到強烈約束或趨勢的引導」。","definition":"certain to happen; inevitable.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This decision is bound to have serious consequences.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個決定必然會產生嚴重後果。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is bound to win the championship this year.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他今年註定會贏得錦標賽。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個決定必然會產生嚴重後果。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5771,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::boundary::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The fence marks the ____ between our property and theirs.","expectedAnswer":"boundary","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The fence marks the ____ between our property and theirs.","clozeAnswer":"boundary","exampleTranslation":"籬笆標示了我們的地產與他們的之間的界線。","reference":{"eng":"boundary","kk":"ˈbaʊndəri","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"界限\"  ],  [    \"邊界\"  ],  [    \"範圍\"  ],  [    \"極限\"  ]]","chEntries":["界限","邊界","範圍","極限"],"practiceMeaning":"籬笆標示了我們的地產與他們的之間的界線。","analysis":"此字為名詞，由bind（綁；約束）+ -ary（名詞字尾，表示「地方；性質；或與……相關的事物」）構成。bind源自古英語bindan，意為「捆綁；約束」。-ary字尾源自拉丁語-arius，在中古英語中廣泛使用。因此，boundary的核心語義是「用來約束或區隔的界線」，可以是地理上的邊界，也可以是抽象的限制、範圍或個人界線。語意演變上，從具體的「綑綁或圍起來的線」發展到抽象的「限制或界定範圍」。","definition":"1. a real or imagined line that marks the edge or limit of something; 2. a limit of a subject or sphere of activity; 3. a limit beyond which something cannot or may not go.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The fence marks the boundary between our property and theirs.\",\n    \"ch\": \"籬笆標示了我們的地產與他們的之間的界線。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's important to establish personal boundaries in relationships.\",\n    \"ch\": \"在人際關係中建立個人界限是很重要的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The play explores the boundaries of human endurance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這齣戲探討了人類耐力的極限。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"籬笆標示了我們的地產與他們的之間的界線。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5772,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::boxer::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ trained rigorously for the upcoming championship.","expectedAnswer":"boxer","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ trained rigorously for the upcoming championship.","clozeAnswer":"boxer","exampleTranslation":"這位拳擊手為即將到來的錦標賽進行了嚴格的訓練。","reference":{"eng":"boxer","kk":"ˈbɑksər","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"拳擊手\"  ],  [    \"拳擊運動員\"  ]]","chEntries":["拳擊手","拳擊運動員"],"practiceMeaning":"這位拳擊手為即將到來的錦標賽進行了嚴格的訓練。","analysis":"此字為名詞，由box（拳擊；拳擊比賽）+ -er（名詞字尾，表示「從事某種活動的人」）構成。box作為拳擊比賽的用語，其詞源較為複雜，可能與古法語bouts「圍繞」或與拳頭擊打動作發音有關。-er字尾源自日耳曼語系（如古英語-ere），常用於指代執行某動作或從事某職業的人。因此，boxer的核心語義是指「從事拳擊運動的人」，即拳擊手。此字沒有其他常見的、由box轉品而來的詞義。","definition":"1. a person who fights professionally in the sport of boxing.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The boxer trained rigorously for the upcoming championship.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位拳擊手為即將到來的錦標賽進行了嚴格的訓練。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He became a professional boxer at a young age.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在年輕時成為了一名職業拳擊手。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這位拳擊手為即將到來的錦標賽進行了嚴格的訓練。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3068,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::breed::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This is a rare ____ of dog.","expectedAnswer":"breed","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This is a rare ____ of dog.","clozeAnswer":"breed","exampleTranslation":"這是稀有的犬種。","reference":{"eng":"breed","kk":"/briːd/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['品種；種類'], ['（人、動物的）家系；血統']]","chEntries":["品種","種類","家系","血統"],"practiceMeaning":"這是稀有的犬種。","analysis":"源自古英語 'brēdan' (to nourish, to bring up, to make multiply)。指由繁殖而產生的特定類型或家系。\n1. 品種；種類：指由於特定特徵而區分的動植物類別。\n2. （人、動物的）家系；血統：指同一家族或血緣關係的成員，或其遺傳特質。","definition":"1. a particular type of animal or plant, especially one that has been developed by people; 2. a type of person or thing.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a rare breed of dog.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是稀有的犬種。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He comes from a good breed.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他出身名門（好血統）。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是稀有的犬種。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5073,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::browse::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"I like to ____ the internet in my free time.","expectedAnswer":"browse","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"I like to ____ the internet in my free time.","clozeAnswer":"browse","exampleTranslation":"我喜歡在空閒時間瀏覽網路。","reference":{"eng":"browse","kk":"braʊz","tense":"v.","ch":"[['瀏覽'], ['隨意觀看'], ['吃草']]","chEntries":["瀏覽","隨意觀看","吃草"],"practiceMeaning":"我喜歡在空閒時間瀏覽網路。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 'brosnian'，意為 '腐爛、變質'，後演變為 '漫遊、損耗'，並在中古英語中發展出 '隨意觀看' 的意思。其早期語意帶有 '漫無目的的遊蕩'，這種漫遊感延伸至隨意瀏覽網頁、目錄或商店的商品，強調一種輕鬆、非目的性的搜尋過程。另外，'browse' 也指動物 '吃草'，這是因動物在草地上漫無目的地尋找食物，與人類的隨意瀏覽有相似的動態。","definition":"1. To look through or read in a casual or leisurely way.; 2. To eat grass or other vegetation; to feed on leaves or twigs.; 3. To scan or survey information or a website casually.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I like to browse the internet in my free time.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我喜歡在空閒時間瀏覽網路。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The deer were browsing in the meadow.\",\n    \"ch\": \"鹿正在草地上吃草。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She browsed through the racks of clothing.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她瀏覽了衣服的貨架。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我喜歡在空閒時間瀏覽網路。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5074,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::bruise::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He fell and got a nasty ____ on his leg.","expectedAnswer":"bruise","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He fell and got a nasty ____ on his leg.","clozeAnswer":"bruise","exampleTranslation":"他摔倒了，腿上留下了一塊嚴重的瘀傷。","reference":{"eng":"bruise","kk":"bruːz","tense":"n.","ch":"[['瘀傷'], ['擦傷']]","chEntries":["瘀傷","擦傷"],"practiceMeaning":"他摔倒了，腿上留下了一塊嚴重的瘀傷。","analysis":"此字源自古諾爾斯語 'brus'，意為 '腫塊、傷痕'，可能與 'brjosta' (to break) 有關。其核心語義是因撞擊或壓力造成的身體損傷，表現為皮膚下的出血或腫脹。此字不僅指物理上的傷害，也延伸至情感上的傷害，即 '心靈的創傷'。","definition":"1. An injury to a person or animal in which the skin is not broken but blood vessels beneath the skin are damaged, causing a dark area to appear on the skin.; 2. An emotional hurt or wound.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He fell and got a nasty bruise on his leg.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他摔倒了，腿上留下了一塊嚴重的瘀傷。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her harsh words left him with a bruise to his ego.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她刻薄的話語傷了他的自尊心。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他摔倒了，腿上留下了一塊嚴重的瘀傷。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3127,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::brutal::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The dictator's regime was known for its ____ treatment of political prisoners.","expectedAnswer":"brutal","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The dictator's regime was known for its ____ treatment of political prisoners.","clozeAnswer":"brutal","exampleTranslation":"這位獨裁者的政權以其對政治犯的殘酷待遇而聞名。","reference":{"eng":"brutal","kk":"/ˈbrutl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['殘酷的；野蠻的'], ['（天氣、情況等）嚴酷的；嚴重的'], ['（直率、粗魯地）坦率的']]","chEntries":["殘酷的","野蠻的","嚴酷的","嚴重的","坦率的"],"practiceMeaning":"這位獨裁者的政權以其對政治犯的殘酷待遇而聞名。","analysis":"詞源來自拉丁語 'brutalis'，意為「動物性的，粗野的」，與 'brutus'（笨重的，遲鈍的）有關。最初形容像動物一樣沒有理性、野蠻的行為。'Brutal' 強調的是缺乏人性、殘忍、暴力和極端的嚴酷。其語意延伸至描述極端惡劣的條件或非常直接（甚至令人不舒服）的陳述。","definition":"1. savagely violent; 2. (of a person or their actions) cruel and aggressive; 3. (of weather or other natural phenomena) severe and harsh; 4. (of truth or statements) harsh and direct.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The dictator's regime was known for its brutal treatment of political prisoners.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位獨裁者的政權以其對政治犯的殘酷待遇而聞名。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The winter weather in this region is absolutely brutal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個地區的冬季天氣非常嚴酷。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He delivered the bad news in a brutal, no-nonsense way.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他以一種殘酷、不講情面的方式傳達了壞消息。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這位獨裁者的政權以其對政治犯的殘酷待遇而聞名。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4496,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::bulletproof::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The limousine was equipped with ____ glass.","expectedAnswer":"bulletproof","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The limousine was equipped with ____ glass.","clozeAnswer":"bulletproof","exampleTranslation":"這輛轎車配備了防彈玻璃。","reference":{"eng":"bulletproof","kk":"/ˈbʊlɪtˌpruːf/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['防彈的'], ['（計劃、論點等）無懈可擊的']]","chEntries":["防彈的","無懈可擊的"],"practiceMeaning":"這輛轎車配備了防彈玻璃。","analysis":"由 bullet (子彈) 和 proof (防護) 組成。核心語意是「能抵擋子彈的」。引申為「絕對可靠」、「無懈可擊」的計劃、理論等。","definition":"1. Impervious to bullets; 2. Impossible to disprove or contradict.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The limousine was equipped with bulletproof glass.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這輛轎車配備了防彈玻璃。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His alibi was bulletproof.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的不在場證明無懈可擊。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這輛轎車配備了防彈玻璃。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4745,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::bundle-up::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It's cold outside, so ____!","expectedAnswer":"bundle up","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It's cold outside, so ____!","clozeAnswer":"bundle up","exampleTranslation":"外面很冷，所以穿暖和點！","reference":{"eng":"bundle up","kk":"/ˈbʌndəl ˈʌp/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['穿暖和'], ['包裹起來']]","chEntries":["穿暖和","包裹起來"],"practiceMeaning":"外面很冷，所以穿暖和點！","analysis":"動詞片語，由 'bundle'（捆）和 'up'（向上，表示完成、包好）構成。第一義指將自己或他人穿上厚重的衣物以保暖。第二義指將物品緊密地捆紮在一起。","definition":"1. To dress warmly in many clothes. 2. To wrap or pack something tightly in a bundle.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's cold outside, so bundle up!\",\n    \"ch\": \"外面很冷，所以穿暖和點！\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She bundled up the baby in a thick blanket.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她用厚毯子把嬰兒緊緊包裹起來。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"外面很冷，所以穿暖和點！","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5507,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l5::burst::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There was a ____ of gunfire.","expectedAnswer":"burst","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There was a ____ of gunfire.","clozeAnswer":"burst","exampleTranslation":"傳來一陣槍響。","reference":{"eng":"burst","kk":"bɜːrst","tense":"n.","ch":"[['爆炸'], ['迸發'], ['爆發']]","chEntries":["爆炸","迸發","爆發"],"practiceMeaning":"傳來一陣槍響。","analysis":"此為動詞 'burst' 的名詞形式。作為名詞，它承襲了動詞的核心語義，指「爆炸」的事件或「情感、能量」的突然釋放。無獨立的構詞分析，由動詞轉換而來。語意演變與動詞一致，強調「瞬間的、劇烈的」現象。常用於描述物理爆炸或情感的突然爆發。","definition":"a sudden loud noise made by something bursting; a sudden short period of increased activity or strong emotion.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was a burst of gunfire.\",\n    \"ch\": \"傳來一陣槍響。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She felt a burst of anger.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她感到一陣憤怒。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"傳來一陣槍響。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4221,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::buy::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"I want to ____ a new book.","expectedAnswer":"buy","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"I want to ____ a new book.","clozeAnswer":"buy","exampleTranslation":"我想買一本新書。","reference":{"eng":"buy","kk":"/baɪ/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['買；購買']]","chEntries":["買","購買"],"practiceMeaning":"我想買一本新書。","analysis":"源自古英語 bycgan，意為“購買”，與荷蘭語 biegen 同源，最終可能來自原始印歐語 *bȳg-（擁有）。核心是通過支付貨幣或交換來獲得某物。","definition":"To obtain in exchange for payment.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I want to buy a new book.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我想買一本新書。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She bought the dress on sale.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她趁著打折買了那條連衣裙。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He buys on credit.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他賒帳購買。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我想買一本新書。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5119,"wordRef":"字彙王::u62::canal::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The Panama ____ is a vital shipping route.","expectedAnswer":"Canal","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The Panama ____ is a vital shipping route.","clozeAnswer":"Canal","exampleTranslation":"巴拿馬運河是一條重要的航運路線。","reference":{"eng":"canal","kk":"kəˈnæl","tense":"n.","ch":"[['運河'], ['管道'], ['輸水道']]","chEntries":["運河","管道","輸水道"],"practiceMeaning":"巴拿馬運河是一條重要的航運路線。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 canalis，意為「水渠、管道」，本身來自 canna（蘆葦、管子）。canna 可追溯至希臘語 kanna，意為「蘆葦」。原始印歐語根 *kan- 可能與「蘆葦」或「管狀物」有關。核心語意為「人造的、用於引水或航運的長形水道」。","definition":"an artificial waterway constructed to allow the passage of boats or ships inland or to convey water for irrigation.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The Panama Canal is a vital shipping route.\",\n    \"ch\": \"巴拿馬運河是一條重要的航運路線。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Farmers use canals to irrigate their fields.\",\n    \"ch\": \"農民使用運河灌溉他們的田地。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"巴拿馬運河是一條重要的航運路線。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U62"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3206,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::cane::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The old gentleman walked with a silver-headed ____.","expectedAnswer":"cane","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The old gentleman walked with a silver-headed ____.","clozeAnswer":"cane","exampleTranslation":"這位老先生拄著一根銀頭手杖走路。","reference":{"eng":"cane","kk":"/keɪn/","tense":"n.","c