":[],"clozeSentence":"The artist stretched a fresh ____.","clozeAnswer":"canvas","exampleTranslation":"藝術家準備了一塊新的畫布。","reference":{"eng":"canvas","kk":"ˈkænvəs","tense":"n.","ch":"[['帆布'], ['油畫布'], ['帳篷']]","chEntries":["帆布","油畫布","帳篷"],"practiceMeaning":"藝術家準備了一塊新的畫布。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 cannabis，意為「大麻」。古羅馬人用大麻的纖維製作繩索和帆布。後來，此詞的用法專指用於繪畫的粗麻布（油畫布），以及用於製作帳篷、船帆等堅固材料。","definition":"a strong coarse unbleached cloth made from flax or hemp, used to make sails, tents, etc.; a piece of this cloth used by artists to paint on.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The artist stretched a fresh canvas.\",\n    \"ch\": \"藝術家準備了一塊新的畫布。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They slept in canvas tents.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們睡在帆布帳篷裡。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"藝術家準備了一塊新的畫布。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U62"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4119,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::capable::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She is a very ____ manager.","expectedAnswer":"capable","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She is a very ____ manager.","clozeAnswer":"capable","exampleTranslation":"她是一位非常有能力的經理。","reference":{"eng":"capable","kk":"/ˈkeɪpəbl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['有能力的', '能幹的'], ['能夠（做某事）的']]","chEntries":["有能力的","能幹的","能夠的"],"practiceMeaning":"她是一位非常有能力的經理。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 capabilis，由 capere（抓住、容納）+ -abilis（能夠）組成。核心概念是「有能力抓住（機會或任務）」或「能容納」。引申為具備某種技能、力量或潛力。","definition":"1. having the ability, fitness, or quality necessary to do or achieve a specified thing; 2. intelligent and quick to understand","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a very capable manager.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是一位非常有能力的經理。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is capable of handling this task.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他能夠處理這項任務。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Are you capable of understanding the seriousness of the situation?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你能夠理解局勢的嚴重性嗎？\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她是一位非常有能力的經理。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3211,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::carry::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Please ____ this bag for me.","expectedAnswer":"carry","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Please ____ this bag for me.","clozeAnswer":"carry","exampleTranslation":"請幫我提這個包。","reference":{"eng":"carry","kk":"/ˈkæri/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['攜帶'], ['搬運'], ['運輸'], ['傳播'], ['承受']]","chEntries":["攜帶","搬運","運輸","傳播","承受"],"practiceMeaning":"請幫我提這個包。","analysis":"詞源來自古法語 'cariere'，意為 'cart, wagon'，源自拉丁文 'carrum' (cart)。核心意義是『移動某物從一地到另一地』。此意義延伸至物理上的搬運、傳送，以及抽象的傳遞（信息、疾病）、承擔（責任、重量）。","definition":"1. to support and move (someone or something) from one place to another; 2. to convey or transmit (information, news, etc.); 3. to have or produce (a particular quality or result); 4. to be sold in a particular shop.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please carry this bag for me.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請幫我提這個包。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The news spread quickly, carried by word of mouth.\",\n    \"ch\": \"消息迅速傳開，靠口耳相傳。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This vaccine can carry antibodies.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種疫苗可以攜帶抗體。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He carried the team to victory.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他帶領隊伍贏得了勝利。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"請幫我提這個包。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U41"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5122,"wordRef":"字彙王::u62::casino::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He lost a lot of money at the ____.","expectedAnswer":"casino","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He lost a lot of money at the ____.","clozeAnswer":"casino","exampleTranslation":"他在賭場輸了很多錢。","reference":{"eng":"casino","kk":"kəˈsiːnoʊ","tense":"n.","ch":"[['賭場'], ['娛樂場所']]","chEntries":["賭場","娛樂場所"],"practiceMeaning":"他在賭場輸了很多錢。","analysis":"此字源自義大利語 casino，原意為「小房子、小屋」，是 casa（房子）的指小詞。後來這個詞的意義演變為「提供娛樂、社交活動或賭博的小建築」，最終專指「賭場」。","definition":"a public room or building where gambling games are played; a place for entertainment, especially dancing.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He lost a lot of money at the casino.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在賭場輸了很多錢。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他在賭場輸了很多錢。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U62"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3270,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::chamber::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The king resided in the royal ____.","expectedAnswer":"chamber","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The king resided in the royal ____.","clozeAnswer":"chamber","exampleTranslation":"國王居住在皇家臥室。","reference":{"eng":"chamber","kk":"/ˈtʃeɪmbər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['房間；密室'], ['議院；（立法機構的）會議廳'], ['腔；室（如身體的腔、槍的膛）'], ['（尤指）臥室']]","chEntries":["房間","密室","議院","會議廳","腔","室","臥室"],"practiceMeaning":"國王居住在皇家臥室。","analysis":"源自古法語 'chambre'，來自拉丁語 'camera' (房間)。最初指私人房間，尤其指臥室，後引申指用於特定目的的空間，如會議廳（chamber of commerce）或身體的腔（heart chamber）。","definition":"1. a room, especially a bedroom, or a private room in a larger house; 2. a legislative or administrative body; 3. a hollow space in an organ or other body part; 4. a part of a gun that holds the cartridges.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The king resided in the royal chamber.\",\n    \"ch\": \"國王居住在皇家臥室。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The Senate is the upper chamber of Congress.\",\n    \"ch\": \"參議院是國會的上議院。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The heart has four chambers.\",\n    \"ch\": \"心臟有四個腔室。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"國王居住在皇家臥室。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4624,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::champion::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She is the reigning world ____ in tennis.","expectedAnswer":"champion","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She is the reigning world ____ in tennis.","clozeAnswer":"champion","exampleTranslation":"她是網壇的現任世界冠軍。","reference":{"eng":"champion","kk":"/ˈtʃæmpiən/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['冠軍'], ['優勝者'], ['（為...）辯護者'], ['鬥士']]","chEntries":["冠軍","優勝者","辯護者","鬥士"],"practiceMeaning":"她是網壇的現任世界冠軍。","analysis":"源自古法語 'champion'，拉丁語 'campio' (角鬥士)。原指競技場上的戰士或競賽中的獲勝者。引申義指在某個領域出類拔萃、為某種觀念或事業奮鬥的人。","definition":"a person who has won a competition; a person who fights or argues for a cause or on behalf of someone else.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is the reigning world champion in tennis.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是網壇的現任世界冠軍。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was a champion for human rights.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是人權的倡導者。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她是網壇的現任世界冠軍。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4639,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::charisma::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The leader's ____ inspired millions.","expectedAnswer":"charisma","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The leader's ____ inspired millions.","clozeAnswer":"charisma","exampleTranslation":"這位領導人的魅力鼓舞了數百萬人。","reference":{"eng":"charisma","kk":"/kəˈrɪzmə/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['魅力'], ['感召力'], ['號召力']]","chEntries":["魅力","感召力","號召力"],"practiceMeaning":"這位領導人的魅力鼓舞了數百萬人。","analysis":"源自希臘語 'kharisma'，意為「恩惠、恩賜」。原指一種宗教上的神授能力。現代用法指一種非凡的個人特質，能夠強烈吸引、影響他人，並激發忠誠和追隨。","definition":"a compelling attractiveness or charm that can inspire devotion in others.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The leader's charisma inspired millions.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位領導人的魅力鼓舞了數百萬人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a natural charisma that makes her a great public speaker.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她天生具有一種魅力，使她成為一個優秀的公眾演說家。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這位領導人的魅力鼓舞了數百萬人。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4627,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::charm::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She has a natural ____ that makes people like her.","expectedAnswer":"charm","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She has a natural ____ that makes people like her.","clozeAnswer":"charm","exampleTranslation":"她天生具有一種魅力，讓人喜歡。","reference":{"eng":"charm","kk":"/tʃɑːrm/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['魅力'], ['吸引力'], ['護身符']]","chEntries":["魅力","吸引力","護身符"],"practiceMeaning":"她天生具有一種魅力，讓人喜歡。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'carminare' (唱歌、咒語)。最初指能帶來好運的護身符或咒語。引申義指個人身上散發出的吸引人的氣質、風度或魔力，讓人產生好感。","definition":"the power to attract or delight; a small object worn as a token of good luck or as a reminder.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a natural charm that makes people like her.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她天生具有一種魅力，讓人喜歡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He wore a lucky charm for the exam.\",\n    \"ch\": \"考試時他戴著一個幸運護身符。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她天生具有一種魅力，讓人喜歡。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4328,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::chest::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He suffered a pain in his ____.","expectedAnswer":"chest","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He suffered a pain in his ____.","clozeAnswer":"chest","exampleTranslation":"他感到胸部疼痛。","reference":{"eng":"chest","kk":"/tʃɛst/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['胸部'], ['箱子；櫃子']]","chEntries":["胸部","箱子","櫃子"],"practiceMeaning":"他感到胸部疼痛。","analysis":"源自古英語 'cest'，與古希臘語 'kistē' (box) 和拉丁語 'cista' (box, chest) 同源，原意是指『箱子』。1. 指人體或動物身體的『胸部』，這個含義可能是在使用木箱來比喻胸腔的堅固性或容量後發展而來，或是因為胸部常被認為是承載情感的『箱子』。2. 最原始的含義，指『箱子、櫃子』，特別是較大的、用於存放財物的箱子。","definition":"the part of the front of the body between the neck and the stomach; a large strong box with a lid, used for storing things or for travelling","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He suffered a pain in his chest.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他感到胸部疼痛。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The pirate buried his treasure in a chest.\",\n    \"ch\": \"海盜將他的寶藏埋在一個箱子裡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She keeps her old letters in a wooden chest.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她把舊信件放在一個木箱裡。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他感到胸部疼痛。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5289,"wordRef":"字彙王::u63::chord::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The pianist played a beautiful ____.","expectedAnswer":"chord","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The pianist played a beautiful ____.","clozeAnswer":"chord","exampleTranslation":"鋼琴師彈奏了一個優美的和弦。","reference":{"eng":"chord","kk":"kɔːrd","tense":"n.","ch":"[['和弦'], ['（幾何學）弦'], ['（尤指電線）纜線，線']]","chEntries":["和弦","弦","纜線，線"],"practiceMeaning":"鋼琴師彈奏了一個優美的和弦。","analysis":"此字有兩個主要詞源。一是來自古希臘語 'chordē' (χορδή)，意為「腸線、弦」。這個詞源導向了音樂中的「和弦」和幾何學中的「弦」。二是來自古法語 'corde'（繩索、線），源自拉丁語 'chorda'，與希臘語 'chordē' 同源，均指「腸線、弦、繩索」。在現代英語中，'chord' 作名詞時，最常見的意義是音樂中的「和弦」，幾何學中的「弦」，以及表示「線」或「纜線」時，儘管 'cord' 更常用於此意。","definition":"a group of three or more notes sounded together in harmony; a straight line or curve connecting two points on a curve or circle; a flexible insulated electrical cable.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The pianist played a beautiful chord.\",\n    \"ch\": \"鋼琴師彈奏了一個優美的和弦。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A chord connects two points on the circumference of a circle.\",\n    \"ch\": \"弦連接圓周上的兩個點。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"鋼琴師彈奏了一個優美的和弦。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U63"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5290,"wordRef":"字彙王::u63::chore::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Washing the dishes is my least favorite ____.","expectedAnswer":"chore","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Washing the dishes is my least favorite ____.","clozeAnswer":"chore","exampleTranslation":"洗碗是我最不喜歡的家務雜事。","reference":{"eng":"chore","kk":"tʃɔːr","tense":"n.","ch":"[['家務雜事', '日常瑣事'], ['（尤指例行性的、不令人愉快但必須做的）工作']]","chEntries":["家務雜事","日常瑣事","工作"],"practiceMeaning":"洗碗是我最不喜歡的家務雜事。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 'chore'，意為「一次性工作、小任務」，可能源自古法語 'chose'（事物，來自拉丁語 'causa'），或與古法語 'choer'（共同擁有）有關，最終指向「必需完成的事情」。其核心語意是「必須做的、例行性的、通常不令人愉快的任務」。","definition":"a routine task, especially a household one; a tedious or unpleasant task.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Washing the dishes is my least favorite chore.\",\n    \"ch\": \"洗碗是我最不喜歡的家務雜事。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He does his chores every Saturday morning.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他每週六早上做他的家務。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"洗碗是我最不喜歡的家務雜事。","sourceName":"字彙王、龍騰課本","unitName":"U63、L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4346,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::cinema::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He is a great admirer of French ____.","expectedAnswer":"cinema","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He is a great admirer of French ____.","clozeAnswer":"cinema","exampleTranslation":"他是法國電影藝術的忠實崇拜者。","reference":{"eng":"cinema","kk":"/ˈsɪnəmə/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['電影；電影藝術'], ['電影院']]","chEntries":["電影","電影藝術","電影院"],"practiceMeaning":"他是法國電影藝術的忠實崇拜者。","analysis":"源自希臘語 'kinēma' (movement)，來自 'kinein' (to move)。1. 指『電影』作為一種藝術形式或娛樂，即『電影藝術』。2. 指放映電影的場所，即『電影院』。","definition":"the business or activity of making films; the art or technique of making films; a building in which films are shown","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a great admirer of French cinema.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是法國電影藝術的忠實崇拜者。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Let's go to the cinema tonight.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們今晚去看電影吧。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The history of cinema is fascinating.\",\n    \"ch\": \"電影的歷史非常迷人。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他是法國電影藝術的忠實崇拜者。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5829,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::circuit::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The electrician checked the electrical ____.","expectedAnswer":"circuit","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The electrician checked the electrical ____.","clozeAnswer":"circuit","exampleTranslation":"電工檢查了電路。","reference":{"eng":"circuit","kk":"ˈsɜːrkɪt","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"電路\"  ],  [    \"迴路\"  ],  [    \"巡迴路線\"  ],  [    \"週期\"  ],  [    \"環形\"  ]]","chEntries":["電路","迴路","巡迴路線","週期","環形"],"practiceMeaning":"電工檢查了電路。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'circuitus'，是 'circuire' (to go around) 的過去分詞，由 'circum' (around) 和 'ire' (to go) 構成。'Circuitus' 的字面意思是「繞行」，引申為「圍繞一圈的路線」或「封閉的循環」。在物理學上，'circuit' 指電流沿著封閉路徑流動的「電路」或「迴路」。在地理或旅行語境中，'circuit' 指「巡迴路線」，如馬戲團或表演團體的巡迴演出路線。它強調的是一種「循環」或「繞行」的概念。例如，也可指「一場比賽的賽道」。","definition":"1. A roughly circular or oval area or path.; 2. A complete electrical path, consisting of wires, components, and a power source.; 3. A route or journey that visits a number of places.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The electrician checked the electrical circuit.\",\n    \"ch\": \"電工檢查了電路。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The race car driver completed another circuit of the track.\",\n    \"ch\": \"賽車手又完成了一圈賽道。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They are planning a lecture circuit.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們正在規劃一個演講巡迴路線。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The Formula 1 circuit is known for its speed.\",\n    \"ch\": \"F1 賽道以其速度聞名。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"電工檢查了電路。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4626,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::citizen::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Every ____ has the right to vote.","expectedAnswer":"citizen","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Every ____ has the right to vote.","clozeAnswer":"citizen","exampleTranslation":"每個公民都有投票權。","reference":{"eng":"citizen","kk":"/ˈsɪtɪzən/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['公民'], ['市民']]","chEntries":["公民","市民"],"practiceMeaning":"每個公民都有投票權。","analysis":"源自古法語 'citeien'，拉丁語 'civis' (城市居民)。指一個國家或地區的合法成員，享有權利並負有義務。可指國家公民，也可指城市居民。","definition":"a legally recognized subject or national of a state or commonwealth, either native or naturalized; an inhabitant of a city or town.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Every citizen has the right to vote.\",\n    \"ch\": \"每個公民都有投票權。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has been a proud citizen of this country for twenty years.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她做這個國家的自豪公民已經二十年了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"每個公民都有投票權。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6065,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::citizenship::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He applied for ____ after living in the country for ten years.","expectedAnswer":"citizenship","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He applied for ____ after living in the country for ten years.","clozeAnswer":"citizenship","exampleTranslation":"他在該國居住了十年後申請了公民權。","reference":{"eng":"citizenship","kk":"ˈsɪtɪzənʃɪp","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"公民權\"  ],  [    \"市民身份\"  ],  [    \"國民身份\"  ],  [    \"公民意識\"  ]]","chEntries":["公民權","市民身份","國民身份","公民意識"],"practiceMeaning":"他在該國居住了十年後申請了公民權。","analysis":"此字由 citizen（公民）加上名詞後綴 -ship（表示狀態、身份、技能或集合）構成。Citizen 源自古法語 citeien，來自 civitas（city, state），再追溯至 civis（citizen）。Civitas 最終來源於 proto-Indo-European * (s)kein-「劃分，切割」，引申為「部落、社群」。Citizenship 的核心語義是「作為一個公民的身份、權利和義務」，包括法律上的公民權（公民身份），以及更廣泛的「公民責任」或「公民意識」。","definition":"1. the status of being a citizen of a particular country; 2. the rights and duties of a citizen; 3. the quality of behaving well and being useful to your country or community.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He applied for citizenship after living in the country for ten years.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在該國居住了十年後申請了公民權。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Citizenship education teaches people about their rights and responsibilities.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公民教育教導人們了解他們的權利和責任。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Active citizenship is crucial for a healthy democracy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"積極的公民意識對健康的民主至關重要。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他在該國居住了十年後申請了公民權。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4044,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::civil::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ rights are fundamental to democracy.","expectedAnswer":"Civil","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ rights are fundamental to democracy.","clozeAnswer":"Civil","exampleTranslation":"公民權利是民主的基石。","reference":{"eng":"civil","kk":"/ˈsɪvəl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['公民的', '國民的'], ['文明的', '有禮貌的'], ['國內的', '非軍事的']]","chEntries":["公民的","國民的","文明的","有禮貌的","國內的","非軍事的"],"practiceMeaning":"公民權利是民主的基石。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'civilis'，意為「屬於公民的」、「適合公民的」。'civilis' 又來自 'civis'，意為「市民」、「公民」。核心概念是與「社會」、「國家」或「群體」有關，而非個人或軍事。因此，延伸出「公民的」事務、「文明的」行為（與野蠻相對），以及「國內的」衝突（與戰爭相對）。","definition":"1. relating to a citizen or the state; 2. polite and behaving in a calm and controlled way; 3. relating to the internal affairs of a country, especially in contrast to war or military matters","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"公民權利是民主的基石。\",\n    \"eng\": \"Civil rights are fundamental to democracy.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他對鄰居總是很有禮貌。\",\n    \"eng\": \"He was always civil to his neighbors.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"該國捲入了內戰。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The country has been involved in a civil war.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"公民權利是民主的基石。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3130,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::claw::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The angry dog began to ____ at the door.","expectedAnswer":"claw","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The angry dog began to ____ at the door.","clozeAnswer":"claw","exampleTranslation":"那隻生氣的狗開始抓門。","reference":{"eng":"claw","kk":"/klɔː/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['（用爪）抓；（用指甲）抓'], ['（用力）抓，扯']]","chEntries":["抓","抓，扯"],"practiceMeaning":"那隻生氣的狗開始抓門。","analysis":"動詞用法，來自名詞 'claw'。強調用尖銳、類似爪子的工具（如爪子、指甲、鉤子）進行抓、撕、刮或挖掘的動作。這種動作通常是強力的、有侵略性的，或是為了獲得、抓住東西。語意延伸至比喻性的「緊緊抓住」或「奮力爭取」。","definition":"1. (of an animal) scratch or grip with claws; 2. scratch or tear with one's fingernails or anything sharp; 3. grasp or seize tightly.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The angry dog began to claw at the door.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那隻生氣的狗開始抓門。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She clawed her way up the career ladder through sheer hard work.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她憑藉純粹的努力，奮力爬上了事業的階梯。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He clawed the fabric with his fingernails.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他用指甲抓撓著布料。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"那隻生氣的狗開始抓門。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4506,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::clumsy::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He was a ____ child, always tripping over his own feet.","expectedAnswer":"clumsy","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He was a ____ child, always tripping over his own feet.","clozeAnswer":"clumsy","exampleTranslation":"他是一個笨拙的孩子，總是絆倒自己的腳。","reference":{"eng":"clumsy","kk":"/ˈklʌmzi/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['笨拙的'], ['不靈巧的'], ['（東西）笨重的']]","chEntries":["笨拙的","不靈巧的","笨重的"],"practiceMeaning":"他是一個笨拙的孩子，總是絆倒自己的腳。","analysis":"源自古挪威語 klumsa，意為「笨拙」、「無能」。核心語意是「動作不協調」、「不靈巧」。","definition":"1. Awkward in movement or in handling things; 2. (of an object) large, heavy, and awkward to use.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was a clumsy child, always tripping over his own feet.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一個笨拙的孩子，總是絆倒自己的腳。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The clumsy waiter dropped the tray.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那個笨拙的服務員打翻了托盤。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The furniture was old and clumsy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這些傢俱又老又笨重。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他是一個笨拙的孩子，總是絆倒自己的腳。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4076,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::coach::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ motivated the team to win.","expectedAnswer":"coach","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ motivated the team to win.","clozeAnswer":"coach","exampleTranslation":"教練激勵隊伍取勝。","reference":{"eng":"coach","kk":"/koʊtʃ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['教練'], ['長途馬車', '巴士'], ['（火車的）頭等車廂']]","chEntries":["教練","長途馬車","巴士","頭等車廂"],"practiceMeaning":"教練激勵隊伍取勝。","analysis":"第一個義項「教練」的詞源來自匈牙利語 'kocsi' (a carriage)，最初指15世紀匈牙利科西鎮（Kocs）生產的一種馬車。後來，牛津大學的學生用它來比喻「（能載人順利通過考試的）導師」或「私人教師」。引申到體育領域，即「訓練運動員的教練」。第二個義項「長途馬車」、「巴士」則是直接繼承了馬車的原意。第三個義項「火車車廂」也是由馬車引申而來，指專門的車廂。","definition":"1. a person who trains athletes or sports teams; 2. a large bus used for carrying passengers, especially on long journeys; 3. a private railway carriage","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"教練激勵隊伍取勝。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The coach motivated the team to win.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"我們搭乘長途巴士去了倫敦。\",\n    \"eng\": \"We took a coach to London.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他是籃球隊的主教練。\",\n    \"eng\": \"He is the head coach of the basketball team.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"教練激勵隊伍取勝。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6117,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::coffin::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ was made of dark wood.","expectedAnswer":"coffin","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ was made of dark wood.","clozeAnswer":"coffin","exampleTranslation":"棺材是由深色木材製成的。","reference":{"eng":"coffin","kk":"ˈkɔːfɪn","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"棺材\"  ],  [    \"靈柩\"  ]]","chEntries":["棺材","靈柩"],"practiceMeaning":"棺材是由深色木材製成的。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 cofin，意為「盒子」，來自拉丁語 cophinus，來自希臘語 kophinos，意為「籃子」。因此，coffin 的核心語義是「一種容器」。在 modern English 中，它特指用於存放死者遺體的「棺材」。其語意演變是從「籃子」到「盒子」，再到「棺材」。","definition":"A box-like container for a dead body.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The coffin was made of dark wood.\",\n    \"ch\": \"棺材是由深色木材製成的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They lowered the coffin into the grave.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們將棺材下葬。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"棺材是由深色木材製成的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5716,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l9::come-over::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Please ____ for dinner tonight.","expectedAnswer":"come over","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Please ____ for dinner tonight.","clozeAnswer":"come over","exampleTranslation":"今晚請過來吃晚餐。","reference":{"eng":"come over","kk":"kʌm oʊvər","tense":"v.","ch":"[['過來'], ['來訪'], ['佔據（某人的思想）'], ['感染']]","chEntries":["過來","來訪","佔據","感染"],"practiceMeaning":"今晚請過來吃晚餐。","analysis":"這是一個片語動詞。'come' 源自古英語 cuman（來）。'over' 表示「越過，在另一側」。字面意思是「來到這邊」。引申有多種用法：1. 表示「來到某個地方」（特別是對方所在地），如「過來」；2. 表示「來訪」；3. 比喻指「某種感覺或想法突然產生並影響某人」，如「佔據（某人的思想）」；4. 指「疾病或情緒突然影響某人」，如「感染」。核心語意是「從一個地方或狀態移動到另一個地方或狀態，特別是來到說話者所在的或相關的地方」。","definition":"to move from one place to another; to visit someone's home; to affect someone (e.g., a feeling or illness).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please come over for dinner tonight.\",\n    \"ch\": \"今晚請過來吃晚餐。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A strange feeling came over her.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一種奇怪的感覺襲上了她。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"今晚請過來吃晚餐。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5500,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::come-with::idiom","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Would you like to ____ us to the cinema?","expectedAnswer":"come with","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Would you like to ____ us to the cinema?","clozeAnswer":"come with","exampleTranslation":"你想跟我們一起去看電影嗎？","reference":{"eng":"come with","kk":"kʌm wɪð","tense":"idiom","ch":"[['隨同而來'], ['附帶'], ['具有……的特點']]","chEntries":["隨同而來","附帶","具有……的特點"],"practiceMeaning":"你想跟我們一起去看電影嗎？","analysis":"這是一個常見的動詞片語。'Come' 是動詞，表示「來到」。'With' 是介詞，表示「和、帶著、伴隨」。'Come with' 的基本語意是「跟隨某人或某物來到某處」，或「附帶、包含」。它可以指人一起來，也可以指物品隨同出現。在某些語境下，也表示「具有某種特性或條件」。核心語意是「伴隨或附帶」。","definition":"1. Accompany; go or come along with.; 2. Be included or provided with; be associated with.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Would you like to come with us to the cinema?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你想跟我們一起去看電影嗎？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This car comes with a navigation system.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這輛車配備了導航系統。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The package comes with a detailed instruction manual.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個包裹附帶了詳細的使用手冊。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"你想跟我們一起去看電影嗎？","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4657,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::comedy::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They went to see a ____ last night.","expectedAnswer":"comedy","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They went to see a ____ last night.","clozeAnswer":"comedy","exampleTranslation":"他們昨晚去看了一部喜劇。","reference":{"eng":"comedy","kk":"/ˈkɒmədi/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['喜劇'], ['喜劇作品']]","chEntries":["喜劇","喜劇作品"],"practiceMeaning":"他們昨晚去看了一部喜劇。","analysis":"源自希臘語 'komoidia'，意為「喜劇」。指以引人發笑為目的的戲劇、電影、文學作品或表演。其特點通常是幽默、諷刺、誇張或滑稽的情節和人物。","definition":"a genre of film or theatre in which the primary purpose is to amuse and entertain the audience, often through humor.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They went to see a comedy last night.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們昨晚去看了一部喜劇。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His stand-up routine was a great comedy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的單口相聲表演非常搞笑。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們昨晚去看了一部喜劇。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6215,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::commentator::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He is a well-known political ____.","expectedAnswer":"commentator","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He is a well-known political ____.","clozeAnswer":"commentator","exampleTranslation":"他是一位知名的政治評論員。","reference":{"eng":"commentator","kk":"ˈkɒmənˌteɪtər","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"評論員\"  ],  [    \"講評員\"  ],  [    \"註釋者\"  ]]","chEntries":["評論員","講評員","註釋者"],"practiceMeaning":"他是一位知名的政治評論員。","analysis":"此字由名詞 commentary（評論）加上字尾 -or（表示人，從事某種職業者）構成。commentary 源自拉丁語 commentum。字尾 -or 標示從事評論或提供講評的人。因此，commentator 指撰寫或發表評論、講評或分析的人，特別是在新聞、體育、政治等領域。中文翻譯為「評論員；講評員；註釋者」。","definition":"1. a person who explains or discusses something, especially in a newspaper or magazine; 2. a person who describes a sports event or other public event on the radio or television.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a well-known political commentator.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一位知名的政治評論員。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The football match was broadcast with live commentary.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這場足球賽事有現場講評播出。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a respected cultural commentator.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是一位受尊敬的文化評論員。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他是一位知名的政治評論員。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3945,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::committee::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ will meet next week to discuss the proposal.","expectedAnswer":"committee","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ will meet next week to discuss the proposal.","clozeAnswer":"committee","exampleTranslation":"委員會將於下週開會討論該提案。","reference":{"eng":"committee","kk":"/kəˈmɪti/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['委員會']]","chEntries":["委員會"],"practiceMeaning":"委員會將於下週開會討論該提案。","analysis":"源自中古英語 'committé' (意為「被託付的人」)，源自拉丁語 'committere' (意為「託付、委託」)。指為特定目的而設立的、由若干人組成的專門小組。","definition":"a group of people appointed for a specific function by a larger group and typically holding regular meetings.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The committee will meet next week to discuss the proposal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"委員會將於下週開會討論該提案。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a member of the planning committee.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是計畫委員會的成員。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The committee made a decision.\",\n    \"ch\": \"委員會做出了決定。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"委員會將於下週開會討論該提案。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4651,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::communicate-with::idiom","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It's hard to ____ him when he's angry.","expectedAnswer":"communicate with","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It's hard to ____ him when he's angry.","clozeAnswer":"communicate with","exampleTranslation":"當他生氣時，很難與他溝通。","reference":{"eng":"communicate with","kk":"/kəˈmjuːnɪkeɪt wɪð/","tense":"idiom","ch":"[['與...溝通'], ['與...交流']]","chEntries":["與...溝通","與...交流"],"practiceMeaning":"當他生氣時，很難與他溝通。","analysis":"此為固定片語，'communicate' (溝通) + 'with' (介詞)。強調與特定對象建立溝通管道，進行訊息、情感的交換。比單獨使用 'communicate' 更強調互動的對象。","definition":"to share or exchange information or feelings with someone.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's hard to communicate with him when he's angry.\",\n    \"ch\": \"當他生氣時，很難與他溝通。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Doctors need to communicate effectively with patients.\",\n    \"ch\": \"醫生需要有效地與病人交流。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"當他生氣時，很難與他溝通。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5559,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::commute::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"My daily ____ takes about an hour each way.","expectedAnswer":"commute","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"My daily ____ takes about an hour each way.","clozeAnswer":"commute","exampleTranslation":"我每天的通勤單程大約要一個小時。","reference":{"eng":"commute","kk":"kəˈmjuːt","tense":"n.","ch":"[['通勤']]","chEntries":["通勤"],"practiceMeaning":"我每天的通勤單程大約要一個小時。","analysis":"這是 \"commute\" 作動詞的相關名詞形式，源自拉丁語 \"commūtāre\"（to exchange, change，交換，改變）。\"com-\"（together, with，一起）和 \"mūtāre\"（to change，改變）。\"commūtāre\" 的語義演變是指「改變居住地與工作地之間的距離，透過往返移動來完成」。因此，\"commute\" 作為名詞，指「每天從家往返工作地點或學校的行為」，也就是「通勤」。此名詞形式主要與其動詞形式的「通勤」義相關聯。","definition":"1. The act or instance of commuting; 2. The journey made when one commutes.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"My daily commute takes about an hour each way.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我每天的通勤單程大約要一個小時。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He complained about the long commute.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他抱怨通勤時間太長。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我每天的通勤單程大約要一個小時。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3069,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::companion::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She found a loyal ____ in her dog.","expectedAnswer":"companion","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She found a loyal ____ in her dog.","clozeAnswer":"companion","exampleTranslation":"她在她的狗身上找到了忠實的伴侶。","reference":{"eng":"companion","kk":"/kəmˈpænjən/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['同伴；夥伴'], ['陪伴者；伴侶'], ['（用於某些頭銜）同列的']]","chEntries":["同伴","夥伴","陪伴者","伴侶","同列的"],"practiceMeaning":"她在她的狗身上找到了忠實的伴侶。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'compāniō'，'com-' (with) + 'pānis' (bread)，字面意思是「分享麵包的人」。核心意義是「一起生活或旅行的人」。\n1. 同伴；夥伴：指與某人同行或共同參與某項活動的人。\n2. 陪伴者；伴侶：指經常陪伴某人，提供支持或友誼的人，可以是人或動物。\n3. （用於某些頭銜）同列的：在名稱中表示與另一人或事物並列，例如 'Companion of Honour'。","definition":"1. a person who is with someone else; 2. a person or animal that travels with or lives with someone; 3. a person who is included in a group or order.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She found a loyal companion in her dog.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在她的狗身上找到了忠實的伴侶。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He traveled across Europe with a companion.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他與一位旅伴一同遊歷歐洲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was appointed a Companion of Honour.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他被任命為榮譽會員。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她在她的狗身上找到了忠實的伴侶。","sourceName":"字彙王、龍騰課本","unitName":"U39、L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5513,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l5::compassion::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She felt great ____ for the refugees.","expectedAnswer":"compassion","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She felt great ____ for the refugees.","clozeAnswer":"compassion","exampleTranslation":"她對難民們感到非常同情。","reference":{"eng":"compassion","kk":"kəmˈpæʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[['同情心'], ['憐憫'], ['慈悲']]","chEntries":["同情心","憐憫","慈悲"],"practiceMeaning":"她對難民們感到非常同情。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'compassio'，由 'com-' (together) + 'passio' (suffering) 構成，意為「共同感受痛苦」。'passio' 本身來自 'patior' (to suffer)。構詞上，'com-' 強調「一同、共同」，'passio' 提供了「痛苦、苦難」的核心語意。原始語義是「與他人一同承受痛苦」。引申為一種感同身受的能力，並因此產生關懷與幫助他人的動機。這是一種強調情感共鳴和互助精神的抽象概念。","definition":"sympathetic pity and concern for the sufferings or misfortunes of others.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She felt great compassion for the refugees.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對難民們感到非常同情。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The organization works to alleviate suffering and promote compassion.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該組織致力於減輕痛苦並推廣慈悲。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她對難民們感到非常同情。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5832,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::compatible::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This software is not ____ with older versions.","expectedAnswer":"compatible","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This software is not ____ with older versions.","clozeAnswer":"compatible","exampleTranslation":"此軟體與舊版本不兼容。","reference":{"eng":"compatible","kk":"kəmˈpætəbl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"兼容的\"  ],  [    \"相容的\"  ],  [    \"協調的\"  ],  [    \"適合的\"  ]]","chEntries":["兼容的","相容的","協調的","適合的"],"practiceMeaning":"此軟體與舊版本不兼容。","analysis":"此字由拉丁語 'compatibilis' 演變而來，由 'com-' (with) 和 'pati' (to suffer, endure) 構成。'Patibilis' 意為「可承受的」。'Compatibilis' 的字面意思是「可以一起承受」或「可以共存」。在現代英語中，'compatible' 指兩個或多個事物能夠一起良好運作、和諧共處，或在功能上相互適用。這可以是指電腦系統、軟體、硬體之間的「兼容性」，也可以是指人際關係中的「協調」或「適合」。核心概念是「能夠和諧共存或協作」。例如，也可指「性情相投的」。","definition":"1. (of two things) able to exist or occur together without conflict.; 2. (of computer hardware or software) able to be used or run together.; 3. (of a person) having a compatible nature or disposition.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This software is not compatible with older versions.\",\n    \"ch\": \"此軟體與舊版本不兼容。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They are a compatible couple.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們是一對很合適的伴侶。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Ensure the devices are compatible before connecting them.\",\n    \"ch\": \"連接設備前，請確保它們是兼容的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Their personalities were highly compatible.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們的性情非常協調。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"此軟體與舊版本不兼容。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5033,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::competence::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Her ____ in financial management is outstanding.","expectedAnswer":"competence","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Her ____ in financial management is outstanding.","clozeAnswer":"competence","exampleTranslation":"她在財務管理方面的能力非常傑出。","reference":{"eng":"competence","kk":"ˈkɑːmpɪtəns","tense":"n.","ch":"[['能力'], ['勝任'], ['才幹']]","chEntries":["能力","勝任","才幹"],"practiceMeaning":"她在財務管理方面的能力非常傑出。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語competentem（有資格的、夠格的），是動詞 competere 的現在分詞。competere 由 com-（共同、一起）+ petere（尋求、爭取、達到）組成，原意為「共同努力以達成目標」、「相等、適合」。competence 意指「有能力完成某事的能力或資格」，強調的是具備完成任務所需的技能、知識和素質。","definition":"1. the ability to do something successfully or efficiently; 2. the ability to meet the needs of a situation.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her competence in financial management is outstanding.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在財務管理方面的能力非常傑出。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company has proven its competence in software development.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司已證明了其在軟體開發方面的能力。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她在財務管理方面的能力非常傑出。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5036,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::compliment::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"I must ____ you on your excellent work.","expectedAnswer":"compliment","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"I must ____ you on your excellent work.","clozeAnswer":"compliment","exampleTranslation":"我必須讚美您卓越的工作。","reference":{"eng":"compliment","kk":"ˈkɑːmplɪmənt","tense":"v.","ch":"[['讚美'], ['恭維'], ['致意']]","chEntries":["讚美","恭維","致意"],"practiceMeaning":"我必須讚美您卓越的工作。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語complimentum，意為「達成、圓滿」，來自 complere（使完整）。動詞 compliment 意為「讚美、恭維」，表達對某人或某事的讚賞。此用法與名詞 complement（補充、完成）拼寫相似但詞源與意義不同。此動詞語意直接來自名詞「讚美」的動作。","definition":"1. praise (someone) enthusiastically and often formally; 2. congratulate (someone).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I must compliment you on your excellent work.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我必須讚美您卓越的工作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He complimented his host on the delicious meal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他稱讚主人的美味佳餚。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我必須讚美您卓越的工作。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5037,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::conceive::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It's difficult to ____ of a world without the internet.","expectedAnswer":"conceive","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It's difficult to ____ of a world without the internet.","clozeAnswer":"conceive","exampleTranslation":"很難想像一個沒有網際網路的世界。","reference":{"eng":"conceive","kk":"kənˈsiːv","tense":"v.","ch":"[['構想'], ['設想'], ['懷孕']]","chEntries":["構想","設想","懷孕"],"practiceMeaning":"很難想像一個沒有網際網路的世界。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語concipere，由 con-（一起、完全）+ capere（抓住、拿）組成，原意為「共同抓住」、「理解」或「懷孕」。在英語中，conceive 演變出多重語意：1. 「在心中形成概念、構想」，強調思維的創造性；2. 「懷孕」，指女性受孕；3. 「理解、認為」，表示對某事的看法。OCR 掃描時可能將 'c' 誤判為 'l' 或 'e' 誤判為 'c'。此處修正為 conceive，其多樣語意都圍繞著「形成」或「包含」的核心概念。","definition":"1. to form or have a mental concept or plan; 2. to become pregnant; 3. to form or devise (a plan or idea).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's difficult to conceive of a world without the internet.\",\n    \"ch\": \"很難想像一個沒有網際網路的世界。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She conceived a plan for the new project.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她為新專案構想了一個計畫。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The couple hoped to conceive a child.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這對夫婦希望懷孕生子。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"很難想像一個沒有網際網路的世界。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4484,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::concert::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We went to a classical music ____ last night.","expectedAnswer":"concert","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We went to a classical music ____ last night.","clozeAnswer":"concert","exampleTranslation":"我們昨晚去聽了一場古典音樂會。","reference":{"eng":"concert","kk":"/ˈkɒnsərt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['音樂會'], ['（尤指）演奏會'], ['（群體或個人之間的）協同，一致']]","chEntries":["音樂會","演奏會","協同，一致"],"practiceMeaning":"我們昨晚去聽了一場古典音樂會。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 concertare，意為「競爭」、「爭論」，後來在義大利語中演變成「協調」、「協同」。核心語意從「一起行動」引申為「（音樂）合奏」、「音樂會」。也保留了「協調一致」的語意。","definition":"1. A musical performance for an audience; 2. An agreement or concord; harmony.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We went to a classical music concert last night.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們昨晚去聽了一場古典音樂會。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The two companies worked in concert to develop the new product.\",\n    \"ch\": \"兩家公司協同合作開發新產品。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們昨晚去聽了一場古典音樂會。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4055,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::conclusion::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"What is your ____ about the experiment?","expectedAnswer":"conclusion","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"What is your ____ about the experiment?","clozeAnswer":"conclusion","exampleTranslation":"你對這個實驗的結論是什麼？","reference":{"eng":"conclusion","kk":"/kənˈkluʒən/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['結論', '結局'], ['結束']]","chEntries":["結論","結局","結束"],"practiceMeaning":"你對這個實驗的結論是什麼？","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'conclusio'，由 'con-' (together) + 'claudere' (to shut) 構成，字面意思是「關閉在一起」。核心是「結束」、「完結」。因此，'conclusion' 指一個過程或事件的「結束」，也指通過推理或討論得出的「結論」。","definition":"1. the end or final part of something; 2. a judgment or decision reached by reasoning; 3. a final statement or summary","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"你對這個實驗的結論是什麼？\",\n    \"eng\": \"What is your conclusion about the experiment?\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"這部電影有一個出人意料的結局。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The movie had a surprising conclusion.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"經過長時間的討論，我們達成了一個結論。\",\n    \"eng\": \"We reached a conclusion after a long discussion.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"你對這個實驗的結論是什麼？","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U4、L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4410,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u9::cone::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ice cream was served in a sugar ____.","expectedAnswer":"cone","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ice cream was served in a sugar ____.","clozeAnswer":"cone","exampleTranslation":"冰淇淋裝在甜筒裡。","reference":{"eng":"cone","kk":"/kəʊn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['圓錐體'], ['圓錐形的物體', '交通錐']]","chEntries":["圓錐體","圓錐形的物體","交通錐"],"practiceMeaning":"冰淇淋裝在甜筒裡。","analysis":"詞源自希臘語 'kōnos'，意為「球果、圓錐」。指一種幾何形狀，以及由其發展而來的各種物體。","definition":"a solid or hollow object that tapers from a circular or oval base to a point; a cone-shaped object used as a warning or marker on the road.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The ice cream was served in a sugar cone.\",\n    \"ch\": \"冰淇淋裝在甜筒裡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Place the traffic cones to direct the traffic.\",\n    \"ch\": \"放置交通錐來疏導交通。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"冰淇淋裝在甜筒裡。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3070,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::conference::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The annual ____ on artificial intelligence will be held next month.","expectedAnswer":"conference","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The annual ____ on artificial intelligence will be held next month.","clozeAnswer":"conference","exampleTranslation":"一年一度的人工智慧會議將於下個月舉行。","reference":{"eng":"conference","kk":"/ˈkɑːnfərəns/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['會議；討論會'], ['（體育）聯盟；賽區']]","chEntries":["會議","討論會","聯盟","賽區"],"practiceMeaning":"一年一度的人工智慧會議將於下個月舉行。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'conferentia'，'con-' (together) + 'ferre' (to bring)。核心意義是「將事物帶到一起討論」。\n1. 會議；討論會：指為特定目的聚集一群人進行討論、交流或決策的正式場合。\n2. （體育）聯盟；賽區：指在體育比賽中，由多支隊伍組成的聯合體。","definition":"1. a formal meeting for discussion; 2. a large meeting where people with the same interests or profession come together to share ideas and information; 3. a group of teams in sports that compete against each other.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The annual conference on artificial intelligence will be held next month.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一年一度的人工智慧會議將於下個月舉行。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The Lakers won the Western Conference championship.\",\n    \"ch\": \"湖人隊贏得了西區聯盟的冠軍。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"一年一度的人工智慧會議將於下個月舉行。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5491,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::consequent::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ reduction in traffic was noticeable.","expectedAnswer":"consequent","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ reduction in traffic was noticeable.","clozeAnswer":"consequent","exampleTranslation":"隨之而來的交通量減少是顯而易見的。","reference":{"eng":"consequent","kk":"ˈkɑnsəkwɛnt","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['因此而起的'], ['必然的'], ['結果的']]","chEntries":["因此而起的","必然的","結果的"],"practiceMeaning":"隨之而來的交通量減少是顯而易見的。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'consequens'，是動詞 'consequi'（跟隨、達成）的現在分詞。'Con-'（一起）+ 'sequi'（跟隨）。'Consequent' 作形容詞，意思是「隨之發生的、結果性的」。它用來描述某事是某個原因或事件的直接結果。與 'consequence'（名詞）對應，'consequent' 強調的是「由先前的事件所引發的」這種關聯性。","definition":"1. Happening as a result of something.; 2. Following as a logical or natural result.; 3. Following in order or succession.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The consequent reduction in traffic was noticeable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"隨之而來的交通量減少是顯而易見的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She made some unwise choices, and the consequent problems were severe.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她做出了一些不明智的選擇，隨之而來的問題也很嚴重。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This policy change has many consequent effects.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這項政策變更會產生許多連帶影響。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"隨之而來的交通量減少是顯而易見的。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4069,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::considerable::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The project requires ____ time and effort.","expectedAnswer":"considerable","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The project requires ____ time and effort.","clozeAnswer":"considerable","exampleTranslation":"這個項目需要相當多的時間和精力。","reference":{"eng":"considerable","kk":"/kənˈsɪdərəbəl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['相當大的', '可觀的'], ['值得考慮的', '重要的']]","chEntries":["相當大的","可觀的","值得考慮的","重要的"],"practiceMeaning":"這個項目需要相當多的時間和精力。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'considerare' (to observe, to examine)，由 'con-' (together) + 'sidus, sideris' (star) 構成，原意是「觀察星辰」，引申為「仔細考慮」、「審視」。因此，'considerable' 指「值得仔細考慮的」、「重要的」，進而延伸為「數量或程度非常大」、「可觀的」。","definition":"1. notably large in size, amount, or extent; 2. large or great enough to be worthy of attention or notice","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"這個項目需要相當多的時間和精力。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The project requires considerable time and effort.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"價格有顯著的增長。\",\n    \"eng\": \"There has been a considerable increase in prices.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"這是一項了不起的成就。\",\n    \"eng\": \"This is a considerable achievement.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個項目需要相當多的時間和精力。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5776,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::contend::vi","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The two companies will ____ for the leading market share.","expectedAnswer":"contend","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The two companies will ____ for the leading market share.","clozeAnswer":"contend","exampleTranslation":"這兩家公司將爭奪市場領導地位。","reference":{"eng":"contend","kk":"kənˈtɛnd","tense":"vi.","ch":"[  [    \"競爭\"  ],  [    \"爭奪\"  ],  [    \"奮鬥\"  ],  [    \"認為（某事）是真的\"  ]]","chEntries":["競爭","爭奪","奮鬥","認為是真的"],"practiceMeaning":"這兩家公司將爭奪市場領導地位。","analysis":"此字為不及物動詞，源自拉丁語contendere，由con-（一起；加強）+ tendere（伸展；努力）組成。tendere的原始印歐語詞根是\\\\*ten-（伸展）。因此，contend的核心語義是「一起努力；爭取」。語意演變上，從「一起伸展爭取」引申出「競爭」、「爭奪」，以及在辯論或論證中的「主張」或「認為」。此字作為vi.時，常接with（與……競爭/抗爭）或for（爭奪……）。","definition":"1. to try hard to deal with a difficult situation; 2. to compete with someone in order to win something; 3. to state something as a fact; compete or argue vigorously.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The two companies will contend for the leading market share.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這兩家公司將爭奪市場領導地位。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She had to contend with a lot of opposition.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她必須面對許多反對的聲音。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He contended that the evidence was insufficient.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他認為證據不足。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這兩家公司將爭奪市場領導地位。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4491,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::controller::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The pilot is the ____ of the aircraft.","expectedAnswer":"controller","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The pilot is the ____ of the aircraft.","clozeAnswer":"controller","exampleTranslation":"飛行員是飛機的操控者。","reference":{"eng":"controller","kk":"/kənˈtroʊlər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['控制者'], ['控制器'], ['（公司）財務主管']]","chEntries":["控制者","控制器","財務主管"],"practiceMeaning":"飛行員是飛機的操控者。","analysis":"源自 control (控制)。加上 -er (表示「做某事的人或物」的名詞後綴)。核心語意是「負責控制者」。引申為控制裝置（如飛機的操縱桿），或公司中負責財務管理的人員（財務主管）。","definition":"1. A person or thing that controls or directs something; 2. A device used to control the operation of a machine or system; 3. (in business) A person who manages the finances of a company or organization.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The pilot is the controller of the aircraft.\",\n    \"ch\": \"飛行員是飛機的操控者。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The thermostat is a temperature controller.\",\n    \"ch\": \"恆溫器是一個溫度控制器。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company's controller presented the quarterly financial report.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司的財務主管提出了季度財務報告。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"飛行員是飛機的操控者。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3902,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::costly::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This is a ____ mistake.","expectedAnswer":"costly","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This is a ____ mistake.","clozeAnswer":"costly","exampleTranslation":"這是一個代價高昂的錯誤。","reference":{"eng":"costly","kk":"/ˈkɔːstli/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['昂貴的'], ['代價高昂的']]","chEntries":["昂貴的","代價高昂的"],"practiceMeaning":"這是一個代價高昂的錯誤。","analysis":"由 'cost' (成本) 加上形容詞後綴 '-ly' 組成。核心是「有高成本」。指價格高昂，或需要付出巨大代價（不一定是金錢）才能達成或維持。","definition":"1. costing a great deal of money; expensive. 2. involving a great loss or sacrifice.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a costly mistake.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個代價高昂的錯誤。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Expensive cars can be very costly to maintain.\",\n    \"ch\": \"昂貴的汽車可能維護費用很高。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The war proved to be very costly for both sides.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這場戰爭對雙方都 proved to be very costly。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是一個代價高昂的錯誤。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4168,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::costs::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The steep rise in living ____ made it hard to make ends meet.","expectedAnswer":"costs","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The steep rise in living ____ made it hard to make ends meet.","clozeAnswer":"costs","exampleTranslation":"生活成本的急劇上漲使得人們難以為繼。","reference":{"eng":"costs","kk":"/kɒsts/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['費用', '成本']]","chEntries":["費用","成本"],"practiceMeaning":"生活成本的急劇上漲使得人們難以為繼。","analysis":"由 cost（成本，價值）的複數形式。源自古法語 cost（價值，報酬）。核心概念是「為獲得某物或完成某事所付出的代價」。","definition":"the amount of money needed to buy, produce, or do something","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The steep rise in living costs made it hard to make ends meet.\",\n    \"ch\": \"生活成本的急劇上漲使得人們難以為繼。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to reduce production costs.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要降低生產成本。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"What are the associated costs?\",\n    \"ch\": \"相關費用有哪些？\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"生活成本的急劇上漲使得人們難以為繼。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4541,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::crab::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He caught a large ____ at the beach.","expectedAnswer":"crab","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He caught a large ____ at the beach.","clozeAnswer":"crab","exampleTranslation":"他在海灘抓到一隻大螃蟹。","reference":{"eng":"crab","kk":"/kræb/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['螃蟹'], ['（用於指責或抱怨的）抱怨者，批評者']]","chEntries":["螃蟹","抱怨者，批評者"],"practiceMeaning":"他在海灘抓到一隻大螃蟹。","analysis":"源自古英語 'crabba'，與斯堪地那維亞語系語言中的同類詞有關。\n    1. 螃蟹：指甲殼類動物。\n    2. 抱怨者、批評者：此用法較為俚語化，指那些習慣性抱怨或挑剔的人，可能與螃蟹橫行的移動方式或其鉗子的攻擊性有關。","definition":"1. a decapod crustacean with a broad, flat body, stalked eyes, and five pairs of limbs, the first pair of which are modified as large, strong pincers.; 2. a person who is always complaining or finding fault.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He caught a large crab at the beach.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在海灘抓到一隻大螃蟹。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Don't be such a crab; try to be more positive.\",\n    \"ch\": \"別那麼愛抱怨；試著積極一點。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他在海灘抓到一隻大螃蟹。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4437,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u9::creature-of-habit::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"My grandfather is a ____; he always wakes up at 6 AM.","expectedAnswer":"creature of habit","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"My grandfather is a ____; he always wakes up at 6 AM.","clozeAnswer":"creature of habit","exampleTranslation":"我爺爺是個習慣性動物；他總是早上六點起床。","reference":{"eng":"creature of habit","kk":"/ˈkriːtʃər əv ˈhæbɪt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['習慣性動物', '習慣於某種模式的人']]","chEntries":["習慣性動物","習慣於某種模式的人"],"practiceMeaning":"我爺爺是個習慣性動物；他總是早上六點起床。","analysis":"複合名詞片語。'creature' (生物) + 'of habit' (習慣的)。指一個人的生活或行為模式非常固定，難以改變。","definition":"a person who does the same things at the same times every day and finds it difficult to change their routine.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"My grandfather is a creature of habit; he always wakes up at 6 AM.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我爺爺是個習慣性動物；他總是早上六點起床。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我爺爺是個習慣性動物；他總是早上六點起床。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4222,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::credit::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He has good ____ and can easily get a loan.","expectedAnswer":"credit","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He has good ____ and can easily get a loan.","clozeAnswer":"credit","exampleTranslation":"他的信用很好，很容易獲得貸款。","reference":{"eng":"credit","kk":"/ˈkredɪt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['信用；信譽'], ['（金融機構的）信貸；延期付款'], ['（在帳戶中的）貸方餘額；進帳'], ['功勞；讚揚']]","chEntries":["信用","信譽","信貸","延期付款","貸方餘額","進帳","功勞","讚揚"],"practiceMeaning":"他的信用很好，很容易獲得貸款。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 creditum，'credere'（相信，信任）的派生詞。核心是“相信”或“信任”。1. “信用；信譽”指個人或機構的良好聲譽，使人願意相信其承諾。2. “信貸；延期付款”指金融機構基於信任而提供的貸款或允許延期支付。3. “貸方餘額；進帳”指銀行帳戶中的正面餘額。4. “功勞；讚揚”指因某人的貢獻而給予的肯定，基於相信其功績。","definition":"1. the ability of a customer to obtain goods or services before payment, based on the trust that payment will be made in the future; 2. trust in the believe that someone will do what they are expected or supposed to do; 3. an amount of money added to an account; 4. praise or admiration for an achievement.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has good credit and can easily get a loan.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的信用很好，很容易獲得貸款。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"You can buy this item on credit.\",\n    \"ch\": \"你可以賒帳購買這個物品。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She was given credit for her hard work.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她因辛勤工作而受到讚揚。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The deposit will be shown as a credit on your statement.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這筆存款將顯示為您對帳單上的進帳。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他的信用很好，很容易獲得貸款。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6217,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::cripple::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The term '____' is considered offensive and should be avoided.","expectedAnswer":"cripple","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The term '____' is considered offensive and should be avoided.","clozeAnswer":"cripple","exampleTranslation":"「殘疾人」這個詞被認為具有冒犯性，應避免使用。","reference":{"eng":"cripple","kk":"ˈkrɪpl","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"殘疾人\"  ],  [    \"跛子\"  ]]","chEntries":["殘疾人","跛子"],"practiceMeaning":"「殘疾人」這個詞被認為具有冒犯性，應避免使用。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 crypel，意為「跛的，殘疾的」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。名詞義指因身體殘疾、損傷或疾病而導致行動不便或嚴重影響生活功能的人。然而，這個詞彙帶有貶義，通常被認為是不尊重且冒犯的，現代更傾向使用 person with a disability 或 disabled person。中文翻譯為「殘疾人；跛子」。","definition":"1. a person who is unable to walk or move properly because of a physical injury or a long-term illness (offensive term).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The term 'cripple' is considered offensive and should be avoided.\",\n    \"ch\": \"「殘疾人」這個詞被認為具有冒犯性，應避免使用。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"「殘疾人」這個詞被認為具有冒犯性，應避免使用。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4245,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::crispy::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"I love the ____ crust of the freshly baked bread.","expectedAnswer":"crispy","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"I love the ____ crust of the freshly baked bread.","clozeAnswer":"crispy","exampleTranslation":"我喜歡剛烤好的麵包酥脆的表皮。","reference":{"eng":"crispy","kk":"/ˈkrɪspi/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['酥脆的'], ['脆的']]","chEntries":["酥脆的","脆的"],"practiceMeaning":"我喜歡剛烤好的麵包酥脆的表皮。","analysis":"源自中古英語 'crisp'（捲曲、有彈性的），與古法語 'crespe'（捲曲）有關。'Crispy' 最初指物體的質地，後來引申為食品的「酥脆」口感，強調其斷裂時的聲音和質地。此詞的語意從「捲曲」延伸到「易碎、有聲響的斷裂」。","definition":"firm enough to break with a snapping sound; pleasantly hard and dry","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I love the crispy crust of the freshly baked bread.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我喜歡剛烤好的麵包酥脆的表皮。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The fried chicken was perfectly crispy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"炸雞炸得非常酥脆。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我喜歡剛烤好的麵包酥脆的表皮。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3076,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::critical::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She has a ____ attitude towards any new proposal.","expectedAnswer":"critical","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She has a ____ attitude towards any new proposal.","clozeAnswer":"critical","exampleTranslation":"她對任何新提案都持批判態度。","reference":{"eng":"critical","kk":"/ˈkrɪtɪkl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['批判性的；挑剔的'], ['關鍵性的；重要的'], ['（情況）危急的；嚴重的'], ['（意見、評論）批評性的；評價性的']]","chEntries":["批判性的","挑剔的","關鍵性的","重要的","危急的","嚴重的","批評性的","評價性的"],"practiceMeaning":"她對任何新提案都持批判態度。","analysis":"源自希臘語 'kritikos' (able to judge)，是 'critic' 的形容詞形式。核心意義是「與判斷或評價相關」。\n1. 批判性的；挑剔的：指對事物進行仔細檢查，並指出其缺點或錯誤的態度。\n2. 關鍵性的；重要的：指對某事物的發展或成功至關重要的。\n3. （情況）危急的；嚴重的：指處於非常重要或危險的關頭，需要緊急處理。\n4. （意見、評論）批評性的；評價性的：指旨在分析和評價某事物優缺點的。","definition":"1. involving careful judgment or discriminating analysis; 2. extremely important or necessary; 3. involving the danger of failure or disaster; 4. expressing adverse or disapproving comments or judgments.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a critical attitude towards any new proposal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對任何新提案都持批判態度。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a critical moment in the negotiations.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是談判中的關鍵時刻。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The patient is in critical condition.\",\n    \"ch\": \"病人的情況危急。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His critical review of the book was widely read.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對這本書的評價性評論被廣泛閱讀。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她對任何新提案都持批判態度。","sourceName":"字彙王、龍騰課本","unitName":"U39、L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3073,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::criticize::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It's easy to ____ others, but hard to improve yourself.","expectedAnswer":"criticize","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It's easy to ____ others, but hard to improve yourself.","clozeAnswer":"criticize","exampleTranslation":"批評別人很容易，但改進自己卻很難。","reference":{"eng":"criticize","kk":"/ˈkrɪtɪsaɪz/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['批評；評論'], ['（醫學）診斷']]","chEntries":["批評","評論","診斷"],"practiceMeaning":"批評別人很容易，但改進自己卻很難。","analysis":"源自希臘語 'kritēs' (judge)，經由拉丁語 'criticus' 演變而來。核心意義是「評斷」或「判斷」。\n1. 批評；評論：指基於優缺點對某人、某事或某物做出評價，通常帶有負面含義，但也可能指出改進之處。\n2. （醫學）診斷：指通過檢查判斷疾病或病症。","definition":"1. to say or write that you think someone or something is bad; 2. to judge or form an opinion about something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's easy to criticize others, but hard to improve yourself.\",\n    \"ch\": \"批評別人很容易，但改進自己卻很難。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The movie was criticized for its weak plot.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這部電影因其薄弱的情節而受到批評。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The doctor criticized the patient's condition.\",\n    \"ch\": \"醫生診斷了病人的病情。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"批評別人很容易，但改進自己卻很難。","sourceName":"字彙王、龍騰課本","unitName":"U39、L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5123,"wordRef":"字彙王::u62::custody::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The court granted her sole ____ of the children.","expectedAnswer":"custody","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The court granted her sole ____ of the children.","clozeAnswer":"custody","exampleTranslation":"法院授予她對孩子們的單獨監護權。","reference":{"eng":"custody","kk":"ˈkʌstədi","tense":"n.","ch":"[['監護權'], ['拘留'], ['保管']]","chEntries":["監護權","拘留","保管"],"practiceMeaning":"法院授予她對孩子們的單獨監護權。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 custodia，意為「看守、保護」，來自 custos（守衛者、保護者）。custos 可能來自古拉丁語 *cos-tos，與 *kes-（切、削減）或 *kew-（守護）有關。核心語意是「被看管、被保護的狀態」。在法律語境中，引申為「對子女的監護權」或「對嫌疑人的拘留」。","definition":"the care and control of a child; the state of being kept in prison or in police detention; protection or safekeeping.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The court granted her sole custody of the children.\",\n    \"ch\": \"法院授予她對孩子們的單獨監護權。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police took him into custody for questioning.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警方將他拘留以進行訊問。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"法院授予她對孩子們的單獨監護權。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U62"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4661,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::cut-in-on::idiom","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Don't ____ my conversation!","expectedAnswer":"cut in on","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Don't ____ my conversation!","clozeAnswer":"cut in on","exampleTranslation":"別打斷我的談話！","reference":{"eng":"cut in on","kk":"/kʌt ɪn ɒn/","tense":"idiom","ch":"[['插話'], ['打斷（談話）'], ['干擾（活動）']]","chEntries":["插話","打斷","干擾"],"practiceMeaning":"別打斷我的談話！","analysis":"此為固定片語。'Cut in' (插入) + 'on' (介詞，表示對象)。指在別人說話時突然介入、打斷，或者在別人做某事時干預。","definition":"to interrupt someone who is speaking; to join a conversation or activity without being invited.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Don't cut in on my conversation!\",\n    \"ch\": \"別打斷我的談話！\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He always cuts in on other people's arguments.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他總是喜歡插話干擾別人的爭論。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"別打斷我的談話！","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4407,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u9::dare::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It was a ____ to jump into the cold water.","expectedAnswer":"dare","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It was a ____ to jump into the cold water.","clozeAnswer":"dare","exampleTranslation":"跳進冷水裡是一種挑戰/冒險。","reference":{"eng":"dare","kk":"/dɛər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['（冒險的）挑戰']]","chEntries":["挑戰"],"practiceMeaning":"跳進冷水裡是一種挑戰/冒險。","analysis":"承襲動詞的語意，指一種敢於嘗試的行為，通常帶有挑戰或冒險意味。","definition":"an act of bravery or boldness.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was a dare to jump into the cold water.\",\n    \"ch\": \"跳進冷水裡是一種挑戰/冒險。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"跳進冷水裡是一種挑戰/冒險。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5627,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l7::day-off::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"I'm taking a ____ next Friday to go to the dentist.","expectedAnswer":"day off","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"I'm taking a ____ next Friday to go to the dentist.","clozeAnswer":"day off","exampleTranslation":"我下週五要請一天假去看牙醫。","reference":{"eng":"day off","kk":"deɪ ɔf","tense":"n.","ch":"[['休假日'], ['休息日']]","chEntries":["休假日","休息日"],"practiceMeaning":"我下週五要請一天假去看牙醫。","analysis":"此片語由 'day'（天）和 'off'（離開、關閉）組成。'day' 源自古英語 'dæg'，意為「一天」；'off' 源自古英語 'off'，表示「離開、遠離」。構詞學上，這是一個固定的片語，'off' 在此作為一個表示「暫停」、「停止」或「不工作」狀態的副詞或介詞，與 'day' 結合，表示「停止工作的一天」或「不工作的日子」。語意上，它代表一天無需工作、可以休息或做其他事情的時間。","definition":"A day on which one does not have to work.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I'm taking a day off next Friday to go to the dentist.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我下週五要請一天假去看牙醫。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's been a long week; I'm looking forward to my day off.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這週很漫長；我很期待我的休假日。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我下週五要請一天假去看牙醫。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3286,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::deadly::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The snake's venom is ____.","expectedAnswer":"deadly","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The snake's venom is ____.","clozeAnswer":"deadly","exampleTranslation":"蛇的毒液是致命的。","reference":{"eng":"deadly","kk":"/ˈdɛdli/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['致命的；可致死的'], ['極度的；極為的'], ['（尤指）極其安靜的；死一般的']]","chEntries":["致命的","可致死的","極度的","極為的","極其安靜的","死一般的"],"practiceMeaning":"蛇的毒液是致命的。","analysis":"由 'dead' (死的) 加上 '-ly' (形容詞後綴) 構成。直接表示與死亡相關，即可以致人於死地。也可作副詞，形容程度之深，如「極度」。","definition":"1. causing or able to cause death; 2. extreme or very great; 3. very quiet.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The snake's venom is deadly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"蛇的毒液是致命的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The situation was deadly serious.\",\n    \"ch\": \"情況極其嚴重。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The room was deadly silent after the announcement.\",\n    \"ch\": \"宣布後，房間裡一片死寂。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"蛇的毒液是致命的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4552,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::dealer::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He is a reputable car ____.","expectedAnswer":"dealer","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He is a reputable car ____.","clozeAnswer":"dealer","exampleTranslation":"他是一位信譽良好的汽車經銷商。","reference":{"eng":"dealer","kk":"/ˈdilər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['經銷商', '代理商'], ['（毒品、贓物等的）販子']]","chEntries":["經銷商","代理商","販子"],"practiceMeaning":"他是一位信譽良好的汽車經銷商。","analysis":"由 'deal' (交易、買賣) 加上名詞字尾 '-er' (表示從事某種職業或活動的人) 構成。\n    1. 經銷商、代理商：指合法買賣商品或服務的人。\n    2. 販子：指從事非法交易的人，如毒品販子 'drug dealer'。","definition":"1. a person or company whose occupation is trading in a specified commodity.; 2. a person who sells illicit drugs.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a reputable car dealer.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一位信譽良好的汽車經銷商。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police arrested a major drug dealer.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警方逮捕了一名主要的毒品販子。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他是一位信譽良好的汽車經銷商。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5124,"wordRef":"字彙王::u62::debris::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Rescuers searched through the ____ for survivors.","expectedAnswer":"debris","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Rescuers searched through the ____ for survivors.","clozeAnswer":"debris","exampleTranslation":"救援人員在瓦礫中搜尋倖存者。","reference":{"eng":"debris","kk":"ˈdeɪbriː","tense":"n.","ch":"[['碎片'], ['殘骸'], ['瓦礫']]","chEntries":["碎片","殘骸","瓦礫"],"practiceMeaning":"救援人員在瓦礫中搜尋倖存者。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 debriser，意為「打碎、破壞」，由 de-（否定、徹底）+ briser（打碎）組成。briser 來自拉丁語 brisare（打碎），可能是來自 *brevianis（短暫的）。核心語意是「被打破、被破壞後留下的零散物」。","definition":"scattered pieces of something left after it has been destroyed or broken; rubble.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Rescuers searched through the debris for survivors.\",\n    \"ch\": \"救援人員在瓦礫中搜尋倖存者。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The explosion left a trail of debris.\",\n    \"ch\": \"爆炸留下了碎片痕跡。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"救援人員在瓦礫中搜尋倖存者。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U62"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4114,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::decade::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company has been successful for over a ____.","expectedAnswer":"decade","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company has been successful for over a ____.","clozeAnswer":"decade","exampleTranslation":"這家公司已經成功經營了十多年。","reference":{"eng":"decade","kk":"/ˈdɛkeɪd/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['十年']]","chEntries":["十年"],"practiceMeaning":"這家公司已經成功經營了十多年。","analysis":"源自希臘語 dekas，意為「十個」。引申為一個持續十年的時間段。","definition":"a period of ten years","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company has been successful for over a decade.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司已經成功經營了十多年。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The world has changed a lot in the past decade.\",\n    \"ch\": \"在過去的十年裡，世界發生了巨大的變化。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He lived abroad for a decade.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在國外住了十年。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這家公司已經成功經營了十多年。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4591,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::decayed::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The old house looked ____ and abandoned.","expectedAnswer":"decayed","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The old house looked ____ and abandoned.","clozeAnswer":"decayed","exampleTranslation":"這座老房子看起來腐朽且被遺棄。","reference":{"eng":"decayed","kk":"/dɪˈkeɪd/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['腐爛的', '衰退的']]","chEntries":["腐爛的","衰退的"],"practiceMeaning":"這座老房子看起來腐朽且被遺棄。","analysis":"這是動詞 'decay' (腐爛、衰退) 的過去分詞，用作形容詞。 'decay' 源自拉丁語 'decadere'，'de-' (down) 和 'cadere' (to fall - 落下)。\n    1. 腐爛的：指有機物因分解而變得腐敗、發臭。\n    2. 衰退的：指事物（如建築、健康、道德）逐漸惡化、衰敗。","definition":"1. (of organic matter) rot or decompose through the action of bacteria and fungi.; 2. (of something in existence) decline or deteriorate.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The old house looked decayed and abandoned.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座老房子看起來腐朽且被遺棄。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He suffered from decayed teeth.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的牙齒腐爛了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The once-grand theater was now decayed.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座曾經宏偉的劇院如今已衰敗不堪。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這座老房子看起來腐朽且被遺棄。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5713,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l9::definite::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need a ____ answer by Friday.","expectedAnswer":"definite","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need a ____ answer by Friday.","clozeAnswer":"definite","exampleTranslation":"我們週五前需要一個確切的答覆。","reference":{"eng":"definite","kk":"ˈdefɪnɪt","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['明確的'], ['確定的'], ['清晰的'], ['一定的']]","chEntries":["明確的","確定的","清晰的","一定的"],"practiceMeaning":"我們週五前需要一個確切的答覆。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 definitus（被限定的，明確的），是 definire（定義，限定，闡明）的過去分詞。構詞上，'de-'（向下，完全）+ 'finire'（限定，來自 finis，邊界，結束）。核心語意是「完全被限定、明確，沒有模糊之處」。它描述的是事物界限清楚、意義明確、無可懷疑的狀態。","definition":"clearly stated or explained; able to be seen, heard, or understood clearly; not vague or doubtful; clearly defined or determined.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need a definite answer by Friday.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們週五前需要一個確切的答覆。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There is no definite proof of his involvement.\",\n    \"ch\": \"沒有確鑿的證據證明他參與其中。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們週五前需要一個確切的答覆。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5712,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l9::definitely::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"I will ____ be there on time.","expectedAnswer":"definitely","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"I will ____ be there on time.","clozeAnswer":"definitely","exampleTranslation":"我肯定會準時到那裡。","reference":{"eng":"definitely","kk":"ˈdefɪnətli","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['肯定地'], ['無疑地'], ['確實地']]","chEntries":["肯定地","無疑地","確實地"],"practiceMeaning":"我肯定會準時到那裡。","analysis":"此字由形容詞 'definite' 加上副詞化後綴 '-ly' 構成。'definite' 源自拉丁語 definitus（被限定的，明確的），是 definire（定義，限定，闡明）的過去分詞。構詞上，'de-'（向下，完全）+ 'finire'（限定，來自 finis，邊界，結束）。核心語意是「完全被限定、明確」。'-ly' 後綴使形容詞轉化為副詞，表示「以……的方式」。因此，'definitely' 的核心語意是「以一種明確、無疑、毫無疑問的方式」。","definition":"in a way that is clearly defined and clearly stated; without doubt; certainly.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I will definitely be there on time.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我肯定會準時到那裡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She definitely knows the answer.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她肯定知道答案。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我肯定會準時到那裡。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6070,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::defy::vt","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The soldiers were ordered to obey, but they chose to ____ the command.","expectedAnswer":"defy","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The soldiers were ordered to obey, but they chose to ____ the command.","clozeAnswer":"defy","exampleTranslation":"士兵們被命令服從，但他們選擇違抗命令。","reference":{"eng":"defy","kk":"dɪˈfaɪ","tense":"vt.","ch":"[  [    \"違抗\"  ],  [    \"藐視\"  ],  [    \"挑戰\"  ],  [    \"不顧\"  ]]","chEntries":["違抗","藐視","挑戰","不顧"],"practiceMeaning":"士兵們被命令服從，但他們選擇違抗命令。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 defier，來自拉丁語 dis-（away, apart）和 fidere（to trust），引申為「懷疑，不信任」。核心語義是「不信任」或「懷疑」，引申為「拒絕信任」、「反抗」或「違抗」。構詞上，de- 在此表示「否定」或「相反」，-fy 是來自拉丁語 facere（to make）的後綴，表示「使……」。Defy 的核心是「對權威、規則或預期的反抗」。","definition":"1. openly resist or refuse to obey; 2. challenge (someone or something) to do something, especially in a way that shows you are not afraid of them or have no respect for them; 3. be impossible to do or achieve.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The soldiers were ordered to obey, but they chose to defy the command.\",\n    \"ch\": \"士兵們被命令服從，但他們選擇違抗命令。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She defied her parents' wishes and pursued her dream.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她違背了父母的意願，追逐自己的夢想。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The building defied gravity, appearing to float.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座建築物挑戰了地心引力，看似漂浮著。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"士兵們被命令服從，但他們選擇違抗命令。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4728,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::delay::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The bad weather will ____ the construction project.","expectedAnswer":"delay","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The bad weather will ____ the construction project.","clozeAnswer":"delay","exampleTranslation":"惡劣的天氣將會延遲這個建築專案。","reference":{"eng":"delay","kk":"/dɪˈleɪ/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['延遲'], ['耽擱']]","chEntries":["延遲","耽擱"],"practiceMeaning":"惡劣的天氣將會延遲這個建築專案。","analysis":"動詞形式，指使某事發生得比預期晚，或使某人耽擱。","definition":"1. To make something happen later than expected. 2. To cause someone or something to be late or slow.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The bad weather will delay the construction project.\",\n    \"ch\": \"惡劣的天氣將會延遲這個建築專案。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Don't delay your visit to the doctor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"不要延遲看醫生的時間。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"惡劣的天氣將會延遲這個建築專案。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6166,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::democrat::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He is a lifelong ____ who believes in equality.","expectedAnswer":"democrat","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He is a lifelong ____ who believes in equality.","clozeAnswer":"democrat","exampleTranslation":"他是一位畢生信奉民主、相信平等的民主主義者。","reference":{"eng":"democrat","kk":"ˈdɛməkræt","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"民主主義者\"  ],  [    \"民主黨員\"  ]]","chEntries":["民主主義者","民主黨員"],"practiceMeaning":"他是一位畢生信奉民主、相信平等的民主主義者。","analysis":"此字源自希臘語 dēmokratēs，意為「民主的支持者」，由 dēmos (people) + kratos (power, rule) 組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 dēmos「人民」和 kratos「權力、統治」是其核心語意來源。作為名詞，其核心語義是指信奉或支持民主政治制度的人。在美國，通常特指美國民主黨黨員。","definition":"1. a person who believes in or supports democracy; 2. a member of the Democratic Party.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a lifelong democrat who believes in equality.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一位畢生信奉民主、相信平等的民主主義者。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The senator is a prominent democrat.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位參議員是一位著名的民主黨員。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The country is governed by democrats.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個國家由民主主義者統治。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他是一位畢生信奉民主、相信平等的民主主義者。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6219,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::deploy::vt","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The army decided to ____ more troops to the border.","expectedAnswer":"deploy","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The army decided to ____ more troops to the border.","clozeAnswer":"deploy","exampleTranslation":"軍隊決定向邊境部署更多部隊。","reference":{"eng":"deploy","kk":"dɪˈplɔɪ","tense":"vt.","ch":"[  [    \"部署\"  ],  [    \"調遣\"  ],  [    \"展開\"  ],  [    \"運用\"  ]]","chEntries":["部署","調遣","展開","運用"],"practiceMeaning":"軍隊決定向邊境部署更多部隊。","analysis":"此字源自法語 déployer，由 de-（表示否定或撤銷）和 plier（折疊，捲起）組成，意為「展開，鋪開」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作及物動詞時，核心語義是將部隊、設備或人員有計劃地調往特定地點或投入使用。也可引申為「展開」或「運用」某種策略、資源或能力。此及物動詞義必須接受詞，例如 deploy troops、deploy resources、deploy a strategy。中文翻譯為「部署；調遣；展開；運用」。","definition":"1. to move troops or equipment to a place or position where they can be used in an operation; 2. to use something or someone effectively; 3. to spread out or unfold.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The army decided to deploy more troops to the border.\",\n    \"ch\": \"軍隊決定向邊境部署更多部隊。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company will deploy its new marketing strategy next month.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司將於下月運用其新的市場行銷策略。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They deployed a fleet of ships to the area.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們調遣了一支艦隊到該地區。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"軍隊決定向邊境部署更多部隊。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5833,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::descriptive::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The author provided a ____ account of the journey.","expectedAnswer":"descriptive","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The author provided a ____ account of the journey.","clozeAnswer":"descriptive","exampleTranslation":"作者提供了關於這次旅程的詳細描述。","reference":{"eng":"descriptive","kk":"dɪˈskrɪptɪv","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"描述性的\"  ],  [    \"描寫性的\"  ],  [    \"詳盡的\"  ]]","chEntries":["描述性的","描寫性的","詳盡的"],"practiceMeaning":"作者提供了關於這次旅程的詳細描述。","analysis":"此字由名詞 'description' 加上形容詞字尾 '-ive' 構成。'Description' 源自拉丁語 'descriptio'，由 'de-' (down) 和 'scribere' (to write) 構成，字面意思是「寫下」（細節）。'-ive' 是常見的形容詞字尾，表示「具有……性質的」或「傾向於……」。因此，'descriptive' 指「具有描述性質的」或「用來描述的」。它強調的是對事物特徵、細節進行刻畫和描繪的功能。例如，也可指「詳盡的」敘述。","definition":"1. Serving or seeking to describe, especially by giving full, accurate details.; 2. Relating to or characteristic of description.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The author provided a descriptive account of the journey.\",\n    \"ch\": \"作者提供了關於這次旅程的詳細描述。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The book uses descriptive language.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本書使用了描寫性的語言。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He gave a descriptive report of the event.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對這次事件做了一個詳盡的報告。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The teacher asked for a descriptive essay.\",\n    \"ch\": \"老師要求寫一篇描寫性的文章。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"作者提供了關於這次旅程的詳細描述。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5702,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l9::despair::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He sank into ____ after failing the exam.","expectedAnswer":"despair","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He sank into ____ after failing the exam.","clozeAnswer":"despair","exampleTranslation":"考試失敗後，他陷入了絕望。","reference":{"eng":"despair","kk":"dɪˈsper","tense":"n.","ch":"[['絕望'], ['失望']]","chEntries":["絕望","失望"],"practiceMeaning":"考試失敗後，他陷入了絕望。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 desespoir，由 de-（表示『否定』或『失去』，來自拉丁語 de-）+ espoir（希望，來自拉丁語 sperare，意為『希望』）構成。構詞上，'de-' 表示『失去』，'espoir' 表示『希望』。核心語意是「失去希望的狀態」。當希望完全喪失時，便產生極度的痛苦和沮喪感，即「絕望」。","definition":"the complete loss or absence of hope.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He sank into despair after failing the exam.\",\n    \"ch\": \"考試失敗後，他陷入了絕望。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The situation seemed hopeless, filling them with despair.\",\n    \"ch\": \"情況看似無望，讓他們充滿絕望。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"考試失敗後，他陷入了絕望。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4137,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::detect::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The system can ____ unauthorized access.","expectedAnswer":"detect","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The system can ____ unauthorized access.","clozeAnswer":"detect","exampleTranslation":"該系統可以偵測未經授權的訪問。","reference":{"eng":"detect","kk":"/dɪˈtɛkt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['偵測', '探測'], ['察覺', '發現']]","chEntries":["偵測","探測","察覺","發現"],"practiceMeaning":"該系統可以偵測未經授權的訪問。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 detectare，由 de-（揭示）+ tegere（覆蓋）組成。核心概念是「揭開覆蓋物」、「發現隱藏之物」。引申為利用儀器發現、識別或察覺。","definition":"1. discover or identify the presence or existence of; 2. perceive or recognize","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The system can detect unauthorized access.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該系統可以偵測未經授權的訪問。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Scientists detected a new planet.\",\n    \"ch\": \"科學家們探測到了一顆新行星。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She detected a note of sadness in his voice.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在他語氣中察覺到一絲悲傷。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該系統可以偵測未經授權的訪問。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5835,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::dilemma::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He faced a ____: either tell the truth and hurt his friend, or lie and betray his principles.","expectedAnswer":"dilemma","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He faced a ____: either tell the truth and hurt his friend, or lie and betray his principles.","clozeAnswer":"dilemma","exampleTranslation":"他面臨兩難：要么說實話傷害朋友，要么撒謊背叛自己的原則。","reference":{"eng":"dilemma","kk":"dɪˈlɛmə","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"困境\"  ],  [    \"兩難\"  ],  [    \"進退兩難\"  ],  [    \"難題\"  ]]","chEntries":["困境","兩難","進退兩難","難題"],"practiceMeaning":"他面臨兩難：要么說實話傷害朋友，要么撒謊背叛自己的原則。","analysis":"此字源自希臘語 'dilemma'，由 'di-' (two) 和 'lemma' (premise, assumption, proposition) 構成。原意為「兩項前提」或「兩難的論證」。在邏輯學中，'dilemma' 指一種論證形式，其中兩項可能的選擇都導向不希望的結果。在現代英語中，'dilemma' 指一種需要做出艱難選擇的處境，通常是在兩種或多種相互矛盾的選項之間，且每個選項都有其不利之處。核心語意是「必須在兩個或多個不理想的選項中做出選擇的困境」。例如，也可指「一項難以解決的問題」。","definition":"1. A situation in which a difficult choice has to be made between two or more alternatives, especially equally undesirable ones.; 2. A problem offering no satisfactory solution.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He faced a dilemma: either tell the truth and hurt his friend, or lie and betray his principles.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他面臨兩難：要么說實話傷害朋友，要么撒謊背叛自己的原則。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company is in a dilemma about whether to expand or consolidate.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司在是否擴張或整合的問題上陷入了困境。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's a classic ethical dilemma.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個經典的道德困境。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The scientist faced the dilemma of publishing his findings or keeping them secret.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位科學家面臨著是發表研究結果還是保密的兩難。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他面臨兩難：要么說實話傷害朋友，要么撒謊背叛自己的原則。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5040,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::disconnect::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There was a ____ between his words and his actions.","expectedAnswer":"disconnect","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There was a ____ between his words and his actions.","clozeAnswer":"disconnect","exampleTranslation":"他的言行之間存在不一致。","reference":{"eng":"disconnect","kk":"ˌdɪskəˈnekt","tense":"n.","ch":"[['斷開'], ['分離'], ['不連貫']]","chEntries":["斷開","分離","不連貫"],"practiceMeaning":"他的言行之間存在不一致。","analysis":"此字由否定前綴 dis-（分離、相反）和名詞 connection（連接）的動詞 connect（連接）派生。dis- 的否定作用與 connect 的「連接」意義結合，構成了「斷開連接、分離」的名詞用法。此名詞指「斷開的狀態」或「不連貫的感覺」，可指物理上的斷開，也可指抽象概念上的「失去聯繫」或「不一致」。","definition":"1. a state of being disconnected; 2. a lack of connection or continuity.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was a disconnect between his words and his actions.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的言行之間存在不一致。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We experienced a brief disconnect with the internet.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們經歷了一次短暫的網路斷線。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他的言行之間存在不一致。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5345,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l1::disgust::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The sight of the decaying food filled him with ____.","expectedAnswer":"disgust","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The sight of the decaying food filled him with ____.","clozeAnswer":"disgust","exampleTranslation":"腐爛食物的景象讓他感到厭惡。","reference":{"eng":"disgust","kk":"dɪsˈɡʌst","tense":"n.","ch":"[['厭惡'], ['反感']]","chEntries":["厭惡","反感"],"practiceMeaning":"腐爛食物的景象讓他感到厭惡。","analysis":"此字源自法語 dégoût，由 dé-（否定、反對）+ goût（味道、喜好）組成。原始概念是「失去對某事物的喜好」或「味道不對」。構詞上，dis- 在此是加強語氣的否定字首，表示「徹底地」，gust- 來自 gustus（味道，來自拉丁語 gustare「品嚐」）。核心語意為「極度的不喜歡或厭煩」，通常是對令人不快的事物產生的強烈反感。","definition":"a feeling of revulsion or strong disapproval aroused by something unpleasant or offensive.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The sight of the decaying food filled him with disgust.\",\n    \"ch\": \"腐爛食物的景象讓他感到厭惡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her actions were met with disgust by the public.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的行為引起了公眾的反感。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"腐爛食物的景象讓他感到厭惡。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3077,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::dismiss::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The boss decided to ____ the lazy employee.","expectedAnswer":"dismiss","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The boss decided to ____ the lazy employee.","clozeAnswer":"dismiss","exampleTranslation":"老闆決定解僱那個懶惰的員工。","reference":{"eng":"dismiss","kk":"/dɪsˈmɪs/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['解僱；遣散'], ['讓…離開；不予理會'], ['駁回（請求、案件）']]","chEntries":["解僱","遣散","讓…離開","不予理會","駁回"],"practiceMeaning":"老闆決定解僱那個懶惰的員工。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'dismissus'，'dis-' (away) + 'mittere' (to send)。核心意義是「送走」或「不再考慮」。\n1. 解僱；遣散：指終止僱傭關係，讓員工離開工作崗位。\n2. 讓…離開；不予理會：指不再關注、考慮或接受某人或某事。\n3. 駁回（請求、案件）：指法院或權威機構否定或拒絕某項請求、主張或訴訟。","definition":"1. to tell someone that they can go; 2. to remove someone from their job; 3. to decide that something or someone is not important and not worth considering; 4. to refuse to accept something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The boss decided to dismiss the lazy employee.\",\n    \"ch\": \"老闆決定解僱那個懶惰的員工。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She dismissed his comments as unimportant.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她認為他的評論不重要，不予理會。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The judge dismissed the case due to lack of evidence.\",\n    \"ch\": \"法官因證據不足而駁回了此案。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"老闆決定解僱那個懶惰的員工。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5041,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::distract::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Don't ____ the driver while he is operating the vehicle.","expectedAnswer":"distract","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Don't ____ the driver while he is operating the vehicle.","clozeAnswer":"distract","exampleTranslation":"開車時不要讓司機分心。","reference":{"eng":"distract","kk":"dɪˈstrækt","tense":"v.","ch":"[['使分心'], ['分散（注意力）'], ['干擾']]","chEntries":["使分心","分散","干擾"],"practiceMeaning":"開車時不要讓司機分心。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語distrahere，由 dis-（分離）+ trahere（拖曳、拉）組成，原意為「將事物拉開、分散」。在英語中，distract 意為「分散某人的注意力，使其無法集中於某事」，語意上直接體現了「將注意力從一處拉開」的詞源含義。OCR 掃描時可能將 's' 誤判為 '5' 或 'f'，或 't' 誤判為 'l'。此處修正為 distract。","definition":"1. to prevent someone from giving their full attention to something; 2. to divert the attention of (someone) from something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Don't distract the driver while he is operating the vehicle.\",\n    \"ch\": \"開車時不要讓司機分心。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Loud noises can distract students during an exam.\",\n    \"ch\": \"嘈雜的聲音可能會在考試期間分散學生的注意力。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"開車時不要讓司機分心。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5493,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::disturb::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Please don't ____ the baby while she's sleeping.","expectedAnswer":"disturb","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Please don't ____ the baby while she's sleeping.","clozeAnswer":"disturb","exampleTranslation":"睡覺時請不要打擾寶寶。","reference":{"eng":"disturb","kk":"dɪˈstɜrb","tense":"v.","ch":"[['打擾'], ['干擾'], ['擾亂']]","chEntries":["打擾","干擾","擾亂"],"practiceMeaning":"睡覺時請不要打擾寶寶。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'disturbare'，由 'dis-'（表示否定、分離或加強）和 'turbare'（使混亂、擾亂，來自 'turba'「騷亂、混亂」）構成。因此，'disturb' 的核心語意是「使陷入混亂、擾亂原本的平靜或秩序」。它可以用來指「打擾某人」或「擾亂某事物的正常狀態」。","definition":"1. Interference with the normal arrangement or functioning of.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please don't disturb the baby while she's sleeping.\",\n    \"ch\": \"睡覺時請不要打擾寶寶。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The loud noise disturbed the neighbors.\",\n    \"ch\": \"巨大的噪音打擾了鄰居。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Unforeseen events disturbed their plans.\",\n    \"ch\": \"意想不到的事件擾亂了他們的計劃。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"睡覺時請不要打擾寶寶。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5494,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::disturbance::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The loud music caused a ____ in the neighborhood.","expectedAnswer":"disturbance","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The loud music caused a ____ in the neighborhood.","clozeAnswer":"disturbance","exampleTranslation":"吵鬧的音樂引起了社區的騷動。","reference":{"eng":"disturbance","kk":"dɪˈstɜrbəns","tense":"n.","ch":"[['干擾'], ['騷動'], ['妨礙']]","chEntries":["干擾","騷動","妨礙"],"practiceMeaning":"吵鬧的音樂引起了社區的騷動。","analysis":"此字由動詞 'disturb'（打擾、干擾）加上名詞字尾 '-ance'（來自拉丁語 '-antia'）構成。'-ance' 用來形成表示「行為、狀態或過程」的名詞。因此，'disturbance' 指的是「打擾、干擾、擾亂」的行為或狀態。它是一個抽象名詞，描述了某種東西打破了原本的平靜、秩序或正常狀態的情況。","definition":"1. The interruption of a settled or peaceful condition.; 2. An act of disturbing.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The loud music caused a disturbance in the neighborhood.\",\n    \"ch\": \"吵鬧的音樂引起了社區的騷動。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We experienced a power disturbance during the storm.\",\n    \"ch\": \"風暴期間我們經歷了電力中斷（干擾）。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police were called to deal with a disturbance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警察被召來處理一起騷亂事件。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"吵鬧的音樂引起了社區的騷動。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5492,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::dive::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He loves to ____ into the ocean.","expectedAnswer":"dive","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He loves to ____ into the ocean.","clozeAnswer":"dive","exampleTranslation":"他喜歡潛入大海。","reference":{"eng":"dive","kk":"daɪv","tense":"v.","ch":"[['潛水'], ['跳水'], ['俯衝']]","chEntries":["潛水","跳水","俯衝"],"practiceMeaning":"他喜歡潛入大海。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 'diver'，可能是從古法語 'diver'（改道）或與荷蘭語 'duiken'（潛水）相關。其詞源不太確定，但最早的意思是「潛入水中」。後來，這個詞的語意擴展到「身體向前猛衝的動作」，例如「跳水」（從高處躍入水中）或「俯衝」（飛機或動物快速向下飛）。核心語意是「快速、突然地進入或向下移動」。","definition":"1. Plunge headlong into water with one's head and shoulders first.; 2. Jump or plunge from a height into water with one's feet first.; 3. (Of an aircraft or bird) descend rapidly.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He loves to dive into the ocean.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他喜歡潛入大海。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The diver performed a perfect triple somersault.\",\n    \"ch\": \"跳水運動員完成了一個完美的後空翻三周。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The eagle dived towards its prey.\",\n    \"ch\": \"老鷹俯衝向牠的獵物。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他喜歡潛入大海。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4549,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::dock::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ferry will ____ at 8 AM.","expectedAnswer":"dock","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ferry will ____ at 8 AM.","clozeAnswer":"dock","exampleTranslation":"渡輪將於上午八點靠岸。","reference":{"eng":"dock","kk":"/dɒk/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['（船隻）入港', '停靠碼頭'], ['剪短', '削除（尾巴、翅膀等）']]","chEntries":["入港","停靠碼頭","剪短","削除"],"practiceMeaning":"渡輪將於上午八點靠岸。","analysis":"動詞用法源自名詞。\n    1. 入港、停靠碼頭：指船隻進入港口或停泊在碼頭。\n    2. 剪短、削除：指將動物的尾巴或翅膀剪短，減少其長度，類似於將其「停靠」在某個較短的狀態。 'dock a dog's tail' (剪斷狗的尾巴)。","definition":"1. (of a ship) to come into or be brought into a dock.; 2. to cut off the tail of (an animal).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The ferry will dock at 8 AM.\",\n    \"ch\": \"渡輪將於上午八點靠岸。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The rabbit's ears were docked.\",\n    \"ch\": \"兔子的耳朵被剪短了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"渡輪將於上午八點靠岸。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4355,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::domestic::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company focuses on the ____ market.","expectedAnswer":"domestic","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company focuses on the ____ market.","clozeAnswer":"domestic","exampleTranslation":"該公司專注於國內市場。","reference":{"eng":"domestic","kk":"/dəˈmɛstɪk/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['國內的；本土的'], ['家庭的；家用的'], ['（動物）馴養的']]","chEntries":["國內的","本土的","家庭的","家用的","馴養的"],"practiceMeaning":"該公司專注於國內市場。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'domesticus'，意為『家裡的』，來自 'domus' (house)。1. 指發生在國家『國內』的，與『國際』相對。2. 指與『家庭』相關的，如『家庭生活』、『家務』。3. 指被人類馴養的動物，如『家禽』、『家畜』，與『野生的』相對。","definition":"existing or occurring in a country or in domestic policy; relating to the running of a home or to family relations; kept or living at home and not wild","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company focuses on the domestic market.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司專注於國內市場。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Domestic chores include cooking and cleaning.\",\n    \"ch\": \"家務包括烹飪和清潔。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Dogs are domestic animals.\",\n    \"ch\": \"狗是馴養的動物。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該公司專注於國內市場。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U8、L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5780,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::donation::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We received a generous ____ from a local business.","expectedAnswer":"donation","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We received a generous ____ from a local business.","clozeAnswer":"donation","exampleTranslation":"我們收到了一家本地企業的大筆捐款。","reference":{"eng":"donation","kk":"doʊˈneɪʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"捐贈\"  ],  [    \"捐款\"  ],  [    \"捐獻物\"  ]]","chEntries":["捐贈","捐款","捐獻物"],"practiceMeaning":"我們收到了一家本地企業的大筆捐款。","analysis":"此字為名詞，構詞自donate（捐贈）+ -ion（名詞字尾，表示「行為；狀態；結果」）。-ion字尾源自拉丁語-io。donate源自拉丁語donare（給予；捐贈）。因此，donation的核心語義是指「捐贈的行為」或「被捐贈的物品或金錢」。語意演變上，由動詞「捐贈」的動作，發展為抽象的「捐贈行為」和具體的「捐贈物」。","definition":"1. money or goods given to help a charity or other organization; 2. the act of giving something, especially to a charity.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We received a generous donation from a local business.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們收到了一家本地企業的大筆捐款。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The hospital relies on donations to fund its research.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家醫院依靠捐款來資助其研究。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Your donation will make a real difference.\",\n    \"ch\": \"您的捐贈將帶來真正的改變。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們收到了一家本地企業的大筆捐款。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3981,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u3::drugstore::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"I need to go to the ____ to buy some aspirin.","expectedAnswer":"drugstore","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"I need to go to the ____ to buy some aspirin.","clozeAnswer":"drugstore","exampleTranslation":"我需要去藥房買點阿斯匹靈。","reference":{"eng":"drugstore","kk":"/ˈdrʌɡstɔːr/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['藥房', '藥妝店']]","chEntries":["藥房","藥妝店"],"practiceMeaning":"我需要去藥房買點阿斯匹靈。","analysis":"由 'drug' (藥品) 和 'store' (商店) 組成。傳統上指販售藥品的商店，現代也常販售化妝品、個人護理用品等。","definition":"a shop where medicines and other goods are sold.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I need to go to the drugstore to buy some aspirin.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我需要去藥房買點阿斯匹靈。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我需要去藥房買點阿斯匹靈。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4542,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::dumb::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He was born ____ and mute.","expectedAnswer":"dumb","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He was born ____ and mute.","clozeAnswer":"dumb","exampleTranslation":"他生來就又啞又不能說話。","reference":{"eng":"dumb","kk":"/dʌm/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['啞的', '無法說話的'], ['愚蠢的', '笨拙的'], ['（機器等）不發聲的，靜止的']]","chEntries":["啞的","無法說話的","愚蠢的","笨拙的","不發聲的，靜止的"],"practiceMeaning":"他生來就又啞又不能說話。","analysis":"源自古英語 'dumb'，意為 'mute, silent' (啞的、沉默的)。\n    1. 啞的：指無法說話的能力。\n    2. 愚蠢的：指缺乏智慧或理解力，是比較粗俗的用法。\n    3. 不發聲的、靜止的：指機器或設備沒有發出聲音，或處於靜止狀態，如 'dumb waiter' (傳菜電梯)，'dumb terminal' (啞終端)。","definition":"1. unable to speak.; 2. stupid; foolish.; 3. (of a device or machine) not having or performing the functions of speech or sound.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was born dumb and mute.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他生來就又啞又不能說話。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Don't be dumb; think before you speak.\",\n    \"ch\": \"別那麼笨；說話前先想想。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The dumb waiter brought the food up.\",\n    \"ch\": \"傳菜電梯把食物送上來了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他生來就又啞又不能說話。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4185,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::dust::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Please ____ the shelves regularly.","expectedAnswer":"dust","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Please ____ the shelves regularly.","clozeAnswer":"dust","exampleTranslation":"請定期擦拭架子上的灰塵。","reference":{"eng":"dust","kk":"/dʌst/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['撣去…的灰塵'], ['（灑上）粉末']]","chEntries":["撣去…的灰塵","粉末"],"practiceMeaning":"請定期擦拭架子上的灰塵。","analysis":"動詞 'dust' 源於名詞 'dust'，表示移除灰塵的動作（'dust off'）。此義項的詞源可追溯至古英語 'dustian'（撣去灰塵）。另一義項是“灑上粉末”，例如 'dust with flour'（用麵粉撒）。這兩個義項都與灰塵或粉末的物理特性相關：一個是清除，一個是覆蓋。","definition":"1. to remove the dust from something by wiping it with a cloth; 2. to sprinkle something with a powder such as flour or sugar.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please dust the shelves regularly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請定期擦拭架子上的灰塵。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Dust the cake with powdered sugar.\",\n    \"ch\": \"給蛋糕撒上糖粉。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He dusted off his old books.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他撣去了舊書上的灰塵。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"請定期擦拭架子上的灰塵。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3145,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::dynamic::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Innovation is a key ____ for business growth.","expectedAnswer":"dynamic","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Innovation is a key ____ for business growth.","clozeAnswer":"dynamic","exampleTranslation":"創新是企業成長的關鍵動力。","reference":{"eng":"dynamic","kk":"/daɪˈnæmɪk/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['動力；驅動力'], ['（物理學）動力學']]","chEntries":["動力","驅動力","動力學"],"practiceMeaning":"創新是企業成長的關鍵動力。","analysis":"名詞用法，源自形容詞 'dynamic'。指「動力」或「驅動力」，即推動事物發展變化的力量或因素。在物理學中，'dynamics'（通常用複數）指研究物體運動或力的學科，即動力學。","definition":"1. a force that stimulates change or progress; 2. (usually dynamics) the branch of mechanics concerned with the motion of bodies under the action of forces.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Innovation is a key dynamic for business growth.\",\n    \"ch\": \"創新是企業成長的關鍵動力。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The study of the dynamics of a system can reveal its behavior.\",\n    \"ch\": \"對一個系統動力學的研究可以揭示其行為。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"創新是企業成長的關鍵動力。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3080,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::dynasty::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The Ming ____ was known for its porcelain.","expectedAnswer":"Dynasty","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The Ming ____ was known for its porcelain.","clozeAnswer":"Dynasty","exampleTranslation":"明朝以其瓷器聞名。","reference":{"eng":"dynasty","kk":"/ˈdaɪnəsti/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['王朝；朝代'], ['（某一家族或團體的）長時期統治；一系列']]","chEntries":["王朝","朝代","長時期統治","一系列"],"practiceMeaning":"明朝以其瓷器聞名。","analysis":"源自希臘語 'dynasteia' (power, dominion)，'dynastēs' (ruler)。核心意義是「統治」或「權力」。\n1. 王朝；朝代：指由同一家族在一個國家中連續執政的時期。\n2. （某一家族或團體的）長時期統治；一系列：指在某個領域（如商業、政治）由同一家族或團體長期佔據主導地位，或一系列連續發生的事物。","definition":"1. a series of rulers or leaders of the same family; 2. a period of time in which one family rules a country; 3. a succession of rulers from the same family or line.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The Ming Dynasty was known for its porcelain.\",\n    \"ch\": \"明朝以其瓷器聞名。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The family built a business dynasty that lasted for generations.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個家族建立了一個延續了幾代的商業王朝。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"明朝以其瓷器聞名。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4191,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::educate::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The school aims to ____ children from diverse backgrounds.","expectedAnswer":"educate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The school aims to ____ children from diverse backgrounds.","clozeAnswer":"educate","exampleTranslation":"這所學校旨在教育來自不同背景的兒童。","reference":{"eng":"educate","kk":"/ˈedʒukeɪt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['教育；培養'], ['訓練；教授'], ['（用特定觀點）教育，教導（使有某種觀念）']]","chEntries":["教育","培養","訓練","教授","教育，教導"],"practiceMeaning":"這所學校旨在教育來自不同背景的兒童。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 educare，意為“引導出來，培養”，來自 ēdūcere（引導，提出）。'ē-'（出）+ 'dūcere'（引導）。核心意義是“引導，培養”。1. “教育；培養”是最普遍的意義，指傳授知識和技能。2. “訓練；教授”更側重於具體的技能傳授。3. “教導（使有某種觀念）”則指通過教育來塑造人的思想和價值觀。","definition":"1. to teach or train someone, especially at a school or university; 2. to provide knowledge and understanding; 3. to provide with a particular set of ideas or beliefs.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The school aims to educate children from diverse backgrounds.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這所學校旨在教育來自不同背景的兒童。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was educated in England.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在英國接受教育。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to educate the public about the risks.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要向公眾灌輸有關風險的知識。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這所學校旨在教育來自不同背景的兒童。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3280,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::elastic::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This waistband is made of ____ material.","expectedAnswer":"elastic","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This waistband is made of ____ material.","clozeAnswer":"elastic","exampleTranslation":"這條褲子的腰帶是彈性材料製成的。","reference":{"eng":"elastic","kk":"/ɪˈlæstɪk/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['有彈性的；彈性的'], ['（價格、需求等）可變的；靈活的']]","chEntries":["有彈性的","彈性的","可變的","靈活的"],"practiceMeaning":"這條褲子的腰帶是彈性材料製成的。","analysis":"源自希臘語 'elaunein' (打，鞭打) 的過去分詞 'elastos'，意為「可延展的」。指能夠恢復原狀的物質的屬性，引申至非物質領域，表示具備伸縮性或可調節性。","definition":"1. able to stretch and return to its original shape; 2. able to be changed or adapted to meet different circumstances.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This waistband is made of elastic material.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這條褲子的腰帶是彈性材料製成的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company has an elastic work schedule.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司有靈活的工作時間表。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這條褲子的腰帶是彈性材料製成的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4071,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::elect::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They will ____ a new president next year.","expectedAnswer":"elect","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They will ____ a new president next year.","clozeAnswer":"elect","exampleTranslation":"他們將於明年選舉新總統。","reference":{"eng":"elect","kk":"/ɪˈlɛkt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['選舉', '投票選出'], ['選擇', '決定']]","chEntries":["選舉","投票選出","選擇","決定"],"practiceMeaning":"他們將於明年選舉新總統。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'eligere'，由 'e-' (out) + 'legere' (to choose, to gather) 構成，字面意思是「挑選出來」。核心是「選擇」。因此，'elect' 主要指通過投票「選舉」出某人擔任職務，也可泛指「選擇」、「決定」某事。","definition":"1. to choose someone for a public office by voting; 2. to choose to do something","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他們將於明年選舉新總統。\",\n    \"eng\": \"They will elect a new president next year.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"會員們選她為代表。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The members elected her as their representative.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他選擇保持沉默。\",\n    \"eng\": \"He elected to remain silent.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們將於明年選舉新總統。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4043,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::election::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ will be held next month.","expectedAnswer":"election","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ will be held next month.","clozeAnswer":"election","exampleTranslation":"選舉將於下個月舉行。","reference":{"eng":"election","kk":"/ɪˈlɛkʃən/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['選舉', '競選']]","chEntries":["選舉","競選"],"practiceMeaning":"選舉將於下個月舉行。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'electio'，由 'eligere' (to choose, to select) 演變而來。'eligere' 又由 'e-' (out) + 'legere' (to gather, to choose) 構成。核心是「選擇」或「挑選」。因此，'election' 指的是通過投票等方式選出代表或領導人的過程。","definition":"the process of choosing someone for a public office by voting","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"選舉將於下個月舉行。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The election will be held next month.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他在這次選舉中以壓倒性優勢獲勝。\",\n    \"eng\": \"He won the election by a landslide.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"選舉將於下個月舉行。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3284,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::elegance::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Her ____ on the dance floor was captivating.","expectedAnswer":"elegance","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Her ____ on the dance floor was captivating.","clozeAnswer":"elegance","exampleTranslation":"她在舞池中的優雅令人著迷。","reference":{"eng":"elegance","kk":"/ˈɛlɪɡəns/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['優雅；高雅'], ['巧妙；別緻']]","chEntries":["優雅","高雅","巧妙","別緻"],"practiceMeaning":"她在舞池中的優雅令人著迷。","analysis":"由 'elegant' 加上 '-ce' (名詞後綴) 構成。指優雅、高貴、精緻的品質或狀態。也指事物（如設計、解決方案）的巧妙和簡潔。","definition":"the quality of being graceful and stylish in appearance or manner; a pleasingly ingenious and simple quality.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her elegance on the dance floor was captivating.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在舞池中的優雅令人著迷。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The elegance of the design impressed everyone.\",\n    \"ch\": \"設計的巧妙讓每個人都印象深刻。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她在舞池中的優雅令人著迷。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5623,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l7::eliminate::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need to ____ waste from the production process.","expectedAnswer":"eliminate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need to ____ waste from the production process.","clozeAnswer":"eliminate","exampleTranslation":"我們需要從生產過程中消除浪費。","reference":{"eng":"eliminate","kk":"ɪˈlɪmɪneɪt","tense":"v.","ch":"[['消除'], ['排除'], ['淘汰']]","chEntries":["消除","排除","淘汰"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要從生產過程中消除浪費。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'eliminare'，意為「移出門外」、「排除」，由 'e-'（出）和 'limen'（門檻）組成。構詞學上，'e-' 是表示「出」或「離開」的字首，'limen' 是「門檻」的核心詞根，'-ate' 是動詞化字尾。原始語意是「將某物移出門檻之外」，引申為「清除」、「排除」、「消除」或「淘汰」。","definition":"1. Remove or get rid of (something unwanted); 2. Completely destroy or put an end to; 3. Exclude or expel from a contest or place.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to eliminate waste from the production process.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要從生產過程中消除浪費。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The team was eliminated in the semi-finals.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該隊在半決賽中被淘汰了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This diet plan helps to eliminate unhealthy cravings.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個飲食計畫有助於消除不健康的渴望。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要從生產過程中消除浪費。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4403,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u9::emergency::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"In case of ____, call this number.","expectedAnswer":"emergency","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"In case of ____, call this number.","clozeAnswer":"emergency","exampleTranslation":"若遇緊急情況，請撥打此電話號碼。","reference":{"eng":"emergency","kk":"/ɪˈmɜːdʒənsi/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['緊急情況', '急事'], ['（突發的）危機']]","chEntries":["緊急情況","急事","危機"],"practiceMeaning":"若遇緊急情況，請撥打此電話號碼。","analysis":"詞源自拉丁語 'emergentia'，'emergere' (to arise)。指一種突發的、需要立即採取行動的情況，通常是危險或嚴重的。","definition":"a serious, unexpected, and often dangerous situation that requires immediate action.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"In case of emergency, call this number.\",\n    \"ch\": \"若遇緊急情況，請撥打此電話號碼。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The hospital has a special unit for emergencies.\",\n    \"ch\": \"醫院設有專門的急診部門。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"若遇緊急情況，請撥打此電話號碼。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4367,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::emotional-quotient::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"High ____ is crucial for leadership.","expectedAnswer":"emotional quotient","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"High ____ is crucial for leadership.","clozeAnswer":"emotional quotient","exampleTranslation":"高情商對於領導力至關重要。","reference":{"eng":"emotional quotient","kk":"None","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['情商']]","chEntries":["情商"],"practiceMeaning":"高情商對於領導力至關重要。","analysis":"此為片語分析。'emotional' (adj.) 源自拉丁語 'emotio'，指『情緒的，感情的』。'quotient' (n.) 源自拉丁語 'quotiens'，意為『多少次』，在此指『指數、測量值』。結合起來，指衡量一個人『情緒管理、自我認知、同理心等能力』的指標，即『情商』（EQ）。","definition":"a measure of a person's ability to be aware of and to control their own emotions, and to understand and deal with the emotions of others","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"High emotional quotient is crucial for leadership.\",\n    \"ch\": \"高情商對於領導力至關重要。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Developing your emotional quotient can improve your relationships.\",\n    \"ch\": \"培養你的情商可以改善你的人際關係。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"高情商對於領導力至關重要。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4674,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::emperor::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The Roman ____ ruled with absolute power.","expectedAnswer":"emperor","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The Roman ____ ruled with absolute power.","clozeAnswer":"emperor","exampleTranslation":"羅馬皇帝擁有絕對的統治權。","reference":{"eng":"emperor","kk":"/ˈɛmpərər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['皇帝']]","chEntries":["皇帝"],"practiceMeaning":"羅馬皇帝擁有絕對的統治權。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 *imperator*，意為「指揮官」、「統帥」，最初指羅馬共和時期擁有絕對權力的軍事首長。後來演變為帝國最高統治者的稱號，具有至高無上的權力。","definition":"1. The ruler of an empire.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The Roman emperor ruled with absolute power.\",\n    \"ch\": \"羅馬皇帝擁有絕對的統治權。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The emperor decreed a new law for his subjects.\",\n    \"ch\": \"皇帝為他的臣民頒布了一項新法律。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"羅馬皇帝擁有絕對的統治權。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5424,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::endanger::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Pollution can ____ the health of the population.","expectedAnswer":"endanger","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Pollution can ____ the health of the population.","clozeAnswer":"endanger","exampleTranslation":"污染會危害人口的健康。","reference":{"eng":"endanger","kk":"ɪnˈdeɪndʒər","tense":"v.","ch":"[['危及'], ['危害'], ['使處於危險之中']]","chEntries":["危及","危害","使處於危險之中"],"practiceMeaning":"污染會危害人口的健康。","analysis":"此字為派生詞，由字首 \"en-\" (表示\"使……成為\"、\"使……進入……狀態\") 和名詞 \"danger\" (危險) 構成。\"danger\" 源自古法語 \"dangier\"，其詞源與\"domino\" (控制、擁有權) 有關，引申為「被控制的危險」或「潛在的威脅」。構詞上，\"en-\" 將抽象名詞 \"danger\" 變為動詞，表示「使某人或某物處於危險之中」。因此，\"endanger\" 的核心語意是「將……置於危險境地」。","definition":"to put someone or something in a situation where there is a risk of harm or death; to imperil; to expose to danger.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Pollution can endanger the health of the population.\",\n    \"ch\": \"污染會危害人口的健康。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The endangered species are at risk of extinction.\",\n    \"ch\": \"瀕臨滅絕的物種面臨滅絕的危險。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His reckless driving endangered the lives of other motorists.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他魯莽的駕駛危及了其他駕駛者的生命。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"污染會危害人口的健康。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4146,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::engage::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The teacher tried to ____ the students' interest.","expectedAnswer":"engage","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The teacher tried to ____ the students' interest.","clozeAnswer":"engage","exampleTranslation":"老師試圖吸引學生的興趣。","reference":{"eng":"engage","kk":"/ɪnˈɡeɪdʒ/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['從事', '參與'], ['僱用', '聘請'], ['吸引（注意力、興趣）'], ['（機器）嚙合', '結合'], ['訂婚']]","chEntries":["從事","參與","僱用","聘請","吸引","嚙合","結合","訂婚"],"practiceMeaning":"老師試圖吸引學生的興趣。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 angere（引誘，捆綁）。核心概念是「被牽連」或「投入」。引申為積極參與、吸引他人注意、機器部件的咬合，以及婚姻的承諾（訂婚）。","definition":"1. occupy, attract, or involve (someone's interest or attention); 2. enter into conflict with (an enemy); 3. employ or hire someone; 4. (of gears) mesh or interlock; 5. lodge or carry on (a war); 6. promise to marry","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The teacher tried to engage the students' interest.\",\n    \"ch\": \"老師試圖吸引學生的興趣。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company engages in international trade.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司從事國際貿易。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The gears failed to engage.\",\n    \"ch\": \"齒輪未能嚙合。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They became engaged last year.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們去年訂婚了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"老師試圖吸引學生的興趣。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5447,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::enormous::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company made an ____ profit last year.","expectedAnswer":"enormous","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company made an ____ profit last year.","clozeAnswer":"enormous","exampleTranslation":"這家公司去年獲得了巨額利潤。","reference":{"eng":"enormous","kk":"ɪˈnɔːrməs","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['巨大的'], ['龐大的'], ['極大的']]","chEntries":["巨大的","龐大的","極大的"],"practiceMeaning":"這家公司去年獲得了巨額利潤。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 \"enormis\"，原意為\"不規則的\"、\"畸形的\"、\"巨大的\"。它由 \"e-\" (變體，源於 \"ex-\"，表示\"出\"、\"之外\") 和 \"norma\" (規則、標準、準則) 構成。構詞上，\"e-\" 提供了「超出」的語意，\"norma\" 提供了「標準」或「規則」。因此，\"enormous\" 的原始語義是「超出標準、規則的」，引申為「巨大的」、「龐大的」。","definition":"very large in size, quantity, or extent; extremely large; immense.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company made an enormous profit last year.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司去年獲得了巨額利潤。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They live in an enormous house in the countryside.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們住在鄉村的一棟巨大的房子裡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The project faced enormous challenges.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個專案面臨著巨大的挑戰。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這家公司去年獲得了巨額利潤。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5551,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::enterprise::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company has grown into a large international ____.","expectedAnswer":"enterprise","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company has grown into a large international ____.","clozeAnswer":"enterprise","exampleTranslation":"這家公司已發展成為一家大型的國際企業。","reference":{"eng":"enterprise","kk":"ˈɛntərˌpraɪz","tense":"n.","ch":"[['企業'], ['事業'], ['公司'], ['進取心'], ['膽量'], ['冒險精神']]","chEntries":["企業","事業","公司","進取心","膽量","冒險精神"],"practiceMeaning":"這家公司已發展成為一家大型的國際企業。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 \"entreprendre\"，意為 \"to undertake\"（承擔、著手做）。\"entre-\" 意為 \"between, among\"（在……之間），\"prendre\" 則意為 \"to take\"（拿取）。因此，\"enterprise\" 在語源上表示「承擔、著手去做的事情」。早期語義多指「冒險性的、艱鉅的任務」，引申出「膽量、進取心」。隨著商業發展，逐漸演變成指「企業、公司、事業」，尤其指那些有規模、有冒險精神的商業組織。因此，核心語義是「承擔某事」，進而發展出「任務、事業、企業」以及驅動這些事業所需的「進取心」和「膽量」。","definition":"1. A business organization, such as a company or a firm; also, the people who work for it; 2. A project or undertaking, especially one that is difficult, complicated, or requires effort; 3. Resourcefulness and readiness to undertake bold or difficult projects; courage and shrewdness.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company has grown into a large international enterprise.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司已發展成為一家大型的國際企業。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Starting a new business is always a risky enterprise.\",\n    \"ch\": \"創辦新事業總是一項充滿風險的冒險。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She admired his entrepreneurial enterprise and determination.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她讚賞他那創業的膽識與決心。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這家公司已發展成為一家大型的國際企業。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3254,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::entertainment::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The concert was a great source of ____.","expectedAnswer":"entertainment","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The concert was a great source of ____.","clozeAnswer":"entertainment","exampleTranslation":"這場音樂會是極好的娛樂來源。","reference":{"eng":"entertainment","kk":"/ˌɛntərˈteɪnmənt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['娛樂'], ['款待'], ['演出']]","chEntries":["娛樂","款待","演出"],"practiceMeaning":"這場音樂會是極好的娛樂來源。","analysis":"源自 'entertain'，指『使人愉快』、『款待』。指提供令人愉悅的活動、表演或內容，以供人們消遣和娛樂。","definition":"the action of providing or being provided with amusement or enjoyment.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The concert was a great source of entertainment.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這場音樂會是極好的娛樂來源。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They offer live entertainment every weekend.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們每週末都提供現場演出。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這場音樂會是極好的娛樂來源。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U41"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5838,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::evolve::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Species ____ over time.","expectedAnswer":"evolve","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Species ____ over time.","clozeAnswer":"evolve","exampleTranslation":"物種會隨時間演化。","reference":{"eng":"evolve","kk":"ɪˈvɑːlv","tense":"v.","ch":"[  [    \"演化\"  ],  [    \"進化\"  ],  [    \"發展\"  ],  [    \"演變\"  ]]","chEntries":["演化","進化","發展","演變"],"practiceMeaning":"物種會隨時間演化。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'evolvere'，由 'e-' (out) 和 'volvere' (to roll) 組成，意為「展開」、「揭示」、「演變」。'Evolve' 作動詞時，與名詞 'evolution' 語意緊密相連。在生物學上，指生物體通過遺傳變異和自然選擇等機制，從簡單形式發展到複雜形式的過程。在更廣泛的語境中，指事物（如計劃、組織、思想）從一個階段發展到另一個更複雜或不同的階段。核心概念是「逐步發展」或「演變」。","definition":"1. (of an organism) develop gradually, especially from a simple to a more complex form.; 2. Develop gradually, especially from one thing to another.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Species evolve over time.\",\n    \"ch\": \"物種會隨時間演化。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The plan evolved from a simple idea.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個計劃從一個簡單的想法逐漸發展而來。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company has evolved into a global enterprise.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司已發展成一家跨國企業。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"New technologies are constantly evolving.\",\n    \"ch\": \"新技術在不斷演進。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"物種會隨時間演化。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5044,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::exaggeration::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His account of the event was a clear ____.","expectedAnswer":"exaggeration","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His account of the event was a clear ____.","clozeAnswer":"exaggeration","exampleTranslation":"他對事件的描述明顯是誇大的。","reference":{"eng":"exaggeration","kk":"ɪɡˌzædʒəˈreɪʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[['誇張'], ['言過其實']]","chEntries":["誇張","言過其實"],"practiceMeaning":"他對事件的描述明顯是誇大的。","analysis":"此字由動詞 exaggerate（誇大）的名詞化而來。exaggerate 源自拉丁語exaggerare，由 ex-（出、極度）+ aggerare（堆積）組成，原意為「堆積起來」。引申為「極度誇大、渲染」。exaggeration 指「誇大事物的行為或結果」，強調將事物描述得比實際情況更嚴重、更重要或更大。OCR 掃描時可能將 'g' 誤判為 'l' 或 'c'，或 'a' 誤判為 'e'。此處修正為 exaggeration。","definition":"the action of representing something as being larger, greater, or more important than it really is.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His account of the event was a clear exaggeration.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對事件的描述明顯是誇大的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Avoid exaggeration when describing your skills.\",\n    \"ch\": \"描述你的技能時，要避免誇張。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他對事件的描述明顯是誇大的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5586,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::excellence::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The restaurant is known for its culinary ____.","expectedAnswer":"excellence","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The restaurant is known for its culinary ____.","clozeAnswer":"excellence","exampleTranslation":"這家餐廳以其卓越的烹飪技藝聞名。","reference":{"eng":"excellence","kk":"ˈɛksələns","tense":"n.","ch":"[['卓越'], ['優秀'], ['傑出']]","chEntries":["卓越","優秀","傑出"],"practiceMeaning":"這家餐廳以其卓越的烹飪技藝聞名。","analysis":"此字由 \"excellent\" 加上名詞化字尾 \"-ce\" 構成。\"excellent\" 源自拉丁語 \"excellēns\"，是 \"excellere\"（to be eminent, surpass, excel，卓越，超越）的現在分詞。\"excellere\" 由 \"ex-\"（out）和 \"cellere\"（to rise, to be eminent，上升，卓越）組成，意為「突出，超越眾人」。 \"-ce\" 是構成抽象名詞的字尾。因此，\"excellence\" 的核心語義是「卓越的品質、極高的水準或傑出的表現」。它強調的是在某個領域達到的頂尖水準。","definition":"1. The quality of being outstanding or extremely good; 2. Great and distinguished ability or quality.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The restaurant is known for its culinary excellence.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家餐廳以其卓越的烹飪技藝聞名。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She strives for excellence in everything she does.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她力求在她所做的一切事情上都做到最好。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The award recognizes excellence in scientific research.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該獎項旨在表彰科學研究的傑出成就。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這家餐廳以其卓越的烹飪技藝聞名。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5536,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l5::execute::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The government decided to ____ the new policy.","expectedAnswer":"execute","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The government decided to ____ the new policy.","clozeAnswer":"execute","exampleTranslation":"政府決定執行這項新政策。","reference":{"eng":"execute","kk":"ˈeksɪkjuːt","tense":"v.","ch":"[['執行'], ['處決'], [' تنفيذ'], ['實施']]","chEntries":["執行","處決","تنفيذ","實施"],"practiceMeaning":"政府決定執行這項新政策。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'exsequi'，由 'ex-' (out) + 'sequi' (to follow) 構成，意為「跟隨到底，執行」。'exsequi' 的本意是「跟隨（送葬隊伍）」，引申為「完成、執行」。構詞上，'ex-' 表「完成」，'secut-' 是 'sequi' 的詞幹，意為「跟隨」。'execute' 的核心語義是「將計劃、命令或判決付諸實施」。這包括法律上的「處決」，以及一般意義上的「執行」某項任務、計劃或程序。在計算機領域，它還指「運行（程式）」。","definition":"to carry out or put into effect (a plan, order, or course of action); to carry out a sentence of death on (a legally condemned person).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government decided to execute the new policy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府決定執行這項新政策。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The commander ordered his troops to execute the attack.\",\n    \"ch\": \"指揮官命令他的部隊執行攻擊任務。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The court ruled that the death penalty would be executed.\",\n    \"ch\": \"法院裁定將執行死刑。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"政府決定執行這項新政策。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4448,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u9::exhale::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ slowly and smoothly.","expectedAnswer":"Exhale","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ slowly and smoothly.","clozeAnswer":"Exhale","exampleTranslation":"緩慢而平穩地呼氣。","reference":{"eng":"exhale","kk":"/ɛksˈheɪl/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['呼出']]","chEntries":["呼出"],"practiceMeaning":"緩慢而平穩地呼氣。","analysis":"詞源自拉丁語 'exhālare'，'ex-' (out) + 'hālāre' (to breathe)。指將氣體從肺部呼出。","definition":"to breathe out.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Exhale slowly and smoothly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"緩慢而平穩地呼氣。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"緩慢而平穩地呼氣。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4397,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u9::exhibition::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The museum is holding an ____ of Impressionist paintings.","expectedAnswer":"exhibition","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The museum is holding an ____ of Impressionist paintings.","clozeAnswer":"exhibition","exampleTranslation":"這家博物館正在舉辦印象派畫作展。","reference":{"eng":"exhibition","kk":"/ˌeksɪˈbɪʃn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['展覽會', '陳列']]","chEntries":["展覽會","陳列"],"practiceMeaning":"這家博物館正在舉辦印象派畫作展。","analysis":"詞源自拉丁語 'exhibere'，'ex-' (out) + 'habere' (to hold, have)。原意是「展示、呈現」。指公開展示藝術品、商品或資訊的活動。","definition":"an event at which objects of interest are displayed, e.g. works of art or items of antiquarian value; a public display of works of art or items of interest.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The museum is holding an exhibition of Impressionist paintings.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家博物館正在舉辦印象派畫作展。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The new products will be on exhibition next month.\",\n    \"ch\": \"新產品將於下個月展出。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這家博物館正在舉辦印象派畫作展。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5295,"wordRef":"字彙王::u63::exile::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The political leader became an ____ after the revolution.","expectedAnswer":"exile","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The political leader became an ____ after the revolution.","clozeAnswer":"exile","exampleTranslation":"那位政治領袖在革命後成為了流亡者。","reference":{"eng":"exile","kk":"ˈɛkˌsaɪl","tense":"n.","ch":"[['流亡者', '被放逐者'], ['流亡', '放逐']]","chEntries":["流亡者","被放逐者","流亡","放逐"],"practiceMeaning":"那位政治領袖在革命後成為了流亡者。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'exilium'（放逐），'exsul'（被放逐者）。'exsul' 本身由 'ex-'（out）和 'sule'（to wander）構成。構詞上，'ex-' 為前綴，'sul-' 為詞根。原始語義為「被逐出家園、四處流浪」。'exile' 作為名詞，指代被放逐的人或被放逐的狀態。作動詞時，表示「迫使某人離開家園」。","definition":"the state of being barred from one's native country, typically for political or punitive reasons; a person who lives in exile.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The political leader became an exile after the revolution.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那位政治領袖在革命後成為了流亡者。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He lived in exile for twenty years.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他流亡了二十年。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"那位政治領袖在革命後成為了流亡者。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U63"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5646,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l8::expand::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need to ____ our business.","expectedAnswer":"expand","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need to ____ our business.","clozeAnswer":"expand","exampleTranslation":"我們需要擴展我們的業務。","reference":{"eng":"expand","kk":"ɪkˈspænd","tense":"v.","ch":"[['擴大'], ['擴展'], ['膨脹'], ['展開']]","chEntries":["擴大","擴展","膨脹","展開"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要擴展我們的業務。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 expandere，由 ex-（出，out）+ pandere（展開，to spread）組成。pandere 來自原始印歐語 *paə-（保護；餵養；展開）。核心語義為「向外展開」或「擴大」。構詞上，ex- 表示「向外」，pandere 提供「展開」的核心動作。此處為動詞用法，表示主體「變大」、「範圍變廣」或主動「使之變大」。","definition":"to become or make larger or wider; to increase in size, volume, or scope; to develop or spread to a wider area.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to expand our business.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要擴展我們的業務。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The balloon expanded as it was filled with air.\",\n    \"ch\": \"氣球在充滿空氣時膨脹了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要擴展我們的業務。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3082,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::explanation::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The teacher gave a clear ____ of the difficult concept.","expectedAnswer":"explanation","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The teacher gave a clear ____ of the difficult concept.","clozeAnswer":"explanation","exampleTranslation":"老師對這個難懂的概念給出了清晰的解釋。","reference":{"eng":"explanation","kk":"/ˌɛkspləˈneɪʃn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['解釋；說明'], ['闡明；辯解']]","chEntries":["解釋","說明","闡明","辯解"],"practiceMeaning":"老師對這個難懂的概念給出了清晰的解釋。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'explanatio'，'explanare' (to make plain, to explain)。是 'explain' 的名詞形式。指「使事物變得清楚」的過程或結果。\n1. 解釋；說明：指對事物的原因、性質、意義等進行闡述，使其易於理解。\n2. 闡明；辯解：指對自己的行為、決定等進行的辯護或說明。","definition":"1. a statement or account that makes something clear; 2. the reasons given for something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The teacher gave a clear explanation of the difficult concept.\",\n    \"ch\": \"老師對這個難懂的概念給出了清晰的解釋。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He offered no explanation for his absence.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他沒有對自己的缺席給出任何解釋。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"老師對這個難懂的概念給出了清晰的解釋。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4284,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::explore-every-avenue::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We must ____ to find a cure for the disease.","expectedAnswer":"explore every avenue","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We must ____ to find a cure for the disease.","clozeAnswer":"explore every avenue","exampleTranslation":"我們必須探索所有途徑來找到該疾病的治癒方法。","reference":{"eng":"explore every avenue","kk":"/ɪkˈsplɔːr ˈɛvri ˈævənuː/","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['探索所有途徑'], ['嘗試一切方法']]","chEntries":["探索所有途徑","嘗試一切方法"],"practiceMeaning":"我們必須探索所有途徑來找到該疾病的治癒方法。","analysis":"結合了動詞 'explore'（探索）和名詞 'avenue'（途徑、方法）。'Explore every avenue' 是一個慣用語，意思是「嘗試所有可能的途徑、方法或解決方案」，以找到一個答案或解決問題。","definition":"to investigate all possible ways of achieving something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We must explore every avenue to find a cure for the disease.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們必須探索所有途徑來找到該疾病的治癒方法。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police are exploring every avenue in their search for the missing child.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警方正在探索所有途徑尋找失蹤的孩子。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們必須探索所有途徑來找到該疾病的治癒方法。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4060,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::expressive::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Her face is very ____.","expectedAnswer":"expressive","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Her face is very ____.","clozeAnswer":"expressive","exampleTranslation":"她的臉表情非常豐富。","reference":{"eng":"expressive","kk":"/ɪkˈsprɛsɪv/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['富於表情的', '生動的'], ['表達的', '表示的']]","chEntries":["富於表情的","生動的","表達的","表示的"],"practiceMeaning":"她的臉表情非常豐富。","analysis":"源自 'express' (表達)，加上 '-ive' 後綴。'express' 源自拉丁語 'exprimere'，由 'ex-' (out) + 'premere' (to press) 構成，原意是「壓榨出來」。因此，'expressive' 指「能清晰表達情感或思想的」（富於表情的、生動的），或「用於表達的」、「表示的」。","definition":"1. showing or conveying feelings or thoughts; 2. serving to express or represent","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"她的臉表情非常豐富。\",\n    \"eng\": \"Her face is very expressive.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他發出了一個充滿情感的嘆息。\",\n    \"eng\": \"He gave an expressive sigh.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"這音樂極富表現力。\",\n    \"eng\": \"This music is highly expressive.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她的臉表情非常豐富。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4096,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::extensive-reading::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ is crucial for improving language fluency.","expectedAnswer":"Extensive reading","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ is crucial for improving language fluency.","clozeAnswer":"Extensive reading","exampleTranslation":"廣泛閱讀對於提高語言流暢度至關重要。","reference":{"eng":"extensive reading","kk":"/ɪkˈstɛnsɪv ˈridɪŋ/","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['廣泛閱讀']]","chEntries":["廣泛閱讀"],"practiceMeaning":"廣泛閱讀對於提高語言流暢度至關重要。","analysis":"'Extensive' (廣泛的) 源自拉丁語 'extensus' (stretched out)，是 'extend' 的過去分詞。'Reading' (閱讀) 是動名詞。'Extensive reading' 指閱讀大量不同主題或類型的材料，以擴展知識和詞彙量。","definition":"reading a