":"fond","kk":"fɑːnd","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['喜愛的'], ['深情的'], ['寵愛的'], ['喜歡的']]","chEntries":["喜愛的","深情的","寵愛的","喜歡的"],"practiceMeaning":"她非常喜愛她的孫子孫女。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 \"fonned\"，意為\"愚蠢的\"、\"裝模作樣的\"，後來演變成\"喜愛的\"。其詞源與\"fool\" (傻瓜) 可能有關，但語義發生了轉變。構詞上沒有明顯的字首、字根或字尾可拆解，應視為一個整體詞源的演變。原始的「愚蠢」語義可能在某些情境下轉化為「過度的愛」、「溺愛」，進而演變為現代意義上的「喜愛的」、「深情的」。","definition":"having an affection or liking for someone or something; loving or caring deeply for someone or something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is very fond of her grandchildren.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她非常喜愛她的孫子孫女。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has fond memories of his childhood.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對童年有著美好的回憶。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They are fond of classical music.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們喜歡古典音樂。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她非常喜愛她的孫子孫女。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4526,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::for::prep","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This gift is ____ you.","expectedAnswer":"for","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This gift is ____ you.","clozeAnswer":"for","exampleTranslation":"這份禮物是給你的。","reference":{"eng":"for","kk":"/fər/, /fɔːr/","tense":"prep.","ch":"[['為了'], ['給'], ['支持'], ['持續（一段時間）']]","chEntries":["為了","給","支持","持續"],"practiceMeaning":"這份禮物是給你的。","analysis":"源自古英語 for。是一個極其常見且語意複雜的介詞。核心語意是「目的」、「原因」、「受益者」。引申義廣泛，包括「持續時間」、「代表」、「傾向」等。","definition":"1. Intended to achieve or affect; 2. In order to benefit or be given to; 3. In support of or in agreement with; 4. During (a period of time).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This gift is for you.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這份禮物是給你的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He works for a large company.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在一家大公司工作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She stayed for two weeks.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她待了兩週。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They are fighting for their freedom.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們正在為自由而戰。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這份禮物是給你的。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6172,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::forge::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The blacksmith worked in his ____.","expectedAnswer":"forge","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The blacksmith worked in his ____.","clozeAnswer":"forge","exampleTranslation":"鐵匠在他的鍛造廠裡工作。","reference":{"eng":"forge","kk":"fɔrdʒ","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"鍛造廠\"  ],  [    \"熔爐\"  ]]","chEntries":["鍛造廠","熔爐"],"practiceMeaning":"鐵匠在他的鍛造廠裡工作。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 forge，是動詞 forge「鍛造」的名詞化，最終源自拉丁語 fabrica「工廠、製造、工藝」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作為名詞，其核心語義是指「用於鍛造金屬的工廠或設備」。此義項由動詞「鍛造」延伸出動作發生的場所。","definition":"1. a furnace or fire for heating metal; 2. a workshop where metal is forged.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The blacksmith worked in his forge.\",\n    \"ch\": \"鐵匠在他的鍛造廠裡工作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The intense heat of the forge was palpable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"鍛造爐的熾熱讓人觸手可及。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He learned the art of metalworking in the forge.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在鍛造廠學到了金屬加工的技藝。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"鐵匠在他的鍛造廠裡工作。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5086,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::foul::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The oil spill will ____ the waters.","expectedAnswer":"foul","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The oil spill will ____ the waters.","clozeAnswer":"foul","exampleTranslation":"漏油將會污染水域。","reference":{"eng":"foul","kk":"faʊl","tense":"v.","ch":"[['弄髒'], ['玷污'], ['犯規']]","chEntries":["弄髒","玷污","犯規"],"practiceMeaning":"漏油將會污染水域。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 'fūl'，原始語義為 '腐爛的、惡臭的'。作為動詞，'foul' 表示使某物變得 '骯髒、汙穢'。在體育運動中，它特指 '違犯規則'，因為這種行為通常被視為不公平、不正當，甚至帶有 '污穢' 的意味，破壞了比賽的純潔性。","definition":"1. To make or become dirty or polluted.; 2. To commit a foul in a game or sport.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The oil spill will foul the waters.\",\n    \"ch\": \"漏油將會污染水域。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The player fouled