hoices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need to address the ____ issues.","clozeAnswer":"fundamental","exampleTranslation":"我們需要解決根本問題。","reference":{"eng":"fundamental","kk":"/ˌfʌndəˈmentl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['根本的；基礎的'], ['根本性的；原則性的'], ['重要的']]","chEntries":["根本的","基礎的","根本性的","原則性的","重要的"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要解決根本問題。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'fundamentum' (foundation)。核心意義是「作為基礎」。\n1. 根本的；基礎的：指事物的最基本、最底層的組成部分或原理。\n2. 根本性的；原則性的：指與核心原則或基本結構相關的。\n3. 重要的：指非常重要，是其他一切事物的前提。","definition":"1. forming the most important part of something; 2. relating to the most basic or important ideas or principles; 3. forming a necessary base or core; of central importance.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to address the fundamental issues.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要解決根本問題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a fundamental principle of democracy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是民主的一個基本原則。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It is fundamental to our success.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這對我們的成功至關重要。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要解決根本問題。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4610,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::gap::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There is a small ____ in the fence.","expectedAnswer":"gap","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There is a small ____ in the fence.","clozeAnswer":"gap","exampleTranslation":"籬笆上有個小裂縫。","reference":{"eng":"gap","kk":"/ɡæp/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['裂縫'], ['間隙'], ['差距 (意見、年齡、收入等)'], ['缺口']]","chEntries":["裂縫","間隙","差距","缺口"],"practiceMeaning":"籬笆上有個小裂縫。","analysis":"源自古挪威語 'gap'，意為「開口、裂縫」。核心概念是兩個事物之間存在的空間或差異。可以是物理上的空間（裂縫、間隙），也可以是抽象的差異（意見、知識、社會經濟地位上的差距）。","definition":"a break or hole in an object or between two things; a difference between two things, especially amounts or qualities.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There is a small gap in the fence.\",\n    \"ch\": \"籬笆上有個小裂縫。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The generation gap is a common issue in families.\",\n    \"ch\": \"世代差距是家庭中常見的問題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to bridge the gap between the rich and the poor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要縮小貧富之間的差距。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"籬笆上有個小裂縫。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U16、L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5592,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l7::gender::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The study examined the influence of ____ on career choices.","expectedAnswer":"gender","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The study examined the influence of ____ on career choices.","clozeAnswer":"gender","exampleTranslation":"這項研究檢視了性別對職涯選擇的影響。","reference":{"eng":"gender","kk":"ˈdʒɛndər","tense":"n.","ch":"[['性別'], ['社會性別']]","chEntries":["性別","社會性別"],"practiceMeaning":"這項研究檢視了性別對職涯選擇的影響。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'genus'（種類、血統），經由古法語 'gendre' 傳入英語。在構詞學上，'gender' 主要是作為一個整體詞，但其詞源與表示「種類」或「出生」的概念相關。原始語意指向生物學上的性別，後來在社會科學領域，特別是女性主義和性別研究中，延伸出 '社會性別' (social gender) 的概念，用以區分生理性別 (sex) 與個人或社會建構的性別角色、行為和認同。這種區分是為了強調性別並非全然由生物學決定，而是受到社會文化因素的深刻影響。","definition":"1. The state of being male or female or, in some contexts, neither or both, as determined by biology or social or cultural factors; 2. The classification of nouns and pronouns in some languages as masculine, feminine, or neuter; 3. A social or cultural construct relating to aspects of personality and identity.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The study examined the influence of gender on career choices.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這項研究檢視了性別對職涯選擇的影響。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Gender roles can vary significantly across different cultures.\",\n    \"ch\": \"社會性別角色在不同文化間可能存在顯著差異。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這項研究檢視了性別對職涯選擇的影響。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4659,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::generation-gap::idiom","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ can lead to misunderstandings between parents and children.","expectedAnswer":"generation gap","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ can lead to misunderstandings between parents and children.","clozeAnswer":"generation gap","exampleTranslation":"代溝可能導致父母與子女之間的誤解。","reference":{"eng":"generation gap","kk":"/ˌdʒenəˈreɪʃən ɡæp/","tense":"idiom","ch":"[['代溝']]","chEntries":["代溝"],"practiceMeaning":"代溝可能導致父母與子女之間的誤解。","analysis":"此為固定片語。'Generation' (世代) + 'gap' (差距)。指不同世代之間在觀念、價值觀、生活方式、興趣等方面存在的顯著差異和隔閡。","definition":"a difference in attitudes or understanding between older and younger generations.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The generation gap can lead to misunderstandings between parents and children.\",\n    \"ch\": \"代溝可能導致父母與子女之間的誤解。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They discussed the challenges of the generation gap.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們討論了代溝帶來的挑戰。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"代溝可能導致父母與子女之間的誤解。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3159,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::genuine::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Her apology seemed ____.","expectedAnswer":"genuine","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Her apology seemed ____.","clozeAnswer":"genuine","exampleTranslation":"她的道歉似乎是真誠的。","reference":{"eng":"genuine","kk":"/ˈdʒɛnjuɪn/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['真誠的；真實的'], ['（物品）名副其實的；正宗的']]","chEntries":["真誠的","真實的","名副其實的","正宗的"],"practiceMeaning":"她的道歉似乎是真誠的。","analysis":"詞源來自拉丁語 'genuinus'，意為「天然的，固有的」，與 'genus'（種類，出生）有關，原意是「屬於某個家族的」。'Genuine' 強調的是真實性、純正性，不存在虛假、偽造或模仿。用於描述情感、意圖或人時，指真誠、沒有虛偽。用於描述物品時，指正宗、非仿冒品。","definition":"1. truly what something is said to be; authentic; 2. sincere and honest; 3. (of a person) not trying to deceive anyone.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her apology seemed genuine.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的道歉似乎是真誠的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a genuine antique vase.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個真正的古董花瓶。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He showed genuine concern for her well-being.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對她的健康表現出真誠的關心。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她的道歉似乎是真誠的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5401,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l2::geographical::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The region has unique ____ characteristics.","expectedAnswer":"geographical","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The region has unique ____ characteristics.","clozeAnswer":"geographical","exampleTranslation":"該地區具有獨特的地理特徵。","reference":{"eng":"geographical","kk":"ˌdʒiːəˈɡræfɪkl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['地理的'], ['地理學的']]","chEntries":["地理的","地理學的"],"practiceMeaning":"該地區具有獨特的地理特徵。","analysis":"此字源自名詞 'geography' (地理學)。'-ical' 是常見的形容詞字尾，表示「與……有關的」。'geography' 源自希臘語 geōgraphia，由 'gē' (earth) + 'graphein' (to write) 組成，意為「描寫地球」。核心語意是「與地球的表面、地形、氣候、人口等相關的」。","definition":"1. relating to the physical features of the earth's surface; 2. relating to the study of geography.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The region has unique geographical characteristics.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該地區具有獨特的地理特徵。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We studied the geographical distribution of the species.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們研究了該物種的地理分佈。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該地區具有獨特的地理特徵。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4373,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::get-confused::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"I ____ when there are too many numbers.","expectedAnswer":"get confused","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"I ____ when there are too many numbers.","clozeAnswer":"get confused","exampleTranslation":"當數字太多時，我會感到困惑。","reference":{"eng":"get confused","kk":"None","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['感到困惑；迷失方向']]","chEntries":["感到困惑","迷失方向"],"practiceMeaning":"當數字太多時，我會感到困惑。","analysis":"此為片語分析。'get' (v.) 在此表示『變得』，引導狀態的改變。'confused' (adj.) 源自 'confuse' (v.)，意為『困惑的，糊塗的』。整個片語表示『變得感到困惑、不理解、或迷失了方向』。","definition":"to become confused; to not understand something","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I get confused when there are too many numbers.\",\n    \"ch\