  \"eng\": \"He often goes to the cinema alone.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他經常一個人去看電影。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們這個週末去看電影吧。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4045,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::governor::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ signed the new bill into law.","expectedAnswer":"governor","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ signed the new bill into law.","clozeAnswer":"governor","exampleTranslation":"州長簽署了新法案，使其成為法律。","reference":{"eng":"governor","kk":"/ˈɡʌvərnər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['州長', '總督'], ['主管', '管理者']]","chEntries":["州長","總督","主管","管理者"],"practiceMeaning":"州長簽署了新法案，使其成為法律。","analysis":"源自古法語 'governour'，來自拉丁語 'gubernator'，意為「舵手」、「領航員」，進而引申為「管理者」、「統治者」。'gubernator' 本身來自希臘語 'kybernetes' (steersman, governor)。核心是「控制」和「引導」方向。因此，指負責管理或統治一個地區或機構的官員。","definition":"1. the elected head of a U.S. state; 2. a person appointed to govern a colony or province; 3. a person who is in charge of an organization or a part of it","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"州長簽署了新法案，使其成為法律。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The governor signed the new bill into law.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他被任命為新地區的總督。\",\n    \"eng\": \"He was appointed governor of the new territory.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"中央銀行行長宣布了新政策。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The governor of the central bank announced new policies.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"州長簽署了新法案，使其成為法律。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3088,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::graceful::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ballerina performed a ____ dance.","expectedAnswer":"graceful","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ballerina performed a ____ dance.","clozeAnswer":"graceful","exampleTranslation":"這位芭蕾舞演員跳了一支優雅的舞蹈。","reference":{"eng":"graceful","kk":"/ˈɡreɪsfl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['優雅的；雅緻的'], ['（動作、姿態）好看的；得體的']]","chEntries":["優雅的","雅緻的","好看的","得體的"],"practiceMeaning":"這位芭蕾舞演員跳了一支優雅的舞蹈。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'gratia' (grace, favor)，經由古法語 'grace' 演變而來。核心意義是「優美」、「迷人」。\n1. 優雅的；雅緻的：指姿態、舉止、風格等方面具有美感，令人賞心悅目。\n2. （動作、姿態）好看的；得體的：形容動作自然、協調，給人以美感和得體之感。","definition":"1. elegant and stylish in form or movement; 2. pleasing and attractive.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The ballerina performed a graceful dance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位芭蕾舞演員跳了一支優雅的舞蹈。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a graceful way of speaking.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的說話方式很優雅。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這位芭蕾舞演員跳了一支優雅的舞蹈。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3160,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::graph::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ shows a steady increase in sales over the past year.","expectedAnswer":"graph","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ shows a steady increase in sales over the past year.","clozeAnswer":"graph","exampleTranslation":"這張圖表顯示了過去一年銷售額的穩定增長。","reference":{"eng":"graph","kk":"/ɡræf/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['圖；圖表； graf']]","chEntries":["圖","圖表","graf"],"practiceMeaning":"這張圖表顯示了過去一年銷售額的穩定增長。","analysis":"源自希臘語 'graphein'，意為「書寫，繪製」。'Graph' 是一種用線條、點或其他符號在平面上表示數據、關係或統計結果的視覺工具。它幫助我們理解數據的趨勢、比較不同的數值或展示變數之間的關係。常見的有折線圖、長條圖、圓形圖等。","definition":"a diagram showing the relation between two or more variables, typically of the form of a curve or a series of points lying on a grid.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The graph shows a steady increase in sales over the past year.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這張圖表顯示了過去一年銷售額的穩定增長。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please plot the data points on the graph.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請將數據點繪製在這張圖上。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The bar graph clearly illustrates the comparison between the two groups.\",\n    \"ch\": \"長條圖清晰地展示了兩組之間的比較。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這張圖表顯示了過去一年銷售額的穩定增長。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3161,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::grief::n","mode":"cloz