road, she started to feel ____.","clozeAnswer":"homesick","exampleTranslation":"在國外一個月後，她開始感到想家。","reference":{"eng":"homesick","kk":"/ˈhoʊmˌsɪk/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['想家的', '思鄉的']]","chEntries":["想家的","思鄉的"],"practiceMeaning":"在國外一個月後，她開始感到想家。","analysis":"由 'home' (家) 和 'sick' (生病的) 組成。核心是「因思念家而感到不適」。形容因離家太久而產生的鄉愁或思念之情。","definition":"suffering from depression caused by longing for one's home.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"After a month abroad, she started to feel homesick.\",\n    \"ch\": \"在國外一個月後，她開始感到想家。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The child was homesick and wanted to go back home.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子想家了，想要回家。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"在國外一個月後，她開始感到想家。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4120,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::honor::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Winning the award brought him great ____.","expectedAnswer":"honor","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Winning the award brought him great ____.","clozeAnswer":"honor","exampleTranslation":"贏得這個獎項給他帶來了極大的榮譽。","reference":{"eng":"honor","kk":"/ˈɑːnər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['榮譽', '光榮'], ['尊敬', '敬意'], ['（尤指女性的）貞節', '名節'], ['（債務的）償還', '履約']]","chEntries":["榮譽","光榮","尊敬","敬意","貞節","名節","償還","履約"],"practiceMeaning":"贏得這個獎項給他帶來了極大的榮譽。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 honor（尊敬、名譽）。核心概念是「價值」、「尊嚴」或「受到的高度評價」。引申為社會認可的榮譽、對個人的尊敬、個人品德的貞潔，以及對承諾的履行。","definition":"1. high respect; esteem; 2. privilege; 3. a thing conferred as a mark of respect; an award; 4. good reputation and integrity; 5. the fulfillment of an obligation","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Winning the award brought him great honor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"贏得這個獎項給他帶來了極大的榮譽。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has been honored for her contributions to science.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她因對科學的貢獻而受到表彰。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He always keeps his honor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他始終信守承諾。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The bank will honor the check.\",\n    \"ch\": \"銀行將兌現這張支票。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"贏得這個獎項給他帶來了極大的榮譽。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4721,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::humor::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He always tries to ____ his demanding boss.","expectedAnswer":"humor","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He always tries to ____ his demanding boss.","clozeAnswer":"humor","exampleTranslation":"他總是試圖遷就他那要求嚴苛的老闆。","reference":{"eng":"humor","kk":"/ˈhjumər/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['迎合'], ['遷就']]","chEntries":["迎合","遷就"],"practiceMeaning":"他總是試圖遷就他那要求嚴苛的老闆。","analysis":"動詞形式，指為了取悅或避免冒犯某人而遷就或滿足他們。通常用於負面語境，暗示不是真心同意，只是為了保持和諧。","definition":"1. To try to please or satisfy someone, especially by doing or saying what they want.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He always tries to humor his demanding boss.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他總是試圖遷就他那要求嚴苛的老闆。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The teacher tried to humor the crying child.\",\n    \"ch\": \"老師試圖安撫那個哭泣的孩子。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他總是試圖遷就他那要求嚴苛的老闆。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5388,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l2::hygiene::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Good personal ____ is important to prevent the spread of germs.","expectedAnswer":"hygiene","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Good personal ____ is important to prevent the spread of germs.","clozeAnswer":"hygiene","exampleTranslation":"良好的個人衛生對於防止細菌傳播很重要。","reference":{"eng":"hygiene","kk":"ˈhaɪdʒiːn","tense":"n.","ch":"[['衛生'], ['（個人）清潔']]","chEntries":["衛生","清潔"],"practiceMeaning":"良好的個人衛生對於防止細菌傳播很重要。","analysis":"此字源自希臘語 Hygieia (健康女神的名字)，引申出 'hygienic' (衛生的)。'-e' 是名詞結尾。核心語意是「與健康和清潔相關的狀態或實踐」。'Hygiene' 指維持健康和預防疾病所需的衛生習慣和條件，包括個人清潔、環境清潔等。","definition":"Conditions or practices conducive to maintaining health and preventing disease, especially through cleanliness.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Good personal hygiene is important to prevent the spread of germs.\",\n    \"ch\": \"良好的個人衛生對於防止細菌傳播很重要。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Food hygiene standards must be strictly followed.\",\n    \"ch\": \"食品衛生標準必須嚴格遵守。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"良好的個人衛生對於防止細菌傳播很重要。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4512,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::idea::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"That's a great ____!","expectedAnswer":"idea","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"That's a great ____!","clozeAnswer":"idea","exampleTranslation":"這真是個好主意！","reference":{"eng":"idea","kk":"/aɪˈdiːə/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['主意'], ['想法'], ['概念']]","chEntries":["主意","想法","概念"],"practiceMeaning":"這真是個好主意！","analysis":"源自希臘語 idea，意為「形狀」、「外觀」、「理念」。核心語意是「心智中產生的概念或圖像」。引申為「想法」、「概念」、「意圖」。","definition":"1. A thought or suggestion as to a possible course of action; 2. A conception of or belief about something; 3. A plan or suggestion.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"That's a great idea!\",\n    \"ch\": \"這真是個好主意！\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I have no idea what you are talking about.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我完全不知道你在說什麼。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The idea of democracy spread rapidly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"民主的概念迅速傳播。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這真是個好主意！","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5418,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::identity::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He struggled to find his ____ after the accident.","expectedAnswer":"identity","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He struggled to find his ____ after the accident.","clozeAnswer":"identity","exampleTranslation":"事故後他努力尋找自己的身份認同。","reference":{"eng":"identity","kk":"aɪˈdentəti","tense":"n.","ch":"[['身份'], ['身分'], ['認同'], ['特性'], ['同一性']]","chEntries":["身份","身分","認同","特性","同一性"],"practiceMeaning":"事故後他努力尋找自己的身份認同。","analysis":"此字由形容詞 \"identical\" 加上名詞化字尾 \"-ity\" 構成。\"identical\" 源自拉丁語 \"identicus\"，其詞源為 \"idem\"，意為\"相同\"。構詞上，\"ident-\" 提供了核心的\"相同\"或\"同一\"語意，\"-ical\" 是形容詞字尾，將「相同」的概念描述為一種屬性。而字尾 \"-ity\" 則將形容詞的「相同性」或「同一性」轉化為抽象名詞，形成 \"identity\"。因此，\"identity\" 首先表示「同一性」，即事物是其本身且與其他事物不同；進而引申為「身份」或「身分」，指一個人或物之所以是其自身、其獨特性；也引申為「認同」，即與某人、某群體或某物產生連結感和歸屬感。","definition":"the fact of being who or what a person or thing is; the characteristics and qualities that form who a person is and make them different from others; the state of being the same; the condition of being oneself and not someone else; a sense of self; sameness.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He struggled to find his identity after the accident.\",\n    \"ch\": \"事故後他努力尋找自己的身份認同。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The passport confirms the traveler's identity.\",\n    \"ch\": \"護照證實了旅客的身份。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Cultural identity plays a big role in shaping our values.\",\n    \"ch\": \"文化認同在塑造我們的價值觀方面扮演著重要角色。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"事故後他努力尋找自己的身份認同。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6125,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::ideology::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They shared the same political ____.","expectedAnswer":"ideology","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They shared the same political ____.","clozeAnswer":"ideology","exampleTranslation":"他們持有相同的政治意識形態。","reference":{"eng":"ideology","kk":"ˌɪdiˈɑːlədʒi","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"意識形態\"  ],  [    \"思想體系\"  ],  [    \"理念\"  ]]","chEntries":["意識形態","思想體系","理念"],"practiceMeaning":"他們持有相同的政治意識形態。","analysis":"此字源自法語 idéologie，由希臘語 idea（形式；理念；思想）和 -logia（學說；研究）組成。Idea 源自 idea（看；看見）。-logia 來自 logos（詞；言論；學說）。因此，ideology 的核心語義是「關於思想的學說」或「思想體系」。此名詞指一套關於社會、政治或經濟的觀念、信念和價值觀的系統。其語意演變是從「思想的研究」到「一套系統化的思想」。","definition":"A system of ideas and ideals, especially one which forms the basis of economic or political theory and policy.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They shared the same political ideology.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們持有相同的政治意識形態。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The novel explores themes of freedom and ideology.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這部小說探討了自由與意識形態的主題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His actions were driven by a strong ideology.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的行為是由強烈的理念驅動的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們持有相同的政治意識形態。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3226,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::idiom::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"'Kick the bucket' is a common English ____.","expectedAnswer":"idiom","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"'Kick the bucket' is a common English ____.","clozeAnswer":"idiom","exampleTranslation":"「踢水桶」（指死亡）是一個常見的英文慣用語。","reference":{"eng":"idiom","kk":"/ˈɪdiəm/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['習語'], ['慣用語'], ['成語']]","chEntries":["習語","慣用語","成語"],"practiceMeaning":"「踢水桶」（指死亡）是一個常見的英文慣用語。","analysis":"詞源來自希臘文 'idiōma'，意為 'private property, peculiarity'，來自 'idios' (one's own)。指一種獨特的、非字面意思的表達方式，其意義不能僅從組成單字的字面意義推斷出來，屬於特定語言的特徵。","definition":"a group of words established by usage as having a meaning not deducible from those of the individual words.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"'Kick the bucket' is a common English idiom.\",\n    \"ch\": \"「踢水桶」（指死亡）是一個常見的英文慣用語。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Learning idioms is crucial for mastering a language.\",\n    \"ch\": \"學習慣用語對於精通一門語言至關重要。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"「踢水桶」（指死亡）是一個常見的英文慣用語。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U41"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3917,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::imagination::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Children have a great ____.","expectedAnswer":"imagination","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Children have a great ____.","clozeAnswer":"imagination","exampleTranslation":"孩子們有很強的想像力。","reference":{"eng":"imagination","kk":"/ɪˌmædʒɪˈneɪʃn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['想像力'], ['幻想', '虛構']]","chEntries":["想像力","幻想","虛構"],"practiceMeaning":"孩子們有很強的想像力。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'imaginatio'，與 'imago' (意為「圖像、影像」) 有關，最終源自 'imagines' (意為「形象」)。指在心中形成圖像、概念的能力，即「想像力」；也可指由此產生的「幻想」或「虛構」。","definition":"1. the faculty or action of forming new ideas, or images or concepts of external objects not present to the senses; 2. the ability of the mind to be creative or resourceful.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Children have a great imagination.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子們有很強的想像力。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"You need imagination to be a writer.\",\n    \"ch\": \"你需要想像力才能成為一名作家。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"That story is pure imagination.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那個故事純粹是虛構的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"孩子們有很強的想像力。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3311,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::impartial::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The jury must remain ____ throughout the trial.","expectedAnswer":"impartial","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The jury must remain ____ throughout the trial.","clozeAnswer":"impartial","exampleTranslation":"陪審團在整個審判過程中必須保持公正。","reference":{"eng":"impartial","kk":"/ɪmˈpɑːrʃl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['公正的；不偏不倚的'], ['無私的']]","chEntries":["公正的","不偏不倚的","無私的"],"practiceMeaning":"陪審團在整個審判過程中必須保持公正。","analysis":"由 'im-' (否定前綴) + 'partial' (偏心的) 組成。與 'partial' 相反，指不偏向任何一方，公平地對待。","definition":"treating all rivals or disputants equally; fair and just.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The jury must remain impartial throughout the trial.\",\n    \"ch\": \"陪審團在整個審判過程中必須保持公正。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A good teacher should be impartial to all students.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一個好老師應該對所有學生都一視同仁。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"陪審團在整個審判過程中必須保持公正。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5326,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l1::imprison::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The government decided to ____ the rebels.","expectedAnswer":"imprison","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The government decided to ____ the rebels.","clozeAnswer":"imprison","exampleTranslation":"政府決定監禁這些叛亂分子。","reference":{"eng":"imprison","kk":"ɪmˈprɪzən","tense":"v.","ch":"[['監禁'], ['囚禁']]","chEntries":["監禁","囚禁"],"practiceMeaning":"政府決定監禁這些叛亂分子。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 enprisoner，由 in-（進入）+ pris（被抓、被捕，來自拉丁語 prehendere「抓住」）+ -on（動詞字尾）組成，字面意思為「使被捕、被關入」。構詞上，in- 表示「進入」或「使處於某狀態」，pris 來自 prehendere 的過去分詞，意為「抓住」或「佔有」。核心語意為「使人處於被拘禁的狀態」，引申為「監禁」或「囚禁」。","definition":"to put or keep someone in prison or in jail as a punishment for a crime; to confine someone.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government decided to imprison the rebels.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府決定監禁這些叛亂分子。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was imprisoned for treason.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他因叛國罪被監禁。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"政府決定監禁這些叛亂分子。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5325,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l1::imprisonment::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He served five years of ____ for his crimes.","expectedAnswer":"imprisonment","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He served five years of ____ for his crimes.","clozeAnswer":"imprisonment","exampleTranslation":"他因罪行服刑五年監禁。","reference":{"eng":"imprisonment","kk":"ɪmˈprɪzənmənt","tense":"n.","ch":"[['監禁'], ['囚禁']]","chEntries":["監禁","囚禁"],"practiceMeaning":"他因罪行服刑五年監禁。","analysis":"此字由動詞 imprison 加上名詞字尾 -ment 構成。imprison 源自古法語 enprisoner，由 in-（進入）+ pris（被抓、被捕，來自拉丁語 prehendere「抓住」）+ -on（動詞字尾）組成，字面意思為「使被捕、被關入」。-ment 是常見的名詞化字尾，表示狀態、動作或結果。因此，imprisonment 的核心語意是「被監禁的狀態或行為」。","definition":"the state of being imprisoned; the action of imprisoning someone.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He served five years of imprisonment for his crimes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他因罪行服刑五年監禁。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The court ordered his imprisonment.\",\n    \"ch\": \"法院判處他監禁。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他因罪行服刑五年監禁。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5588,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::in-large-part::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The success of the project was ____ due to her efforts.","expectedAnswer":"in large part","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The success of the project was ____ due to her efforts.","clozeAnswer":"in large part","exampleTranslation":"這個專案的成功在很大程度上歸功於她的努力。","reference":{"eng":"in large part","kk":"ɪn lɑrdʒ pɑrt","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['在很大程度上'], ['主要地']]","chEntries":["在很大程度上","主要地"],"practiceMeaning":"這個專案的成功在很大程度上歸功於她的努力。","analysis":"此片語由介詞 \"in\"，形容詞 \"large\"（大的），名詞 \"part\"（部分）組成。\"in large part\" 是一個慣用語，意思是指「由於大部分的原因」或「在很大程度上」。\"large\" 形容 \"part\"，強調「比例的巨大」。 \"in\" 則表示「在……範圍內」。因此，整個片語表示「原因或影響是佔據了主要部分的」。","definition":"1. To a great extent; largely; 2. For the most part.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The success of the project was in large part due to her efforts.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個專案的成功在很大程度上歸功於她的努力。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"In large part, the changes were driven by new technology.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這些改變主要由新技術推動。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個專案的成功在很大程度上歸功於她的努力。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5452,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::in-need-of::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The organization provides aid to those ____ food and shelter.","expectedAnswer":"in need of","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The organization provides aid to those ____ food and shelter.","clozeAnswer":"in need of","exampleTranslation":"該組織為那些需要食物和住所的人提供援助。","reference":{"eng":"in need of","kk":"ɪn niːd ɒv","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['需要'], ['有所需求']]","chEntries":["需要","有所需求"],"practiceMeaning":"該組織為那些需要食物和住所的人提供援助。","analysis":"此片語由介系詞 \"in\"，名詞 \"need\" (需求)，以及介系詞 \"of\" 組成。\"need\" 源自古英語 \"nēod\"。此片語表示「處於需要……的狀態」，強調對某物或某種幫助的匱乏感。","definition":"requiring something that you do not have.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The organization provides aid to those in need of food and shelter.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該組織為那些需要食物和住所的人提供援助。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Many elderly people are in need of assistance with daily tasks.\",\n    \"ch\": \"許多老年人需要日常事務的協助。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該組織為那些需要食物和住所的人提供援助。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4025,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u3::in-practice::adv-phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"In theory, everyone should be equal, but ____, that is not always the case.","expectedAnswer":"in practice","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"In theory, everyone should be equal, but ____, that is not always the case.","clozeAnswer":"in practice","exampleTranslation":"理論上每個人都應該平等，但實際上情況並非總是如此。","reference":{"eng":"in practice","kk":"/ɪn ˈpræktɪs/","tense":"adv. phrase","ch":"[['實際上'], ['在實踐中']]","chEntries":["實際上","在實踐中"],"practiceMeaning":"理論上每個人都應該平等，但實際上情況並非總是如此。","analysis":"結合介詞 'in' (在) 和名詞 'practice' (實踐)。表示實際操作或執行時的情況，與理論可能不同。","definition":"in actual use or application; in reality.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"In theory, everyone should be equal, but in practice, that is not always the case.\",\n    \"ch\": \"理論上每個人都應該平等，但實際上情況並非總是如此。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"理論上每個人都應該平等，但實際上情況並非總是如此。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3966,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::in-response-to::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He acted ____ the urgent request.","expectedAnswer":"in response to","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He acted ____ the urgent request.","clozeAnswer":"in response to","exampleTranslation":"他根據緊急請求採取了行動。","reference":{"eng":"in response to","kk":"None","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['回應', '作為對…的回應']]","chEntries":["回應","作為對…的回應"],"practiceMeaning":"他根據緊急請求採取了行動。","analysis":"介詞片語，表示某個行動是為了回應或針對某事而發生的。","definition":"as an answer or reaction to something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He acted in response to the urgent request.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他根據緊急請求採取了行動。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\"