ment.\",\n    \"ch\": \"理論上，新政策應該能降低失業率。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"理論上，新政策應該能降低失業率。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4578,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::inaccurate::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The report contained several ____ figures.","expectedAnswer":"inaccurate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The report contained several ____ figures.","clozeAnswer":"inaccurate","exampleTranslation":"報告包含幾個不準確的數字。","reference":{"eng":"inaccurate","kk":"/ɪnˈækjərət/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['不準確的', '不精確的'], ['錯誤的']]","chEntries":["不準確的","不精確的","錯誤的"],"practiceMeaning":"報告包含幾個不準確的數字。","analysis":"由否定字首 'in-' (not) 和 'accurate' (準確的) 組成。與 'accurate' 相反，指不準確、不精確或錯誤的。","definition":"1. not correct or precise.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The report contained several inaccurate figures.\",\n    \"ch\": \"報告包含幾個不準確的數字。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His memory of the event was inaccurate.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對那次事件的記憶並不準確。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The map is inaccurate and outdated.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這張地圖既不準確又過時了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"報告包含幾個不準確的數字。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5404,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l2::indeed::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It was ____ a beautiful day.","expectedAnswer":"indeed","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It was ____ a beautiful day.","clozeAnswer":"indeed","exampleTranslation":"這確實是個美好的一天。","reference":{"eng":"indeed","kk":"ɪnˈdiːd","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['確實'], ['的確'], ['實在']]","chEntries":["確實","的確","實在"],"practiceMeaning":"這確實是個美好的一天。","analysis":"此字是中古英語 in dede 的組合，意為「在事實中」。'in' (in) + 'dede' (deed, deed)。核心語意是「強調事實或真實性」。'Indeed' 用來加強語氣，表示肯定、確認，或用於引出更具體的解釋、進一步的資訊，或者表示同意。","definition":"1. used to emphasize a statement or response; truly; certainly; 2. used to express polite disbelief, surprise, or incredulity.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was indeed a beautiful day.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這確實是個美好的一天。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a very talented musician, indeed.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他確實是一位非常有才華的音樂家。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這確實是個美好的一天。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5461,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::indigenous::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ people of Australia have a rich cultural heritage.","expectedAnswer":"indigenous","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ people of Australia have a rich cultural heritage.","clozeAnswer":"indigenous","exampleTranslation":"澳大利亞的原住民擁有豐富的文化遺產。","reference":{"eng":"indigenous","kk":"ɪnˈdɪdʒənəs","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['原住民的'], ['本地的'], ['土生土長的']]","chEntries":["原住民的","本地的","土生土長的"],"practiceMeaning":"澳大利亞的原住民擁有豐富的文化遺產。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'indigena'，意為「土著、原住民」。'Indigena' 是由 'indi-'（在此處作強調，可能與 'in'「在……裡面」有關）和 'gen-'（出生、產生，來自 'gignere'「產生」）組合而成，直譯為「從內部出生」，引申為「當地出生、本地的、原生的」。'-ous' 是拉丁語 '-osus' 的英語化形式，用於構成形容詞，表示「充滿……的」。因此，'indigenous' 指的是「屬於某地方、某國家或某特定地區的，從該地方發源或產生的」，特別常用來指「原住民」或「當地特有」的動植物、文化等。","definition":"1. Originating or occurring naturally in a particular place; native.; 2. Relating to or characteristic of a particular region or people.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The indigenous people of Australia have a rich cultural heritage.\",\n    \"ch\": \"澳大利亞的原住民擁有豐富的文化遺產。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Eucalyptus is indigenous to Australia.\",\n    \"ch\": \"桉樹是澳大利亞的原生植物。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company uses indigenous materials in its products.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司在其產品中使用當地材料。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"澳大利亞的原住民擁有豐富的文化遺產。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3297,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::infant::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ slept peacefully in its crib.","expectedAnswer":"infant","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ slept peacefully in its crib.","clozeAnswer":"infant","exampleTranslation":"嬰兒安詳地睡在搖籃裡。","reference":{"eng":"infant","kk":"/ˈɪnfənt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['嬰兒；嬰孩']]","chEntries":["嬰兒","嬰孩"],"practiceMeaning":"嬰兒安詳地睡在搖籃裡。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'infans'，由 'in-' (不) + 'fari' (說話) 組成，意為「不會說話的」。指年幼的兒童，特別是剛出生的到一歲左右的嬰兒。","definition":"a baby or very young child.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The infant slept peacefully in its crib.\",\n    \"ch\": \"嬰兒安詳地睡在搖籃裡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The hospital has a special ward for infants.\",\n    \"ch\": \"醫院設有專門的嬰兒病房。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"嬰兒安詳地睡在搖籃裡。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6229,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::infrastructure::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The government plans to invest heavily in ____.","expectedAnswer":"infrastructure","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The government plans to invest heavily in ____.","clozeAnswer":"infrastructure","exampleTranslation":"政府計劃大力投資基礎設施。","reference":{"eng":"infrastructure","kk":"ˈɪnfrəˌstrʌktʃər","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"基礎設施\"  ],  [    \"基礎建設\"  ],  [    \"結構\"  ]]","chEntries":["基礎設施","基礎建設","結構"],"practiceMeaning":"政府計劃大力投資基礎設施。","analysis":"此字為複合詞，由 infra-（在…之下）和 structure（結構）構成。infra- 源自拉丁語，意為「下面」。structure 源自拉丁語 structura，意為「建造，構築」。此字在現代英語中可視為由 infra- 和 structure 組合而成。名詞義指支撐一個社會或組織運作的基本設施和系統，包括交通、通訊、能源、公共工程、社會服務等。中文翻譯為「基礎設施；基礎建設；結構」。","definition":"1. the basic physical and organizational structures and facilities (e.g. buildings, roads, power supplies) that a country or organization needs to operate; 2. the basic framework or structure of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government plans to invest heavily in infrastructure.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府計劃大力投資基礎設施。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Poor infrastructure can hinder economic development.\",\n    \"ch\": \"薄弱的基礎建設會阻礙經濟發展。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The internet is an essential part of modern infrastructure.\",\n    \"ch\": \"網際網路是現代基礎設施的重要組成部分。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"政府計劃大力投資基礎設施。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4447,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u9::inhale::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Please ____ deeply and hold your breath.","expectedAnswer":"inhale","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Please ____ deeply and hold your breath.","clozeAnswer":"inhale","exampleTranslation":"請深吸一口氣並憋住。","reference":{"eng":"inhale","kk":"/ɪnˈheɪl/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['吸入']]","chEntries":["吸入"],"practiceMeaning":"請深吸一口氣並憋住。","analysis":"詞源自拉丁語 'inhālare'，'in-' (in) + 'hālāre' (to breathe)。指將空氣或其他物質吸入肺部。","definition":"to breathe in.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please inhale deeply and hold your breath.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請深吸一口氣並憋住。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"請深吸一口氣並憋住。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3188,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::inject::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The doctor will ____ the vaccine into your arm.","expectedAnswer":"inject","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The doctor will ____ the vaccine into your arm.","clozeAnswer":"inject","exampleTranslation":"醫生會將疫苗注射到你的手臂。","reference":{"eng":"inject","kk":"/ɪnˈdʒɛkt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['注射；注射給藥'], ['注入；灌輸（尤指想法、情感）']]","chEntries":["注射","注射給藥","注入","灌輸"],"practiceMeaning":"醫生會將疫苗注射到你的手臂。","analysis":"詞源來自拉丁語 'injectare'，意為「注入，投擲」，由 'in-'（在...中）+ 'jacere'（扔）組成。'Inject' 的核心是「將某物推入或注入」。最常見的是醫學上的「注射」，將藥物或液體通過針頭注入體內。也可引申為將某物（如想法、情感、資金）注入到某個系統、情況或人身上。","definition":"1. administer (a drug or vaccine) by inserting a needle into a muscle or into a cavity in the body; 2. force (fluid, especially blood) into a vessel or cavity; 3. introduce (a substance) into something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The doctor will inject the vaccine into your arm.\",\n    \"ch\": \"醫生會將疫苗注射到你的手臂。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The new funding will inject life into the struggling arts program.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這筆新資金將為這個陷入困境的藝術項目注入活力。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He needs to inject more confidence into his presentation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他需要在演講中注入更多信心。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"醫生會將疫苗注射到你的手臂。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5597,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l7::injustice::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The report highlighted cases of systemic ____.","expectedAnswer":"injustice","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The report highlighted cases of systemic ____.","clozeAnswer":"injustice","exampleTranslation":"這份報告強調了系統性不公的案例。","reference":{"eng":"injustice","kk":"ɪnˈdʒʌstɪs","tense":"n.","ch":"[['不公'], ['不義'], ['不公之事']]","chEntries":["不公","不義","不公之事"],"practiceMeaning":"這份報告強調了系統性不公的案例。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'injustitia'，由否定字首 'in-'（不）加上 'justitia'（正義）組成。'-ia' 字尾表示狀態或品質。'justitia' 本身源自 'justus'（公正的、合法的），而 'justus' 又源於 'jus'（法律、權利）。構詞學上，'in-' 字首的加入直接否定了「正義」的概念，形成「不正義」或「不公」的狀態。原始語意是「缺乏正義」，演變為指「不公平的行為、待遇或情況」。","definition":"1. Lack of fairness or justice; 2. An unjust act or occurrence.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The report highlighted cases of systemic injustice.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這份報告強調了系統性不公的案例。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She dedicated her life to fighting against injustice.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她畢生致力於反對不公。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這份報告強調了系統性不公的案例。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4731,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::inn::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They stayed at a charming old ____ in the countryside.","expectedAnswer":"inn","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They stayed at a charming old ____ in the countryside.","clozeAnswer":"inn","exampleTranslation":"他們住在鄉村一家迷人的老客棧。","reference":{"eng":"inn","kk":"/ˈɪn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['小旅館'], ['客棧']]","chEntries":["小旅館","客棧"],"practiceMeaning":"他們住在鄉村一家迷人的老客棧。","analysis":"源自古英語 *inne*，指「內部」。原指房屋內部，後演變為提供食宿的小型公共場所，特別是鄉村或公路旁的地方。與 'hotel' 相比，規模較小，通常更傳統。","definition":"1. A small hotel or lodging house, typically in the country.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They stayed at a charming old inn in the countryside.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們住在鄉村一家迷人的老客棧。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The inn offered hearty meals and local ale.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家客棧提供豐盛的餐點和當地啤酒。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們住在鄉村一家迷人的老客棧。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4256,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::inner::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She possessed great ____ strength.","expectedAnswer":"inner","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She possessed great ____ strength.","clozeAnswer":"inner","exampleTranslation":"她擁有巨大的內在力量。","reference":{"eng":"inner","kk":"/ˈɪnər/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['內部的'], ['內在的'], ['隱藏的']]","chEntries":["內部的","內在的","隱藏的"],"practiceMeaning":"她擁有巨大的內在力量。","analysis":"比較級形式，源自古英語 'in'（內）。'Inner' 指的是「在裡面」，與「外面」相對。它可以指物理上的內部，也可以指抽象的、情感或精神層面的內部。","definition":"situated on or toward the inside; internal; relating to the mind or spirit.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She possessed great inner strength.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她擁有巨大的內在力量。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The inner workings of the machine were complex.\",\n    \"ch\": \"機器的內部運作非常複雜。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她擁有巨大的內在力量。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5377,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l2::install::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need to ____ a new air conditioner.","expectedAnswer":"install","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need to ____ a new air conditioner.","clozeAnswer":"install","exampleTranslation":"我們需要安裝一台新空調。","reference":{"eng":"install","kk":"ɪnˈstɔːl","tense":"v.","ch":"[['安裝'], ['設置'], ['就職'], ['配備']]","chEntries":["安裝","設置","就職","配備"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要安裝一台新空調。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 installen，來自古法語 installer，最終來自拉丁語 installare，意為「使就座，安置」。'in-' (in) + stallum (位置、攤位)。核心語意是「將某物放置在預定位置並使其固定或準備就緒」。因此，可用於指「安裝設備」，「設置軟體」，以及「就職」或「冊封」（將某人安置於特定職位）。","definition":"1. place or fix (equipment or machinery) in position ready for use; 2. establish (someone) in a particular position or place, especially in a formal ceremony.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to install a new air conditioner.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要安裝一台新空調。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The new CEO will be installed next month.\",\n    \"ch\": \"新任執行長將於下個月就職。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要安裝一台新空調。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3170,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::instinct::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Birds have an ____ to migrate south for the winter.","expectedAnswer":"instinct","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Birds have an ____ to migrate south for the winter.","clozeAnswer":"instinct","exampleTranslation":"鳥類有向南遷徙以度過冬天的本能。","reference":{"eng":"instinct","kk":"/ˈɪnstɪŋkt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['本能；天性'], ['（對某事的）直覺；天賦']]","chEntries":["本能","天性","直覺","天賦"],"practiceMeaning":"鳥類有向南遷徙以度過冬天的本能。","analysis":"詞源來自拉丁語 'instinctus'，意為「衝動，刺激」，源於 'instinguere'（激勵，驅使）。'Instinct' 指的是一種天生的、非學習而來的行為模式或反應，由生物體的遺傳基因決定，用於應對特定的環境刺激。它也可以引申為對某事的強烈直覺或天賦，一種無需理性思考就能產生的判斷或傾向。","definition":"1. an innate, typically fixed pattern of behavior in animals in response to certain stimuli; 2. a natural or intuitive impulse or tendency.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Birds have an instinct to migrate south for the winter.\",\n    \"ch\": \"鳥類有向南遷徙以度過冬天的本能。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"My instinct told me not to trust him.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我的直覺告訴我不要相信他。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a natural instinct for business.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她有經營生意的天賦。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"鳥類有向南遷徙以度過冬天的本能。","sourceName":"字彙王、龍騰課本","unitName":"U40、L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5699,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l9::instinctive::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Babies have an ____ need to be held.","expectedAnswer":"instinctive","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Babies have an ____ need to be held.","clozeAnswer":"instinctive","exampleTranslation":"嬰兒有一種被擁抱的本能需求。","reference":{"eng":"instinctive","kk":"ɪnˈstɪŋktɪv","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['憑本能的'], ['直覺的'], ['本能的']]","chEntries":["憑本能的","直覺的","本能的"],"practiceMeaning":"嬰兒有一種被擁抱的本能需求。","analysis":"此字由名詞 'instinct' 加上形容詞化後綴 '-ive' 構成。'instinct' 源自拉丁語 instinctus（驅使，激勵），由 instinguere（驅使，激勵）演變而來。'-ive' 後綴使名詞轉化為形容詞，表示「具有……的特性的」。因此，'instinctive' 的核心語意是「與本能、天性或內在驅動力相關的，而非學習或思考的結果」。它描述的是一種發生在意識層面之下的、自動的反應或行為。","definition":"based on or resulting from a natural feeling or urge that is not conscious; natural; not learned.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Babies have an instinctive need to be held.\",\n    \"ch\": \"嬰兒有一種被擁抱的本能需求。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His reaction was instinctive, not deliberate.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的反應是本能的，而非刻意的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"嬰兒有一種被擁抱的本能需求。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4396,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u9::intelligent::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She is an ____ and hardworking student.","expectedAnswer":"intelligent","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She is an ____ and hardworking student.","clozeAnswer":"intelligent","exampleTranslation":"她是一位聰明勤奮的學生。","reference":{"eng":"intelligent","kk":"/ɪnˈtelɪdʒənt/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['聰明的', '有智慧的'], ['（機器、系統）智能的']]","chEntries":["聰明的","有智慧的","智能的"],"practiceMeaning":"她是一位聰明勤奮的學生。","analysis":"詞源自拉丁語 'intelligens'，'inter-' (between) + 'legere' (to choose, gather)。原意是「能夠理解、辨別」。指具備良好理解力、學習能力和判斷力。","definition":"having or showing intelligence, especially of a high level; able to learn, understand, and think knowledgeably.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is an intelligent and hardworking student.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是一位聰明勤奮的學生。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Artificial intelligence is a rapidly developing field.\",\n    \"ch\": \"人工智能是一個快速發展的領域。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她是一位聰明勤奮的學生。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5351,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l1::intend::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"I ____ to finish this book by tonight.","expectedAnswer":"intend","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"I ____ to finish this book by tonight.","clozeAnswer":"intend","exampleTranslation":"我打算今晚讀完這本書。","reference":{"eng":"intend","kk":"ɪnˈtɛnd","tense":"v.","ch":"[['打算'], ['意欲'], ['意圖']]","chEntries":["打算","意欲","意圖"],"practiceMeaning":"我打算今晚讀完這本書。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 intendere，由 in-（朝向）+ tendere（伸展）組成。構詞上，in- 表示「朝向」，tend- 是字根，表示「伸展、拉緊」。原始語意為「朝著某方向伸展」，引申為「心理上朝著某目標努力」，即「意圖、打算」。","definition":"to plan to do something; to have as one's purpose or aim.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I intend to finish this book by tonight.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我打算今晚讀完這本書。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They intend to get married next year.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們打算明年結婚。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我打算今晚讀完這本書。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5350,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l1::intention::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His ____ was to help, not to harm.","expectedAnswer":"intention","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His ____ was to help, not to harm.","clozeAnswer":"intention","exampleTranslation":"他的意圖是幫助，而不是傷害。","reference":{"eng":"intention","kk":"ɪnˈtɛnʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[['意圖'], ['打算'], ['目的']]","chEntries":["意圖","打算","目的"],"practiceMeaning":"他的意圖是幫助，而不是傷害。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 intentio，來自 intendere（伸展、意向、打算），由 in-（朝向）+ tendere（伸展）組成。構詞上，in- 表示「朝向」，tend- 是字根，表示「伸展、拉緊」。原始語意為「朝著某方向伸展」，引申為「心理上朝著某目標努力」，即「意圖、打算」。","definition":"an aim or purpose; a plan or aim.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His intention was to help, not to harm.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的意圖是幫助，而不是傷害。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"What are your intentions regarding this project?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你對這個專案有什麼打算？\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他的意圖是幫助，而不是傷害。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3093,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::interfere::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Please don't ____ in my personal matters.","expectedAnswer":"interfere","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Please don't ____ in my personal matters.","clozeAnswer":"interfere","exampleTranslation":"請不要干涉我的個人事務。","reference":{"eng":"interfere","kk":"/ˌɪntərˈfɪr/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['干涉；干預'], ['妨礙；阻礙']]","chEntries":["干涉","干預","妨礙","阻礙"],"practiceMeaning":"請不要干涉我的個人事務。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'inter-' (between) + 'ferire' (to strike)。核心意義是「在兩者之間插入」，引申為「干涉」。\n1. 干涉；干預：指未經允許介入他人的事務，試圖控制或影響。\n2. 妨礙；阻礙：指阻礙事物的正常進行或發展。","definition":"1. to get involved in a situation in order to influence the outcome; 2. to prevent something from continuing or being able to do something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please don't interfere in my personal matters.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請不要干涉我的個人事務。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Loud noises can interfere with sleep.\",\n    \"ch\": \"嘈雜的噪音會妨礙睡眠。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"請不要干涉我的個人事務。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4635,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::interrupt::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Please don't ____ when I'm speaking.","expectedAnswer":"interrupt","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Please don't ____ when I'm speaking.","clozeAnswer":"interrupt","exampleTranslation":"請在我說話時不要打斷。","reference":{"eng":"interrupt","kk":"/ˌɪntəˈrʌpt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['打斷'], ['中斷'], ['干擾']]","chEntries":["打斷","中斷","干擾"],"practiceMeaning":"請在我說話時不要打斷。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'interrumpere'，意為「打斷、中斷」。'Inter-' (之間) + 'rumpere' (打破、撕裂)。核心概念是使正在進行的過程（對話、活動、流程）停止或延遲。這種中斷通常是突然的、非預期的。","definition":"to stop or break the continuity of; to speak or act so as to prevent someone else from continuing.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please don't interrupt when I'm speaking.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請在我說話時不要打斷。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The rain interrupted the outdoor concert.\",\n    \"ch\": \"雨水打斷了戶外音樂會的進行。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Noise from the street interrupted his sleep.\",\n    \"ch\": \"街道上的噪音中斷了他的睡眠。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"請在我說話時不要打斷。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5647,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l8::invasion::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of the enemy forces was swift.","expectedAnswer":"invasion","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of the enemy forces was swift.","clozeAnswer":"invasion","exampleTranslation":"敵軍的入侵行動迅速。","reference":{"eng":"invasion","kk":"ɪnˈveɪʒən","tense":"n.","ch":"[['入侵'], ['侵略'], ['湧入'], ['（意見、要求等）干擾']]","chEntries":["入侵","侵略","湧入","干擾"],"practiceMeaning":"敵軍的入侵行動迅速。","analysis":"此字由 invade（入侵）+ -sion（名詞字尾）構成。invade 源自拉丁語 invadere，由 in-（進入，into）+ vadere（行走，to go）組成。vadere 來自原始印歐語 *gwem-（行走，to come）。-sion 是常見的名詞字尾，用於將動詞轉為名詞，表示「動作」、「狀態」或「結果」。構詞上，in- 表示「進入」，vadere 提供「行走」或「進入」的核心動作，-sion 將其名詞化。核心語義為「進入」某地，尤指帶有敵意或強制性地。","definition":"an act or instance of invading a country or region with an armed force; an encroachment or intrusion; a sudden rush or influx.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The invasion of the enemy forces was swift.\",\n    \"ch\": \"敵軍的入侵行動迅速。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The city experienced an invasion of tourists during the summer.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座城市在夏季湧入了大量的遊客。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"敵軍的入侵行動迅速。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3889,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::invitation::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We received an ____ to the wedding.","expectedAnswer":"invitation","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We received an ____ to the wedding.","clozeAnswer":"invitation","exampleTranslation":"我們收到了婚禮的邀請。","reference":{"eng":"invitation","kk":"/ˌɪnvɪˈteɪʃən/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['邀請'], ['邀請函']]","chEntries":["邀請","邀請函"],"practiceMeaning":"我們收到了婚禮的邀請。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'invitatio'，'invitare' (to invite) 的名詞形式，意為「邀請」。核心是「呼喚」、「邀請」。指請人參加某事物的請求，或表示這種請求的文件。","definition":"1. a request or order to come somewhere or do something. 2. a written or verbal communication asking someone to attend an event or perform a task.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We received an invitation to the wedding.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們收到了婚禮的邀請。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His invitation was very formal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的邀請非常正式。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Thank you for your kind invitation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"感謝您的盛情邀請。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們收到了婚禮的邀請。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5523,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l5::isolated::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The village is ____ in the mountains.","expectedAnswer":"isolated","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The village is ____ in the mountains.","clozeAnswer":"isolated","exampleTranslation":"這個村莊孤立在山區。","reference":{"eng":"isolated","kk":"ˈaɪsəleɪtɪd","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['孤立的'], ['偏僻的'], ['隔絕的']]","chEntries":["孤立的","偏僻的","隔絕的"],"practiceMeaning":"這個村莊孤立在山區。","analysis":"此字是動詞 'isolate' 的過去分詞，用作形容詞。'isolate' 源自西班牙語 'isla' (island)，透過意語 'isola' 傳入，意為「島嶼」。構詞上，'island' + '-ate'（動詞化字尾）。語意上，'isolate' 指「使成為孤島」，即「使隔絕、使孤立」。因此，'isolated' 作形容詞時，描述的是「被隔離開來、處於孤獨或偏僻狀態」的。它涵蓋了地理上的「偏僻」和社交上的「孤立」兩種情境。","definition":"far away from other places, buildings, or people; remote; forming a separate unit or units.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The village is isolated in the mountains.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個村莊孤立在山區。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He felt isolated after his friends moved away.\",\n    \"ch\": \"朋友們搬走後，他感到孤立無援。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個村莊孤立在山區。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5384,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l2::issue::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Climate change is a major global ____.","expectedAnswer":"issue","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Climate change is a major global ____.","clozeAnswer":"issue","exampleTranslation":"氣候變遷是一個主要的全球性議題。","reference":{"eng":"issue","kk":"ˈɪʃuː","tense":"n.","ch":"[['問題'], ['議題'], ['爭議'], ['（報刊）期'], ['（小孩、動物的）後代'], ['發行']]","chEntries":["問題","議題","爭議","期","後代","發行"],"practiceMeaning":"氣候變遷是一個主要的全球性議題。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 escuë (出去、發出)，來自拉丁語 exire (出來)。核心語意是「從某處出來、出現」。因此，'issue' 作名詞時，可以指「一個出現或引起關注的事件或情況」（問題、議題），「報刊的某一期」（出版物從發行源出來），或「子女」（從父母那裡出現）等。","definition":"1. an important topic or problem for debate or discussion; 2. a regular weekly or monthly magazine or newspaper; 3. the act of supplying or distributing something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Climate change is a major global issue.\",\n    \"ch\": \"氣候變遷是一個主要的全球性議題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is the latest issue of the magazine.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是最新一期的雜誌。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"氣候變遷是一個主要的全球性議題。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4363,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::it-s-pouring-now::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We can't go out, ____!","expectedAnswer":"it’s pouring now","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We can't go out, ____!","clozeAnswer":"it’s pouring now","exampleTranslation":"我們不能出去，現在正在下大雨！","reference":{"eng":"it’s pouring now","kk":"None","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['現在正在下大雨']]","chEntries":["現在正在下大雨"],"practiceMeaning":"我們不能出去，現在正在下大雨！","analysis":"此為片語分析。'it's' (it is) 指『這是』。'pouring' (v. present participle) 源自 'pour' (v.)，意為『傾倒』，在此引申為『（雨）傾瀉』。'now' (adv.) 指『現在』。整個片語表示『現在雨下得非常大』。","definition":"it is raining very heavily at the present time","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We can't go out, it’s pouring now!\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們不能出去，現在正在下大雨！\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Look outside – it’s pouring now.\",\n    \"ch\": \"看看外面——現在正在下大雨。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們不能出去，現在正在下大雨！","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3901,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::jealous::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He was ____ of his brother's success.","expectedAnswer":"jealous","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He was ____ of his brother's success.","clozeAnswer":"jealous","exampleTranslation":"他嫉妒他哥哥的成功。","reference":{"eng":"jealous","kk":"/ˈdʒɛləs/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['嫉妒的'], ['羨慕的'], ['提防的']]","chEntries":["嫉妒的","羨慕的","提防的"],"practiceMeaning":"他嫉妒他哥哥的成功。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'zelus'，'zelotypus' (zealous)，意為「熱情的」。其詞源演變較為複雜，但現代意義主要指因擔心失去所愛或所擁有的東西，或因他人擁有自己所沒有的而產生的不滿、敵意或不安。也可指對某事物極為小心、防護的。","definition":"1. feeling or showing envy of someone or their achievements and advantages. 2. feeling or showing suspicion of someone's unfaithfulness to you. 3. fiercely protective or suspicious of (someone or something).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was jealous of his brother's success.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他嫉妒他哥哥的成功。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She felt jealous when her friend got the promotion.\",\n    \"ch\": \"當她的朋友獲得晉升時，她感到嫉妒。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Be careful, he's jealous of anyone who tries to get close to his wife.\",\n    \"ch\": \"小心點，他嫉妒任何試圖接近他妻子的人。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他嫉妒他哥哥的成功。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4691,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::jeep::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They hired a ____ to explore the rugged terrain.","expectedAnswer":"jeep","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They hired a ____ to explore the rugged terrain.","clozeAnswer":"jeep","exampleTranslation":"他們租了一輛吉普車來探索崎嶇的地形。","reference":{"eng":"jeep","kk":"/ˈdʒip/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['吉普車（越野車）']]","chEntries":["吉普車"],"practiceMeaning":"他們租了一輛吉普車來探索崎嶇的地形。","analysis":"原為第二次世界大戰時期軍用車輛的通用名稱，據信源自 GP（General Purpose，通用）的縮寫，或是由士兵口語發音演變而成。後成為一種註冊商標，但廣泛用於指代多功能、輕便的越野車。","definition":"1. A robust, four-wheel-drive vehicle, typically with an open top and removable hood, designed for off-road use.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They hired a jeep to explore the rugged terrain.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們租了一輛吉普車來探索崎嶇的地形。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The jeep was equipped for all kinds of weather.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這輛吉普車配備了應對各種天氣的設備。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們租了一輛吉普車來探索崎嶇的地形。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5701,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l9::jury::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ reached a unanimous verdict.","expectedAnswer":"jury","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ reached a unanimous verdict.","clozeAnswer":"jury","exampleTranslation":"陪審團達成了一致的裁決。","reference":{"eng":"jury","kk":"ˈdʒʊəri","tense":"n.","ch":"[['陪審團']]","chEntries":["陪審團"],"practiceMeaning":"陪審團達成了一致的裁決。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 juree（宣誓，陪審員），來自拉丁語 iurare（發誓），源自 ius（法律）。構詞上，此字表示「一群被召喚來聽取證據並做出裁決的人」。其核心語意與「發誓」和「法律」緊密相關，指代在法庭上，由一群普通公民組成的、負責判斷事實真相的組織。","definition":"a group of people, typically twelve in number, who together consider the case of a defendant in a trial, and reach a verdict.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The jury reached a unanimous verdict.\",\n    \"ch\": \"陪審團達成了一致的裁決。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was acquitted by the jury.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他被陪審團判無罪。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"陪審團達成了一致的裁決。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4667,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::keep-a-record::idiom","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It's important to ____ of all your expenses.","expectedAnswer":"keep a record","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It's important to ____ of all your expenses.","clozeAnswer":"keep a record","exampleTranslation":"記錄下你所有的開銷是很重要的。","reference":{"eng":"keep a record","kk":"/kiːp ə ˈrɛkərd/","tense":"idiom","ch":"[['記錄'], ['保存紀錄']]","chEntries":["記錄","保存紀錄"],"practiceMeaning":"記錄下你所有的開銷是很重要的。","analysis":"此為固定片語。'Keep' (保持、維護) + 'a record' (一個紀錄)。指系統地記錄、保存資訊或數據，以便日後查閱或參考。","definition":"to maintain a systematic collection of information or data.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's important to keep a record of all your expenses.\",\n    \"ch\": \"記錄下你所有的開銷是很重要的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The library keeps a record of all borrowed books.\",\n    \"ch\": \"圖書館保存著所有借出書籍的紀錄。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"記錄下你所有的開銷是很重要的。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4298,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::keep-up-with-the-trends::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It's important for fashion designers to ____.","expectedAnswer":"keep up with the trends","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It's important for fashion designers to ____.","clozeAnswer":"keep up with the trends","exampleTranslation":"對於時尚設計師來說，跟上趨勢非常重要。","reference":{"eng":"keep up with the trends","kk":"/kiːp ʌp wɪð ðə trɛndz/","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['跟上趨勢']]","chEntries":["跟上趨勢"],"practiceMeaning":"對於時尚設計師來說，跟上趨勢非常重要。","analysis":"這是包含動詞 'keep up with'（跟上、保持同步）和名詞 'trends'（趨勢）的片語。'Keep up with the trends' 指「了解並適應當前的流行、發展方向或時尚」。","definition":"to stay informed about and follow the current popular styles or developments.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's important for fashion designers to keep up with the trends.\",\n    \"ch\": \"對於時尚設計師來說，跟上趨勢非常重要。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Young people tend to keep up with the latest technological trends.\",\n    \"ch\": \"年輕人傾向於跟上最新的科技趨勢。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"對於時尚設計師來說，跟上趨勢非常重要。","sourc