的界線/極限」到「範圍僅限於此」的概念，進而發展出「僅僅是」、「不過是」的含義。另一說法是，它可能與強調「單一」或「微小」的概念有關。現代用法中，\"mere\" 作形容詞，常用來強調事物之少、之小、之普通，或僅僅是某種狀態，與 \"only\" 或 \"just\" 類似，但常帶有一點貶低或不以為然的語氣，強調其不重要性或缺乏其他特質。例如 \"a mere child\"（只是一個小孩），暗示經驗或能力不足。","definition":"1. That is only or no more than what is stated; 2. Small or insignificant.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It took me a mere ten minutes to finish the task.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我只花了短短十分鐘就完成了任務。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a mere beginner in this field.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在這個領域只是一個初學者。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The accident was caused by a mere oversight.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這次意外僅僅是一個疏忽造成的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我只花了短短十分鐘就完成了任務。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4747,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::mess-up::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Be careful not to ____ the papers.","expectedAnswer":"mess up","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Be careful not to ____ the papers.","clozeAnswer":"mess up","exampleTranslation":"小心不要把文件弄亂。","reference":{"eng":"mess up","kk":"/ˈmɛs ʌp/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['弄亂'], ['搞砸'], ['（非正式）犯錯']]","chEntries":["弄亂","搞砸","犯錯"],"practiceMeaning":"小心不要把文件弄亂。","analysis":"動詞片語，由 'mess'（混亂）和 'up'（向上，表示完成、徹底）構成。指使某物變得混亂、髒亂，或將某事搞砸。也可用於形容非正式地犯錯。","definition":"1. To make something untidy or dirty. 2. To spoil or ruin something. 3. (informal) To make a mistake.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Be careful not to mess up the papers.\",\n    \"ch\": \"小心不要把文件弄亂。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He really messed up his chances of getting the job.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他真的搞砸了他獲得那份工作的機會。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I'm sorry, I really messed up.\",\n    \"ch\": \"對不起，我真的搞砸了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"小心不要把文件弄亂。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6128,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::metropolitan::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ area","expectedAnswer":"metropolitan","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ area","clozeAnswer":"metropolitan","exampleTranslation":"都會區","reference":{"eng":"metropolitan","kk":"ˌmɛtrəˈpɑːlɪtən","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"都會的\"  ],  [    \"大都會的\"  ],  [    \"首府的\"  ]]","chEntries":["都會的","大都會的","首府的"],"practiceMeaning":"都會區","analysis":"此字源自希臘語 mētropolis，由 mētēr（母親）和 polis（城市）組成，意為「母城」，指一個地區的中心城市或首府。構詞上，mētēr 意為「母親」，polis 意為「城市」。因此，metropolitan 的核心語義是「與大城市相關」。此形容詞指與大都市、其區域或居民相關的。其語意演變是從「母城」到「大城市」。","definition":"1. relating to or denoting a metropolis or its inhabitants; 2. the capital or chief city of a country or region.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"metropolitan area\",\n    \"ch\": \"都會區\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The city has a large metropolitan population.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座城市擁有龐大的都會人口。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"metropolitan opera\",\n    \"ch\": \"大都會歌劇院\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"都會區","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5791,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::midst::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He found himself in the ____ of a crowd.","expectedAnswer":"midst","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He found himself in the ____ of a crowd.","clozeAnswer":"midst","exampleTranslation":"他發現自己身處人群之中。","reference":{"eng":"midst","kk":"mɪdst","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"中間\"  ],  [    \"當中\"  ],  [    \"人群中\"  ]]","chEntries":["中間","當中","人群中"],"practiceMeaning":"他發現自己身處人群之中。","analysis":"此字為名詞，源自古英語middel（中間）+ -est（最高級後綴），是middle的最高級形式。然而，它後來演變為獨立的名詞，表示「中間」或「中央」。其詞源可追溯至原始日耳曼語\\\\*midjilastaz。核心語義是指「某事物或某群人、事物的中心或中間位置」。通常用於固定搭配，如in the midst of。語意演變上，從「最中間」的比較級概念，演變為表示「中間」或「中央」的狀態或位置。","definition":"1. the middle of a place or area; 2. the middle of a group of people or things.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He found himself in the midst of a crowd.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他發現自己身處人群之中。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"In the midst of the chaos, she remained calm.\",\n    \"ch\": \"在混亂之中，她保持了鎮定。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The small village lies in the midst of rolling hills.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個小村莊坐落在連綿起伏的丘陵之間。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他發現自己身處人群之中。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6231,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::minimal::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The cost of the repairs was ____.","expectedAnswer":"minimal","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The cost of the repairs was ____.","clozeAnswer":"minimal","exampleTranslation":"維修費用是極小的。","reference":{"eng":"minimal","kk":"ˈmɪnɪml","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"最小的\"  ],  [    \"極小的\"  ],  [    \"最低限度的\"  ]]","chEntries":["最小的","極小的","最低限度的"],"practiceMeaning":"維修費用是極小的。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 minimus，是 parvus（小的）的最高級，意為「最小的」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作形容詞時，指數量、程度或大小極小，是可能的最低水平。中文翻譯為「最小的；極小的；最低限度的」。","definition":"1. the smallest possible amount or degree; 2. very small.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The cost of the repairs was minimal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"維修費用是極小的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to make minimal changes to the design.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們只需要對設計做最低限度的修改。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The artist used a minimal color palette.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位藝術家使用了極簡的調色盤。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"維修費用是極小的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6232,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::minimize::vt","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We should try to ____ our environmental impact.","expectedAnswer":"minimize","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We should try to ____ our environmental impact.","clozeAnswer":"minimize","exampleTranslation":"我們應該盡量減少我們的環境影響。","reference":{"eng":"minimize","kk":"ˈmɪnɪmaɪz","tense":"vt.","ch":"[  [    \"使最小化\"  ],  [    \"減到最低\"  ],  [    \"輕視\"  ],  [    \"低估\"  ]]","chEntries":["使最小化","減到最低","輕視","低估"],"practiceMeaning":"我們應該盡量減少我們的環境影響。","analysis":"此字由形容詞 minimal（最小的）加上動詞字尾 -ize（使…）構成。minimal 源自拉丁語 minimus。字尾 -ize 將形容詞轉為動詞，表示「使達到最小的程度」。核心語義是將某事物（如成本、損失、影響、風險）減少到可能的最少程度，或低估其重要性。此及物動詞義必須接受詞，例如 minimize costs、minimize risk、minimize damage。中文翻譯為「使最小化；減到最低；輕視；低估」。","definition":"1. to reduce something to the smallest possible amount or degree; 2. to treat or regard something as unimportant.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We should try to minimize our environmental impact.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們應該盡量減少我們的環境影響。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company is working to minimize losses.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司正努力將損失減到最低。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Don't minimize the importance of this issue.\",\n    \"ch\": \"不要輕視這個問題的重要性。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們應該盡量減少我們的環境影響。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3094,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::minimum::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need to maintain a ____ level of safety.","expectedAnswer":"minimum","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need to maintain a ____ level of safety.","clozeAnswer":"minimum","exampleTranslation":"我們需要維持最低的安全水平。","reference":{"eng":"minimum","kk":"/ˈmɪnɪməm/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['最小的；最低的']]","chEntries":["最小的","最低的"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要維持最低的安全水平。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'minimus' (smallest)。核心意義是「最小」。\n1. 最小的；最低的：指數量、程度、或尺寸上的最小可能值。","definition":"1. the smallest possible amount or degree; 2. the least quantity.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to maintain a minimum level of safety.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要維持最低的安全水平。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The minimum wage has been increased.\",\n    \"ch\": \"最低工資已經提高了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要維持最低的安全水平。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4544,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::minus::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He received a ____ score on the test.","expectedAnswer":"minus","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He received a ____ score on the t