ar one another","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We live in a quiet neighborhood.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們住的社區很寧靜。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The children play in the neighborhood.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子們在鄰近地區玩耍。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He's a well-respected member of the neighborhood.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是社區裡備受尊敬的一員。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們住的社區很寧靜。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3931,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::normal::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His behavior is not ____ for him.","expectedAnswer":"normal","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His behavior is not ____ for him.","clozeAnswer":"normal","exampleTranslation":"他的行為對他來說很不正常。","reference":{"eng":"normal","kk":"/ˈnɔːrməl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['正常的'], ['標準的']]","chEntries":["正常的","標準的"],"practiceMeaning":"他的行為對他來說很不正常。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'normalis'，由 'norma' (意為「規則、準則」) 演變而來。指符合標準、規則或常規的。","definition":"1. conforming to a standard; usual, typical, or expected; 2. the average or standard condition.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His behavior is not normal for him.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的行為對他來說很不正常。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It is normal to feel tired after a long day.\",\n    \"ch\": \"長日結束後感到疲倦是正常的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The patient's temperature returned to normal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"病人的體溫恢復正常。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他的行為對他來說很不正常。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5792,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::notify::vt","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Please ____ us if you plan to change your address.","expectedAnswer":"notify","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Please ____ us if you plan to change your address.","clozeAnswer":"notify","exampleTranslation":"如果您打算更改地址，請通知我們。","reference":{"eng":"notify","kk":"ˈnoʊtɪˌfaɪ","tense":"vt.","ch":"[  [    \"通知\"  ],  [    \"告知\"  ],  [    \"警告\"  ]]","chEntries":["通知","告知","警告"],"practiceMeaning":"如果您打算更改地址，請通知我們。","analysis":"此字為及物動詞，源自拉丁語notificare，由nota（標記；標誌）+facere（製作；使）組成。notus是notare（標記）的過去分詞。核心語義是「用標記或訊息告知某人」。語意演變上，從「做標記」的概念，引申為「透過某種方式（書面、口頭）告知某人事實或訊息」。","definition":"1. to inform someone about something formally or officially; 2. to give notice of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please notify us if you plan to change your address.\",\n    \"ch\": \"如果您打算更改地址，請通知我們。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The authorities notified the public about the upcoming storm.\",\n    \"ch\": \"當局向公眾發布了關於即將到來的風暴的通知。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"You must notify the bank of any suspicious transactions.\",\n    \"ch\": \"您必須向銀行報告任何可疑交易。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"如果您打算更改地址，請通知我們。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5606,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l7::nursery::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The baby slept soundly in the ____.","expectedAnswer":"nursery","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The baby slept soundly in the ____.","clozeAnswer":"nursery","exampleTranslation":"嬰兒在育嬰室裡睡得很香。","reference":{"eng":"nursery","kk":"ˈnɜrsəri","tense":"n.","ch":"[['育嬰室'], ['托兒所'], ['苗圃'], ['（植物）繁殖場']]","chEntries":["育嬰室","托兒所","苗圃","繁殖場"],"practiceMeaning":"嬰兒在育嬰室裡睡得很香。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 'nursen'（哺乳、照料），而 'nursen' 又源於古法語 'nourrir'（餵養、滋養），最終可追溯至拉丁語 'nutrire'（餵養、滋養）。構詞學上，核心是與「餵養」、「照料」相關的詞根，加上名詞化後綴 '-ery'。'-ery' 字尾常指「地方」、「場所」、「行業」或「收藏」。因此，'nursery' 最初意為「照料嬰兒的地方」，引申為「托兒所」或「育嬰室」。同時，由於「滋養」的概念也適用於植物，故引申出「苗圃」或「繁殖場」的用法。","definition":"1. A room in a house or apartment in which a baby sleeps or plays; 2. A place where children are cared for during the day; 3. A place where young plants are grown for sale.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The baby slept soundly in the nursery.\",\n    \"ch\": \"嬰兒在育嬰室裡睡得很香。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She enrolled her child in a local nursery school.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她為她的孩子報名了一所當地的托兒所。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\