"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Vegetables are highly nutritious.\",\n    \"ch\": \"蔬菜營養豐富。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A nutritious diet is important for overall health.\",\n    \"ch\": \"營養豐富的飲食對整體健康很重要。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"蔬菜營養豐富。","sourceName":"字彙王、龍騰課本","unitName":"U41、L2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4090,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::obey-the-traffic-signals::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Drivers must ____.","expectedAnswer":"obey the traffic signals","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Drivers must ____.","clozeAnswer":"obey the traffic signals","exampleTranslation":"駕駛員必須遵守交通號誌。","reference":{"eng":"obey the traffic signals","kk":"/əˈbeɪ ðə ˈtræfɪk ˈsɪɡnəlz/","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['遵守交通號誌']]","chEntries":["遵守交通號誌"],"practiceMeaning":"駕駛員必須遵守交通號誌。","analysis":"此片語由 'obey' (遵守), 'the' (定冠詞), 'traffic' (交通), 'signals' (信號) 組成。'obey' 源自拉丁語 'oboedire' (to listen to)。'traffic signals' 指用於控制交通流動的信號燈。整個片語強調按照交通號誌的指示行動。","definition":"to follow the directions given by traffic lights","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"駕駛員必須遵守交通號誌。\",\n    \"eng\": \"Drivers must obey the traffic signals.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"不遵守交通號誌 rất nguy hiểm。\",\n    \"eng\": \"It is dangerous not to obey the traffic signals.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"駕駛員必須遵守交通號誌。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3190,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::object::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The police found a strange ____ at the scene of the crime.","expectedAnswer":"object","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The police found a strange ____ at the scene of the crime.","clozeAnswer":"object","exampleTranslation":"警方在犯罪現場發現了一個奇怪的物體。","reference":{"eng":"object","kk":"/ˈɒbdʒɪkt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['物體；物品'], ['（名詞、動詞等的）賓語'], ['目的；目標']]","chEntries":["物體","物品","賓語","目的","目標"],"practiceMeaning":"警方在犯罪現場發現了一個奇怪的物體。","analysis":"詞源來自拉丁語 'obiectum'，意為「被提出來的東西」。'Object' 作名詞時，有幾個主要含義：一是物理上可見、可觸摸的「物體」。二是語言學上，句子中承受動作的「賓語」。三是引申義，指某事的「目標」、「目的」或「對象」。這三個意思都圍繞著「被感知、被處理或被指向」的概念。","definition":"1. a material thing that can be seen and touched; 2. a person, thing, or idea that is the subject of an action or feeling; 3. (grammar) a word or phrase naming the person or thing that is affected by the action of a verb.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police found a strange object at the scene of the crime.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警方在犯罪現場發現了一個奇怪的物體。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her main object in life is to help others.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她人生的主要目標是幫助他人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"In the sentence 'He kicked the ball', 'ball' is the direct object.\",\n    \"ch\": \"在句子「他踢了球」中，「球」是直接賓語。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"警方在犯罪現場發現了一個奇怪的物體。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4280,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::observe::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Scientists ____ the stars through telescopes.","expectedAnswer":"observe","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Scientists ____ the stars through telescopes.","clozeAnswer":"observe","exampleTranslation":"科學家透過望遠鏡觀測星體。","reference":{"eng":"observe","kk":"/əbˈzɜːrv/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['觀察'], ['觀測'], ['遵守（法律、規則）'], ['說（道）']]","chEntries":["觀察","觀測","遵守","說"],"practiceMeaning":"科學家透過望遠鏡觀測星體。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'observare'，由 'ob-'（朝向、針對）+ 'servare'（保存、保持、注意）組成。'Observe' 有多個義項：1. 「仔細觀看、觀察」；2. 「遵守、履行（法律、規定）」；3. 「說、評論」。這些義項都與「注意」、「關注」或「對事物有一定方式的反應」有關。","definition":"to watch carefully; to notice; to obey (a law, rule, or custom); to make a remark.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Scientists observe the stars through telescopes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"科學家透過望遠鏡觀測星體。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It is important to observe traffic laws.\",\n    \"ch\": \"遵守交通法規很重要。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He observed that the weather was changing.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他说道天氣正在改變。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"科學家透過望遠鏡觀測星體。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5526,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l5::obtain::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need to ____ permission before starting the project.","expectedAnswer":"obtain","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need to ____ permission before starting the project.","clozeAnswer":"obtain","exampleTranslation":"在開始這個專案之前，我們需要獲得許可。","reference":{"eng":"obtain","kk":"əbˈteɪn","tense":"v.","ch":"[['獲得'], ['得到'], ['購得']]","chEntries":["獲得","得到","購得"],"practiceMeaning":"在開始這個專案之前，我們需要獲得許可。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 'obtenir'，來自拉丁語 'obtinere'，由 'ob-' (against, before, by) + 'tenere' (to hold) 構成。原始語義是「堅持持有」或「通過努力獲得」。構詞上，'ob-' 可表示「獲得」或「到達」，'ten-' 是 'tenere' 的詞幹，意為「持有、擁有」。'obtain' 的核心語意是「通過努力、請求或購買等方式得到」。它強調的不是單純的取得，而是包含了一定的過程或手段。語意演變是從「堅持持有」到「努力取得」的過程。","definition":"to get, acquire, or secure (something).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to obtain permission before starting the project.\",\n    \"ch\": \"在開始這個專案之前，我們需要獲得許可。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It is difficult to obtain rare books.\",\n    \"ch\": \"獲得稀有書籍很困難。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"在開始這個專案之前，我們需要獲得許可。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4514,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::on::prep","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The book is ____ the table.","expectedAnswer":"on","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The book is ____ the table.","clozeAnswer":"on","exampleTranslation":"書在桌子上。","reference":{"eng":"on","kk":"/ɔːn/","tense":"prep.","ch":"[['在...之上'], ['關於'], ['正在進行（演出、廣播等）'], ['附著於'], ['持續（一段時間）']]","chEntries":["在...之上","關於","正在進行","附著於","持續"],"practiceMeaning":"書在桌子上。","analysis":"源自古英語 on。是一個表示位置、時間、狀態的多功能介詞。核心語意是「接觸」、「附著」或「覆蓋」。引申義包括「關於」、「處於某種狀態」等。","definition":"1. Physically in contact with and supported by (a surface); 2. Used to indicate the subject or topic of a conversation or piece of writing; 3. Occupying a particular position or place; 4. In the course of being broadcast or performed.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The book is on the table.\",\n    \"ch\": \"書在桌子上。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They are working on a new project.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們正在進行一個新項目。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The concert is on Saturday.\",\n    \"ch\": \"音樂會在星期六。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He lectured on ancient history.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他講授了古代史。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"書在桌子上。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4359,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::on-a-massive-scale::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company is expanding ____.","expectedAnswer":"on a massive scale","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company is expanding ____.","clozeAnswer":"on a massive scale","exampleTranslation":"這家公司正在大規模擴張。","reference":{"eng":"on a massive scale","kk":"None","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['大規模地']]","chEntries":["大規模地"],"practiceMeaning":"這家公司正在大規模擴張。","analysis":"此為片語分析。'on a scale' 指『以…的規模』。'massive' (adj.) 源自拉丁語 'massa' (mass, lump)，意為『巨大的、大量的』。結合起來，表示『以極大的規模』，『大規模地』進行某事。","definition":"very large in size or amount","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company is expanding on a massive scale.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司正在大規模擴張。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The disaster relief efforts were carried out on a massive scale.\",\n    \"ch\": \"災難救援工作是大規模進行的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這家公司正在大規模擴張。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4084,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::on-formal-occasions::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She always dresses elegantly ____.","expectedAnswer":"on formal occasions","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She always dresses elegantly ____.","clozeAnswer":"on formal occasions","exampleTranslation":"她在正式場合總是穿著優雅。","reference":{"eng":"on formal occasions","