y","kk":"/ˈpɑːrʃəli/","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['部分地；不完全地']]","chEntries":["部分地","不完全地"],"practiceMeaning":"那棟建築在火災中被部分摧毀。","analysis":"由 'partial' 加上 '-ly' (副詞後綴) 構成。指在一定程度上，但不完全。","definition":"to some extent; not completely.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The building was partially destroyed in the fire.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那棟建築在火災中被部分摧毀。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He understood the explanation partially.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他只是部分地理解了那個解釋。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"那棟建築在火災中被部分摧毀。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3316,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::particular::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Do you have any ____ reason for asking?","expectedAnswer":"particular","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Do you have any ____ reason for asking?","clozeAnswer":"particular","exampleTranslation":"你問這個有什麼特別的原因嗎？","reference":{"eng":"particular","kk":"/pərˈtɪkjələr/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['特定的；具體的'], ['特別的；過分的；苛求的'], ['堅持己見的；固執的']]","chEntries":["特定的","具體的","特別的","過分的","苛求的","堅持己見的","固執的"],"practiceMeaning":"你問這個有什麼特別的原因嗎？","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'particularis'，由 'pars' (部分) 演變而來。指單獨的、特定的、非普遍的。也可用於形容對細節要求嚴格、挑剔，或對某事非常堅持。","definition":"1. used to refer to a specific person or thing rather than to all people or things; 2. very fussy or demanding; 3. having a strong opinion about something and refusing to change it.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Do you have any particular reason for asking?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你問這個有什麼特別的原因嗎？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is very particular about his food.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對食物非常講究。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a particular dislike for loud music.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她特別討厭吵鬧的音樂。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"你問這個有什麼特別的原因嗎？","sourceName":"字彙王、龍騰課本","unitName":"U42、L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5305,"wordRef":"字彙王::u63::patch::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He put a ____ on his torn trousers.","expectedAnswer":"patch","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He put a ____ on his torn trousers.","clozeAnswer":"patch","exampleTranslation":"他給他破了的褲子打了一個補丁。","reference":{"eng":"patch","kk":"pætʃ","tense":"n.","ch":"[['補丁', '修補處'], ['小塊（土地、區域）'], ['（電子設備上的）修補程式、補丁']]","chEntries":["補丁","修補處","小塊","修補程式、補丁"],"practiceMeaning":"他給他破了的褲子打了一個補丁。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 'pach'，意為「縫補、修補」，可能與低地德語 'patsken'（輕拍、修補）有關。核心語意為「用於修補的塊狀物」或「修補後的小區域」。廣泛用於衣物上的補丁、土地上的一小塊區域、或軟體上的修正檔。","definition":"a piece of material used to cover a hole or mend a tear; a small area of something that is different from the rest of it; a piece of software code designed to fix bugs or improve performance.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He put a patch on his torn trousers.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他給他破了的褲子打了一個補丁。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There's a small patch of garden behind the house.\",\n    \"ch\": \"房子後面有一小塊花園。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The software update includes several security patches.\",\n    \"ch\": \"軟體更新包含幾個安全補丁。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他給他破了的褲子打了一個補丁。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U63"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5306,"wordRef":"字彙王::u63::pathetic::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The lost dog looked ____.","expectedAnswer":"pathetic","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The lost dog looked ____.","clozeAnswer":"pathetic","exampleTranslation":"那隻走失的狗看起來很可憐。","reference":{"eng":"pathetic","kk":"pəˈθɛtɪk","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['可憐的', '悲哀的'], ['令人同情的', '惹人憐愛的'], ['（令人）不滿的，遜的，可笑的']]","chEntries":["可憐的","悲哀的","令人同情的","惹人憐愛的","不滿的，遜的，可笑的"],"practiceMeaning":"那隻走失的狗看起來很可憐。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'patheticus'，來自希臘語 'pathētikos' (παθητικός)，意為「感受到的，情感的」，來自 'pathos' (πάθος)，意為「苦難，情感」。構詞上，'path-' 為詞根，'-etikos' 為形容詞後綴。原始語意與「情感」或「痛苦」有關。現代英語中的 'pathetic' 涵蓋了「引起同情、可憐」的意思，但更常用來形容「令人同情到覺得可笑、遜」的情況，帶有輕蔑意味。","definition":"arousing pity, especially through vulnerability or sadness; miserably weak or inadequate.","example":"[\n  {\n