aking a rule.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The penalty for speeding is a fine.\",\n    \"ch\": \"超速的罰款是罰金。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The team was given a penalty for a foul.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該隊因犯規受到懲罰。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"超速的罰款是罰金。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5308,"wordRef":"字彙王::u63::pension::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She receives a modest ____ from her former employer.","expectedAnswer":"pension","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She receives a modest ____ from her former employer.","clozeAnswer":"pension","exampleTranslation":"她從前雇主那裡領取一筆不多的退休金。","reference":{"eng":"pension","kk":"ˈpɛnʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[['養老金', '退休金'], ['（政府給予的）津貼、補助金']]","chEntries":["養老金","退休金","津貼、補助金"],"practiceMeaning":"她從前雇主那裡領取一筆不多的退休金。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'pensio'（支付，稱重），來自 'pendere'（to hang, to weigh, to pay）。構詞上，'pens-' 為詞根，'-ion' 為名詞後綴。原始語意為「支付」。此語意引申為定期支付的款項，尤其是指退休後從雇主或政府處獲得的「養老金」。","definition":"a regular payment made during a person's retirement from a former employer or the state; a sum paid regularly to a person.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She receives a modest pension from her former employer.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她從前雇主那裡領取一筆不多的退休金。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government plans to increase the state pension.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府計劃增加國家養老金。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她從前雇主那裡領取一筆不多的退休金。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U63"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3944,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::performance::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The band's ____ was electrifying.","expectedAnswer":"performance","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The band's ____ was electrifying.","clozeAnswer":"performance","exampleTranslation":"樂團的表演令人振奮。","reference":{"eng":"performance","kk":"/pərˈfɔːrməns/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['表演', '演出'], ['表現', '績效'], ['性能']]","chEntries":["表演","演出","表現","績效","性能"],"pr