Ref":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::put-off::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They decided to ____ the meeting until Friday.","expectedAnswer":"put off","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They decided to ____ the meeting until Friday.","clozeAnswer":"put off","exampleTranslation":"他們決定將會議推遲到週五。","reference":{"eng":"put off","kk":"/pʊt ˈɔf/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['推遲'], ['使反感'], ['使人分心']]","chEntries":["推遲","使反感","使人分心"],"practiceMeaning":"他們決定將會議推遲到週五。","analysis":"動詞片語，由 'put'（放置）和 'off'（離開、關閉）構成。第一義指將事情延後、推遲。第二義指因厭惡或不喜而產生距離感，使人產生反感。第三義指使人的注意力從某事轉移開。","definition":"1. To postpone or defer something. 2. To cause someone to dislike someone or something. 3. To distract someone.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They decided to put off the meeting until Friday.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們決定將會議推遲到週五。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His rude behavior really put me off.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他粗魯的行為真的讓我反感。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Don't let these minor issues put you off your main goal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"不要讓這些小問題使你分心於你的主要目標。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們決定將會議推遲到週五。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5800,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::questionnaire::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Please complete the ____ honestly.","expectedAnswer":"questionnaire","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Please complete the ____ honestly.","clozeAnswer":"questionnaire","exampleTranslation":"請誠實地填寫問卷。","reference":{"eng":"questionnaire","kk":"ˌkwɛstʃəˈnɛr","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"問卷\"  ],  [    \"調查表\"  ]]","chEntries":["問卷","調查表"],"practiceMeaning":"請誠實地填寫問卷。","analysis":"此字為名詞，源自法語questionnaire，是question（問題）的指小詞或名詞形式。question源自拉丁語quaestio，意為「詢問；搜查」，來自quaerere（尋找；詢問）。核心語義是指「一組用於收集訊息或意見的書面問題」。語意演變上，由「問題」的概念，發展為「收集問題的表格」這一具體物品。","definition":"1. a set of printed or written questions, especially one that is filled out by many people to collect information.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please complete the questionnaire honestly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請誠實地填寫問卷。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We will send out a questionnaire to gather customer feedback.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們將發送一份問卷來收集客戶意見。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The survey includes a detailed questionnaire on living habits.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該調查包含了一份關於生活習慣的詳細問卷。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"請誠實地填寫問卷。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4433,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u9::quit::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He decided to ____ smoking.","expectedAnswer":"quit","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He decided to ____ smoking.","clozeAnswer":"quit","exampleTranslation":"他決定戒菸。","reference":{"eng":"quit","kk":"/kwɪt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['停止', '放棄'], ['辭職', '離開']]","chEntries":["停止","放棄","辭職","離開"],"practiceMeaning":"他決定戒菸。","analysis":"詞源自古法語 'quiter'，源自拉丁語 'quietus' (at rest)。核心概念是「停止、結束」，引申為離開工作崗位或停止做某事。","definition":"to stop doing something; to leave your job or school.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He decided to quit smoking.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他決定戒菸。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She quit her job after only six months.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她工作了僅六個月就辭職了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他決定戒菸。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5856,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::ragged::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He wore ____ clothes.","expectedAnswer":"ragged","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He wore ____ clothes.","clozeAnswer":"ragged","exampleTranslation":"他穿著襤褸的衣服。","reference":{"eng":"ragged","kk":"ˈræɡɪd","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"破舊的\"  ],  [    \"襤褸的\"  ],  [    \"參差不齊的\"  ],  [    \"沙啞的\"  ]]","chEntries":["破舊的","襤褸的","參差不齊的","沙啞的"],"practiceMeaning":"他穿著襤褸的衣服。","analysis":"此字源於 'rag' (碎布)，'-ed' 是過去分詞字尾，在這裡用作形容詞，表示「像碎布一樣的」。'Rag' 本身來源不明，可能與「撕裂」、「破舊」的語感有關。'Ragged' 的核心語意是「由碎布構成的」、「破舊的」或「邊緣參差不齊的」。它描述的是一種不整齊、不規則、破爛的狀態，可以形容衣物、頭