'resignare'，'re-' (back) + 'signare' (to sign)。核心意義是「撤銷簽署」或「放棄」。\n1. 辭職；放棄（職位）：指正式退出一個職位或工作。\n2. 順從；聽任：指接受某個不愉快的局面或命運，不再反抗。","definition":"1. to leave your job officially; 2. to accept that something unpleasant must happen.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He decided to resign from his position as manager.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他決定辭去經理職位。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They had to resign themselves to the loss.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們不得不聽任損失的發生。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他決定辭去經理職位。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4530,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::resist::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The army was ordered to ____ the enemy invasion.","expectedAnswer":"resist","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The army was ordered to ____ the enemy invasion.","clozeAnswer":"resist","exampleTranslation":"軍隊奉命抵抗敵軍入侵。","reference":{"eng":"resist","kk":"/rɪˈzɪst/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['抵抗', '抵制'], ['忍耐', '抗拒']]","chEntries":["抵抗","抵制","忍耐","抗拒"],"practiceMeaning":"軍隊奉命抵抗敵軍入侵。","analysis":"詞根 'sist' 或 'sister' 源自拉丁語 'sistere'，意為 'to stand' (站立)。字首 're-' 表示 'back' (向後) 或 'against' (反對)。因此 'resist' 的核心意思是 'to stand against' (站立對抗)，引申為抵抗、抵制、不屈服。","definition":"1. to withstand the action or effect of.; 2. to oppose or fight against.; 3. to keep from doing, accepting, or yielding to.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The army was ordered to resist the enemy invasion.\",\n    \"ch\": \"軍隊奉命抵抗敵軍入侵。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's hard to resist temptation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"很難抗拒誘惑。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The material resists wear and tear.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種材料耐磨損。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"軍隊奉命抵抗敵軍入侵。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U11、L2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5391,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l2::resistance::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There was strong ____ to the new law.","expectedAnswer":"resistance","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There was strong ____ to the new law.","clozeAnswer":"resistance","exampleTranslation":"對新法律有強烈的抵抗。","reference":{"eng":"resistance","kk":"rɪˈzɪstəns","tense":"n.","ch":"[['抵抗'], ['阻力'], ['反抗'], ['（電）電阻']]","chEntries":["抵抗","阻力","反抗","電阻"],"practiceMeaning":"對新法律有強烈的抵抗。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 resistentia，是動詞 'resistere' (抵抗) 的名詞形式。'-ia' 是名詞字尾。核心語意是「抵抗的行為、狀態或能力」。因此，'resistance' 指「對抗、反對、不順從」的行為，也可以是「物體或力量所產生的阻力」，例如物理學中的電阻。","definition":"1. the refusal to accept or comply with something; 2. the attempt to prevent something by action or argument; 3. the opposition to a force or effect.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was strong resistance to the new law.\",\n    \"ch\": \"對新法律有強烈的抵抗。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The metal showed high resistance to heat.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種金屬對高溫顯示出高阻力。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"對新法律有強烈的抵抗。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5389,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l2::resistant::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This fabric is ____ to stains.","expectedAnswer":"resistant","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This fabric is ____ to stains.","clozeAnswer":"resistant","exampleTranslation":"這種布料抗污漬。","reference":{"eng":"resistant","kk":"rɪˈzɪstənt","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['抵抗的'], ['耐受的'], ['有抵抗力的']]","chEntries":["抵抗的","耐受的","有抵抗力的"],"practiceMeaning":"這種布料抗污漬。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 resistens，是動詞 'resistere' (抵抗、站立、反抗) 的現在分詞。're-' (back, against) + sistere (to stand)。核心語意是「站立對抗，不屈服」。因此，'resistant' 形容「能夠抵禦外力、影響或損害」，例如抵抗疾病、抵抗壓力、抵抗化學物質等。","definition":"1. offering or showing resistance; 2. not affected or harmed by something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This fabric is resistant to stains.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種布料抗污漬。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The population became resistant to the antibiotic.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該族群對這種抗生素產生了抗藥性。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這種布料抗污漬。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3111,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::restore::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The doctor helped him to ____ his health.","expectedAnswer":"restore","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The doctor helped him to ____ his health.","clozeAnswer":"restore","exampleTranslation":"醫生幫助他恢復了健康。","reference":{"eng":"restore","kk":"/rɪˈstɔːr/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['恢復；復原'], ['修復；重建'], ['歸還；恢復（權利、地位）']]","chEntries":["恢復","復原","修復","重建","歸還"],"practiceMeaning":"醫生幫助他恢復了健康。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'restaurare'，'re-' (again) + 'staurare' (to set up, to renew)。核心意義是「重新建立」或「恢復」。\n1. 恢復；復原：指使事物回到原來的狀態、健康或功能。\n2. 修復；重建：指修繕破損的建築物、藝術品或其他事物，使其恢復原貌。\n3. 歸還；恢復（權利、地位）：指將先前被剝奪或失去的東西歸還給原主，或恢復其原有的權力或地位。","definition":"1. to bring back a situation or thing to its former condition; 2. to repair something that is old or damaged; 3. to give someone back something that was lost or taken away.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The doctor helped him to restore his health.\",\n    \"ch\": \"醫生幫助他恢復了健康。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They are working to restore the ancient castle.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們正在努力修復這座古老的城堡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government promised to restore public trust.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府承諾恢復公眾的信任。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"醫生幫助他恢復了健康。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5802,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::resume::vt","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He decided to ____ his studies after a year off.","expectedAnswer":"resume","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He decided to ____ his studies after a year off.","clozeAnswer":"resume","exampleTranslation":"他決定休學一年後重拾學業。","reference":{"eng":"resume","kk":"rɪˈzum","tense":"vt.","ch":"[  [    \"恢復（某事）\"  ],  [    \"重新開始\"  ]]","chEntries":["恢復","重新開始"],"practiceMeaning":"他決定休學一年後重拾學業。","analysis":"此字為及物動詞，源自拉丁語resumere，由re-（再次）+sumere（拿起；採取）組成。sumere本身來自sub-（在……下面）+emere（拿；購買）。核心語義是「再次拿起」或「重新開始」。語意演變上，從「再次拿取」引申為「恢復中斷的活動或狀態」。","definition":"1. to begin again or continue after a pause or interruption; 2. to take up again.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He decided to resume his studies after a year off.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他決定休學一年後重拾學業。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The meeting will resume at 2 PM.\",\n    \"ch\": \"會議將於下午兩點恢復。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please resume your seat.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請回到您的座位上。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他決定休學一年後重拾學業。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4019,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u3::reveal-secrets::v-phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The spy was caught trying to ____ to the enemy.","expectedAnswer":"reveal secrets","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The spy was caught trying to ____ to the enemy.","clozeAnswer":"reveal secrets","exampleTranslation":"這個間諜被抓到試圖向敵人洩漏秘密。","reference":{"eng":"reveal secrets","kk":"/rɪˈviːl ˈsiːkrəts/","tense":"v. phrase","ch":"[['揭露秘密']]","chEntries":["揭露秘密"],"practiceMeaning":"這個間諜被抓到試圖向敵人洩漏秘密。","analysis":"結合動詞 'reveal' (揭露) 和名詞 'secrets' (秘密)。指將隱藏的信息或真相公開。","definition":"to make known information that was previously secret or unknown.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The spy was caught trying to reveal secrets to the enemy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個間諜被抓到試圖向敵人洩漏秘密。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個間諜被抓到試圖向敵人洩漏秘密。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5618,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l7::revolutionary::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The invention of the internet brought about ____ changes in communication.","expectedAnswer":"revolutionary","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The invention of the internet brought about ____ changes in communication.","clozeAnswer":"revolutionary","exampleTranslation":"網際網路的發明帶來了革命性的通訊變革。","reference":{"eng":"revolutionary","kk":"ˌrɛvəˈluʃəneri","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['革命的'], ['革新的'], ['顛覆性的']]","chEntries":["革命的","革新的","顛覆性的"],"practiceMeaning":"網際網路的發明帶來了革命性的通訊變革。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'revolutio'（革命、循環），由 'revolvere'（捲回、翻轉）派生，'revolvere' 由 're-'（回、再次）和 'volvere'（捲、轉）組成。構詞學上，'re-' 是表示「回」或「再次」的字首，'volut-' 是「捲」或「轉」的詞根，'-ion' 是名詞化字尾。'revolution'（革命）指「徹底的變革」，而 '-ary' 是形容詞化字尾，表示「與……有關的」。因此，'revolutionary' 的意思就是「與革命有關的」或「導致根本性變革的」。","definition":"1. Involving or causing a complete or dramatic change; 2. Relating to or characteristic of a revolution.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The invention of the internet brought about revolutionary changes in communication.\",\n    \"ch\": \"網際網路的發明帶來了革命性的通訊變革。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a revolutionary leader fighting for social justice.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是一位為社會正義而戰的革命領袖。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"網際網路的發明帶來了革命性的通訊變革。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3256,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::rhyme::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The words 'love' and 'dove' ____.","expectedAnswer":"rhyme","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The words 'love' and 'dove' ____.","clozeAnswer":"rhyme","exampleTranslation":"單詞 'love' 和 'dove' 押韻。","reference":{"eng":"rhyme","kk":"/raɪm/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['押韻'], ['作韻腳']]","chEntries":["押韻","作韻腳"],"practiceMeaning":"單詞 'love' 和 'dove' 押韻。","analysis":"動詞形式，指使詞語或詩句產生『韻腳』。與名詞『rhyme』的意義一致。","definition":"have or end with a word that has the same or similar sound as another word.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The words 'love' and 'dove' rhyme.\",\n    \"ch\": \"單詞 'love' 和 'dove' 押韻。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He tried to rhyme 'orange' but couldn't.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他試圖給 'orange' 找韻腳，但沒成功。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"單詞 'love' 和 'dove' 押韻。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U41"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3193,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::rhythm::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The music had a catchy ____ that made people want to dance.","expectedAnswer":"rhythm","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The music had a catchy ____ that made people want to dance.","clozeAnswer":"rhythm","exampleTranslation":"這首音樂有著 catchy 的節奏，讓人想跳舞。","reference":{"eng":"rhythm","kk":"/ˈrɪðəm/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['節奏；韻律'], ['（事物、活動的）規律；週期']]","chEntries":["節奏","韻律","規律","週期"],"practiceMeaning":"這首音樂有著 catchy 的節奏，讓人想跳舞。","analysis":"詞源來自希臘語 'rhythmos'，意為「週期，流動」。'Rhythm' 指的是一種有規律的、重複出現的模式，特別是聲音、運動或事件的模式。在音樂中，它是聲音的高低、長短和強弱的組織。在日常生活中，它可以指一種規律的模式或週期，如工作節奏、生活規律等。","definition":"1. a strong, regular, repeated pattern of movement or sound; 2. a regular pattern of changes or activities.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The music had a catchy rhythm that made people want to dance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這首音樂有著 catchy 的節奏，讓人想跳舞。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The rhythm of the waves was soothing.\",\n    \"ch\": \"海浪的節奏令人舒緩。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He tried to find a rhythm in his writing process.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他試圖在寫作過程中找到一種節奏。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這首音樂有著 catchy 的節奏，讓人想跳舞。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5099,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::rigid::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The metal bar was ____ and could not be bent.","expectedAnswer":"rigid","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The metal bar was ____ and could not be bent.","clozeAnswer":"rigid","exampleTranslation":"金屬棒是堅硬的，無法彎曲。","reference":{"eng":"rigid","kk":"ˈrɪdʒɪd","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['僵化的'], ['堅硬的'], ['嚴格的']]","chEntries":["僵化的","堅硬的","嚴格的"],"practiceMeaning":"金屬棒是堅硬的，無法彎曲。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'rigidus'，意為 '硬的、僵硬的'，源於 'rigere' (to be stiff)。'Rigid' 的核心語義是 '缺乏彈性、不易彎曲或改變'。這可以指物理上的堅硬，如 'rigid material' (堅硬的材料)；也可以指觀念、規則或體制的僵化，如 'rigid rules' (嚴格的規則) 或 'rigid thinking' (僵化的思維)，強調其不靈活、不變通的特性。","definition":"1. Unable to bend or be deformed.; 2. Stiff and unmoving.; 3. Unable to change or be changed; fixed.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The metal bar was rigid and could not be bent.\",\n    \"ch\": \"金屬棒是堅硬的，無法彎曲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company has rigid rules about punctuality.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司對準時有嚴格的規定。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has a rigid approach to problem-solving.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他解決問題的方法很僵化。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"金屬棒是堅硬的，無法彎曲。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4197,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::roast::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We will ____ a chicken for dinner.","expectedAnswer":"roast","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We will ____ a chicken for dinner.","clozeAnswer":"roast","exampleTranslation":"我們晚餐要烤一隻雞。","reference":{"eng":"roast","kk":"/roʊst/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['烤；烘；焙'], ['（嚴肅地）批評，嘲弄'], ['（使）變熱']]","chEntries":["烤","烘","焙","批評，嘲弄","變熱"],"practiceMeaning":"我們晚餐要烤一隻雞。","analysis":"源自古法語 rostir，意為“在火上烤”。詞源可能來自日耳曼語。核心是通過加熱烹飪食物。1. “烤；烘”是最基本的意思。2. “批評，嘲弄”來自於古羅馬時期，將被定罪者在公共場合的諷刺或譴責稱為 'to roast'，引申為嚴厲的批評或嘲笑。3. “使變熱”或“烤焦”是高溫作用的結果。","definition":"1. to cook food in an oven or over a fire; 2. to criticize or mock someone in a humorous but often harsh way; 3. to make very hot.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We will roast a chicken for dinner.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們晚餐要烤一隻雞。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The comedian roasted the politician mercilessly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位喜劇演員毫不留情地嘲諷了那位政治家。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The sun roasted us during the hike.\",\n    \"ch\": \"在徒步旅行中，太陽讓我們熱得難受。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們晚餐要烤一隻雞。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5145,"wordRef":"字彙王::u62::rod::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He used a long ____ to fish.","expectedAnswer":"rod","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He used a long ____ to fish.","clozeAnswer":"rod","exampleTranslation":"他用一根長桿釣魚。","reference":{"eng":"rod","kk":"rɔːd","tense":"n.","ch":"[['桿'], ['釣竿'], ['權杖'], ['（羅馬）束棒']]","chEntries":["桿","釣竿","權杖","束棒"],"practiceMeaning":"他用一根長桿釣魚。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 rodd，意為「樹枝、棍棒」。詞源不確定，可能與原始日耳曼語 *ruddaz（粗糙的）有關。核心語意是「長而細的硬物」，常作為工具、武器或象徵物。例如釣竿、旗桿、權杖。","definition":"a long, slender, straight pole, used as a support, in sports, or as a weapon; a measuring stick; a symbol of authority.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He used a long rod to fish.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他用一根長桿釣魚。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The king carried a royal rod.\",\n    \"ch\": \"國王手持權杖。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他用一根長桿釣魚。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U62"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5564,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::roughly::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There were ____ 50 people at the meeting.","expectedAnswer":"roughly","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There were ____ 50 people at the meeting.","clozeAnswer":"roughly","exampleTranslation":"會議上大約有 50 人。","reference":{"eng":"roughly","kk":"ˈrʌfli","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['大致上'], ['粗略地'], ['約略地']]","chEntries":["大致上","粗略地","約略地"],"practiceMeaning":"會議上大約有 50 人。","analysis":"此字由形容詞 \"rough\" 加上副詞字尾 \"-ly\" 構成。\"rough\" 的詞源較複雜，可能源自古諾爾斯語 \"hruggr\"（rough, coarse，粗糙的），或與原始日耳曼語 \\*ruhhaz（rough，粗糙的）有關。其原始語義與「粗糙、不平滑」有關。因此，\"roughly\" 作為副詞，主要有兩層語義：一是形容「以粗糙、不精確的方式」進行，例如 \"roughly handled\"（被粗魯地對待）；二是形容「不精確、大致的程度」，例如 \"roughly 100 people\"（大約 100 人）。這種語義上的演變是從「物理上的不平滑、不精細」延伸到「抽象上的不精確、不詳細」。","definition":"1. In a way that is approximate or not exact; 2. In a way that is harsh or violent.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There were roughly 50 people at the meeting.\",\n    \"ch\": \"會議上大約有 50 人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He explained the plan roughly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他粗略地解釋了計畫。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The box was roughly made.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個盒子做得很粗糙。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"會議上大約有 50 人。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5358,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l1::rumor::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There's a ____ that the company will be sold.","expectedAnswer":"rumor","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There's a ____ that the company will be sold.","clozeAnswer":"rumor","exampleTranslation":"有傳言說公司將被出售。","reference":{"eng":"rumor","kk":"ˈruːmər","tense":"n.","ch":"[['謠言'], ['傳聞']]","chEntries":["謠言","傳聞"],"practiceMeaning":"有傳言說公司將被出售。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 rumour，來自拉丁語 rumor，意為「喧囂、叫喊、傳聞」。原始語意為「人群的嘈雜聲」，引申為「未經證實的、廣泛流傳的消息」。構詞上，rum- 是字根，表示「叫喊、喧鬧」。","definition":"a piece of information that is spread from person to person without any source or evidence of its truth; a current story or report of uncertain origin.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There's a rumor that the company will be sold.\",\n    \"ch\": \"有傳言說公司將被出售。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Don't believe every rumor you hear.\",\n    \"ch\": \"不要相信你聽到的每一個謠言。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"有傳言說公司將被出售。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4553,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::satisfactory::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The results of the experiment were ____.","expectedAnswer":"satisfactory","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The results of the experiment were ____.","clozeAnswer":"satisfactory","exampleTranslation":"實驗結果是令人滿意的。","reference":{"eng":"satisfactory","kk":"/ˌsætɪsˈfæktəri/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['滿意的', '令人滿意的'], ['合格的', '令人滿意的']]","chEntries":["滿意的","令人滿意的","合格的"],"practiceMeaning":"實驗結果是令人滿意的。","analysis":"由 'satisfy' (使滿意) 加上形容詞字尾 '-ory' (表示具有某種性質或傾向) 構成。核心概念是能滿足需求或期望。\n    1. 滿意的、令人滿意的：指結果、表現等達到了期望或要求，讓人感到高興或認可。\n    2. 合格的、令人滿意的：指事物達到了基本的標準，雖然不一定突出，但足以接受。","definition":"1. fulfilling expectations or needs adequately.; 2. acceptable and meeting the required standards.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The results of the experiment were satisfactory.\",\n    \"ch\": \"實驗結果是令人滿意的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her performance in the exam was satisfactory.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在考試中的表現尚可。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We are pleased with the satisfactory progress made so far.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們對迄今為止令人滿意的進展感到高興。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"實驗結果是令人滿意的。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4342,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::scale::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The project was carried out on a large ____.","expectedAnswer":"scale","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The project was carried out on a large ____.","clozeAnswer":"scale","exampleTranslation":"這個專案是以大規模進行的。","reference":{"eng":"scale","kk":"/skeɪl/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['規模；尺度'], ['（測量儀器的）刻度'], ['（魚、爬蟲等的）鱗'], ['級別；等級']]","chEntries":["規模","尺度","刻度","鱗","級別","等級"],"practiceMeaning":"這個專案是以大規模進行的。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'scala'，意為 'ladder, staircase, scale'。1. 指事物的『大小、範圍』，即『規模、尺度』。2. 指測量儀器上的『刻度、標尺』。3. 指魚類、爬行動物體表的『鱗片』。4. 指事物系統化的『等級、級別』。","definition":"the size or extent of something; a series of marks or lines at fixed distances on a ruler, thermometer, etc., showing measurements; one of the small, flat plates that cover the skin of fish and reptiles; a system of measuring the size or amount of something","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The project was carried out on a large scale.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個專案是以大規模進行的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The thermometer has a scale from 0 to 100 degrees.\",\n    \"ch\": \"溫度計的刻度從0到100度。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The fish's scales shimmered in the light.\",\n    \"ch\": \"魚鱗在燈光下閃閃發光。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company is trying to move up the scale of quality.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司正試圖提升品質等級。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個專案是以大規模進行的。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5311,"wordRef":"字彙王::u63::scar::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He has a ____ on his forehead from a childhood accident.","expectedAnswer":"scar","choices"