「偷偷摸摸地移動」有關。構詞上無明顯字首、字根、字尾，為整體詞源演變。原始語義指向「秘密地、非法地運輸」。'smuggle' 指的是「非法地、秘密地運輸（商品、人等）」，通常是為了逃避關稅、禁令或法律管制。","definition":"to import or export (goods or people) secretly and illegally.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They were caught trying to smuggle diamonds into the country.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們在試圖走私鑽石入境時被抓獲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The organization was involved in smuggling refugees across the border.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該組織參與了偷渡難民越境的活動。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們在試圖走私鑽石入境時被抓獲。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5532,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l5::smuggler::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ was arrested at the border.","expectedAnswer":"smuggler","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ was arrested at the border.","clozeAnswer":"smuggler","exampleTranslation":"走私者在邊境被捕。","reference":{"eng":"smuggler","kk":"ˈsmʌɡlər","tense":"n.","ch":"[['走私者']]","chEntries":["走私者"],"practiceMeaning":"走私者在邊境被捕。","analysis":"此字由動詞 'smuggle' 加上執行者字尾 '-er' 構成。'-er' 是常見的字尾，源自古英語，用於將動詞轉化為指代執行該動作的人或事物。'smuggle' 源自低地德語 'smuggeln'。因此，'smuggler' 的構詞結構清晰地表明其含義是「從事走私活動的人」。語意上，它指進行非法運輸商品或人員活動的人。","definition":"a person who smuggles goods.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The smuggler was arrested at the border.\",\n    \"ch\": \"走私者在邊境被捕。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He made a fortune as a diamond smuggler.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他作為鑽石走私者賺了大錢。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"走私者在邊境被捕。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6248,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::snatch::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of the necklace caused panic in the crowd.","expectedAnswer":"snatch","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of the necklace caused panic in the crowd.","clozeAnswer":"snatch","exampleTranslation":"項鍊被搶奪引起了人群的恐慌。","reference":{"eng":"snatch","kk":"snætʃ","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"搶奪\"  ],  [    \"奪取\"  ],  [    \"一小段時間\"  ],  [    \"短暫的機會\"  ]]","chEntries":["搶奪","奪取","一小段時間","短暫的機會"],"practiceMeaning":"項鍊被搶奪引起了人群的恐慌。","analysis":"此字源自擬聲詞，模仿突然抓住的動作。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。名詞義指突然、快速地抓住或拿走某物的行為。也可引申為一段短暫的時間或機會。中文翻譯為「搶奪；奪取；一小段時間；短暫的機會」。","definition":"1. the act of grabbing or taking something quickly; 2. a short period of time or a brief opportunity.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The snatch of the necklace caused panic in the crowd.\",\n    \"ch\": \"項鍊被搶奪引起了人群的恐慌。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He used the brief snatch of silence to escape.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他利用那短暫的寂靜逃脫了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was a desperate snatch for freedom.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那是一次對自由的絕望的奪取。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"項鍊被搶奪引起了人群的恐慌。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5521,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l5::sneak::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He tried to ____ out of the room without being noticed.","expectedAnswer":"sneak","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He tried to ____ out of the room without being noticed.","clozeAnswer":"sneak","exampleTranslation":"他試圖不被注意到地悄悄溜出房間。","reference":{"eng":"sneak","kk":"sniːk","tense":"v.","ch":"[['偷偷地走'], ['潛行'], ['鬼鬼祟祟地行動'], ['偷偷地拿（或做）']]","chEntries":["偷偷地走","潛行","鬼鬼祟祟地行動","偷偷地拿"],"practiceMeaning":"他試圖不被注意到地悄悄溜出房間。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 'sneken'，與古英語 'snēcan' 同源，可能來自原始日耳曼語 *snēkanan。其原始語義與「爬行」、「潛行」或「緩慢移動」有關。構詞上無明顯字首、字根、字尾。語意演變從「緩慢、不易察覺地移動」引申為「偷偷地、鬼鬼祟祟地行動」，尤其強調避免被發現。引申義還包括「偷偷地拿走」或「偷偷地做某事」。","definition":"to move furtively and stealthily; to carry or place (something) somewhere secretly.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He tried to sneak out of the room without being noticed.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他試圖不被注意到地悄悄溜出房間。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She managed to sneak a cookie before dinner.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她設法在晚飯前偷偷拿了一塊餅乾。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他試圖不被注意到地悄悄溜出房間。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3118,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::software::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This ____ is compatible with most operating systems.","expectedAnswer":"software","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This ____ is compatible with most operating systems.","clozeAnswer":"software","exampleTranslation":"這款軟體與大多數作業系統相容。","reference":{"eng":"software","kk":"/ˈsɔːftwɛər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['軟體；軟件']]","chEntries":["軟體","軟件"],"practiceMeaning":"這款軟體與大多數作業系統相容。","analysis":"由 'soft' (soft) + 'ware' (suffix for manufactured goods) 組成。與 'hardware' (硬體) 相對，指非實體的計算機程序。\n1. 軟體；軟件：指計算機系統中用於執行特定任務的程序、數據和指令。","definition":"1. the programs, data, etc. used by a computer; 2. the set of instructions that a computer needs to work.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This software is compatible with most operating systems.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這款軟體與大多數作業系統相容。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is developing new software for graphic design.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他正在開發用於平面設計的新軟體。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這款軟體與大多數作業系統相容。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3119,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::solar::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The house is powered by ____ energy.","expectedAnswer":"solar","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The house is powered by ____ energy.","clozeAnswer":"solar","exampleTranslation":"這房子由太陽能供電。","reference":{"eng":"solar","kk":"/ˈsoʊlər/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['太陽的；日光的']]","chEntries":["太陽的","日光的"],"practiceMeaning":"這房子由太陽能供電。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'solaris'，'sol' (sun)。核心意義是「與太陽有關」。\n1. 太陽的；日光的：指與太陽、太陽光或太陽能相關的。","definition":"1. relating to or determined by the sun; 2. using the sun's light or heat.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The house is powered by solar energy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這房子由太陽能供電。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The solar system includes the sun and all the planets.\",\n    \"ch\": \"太陽系包括太陽和所有行星。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這房子由太陽能供電。","sourceName":"字彙王、龍騰課本","unitName":"U39、L2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3977,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u3::somehow::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____, I always manage to find my keys.","expectedAnswer":"Somehow","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____, I always manage to find my keys.","clozeAnswer":"Somehow","exampleTranslation":"不知何故，我總是能找到我的鑰匙。","reference":{"eng":"somehow","kk":"/ˈsʌmhaʊ/","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['以某種方式', '不知何故']]","chEntries":["以某種方式","不知何故"],"practiceMeaning":"不知何故，我總是能找到我的鑰匙。","analysis":"由 'some' (一些) 和 'how' (如何) 組成，表示「以某種方式，但具體方式不清楚」。","definition":"in some way not yet known or stated; for some reason.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Somehow, I always manage to find my keys.\",\n    \"ch\": \"不知何故，我總是能找到我的鑰匙。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She will arrive here somehow.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她會以某種方式抵達這裡。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"不知何故，我總是能找到我的鑰匙。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5569,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::sort::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He is a ____ of person who always tries to help.","expectedAnswer":"sort","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He is a ____ of person who always tries to help.","clozeAnswer":"sort","exampleTranslation":"他是那種總是試圖幫忙的人。","reference":{"eng":"sort","kk":"sɔrt","tense":"n.","ch":"[['種類'], ['類型'], ['類別'], ['品級']]","chEntries":["種類","類型","類別","品級"],"practiceMeaning":"他是那種總是試圖幫忙的人。","analysis":"這是 \"sort\" 作動詞的相關名詞形式，源自古法語 \"sortir\"，意為 \"to draw lots, to choose\"（抽籤，選擇），來自拉丁語 \"sors, sortis\"（lot, fate, share，籤，命運，份額）。\"sors\" 最初與「抽籤」或「命運」相關，引申出「一份」、「一部分」的概念，進而演變為「同一類的事物」或「某一類型的東西」。因此，\"sort\" 作為名詞，指「由共同特徵或標準劃分出來的群體或類別」，即「種類」或「類型」。","definition":"1. A category of people or things having common characteristics; 2. A number of people or things that are grouped together because they are similar to each other.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a sort of person who always tries to help.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是那種總是試圖幫忙的人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This sort of behavior is unacceptable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種行為是不可接受的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"What sort of music do you like?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你喜歡哪一類的音樂？\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他是那種總是試圖幫忙的人。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5464,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::span::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The bridge has a ____ of over 500 meters.","expectedAnswer":"span","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The bridge has a ____ of over 500 meters.","clozeAnswer":"span","exampleTranslation":"這座橋的跨度超過 500 公尺。","reference":{"eng":"span","kk":"spæn","tense":"n.","ch":"[['跨度'], ['期間'], ['範圍']]","chEntries":["跨度","期間","範圍"],"practiceMeaning":"這座橋的跨度超過 500 公尺。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 'spanne'，最初指「兩端之間的距離」，特別是張開拇指和中指（或小指）所能測量的長度，大約是九英寸。這個詞與古諾爾斯語 'spann'（跨度、尺度）以及荷蘭語 'span'（跨度）有關。隨著時間推移，'span' 的語意從具體的物理長度擴展到抽象的「時間長度」或「範圍」。核心語意是「兩個點之間的最大距離或持續時間」。","definition":"1. The full extent of something from end to end; the length, breadth, or width of a space or object.; 2. The period of time between the beginning and the end of something, especially a life, an event, or a period of activity.; 3. The distance between the two points of support of a bridge or other structure.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The bridge has a span of over 500 meters.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座橋的跨度超過 500 公尺。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her career spanned four decades.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的職業生涯橫跨了四十年。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The span of their control was limited.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們控制的範圍有限。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這座橋的跨度超過 500 公尺。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4127,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::spill::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Be careful not to ____ your coffee.","expectedAnswer":"spill","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Be careful not to ____ your coffee.","clozeAnswer":"spill","exampleTranslation":"小心別把咖啡灑了。","reference":{"eng":"spill","kk":"/spɪl/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['（液體）溢出', '灑出'], ['（數量）大量湧入']]","chEntries":["溢出","灑出","大量湧入"],"practiceMeaning":"小心別把咖啡灑了。","analysis":"源自古英語 spillan（毀壞，浪費）。核心概念是「意外地使液體流出」。引申為無意間洩露秘密，或指大量的東西（尤指人）湧入某處。","definition":"1. (of a liquid) flow or cause to flow over the rim of a container, typically accidentally; 2. (of a substance) fall or flow out of a container; 3. (of people) arrive or move in large numbers","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Be careful not to spill your coffee.\",\n    \"ch\": \"小心別把咖啡灑了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He accidentally spilled the beans about the surprise party.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他不小心洩露了關於驚喜派對的秘密。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Thousands of refugees spilled into the neighboring country.\",\n    \"ch\": \"數千名難民湧入鄰國。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"小心別把咖啡灑了。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5489,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::spoil::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Don't ____ the child by giving him everything he wants.","expectedAnswer":"spoil","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Don't ____ the child by giving him everything he wants.","clozeAnswer":"spoil","exampleTranslation":"別因為給他他想要的一切而寵壞他。","reference":{"eng":"spoil","kk":"spɔɪl","tense":"v.","ch":"[['寵壞'], ['損壞'], ['糟蹋']]","chEntries":["寵壞","損壞","糟蹋"],"practiceMeaning":"別因為給他他想要的一切而寵壞他。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'spoliare'，意為「剝去、掠奪」。這個詞在中古英語中演變為 'spoilien'，最初的意思是「掠奪、搶劫」。後來，語意擴展到「破壞、損壞」，例如「損壞戰利品」。再後來，又引申出「寵壞、溺愛」的意思，即「給予過多的好處，使其變壞」，這可以看作是「損壞」的一種比喻用法，指破壞了好的性格或習慣。核心語意是「破壞或損害」。","definition":"1. Diminish or destroy the value or quality of.; 2. Harm the character of (a child) by being too lenient or indulgent.; 3. Ruin or destroy.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Don't spoil the child by giving him everything he wants.\",\n    \"ch\": \"別因為給他他想要的一切而寵壞他。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The rain spoiled our picnic plans.\",\n    \"ch\": \"下雨糟蹋了我們的野餐計劃。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The old buildings were spoiled by neglect.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這些老建築因疏於打理而損壞了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"別因為給他他想要的一切而寵壞他。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4193,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::squirrel::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ quickly climbed up the tree.","expectedAnswer":"squirrel","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ quickly climbed up the tree.","clozeAnswer":"squirrel","exampleTranslation":"那隻松鼠迅速爬上了樹。","reference":{"eng":"squirrel","kk":"/ˈskwɜːrəl/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['松鼠']]","chEntries":["松鼠"],"practiceMeaning":"那隻松鼠迅速爬上了樹。","analysis":"源自古希臘語 skiouros，意為“影子尾巴”。'skia'（影子）+ 'oura'（尾巴）。此名來自松鼠常將尾巴搭在背上的習性。該詞在14世紀經由古法語 écureuil 進入英語。是一個典型的動物名稱，沒有明顯的引申義，主要指這種哺乳動物。","definition":"A gnawing mammal that typically has a bushy tail and lives in trees.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The squirrel quickly climbed up the tree.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那隻松鼠迅速爬上了樹。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I saw a squirrel burying nuts in the garden.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我看見一隻松鼠在花園裡埋堅果。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"那隻松鼠迅速爬上了樹。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4027,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u3::staff-members::n-phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"All ____ are required to attend the meeting.","expectedAnswer":"staff members","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"All ____ are required to attend the meeting.","clozeAnswer":"staff members","exampleTranslation":"所有員工成員都必須參加會議。","reference":{"eng":"staff members","kk":"/stæf ˈmɛmbərz/","tense":"n. phrase","ch":"[['員工成員']]","chEntries":["員工成員"],"practiceMeaning":"所有員工成員都必須參加會議。","analysis":"結合名詞 'staff' (員工) 和 'members' (成員)。指組織或機構中的個別工作人員。","definition":"individuals who are employed by an organization.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"All staff members are required to attend the meeting.\",\n    \"ch\": \"所有員工成員都必須參加會議。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"所有員工成員都必須參加會議。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5714,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l9::stand-up-for::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"You should ____ your rights.","expectedAnswer":"stand up for","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"You should ____ your rights.","clozeAnswer":"stand up for","exampleTranslation":"你應該為你的權利辯護。","reference":{"eng":"stand up for","kk":"ˈstænd ʌp fɔːr","tense":"v.","ch":"[['支持'], ['維護'], ['為……辯護']]","chEntries":["支持","維護","為……辯護"],"practiceMeaning":"你應該為你的權利辯護。","analysis":"這是一個片語動詞，由動詞 'stand'（站立）+ 副詞 'up'（向上）+ 介詞 'for'（為了）構成。'stand' 源自古英語 standan（站立）。'up' 表示向上或起身。'for' 表示目的或對象。字面意思為「為了某事站起來」。引申為「為某人或某事公開表達支持、辯護，或捍衛其權利和觀點」。核心語意是「積極地站出來支持」。","definition":"to defend or support someone or something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"You should stand up for your rights.\",\n    \"ch\": \"你應該為你的權利辯護。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She always stands up for the underdog.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她總是支持弱者。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"你應該為你的權利辯護。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5515,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l5::starvation::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The war led to widespread ____ in the region.","expectedAnswer":"starvation","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The war led to widespread ____ in the region.","clozeAnswer":"starvation","exampleTranslation":"戰爭導致該地區普遍挨餓。","reference":{"eng":"starvation","kk":"stɑːrˈveɪʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[['餓死'], ['挨餓'], ['食物匱乏']]","chEntries":["餓死","挨餓","食物匱乏"],"practiceMeaning":"戰爭導致該地區普遍挨餓。","analysis":"此字由動詞 'starve' 加上名詞化字尾 '-ation' 構成。'-ation' 是拉丁語來源的字尾，用於將動詞轉化為表示行為、狀態或結果的名詞。'starve' 本身源自古英語 'stærfian'，意為 'to die of hunger'，與原始日耳曼語 *starfōjan 同源，可能與「僵硬」、「死亡」有關。原始語義是「因缺乏食物而死亡」。'starvation' 作為名詞，指「挨餓」的狀態或「餓死」的結果。它是一個抽象名詞，描述了極度缺乏食物的嚴重狀況。","definition":"the state or condition of suffering or dying from lack of food.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The war led to widespread starvation in the region.\",\n    \"ch\": \"戰爭導致該地區普遍挨餓。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Many children are dying of starvation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"許多兒童正因飢餓而死亡。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"戰爭導致該地區普遍挨餓。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4617,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::statue::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"A ____ of the founder stood in front of the building.","expectedAnswer":"statue","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"A ____ of the founder stood in front of the building.","clozeAnswer":"statue","exampleTranslation":"創辦人的雕像矗立在建築物前。","reference":{"eng":"statue","kk":"/ˈstætʃuː/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['雕像'], ['塑像']]","chEntries":["雕像","塑像"],"practiceMeaning":"創辦人的雕像矗立在建築物前。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'statua'，是 'statuere' (建立、設置) 的變體，意為「被建立起來的東西」。指用石、木、金屬、黏土等材料雕刻或塑造的人物或動物形象。","definition":"a sculpture representing a person or animal.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A statue of the founder stood in front of the building.\",\n    \"ch\": \"創辦人的雕像矗立在建築物前。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The museum displayed a collection of ancient statues.\",\n    \"ch\": \"博物館展出了一系列古代雕像。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"創辦人的雕像矗立在建築物前。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4267,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::steal::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He was caught trying to ____ a car.","expectedAnswer":"steal","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He was caught trying to ____ a car.","clozeAnswer":"steal","exampleTranslation":"他被抓到試圖偷車。","reference":{"eng":"steal","kk":"/stiːl/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['偷竊'], ['竊取'], ['悄悄地移動']]","chEntries":["偷竊","竊取","悄悄地移動"],"practiceMeaning":"他被抓到試圖偷車。","analysis":"源自古英語 'stelan'，與日耳曼語族同源。'Steal' 的核心意義是「未經允許拿走屬於別人的東西」，強調其非法性和秘密性。它也可以引申為「悄悄地、不引人注意地移動」。","definition":"to take something that belongs to someone else without permission; to move quietly and secretively.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was caught trying to steal a car.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他被抓到試圖偷車。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The cat stole silently across the room.\",\n    \"ch\": \"貓悄無聲息地穿過房間。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他被抓到試圖偷車。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5105,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::stereotype::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It is wrong to ____ people based on their appearance.","expectedAnswer":"stereotype","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It is wrong to ____ people based on their appearance.","clozeAnswer":"stereotype","exampleTranslation":"根據外貌給人貼上刻板印象是錯誤的。","reference":{"eng":"stereotype","kk":"ˈsteriəˌtaɪp","tense":"v.","ch":"[['給……貼上刻板印象'], ['使……模式化']]","chEntries":["給……貼上刻板印象","使……模式化"],"practiceMeaning":"根據外貌給人貼上刻板印象是錯誤的。","analysis":"此字源自希臘語 'stereos' (solid) + 'typos' (impression, mark)，原意是 '堅固的印模'。作為動詞，'stereotype' 指 '對某人或某物形成並應用刻板印象'，即將其歸入一個固定、簡化的類別，忽略其獨特性。這個過程就像使用一個 '印模'，將所有事物都壓印成相同的模式，而不考慮個體差異，從而產生偏見。","definition":"1. To have or give a fixed, oversimplified image or idea of a particular type of person or thing.; 2. To treat or classify or think of as a stereotype.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It is wrong to stereotype people based on their appearance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"根據外貌給人貼上刻板印象是錯誤的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The film was criticized for stereotyping certain ethnic groups.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這部電影因對某些族裔群體進行刻板化而被批評。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"根據外貌給人貼上刻板印象是錯誤的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4488,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::stir::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"A ____ of excitement went through the crowd.","expectedAnswer":"stir","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"A ____ of excitement went through the crowd.","clozeAnswer":"stir","exampleTranslation":"人群中引起了一陣騷動。","reference":{"eng":"stir","kk":"/stɜːr/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['攪拌'], ['騷動'], ['（情感）激動']]","chEntries":["攪拌","騷動","激動"],"practiceMeaning":"人群中引起了一陣騷動。","analysis":"名詞形式，源自動詞 stir。意為「攪拌的動作」，「引起注意或騷動的情況」，「情感的波動」。","definition":"1. An act of stirring; 2. A slight movement; 3. A commotion or disturbance; 4. A strong feeling of excitement or activity.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A stir of excitement went through the crowd.\",\n    \"ch\": \"人群中引起了一陣騷動。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She gave the mixture a quick stir.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她快速地攪拌了一下混合物。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"人群中引起了一陣騷動。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4644,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::stitch::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She can ____ a dress by hand.","expectedAnswer":"stitch","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She can ____ a dress by hand.","clozeAnswer":"stitch","exampleTranslation":"她可以手工縫製一件洋裝。","reference":{"eng":"stitch","kk":"/stɪtʃ/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['縫合'], ['縫補']]","chEntries":["縫合","縫補"],"practiceMeaning":"她可以手工縫製一件洋裝。","analysis":"源自古英語 'sticce'，與「刺、戳」有關，指用針和線將布料連接起來的動作。核心是通過反覆穿針引線來連接或修補物體。","definition":"to sew or fasten something with stitches.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She can stitch a dress by hand.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她可以手工縫製一件洋裝。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He had to stitch up the wound.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他必須縫合傷口。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她可以手工縫製一件洋裝。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3257,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::stocking::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She hung her ____ by the fireplace on Christmas Eve.","expectedAnswer":"stocking","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She hung her ____ by the fireplace on Christmas Eve.","clozeAnswer":"stocking","exampleTranslation":"聖誕夜，她把長襪