ation":"火車駛入了隧道。","reference":{"eng":"tunnel","kk":"/ˈtʌnl/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['隧道'], ['（動物的）地道']]","chEntries":["隧道","地道"],"practiceMeaning":"火車駛入了隧道。","analysis":"詞源自古法語 'tonnel'，意為「酒桶」，因其圓柱形的形狀。指一種在地底、山體或水下挖掘的通道。","definition":"a long passage, typically underground, connecting two places; an underground passage made by an animal.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The train entered the tunnel.\",\n    \"ch\": \"火車駛入了隧道。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They dug a tunnel to escape from prison.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們挖了一條地道從監獄逃脫。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"火車駛入了隧道。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3951,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::turn-the-volume-up::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Can you ____? I can't hear the music.","expectedAnswer":"turn the volume up","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Can you ____? I can't hear the music.","clozeAnswer":"turn the volume up","exampleTranslation":"你能把音量調高嗎？我聽不到音樂。","reference":{"eng":"turn the volume up","kk":"None","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['調高音量']]","chEntries":["調高音量"],"practiceMeaning":"你能把音量調高嗎？我聽不到音樂。","analysis":"此為動詞片語。'turn up' (片語動詞，意為「調高」) 加上名詞 'volume' (音量)。表示將音量增強。","definition":"to increase the loudness of a sound.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Can you turn the volume up? I can't hear the music.\",\n    \"ch\": \"你能把音量調高嗎？我聽不到音樂。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He turned the volume up on the radio.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他調高了收音機的音量。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"你能把音量調高嗎？我聽不到音樂。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4625,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::twin::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She is the ____ sister of John.","expectedAnswer":"twin","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She is the ____ sister of John.","clozeAnswer":"twin","exampleTranslation":"她是約翰的孿生姐妹。","reference":{"eng":"twin","kk":"/twɪn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['雙胞胎之一'], ['孿生子']]","chEntries":["雙胞胎之一","孿生子"],"practiceMeaning":"她是約翰的孿生姐妹。","analysis":"源自古英語 'twinna'，是 'two' (二) 的變體。指成對出現的兩者之一，特別是懷孕所生的兩名嬰兒。引申義也可指兩個極其相似或相關的事物。","definition":"one of two children born at the same birth.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is the twin sister of John.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是約翰的孿生姐妹。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The twins look identical.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這對雙胞胎長得一模一樣。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她是約翰的孿生姐妹。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5320,"wordRef":"字彙王::u63::undergo::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The patient will ____ surgery next week.","expectedAnswer":"undergo","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The patient will ____ surgery next week.","clozeAnswer":"undergo","exampleTranslation":"這位病人下週將接受手術。","reference":{"eng":"undergo","kk":"ˌʌndərˈɡoʊ","tense":"v.","ch":"[['經歷', '承受']]","chEntries":["經歷","承受"],"practiceMeaning":"這位病人下週將接受手術。","analysis":"此字由介詞/前綴 'under-'（在...之下）和動詞 'go'（去）複合而成。'under-' 表示「在...之下、經歷」。'go' 則提供「進行、發生」的核心語意。'undergo' 的核心語意為「在某種情況或過程下進行、發生」，引申為「經歷、承受」（尤指不愉快的、困難的或必然發生的事）。","definition":"to experience or be subjected to (something, typically something unpleasant, painful, or arduous).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The patient will undergo surgery next week.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位病人下週將接受手術。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The country is undergoing a period of economic hardship.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個國家正經歷一段經濟困境時期。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這位病人下週將接受手術。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U63"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5321,"wordRef":"字彙王::u63::undergraduate::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She is an ____ student at Harvard University.","expectedAnswer":"undergraduate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She is an ____ student at Harvard University.","clozeAnswer":"undergraduate","exampleTranslation":"她是哈佛大學的一名大學生。","reference":{"eng":"undergraduate","kk":"ˈʌndərˌɡrædʒuət","tense":"n.","ch":"[['大學生（指未獲學位者）']]","chEntries":["大學生"],"practiceMeaning":"她是哈佛大學的一名大學生。","analysis":"此字由前綴 'under-'（在...之下）和名詞 'graduate'（畢業生）複合而成。'graduate' 本身源自拉丁語 'gradus'（步、等級），'graduatus'（獲得等級）。'under-' 在此處表示「在...之下」或「在...的早期階段」。'undergraduate' 的核心語意指「在（學士）等級之下」，即指尚未獲得學士學位、仍在大學就讀的學生。","definition":"a student at a college or university who has not yet earned their first degree.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is an undergraduate student at Harvard University.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是哈佛大學的一名大學生。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The university offers programs for both undergraduates and graduates.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這所大學為大學生和研究生都提供課程。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她是哈佛大學的一名大學生。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U63"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5814,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::underline::vt","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Please ____ the key terms in the text.","expectedAnswer":"underline","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Please ____ the key terms in the text.","clozeAnswer":"underline","exampleTranslation":"請在課文中的關鍵詞下方劃線。","reference":{"eng":"underline","kk":"ˌʌndərˈlaɪn","tense":"vt.","ch":"[  [    \"在……下劃線\"  ],  [    \"強調\"  ],  [    \"標示\"  ]]","chEntries":["在……下劃線","強調","標示"],"practiceMeaning":"請在課文中的關鍵詞下方劃線。","analysis":"此字為及物動詞，構詞自under（在……下面）+line（線）+ate（動詞字尾）。under是介系詞，line是名詞。這個字構詞非常透明，字面意思是「在……下面畫一條線」。語意演變上，從具體的「在文字下方畫線」，引申為「強調」某個重點或觀點，使其更醒目。此字無明顯字根，是現代構詞的複合詞。","definition":"1. to draw a line under something; 2. to emphasize or indicate the importance of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please underline the key terms in the text.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請在課文中的關鍵詞下方劃線。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her speech underlined the importance of environmental protection.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的演講強調了環境保護的重要性。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The report underlines the need for immediate action.\",\n    \"ch\": \"報告標示了立即採取行動的必要性。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"請在課文中的關鍵詞下方劃線。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6102,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::undermine::vt","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His constant criticism began to ____ her confidence.","expectedAnswer":"undermine","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His constant criticism began to ____ her confidence.","clozeAnswer":"undermine","exampleTranslation":"他不斷的批評開始削弱她的信心。","reference":{"eng":"undermine","kk":"ˌʌndərˈmaɪn","tense":"vt.","ch":"[  [    \"破壞\"  ],  [    \"侵蝕\"  ],  [    \"削弱\"  ],  [    \"暗中破壞\"  ]]","chEntries":["破壞","侵蝕","削弱","暗中破壞"],"practiceMeaning":"他不斷的批評開始削弱她的信心。","analysis":"此字由 under-（under, below）和 mine（挖掘）構成。核心語義是「從下面挖掘」，引申為「削弱」或「暗中破壞」某物（如基礎、權威、信心）。","definition":"1. to lessen the strength or effectiveness of someone or something, especially gradually and stealthily; 2. to erode or excavate the base or foundation of.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His constant criticism began to undermine her confidence.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他不斷的批評開始削弱她的信心。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The protesters tried to undermine the government's authority.\",\n    \"ch\": \"抗議者試圖破壞政府的權威。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The constant rain undermined the foundations of the building.\",\n    \"ch\": \"持續不斷的降雨侵蝕了建築物的基礎。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他不斷的批評開始削弱她的信心。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6103,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::undo::vt","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Please ____ the knots in the rope.","expectedAnswer":"undo","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Please ____ the knots in the rope.","clozeAnswer":"undo","exampleTranslation":"請解開繩子上的結。","reference":{"eng":"undo","kk":"ʌnˈdu","tense":"vt.","ch":"[  [    \"解開\"  ],  [    \"撤銷\"  ],  [    \"取消\"  ],  [    \"毀掉\"  ]]","chEntries":["解開","撤銷","取消","毀掉"],"practiceMeaning":"請解開繩子上的結。","analysis":"此字由 un-（not, the opposite of）和 do（做）構成。核心語義是「與『做』相反的動作」，即「撤銷」、「取消」或「恢復到未做之前的狀態」。可指物理上的解開（如解開釦子），或抽象上的取消（如撤銷決定）。","definition":"1. unfasten or loosen (something that is tied, fastened, or wrapped); 2. cancel or reverse the effect or consequence of (an action or event); 3. spoil or destroy (a positive result or achievement).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please undo the knots in the rope.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請解開繩子上的結。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The king decided to undo the decree.\",\n    \"ch\": \"國王決定撤銷那項法令。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His mistake undid all his hard work.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的錯誤毀掉了他所有的辛勤工作。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"請解開繩子上的結。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5109,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::undoubtedly::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She is ____ the best candidate for the job.","expectedAnswer":"undoubtedly","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She is ____ the best candidate for the job.","clozeAnswer":"undoubtedly","exampleTranslation":"她無疑是這份工作最好的候選人。","reference":{"eng":"undoubtedly","kk":"ʌnˈdaʊtɪdli","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['毫無疑問地'], ['確定地']]","chEntries":["毫無疑問地","確定地"],"practiceMeaning":"她無疑是這份工作最好的候選人。","analysis":"此字由 'un-' (not) + 'doubt' (懷疑) + '-ed' (過去分詞或形容詞後綴) + '-ly' (副詞化後綴) 構成。'Doubt' 源自古英語 'dūfan' (to dive, to sink)，引申為 '懷疑'。'Undoubtedly' 的核心語義是 '沒有任何懷疑的餘地'，強調某事是確鑿的、無可置疑的。它用來加強語氣，表明說話者對所述內容的高度確定性。","definition":"1. Without doubt; certainly.; 2. Beyond doubt; unquestionably.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is undoubtedly the best candidate for the job.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她無疑是這份工作最好的候選人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The project was undoubtedly a success.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個專案無疑是成功的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她無疑是這份工作最好的候選人。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6147,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::unfold::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Please ____ the map.","expectedAnswer":"unfold","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Please ____ the map.","clozeAnswer":"unfold","exampleTranslation":"請展開地圖。","reference":{"eng":"unfold","kk":"ʌnˈfoʊld","tense":"v.","ch":"[  [    \"展開\"  ],  [    \"打開\"  ],  [    \"闡明\"  ],  [    \"發展\"  ]]","chEntries":["展開","打開","闡明","發展"],"practiceMeaning":"請展開地圖。","analysis":"此字由否定字首 un-（不；相反）和動詞 fold（折疊）構成。fold 源自古英語 faldan，意為「摺疊；纏繞」。unfold 的核心語義是「不折疊」，即將折疊的物體打開，使其平展。引申為揭示、闡明事實或情況，或指事件的發展。此處使用 v. 詞性，表示及物與不及物皆可。及物用法如 unfold a map。不及物用法如 the story unfolds。其語意演變是從具體的「打開」到抽象的「揭示；發展」。","definition":"1. to open or spread out something that has been folded; 2. to become clear or revealed; 3. to develop or become clear.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please unfold the map.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請展開地圖。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The mystery began to unfold.\",\n    \"ch\": \"謎團開始被揭開。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"As the events unfold, we will learn more.\",\n    \"ch\": \"隨著事件的發展，我們將了解更多。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"請展開地圖。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6148,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::unlock::vt","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He used the key to ____ the door.","expectedAnswer":"unlock","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He used the key to ____ the door.","clozeAnswer":"unlock","exampleTranslation":"他用鑰匙解鎖了門。","reference":{"eng":"unlock","kk":"ʌnˈlɑːk","tense":"vt.","ch":"[  [    \"解鎖\"  ],  [    \"打開\"  ],  [    \"揭示\"  ]]","chEntries":["解鎖","打開","揭示"],"practiceMeaning":"他用鑰匙解鎖了門。","analysis":"此字由否定字首 un-（不；相反）和動詞 lock（鎖）構成。lock 源自古英語 loca，意為「鎖；閂」。unlock 的核心語義是「解除鎖定」，即打開鎖著的東西。引申為揭示秘密、答案或潛在的可能性。此及物動詞表示打開被鎖住的門、盒子、密碼等，或揭示隱藏的信息。其語意演變是從具體的「開鎖」到抽象的「揭示」。","definition":"1. to open (a door, window, or container) by unlocking it; 2. to make something accessible or available; to reveal.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He used the key to unlock the door.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他用鑰匙解鎖了門。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The discovery unlocked the secrets of the ancient civilization.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這項發現揭開了古代文明的秘密。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Unlock your phone with a passcode.\",\n    \"ch\": \"用密碼解鎖你的手機。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他用鑰匙解鎖了門。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5446,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::urgency::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of the situation became clear immediately.","expectedAnswer":"urgency","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of the situation became clear immediately.","clozeAnswer":"urgency","exampleTranslation":"局勢的緊急性立即可見。","reference":{"eng":"urgency","kk":"ˈɜːrdʒənsi","tense":"n.","ch":"[['緊急'], ['急迫'], ['緊迫']]","chEntries":["緊急","急迫","緊迫"],"practiceMeaning":"局勢的緊急性立即可見。","analysis":"此字為派生詞，由形容詞 \"urgent\" (緊急的) 加上名詞化字尾 \"-cy\" (或 \"-cy\") 構成。\"urgent\" 源自拉丁語 \"urgens\" (催促、緊迫)，是動詞 \"urgere\" 的現在分詞。構詞上，\"urg-\" 提供了核心的「催促」、「緊迫」語意，\"-ency\" 是常見的名詞字尾，表示「狀態」、「品質」或「情況」。因此，\"urgency\" 指的是「需要立即關注或處理的緊急、急迫或緊迫的狀態」。","definition":"an important and urgent need or demand; the quality or state of being urgent.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The urgency of the situation became clear immediately.\",\n    \"ch\": \"局勢的緊急性立即可見。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There is a sense of urgency in their voices.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們的語氣中帶著一種急迫感。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The organization stressed the urgency of climate action.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該組織強調了氣候行動的緊迫性。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"局勢的緊急性立即可見。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5152,"wordRef":"字彙王::u62::utility::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of this tool is immense.","expectedAnswer":"utility","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of this tool is immense.","clozeAnswer":"utility","exampleTranslation":"這個工具的效用是巨大的。","reference":{"eng":"utility","kk":"juːˈtɪləti","tense":"n.","ch":"[['效用'], ['功用'], ['公共事業（水、電、煤氣等）']]","chEntries":["效用","功用","公共事業"],"practiceMeaning":"這個工具的效用是巨大的。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 utilitas，意為「有用性、好處」，來自 utilis（有用的），而 utilis 來自 uti（使用）。核心語意是「有用性、功能性」。引申為「能滿足人類需求的服務」（如水、電、瓦斯等公共事業），以及「具有實用價值的東西」。","definition":"the state or quality of being useful; usefulness; an organization or company that provides a basic service, such as electricity, water, or gas, to the public.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The utility of this tool is immense.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個工具的效用是巨大的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We pay our utility bills every month.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們每月支付公共事業的帳單。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個工具的效用是巨大的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U62"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6204,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::variable::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The weather in this region is very ____.","expectedAnswer":"variable","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The weather in this region is very ____.","clozeAnswer":"variable","exampleTranslation":"這個地區的天氣變化很大。","reference":{"eng":"variable","kk":"ˈveriəbl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"變化的\"  ],  [    \"易變的\"  ],  [    \"可變的\"  ],  [    \"不定的\"  ]]","chEntries":["變化的","易變的","可變的","不定的"],"practiceMeaning":"這個地區的天氣變化很大。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 variabilis，是動詞 variare「改變」的衍生形容詞。variare 源自 varus「彎曲的、扭曲的」，可能與 varia（斑駁）有關。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 variare「改變」是其核心語意來源。作為形容詞，其核心語義是「能夠或傾向於改變；不穩定的」。詞源中的「改變」概念直接體現了此義。","definition":"1. not always the same; liable to change; 2. able to be changed or adapted.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The weather in this region is very variable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個地區的天氣變化很大。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has a variable temper.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的脾氣很不穩定。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The amount of interest is variable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"利率是可變的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her mood was variable throughout the day.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她一天之間情緒多變。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個地區的天氣變化很大。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}}