多年。","analysis":"此字是動詞 'widen' 的過去分詞，用作形容詞。'widen' 源自古英語 wuduwe（寡婦），原始日耳曼語 \\*widuwō，最終可追溯至原始印歐語 \\*h₃dʰew-（被動的、喪失的，與「失去配偶」相關）。構詞上，'widow' 作為名詞，加上過去分詞的語法功能，形容「遭受喪偶之痛」的狀態，即「成為寡婦或鰥夫的」。核心語意是「失去配偶」，因此演變為形容「喪偶的」狀態。","definition":"having lost one's spouse by death.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She lived as a widowed woman for many years.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她以寡婦的身分獨居了許多多年。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她以寡婦的身分獨居了許多多年。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5680,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l9::widower::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ raised his children alone.","expectedAnswer":"widower","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ raised his children alone.","clozeAnswer":"widower","exampleTranslation":"這位鰥夫獨自撫養他的孩子們。","reference":{"eng":"widower","kk":"ˈwɪdoʊər","tense":"n.","ch":"[['鰥夫']]","chEntries":["鰥夫"],"practiceMeaning":"這位鰥夫獨自撫養他的孩子們。","analysis":"此字由名詞 'widow' 加上表示「人」的後綴 '-er' 構成。'widow' 源自古英語 wuduwe（寡婦），詞源可追溯至原始印歐語 \\*h₃dʰew-（被動的、喪失的）。'-er' 後綴在構詞上是將一個名詞（通常是與某個行為、狀態或事物相關的）轉化為執行該行為、處於該狀態或與該事物相關的人。在此，它將「寡婦」這個女性的喪偶狀態，透過 '-er' 擴展為男性處於相似狀態的稱謂，即「失去妻子的男人」，即「鰥夫」。","definition":"a man whose wife has died and who has not remarried.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The widower raised his children alone.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位鰥夫獨自撫養他的孩子們。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這位鰥夫獨自撫養他的孩子們。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5348,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l1::worship::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Religious ____ often involves prayer and hymns.","expectedAnswer":"worship","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Religious ____ often involves prayer and hymns.","clozeAnswer":"worship","exampleTranslation":"宗教崇拜通常包括祈禱和聖歌。","reference":{"eng":"worship","kk":"ˈwɜːrʃɪp","tense":"n.","ch":"[['崇拜'], ['敬拜'], ['禮拜']]","chEntries":["崇拜","敬拜","禮拜"],"practiceMeaning":"宗教崇拜通常包括祈禱和聖歌。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 weorþscipe，由 weorþ（價值、尊嚴）+ -scipe（狀態、職位，相當於現代的 -ship）組成。原始語意為「價值、尊嚴的狀態」。後演變為「對神祇或崇高事物的尊敬與崇拜」。構詞上，weorþ- 表示「價值、值得」，-scipe 構成抽象名詞。現代語意主要指宗教上的「崇拜、敬拜」。","definition":"adoration and devotion accorded to a deity or to something considered divine or sacred; great love or admiration for someone or something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Religious worship often involves prayer and hymns.\",\n    \"ch\": \"宗教崇拜通常包括祈禱和聖歌。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He felt a sense of worship for his idol.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對他的偶像感到一種崇拜之情。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"宗教崇拜通常包括祈禱和聖歌。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4676,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::wrap::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The present had a beautiful gift ____.","expectedAnswer":"wrap","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The present had a beautiful gift ____.","clozeAnswer":"wrap","exampleTranslation":"這份禮物有著美麗的包裝紙。","reference":{"eng":"wrap","kk":"/ˈræp/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['包裹物'], ['（食物）捲餅']]","chEntries":["包裹物","捲餅"],"practiceMeaning":"這份禮物有著美麗的包裝紙。","analysis":"名詞形式，指動詞 wrap 的結果，即被包裹起來的東西。可以是禮物、文件等，也專指用薄餅包裹餡料的食物。","definition":"1. An outer covering or wrapping. 2. A large flatbread folded around a filling.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The present had a beautiful gift wrap.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這份禮物有著美麗的包裝紙。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I ordered a chicken wrap for lunch.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我午餐點了一個雞肉捲餅。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這份禮物有著美麗的包裝紙。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4511,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::a::art","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She is ____ doctor.","expectedAnswer":"a","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She is ____ doctor.","clozeAnswer":"a","exampleTranslation":"她是一位醫生。","reference":{"eng":"a","kk":"/ə/, /eɪ/","tense":"art.","ch":"[['一個']]","chEntries":["一個"],"practiceMeaning":"她是一位醫生。","analysis":"不定冠詞，源自古英語 ān，意為「一」。用於單數可數名詞前，表示「一個」、「某個」、「任何一個」。","definition":"1. Used before singular countable nouns to refer to a non-specific or non-particular member of a group or category; 2. Used when mentioning something for the first time.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I saw a dog in the park.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我在公園裡看到了一隻狗。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a doctor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是一位醫生。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她是一位醫生。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5502,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::a-fish-out-of-water::idiom","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She's always been shy, so starting a new job made her feel like ____.","expectedAnswer":"a fish out of water","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She's always been shy, so starting a new job made her feel like ____.","clozeAnswer":"a fish out of water","exampleTranslation":"她一向很害羞，所以開始一份新工作讓她感到渾身不自在。","reference":{"eng":"a fish out of water","kk":"ə fɪʃ aʊt əv ˈwɔtər","tense":"idiom","ch":"[['格格不入'], ['不適應環境'], ['渾身不自在']]","chEntries":["格格不入","不適應環境","渾身不自在"],"practiceMeaning":"她一向很害羞，所以開始一份新工作讓她感到渾身不自在。","analysis":"這個片語字面意思是「一條離開水的魚」。'Fish' 是魚，'out of water' 指「離開水的」。魚在水中才能生存和自由活動，一旦離開水，牠就會感到極度不適、無法呼吸、行動困難，甚至死亡。因此，'a fish out of water' 用來比喻「處在一個完全陌生、不習慣或不適合的環境中，感到非常不自在、尷尬或無所適從」。核心語意是「在不熟悉或不適合的環境中感到不適」。","definition":"1. A person who is out of place or uncomfortable in a particular situation or environment.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"As a city person, he felt like a fish out of water on the farm.\",\n    \"ch\": \"作為一個城市人，他在農場裡感到格格不入。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She's always been shy, so starting a new job made her feel like a fish out of water.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她一向很害羞，所以開始一份新工作讓她感到渾身不自在。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"During the meeting, I felt like a fish out of water, not understanding any of the technical jargon.\",\n    \"ch\": \"會議期間，我感到很不適應，聽不懂任何專業術語。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她一向很害羞，所以開始一份新工作讓她感到渾身不自在。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4366,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::a-garage-sale::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They are holding ____ next weekend to clear out old items.","expectedAnswer":"a garage sale","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They are holding ____ next weekend to clear out old items.","clozeAnswer":"a garage sale","exampleTranslation":"他們下週末將舉辦舊物拍賣會來清理舊物品。","reference":{"eng":"a garage sale","kk":"None","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['舊物拍賣會；車庫拍賣']]","chEntries":["舊物拍賣會","車庫拍賣"],"practiceMeaning":"他們下週末將舉辦舊物拍賣會來清理舊物品。","analysis":"此為片語分析。'garage' (n.) 指『車庫』。'sale' (n.) 源自 'sell' (v.)，意為『銷售』。結合起來，指人們在自家車庫或庭院裡舉辦的，用來出售家中不再需要的二手物品的『舊物拍賣會』。","definition":"an event where people sell unwanted possessions from their home, often from their garage or front yard","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We found some great bargains at the garage sale.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們在舊物拍賣會上找到了一些很便宜的東西。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They are holding a garage sale next weekend to clear out old items.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們下週末將舉辦舊物拍賣會來清理舊物品。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們下週末將舉辦舊物拍賣會來清理舊物品。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4285,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::a-narrow-alley::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The team found a hidden entrance in ____.","expectedAnswer":"a narrow alley","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The team found a hidden entrance in ____.","clozeAnswer":"a narrow alley","exampleTranslation":"隊伍在一個狹窄的小巷裡發現了一個隱藏的入口。","reference":{"eng":"a narrow alley","kk":"/ə ˈnɛroʊ ˈæli/","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['一條狹窄的小巷']]","chEntries":["一條狹窄的小巷"],"practiceMeaning":"隊伍在一個狹窄的小巷裡發現了一個隱藏的入口。","analysis":"由不定冠詞 'a'、形容詞 'narrow'（狹窄的）和名詞 'alley'（小巷）組成。'A narrow alley' 描述的是一個「狹窄的、兩側有建築物的小通道」，強調其空間的侷促。","definition":"a small, narrow passage between buildings.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He walked down a narrow alley, looking for the restaurant.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他沿著一條狹窄的小巷走，尋找那家餐廳。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The team found a hidden entrance in a narrow alley.\",\n    \"ch\": \"隊伍在一個狹窄的小巷裡發現了一個隱藏的入口。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"隊伍在一個狹窄的小巷裡發現了一個隱藏的入口。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4297,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::a-pile-of::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He had ____ work to complete before the deadline.","expectedAnswer":"a pile of","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He had ____ work to complete before the deadline.","clozeAnswer":"a pile of","exampleTranslation":"截止日期前他有一大堆工作要完成。","reference":{"eng":"a pile of","kk":"/ə paɪl əv/","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['一堆...'], ['許多...']]","chEntries":["一堆...","許多..."],"practiceMeaning":"截止日期前他有一大堆工作要完成。","analysis":"由不定冠詞 'a'、名詞 'pile'（堆）和介詞 'of'（的）組成。'A pile of' 用於指代「許多、大量的某物，堆積在一起」或「許多不整齊的某物」。","definition":"a heap of things laid or lying one on top of another; a large quantity of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She found a pile of old letters in the attic.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在閣樓裡找到一堆舊信件。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He had a pile of work to complete before the deadline.\",\n    \"ch\": \"截止日期前他有一大堆工作要完成。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"截止日期前他有一大堆工作要完成。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4648,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::a-ray-of-sun::idiom","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"In the darkness, ____ offered some hope.","expectedAnswer":"a ray of sun","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"In the darkness, ____ offered some hope.","clozeAnswer":"a ray of sun","exampleTranslation":"在黑暗中，一線陽光帶來了一絲希望。","reference":{"eng":"a ray of sun","kk":"/ə reɪ əv sʌn/","tense":"idiom","ch":"[['一線陽光']]","chEntries":["一線陽光"],"practiceMeaning":"在黑暗中，一線陽光帶來了一絲希望。","analysis":"此為固定片語。'Ray' (射線、光線) 是指從光源發出的直線光束。'Sun' (太陽) 是光源。整個片語描繪了陽光穿透雲層或陰影，照射下來的微小光束，常被用來比喻微弱的希望或光明。","definition":"a thin line of light from the sun.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A ray of sun broke through the clouds.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一線陽光穿破雲層。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"In the darkness, a ray of sun offered some hope.\",\n    \"ch\": \"在黑暗中，一線陽光帶來了一絲希望。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"在黑暗中，一線陽光帶來了一絲希望。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4287,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::a-reminder::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The calendar alert served as ____ for the meeting.","expectedAnswer":"a reminder","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The calendar alert served as ____ for the meeting.","clozeAnswer":"a reminder","exampleTranslation":"日曆的提醒作為會議的通知。","reference":{"eng":"a reminder","kk":"/ə rɪˈmaɪndər/","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['一個提醒物'], ['一個提醒']]","chEntries":["一個提醒物","一個提醒"],"practiceMeaning":"日曆的提醒作為會議的通知。","analysis":"由不定冠詞 'a' 和名詞 'reminder'（提醒物、提醒）組成。'A reminder' 指「一個能夠幫助某人記住某事的事物」，可以是物品、訊息或事件。","definition":"something that makes you remember something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The wilting flowers were a sad reminder of summer's end.\",\n    \"ch\": \"枯萎的花朵是夏天結束的一個悲傷的提醒。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The calendar alert served as a reminder for the meeting.\",\n    \"ch\": \"日曆的提醒作為會議的通知。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"日曆的提醒作為會議的通知。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4294,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::a-sensible-approach::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The manager adopted ____ to resolving the conflict.","expectedAnswer":"a sensible approach","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The manager adopted ____ to resolving the conflict.","clozeAnswer":"a sensible approach","exampleTranslation":"經理採取了合理的方法來解決衝突。","reference":{"eng":"a sensible approach","kk":"/ə ˈsɛnsəbəl əˈproʊtʃ/","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['明智的方法'], ['合理的做法']]","chEntries":["明智的方法","合理的做法"],"practiceMeaning":"經理採取了合理的方法來解決衝突。","analysis":"由不定冠詞 'a'、形容詞 'sensible'（明智的、理性的）和名詞 'approach'（方法、途徑）組成。'A sensible approach' 指「一個基於良好判斷、理性、實用且有效的處理問題或達成目標的方式」。","definition":"a practical and reasonable way of dealing with a situation or problem.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Taking a gradual approach is sensible for learning a new skill.\",\n    \"ch\": \"學習新技能採取循序漸進的方法是很明智的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The manager adopted a sensible approach to resolving the conflict.\",\n    \"ch\": \"經理採取了合理的方法來解決衝突。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"經理採取了合理的方法來解決衝突。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4286,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::a-shopping-paradise::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"With its numerous boutiques, the city is ____ for fashion lovers.","expectedAnswer":"a shopping paradise","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"With its numerous boutiques, the city is ____ for fashion lovers.","clozeAnswer":"a shopping paradise","exampleTranslation":"這座城市擁有眾多精品店，是時尚愛好者的購物天堂。","reference":{"eng":"a shopping paradise","kk":"/ə ˈʃɑːpɪŋ ˈpærədaɪs/","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['購物天堂']]","chEntries":["購物天堂"],"practiceMeaning":"這座城市擁有眾多精品店，是時尚愛好者的購物天堂。","analysis":"結合了動名詞 'shopping'（購物）和名詞 'paradise'（天堂、樂園）。'A shopping paradise' 指一個「提供極多樣化、高品質商品，且購物體驗極佳的地方」，讓熱愛購物的人感到非常滿足。","definition":"a place where people can buy a very wide range of goods, or enjoy shopping very much.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Dubai is often described as a shopping paradise for luxury goods.\",\n    \"ch\": \"杜拜常被形容為奢侈品的購物天堂。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"With its numerous boutiques, the city is a shopping paradise for fashion lovers.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座城市擁有眾多精品店，是時尚愛好者的購物天堂。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這座城市擁有眾多精品店，是時尚愛好者的購物天堂。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4351,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::a-stormy-argument::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The committee meeting ended with ____.","expectedAnswer":"a stormy argument","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The committee meeting ended with ____.","clozeAnswer":"a stormy argument","exampleTranslation":"委員會會議以一場激烈的爭論結束。","reference":{"eng":"a stormy argument","kk":"None","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['一場激烈的爭吵']]","chEntries":["一場激烈的爭吵"],"practiceMeaning":"委員會會議以一場激烈的爭論結束。","analysis":"此為片語分析。'stormy' (adj.) 源自 'storm' (n.)，意為『暴風雨的』，比喻『激烈的、動盪的』。'argument' (n.) 源自拉丁語 'argumentum'，指『爭論、辯論』。兩者結合，形容一場充滿激烈情緒、口角、衝突的爭吵。","definition":"an argument that is very angry and full of strong feelings or disagreements","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They had a stormy argument about the division of property.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們為了財產分割而進行了一場激烈的爭吵。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The committee meeting ended with a stormy argument.\",\n    \"ch\": \"委員會會議以一場激烈的爭論結束。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"委員會會議以一場激烈的爭論結束。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4583,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::a-wildlife-reserve::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The government established ____ to protect endangered species.","expectedAnswer":"a wildlife reserve","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The government established ____ to protect endangered species.","clozeAnswer":"a wildlife reserve","exampleTranslation":"政府設立了一個野生動物保護區來保護瀕危物種。","reference":{"eng":"a wildlife reserve","kk":"/ə ˈwaɪldlaɪf rɪˈzɜːrv/","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['野生動物保護區']]","chEntries":["野生動物保護區"],"practiceMeaning":"政府設立了一個野生動物保護區來保護瀕危物種。","analysis":"此片語由 'a' (不定冠詞), 'wildlife' (野生動物) 和 'reserve' (保護區) 組成。 'reserve' 源自拉丁語 'reservare' (to keep back - 留存)，在此指為特定目的（保護野生動植物）而保留的土地。 'wildlife' 指未經馴化的動植物。","definition":"1. an area of land where animals and plants are protected.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They visited a wildlife reserve to see elephants and lions.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們參觀了一個野生動物保護區，看到了大象和獅子。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government established a wildlife reserve to protect endangered species.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府設立了一個野生動物保護區來保護瀕危物種。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"政府設立了一個野生動物保護區來保護瀕危物種。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5353,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l1::abandon::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He decided to ____ his dreams of becoming a musician.","expectedAnswer":"abandon","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He decided to ____ his dreams of becoming a musician.","clozeAnswer":"abandon","exampleTranslation":"他決定放棄成為音樂家的夢想。","reference":{"eng":"abandon","kk":"əˈbændən","tense":"v.","ch":"[['拋棄'], ['放棄'], ['離棄']]","chEntries":["拋棄","放棄","離棄"],"practiceMeaning":"他決定放棄成為音樂家的夢想。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 abandonner，來自 an-（在……情況下）+ bandon（法語的控制權、禁止）。原始概念為「脫離控制」、「在沒有保護的情況下」。構詞上，a- 是加強語氣或表示「給予」的字首，bandon- 來自 banna（命令、禁止）。核心語意是「將某物置於無人管轄、無人保護的狀態」，引申為「拋棄」、「放棄」或「離棄」。","definition":"to give up completely a course of action, a practice, or a way of thinking; to cease to support or look after (someone); desert.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They had to abandon their car in the snow.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們不得不把車子丟在雪中。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He decided to abandon his dreams of becoming a musician.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他決定放棄成為音樂家的夢想。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他決定放棄成為音樂家的夢想。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5114,"wordRef":"字彙王::u62::abnormal::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The test results showed some ____ readings.","expectedAnswer":"abnormal","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The test results showed some ____ readings.","clozeAnswer":"abnormal","exampleTranslation":"檢測結果顯示了一些異常讀數。","reference":{"eng":"abnormal","kk":"æbˈnɔːrməl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['反常的'], ['變態的'], ['不規則的']]","chEntries":["反常的","變態的","不規則的"],"practiceMeaning":"檢測結果顯示了一些異常讀數。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 abnormalis，由 ab-（離開、遠離）+ norma（規則、標準）+ -al（形容詞字尾）組成。ab- 來自印歐語系 *apo-，意為「離開、遠離」。norma 來自拉丁語，意為「角尺、規範、標準」，可能與 *ǵnō-（知道、辨認）有關。-al 是常見的拉丁形容詞字尾，用於將名詞轉為形容詞。核心語意為「偏離標準」或「不符合規則」，由此引申出「反常的、不尋常的、變態的」等義。","definition":"deviating from what is normal or usual; unusual; irregular; pathological.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His behavior was abnormal for a child his age.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的行為對他這個年紀的孩子來說很不尋常。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The test results showed some abnormal readings.\",\n    \"ch\": \"檢測結果顯示了一些異常讀數。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"檢測結果顯示了一些異常讀數。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U62"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3198,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::abstract::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The artist's latest work is an ____.","expectedAnswer":"abstract","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The artist's latest work is an ____.","clozeAnswer":"abstract","exampleTranslation":"這位藝術家最新的作品是一件抽象畫。","reference":{"eng":"abstract","kk":"/ˈæbstrækt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['摘要'], ['概要'], ['抽象概念']]","chEntries":["摘要","概要","抽象概念"],"practiceMeaning":"這位藝術家最新的作品是一件抽象畫。","analysis":"名詞形式，源自形容詞，指將事物的核心或主要觀點獨立出來，形成一個簡要的概述，如同將具體的內容提煉為抽象的重點。也指非具體的概念。","definition":"1. a summary of the contents of a book, article, or speech; 2. a piece of abstract art.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please read the abstract before the full paper.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請在閱讀整篇論文前先看摘要。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The artist's latest work is an abstract.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位藝術家最新的作品是一件抽象畫。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這位藝術家最新的作品是一件抽象畫。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U41"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5425,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::abundance::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There was an ____ of food at the party.","expectedAnswer":"abundance","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There was an ____ of food at the party.","clozeAnswer":"abundance","exampleTranslation":"派對上有豐富的食物。","reference":{"eng":"abundance","kk":"əˈbʌndəns","tense":"n.","ch":"[['豐富'], ['充裕'], ['大量'], ['豐盛']]","chEntries":["豐富","充裕","大量","豐盛"],"practiceMeaning":"派對上有豐富的食物。","analysis":"此字為派生詞，由形容詞 \"abundant\" 加上名詞化字尾 \"-ance\" 構成。\"abundant\" 源自拉丁語 \"abundans\"，是動詞 \"abundare\" 的現在分詞，意為\"充溢\"、\"豐富\"。\"abundare\" 由 \"ab-\" (離開、遠離，在此表示\"過多\"或\"溢出\") 和 \"undare\" (波浪般流動) 構成，\"undare\" 又源於 \"unda\" (波浪)。構詞上，\"ab-\" 提供了「過量」的語意，\"undare\" 提供了「流動」的圖像，整體表示「如波浪般湧出、充溢」。字尾 \"-ance\" 將形容詞的「充裕」狀態轉化為抽象名詞，表示「豐富」、「充裕」或「大量」的狀態或性質。","definition":"a large quantity of something; a great amount of something; plenty; profusion; more than enough.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The region is known for its abundance of natural resources.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該地區以其豐富的自然資源而聞名。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was an abundance of food at the party.\",\n    \"ch\": \"派對上有豐富的食物。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The abundance of information online can be overwhelming.\",\n    \"ch\": \"網路上豐富的資訊可能會讓人不知所措。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"派對上有豐富的食物。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3259,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::accent::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The word 'father' has the ____ on the first syllable.","expectedAnswer":"accent","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The word 'father' has the ____ on the first syllable.","clozeAnswer":"accent","exampleTranslation":"單字 'father' 的重音在第一個音節。","reference":{"eng":"accent","kk":"/ˈæksənt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['口音；腔調'], ['強調；重音'], ['（尤指演講或寫作中的）標音符號']]","chEntries":["口音","腔調","強調","重音","標音符號"],"practiceMeaning":"單字 'father' 的重音在第一個音節。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'accentus'，意為「曲調，音調」，由 'ad-'（朝向）+ 'cantus'（歌唱，歌曲）組成。最初指音樂中的音調，後引申至語言中的語音特徵（口音、重音）以及書寫中表示重音的符號。","definition":"1. a distinct way of pronouncing a language, especially one that is characteristic of a particular country, region, or social group; 2. an emphasis given to a particular syllable or word in speech; 3. a mark written above a letter to indicate the pronunciation or stress of a syllable.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She speaks with a strong Southern accent.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她說話帶著濃重的南方口音。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The word 'father' has the accent on the first syllable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"單字 'father' 的重音在第一個音節。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The acute accent (´) is used in some languages.\",\n    \"ch\": \"銳音符號（´）在某些語言中使用。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"單字 'father' 的重音在第一個音節。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4616,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::acceptable::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His performance was ____, but not outstanding.","expectedAnswer":"acceptable","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His performance was ____, but not outstanding.","clozeAnswer":"acceptable","exampleTranslation":"他的表現尚可，但並不突出。","reference":{"eng":"acceptable","kk":"/əkˈseptəbəl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['可接受的'], ['令人滿意的'], ['尚可的']]","chEntries":["可接受的","令人滿意的","尚可的"],"practiceMeaning":"他的表現尚可，但並不突出。","analysis":"由 'accept' (接受) + '-able' (能夠...的) 組成。'Accept' 源自拉丁語 'accipere' (接受、拿到)。此字指事物達到某種最低標準，雖然不一定完美，但足以被容忍、接受或認為可以。","definition":"satisfactory or good enough; able to be accepted.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The proposal is acceptable to all parties.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這項提議對所有相關方來說都是可以接受的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His performance was acceptable, but not outstanding.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的表現尚可，但並不突出。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他的表現尚可，但並不突出。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3261,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::accountant::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company's ____ discovered a discrepancy in the records.","expectedAnswer":"accountant","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company's ____ discovered a discrepancy in the records.","clozeAnswer":"accountant","exampleTranslation":"公司的會計師發現記錄中有出入。","reference":{"eng":"accountant","kk":"/əˈkaʊntənt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['會計師']]","chEntries":["會計師"],"practiceMeaning":"公司的會計師發現記錄中有出入。","analysis":"源自 'account' (帳目，敘述)，加上 '-ant'（從事某事的人）後綴。指專門負責管理和審核帳目的人。","definition":"a person whose job is to keep the financial accounts of a business and to check them.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I need to hire an accountant to help with my taxes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我需要聘請一位會計師來幫我處理稅務。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company's accountant discovered a discrepancy in the records.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司的會計師發現記錄中有出入。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"公司的會計師發現記錄中有出入。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4562,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::accurate::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His estimate of the cost was remarkably ____.","expectedAnswer":"accurate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His estimate of the cost was remarkably ____.","clozeAnswer":"accurate","exampleTranslation":"他對費用的估計非常準確。","reference":{"eng":"accurate","kk":"/ˈækjərət/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['準確的', '精確的'], ['（陳述、測量等）正確的']]","chEntries":["準確的","精確的","正確的"],"practiceMeaning":"他對費用的估計非常準確。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'accuratus'，'ad-' (to) 和 'cura' (care - 關心、小心) 的組合。核心概念是「非常小心地」進行，從而達到精確。\n    1. 準確的、精確的：指測量、數據、預測等非常接近真實值或目標。\n    2. 正確的：指陳述或判斷符合事實。","definition":"1. (of information, measurements, etc.) precise; exact.; 2. correct in all details; error-free.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The report provided an accurate account of the events.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這份報告提供了對事件的準確敘述。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His estimate of the cost was remarkably accurate.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對費用的估計非常準確。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need accurate data to make a decision.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要準確的數據來做決定。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他對費用的估計非常準確。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5337,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l1::acquire::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Children ____ language naturally.","expectedAnswer":"acquire","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Children ____ language naturally.","clozeAnswer":"acquire","exampleTranslation":"兒童能自然地學到語言。","reference":{"eng":"acquire","kk":"əˈkwaɪər","tense":"v.","ch":"[['獲得'], ['學到'], ['購得']]","chEntries":["獲得","學到","購得"],"practiceMeaning":"兒童能自然地學到語言。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 aquerre，來自拉丁語 adquirere，由 ad-（朝向、加上）+ quirere（尋找、獲得）組成， quirere 為 quaerere（尋找、詢問）的變體。構詞上，ad- 表示「朝向」，quir- 是字根，表示「尋找、獲得」。原始語意為「主動尋找並獲得」。現代語意涵蓋「透過努力或購買獲得」、「學到（知識、技能）」等。","definition":"to gain something by purchase or by birth, or by effort, skill, or the like; to learn or develop a skill or habit.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He managed to acquire a valuable collection of stamps.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他設法獲得了大量珍貴的郵票收藏。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Children acquire language naturally.\",\n    \"ch\": \"兒童能自然地學到語言。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"兒童能自然地學到語言。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3898,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::actually::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"What ____ happened was different.","expectedAnswer":"actually","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"What ____ happened was different.","clozeAnswer":"actually","exampleTranslation":"實際上發生的情況是不同的。","reference":{"eng":"actually","kk":"/ˈæktʃuəli/","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['實際上', '事實上'], ['真的', '確實']]","chEntries":["實際上","事實上","真的","確實"],"practiceMeaning":"實際上發生的情況是不同的。","analysis":"由 'actual' (實際的) 加上副詞後綴 '-ly' 組成。核心是「依據事實」。用來強調某事物是真實的，與預期或表面情況不同，或用來引出真實情況。","definition":"1. in fact; in reality. 2. used to emphasize a statement or to correct a misconception.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I thought he was joking, but he was actually serious.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我以為他在開玩笑，但他實際上是認真的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"What actually happened was different.\",\n    \"ch\": \"實際上發生的情況是不同的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's actually quite a simple process.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這實際上是一個相當簡單的過程。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"實際上發生的情況是不同的。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3122,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::addict::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She's a total coffee ____; she needs at least three cups a day.","expectedAnswer":"addict","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She's a total coffee ____; she needs at least three cups a day.","clozeAnswer":"addict","exampleTranslation":"她是個徹頭徹尾的咖啡愛好者；她每天至少需要三杯咖啡。","reference":{"eng":"addict","kk":"/ˈædɪkt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['癮君子；對...有強烈癮頭的人'], ['（非正式）熱衷者']]","chEntries":["癮君子","對...有強烈癮頭的人","熱衷者"],"practiceMeaning":"她是個徹頭徹尾的咖啡愛好者；她每天至少需要三杯咖啡。","analysis":"此為名詞用法，源自動詞 'addict'。指代被某種物質（如毒品、酒精）或活動（如賭博、網路）嚴重依賴或沉迷的人。'addict' 的核心概念是「被某物牢牢抓住、無法擺脫」。","definition":"1. a person who is addicted to a particular substance or activity; 2. an enthusiast or devotee of a particular activity.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The organization provides support for former drug addicts.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該組織為前吸毒癮君子提供支援。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She's a total coffee addict; she needs at least three cups a day.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是個徹頭徹尾的咖啡愛好者；她每天至少需要三杯咖啡。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她是個徹頭徹尾的咖啡愛好者；她每天至少需要三杯咖啡。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3123,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::addicted::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She felt miserable and withdrawn, clearly ____ to her medication.","expectedAnswer":"addicted","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She felt miserable and withdrawn, clearly ____ to her medication.","clozeAnswer":"addicted","exampleTranslation":"她感到痛苦且孤僻，顯然對她的藥物上癮了。","reference":{"eng":"addicted","kk":"/əˈdɪktɪd/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['上癮的；沉迷的']]","chEntries":["上癮的","沉迷的"],"practiceMeaning":"她感到痛苦且孤僻，顯然對她的藥物上癮了。","analysis":"這是動詞 'addict' 的過去分詞，用作形容詞。表示某人處於對某種物質或活動上癮或極度沉迷的狀態。其語意直接承襲了動詞『使沉迷』的概念，強調結果。","definition":"physically or mentally dependent on a particular substance or activity.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He admitted he was addicted to video games.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他承認自己對電子遊戲上癮了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She felt miserable and withdrawn, clearly addicted to her medication.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她感到痛苦且孤僻，顯然對她的藥物上癮了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她感到痛苦且孤僻，顯然對她的藥物上癮了。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5603,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l7::additionally::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He is a talented musician and, ____, a skilled writer.","expectedAnswer":"additionally","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He is a talented musician and, ____, a skilled writer.","clozeAnswer":"additionally","exampleTranslation":"他是一位才華橫溢的音樂家，而且，他也是一位技巧嫻熟的作家。","reference":{"eng":"additionally","kk":"əˈdɪʃənəli","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['此外'], ['而且'], ['另外']]","chEntries":["此外","而且","另外"],"practiceMeaning":"他是一位才華橫溢的音樂家，而且，他也是一位技巧嫻熟的作家。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'additio'，意為「添加」，由 'addere'（添加）派生而來。構詞上，'addition' 是核心名詞（意為「加法」或「添加物」），加上了形容詞化後綴 '-al'，成為 'additional'（附加的），最後再接副詞化後綴 '-ly'，形成副詞 'additionally'。'-ly' 後綴將形容詞轉換為副詞，表示「以……的方式」或「具有……的性質」。'additional' 的「附加的」語意，透過 '-ly' 轉化為副詞，表示「額外地」、「此外」。原始語意是「增加的、額外的」，在副詞形式中，它用於引入額外的資訊或論點。","definition":"1. In addition; also; 2. Furthermore.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The hotel offers free breakfast; additionally, guests can use the gym.\",\n    \"ch\": \"飯店提供免費早餐；此外，客人還可以使用健身房。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a talented musician and, additionally, a skilled writer.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一位才華橫溢的音樂家，而且，他也是一位技巧嫻熟的作家。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他是一位才華橫溢的音樂家，而且，他也是一位技巧嫻熟的作家。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5543,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l5::admit::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The hospital can ____ up to 200 patients.","expectedAnswer":"admit","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The hospital can ____ up to 200 patients.","clozeAnswer":"admit","exampleTranslation":"這家醫院最多可以接納 200 名病人。","reference":{"eng":"admit","kk":"ədˈmɪt","tense":"v.","ch":"[['承認'], ['允許進入'], ['接納']]","chEntries":["承認","允許進入","接納"],"practiceMeaning":"這家醫院最多可以接納 200 名病人。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'admittere'，由 'ad-' (to) + 'mittere' (to send, to let go) 構成。原始語義是「讓……進去」或「允許……進入」。構詞上，'ad-' 表示「朝向、到……」，'mit-' 是 'mittere' 的詞幹，意為「派遣、發送、讓」。'admit' 的核心語義是「讓某事物或某人進入」，這引申出兩大類含義：1. 允許進入（場所、組織）；2. 承認（錯誤、事實）。後者是從「讓事實進入你的認知」或「讓真相被承認」演變而來。","definition":"to confess to be true or to be the case, typically with reluctance; to allow (someone) to enter a place or organization.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He admitted that he had made a mistake.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他承認自己犯了錯誤。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The hospital can admit up to 200 patients.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家醫院最多可以接納 200 名病人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She was admitted to the university.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她被大學錄取了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這家醫院最多可以接納 200 名病人。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5460,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::adventure::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The novel tells the story of a young explorer's ____ in the jungle.","expectedAnswer":"adventure","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The novel tells the story of a young explorer's ____ in the jungle.","clozeAnswer":"adventure","exampleTranslation":"這本小說講述了一位年輕探險家在叢林中的冒險故事。","reference":{"eng":"adventure","kk":"ædvɛnˈtʃɜr","tense":"n.","ch":"[['冒險'], ['奇遇'], ['歷險']]","chEntries":["冒險","奇遇","歷險"],"practiceMeaning":"這本小說講述了一位年輕探險家在叢林中的冒險故事。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 'aventure'，意指「機遇、事件、奇遇」。'Aventure' 又來自拉丁語 'adventura'，字面意思是「將要發生的事」，'ad-' 是「朝向」的意思，'ventura' 是 'venire'（來）的將來分詞。在中古英語中，'adventure' 最初常用來指「意外的事件」或「幸運的機會」，後來逐漸演變成「充滿刺激、危險或新奇的經歷」。核心語意是「未知的、可能充滿挑戰或驚喜的事件或經歷」。","definition":"1. An unusual and exciting or daring experience or activity.; 2. A commercial enterprise undertaken with the hope of succeeding.; 3. A series of exciting or unusual events or experiences.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He sought adventure in far-off lands.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他到遠方尋求冒險。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The novel tells the story of a young explorer's adventure in the jungle.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本小說講述了一位年輕探險家在叢林中的冒險故事。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was an adventure to travel without any plans.\",\n    \"ch\": \"沒有任何計劃的旅行是一場冒險。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這本小說講述了一位年輕探險家在叢林中的冒險故事。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5459,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::adventurous::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They planned an ____ journey through the Amazon rainforest.","expectedAnswer":"adventurous","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They planned an ____ journey through the Amazon rainforest.","clozeAnswer":"adventurous","exampleTranslation":"他們計劃了一次穿越亞馬遜雨林的冒險旅程。","reference":{"eng":"adventurous","kk":"ædvɛnˈtʃɜrəs","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['愛冒險的'], ['大膽的'], ['富於冒險精神的']]","chEntries":["愛冒險的","大膽的","富於冒險精神的"],"practiceMeaning":"他們計劃了一次穿越亞馬遜雨林的冒險旅程。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 'æfentyrlic'，由 'adventure'（冒險）加上形容詞字尾 '-ous' 構成，意為「充滿冒險的」。'Adventure' 本身來自古法語 'aventure'，意指「機遇、事件」，源自拉丁語 'adventura'，意為「即將發生的事」。'-ous' 是拉丁語 '-osus' 的英語化形式，用來構成形容詞，表示「充滿……的」或「具有……特性的」。因此，'adventurous' 的核心語意是「喜歡經歷或尋求冒險」，引申為「大膽的、樂於嘗試新事物」。","definition":"1. Eager to take risks or to embark on new, daring ventures; bold; daring; brave; intrepid; courageous; valiant.; 2. Characterized by or involving adventure; exciting; hazardous; risky; dangerous.; 3. Willing to undertake a risky or daring personal project, enterprise, or undertaking.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She was an adventurous child who loved exploring the woods behind her house.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是個熱愛探索屋後森林的冒險兒童。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They planned an adventurous journey through the Amazon rainforest.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們計劃了一次穿越亞馬遜雨林的冒險旅程。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has an adventurous spirit and is always looking for new challenges.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他有冒險精神，總是在尋找新的挑戰。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們計劃了一次穿越亞馬遜雨林的冒險旅程。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5021,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::advocate::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The lawyer served as an ____ for the defendant.","expectedAnswer":"advocate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The lawyer served as an ____ for the defendant.","clozeAnswer":"advocate","exampleTranslation":"該律師擔任了被告的辯護律師。","reference":{"eng":"advocate","kk":"ˈædvəˌkeɪt","tense":"n.","ch":"[['提倡者'], ['辯護律師'], ['支持者']]","chEntries":["提倡者","辯護律師","支持者"],"practiceMeaning":"該律師擔任了被告的辯護律師。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 advocare，意為「呼喚（給予支持）」。其中 ad- 為「靠近、朝向」的前綴，vocare 為「呼喚、說話」的動詞。透過 ad- 的「朝向」與 vocare 的「說話」，構成了「為某人說話、辯護」的核心概念。在名詞用法中，advocate 指的是「為某人或某事說話、辯護的人」，引申為「提倡者」或「辯護律師」。","definition":"1. a person who publicly supports or recommends a particular cause or policy; 2. a person who argues a case or gives advice on a legal subject in a court of law.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a strong advocate for animal rights.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是動物權利的一位堅定提倡者。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The lawyer served as an advocate for the defendant.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該律師擔任了被告的辯護律師。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該律師擔任了被告的辯護律師。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4508,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::after::prep","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He arrived shortly ____.","expectedAnswer":"after","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He arrived shortly ____.","clozeAnswer":"after","exampleTranslation":"他不久後就到了。","reference":{"eng":"after","kk":"/ˈæftər/","tense":"prep.","ch":"[['在...之後'], ['跟隨']]","chEntries":["在...之後","跟隨"],"practiceMeaning":"他不久後就到了。","analysis":"源自古英語 æfter。是一個表示時間、順序或位置的介詞。核心語意是「緊隨其後」。","definition":"1. At a time subsequent to (a particular event or time); 2. Following behind in order or position.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The meeting will be held after lunch.\",\n    \"ch\": \"會議將在午餐後舉行。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He arrived shortly after.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他不久後就到了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She always follows in her mother's footsteps.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她總是追隨她母親的腳步。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他不久後就到了。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5505,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l5::agency::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ reported a significant increase in tourism.","expectedAnswer":"agency","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ reported a significant increase in tourism.","clozeAnswer":"agency","exampleTranslation":"該旅遊局報告稱旅遊業顯著增長。","reference":{"eng":"agency","kk":"ˈeɪdʒənsi","tense":"n.","ch":"[['代理機構'], ['經紀公司'], ['情報機構'], ['作用'], ['效力'], ['媒介']]","chEntries":["代理機構","經紀公司","情報機構","作用","效力","媒介"],"practiceMeaning":"該旅遊局報告稱旅遊業顯著增長。","analysis":"此字由 'agent' 加上抽象名詞字尾 '-cy' 構成，表示『代理人的職位、權力或機構』。'-cy' 源自拉丁語 '-tia' 或 '-cia'，用於形成名詞，表示狀態、品質或職位。因此，'agency' 的核心語義是與 'agent' 相關的抽象概念或場所。從「代理權」延伸出「代理機構」（如旅行社、經紀公司），再引申為「情報機構」。此外，它也表示「起作用的能力」或「作用力」，強調的是「執行者」或「媒介物」所展現出的效力。","definition":"a business or organization that provides a particular service; the capacity to act or exert power; an organization that operates on behalf of another.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He signed with a talent agency.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他簽約了一家演藝經紀公司。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The agency reported a significant increase in tourism.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該旅遊局報告稱旅遊業顯著增長。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to understand the agency of the virus.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要了解這種病毒的作用。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該旅遊局報告稱旅遊業顯著增長。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6106,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::agenda::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They have their own political ____.","expectedAnswer":"agenda","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They have their own political ____.","clozeAnswer":"agenda","exampleTranslation":"他們有自己的政治議程。","reference":{"eng":"agenda","kk":"əˈdʒɛndə","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"議程\"  ],  [    \"待辦事項\"  ],  [    \"計劃\"  ],  [    \"潛藏目的\"  ]]","chEntries":["議程","待辦事項","計劃","潛藏目的"],"practiceMeaning":"他們有自己的政治議程。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 agenda，是動詞 agere（做；行動）的女性複數主格形式，意為「該做的事」。原為教務用語，指「應當處理的事項」。在現代英語中，agenda 主要指會議或討論的「議程」，即計劃要討論的事項列表。也可引申為某人或組織隱藏的「計劃」或「目的」，帶有負面含義。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆，應視為整體詞源演變。其語意演變是從「該做的事」到具體的「會議議程」，再到抽象的「計劃、目的」。","definition":"1. a list of things to be done or discussed at a meeting; 2. a set of principles or beliefs that guide someone's actions or a group's behavior; a hidden plan.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The first item on the agenda is the budget report.\",\n    \"ch\": \"議程上的第一項是預算報告。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They have their own political agenda.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們有自己的政治議程。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to set the agenda for tomorrow's meeting.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要擬定明天會議的議程。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們有自己的政治議程。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5686,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l9::alcohol::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Excessive consumption of ____ can be harmful.","expectedAnswer":"alcohol","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Excessive consumption of ____ can be harmful.","clozeAnswer":"alcohol","exampleTranslation":"過量飲酒會對身體有害。","reference":{"eng":"alcohol","kk":"ˈælkəhɒl","tense":"n.","ch":"[['酒精'], ['酒']]","chEntries":["酒精","酒"],"practiceMeaning":"過量飲酒會對身體有害。","analysis":"此字源自阿拉伯語 al-kuḥl，最初指一種細粉狀的化妝品（如眼影粉），後來指「純淨物」或「蒸餾物」，最終用於指代「乙醇」。'al-' 是阿拉伯語定冠詞「the」。'kuḥl' 源自古希臘語 kôlon，指「膽汁」，也可能與「蒸餾」過程相關。構詞上，此字是一個直接借詞，語意演變從「精細粉末」到「蒸餾物」，再專指「乙醇」。","definition":"a colorless volatile flammable liquid which is produced by the normal fermentation of sugars and is the intoxicating constituent of wine, beer, spirits and other drinks; an intoxicating liquor.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The drink contained a high percentage of alcohol.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這杯飲料含有高比例的酒精。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Excessive consumption of alcohol can be harmful.\",\n    \"ch\": \"過量飲酒會對身體有害。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"過量飲酒會對身體有害。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5687,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l9::alcoholic::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The effects of ____ beverages are well-known.","expectedAnswer":"alcoholic","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The effects of ____ beverages are well-known.","clozeAnswer":"alcoholic","exampleTranslation":"酒精飲料的影響是眾所周知的。","reference":{"eng":"alcoholic","kk":"ˌælkəˈhɒlɪk","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['酒精的'], ['患酒精中毒的'], ['酗酒的']]","chEntries":["酒精的","患酒精中毒的","酗酒的"],"practiceMeaning":"酒精飲料的影響是眾所周知的。","analysis":"此字由名詞 'alcohol' 加上形容詞化後綴 '-ic' 構成。'alcohol' 是阿拉伯語 al-kuḥl 的音譯。'-ic' 後綴用於將名詞轉化為形容詞，表示「與……有關的」或「具有……特性的」。因此，'alcoholic' 主要指「與酒精有關的」，包括「由酒精引起的」（如酒精中毒）或「與過量飲酒有關的」（如酗酒的）。","definition":"relating to or caused by alcohol; suffering from alcoholism.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has an alcoholic problem.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他有酗酒的問題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The effects of alcoholic beverages are well-known.\",\n    \"ch\": \"酒精飲料的影響是眾所周知的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"酒精飲料的影響是眾所周知的。","sourceName":"龍騰課本、字彙王","unitName":"L9、U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5454,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::all-in-all::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The food was a bit expensive, but ____, we had a good time.","expectedAnswer":"all in all","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The food was a bit expensive, but ____, we had a good time.","clozeAnswer":"all in all","exampleTranslation":"食物有點貴，但總體來說，我們玩得很開心。","reference":{"eng":"all in all","kk":"ɔːl ɪn ɔːl","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['總而言之'], ['總體來說']]","chEntries":["總而言之","總體來說"],"practiceMeaning":"食物有點貴，但總體來說，我們玩得很開心。","analysis":"此片語是一個慣用語，由不定代名詞 \"all\"，介系詞 \"in\"，以及不定代名詞 \"all\" 重複構成。其含義是考慮了所有相關因素後，對整體情況做出總結或判斷，與 \"as a whole\" 和 \"in conclusion\" 類似。","definition":"considering everything; taking everything into account.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"All in all, it was a successful event.\",\n    \"ch\": \"總而言之，這是一次成功的活動。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The food was a bit expensive, but all in all, we had a good time.\",\n    \"ch\": \"食物有點貴，但總體來說，我們玩得很開心。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"食物有點貴，但總體來說，我們玩得很開心。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4238,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::alley::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He emerged from the dark ____.","expectedAnswer":"alley","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He emerged from the dark ____.","clozeAnswer":"alley","exampleTranslation":"他從黑暗的小巷裡走出來。","reference":{"eng":"alley","kk":"/ˈæli/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['小巷'], ['弄']]","chEntries":["小巷","弄"],"practiceMeaning":"他從黑暗的小巷裡走出來。","analysis":"源自古法語 'ale', 'allee'，意為「走道、通道」。最初指「經過或走到某處的通道」，後來演變成狹窄的後街或小巷。詞源與「行走」的動作有關。","definition":"a narrow passage between buildings or houses","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The children played hide-and-seek in the narrow alley behind the shops.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子們躲在商店後面的狹窄小巷裡玩捉迷藏。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He emerged from the dark alley.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他從黑暗的小巷裡走出來。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他從黑暗的小巷裡走出來。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6153,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::alliance::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This ____ was strategic for both sides.","expectedAnswer":"alliance","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This ____ was strategic for both sides.","clozeAnswer":"alliance","exampleTranslation":"這個聯盟對雙方來說都是戰略性的。","reference":{"eng":"alliance","kk":"əˈlaɪəns","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"聯盟\"  ],  [    \"聯合\"  ],  [    \"結合\"  ],  [    \"姻親關係\"  ]]","chEntries":["聯盟","聯合","結合","姻親關係"],"practiceMeaning":"這個聯盟對雙方來說都是戰略性的。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 aliance「聯盟」，源自動詞 alier「聯合」，最終可追溯至拉丁語 alligare，意為「綁縛、聯合」，由 ad- (to) + ligare (to bind) 組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 ligare「綁縛」是其核心語意來源。作為名詞，其核心語義是兩個或多個實體（國家、組織、個人）基於共同目標或利益而形成的聯合或結合。詞源中的「綁縛」概念清晰地體現了聯盟的緊密聯繫。此義項由「聯合」的動作延伸出「聯盟」的狀態或組織。","definition":"1. a union or association formed for mutual benefit, especially between countries or organizations; 2. a close connection or relationship, especially one involving shared interests or goals; 3. a relationship by marriage between two families or groups.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The two countries formed a military alliance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"兩國組成了一個軍事聯盟。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This alliance was strategic for both sides.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個聯盟對雙方來說都是戰略性的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The alliance of their families was beneficial.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們家族之間的結合是有益的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A political alliance was formed to contest the election.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一個政治聯盟為了競選而成立。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個聯盟對雙方來說都是戰略性的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6206,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::allocate::vt","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need to ____ the tasks among the team members.","expectedAnswer":"allocate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need to ____ the tasks among the team members.","clozeAnswer":"allocate","exampleTranslation":"我們需要將任務分配給團隊成員。","reference":{"eng":"allocate","kk":"ˈæləkeɪt","tense":"vt.","ch":"[  [    \"分配\"  ],  [    \"撥款\"  ],  [    \"安置\"  ],  [    \"配置\"  ]]","chEntries":["分配","撥款","安置","配置"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要將任務分配給團隊成員。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 alloco，由 ad-（朝向）和 locus（地方）組合而成，意為「將某物安置到某個地方」或「分配到某個位置」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，應視為整體詞源演變。作及物動詞時，核心語義是用力將資源、職責或空間分配給特定的用途、人員或地點。此字常與介詞 to 或 for 連用，表示分配的對象。中文翻譯為「分配；撥款；安置；配置」。","definition":"1. to distribute resources, especially money, or to assign a task, job, or space to someone or something; 2. to put something in a particular place or position.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government decided to allocate more funds to education.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府決定撥更多款項給教育。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to allocate the tasks among the team members.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要將任務分配給團隊成員。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The architect allocated a small space for the balcony.\",\n    \"ch\": \"建築師為陽台分配了一個小空間。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要將任務分配給團隊成員。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4261,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::almond::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ milk is a popular dairy alternative.","expectedAnswer":"Almond","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ milk is a popular dairy alternative.","clozeAnswer":"Almond","exampleTranslation":"杏仁奶是一種流行的非乳製品替代品。","reference":{"eng":"almond","kk":"/ˈɑːmənd/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['杏仁']]","chEntries":["杏仁"],"practiceMeaning":"杏仁奶是一種流行的非乳製品替代品。","analysis":"源自古英語 'alemonde'，經過多種語言（如希臘語 'amygdale'）的演變，最終來自古地中海語。'Almond' 指一種堅果，也是一種樹。","definition":"a type of nut that has a hard shell and a soft kernel, eaten as food.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She enjoys a handful of almonds as a snack.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她喜歡抓一把杏仁當零食。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Almond milk is a popular dairy alternative.\",\n    \"ch\": \"杏仁奶是一種流行的非乳製品替代品。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"杏仁奶是一種流行的非乳製品替代品。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4574,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::alphabet::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He is still learning his ____.","expectedAnswer":"alphabet","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He is still learning his ____.","clozeAnswer":"alphabet","exampleTranslation":"他還在學習字母表。","reference":{"eng":"alphabet","kk":"/ˈælfəˌbɛt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['字母表']]","chEntries":["字母表"],"practiceMeaning":"他還在學習字母表。","analysis":"源自希臘語 'alphabētos'，由希臘字母表的前兩個字母 'alpha' (α) 和 'beta' (β) 組成。指一套用於書寫某種語言的符號系統。","definition":"1. a set of letters or symbols in a fixed order, used to represent the basic sounds of a language.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Can you recite the English alphabet?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你能背誦英文字母表嗎？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is still learning his alphabet.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他還在學習字母表。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他還在學習字母表。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3124,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::ambiguous::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His intentions were ____, making it hard to trust him.","expectedAnswer":"ambiguous","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His intentions were ____, making it hard to trust him.","clozeAnswer":"ambiguous","exampleTranslation":"他的意圖不明確，讓人難以信任他。","reference":{"eng":"ambiguous","kk":"/æmˈbɪɡjuəs/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['模棱兩可的；含糊不清的'], ['（意義、動機等）不明確的'], ['（事物）有歧義的']]","chEntries":["模棱兩可的","含糊不清的","不明確的","有歧義的"],"practiceMeaning":"他的意圖不明確，讓人難以信任他。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'ambiguus'，意為「不確定的，變換不定的」。'ambi-'（兩邊，周圍）+ 'agere'（行動，推動）。原意是「可以從兩邊走的」，引申為「不確定的」、「模棱兩可的」。形容詞 'ambiguous' 用來描述語言、指示、行為或情況，其意義不單一，可以有多種解釋，因而造成不確定或混淆。","definition":"1. open to more than one interpretation; having a double meaning; 2. unclear or inexact because a choice between alternative meanings has not been made; 3. (of a situation) not having one obvious meaning or outcome.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The politician gave an ambiguous answer to the reporter's question.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位政治家對記者的問題給出了模棱兩可的答案。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His intentions were ambiguous, making it hard to trust him.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的意圖不明確，讓人難以信任他。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The meaning of the poem is deliberately ambiguous.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這首詩的意義是刻意含糊不清的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他的意圖不明確，讓人難以信任他。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4093,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::an-elective-course::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This is ____ for students interested in filmmaking.","expectedAnswer":"an elective course","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This is ____ for students interested in filmmaking.","clozeAnswer":"an elective course","exampleTranslation":"這是為對電影製作感興趣的學生開設的選修課程。","reference":{"eng":"an elective course","kk":"/ən ɪˈlɛktɪv kɔrs/","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['選修課程']]","chEntries":["選修課程"],"practiceMeaning":"這是為對電影製作感興趣的學生開設的選修課程。","analysis":"'Elective' (選修的) 源自拉丁語 'electus' (chosen)，是 'elect' 的形容詞形式，指「可供選擇的」。'Course' (課程) 源自拉丁語 'cursus' (course, race)。'An elective course' 指學生可以自由選擇是否要學習的課程。","definition":"a course that a student can choose to study but is not required","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"她決定選修一門藝術史課程。\",\n    \"eng\": \"She decided to take an elective course in art history.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"這是為對電影製作感興趣的學生開設的選修課程。\",\n    \"eng\": \"This is an elective course for students interested in filmmaking.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是為對電影製作感興趣的學生開設的選修課程。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3960,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::an-immediate-response::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The government promised ____ to the disaster.","expectedAnswer":"an immediate response","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The government promised ____ to the disaster.","clozeAnswer":"an immediate response","exampleTranslation":"政府承諾對災難做出緊急回應。","reference":{"eng":"an immediate response","kk":"None","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['立即的回應']]","chEntries":["立即的回應"],"practiceMeaning":"政府承諾對災難做出緊急回應。","analysis":"不定冠詞 'an' 加上形容詞 'immediate' (立即的) 和名詞 'response' (回應)。表示迅速、毫不延遲的回應。","definition":"a reply or reaction that is given without any delay.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need an immediate response to the customer's complaint.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要立即回應顧客的投訴。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government promised an immediate response to the disaster.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府承諾對災難做出緊急回應。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"政府承諾對災難做出緊急回應。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5615,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l7::anniversary::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company is celebrating its 50th ____.","expectedAnswer":"anniversary","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company is celebrating its 50th ____.","clozeAnswer":"anniversary","exampleTranslation":"公司正在慶祝其成立五十週年。","reference":{"eng":"anniversary","kk":"ˌænəˈvɜrsəri","tense":"n.","ch":"[['週年紀念日'], ['紀念日']]","chEntries":["週年紀念日","紀念日"],"practiceMeaning":"公司正在慶祝其成立五十週年。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'anniversarius'，意為「一年一度的」，由 'annus'（年）和 'vertere'（轉動）組成，再加上形容詞化後綴 '-arius'。構詞學上，'ann-' 是「年」的詞根，'vers-'（來自 'vertere'）是「轉動」的詞根，'-ary' 是形容詞化後綴。組合起來意為「每年都會轉動的」或「一年輪迴一次的」。原始語意是「一年一度的事件」，引申為「週年紀念日」，指每年一次、紀念特定事件的日子。","definition":"1. The date on which an event took place in a previous year, or the celebration of this; 2. The yearly recurrence of a date marking a notable event.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Today is their wedding anniversary.\",\n    \"ch\": \"今天是他們的結婚週年紀念日。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company is celebrating its 50th anniversary.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司正在慶祝其成立五十週年。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"公司正在慶祝其成立五十週年。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4012,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u3::anxious::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He was ____ to start his new job.","expectedAnswer":"anxious","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He was ____ to start his new job.","clozeAnswer":"anxious","exampleTranslation":"他急切地想開始他的新工作。","reference":{"eng":"anxious","kk":"/ˈæŋkʃəs/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['焦慮的', '不安的'], ['渴望的', '急切的']]","chEntries":["焦慮的","不安的","渴望的","急切的"],"practiceMeaning":"他急切地想開始他的新工作。","analysis":"詞源：拉丁文 'anxius' (擔憂的)，源自 'angere' (使痛苦)。指因擔憂未來或未知情況而產生的不安感，也指對某事極度渴望。","definition":"1. feeling or showing worry about what may happen; 2. eager or desirous to do something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She was anxious about her upcoming exam.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對即將到來的考試感到焦慮。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was anxious to start his new job.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他急切地想開始他的新工作。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他急切地想開始他的新工作。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4135,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::appeal::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This music doesn't ____ to me.","expectedAnswer":"appeal","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This music doesn't ____ to me.","clozeAnswer":"appeal","exampleTranslation":"這種音樂對我沒有吸引力。","reference":{"eng":"appeal","kk":"/əˈpiːl/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['懇求', '呼籲'], ['（使）有吸引力', '對...有魅力'], ['上訴']]","chEntries":["懇求","呼籲","有吸引力","對...有魅力","上訴"],"practiceMeaning":"這種音樂對我沒有吸引力。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 appellare（向...呼籲，控告）。核心概念是「正式向某人請求」或「引起某人的興趣」。引申為向法院請求，或對某人產生吸引力。","definition":"1. make a serious or urgent or heartfelt request; 2. be attractive or interesting to; 3. take an application or request to a higher court for review","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police appealed for witnesses.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警方呼籲目擊者出面。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This music doesn't appeal to me.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種音樂對我沒有吸引力。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He decided to appeal the court's decision.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他決定就法院的判決提出上訴。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這種音樂對我沒有吸引力。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U5、L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5770,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::applause::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Her speech was met with thunderous ____.","expectedAnswer":"applause","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Her speech was met with thunderous ____.","clozeAnswer":"applause","exampleTranslation":"她的演講獲得了雷鳴般的掌聲。","reference":{"eng":"applause","kk":"əˈplɔz","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"掌聲\"  ],  [    \"讚賞\"  ],  [    \"喝采\"  ]]","chEntries":["掌聲","讚賞","喝采"],"practiceMeaning":"她的演講獲得了雷鳴般的掌聲。","analysis":"此字為名詞，源自中古英語 applaus，由拉丁語 applausus（讚許；喝采）而來，後者是動詞 applaud（鼓掌；讚美）的過去分詞。applaud來自拉丁語applaudere，由ad-（朝向；加強）+ plaudere（鼓掌；拍手）組成。plaudere本身可能與拉丁語plausus（拍擊；鼓掌）及希臘語plosion（爆發；撞擊）有關。因此，applause的核心語義是「因讚賞或喜愛而發出的拍手聲」，引申為「讚賞」或「喝采」。其語意演變是從具體的拍手動作發展到抽象的讚揚和認可。","definition":"1. the act of clapping your hands to show you have enjoyed a performance or someone has done well; 2. enthusiastic approval.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The audience gave the performers a standing ovation and loud applause.\",\n    \"ch\": \"觀眾起立鼓掌，給予表演者熱烈的掌聲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her speech was met with thunderous applause.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的演講獲得了雷鳴般的掌聲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We appreciate your applause and support.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們感謝您的讚賞與支持。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她的演講獲得了雷鳴般的掌聲。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5682,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l9::appointment::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"I have an ____ with the dentist at 3 PM.","expectedAnswer":"appointment","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"I have an ____ with the dentist at 3 PM.","clozeAnswer":"appointment","exampleTranslation":"我下午三點有一個牙醫的預約。","reference":{"eng":"appointment","kk":"əˈpɔɪntmənt","tense":"n.","ch":"[['任命'], ['委派'], ['職位'], ['約會'], ['預約']]","chEntries":["任命","委派","職位","約會","預約"],"practiceMeaning":"我下午三點有一個牙醫的預約。","analysis":"此字由動詞 'appoint' 加上名詞化後綴 '-ment' 構成。'appoint' 源自古法語 apointier（來自拉丁語 pungere，意為『刺，戳，使之明確』），核心語意是「明確指定」。'-ment' 後綴用於將動詞轉化為名詞，表示動作、狀態、結果或所產生的事物。因此，'appointment' 可以指「被任命的動作或結果」（任命、委派、職位），也可以指「被約定的動作或結果」（約會、預約）。語意上的區別體現在「對人」的指定（任命）與「對事」的指定（約會）上。","definition":"the act of appointing someone to a job or position; an arrangement to meet someone at a particular time and place; a job or position to which someone is appointed.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her appointment as CEO was controversial.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她被任命為執行長的決定備受爭議。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I have an appointment with the dentist at 3 PM.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我下午三點有一個牙醫的預約。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我下午三點有一個牙醫的預約。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5369,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l2::appropriate::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Please wear ____ attire for the formal event.","expectedAnswer":"appropriate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Please wear ____ attire for the formal event.","clozeAnswer":"appropriate","exampleTranslation":"請穿著適合正式場合的服裝。","reference":{"eng":"appropriate","kk":"əˈproʊpriɪt","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['適當的'], ['恰當的'], ['合適的']]","chEntries":["適當的","恰當的","合適的"],"practiceMeaning":"請穿著適合正式場合的服裝。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 appropriat，來自拉丁語 appropriatus，是動詞 'appropriare' (使屬於某人，佔有) 的過去分詞。'appropriare' 由 ad- (to) + proprius (one's own) 構成。核心概念是「屬於某人、符合某人所有」。因此，引申為「符合某目的、場合或標準」，即「適當的、恰當的」。","definition":"Suitable or proper in the circumstances.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is not the appropriate time to discuss such matters.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這不是討論這類事情的適當時機。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please wear appropriate attire for the formal event.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請穿著適合正式場合的服裝。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"請穿著適合正式場合的服裝。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5373,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l2::arch::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The rainbow formed a perfect ____ in the sky.","expectedAnswer":"arch","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The rainbow formed a perfect ____ in the sky.","clozeAnswer":"arch","exampleTranslation":"彩虹在天上形成了一個完美的拱形。","reference":{"eng":"arch","kk":"ɑːrtʃ","tense":"n.","ch":"[['拱門'], ['拱形'], ['拱狀結構']]","chEntries":["拱門","拱形","拱狀結構"],"practiceMeaning":"彩虹在天上形成了一個完美的拱形。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 arche，最終來自拉丁語 arcus，意為「弓、拱」。核心語意是「一種彎曲的結構，通常用於支撐上方重量或形成開口」。在建築中，拱門是最常見的應用。引申語意包括「拱形」本身，或任何類似拱形的結構。","definition":"1. a curved symmetrical structure spanning an opening and typically supporting the weight of a bridge, roof, or wall; 2. a structure like an arch, especially one that frames a doorway or opening.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The old church had a beautiful stone arch.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座古老的教堂有一個美麗的石拱門。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The rainbow formed a perfect arch in the sky.\",\n    \"ch\": \"彩虹在天上形成了一個完美的拱形。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"彩虹在天上形成了一個完美的拱形。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5372,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l2::arched::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Her eyebrows were neatly ____.","expectedAnswer":"arched","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Her eyebrows were neatly ____.","clozeAnswer":"arched","exampleTranslation":"她的眉毛被整齊地畫成了弓形。","reference":{"eng":"arched","kk":"ɑːrtʃt","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['拱形的'], ['有拱門的']]","chEntries":["拱形的","有拱門的"],"practiceMeaning":"她的眉毛被整齊地畫成了弓形。","analysis":"此字是名詞 'arch' (拱門) 的過去分詞 'arched' 用作形容詞。'arch' 源自古法語 arche，來自拉丁語 arcus，意為「弓、拱」。核心語意是「彎曲的線條，形成一個向上或向外的弧形」。因此，'arched' 形容事物「呈現拱形」的狀態。","definition":"Having the form of an arch.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The bridge had a series of arched spans.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座橋有一系列的拱形跨度。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her eyebrows were neatly arched.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的眉毛被整齊地畫成了弓形。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她的眉毛被整齊地畫成了弓形。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5509,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l5::arrest::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of the fugitive brought the operation to an end.","expectedAnswer":"arrest","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of the fugitive brought the operation to an end.","clozeAnswer":"arrest","exampleTranslation":"對逃犯的逮捕行動為此次行動劃上了句號。","reference":{"eng":"arrest","kk":"əˈrest","tense":"n.","ch":"[['逮捕'], ['拘留'], ['制止']]","chEntries":["逮捕","拘留","制止"],"practiceMeaning":"對逃犯的逮捕行動為此次行動劃上了句號。","analysis":"此為動詞 'arrest' 的名詞形式。作為名詞，它指「逮捕」的行為或事件，或者「阻止」的動作。構詞與語意演變與動詞一致，承襲了「使停止」的核心概念。","definition":"the act of arresting someone; the state of being stopped or checked.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There have been several arrests in connection with the robbery.\",\n    \"ch\": \"與這次搶劫案有關的逮捕行動已有數起。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The arrest of the fugitive brought the operation to an end.\",\n    \"ch\": \"對逃犯的逮捕行動為此次行動劃上了句號。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"對逃犯的逮捕行動為此次行動劃上了句號。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5453,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::as-a-whole::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The country, ____, is experiencing economic recovery.","expectedAnswer":"as a whole","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The country, ____, is experiencing economic recovery.","clozeAnswer":"as a whole","exampleTranslation":"整個國家正在經歷經濟復甦。","reference":{"eng":"as a whole","kk":"æz ə hoʊl","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['總體而言'], ['整體來說']]","chEntries":["總體而言","整體來說"],"practiceMeaning":"整個國家正在經歷經濟復甦。","analysis":"此片語由介系詞 \"as\" (如同)，不定冠詞 \"a\"，以及形容詞 \"whole\" (整個的) 組成。\"whole\" 源自古英語 \"hāl\"。此片語意指將事物視為一個單一、不可分割的整體來考量，強調其整體性而非個別部分。","definition":"considering everything or everyone as a single unit; on the whole.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"As a whole, the team performed well.\",\n    \"ch\": \"總體而言，這支隊伍表現不錯。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The country, as a whole, is experiencing economic recovery.\",\n    \"ch\": \"整個國家正在經歷經濟復甦。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"整個國家正在經歷經濟復甦。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4141,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::aside::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Let's set this problem ____ for now.","expectedAnswer":"aside","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Let's set this problem ____ for now.","clozeAnswer":"aside","exampleTranslation":"我們暫時把這個問題擱置一邊。","reference":{"eng":"aside","kk":"/əˈsaɪd/","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['在一旁', '到旁邊'], ['（暫時）擱置', '另外']]","chEntries":["在一旁","到旁邊","擱置","另外"],"practiceMeaning":"我們暫時把這個問題擱置一邊。","analysis":"由 a-（介詞）+ side（邊）組成。核心概念是「在邊緣位置」或「與主要事物分開」。","definition":"1. on or to one side; 2. out of the way; 3. separately, or to one side, from what is being done or considered","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He put the book aside.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他把書放在一旁。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Let's set this problem aside for now.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們暫時把這個問題擱置一邊。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She stepped aside to let him pass.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她往旁邊一讓，讓他通過。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們暫時把這個問題擱置一邊。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3125,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::assemble::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The students will ____ in the auditorium for the assembly.","expectedAnswer":"assemble","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The students will ____ in the auditorium for the assembly.","clozeAnswer":"assemble","exampleTranslation":"學生們將在禮堂集合參加集會。","reference":{"eng":"assemble","kk":"/əˈsɛmbl/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['組裝；裝配'], ['集合；聚集']]","chEntries":["組裝","裝配","集合","聚集"],"practiceMeaning":"學生們將在禮堂集合參加集會。","analysis":"詞源來自古法語 'assembler'，意為「聚集，集合」，由 'as-'（朝向）+ 'sembler'（聚集，類似）。'sembler' 又來自拉丁語 'simulare'（模仿，使其相似），最終源於 'similis'（相似的）。最初指將相似或相關的事物聚集在一起，引申為將零件組裝成一個整體，或將人聚集在一起。動詞 'assemble' 涵蓋了將分散的部分變成一個完整單位的概念，無論是物理上的組裝還是人員的聚集。","definition":"1. to bring together or come together in one place for a common purpose; 2. to fit together the separate component parts of (a machine or other object).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to assemble all the furniture before the guests arrive.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要在客人到達前組裝好所有家具。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The students will assemble in the auditorium for the assembly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"學生們將在禮堂集合參加集會。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The engineers assembled the prototype car in just two weeks.\",\n    \"ch\": \"工程師們僅用了兩週就組裝好了原型車。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"學生們將在禮堂集合參加集會。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3126,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::assembly::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The final ____ of the aircraft takes several weeks.","expectedAnswer":"assembly","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The final ____ of the aircraft takes several weeks.","clozeAnswer":"assembly","exampleTranslation":"這架飛機的最終組裝需要數週時間。","reference":{"eng":"assembly","kk":"/əˈsɛmblɪ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['集會；集會場所'], ['組裝；裝配'], ['（尤指公司、組織的）大會；議會']]","chEntries":["集會","集會場所","組裝","裝配","大會","議會"],"practiceMeaning":"這架飛機的最終組裝需要數週時間。","analysis":"名詞，源自動詞 'assemble'。第一個核心意義是「集合」，指一群人為了特定目的聚集在一起，這可以是正式的（如會議、議會）或非正式的。第二個核心意義是「組裝」，指將零件組合起來的過程或結果。'Assembly' 強調的是『聚集』或『組成』的動作或狀態。","definition":"1. a group of people gathered together in one place for a common purpose; 2. the action of assembling a piece of equipment or a machine; 3. a legislative body.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The school holds an assembly every Monday morning.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這所學校每週一早上都會舉行集會。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The final assembly of the aircraft takes several weeks.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這架飛機的最終組裝需要數週時間。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The general assembly of the United Nations meets annually.\",\n    \"ch\": \"聯合國大會每年都會召開。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這架飛機的最終組裝需要數週時間。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3060,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::associate::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He started his career as a junior ____ in a law firm.","expectedAnswer":"associate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He started his career as a junior ____ in a law firm.","clozeAnswer":"associate","exampleTranslation":"他最初是一家律師事務所的初級助理。","reference":{"eng":"associate","kk":"/əˈsoʊʃiət/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['同事；夥伴'], ['副手；助理']]","chEntries":["同事","夥伴","副手","助理"],"practiceMeaning":"他最初是一家律師事務所的初級助理。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'associatus'，'ad-' (to, toward) + 'sociatus' (companion)。指與某人或組織有連結、合作關係的人。\n1. 同事；夥伴：指在同一公司、組織或共同目標下工作的人。\n2. 副手；助理：在特定職位上，協助較高級別人員工作的人。","definition":"1. a person who works with or is connected with someone else in a profession or business; 2. a person who is on the same team, in the same group, or in partnership with someone.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is an associate professor at the university.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是大學的副教授。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He started his career as a junior associate in a law firm.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他最初是一家律師事務所的初級助理。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他最初是一家律師事務所的初級助理。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4291,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::at-first-glance::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The house looked ordinary ____, but it had many hidden features.","expectedAnswer":"at first glance","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The house looked ordinary ____, but it had many hidden features.","clozeAnswer":"at first glance","exampleTranslation":"這棟房子乍一看很普通，但它有很多隱藏的特色。","reference":{"eng":"at first glance","kk":"/æt fɜːrst ˈɡlæns/","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['乍一看'], ['第一眼看去']]","chEntries":["乍一看","第一眼看去"],"practiceMeaning":"這棟房子乍一看很普通，但它有很多隱藏的特色。","analysis":"由介詞 'at'、名詞 'first'（第一）和名詞 'glance'（一瞥）組成。'At first glance' 意為「僅僅從第一次、簡短的觀察來看」，強調初步印象，可能與實際情況有所不同。","definition":"from the first look; seemingly.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"At first glance, the task seemed impossible.\",\n    \"ch\": \"乍一看，這項任務似乎是不可能的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The house looked ordinary at first glance, but it had many hidden features.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這棟房子乍一看很普通，但它有很多隱藏的特色。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這棟房子乍一看很普通，但它有很多隱藏的特色。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4237,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::attractive::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The new marketing campaign is designed to be ____ to young consumers.","expectedAnswer":"attractive","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The new marketing campaign is designed to be ____ to young consumers.","clozeAnswer":"attractive","exampleTranslation":"新的行銷活動旨在吸引年輕消費者。","reference":{"eng":"attractive","kk":"/əˈtræktɪv/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['吸引人的'], ['有魅力的']]","chEntries":["吸引人的","有魅力的"],"practiceMeaning":"新的行銷活動旨在吸引年輕消費者。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'attrahere'（吸引），由 'ad-'（朝向）+ 'trahere'（拉）組成。'Attractive' 意指能夠吸引人注意或喜愛。此詞語根 'tract' 意為「拉、拖」，延伸出「吸引」的意義。","definition":"pleasing or appealing to the senses; having the power to attract","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She found the candidate's proposals very attractive.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她覺得該候選人的提議非常有吸引力。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The new marketing campaign is designed to be attractive to young consumers.\",\n    \"ch\": \"新的行銷活動旨在吸引年輕消費者。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"新的行銷活動旨在吸引年輕消費者。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4001,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u3::audience::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He had a private ____ with the Pope.","expectedAnswer":"audience","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He had a private ____ with the Pope.","clozeAnswer":"audience","exampleTranslation":"他有機會私下謁見教宗。","reference":{"eng":"audience","kk":"/ˈɔːdiəns/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['聽眾', '觀眾'], ['（謁見）謁見']]","chEntries":["聽眾","觀眾","謁見"],"practiceMeaning":"他有機會私下謁見教宗。","analysis":"詞源：拉丁文 'audientia' (聽)，源自 'audire' (聽)。指聽眾或觀眾，也指覲見權貴的場合。","definition":"1. the assembled spectators or listeners at a public event, such as a play, concert, or meeting; 2. an interview given by a person in authority.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The audience applauded enthusiastically.\",\n    \"ch\": \"觀眾熱烈鼓掌。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He had a private audience with the Pope.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他有機會私下謁見教宗。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他有機會私下謁見教宗。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4040,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::aware::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She was keenly ____ of his discomfort.","expectedAnswer":"aware","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She was keenly ____ of his discomfort.","clozeAnswer":"aware","exampleTranslation":"她敏銳地察覺到他的不適。","reference":{"eng":"aware","kk":"/əˈwɛr/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['意識到的', '知道的'], ['明白的', '察覺到的']]","chEntries":["意識到的","知道的","明白的","察覺到的"],"practiceMeaning":"她敏銳地察覺到他的不適。","analysis":"源自古英語 'gewaer'，由 'ge-' (a past participle prefix) + 'wær' (aware) 構成。'wær' 本身與 'watch' 有關。核心概念是「看到」、「注意」，引申為「意識到」、「知道」或「察覺到」。","definition":"1. knowing or realizing that something is happening or that something exists; 2. having knowledge or understanding","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"你意識到其中存在的危險了嗎？\",\n    \"eng\": \"Are you aware of the dangers involved?\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"她敏銳地察覺到他的不適。\",\n    \"eng\": \"She was keenly aware of his discomfort.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他並不了解事實。\",\n    \"eng\": \"He is not aware of the facts.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她敏銳地察覺到他的不適。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5024,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::awe::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We looked in ____ at the magnificent view.","expectedAnswer":"awe","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We looked in ____ at the magnificent view.","clozeAnswer":"awe","exampleTranslation":"我們驚嘆地看著壯麗的景色。","reference":{"eng":"awe","kk":"ɔː","tense":"n.","ch":"[['敬畏'], ['驚嘆'], ['敬畏感']]","chEntries":["敬畏","驚嘆","敬畏感"],"practiceMeaning":"我們驚嘆地看著壯麗的景色。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 ege，意為「恐懼、敬畏」。與現代德語 Ehrfurcht（敬畏）同源。其語意核心為一種強烈的、帶有恐懼感的驚嘆，通常是對超乎尋常、強大或神聖的事物產生的反應。在現代英語中，awe 仍然保留了這種「既敬又畏」的語意，但恐懼成分有所減弱，更多強調「驚嘆、崇敬」。","definition":"a feeling of reverential respect mixed with fear or wonder.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The vastness of the desert filled him with awe.\",\n    \"ch\": \"沙漠的廣袤讓他充滿敬畏。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We looked in awe at the magnificent view.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們驚嘆地看著壯麗的景色。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們驚嘆地看著壯麗的景色。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5359,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l1::back-and-forth::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They argued ____ for hours.","expectedAnswer":"back and forth","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They argued ____ for hours.","clozeAnswer":"back and forth","exampleTranslation":"他們爭論了好幾個小時。","reference":{"eng":"back and forth","kk":"ˌbæk ən ˈfɔːrθ","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['來來回回'], ['來回地'], ['前後地']]","chEntries":["來來回回","來回地","前後地"],"practiceMeaning":"他們爭論了好幾個小時。","analysis":"此片語由 back（後退）和 forth（往前）組合而成，直接描述了來回移動或方向的變換。back- 和 forth- 都是副詞，共同強調了在兩個方向之間的持續運動。常用來形容物體或人的移動方式，或抽象概念的拉鋸。","definition":"moving from one place to another and in again; repeatedly in opposite directions.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The pendulum swung back and forth.\",\n    \"ch\": \"鐘擺來回擺動。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They argued back and forth for hours.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們爭論了好幾個小時。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們爭論了好幾個小時。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4126,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::background::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She has a strong academic ____.","expectedAnswer":"background","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She has a strong academic ____.","clozeAnswe