n betrayed his fear.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他緊張的表情暴露了他的恐懼。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"不要辜負我的信任。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4175,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::between::prep","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She sat ____ her parents.","expectedAnswer":"between","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She sat ____ her parents.","clozeAnswer":"between","exampleTranslation":"她坐在父母之間。","reference":{"eng":"between","kk":"/bɪˈtwiːn/","tense":"prep.","ch":"[['在...之間']]","chEntries":["在...之間"],"practiceMeaning":"她坐在父母之間。","analysis":"源自古英語 betwēonan（在兩者之間）。核心概念是「位於兩個點、區域或事物的中間」。","definition":"1. in or into the space separating (two points, objects, etc.); 2. intermediate to (two points, limits, etc.); 3. in relation to (two or more people or things) considered together","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There is a significant difference between A and B.\",\n    \"ch\": \"A 和 B 之間存在顯著的差異。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She sat between her parents.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她坐在父母之間。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The agreement is between the two countries.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這項協議是在兩國之間達成的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她坐在父母之間。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5824,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::blur::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Tears made his vision a ____.","expectedAnswer":"blur","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Tears made his vision a ____.","clozeAnswer":"blur","exampleTranslation":"淚水使他的視線變得模糊。","reference":{"eng":"blur","kk":"blər","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"模糊不清\"  ],  [    \"污點\"  ],  [    \"模糊的影像\"  ],  [    \"渾淆不清的狀態\"  ]]","chEntries":["模糊不清","污點","模糊的影像","渾淆不清的狀態"],"practiceMeaning":"淚水使他的視線變得模糊。","analysis":"此字詞源不明，可能與「模糊」的聲音或視覺有關。字義的演變傾向於指代一種不清晰、不確定的視覺或狀態。'Blur' 作名詞時，指一個不清晰的影像、一個模糊的區域，或一種混淆的狀態，使其難以分辨。這種不清晰感可能是由於移動、距離、視覺障礙或概念上的混淆所致。它描述了一種「失去清晰邊界」或「失去準確性」的狀態。例如，有時也指「一種使人興奮或眼花繚亂的迅速變化」。","definition":"1. A thing that is seen or heard indistinctly.; 2. A smudge or stain.; 3. A confused or disordered state.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The city lights were a blur in the distance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"城市燈火在遠方是一片模糊。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Tears made his vision a blur.\",\n    \"ch\": \"淚水使他的視線變得模糊。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The memory of that day is just a blur.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那天的記憶只是一片模糊。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The past few weeks have been a blur of activity.\",\n    \"ch\": \"過去幾周是一段忙碌到眼花繚亂的時期。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"淚水使他的視線變得模糊。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6157,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::blush::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He could not hide his ____.","expectedAnswer":"blush","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He could not hide his ____.","clozeAnswer":"blush","exampleTranslation":"他無法掩飾自己的臉紅。","reference":{"eng":"blush","kk":"blʌʃ","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"臉紅\"  ],  [    \"羞紅\"  ],  [    \"羞愧\"  ]]","chEntries":["臉紅","羞紅","羞愧"],"practiceMeaning":"他無法掩飾自己的臉紅。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 blyscan、blioxidan，意為「發紅、臉紅」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，應視為整體詞源演變。作為名詞，是動詞 blush「臉紅」的衍生物。其核心語義是因害羞、尷尬或羞愧而臉部皮膚變紅的現象或表情。","definition":"1. a reddening of the face, especially from embarrassment or shame.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A slight blush spread across her cheeks.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一抹淡淡的紅暈爬上她的臉頰。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He could not hide his blush.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他無法掩飾自己的臉紅。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The teacher noticed the student's blush.\",\n    \"ch\": \"老師注意到了學生的臉紅。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他無法掩飾自己的臉紅。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5028,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::boost::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This is a real ____ for our team's morale.","expectedAnswer":"boost","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This is a real ____ for our team's morale.","clozeAnswer":"boost","exampleTranslation":"這對我們隊伍的士氣是個真正的鼓舞。","reference":{"eng":"boost","kk":"buːst","tense":"n.","ch":"[['提升'], ['促進'], ['推動（尤指一次性的）']]","chEntries":["提升","促進","推動"],"practiceMeaning":"這對我們隊伍的士氣是個真正的鼓舞。","analysis":"此字來源不確定，可能與低地德語 bost（隆起）或荷蘭語 botsen（碰撞）有關。現代意義的 boost，尤其是在 18 世紀後期出現，意為「推、頂、抬高」，引申為「促進、增加」。此名詞用法表示「一次顯著的提升或促進」，強調的是其積極的作用。OCR 掃描時可能將 'o' 誤判為 '0'，或將 'st' 誤判。此處修正為 boost，其語意為「一次性的促進或提升」。","definition":"1. a rise or increase, typically one that is significant or dramatic; 2. an act of helping or encouraging someone or something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The new policy provided a boost to the economy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"新政策為經濟提供了促進。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a real boost for our team's morale.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這對我們隊伍的士氣是個真正的鼓舞。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這對我們隊伍的士氣是個真正的鼓舞。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4047,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::bowling::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He is a professional ____ player.","expectedAnswer":"bowling","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He is a professional ____ player.","clozeAnswer":"bowling","exampleTranslation":"他是一位職業保齡球選手。","reference":{"eng":"bowling","kk":"/ˈboʊlɪŋ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['保齡球運動']]","chEntries":["保齡球運動"],"practiceMeaning":"他是一位職業保齡球選手。","analysis":"源自動詞 'bowl'，指「滾動」（球）。'bowl' 一詞的詞源較為複雜，可能與古英語 'boll' (a ball) 有關。'bowling' 作為名詞，特指一種滾動球的運動，即保齡球。","definition":"the sport or activity of rolling a ball down a lane to knock over ten pins","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"我們上週六去打了保齡球。\",\n    \"eng\": \"We went bowling last Saturday.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他是一位職業保齡球選手。\",\n    \"eng\": \"He is a professional bowling player.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他是一位職業保齡球選手。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4214,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::branch::n","mode":"cloze_en",