dRef":"字彙王::u62::debut::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The band's ____ album was a huge success.","expectedAnswer":"debut","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The band's ____ album was a huge success.","clozeAnswer":"debut","exampleTranslation":"該樂團的首張專輯取得了巨大成功。","reference":{"eng":"debut","kk":"ˈdeɪbjuː","tense":"n.","ch":"[['首次亮相'], ['初次登場'], ['首次演出']]","chEntries":["首次亮相","初次登場","首次演出"],"practiceMeaning":"該樂團的首張專輯取得了巨大成功。","analysis":"此字源自法語 début，意為「開始、開端」，來自 débuter（開始、首次登場）。débuter 本身是法語中表示「開始」的動詞。核心語意是「第一次公開露面或表演」，常用於演藝界、體育界或時尚界。","definition":"a person's first appearance or performance in public, in a particular role or capacity; the first of a series of performances of a show.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The young actress made her debut on Broadway.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位年輕女演員在百老匯首次亮相。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The band's debut album was a huge success.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該樂團的首張專輯取得了巨大成功。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該樂團的首張專輯取得了巨大成功。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U62"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5292,"wordRef":"字彙王::u63::deceive::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Don't let them ____ you.","expectedAnswer":"deceive","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Don't let them ____ you.","clozeAnswer":"deceive","exampleTranslation":"別讓他們欺騙了你。","reference":{"eng":"deceive","kk":"dɪˈsiːv","tense":"v.","ch":"[['欺騙', '騙取']]","chEntries":["欺騙","騙取"],"practiceMeaning":"別讓他們欺騙了你。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'decipere'，由 'de-'（down, away）和 'capere'（to take）組成。構詞上，'de-' 作為否定或錯誤前綴，'capere' 是詞根，'-ere' 是動詞後綴。原始語義為「向下拿取」，引申為「欺騙、使受騙」。'deceive' 強調通過虛假信息或行為來誤導他人，使其相信不真實的事物。","definition":"to deliberately cause someone to believe something that is not true, especially for the gain of the deceiver.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He tried to deceive the public with false promises.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他試圖用虛假的承諾來欺騙公眾。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Don't let them deceive you.\",\n    \"ch\": \"別讓他們欺騙了你。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"別讓他們欺騙了你。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U63"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5640,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l8::decline::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The country experienced an economic ____.","expectedAnswer":"decline","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The country experienced an economic ____.","clozeAnswer":"decline","exampleTranslation":"這個國家經歷了經濟衰退。","reference":{"eng":"decline","kk":"dɪˈklaɪn","tense":"n.","ch":"[['下降'], ['衰退'], ['減少']]","chEntries":["下降","衰退","減少"],"practiceMeaning":"這個國家經歷了經濟衰退。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 declinen，來自拉丁語 declinare，由 de-（向下，away）+ clinare（彎曲，to bend）組成。clinare 來自原始印歐語 *klei-（傾斜；依偎）。因此，decline 的核心語義是「向下彎曲」或「轉向」。從物理的「向下」延伸至抽象的「減少」、「衰退」。此處為名詞用法，指代「下降」、「衰退」或「減少」的現象或趨勢。構詞上，de- 表達「向下」或「遠離」，clinare 提供「彎曲」或「傾斜」的核心動作。","definition":"a downward movement or trend; a decrease in quantity or quality; a deterioration.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We observed a sharp decline in sales.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們觀察到銷售額急劇下降。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The country experienced an economic decline.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個國家經歷了經濟衰退。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個國家經歷了經濟衰退。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4349,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::decrease::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We observed a significant ____ in temperature.","expectedAnswer":"decrease","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We observed a significant ____ in temperature.","clozeAnswer":"decrease","exampleTranslation":"我們觀察到氣溫顯著下降。","reference":{"eng":"decrease","kk":"/ˈdiːkriːs/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['減少；降低']]","chEntries":["減少","降低"],"practiceMeaning":"我們觀察到氣溫顯著下降。","analysis":"名詞形式，源自動詞 'decrease'，指『減少的數量或程度』，與『增加』相對。","definition":"a reduction in the size, amount, or number of something","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There has been a decrease in violent crime.\",\n    \"ch\": \"暴力犯罪有所減少。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We observed a significant decrease in temperature.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們觀察到氣溫顯著下降。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The decrease in demand led to lower prices.\",\n    \"ch\": \"需求的減少導致價格下跌。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們觀察到氣溫顯著下降。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4686,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::deed::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The heroic ____ of the firefighters saved many lives.","expectedAnswer":"deed","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The heroic ____ of the firefighters saved many lives.","clozeAnswer":"deed","exampleTranslation":"消防員的英勇事蹟拯救了許多生命。","reference":{"eng":"deed","kk":"/ˈdid/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['行為'], ['事蹟'], ['（法律）契據']]","chEntries":["行為","事蹟","契據"],"practiceMeaning":"消防員的英勇事蹟拯救了許多生命。","analysis":"源自古英語 *dēd*，與 'do'（做）同源。核心是「做出來的事情」。引申至具有重要性或價值的事蹟，以及法律上證明財產權的書面文件。","definition":"1. An action that is done. 2. An act or achievement, especially one that is brave or worthy of admiration. 3. A legal document that transfers ownership of property from one person to another.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His good deed was recognized by the community.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他這個善舉得到了社區的認可。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The heroic deed of the firefighters saved many lives.\",\n    \"ch\": \"消防員的英勇事蹟拯救了許多生命。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He signed the deed to the house.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他簽署了房子的契據。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"消防員的英勇事蹟拯救了許多生命。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6069,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::deficit::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There is a ____ of skilled workers in the industry.","expectedAnswer":"deficit","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There is a ____ of skilled workers in the industry.","clozeAnswer":"deficit","exampleTranslation":"這個行業缺乏技術工人。","reference":{"eng":"deficit","kk":"ˈdɛfɪsɪt","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"赤字\"  ],  [    \"虧損\"  ],  [    \"不足額\"  ],  [    \"缺陷\"  ]]","chEntries":["赤字","虧損","不足額","缺陷"],"practiceMeaning":"這個行業缺乏技術工人。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 deficit，是 deficere（to be wanting, to fail）的第三人稱單數現在時形式，由 de-（down, away）和 facere（to make, to do）組成。核心語義是「缺少」或「不足」。在經濟和財政領域，deficit 通常指「赤字」，即支出超過收入的金額。它也可以指在其他方面，如人才、資源上的「不足」。","definition":"1. the amount by which something, especially a sum of money, is too small; 2. a shortfall or lack.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The country is facing a significant budget deficit.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該國正面臨嚴重的預算赤字。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There is a deficit of skilled workers in the industry.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個行業缺乏技術工人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company reported a net deficit for the third quarter.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司報告第三季度出現淨虧損。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個行業缺乏技術工人。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6073,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::delegation::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ will meet with government officials tomorrow.","expectedAnswer":"delegation","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ will meet with government officials tomorrow.","clozeAnswer":"delegation","exampleTranslation":"代表團將於明天與政府官員會面。","reference":{"eng":"delegation","kk":"ˌdɛləˈɡeɪʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"代表團\"  ],  [    \"授權\"  ],  [    \"委派\"  ]]","chEntries":["代表團","授權","委派"],"practiceMeaning":"代表團將於明天與政府官員會面。","analysis":"此字由 delegate（委派）加上名詞後綴 -ion（表示動作或狀態）構成。Delegate 源自拉丁語 delegare，意為「委派」。Delegation 的核心語義是「委派」這個動作或「被委派的人群」。作為名詞，它可以指一個由被委派的代表組成的「代表團」，也可以指「授權」或「委派」本身這個行為。","definition":"1. a group of people sent or authorized to represent others, in particular, government representatives; 2. the action of delegating a task or responsibility.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A large delegation of business leaders visited the country.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一個龐大的商業領袖代表團訪問了該國。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The delegation will meet with government officials tomorrow.\",\n    \"ch\": \"代表團將於明天與政府官員會面。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The process of delegation requires trust and clear communication.\",\n    \"ch\": \"授權過程需要信任和清晰的溝通。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"代表團將於明天與政府官員會面。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6165,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::deliberate::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The committee will ____ on the proposal.","expectedAnswer":"deliberate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The committee will ____ on the proposal.","clozeAnswer":"deliberate","exampleTranslation":"委員會將仔細考慮這項提案。","reference":{"eng":"deliberate","kk":"dɪˈlɪbərət","tense":"v.","ch":"[  [    \"仔細考慮\"  ],  [    \"商議\"  ],  [    \"權衡\"  ]]","chEntries":["仔細考慮","商議","權衡"],"practiceMeaning":"委員會將仔細考慮這項提案。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 dēlīberāre「仔細考慮、權衡」，由 de- (down, completely) + lībra (balance, scale) 組成，意為「權衡、仔細考慮」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 de-「完全」和 lībra「秤」是其核心語意來源。作為動詞，其核心語義是「仔細地、持續地思考某事，以做出決定」。詞源中的「權衡」概念是其核心。此動詞義是該字的最早用法，其形容詞和名詞形式都由此衍生。","definition":"1. engage in long and careful consideration; 2. to discuss or consider something carefully.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They deliberated for hours before reaching a verdict.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們商議了數小時才達成判決。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The committee will deliberate on the proposal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"委員會將仔細考慮這項提案。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He deliberated on the best course of action.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他權衡了最佳的行動方案。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The jury deliberated in secret.\",\n    \"ch\": \"陪審團秘密商議。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"委員會將仔細考慮這項提案。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5614,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l7::democracy::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The transition to ____ was difficult but ultimately successful.","expectedAnswer":"democracy","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The transition to ____ was difficult but ultimately successful.","clozeAnswer":"democracy","exampleTranslation":"向民主制度的轉變雖然艱難，但最終是成功的。","reference":{"eng":"democracy","kk":"dəˈmɑkrəsi","tense":"n.","ch":"[['民主'], ['民主制度'], ['民主國家']]","chEntries":["民主","民主制度","民主國家"],"practiceMeaning":"向民主制度的轉變雖然艱難，但最終是成功的。","analysis":"此字源自希臘語 'dēmokratía' (δημοκρατία)，意為「人民統治」，由 'dēmos'（人民）和 'kratos'（權力、統治）組成，加上名詞化後綴 '-ia'。構詞學上，'dēmo-' 是「人民」的詞根，'-krat-' 是「權力」或「統治」的詞根，'-cy'（來自 '-ia'）是表示「狀態」、「政府」或「制度」的名詞化後綴。原始語意是「人民的統治」。現代意義指一種由人民透過直接或間接方式掌握政治權力的政府形式或社會制度。","definition":"1. Government by the people, especially rule of the majority, either directly or through elected representatives; 2. A state or society characterized by such government.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Many countries around the world strive for democracy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"世界各國許多國家都在努力爭取民主。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The transition to democracy was difficult but ultimately successful.\",\n    \"ch\": \"向民主制度的轉變雖然艱難，但最終是成功的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"向民主制度的轉變雖然艱難，但最終是成功的。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4143,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::democratic::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The organization is run on ____ principles.","expectedAnswer":"democratic","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The organization is run on ____ principles.","clozeAnswer":"democratic","exampleTranslation":"這個組織依照民主原則運作。","reference":{"eng":"democratic","kk":"/ˌdɛməˈkrætɪk/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['民主的']]","chEntries":["民主的"],"practiceMeaning":"這個組織依照民主原則運作。","analysis":"源自 democracy（民主），democracy 源自希臘語 dēmos（人民）+ kratos（統治）。核心概念是「人民統治」或「支持民主原則」。","definition":"1. relating to or supporting democracy or its principles; 2. (of a country or system of government) controlled by or having elected representatives elected by the people","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They live in a democratic society.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們生活在一個民主社會。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The organization is run on democratic principles.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個組織依照民主原則運作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a staunch supporter of democratic ideals.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是民主理想的堅定支持者。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個組織依照民主原則運作。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U5、L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5458,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::depend-on::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Children often ____ their parents for support.","expectedAnswer":"depend on","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Children often ____ their parents for support.","clozeAnswer":"depend on","exampleTranslation":"孩子們經常依靠父母的支持。","reference":{"eng":"depend on","kk":"dɪˈpend ɒn","tense":"v.","ch":"[['依賴'], ['依靠'], ['取決於']]","chEntries":["依賴","依靠","取決於"],"practiceMeaning":"孩子們經常依靠父母的支持。","analysis":"此片語由動詞 \"depend\" (依賴) 和介系詞 \"on\" 組成。\"depend\" 源自拉丁語 \"dependere\"，由 \"de-\" (來自、向下) 和 \"pendere\" (懸掛、稱重) 構成，原始語義是「懸掛在……之下」，引申為「依賴」、「取決於」。\"on\" 在此處表示依附或關聯。因此，\"depend on\" 表示「將……視為支持或基礎」，「需要……才能存在或發生」。","definition":"to rely on or trust someone or something; to be determined by or contingent on something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The success of the project depends on your cooperation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個項目的成功取決於你的合作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Children often depend on their parents for support.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子們經常依靠父母的支持。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We can depend on him to finish the job.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們可以信賴他完成這項工作。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"孩子們經常依靠父母的支持。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3883,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::determine::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Scientists are trying to ____ the cause of the disease.","expectedAnswer":"determine","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Scientists are trying to ____ the cause of the disease.","clozeAnswer":"determine","exampleTranslation":"科學家們正試圖確定這種疾病的原因。","reference":{"eng":"determine","kk":"/dɪˈtɜːrmɪn/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['決定', '決心'], ['確定', '查明'], ['導致', '使得']]","chEntries":["決定","決心","確定","查明","導致","使得"],"practiceMeaning":"科學家們正試圖確定這種疾病的原因。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'determinare'，'de-' (utterly) + 'terminare' (to limit, to end)。核心是「設定界限」或「了結」。引申為做出最終決定、確定事實或原因，或導致某種結果。","definition":"1. to decide firmly on a course of action. 2. to find out or establish exactly, by research or calculation. 3. to cause (something) to be limited or determined; fix or decide.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They determined to find a solution.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們決心找到一個解決方案。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Scientists are trying to determine the cause of the disease.\",\n    \"ch\": \"科學家們正試圖確定這種疾病的原因。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The temperature determines the state of water.\",\n    \"ch\": \"溫度決定了水的狀態。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"科學家們正試圖確定這種疾病的原因。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5612,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l7::discriminate::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Babies can ____ between familiar and unfamiliar faces.","expectedAnswer":"discriminate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Babies can ____ between familiar and unfamiliar faces.","clozeAnswer":"discriminate","exampleTranslation":"嬰兒可以辨別熟悉的和不熟悉的臉孔。","reference":{"eng":"discriminate","kk":"dɪˈskrɪmɪneɪt","tense":"v.","ch":"[['歧視'], ['區別對待'], ['辨別']]","chEntries":["歧視","區別對待","辨別"],"practiceMeaning":"嬰兒可以辨別熟悉的和不熟悉的臉孔。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'discriminare'，意為「區分」，由 'dis-'（分開）和 'cernere'（分辨）組成。構詞學上，'dis-' 字首表示「分開」、「分離」，'cernere' 詞根提供「分辨」、「篩選」的核心語意。'-ate' 是常見的動詞化字尾。原始語意是「將事物分開、區別開來」。引申出兩個主要用法：一是「分辨、辨別」（distinguish），即識別細微差異的能力；二是「不公平地對待、區別對待」，即「歧視」。","definition":"1. Make an unjust or prejudicial distinction in the treatment of different categories of people or things, especially on the grounds of race, sex, or age; 2. Recognize or afford indication of the difference between.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It is important not to discriminate against any job applicants.\",\n    \"ch\": \"重要的是不要歧視任何求職者。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Babies can discriminate between familiar and unfamiliar faces.\",\n    \"ch\": \"嬰兒可以辨別熟悉的和不熟悉的臉孔。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The law prohibits employers from discriminating on the basis of age.\",\n    \"ch\": \"法律禁止雇主基於年齡進行歧視。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"嬰兒可以辨別熟悉的和不熟悉的臉孔。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5611,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l7::discrimination::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Children develop the ability for visual ____ at an early age.","expectedAnswer":"discrimination","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Children develop the ability for visual ____ at an early age.","clozeAnswer":"discrimination","exampleTranslation":"兒童早期就會發展出視覺辨別能力。","reference":{"eng":"discrimination","kk":"dɪˌskrɪməˈneɪʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[['歧視'], ['區別對待'], ['識別能力']]","chEntries":["歧視","區別對待","識別能力"],"practiceMeaning":"兒童早期就會發展出視覺辨別能力。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'discriminatio'，意為「區別」，由 'discriminare'（區分）派生，'discriminare' 又由 'dis-'（分開）和 'cernere'（分辨）組成。構詞學上，'dis-' 字首表示「分開」、「分離」，'cernere' 詞根提供「分辨」、「篩選」的核心語意。'-ation' 字尾將動詞轉換為名詞，表示「過程」或「狀態」。原始語意是「將事物分開、區別開來」。引申出兩個主要用法：一是「識別能力」（分辨細微差異的能力），二是「不公平的區別對待」，即「歧視」，特別是在種族、性別、年齡等方面。後者是現代社會語境中較常見的用法。","definition":"1. The unjust or prejudicial treatment of different categories of people, especially on grounds of race, age, or sex; 2. The ability to discern or distinguish between different things; 3. The action of treating a difference between things differently.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company has a strict policy against discrimination.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司有嚴格的反歧視政策。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Children develop the ability for visual discrimination at an early age.\",\n    \"ch\": \"兒童早期就會發展出視覺辨別能力。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Discrimination based on sexual orientation is illegal in many countries.\",\n    \"ch\": \"基於性取向的歧視在許多國家都是非法的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"兒童早期就會發展出視覺辨別能力。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4011,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u3::dizzy::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The sheer number of choices made her ____.","expectedAnswer":"dizzy","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The sheer number of choices made her ____.","clozeAnswer":"dizzy","exampleTranslation":"琳瑯滿目的選擇讓她眼花繚亂。","reference":{"eng":"dizzy","kk":"/ˈdɪzi/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['頭暈的', '暈眩的'], ['眼花繚亂的']]","chEntries":["頭暈的","暈眩的","眼花繚亂的"],"practiceMeaning":"琳瑯滿目的選擇讓她眼花繚亂。","analysis":"詞源：來自 'daze' (使發呆)。指頭部失去平衡感，感覺天旋地轉。","definition":"1. having or causing a sensation of spinning around and losing one's balance; 2. bewildered or confused.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The roller coaster ride made me feel dizzy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"坐雲霄飛車讓我感到頭暈。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The sheer number of choices made her dizzy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"琳瑯滿目的選擇讓她眼花繚亂。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"琳瑯滿目的選擇讓她眼花繚亂。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5540,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l5::document::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The historical ____ provided valuable insights.","expectedAnswer":"document","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The historical ____ provided valuable insights.","clozeAnswer":"document","exampleTranslation":"這份歷史文獻提供了寶貴的見解。","reference":{"eng":"document","kk":"ˈdɒkjʊmənt","tense":"n.","ch":"[['文件'], ['文獻'], ['紀錄']]","chEntries":["文件","文獻","紀錄"],"practiceMeaning":"這份歷史文獻提供了寶貴的見解。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'documentum'，意為「教訓、榜樣、證明」，是動詞 'docere' (to teach) 的派生詞。'docere' 的詞根 'doc-' 意為「教導、知識」。'documentum' 的原始語義是「被教導的材料」或「用來證明某事的證據」。構詞上，'doc-' (teach) + '-ment' (名詞化字尾)。'document' 作名詞，指「一份書面或電子記錄，用於提供證據、資訊或作為正式憑證」。它強調的是「知識的載體」或「證據的形式」。","definition":"a piece of written, printed, or electronic matter that provides information or evidence or that serves as an official record.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please submit all relevant documents by Friday.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請在週五前提交所有相關文件。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The historical document provided valuable insights.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這份歷史文獻提供了寶貴的見解。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這份歷史文獻提供了寶貴的見解。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5042,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::domain::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company is expanding its ____ into new markets.","expectedAnswer":"domain","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company is expanding its ____ into new markets.","clozeAnswer":"domain","exampleTranslation":"該公司正在將其業務範圍擴展到新市場。","reference":{"eng":"domain","kk":"doʊˈmeɪn","tense":"n.","ch":"[['領域'], ['範圍'], ['域名']]","chEntries":["領域","範圍","域名"],"practiceMeaning":"該公司正在將其業務範圍擴展到新市場。","analysis":"此字源自古法語domaine，本身又來自拉丁語dominium，意為「所有權、領地」，來自 dominus（主人）。原意指「屬於領主的地產」。在英語中，domain 演變出多重語意：1. 「領地、領土」，指某人或某事物所擁有的或控制的範圍；2. 「領域、專業範圍」，指某個學科、知識或活動的專屬範疇；3. 在網路語境中，指「域名」(domain name)。OCR 掃描時可能將 'o' 誤判為 '0'。此處修正為 domain。","definition":"1. an area of territory owned or controlled by a ruler or government; 2. an area of knowledge or activity; 3. a set of possible values for a variable.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Physics is a complex scientific domain.\",\n    \"ch\": \"物理學是一個複雜的科學領域。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company is expanding its domain into new markets.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司正在將其業務範圍擴展到新市場。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"You need to register a domain name for your website.\",\n    \"ch\": \"你需要為你的網站註冊一個域名。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該公司正在將其業務範圍擴展到新市場。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3141,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::dominant::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Red is the ____ color in the painting.","expectedAnswer":"dominant","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Red is the ____ color in the painting.","clozeAnswer":"dominant","exampleTranslation":"紅色是這幅畫的主導色彩。","reference":{"eng":"dominant","kk":"/ˈdɒmɪnənt/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['占主導地位的；有影響力的'], ['（基因）顯性的'], ['（地理、建築等）顯著的，突出的']]","chEntries":["占主導地位的","有影響力的","顯性的","顯著的，突出的"],"practiceMeaning":"紅色是這幅畫的主導色彩。","analysis":"形容詞，源自動詞 'dominate'。表示處於權力、控制或影響力的頂峰，是最重要的、最強勢的或最明顯的部分。在生物學中，'dominant gene' 指的是會壓倒另一條基因（隱性基因）並決定性狀的基因。其語意核心是「最重要」、「最強」或「最顯著」。","definition":"1. having power and influence over others; 2. the most important or noticeable; 3. (of a gene) expressing its phenotype readily over a corresponding recessive gene.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She played a dominant role in the negotiations.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在談判中扮演了主導角色。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Red is the dominant color in the painting.\",\n    \"ch\": \"紅色是這幅畫的主導色彩。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"In genetics, the dominant allele masks the effect of the recessive allele.\",\n    \"ch\": \"在遺傳學中，顯性等位基因會掩蓋隱性等位基因的作用。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"紅色是這幅畫的主導色彩。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5781,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::donor::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He became an organ ____ after his death.","expectedAnswer":"donor","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He became an organ ____ after his death.","clozeAnswer":"donor","exampleTranslation":"他在去世後成為了器官捐贈者。","reference":{"eng":"donor","kk":"ˈdoʊnər","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"捐贈者\"  ],  [    \"捐助者\"  ],  [    \"獻血者\"  ],  [    \"器官捐贈者\"  ]]","chEntries":["捐贈者","捐助者","獻血者","器官捐贈者"],"practiceMeaning":"他在去世後成為了器官捐贈者。","analysis":"此字為名詞，構詞自donate（捐贈）+ -or（名詞字尾，表示「從事某種活動的人」）。-or字尾源自拉丁語-or。donate源自拉丁語donare（給予；捐贈）。因此，donor的核心語義是指「進行捐贈的人」，即捐贈者。語意演變上，由動詞「捐贈」轉化為執行該動作的人。","definition":"1. a person who gives money, goods, or help to a charity or organization; 2. a person who gives blood or an organ for medical use.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The organization is seeking new donors to support its programs.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該組織正在尋找新的捐助者來支持其計劃。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He became an organ donor after his death.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在去世後成為了器官捐贈者。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The blood bank is in urgent need of donors.\",\n    \"ch\": \"血庫急需捐血者。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他在去世後成為了器官捐贈者。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3938,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::downtown::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He bought a new apartment in the ____ district.","expectedAnswer":"downtown","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He bought a new apartment in the ____ district.","clozeAnswer":"downtown","exampleTranslation":"他在市中心區買了一間新公寓。","reference":{"eng":"downtown","kk":"/ˈdaʊntaʊn/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['市中心的']]","chEntries":["市中心的"],"practiceMeaning":"他在市中心區買了一間新公寓。","analysis":"同上，此處作形容詞用，修飾名詞。","definition":"situated in or relating to the central area of a city or town.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We stayed at a hotel in the downtown area.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們住在一間位於市中心區域的旅館。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He bought a new apartment in the downtown district.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在市中心區買了一間新公寓。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他在市中心區買了一間新公寓。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5641,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l8::dramatically::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Her life changed ____ after winning the lottery.","expectedAnswer":"dramatically","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Her life changed ____ after winning the lottery.","clozeAnswer":"dramatically","exampleTranslation":"贏得樂透後，她的生活發生了戲劇性的變化。","reference":{"eng":"dramatically","kk":"drəˈmætɪkli","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['戲劇性地'], ['引人注目地'], ['劇烈地']]","chEntries":["戲劇性地","引人注目地","劇烈地"],"practiceMeaning":"贏得樂透後，她的生活發生了戲劇性的變化。","analysis":"此字為 dramatic（戲劇性的）的副詞形式，由 dramatic + -ally（副詞字尾）構成。dramatic 源自拉丁語 dramaticus，來自希臘語 dramatikos，意為「戲劇的」，其根源為 drama（戲劇），來自希臘語 dromos（奔跑，賽跑），再追溯至動詞 δρα- (dran) / δράω (draō)（做，行動）。核心語義與「戲劇」相關，引申為「誇張的」、「引人注目的」、「激烈的」。-ally 是常見的副詞字尾，由 -al + -ly 構成，將形容詞轉為副詞，表示「以……的方式」。構詞上，drama 是核心，-tic 表「相關的」，-ally 表「方式」。","definition":"in a very noticeable and striking way; to a very great extent; suddenly and to a surprising degree.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The stock market fell dramatically.\",\n    \"ch\": \"股市劇烈下跌。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her life changed dramatically after winning the lottery.\",\n    \"ch\": \"贏得樂透後，她的生活發生了戲劇性的變化。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"贏得樂透後，她的生活發生了戲劇性的變化。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3143,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::dread::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of war hung over the nation.","expectedAnswer":"dread","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of war hung over the nation.","clozeAnswer":"dread","exampleTranslation":"戰爭的恐懼籠罩著這個國家。","reference":{"eng":"dread","kk":"/drɛd/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['恐懼；害怕'], ['（預期中的）災禍；禍患']]","chEntries":["恐懼","害怕","災禍","禍患"],"practiceMeaning":"戰爭的恐懼籠罩著這個國家。","analysis":"名詞用法，源自動詞 'dread'。指「強烈的恐懼」、「畏懼」或「恐慌」，特別是對即將發生的不好的事情的預期。它也可以指「災禍」或「禍患」，暗示著一件令人感到恐懼或憂慮的事情。","definition":"1. great fear or apprehension; 2. a cause of great fear or apprehension.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The thought of failing the exam filled him with dread.\",\n    \"ch\": \"考試不及格的想法讓他充滿恐懼。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The dread of war hung over the nation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"戰爭的恐懼籠罩著這個國家。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He lived in constant dread of being discovered.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他生活在被發現的持續恐懼中。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"戰爭的恐懼籠罩著這個國家。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5080,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::dreadful::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The weather was ____ all week.","expectedAnswer":"dreadful","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The weather was ____ all week.","clozeAnswer":"dreadful","exampleTranslation":"整個星期天氣都糟透了。","reference":{"eng":"dreadful","kk":"ˈdredfl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['可怕的'], ['糟糕的'], ['極度的']]","chEntries":["可怕的","糟糕的","極度的"],"practiceMeaning":"整個星期天氣都糟透了。","analysis":"此字由 'dread' (恐懼) + '-ful' (形容詞化後綴，表示充滿、具有某種性質) 構成。'-ful' 在此強調充滿了 'dread' 的特質。核心語義是 '引發極度恐懼或憂慮的'。因此，它可以用來形容令人不安、可怕的事物。也可用來表示程度，如 '極度糟糕的'、'非常嚴重的'，強調其負面或強烈的影響。","definition":"1. Causing or involving great suffering, fear, or unhappiness; extremely bad.; 2. Of very low quality; very unpleasant.; 3. Inspiring dread or fear.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The news of the accident was dreadful.\",\n    \"ch\": \"事故的消息是可怕的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The weather was dreadful all week.\",\n    \"ch\": \"整個星期天氣都糟透了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has a dreadful habit of interrupting.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他有打斷別人說話的可怕習慣。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"整個星期天氣都糟透了。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3079,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::durable::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They are looking for ____ solutions to environmental problems.","expectedAnswer":"durable","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They are looking for ____ solutions to environmental problems.","clozeAnswer":"durable","exampleTranslation":"他們正在尋找持久的環境問題解決方案。","reference":{"eng":"durable","kk":"/ˈdʊrəbl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['耐用的；持久的'], ['堅固的；強韌的']]","chEntries":["耐用的","持久的","堅固的","強韌的"],"practiceMeaning":"他們正在尋找持久的環境問題解決方案。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'durare' (to last, to endure)。核心意義是「能夠長時間存在或使用」。\n1. 耐用的；持久的：指能夠承受長時間的使用或磨損而不損壞。\n2. 堅固的；強韌的：形容物質材料或結構的穩固和強壯。","definition":"1. able to last for a long time without being damaged; 2. strong and not easily damaged.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This material is very durable and resistant to wear.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種材料非常耐用，抗磨損。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They are looking for durable solutions to environmental problems.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們正在尋找持久的環境問題解決方案。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們正在尋找持久的環境問題解決方案。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5082,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::ecosystem::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The introduction of this species disrupted the local ____.","expectedAnswer":"ecosystem","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The introduction of this species disrupted the local ____.","clozeAnswer":"ecosystem","exampleTranslation":"引入這個物種擾亂了當地的生態系統。","reference":{"eng":"ecosystem","kk":"ˈiːkoʊˌsɪstəm","tense":"n.","ch":"[['生態系統'], ['生態圈']]","chEntries":["生態系統","生態圈"],"practiceMeaning":"引入這個物種擾亂了當地的生態系統。","analysis":"此字由希臘語 'oikos' (house, dwelling, household) + 'system' (系統) 構成。'Oikos' 在這裡引申為 '環境' 或 '棲息地'。因此，'ecosystem' 指的是一個特定區域內，生物群落（動植物、微生物）與其非生物環境（空氣、水、土壤、陽光）之間相互作用、相互依存的統一整體。它強調的是生物與環境的複雜互動網絡。","definition":"1. A biological community of interacting organisms and their physical environment.; 2. A complex network or interconnected system.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Coral reefs are fragile marine ecosystems.\",\n    \"ch\": \"珊瑚礁是脆弱的海洋生態系統。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The introduction of this species disrupted the local ecosystem.\",\n    \"ch\": \"引入這個物種擾亂了當地的生態系統。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"引入這個物種擾亂了當地的生態系統。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5562,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::efficiency::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We are always looking for ways to increase our energy ____.","expectedAnswer":"efficiency","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We are always looking for ways to increase our energy ____.","clozeAnswer":"efficiency","exampleTranslation":"我們一直在尋找提高能源效率的方法。","reference":{"eng":"efficiency","kk":"ɪˈfɪʃənsi","tense":"n.","ch":"[['效率'], ['效能']]","chEntries":["效率","效能"],"practiceMeaning":"我們一直在尋找提高能源效率的方法。","analysis":"此字由 \"efficient\" 加上名詞化字尾 \"-cy\" 構成。\"efficient\" 源自拉丁語 \"efficiēns\"，是 \"efficere\"（to work out, accomplish, produce，完成，達成，生產）的現在分詞。\"efficere\" 由 \"ex-\"（out）和 \"facere\"（to make, to do，製造，做）組成，意為「製造出來，完成」。\"-cy\" 是構成抽象名詞的字尾。因此，\"efficiency\" 的核心語義是「有效完成某事的能力或狀態」，即「效率」或「效能」。它強調的是以最少的資源（時間、精力、金錢）達成最大的產出或目標。","definition":"1. The state or quality of being efficient; 2. The ability to accomplish something with the least amount of wasted time, effort, or resources.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The new system has greatly improved the efficiency of our operations.\",\n    \"ch\": \"新系統大大提高了我們營運的效率。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We are always looking for ways to increase our energy efficiency.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們一直在尋找提高能源效率的方法。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her efficiency in handling multiple tasks is remarkable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她同時處理多項任務的效率令人稱道。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們一直在尋找提高能源效率的方法。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5126,"wordRef":"字彙王::u62::ego::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The psychologist discussed the concept of the ____.","expectedAnswer":"ego","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The psychologist discussed the concept of the ____.","clozeAnswer":"ego","exampleTranslation":"心理學家討論了「自我」的概念。","reference":{"eng":"ego","kk":"ˈiːgoʊ","tense":"n.","ch":"[['自我'], ['自尊心'], ['自我意識']]","chEntries":["自我","自尊心","自我意識"],"practiceMeaning":"心理學家討論了「自我」的概念。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 ego，意為「我」。這是拉丁語的第一人稱單數主格代名詞。在心理學上，由佛洛伊德提出，ego 指的是人格結構中負責現實原則的部分，是「自我」的概念。在日常用語中，ego 也指「自尊心」或「自我中心」。","definition":"a person's sense of self-esteem or self-importance; the part of the mind that mediates between the conscious and the unconscious and is responsible for reality testing and a sense of personal identity.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His ego was badly bruised by the criticism.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的自尊心因批評而大受打擊。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The psychologist discussed the concept of the ego.\",\n    \"ch\": \"心理學家討論了「自我」的概念。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"心理學家討論了「自我」的概念。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U62"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4611,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::elderly::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Many ____ people live alone.","expectedAnswer":"elderly","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Many ____ people live alone.","clozeAnswer":"elderly","exampleTranslation":"許多老年人獨居。","reference":{"eng":"elderly","kk":"/ˈeldərli/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['年長的'], ['老年的']]","chEntries":["年長的","老年的"],"practiceMeaning":"許多老年人獨居。","analysis":"由 'elder' (年長者) + '-ly' (形容詞後綴) 組成。'Elder' 源自古英語 'ældra' (較老的)，是 'old' 的比較級。此字是比較客氣和尊重的說法，指年齡較大的人，通常帶有同情和關懷的意味。","definition":"old or aging; of advanced age.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The bus offered a seat to an elderly woman.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公車上給了一位年長婦人座位。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Many elderly people live alone.\",\n    \"ch\": \"許多老年人獨居。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"許多老年人獨居。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4449,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::electronic::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ mail has revolutionized communication.","expectedAnswer":"Electronic","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ mail has revolutionized communication.","clozeAnswer":"Electronic","exampleTranslation":"電子郵件徹底改變了通訊方式。","reference":{"eng":"electronic","kk":"/ɪˈlɛktrɪk/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['電子的'], ['電腦化的'], ['（尤指）電流通過裝置的']]","chEntries":["電子的","電腦化的","電流通過裝置的"],"practiceMeaning":"電子郵件徹底改變了通訊方式。","analysis":"源自 electro- (來自希臘語 ēlektron, 意為琥珀，因其摩擦生電的性質而得名) 加上 -ic (形容詞後綴)。核心概念是與電有關。語意從「與電有關」延伸至「由電力驅動的」、「通過電子元件運作的」，如電子設備 (electronic devices)。","definition":"1. Operated by or using electricity, especially in an advanced or complex way; relating to or using devices that operate by the flow of electrons.; 2. Relating to or concerned with the production and emission of electrons.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She bought a new electronic gadget for her kitchen.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她買了一個新的電子小工具給她的廚房。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Electronic mail has revolutionized communication.\",\n    \"ch\": \"電子郵件徹底改變了通訊方式。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company specializes in electronic components.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司專門生產電子零件。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"電子郵件徹底改變了通訊方式。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5294,"wordRef":"字彙王::u63::eligible::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He is not ____ for the scholarship.","expectedAnswer":"eligible","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He is not ____ for the scholarship.","clozeAnswer":"eligible","exampleTranslation":"他不符合獎學金的資格。","reference":{"eng":"eligible","kk":"ˈɛlɪdʒəbəl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['合格的', '有資格的']]","chEntries":["合格的","有資格的"],"practiceMeaning":"他不符合獎學金的資格。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'eligibilis'，由 'eligere'（to choose, to select）和 '-ibilis'（-ible, capable of）組成。'eligere' 本身由 'e-'（out）和 'legere'（to choose）構成。構詞上，'elig-' 為詞根（來自 'eligere'），'-ibilis' 為形容詞後綴，表示「能夠做……的」。核心語意為「可以被選擇的」，引申為「有資格的」、「符合條件的」。","definition":"having the right to do or obtain something; satisfying the appropriate conditions for something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Only adults over 18 are eligible to vote.\",\n    \"ch\": \"只有 18 歲以上的成年人有資格投票。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is not eligible for the scholarship.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他不符合獎學金的資格。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他不符合獎學金的資格。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U63"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6118,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::eloquent::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Her eyes were ____ in their sorrow.","expectedAnswer":"eloquent","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Her eyes were ____ in their sorrow.","clozeAnswer":"eloquent","exampleTranslation":"她眼中流露出的悲傷鮮明動人。","reference":{"eng":"eloquent","kk":"ˈɛləkwənt","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"雄辯的\"  ],  [    \"口才好的\"  ],  [    \"有說服力的\"  ],  [    \"鮮明的\"  ]]","chEntries":["雄辯的","口才好的","有說服力的","鮮明的"],"practiceMeaning":"她眼中流露出的悲傷鮮明動人。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 ēloquēns，是 ēloquī（說出；流利地說）的現在分詞。構詞上，ē- 是強調字首，loquī 意為「說話」，與 loquor（說）有關。因此，eloquent 的核心語義是「說話有力、流利」。此形容詞用於描述演講、作家、言論或表達方式，強調其具有說服力、感染力和清晰度。其語意演變是從具體的「能說會道」到抽象的「有說服力的、鮮明的」。","definition":"1. fluent or persuasive in speaking or writing; 2. clearly expressing or indicating something; vivid.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is an eloquent speaker.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一位雄辯的演講者。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her eyes were eloquent in their sorrow.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她眼中流露出的悲傷鮮明動人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The book provides an eloquent defense of human rights.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本書有力地捍衛了人權。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她眼中流露出的悲傷鮮明動人。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3146,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::energetic::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He is an ____ advocate for environmental protection.","expectedAnswer":"energetic","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He is an ____ advocate for environmental protection.","clozeAnswer":"energetic","exampleTranslation":"他是環保運動的積極倡導者。","reference":{"eng":"energetic","kk":"/ˌɛnərˈdʒɛtɪk/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['精力充沛的；充滿活力的'], ['（行動、過程）需要大量體力的']]","chEntries":["精力充沛的","充滿活力的","需要大量體力的"],"practiceMeaning":"他是環保運動的積極倡導者。","analysis":"源自名詞 'energy'，意為「能量」。'Energetic' 形容詞表示擁有或顯示出大量的能量、活力和熱情。它強調的是積極、活躍、有幹勁的狀態，常與體力活動或強烈的情緒反應相關。與 'dynamic' 相似，但更側重於個體的活力和行動力。","definition":"1. showing or involving great energy and enthusiasm; 2. requiring a lot of energy.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The children were energetic and full of fun.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子們精力充沛，充滿樂趣。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is an energetic advocate for environmental protection.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是環保運動的積極倡導者。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Renovating the old house was an energetic undertaking.\",\