as an exhausting experience.\",\n    \"ch\": \"攀登這座山是一次令人精疲力竭的經歷。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Dealing with difficult customers can be very exhausting.\",\n    \"ch\": \"應付難纏的顧客會非常累人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The long and exhausting search finally yielded results.\",\n    \"ch\": \"漫長而令人疲憊的搜尋終於有了結果。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"應付難纏的顧客會非常累人。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5645,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l8::expansion::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The rapid ____ of the universe is a mystery.","expectedAnswer":"expansion","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The rapid ____ of the universe is a mystery.","clozeAnswer":"expansion","exampleTranslation":"宇宙的快速膨脹是一個謎。","reference":{"eng":"expansion","kk":"ɪkˈspænʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[['擴張'], ['擴大'], ['膨脹'], ['擴展']]","chEntries":["擴張","擴大","膨脹","擴展"],"practiceMeaning":"宇宙的快速膨脹是一個謎。","analysis":"此字由 expand（擴大）+ -sion（名詞字尾）構成。expand 源自拉丁語 expandere，由 ex-（出，out）+ pandere（展開，to spread）組成。pandere 來自原始印歐語 *paə-（保護；餵養；展開）。-sion 是常見的名詞字尾，用於將動詞轉為名詞，表示「動作」、「狀態」或「結果」。構詞上，ex- 表示「向外」，pandere 提供「展開」的核心動作，-sion 將其名詞化。核心語義為「向外展開」或「擴大」的動作或結果。","definition":"the action of becoming larger or more extensive; the process of increasing in size, volume, or scope; a large increase in the size or amount of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company announced its plans for expansion into Asia.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司宣布了其擴張至亞洲的計畫。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The rapid expansion of the universe is a mystery.\",\n    \"ch\": \"宇宙的快速膨脹是一個謎。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"宇宙的快速膨脹是一個謎。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6074,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::expedition::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They prepared for a polar ____.","expectedAnswer":"expedition","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They prepared for a polar ____.","clozeAnswer":"expedition","exampleTranslation":"他們為極地考察做好了準備。","reference":{"eng":"expedition","kk":"ˌɛkspəˈdɪʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"遠征\"  ],  [    \"考察\"  ],  [    \"探險\"  ],  [    \"遠足\"  ],  [    \"迅速\"  ]]","chEntries":["遠征","考察","探險","遠足","迅速"],"practiceMeaning":"他們為極地考察做好了準備。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 expeditio，是 expédire（to send out, to dispatch）的結果名詞。Expédire 由 ex-（out）和 pes, pedis（foot）組成，字面意思是「派腳出去」，引申為「派遣」，再引申為「迅速完成」、「派出以達成目的」。構詞上，ex- 表「出」，ped- 表「腳」，-ition 是名詞後綴。Expedition 的核心語義是「為特定目的（通常是探索、考察、科學研究或軍事行動）而進行的、有組織的、較長距離的出行」。它也引申為「迅速」這個較少用的意義。","definition":"1. a journey undertaken by a group of people with a particular purpose, especially exploration, scientific research, or war; 2. efficiency and speed in doing something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The expedition set out to explore the Amazon rainforest.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這次探險隊出發去探索亞馬遜雨林。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They prepared for a polar expedition.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們為極地考察做好了準備。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The relief expedition arrived quickly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"救援隊迅速抵達。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們為極地考察做好了準備。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4067,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::experiment::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This is a dangerous ____.","expectedAnswer":"experiment","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This is a dangerous ____.","clozeAnswer":"experiment","exampleTranslation":"這是一個危險的實驗。","reference":{"eng":"experiment","kk":"/ɪkˈspɛrɪmənt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['實驗']]","chEntries":["實驗"],"practiceMeaning":"這是一個危險的實驗。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'experimentum'，由 'experiri' (to try, to test) 構成，'experiri' 又由 'ex-' (out) + 'periri' (to try) 構成。核心是「嘗試」、「測試」。因此，'experiment' 指通過觀察和測試來檢驗某個理論或發現新知識的過程。","definition":"a scientific test done in order to learn how something happens or to check if a particular idea is true","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"這位科學家進行了一項實驗來驗證他的理論。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The scientist conducted an experiment to test his theory.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個危險的實驗。\",\n    \"eng\": \"This is a dangerous experiment.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"實驗結果沒有定論。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The results of the experiment were inconclusive.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是一個危險的實驗。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3083,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::explain::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He tried to ____ his behavior.","expectedAnswer":"explain","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He tried to ____ his behavior.","clozeAnswer":"explain","exampleTranslation":"他試圖解釋自己的行為。","reference":{"eng":"explain","kk":"/ɪkˈspleɪn/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['解釋；說明'], ['闡明；辨明']]","chEntries":["解釋","說明","闡明","辨明"],"practiceMeaning":"他試圖解釋自己的行為。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'explanare'，'ex-' (out) + 'planus' (plain)。核心意義是「使事物變得平坦、清晰」。\n1. 解釋；說明：指闡述事物的性質、原因、過程、意義等，使其易於理解。\n2. 闡明；辨明：指辨別或說明某事物與另一事物的區別，或說明其真實情況。","definition":"1. to make something clear or easy to understand by describing it or giving reasons; 2. to give the reason for something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Can you explain the rules of the game to me?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你能向我解釋一下遊戲規則嗎？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He tried to explain his behavior.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他試圖解釋自己的行為。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他試圖解釋自己的行為。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4061,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::explore::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need to ____ all possible solutions.","expectedAnswer":"explore","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need to ____ all possible solutions.","clozeAnswer":"explore","exampleTranslation":"我們需要研究所有可能的解決方案。","reference":{"eng":"explore","kk":"/ɪkˈsplɔr/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['探索', '探險'], ['研究', '調查']]","chEntries":["探索","探險","研究","調查"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要研究所有可能的解決方案。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'explorare'，由 'ex-' (out) + 'plorare' (to cry out, to search) 構成，原意是「大聲呼喊尋找」。核心是「尋找」、「探究」。因此，'explore' 指「深入探究」未知的事物（地理、概念、理論等）。","definition":"1. to travel to or around (a place) in order to learn about it; 2. to discuss or examine (a subject or problem) in detail","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"這個團隊將探索新的地域。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The team will explore new territories.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要研究所有可能的解決方案。\",\n    \"eng\": \"We need to explore all possible solutions.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"科學家們正在探索海洋深處。\",\n    \"eng\": \"Scientists are exploring the depths of the ocean.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要研究所有可能的解決方案。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5638,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l8::extent::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of his knowledge is impressive.","expectedAnswer":"extent","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of his knowledge is impressive.","clozeAnswer":"extent","exampleTranslation":"他知識的廣度令人印象深刻。","reference":{"eng":"extent","kk":"ɪkˈstɛnt","tense":"n.","ch":"[['程度'], ['範圍'], ['面積'], ['廣度']]","chEntries":["程度","範圍","面積","廣度"],"practiceMeaning":"他知識的廣度令人印象深刻。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 extent，意為「測量」。其來自拉丁語 extentus，是 extend（伸展，擴展）的過去分詞。extend 來自拉丁語 extendere，由 ex-（出，out）+ tendere（伸展，to stretch）組成。tendere 來自原始印歐語 *ten-（伸展）。因此，extent 的核心語義是「被伸展或擴展到的範圍或程度」。構詞上，ex- 提供「出」或「向外」的方向，tendere 提供「伸展」的核心動作。此處為名詞用法，指代事物的「程度」、「範圍」、「廣度」或「規模」。","definition":"the degree or scope to which something is the case; the size or amount of something; the area covered by something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The full extent of the damage is not yet known.\",\n    \"ch\": \"損壞的全部程度尚不明確。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The extent of his knowledge is impressive.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他知識的廣度令人印象深刻。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"To what extent do you agree with him?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你在多大程度上同意他的看法？\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他知識的廣度令人印象深刻。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3171,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::extinct::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The dodo is an example of an ____ bird.","expectedAnswer":"extinct","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The dodo is an example of an ____ bird.","clozeAnswer":"extinct","exampleTranslation":"渡渡鳥是一種已滅絕的鳥類。","reference":{"eng":"extinct","kk":"/ɪkˈstɪŋkt/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['滅絕的；絕種的'], ['（物種、制度、語言等）已消失的；不復存在的']]","chEntries":["滅絕的","絕種的","已消失的","不復存在的"],"practiceMeaning":"渡渡鳥是一種已滅絕的鳥類。","analysis":"詞源來自拉丁語 'extinctus'，意為「熄滅，毀滅」，源於 'exstinguere'（熄滅，毀滅）。'Extinct' 指的是某個物種、族群、制度、語言或事物完全消失，不再存在。最常見的用法是形容已滅絕的動物或植物。它強調的是「徹底消失」和「不復存在」的狀態。","definition":"1. (of a species, family, or other larger group) having no living members; 2. no longer in existence; having died out.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Dinosaurs have been extinct for millions of years.\",\n    \"ch\": \"恐龍已經滅絕數百萬年了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The dodo is an example of an extinct bird.\",\n    \"ch\": \"渡渡鳥是一種已滅絕的鳥類。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The tradition became extinct after the war.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個傳統在戰後消失了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"渡渡鳥是一種已滅絕的鳥類。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40、U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5297,"wordRef":"字彙王::u63::facilitate::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Good planning will ____ the project's success.","expectedAnswer":"facilitate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Good planning will ____ the project's success.","clozeAnswer":"facilitate","exampleTranslation":"良好的規劃將有助於專案的成功。","reference":{"eng":"facilitate","kk":"fəˈsɪlɪˌteɪt","tense":"v.","ch":"[['促進', '幫助', '使容易']]","chEntries":["促進","幫助","使容易"],"practiceMeaning":"良好的規劃將有助於專案的成功。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'facere'（to make, to do）和 'facilis'（easy）。'facilitate' 由 'facilis' 加上動詞後綴 '-tate' 構成，意為「使變得容易」。構詞上，'facil-' 為詞根（來自 'facilis'），'-itate' 為動詞化後綴。核心語意為「使事情更容易發生或完成」。","definition":"to make an action or process easy or easier; to help bring about.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The internet facilitates communication worldwide.\",\n    \"ch\": \"網際網路促進了全球溝通。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Good planning will facilitate the project's success.\",\n    \"ch\": \"良好的規劃將有助於專案的成功。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"良好的規劃將有助於專案的成功。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U63"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4534,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::faint::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He felt ____ and had to sit down.","expectedAnswer":"faint","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He felt ____ and had to sit down.","clozeAnswer":"faint","exampleTranslation":"他感到頭暈，不得不坐下。","reference":{"eng":"faint","kk":"/feɪnt/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['微弱的', '模糊的'], ['昏眩的', '無力的']]","chEntries":["微弱的","模糊的","昏眩的","無力的"],"practiceMeaning":"他感到頭暈，不得不坐下。","analysis":"源自古法語 'feint'，意為 'feigned, false, weak' (偽裝的、虛假的、軟弱的)。此字根與 'feign' (假裝) 同源。\n    'adj.' 意義延伸：\n    1. 微弱、模糊：指感官可察覺的程度極低，如 'faint sound' (微弱的聲音)，'faint light' (微弱的光)。\n    2. 虛弱、無力：指身體或精神上的狀態，如 'faint with hunger' (因飢餓而無力)，'faint hope' (渺茫的希望)。","definition":"1. (of a light, sound, smell, or colour) scarcely perceptible; faint.; 2. feeling weak and dizzy and liable to collapse.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She heard a faint cry for help.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她聽到微弱的求救聲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He felt faint and had to sit down.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他感到頭暈，不得不坐下。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was a faint smell of gas in the air.\",\n    \"ch\": \"空氣中有微弱的瓦斯味。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他感到頭暈，不得不坐下。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4053,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::faith::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They have lost ____ in the government.","expectedAnswer":"faith","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They have lost ____ in the government.","clozeAnswer":"faith","exampleTranslation":"他們對政府已經失去了信心。","reference":{"eng":"faith","kk":"/feɪθ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['信仰', '信念'], ['信任', '信賴'], ['保證', '承諾']]","chEntries":["信仰","信念","信任","信賴","保證","承諾"],"practiceMeaning":"他們對政府已經失去了信心。","analysis":"源自古法語 'feid'，來自拉丁語 'fides' (faith, trust, belief)，與 'fidelis' (faithful) 同源。核心是「相信」、「信任」。因此，'faith' 可以指宗教上的「信仰」、對某人或某事的「信任」，或是對某事成功或發生的「信念」、「希望」。第四個義項「保證」則是由「信任」引申，表示基於信任而產生的承諾或保證。","definition":"1. strong belief in God or in the doctrines of a religion; 2. complete trust or confidence in someone or something; 3. a strong feeling of trust or confidence","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"她對她醫生的能力深具信心。\",\n    \"eng\": \"She has great faith in her doctor's abilities.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他們對政府已經失去了信心。\",\n    \"eng\": \"They have lost faith in the government.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他對上帝的信仰給予他力量。\",\n    \"eng\": \"His faith in God gives him strength.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們對政府已經失去了信心。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5539,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l5::fake::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The whole story turned out to be a ____.","expectedAnswer":"fake","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The whole story turned out to be a ____.","clozeAnswer":"fake","exampleTranslation":"整個故事原來是個騙局。","reference":{"eng":"fake","kk":"feɪk","tense":"n.","ch":"[['假貨'], ['仿製品'], ['騙局']]","chEntries":["假貨","仿製品","騙局"],"practiceMeaning":"整個故事原來是個騙局。","analysis":"此為形容詞 'fake' 的名詞形式。作為名詞，它指「偽造品、仿製品」，或者是「騙局、虛假的東西」。構詞與語意演變與形容詞、動詞一致，都指向「非真實、偽造」的概念。","definition":"something that is not genuine; a counterfeit or imitation; a deception.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The store was selling a lot of fakes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那家商店賣很多假貨。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The whole story turned out to be a fake.\",\n    \"ch\": \"整個故事原來是個騙局。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"整個故事原來是個騙局。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3216,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::farewell::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It was a tearful ____.","expectedAnswer":"farewell","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It was a tearful ____.","clozeAnswer":"farewell","exampleTranslation":"這是一場含淚的告別。","reference":{"eng":"farewell","kk":"/ˌfɛrˈwɛl/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['告別'], ['離別']]","chEntries":["告別","離別"],"practiceMeaning":"這是一場含淚的告別。","analysis":"源自古英語 'fāran wel'，字面意思是『去得好』，是離別時的祝福語。演變成名詞，指告別的時刻或行為。","definition":"an act of saying goodbye or parting.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We held a small party for his farewell.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們為他的告別舉行了一個小型派對。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was a tearful farewell.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一場含淚的告別。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是一場含淚的告別。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U41"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3287,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::fax::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"I received a ____ from our overseas office.","expectedAnswer":"fax","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"I received a ____ from our overseas office.","clozeAnswer":"fax","exampleTranslation":"我收到了一份來自海外辦公室的傳真。","reference":{"eng":"fax","kk":"/fæks/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['傳真；傳真文件']]","chEntries":["傳真","傳真文件"],"practiceMeaning":"我收到了一份來自海外辦公室的傳真。","analysis":"縮寫自 'facsimile' (副本)，源自拉丁語 'fac simile' (照樣製作)。指將文件副本通過電話線傳輸的技術和其產生的文件。","definition":"a system for sending documents by telephone line, or a document sent in this way.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please send the report by fax.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請將報告以傳真方式發送。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I received a fax from our overseas office.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我收到了一份來自海外辦公室的傳真。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我收到了一份來自海外辦公室的傳真。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3923,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::fearful::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ news spread quickly through the town.","expectedAnswer":"fearful","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ news spread quickly through the town.","clozeAnswer":"fearful","exampleTranslation":"令人恐懼的消息迅速傳遍了整個城鎮。","reference":{"eng":"fearful","kk":"/ˈfɪərfəl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['害怕的', '恐懼的'], ['令人害怕的']]","chEntries":["害怕的","恐懼的","令人害怕的"],"practiceMeaning":"令人恐懼的消息迅速傳遍了整個城鎮。","analysis":"源自古英語 'fēarlīc'，由 'fēar' (意為「恐懼」) 和 '-ful' (形容詞後綴) 組成。有兩層意思：一是指「感到恐懼」，二是指「引起恐懼」。","definition":"1. feeling fear or anxiety; frightened; 2. feeling or showing fear; 3. causing fear.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was fearful of the dark.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他害怕黑暗。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The fearful news spread quickly through the town.\",\n    \"ch\": \"令人恐懼的消息迅速傳遍了整個城鎮。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She gave a fearful glance at the approaching storm.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對逼近的風暴投以恐懼的一瞥。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"令人恐懼的消息迅速傳遍了整個城鎮。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3289,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::feast::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The mountain scenery was a ____ for the eyes.","expectedAnswer":"feast","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The mountain scenery was a ____ for the eyes.","clozeAnswer":"feast","exampleTranslation":"山景令人賞心悅目。","reference":{"eng":"feast","kk":"/fiːst/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['盛宴；宴會'], ['（令人高興的）享受；樂事'], ['節日；齋戒日']]","chEntries":["盛宴","宴會","享受","樂事","節日","齋戒日"],"practiceMeaning":"山景令人賞心悅目。","analysis":"源自古法語 'feste'，來自拉丁語 'festum' (節日，慶祝)。原指宗教節日或慶祝活動，後主要指大規模、豐盛的宴會。","definition":"1. a large meal, typically one to celebrate something; 2. something that provides great pleasure to the senses; 3. a religious festival or anniversary.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The wedding feast lasted all night.\",\n    \"ch\": \"婚宴持續了一整夜。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The mountain scenery was a feast for the eyes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"山景令人賞心悅目。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They celebrated the harvest with a feast.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們舉辦盛宴慶祝豐收。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"山景令人賞心悅目。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4593,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::feel-faint::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The smell of the chemicals made him ____.","expectedAnswer":"feel faint","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The smell of the chemicals made him ____.","clozeAnswer":"feel faint","exampleTranslation":"化學品的氣味讓他感到頭暈。","reference":{"eng":"feel faint","kk":"/fil feɪnt/","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['感到頭暈', '覺得快要昏倒']]","chEntries":["感到頭暈","覺得快要昏倒"],"practiceMeaning":"化學品的氣味讓他感到頭暈。","analysis":"此片語由 'feel' (感覺) 和 'faint' (頭暈的、無力的) 組成。 'faint' 源自古法語 'feint' (weak, false)。此片語描述因身體極度不適、虛弱或失血等原因，導致暫時失去體力、頭暈目眩，甚至可能失去知覺的感覺。","definition":"1. to feel weak and dizzy, as if about to collapse.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She felt faint after standing up too quickly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她站起來太快，感到一陣頭暈。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The smell of the chemicals made him feel faint.\",\n    \"ch\": \"化學品的氣味讓他感到頭暈。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"化學品的氣味讓他感到頭暈。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3290,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::ferry::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ schedule is available online.","expectedAnswer":"ferry","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ schedule is available online.","clozeAnswer":"ferry","exampleTranslation":"渡輪的班次表可以在網上查到。","reference":{"eng":"ferry","kk":"/ˈfɛri/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['渡輪；擺渡船'], ['（渡輪的）航線']]","chEntries":["渡輪","擺渡船","航線"],"practiceMeaning":"渡輪的班次表可以在網上查到。","analysis":"源自古英語 'ferigan' (運輸)。指用於在兩岸之間運送乘客或車輛的船隻，以及其運營的固定路線。","definition":"a boat or ship for taking passengers and often vehicles across a river or narrow area of water; the service provided by such a boat or ship.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We took the ferry to cross to the island.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們搭乘渡輪前往島上。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The ferry schedule is available online.\",\n    \"ch\": \"渡輪的班次表可以在網上查到。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"渡輪的班次表可以在網上查到。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5396,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l2::financial::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He is studying ____ management.","expectedAnswer":"financial","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He is studying ____ management.","clozeAnswer":"financial","exampleTranslation":"他正在學習財務管理。","reference":{"eng":"financial","kk":"faɪˈnænʃəl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['財務的'], ['金融的'], ['財政的']]","chEntries":["財務的","金融的","財政的"],"practiceMeaning":"他正在學習財務管理。","analysis":"此字源自名詞 'finance' (財政、金融)。'-ial' 是常見的形容詞字尾，表示「與……有關的」。'finance' 源自古法語 fin (結束、結算)，引申至「財務管理」。核心語意是「與金錢、資金、投資、銀行等相關的」。","definition":"Relating to finance, especially public finance, or the management of large amounts of money.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company is facing serious financial difficulties.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司正面臨嚴重的財務困難。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is studying financial management.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他正在學習財務管理。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他正在學習財務管理。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5643,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l8::flock::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"A ____ of tourists gathered around the guide.","expectedAnswer":"flock","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"A ____ of tourists gathered around the guide.","clozeAnswer":"flock","exampleTranslation":"一群遊客圍繞著導遊。","reference":{"eng":"flock","kk":"flɑːk","tense":"n.","ch":"[['（鳥、羊等）群'], ['（人）群眾']]","chEntries":["群","群眾"],"practiceMeaning":"一群遊客圍繞著導遊。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 flocc，意為「群」。其詞源不確定，但與原始日耳曼語 *flukaz（群）有關。核心語義指代「一群相似的動物」或「聚集的人」。構詞上，此字為單一詞根，無明顯字首字尾。此處為名詞用法，表示一群動物（尤指鳥類或羊）或聚集在一起的人。","definition":"a number of birds, sheep, or other animals gathered together; a group of people.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A flock of birds flew overhead.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一群鳥從頭頂飛過。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A flock of tourists gathered around the guide.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一群遊客圍繞著導遊。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"一群遊客圍繞著導遊。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4395,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u9::flour::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The baker used whole wheat ____ for the bread.","expectedAnswer":"flour","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The baker used whole wheat ____ for the bread.","clozeAnswer":"flour","exampleTranslation":"麵包師傅用全麥麵粉做麵包。","reference":{"eng":"flour","kk":"/ˈflaʊər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['麵粉', '粉']]","chEntries":["麵粉","粉"],"practiceMeaning":"麵包師傅用全麥麵粉做麵包。","analysis":"詞源自古法語 'flor de farine'，意為「麵粉中最精細的部分」（'flor' 意為花）。發音與 'flower' (花) 相同，兩者為同音異義詞。","definition":"a powder obtained by grinding grain, typically wheat, and used to make bread, cakes, and pastry.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"You need flour, eggs, and sugar to make a cake.\",\n    \"ch\": \"做蛋糕需要麵粉、雞蛋和糖。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The baker used whole wheat flour for the bread.\",\n    \"ch\": \"麵包師傅用全麥麵粉做麵包。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"麵包師傅用全麥麵粉做麵包。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6122,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::fluency::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His ____ in Spanish impressed the interviewers.","expectedAnswer":"fluency","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His ____ in Spanish impressed the interviewers.","clozeAnswer":"fluency","exampleTranslation":"他西班牙語的流暢度給面試官留下了深刻印象。","reference":{"eng":"fluency","kk":"ˈfluːənsi","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"流利\"  ],  [    \"流暢\"  ],  [    \"流利性\"  ]]","chEntries":["流利","流暢","流利性"],"practiceMeaning":"他西班牙語的流暢度給面試官留下了深刻印象。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 fluēns，是 fluere（流動）的現在分詞。構詞上，fluere 的核心語義是「流動」。此名詞表示說話或寫作時的流利、順暢，沒有停頓或困難。也可指事物或過程的流暢性。其語意演變是從具體的「流動」到抽象的「說話順暢」。","definition":"1. the ability to speak or write a language easily, smoothly, and expressively; 2. the quality of flowing easily or smoothly.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She speaks English with great fluency.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她能流利地說英語。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His fluency in Spanish impressed the interviewers.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他西班牙語的流暢度給面試官留下了深刻印象。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The fluency of the river's flow.\",\n    \"ch\": \"河流順暢的流動。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他西班牙語的流暢度給面試官留下了深刻印象。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3085,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::fluent::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His explanation was ____ and easy to understand.","expectedAnswer":"fluent","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His explanation was ____ and easy to understand.","clozeAnswer":"fluent","exampleTranslation":"他的解釋流暢且易於理解。","reference":{"eng":"fluent","kk":"/ˈfluːənt/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['流利的；流暢的'], ['（思想、表達）暢達的']]","chEntries":["流利的","流暢的","暢達的"],"practiceMeaning":"他的解釋流暢且易於理解。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'fluens'，'fluere' (to flow)。核心意義是「像水一樣流動」。\n1. 流利的；流暢的：指說話或寫作時，語言運用自如，沒有間斷或困難。\n2. （思想、表達）暢達的：指思想清晰，表達順暢，沒有阻礙。","definition":"1. able to speak or write a language easily, quickly, and well; 2. speaking or writing easily, smoothly, and clearly.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is fluent in three languages.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她精通三種語言。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His explanation was fluent and easy to understand.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的解釋流暢且易於理解。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他的解釋流暢且易於理解。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4688,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::fold::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He sat down on the ____-out chair.","expectedAnswer":"fold","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He sat down on the ____-out chair.","clozeAnswer":"fold","exampleTranslation":"他坐到折疊椅上。","reference":{"eng":"fold","kk":"/ˈfoʊld/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['摺痕'], ['（帳篷、椅子等）折疊式結構'], ['（羊的）圍欄']]","chEntries":["摺痕","折疊式結構","圍欄"],"practiceMeaning":"他坐到折疊椅上。","analysis":"名詞形式，指動詞 fold 的結果，即被摺疊的部分或結構。也指用來圍住羊群的柵欄，與動詞的「包圍」義有關。","definition":"1. A crease or pleat in something. 2. A folding structure, such as a chair or table, that can be collapsed for storage. 3. A pen or enclosure for sheep or other livestock.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was a fold in the paper where it had been creased.\",\n    \"ch\": \"紙上有一個被摺痕的地方。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He sat down on the fold-out chair.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他坐到折疊椅上。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他坐到折疊椅上。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5784,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::format::vt","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The software can ____ the hard drive for you.","expectedAnswer":"format","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The software can ____ the hard drive for you.","clozeAnswer":"format","exampleTranslation":"該軟體可以為您格式化硬碟。","reference":{"eng":"format","kk":"ˈfɔrmæt","tense":"vt.","ch":"[  [    \"格式化\"  ],  [    \"設計（版面）\"  ],  [    \"安排（程序）\"  ]]","chEntries":["格式化","設計","安排"],"practiceMeaning":"該軟體可以為您格式化硬碟。","analysis":"此字為及物動詞，源自拉丁語formare（形成；塑造）。formare來自forma（形式；形狀）。-at是拉丁語動詞字尾。因此，format的核心語義是「按照特定的形式或結構來組織或安排」。在電腦領域，尤指「格式化」磁碟，即準備其儲存資料。在印刷或出版領域，指「設計版面」。在活動或節目上，指「安排流程」。語意演變上，從「賦予形式」的廣泛概念，具體化到不同領域的「編排」或「設置」。","definition":"1. to arrange or present something in a particular form or style; 2. to prepare a computer disk so that data can be stored on it.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please format your essay according to the guidelines.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請根據指南格式化您的論文。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The software can format the hard drive for you.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該軟體可以為您格式化硬碟。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They formatted the conference schedule efficiently.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們有效地安排了會議日程。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該軟體可以為您格式化硬碟。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4385,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u9::freeze::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The government decided to ____ all foreign assets.","expectedAnswer":"freeze","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The government decided to ____ all foreign assets.","clozeAnswer":"freeze","exampleTranslation":"政府決定凍結所有外國資產。","reference":{"eng":"freeze","kk":"/friːz/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['結冰', '凝固'], ['凍結（溫度）'], ['凍結（存款、活動等）', '停止'], ['使（人）動彈不得', '嚇得呆住']]","chEntries":["結冰","凝固","凍結","停止","使動彈不得","嚇得呆住"],"practiceMeaning":"政府決定凍結所有外國資產。","analysis":"詞源自古英語 'frēosan'，意為「結冰」。核心概念是從液態轉為固態，引申至停止、靜止的狀態。亦可指因寒冷或恐懼而導致身體僵硬。","definition":"to become solid or turn into ice; to become very cold and turn into ice; to stop moving or become motionless, often because of fear or cold; to prevent money or other assets from being used.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Water freezes at 0 degrees Celsius.\",\n    \"ch\": \"水在攝氏零度時結冰。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government decided to freeze all foreign assets.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府決定凍結所有外國資產。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was frozen with fear.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他嚇得動彈不得。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"政府決定凍結所有外國資產。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4051,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::frequent::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There are ____ bus services to the city center.","expectedAnswer":"frequent","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There are ____ bus services to the city center.","clozeAnswer":"frequent","exampleTranslation":"到市中心的巴士班次很頻繁。","reference":{"eng":"frequent","kk":"/ˈfrikwənt/ (adj.) /frɪˈkwɛnt/ (v.)/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['頻繁的', '經常發生的']]","chEntries":["頻繁的","經常發生的"],"practiceMeaning":"到市中心的巴士班次很頻繁。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'frequens'，意為「擁擠的」、「頻繁的」。'frequens' 本身可能來自 'farcire' (to stuff, to fill)。核心是「密集」、「經常」。因此，'frequent' 指「經常發生的」或「發生的次數很多的」。","definition":"happening or doing something often","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"她經常探望祖母。\",\n    \"eng\": \"She makes frequent visits to her grandmother.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"到市中心的巴士班次很頻繁。\",\n    \"eng\": \"There are frequent bus services to the city center.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"到市中心的巴士班次很頻繁。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3911,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::frighten::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Don't try to ____ me with your threats.","expectedAnswer":"frighten","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Don't try to ____ me with your threats.","clozeAnswer":"frighten","exampleTranslation":"別想用你的威脅來嚇唬我。","reference":{"eng":"frighten","kk":"/ˈfraɪtn/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['使驚嚇', '嚇唬']]","chEntries":["使驚嚇","嚇唬"],"practiceMeaning":"別想用你的威脅來嚇唬我。","analysis":"由 'fright' (驚恐) 加上動詞後綴 '-en' 組成。核心是「導致驚恐」。指讓某人感到害怕、驚嚇。","definition":"to make someone afraid or anxious; fill with fear.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The loud thunder frightened the dog.\",\n    \"ch\": \"巨大的雷聲嚇壞了狗。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Don't try to frighten me with your threats.\",\n    \"ch\": \"別想用你的威脅來嚇唬我。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"別想用你的威脅來嚇唬我。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3155,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::funeral::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ procession moved slowly through the town.","expectedAnswer":"funeral","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ procession moved slowly through the town.","clozeAnswer":"funeral","exampleTranslation":"送葬隊伍緩慢地穿過城鎮。","reference":{"eng":"funeral","kk":"/ˈfjuːnərəl/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['葬禮；喪禮']]","chEntries":["葬禮","喪禮"],"practiceMeaning":"送葬隊伍緩慢地穿過城鎮。","analysis":"詞源來自拉丁語 'funus'，意為「喪禮，屍體」。'Funeral' 指的是為死者舉行的儀式，通常包括告別、埋葬或火化等環節。它是一個與死亡、哀悼和紀念相關的莊重儀式。","definition":"a ceremony for burying or cremating a dead person.","exampl