源自古英語 'gang' (旅程、行進)，後來演變為「一群人」。最初可能指一起工作或旅行的團體。現代用法多指由犯罪分子組成的非法組織（幫派），或指一群目標一致但有時帶有負面含義的人（如工頭帶領的團隊）。","definition":"a group of criminals who associate together; a group of people working or doing something together.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police are cracking down on street gangs.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警方正在嚴厲打擊街頭幫派。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A gang of workers arrived to repair the road.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一群工人來了，要修理道路。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"一群工人來了，要修理道路。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3219,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::gaze::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He gave her a long, lingering ____.","expectedAnswer":"gaze","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He gave her a long, lingering ____.","clozeAnswer":"gaze","exampleTranslation":"他給了她一個長久、流連的凝視。","reference":{"eng":"gaze","kk":"/ɡeɪz/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['凝視'], ['注視']]","chEntries":["凝視","注視"],"practiceMeaning":"他給了她一個長久、流連的凝視。","analysis":"名詞形式，指『凝視』或『注視』的行為。由動詞 'gaze' 衍生。","definition":"a steady look.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her gaze was fixed on the horizon.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的目光固定在地平線上。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He gave her a long, lingering gaze.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他給了她一個長久、流連的凝視。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他給了她一個長久、流連的凝視。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U41"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3157,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::generosity::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We were touched by the ____ of the donors.","expectedAnswer":"generosity","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We were touched by the ____ of the donors.","clozeAnswer":"generosity","exampleTranslation":"我們對捐助者的慷慨深受感動。","reference":{"eng":"generosity","kk":"/ˌdʒɛnəˈrɒsɪtɪ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['慷慨；大方'], ['（尤指對窮人）慷慨的捐贈']]","chEntries":["慷慨","大方","慷慨的捐贈"],"practiceMeaning":"我們對捐助者的慷慨深受感動。","analysis":"名詞，源自形容詞 'generous'。'Generosity' 是指樂於給予、分享或幫助他人的品質，特別是慷慨地付出金錢、時間或情感，且不求回報。它強調的是一種寬宏大量、無私的品格。","definition":"the quality of being kind and generous; the quality of being willing to give more of something, especially money, than is expected or needed.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her generosity in helping the homeless was admirable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她幫助無家可歸者的慷慨令人欽佩。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We were touched by the generosity of the donors.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們對捐助者的慷慨深受感動。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The generosity of spirit shown by the community was inspiring.\",\n    \"ch\": \"社區所展現的精神上的慷慨鼓舞人心。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們對捐助者的慷慨深受感動。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5402,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l2::geography::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Understanding the ____ of the region is crucial for trade.","expectedAnswer":"geography","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Understanding the ____ of the region is crucial for trade.","clozeAnswer":"geography","exampleTranslation":"了解該地區的地理對於貿易至關重要。","reference":{"eng":"geography","kk":"dʒiˈɒɡrəfi","tense":"n.","ch":"[['地理'], ['地理學']]","chEntries":["地理","地理學"],"practiceMeaning":"了解該地區的地理對於貿易至關重要。","analysis":"此字源自希臘語 geōgraphia，由 'gē' (earth) + 'graphein' (to write) 組成，原意是「地球的描寫」。核心語意是「對地球表面及其現象的學術研究和描述」。","definition":"1. the study of the physical features of the earth's surface, including landforms, climate, population distribution, etc.; 2. the physical features of an area.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She excelled in geography and history at school.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在學校的地理和歷史科目上表現優異。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Understanding the geography of the region is crucial for trade.\",\n    \"ch\": \"了解該地區的地理對於貿易至關重要。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"了解該地區的地理對於貿易至關重要。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3292,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::germ::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of an idea began to form in his mind.","expectedAnswer":"germ","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of an idea began to form in his mind.","clozeAnswer":"germ","exampleTranslation":"一個想法的萌芽開始在他腦中形成。","reference":{"eng":"germ","kk":"/dʒɜːm/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['病菌；細菌'], ['（不良思想、情感等的）萌芽；發端']]","chEntries":["病菌","細菌","萌芽","發端"],"practiceMeaning":"一個想法的萌芽開始在他腦中形成。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'germen' (發芽，種子)。原指植物的萌芽，後轉指引起疾病的微生物（細菌、病毒等），引申至抽象事物，指不良思想、情緒或情況的最初階段或萌芽。","definition":"1. a microscopic living organism, especially a bacterium, virus, or fungus, that can cause disease; 2. the seed or beginning of an idea or feeling.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Washing your hands helps to kill harmful germs.\",\n    \"ch\": \"洗手有助於殺死有害的病菌。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The germ of an idea began to form in his mind.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一個想法的萌芽開始在他腦中形成。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"一個想法的萌芽開始在他腦中形成。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4592,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::global-warming::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Reducing carbon emissions is crucial to combat ____.","expectedAnswer":"global warming","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Reducing carbon emissions is crucial to combat ____.","clozeAnswer":"global warming","exampleTranslation":"減少碳排放對於應對全球暖化至關重要。","reference":{"eng":"global warming","kk":"/ˈɡloʊbəl ˈwɔːrmɪŋ/","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['全球暖化']]","chEntries":["全球暖化"],"practiceMeaning":"減少碳排放對於應對全球暖化至關重要。","analysis":"此片語由 'global' (全球的) 和 'warming' (暖化) 組成。 'global' 源自拉丁語 'globus' (ball)，指涉及整個地球。 'warming' 是動詞 'warm' (變暖) 的現在分詞形式。此片語專指由於人類活動（主要是燃燒化石燃料）導致大氣中溫室氣體濃度增加，進而引起的地球表面平均溫度上升的現象。","definition":"1. the gradual heating of Earth's surface, oceans, and atmosphere, primarily caused by human activities, such as the burning of fossil fuels, that increase the level of greenhouse gases in the atmosphere.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Scientists are concerned about the effects of global warming.\",\n    \"ch\": \"科學家們對全球暖化的影響感到擔憂。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Reducing carbon emissions is crucial to combat global warming.\",\n    \"ch\": \"減少碳排放對於應對全球暖化至關重要。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"減少碳排放對於應對全球暖化至關重要。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4590,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::go-stale::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"After a while, the conversation began to ____.","expectedAnswer":"go stale","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"After a while, the conversation began to ____.","clozeAnswer":"go stale","exampleTranslation":"過了一會兒，談話開始變得乏味了。","reference":{"eng":"go stale","kk":"/ɡoʊ steɪl/","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['（食物）變質', '不新鮮'], ['（想法、興趣等）變得陳舊', '乏味']]","chEntries":["變質","不新鮮","變得陳舊","乏味"],"practiceMeaning":"過了一會兒，談話開始變得乏味了。","analysis":"此片語由 'go' (變得) 和 'stale' (不新鮮的、陳舊的) 組成。 'stale' 源自古法語 'estale' (old)。\n    1. （食物）變質、不新鮮：指食物失去原有的新鮮度和風味，不再適合食用。\n    2. （想法、興趣等）變得陳舊、乏味：指事物失去新意或吸引力，變得單調無聊。","definition":"1. become no longer fresh or appealing; become old-fashioned or boring.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The bread will go stale if you don't eat it soon.\",\n    \"ch\": \"如果你不快點吃，麵包就會變不新鮮。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"After a while, the conversation began to go stale.\",\n    \"ch\": \"過了一會兒，談話開始變得乏味了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"過了一會兒，談話開始變得乏味了。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4062,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::golf::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This is a difficult ____ course.","expectedAnswer":"golf","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This is a difficult ____ course.","clozeAnswer":"golf","exampleTranslation":"這是一個很有挑戰性的高爾夫球場。","reference":{"eng":"golf","kk":"/ɡɔlf/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['高爾夫球運動']]","chEntries":["高爾夫球運動"],"practiceMeaning":"這是一個很有挑戰性的高爾夫球場。","analysis":"詞源有爭議，但普遍認為源自荷蘭語 'kolf' 或 'kolve'，意為「球棒」。此詞在16世紀從荷蘭傳入蘇格蘭，演變成 'golf'。核心是使用球桿擊球的運動。","definition":"a game played by hitting a small ball into a series of holes on a course, using clubs","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他每個週末都打高爾夫球。\",\n    \"eng\": \"He plays golf every weekend.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個很有挑戰性的高爾夫球場。\",\n    \"eng\": \"This is a difficult golf course.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是一個很有挑戰性的高爾夫球場。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3087,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::grateful::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She felt ____ for the opportunity.","expectedAnswer":"grateful","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She felt ____ for the opportunity.","clozeAnswer":"grateful","exampleTranslation":"她對這個機會感到感激。","reference":{"eng":"grateful","kk":"/ˈɡreɪtfl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['感激的；感謝的']]","chEntries":["感激的","感謝的"],"practiceMeaning":"她對這個機會感到感激。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'gratus' (pleasing, thankful)。核心意義是「令人愉悅的」或「感激的」。\n1. 感激的；感謝的：指對他人給予的幫助、恩惠或善意感到高興和感激。","definition":"1. feeling or showing thanks to someone; 2. thankful.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I am deeply grateful for your help.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我對您的幫助深表感激。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She felt grateful for the opportunity.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對這個機會感到感激。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她對這個機會感到感激。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3090,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::guarantee::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need a ____ that the work will be completed on time.","expectedAnswer":"guarantee","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need a ____ that the work will be completed on time.","clozeAnswer":"guarantee","exampleTranslation":"我們需要一個關於工作能準時完成的保證。","reference":{"eng":"guarantee","kk":"/ˌɡærənˈtiː/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['保證；擔保'], ['保證書']]","chEntries":["保證","擔保","保證書"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要一個關於工作能準時完成的保證。","analysis":"源自古法語 'garantie' (warrant, security)。是 'guarantee' 動詞的名詞形式。指「保證」的承諾或憑證。\n1. 保證；擔保：指對品質、條件或結果的承諾，給予對方信心。\n2. 保證書：指書面文件，證明某事物的品質、可靠性或提供的保障。","definition":"1. a formal promise that something will happen or that something is of the quality stated; 2. a written promise by a company to repair or change a product if it is faulty.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The phone comes with a one-year guarantee.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這款手機附有一年保固。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need a guarantee that the work will be completed on time.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要一個關於工作能準時完成的保證。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要一個關於工作能準時完成的保證。","sourceName":"字彙王、龍騰課本","unitName":"U39、L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3091,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::guardian::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The statue served as a ____ of the city gate.","expectedAnswer":"guardian","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The statue served as a ____ of the city gate.","clozeAnswer":"guardian","exampleTranslation":"這座雕像作為城門的守護者。","reference":{"eng":"guardian","kk":"/ˈɡɑːrdiən/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['守護者；保護者'], ['監護人']]","chEntries":["守護者","保護者","監護人"],"practiceMeaning":"這座雕像作為城門的守護者。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'guardia' (guard)，經由古法語 'gardien' 演變而來。核心意義是「看守」或「保護」。\n1. 守護者；保護者：指保護某人或某物免受傷害的人。\n2. 監護人：指依法負責照顧未成年人或無行為能力者的法定代理人。","definition":"1. a person who is legally responsible for the care of someone who is unable to care for themselves, such as a child; 2. a person who protects or watches over someone or something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is the legal guardian of her younger sister.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是她妹妹的法定監護人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The statue served as a guardian of the city gate.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座雕像作為城門的守護者。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這座雕像作為城門的守護者。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4546,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::guidance::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The teacher provided ____ on how to write the essay.","expectedAnswer":"guidance","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The teacher provided ____ on how to write the essay.","clozeAnswer":"guidance","exampleTranslation":"老師就如何寫論文提供了指導。","reference":{"eng":"guidance","kk":"/ˈɡaɪdəns/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['指導', '引導'], ['建議', '意見']]","chEntries":["指導","引導","建議","意見"],"practiceMeaning":"老師就如何寫論文提供了指導。","analysis":"由 'guide' (指導) 加上名詞字尾 '-ance' (表示狀態、行為) 構成。 'guide' 源自古法語 'guider'，最終源自日耳曼語，意為 'to show the way' (指引方向)。 'guidance' 指提供方向、建議或幫助的行為或過程。","definition":"1. advice or information aimed at resolving a problem or difficulty.; 2. the process of showing or telling someone the way to a place or destination.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She received excellent guidance from her mentor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她從導師那裡得到了極好的指導。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The teacher provided guidance on how to write the essay.\",\n    \"ch\": \"老師就如何寫論文提供了指導。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need clear guidance on this matter.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要關於這件事的明確指導。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"老師就如何寫論文提供了指導。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5048,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::habitat::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Coral reefs are a unique marine ____.","expectedAnswer":"habitat","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Coral reefs are a unique marine ____.","clozeAnswer":"habitat","exampleTranslation":"珊瑚礁是獨特的海洋棲息地。","reference":{"eng":"habitat","kk":"ˈhæbɪtæt","tense":"n.","ch":"[['棲息地'], ['生境'], ['（人、動物、植物）的自然環境']]","chEntries":["棲息地","生境","的自然環境"],"practiceMeaning":"珊瑚礁是獨特的海洋棲息地。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語habitare，意為「居住」，來自habere（擁有）。habitare的現在分詞為habitans（居住者）。habitat 的核心語意是「生物的自然棲息地或居住場所」。在生態學中，指特定生物賴以生存的環境。OCR 掃描時可能將 'h' 誤判為 'li'，或 't' 誤判為 'i'。此處修正為 habitat。","definition":"the natural home or environment of an animal, plant, or other organism.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Deforestation destroys the habitat of many species.\",\n    \"ch\": \"森林砍伐破壞了許多物種的棲息地。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Coral reefs are a unique marine habitat.\",\n    \"ch\": \"珊瑚礁是獨特的海洋棲息地。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"珊瑚礁是獨特的海洋棲息地。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3223,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::halt::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The unexpected ____ caused a traffic jam.","expectedAnswer":"halt","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The unexpected ____ caused a traffic jam.","clozeAnswer":"halt","exampleTranslation":"意外的停車造成了交通堵塞。","reference":{"eng":"halt","kk":"/hɔlt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['停止'], ['停頓']]","chEntries":["停止","停頓"],"practiceMeaning":"意外的停車造成了交通堵塞。","analysis":"名詞形式，指『停止』的行為或狀態。由動詞 'halt' 衍生。","definition":"an action of stopping or ceasing.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was a brief halt in the proceedings.\",\n    \"ch\": \"會議程序中有短暫的停頓。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The unexpected halt caused a traffic jam.\",\n    \"ch\": \"意外的停車造成了交通堵塞。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"意外的停車造成了交通堵塞。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U41"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5574,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::handle::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Please ____ the fragile items with care.","expectedAnswer":"handle","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Please ____ the fragile items with care.","clozeAnswer":"handle","exampleTranslation":"請小心處理易碎物品。","reference":{"eng":"handle","kk":"ˈhændl","tense":"v.","ch":"[['處理'], ['應付'], ['操作'], ['觸摸'], ['交易']]","chEntries":["處理","應付","操作","觸摸","交易"],"practiceMeaning":"請小心處理易碎物品。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 \"handlian\"，意為 \"to touch with the hands, to manage\"（用手觸摸，管理），來自 \"hand\"（手）。\"handlian\" 的原始語義是「用手進行的動作」。因此，\"handle\" 的核心語義是「用手接觸、操作或控制」。引申義則非常廣泛：指「處理、應付」（manage or deal with），例如「處理問題」；指「經營、交易」（deal in），例如「處理商品」；指「對待」（treat），例如「小心處理易碎品」；也可用於指「觸摸」或「拿取」。","definition":"1. To touch, hold, or move (something) with the hands; 2. To deal with or manage (a situation or problem); 3. To buy and sell (goods); 4. To treat or behave towards (a person or thing) in a certain way.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She can handle the pressure very well.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她能很好地應付壓力。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please handle the fragile items with care.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請小心處理易碎物品。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The shop handles a wide range of products.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家店經營各式各樣的產品。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He refused to handle the delicate negotiations.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他拒絕處理這些敏感的談判。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"請小心處理易碎物品。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4211,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::handsome::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They bought a ____ antique desk.","expectedAnswer":"handsome","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They bought a ____ antique desk.","clozeAnswer":"handsome","exampleTranslation":"他們買了一張漂亮的古董書桌。","reference":{"eng":"handsome","kk":"/ˈhænsəm/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['英俊的；漂亮的（用於男性）'], ['（物體、建築）好看的；體面的'], ['（金額）相當可觀的；豐厚的']]","chEntries":["英俊的","漂亮的","好看的","體面的","相當可觀的","豐厚的"],"practiceMeaning":"他們買了一張漂亮的古董書桌。","analysis":"詞源不確定，可能與古英語 'hæðnes'（健康）有關，強調“健壯”的特質。1. “英俊的”指外表吸引人，通常用於男性。2. “好看的；體面的”形容物體或建築物外觀令人愉悅。3. “相當可觀的；豐厚的”是抽象意義，指金額大，令人滿意。","definition":"1. good-looking (esp. of a man); 2. good in appearance or pleasing to look at (esp. of things or buildings); 3. (of a sum of money) large or impressive.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a tall, handsome man.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一位高大英俊的男人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They bought a handsome antique desk.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們買了一張漂亮的古董書桌。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She received a handsome inheritance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她繼承了一筆可觀的遺產。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們買了一張漂亮的古董書桌。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3224,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::handwriting::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":