584,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::harbor-a-grudge-against::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It's unhealthy to ____ someone for so long.","expectedAnswer":"harbor a grudge against","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It's unhealthy to ____ someone for so long.","clozeAnswer":"harbor a grudge against","exampleTranslation":"對一個人懷有長久的怨恨是不健康的。","reference":{"eng":"harbor a grudge against","kk":"/ˈhɑːrbər ə ˈɡrʌdʒ əˈɡɛnst/","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['對…懷有怨恨']]","chEntries":["對…懷有怨恨"],"practiceMeaning":"對一個人懷有長久的怨恨是不健康的。","analysis":"此片語由 'harbor' (懷有、藏有), 'a grudge' (怨恨), 和 'against' (針對) 組成。 'harbor' 源自古英語 'herebeorg' (shelter)，引申為心中藏匿。 'grudge' 指因過去的不滿或不公而產生的長期怨恨。此片語描述心中長期存有對某人的不滿和敵意。","definition":"1. to feel a strong feeling of anger or dislike towards someone for something they have done in the past.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He still harbors a grudge against his former business partner.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他仍然對他以前的生意夥伴懷有怨恨。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's unhealthy to harbor a grudge against someone for so long.\",\n    \"ch\": \"對一個人懷有長久的怨恨是不健康的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"對一個人懷有長久的怨恨是不健康的。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3296,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::hardship::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The community offered support to those suffering from financial ____.","expectedAnswer":"hardship","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The community offered support to those suffering from financial ____.","clozeAnswer":"hardship","exampleTranslation":"社區向那些遭受經濟困苦的人們提供了支持。","reference":{"eng":"hardship","kk":"/ˈhɑːrdʃɪp/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['艱苦；困苦；苦難']]","chEntries":["艱苦","困苦","苦難"],"practiceMeaning":"社區向那些遭受經濟困苦的人們提供了支持。","analysis":"由 'hard' (困難的) 加上 '-ship' (狀態，性質) 後綴構成。指經歷極度艱難、匱乏或痛苦的狀況。","definition":"severe suffering or privation.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They faced many hardships during the war.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們在戰爭中經歷了許多艱辛。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The community offered support to those suffering from financial hardship.\",\n    \"ch\": \"社區向那些遭受經濟困苦的人們提供了支持。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"社區向那些遭受經濟困苦的人們提供了支持。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5479,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::harmony::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The choir sang in perfect ____.","expectedAnswer":"harmony","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The choir sang in perfect ____.","clozeAnswer":"harmony","exampleTranslation":"合唱團以完美的和聲演唱。","reference":{"eng":"harmony","kk":"ˈhɑrməni","tense":"n.","ch":"[['和諧'], ['融洽'], ['和聲']]","chEntries":["和諧","融洽","和聲"],"practiceMeaning":"合唱團以完美的和聲演唱。","analysis":"此字源自希臘語 'harmonia'（結合、協調、和聲），後來經由拉丁語 'harmonia' 傳入古英語 'harmoie'，再到中古英語 'harmony'。'Harmonia' 本身來自 'harmos'（連接、鎖扣）。在音樂上，它指「不同音高並存時產生的悅耳聲音」。在社會和人際關係上，它引申為「各方之間協調、融洽、沒有衝突的狀態」。核心語意是「各部分組合在一起時產生的協調與一致」。","definition":"1. The quality of forming a pleasing and consistent whole.; 2. Agreement or concord; peaceful relations.; 3. (Music) The combination of notes played or sung simultaneously to produce a pleasing effect.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The two nations lived in harmony for many years.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這兩個國家和諧相處了許多年。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The choir sang in perfect harmony.\",\n    \"ch\": \"合唱團以完美的和聲演唱。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to find a way to live in harmony with nature.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要找到一種與大自然和諧共處的方式。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"合唱團以完美的和聲演唱。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3092,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::harsh::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The desert climate is ____.","expectedAnswer":"harsh","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The desert climate is ____.","clozeAnswer":"harsh","exampleTranslation":"沙漠氣候十分嚴酷。","reference":{"eng":"harsh","kk":"/hɑːrʃ/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['嚴厲的；殘酷的'], ['刺耳的；粗糙的'], ['嚴酷的（天氣、條件）']]","chEntries":["嚴厲的","殘酷的","刺耳的","粗糙的","嚴酷的"],"practiceMeaning":"沙漠氣候十分嚴酷。","analysis":"起源不明，可能與古挪威語 'harskr' (dry) 有關。核心意義是「不舒適」或「令人不快」。\n1. 嚴厲的；殘酷的：指對待人或事物的方式不寬容、不友好、或過於嚴苛。\n2. 刺耳的；粗糙的：指聲音不悅耳，或觸感粗糙，令人不適。\n3. 嚴酷的（天氣、條件）：指天氣惡劣，環境艱難，難以忍受。","definition":"1. unpleasantly rough or shocking to the senses; 2. severe or cruel; 3. (of a sound or voice) unpleasantly harsh or grating.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The teacher gave him harsh criticism.\",\n    \"ch\": \"老師對他進行了嚴厲的批評。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The desert climate is harsh.\",\n    \"ch\": \"沙漠氣候十分嚴酷。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The noise was harsh and loud.\",\n    \"ch\": \"噪音刺耳而響亮。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"沙漠氣候十分嚴酷。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5480,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::harvest::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This year's ____ was particularly good.","expectedAnswer":"harvest","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This year's ____ was particularly good.","clozeAnswer":"harvest","exampleTranslation":"今年的收成特別好。","reference":{"eng":"harvest","kk":"ˈhɑrvəst","tense":"n.","ch":"[['收成'], ['收穫'], ['收割']]","chEntries":["收成","收穫","收割"],"practiceMeaning":"今年的收成特別好。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 'hærfest'，與許多日耳曼語族語言（如荷蘭語 'herfst'，德語 'Herbst'）中表示「秋天」的詞相關。最初，'harvest' 指的是「秋季」，因為這是農作物收成的季節。隨著時間演變，'harvest' 的主要語意轉移到了「收成」或「收穫」這個動作和結果上，也保留了「秋季」或「收割季節」的含義。核心語意是「農作物成熟並被收割的季節或過程」。","definition":"1. The process or period of gathering in crops.; 2. The crops gathered (esp. during an autumn harvest).; 3. The season when ripened crops are gathered.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The farmers rejoiced at the abundant harvest.\",\n    \"ch\": \"農民們為豐收而歡欣鼓舞。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This year's harvest was particularly good.\",\n    \"ch\": \"今年的收成特別好。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They celebrated the harvest festival.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們慶祝了豐收節。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"今年的收成特別好。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":