對未來抱有樂觀的期望，或表示有成功的可能。","definition":"1. feeling or inspiring optimism about a future event; 2. having or characterized by hope.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is hopeful about her job prospects.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對自己的工作前景感到樂觀。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's a hopeful sign for the economy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是經濟的一個好兆頭。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They are hopeful that a solution can be found.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們對找到解決方案抱有希望。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是經濟的一個好兆頭。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4631,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::horrible::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The food tasted ____.","expectedAnswer":"horrible","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The food tasted ____.","clozeAnswer":"horrible","exampleTranslation":"這食物嚐起來糟透了。","reference":{"eng":"horrible","kk":"/ˈhɔːrəbəl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['可怕的'], ['駭人的'], ['糟糕的']]","chEntries":["可怕的","駭人的","糟糕的"],"practiceMeaning":"這食物嚐起來糟透了。","analysis":"由 'horror' (恐怖) + '-ible' (能夠...的) 組成。此字描述事物引起強烈恐懼、厭惡或不適感，其程度比 'scary' 更深。也可引申形容非常糟糕、令人難受的體驗。","definition":"causing or likely to cause horror; shocking; extremely unpleasant.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was a horrible accident.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那是一場可怕的事故。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The food tasted horrible.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這食物嚐起來糟透了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They heard a horrible scream in the night.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們在夜裡聽到一聲駭人的尖叫。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這食物嚐起來糟透了。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5129,"wordRef":"字彙王::u62::housing::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They are responsible for the ____ of the refugees.","expectedAnswer":"housing","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They are responsible for the ____ of the refugees.","clozeAnswer":"housing","exampleTranslation":"他們負責難民的安置。","reference":{"eng":"housing","kk":"ˈhaʊzɪŋ","tense":"n.","ch":"[['房屋'], ['住房'], ['住宅（的）']]","chEntries":["房屋","住房","住宅"],"practiceMeaning":"他們負責難民的安置。","analysis":"此字是動詞 house（提供住所、容納）的現在分詞（gerund 或 present participle），後轉為名詞。house 源自古英語 hūs（房子），與原始日耳曼語 *hūsan- 相關。核心語意為「提供住所的行為或狀態」，引申為「集合的房屋」、「住房供給」或「建築材料（如外殼、框架）」。","definition":"houses and apartments considered collectively; accommodation; a protective casing or covering.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The city is facing a severe housing shortage.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座城市面臨嚴重的住房短缺。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They are responsible for the housing of the refugees.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們負責難民的安置。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們負責難民的安置。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U62"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4637,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::hunger::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He has a ____ for knowledge.","expectedAnswer":"hunger","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He has a ____ for knowledge.","clozeAnswer":"hunger","exampleTranslation":"他對知識有強烈的渴望。","reference":{"eng":"hunger","kk":"/ˈhʌŋɡər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['飢餓'], ['渴望'], ['熱望']]","chEntries":["飢餓","渴望","熱望"],"practiceMeaning":"他對知識有強烈的渴望。","analysis":"源自古英語 'hungor'，與「飢餓」的生理感受相關。核心是對食物的強烈需求。引申義指對某事物（知識、成功、權力等）的強烈渴望，這種渴望的程度類似於生理上的飢餓。","definition":"a strong desire or craving, especially for food; a strong desire for something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The child cried from hunger.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子因飢餓而哭泣。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has a hunger for knowledge.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對知識有強烈的渴望。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The hunger for power is a dangerous thing.\",\n    \"ch\": \"對權力的渴望是一件危險的事。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他對知識有強烈的渴望。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6123,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::hypothesis::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The scientist tested the ____ through experiments.","expectedAnswer":"hypothesis","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The scientist tested the ____ through experiments.","clozeAnswer":"hypothesis","exampleTranslation":"科學家通過實驗來驗證這個假說。","reference":{"eng":"hypothesis","kk":"haɪˈpɑːθəsɪs","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"假設\"  ],  [    \"假說\"  ],  [    \"設想\"  ]]","chEntries":["假設","假說","設想"],"practiceMeaning":"科學家通過實驗來驗證這個假說。","analysis":"此字源自希臘語 hypothesis，由 hypo-（在……下面；次要的）和 thesis（放置；論點；主張）組成。hypo- 意為「在下面」，thesis 意為「放置；主張」。因此，hypothesis 的核心語義是「放在……下面做基礎的主張」，即一個初步的、待驗證的解釋或主張。此名詞常用於科學研究，指對現象的初步解釋，有待實驗驗證。其語意演變是從「放在下面」到「作為基礎的論點」。","definition":"A supposition or proposed explanation made on the basis of limited evidence as a starting point for further investigation.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We formed a hypothesis about the cause of the disease.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們對疾病的成因提出了一個假設。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The scientist tested the hypothesis through experiments.\",\n    \"ch\": \"科學家通過實驗來驗證這個假說。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is just a hypothesis, not a proven fact.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這只是一個假設，不是已證實的事實。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"科學家通過實驗來驗證這個假說。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3227,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::idol::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ancient civilization worshipped an ____ of the sun god.","expectedAnswer":"idol","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ancient civilization worshipped an ____ of the sun god.","clozeAnswer":"idol","exampleTranslation":"古代文明崇拜太陽神的偶像。","reference":{"eng":"idol","kk":"/ˈaɪdl/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['偶像'], ['崇拜對象'], ['假神']]","chEntries":["偶像","崇拜對象","假神"],"practiceMeaning":"古代文明崇拜太陽神的偶像。","analysis":"詞源來自希臘文 'eidolon'，意為『影像』、『肖像』。引申為被崇拜的形象，可以是宗教上的神像（假神），也可以是受大眾熱愛和追捧的文化或個人人物（流行偶像）。","definition":"1. an image or representation of a god used as an object of worship; 2. a person or thing that is admired, loved, or revered.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Many teenagers consider pop stars their idols.\",\n    \"ch\": \"許多青少年將流行歌星視為他們的偶像。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The ancient civilization worshipped an idol of the sun god.\",\n    \"ch\": \"古代文明崇拜太陽神的偶像。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"古代文明崇拜太陽神的偶像。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U41"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3164,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::ignorance::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His comments revealed his ____ about the topic.","expectedAnswer":"ignorance","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His comments revealed his ____ about the topic.","clozeAnswer":"ignorance","exampleTranslation":"他的評論顯示了他對這個話題的無知。","reference":{"eng":"ignorance","kk":"/ˈɪɡnərəns/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['無知；缺乏知識'], ['（對某事的）不知情；無知']]","chEntries":["無知","缺乏知識","不知情"],"practiceMeaning":"他的評論顯示了他對這個話題的無知。","analysis":"名詞，源自形容詞 'ignorant'。'Ignorance' 指的是缺乏知識、信息或理解的狀態。它可以是對廣泛領域的普遍無知，也可以是對特定情況、事實或問題的不知情。這種無知可能是有意為之，也可能是由於缺乏接觸或學習機會。","definition":"1. lack of knowledge or information; 2. a lack of acquaintance with or understanding of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Ignorance of the law is no excuse.\",\n    \"ch\": \"不知法律是無法作為藉口的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His comments revealed his ignorance about the topic.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的評論顯示了他對這個話題的無知。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The project aims to combat ignorance about climate change.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該項目旨在消除人們對氣候變化的無知。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他的評論顯示了他對這個話題的無知。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3165,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::ignorant::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Some people are ____ of the facts.","expectedAnswer":"ignorant","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Some people are ____ of the facts.","clozeAnswer":"ignorant","exampleTranslation":"有些人對事實一無所知。","reference":{"eng":"ignorant","kk":"/ˈɪɡnərənt/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['無知的；缺乏知識的'], ['（對某事）不知情的']]","chEntries":["無知的","缺乏知識的","不知情的"],"practiceMeaning":"有些人對事實一無所知。","analysis":"詞源來自拉丁語 'ignorans'，意為「不知道的」，'ignorare'（不知道）。'Ignorant' 形容的是一個人缺乏必要的知識、信息或理解。它可以指普遍缺乏教育，也可以指對某特定情況、事實或問題不了解。有時也帶有不禮貌或粗魯的含義，指未受過良好教育或缺乏禮儀。","definition":"1. lacking knowledge or information; uneducated; 2. not aware of or concerned about something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He remained ignorant of the danger he was in.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對自己身處的危險毫無所知。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Some people are ignorant of the facts.\",\n    \"ch\": \"有些人對事實一無所知。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The teacher warned the students against being ignorant of current events.\",\n    \"ch\": \"老師告誡學生不要對時事無知。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"有些人對事實一無所知。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3166,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::ignore::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We cannot ____ the environmental consequences of our actions.","expectedAnswer":"ignore","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We cannot ____ the environmental consequences of our actions.","clozeAnswer":"ignore","exampleTranslation":"我們不能忽視我們行動對環境造成的後果。","reference":{"eng":"ignore","kk":"/ɪɡˈnɔːr/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['故意不理睬；忽視'], ['忽略；不顧（事實、忠告等）']]","chEntries":["故意不理睬","忽視","忽略","不顧"],"practiceMeaning":"我們不能忽視我們行動對環境造成的後果。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'ignorare'，意為「不知道，不知道」。'Ignore' 指的是故意不注意、不回應或不理睬某人、某事或某個事實。這種行為可能源於不感興趣、不認可、或者試圖迴避。它與「ignorance」（無知）在詞源上有關，但 'ignore' 更強調主動的「不予理會」。","definition":"1. refuse to take notice of or acknowledge; disregard; 2. deliberately pay no attention to.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She tried to talk to him, but he ignored her.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她試圖和他講話，但他卻不理她。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We cannot ignore the environmental consequences of our actions.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們不能忽視我們行動對環境造成的後果。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He ignored the warning signs and continued driving.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他無視警告標誌，繼續開車。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們不能忽視我們行動對環境造成的後果。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6174,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::illusion::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He lives under the ____ that he is rich.","expectedAnswer":"illusion","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He lives under the ____ that he is rich.","clozeAnswer":"illusion","exampleTranslation":"他活在自己是富翁的幻想中。","reference":{"eng":"illusion","kk":"ɪˈluːʒən","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"幻覺\"  ],  [    \"錯覺\"  ],  [    \"幻想\"  ],  [    \"海市蜃樓\"  ]]","chEntries":["幻覺","錯覺","幻想","海市蜃樓"],"practiceMeaning":"他活在自己是富翁的幻想中。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 illūsiōnem，是動詞 illudere「欺騙、嘲弄」的名詞化。illudere 由 in- (in, into) + lūdere (to play, mock) 組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 in-「進入」和 lūdere「玩弄、嘲弄」是其核心語意來源。作為名詞，其核心語義是「一種由感官誤解或心理作用產生的虛假感知」，即「幻覺」或「錯覺」。詞源中的「玩弄、嘲弄」引申為「欺騙」，進而產生「虛假的感知」。","definition":"1. a false idea or belief; 2. the state of being deceived; 3. a thing that is or is likely to become or prove false; 4. a deceptive appearance or impression.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The magician created the illusion that he had disappeared.\",\n    \"ch\": \"魔術師製造了他消失的幻覺。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He lives under the illusion that he is rich.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他活在自己是富翁的幻想中。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Mirages are optical illusions.\",\n    \"ch\": \"海市蜃樓是光學錯覺。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company's success was an illusion; they were close to bankruptcy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司的成功是假象；他們離破產不遠了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他活在自己是富翁的幻想中。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3932,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::immediate::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ family gathered at the hospital.","expectedAnswer":"immediate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ family gathered at the hospital.","clozeAnswer":"immediate","exampleTranslation":"直系親屬聚集在醫院。","reference":{"eng":"immediate","kk":"/ɪˈmiːdiət/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['立即的', '即刻的'], ['緊鄰的', '直接的']]","chEntries":["立即的","即刻的","緊鄰的","直接的"],"practiceMeaning":"直系親屬聚集在醫院。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'immediatus'，由 'in-' (意為「不」) 和 'mediatus' (意為「中間的」) 組成。原意是「沒有中間步驟的」，引申為「立刻發生的」或「緊鄰的」。","definition":"1. happening or done at once; instant; 2. happening or done right after something else, with no delay; 3. next to or very close to someone or something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need an immediate response to this crisis.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要對這次危機做出立即的回應。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The immediate family gathered at the hospital.\",\n    \"ch\": \"直系親屬聚集在醫院。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was no immediate danger.\",\n    \"ch\": \"沒有立即的危險。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"直系親屬聚集在醫院。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5842,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::implement::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This is a versatile kitchen ____.","expectedAnswer":"implement","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This is a versatile kitchen ____.","clozeAnswer":"implement","exampleTranslation":"這是一個多功能的廚房器具。","reference":{"eng":"implement","kk":"ˈɪmplɪmənt","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"工具\"  ],  [    \"器具\"  ],  [    \"裝備\"  ],  [    \"用具\"  ]]","chEntries":["工具","器具","裝備","用具"],"practiceMeaning":"這是一個多功能的廚房器具。","analysis":"此名詞形式源自拉丁語 'implementum'，意為「填補」、「完成」的工具或手段。其語源與動詞形式相同，都與「填充」、「完成」有關。作為名詞，'implement' 指用於完成特定工作或任務的工具、器具、裝置或設備。它強調的是一種「用來達成目的的實體工具」。例如，也可指「農具」或「手術用具」。","definition":"1. A tool or utensil used for a particular purpose.; 2. Equipment or device.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He bought new gardening implements.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他購買了新的園藝工具。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a versatile kitchen implement.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個多功能的廚房器具。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company provides its employees with the necessary implements.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司為員工提供必要的設備。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A surgeon's implements must be sterilized.\",\n    \"ch\": \"外科醫生的手術用具必須消毒。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是一個多功能的廚房器具。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6175,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::implication::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of the new policy on employment is uncertain.","expectedAnswer":"implication","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of the new policy on employment is uncertain.","clozeAnswer":"implication","exampleTranslation":"新政策對就業的影響尚不確定。","reference":{"eng":"implication","kk":"ˌɪmplɪˈkeɪʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"暗示\"  ],  [    \"含義\"  ],  [    \"牽連\"  ],  [    \"牽涉\"  ]]","chEntries":["暗示","含義","牽連","牽涉"],"practiceMeaning":"新政策對就業的影響尚不確定。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 implicatiōnem，是動詞 implicare「捲入、包含」的名詞化。implicare 由 in- (in, into) + plicare (to fold) 組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 in-「進入」和 plicare「折疊、捲入」是其核心語意來源。作為名詞，其核心語義是由動詞 implicate「暗示、牽連」名詞化而來，指「間接表達的意義」或「某事所涉及或牽連的範圍」。詞源中的「折疊、捲入」引申為「隱藏、暗示」和「牽連、涉及」。","definition":"1. the conclusion that can be drawn from something, although it is not directly stated; 2. the involvement of someone or something in a crime or other         wrongdoing; 3. a likely consequence or effect of an action or situation.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The implication of his words was clear.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他言語的含義很清楚。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The implication of the new policy on employment is uncertain.\",\n    \"ch\": \"新政策對就業的影響尚不確定。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His implication in the scandal damaged his reputation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在此醜聞中的牽連損害了他的聲譽。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The results have important implications for future research.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這些結果對未來的研究具有重要的含義。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"新政策對就業的影響尚不確定。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3167,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::impose::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The government decided to ____ a new tax on luxury goods.","expectedAnswer":"impose","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The government decided to ____ a new tax on luxury goods.","clozeAnswer":"impose","exampleTranslation":"政府決定對奢侈品徵收新稅。","reference":{"eng":"impose","kk":"/ɪmˈpoʊz/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['強加；硬塞'], ['強制實施；推行']]","chEntries":["強加","硬塞","強制實施","推行"],"practiceMeaning":"政府決定對奢侈品徵收新稅。","analysis":"詞源來自拉丁語 'imponere'，意為「放置，加在...之上」，由 'in-'（在...之上）+ 'ponere'（放置）組成。'Impose' 強調的是將某物（想法、規則、負擔、人）強行施加或強加於他人，使之接受，通常是在對方不情願或沒有選擇的情況下。也可以指強制實施法律、稅收或限制。","definition":"1. force (someone) to accept or put up with something; 2. inflict (something unwelcome or unpleasant) on someone; 3. establish or apply (a tax, fine, rule, etc.) by authority.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He didn't want to impose his political views on others.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他不想將自己的政治觀點強加於人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government decided to impose a new tax on luxury goods.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府決定對奢侈品徵收新稅。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She felt that her relatives were imposing on her kindness.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她覺得她的親戚在利用她的善良。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"政府決定對奢侈品徵收新稅。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5049,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::impulse::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"A sudden ____ made him turn around.","expectedAnswer":"impulse","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"A sudden ____ made him turn around.","clozeAnswer":"impulse","exampleTranslation":"一股突如其來的衝動讓他轉過身。","reference":{"eng":"impulse","kk":"ˈɪmpʌls","tense":"n.","ch":"[['衝動'], ['心血來潮'], ['（物理學）衝量'], ['（神經）衝動']]","chEntries":["衝動","心血來潮","衝量"],"practiceMeaning":"一股突如其來的衝動讓他轉過身。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語impulsus，是動詞impellere（推動、驅使）的過去分詞。impellere 由 im-（朝向、進入）+ pellere（推動）組成。impulse 的核心語意是「一種突然的、強烈的驅動力或推動」。引申為「衝動」（未經思考的行為）、生理學上的「神經衝動」以及物理學上的「衝量」。OCR 掃描時可能將 'p' 誤判為 'r'。此處修正為 impulse。","definition":"1. a sudden strong and unreflective urge or desire to act; 2. a sudden brief command signal in physiology; 3. (in physics) the product of the force and time during which it acts.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She bought the dress on impulse.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她一時衝動買了那件洋裝。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A sudden impulse made him turn around.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一股突如其來的衝動讓他轉過身。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Nerve impulses are transmitted along the axon.\",\n    \"ch\": \"神經衝動沿著軸突傳遞。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"一股突如其來的衝動讓他轉過身。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5672,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l8::in-question::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The suitability of the candidate is ____.","expectedAnswer":"in question","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The suitability of the candidate is ____.","clozeAnswer":"in question","exampleTranslation":"這位候選人的適任性受到質疑。","reference":{"eng":"in question","kk":"ɪn ˈkwɛstʃən","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['所討論的'], ['所提及的'], ['有疑問的']]","chEntries":["所討論的","所提及的","有疑問的"],"practiceMeaning":"這位候選人的適任性受到質疑。","analysis":"此片語由介詞 in + 名詞 question（問題）構成。question 源自古法語 queste（詢問，search），來自拉丁語 quaestio（詢問，subject of inquiry）。其核心語義為「需要解答的疑問」或「所討論的議題」。in question 字面意思為「在問題之中」，引申為「被討論、被考慮或有爭議的」事物。此片語作為形容詞片語，用於修飾名詞，指出其是當前討論或爭議的焦點。沒有單獨的構詞分析，應視為固定片語。","definition":"being discussed or considered; the subject of discussion; causing doubt or uncertainty.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Let's focus on the issue in question.\",\n    \"ch\": \"讓我們關注所討論的問題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The suitability of the candidate is in question.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位候選人的適任性受到質疑。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這位候選人的適任性受到質疑。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4306,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::in-summary::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____, the meeting was productive and achieved its goals.","expectedAnswer":"In summary","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____, the meeting was productive and achieved its goals.","clozeAnswer":"In summary","exampleTranslation":"總括來說，這次會議富有成效並達成了目標。","reference":{"eng":"in summary","kk":"/ɪn ˈsʌməri/","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['總之'], ['概括地說']]","chEntries":["總之","概括地說"],"practiceMeaning":"總括來說，這次會議富有成效並達成了目標。","analysis":"由介詞 'in'（在）和名詞 'summary'（摘要）組成。'In summary' 是用於引導結語的片語，表示「將前面討論的內容做一個簡短的總結」。","definition":"briefly; in a short statement.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"In summary, the new policy is expected to improve efficiency.\",\n    \"ch\": \"總之，新政策預計將提高效率。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"In summary, the meeting was productive and achieved its goals.\",\n    \"ch\": \"總括來說，這次會議富有成效並達成了目標。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"總括來說，這次會議富有成效並達成了目標。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5503,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::in-the-same-boat::idiom","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Don't worry, you're not alone; we're all ____.","expectedAnswer":"in the same boat","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Don't worry, you're not alone; we're all ____.","clozeAnswer":"in the same boat","exampleTranslation":"別擔心，你不是一個人；我們都處境相同。","reference":{"eng":"in the same boat","kk":"ɪn ðə seɪm boʊt","tense":"idiom","ch":"[['處境相同'], ['同舟共濟'], ['處於同樣的困境']]","chEntries":["處境相同","同舟共濟","處於同樣的困境"],"practiceMeaning":"別擔心，你不是一個人；我們都處境相同。","analysis":"這個片語字面意思是「在同一條船上」。'In the same boat' 表示「與他人共享相同的處境、情況或命運」。如果一群人都在同一條船上，那麼他們面臨的危險、挑戰或經歷都是相同的。這個片語常用來描述「大家都在同一種困難或不利的處境中」。核心語意是「共享相同的處境」。","definition":"1. In the same difficult or unpleasant situation as someone else.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We're all in the same boat when it comes to saving money.\",\n    \"ch\": \"在省錢這件事上，我們都處境相同。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Don't worry, you're not alone; we're all in the same boat.\",\n    \"ch\": \"別擔心，你不是一個人；我們都處境相同。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"With the company facing bankruptcy, all the employees are in the same boat.\",\n    \"ch\": \"隨著公司面臨破產，所有員工都處境相同。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"別擔心，你不是一個人；我們都處境相同。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5633,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l7::in-this-regard::adv-phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Customer satisfaction is important. ____, we need to improve our service.","expectedAnswer":"In this regard","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Customer satisfaction is important. ____, we need to improve our service.","clozeAnswer":"In this regard","exampleTranslation":"顧客滿意度很重要。在這方面，我們需要改進我們的服務。","reference":{"eng":"in this regard","kk":"ɪn ðɪs rɪˈɡɑrd","tense":"adv. phrase","ch":"[['在這方面']]","chEntries":["在這方面"],"practiceMeaning":"顧客滿意度很重要。在這方面，我們需要改進我們的服務。","analysis":"此片語由介詞 'in'（在……中），指示代名詞 'this'（這個）和名詞 'regard'（方面、考慮）組成。'in' 源自古英語 'in'；'this' 源自古英語 'þis'；'regard' 源自古法語 'reguarder'（看、注意），意為「目光」、「考慮」、「方面」。構詞學上，'regard' 本身是個多義詞，在此作為名詞，與 'in this' 結合，表示「就這個特定提到的方面而言」。它用於指代前面剛說過或暗示過的主題、情況或觀點，作為進一步討論的依據。","definition":"With reference to this matter; concerning this.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company has invested heavily in new technology; in this regard, they are ahead of their competitors.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司在新能源技術上投入巨資；在這方面，他們領先於競爭對手。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Customer satisfaction is important. In this regard, we need to improve our service.\",\n    \"ch\": \"顧客滿意度很重要。在這方面，我們需要改進我們的服務。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"顧客滿意度很重要。在這方面，我們需要改進我們的服務。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3104,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::income::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She has a stable ____ from her job.","expectedAnswer":"income","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She has a stable ____ from her job.","clozeAnswer":"income","exampleTranslation":"她的工作有穩定的收入。","reference":{"eng":"income","kk":"/ˈɪnkʌm/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['收入；收益']]","chEntries":["收入","收益"],"practiceMeaning":"她的工作有穩定的收入。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'invenire' (to come in)。指「進入」的錢財。\n1. 收入；收益：指個人、家庭或公司在一段時期內賺取的金錢。","definition":"1. money that you earn from doing work or through investment; 2. the amount of money that a person or country receives.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company's annual income increased by 10%.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司的年收入增加了10%。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a stable income from her job.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的工作有穩定的收入。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她的工作有穩定的收入。","sourceName":"字彙王、龍騰課本","unitName":"U39、L2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6228,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::inevitable::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Given the circumstances, the outcome was ____.","expectedAnswer":"inevitable","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Given the circumstances, the outcome was ____.","clozeAnswer":"inevitable","exampleTranslation":"鑑於當時的情況，這個結果是必然的。","reference":{"eng":"inevitable","kk":"ɪnˈɛvɪtəbl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"不可避免的\"  ],  [    \"必然的\"  ],  [    \"注定的\"  ]]","chEntries":["不可避免的","必然的","注定的"],"practiceMeaning":"鑑於當時的情況，這個結果是必然的。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 inevitabilis，由 in-（否定）和 evadere（逃脫）構成，意為「不能逃脫的」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作形容詞時，指某種情況或結果是無法避免的，必然會發生。中文翻譯為「不可避免的；必然的；注定的」。","definition":"certain to happen; unavoidable.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Change is inevitable in life.\",\n    \"ch\": \"改變在生活中是不可避免的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Given the circumstances, the outcome was inevitable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"鑑於當時的情況，這個結果是必然的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Their success seemed inevitable from the start.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們的成功從一開始似乎就已注定。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"鑑於當時的情況，這個結果是必然的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5088,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::infinite::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She has ____ patience with the children.","expectedAnswer":"infinite","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She has ____ patience with the children.","clozeAnswer":"infinite","exampleTranslation":"她對孩子們有無限的耐心。","reference":{"eng":"infinite","kk":"ˈɪnfɪnət","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['無限的'], ['無窮的'], ['極大的']]","chEntries":["無限的","無窮的","極大的"],"practiceMeaning":"她對孩子們有無限的耐心。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'in-' (not) + 'finitus' (bounded, finite)，原意為 '無邊界的、無窮的'。'Infinite' 的核心語義是 '沒有盡頭、沒有限制'。這可以指空間上的無限，時間上的無限，數量的無限，也可以指品質上的極致，如 'infinite patience' (極大的耐心)，強調其程度之深，幾乎沒有極限。","definition":"1. Limitless or endless in space, extent, or size; impossible to measure or calculate.; 2. Extremely large or great, especially in scope or ability.; 3. (Of a mathematical quantity) larger than any assignable quantity or number.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The universe is thought to be infinite.\",\n    \"ch\": \"宇宙被認為是無限的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has infinite patience with the children.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對孩子們有無限的耐心。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The possibilities are infinite.\",\n    \"ch\": \"可能性是無限的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她對孩子們有無限的耐心。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4056,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::information::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This is important ____ for the investigation.","expectedAnswer":"information","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This is important ____ for the investigation.","clozeAnswer":"information","exampleTranslation":"這是對調查很重要的情報。","reference":{"eng":"information","kk":"/ˌɪnfərˈmeɪʃən/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['資訊', '情報'], ['消息']]","chEntries":["資訊","情報","消息"],"practiceMeaning":"這是對調查很重要的情報。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'informatio'，由 'informare' (to inform) 構成。核心是「被告知」、「被形成的知識」。因此，'information' 指 facts provided or learned about something or someone; knowledge.","definition":"1. facts provided or learned about something or someone; 2. knowledge or facts obtained about something or someone","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"請提供我們更多資訊。\",\n    \"eng\": \"Please provide us with more information.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"這是對調查很重要的情報。\",\n    \"eng\": \"This is important information for the investigation.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他給我了一些有用的消息。\",\n    \"eng\": \"He gave me some useful information.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是對調查很重要的情報。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4、C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5497,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::inhabit::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They plan to ____ the newly built houses.","expectedAnswer":"inhabit","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They plan to ____ the newly built houses.","clozeAnswer":"inhabit","exampleTranslation":"他們計劃入住新蓋的房子。","reference":{"eng":"inhabit","kk":"ɪnˈhæbɪt","tense":"v.","ch":"[['居住'], ['棲息'], ['佔據']]","chEntries":["居住","棲息","佔據"],"practiceMeaning":"他們計劃入住新蓋的房子。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'inhabitatare'，由 'in-'（在……裡面）和 'habitatare'（居住，來自 'habitare'）構成。'Habitare' 源於 'habere'（擁有）。因此，'inhabit' 的基本語意是「居住在某個地方」，特別是指「在某個地方建立家園或生活」。它可以指人，也可以指動植物。核心語意是「在某處生活或棲息」。","definition":"1. Live in or occupy (a place or environment).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Many species inhabit the deep ocean.\",\n    \"ch\": \"許多物種棲息在深海。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They plan to inhabit the newly built houses.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們計劃入住新蓋的房子。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This cave was inhabited by bats.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個洞穴曾由蝙蝠居住。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們計劃入住新蓋的房子。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6230,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::inherent::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The beauty of the natural landscape is ____.","expectedAnswer":"inherent","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The beauty of the natural landscape is ____.","clozeAnswer":"inherent","exampleTranslation":"自然景觀的美是固有的。","reference":{"eng":"inherent","kk":"ɪnˈhɪərənt","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"內在的\"  ],  [    \"固有的\"  ],  [    \"與生俱來的\"  ],  [    \"本質的\"  ]]","chEntries":["內在的","固有的","與生俱來的","本質的"],"practiceMeaning":"自然景觀的美是固有的。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 inhærens，是 inhærere（附著在…上）的現在分詞。由 in-（在…裡面）和 hærebere（附著）組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作形容詞時，指某事物與生俱來、屬於其本質的一部分，不可分割。中文翻譯為「內在的；固有的；與生俱來的；本質的」。","definition":"existing in something as a permanent, essential, or characteristic attribute.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There are inherent risks in every investment.\",\n    \"ch\": \"每項投資都存在內在的風險。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The beauty of the natural landscape is inherent.\",\n    \"ch\": \"自然景觀的美是固有的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Courage is an inherent quality of a leader.\",\n    \"ch\": \"勇氣是領導者與生俱來的品質。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"自然景觀的美是固有的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4289,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::inner-beauty::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Her kindness and compassion are examples of her ____.","expectedAnswer":"inner beauty","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Her kindness and compassion are examples of her ____.","clozeAnswer":"inner beauty","exampleTranslation":"她的善良和同情心是她內在美的體現。","reference":{"eng":"inner beauty","kk":"/ˈɪnər ˈbjuːti/","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['內在美']]","chEntries":["內在美"],"practiceMeaning":"她的善良和同情心是她內在美的體現。","analysis":"結合了形容詞 'inner'（內部的、內在的）和名詞 'beauty'（美）。'Inner beauty' 指「一個人的品格、個性、精神特質等非外在的、來自內心的美」，與外表美相對。","definition":"the attractive qualities of a person's character or personality, rather than their physical appearance.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"True happiness comes from inner beauty, not just looks.\",\n    \"ch\": \"真正的幸福來自內在美，而不僅僅是外表。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her kindness and compassion are examples of her inner beauty.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的善良和同情心是她內在美的體現。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她的善良和同情心是她內在美的體現。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5132,"wordRef":"字彙王::u62::insight::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Her ____ into the problem was remarkable.","expectedAnswer":"insight","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Her ____ into the problem was remarkable.","clozeAnswer":"insight","exampleTranslation":"她對這個問題的洞察力非常卓越。","reference":{"eng":"insight","kk":"ˈɪnsaɪt","tense":"n.","ch":"[['洞察力'], ['見解'], ['深刻理解']]","chEntries":["洞察力","見解","深刻理解"],"practiceMeaning":"她對這個問題的洞察力非常卓越。","analysis":"此字為複合詞，由 in-（在…裡面）+ sight（視力、視野、看見）組成。in- 在此表示「向內」或「進入」。sight 源自古英語 sīht，與 sīehþ（看見）相關。核心語意是「從內部看見、深入地理解」，引申為「深刻的理解能力、獨到的見解」。","definition":"the capacity to gain an accurate and deep intuitive understanding of a person or thing; a deep understanding of a person or thing.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The book offers valuable insights into the human mind.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本書提供了對人類心智的寶貴見解。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her insight into the problem was remarkable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對這個問題的洞察力非常卓越。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她對這個問題的洞察力非常卓越。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U62"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5698,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l9::instinctively::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He ____ dodged the ball.","expectedAnswer":"instinctively","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He ____ dodged the ball.","clozeAnswer":"instinctively","exampleTranslation":"他本能地躲開了球。","reference":{"eng":"instinctively","kk":"ɪnˈstɪŋktɪvli","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['憑本能地'], ['直覺地'], ['本能地']]","chEntries":["憑本能地","直覺地","本能地"],"practiceMeaning":"他本能地躲開了球。","analysis":"此字由名詞 'instinct' 加上形容詞化後綴 '-ive'，再接副詞化後綴 '-ly' 構成。'instinct' 源自拉丁語 instinctus（驅使，激勵），由 instinguere（驅使，激勵）演變而來。'-ive' 後綴使名詞轉化為形容詞，表示「具有……的特性的」。'-ly' 後綴將形容詞轉化為副詞，表示「以……的方式」。核心語意是「與本能、內在驅動力相關的」，因此「instinctively」表示「以一種不受意識思考控制、而是由內在驅動或本能反應的方式進行」。","definition":"in a way that is automatic and unthinking; by natural impulse or inclination.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She instinctively knew that something was wrong.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她憑本能就知道有些事不對勁。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He instinctively dodged the ball.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他本能地躲開了球。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他本能地躲開了球。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5352,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l1::intentional::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She gave him an ____ smile.","expectedAnswer":"intentional","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She gave him an ____ smile.","clozeAnswer":"intentional","exampleTranslation":"她對他露出了一個意味深長的微笑。","reference":{"eng":"intentional","kk":"ɪnˈtɛnʃənəl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['故意的'], ['蓄意的'], ['有意的']]","chEntries":["故意的","蓄意的","有意的"],"practiceMeaning":"她對他露出了一個意味深長的微笑。","analysis":"此字由名詞 intention 加上形容詞字尾 -al 構成。intention 源自拉丁語 intentio（意圖、打算）。-al 是常見的形容詞字尾，表示「關於……的」。因此，intentional 的核心語意為「關於意圖的」，引申為「故意的、蓄意的」，與 accidental（意外的）相對。","definition":"done on purpose; deliberate.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The damage to the car was intentional.\",\n    \"ch\": \"汽車的損壞是故意的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She gave him an intentional smile.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對他露出了一個意味深長的微笑。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她對他露出了一個意味深長的微笑。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5648,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l8::invade::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Don't let your problems ____ your peace of mind.","expectedAnswer":"invade","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Don't let your problems ____ your peace of mind.","clozeAnswer":"invade","exampleTranslation":"不要讓你的問題侵擾你的心靈平靜。","reference":{"eng":"invade","kk":"ɪnˈveɪd","tense":"v.","ch":"[['入侵'], ['侵略'], ['侵擾'], ['（事物）湧入']]","chEntries":["入侵","侵略","侵擾","湧入"],"practiceMeaning":"不要讓你的問題侵擾你的心靈平靜。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 invadere，由 in-（進入，into）+ vadere（行走，to go）組成。vadere 來自原始印歐語 *gwem-（行走，to come）。核心語義為「進入」某地，尤指帶有敵意或強制性地。構詞上，in- 表示「進入」，vadere 提供「行走」或「進入」的核心動作。此處為動詞用法，表示「進入」（通常是武力或強制地）或「侵擾」。","definition":"to enter a country or region by force with an army; to encroach or intrude; to enter a place in large numbers.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The army invaded the neighboring country.\",\n    \"ch\": \"軍隊入侵了鄰國。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Don't let your problems invade your peace of mind.\",\n    \"ch\": \"不要讓你的問題侵擾你的心靈平靜。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"不要讓你的問題侵擾你的心靈平靜。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4361,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::it-is-fairly-difficult-to::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ finish the project on time.","expectedAnswer":"It is fairly difficult to","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ finish the project on time.","clozeAnswer":"It is fairly difficult to","exampleTranslation":"要在期限內完成這個項目相當困難。","reference":{"eng":"it is fairly difficult to","kk":"None","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['這相當難以…']]","chEntries":["這相當難以…"],"practiceMeaning":"要在期限內完成這個項目相當困難。","analysis":"此為片語分析。'it is' (pronoun + verb) 指『這是』。'fairly' (adv.) 源自 'fair'，意為『相當地，頗為』。'difficult' (adj.) 源自拉丁語 'difficilis'，意為『困難的』。'to' (prep.) 帶出不定詞。整個片語表示『做某事相當困難』，『其難度在中等偏上』。","definition":"it is quite hard or challenging to do something","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It is fairly difficult to understand his accent.\",\n    \"ch\": \"要聽懂他的口音相當困難。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It is fairly difficult to finish the project on time.\",\n    \"ch\": \"要在期限內完成這個項目相當困難。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"要在期限內完成這個項目相當困難。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4726,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::jazz::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He didn't mean to ____ up the project, but he did.","expectedAnswer":"jazz","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He didn't mean to ____ up the project, but he did.","clozeAnswer":"jazz","exampleTranslation":"他並無意搞砸這個專案，但他確實這麼做了。","reference":{"eng":"jazz","kk":"/ˈdʒæz/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['（非正式）弄亂'], ['（非正式）把…裝飾得花俏'], ['（非正式）把…搞砸']]","chEntries":["弄亂","把…裝飾得花俏","把…搞砸"],"practiceMeaning":"他並無意搞砸這個專案，但他確實這麼做了。","analysis":"動詞形式，取自名詞的非正式用法，指弄亂、裝飾得花俏，或將事情搞砸。","definition":"1. (informal) To make something more lively or attractive. 2. (informal) To spoil or mess up something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She jazzed up her outfit with a colorful scarf.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她用一條色彩繽紛的圍巾讓自己的裝扮更顯亮眼。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He didn't mean to jazz up the project, but he did.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他並無意搞砸這個專案，但他確實這麼做了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他並無意搞砸這個專案，但他確實這麼做了。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4249,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::junior::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ high school has students from grades 7 to 9.","expectedAnswer":"junior","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ high school has students from grades 7 to 9.","clozeAnswer":"junior","exampleTranslation":"初中部有七到九年級的學生。","reference":{"eng":"junior","kk":"/ˈdʒuːnjər/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['資淺的'], ['低年級的'], ['年幼的']]","chEntries":["資淺的","低年級的","年幼的"],"practiceMeaning":"初中部有七到九年級的學生。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'iunior'，比較級形式，意為「更年輕的」。'Junior' 在用法上多用於比較，表示在年齡、職位或學業上的較低層級。","definition":"lower in rank or shorter in length of service; younger","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a junior partner in the law firm.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是這家律師事務所的資淺合夥人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The junior high school has students from grades 7 to 9.\",\n    \"ch\": \"初中部有七到九年級的學生。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"初中部有七到九年級的學生。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5598,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l7::justice::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The court system aims to deliver ____ to all citizens.","expectedAnswer":"justice","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The court system aims to deliver ____ to all citizens.","clozeAnswer":"justice","exampleTranslation":"法院系統旨在為所有公民伸張正義。","reference":{"eng":"justice","kk":"ˈdʒʌstɪs","tense":"n.","ch":"[['正義'], ['公正'], ['司法'], ['審判']]","chEntries":["正義","公正","司法","審判"],"practiceMeaning":"法院系統旨在為所有公民伸張正義。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'justitia'（正義、公正），它本身由 'justus'（正確的、合法的）和 '-itia'（名詞化後綴，表示狀態或品質）構成，而 'justus' 又源於 'jus'（法律、權利）。構詞學上，核心是 'jus'（法律、權利）加上形容詞化及名詞化後綴。原始語意是「合乎法律」或「符合權利」，演變為指「公平與正義的原則」、「公正的待遇」以及「司法的系統或權威」。多個義項之間的核心關聯在於「正確性」、「公平性」和「依循規則」。","definition":"1. The quality of being fair and reasonable; 2. The administration of the law or authority in maintaining this; 3. A judge or the authority to administer justice.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The pursuit of justice is a fundamental principle of law.\",\n    \"ch\": \"追求正義是法律的基本原則。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The court system aims to deliver justice to all citizens.\",\n    \"ch\": \"法院系統旨在為所有公民伸張正義。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He believed that true justice could only be achieved through reform.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他相信真正的公正只能透過改革實現。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"法院系統旨在為所有公民伸張正義。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3298,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::kettle::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ whistled when the water was boiling.","expectedAnswer":"kettle","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ whistled when the water was boiling.","clozeAnswer":"kettle","exampleTranslation":"水燒開時，水壺發出了嘯叫聲。","reference":{"eng":"kettle","kk":"/ˈkɛtl/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['水壺；茶壺（燒水用的）']]","chEntries":["水壺","茶壺"],"practiceMeaning":"水燒開時，水壺發出了嘯叫聲。","analysis":"源自古法語 'ketel'，來自拉丁語 'cattos'，意為「鍋」。專指用來煮水或燒水的器具，通常帶有壺嘴和把手。","definition":"a container, typically with a lid, handle, and spout, used for boiling water.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please put the kettle on, I'd like some tea.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請燒壺水，我想喝點茶。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The kettle whistled when the water was boiling.\",\n    \"ch\": \"水燒開時，水壺發出了嘯叫聲。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"水燒開時，水壺發出了嘯叫聲。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4080,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::kindergarten::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Children learn through play in ____.","expectedAnswer":"kindergarten","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Children learn through play in ____.","clozeAnswer":"kindergarten","exampleTranslation":"孩子們在幼稚園裡通過遊戲學習。","reference":{"eng":"kindergarten","kk":"/ˈkɪndərˌɡɑrtən/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['幼稚園']]","chEntries":["幼稚園"],"practiceMeaning":"孩子們在幼稚園裡通過遊戲學習。","analysis":"源自德語 'Kindergarten'，由 'Kinder' (children) + 'Garten' (garden) 構成，字面意思是「兒童的花園」。由德國教育家福祿貝爾 (Friedrich Fröbel) 於19世紀提出，強調在遊戲中學習和成長的環境。","definition":"a school or class for children aged about three to five","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"我兒子今年開始上幼稚園。\",\n    \"eng\": \"My son started kindergarten this year.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"孩子們在幼稚園裡通過遊戲學習。\",\n    \"eng\": \"Children learn through play in kindergarten.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"孩子們在幼稚園裡通過遊戲學習。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4670,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::knit::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The doctor said the cut would ____ up nicely.","expectedAnswer":"knit","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The doctor said the cut would ____ up nicely.","clozeAnswer":"knit","exampleTranslation":"醫生說傷口會很好地癒合。","reference":{"eng":"knit","kk":"/ˈnɪt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['編織（毛線等）'], ['（傷口）癒合']]","chEntries":["編織","癒合"],"practiceMeaning":"醫生說傷口會很好地癒合。","analysis":"源自古英語 *knittan*，與荷蘭語 *knippen*（剪、捏）同源，可能與原始印歐語 *gned-*（編織、結合）有關。核心概念是將線或纖維纏繞、結合在一起。此動作延伸至生物體的癒合過程，將斷裂處重新連結。","definition":"1. To form (fabric or a garment) by interlocking loops of wool, yarn, or other fibres with knitting needles; (of fabric) to be formed in this way. 2. (of a wound or broken bone) To heal or join together by forming new tissue.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She loves to knit scarves for her grandchildren.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她喜歡為孫子孫女編織圍巾。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The 