one else.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The landlord refused to renew the lease.\",\n    \"ch\": \"房東拒絕續簽租約。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He inherited the title of landlord.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他繼承了地主的頭銜。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他繼承了地主的頭銜。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5133,"wordRef":"字彙王::u62::legislation::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This ____ aims to improve public health.","expectedAnswer":"legislation","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This ____ aims to improve public health.","clozeAnswer":"legislation","exampleTranslation":"這項法律旨在改善公共衛生。","reference":{"eng":"legislation","kk":"ˌledʒɪsˈleɪʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[['立法'], ['法律']]","chEntries":["立法","法律"],"practiceMeaning":"這項法律旨在改善公共衛生。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 legislatio，由 lex, legis（法律）+ latio（提出、通過）組成。lex 來自印歐語系 *leg-（收集、說）。atio 是拉丁語中表示「動作」或「結果」的名詞字尾。核心語意為「制定法律的過程或產生的法律」。","definition":"laws, considered collectively; the process of making or passing laws.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government is considering new legislation on environmental protection.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府正在考慮關於環境保護的新立法。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This legislation aims to improve public health.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這項法律旨在改善公共衛生。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這項法律旨在改善公共衛生。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U62"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5134,"wordRef":"字彙王::u62::legislative::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They discussed ____ reforms.","expectedAnswer":"legislative","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They discussed ____ reforms.","clozeAnswer":"legislative","exampleTranslation":"他們討論了立法改革。","reference":{"eng":"legislative","kk":"ˈledʒɪsleɪtɪv","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['立法的'], ['立法機關的']]","chEntries":["立法的","立法機關的"],"practiceMeaning":"他們討論了立法改革。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 legislativus，是 legislation 的形容詞形式。由 lex, legis（法律）+ latio（提出、通過）+ -ivus（形容詞字尾）組成。核心語意是「與制定法律有關的」或「屬於立法機關的」。","definition":"concerning or relating to the preparation and enactment of laws; having the power to make laws.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The legislative branch of government makes laws.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府的立法部門負責制定法律。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They discussed legislative reforms.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們討論了立法改革。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們討論了立法改革。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U62"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5089,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::lest::conj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He spoke quietly, ____ he should disturb the baby.","expectedAnswer":"lest","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He spoke quietly, ____ he should disturb the baby.","clozeAnswer":"lest","exampleTranslation":"他輕聲說話，唯恐吵醒了嬰兒。","reference":{"eng":"lest","kk":"lest","tense":"conj.","ch":"[['以免'], ['唯恐']]","chEntries":["以免","唯恐"],"practiceMeaning":"他輕聲說話，唯恐吵醒了嬰兒。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 'þæs læs þe'，意為 '以致較少地'，後來縮短為 'lest'。它引導一個從句，表示 '害怕發生某事'，從而採取預防措施。其語義與 'in case' (萬一) 相似，但 'lest' 更強調潛在的危險或負面結果，並通常後接虛擬語氣 (subjunctive mood) 的動詞。","definition":"1. In order to make sure that something will not happen; for fear that.; 2. For fear that; so that... not.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Study hard, lest you fail the exam.\",\n    \"ch\": \"努力學習，以免考試不及格。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He spoke quietly, lest he should disturb the baby.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他輕聲說話，唯恐吵醒了嬰兒。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他輕聲說話，唯恐吵醒了嬰兒。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4326,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::liberty::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Students were given more ____ in choosing their courses.","expectedAnswer":"liberty","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Students were given more ____ in choosing their courses.","clozeAnswer":"liberty","exampleTranslation":"學生們在選擇課程方面被賦予了更多的自由。","reference":{"eng":"liberty","kk":"/ˈlɪbərti/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['自由'], ['（對規則、禮節等的）失禮；過分鹵莽']]","chEntries":["自由","失禮","過分鹵莽"],"practiceMeaning":"學生們在選擇課程方面被賦予了更多的自由。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'libertas' (freedom)，來自 'liber' (free)。核心是『自由』的概念。1. 指享有政治、社會、個人不受約束的權利和狀態，即『自由』。2. 指過度行使自由，不受約束，導致『失禮』或『鹵莽』的行為，超過了應有的界限。","definition":"the state of being free to make your own choices and decisions and to live as you want to live; freedom to behave or act in a way you choose","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Millions of people fought for their liberty.\",\n    \"ch\": \"數百萬人為他們的自由而戰。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Students were given more liberty in choosing their courses.\",\n    \"ch\": \"學生們在選擇課程方面被賦予了更多的自由。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He took the liberty of borrowing my car without asking.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他擅自借了我的車，沒有經過我的允許。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"學生們在選擇課程方面被賦予了更多的自由。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5666,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l8::license::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The artist was granted a ____ to practice.","expectedAnswer":"license","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The artist was granted a ____ to practice.","clozeAnswer":"license","exampleTranslation":"該藝術家獲得了執業許可。","reference":{"eng":"license","kk":"ˈlaɪsəns","tense":"n.","ch":"[['執照'], ['許可證'], ['執業許可'], ['放縱']]","chEntries":["執照","許可證","執業許可","放縱"],"practiceMeaning":"該藝術家獲得了執業許可。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 licence，來自古法語 licence，再追溯至拉丁語 licentia，意為「自由」，來自 licēre（被允許，to be permitted）。licēre 來自原始印歐語 *legʰ-（允許）。核心語義為「被允許」或「給予自由」。構詞上，licēre 提供「允許」的核心概念，-entia 是拉丁語名詞字尾，-ia 演變為中古英語的 -ce。此處為名詞用法，指代「官方許可」或「允許的自由」。","definition":"a permit from an official authority to own or use something, do a particular activity, or carry on a trade; freedom to behave as one wishes.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"You need a license to drive a car.\",\n    \"ch\": \"你需要駕照才能開車。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The artist was granted a license to practice.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該藝術家獲得了執業許可。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The story took liberties with historical facts.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個故事對史實有所歪曲（利用了虛構的自由）。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該藝術家獲得了執業許可。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3147,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::lively::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The conversation became quite ____ after a few drinks.","expectedAnswer":"lively","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The conversation became quite ____ after a few drinks.","clozeAnswer":"lively","exampleTranslation":"喝了幾杯酒後，談話變得相當熱烈。","reference":{"eng":"lively","kk":"/ˈlaɪvlɪ/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['活潑的；生氣勃勃的'], ['（討論、場景等）熱烈的；活躍的'], ['（顏色）鮮豔的；（氣味）濃郁的']]","chEntries":["活潑的","生氣勃勃的","熱烈的","活躍的","鮮豔的","濃郁的"],"practiceMeaning":"喝了幾杯酒後，談話變得相當熱烈。","analysis":"源自古英語 'liflic'，與 'life'（生命）有關。'Lively' 描述的是充滿生命力、活力和興奮的狀態。它可以用來形容人（活潑、精力充沛）、地方（熱鬧、充滿生氣）、活動（熱烈、引人入勝）或事物（鮮豔、濃郁）。'Lively' 的核心概念是「充滿生命力」和「活躍」。","definition":"1. (of a person or their manner) full of energy and enthusiasm; animated; 2. (of a place or event) bustling with activity and excitement; 3. (of a colour or smell) bright and pleasant.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The children were playing a lively game of tag.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子們正在玩一場熱鬧的捉迷藏遊戲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The conversation became quite lively after a few drinks.\",\n    \"ch\": \"喝了幾杯酒後，談話變得相當熱烈。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a lively personality and is always smiling.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她個性活潑，總是面帶笑容。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"喝了幾杯酒後，談話變得相當熱烈。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3999,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u3::look::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"You ____ very happy today.","expectedAnswer":"look","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"You ____ very happy today.","clozeAnswer":"look","exampleTranslation":"你今天看起來很高興。","reference":{"eng":"look","kk":"/lʊk/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['看', '瞧'], ['顯得', '看起來'], ['尋找']]","chEntries":["看","瞧","顯得","看起來","尋找"],"practiceMeaning":"你今天看起來很高興。","analysis":"詞源：古英語 'lōcian'。指將眼睛的焦點集中在某處，引申為外觀、樣貌，或尋找某物。","definition":"1. direct one's gaze towards someone or something; 2. have a particular appearance or outward impression; 3. try to find.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Look at this beautiful painting!\",\n    \"ch\": \"看看這幅美麗的畫！\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"You look very happy today.\",\n    \"ch\": \"你今天看起來很高興。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I'm looking for my lost keys.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我正在找我丟失的鑰匙。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"你今天看起來很高興。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4427,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u9::loose::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He gave a ____ description of the suspect.","expectedAnswer":"loose","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He gave a ____ description of the suspect.","clozeAnswer":"loose","exampleTranslation":"他對嫌疑犯的描述很含糊。","reference":{"eng":"loose","kk":"/luːs/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['鬆的', '不緊的'], ['不精確的', '寬鬆的'], ['（道德、紀律）鬆懈的'], ['（不受約束的）自由的']]","chEntries":["鬆的","不緊的","不精確的","寬鬆的","鬆懈的","自由的"],"practiceMeaning":"他對嫌疑犯的描述很含糊。","analysis":"詞源自古挪威語 'lauss'。核心概念是「未被固定、束縛或限制」。引申到物理上的不緊、概念上的不明確，以及行為上的不受約束。","definition":"not firmly fixed or attached; not tight; not precise or exact; not strict.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The button on my shirt is loose.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我襯衫上的鈕扣鬆了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He gave a loose description of the suspect.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對嫌疑犯的描述很含糊。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The dog is loose.\",\n    \"ch\": \"狗跑出來了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他對嫌疑犯的描述很含糊。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4138,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::loser::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Nobody wants to be the ____.","expectedAnswer":"loser","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Nobody wants to be the ____.","clozeAnswer":"loser","exampleTranslation":"沒有人想成為失敗者。","reference":{"eng":"loser","kk":"/ˈluːzər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['失敗者']]","chEntries":["失敗者"],"practiceMeaning":"沒有人想成為失敗者。","analysis":"源自 lose（輸掉，失去）+ -er（名詞後綴，表示人或物）。核心概念是「輸掉比賽或競爭的人」。","definition":"a person who is defeated or does not succeed","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He's a sore loser.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一個輸不起的人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Nobody wants to be the loser.\",\n    \"ch\": \"沒有人想成為失敗者。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The team accepted their role as the losers.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這支隊伍接受了他們身為失敗者的角色。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"沒有人想成為失敗者。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4140,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::lover::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He is a ____ of classical music.","expectedAnswer":"lover","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He is a ____ of classical music.","clozeAnswer":"lover","exampleTranslation":"他是古典音樂的愛好者。","reference":{"eng":"lover","kk":"/ˈlʌvər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['戀人', '愛人'], ['愛好者', '愛好者（從事某事的人）']]","chEntries":["戀人","愛人","愛好者"],"practiceMeaning":"他是古典音樂的愛好者。","analysis":"源自 love（愛）+ -er（名詞後綴）。核心概念是「充滿愛意的人」。引申為浪漫關係中的伴侶，或指對某事有強烈興趣或熱愛的人。","definition":"1. a person who loves another; 2. a person who enjoys or is fond of something","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They are lovers who have been together for years.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們是在一起多年的戀人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a lover of classical music.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是古典音樂的愛好者。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a secret lover of chocolate.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是巧克力的忠實擁趸。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他是古典音樂的愛好者。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3230,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::machine::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This sewing ____ is very old but still works well.","expectedAnswer":"machine","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This sewing ____ is very old but still works well.","clozeAnswer":"machine","exampleTranslation":"這台縫紉機很舊了，但仍然能正常工作。","reference":{"eng":"machine","kk":"/məˈʃiːn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['機器'], ['機械']]","chEntries":["機器","機械"],"practiceMeaning":"這台縫紉機很舊了，但仍然能正常工作。","analysis":"詞源來自法語 'machine'，最終來自拉丁文 'machina'，源自希臘文 'mēkhanē' (device, contrivance)。指由各種零件組合而成，能將一種能量轉化為另一種能量以完成特定工作的裝置。","definition":"an apparatus using mechanical power and having several parts, each with a definite function and together performing a particular task.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He bought a new washing machine.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他買了一台新洗衣機。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This sewing machine is very old but still works well.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這台縫紉機很舊了，但仍然能正常工作。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這台縫紉機很舊了，但仍然能正常工作。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U41"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3946,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::magical::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She performed a ____ trick.","expectedAnswer":"magical","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She performed a ____ trick.","clozeAnswer":"magical","exampleTranslation":"她表演了一個魔術把戲。","reference":{"eng":"magical","kk":"/ˈmædʒɪkl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['魔法的', '神奇的'], ['迷人的']]","chEntries":["魔法的","神奇的","迷人的"],"practiceMeaning":"她表演了一個魔術把戲。","analysis":"源自 'magic' (名詞，魔法) 加上形容詞後綴 '-al'。指與魔法相關的，或像魔法一樣的，引申為「神奇的、迷人的」。","definition":"1. relating to or resembling magic; 2. having or using the power to produce supernatural effects; 3. very pleasant or attractive.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The story had a magical quality.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個故事有一種神奇的特質。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She performed a magical trick.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她表演了一個魔術把戲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The view from the top of the mountain was magical.\",\n    \"ch\": \"山頂的景色令人迷醉。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她表演了一個魔術把戲。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5301,"wordRef":"字彙王::u63::mandate::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The UN ____ expired last year.","expectedAnswer":"mandate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The UN ____ expired last year.","clozeAnswer":"mandate","exampleTranslation":"聯合國的託管期去年已滿。","reference":{"eng":"mandate","kk":"ˈmændeɪt","tense":"n.","ch":"[['授權', '命令'], ['（國際聯盟或聯合國託管下的）委任統治區'], ['（某群體或個人）的權力或授權']]","chEntries":["授權","命令","委任統治區","的權力或授權"],"practiceMeaning":"聯合國的託管期去年已滿。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'mandatum'（命令，委託，來自 'mandare'，意為「命令，委派」）。'mandare' 由 'manus'（hand）和 'dare'（to give）構成，原意是「將（某事）交到手中」。構詞上，'mand-' 為詞根，'-ate' 為後綴。核心語意是「被給予的權力」或「被給予的指令」。在現代英語中，'mandate' 可以指正式的命令、授權，也可以指由選舉產生的政府所擁有的民意授權。","definition":"an official order or commission to do something; the authority to carry out a policy or course of action, regarded as given by the electorate to a representative; a territory administered by another country.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government has a clear mandate from the people.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府擁有人民的明確授權。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The UN mandate expired last year.\",\n    \"ch\": \"聯合國的託管期去年已滿。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"聯合國的託管期去年已滿。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U63"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5625,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l7::marvel::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Her recovery was nothing short of a medical ____.","expectedAnswer":"marvel","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Her recovery was nothing short of a medical ____.","clozeAnswer":"marvel","exampleTranslation":"她的康復簡直是醫學上的奇蹟。","reference":{"eng":"marvel","kk":"ˈmɑrvl","tense":"n.","ch":"[['奇蹟'], ['奇觀'], ['令人驚奇的事物']]","chEntries":["奇蹟","奇觀","令人驚奇的事物"],"practiceMeaning":"她的康復簡直是醫學上的奇蹟。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'mirabil '，意為「奇妙的、驚人的」，來自 'mirari'（驚奇）。構詞學上，此字通常被視為一個整體詞，詞源直接指向「奇蹟」或「令人驚奇的事物」。原始語意是「值得驚奇的事物」，引申為「奇蹟」、「奇觀」或「令人讚嘆的人或事物」。","definition":"1. A wonderful or astonishing thing; 2. A person exhibiting the qualities of being wonderful or astonishing.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The Pyramids of Giza are considered one of the ancient wonders of the world.\",\n    \"ch\": \"吉薩金字塔被認為是古代世界七大奇蹟之一。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her recovery was nothing short of a medical marvel.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的康復簡直是醫學上的奇蹟。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她的康復簡直是醫學上的奇蹟。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5303,"wordRef":"字彙王::u63::masculine::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The adjective 'le' is ____ in French.","expectedAnswer":"masculine","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The adjective 'le' is ____ in French.","clozeAnswer":"masculine","exampleTranslation":"形容詞 'le' 在法語中是陽性的。","reference":{"eng":"masculine","kk":"ˈmæskjəlɪn","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['男性的', '男子氣概的'], ['（語法）陽性的']]","chEntries":["男性的","男子氣概的","陽性的"],"practiceMeaning":"形容詞 'le' 在法語中是陽性的。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'masculinus'（男性的），來自 'masculus'（雄性的，來自 'mas'，意為「男性」）。構詞上，'mascul-' 為詞根，'-ine' 為形容詞後綴。核心語意與「男性」相關，可用於生理性別、社會性別特徵（男子氣概），以及語法中的「陽性」詞性。","definition":"having or denoting qualities traditionally associated with men; relating to or denoting words or phrases that refer to males; male.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has a very masculine voice.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的聲音非常男性化。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The adjective 'le' is masculine in French.\",\n    \"ch\": \"形容詞 'le' 在法語中是陽性的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"形容詞 'le' 在法語中是陽性的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U63"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5573,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::massive::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The project required ____ amounts of funding.","expectedAnswer":"massive","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The project required ____ amounts of funding.","clozeAnswer":"massive","exampleTranslation":"這個計畫需要巨額的資金。","reference":{"eng":"massive","kk":"ˈmæsɪv","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['巨大的'], ['大規模的'], ['沉重的'], ['大量的']]","chEntries":["巨大的","大規模的","沉重的","大量的"],"practiceMeaning":"這個計畫需要巨額的資金。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 \"massīvus\"，意為 \"solid, dense\"（固態的，密集的），來自 \"massa\"（mass, lump，團塊，塊狀物）。\"massa\" 的語義是「未經分割的、大塊的物質」。因此，\"massive\" 的核心語義是「像一個大塊物體一樣，巨大、厚重、密集」。它強調的是規模、體積或重量上的龐大。它可以形容物理上的尺寸（e.g., massive building），也可以形容抽象上的數量或影響力（e.g., massive impact）。","definition":"1. Large and heavy or solid; 2. Large in scale or extent; 3. Very large in amount or degree.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They live in a massive house in the countryside.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們住在鄉間一棟巨大的房子裡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The project required massive amounts of funding.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個計畫需要巨額的資金。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company experienced massive layoffs.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司進行了大規模裁員。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個計畫需要巨額的資金。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4158,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::materials::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The relief ____ included food and medicine.","expectedAnswer":"materials","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The relief ____ included food and medicine.","clozeAnswer":"materials","exampleTranslation":"救濟物資包括食物和藥品。","reference":{"eng":"materials","kk":"/məˈtɪəriəlz/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['材料', '物資']]","chEntries":["材料","物資"],"practiceMeaning":"救濟物資包括食物和藥品。","analysis":"由 material（物質的，材料）的複數形式。來自拉丁語 materialis（物質的）。核心概念是「構成某物的東西」。","definition":"things such as physical objects and substances that are needed for the particular activity or purpose you are referring to","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to buy building materials.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要購買建築材料。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The relief materials included food and medicine.\",\n    \"ch\": \"救濟物資包括食物和藥品。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The artist uses various materials in his work.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位藝術家在他的作品中使用各種材料。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"救濟物資包括食物和藥品。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4606,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::meaningful::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It was a ____ gesture of friendship.","expectedAnswer":"meaningful","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It was a ____ gesture of friendship.","clozeAnswer":"meaningful","exampleTranslation":"這是友誼的充滿意義的表示。","reference":{"eng":"meaningful","kk":"/ˈmiːnɪŋfəl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['有意義的'], ['意味深長的'], ['有目的的']]","chEntries":["有意義的","意味深長的","有目的的"],"practiceMeaning":"這是友誼的充滿意義的表示。","analysis":"由 'meaning' (意義) + '-ful' (充滿) 組成。'Meaning' 源自古英語 'mænan' (意指、表達)，與 'mean' (意圖) 同源。'-ful' 是表示「充滿」或「具有」的後綴。此字指事物具有重要的價值、目的或深刻的內涵，能夠引起情感共鳴或啟發思考。","definition":"having or conveying a serious emotion, importance, or purpose.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He gave a meaningful speech that inspired many.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他做了一場意味深長的演講，激勵了許多人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was a meaningful gesture of friendship.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是友誼的充滿意義的表示。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She sought a more meaningful career.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她尋求一份更有意義的職業。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是友誼的充滿意義的表示。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5664,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l8::measurable::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The success of the project is not easily ____.","expectedAnswer":"measurable","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The success of the project is not easily ____.","clozeAnswer":"measurable","exampleTranslation":"該專案的成功難以衡量。","reference":{"eng":"measurable","kk":"ˈmɛʒərəbl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['可測量的'], ['可衡量的']]","chEntries":["可測量的","可衡量的"],"practiceMeaning":"該專案的成功難以衡量。","analysis":"此字由 measure（測量）+ -able（形容詞字尾）構成。measure 源自拉丁語 mensura（測量）。-able 是常見的形容詞字尾，表示「能夠……的」。構詞上，measure 提供核心的「測量」概念，-able 使其成為形容詞。核心語義為「能夠被測量」或「能夠被衡量的」。此處為形容詞用法，描述事物「可以用來測量」或「其程度可以被估計」。","definition":"able to be measured or estimated; quantifiable.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The temperature is measurable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"溫度是可測量的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The success of the project is not easily measurable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該專案的成功難以衡量。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該專案的成功難以衡量。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4389,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u9::media::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The lab technician prepared the culture ____.","expectedAnswer":"media","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The lab technician prepared the culture ____.","clozeAnswer":"media","exampleTranslation":"實驗室技術員準備了培養基。","reference":{"eng":"media","kk":"/ˈmiːdiə/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['媒體（報紙、電視、廣播、網路等的總稱）'], ['（生物學）培養基']]","chEntries":["媒體","培養基"],"practiceMeaning":"實驗室技術員準備了培養基。","analysis":"詞源自拉丁語 'medium'（中間、媒介、工具）的複數形式。最初指傳播資訊的各種工具或管道，現已成為一個常用詞，涵蓋所有大眾傳播媒介。生物學上的「培養基」是指用於生長微生物的介質，也是一種「媒介」。","definition":"the main ways that large numbers of people receive information and entertainment, e.g. television, radio, newspapers, and the internet; a substance used to grow microorganisms in a laboratory.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The media plays an important role in shaping public opinion.\",\n    \"ch\": \"媒體在塑造公眾輿論方面扮演著重要角色。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The lab technician prepared the culture media.\",\n    \"ch\": \"實驗室技術員準備了培養基。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"實驗室技術員準備了培養基。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4679,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::mess::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He got himself into a terrible ____ with his finances.","expectedAnswer":"mess","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He got himself into a terrible ____ with his finances.","clozeAnswer":"mess","exampleTranslation":"他在財務上讓自己陷入了可怕的困境。","reference":{"eng":"mess","kk":"/ˈmɛs/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['混亂'], ['髒亂'], ['（令人不快的）處境'], ['（非正式）相當數量']]","chEntries":["混亂","髒亂","處境","相當數量"],"practiceMeaning":"他在財務上讓自己陷入了可怕的困境。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 *missus*（投擲），與 *mittere*（發送）有關，可能指「被丟棄、攪亂的東西」。核心概念是無序、不整潔的狀態。延伸至令人不快的困境，或非正式地指「相當多」的某物。","definition":"1. A situation or state of untidiness or disorder. 2. A situation that is confused, difficult, or unpleasant. 3. (informal) A large amount or number of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The room was a complete mess after the party.\",\n    \"ch\": \"派對結束後，房間一片狼藉。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He got himself into a terrible mess with his finances.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在財務上讓自己陷入了可怕的困境。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was a mess of papers on his desk.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的桌上有一大堆文件。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他在財務上讓自己陷入了可怕的困境。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6177,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::migration::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The region experienced significant ____ of people seeking work.","expectedAnswer":"migration","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The region experienced significant ____ of people seeking work.","clozeAnswer":"migration","exampleTranslation":"該地區經歷了大量尋找工作的移民。","reference":{"eng":"migration","kk":"maɪˈɡreɪʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"遷徙\"  ],  [    \"移民\"  ]]","chEntries":["遷徙","移民"],"practiceMeaning":"該地區經歷了大量尋找工作的移民。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 migratioinem，是動詞 migrare「遷徙、移居」的名詞化。migrare 的詞源不確定，可能與拉丁語 mīgrāre (to move from one place to another) 或拉丁語 magna (great) 有關，但最常見的說法是源自詞根 *mei- (to go, pass)。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作為名詞，其核心語義是由動詞 migrate「遷徙」名詞化而來，指「為了尋找食物、繁殖地或更好的生存條件而從一個地方移動到另一個地方的行為」。此義項由「移動」的動作延伸出「遷徙」的行為與「移民」的結果。","definition":"1. the movement of persons from one country or locality to another; 2. seasonal movement of animals from one region to another.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Bird migration occurs in the spring and fall.\",\n    \"ch\": \"鳥類遷徙發生在春秋兩季。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The region experienced significant migration of people seeking work.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該地區經歷了大量尋找工作的移民。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Human migration patterns have changed throughout history.\",\n    \"ch\": \"人類的移民模式在歷史上一直變化。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The great migration of African Americans from the South to the North was a major demographic shift.\",\n    \"ch\": \"非裔美國人從南方大規模遷往北方的運動是人口結構的重大轉變。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該地區經歷了大量尋找工作的移民。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4722,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::misery::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He lived in abject ____ after losing his job.","expectedAnswer":"misery","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He lived in abject ____ after losing his job.","clozeAnswer":"misery","exampleTranslation":"失業後，他過著極度悲慘的生活。","reference":{"eng":"misery","kk":"/ˈmɪzəri/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['悲慘'], ['痛苦'], ['苦難']]","chEntries":["悲慘","痛苦","苦難"],"practiceMeaning":"失業後，他過著極度悲慘的生活。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 *miserabilis*（可憐的），與 *miser*（不幸的）同源。核心是極度的不幸、痛苦和悲慘的狀態。","definition":"1. A state or feeling of great distress or unhappiness.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The war brought widespread misery to the people.\",\n    \"ch\": \"戰爭給人民帶來了廣泛的悲慘。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He lived in abject misery after losing his job.\",\n    \"ch\": \"失業後，他過著極度悲慘的生活。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"失業後，他過著極度悲慘的生活。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4183,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::missing::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There is a ____ page in this book.","expectedAnswer":"missing","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There is a ____ page in this book.","clozeAnswer":"missing","exampleTranslation":"這本書缺了一頁。","reference":{"eng":"missing","kk":"/ˈmɪsɪŋ/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['失蹤的；不見的'], ['缺少的；遺漏的']]","chEntries":["失蹤的","不見的","缺少的","遺漏的"],"practiceMeaning":"這本書缺了一頁。","analysis":"來自動詞 'miss' 的現在分詞，原意為“錯過”。'Missing' 作形容詞時，表示某人或某物不在應在的地方，因此找不到。'Miss' 本身源自古諾爾斯語 missa，意為“缺乏，失去”。引申義是指某物本應存在但卻不存在，例如 'missing piece'（缺少的一塊）。","definition":"1. not present in a place or at a time when you would expect it to be; 2. not found or lost.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police are searching for a missing child.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警方正在尋找一個失蹤的兒童。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There is a missing page in this book.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本書缺了一頁。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We noticed something missing from the collection.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們注意到收藏品中少了些東西。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這本書缺了一頁。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3994,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u3::mission::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She felt a strong sense of ____ to help the poor.","expectedAnswer":"mission","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She felt a strong sense of ____ to help the poor.","clozeAnswer":"mission","exampleTranslation":"她覺得自己有幫助窮人的強烈使命感。","reference":{"eng":"mission","kk":"/ˈmɪʃən/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['任務', '使命'], ['（外交）使團'], ['傳教']]","chEntries":["任務","使命","使團","傳教"],"practiceMeaning":"她覺得自己有幫助窮人的強烈使命感。","analysis":"詞源：拉丁文 'missio' (派遣)，源自 'mittere' (派遣)。指被賦予的重要任務或目標，也指被派遣執行某項任務的團體。","definition":"1. an important assignment given to a person or group of people; 2. a body of people sent to a foreign country to act as representatives; 3. an organisation set up to achieve a particular purpose, especially religious or charitable.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The astronauts completed their mission successfully.\",\n    \"ch\": \"太空人成功完成了他們的任務。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She felt a strong sense of mission to help the poor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她覺得自己有幫助窮人的強烈使命感。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The UN sent a mission to the conflict zone.\",\n    \"ch\": \"聯合國派了一個使團前往衝突地區。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她覺得自己有幫助窮人的強烈使命感。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U3、L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4641,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::mobbed::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The politician was ____ as he tried to leave the rally.","expectedAnswer":"mobbed","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The politician was ____ as he tried to leave the rally.","clozeAnswer":"mobbed","exampleTranslation":"這位政治家試圖離開集會時被人群圍堵。","reference":{"eng":"mobbed","kk":"/mɒbd/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['（人群）圍住'], ['（人群）蜂擁而上']]","chEntries":["圍住","蜂擁而上"],"practiceMeaning":"這位政治家試圖離開集會時被人群圍堵。","analysis":"由 'mob' (一群人，尤指暴徒) + '-bed' (過去式) 組成。'Mob' 源自拉丁語 'mobile vulgus' (易變的群眾)。指被大量人群圍繞、騷擾或衝擊，通常是因為明星、名人或重要人物的出現，導致混亂和難以脫身。","definition":"to crowd around someone in an aggressive or excited way.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The celebrity was mobbed by fans outside the hotel.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位名人在飯店外被粉絲圍住。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The politician was mobbed as he tried to leave the rally.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位政治家試圖離開集會時被人群圍堵。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這位政治家試圖離開集會時被人群圍堵。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3098,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::moderate::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She has ____ views on environmental issues.","expectedAnswer":"moderate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She has ____ views on environmental issues.","clozeAnswer":"moderate","exampleTranslation":"她在環境問題上有溫和的觀點。","reference":{"eng":"moderate","kk":"/ˈmɑːdərət/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['適度的；溫和的'], ['中等的；不過分的']]","chEntries":["適度的","溫和的","中等的","不過分的"],"practiceMeaning":"她在環境問題上有溫和的觀點。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'moderatus' (temperate, restrained)，'modus' (measure)。核心意義是「在中間」。\n1. 適度的；溫和的：指不極端，不過分，保持中間立場。\n2. 中等的；不過分的：形容程度、強度、或意見位於中間水平。","definition":"1. neither small nor large, much nor little, easy nor hard, etc.; 2. not extreme or excessive.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has a moderate income.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的收入屬於中等。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has moderate views on environmental issues.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在環境問題上有溫和的觀點。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她在環境問題上有溫和的觀點。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3100,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::monitor::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She was appointed as a ____ for the student council.","expectedAnswer":"monitor","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She was appointed as a ____ for the student council.","clozeAnswer":"monitor","exampleTranslation":"她被任命為學生會的監督員。","reference":{"eng":"monitor","kk":"/ˈmɑːnɪtər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['顯示器；螢幕'], ['（學習、進展等的）監督者；指導者'], ['（飛機、艦船等）監視器']]","chEntries":["顯示器","螢幕","監督者","指導者","監視器"],"practiceMeaning":"她被任命為學生會的監督員。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'monitor' (one who warns)，'monere' (to warn, remind)。指「觀察」或「警告」的工具或人。\n1. 顯示器；螢幕：指用於顯示電腦圖像或影片的設備。\n2. （學習、進展等的）監督者；指導者：指負責觀察、指導或評估某人學習或進展的人。\n3. （飛機、艦船等）監視器：指用於監測、觀察或控制特定設備或系統的裝置。","definition":"1. a screen used with a computer; 2. a person who monitors something; 3. a device used to watch or record something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Connect the cable to the computer monitor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"將電纜連接到電腦顯示器。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She was appointed as a monitor for the student council.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她被任命為學生會的監督員。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The ship's monitor tracked the enemy aircraft.\",\n    \"ch\": \"艦船的監視器追蹤了敵機。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她被任命為學生會的監督員。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4699,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::motel::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ offered free breakfast and Wi-Fi.","expectedAnswer":"motel","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ offered free breakfast and Wi-Fi.","clozeAnswer":"motel","exampleTranslation":"這家汽車旅館提供免費早餐和無線網路。","reference":{"eng":"motel","kk":"/moʊˈtɛl/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['汽車旅館']]","chEntries":["汽車旅館"],"practiceMeaning":"這家汽車旅館提供免費早餐和無線網路。","analysis":"由 'motor'（汽車）和 'hotel'（旅館）組合而成。專指為駕車旅客提供住宿的旅館，通常位於公路旁，停車方便。","definition":"1. A hotel located by a highway, with rooms accessible from the parking area.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We stopped at a motel for the night on our road trip.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們在公路旅行中找了一家汽車旅館過夜。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The motel offered free breakfast and Wi-Fi.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家汽車旅館提供免費早餐和無線網路。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這家汽車旅館提供免費早餐和無線網路。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3102,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::motivation::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His primary ____ for moving was a better job.","expectedAnswer":"motivation","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His primary ____ for moving was a better job.","clozeAnswer":"motivation","exampleTranslation":"他搬遷的主要動機是為了更好的工作。","reference":{"eng":"motivation","kk":"/ˌmoʊtɪˈveɪʃn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['動機；誘因'], ['積極性；學習動力']]","chEntries":["動機","誘因","積極性","學習動力"],"practiceMeaning":"他搬遷的主要動機是為了更好的工作。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'motivus' (moving)，'movere' (to move)。是 'motivate' 的名詞形式。指「促使行動」的原因或動力。\n1. 動機；誘因：指導致某人採取行動或追求某個目標的原因。\n2. 積極性；學習動力：指一個人內在的熱情、興趣和努力的程度。","definition":"1. the reason or reasons for acting or behaving in a particular way; 2. the general desire or willingness of someone to do something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Lack of motivation is a common problem for students.\",\n    \"ch\": \"缺乏學習動力是學生的常見問題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His primary motivation for moving was a better job.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他搬遷的主要動機是為了更好的工作。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他搬遷的主要動機是為了更好的工作。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3231,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::mule::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He's as stubborn as a ____.","expectedAnswer":"mule","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He's as stubborn as a ____.","clozeAnswer":"mule","exampleTranslation":"他像騾子一樣固執。","reference":{"eng":"mule","kk":"/mjuːl/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['騾子'], ['倔強的人'], ['（鞋）拖鞋']]","chEntries":["騾子","倔強的人","拖鞋"],"practiceMeaning":"他像騾子一樣固執。","analysis":"詞源來自拉丁文 'mulus'。指驢與馬雜交產生的不育雌性後代。因其固執和強壯的特性，引申指『倔強的人』。另外，特指一種無後跟的鞋子，稱為『mule shoes』。","definition":"1. a sterile hybrid animal between a male donkey and a female horse; 2. a type of shoe that is backless and typically has a pointed toe.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The mule was strong enough to carry heavy loads.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那頭騾子強壯到足以馱載重物。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He's as stubborn as a mule.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他像騾子一樣固執。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She wore a pair of comfortable mules around the house.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在家裡穿著一雙舒適的拖鞋。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他像騾子一樣固執。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U41"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4181,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::murder::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They were accused of committing ____.","expectedAnswer":"murder","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They were accused of committing ____.","clozeAnswer":"murder","exampleTranslation":"他們被控犯有謀殺罪。","reference":{"eng":"murder","kk":"/ˈmɜːrdər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['謀殺；兇殺案'], ['（尤指）嚴酷的毀滅']]","chEntries":["謀殺","兇殺案","嚴酷的毀滅"],"practiceMeaning":"他們被控犯有謀殺罪。","analysis":"源自古英語 morthor，意為“謀殺”。詞源學上與古諾爾斯語 morð、古高地德語 mord 相關，最終可追溯至原始印歐語 *mer-，意為“殺死”。其核心概念是蓄意且非法地奪取生命。引申義則是任何極其殘酷的毀滅或傷害，例如 'murder the landscape'（毀壞景觀）。","definition":"1. the unlawful killing of another human being with malice aforethought; 2. a brutal or violent destruction or damage.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police are investigating a brutal murder.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警方正在調查一起殘酷的謀殺案。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They were accused of committing murder.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們被控犯有謀殺罪。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This decision was a murder of artistic integrity.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個決定是對藝術完整性的嚴重破壞。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們被控犯有謀殺罪。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U6、L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4207,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::muscle::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company has the financial ____ to expand.","expectedAnswer":"muscle","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company has the financial ____ to expand.","clozeAnswer":"muscle","exampleTranslation":"這家公司有足夠的財力實力來擴張。","reference":{"eng":"muscle","kk":"/ˈmʌsl/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['肌肉'], ['力量；實力']]","chEntries":["肌肉","力量","實力"],"practiceMeaning":"這家公司有足夠的財力實力來擴張。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 musculus，意為“小老鼠”。'Mus'（老鼠）+ '-culus'（指小）。這個名字的由來是因為古羅馬人認為彎曲的肌肉看起來像老鼠在皮膚下蠕動。1. “肌肉”是其生理學上的主要含義。2. “力量；實力”是引申義，指人或組織所擁有的實際能力和影響力。","definition":"1. a band of fibrous tissue in a human or animal in which the chief function is contraction and relaxation so as to produce movement in a part of the body; 2. strength or power.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has strong muscles from weightlifting.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他通過舉重鍛鍊出了強壯的肌肉。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company has the financial muscle to expand.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司有足夠的財力實力來擴張。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"You need to flex your muscles to open this jar.\",\n    \"ch\": \"你需要用力才能打開這個罐子。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這家公司有足夠的財力實力來擴張。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5135,"wordRef":"字彙王::u62::muscular::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The athlete underwent ____ training.","expectedAnswer":"muscular","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The athlete underwent ____ training.","clozeAnswer":"muscular","exampleTranslation":"這位運動員接受了肌肉訓練。","reference":{"eng":"muscular","kk":"ˈmʌskjələr","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['肌肉的'], ['強壯的'], ['肌肉發達的']]","chEntries":["肌肉的","強壯的","肌肉發達的"],"practiceMeaning":"這位運動員接受了肌肉訓練。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 muscularis，由 musculus（肌肉，是 mus 的指小詞，意為「小老鼠」）+ -aris（形容詞字尾）組成。musculus 之所以稱為「小老鼠」，是因為古羅馬人認為肌肉收縮時的形狀像老鼠在皮膚下移動。核心語意是「與肌肉有關的」，引申為「強壯的、肌肉發達的」。","definition":"relating to or consisting of muscle; having well-developed muscles; strong.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has a muscular physique.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他有著肌肉發達的體格。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The athlete underwent muscular training.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位運動員接受了肌肉訓練。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這位運動員接受了肌肉訓練。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U62"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5136,"wordRef":"字彙王::u62::myth::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The idea that you can get rich quickly is a ____.","expectedAnswer":"myth","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The idea that you can get rich quickly is a ____.","clozeAnswer":"myth","exampleTranslation":"快速致富的想法是一個迷思。","reference":{"eng":"myth","kk":"mɪθ","tense":"n.","ch":"[['神話'], ['傳說'], ['虛構的事']]","chEntries":["神話","傳說","虛構的事"],"practiceMeaning":"快速致富的想法是一個迷思。","analysis":"此字源自希臘語 mythos，意為「言語、講述、傳說、故事」。與 *muthos（嘴、言語）有關。核心語意是「傳統的、關於超自然力量或英雄人物的故事」，常被用來解釋世界的起源、自然現象或文化習俗。","definition":"a traditional story, especially one concerning the early history of a people or explaining some natural or social phenomenon, and typically involving supernatural beings or events; a widely held but false belief or idea.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Greek mythology is full of fascinating stories.\",\n    \"ch\": \"希臘神話充滿了引人入勝的故事。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The idea that you can get rich quickly is a myth.\",\n    \"ch\": \"快速致富的想法是一個迷思。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"快速致富的想法是一個迷思。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U62"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5636,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l8::narrow::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company faces ____ profit margins.","expectedAnswer":"narrow","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company faces ____ profit margins.","clozeAnswer":"narrow","exampleTranslation":"這家公司面臨著狹窄的利潤空間。","reference":{"eng":"narrow","kk":"ˈnæroʊ","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['狹窄的'], ['狹小的'], ['（範圍、機會等）有限的'], ['（視野、思想等）狹隘的'], ['（聲音）尖銳的']]","chEntries":["狹窄的","狹小的","有限的","狹隘的","尖銳的"],"practiceMeaning":"這家公司面臨著狹窄的利潤空間。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 narow，可能來自古英語 nearu，意為「窄的」。其詞源與原始日耳曼語 *nauraz（窄）相關，更上溯至原始印歐語 *ner-（左；左邊；在左邊）或 *en-（在內）。此字的核心語義是「空間上的狹窄」，並由此引申出範圍、機會、思想、視野的「有限」或「狹隘」。構詞上，此字為單一詞根，無明顯字首字尾。此處為形容詞用法，描述名詞的空間、範圍、程度或性質。","definition":"limited in width; small in distance from one side to the other; restricted in scope, opportunity, or vision; sharp or high-pitched in sound.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We walked down a narrow alley.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們走過一條狹窄的巷子。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company faces narrow profit margins.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司面臨著狹窄的利潤空間。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has very narrow views on social issues.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在社會議題上有著非常狹隘的觀點。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這家公司面臨著狹窄的利潤空間。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4500,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::nationwide::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There was a ____ shortage of the drug.","expectedAnswer":"nationwide","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There was a ____ shortage of the drug.","clozeAnswer":"nationwide","exampleTranslation":"全國範圍內都出現了該藥物的短缺。","reference":{"eng":"nationwide","kk":"/ˌneɪʃnˈwaɪd/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['全國性的']]","chEntries":["全國性的"],"practiceMeaning":"全國範圍內都出現了該藥物的短缺。","analysis":"由 nation (國家) 和 wide (廣泛的) 組成。核心語意是「遍及整個國家的」。","definition":"1. Extending or spread throughout a whole nation.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government launched a nationwide campaign against pollution.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府發起了全國性的反污染運動。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was a nationwide shortage of the drug.\",\n    \"ch\": \"全國範圍內都出現了該藥物的短缺。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"全國範圍內都出現了該藥物的短缺。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4353,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::native-language::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She is fluent in her ____ and two foreign languages.","expectedAnswer":"native language","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She is fluent in her ____ and two foreign languages.","clozeAnswer":"native language","exampleTranslation":"她精通她的母語和兩種外語。","reference":{"eng":"native language","kk":"None","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['母語']]","chEntries":["母語"],"practiceMeaning":"她精通她的母語和兩種外語。","analysis":"此為片語分析。'native' (adj.) 源自拉丁語 'nativus'，意為『天生的，出生的』，指『本國的，土生土長的』。'language' (n.) 源自拉丁語 'lingua'，指『語言』。兩者結合，指一個人出生時起就學會的、最熟悉的語言，即『母語』。","definition":"the language that someone has spoken since they were a child","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"English is my native language.\",\n    \"ch\": \"英語是我的母語。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is fluent in her native language and two foreign languages.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她精通她的母語和兩種外語。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她精通她的母語和兩種外語。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4354,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::natives::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Tourists should respect the customs of the ____.","expectedAnswer":"natives","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Tourists should respect the customs of the ____.","clozeAnswer":"natives","exampleTranslation":"遊客應尊重當地居民的習俗。","reference":{"eng":"natives","kk":"/ˈneɪtɪvz/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['本地人；原住民']]","chEntries":["本地人","原住民"],"practiceMeaning":"遊客應尊重當地居民的習俗。","analysis":"此為單字分析。'native' (n.) 源自拉丁語 'nativus'，意為『天生的，出生的』，在此為複數形式，指『本地人』或『原住民』，強調他們是特定地區出生並長期居住的居民。","definition":"people who were born in a particular place, rather than coming to live there from somewhere else","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The culture of the natives was preserved through oral traditions.\",\n    \"ch\": \"原住民的文化通過口述傳統得以保存。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Tourists should respect the customs of the natives.\",\n    \"