"研討會","講座","討論會"],"practiceMeaning":"教授正在主持一個研究生研討會。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 seminarium，意為「種子田」，來自 semen（seed）。核心語義是「播種」，引申為知識、思想的「播種」或傳播之地。在學術語境中，seminar 指一種小型的、通常由專家主持的、參與者進行深入討論或學習的會議。","definition":"a meeting for discussion or exchange of information on a particular subject.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We attended an interesting seminar on climate change.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們參加了一個關於氣候變遷的有趣研討會。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The professor is leading a seminar for graduate students.\",\n    \"ch\": \"教授正在主持一個研究生研討會。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She gave a presentation at the international seminar.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在國際研討會上做了一個報告。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"教授正在主持一個研究生研討會。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4265,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::senior::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The college offers programs for both junior and ____ students.","expectedAnswer":"senior","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The college offers programs for both junior and ____ students.","clozeAnswer":"senior","exampleTranslation":"這所大學提供給大學部低年級和高年級學生的課程。","reference":{"eng":"senior","kk":"/ˈsiːnjər/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['資深的'], ['高年級的'], ['年長的']]","chEntries":["資深的","高年級的","年長的"],"practiceMeaning":"這所大學提供給大學部低年級和高年級學生的課程。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'senior'，比較級形式，意為「更年長的」。'Senior' 在用法上多用於比較，表示在年齡、職位或學業上的較高層級。與 'junior' 相對。","definition":"older; having a higher rank or longer period of service.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a senior engineer with over 20 years of experience.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一位擁有超過20年經驗的資深工程師。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The college offers programs for both junior and senior students.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這所大學提供給大學部低年級和高年級學生的課程。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這所大學提供給大學部低年級和高年級學生的課程。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4260,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::sensible::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She wore ____ shoes for the hike.","expectedAnswer":"sensible","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She wore ____ shoes for the hike.","clozeAnswer":"sensible","exampleTranslation":"她為徒步旅行穿了實用的鞋子。","reference":{"eng":"sensible","kk":"/ˈsɛnsəbəl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['明智的'], ['理性的'], ['切實可行的'], ['（指衣物、顏色等）實用的']]","chEntries":["明智的","理性的","切實可行的","實用的"],"practiceMeaning":"她為徒步旅行穿了實用的鞋子。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'sensibilis'（有感覺的、可感覺到的），與 'sentire'（感覺、思考）有關。'Sensible' 指「基於理性、判斷力或常識的」，能夠做出好的、明智的決策。它強調一種務實和理性的態度。","definition":"having or showing good judgment; practical and reasonable; aware of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's sensible to save money for emergencies.\",\n    \"ch\": \"為應急情況存錢是很明智的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She wore sensible shoes for the hike.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她為徒步旅行穿了實用的鞋子。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她為徒步旅行穿了實用的鞋子。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U7、L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6135,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::sensor::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"A smoke ____ detected the fire.","expectedAnswer":"sensor","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"A smoke ____ detected the fire.","clozeAnswer":"sensor","exampleTranslation":"煙霧感測器偵測到了火災。","reference":{"eng":"sensor","kk":"ˈsɛnsər","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"感測器\"  ],  [    \"探測器\"  ],  [    \"感應器\"  ]]","chEntries":["感測器","探測器","感應器"],"practiceMeaning":"煙霧感測器偵測到了火災。","analysis":"此字由動詞 sense（感覺；感知）加上名詞後綴 -or（表示施事者或工具）構成。sense 源自拉丁語 sensus，意為「感覺；知覺」，來自 sentire（感覺）。因此，sensor 的核心語義是「感知或偵測的工具」。此名詞指能夠偵測物理現象（如光、熱、運動、濕度、壓力等）並將其轉化為電信號的裝置。其語意演變是從「感知者」到「偵測裝置」。","definition":"A device that detects and responds to some type of input from the physical environment.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The car is equipped with several sensors.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這輛車配備了多個感測器。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A smoke sensor detected the fire.\",\n    \"ch\": \"煙霧感測器偵測到了火災。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The motion sensor activated the alarm.\",\n    \"ch\": \"運動感測器啟動了警報。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"煙霧感測器偵測到了火災。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6137,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::sentimental::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He is ____ about his childhood.","expectedAnswer":"sentimental","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He is ____ about his childhood.","clozeAnswer":"sentimental","exampleTranslation":"他對童年充滿感傷。","reference":{"eng":"sentimental","kk":"ˌsɛntɪˈmɛntl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"感傷的\"  ],  [    \"情感的\"  ],  [    \"多愁善感的\"  ],  [    \"情意的\"  ]]","chEntries":["感傷的","情感的","多愁善感的","情意的"],"practiceMeaning":"他對童年充滿感傷。","analysis":"此字由 sentiment（情感）加上形容詞後綴 -al 構成。sentiment 源自拉丁語 sentimentum（感覺；思想）。因此，sentimental 的核心語義是「與情感相關的」。此形容詞描述傾向於表達或受到強烈情感（尤其是感傷、溫情）影響的。其語意演變是從「情感的」到「過於感傷的」或「充滿溫情的」。","definition":"1. of or prompted by sentiment or emotion; 2. of or relating to feelings of tenderness, sadness, or nostalgia; 3. characterized by or showing excessive tenderness, sadness, or nostalgia.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"a sentimental song\",\n    \"ch\": \"一首感傷的歌\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is sentimental about his childhood.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對童年充滿感傷。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was a sentimental journey down memory lane.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一次回憶往昔的感傷之旅。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他對童年充滿感傷。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4700,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::separation::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They have been living in ____ for a year.","expectedAnswer":"separation","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They have been living in ____ for a year.","clozeAnswer":"separation","exampleTranslation":"他們已經分居一年了。","reference":{"eng":"separation","kk":"/ˌsɛpəˈreɪʃən/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['分離'], ['分居'], ['（科學）分離，（化學）分餾']]","chEntries":["分離","分居","分離，分餾"],"practiceMeaning":"他們已經分居一年了。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 *separatio*，由 *separare*（分開）演變而來。核心是將事物或個體分開的狀態或過程。引申至人際關係的分居，以及科學上將不同物質或成分分開的技術。","definition":"1. The state of being separated or divided. 2. The act of ending a marriage or relationship. 3. The process of dividing substances or components.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The separation of the two elements was difficult.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這兩種元素的 the separation 過程很困難。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They have been living in separation for a year.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們已經分居一年了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The separation of milk into cream and skimmed milk is a common process.\",\n    \"ch\": \"牛奶分離成鮮奶油和脫脂牛奶是一個常見的過程。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們已經分居一年了。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5061,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::sequence::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He learned the dance steps in ____.","expectedAnswer":"sequence","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He learned the dance steps in ____.","clozeAnswer":"sequence","exampleTranslation":"他按順序學會了舞蹈動作。","reference":{"eng":"sequence","kk":"ˈsiːkwəns","tense":"n.","ch":"[['序列'], ['順序'], ['連續發生的事情']]","chEntries":["序列","順序","連續發生的事情"],"practiceMeaning":"他按順序學會了舞蹈動作。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語sequentia，是動詞sequi（跟隨）的派生詞。sequi 又來自原始印歐語 *sekʷ-（跟隨）。sequence 的核心語意是「事物按照特定順序排列或接續」，強調的是「先後關係」或「連續性」。OCR 掃描時可能將 's' 誤判為 '5'，或 'q' 誤判為 'g'。此處修正為 sequence。","definition":"1. a set of related events, movements, or things that follow each other in a particular order; 2. a continuous series of events.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The sequence of events was unclear.\",\n    \"ch\": \"事件的順序不清楚。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He learned the dance steps in sequence.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他按順序學會了舞蹈動作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is the first sequence in the film.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是電影的第一個鏡頭（連續畫面）。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他按順序學會了舞蹈動作。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6138,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::server::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The waiter, or ____, took our order.","expectedAnswer":"server","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The waiter, or ____, took our order.","clozeAnswer":"server","exampleTranslation":"服務員，也就是侍者，為我們點餐。","reference":{"eng":"server","kk":"ˈsɜːrvər","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"伺服器\"  ],  [    \"服務員\"  ],  [    \"侍者\"  ]]","chEntries":["伺服器","服務員","侍者"],"practiceMeaning":"服務員，也就是侍者，為我們點餐。","analysis":"此字由動詞 serve（服務）加上名詞後綴 -er（表示施事者或工具）構成。serve 源自拉丁語 servīre（服務；服從），來自 servus（奴隸）。因此，server 的核心語義是「提供服務者」。在電腦領域，指提供數據、資源或服務的電腦系統（伺服器）。在餐飲業，指提供服務的人（服務員，侍者）。其語意演變是從「服務者」到具體的「伺服器」和「服務員」。","definition":"1. a computer or computer program that manages access to a centralized resource or service; 2. a person who serves food or drinks in a restaurant or bar.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The website is down because the server is overloaded.\",\n    \"ch\": \"網站無法訪問，因為伺服器過載了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The waiter, or server, took our order.\",\n    \"ch\": \"服務員，也就是侍者，為我們點餐。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The database server stores all the user information.\",\n    \"ch\": \"資料庫伺服器儲存了所有使用者資訊。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"服務員，也就是侍者，為我們點餐。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5062,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::session::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She has a therapy ____ every Tuesday.","expectedAnswer":"session","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She has a therapy ____ every Tuesday.","clozeAnswer":"session","exampleTranslation":"她每週二都有一次治療時間。","reference":{"eng":"session","kk":"ˈseʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[['會議'], ['會議期間'], ['（活動或課程的）一次（時間段）']]","chEntries":["會議","會議期間","一次"],"practiceMeaning":"她每週二都有一次治療時間。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語sessio，是動詞sedere（坐）的派生詞。sedere 又來自原始印歐語 *sed-（坐）。session 的核心語意是「人們聚集在一起進行某項活動（如開會、上課、治療）的一段時間」。它強調的是活動的持續時間和集體性。OCR 掃描時可能將 's' 誤判為 '5'，或 'o' 誤判為 '0'。此處修正為 session。","definition":"1. a period devoted to a particular activity or meeting; 2. a period of time during which a court, legislature, or other body is assembled.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The parliament will convene for a special session next week.\",\n    \"ch\": \"議會將於下週召開特別會議。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a therapy session every Tuesday.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她每週二都有一次治療時間。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The training session lasted for three hours.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這次培訓持續了三個小時。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她每週二都有一次治療時間。","sourceName":"字彙王、龍騰課本","unitName":"U59、L2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4666,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::set-a-record::idiom","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company ____ for sales this year.","expectedAnswer":"set a record","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company ____ for sales this year.","clozeAnswer":"set a record","exampleTranslation":"公司今年創下了銷售紀錄。","reference":{"eng":"set a record","kk":"/sɛt ə ˈrɛkərd/","tense":"idiom","ch":"[['創紀錄'], ['創下紀錄']]","chEntries":["創紀錄","創下紀錄"],"practiceMeaning":"公司今年創下了銷售紀錄。","analysis":"此為固定片語。'Set' (設定、創立) + 'a record' (一個紀錄)。指在某項活動或競賽中，取得前所未有的最佳成績或最高紀錄。","definition":"to achieve the best result or highest score ever in a competition or activity.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The athlete set a new Olympic record.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這名運動員創下了新的奧運紀錄。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company set a record for sales this year.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司今年創下了銷售紀錄。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"公司今年創下了銷售紀錄。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4337,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::shadow::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He walked in the ____ of the building.","expectedAnswer":"shadow","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He walked in the ____ of the building.","clozeAnswer":"shadow","exampleTranslation":"他走在建築物的陰影裡。","reference":{"eng":"shadow","kk":"/ˈʃædoʊ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['陰影；影子'], ['（光線被遮擋形成的）暗區'], ['（對某事物的）影響；不安；沮喪'], ['鬼魂；幽靈']]","chEntries":["陰影","影子","暗區","影響","不安","沮喪","鬼魂","幽靈"],"practiceMeaning":"他走在建築物的陰影裡。","analysis":"源自古英語 'sceadwa'，與『遮蔽』、『陰影』相關。1. 光線被物體遮擋而形成的『影子』。2. 物理空間上的『陰影、暗區』。3. 作為比喻，指事物『受到的影響』，可以是負面的，如『不安、沮喪』，或是一個長期存在、難以擺脫的『陰影』。4. 在文學或宗教語境中，指『鬼魂、幽靈』，即沒有實體的影子。","definition":"an area of darkness where light is blocked by an object; a dark area or shape that is produced when an object is between a light source and a surface; an unpleasant feeling that spoils something; the ghost of a dead person","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The tree cast a long shadow.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這棵樹投下了一道長長的影子。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He walked in the shadow of the building.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他走在建築物的陰影裡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The war left a shadow over the country's future.\",\n    \"ch\": \"戰爭給國家的未來蒙上了陰影。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The ghost appeared as a shadowy figure.\",\n    \"ch\": \"鬼魂出現時，像一個模糊的影子。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他走在建築物的陰影裡。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6140,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::sheer::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The cliff was ____.","expectedAnswer":"sheer","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The cliff was ____.","clozeAnswer":"sheer","exampleTranslation":"懸崖很陡峭。","reference":{"eng":"sheer","kk":"ʃɪr","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"純粹的\"  ],  [    \"徹底的\"  ],  [    \"極度的\"  ],  [    \"陡峭的\"  ],  [    \"透明的\"  ]]","chEntries":["純粹的","徹底的","極度的","陡峭的","透明的"],"practiceMeaning":"懸崖很陡峭。","analysis":"此字詞源不確定，可能源自古英語 scīr（純淨的，清澈的）或中古英語 sheer（陡峭的）。modern 用法包含「純粹的、徹底的、極度的」以及「陡峭的、險峻的」。前者語意演變是從「純淨」到「無混雜」，後者則是「垂直的」。","definition":"1. nothing other than; unmitigated; 2. steep or vertical; 3. (of fabric) thin and transparent.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Sheer joy filled the room.\",\n    \"ch\": \"純粹的喜悅充滿了房間。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The cliff was sheer.\",\n    \"ch\": \"懸崖很陡峭。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Sheer determination helped her succeed.\",\n    \"ch\": \"純粹的決心幫助她取得了成功。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"懸崖很陡峭。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6141,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::shield::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ protected him from the rain.","expectedAnswer":"shield","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ protected him from the rain.","clozeAnswer":"shield","exampleTranslation":"這個遮蔽物保護他免受雨淋。","reference":{"eng":"shield","kk":"ʃild","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"盾牌\"  ],  [    \"保護物\"  ],  [    \"防護罩\"  ],  [    \"遮蔽\"  ]]","chEntries":["盾牌","保護物","防護罩","遮蔽"],"practiceMeaning":"這個遮蔽物保護他免受雨淋。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 scield，與荷蘭語 schild、德語 Schild 同源。原始日耳曼語詞根 *skjalda-，意為「盾牌」。此名詞指古代戰士用來抵擋攻擊的「盾牌」，引申為任何用來保護、遮蔽或防禦的事物。其語意演變是從具體的「盾牌」到抽象的「保護、遮蔽」。","definition":"1. a piece of armor carried on the arm or held in the hand, used by soldiers in ancient times for protection against blows or missiles; 2. a person or thing that protects or defends someone or something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The knight raised his shield to block the attack.\",\n    \"ch\": \"騎士舉起盾牌抵擋攻擊。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The shield protected him from the rain.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個遮蔽物保護他免受雨淋。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company acted as a shield against criticism.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司充當了批評的擋箭牌。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個遮蔽物保護他免受雨淋。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6190,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::shiver::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She felt a ____ of anticipation.","expectedAnswer":"shiver","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She felt a ____ of anticipation.","clozeAnswer":"shiver","exampleTranslation":"她感到一陣期待的顫抖。","reference":{"eng":"shiver","kk":"ˈʃɪvər","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"發抖\"  ],  [    \"顫抖\"  ]]","chEntries":["發抖","顫抖"],"practiceMeaning":"她感到一陣期待的顫抖。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 shiveren。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作為名詞，是動詞 shiver「發抖、顫抖」的名詞化。其核心語義是指「由於寒冷、恐懼或興奮而身體不由自主地顫抖的動作」。","definition":"1. an act of shivering.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He gave a shiver and pulled his coat tighter.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他打了一個寒顫，把外套裹得更緊了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She felt a shiver of anticipation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她感到一陣期待的顫抖。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A shiver of disgust crossed his face.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一絲厭惡的顫抖劃過他的臉。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她感到一陣期待的顫抖。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4151,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::shorten::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company is trying to ____ the delivery time.","expectedAnswer":"shorten","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company is trying to ____ the delivery time.","clozeAnswer":"shorten","exampleTranslation":"公司正試圖縮短交貨時間。","reference":{"eng":"shorten","kk":"/ˈʃɔːrtn/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['縮短', '變短']]","chEntries":["縮短","變短"],"practiceMeaning":"公司正試圖縮短交貨時間。","analysis":"由 short（短的）+ -en（動詞後綴，表示使...變）組成。核心概念是「使長度、時間或範圍變短」。","definition":"1. make or become shorter; 2. reduce the length of (a piece of writing or speech)","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They decided to shorten the meeting.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們決定縮短會議時間。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company is trying to shorten the delivery time.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司正試圖縮短交貨時間。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Can you shorten this skirt?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你能把這條裙子改短些嗎？\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"公司正試圖縮短交貨時間。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4463,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::shortly::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She replied ____, 'No'.","expectedAnswer":"shortly","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She replied ____, 'No'.","clozeAnswer":"shortly","exampleTranslation":"她簡潔地回答：「不」。