:"她的第一次單獨飛行令人緊張。","reference":{"eng":"solo","kk":"ˈsolo","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"獨奏\"  ],  [    \"獨唱\"  ],  [    \"獨自一人\"  ]]","chEntries":["獨奏","獨唱","獨自一人"],"practiceMeaning":"她的第一次單獨飛行令人緊張。","analysis":"此字源自義大利語 solo（alone）。作為名詞，指「單獨的表演」，如音樂的「獨奏」或「獨唱」。也可以指「獨自的行為」或「獨自一人」。","definition":"1. a thing done alone; 2. a performance by one person, especially in music.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The pianist played a difficult solo.\",\n    \"ch\": \"鋼琴家演奏了一首高難度的獨奏曲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her first solo flight was nerve-wracking.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的第一次單獨飛行令人緊張。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The singer's solo was met with thunderous applause.\",\n    \"ch\": \"歌手的獨唱贏得了雷鳴般的掌聲。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她的第一次單獨飛行令人緊張。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4498,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::soundproof::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They installed ____ windows to reduce noise.","expectedAnswer":"soundproof","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They installed ____ windows to reduce noise.","clozeAnswer":"soundproof","exampleTranslation":"他們安裝了隔音窗戶以減少噪音。","reference":{"eng":"soundproof","kk":"/ˈsaʊndˌpruːf/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['隔音的'], ['防音的']]","chEntries":["隔音的","防音的"],"practiceMeaning":"他們安裝了隔音窗戶以減少噪音。","analysis":"由 sound (聲音) 和 proof (防護) 組成。核心語意是「能阻止聲音通過的」。","definition":"1. Impervious to sound.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The recording studio is soundproof.\",\n    \"ch\": \"錄音室是隔音的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They installed soundproof windows to reduce noise.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們安裝了隔音窗戶以減少噪音。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們安裝了隔音窗戶以減少噪音。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5102,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::sow::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The teacher tried to ____ seeds of curiosity in her students.","expectedAnswer":"sow","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The teacher tried to ____ seeds of curiosity in her students.","clozeAnswer":"sow","exampleTranslation":"老師試圖在學生心中播下好奇的種子。","reference":{"eng":"sow","kk":"soʊ","tense":"v.","ch":"[['播種']]","chEntries":["播種"],"practiceMeaning":"老師試圖在學生心中播下好奇的種子。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 'sāwan'，與德語 'säen' 和荷蘭語 'zaaien' 同源，原始印歐語詞根為 '*seh₁-' (to sow)。其核心語義是 '將種子撒播到土地裡，以便將來生長'。這個動作是農業的基礎，也引申為 '播下（某種事物，如想法、情感、影響）'，強調其開始和傳播的過程。","definition":"1. To plant seed or plants in or on the ground.; 2. To be the source of or cause of (something, especially something bad).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Farmers sow seeds in the spring.\",\n    \"ch\": \"農民在春天播種。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The teacher tried to sow seeds of curiosity in her students.\",\n    \"ch\": \"老師試圖在學生心中播下好奇的種子。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"老師試圖在學生心中播下好奇的種子。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3989,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u3::spice::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"A little ____ makes life more interesting.","expectedAnswer":"spice","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"A little ____ makes life more interesting.","clozeAnswer":"spice","exampleTranslation":"一點情趣能讓生活更有趣。","reference":{"eng":"spice","kk":"/spaɪs/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['香料', '調味料'], ['情趣', '趣味']]","chEntries":["香料","調味料","情趣","趣味"],"practiceMeaning":"一點情趣能讓生活更有趣。","analysis":"詞源：古法語 'espice' (香料)，來自拉丁文 'species' (種類，這裡指特定的、有價值的物品)。名詞指用於增添食物風味的植物性調味料，引申為能增添生活樂趣或趣味的事物。","definition":"1. a substance obtained from a plant, used to flavor food; 2. a quality that adds interest or excitement.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Cinnamon is a common spice used in baking.\",\n    \"ch\": \"肉桂是烘焙中常用的香料。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A little spice makes life more interesting.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一點情趣能讓生活更有趣。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"一點情趣能讓生活更有趣。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4278,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::spinach::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ is rich in vitamins.","expectedAnswer":"Spinach","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ is rich in vitamins.","clozeAnswer":"Spinach","exampleTranslation":"菠菜富含維生素。","reference":{"eng":"spinach","kk":"/ˈspɪnɪtʃ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['菠菜']]","chEntries":["菠菜"],"practiceMeaning":"菠菜富含維生素。","analysis":"源自古法語 'espinache'，可能來自阿拉伯語 'isfanākh'。'Spinach' 指一種常見的綠葉蔬菜。","definition":"a plant with large, dark green leaves that are eaten as a vegetable.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Popeye the Sailor Man loved to eat spinach.\",\n    \"ch\": \"大力水手熱愛吃菠菜。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Spinach is rich in vitamins.\",\n    \"ch\": \"菠菜富含維生素。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"菠菜富含維生素。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4003,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u3::staff::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The wizard carried a magic ____.","expectedAnswer":"staff","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The wizard carried a magic ____.","clozeAnswer":"staff","exampleTranslation":"巫師拿著一根魔法杖。","reference":{"eng":"staff","kk":"/stæf/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['全體員工', '職員'], ['（樂器）棍棒', '（旗幟）旗杆']]","chEntries":["全體員工","職員","棍棒","旗杆"],"practiceMeaning":"巫師拿著一根魔法杖。","analysis":"詞源：古英語 'stæf' (權杖、棍子)。最初指權杖或棍棒，引申為武器，再引申為組織中的服務人員，以及用於支撐或懸掛的長條狀物。","definition":"1. a group of people working in a particular organization or department; 2. a long stick used as a support when walking or as a weapon.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The hotel staff were very helpful.\",\n    \"ch\": \"酒店員工非常樂於助人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The wizard carried a magic staff.\",\n    \"ch\": \"巫師拿著一根魔法杖。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"巫師拿著一根魔法杖。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4540,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::stale::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The conversation became ____ after a while.","expectedAnswer":"stale","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The conversation became ____ after a while.","clozeAnswer":"stale","exampleTranslation":"談話過了一會兒就變得乏味了。","reference":{"eng":"stale","kk":"/steɪl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['不新鮮的', '變質的'], ['陳舊的', '乏味的'], ['（空氣）不流通的']]","chEntries":["不新鮮的","變質的","陳舊的","乏味的","不流通的"],"practiceMeaning":"談話過了一會兒就變得乏味了。","analysis":"源自古法語 'estale'，意為 'stale, immovable' (陳舊的、不動的)。\n    1. 不新鮮、變質：指食物失去新鮮度，如 'stale bread' (不新鮮的麵包)。\n    2. 陳舊、乏味：指事物缺乏新意、吸引力，如 'stale jokes' (陳舊的笑話)。\n    3. 空氣不流通：指室內空氣因缺乏流通而變得污濁。 'go stale' 指變質或變得乏味。","definition":"1. no longer fresh and therefore unpleasant to eat or smell.; 2. lacking in originality or freshness; dull.; 3. (of air) no longer fresh and pleasant; stagnant.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The bread had gone stale.\",\n    \"ch\": \"麵包已經不新鮮了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The conversation became stale after a while.\",\n    \"ch\": \"談話過了一會兒就變得乏味了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Open the window to let in some fresh air; the room is stale.\",\n    \"ch\": \"打開窗戶讓新鮮空氣進來；房間裡的空氣不流通。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"談話過了一會兒就變得乏味了。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4274,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::stare::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Don't ____ at people; it's rude.","expectedAnswer":"stare","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Don't ____ at people; it's rude.","clozeAnswer":"stare","exampleTranslation":"不要盯著人看，這很不禮貌。","reference":{"eng":"stare","kk":"/stɛr/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['盯著'], ['凝視']]","chEntries":["盯著","凝視"],"practiceMeaning":"不要盯著人看，這很不禮貌。","analysis":"源自古英語 'starian'。'Stare' 強調「長時間、直接地、固定地看」，通常帶有驚訝、好奇、困惑或敵意的意味，與 'look'（看）或 'glance'（瞥）的短暫性不同。","definition":"to look fixedly or intently at someone or something with the eyes wide open.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She stared at him in disbelief.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她難以置信地盯著他。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Don't stare at people; it's rude.\",\n    \"ch\": \"不要盯著人看，這很不禮貌。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"不要盯著人看，這很不禮貌。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4567,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::steady::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company has shown ____ growth over the past decade.","expectedAnswer":"steady","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company has shown ____ growth over the past decade.","clozeAnswer":"steady","exampleTranslation":"這家公司在過去十年中一直保持穩定增長。","reference":{"eng":"steady","kk":"/ˈstɛdi/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['穩定的', '平穩的'], ['持續的', '不變的'], ['鎮定的', '冷靜的']]","chEntries":["穩定的","平穩的","持續的","不變的","鎮定的","冷靜的"],"practiceMeaning":"這家公司在過去十年中一直保持穩定增長。","analysis":"源自古法語 'esté'，'ester' (to stand - 站立) 的派生詞。核心概念是「穩固地站著」。\n    1. 穩定的、平穩的：指不搖晃、不顛簸，狀態持續。\n    2. 持續的、不變的：指時間長久，沒有顯著變化。\n    3. 鎮定的、冷靜的：指情緒或反應沉著，不易受影響。","definition":"1. firmly fixed, supported, or balanced; not shaking or moving.; 2. not changing or fluctuating; regular and continuous.; 3. (of a person or their behavior) not showing extreme emotion; calm and sensible.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a steady hand for surgery.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她做手術時手很穩。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company has shown steady growth over the past decade.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司在過去十年中一直保持穩定增長。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He remained steady in the face of danger.\",\n    \"ch\": \"面對危險，他保持鎮定。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這家公司在過去十年中一直保持穩定增長。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5450,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::strike-a-balance::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The government is trying to ____ between economic growth and environmental protection.","expectedAnswer":"strike a balance","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The government is trying to ____ between economic growth and environmental protection.","clozeAnswer":"strike a balance","exampleTranslation":"政府正試圖在經濟成長和環境保護之間取得平衡。","reference":{"eng":"strike a balance","kk":"ˈstraɪk ə ˈbælən(t)s","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['達成平衡'], ['取得平衡']]","chEntries":["達成平衡","取得平衡"],"practiceMeaning":"政府正試圖在經濟成長和環境保護之間取得平衡。","analysis":"此片語由動詞 \"strike\" (在此意為「達成」、「取得」) 和名詞 \"balance\" (平衡) 組成。\"strike\" 在此是比喻用法，指成功地達到某個點或狀態。\"balance\" 源自拉丁語 \"bilancia\"，意為\"天平\"，引申為\"平衡\"。此片語意指在兩種對立或不同的事物之間找到一個適當的、中庸的點，使其既能實現一方面的需求，又不犧牲另一方面的利益。","definition":"to achieve a situation where two opposite things exist together in a reasonable or acceptable way.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's important to strike a balance between work and personal life.\",\n    \"ch\": \"在工作和個人生活之間取得平衡是很重要的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government is trying to strike a balance between economic growth and environmental protection.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府正試圖在經濟成長和環境保護之間取得平衡。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"政府正試圖在經濟成長和環境保護之間取得平衡。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5146,"wordRef":"字彙王::u62::striking::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The dancer had ____ eyes.","expectedAnswer":"striking","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The dancer had ____ eyes.","clozeAnswer":"striking","exampleTranslation":"這位舞者有著引人注目的雙眼。","reference":{"eng":"striking","kk":"ˈstraɪkɪŋ","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['引人注目的'], ['顯著的'], ['令人驚訝的']]","chEntries":["引人注目的","顯著的","令人驚訝的"],"practiceMeaning":"這位舞者有著引人注目的雙眼。","analysis":"此字是動詞 strike（擊打、觸動）的現在分詞，在此處用作形容詞。strike 源自古英語 strīcan（撫摸、擊打），與原始日耳曼語 *strīkan- 相關。核心語意是「有力地觸碰或發生關聯」，引申為「觸動人心、給人留下深刻印象」，因此形容詞 striking 表示「引人注目的、顯著的、美麗的」。","definition":"attractive or impressive; noticeable or remarkable.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a striking resemblance to her mother.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她與她母親有驚人的相似之處。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The dancer had striking eyes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位舞者有著引人注目的雙眼。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這位舞者有著引人注目的雙眼。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U62"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3987,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u3::structure::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The Eiffel Tower is a famous ____ in Paris.","expectedAnswer":"structure","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The Eiffel Tower is a famous ____ in Paris.","clozeAnswer":"structure","exampleTranslation":"艾菲爾鐵塔是巴黎一座著名的建築物。","reference":{"eng":"structure","kk":"/ˈstrʌktʃər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['結構', '構造'], ['建築物', '建築']]","chEntries":["結構","構造","建築物","建築"],"practiceMeaning":"艾菲爾鐵塔是巴黎一座著名的建築物。","analysis":"詞源：拉丁文 'structura' (建造、結構)，源自 'struere' (建造)。核心意義是組成的部分如何組織在一起，引申為由這些部分構成的實體。","definition":"1. the arrangement of and relations between the parts or elements of something complex; 2. a building or other edifice.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The structure of the novel is complex.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本小說的結構很複雜。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The Eiffel Tower is a famous structure in Paris.\",\n    \"ch\": \"艾菲爾鐵塔是巴黎一座著名的建築物。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"艾菲爾鐵塔是巴黎一座著名的建築物。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4082,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::substitute-teacher::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The regular teacher was sick, so we had a ____.","expectedAnswer":"substitute teacher","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The regular teacher was sick, so we had a ____.","clozeAnswer":"substitute teacher","exampleTranslation":"原來的老師生病了，所以我們有了一位代課老師。","reference":{"eng":"substitute teacher","kk":"/ˈsʌbstɪtut ˈtitʃər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['代課老師']]","chEntries":["代課老師"],"practiceMeaning":"原來的老師生病了，所以我們有了一位代課老師。","analysis":"'Substitute' 源自拉丁語 'substituere' (to put under, to place instead of)，由 'sub-' (under) + 'stituere' (to place) 構成，意為「代替」。'Teacher' 是「老師」。'Substitute teacher' 指「代替正式老師上課的老師」。","definition":"a person who takes the place of a regular teacher who is absent","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"一位代課老師上了今天的課。\",\n    \"eng\": \"A substitute teacher led today's class.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"原來的老師生病了，所以我們有了一位代課老師。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The regular teacher was sick, so we had a substitute teacher.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"原來的老師生病了，所以我們有了一位代課老師。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5557,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::suburb::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The house is located in a pleasant ____.","expectedAnswer":"suburb","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The house is located in a pleasant ____.","clozeAnswer":"suburb","exampleTranslation":"這房子坐落在一個宜人的郊區。","reference":{"eng":"suburb","kk":"ˈsʌbɜrb","tense":"n.","ch":"[['郊區'], ['郊外']]","chEntries":["郊區","郊外"],"practiceMeaning":"這房子坐落在一個宜人的郊區。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 \"suburbium\"，由 \"sub-\"（under, near，在……之下，在……附近）和 \"urbs, urbis\"（city，城市）組成。\"suburbium\" 原意指「城市附近的地方」。因此，\"suburb\" 的核心語義是「靠近城市、但又與城市中心有所區隔的區域」。在現代英語中，\"suburb\" 通常指住宅區，是人們從市區通勤到市中心工作而居住的地方。它代表一種生活模式，即居住在相對安靜、綠化較好的郊區，但仍能便利地前往市區。","definition":"1. A residential area or community just outside a city or town; 2. An outlying district of a city or town.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They moved to the suburbs for a quieter life.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們搬到郊區去過更寧靜的生活。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The house is located in a pleasant suburb.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這房子坐落在一個宜人的郊區。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Commuting from the suburbs can be time-consuming.\",\n    \"ch\": \"從郊區通勤可能會耗費大量時間。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這房子坐落在一個宜人的郊區。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4296,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::sufficient-food::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Make sure you pack ____ and water for the hike.","expectedAnswer":"sufficient food","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Make sure you pack ____ and water for the hike.","clozeAnswer":"sufficient food","exampleTranslation":"確保你為徒步旅行打包了足夠的食物和水。","reference":{"eng":"sufficient food","kk":"/səˈfɪʃənt fuːd/","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['足夠的食物']]","chEntries":["足夠的食物"],"practiceMeaning":"確保你為徒步旅行打包了足夠的食物和水。","analysis":"由形容詞 'sufficient'（足夠的）和名詞 'food'（食物）組成。'Sufficient food' 指「量、種類或質量能滿足需求的食物」，強調其滿足感和足夠性。","definition":"enough food for a particular purpose or need.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The supply ship brought sufficient food for the entire expedition.\",\n    \"ch\": \"補給船帶來了足夠整個探險隊的食物。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Make sure you pack sufficient food and water for the hike.\",\n    \"ch\": \"確保你為徒步旅行打包了足夠的食物和水。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"確保你為徒步旅行打包了足夠的食物和水。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4259,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::sum::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He paid a large ____ of money for the car.","expectedAnswer":"sum","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He paid a large ____ of money for the car.","clozeAnswer":"sum","exampleTranslation":"他為這輛車支付了一大筆錢。","reference":{"eng":"sum","kk":"/sʌm/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['總數'], ['金額'], ['摘要']]","chEntries":["總數","金額","摘要"],"practiceMeaning":"他為這輛車支付了一大筆錢。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'summa'（頂部、總數、總結）。'Sum' 可以指數字的「總和」，或是一段時期、一段文字的「總結」。其核心概念是「總體」或「整體」。","definition":"the result of adding two or more numbers together; the total amount of money; a brief statement or essay.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The sum of 5 and 3 is 8.\",\n    \"ch\": \"5加3的總數是8。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He paid a large sum of money for the car.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他為這輛車支付了一大筆錢。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他為這輛車支付了一大筆錢。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4275,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::summary::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"In ____, the project was a great success.","expectedAnswer":"summary","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"In ____, the project was a great success.","clozeAnswer":"summary","exampleTranslation":"總之，這個專案非常成功。","reference":{"eng":"summary","kk":"/ˈsʌməri/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['摘要'], ['概要'], ['總結']]","chEntries":["摘要","概要","總結"],"practiceMeaning":"總之，這個專案非常成功。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'summare'，意為「總結」。'Summary' 是名詞形式，指對長篇文字、事件或情況的「簡短概述」。其核心是「提煉要點，概括整體」。","definition":"a brief statement or account of the main points of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please provide a summary of the report.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請提供一份報告的摘要。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"In summary, the project was a great success.\",\n    \"ch\": \"總之，這個專案非常成功。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"總之，這個專案非常成功。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4623,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::summit::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The two leaders will meet at the ____ next week.","expectedAnswer":"summit","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The two leaders will meet at the ____ next week.","clozeAnswer":"summit","exampleTranslation":"兩位領導人將於下週在峰會上會面。","reference":{"eng":"summit","kk":"/ˈsʌmɪt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['頂峰'], ['最高點'], ['（國家領導人等的）峰會']]","chEntries":["頂峰","最高點","峰會"],"practiceMeaning":"兩位領導人將於下週在峰會上會面。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'summitas' (頂端)，是 'summus' (最高的) 的名詞形式。指山脈、丘陵或任何物體的最高處。引申義指某事物發展的最高階段或最高級別的會議，如國際峰會。","definition":"the highest point, especially of a mountain; a meeting between leaders of governments.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They reached the summit of the mountain after a long climb.\",\n    \"ch\": \"經過漫長的攀登，他們到達了山頂。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The two leaders will meet at the summit next week.\",\n    \"ch\": \"兩位領導人將於下週在峰會上會面。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"兩位領導人將於下週在峰會上會面。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4645,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::summit-talks::idiom","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ are crucial for global peace.","expectedAnswer":"Summit talks","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ are crucial for global peace.","clozeAnswer":"Summit talks","exampleTranslation":"峰會談判對全球和平至關重要。","reference":{"eng":"summit talks","kk":"/ˈsʌmɪt tɔːks/","tense":"idiom","ch":"[['峰會談判'], ['高峰會談']]","chEntries":["峰會談判","高峰會談"],"practiceMeaning":"峰會談判對全球和平至關重要。","analysis":"此為固定片語。'Summit' (頂峰，引申為最高級別) + 'talks' (談判，會談)。指國家領導人或高級官員之間舉行的最高級別的討論或談判，旨在解決重大國際問題。","definition":"negotiations or discussions held between the highest-level leaders of countries.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The two countries agreed to hold summit talks.\",\n    \"ch\": \"兩國同意舉行峰會談判。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Summit talks are crucial for global peace.\",\n    \"ch\": \"峰會談判對全球和平至關重要。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"峰會談判對全球和平至關重要。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5064,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::superstition::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It's just a ____; there's no scientific basis for it.","expectedAnswer":"superstition","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It's just a ____; there's no scientific basis for it.","clozeAnswer":"superstition","exampleTranslation":"這只是一種迷信，沒有科學根據。","reference":{"eng":"superstition","kk":"ˌsuːpərˈstɪʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[['迷信'], ['（某種）迷信的觀念或行為']]","chEntries":["迷信","迷信的觀念或行為"],"practiceMeaning":"這只是一種迷信，沒有科學根據。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語superstitio，由super（之上、過度）+ stare（站立）組成，原意可能是「過度的、非理性的信仰」或「在某事之上（過度）站立」。superstition 指「一種基於非理性信仰、常與魔法、命運或超自然力量相關的觀念或實踐」，相信某些巧合、跡象或儀式能影響未來。OCR 掃描時可能將 's' 誤判為 '5'，或 't' 誤判為 'l'。此處修正為 superstition。","definition":"a belief or way of behaving that is based on fear of the unknown and of the supernatural.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Black cats are often associated with superstition.\",\n    \"ch\": \"黑貓常與迷信聯繫在一起。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's just a superstition; there's no scientific basis for it.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這只是一種迷信，沒有科學根據。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這只是一種迷信，沒有科學根據。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5354,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l1::surrender::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"After a long siege, the rebels agreed to ____.","expectedAnswer":"surrender","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"After a long siege, the rebels agreed to ____.","clozeAnswer":"surrender","exampleTranslation":"經過長期圍困，叛軍同意投降。","reference":{"eng":"surrender","kk":"səˈrɛndər","tense":"n.","ch":"[['投降'], ['屈服'], ['交出']]","chEntries":["投降","屈服","交出"],"practiceMeaning":"經過長期圍困，叛軍同意投降。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 surrender，來自 sur-（在……之上）+ render（給予、遞交，來自拉丁語 redere，意為「歸還」）。原始語意為「將某物交還或歸還給他人」，引申為「在壓力下交出控制權」或「投降」。構詞上，sur- 表示「在……之上」或「超過」，render 則意為「給予、交付」。","definition":"the act of surrendering; an act of yielding to the control of another person or force.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The surrender of the fortress was inevitable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"要塞的投降是不可避免的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"After a long siege, the rebels agreed to surrender.\",\n    \"ch\": \"經過長期圍困，叛軍同意投降。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"經過長期圍困，叛軍同意投降。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5708,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l9::sway::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The gentle ____ of the boat made him seasick.","expectedAnswer":"sway","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The gentle ____ of the boat made him seasick.","clozeAnswer":"sway","exampleTranslation":"船的輕柔搖擺讓他暈船。","reference":{"eng":"sway","kk":"sweɪ","tense":"n.","ch":"[['搖擺'], ['影響力']]","chEntries":["搖擺","影響力"],"practiceMeaning":"船的輕柔搖擺讓他暈船。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 swæġe（洪水，溪流，源自原始日耳曼語 \\*swag-），與原始印歐語 \\*swēg-（流動）相關。作為名詞，它指「搖擺的動作」或「影響、左右的能力」。從物理上的「搖擺、搖動」的動作，演變成抽象的「影響力」。","definition":"the power to decide an outcome; the motion of swaying.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her sway over the members was immense.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對成員們的影響力是巨大的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The gentle sway of the boat made him seasick.\",\n    \"ch\": \"船的輕柔搖擺讓他暈船。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"船的輕柔搖擺讓他暈船。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4690,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::tag::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Don't ____ me with that label!","expectedAnswer":"tag","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Don't ____ me with that label!","clozeAnswer":"tag","exampleTranslation":"別給我貼上那樣的標籤！","reference":{"eng":"tag","kk":"/ˈtæɡ/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['貼上標籤'], ['（非正式）稱呼'], ['（追蹤）標記']]","chEntries":["貼上標籤","稱呼","標記"],"practiceMeaning":"別給我貼上那樣的標籤！","analysis":"動詞形式，與名詞意義對應。指為某物貼上標籤、給予稱呼或標記。","definition":"1. To attach a label to something. 2. (informal) To call or identify someone or something by a particular name or description. 3. To mark something for tracking or identification.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The luggage was tagged with his name and address.\",\n    \"ch\": \"行李上貼有他的姓名和地址標籤。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Don't tag me with that label!\",\n    \"ch\": \"別給我貼上那樣的標籤！\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The system tags all outgoing emails.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該系統標記所有發出的電子郵件。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"別給我貼上那樣的標籤！","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5631,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l7::take-care-of::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Don't worry about the arrangements; I'll ____ everything.","expectedAnswer":"take care of","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Don't worry about the arrangements; I'll ____ everything.","clozeAnswer":"take care of","exampleTranslation":"別擔心安排事宜；我會處理好一切的。","reference":{"eng":"take care of","kk":"teɪk kɛər ɒv","tense":"v.","ch":"[['照顧'], ['負責'], ['處理']]","chEntries":["照顧","負責","處理"],"practiceMeaning":"別擔心安排事宜；我會處理好一切的。","analysis":"此片語由動詞 'take'（拿、取），名詞 'care'（關懷、照料）和介詞 'of'（的）組成。'take' 源自古英語 'tacan'；'care' 源自古英語 'caru'（關心、憂慮），後發展為「照料」；'of' 源自古英語 'of'。構詞學上，這是一個慣用語。'take care' 本身有「小心」的意思，但與介詞 'of' 連用時，'take care of' 專指「對某人或某物給予關照和照料」，即「照顧」。也可以引申為「負責處理某事」。","definition":"1. Look after (someone or something) and provide for their needs; 2. Deal with (a problem or task).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has to take care of her younger siblings.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她必須照顧她年幼的弟妹。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Don't worry about the arrangements; I'll take care of everything.\",\n    \"ch\": \"別擔心安排事宜；我會處理好一切的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"別擔心安排事宜；我會處理好一切的。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5548,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l5::take-in::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They decided to ____ the stray cat.","expectedAnswer":"take in","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They decided to ____ the stray cat.","clozeAnswer":"take in","exampleTranslation":"他們決定收留這隻流浪貓。","reference":{"eng":"take in","kk":"teɪk ɪn","tense":"v.","ch":"[['吸收'], ['理解'], ['接受'], ['容納'], ['欺騙']]","chEntries":["吸收","理解","接受","容納","欺騙"],"practiceMeaning":"他們決定收留這隻流浪貓。","analysis":"此為多義片語動詞。'take' (拿、取) + 'in' (裡面)。其語義多樣，主要包括：1. 吸收/攝取 (如食物、資訊)；2. 理解/領會；3. 接受/容納 (如客人、規定)；4. 欺騙/愚弄。這裡需要根據上下文判斷具體含義。例如，'take in information' 表示吸收資訊，'take in a guest' 表示容納客人，'take someone in' 表示欺騙某人。其核心概念是「將某物或某人納入內部」。","definition":"to absorb or understand information; to receive or accommodate; to deceive or trick.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's hard to take in all this new information.\",\n    \"ch\": \"很難吸收所有這些新資訊。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They decided to take in the stray cat.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們決定收留這隻流浪貓。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Don't let him take you in; he's a con artist.\",\n    \"ch\": \"別讓他騙了你；他可是個騙子。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們決定收留這隻流浪貓。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3957,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::take-responsibility-for::p