率）。","definition":"1. the state of being unemployed; 2. the number of people who are unemployed.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government is trying to reduce unemployment.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府正試圖降低失業率。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Unemployment rates have been rising.\",\n    \"ch\": \"失業率一直在上升。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has been facing long-term unemployment.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他一直面臨長期失業。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"失業率一直在上升。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4502,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::unwind::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Please ____ the string from the spool.","expectedAnswer":"unwind","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Please ____ the string from the spool.","clozeAnswer":"unwind","exampleTranslation":"請將繩子從線軸上鬆開。","reference":{"eng":"unwind","kk":"/ʌnˈwaɪnd/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['鬆開（纏繞的東西）'], ['放鬆（身心）']]","chEntries":["鬆開","放鬆"],"practiceMeaning":"請將繩子從線軸上鬆開。","analysis":"由 un- (相反) 和 wind (纏繞) 組成。核心語意是「將纏繞的東西解開、鬆開」。引申為「放鬆心情」、「解除緊張」。","definition":"1. To undo the winding of (something wound up); 2. To relax after a period of work or tension.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He needed to unwind after a stressful day at work.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他需要在一天的緊張工作後放鬆一下。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please unwind the string from the spool.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請將繩子從線軸上鬆開。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"請將繩子從線軸上鬆開。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6202,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::upgrade::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They are offering a free ____ to premium.","expectedAnswer":"upgrade","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They are offering a free ____ to premium.","clozeAnswer":"upgrade","exampleTranslation":"他們提供免費升級到高級版。","reference":{"eng":"upgrade","kk":"ˈʌpɡreɪd","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"升級\"  ],  [    \"提升\"  ]]","chEntries":["升級","提升"],"practiceMeaning":"他們提供免費升級到高級版。","analysis":"此字由 up (上) + grade (等級、品質) 構成。此字在現代英語中可視為由 up 和 grade 組合的複合詞。up 表示方向上的「向上」，grade 表示「等級、品質」。作為名詞，其核心語義是由動詞 upgrade「升級」名詞化而來，指「將某物提升到更高等級、標準或性能的行為或結果」。詞源中的「向上」和「等級」概念清晰地體現了此義。","definition":"1. an act of raising something to a higher standard, quality, or level; 2. an improved version of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The recent upgrade of the network improved its speed.\",\n    \"ch\": \"最近的網路升級提高了它的速度。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They are offering a free upgrade to premium.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們提供免費升級到高級版。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The hotel provided a complimentary room upgrade.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家旅館提供了免費的房間升級。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The upgrade to the operating system was successful.\",\n    \"ch\": \"操作系統的升級是成功的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們提供免費升級到高級版。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4257,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::vacant::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His expression was ____, as if he wasn't listening.","expectedAnswer":"vacant","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His expression was ____, as if he wasn't listening.","clozeAnswer":"vacant","exampleTranslation":"他的表情茫然，彷彿沒有在聽。","reference":{"eng":"vacant","kk":"/ˈveɪkənt/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['空的'], ['未被佔用的'], ['茫然的']]","chEntries":["空的","未被佔用的","茫然的"],"practiceMeaning":"他的表情茫然，彷彿沒有在聽。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'vacans'，'vacare'（空著、空閒）的現在分詞。'Vacant' 指「沒有被佔用、沒有人或物在裡面」，可以是物理空間（如房間、座位）或抽象的狀態（如職位）。","definition":"not occupied or used; empty; not filled with thought or expression.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The hotel had several vacant rooms.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家旅館有幾個空房間。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His expression was vacant, as if he wasn't listening.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的表情茫然，彷彿沒有在聽。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他的表情茫然，彷彿沒有在聽。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5347,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l1::vain::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She is very ____ about her appearance.","expectedAnswer":"vain","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She is very ____ about her appearance.","clozeAnswer":"vain","exampleTranslation":"她對自己的外表非常虛榮。","reference":{"eng":"vain","kk":"veɪn","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['徒勞的'], ['無用的'], ['虛榮的'], ['自負的']]","chEntries":["徒勞的","無用的","虛榮的","自負的"],"practiceMeaning":"她對自己的外表非常虛榮。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 vain，來自拉丁語 vanus（空的、無意義的、虛假的）。構詞上，van- 是字根，意為「空虛」。原始語意為「空洞無物」。現代語意發展為兩條主要分支：1. 「徒勞無用的」（沒有實質內容或結果）；2. 「虛榮自負的」（對外表或成就過度看重，內心空虛）。","definition":"having or showing an excessively high opinion of one's appearance, abilities, or worth; producing no result; useless.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"All our efforts to save the company were in vain.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們拯救公司的所有努力都徒勞無功。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is very vain about her appearance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對自己的外表非常虛榮。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她對自己的外表非常虛榮。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5068,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::vendor::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We are looking for a reliable software ____.","expectedAnswer":"vendor","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We are looking for a reliable software ____.","clozeAnswer":"vendor","exampleTranslation":"我們正在尋找一個可靠的軟體供應商。","reference":{"eng":"vendor","kk":"ˈvɛndər","tense":"n.","ch":"[['賣家'], ['銷售商'], ['供應商']]","chEntries":["賣家","銷售商","供應商"],"practiceMeaning":"我們正在尋找一個可靠的軟體供應商。","analysis":"此字源自古法語vendeor，來自拉丁語vendere（出售），是動詞vendere的派生。vendere由venum（出售）+ dare（給予）組成。vendor 的核心語意是「銷售商品或服務的人或公司」。通常指小型或個人化的銷售者，但也可用於較大公司。OCR 掃描時可能將 'v' 誤判為 'u'，或 'd' 誤判為 'cl'。此處修正為 vendor。","definition":"1. a person or company that sells goods or services; 2. a person or company that sells goods, especially on the street.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The street vendor sold hot dogs and pretzels.\",\n    \"ch\": \"街頭小販賣熱狗和椒鹽捲餅。\