indicates a possible or impending danger, problem, or unpleasant situation.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The alarm is a warning of fire.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警報是火災的預警。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He received a stern warning from his boss.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他接到了老闆嚴厲的警告。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The warning signs were ignored.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警告標誌被忽略了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他接到了老闆嚴厲的警告。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4279,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u7::weaken::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The disease can ____ the immune system.","expectedAnswer":"weaken","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The disease can ____ the immune system.","clozeAnswer":"weaken","exampleTranslation":"這種疾病會削弱免疫系統。","reference":{"eng":"weaken","kk":"/ˈwiːkən/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['削弱'], ['減弱'], ['使衰弱']]","chEntries":["削弱","減弱","使衰弱"],"practiceMeaning":"這種疾病會削弱免疫系統。","analysis":"由形容詞 'weak'（虛弱的、軟弱的）加上後綴 '-en'（使...）構成。'Weaken' 的意思是「使變得更弱」或「使減弱」。它強調力量、強度或影響力的下降。","definition":"to make or become weaker.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The strong wind began to weaken.\",\n    \"ch\": \"強風開始減弱。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The disease can weaken the immune system.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種疾病會削弱免疫系統。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這種疾病會削弱免疫系統。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5341,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l1::wealth::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The country is rich in natural ____.","expectedAnswer":"wealth","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The country is rich in natural ____.","clozeAnswer":"wealth","exampleTranslation":"這個國家擁有豐富的自然資源。","reference":{"eng":"wealth","kk":"wɛlθ","tense":"n.","ch":"[['財富'], ['財產'], ['富裕']]","chEntries":["財富","財產","富裕"],"practiceMeaning":"這個國家擁有豐富的自然資源。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 wela，意為「富裕、幸福」，與 Wealh（威爾斯人）同源，但語意已分開。構詞上，wel- 是字根，表示「富裕、好、幸福」，-th 是常見的名詞字尾，表示「狀態」。原始語意為「幸福、充裕的狀態」。現代語意主要指「財富」，但也保留了「富裕」或「豐富」的廣義涵義。","definition":"an abundance of money, property, or possessions; riches; a great quantity of anything.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He accumulated great wealth during his lifetime.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在一生中積累了巨大的財富。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The country is rich in natural wealth.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個國家擁有豐富的自然資源。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個國家擁有豐富的自然資源。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5340,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l1::wealthy::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The city is home to many ____ individuals.","expectedAnswer":"wealthy","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The city is home to many ____ individuals.","clozeAnswer":"wealthy","exampleTranslation":"這座城市是許多富裕人士的家鄉。","reference":{"eng":"wealthy","kk":"ˈwɛlθi","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['富有的'], ['富裕的'], ['財力雄厚的']]","chEntries":["富有的","富裕的","財力雄厚的"],"practiceMeaning":"這座城市是許多富裕人士的家鄉。","analysis":"此字由名詞 wealth 加上形容詞字尾 -y 構成。wealth 源自古英語 wela（富裕、幸福），與 Wealh（威爾斯人）同源，但語意已分開。構詞上，wealth- 是字根，表示「富裕、豐富」，-th 是名詞字尾，表示「狀態」。-y 是形容詞字尾，表示「充滿……的」。因此，wealthy 的核心語意為「充滿財富的」、「富裕的」。","definition":"having a lot of money and possessions; affluent.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She comes from a wealthy family.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她出身於一個富裕的家庭。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The city is home to many wealthy individuals.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座城市是許多富裕人士的家鄉。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這座城市是許多富裕人士的家鄉。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5360,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l1::wear-on::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The constant noise began to ____ her nerves.","expectedAnswer":"wear on","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The constant noise began to ____ her nerves.","clozeAnswer":"wear on","exampleTranslation":"持續不斷的噪音開始讓她神經衰弱。","reference":{"eng":"wear on","kk":"wer ˈɑːn","tense":"v.","ch":"[['（時間）流逝'], ['磨損'], ['使人疲倦']]","chEntries":["流逝","磨損","使人疲倦"],"practiceMeaning":"持續不斷的噪音開始讓她神經衰弱。","analysis":"此為一個常見的片語動詞。wear 源自古英語 werian（穿著、消耗），後演變成 wear（穿著、磨損）。on 在此有「持續進行」或「作用於」的意思。組合起來，wear on 主要有兩層語意：1. （時間）不知不覺地過去，漸漸地消耗；2. （事物）因持續使用而磨損。也可引申為「使人感到疲倦」。","definition":"to continue for too long without changing, often in a way that is boring or annoying; to cause someone to become tired, especially mentally.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"As the days wore on, his hope began to fade.\",\n    \"ch\": \"隨著日子一天天過去，他的希望開始減弱。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The constant noise began to wear on her nerves.\",\n    \"ch\": \"持續不斷的噪音開始讓她神經衰弱。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"持續不斷的噪音開始讓她神經衰弱。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3875,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::wed::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The couple ____ in a private ceremony.","expectedAnswer":"wed","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The couple ____ in a private ceremony.","clozeAnswer":"wed","exampleTranslation":"這對情侶在一個私人的儀式中結婚。","reference":{"eng":"wed","kk":"/wɛd/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['結婚']]","chEntries":["結婚"],"practiceMeaning":"這對情侶在一個私人的儀式中結婚。","analysis":"源自古英語 'weddian'，意為「訂婚」、「發誓」。核心是「承諾」或「結合」。在現代英語中，主要指舉行婚禮，正式結為夫婦。","definition":"to marry; become husband and wife.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They decided to wed next spring.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們決定明年春天結婚。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The couple wed in a private ceremony.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這對情侶在一個私人的儀式中結婚。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這對情侶在一個私人的儀式中結婚。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4489,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::wisdom::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It takes ____ to understand complex issues.","expectedAnswer":"wisdom","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It takes ____ to understand complex issues.","clozeAnswer":"wisdom","exampleTranslation":"理解複雜的問題需要智慧。","reference":{"eng":"wisdom","kk":"/ˈwɪzdəm/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['智慧'], ['明智']]","chEntries":["智慧","明智"],"practiceMeaning":"理解複雜的問題需要智慧。","analysis":"源自古英語 wīsdōm，由 wīs (智慧的) 和 -dōm (表示「狀態」、「領域」或「品質」的名詞後綴) 組成。核心語意是「理解深刻事實或情況的能力」，「明辨是非的能力」。","definition":"1. The quality of having experience, knowledge, and good judgment; 2. The quality of being wise.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She offered her wisdom and advice.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她提供了她的智慧和建議。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It takes wisdom to understand complex issues.\",\n    \"ch\": \"理解複雜的問題需要智慧。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is known for his deep wisdom.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他以其深邃的智慧而聞名。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"理解複雜的問題需要智慧。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U10、L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4520,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::with::prep","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He cut the cake ____ a knife.","expectedAnswer":"with","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He cut the cake ____ a knife.","clozeAnswer":"with","exampleTranslation":"他用刀切蛋糕。","reference":{"eng":"with","kk":"/wɪð/","tense":"prep.","ch":"[['和...一起'], ['帶著'], ['使用'], ['關於']]","chEntries":["和...一起","帶著","使用","關於"],"practiceMeaning":"他用刀切蛋糕。","analysis":"源自古英語 wið。是一個表示陪伴、工具、原因、方式等的多功能介詞。核心語意是「一起」、「伴隨」。","definition":"1. Accompanied by (another person or people); 2. Indicating the instrument or agent used to perform an action; 3. In the company of or in addition to; 4. Having or possessing (a particular quality or characteristic).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is talking with her friend.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她正在和她的朋友說話。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He cut the cake with a knife.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他用刀切蛋糕。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a problem with the software.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是軟體的一個問題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a man with great courage.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一個有巨大勇氣的人。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他用刀切蛋糕。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5070,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::worthy::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This is a cause ____ of our support.","expectedAnswer":"worthy","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This is a cause ____ of our support.","clozeAnswer":"worthy","exampleTranslation":"這是一個值得我們支持的事業。","reference":{"eng":"worthy","kk":"ˈwɜːrði","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['值得的'], ['有價值的'], ['品格高尚的']]","chEntries":["值得的","有價值的","品格高尚的"],"practiceMeaning":"這是一個值得我們支持的事業。","analysis":"此字由word（詞）加上字尾-y（形容詞化）構成，但其詞源並非來自word，而是源自古英語wierðe，意為「有價值的、值得的」。其核心語意是「值得尊敬、重視或獲得某事物（如讚揚、關注、獎勵）」。此用法與名詞 worth（價值）相關。OCR 掃描時可能將 'w' 誤判為 'u'，或 'rd' 誤判為 'nd'。此處修正為 worthy。","definition":"1. deserving effort or attention; 2. having or showing the merits or character to deserve attention, honor, or respect.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a worthy recipient of the award.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是該獎項當之無愧的得主。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a cause worthy of our support.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個值得我們支持的事業。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a worthy opponent.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是一位值得尊敬的對手。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是一個值得我們支持的事業。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5116,"wordRef":"字彙王::u62::abrupt::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The road became ____ at the cliff edge.","expectedAnswer":"abrupt","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The road became ____ at the cliff edge.","clozeAnswer":"abrupt","exampleTranslation":"道路在懸崖邊變得陡峭。","reference":{"eng":"abrupt","kk":"əˈbrʌpt","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['突然的'], ['粗魯的'], ['陡峭的']]","chEntries":["突然的","粗魯的","陡峭的"],"practiceMeaning":"道路在懸崖邊變得陡峭。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 abruptus，是 ab-, abs-（離開、遠離）+ rumpere（弄斷、打破）的過去分詞。rumpere 來自印歐語系 *h₂rem-（停止、休息）或 *reup-（撕裂、拔出）。abruptus 的字面意思是「被弄斷的、被打破的」，引申為「突然發生的、急促的」。由此衍生出「出乎意料的、唐突的、不順暢的」。當用於人際互動時，表示「粗魯、生硬」；當用於地形時，表示「突然中斷、陡峭」。","definition":"sudden and unexpected; brief to the point of rudeness; steep or broken.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was an abrupt change in the weather.\",\n    \"ch\": \"天氣突然發生了變化。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He gave an abrupt answer and walked away.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他唐突地回答了一下就走開了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The road became abrupt at the cliff edge.\",\n    \"ch\": \"道路在懸崖邊變得陡峭。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"道路在懸崖邊變得陡峭。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U62"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5556,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::accuracy::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need to ensure the ____ of the translation.","expectedAnswer":"accuracy","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need to ensure the ____ of the translation.","clozeAnswer":"accuracy","exampleTranslation":"我們需要確保翻譯的準確性。","reference":{"eng":"accuracy","kk":"ˈækjərəsi","tense":"n.","ch":"[['精確度'], ['準確性'], ['正確性']]","chEntries":["精確度","準確性","正確性"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要確保翻譯的準確性。","analysis":"此字由 \"accurate\" 加上名詞化字尾 \"-cy\" 構成。\"accurate\" 源自拉丁語 \"accurrere\"，意為 \"to run to, run up\"（跑到，跑近），由 \"ad-\"（to, toward，向，朝）和 \"currere\"（to run，跑）組成。\"accurrere\" 的引申義是指「達到目標」，因此 \"accurate\" 指「能夠精確地達到目標」或「符合標準」。\"-cy\" 是構成抽象名詞的字尾，表示「狀態、品質」。因此，\"accuracy\" 的核心語義是「達到目標、符合標準的品質或狀態」，即「精確性」或「準確性」。","definition":"1. The condition or quality of being accurate; freedom from error or defect; 2. The degree to which the result of a measurement, calculation, or specification conforms to the correct or a predicted result.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The accuracy of the data is crucial for our research.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這些數據的準確性對我們的研究至關重要。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The pilot maintained a high level of accuracy in navigation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"飛行員在導航中保持了高度的精確性。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to ensure the accuracy of the translation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要確保翻譯的準確性。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要確保翻譯的準確性。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6062,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::acute::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The situation is becoming increasingly ____.","expectedAnswer":"acute","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The situation is becoming increasingly ____.","clozeAnswer":"acute","exampleTranslation":"局勢正變得日益嚴峻。","reference":{"eng":"acute","kk":"əˈkjut","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"尖銳的\"  ],  [    \"敏銳的\"  ],  [    \"嚴重的\"  ],  [    \"急性的\"  ]]","chEntries":["尖銳的","敏銳的","嚴重的","急性的"],"practiceMeaning":"局勢正變得日益嚴峻。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 acutus，意為「尖的，銳利的」，是動詞 acuere（to sharpen）的過去分詞。構詞上，ac- 來自 acu-，意為「尖、銳利」，-ute 是形容詞後綴。此字的核心語義與「尖銳」相關，引申出多種含義：物理上的「尖銳」形狀；感知上的「敏銳」；情況上的「嚴重」或「劇烈」；醫學上的「急性」發作。這些義項都體現了「程度極高」或「非常明顯」的特點。","definition":"1. sharp or penetrating, especially in intellect, perception, or physical appearance (e.g., an acute angle); 2. (of a bad situation or feeling) intense; severe; 3. (of a disease or condition) of sudden onset, sharp rise, and short course.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The triangle has an acute angle.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個三角形有一個銳角。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has an acute sense of smell.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他有靈敏的嗅覺。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The situation is becoming increasingly acute.\",\n    \"ch\": \"局勢正變得日益嚴峻。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She suffers from acute appendicitis.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她患有急性闌尾炎。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"局勢正變得日益嚴峻。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5604,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l7::addition::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The new feature is a welcome ____ to the software.","expectedAnswer":"addition","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The new feature is a welcome ____ to the software.","clozeAnswer":"addition","exampleTranslation":"這項新功能是該軟體一個受歡迎的補充。","reference":{"eng":"addition","kk":"əˈdɪʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[['加法'], ['增加'], ['添加物']]","chEntries":["加法","增加","添加物"],"practiceMeaning":"這項新功能是該軟體一個受歡迎的補充。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'additio'，由動詞 'addere'（添加）派生，'addere' 由 'ad-'（向）和 'dare'（給予）組成。構詞學上，它是由動詞 'add'（添加）加上名詞化後綴 '-tion' 所構成。'-tion' 字尾常將動詞轉換為表示「行動」、「過程」或「結果」的名詞。原始語意是「給予」或「添加」，演變為「加法」（數學上的）、「增加的行為或過程」，以及「被添加的物品」。","definition":"1. The action or process of adding something to something else; 2. The process of adding up numbers; 3. A thing added to something else.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The addition of a new wing significantly increased the museum's exhibition space.\",\n    \"ch\": \"新翼樓的增加顯著擴大了博物館的展覽空間。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The children are learning basic addition in school.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子們正在學校學習基本的加法。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The new feature is a welcome addition to the software.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這項新功能是該軟體一個受歡迎的補充。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這項新功能是該軟體一個受歡迎的補充。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4569,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::admire::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Many people ____ his dedication to his work.","expectedAnswer":"admire","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Many people ____ his dedication to his work.","clozeAnswer":"admire","exampleTranslation":"許多人讚賞他對工作的投入。","reference":{"eng":"admire","kk":"/ədˈmaɪər/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['欽佩', '讚賞'], ['欣賞', '仰慕']]","chEntries":["欽佩","讚賞","欣賞","仰慕"],"practiceMeaning":"許多人讚賞他對工作的投入。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'admirari'，'ad-' (to) 和 'mirari' (to wonder at - 驚奇、讚嘆)。核心概念是因某人的優點、成就或特質而感到驚嘆和讚賞。\n    1. 欽佩、讚賞：指對某人的品德、能力或成就給予高度評價。\n    2. 欣賞、仰慕：指欣賞美麗的事物、景色或某人，帶有讚美的意味。","definition":"1. regard with respect or warm approval.; 2. look at with pleasure; find beautiful or delightful.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I truly admire your courage.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我真心欽佩你的勇氣。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She admired the stunning view from the mountaintop.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她欣賞山頂上壯麗的景色。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Many people admire his dedication to his work.\",\n    \"ch\": \"許多人讚賞他對工作的投入。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"許多人讚賞他對工作的投入。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6105,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::adverse::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He had to overcome ____ circumstances.","expectedAnswer":"adverse","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He had to overcome ____ circumstances.","clozeAnswer":"adverse","exampleTranslation":"他不得不克服不利的環境。","reference":{"eng":"adverse","kk":"ˈædvɜːrs","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"不利的\"  ],  [    \"有害的\"  ],  [    \"敵對的\"  ],  [    \"相反的\"  ]]","chEntries":["不利的","有害的","敵對的","相反的"],"practiceMeaning":"他不得不克服不利的環境。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 adversus，意為「朝向；反對」。構詞上，ad- 是方向字首，表示「朝向」或「趨向」；versus 則是拉丁語 vertō（轉動）的過去分詞，意為「轉向」。因此，adverse 的核心語義是「轉向相反方向」，引申為「不利的、敵對的、相反的」。此形容詞用於描述條件、影響、結果等，表示對某事造成負面影響或阻礙。其語意演變是從具體的「面對面、反向」到抽象的「不利、有害」。","definition":"1. preventing success or development; harmful; unfavorable; 2. opposing or contrary.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"adverse weather conditions\",\n    \"ch\": \"惡劣的天氣狀況\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The drug had adverse side effects.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種藥物有不良副作用。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He had to overcome adverse circumstances.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他不得不克服不利的環境。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他不得不克服不利的環境。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4190,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::afford::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Can you ____ to take a week off?","expectedAnswer":"afford","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Can you ____ to take a week off?","clozeAnswer":"afford","exampleTranslation":"你承受得起請一週假嗎？","reference":{"eng":"afford","kk":"/əˈfɔːrd/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['（因有足夠的錢）買得起；負擔得起'], ['提供；給予（尤指優勢、機會）'], ['（時間、精力上）能承擔']]","chEntries":["買得起","負擔得起","提供","給予","能承擔"],"practiceMeaning":"你承受得起請一週假嗎？","analysis":"源自古英語 geforþian，意為“推進，支持”。後來受中古英語 'ford'（便宜）的影響而改變。核心意義是“提供財力上的支持，使其能夠得到”。1. “買得起”是最常見的經濟意義。2. “提供”則延伸至提供非物質的優勢或機會，例如 'afford an opportunity'。3. “能承擔”強調不因付出（時間、精力、金錢）而造成困難。","definition":"1. to have enough money to pay for something; 2. to provide or supply (something, esp. an opportunity or advantage); 3. to be able to bear or endure (the cost, strain, etc.).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We cannot afford to buy a new car.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們買不起新車。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This policy affords protection to citizens.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這項政策為公民提供了保護。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Can you afford to take a week off?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你承受得起請一週假嗎？\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"你承受得起請一週假嗎？","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6107,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::aggression::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The team displayed great ____ on the field.","expectedAnswer":"aggression","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The team displayed great ____ on the field.","clozeAnswer":"aggression","exampleTranslation":"球隊在場上展現了極大的拼勁。","reference":{"eng":"aggression","kk":"əˈɡrɛʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"侵略\"  ],  [    \"攻擊性\"  ],  [    \"敵意\"  ],  [    \"侵犯\"  ]]","chEntries":["侵略","攻擊性","敵意","侵犯"],"practiceMeaning":"球隊在場上展現了極大的拼勁。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 aggressiō，由動詞 adgredī（接近；攻擊）演變而來。構詞上，ad- 是方向字首，表示「朝向」；gredī 來自 gradī（行走，前進），與 gradus（步；等級）有關。因此，aggression 的核心語義是「朝向某物前進並發動攻擊」。此名詞表示行為上的主動攻擊、侵略，或態度上的敵意、攻擊性。語意演變是從具體的「走上前去攻擊」到抽象的「侵略性行為或態度」。","definition":"1. hostile or violent behavior or attitudes toward another, especially in readiness or shown willingness to attack; 2. the act of attacking or invading.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The country was accused of unprovoked aggression.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該國被指控發動無端侵略。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His aggressive behavior was a result of insecurity.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他具攻擊性的行為源於不安全感。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The team displayed great aggression on the field.\",\n    \"ch\": \"球隊在場上展現了極大的拼勁。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"球隊在場上展現了極大的拼勁。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6150,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::agony::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The final moments of his life were filled with ____.","expectedAnswer":"agony","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The final moments of his life were filled with ____.","clozeAnswer":"agony","exampleTranslation":"他生命的最後時刻充滿了痛苦的掙扎。","reference":{"eng":"agony","kk":"ˈæɡəni","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"極度痛苦\"  ],  [    \"煎熬\"  ],  [    \"苦惱\"  ],  [    \"臨死前的掙扎\"  ]]","chEntries":["極度痛苦","煎熬","苦惱","臨死前的掙扎"],"practiceMeaning":"他生命的最後時刻充滿了痛苦的掙扎。","analysis":"此字源自古希臘語 ἀγωνία (agōnia)，意為「掙扎、角鬥、痛苦」，與 ἀγών (agōn)「競技、集會、掙扎」同源。它進入中古英語 via 古法語 agonie。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，應視為整體詞源演變。作為名詞，其核心語義是極度的身體或精神痛苦，常與死亡前的掙扎或嚴重的心理煎熬聯繫。此義項由古希臘語中「掙扎」的含義演變而來。","definition":"1. extreme physical or mental suffering; 2. the pain of childbirth.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He died in agony after the accident.\",\n    \"ch\": \"事故發生後，他痛苦地死去。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She was in agony for days before the diagnosis was made.\",\n    \"ch\": \"在做出診斷的前幾天，她一直承受著極度的痛苦。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The final moments of his life were filled with agony.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他生命的最後時刻充滿了痛苦的掙扎。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他生命的最後時刻充滿了痛苦的掙扎。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6207,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::ally::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She is a trusted ____ of the senator.","expectedAnswer":"ally","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She is a trusted ____ of the senator.","clozeAnswer":"ally","exampleTranslation":"她是參議員的信任夥伴。","reference":{"eng":"ally","kk":"ˈælaɪ","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"盟友\"  ],  [    \"同盟國\"  ],  [    \"夥伴\"  ],  [    \"支持者\"  ]]","chEntries":["盟友","同盟國","夥伴","支持者"],"practiceMeaning":"她是參議員的信任夥伴。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 aleier，意為「結合，聯合」，向上可追溯至拉丁語 alligare，由 ad-（朝向）和 ligare（綁，連結）組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，應視為整體詞源演變。名詞義指基於共同利益、目標或情感而結成聯盟、夥伴關係或互相支持的個人、團體或國家。中文翻譯為「盟友；同盟國；夥伴；支持者」。","definition":"1. a country or person that you have agreed to support or work with; 2. a person who helps or supports you.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The two nations have been long-standing allies.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這兩個國家是長期的盟友。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He found an ally in his fight for justice.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在爭取正義的鬥爭中找到了一位夥伴。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a trusted ally of the senator.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是參議員的信任夥伴。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她是參議員的信任夥伴。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6209,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::alongside::prep","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We are working ____ our international partners.","expectedAnswer":"alongside","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We are working ____ our international partners.","clozeAnswer":"alongside","exampleTranslation":"我們正與我們的國際夥伴一同合作。","reference":{"eng":"alongside","kk":"əˈlɔŋˈsaɪd","tense":"prep.","ch":"[  [    \"在…旁邊\"  ],  [    \"與…並排\"  ],  [    \"與…同時\"  ],  [    \"除了…之外\"  ]]","chEntries":["在…旁邊","與…並排","與…同時","除了…之外"],"practiceMeaning":"我們正與我們的國際夥伴一同合作。","analysis":"此片語由介詞 along 和名詞 side 組成。along 源自古英語，意為「 along（沿著）」，side 源自古英語 sīde，意為「邊緣，側面」。此字在現代英語中可視為固定搭配，不需拆解。作介詞時，表示空間上的「在…旁邊；與…並排」，或表示時間、行動上的「與…同時；與…一起」，以及表示比較或支持的「與…相比；支持…」。","definition":"1. next to someone or something; 2. at the same time as someone or something else; 3. in addition to someone or something else; 4. supporting or cooperating with someone or something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The ship sailed alongside the coast.\",\n    \"ch\": \"船隻沿著海岸航行。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He sat alongside his wife at the wedding.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在婚禮上坐在他妻子旁邊。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We are working alongside our international partners.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們正與我們的國際夥伴一同合作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Alongside his main job, he volunteers at a shelter.\",\n    \"ch\": \"除了他的主要工作之外，他還在收容所做志工。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們正與我們的國際夥伴一同合作。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4177,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::apart::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The team won the championship, beating their rivals by a wide margin ____.","expectedAnswer":"apart","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The team won the championship, beating their rivals by a wide margin ____.","clozeAnswer":"apart","exampleTranslation":"這支隊伍以巨大的優勢擊敗對手，贏得了冠軍。","reference":{"eng":"apart","kk":"/əˈpɑːrt/","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['分開', '分開地'], ['（差異）懸殊地']]","chEntries":["分開","分開地","懸殊地"],"practiceMeaning":"這支隊伍以巨大的優勢擊敗對手，贏得了冠軍。","analysis":"由 a-（介詞）+ part（部分）組成。核心概念是「從整體中分離出來」或「獨立存在」。","definition":"1. separated by a distance; 2. into different pieces or parts; 3. distinct from others","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The two buildings are far apart.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這兩棟建築相距甚遠。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They have to tell A and B apart.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們必須分辨 A 和 B。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The team won the championship, beating their rivals by a wide margin apart.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這支隊伍以巨大的優勢擊敗對手，贏得了冠軍。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這支隊伍以巨大的優勢擊敗對手，贏得了冠軍。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4509,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::assumption::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of power by the new leader was widely welcomed.","expectedAnswer":"assumption","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of power by the new leader was widely welcomed.","clozeAnswer":"assumption","exampleTranslation":"新領導人掌權的行為受到廣泛歡迎。","reference":{"eng":"assumption","kk":"/əˈsʌmpʃn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['假設'], ['設想'], ['承擔（責任、職責等）'], ['（態度）傲慢，自以為是']]","chEntries":["假設","設想","承擔","傲慢，自以為是"],"practiceMeaning":"新領導人掌權的行為受到廣泛歡迎。","analysis":"源自 assume (假設、承擔)。加上 -tion (名詞後綴)。核心語意是「假設的行為或狀態」，或「承擔的行為或狀態」。","definition":"1. A thing that is accepted as true or as certain to happen, without proof; 2. The act of taking possession of or taking on something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We made the assumption that the project would be funded.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們假設該項目將會獲得資金。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He rejected the assumption that he was responsible.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他駁斥了他應負責的假設。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The assumption of power by the new leader was widely welcomed.\",\n    \"ch\": \"新領導人掌權的行為受到廣泛歡迎。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"新領導人掌權的行為受到廣泛歡迎。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3063,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::assurance::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Her ____ of success gave him hope.","expectedAnswer":"assurance","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Her ____ of success gave him hope.","clozeAnswer":"assurance","exampleTranslation":"她成功的保證給了他希望。","reference":{"eng":"assurance","kk":"/əˈʃʊərəns/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['保證；信心'], ['擔保；確信'], ['（購買的）保險；保證書']]","chEntries":["保證","信心","擔保","確信","保險","保證書"],"practiceMeaning":"她成功的保證給了他希望。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'securus' (safe, secure)，經由古法語 'asseurance' 演變而來，是 'assure' 的名詞形式。指「確定」或「使確信」的狀態或行為。\n1. 保證；信心：指說話或行為中表現出的確定感，給予聽者信心。\n2. 擔保；確信：指對某事物的肯定或相信，使其變得確定。\n3. （購買的）保險；保證書：指一種承諾或文件，提供對某種結果的保障。","definition":"1. a statement that something will certainly happen or be true; 2. a feeling of confidence that you can do something well or succeed; 3. a promise or guarantee.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He spoke with great assurance, calming everyone's fears.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他充滿信心地說話，平息了所有人的恐懼。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company offers a money-back assurance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司提供退款保證。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her assurance of success gave him hope.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她成功的保證給了他希望。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她成功的保證給了他希望。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5820,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::attribute::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Honesty is a key ____ of his character.","expectedAnswer":"attribute","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Honesty is a key ____ of his character.","clozeAnswer":"attribute","exampleTranslation":"誠實是他性格的關鍵屬性。","reference":{"eng":"attribute","kk":"ˈætrɪbjuːt","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"特質\"  ],  [    \"屬性\"  ],  [    \"特徵\"  ],  [    \"特性\"  ]]","chEntries":["特質","屬性","特徵","特性"],"practiceMeaning":"誠實是他性格的關鍵屬性。","analysis":"此名詞形式的 'attribute' 源自拉丁語 'attributum' (something bestowed or assigned)，是 'attribuere' 的過去分詞中性形式。其核心語意為「被分配或賦予給某物的一項」。在構詞上，'ad-' (to) + 'tribuere' (to assign)。作為名詞，'attribute' 指的是屬於某人或某物的特質、品質、性質或特徵，這些都是被「賦予」或「歸屬於」主體的。它與動詞形式的「歸因於」密切相關，因為特質（名詞）就是被認為是某事物「歸因於」的那個東西。例如，也可指「一項特殊能力或才能」。","definition":"1. A quality or feature regarded as a characteristic or inherent part of someone or something.; 2. A thing regarded as a property of a person or thing.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Patience is an important attribute for a teacher.\",\n    \"ch\": \"耐心是老師重要的特質。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The book is rich in historical attributes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本書富含歷史特徵。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Honesty is a key attribute of his character.\",\n    \"ch\": \"誠實是他性格的關鍵屬性。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Intelligence is a valuable attribute.\",\n    \"ch\": \"智慧是一種寶貴的特質。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"誠實是他性格的關鍵屬性。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3203,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::beg::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Don't ____ for mercy; you don't deserve it.","expectedAnswer":"beg","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Don't ____ for mercy; you don't deserve it.","clozeAnswer":"beg","exampleTranslation":"不要乞求憐憫；你不配。","reference":{"eng":"beg","kk":"/bɛɡ/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['乞求'], ['懇求'], ['請求']]","chEntries":["乞求","懇求","請求"],"practiceMeaning":"不要乞求憐憫；你不配。","analysis":"詞源可能來自古英語 'beggan'，意為 'to pray'，引申為『向他人祈求，尤指金錢或食物』。也可用於比喻，表示極度懇切地請求或期望某事，即使非物質性的。其名詞是 'beggar'。","definition":"1. ask someone earnestly or humbly for something; 2. ask for (something) in order to live; 3. implore or entreat.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He had to beg for food after losing his job.\",\n    \"ch\": \"失業後，他不得不乞求食物。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I beg you to reconsider your decision.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我懇求您重新考慮您的決定。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Don't beg for mercy; you don't deserve it.\",\n    \"ch\": \"不要乞求憐憫；你不配。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"不要乞求憐憫；你不配。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U41"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6110,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::bias::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The experiment was designed to minimize ____.","expectedAnswer":"bias","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The experiment was designed to minimize ____.","clozeAnswer":"bias","exampleTranslation":"該實驗的設計旨在將偏差降至最低。","reference":{"eng":"bias","kk":"ˈbaɪəs","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"偏見\"  ],  [    \"偏差\"  ],  [    \"偏心\"  ]]","chEntries":["偏見","偏差","偏心"],"practiceMeaning":"該實驗的設計旨在將偏差降至最低。","analysis":"此字詞源複雜，可能源自古法語 bis、「斜線；斜倚」，或來自義大利語 bias，意為「斜；偏見」。另一說法與骰子不均勻有關。在現代英語中，bias 主要指不公平的傾向、預斷或對某人、某事或某群體的預設偏愛或反感。也可指統計上的偏差。此名詞的語意演變是從具體的「斜向、傾斜」到抽象的「傾向、偏頗」。","definition":"1. prejudice in favor of or against one thing, person, or group compared with another, usually in a way considered to be unfair; 2. the tendency of a statistical sample to over-represent or under-represent some part of the population.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The judge was accused of bias.\",\n    \"ch\": \"法官被指控有偏見。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This report is free from political bias.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這份報告沒有政治偏見。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The experiment was designed to minimize bias.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該實驗的設計旨在將偏差降至最低。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該實驗的設計旨在將偏差降至最低。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3266,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::blink::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She didn't ____ when faced with the difficult question.","expectedAnswer":"blink","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She didn't ____ when faced with the difficult question.","clozeAnswer":"blink","exampleTranslation":"面對難題，她沒有絲毫退縮。","reference":{"eng":"blink","kk":"/blɪŋk/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['眨眼（眼皮快速開合）'], ['閃爍；閃滅'], ['（尤指）驚慌、退縮、猶豫']]","chEntries":["眨眼","閃爍","閃滅","驚慌、退縮、猶豫"],"practiceMeaning":"面對難題，她沒有絲毫退縮。","analysis":"詞源不明，可能與古英語 'blincan' (發光，眨眼) 或荷蘭語 'blinken' (閃耀) 有關。最初指眼皮的快速運動，引申至光線的快速閃爍，以及人對壓力或困難的快速反應（如退縮）。","definition":"1. to close and open your eyes quickly; 2. to shine with a light that flashes on and off; 3. to hesitate or become suddenly frightened and stop doing something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He blinked a few times to clear his vision.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他眨了幾次眼以看清。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The traffic lights blinked red.\",\n    \"ch\": \"交通號誌燈閃爍著紅光。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She didn't blink when faced with the difficult question.\",\n    \"ch\": \"面對難題，她沒有絲毫退縮。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"面對難題，她沒有絲毫退縮。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5826,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::bolt::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"A ____ of lightning lit up the sky.","expectedAnswer":"bolt","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"A ____ of lightning lit up the sky.","clozeAnswer":"bolt","exampleTranslation":"一道閃電劃破天空。","reference":{"eng":"bolt","kk":"boʊlt","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"螺栓\"  ],  [    \"門閂\"  ],  [    \"閃電\"  ],  [    \"閃電般的光\"  ]]","chEntries":["螺栓","門閂","閃電","閃電般的光"],"practiceMeaning":"一道閃電劃破天空。","analysis":"此字有多個同形異源的來源。一來源是表示「門閂」、「槓桿」，來自古英語 'bolta' 或「橫樑」；另一來源是表示「閃電」、「快速跑」，可能與原始日耳曼語 *bult- (to bolt, to build) 或 *baltaz (swift) 有關。當指「門閂」時，其語意與「關閉」、「鎖定」相關。當指「閃電」時，則強調其突然、快速的爆發。另一常見義「螺栓」則是現代引申，借用了「鎖定」或「固定」的意象。還有「快速跑」的動詞義，也與「閃電」的突然性及速度相關。這裡的「閃電般的光」更側重於視覺上的突然出現。","definition":"1. A metal pin used to fasten things together, typically with a nut on the end.; 2. A bar used to fasten a door or gate.; 3. A flash of lightning.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He tightened the bolt on the door.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他擰緊了門上的螺栓。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She slid the bolt across the door.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她拉上門閂。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A bolt of lightning lit up the sky.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一道閃電劃破天空。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A bolt of light shot across the sky.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一道閃光劃過天際。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"一道閃電劃破天空。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4677,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::bunch::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"A ____ of us are going to the concert.","expectedAnswer":"bunch","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"A ____ of us are going to the concert.","clozeAnswer":"bunch","exampleTranslation":"我們一群人要去聽演唱會。","reference":{"eng":"bunch","kk":"/ˈbʌntʃ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['一束'], ['一串'], ['（非正式）一群人']]","chEntries":["一束","一串","一群人"],"practiceMeaning":"我們一群人要去聽演唱會。","analysis":"源自荷蘭語 *bonk*，意為「塊」、「團」，後演變為指將許多相似的物體聚集在一起形成的集合體。引申至一群人，帶有非正式、親切的語氣。","definition":"1. A number of things or people of the same kind growing or fastened together. 2. (informal) A group of people.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She bought a bunch of flowers at the market.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在市場買了一束花。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A bunch of grapes fell from the table.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一串葡萄從桌子上掉了下來。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A bunch of us are going to the concert.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們一群人要去聽演唱會。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們一群人要去聽演唱會。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3880,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::captain::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of the aircraft announced our descent.","expectedAnswer":"captain","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of the aircraft announced our descent.","clozeAnswer":"captain","exampleTranslation":"機長宣布了我們的下降。","reference":{"eng":"captain","kk":"/ˈkæptən/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['船長'], ['隊長'], ['機長'], ['上尉']]","chEntries":["船長","隊長","機長","上尉"],"practiceMeaning":"機長宣布了我們的下降。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'capitaneus'，'caput' (head) 的衍生詞。核心是「首領」、「領導者」。最初指船的領導者，後引申為運動隊、飛行器、軍隊等團體的領導人。","definition":"1. the commander of a ship or large boat. 2. the leader of a sports team. 3. the pilot of an aircraft. 4. a rank of officer in the army and air force.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The captain steered the ship through the storm.\",\n    \"ch\": \"船長駕馭著船隻穿越風暴。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was chosen as the captain of the basketball team.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他被選為籃球隊隊長。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The captain of the aircraft announced our descent.\",\n    \"ch\": \"機長宣布了我們的下降。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"機長宣布了我們的下降。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3879,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::career::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"After college, he pursued a ____ in finance.","expectedAnswer":"career","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"After college, he pursued a ____ in finance.","clozeAnswer":"career","exampleTranslation":"大學畢業後，他追求金融業的事業。","reference":{"eng":"career","kk":"/kəˈrɪr/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['職業生涯', '事業']]","chEntries":["職業生涯","事業"],"practiceMeaning":"大學畢業後，他追求金融業的事業。","analysis":"源自法語 'carrière' (road, racecourse)，其根源是拉丁語 'carrum' (cart)。核心是「奔跑的道路」。引申為一個人一生中所從事的職業或事業發展過程。","definition":"an occupation undertaken for a significant period of a person's life and with opportunities for progress.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She had a successful career in medicine.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在醫學領域擁有成功的職業生涯。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is planning his career path.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他正在規劃他的職業道路。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"After college, he 