了一片反對的呼聲。","reference":{"eng":"chorus","kk":"/ˈkɔːrəs/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['合唱；合唱團'], ['（歌曲的）副歌；（戲劇的）合唱隊'], ['（眾人的）齊聲發言；呼聲']]","chEntries":["合唱","合唱團","副歌","合唱隊","齊聲發言","呼聲"],"practiceMeaning":"對這項提議響起了一片反對的呼聲。","analysis":"詞源來自希臘語 'khoros'，原指「跳舞的地方」，後來指「一隊跳舞或歌唱的人」，再演變為「合唱」。'Chorus' 的核心概念是「集合的聲音」或「共同的聲音」。它可以指一群人一起唱歌（合唱團、合唱），也可以指歌曲或詩歌中重複出現的部分（副歌），或者是一群人同時表達的共同意見或呼聲。","definition":"1. a part of a song that is repeated after each verse; 2. a group of people or animals singing or speaking together; 3. a large choir or choir of singers.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The audience joined in to sing the chorus.\",\n    \"ch\": \"觀眾們加入進來一起唱副歌。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The church choir practiced for the Sunday service.\",\n    \"ch\": \"教堂的合唱團為週日禮拜進行練習。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A chorus of disapproval met the proposal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"對這項提議響起了一片反對的呼聲。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"對這項提議響起了一片反對的呼聲。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5828,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::chubby::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She has a ____ face.","expectedAnswer":"chubby","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She has a ____ face.","clozeAnswer":"chubby","exampleTranslation":"她有一張豐滿的臉。","reference":{"eng":"chubby","kk":"ˈtʃʌbi","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"豐滿的\"  ],  [    \"胖乎乎的\"  ],  [    \"圓胖的\"  ],  [    \"圓潤的\"  ]]","chEntries":["豐滿的","胖乎乎的","圓胖的","圓潤的"],"practiceMeaning":"她有一張豐滿的臉。","analysis":"此字源於 'chub'，原指一種胖魚（如鯉魚的一種），後來用來形容人或物的圓胖、豐滿。'Chub' 本身來源不明，可能與「腫脹」或「凸起」的語感有關。'-y' 是常見的形容詞字尾，表示「具有……性質的」。'Chubby' 的語意核心是「圓胖、豐滿」，通常帶有可愛、健康的意味，多用於形容嬰兒、兒童或臉頰。它描述的是一種溫和、無攻擊性的肥胖感。例如，也可指「圓潤的」手指或四肢。","definition":"1. (of a person, especially a child) plump; well-rounded.; 2. (of a part of a person's body) rounded and plump.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The baby had chubby cheeks.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那個嬰兒有著圓胖的臉頰。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was a chubby boy with a cheerful smile.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一個胖乎乎但笑容開朗的男孩。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a chubby face.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她有一張豐滿的臉。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The child's chubby fingers reached for the toy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子圓潤的手指伸向了玩具。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她有一張豐滿的臉。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6064,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::chunk::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need to allocate a big ____ of our budget to marketing.","expectedAnswer":"chunk","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need to allocate a big ____ of our budget to marketing.","clozeAnswer":"chunk","exampleTranslation":"我們需要將很大一部分預算分配給市場行銷。","reference":{"eng":"chunk","kk":"tʃʌŋk","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"大塊\"  ],  [    \"厚片\"  ],  [    \"一段\"  ],  [    \"大量\"  ]]","chEntries":["大塊","厚片","一段","大量"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要將很大一部分預算分配給市場行銷。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 chunk，語源不清，可能與「厚」或「大塊」的意象相關。在此作名詞，核心語義是一個「大而厚實的部分」。引申用法包括表示「一段」連續的內容（如一段文本或程式碼），或引申為「大量」的某物，特別是未經處理的材料。構詞上，這是一個單純的詞根詞，沒有顯著的前綴或後綴。","definition":"1. a thick, solid piece of something; 2. a large part or amount of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He ate a large chunk of cake.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他吃了一大塊蛋糕。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The report contained a long chunk of technical jargon.\",\n    \"ch\": \"報告中包含一大段技術術語。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to allocate a big chunk of our budget to marketing.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要將很大一部分預算分配給市場行銷。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要將很大一部分預算分配給市場行銷。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6066,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::civic::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ duty requires citizens to vote in elections.","expectedAnswer":"Civic","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ duty requires citizens to vote in elections.","clozeAnswer":"Civic","exampleTranslation":"公民責任要求市民在選舉中投票。","reference":{"eng":"civic","kk":"ˈsɪvɪk","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"公民的\"  ],  [    \"市民的\"  ],  [    \"市政的\"  ]]","chEntries":["公民的","市民的","市政的"],"practiceMeaning":"公民責任要求市民在選舉中投票。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 civicus，意為「屬於一個市民的」，來自 civis（citizen）。Civis 最終來源於 proto-Indo-European * (s)kein-「劃分，切割」，引申為「社群、部落」。Civic 作為形容詞，修飾與公民、市民、城市或市政事務相關的事物。核心語義是「與城市或其居民相關的」。","definition":"relating to a town or city, or to the people who live there; relating to the duties or activities of people in a town or city.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government launched a new civic engagement program.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府推出了一項新的公民參與計畫。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They attended a civic ceremony in the town hall.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們參加了市政廳的市民儀式。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Civic duty requires citizens to vote in elections.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公民責任要求市民在選舉中投票。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"公民責任要求市民在選舉中投票。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5583,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::classic::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He drives a ____ car.","expectedAnswer":"classic","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He drives a ____ car.","clozeAnswer":"classic","exampleTranslation":"他開一輛經典老爺車。","reference":{"eng":"classic","kk":"ˈklæsɪk","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['經典的'], ['古典的'], ['典型的'], ['一流的']]","chEntries":["經典的","古典的","典型的","一流的"],"practiceMeaning":"他開一輛經典老爺車。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 \"classicus\"，意為 \"of or belonging to the highest class, first-class\"（屬於最高級別的，一流的），來自 \"classis\"（a class, fleet, order，階級，艦隊，秩序）。\"classis\" 最初指「羅馬貴族階層」，後來也指「海軍艦隊」，再引申為「類別」或「等級」。因此，\"classic\" 的核心語義是「屬於最高等級、最經典、最受推崇的」。它可以用來形容「古希臘羅馬時期的」（classical antiquity）；指「代表某一類型最高水準的、永恆的」（exemplary, timeless）；或指「典型的、代表性的」（typical）。","definition":"1. Judged over a period of time to be of the highest quality and significance; timeless; 2. Characteristic of or belonging to a past period, especially of ancient Greece or Rome; 3. Familiarly typical or representative.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a classic example of her early work.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是她早期作品的一個經典範例。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The play is a classic of English literature.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這齣戲是英國文學的經典之作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He drives a classic car.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他開一輛經典老爺車。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was a classic case of misunderstanding.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個典型的誤會案例。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他開一輛經典老爺車。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6068,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::clause::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Each ____ in the bill was debated thoroughly.","expectedAnswer":"clause","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Each ____ in the bill was debated thoroughly.","clozeAnswer":"clause","exampleTranslation":"法案中的每一條都被詳細辯論了。","reference":{"eng":"clause","kk":"klɔz","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"條款\"  ],  [    \"子句\"  ],  [    \"從句\"  ]]","chEntries":["條款","子句","從句"],"practiceMeaning":"法案中的每一條都被詳細辯論了。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 clausa（closed thing, conclusion），是 claudere（to close）的過去分詞。核心語義是「關閉」或「封閉」，引申為「段落」、「條款」或「獨立的部分」。在法律或契約中，clause 指的是一份文件的「條款」。在語法中，clause 指的是一個包含主語和謂語的「子句」或「從句」。構詞上，-clause 是來自 claudere 的詞幹，沒有顯著的現代前綴或後綴。","definition":"1. a particular statement or condition in a treaty, law, or contract; 2. a group of words containing a subject and a verb, forming part of a sentence.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The contract includes a clause that allows for early termination.\",\n    \"ch\": \"合約包含一條允許提前終止的條款。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a subordinate clause.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個從句。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Each clause in the bill was debated thoroughly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"法案中的每一條都被詳細辯論了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"法案中的每一條都被詳細辯論了。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4320,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::clay::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Ancient houses were often built of ____ bricks.","expectedAnswer":"clay","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Ancient houses were often built of ____ bricks.","clozeAnswer":"clay","exampleTranslation":"古代的房屋常由黏土磚建造。","reference":{"eng":"clay","kk":"/kleɪ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['黏土；陶土']]","chEntries":["黏土","陶土"],"practiceMeaning":"古代的房屋常由黏土磚建造。","analysis":"源自古英語 'clæg'，與荷蘭語 'klei' 和德語 'Klei' 同源。指的是一種由細小的礦物顆粒組成的泥土，遇水後有黏性，可塑性強，是製作陶器、磚塊等的材料。其核心特徵是『黏性』和『可塑性』。","definition":"earth that is soft and sticky when wet, and becomes hard when it is dry or when it is baked, used for making pots, bricks, etc.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The potter shaped the clay into a beautiful vase.\",\n    \"ch\": \"陶工將黏土塑造成一個美麗的花瓶。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The children played with modeling clay.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子們玩黏土。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Ancient houses were often built of clay bricks.\",\n    \"ch\": \"古代的房屋常由黏土磚建造。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"古代的房屋常由黏土磚建造。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6113,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::clinical::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The doctor gave him a ____ examination.","expectedAnswer":"clinical","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The doctor gave him a ____ examination.","clozeAnswer":"clinical","exampleTranslation":"醫生對他進行了臨床檢查。","reference":{"eng":"clinical","kk":"ˈklɪnɪkəl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"臨床的\"  ],  [    \"診所的\"  ],  [    \"冷淡的\"  ],  [    \"客觀的\"  ],  [    \"嚴謹的\"  ]]","chEntries":["臨床的","診所的","冷淡的","客觀的","嚴謹的"],"practiceMeaning":"醫生對他進行了臨床檢查。","analysis":"此字源自希臘語 klinikos，意為「臥室的；床邊的」，與 klinikē（醫術；臨床醫學）有關，而 klinikē 又源自 kline（床）。因此，clinical 的核心語義是與「床邊」或「病床旁」相關，即與直接醫治病人相關。現代用法包括與醫療診斷、治療和研究相關（臨床的），以及引申為冷淡、客觀、不帶感情的（冷淡的；客觀的）。此形容詞的語意演變是從具體的「病床邊」到抽象的「客觀、不帶感情」。","definition":"1. relating to or used in a clinic or the observation and treatment of patients; 2. clinically detached or objective; unemotional.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"clinical trials of the new drug\",\n    \"ch\": \"新藥的臨床試驗\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a very clinical approach to her work.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對工作有非常客觀的態度。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The doctor gave him a clinical examination.\",\n    \"ch\": \"醫生對他進行了臨床檢查。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"醫生對他進行了臨床檢查。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6114,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::cluster::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"a ____ of grapes","expectedAnswer":"cluster","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"a ____ of grapes","clozeAnswer":"cluster","exampleTranslation":"一串葡萄","reference":{"eng":"cluster","kk":"ˈklʌstər","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"一簇\"  ],  [    \"一叢\"  ],  [    \"一群\"  ],  [    \"集結\"  ]]","chEntries":["一簇","一叢","一群","集結"],"practiceMeaning":"一串葡萄","analysis":"此字詞源不確定，可能與古英語 clūst（關閉）或北歐語 klustr（院子）有關，核心語義是「聚集」。此名詞指由許多相似的物體聚集而成的「一簇」或「一叢」，或指人、物的「一群」、「集合」。其語意演變是從具體的「聚集體」到抽象的「群體」。","definition":"1. a group of similar things or people positioned or occurring closely together; 2. a number of things of the same kind growing or occurring together.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"a cluster of stars\",\n    \"ch\": \"一簇星星\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"a cluster of houses\",\n    \"ch\": \"一群房屋\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"a cluster of grapes\",\n    \"ch\": \"一串葡萄\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"一串葡萄","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5575,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::code::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He used a secret ____ to send the message.","expectedAnswer":"code","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He used a secret ____ to send the message.","clozeAnswer":"code","exampleTranslation":"他使用一種密碼發送了這則訊息。","reference":{"eng":"code","kk":"koʊd","tense":"n.","ch":"[['代碼'], ['密碼'], ['編碼'], ['規範'], ['程式碼']]","chEntries":["代碼","密碼","編碼","規範","程式碼"],"practiceMeaning":"他使用一種密碼發送了這則訊息。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 \"codex\"，意為 \"book, manuscript, trunk of a tree\"（書本，手稿，樹幹）。\"codex\" 最初是指一種由多張羊皮紙或蠟板黏合而成的書寫形式，與捲軸形式相對。因此，\"code\" 最初指「裝訂好的書冊」或「手稿」。其語義演變包括：指「法律條文的彙編」（a body of laws）；指「一套規則或準則」（a system of rules or principles），例如「行為準則」；在現代，尤其指「用於數據傳輸或儲存的符號系統」（a system of symbols used to transmit or store data），例如「電腦程式碼」、「密碼」或「暗碼」。","definition":"1. A system of words, letters, figures, or symbols used to represent others, especially for the purposes of secrecy; 2. A set of rules or principles, especially one governing the conduct of people or the procedure in a particular activity; 3. A program for a computer written in a particular programming language.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The programmer wrote the code for the new app.\",\n    \"ch\": \"程式設計師編寫了新應用程式的代碼。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This building has strict building codes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這棟建築有嚴格的建築規範。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He used a secret code to send the message.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他使用一種密碼發送了這則訊息。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company has a code of conduct for its employees.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司有員工行為準則。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他使用一種密碼發送了這則訊息。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6159,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::coincidence::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"What a ____! I was just thinking about you.","expectedAnswer":"coincidence","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"What a ____! I was just thinking about you.","clozeAnswer":"coincidence","exampleTranslation":"真是巧合！我剛在想你。","reference":{"eng":"coincidence","kk":"koʊˈɪnsɪdəns","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"巧合\"  ],  [    \"同時發生\"  ]]","chEntries":["巧合","同時發生"],"practiceMeaning":"真是巧合！我剛在想你。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 coincidentia，是 coincidentem (coincidens)「同時發生、一致」的現在分詞名詞化。coincidentem 由 com- (together) + inciderē (to fall upon, happen) 組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 com-「一起」和 inciderē「發生、落下」是其核心語意來源。作為名詞，核心語義是「兩個或多個事件恰好同時發生，且彼此之間沒有明顯的因果關係」。詞源中的「一起發生」清楚地體現了此義。","definition":"1. the occurrence and development of events in a happy or beneficial way; 2. a situation in which events happen at the same time in a way that has no obvious connection.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was a remarkable coincidence that they met on the same day.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們在同一天見面真是個令人驚嘆的巧合。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Their birthdays falling on the same day is a strange coincidence.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們的生日落在同一天是一個奇怪的巧合。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"What a coincidence! I was just thinking about you.\",\n    \"ch\": \"真是巧合！我剛在想你。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The coincidence of their arriving at the same time was surprising.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們同時到達的巧合令人驚訝。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"真是巧合！我剛在想你。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6160,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::collaboration::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Artistic ____ often leads to innovative results.","expectedAnswer":"collaboration","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Artistic ____ often leads to innovative results.","clozeAnswer":"collaboration","exampleTranslation":"藝術上的合作經常帶來創新的成果。","reference":{"eng":"collaboration","kk":"kəˌlæbəˈreɪʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"合作\"  ],  [    \"協作\"  ]]","chEntries":["合作","協作"],"practiceMeaning":"藝術上的合作經常帶來創新的成果。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 collaboratio，由 collaborare「一起工作」名詞化而來。collaborare 由 com- (together) + laborare (to work) 組成，laborare 又源自 labor (work)。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 com-「一起」和 labor「工作」是其核心語意來源。作為名詞，其核心語義是「兩個或多個個體或團體為達成共同目標而共同工作」。詞源中的「一起工作」清晰地表達了此義。","definition":"1. the action of working with someone to produce or create something; 2. a joint effort.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The project was a successful collaboration between the two departments.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個專案是兩個部門之間成功的合作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Their collaboration resulted in a groundbreaking discovery.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們的協作促成了一項開創性的發現。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Artistic collaboration often leads to innovative results.\",\n    \"ch\": \"藝術上的合作經常帶來創新的成果。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The collaboration lasted for five years.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這次合作持續了五年。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"藝術上的合作經常帶來創新的成果。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4070,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::collection::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of taxes is the responsibility of the government.","expectedAnswer":"collection","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of taxes is the responsibility of the government.","clozeAnswer":"collection","exampleTranslation":"徵收稅款是政府的職責。","reference":{"eng":"collection","kk":"/kəˈlɛkʃən/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['收藏品', '蒐集物'], ['集合', '聚集'], ['（稅款、款項的）徵收', '收取']]","chEntries":["收藏品","蒐集物","集合","聚集","徵收","收取"],"practiceMeaning":"徵收稅款是政府的職責。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'collectio'，由 'col-' (together) + 'legere' (to gather) 構成，字面意思是「一起收集」。核心是「聚集」、「蒐集」。因此，'collection' 指「蒐集到的物品」（收藏品），「蒐集的行為」，以及「聚集」本身。第四個義項「徵收」則指按規定「收集」款項或稅款。","definition":"1. a group of things that have been collected; 2. the act of collecting things; 3. a number of people or things that are gathered together; 4. the process of gathering money or other items","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"她有很多郵票收藏品。\",\n    \"eng\": \"She has a large collection of stamps.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"博物館展出了一批新的藝術收藏品。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The museum displayed a new collection of art.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"徵收稅款是政府的職責。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The collection of taxes is the responsibility of the government.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"徵收稅款是政府的職責。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6163,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::collector::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She is a ____ of antique furniture.","expectedAnswer":"collector","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She is a ____ of antique furniture.","clozeAnswer":"collector","exampleTranslation":"她是古董傢俱的收藏家。","reference":{"eng":"collector","kk":"kəˈlɛktər","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"收集者\"  ],  [    \"收藏家\"  ],  [    \"稅吏\"  ],  [    \"收賬員\"  ]]","chEntries":["收集者","收藏家","稅吏","收賬員"],"practiceMeaning":"她是古董傢俱的收藏家。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 collectorem，是動詞 colligere「收集、聚集」的施事者名詞。colligere 由 com- (together) + legere (to gather) 組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 com-「一起」和 legere「收集」是其核心語意來源。作為名詞，其核心語義是「收集某物的人」。詞源中的「一起收集」概念引申為「從眾多事物中聚集、收起」的動作者。除了指收藏家，也用於指負責徵收稅款或債務的人。","definition":"1. a person who collects things of a particular type as a hobby or profession; 2. a person whose job is to collect money that is owed to a company or the government.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is an avid collector of rare stamps.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一位熱情的稀有郵票收藏家。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The tax collector visited the household.\",\n    \"ch\": \"稅吏拜訪了這個家庭。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a collector of antique furniture.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是古董傢俱的收藏家。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The collector ensured all debts were paid.\",\n    \"ch\": \"收賬員確保所有債務都已支付。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她是古董傢俱的收藏家。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3948,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::colorful::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The painting uses bold, ____ strokes.","expectedAnswer":"colorful","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The painting uses bold, ____ strokes.","clozeAnswer":"colorful","exampleTranslation":"這幅畫使用了大膽、色彩鮮豔的筆觸。","reference":{"eng":"colorful","kk":"/ˈkʌlərfəl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['色彩繽紛的'], ['生動有趣的']]","chEntries":["色彩繽紛的","生動有趣的"],"practiceMeaning":"這幅畫使用了大膽、色彩鮮豔的筆觸。","analysis":"由 'color' (名詞，顏色) 和 '-ful' (形容詞後綴) 組成。指擁有許多鮮豔顏色；也可引申為「生動有趣、豐富多彩」。","definition":"1. having a lot of different colors; 2. interesting or exciting; full of variety.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The market was filled with colorful fruits and vegetables.\",\n    \"ch\": \"市場裡擺滿了色彩繽紛的水果和蔬菜。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a colorful personality.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她擁有一個豐富多彩的個性。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The painting uses bold, colorful strokes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這幅畫使用了大膽、色彩鮮豔的筆觸。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這幅畫使用了大膽、色彩鮮豔的筆觸。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6212,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::combat::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This organization is dedicated to the ____ of poverty.","expectedAnswer":"combat","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This organization is dedicated to the ____ of poverty.","clozeAnswer":"combat","exampleTranslation":"這個組織致力於與貧困作鬥爭。","reference":{"eng":"combat","kk":"ˈkɒmbæt","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"戰鬥\"  ],  [    \"戰爭\"  ],  [    \"鬥爭\"  ],  [    \"搏鬥\"  ]]","chEntries":["戰鬥","戰爭","鬥爭","搏鬥"],"practiceMeaning":"這個組織致力於與貧困作鬥爭。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 combat，由 com-（一起）和 batre（打擊）組成，意為「共同打擊」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。名詞義指軍隊或個人之間進行的激烈對抗、武裝衝突或搏鬥，也引申為任何形式的鬥爭或抗爭。中文翻譯為「戰鬥；戰爭；鬥爭；搏鬥」。","definition":"1. fighting between armed forces; 2. fighting or struggling against something, such as a problem or a disease.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The soldiers were trained for combat.\",\n    \"ch\": \"士兵們接受了戰鬥訓練。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The country has been involved in a protracted combat with rebels.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該國捲入了與叛軍的長期戰鬥。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This organization is dedicated to the combat of poverty.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個組織致力於與貧困作鬥爭。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個組織致力於與貧困作鬥爭。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4340,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::comfort::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She found ____ in listening to music.","expectedAnswer":"comfort","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She found ____ in listening to music.","clozeAnswer":"comfort","exampleTranslation":"她從聽音樂中找到了慰藉。","reference":{"eng":"comfort","kk":"/ˈkʌmfərt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['舒適；安慰'], ['令人感到舒適的東西或人']]","chEntries":["舒適","安慰","令人感到舒適的東西或人"],"practiceMeaning":"她從聽音樂中找到了慰藉。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'confortare'，意為 'to make strong, strengthen'，由 'con-' (with) 和 'fortis' (strong) 構成。最初是『使堅強、使有力』，引申為『使心情舒暢、得到慰藉』，從而產生『舒適』和『安慰』的含義。1. 指身心上的『舒適、安慰』的狀態。2. 指提供這種感受的『人或物』。","definition":"a state of physical ease and freedom from pain or constraint; the relief of a person's feelings of grief or distress","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The warm room provided great comfort.\",\n    \"ch\": \"溫暖的房間帶來極大的舒適。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His words offered comfort to the grieving family.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的話語給悲傷的家庭帶來了安慰。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She found comfort in listening to music.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她從聽音樂中找到了慰藉。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她從聽音樂中找到了慰藉。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U8、L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6214,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::commentary::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Her ____ on the political situation was insightful.","expectedAnswer":"commentary","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Her ____ on the political situation was insightful.","clozeAnswer":"commentary","exampleTranslation":"她對政治局勢的評論頗具見地。","reference":{"eng":"commentary","kk":"ˈkɒmənˌtɛri","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"評論\"  ],  [    \"註釋\"  ],  [    \"旁白\"  ],  [    \"講評\"  ]]","chEntries":["評論","註釋","旁白","講評"],"practiceMeaning":"她對政治局勢的評論頗具見地。","analysis":"此字由名詞 comment（評論）加上字尾 -ary（表示與…相關的；集合的；地方）構成。comment 源自拉丁語 commentum，意為「思想，解釋」，後來演變為「意見，評論」。字尾 -ary 在此表示「與評論相關的」或「評論的集合」。因此，commentary 指對某事物的解釋、評論、分析，或在體育賽事、新聞節目中的旁白或講評。中文翻譯為「評論；註釋；旁白；講評」。","definition":"1. an explanation or discussion of something, especially a written one in a book or article; 2. a set of remarks on an event or situation, especially by an expert; 3. spoken descriptions of an event, especially a sports event, that are broadcast on television or radio.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The book includes extensive commentary on Shakespeare's plays.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本書包含對莎士比亞劇作的詳盡評論。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The sports commentator provided expert analysis during the game.\",\n    \"ch\": \"體育節目講評員在比賽期間提供了專業分析。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her commentary on the political situation was insightful.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對政治局勢的評論頗具見地。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她對政治局勢的評論頗具見地。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6216,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::commitment::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Marriage is a serious ____.","expectedAnswer":"commitment","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Marriage is a serious ____.","clozeAnswer":"commitment","exampleTranslation":"婚姻是一項嚴肅的承諾。","reference":{"eng":"commitment","kk":"kəˈmɪtmənt","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"承諾\"  ],  [    \"保證\"  ],  [    \"投入\"  ],  [    \"奉獻\"  ],  [    \"責任\"  ],  [    \"委身\"  ]]","chEntries":["承諾","保證","投入","奉獻","責任","委身"],"practiceMeaning":"婚姻是一項嚴肅的承諾。","analysis":"此字由動詞 commit（承諾；委託；犯罪）加上名詞字尾 -ment（表示狀態、行為、結果）構成。commit 源自拉丁語 committere，意為「交付；委託」。字尾 -ment 將動詞轉為名詞，表示「承諾的行為或狀態」、「盡責的狀態」、「奉獻的狀態」。核心語義是將自己投入某事，或對某事做出堅定的保證。中文翻譯為「承諾；保證；投入；奉獻；責任；委身」。","definition":"1. a promise to do something or to behave in a particular way; 2. the state or quality of being dedicated to a cause, activity, etc.; 3. a long-term obligation or responsibility.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He made a commitment to finish the project on time.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他承諾按時完成這個項目。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her commitment to her work is admirable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對工作的投入令人欽佩。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Marriage is a serious commitment.\",\n    \"ch\": \"婚姻是一項嚴肅的承諾。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They have a strong commitment to environmental protection.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們對環保有堅定的承諾。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"婚姻是一項嚴肅的承諾。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5831,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::commodity::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Water is a vital ____.","expectedAnswer":"commodity","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Water is a vital ____.","clozeAnswer":"commodity","exampleTranslation":"水是一種至關重要的必需品。","reference":{"eng":"commodity","kk":"kəˈmɑːdəti","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"商品\"  ],  [    \"物品\"  ],  [    \"價值\"  ],  [    \"必需品\"  ]]","chEntries":["商品","物品","價值","必需品"],"practiceMeaning":"水是一種至關重要的必需品。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'commoditas'，意為「便利」、「舒適」、「比例」、「益處」。'Commoditas' 來自 'commodus' (fitting, convenient)，由 'con-' (together) 和 'modus' (measure) 構成，意指「以適當的度量」。在早期中古英語中，'commodity' 意指「便利」或「有益之物」。後來，其語意演變為「有用的物品」或「可供交易的商品」。現代語義中，'commodity' 特指在市場上可買賣的標準化產品，如農產品、礦產或能源，強調其可交易性和價值。例如，也可指「一種商品的價值」。","definition":"1. A raw material or primary agricultural product that can be bought and sold, such as copper or coffee.; 2. A useful or valuable thing.; 3. Convenience; advantage.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Oil is a major global commodity.\",\n    \"ch\": \"石油是主要的全球商品。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to improve the production of this commodity.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要提高這種商品的產量。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Water is a vital commodity.\",\n    \"ch\": \"水是一種至關重要的必需品。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The commodity price fluctuated greatly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該商品的價格劇烈波動。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"水是一種至關重要的必需品。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4607,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::communicate::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The software allows us to ____ instantly.","expectedAnswer":"communicate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The software allows us to ____ instantly.","clozeAnswer":"communicate","exampleTranslation":"這款軟體讓我們能夠即時溝通。","reference":{"eng":"communicate","kk":"/kəˈmjuːnɪkeɪt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['溝通'], ['傳達'], ['交流']]","chEntries":["溝通","傳達","交流"],"practiceMeaning":"這款軟體讓我們能夠即時溝通。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'communicare'，意為「分享、交換、使共有」。'Communis' (共同的) 是其詞根。此字的核心在於建立或維持一種連結，透過語言、符號、行動等方式交換訊息、思想或情感，達成彼此理解。","definition":"to share or exchange information, news, or ideas; to convey or impart.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's important to communicate your feelings openly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"坦誠地傳達你的感受是很重要的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They communicated through letters for many years.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們多年來透過書信交流。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The software allows us to communicate instantly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這款軟體讓我們能夠即時溝通。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這款軟體讓我們能夠即時溝通。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5560,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::commuter::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She is a regular ____ to the city center.","expectedAnswer":"commuter","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She is a regular ____ to the city center.","clozeAnswer":"commuter","exampleTranslation":"她是經常往返市中心的通勤者。","reference":{"eng":"commuter","kk":"kəˈmjuːtər","tense":"n.","ch":"[['通勤者'], ['常去某地的人']]","chEntries":["通勤者","常去某地的人"],"practiceMeaning":"她是經常往返市中心的通勤者。","analysis":"此字由動詞 \"commute\"（通勤）加上執行者字尾 \"-er\" 構成。\"commute\" 源自拉丁語 \"commūtāre\"（to exchange, change，交換，改變），引申為「改變居住地與工作地之間的移動」。\"-er\" 是常見的名詞字尾，用於指代執行某動作的人或事物。因此，\"commuter\" 的核心語義是指「從事通勤行為的人」，即「通勤者」，也就是每天從家裡往返工作地點或學校的人。此字尾也可用於指代其他固定往返某地的人，例如「機場通勤者」。","definition":"1. A person who commutes to work or school; 2. A person who travels regularly between home and work.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The train was packed with morning commuters.\",\n    \"ch\": \"火車上擠滿了早晨的通勤者。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Many commuters prefer to drive rather than take public transport.\",\n    \"ch\": \"許多通勤者寧願開車也不願搭乘大眾運輸。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a regular commuter to the city center.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是經常往返市中心的通勤者。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她是經常往返市中心的通勤者。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4316,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::comparison::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There is no ____ between their skills.","expectedAnswer":"comparison","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There is no ____ between their skills.","clozeAnswer":"comparison","exampleTranslation":"他們的技能無法相比。","reference":{"eng":"comparison","kk":"/kəmˈpærɪsən/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['比較；對照'], ['比似；比喻']]","chEntries":["比較","對照","比似","比喻"],"practiceMeaning":"他們的技能無法相比。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'comparare'，意為 'to liken, to compare'，由 'com-' (together) 和 'par' (equal) 構成。字面意思是『使相等』、『使並列』，引申為『放在一起看』，從而產生『比較』、『對照』的含義。也可指事物之間的相似性，即『比似』或在修辭上用作『比喻』。","definition":"the act of comparing two or more people or things; a statement or discussion of how different people or things are similar or different","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A comparison of the two plans shows that the second is cheaper.\",\n    \"ch\": \"比較這兩個計畫顯示，第二個比較便宜。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The book uses vivid comparisons to describe the scenery.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本書使用生動的比喻來描寫風景。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There is no comparison between their skills.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們的技能無法相比。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們的技能無法相比。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5649,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l8::complaint::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The most common ____ is headache.","expectedAnswer":"complaint","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The most common ____ is headache.","clozeAnswer":"complaint","exampleTranslation":"最常見的身體不適是頭痛。","reference":{"eng":"complaint","kk":"kəmˈpleɪnt","tense":"n.","ch":"[['抱怨'], ['投訴'], ['（身體）不適'], ['申訴']]","chEntries":["抱怨","投訴","不適","申訴"],"practiceMeaning":"最常見的身體不適是頭痛。","analysis":"此字由 complain（抱怨）+ -t（名詞字尾）構成。complain 源自中古英語 complainen，來自古法語 complaindre，再追溯至拉丁語 complangere，由 com-（完全，together）+ plangere（哀悼，to lament, to beat one's breast）組成。plangere 來自原始印歐語 *pleh₂g-（打擊）。核心語義為「表達不滿或哀悼」。構詞上，com- 加強語氣，plangere 提供「表達痛苦」或「哀傷」的核心動作，-t 將其名詞化。此處為名詞用法，指代「抱怨」、「投訴」的行為或內容。","definition":"a statement that something is unsatisfactory or unacceptable; an expression of dissatisfaction or discontent; a physical ailment or symptom.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I have a complaint about the service.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我對這項服務有一個投訴。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He made numerous complaints about the noise.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對噪音發出了許多抱怨。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The most common complaint is headache.\",\n    \"ch\": \"最常見的身體不適是頭痛。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"最常見的身體不適是頭痛。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5038,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::conception::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His ____ of justice differs from mine.","expectedAnswer":"conception","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His ____ of justice differs from mine.","clozeAnswer":"conception","exampleTranslation":"他對正義的看法與我的不同。","reference":{"eng":"conception","kk":"kənˈsepʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[['概念'], ['構想'], ['設想'], ['懷孕']]","chEntries":["概念","構想","設想","懷孕"],"practiceMeaning":"他對正義的看法與我的不同。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語conceptio，由 concipere（構想、懷孕）派生而來。con-（一起、完全）+ capere（抓住、拿）。conception 在英語中有多個重要義項：1. 「概念、想法、構想」，指在頭腦中形成的觀念；2. 「懷孕」，指受孕的過程或狀態；3. 「對某事的理解或看法」。這些義項都與其詞源「共同抓住」、「形成」或「包含」的概念相關。OCR 掃描時可能將 'c' 誤判。此處修正為 conception。","definition":"1. the action or capability of forming concepts or ideas; 2. the process of becoming pregnant, involving fertilization or implantation; 3. an idea or understanding of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The conception of democracy has evolved over centuries.\",\n    \"ch\": \"民主的概念已經演變了幾個世紀。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The early stages of conception are critical.\",\n    \"ch\": \"懷孕的早期階段至關重要。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His conception of justice differs from mine.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對正義的看法與我的不同。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他對正義的看法與我的不同。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4066,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::connect::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He can't ____ the facts.","expectedAnswer":"connect","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He can't ____ the facts.","clozeAnswer":"connect","exampleTranslation":"他無法將這些事實聯繫起來。","reference":{"eng":"connect","kk":"/kəˈnɛkt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['連接', '連結'], ['與...取得聯繫', '交往'], ['（思想、事物）聯繫起來']]","chEntries":["連接","連結","與...取得聯繫","交往","聯繫起來"],"practiceMeaning":"他無法將這些事實聯繫起來。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'connectere'，由 'con-' (together) + 'nectere' (to bind, to tie) 構成，字面意思是「一起綁」。核心是「聯合」、「繫在一起」。引申為物理上的「連接」、人際上的「聯繫」，以及觀念上的「連結」或「聯想」。","definition":"1. to join or be joined together; 2. to communicate with someone; 3. to associate one thing with another","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"這些線路將電腦連接到網際網路。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The wires connect the computer to the internet.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"與同事建立良好的聯繫是很重要的。\",\n    \"eng\": \"It's important to connect with your colleagues.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他無法將這些事實聯繫起來。\",\n    \"eng\": \"He can't connect the facts.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他無法將這些事實聯繫起來。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5773,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::consecutive::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Please list the numbers in ____ order.","expectedAnswer":"consecutive","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Please list the numbers in ____ order.","clozeAnswer":"consecutive","exampleTranslation":"請按順序列出數字。","reference":{"eng":"consecutive","kk":"kənˈsɛkjʊtɪv","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"連續的\"  ],  [    \"接連的\"  ],  [    \"相繼的\"  ]]","chEntries":["連續的","接連的","相繼的"],"practiceMeaning":"請按順序列出數字。","analysis":"此字為形容詞，構詞自con-（全部；一起）+ -secut-（跟隨；繼承，來自拉丁語sequi「跟隨」）+ -ive（形容詞字尾，表示「性質的；傾向的」）。con-源自拉丁語cum，表示「一起」或「加強」。-secut-是sequi的詞幹，sequi的過去分詞是secutus。-ive字尾源自拉丁語-ivus。因此，consecutive的核心語義是「連續跟隨的；一個接一個的」。語意演變上，從「跟隨」的動作引申為「時間或空間上連續不斷」的狀態。","definition":"1. following continuously or without interruption; 2. in unbroken or logical sequence.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She won the award for three consecutive years.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她連續三年贏得該獎項。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The team had a streak of five consecutive victories.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這支隊伍取得了五連勝。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please list the numbers in consecutive order.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請按順序列出數字。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"請按順序列出數字。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5774,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::considerate::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They made a ____ effort to include everyone in the discussion.","expectedAnswer":"considerate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They made a ____ effort to include everyone in the discussion.","clozeAnswer":"considerate","exampleTranslation":"他們費盡心思，盡力讓每個人都參與討論。","reference":{"eng":"considerate","kk":"kənˈsɪdərət","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"體貼的\"  ],  [    \"考慮周到的\"  ],  [    \"關懷的\"  ]]","chEntries":["體貼的","考慮周到的","關懷的"],"practiceMeaning":"他們費盡心思，盡力讓每個人都參與討論。","analysis":"此字為形容詞，由consider（考慮）+ -ate（形容詞字尾，表示「具有……特性的」）構成。consider本身源自拉丁語considerare，由con-（一起）+sider-（星星，來自sidus）組成，原意可能與「觀星」、「審視星象」有關，後演變為「仔細思考；考慮」。-ate字尾有時也來自拉丁語-atus。因此，considerate的核心語義是指「經常考慮他人感受或需求的人」，即體貼周到的。語意演變上，從「仔細考慮」的動作，引申為「因考慮他人而表現出的體貼行為」。","definition":"1. showing careful thought for the rights and feelings of others; 2. characterized by careful thought or attention.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was very considerate and helped her with her heavy bags.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他非常體貼，幫她拿沈重的行李。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was considerate of you to bring me soup when I was sick.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我生病時你還帶來湯，真是體貼。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They made a considerate effort to include everyone in the discussion.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們費盡心思，盡力讓每個人都參與討論。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們費盡心思，盡力讓每個人都參與討論。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4205,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::constant::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He remained ____ in his loyalty to his friends.","expectedAnswer":"constant","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He remained ____ in his loyalty to his friends.","clozeAnswer":"constant","exampleTranslation":"他對朋友們的忠誠始終如一。","reference":{"eng":"constant","kk":"/ˈkɑːnstənt/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['持續的；不變的'], ['（忠誠、堅持等）堅定的；忠實的']]","chEntries":["持續的","不變的","堅定的","忠實的"],"practiceMeaning":"他對朋友們的忠誠始終如一。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 constans，'con-'（一起）+ 'stare'（站立）。字面意思是“一起站立”，引申為“穩定，不變”。1. “持續的；不變的”強調時間或狀態上沒有變化。2. “堅定的；忠實的”強調在情感或關係上的穩定和忠誠。","definition":"1. occurring continuously over a period of time; 2. not changing or varying; 3. faithful and steadfast.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The car requires constant maintenance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這輛車需要持續的維護。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a constant source of inspiration.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是靈感的持續來源。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He remained constant in his loyalty to his friends.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對朋友們的忠誠始終如一。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他對朋友們的忠誠始終如一。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5777,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::controversial::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The new policy is considered ____ by many.","expectedAnswer":"controversial","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The new policy is considered ____ by many.","clozeAnswer":"controversial","exampleTranslation":"許多人認為這項新政策是有爭議的。","reference":{"eng":"controversial","kk":"ˌkɑntrəˈvɜrʃəl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"有爭議的\"  ],  [    \"引起爭議的\"  ]]","chEntries":["有爭議的","引起爭議的"],"practiceMeaning":"許多人認為這項新政策是有爭議的。","analysis":"此字為形容詞，構詞自controversy（爭議）+ -ial（形容詞字尾，表示「關於……的；具有……性質的」）。-ial與-al同源，都源自拉丁語-alis。controversy本身源自拉丁語controversia，由con-（一起）+vertere（轉動；扭轉）組成，原意為「爭辯；爭論」，即雙方觀點不斷轉變、交鋒。因此，controversial的核心語義是指「容易引起爭論或爭議的」。語意演變上，由「爭論」的概念引申為「具有爭議性的」狀態。","definition":"1. giving rise or likely to give rise to public disagreement.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The politician's statement about immigration was highly controversial.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那位政治人物關於移民的聲明引起了極大的爭議。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It is a controversial issue with strong opinions on both sides.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個有爭議的問題，雙方都有強烈的意見。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The new policy is considered controversial by many.\",\n    \"ch\": \"許多人認為這項新政策是有爭議的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"許多人認為這項新政策是有爭議的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5778,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::controversy::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The film's ending generated considerable ____.","expectedAnswer":"controversy","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The film's ending generated considerable ____.","clozeAnswer":"controversy","exampleTranslation":"這部電影的結局引起了相當大的爭議。","reference":{"eng":"controversy","kk":"ˈkɑntrəˌvɜrsi","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"爭議\"  ],  [    \"爭論\"  ]]","chEntries":["爭議","爭論"],"practiceMeaning":"這部電影的結局引起了相當大的爭議。","analysis":"此字為名詞，源自拉丁語controversia，由con-（一起）+vertere（轉動；扭轉）組成，原意是「互相扭轉；爭辯；爭論」。字面意思是指雙方觀點不斷交鋒、扭轉的狀態。核心語義是指「公開的、嚴重的爭論或爭議」，通常涉及對某事物的不同意見或衝突。語意演變上，從「爭辯」的動作發展為「爭論」的狀態或議題。","definition":"1. public disagreement about something that many people have strong opinions about; 2. a lengthy dispute or debate.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The recent art exhibition has sparked a lot of controversy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"最近的藝術展覽引發了許多爭議。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There is ongoing controversy over the new environmental regulations.\",\n    \"ch\": \"關於新的環保條例，持續存在爭議。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The film's ending generated considerable controversy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這部電影的結局引起了相當大的爭議。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這部電影的結局引起了相當大的爭議。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5076,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::coordinate::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The organization works to ____ aid to disaster areas.","expectedAnswer":"coordinate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The organization works to ____ aid to disaster areas.","clozeAnswer":"coordinate","exampleTranslation":"該組織致力於協調對災區的援助。","reference":{"eng":"coordinate","kk":"koʊˈɔːrdnət","tense":"v.","ch":"[['協調'], ['協同工作'], ['使同步']]","chEntries":["協調","協同工作","使同步"],"practiceMeaning":"該組織致力於協調對災區的援助。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'con-' (together) + 'ordinare' (to put in order)，原意是 '共同使之有序'。其核心概念是將獨立的元素、行動或系統安排在一起，使其和諧地共同運作，達到預期目標。這涉及時間、空間、功能上的整合，以避免衝突並提高效率。","definition":"1. To bring the different elements of (a group or organization) into a harmonious or efficient relationship.; 2. To work together efficiently.; 3. To cause two or more things to happen or move at the same time or in the same way.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to coordinate our efforts to finish the project on time.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要協調我們的努力，以便按時完成專案。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The dancers coordinated their movements perfectly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"舞者們完美地協調了他們的動作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The organization works to coordinate aid to disaster areas.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該組織致力於協調對災區的援助。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該組織致力於協調對災區的援助。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5077,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::core::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This is the ____ business of the company.","expectedAnswer":"core","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This is the ____ business of the company.","clozeAnswer":"core","exampleTranslation":"這是公司的核心業務。","reference":{"eng":"core","kk":"kɔːr","tense":"n.","ch":"[['核心'], ['中心'], ['果核']]","chEntries":["核心","中心","果核"],"practiceMeaning":"這是公司的核心業務。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'cor' (heart)。核心概念是事物最內部、最重要、最基本的部分。這可以指一個物體的中心（如蘋果的核心），一個組織的關鍵成員，或一個概念的本質。它引申為事物的基礎、關鍵或主體。","definition":"1. The central or most important part of something.; 2. The hard central part of a fruit, containing the seeds.; 3. The part of the Earth's interior below the mantle.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The core of the problem is a lack of communication.\",\n    \"ch\": \"問題的核心在於缺乏溝通。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She removed the core from the apple.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她取出了蘋果的果核。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is the core business of the company.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是公司的核心業務。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是公司的核心業務。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5608,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l7::council::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The committee serves as an advisory ____ to the president.","expectedAnswer":"council","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The committee serves as an advisory ____ to the president.","clozeAnswer":"council","exampleTranslation":"該委員會作為總統的諮詢委員會。","reference":{"eng":"council","kk":"ˈkaʊnsl","tense":"n.","ch":"[['委員會'], ['理事會'], ['議會']]","chEntries":["委員會","理事會","議會"],"practiceMeaning":"該委員會作為總統的諮詢委員會。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 'conseil'（建議、會議），它本身源於拉丁語 'consilium'（商議、建議、會議），而 'consilium' 又源於 'consulere'（商議、諮詢）。構詞學上，核心是與「商議」、「建議」相關的詞根，加上名詞化後綴。'-cil' 或 '-cilium' 是常見的拉丁語後綴，表示「地方」或「集合」。因此，'council' 的原始語意是「一個進行商議或提供建議的群體或場所」。現代意義主要指「由選出或任命的人組成的、具有諮詢或決策權的機構」。","definition":"1. An advisory, deliberative, or legislative body of people; 2. A body of people elected or appointed to serve in a local government.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The city council voted on the new zoning laws.\",\n    \"ch\": \"市議會就新的分區法案進行了投票。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The student council organized the school fair.\",\n    \"ch\": \"學生會組織了學校的慶典活動。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The committee serves as an advisory council to the president.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該委員會作為總統的諮詢委員會。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該委員會作為總統的諮詢委員會。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3134,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::crash::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He decided to ____ the party since he wasn't invited.","expectedAnswer":"crash","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He decided to ____ the party since he wasn't invited.","clozeAnswer":"crash","exampleTranslation":"既然沒有被邀請，他決定混進派對。","reference":{"eng":"crash","kk":"/kræʃ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['碰撞；墜毀'], ['（電腦系統等的）故障，崩潰'], ['（價格的）暴跌'], ['（尤指在某種場合，為了尋求某物而）混進去；不請自來']]","chEntries":["碰撞","墜毀","故障，崩潰","暴跌","混進去","不請自來"],"practiceMeaning":"既然沒有被邀請，他決定混進派對。","analysis":"名詞用法，源自動詞 'crash'。指「碰撞」或「墜毀」的事件。也指電腦系統或程式的「故障」或「崩潰」，以及金融市場的「暴跌」。'Crash' 也可以指非正式的「混進」某個派對或場合，通常是沒有被邀請的。","definition":"1. a violent impact or collision; 2. a sudden failure of a computer system or program; 3. a sudden and dramatic fall in prices or values; 4. (informal) an act of attending a party or event uninvited.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police are investigating the cause of the car crash.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警方正在調查這起車禍的原因。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A system crash caused the loss of all data.\",\n    \"ch\": \"系統崩潰導致所有數據丟失。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He decided to crash the party since he wasn't invited.\",\n    \"ch\": \"既然沒有被邀請，他決定混進派對。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The stock market crash of 1929 had devastating consequences.\",\n    \"ch\": \"1929年的股市崩盤帶來了毀滅性的後果。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"既然沒有被邀請，他決定混進派對。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4344,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::cricket::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They went to watch a ____ match.","expectedAnswer":"cricket","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They went to watch a ____ match.","clozeAnswer":"cricket","exampleTranslation":"他們去看了一場板球比賽。","reference":{"eng":"cricket","kk":"/ˈkrɪkɪt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['板球（運動）'], ['蟋蟀（昆蟲）']]","chEntries":["板球","蟋蟀"],"practiceMeaning":"他們去看了一場板球比賽。","analysis":"1. 指一種流行的英國球類運動，『板球』。2. 指一種昆蟲，『蟋蟀』，因其發出的鳴叫聲而得名，可能與其聲音的擬聲詞有關。","definition":"a game played with a bat and ball between two teams of eleven players; a small jumping insect that makes a high-pitched sound","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a great cricket player.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一名出色的板球運動員。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The sound of crickets filled the summer night.\",\n    \"ch\": \"蟋蟀的叫聲充滿了夏夜。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They went to watch a cricket match.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們去看了一場板球比賽。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們去看了一場板球比賽。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3074,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::criticism::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ revealed the underlying disease.","expectedAnswer":"criticism","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ revealed the underlying disease.","clozeAnswer":"criticism","exampleTranslation":"診斷揭示了潛在的疾病。","reference":{"eng":"criticism","kk":"/ˈkrɪtɪsɪzəm/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['批評；評論'], ['（藝術、文學等的）評論；分析'], ['（醫學）診斷']]","chEntries":["批評","評論","分析","診斷"],"practiceMeaning":"診斷揭示了潛在的疾病。","analysis":"源自希臘語 'kritēs' (judge)，是 'criticize' 的名詞形式。指「評價」的行為或結果。\n1. 批評；評論：指對某人、某事或某物的評價，通常指出其缺點或錯誤。\n2. （藝術、文學等的）評論；分析：指對作品的風格、內容、結構等進行的專業性評價和分析。\n3. （醫學）診斷：指對病情的判斷。","definition":"1. the act of saying that something is bad or that you disapprove of it; 2. a statement or opinion that expresses disapproval of someone or something; 3. the analysis and judgment of the merits and faults of a literary or artistic work.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The new policy has faced a lot of criticism.\",\n    \"ch\": \"新政策面臨許多批評。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The book received favorable criticism from reviewers.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本書受到了評論家們的好評。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The criticism revealed the underlying disease.\",\n    \"ch\": \"診斷揭示了潛在的疾病。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"診斷揭示了潛在的疾病。","sourceName":"字彙王、龍騰課本","unitName":"U39、L9"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5444,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::crucial::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Water is ____ for all forms of life.","expectedAnswer":"crucial","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Water is ____ for all forms of life.","clozeAnswer":"crucial","exampleTranslation":"水對所有生命形式都至關重要。","reference":{"eng":"crucial","kk":"ˈkruːʃl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['至關重要的'], ['關鍵性的'], ['決定性的']]","chEntries":["至關重要的","關鍵性的","決定性的"],"practiceMeaning":"水對所有生命形式都至關重要。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 \"crucialis\"，意為\"十字架的\"、\"重要的\"。這個詞與 \"crux\" (關鍵、核心、十字架) 有關，而 \"crux\" 又源自拉丁語 \"crux\"，意為\"十字架\"。構詞上，\"cruc-\" 提供了核心的「十字架」或「關卡」的意象，傳統上十字架是處決或重大事件的象徵，因此引申為「極其重要」或「關鍵」。\"-al\" 是形容詞字尾。 \"Crucial\" 形容某事物「極其重要」到足以決定成敗或結果。","definition":"extremely important or necessary; vital; decisive or critical, especially in the success or failure of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This decision is crucial for the future of the company.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個決定對公司的未來至關重要。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Early diagnosis is crucial for effective treatment.\",\n    \"ch\": \"早期診斷對於有效治療至關重要。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Water is crucial for all forms of life.\",\n    \"ch\": \"水對所有生命形式都至關重要。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"水對所有生命形式都至關重要。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5079,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::currency::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of this rumor is unknown.","expectedAnswer":"currency","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of this rumor is unknown.","clozeAnswer":"currency","exampleTranslation":"這個謠言的流通性（或說來源）不明。","reference":{"eng":"currency","kk":"ˈkɜːrənsi","tense":"n.","ch":"[['貨幣'], ['通用性'], ['流通']]","chEntries":["貨幣","通用性","流通"],"practiceMeaning":"這個謠言的流通性（或說來源）不明。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'currere' (to run)，透過中古英語 'curraunt' (running, current) 演變而來，與 'current' (當前的，流動的) 同源。其核心語義是 '流通的'。因此，'currency' 指的是在特定地區或國家被廣泛接受並用於交易的 '貨幣'。引申開來，它也指觀念、意見或事物的 '通用性' 或 '流行度'，即它們在當前社會中的 '流通' 程度。","definition":"1. A system of money in general use in a particular country.; 2. The quality or state of being current or generally accepted.; 3. General acceptance or prevalence.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The US dollar is a major international currency.\",\n    \"ch\": \"美元是主要的國際貨幣。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His ideas gained currency among young people.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的想法在年輕人中獲得了通用性。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The currency of this rumor is unknown.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個謠言的流通性（或說來源）不明。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個謠言的流通性（或說來源）不明。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3137,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::curse::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Poverty can be a ____ for many families.","expectedAnswer":"curse","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Poverty can be a ____ for many families.","clozeAnswer":"curse","exampleTranslation":"貧困對許多家庭來說可能是一場災難。","reference":{"eng":"curse","kk":"/kɜːrs/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['詛咒；咒語'], ['（罵人的）髒話；穢語'], ['禍根；災難']]","chEntries":["詛咒","咒語","髒話","穢語","禍根","災難"],"practiceMeaning":"貧困對許多家庭來說可能是一場災難。","analysis":"名詞用法，源自動詞 'curse'。指「詛咒」或「咒語」，即一種超自然的力量或言語，旨在帶來不幸。也指「咒罵」時所說的髒話或侮辱性言語。引申義為「禍根」或「災難」，指某物或某事帶來的持續性不幸或痛苦。","definition":"1. a supernatural power or spell that is thought to cause evil or misfortune; 2. an offensive word or phrase used when someone is angry; 3. the cause of a great deal of trouble or unhappiness.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The ancient artifact was said to carry a powerful curse.\",\n    \"ch\": \"據說那個古老的文物帶有強大的詛咒。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He muttered a curse under his breath.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他壓低聲音嘟囔了一句髒話。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Poverty can be a curse for many families.\",\n    \"ch\": \"貧困對許多家庭來說可能是一場災難。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"貧困對許多家庭來說可能是一場災難。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5291,"wordRef":"字彙王::u63::customs::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Local ____ dictate how guests are treated.","expectedAnswer":"customs","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Local ____ dictate how guests are treated.","clozeAnswer":"customs","exampleTranslation":"當地的習俗決定了如何對待客人。","reference":{"eng":"customs","kk":"ˈkʌstəmz","tense":"n.","ch":"[['海關'], ['關稅', '進口稅'], ['（個人的）習慣，習俗']]","chEntries":["海關","關稅","進口稅","習慣，習俗"],"practiceMeaning":"當地的習俗決定了如何對待客人。","analysis":"此字是 'custom' 的複數形式，但作為「海關」義時，通常使用複數 'customs'。'custom' 本身源自古法語 'custume'（習慣、稅收），最終來自拉丁語 'consuetudinem'（習慣、慣例）。'customs' 作為「海關」時，是指政府機關負責徵收關稅和管制進出口貨物。其核心語意從「慣例、習慣」引申為「例行徵收的稅款」（關稅），再引申為負責此事務的「海關」機構。","definition":"the place where you go to a country's airport or seaport to check on your luggage and goods, and where officers check if you are carrying anything illegal; taxes paid on goods imported into or exported from a country; the rules or habits that are traditional in a particular society or group.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"You must declare all goods at customs.\",\n    \"ch\": \"您必須在海關申報所有貨物。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The customs officials inspected his luggage.\",\n    \"ch\": \"海關官員檢查了他的行李。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Local customs dictate how guests are treated.\",\n    \"ch\": \"當地的習俗決定了如何對待客人。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"當地的習俗決定了如何對待客人。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U63"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4335,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::decorate::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She likes to ____ cakes.","expectedAnswer":"decorate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She likes to ____ cakes.","clozeAnswer":"decorate","exampleTranslation":"她喜歡裝飾蛋糕。","reference":{"eng":"decorate","kk":"/ˈdɛkəreɪt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['裝飾；修飾'], ['（給…）授予勳章、獎章']]","chEntries":["裝飾","修飾","授予勳章、獎章"],"practiceMeaning":"她喜歡裝飾蛋糕。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'decorare'，意為 'to adorn, to honor'，來自 'decor' (grace, beauty, ornament)。核心意為『使美觀』或『使光榮』。1. 指為使某物或某地更好看而『裝飾、修飾』。2. 指因功績卓著而『授予勳章、獎章』，使其得到榮譽和表彰，是『裝飾』榮譽的一種方式。","definition":"to make something look more attractive by adding extra items or colours; to give an award to someone for bravery or achievement","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They decorated the house for the party.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們為了派對而裝飾了房子。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The soldier was decorated for his bravery in battle.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位士兵因戰場上的英勇表現而獲得勳章。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She likes to decorate cakes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她喜歡裝飾蛋糕。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她喜歡裝飾蛋糕。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4206,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::definition::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The exact ____ of the term is still debated.","expectedAnswer":"definition","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The exact ____ of the term is still debated.","clozeAnswer":"definition","exampleTranslation":"這個術語的確切定義仍在爭論中。","reference":{"eng":"definition","kk":"/ˌdefɪˈnɪʃn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['定義；解釋'], ['清晰度；明確性']]","chEntries":["定義","解釋","清晰度","明確性"],"practiceMeaning":"這個術語的確切定義仍在爭論中。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 definitio，'definire'（確定邊界，定義）的派生詞。'de-'（完全）+ 'finire'（結束，限制）。核心是“確定邊界”或“明確”。1. “定義；解釋”指明確事物的意義或性質。2. “清晰度；明確性”指影像、聲音或想法的清晰程度。","definition":"1. a statement of the exact meaning of a word, especially in a dictionary; 2. the clarity or distinctness of something, such as an image or sound.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"What is the definition of 'onomatopoeia'?\",\n    \"ch\": \"'狀聲詞' 的定義是什麼？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The definition of this photograph is excellent.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這張照片的清晰度非常出色。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The exact definition of the term is still debated.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個術語的確切定義仍在爭論中。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個術語的確切定義仍在爭論中。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6072,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::delegate::vt","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It's important to learn how to ____ effectively.","expectedAnswer":"delegate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It's important to learn how to ____ effectively.","clozeAnswer":"delegate","exampleTranslation":"學會如何有效地授權是很重要的。","reference":{"eng":"delegate","kk":"ˈdɛləɡeɪt","tense":"vt.","ch":"[  [    \"委派\"  ],  [    \"授權\"  ],  [    \"委託\"  ]]","chEntries":["委派","授權","委託"],"practiceMeaning":"學會如何有效地授權是很重要的。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 delegare（to send away, to entrust, to appoint），由 de-（away）和 legare（to send）組成。核心語義是「委派」或「授權」。作為及物動詞，delegate 指的是將權力、任務或職責移交給他人。這通常意味著賦予對方一定的權威去代表或執行。構詞上，de- 表「移開」或「往下」，-gate 是來自 facere（to make）的後綴，表示「使」。","definition":"1. to entrust (a task or responsibility) to another person, typically one who is less senior than oneself; 2. to send as a representative to a conference or meeting.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The manager delegated the task to her assistant.\",\n    \"ch\": \"經理把任務委派給了她的助手。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She was delegated to represent the company at the conference.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她被委派代表公司參加會議。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's important to learn how to delegate effectively.\",\n    \"ch\": \"學會如何有效地授權是很重要的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"學會如何有效地授權是很重要的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6220,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::deputy::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The president's ____ attended the international summit.","expectedAnswer":"deputy","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The president's ____ attended the international summit.","clozeAnswer":"deputy","exampleTranslation":"總統的代表出席了國際峰會。","reference":{"eng":"deputy","kk":"ˈdɛpjuti","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"代理人\"  ],  [    \"代表\"  ],  [    \"副手\"  ],  [    \"副官\"  ]]","chEntries":["代理人","代表","副手","副官"],"practiceMeaning":"總統的代表出席了國際峰會。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 deputé，意為「被派遣的，代表」，向上可追溯至拉丁語 deputare，由 de-（表示除去，關於）和 putare（認為，估計）組成，意為「認為是，指派」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。名詞義指被正式授權代表他人行事的人，或在特定職位上擔任次要或輔助角色的人，通常是該職位的主要負責人的助手或代理。中文翻譯為「代理人；代表；副手；副官」。","definition":"1. a person who is appointed to act for or replace someone else, especially in a political or official role; 2. a person who is second in command or assists someone in a position of authority.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The sheriff appointed a deputy to help manage the jail.\",\n    \"ch\": \"治安官任命了一名副手來協助管理監獄。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is the deputy director of the department.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是該部門的副主任。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The president's deputy attended the international summit.\",\n    \"ch\": \"總統的代表出席了國際峰會。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"總統的代表出席了國際峰會。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4121,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::desert::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Don't ____ me now!","expectedAnswer":"desert","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Don't ____ me now!","clozeAnswer":"desert","exampleTranslation":"現在別拋下我！","reference":{"eng":"desert","kk":"/ˈdɛzərt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['拋棄', '遺棄'], ['擅離（職守）', '開小差']]","chEntries":["拋棄","遺棄","擅離","開小差"],"practiceMeaning":"現在別拋下我！","analysis":"源自拉丁語 desertus（被遺棄的），是動詞 deserere（放棄）的過去分詞。核心概念是「離開」、「放棄」某個職責、地點或人。引申為在關鍵時刻離開，給人留下困境。","definition":"1. abandon (a person, cause, or organization) in a way considered disloyal or treacherous; 2. abandon (a place or settlement)","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He would never desert his family.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他絕不會拋棄他的家人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The soldiers were accused of deserting their posts.\",\n    \"ch\": \"士兵們被指控擅離職守。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Don't desert me now!\",\n    \"ch\": \"現在別拋下我！\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"現在別拋下我！","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4572,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::desirable::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"A stable income is a ____ outcome of education.","expectedAnswer":"desirable","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"A stable income is a ____ outcome of education.","clozeAnswer":"desirable","exampleTranslation":"穩定的收入是教育的一個理想成果。","reference":{"eng":"desirable","kk":"/dɪˈzaɪərəbəl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['令人渴望的', '合意的'], ['有吸引力的', '值得擁有的']]","chEntries":["令人渴望的","合意的","有吸引力的","值得擁有的"],"practiceMeaning":"穩定的收入是教育的一個理想成果。","analysis":"由 'desire' (渴望) 加上形容詞字尾 '-able' (表示能夠、值得) 構成。核心概念是「值得渴望」。\n    1. 令人渴望的、合意的：指事物符合人們的願望或需求，非常想要得到。\n    2. 有吸引力的、值得擁有的：指事物在外表、品質或特點上具有吸引力，使人覺得值得追求。","definition":"1. wanted or wished for as a possibility or luxury.; 2. possessing or displaying qualities that give pleasure or satisfaction.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a desirable candidate for the job.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是這份工作的理想人選。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They live in a desirable neighborhood.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們住在一個令人嚮往的社區。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A stable income is a desirable outcome of education.\",\n    \"ch\": \"穩定的收入是教育的一個理想成果。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"穩定的收入是教育的一個理想成果。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5419,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::development::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company announced a new product ____.","expectedAnswer":"development","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company announced a new product ____.","clozeAnswer":"development","exampleTranslation":"該公司宣布了一項新產品開發。","reference":{"eng":"development","kk":"dɪˈveləpmənt","tense":"n.","ch":"[['發展'], ['開發'], ['進化'], ['成長'], ['事件']]","chEntries":["發展","開發","進化","成長","事件"],"practiceMeaning":"該公司宣布了一項新產品開發。","analysis":"此字為派生詞，由動詞 \"develop\" 加上名詞化字尾 \"-ment\" 構成。\"develop\" 源自古法語 \"desveloper\"，意為\"展開\"、\"解開\"。其詞源可能與 \"velop\" (包裹、覆蓋) 有關，表示「解開包裹」的動作。構詞上，\"de-\" 是表示「去除」或「相反」的字首（在此處語意為「展開」），\"velop\" 提供核心的「包裹」語意。字尾 \"-ment\" 將動詞的「展開」或「發展」行為轉化為抽象名詞。\"Development\" 指從一個較不複雜、較不成熟的狀態轉變為更複雜、更成熟狀態的過程或結果，涵蓋物理、社會、經濟、個人成長等多個層面。也可指一系列發生的「事件」。","definition":"the process of developing or being developed; a new stage in a process of change or improvement; a significant event or change; the process of growing or causing something to grow or become bigger or more advanced.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The development of new technologies is essential for economic growth.\",\n    \"ch\": \"新技術的發展對經濟增長至關重要。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We are monitoring the development of the storm.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們正在監測風暴的發展情況。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company announced a new product development.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司宣布了一項新產品開發。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該公司宣布了一項新產品開發。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3138,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::dew::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"A fine ____ settled on the leaves.","expectedAnswer":"dew","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"A fine ____ settled on the leaves.","clozeAnswer":"dew","exampleTranslation":"細密的露水落在葉子上。","reference":{"eng":"dew","kk":"/djuː/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['露；露水']]","chEntries":["露","露水"],"practiceMeaning":"細密的露水落在葉子上。","analysis":"詞源來自古英語 'deaw'，與「濕潤」的概念相關。'Dew' 是指夜間或清晨，空氣中的水蒸氣在較冷的物體表面凝結成的小水滴。它是一個自然現象，與清晨、新鮮、濕潤的環境聯繫在一起。其語意通常帶有清新、純潔或短暫的美好意象。","definition":"tiny drops of water that form on cool surfaces at night, when condensation occurs.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The grass was covered in dew when I woke up.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我醒來時，草地上覆蓋著露水。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The morning dew glistened on the spiderweb.\",\n    \"ch\": \"晨露在蜘蛛網上閃閃發光。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A fine dew settled on the leaves.\",\n    \"ch\": \"細密的露水落在葉子上。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"細密的露水落在葉子上。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3139,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::diagram::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The manual includes a clear ____ of how to assemble the product.","expectedAnswer":"diagram","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The manual includes a clear ____ of how to assemble the product.","clozeAnswer":"diagram","exampleTranslation":"手冊包含了一個清晰的圖表，說明如何組裝產品。","reference":{"eng":"diagram","kk":"/ˈdaɪəˌɡræm/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['圖表；圖樣'], ['（解剖學、工程學等的）圖解']]","chEntries":["圖表","圖樣","圖解"],"practiceMeaning":"手冊包含了一個清晰的圖表，說明如何組裝產品。","analysis":"源自希臘語 'diagramma'，意為「圖案，設計」，由 'dia-'（穿過）+ 'graphein'（寫，繪製）組成。'Diagram' 是一種視覺表示，旨在展示事物、結構、原理或過程的組成部分、關係或工作方式。它通常是線條、符號和標籤的組合，用於簡化複雜的概念，使其更易於理解。","definition":"a simplified drawing showing the appearance, structure, or workings of something; a schematic representation.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please refer to the diagram on page 10 for instructions.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請參考第10頁的圖表以獲得說明。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The teacher drew a diagram of the solar system on the blackboard.\",\n    \"ch\": \"老師在黑板上畫了太陽系的圖解。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The manual includes a clear diagram of how to assemble the product.\",\n    \"ch\": \"手冊包含了一個清晰的圖表，說明如何組裝產品。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"手冊包含了一個清晰的圖表，說明如何組裝產品。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4174,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::difference::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His contribution made a real ____.","expectedAnswer":"difference","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His contribution made a real ____.","clozeAnswer":"difference","exampleTranslation":"他的貢獻帶來了真正的改變（重要性）。","reference":{"eng":"difference","kk":"/ˈdɪfərəns/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['差異', '區別'], ['（意見的）分歧'], ['重要性']]","chEntries":["差異","區別","分歧","重要性"],"practiceMeaning":"他的貢獻帶來了真正的改變（重要性）。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 differentia（差異），是動詞 differre（不同，延遲）的名詞形式。核心概念是「事物之間的不相同之處」。","definition":"1. a way in which a person or thing is not the same as another; 2. a disagreement or quarrel; 3. importance or relevance","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There is a significant difference between A and B.\",\n    \"ch\": \"A 和 B 之間存在顯著的差異。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"What's the difference between these two products?\",\n    \"ch\": \"這兩款產品有什麼區別？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His contribution made a real difference.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的貢獻帶來了真正的改變（重要性）。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他的貢獻帶來了真正的改變（重要性）。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5836,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::diminish::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The drug is used to ____ pain.","expectedAnswer":"diminish","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The drug is used to ____ pain.","clozeAnswer":"diminish","exampleTranslation":"這種藥物用於減輕疼痛。","reference":{"eng":"diminish","kk":"dɪˈmɪnɪʃ","tense":"v.","ch":"[  [    \"減少\"  ],  [    \"減弱\"  ],  [    \"降低\"  ],  [    \"縮小\"  ]]","chEntries":["減少","減弱","降低","縮小"],"practiceMeaning":"這種藥物用於減輕疼痛。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'diminuere'，由 'di-' (apart, away) 和 'minuere' (to lessen) 構成。'Minuere' 來自 'minus' (less)。'Diminuere' 的字面意思是「使減少」、「使變小」。'-ish' 是常見的動詞字尾，將名詞或形容詞轉化為動詞，表示「使……」或「變得……」。因此，'diminish' 的核心語意是「使之變少、變弱或變小」。它可以指數量、強度、重要性、價值等方面的減少或減弱。例如，也可指「縮小」尺寸或範圍。","definition":"1. To make or become smaller, weaker, or less.; 2. To lessen the authority, dignity, or reputation of.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The threat of war did not diminish.\",\n    \"ch\": \"戰爭的威脅並未減弱。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His responsibilities will diminish as he gets older.\",\n    \"ch\": \"隨著年齡增長，他的責任將會減少。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The drug is used to diminish pain.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種藥物用於減輕疼痛。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The size of the company will diminish after the merger.\",\n    \"ch\": \"合併後公司的規模將會縮小。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這種藥物用於減輕疼痛。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3078,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::disorder::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The protests quickly turned into ____.","expectedAnswer":"disorder","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The protests quickly turned into ____.","clozeAnswer":"disorder","exampleTranslation":"抗議活動很快演變成動亂。","reference":{"eng":"disorder","kk":"/dɪsˈɔːrdər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['混亂；無秩序'], ['失調；疾病'], ['（政治、社會）動亂']]","chEntries":["混亂","無秩序","失調","疾病","動亂"],"practiceMeaning":"抗議活動很快演變成動亂。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'dis-' (not) + 'ordo' (order)。核心意義是「缺乏秩序」。\n1. 混亂；無秩序：指缺乏組織、雜亂無章的狀態。\n2. 失調；疾病：指身體或精神功能的不正常、混亂的狀態，通常表現為疾病。\n3. （政治、社會）動亂：指社會秩序的破壞，例如騷亂或暴動。","definition":"1. a state of confusion; 2. a state of not being neat or tidy; 3. an illness or a medical condition that is not normal; 4. a disturbance of the peace.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The room was in a state of complete disorder.\",\n    \"ch\": \"房間裡一片混亂。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He suffers from a sleep disorder.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他患有睡眠失調症。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The protests quickly turned into disorder.\",\n    \"ch\": \"抗議活動很快演變成動亂。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"抗議活動很快演變成動亂。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5779,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::donate::vt","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company will ____ computers to local schools.","expectedAnswer":"donate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company will ____ computers to local schools.","clozeAnswer":"donate","exampleTranslation":"該公司將向當地學校捐贈電腦。","reference":{"eng":"donate","kk":"ˈdoʊneɪt","tense":"vt.","ch":"[  [    \"捐贈\"  ],  [    \"捐獻\"  ],  [    \"贈送\"  ]]","chEntries":["捐贈","捐獻","贈送"],"practiceMeaning":"該公司將向當地學校捐贈電腦。","analysis":"此字為及物動詞，源自拉丁語donare，意為「給予；捐贈」。donare又來自donum（禮物），donum則源自donare（給予），其詞根是do（給予）。-ate是拉丁語動詞字尾。因此，donate的核心語義是「將物品或金錢自願地給予他人或機構」。語意演變上，從「給予」的廣泛概念，具體化為「出於慈善或支持目的而捐贈」。","definition":"1. to give money, food, or help to a charitable organization or to someone in need; 2. to give blood or organs for medical use.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Many people decided to donate blood after the earthquake.\",\n    \"ch\": \"許多人在地震後決定捐血。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She donates a portion of her salary to charity each month.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她每月將一部分薪水捐給慈善機構。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company will donate computers to local schools.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司將向當地學校捐贈電腦。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該公司將向當地學校捐贈電腦。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4697,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::dose::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She got her ____ of criticism for being late.","expectedAnswer":"dose","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She got her ____ of criticism for being late.","clozeAnswer":"dose","exampleTranslation":"她因為遲到而挨了一頓批評。","reference":{"eng":"dose","kk":"/ˈdoʊs/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['劑量'], ['（一次的）量'], ['（非正式）（尤指治療性的）一份（苦頭、教訓）']]","chEntries":["劑量","量","一份"],"practiceMeaning":"她因為遲到而挨了一頓批評。","analysis":"源自希臘語 *dósis*，意為「給予」、「分量」。核心是指定量的藥物或物質。引申至任何一次性的、一次性的給予，包括非正式地指一次需要承受的苦難或教訓。","definition":"1. A quantity of a medicine or drug taken or prescribed at one time. 2. A quantity of something, especially food or drink, taken at one time. 3. (informal) An unpleasant experience that you have to endure.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The doctor prescribed a daily dose of vitamins.\",\n    \"ch\": \"醫生開了每日維生素劑量。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He took a large dose of medicine.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他服用了大劑量的藥物。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She got her dose of criticism for being late.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她因為遲到而挨了一頓批評。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她因為遲到而挨了一頓批評。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4009,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u3::drag::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ the icon to the trash can.","expectedAnswer":"Drag","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ the icon to the trash can.","clozeAnswer":"Drag","exampleTranslation":"將圖示拖曳到垃圾桶。","reference":{"eng":"drag","kk":"/dræɡ/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['拖', '拉'], ['（緩慢、費力地）移動'], ['（電腦）拖曳']]","chEntries":["拖","拉","移動","拖曳"],"practiceMeaning":"將圖示拖曳到垃圾桶。","analysis":"詞源：古英語 'dragan' (拖)。指用力拉動重物，或緩慢、費力地移動。","definition":"1. pull (someone or something) along forcefully, roughly, or with difficulty; 2. move slowly and with effort; 3. (in computing) move (an icon or file) across the screen using a mouse.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He dragged the heavy suitcase upstairs.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他把沉重的行李箱拖上了樓。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The negotiations dragged on for weeks.\",\n    \"ch\": \"談判持續了數週，拖得很久。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Drag the icon to the trash can.\",\n    \"ch\": \"將圖示拖曳到垃圾桶。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"將圖示拖曳到垃圾桶。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4189,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::dramatic::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He made a ____ entrance.","expectedAnswer":"dramatic","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He made a ____ entrance.","clozeAnswer":"dramatic","exampleTranslation":"他做了一個引人注目的登場。","reference":{"eng":"dramatic","kk":"/drəˈmætɪk/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['戲劇性的；引人注目的'], ['（變化、行動等）突然的；劇烈的'], [' the dramatic arts']]","chEntries":["戲劇性的","引人注目的","突然的","劇烈的","the dramatic arts"],"practiceMeaning":"他做了一個引人注目的登場。","analysis":"源自希臘語 dramatikos，與 drama（戲劇）相關。'Drama' 來自 'dran'，意為“做”。核心是與戲劇表演相關的特質。1. “戲劇性的”指像戲劇一樣引人注目、情緒強烈。2. “突然的；劇烈的”強調戲劇中常見的轉折和強烈效果，引申為現實生活中顯著的、巨大的變化。3. “戲劇藝術的”直接指與戲劇相關的。","definition":"1. sudden and striking; 2. relating to drama or the performance of plays; 3. exciting and attention-grabbing.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There were dramatic changes in the weather.\",\n    \"ch\": \"天氣發生了劇烈的變化。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The film has a dramatic plot.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這部電影有一個戲劇性的情節。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He made a dramatic entrance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他做了一個引人注目的登場。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他做了一個引人注目的登場。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U6、L8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5081,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::drought::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There was a ____ of new ideas in the company.","expectedAnswer":"drought","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There was a ____ of new ideas in the company.","clozeAnswer":"drought","exampleTranslation":"公司裡新點子匱乏。","reference":{"eng":"drought","kk":"draʊt","tense":"n.","ch":"[['乾旱'], ['長期嚴重缺乏']]","chEntries":["乾旱","長期嚴重缺乏"],"practiceMeaning":"公司裡新點子匱乏。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 'drūgath'，與 'dry' (乾燥) 同源。其核心語義是 '長期缺乏降水導致的乾燥狀態'。這個物理上的乾旱被廣泛引申為任何重要事物（如水、食物、金錢、靈感）的長期嚴重匱乏。這是一種比喻意義上的 '枯竭'。","definition":"1. A prolonged period of abnormally low rainfall, leading to a shortage of water.; 2. A long period when there is little or no rain.; 3. A long period during which there is a lack of something that is needed.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The region is suffering from a severe drought.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該地區正遭受嚴重乾旱。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The drought has led to crop failures.\",\n    \"ch\": \"乾旱導致了農作物歉收。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was a drought of new ideas in the company.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司裡新點子匱乏。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"公司裡新點子匱乏。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3982,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u3::easy::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She has an ____ manner.","expectedAnswer":"easy","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She has an ____ manner.","clozeAnswer":"easy","exampleTranslation":"她舉止從容。","reference":{"eng":"easy","kk":"/ˈiːzi/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['容易的', '輕易的'], ['舒服的', '安逸的'], ['隨和的', '從容的']]","chEntries":["容易的","輕易的","舒服的","安逸的","隨和的","從容的"],"practiceMeaning":"她舉止從容。","analysis":"詞源：古法語 'aisé' (舒適、方便)，源自拉丁文 'a' (在) 和 'sedes' (座位)。引申為「不費力的」、「無憂無慮的」、「輕鬆自在的」。","definition":"1. achieved without great effort; 2. not difficult to do or understand; 3. comfortable and free from worry.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This math problem is too easy for me.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這道數學題對我來說太容易了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He leads an easy life in retirement.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他退休後過著安逸的生活。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has an easy manner.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她舉止從容。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她舉止從容。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4074,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::edit::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Please ____ this article for grammar and spelling errors.","expectedAnswer":"edit","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Please ____ this article for grammar and spelling errors.","clozeAnswer":"edit","exampleTranslation":"請校訂這篇文章，修正語法和拼寫錯誤。","reference":{"eng":"edit","kk":"/ˈɛdɪt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['編輯', '剪輯'], ['修訂', '校訂']]","chEntries":["編輯","剪輯","修訂","校訂"],"practiceMeaning":"請校訂這篇文章，修正語法和拼寫錯誤。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'edere' (to publish, to bring forth)，但 'edit' 這個詞是通過反向構詞（back-formation）從 'editor' (編輯) 來的。'editor' 源自拉丁語 'redigere' (to bring back, to reduce)，後來受 'edere' 影響。核心是「準備出版」或「修訂」。因此，'edit' 指對文本、影片、錄音等進行修改、潤飾，使其更適合出版或發布。","definition":"1. to prepare written material or a film for publication or presentation by correcting, condensing, or otherwise modifying it; 2. to cut out parts that are considered unnecessary or offensive","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"她正在一家出版社編輯一本書。\",\n    \"eng\": \"She is editing a book for a publishing house.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"導演剪輯了這部電影，使其更短。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The director edited the film to make it shorter.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"請校訂這篇文章，修正語法和拼寫錯誤。\",\n    \"eng\": \"Please edit this article for grammar and spelling errors.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"請校訂這篇文章，修正語法和拼寫錯誤。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4223,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::education::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He believes in a good ____ for all children.","expectedAnswer":"education","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He believes in a good ____ for all children.","clozeAnswer":"education","exampleTranslation":"他相信所有孩子都應該接受良好的教育。","reference":{"eng":"education","kk":"/ˌedʒuˈkeɪʃn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['教育；栽培'], ['教育制度；教育體系'], ['（道德、品格上的）教養；訓練']]","chEntries":["教育","栽培","教育制度","教育體系","教養","訓練"],"practiceMeaning":"他相信所有孩子都應該接受良好的教育。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 educatio，'educare'（引導，培養）的派生詞。'ē-'（出）+ 'dūcere'（引導）。核心是“引導，培養”。1. “教育；栽培”是最普遍的意義，指傳授知識、技能和價值觀的過程。2. “教育制度”指整個社會的教育體系和結構。3. “教養；訓練”指通過教育塑造人的品格或技能。","definition":"1. the process of receiving or giving systematic instruction, especially at a school or university; 2. the theory and practice of teaching; 3. the enlightenment of a person in a particular subject or field.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government is investing more in education.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府正在增加對教育的投資。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The educational system needs reform.\",\n    \"ch\": \"教育體制需要改革。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He believes in a good education for all children.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他相信所有孩子都應該接受良好的教育。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他相信所有孩子都應該接受良好的教育。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4573,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::efficient::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The new system is more ____ than the old one.","expectedAnswer":"efficient","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The new system is more ____ than the old one.","clozeAnswer":"efficient","exampleTranslation":"新系統比舊系統更有效率。","reference":{"eng":"efficient","kk":"/ɪˈfɪʃənt/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['效率高的', '功效大的'], ['（人）精幹的', '有能力的']]","chEntries":["效率高的","功效大的","精幹的","有能力的"],"practiceMeaning":"新系統比舊系統更有效率。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'efficiens'，'efficere' (to accomplish - 完成、達成) 的現在分詞。核心概念是能夠有效且迅速地達成目標，不浪費資源。\n    1. 效率高的、功效大的：指在生產、工作或運轉時，以最少的投入獲得最大的產出。\n    2. 精幹的、有能力的：指個人在工作方面能夠高效地完成任務。","definition":"1. working or functioning in a way that achieves maximum productivity with minimum wasted effort or expense.; 2. (of a person) competent and capable.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a very efficient method of production.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一種非常高效的生產方法。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is an efficient manager who gets things done.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一位做事有效的經理。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The new system is more efficient than the old one.\",\n    \"ch\": \"新系統比舊系統更有效率。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"新系統比舊系統更有效率。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U11、L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5473,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::elaborate::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The architect designed an ____ building with many ornate features.","expectedAnswer":"elaborate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The architect designed an ____ building with many ornate features.","clozeAnswer":"elaborate","exampleTranslation":"建築師設計了一座精緻的建築，有許多華麗的特色。","reference":{"eng":"elaborate","kk":"iˈlæbərət","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['精緻的'], ['詳盡的'], ['精心製作的']]","chEntries":["精緻的","詳盡的","精心製作的"],"practiceMeaning":"建築師設計了一座精緻的建築，有許多華麗的特色。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'elaboratus'，是動詞 'elaborare'（努力工作、精製）的過去分詞。'Elaborare' 由 'e-'（出、完全）和 'laborare'（工作，來自 'labor'「勞動、工作」）構成。因此，'elaborate' 在形容詞形式下，表示「經過精心製作、詳盡闡述、內容豐富、細節繁多」的狀態。其核心語意是「付出了大量努力和細節」。","definition":"1. Involving many carefully arranged parts or details; detailed and complicated in design and planning.; 2. Developed or executed with great care and thoroughness.; 3. Intricate and richly decorated.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They wore elaborate costumes to the party.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們穿著精心製作的服裝去參加派對。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The report provided an elaborate analysis of the situation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這份報告對情況進行了詳盡的分析。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The architect designed an elaborate building with many ornate features.\",\n    \"ch\": \"建築師設計了一座精緻的建築，有許多華麗的特色。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"建築師設計了一座精緻的建築，有許多華麗的特色。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3283,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::elegant::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The hotel lobby was decorated in an ____ style.","expectedAnswer":"elegant","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The hotel lobby was decorated in an ____ style.","clozeAnswer":"elegant","exampleTranslation":"這家酒店的大廳裝潢風格高雅。","reference":{"eng":"elegant","kk":"/ˈɛlɪɡənt/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['優雅的；高雅的'], ['簡潔而有效的；別緻的'], ['（設計、想法等）巧妙的；精緻的']]","chEntries":["優雅的","高雅的","簡潔而有效的","別緻的","巧妙的","精緻的"],"practiceMeaning":"這家酒店的大廳裝潢風格高雅。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'elegans'，意為「有品味的，精緻的」。指具有高雅、精緻、得體的外表、風格或舉止。也可用於描述事物（如解決方案）的巧妙和簡潔。","definition":"1. graceful and stylish in appearance or manner; 2. pleasingly ingenious and simple.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She wore an elegant black dress to the party.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她穿著一襲優雅的黑裙參加派對。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The mathematician found an elegant solution to the problem.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那位數學家找到了一個巧妙的解法來解決這個問題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The hotel lobby was decorated in an elegant style.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家酒店的大廳裝潢風格高雅。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這家酒店的大廳裝潢風格高雅。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4139,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::elevator::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He pressed the button for the ____.","expectedAnswer":"elevator","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He pressed the button for the ____.","clozeAnswer":"elevator","exampleTranslation":"他按了電梯按鈕。","reference":{"eng":"elevator","kk":"/ˈɛlɪveɪtər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['電梯']]","chEntries":["電梯"],"practiceMeaning":"他按了電梯按鈕。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 elevatus，是動詞 elevare（舉起）的過去分詞。核心概念是「使升高」。引申為用來上下移動的裝置。","definition":"a platform or compartment housed in a shaft for raising and lowering people or things to or from various floors or levels","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please take the elevator to the fifth floor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請搭電梯到五樓。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The elevator was out of order.\",\n    \"ch\": \"電梯故障了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He pressed the button for the elevator.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他按了電梯按鈕。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他按了電梯按鈕。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4323,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::emotional::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The film was an ____ rollercoaster.","expectedAnswer":"emotional","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The film was an ____ rollercoaster.","clozeAnswer":"emotional","exampleTranslation":"這部電影讓人情緒起伏不定。","reference":{"eng":"emotional","kk":"/ɪˈmoʊʃənəl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['情緒的；感情的'], ['（人）易動情的；激動的'], ['（事件）引起強烈情感的']]","chEntries":["情緒的","感情的","易動情的","激動的","引起強烈情感的"],"practiceMeaning":"這部電影讓人情緒起伏不定。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'emotio' (a moving, agitation)，來自 'emovere' (to move out, agitate)，由 'e-' (out) 和 'movere' (to move) 構成。核心意為『移出、攪動』，引申為內在情感的湧動。1. 指與『情感、情緒』相關的。2. 形容人『情感豐富、容易激動』。3. 形容事物『能引起強烈情感的』，觸動人心。","definition":"relating to or affecting the emotions; (of a person) having or showing strong feelings; causing strong feelings","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a very emotional response to music.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對音樂有非常感性的回應。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is an emotional person who cries easily.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一個易感傷的人，很容易哭。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The film was an emotional rollercoaster.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這部電影讓人情緒起伏不定。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這部電影讓人情緒起伏不定。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6222,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::endorse::vt","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Please ____ the check before depositing it.","expectedAnswer":"endorse","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Please ____ the check before depositing it.","clozeAnswer":"endorse","exampleTranslation":"請在存入支票前簽名背書。","reference":{"eng":"endorse","kk":"ɪnˈdɔrs","tense":"vt.","ch":"[  [    \"認可\"  ],  [    \"贊同\"  ],  [    \"背書\"  ],  [    \"簽署\"  ]]","chEntries":["認可","贊同","背書","簽署"],"practiceMeaning":"請在存入支票前簽名背書。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 indorare，由 in-（在…上）和 dorare（給予）組成，意為「在背面簽名」。在中古英語演變為 to write on the back，後來引申為「支持；贊同」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作及物動詞時，核心語義是公開表示支持、贊同或認可某人、某事或某產品。在商業和金融領域，也指在票據背面簽字以表示轉讓或擔保。此及物動詞義必須接受詞，例如 endorse a candidate、endorse a product、endorse a check。中文翻譯為「認可；贊同；背書；簽署」。","definition":"1. to declare your public approval of someone or something; 2. to sign your name on the back of a check, bill of exchange, or other document in order to transfer it to someone else or to authorize payment; 3. to recommend a product or service publicly.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The politician was endorsed by the union.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位政治家得到了工會的認可。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Many celebrities endorse products in commercials.\",\n    \"ch\": \"許多名人在廣告中代言產品。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please endorse the check before depositing it.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請在存入支票前簽名背書。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"請在存入支票前簽名背書。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6223,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::endorsement::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"An ____ on the check is required for transfer.","expectedAnswer":"endorsement","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"An ____ on the check is required for transfer.","clozeAnswer":"endorsement","exampleTranslation":"轉讓支票需要進行背書簽署。","reference":{"eng":"endorsement","kk":"ɪnˈdɔrsmənt","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"認可\"  ],  [    \"贊同\"  ],  [    \"支持\"  ],  [    \"背書\"  ],  [    \"簽署\"  ]]","chEntries":["認可","贊同","支持","背書","簽署"],"practiceMeaning":"轉讓支票需要進行背書簽署。","analysis":"此字由動詞 endorse（認可；背書）加上名詞字尾 -ment（表示行為、狀態、結果）構成。endorse 源自拉丁語 indorare。字尾 -ment 將動詞轉為名詞，表示「認可的行為或聲明」、「贊同的狀態」、「簽署的動作或證明」。核心語義是公開表達支持或認可，或票據背面的簽名。中文翻譯為「認可；贊同；支持；背書；簽署」。","definition":"1. the act of publicly declaring your approval of someone or something; 2. a statement or action that shows you support or approve of someone or something; 3. the act of signing one's name on the back of a check or bill of exchange.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The candidate received the endorsement of several prominent figures.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位候選人獲得了幾位知名人士的背書。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company announced its endorsement of the new environmental policy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司宣布支持新的環保政策。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"An endorsement on the check is required for transfer.\",\n    \"ch\": \"轉讓支票需要進行背書簽署。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"轉讓支票需要進行背書簽署。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5837,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::evolution::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company has undergone significant ____ in recent years.","expectedAnswer":"evolution","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company has undergone significant ____ in recent years.","clozeAnswer":"evolution","exampleTranslation":"該公司近年來經歷了顯著的發展。","reference":{"eng":"evolution","kk":"ˌɛvəˈluːʃn","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"演化\"  ],  [    \"進化\"  ],  [    \"發展\"  ],  [    \"演變\"  ]]","chEntries":["演化","進化","發展","演變"],"practiceMeaning":"該公司近年來經歷了顯著的發展。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'evolutio'，由 'evolvere' (to unfold, to unroll) 構成。'Evolvere' 由 'e-' (out) 和 'volvere' (to roll) 組成。'Evolutio' 的字面意思是「展開」、「展開的過程」。最初用於指「翻書」或「展開捲軸」。後來，其語意引申至生物學，指生物體經過漫長時期，通過自然選擇等機制，發生遺傳變異並適應環境的過程，即「演化」或「進化」。也可用於形容社會、思想、技術等方面的漸進式「發展」或「演變」。","definition":"1. The process by which different kinds of living organism are believed to have developed from earlier forms during the history of the earth.; 2. The gradual development of something, especially from a simple to a more complex form.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Darwin's theory of evolution revolutionized biology.\",\n    \"ch\": \"達爾文的演化論使生物學產生了革命性的變化。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The evolution of language is a fascinating subject.\",\n    \"ch\": \"語言的演變是一個引人入勝的主題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company has undergone significant evolution in recent years.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司近年來經歷了顯著的發展。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The evolution of technology has been rapid.\",\n    \"ch\": \"科技的發展是迅速的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該公司近年來經歷了顯著的發展。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5782,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::exotic::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The island is home to many ____ species of birds.","expectedAnswer":"exotic","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The island is home to many ____ species of birds.","clozeAnswer":"exotic","exampleTranslation":"這個島嶼是許多奇特鳥類的家園。","reference":{"eng":"exotic","kk":"ɪɡˈzɑtɪk","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"外來的\"  ],  [    \"異國風情的\"  ],  [    \"奇特的\"  ],  [    \"新奇的\"  ]]","chEntries":["外來的","異國風情的","奇特的","新奇的"],"practiceMeaning":"這個島嶼是許多奇特鳥類的家園。","analysis":"此字為形容詞，源自中古英語exotique，來自拉丁語exoticus，再追溯至希臘語exōtikos（來自外國的），由exō（在外面）衍生而來。exō本身源自原始印歐語\\\\*eks-（外面）。因此，exotic的核心語義是指「來自外國的」，特別是來自遙遠、不尋常地方的。引申為「奇特的」、「新奇的」或「有異國情調的」。語意演變上，從「來自國外」發展到「與本地不同、奇特、吸引人的」。","definition":"1. originating in or characteristic of a distant foreign country; 2. attractively unusual or different; 3. (of a plant or animal) introduced from another country and not native.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The market was filled with exotic fruits and spices.\",\n    \"ch\": \"市場裡擺滿了各種異國水果和香料。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She wore an exotic dress with vibrant colors.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她穿著一件色彩鮮豔的異國風情連衣裙。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The island is home to many exotic species of birds.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個島嶼是許多奇特鳥類的家園。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個島嶼是許多奇特鳥類的家園。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4153,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::experience::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He gained valuable ____ during his internship.","expectedAnswer":"experience","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He gained valuable ____ during his internship.","clozeAnswer":"experience","exampleTranslation":"他在實習期間獲得了寶貴的經驗。","reference":{"eng":"experience","kk":"/ɪkˈspɪəriəns/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['經驗'], ['（經歷過的）事情，體驗']]","chEntries":["經驗","事情，體驗"],"practiceMeaning":"他在實習期間獲得了寶貴的經驗。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 experientia（嘗試，知識），是動詞 experiri（嘗試）的名詞形式。核心概念是「通過嘗試或參與而獲得的知識或技能」。","definition":"1. practical contact with and observation of facts or events; 2. an event or occurrence which leaves an impression on someone","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has ten years of work experience.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她有十年的工作經驗。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was a terrible experience.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那是一次糟糕的經歷。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He gained valuable experience during his internship.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在實習期間獲得了寶貴的經驗。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他在實習期間獲得了寶貴的經驗。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5783,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::expertise::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need someone with technical ____ to solve this problem.","expectedAnswer":"expertise","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need someone with technical ____ to solve this problem.","clozeAnswer":"expertise","exampleTranslation":"我們需要一位具有技術專長的人來解決這個問題。","reference":{"eng":"expertise","kk":"ˌɛkspərˈtiz","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"專業知識\"  ],  [    \"專長\"  ],  [    \"技能\"  ]]","chEntries":["專業知識","專長","技能"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要一位具有技術專長的人來解決這個問題。","analysis":"此字為名詞，源自法語expertise，意為「專業知識；專家判斷」。法語expertise本身源自拉丁語expertus（經驗豐富的；證實過的），是expert（專家）的名詞後綴。expert來自拉丁語expertus，由ex-（外面）+pertus（經過；試驗，與parere「生產；經驗」相關）組成，原意是「經過考驗的；有經驗的」。因此，expertise的核心語義是指「由於長時間的學習、訓練或經驗而獲得的深入知識和高超技能」。語意演變上，從「有經驗」的概念，發展為「所擁有的專門知識和技能」。","definition":"1. expert skill or knowledge in a particular field.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The consultant brought considerable expertise to the project.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位顧問為該項目帶來了豐富的專業知識。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her expertise in marketing is invaluable to our team.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在市場營銷方面的專長對我們的團隊來說非常寶貴。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need someone with technical expertise to solve this problem.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要一位具有技術專長的人來解決這個問題。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要一位具有技術專長的人來解決這個問題。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6119,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::explicit::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The film contained ____ scenes of violence.","expectedAnswer":"explicit","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The film contained ____ scenes of violence.","clozeAnswer":"explicit","exampleTranslation":"這部電影包含露骨的暴力場面。","reference":{"eng":"explicit","kk":"ɪkˈsplɪsɪt","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"明確的\"  ],  [    \"清晰的\"  ],  [    \"詳盡的\"  ],  [    \"直白的\"  ],  [    \"露骨的\"  ]]","chEntries":["明確的","清晰的","詳盡的","直白的","露骨的"],"practiceMeaning":"這部電影包含露骨的暴力場面。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 explicitus，是 explicāre（展開；解釋）的過去分詞。構詞上，ex- 是字首，表示「出；外面」；plicāre 意為「折疊；纏繞」，因此 explicāre 的核心語義是「展開、攤開、解釋清楚」。explicit 的核心語義是「被完全展開、沒有隱藏」。此形容詞表示清晰、無誤、無含糊或隱藏，直接說明。其語意演變是從具體的「被展開、攤開」到抽象的「清晰、明確、直白」。","definition":"1. stated clearly and in detail, leaving no room for confusion or doubt; 2. showing or describing the act of sex, violence, or illegal activity in a very direct way.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The instructions were explicit.\",\n    \"ch\": \"說明很明確。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He made explicit threats.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他做出了明確的威脅。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The film contained explicit scenes of violence.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這部電影包含露骨的暴力場面。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這部電影包含露骨的暴力場面。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5083,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::exploration::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Their ____ of the Amazon rainforest yielded new discoveries.","expectedAnswer":"exploration","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Their ____ of the Amazon rainforest yielded new discoveries.","clozeAnswer":"exploration","exampleTranslation":"他們對亞馬遜雨林的考察帶來了新發現。","reference":{"eng":"exploration","kk":"ˌekspləˈreɪʃn","tense":"n.","ch":"[['探索'], ['勘探'], ['考察']]","chEntries":["探索","勘探","考察"],"practiceMeaning":"他們對亞馬遜雨林的考察帶來了新發現。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'explorare'，由 'ex-' (out) + 'plorare' (to cry out, to search) 構成，原意是 '喊出以尋找，調查'。'Exploration' 的核心語義是 '對未知或未被充分了解的區域、領域或主題進行深入的調查、發現和研究'。它包含了 '尋找'、'發現' 和 '研究' 的過程，強調的是對新事物的好奇心和求知欲。","definition":"1. The action of exploring an unfamiliar area or subject.; 2. The systematic investigation of a subject or issue.; 3. The activity of traveling around a place to learn about it.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The exploration of space continues to fascinate scientists.\",\n    \"ch\": \"太空探索持續吸引著科學家。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company is involved in oil exploration.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司從事石油勘探。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Their exploration of the Amazon rainforest yielded new discoveries.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們對亞馬遜雨林的考察帶來了新發現。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們對亞馬遜雨林的考察帶來了新發現。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6225,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::exterior::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ damage to the car was minimal.","expectedAnswer":"Exterior","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ damage to the car was minimal.","clozeAnswer":"Exterior","exampleTranslation":"汽車的外部損壞很小。","reference":{"eng":"exterior","kk":"ɪkˈstɪəriər","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"外部的\"  ],  [    \"外面的\"  ],  [    \"戶外的\"  ],  [    \"外在的\"  ]]","chEntries":["外部的","外面的","戶外的","外在的"],"practiceMeaning":"汽車的外部損壞很小。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 exterior，是 externus（外面的）的比較級，意為「更外面的」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作形容詞時，指位於某物或某人的外表、外側或外部。可用於描述物理位置、表面、非實質性方面，或與內部相對。中文翻譯為「外部的；外面的；戶外的；外在的」。","definition":"1. relating to the outside surface or structure of something; 2. happening or done outdoors; 3. relating to a person's outward appearance and behavior rather than their thoughts and feelings.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The exterior walls of the building need painting.\",\n    \"ch\": \"建築物的外部牆壁需要粉刷。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They held the ceremony in the exterior courtyard.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們在戶外的庭院裡舉行了儀式。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Exterior damage to the car was minimal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"汽車的外部損壞很小。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"汽車的外部損壞很小。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6075,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::faculty::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Humans have the ____ of reason.","expectedAnswer":"faculty","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Humans have the ____ of reason.","clozeAnswer":"faculty","exampleTranslation":"人類擁有理性思考的能力。","reference":{"eng":"faculty","kk":"ˈfækəlti","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"系\"  ],  [    \"學院\"  ],  [    \"全體教職員\"  ],  [    \"能力\"  ],  [    \"才能\"  ]]","chEntries":["系","學院","全體教職員","能力","才能"],"practiceMeaning":"人類擁有理性思考的能力。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 facultas，意為「能力，權力，可能性」，來自 facilis（easy），本身由 facere（to make, to do）派生。核心語義是「能力」或「才能」。在學術語境中，faculty 指大學的「教職員」（他們擁有教學和研究的能力），或構成一個學院或學系的「全體教職員」。Also can refer to 'mental or physical power'.","definition":"1. all the teachers at a college or university; 2. a department or group of departments in a university, dealing with a particular subject or range of subjects; 3. an inherent mental or physical power.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The faculty met to discuss the new curriculum.\",\n    \"ch\": \"全體教職員開會討論新課程。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a professor in the Faculty of Arts.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是文學院的教授。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Humans have the faculty of reason.\",\n    \"ch\": \"人類擁有理性思考的能力。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"人類擁有理性思考的能力。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4318,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::fairly::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It's a ____ long walk to the station.","expectedAnswer":"fairly","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It's a ____ long walk to the station.","clozeAnswer":"fairly","exampleTranslation":"走到車站的路程相當遠。","reference":{"eng":"fairly","kk":"/ˈfɛərli/","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['相當地；頗為'], ['公平地；公正地'], ['（路程、時間等）適度地']]","chEntries":["相當地","頗為","公平地","公正地","適度地"],"practiceMeaning":"走到車站的路程相當遠。","analysis":"源自 'fair' (公平的，美麗的)。作為副詞，它繼承了 'fair' 的不同含義。1.『公平地；公正地』：強調判斷或行動的客觀和公正。2.『相當地；頗為』：表示程度，相當於 'quite' 或 'rather'，表示一個中等偏上的程度，有時帶有『還算』的語氣，與『非常』不同，但又比『有點』強。3.『適度地』：指路程、時間等的適中，不遠也不近。","definition":"to a moderate degree; quite; in a fair and honest way","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This book is fairly interesting.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本書相當有趣。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The judge ruled fairly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"法官做出了公平的裁決。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's a fairly long walk to the station.\",\n    \"ch\": \"走到車站的路程相當遠。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"走到車站的路程相當遠。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4075,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::familiar::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They were ____ friends from childhood.","expectedAnswer":"familiar","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They were ____ friends from childhood.","clozeAnswer":"familiar","exampleTranslation":"他們是從小就親近的朋友。","reference":{"eng":"familiar","kk":"/fəˈmɪliər/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['熟悉的', '常見的'], ['親近的', '親密的']]","chEntries":["熟悉的","常見的","親近的","親密的"],"practiceMeaning":"他們是從小就親近的朋友。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'familiaris'，由 'familia' (family) 構成，意為「家庭的」、「屬於家庭的」。核心是與「家」或「親近的人」有關。因此，'familiar' 指「親近的」、「熟悉的」，引申為「常見的」、「容易辨認的」。","definition":"1. well known from long or close contact; 2. closely acquainted; 3. common or ordinary","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他熟悉這座城市。\",\n    \"eng\": \"He is familiar with the city.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"這音樂聽起來很熟悉。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The music sounded familiar.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他們是從小就親近的朋友。\",\n    \"eng\": \"They were familiar friends from childhood.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們是從小就親近的朋友。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4142,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::fashionable::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He has a ____ haircut.","expectedAnswer":"fashionable","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He has a ____ haircut.","clozeAnswer":"fashionable","exampleTranslation":"他的髮型很時髦。","reference":{"eng":"fashionable","kk":"/ˈfæʃənəbl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['時髦的', '流行的']]","chEntries":["時髦的","流行的"],"practiceMeaning":"他的髮型很時髦。","analysis":"源自 fashion（時尚，流行式樣）+ -able（形容詞後綴）。核心概念是「符合當時的流行趨勢」。","definition":"1. conforming to or following the current style or fashion; 2. stylish and elegant","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She wore a fashionable dress.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她穿了一件時髦的連衣裙。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is the most fashionable restaurant in town.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是鎮上最時髦的餐廳。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has a fashionable haircut.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的髮型很時髦。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他的髮型很時髦。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3285,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::fatal::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The judge's decision was ____ to the defendant's case.","expectedAnswer":"fatal","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The judge's decision was ____ to the defendant's case.","clozeAnswer":"fatal","exampleTranslation":"法官的判決對被告的案件是決定性的。","reference":{"eng":"fatal","kk":"/ˈfeɪtl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['致命的；毀滅性的'], ['決定性的；重大的'], ['（尤指對健康）嚴重的，不可挽回的']]","chEntries":["致命的","毀滅性的","決定性的","重大的","嚴重的，不可挽回的"],"practiceMeaning":"法官的判決對被告的案件是決定性的。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'fatalis'，由 'fatum' (命運，神諭) 演變而來。最初指由命運決定的，後主要指導致死亡的，引申至造成嚴重後果或決定性的事物。","definition":"1. causing death; deadly; 2. of, concerning, or ordained by destiny; 3. of great importance or consequence; decisive.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The accident resulted in two fatal injuries.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這次事故造成了兩起致命傷害。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This was a fatal blow to the company's finances.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是對公司財政的毀滅性打擊。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The judge's decision was fatal to the defendant's case.\",\n    \"ch\": \"法官的判決對被告的案件是決定性的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"法官的判決對被告的案件是決定性的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4695,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::feather::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He dipped the ____ of the oar into the water.","expectedAnswer":"feather","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He dipped the ____ of the oar into the water.","clozeAnswer":"feather","exampleTranslation":"他將船槳的槳葉浸入水中。","reference":{"eng":"feather","kk":"/ˈfɛðər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['羽毛'], ['（衣物、飾品等的）羽飾'], ['（船槳、輪子的）羽狀結構']]","chEntries":["羽毛","羽飾","羽狀結構"],"practiceMeaning":"他將船槳的槳葉浸入水中。","analysis":"源自古英語 *feðer*，與拉丁語 *penna*（羽毛、翅膀）同源。核心是鳥類用於飛行、保暖的外部結構。引申至用於裝飾或構成某些器物的羽狀部分。","definition":"1. Each separate article of plumage forming the external covering of a bird. 2. A decoration made from feathers. 3. The blade of an oar or paddle.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A small feather drifted down from the bird's wing.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一根小羽毛從鳥的翅膀上飄落。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The hat was adorned with a single blue feather.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這頂帽子上裝飾著一根藍色的羽毛。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He dipped the feather of the oar into the water.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他將船槳的槳葉浸入水中。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他將船槳的槳葉浸入水中。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3151,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::feedback::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The microphone produced an annoying ____ sound.","expectedAnswer":"feedback","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The microphone produced an annoying ____ sound.","clozeAnswer":"feedback","exampleTranslation":"麥克風發出了一種惱人的聲嘯。","reference":{"eng":"feedback","kk":"/ˈfiːdbæk/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['回饋；意見；反應'], ['（電子設備的）反饋，聲嘯']]","chEntries":["回饋","意見","反應","反饋，聲嘯"],"practiceMeaning":"麥克風發出了一種惱人的聲嘯。","analysis":"由 'feed'（饋送）+ 'back'（回）組成。'Feedback' 指將某個過程的結果或輸出作為輸入，以評估、改進或調整該過程。在人際互動中，它是關於某人表現的意見或評價。在技術領域，它可能是系統對其自身輸出的反應，或用戶對產品的反應。核心概念是「回歸」、「反應」或「評估」。","definition":"1. information about the reactions of customers or others to a product, service, or person; 2. the return of output from one stage of a process as input to a later stage; 3. (in electronics) the modification of a signal by passing it back to an earlier stage.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We received a lot of positive feedback on our new product.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們收到了對我們新產品的大量正面回饋。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Your feedback is important to help us improve.\",\n    \"ch\": \"您的意見對我們改進很重要。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The microphone produced an annoying feedback sound.\",\n    \"ch\": \"麥克風發出了一種惱人的聲嘯。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"麥克風發出了一種惱人的聲嘯。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6076,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::fiscal::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ responsibility is important for economic stability.","expectedAnswer":"Fiscal","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ responsibility is important for economic stability.","clozeAnswer":"Fiscal","exampleTranslation":"財政責任對經濟穩定很重要。","reference":{"eng":"fiscal","kk":"ˈfɪskəl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"財政的\"  ],  [    \"財政上的\"  ],  [    \"稅收的\"  ]]","chEntries":["財政的","財政上的","稅收的"],"practiceMeaning":"財政責任對經濟穩定很重要。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 fiscus，意為「籃子，錢箱」，特別是「國庫」或「公共財政」。核心語義與「財政」、「稅收」、「公共金庫」相關。Fiscal 作為形容詞，用來修飾與政府的收入、支出、預算、稅務和貨幣政策相關的事務。","definition":"relating to government revenue, especially taxes.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government announced new fiscal policies.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府宣布了新的財政政策。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company's fiscal year ends in December.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司的財政年度於十二月結束。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Fiscal responsibility is important for economic stability.\",\n    \"ch\": \"財政責任對經濟穩定很重要。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"財政責任對經濟穩定很重要。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3984,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u3::flash::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We received a ____ report on the incident.","expectedAnswer":"flash","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We received a ____ report on the incident.","clozeAnswer":"flash","exampleTranslation":"我們收到了一份關於該事件的快訊。","reference":{"eng":"flash","kk":"/flæʃ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['閃光', '閃光燈'], ['一陣', '瞬間'], ['（新聞）快訊', '（電視）閃報']]","chEntries":["閃光","閃光燈","一陣","瞬間","快訊","閃報"],"practiceMeaning":"我們收到了一份關於該事件的快訊。","analysis":"詞源：同上。名詞指瞬間發生的光或事件。","definition":"1. a sudden brief burst of bright light; 2. a very short period of time; 3. a brief news report.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A flash of lightning lit up the night.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一道閃電照亮了夜晚。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"In a flash, he was gone.\",\n    \"ch\": \"瞬間，他就消失了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We received a flash report on the incident.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們收到了一份關於該事件的快訊。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們收到了一份關於該事件的快訊。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5582,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::flaw::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Despite this ____, the plan was generally well-received.","expectedAnswer":"flaw","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Despite this ____, the plan was generally well-received.","clozeAnswer":"flaw","exampleTranslation":"儘管有這個缺點，這個計畫總體上還是受到好評。","reference":{"eng":"flaw","kk":"flɔ","tense":"n.","ch":"[['缺點'], ['瑕疵'], ['裂痕'], ['缺陷']]","chEntries":["缺點","瑕疵","裂痕","缺陷"],"practiceMeaning":"儘管有這個缺點，這個計畫總體上還是受到好評。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 \"flau\"，詞源不甚確定，可能與古高地德語 \"flāh\"（flat, smooth，平坦的，光滑的）或與 \"flow\"（流動）有關。原始語義可能與「表面不平坦」或「中間有裂縫」有關。因此，\"flaw\" 的核心語義是指「某物的不完美之處」，特別是「一個細微的、可能影響整體功能的缺陷或裂痕」。它可以是物理上的（e.g., a flaw in a diamond），也可以是抽象上的（e.g., a flaw in an argument）。","definition":"1. A mark, blemish, or other imperfection which mars a substance or object; 2. An instance of being imperfect or defective; 3. A weakness in a person's character.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The vase had a small flaw in the glaze.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個花瓶的釉面有一個小瑕疵。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His argument had a serious flaw.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的論點有一個嚴重的缺陷。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Despite this flaw, the plan was generally well-received.\",\n    \"ch\": \"儘管有這個缺點，這個計畫總體上還是受到好評。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"儘管有這個缺點，這個計畫總體上還是受到好評。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5581,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::flawless::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He made a ____ execution of the plan.","expectedAnswer":"flawless","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He made a ____ execution of the plan.","clozeAnswer":"flawless","exampleTranslation":"他完美地執行了這個計畫。","reference":{"eng":"flawless","kk":"ˈflɔlɪs","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['無瑕疵的'], ['完美的'], ['無可挑剔的']]","chEntries":["無瑕疵的","完美的","無可挑剔的"],"practiceMeaning":"他完美地執行了這個計畫。","analysis":"此字由名詞 \"flaw\" 加上否定字尾 \"-less\" 構成。\"flaw\" 源自古法語 \"flau\"，可能來自古高地德語 \"flāh\"（flat, smooth，平坦的，光滑的），或與 \"flow\"（流動）有關，引申為「缺陷、裂痕」。\"-less\" 是常見的否定字尾，表示「沒有」。因此，\"flawless\" 的核心語義是「沒有任何缺陷、裂痕或瑕疵」。它強調事物達到了完美的狀態，無可挑剔。","definition":"1. Without any blemishes or imperfections; perfect; 2. Without a fault or defect.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her performance was flawless.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的演出無可挑剔。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The diamond was flawless.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這顆鑽石無瑕疵。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He made a flawless execution of the plan.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他完美地執行了這個計畫。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他完美地執行了這個計畫。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5839,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::flexibility::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need to maintain ____ in our strategy.","expectedAnswer":"flexibility","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need to maintain ____ in our strategy.","clozeAnswer":"flexibility","exampleTranslation":"我們需要在策略上保持彈性。","reference":{"eng":"flexibility","kk":"ˌflɛksəˈbɪləti","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"靈活性\"  ],  [    \"彈性\"  ],  [    \"適應性\"  ],  [    \"柔韌性\"  ]]","chEntries":["靈活性","彈性","適應性","柔韌性"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要在策略上保持彈性。","analysis":"此字由形容詞 'flexible' 加上名詞字尾 '-ity' 構成。'Flexible' 源自拉丁語 'flexibilis'，由 'flectere' (to bend) 構成。'-ity' 是常見的名詞字尾，表示「狀態」、「性質」。因此，'flexibility' 指「能夠彎曲」、「容易改變」的性質或狀態。在物理上，指材料的柔韌性；在引申義上，指個人或組織能夠適應變化、靈活應對挑戰的能力。它強調的是一種「可塑性」或「不受拘束」的特質。","definition":"1. The quality of being easily bent or altered.; 2. The ability to adapt or be adapted to new conditions.; 3. Willingness to consider new ideas; open-mindedness.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The job offers flexibility in working hours.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這份工作提供彈性的工作時間。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His flexibility in negotiations was impressive.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在談判中的靈活性令人印象深刻。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to maintain flexibility in our strategy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要在策略上保持彈性。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The flexibility of the material allowed it to be molded into complex shapes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種材料的柔韌性使其能夠被塑造成複雜的形狀。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要在策略上保持彈性。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3282,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::flexible::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company has a ____ approach to problem-solving.","expectedAnswer":"flexible","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company has a ____ approach to problem-solving.","clozeAnswer":"flexible","exampleTranslation":"這家公司在解決問題方面採取靈活的策略。","reference":{"eng":"flexible","kk":"/ˈflɛksəbl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['靈活的；可彎曲的'], ['易於適應的；適應性強的'], ['（價格、時間等）可協商的']]","chEntries":["靈活的","可彎曲的","易於適應的","適應性強的","可協商的"],"practiceMeaning":"這家公司在解決問題方面採取靈活的策略。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'flexibilis'，由 'flectere' (彎曲) + '-ibilis' (可) 組成。指能夠輕易彎曲或改變形狀，引申至行為、計劃或安排，表示容易適應變化、不僵化。","definition":"1. able to be easily bent or changed; 2. able to adapt or be adapted to new conditions; 3. open to change or negotiation.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This material is very flexible and easy to work with.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種材料非常柔軟，易於加工。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We offer flexible working hours for our employees.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們為員工提供彈性工作時間。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company has a flexible approach to problem-solving.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司在解決問題方面採取靈活的策略。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這家公司在解決問題方面採取靈活的策略。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5045,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::fluid::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The political situation remains ____.","expectedAnswer":"fluid","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The political situation remains ____.","clozeAnswer":"fluid","exampleTranslation":"政治局勢仍然不穩定（多變）。","reference":{"eng":"fluid","kk":"ˈfluːɪd","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['流動的'], ['流暢的'], ['不穩定的'], ['變化的']]","chEntries":["流動的","流暢的","不穩定的","變化的"],"practiceMeaning":"政治局勢仍然不穩定（多變）。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語fluidus，是動詞fluere（流動）的形容詞形式。fluere 又來自原始印歐語 *pleu-（流動）。fluid 的核心語意是「能夠流動的，無固定形狀的」。引申為「流暢的、順暢的」（如 fluid movement），或指情況「不穩定的、變化的、彈性的」（如 fluid situation）。OCR 掃描時可能將 'f' 誤判為 'l'。此處修正為 fluid。","definition":"1. able to flow easily; 2. smooth and graceful; 3. (of a situation or plan) changeable; not fixed.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Water is a fluid.\",\n    \"ch\": \"水是流體。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her movements were fluid and elegant.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的動作流暢而優雅。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The political situation remains fluid.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政治局勢仍然不穩定（多變）。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"政治局勢仍然不穩定（多變）。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4575,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::foggy::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The driver couldn't see well because of the ____ conditions.","expectedAnswer":"foggy","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The driver couldn't see well because of the ____ conditions.","clozeAnswer":"foggy","exampleTranslation":"由於霧濛濛的狀況，司機看不清楚。","reference":{"eng":"foggy","kk":"/ˈfɒɡi/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['有霧的', '霧濛濛的'], ['（頭腦、理解等）模糊的', '不清晰的']]","chEntries":["有霧的","霧濛濛的","模糊的","不清晰的"],"practiceMeaning":"由於霧濛濛的狀況，司機看不清楚。","analysis":"由 'fog' (霧) 加上形容詞字尾 '-y' 構成。\n    1. 有霧的：指天氣有霧，能見度低。\n    2. 模糊的、不清晰的：引申為思路、理解或記憶不清，如同在霧中一樣。","definition":"1. (of the weather or a place) full of fog; misty.; 2. (of a person's thoughts or memory) confused or unclear.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was a foggy morning, so we couldn't see the mountains.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那是一個有霧的早晨，所以我們看不到山。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I'm a bit foggy on the details of the plan.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我對計劃的細節有點模糊。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The driver couldn't see well because of the foggy conditions.\",\n    \"ch\": \"由於霧濛濛的狀況，司機看不清楚。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"由於霧濛濛的狀況，司機看不清楚。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4579,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::for-the-sake-of::prep-phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She compromised ____ peace.","expectedAnswer":"for the sake of","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She compromised ____ peace.","clozeAnswer":"for the sake of","exampleTranslation":"為了和平，她做出了讓步。","reference":{"eng":"for the sake of","kk":"/fər ðə seɪk əv/","tense":"prep. phrase","ch":"[['為了（某人或某事的）緣故', '為了（某人或某事的）利益']]","chEntries":["為了緣故","為了利益"],"practiceMeaning":"為了和平，她做出了讓步。","analysis":"此片語由 'for' (為了), 'the' (定冠詞), 'sake' (緣故、利益) 和 'of' (of) 組成。 'sake' 源自古英語 'sacu' (cause, reason)。此片語強調行動的動機是為了某人或某事的益處、目的或緣故。","definition":"1. in the interest of; for the benefit of.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He worked extra hours for the sake of his family.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他加班工作是為了家人的緣故。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"For the sake of argument, let's assume you are right.\",\n    \"ch\": \"為了辯論起見，我們假設你是對的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She compromised for the sake of peace.\",\n    \"ch\": \"為了和平，她做出了讓步。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"為了和平，她做出了讓步。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4529,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::forever::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He seemed to talk ____ about his vacation.","expectedAnswer":"forever","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He seemed to talk ____ about his vacation.","clozeAnswer":"forever","exampleTranslation":"他似乎不斷地談論他的假期。","reference":{"eng":"forever","kk":"/fərˈɛvər/","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['永遠地', '永久地'], ['一直地', '不斷地']]","chEntries":["永遠地","永久地","一直地","不斷地"],"practiceMeaning":"他似乎不斷地談論他的假期。","analysis":"此字由 'for' (為了) 和 'ever' (永遠) 組成。'ever' 源自古英語 'æfre'，意為 'always' (總是)。'for' 則來自古英語 'fōr' (因為、目的)。 'forever' 結合兩者，表示時間上的永恆，引申為持續不斷的狀態。","definition":"1. for all future time; for always; eternally.; 2. continually; constantly.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They promised to love each other forever.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們承諾永遠愛對方。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She will forever be remembered for her kindness.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她將因她的善良而被永遠記住。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He seemed to talk forever about his vacation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他似乎不斷地談論他的假期。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他似乎不斷地談論他的假期。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6226,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::foster::vt","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They decided to ____ a child from the local orphanage.","expectedAnswer":"foster","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They decided to ____ a child from the local orphanage.","clozeAnswer":"foster","exampleTranslation":"他們決定領養當地孤兒院的一個孩子。","reference":{"eng":"foster","kk":"ˈfɔstər","tense":"vt.","ch":"[  [    \"培養\"  ],  [    \"促進\"  ],  [    \"養育\"  ],  [    \"鼓勵\"  ]]","chEntries":["培養","促進","養育","鼓勵"],"practiceMeaning":"他們決定領養當地孤兒院的一個孩子。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 fōster，意為「餵養，養育」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作及物動詞時，核心語義是鼓勵、促進或養育事物的發展，特別是抽象的概念，如成長、進步、關係或情感。也可以指實際養育孩子。此及物動詞義必須接受詞，例如 foster growth、foster understanding、foster children。中文翻譯為「培養；促進；養育；鼓勵」。","definition":"1. to encourage the development or growth of something; 2. to take care of a child, or to provide a home for a child, for a period of time.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The program aims to foster creativity in young children.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該計劃旨在培養幼童的創造力。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to foster a sense of community.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要促進社區意識。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They decided to foster a child from the local orphanage.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們決定領養當地孤兒院的一個孩子。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們決定領養當地孤兒院的一個孩子。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4621,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::fountain::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He is a ____ of knowledge.","expectedAnswer":"fountain","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He is a ____ of knowledge.","clozeAnswer":"fountain","exampleTranslation":"他是知識的源泉。","reference":{"eng":"fountain","kk":"/ˈfaʊntən/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['噴泉'], ['噴水池'], ['源泉']]","chEntries":["噴泉","噴水池","源泉"],"practiceMeaning":"他是知識的源泉。","analysis":"源自古法語 'fontaine'，來自拉丁語 'fons' (泉水)。核心概念是水源或噴出水的裝置。可以是天然的泉水，也可以是人工建造的噴泉或噴水池。引申義可指某事物產生的源頭。","definition":"a structure that sends a stream of water into the air; a source or origin.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Children were playing near the fountain in the park.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子們在公園的噴泉附近玩耍。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The city is famous for its beautiful public fountains.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座城市以其美麗的公共噴泉聞名。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a fountain of knowledge.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是知識的源泉。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他是知識的源泉。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4124,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::frank::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She was ____ with him about her feelings.","expectedAnswer":"frank","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She was ____ with him about her feelings.","clozeAnswer":"frank","exampleTranslation":"她對他坦誠了她的感受。","reference":{"eng":"frank","kk":"/fræŋk/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['坦白的', '直率的']]","chEntries":["坦白的","直率的"],"practiceMeaning":"她對他坦誠了她的感受。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 francus（自由的，不受約束的），後引申為「誠實的」。核心概念是「不受隱瞞、真誠」。","definition":"1. open, direct, and unreserved in speech or expression; 2. (of a letter or document) delivered openly and without secrecy","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He gave a frank assessment of the situation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對情況做了坦白的評估。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I appreciate your frank opinion.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我欣賞你直率的意見。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She was frank with him about her feelings.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對他坦誠了她的感受。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她對他坦誠了她的感受。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3877,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::fright::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He jumped back in ____.","expectedAnswer":"fright","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He jumped back in ____.","clozeAnswer":"fright","exampleTranslation":"他因驚嚇而向後跳。","reference":{"eng":"fright","kk":"/fraɪt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['驚恐', '恐懼'], ['驚嚇']]","chEntries":["驚恐","恐懼","驚嚇"],"practiceMeaning":"他因驚嚇而向後跳。","analysis":"源自古英語 'fyrhto'，與 'fear' (恐懼) 同源。核心是強烈的恐懼感。指突然而來的、強烈的恐懼，常由某事或某物引起。","definition":"1. a sudden, intense feeling of fear. 2. the cause of sudden fear.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The loud noise gave me a fright.\",\n    \"ch\": \"巨大的聲響嚇了我一跳。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She looked at him in fright.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她驚恐地看著他。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He jumped back in fright.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他因驚嚇而向後跳。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他因驚嚇而向後跳。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3154,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::frustration::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Bureaucratic red tape can be a major source of ____.","expectedAnswer":"frustration","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Bureaucratic red tape can be a major source of ____.","clozeAnswer":"frustration","exampleTranslation":"官僚主義的繁文縟節是造成挫折的主要原因。","reference":{"eng":"frustration","kk":"/frʌˈstreɪʃn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['沮喪；挫敗感'], ['阻礙；挫折']]","chEntries":["沮喪","挫敗感","阻礙","挫折"],"practiceMeaning":"官僚主義的繁文縟節是造成挫折的主要原因。","analysis":"名詞用法，源自動詞 'frustrate'。指「沮喪」、「挫敗」或「失落」的感覺，通常是由於目標受阻、期望落空或事情不順利而引起。它也可以指「阻礙」或「挫折」本身，即那些導致沮喪情況發生的因素。","definition":"1. the feeling of being upset or annoyed as a result of being unable to change or achieve something; 2. the state of being prevented from achieving a goal.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He slammed his fist on the table in sheer frustration.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他純粹因為沮喪而一拳砸在桌子上。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The lack of progress led to widespread frustration among the team.\",\n    \"ch\": \"缺乏進展導致團隊成員普遍感到沮喪。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Bureaucratic red tape can be a major source of frustration.\",\n    \"ch\": \"官僚主義的繁文縟節是造成挫折的主要原因。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"官僚主義的繁文縟節是造成挫折的主要原因。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3156,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::furious::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She gave a ____ look to the person who bumped into her.","expectedAnswer":"furious","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She gave a ____ look to the person who bumped into her.","clozeAnswer":"furious","exampleTranslation":"她怒視著撞到她的人。","reference":{"eng":"furious","kk":"/ˈfjʊəriəs/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['狂怒的；暴怒的'], ['（風、風暴等）猛烈的；狂暴的']]","chEntries":["狂怒的","暴怒的","猛烈的","狂暴的"],"practiceMeaning":"她怒視著撞到她的人。","analysis":"詞源來自拉丁語 'furiosus'，意為「瘋狂的，狂怒的」，與 'furia'（狂怒，瘋狂）有關。'Furious' 形容的是極度的憤怒，一種失控的情緒狀態。也可用來形容自然現象（如風、海浪）的猛烈和狂暴，這種猛烈程度類似於狂怒的表現。","definition":"1. extremely angry; 2. (of a storm or other natural phenomenon) extremely violent.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was furious when he discovered his car had been stolen.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他發現汽車被偷後勃然大怒。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The furious waves crashed against the shore.\",\n    \"ch\": \"洶湧的海浪拍打著海岸。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She gave a furious look to the person who bumped into her.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她怒視著撞到她的人。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她怒視著撞到她的人。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4347,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::garage::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ sale will be held on Saturday.","expectedAnswer":"garage","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ sale will be held on Saturday.","clozeAnswer":"garage","exampleTranslation":"跳蚤市場將於週六舉行。","reference":{"eng":"garage","kk":"/ɡəˈrɑːʒ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['汽車修理廠；汽車庫'], ['（蘇聯/東歐）集體農莊']]","chEntries":["汽車修理廠","汽車庫","集體農莊"],"practiceMeaning":"跳蚤市場將於週六舉行。","analysis":"源自法語 'garage'，意為『車庫』。1. 指存放汽車或修理汽車的地方，即『汽車庫、汽車修理廠』。2. 在蘇聯和東歐，曾指由國家或集體擁有和經營的『農業生產單位』，通常是指集體農莊。","definition":"a building for storing a motor vehicle; a place where cars are repaired","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I need to take my car to the garage for a service.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我需要把車開到修車廠去做保養。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He parks his car in the garage.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他把車停在車庫裡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The garage sale will be held on Saturday.\",\n    \"ch\": \"跳蚤市場將於週六舉行。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"跳蚤市場將於週六舉行。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3220,"wordRef":"字彙王::u41::gear::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He shifted the ____ to a lower one.","expectedAnswer":"gear","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He shifted the ____ to a lower one.","clozeAnswer":"gear","exampleTranslation":"他把檔位換到較低的檔。","reference":{"eng":"gear","kk":"/ɡɪər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['齒輪'], ['傳動裝置'], ['設備'], ['裝備']]","chEntries":["齒輪","傳動裝置","設備","裝備"],"practiceMeaning":"他把檔位換到較低的檔。","analysis":"詞源來自古英語 'gear'，意為『裝備』、『服裝』。早期指軍事裝備，後引申為各種工具、設備，尤其是機械中的『齒輪』和『傳動裝置』。也可指個人或活動所需的『裝備』。","definition":"1. a set of toothed wheels that engage with each other to turn or move a part of a machine; 2. equipment or clothing needed for a particular activity.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The car's gears need to be replaced.\",\n    \"ch\": \"汽車的齒輪需要更換。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We packed all the necessary camping gear.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們打包了所有必要的露營裝備。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He shifted the gear to a lower one.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他把檔位換到較低的檔。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他把檔位換到較低的檔。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U41"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3158,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::generous::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She has a ____ spirit and always tries to help others.","expectedAnswer":"generous","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She has a ____ spirit and always tries to help others.","clozeAnswer":"generous","exampleTranslation":"她有著寬宏的 spirit，總是試圖幫助他人。","reference":{"eng":"generous","kk":"/ˈdʒɛnərəs/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['慷慨的；大方的'], ['（尺寸、數量等）豐富的，寬大的'], ['（思想、氣度等）寬宏的']]","chEntries":["慷慨的","大方的","豐富的，寬大的","寬宏的"],"practiceMeaning":"她有著寬宏的 spirit，總是試圖幫助他人。","analysis":"詞源來自拉丁語 'generosus'，意為「出身高貴的，慷慨的」。'Generous' 形容的是一個人樂於給予、分享，並且不吝嗇。其語意也延伸至描述尺寸、份量或提供的東西非常豐富、充足，或是一種寬宏大量、不計較的態度。","definition":"1. showing a readiness to give more of something, especially money, than is strictly necessary or expected; 2. (of a thing) larger or more plentiful than is usual or necessary; 3. showing kindness and openness of mind.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a generous donor to many charities.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是許多慈善機構的慷慨捐助者。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The restaurant served generous portions of food.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家餐廳提供的份量很豐富。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a generous spirit and always tries to help others.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她有著寬宏的 spirit，總是試圖幫助他人。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她有著寬宏的 spirit，總是試圖幫助他人。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4072,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::gesture::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He raised his hand in a ____ of surrender.","expectedAnswer":"gesture","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He raised his hand in a ____ of surrender.","clozeAnswer":"gesture","exampleTranslation":"他舉起手，表示投降。","reference":{"eng":"gesture","kk":"/ˈdʒɛstʃər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['手勢', '姿態'], ['表示', '姿態（尤指善意的）']]","chEntries":["手勢","姿態","表示"],"practiceMeaning":"他舉起手，表示投降。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'gestus'，是 'gerere' (to carry, to bear, to do) 的過去分詞。核心是「做」、「執行」。因此，'gesture' 指通過身體動作（尤其是手和頭）來表達意思的「手勢」或「姿態」，也指為了表示某種情感或意圖而做的「表示」或「姿態」。","definition":"1. a movement of your hand or body to express an idea or meaning; 2. an action that you take in order to show your feelings or intentions","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他做了一個歡迎的手勢。\",\n    \"eng\": \"He made a welcoming gesture.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"她善意的姿態非常受讚賞。\",\n    \"eng\": \"Her gesture of kindness was much appreciated.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"他舉起手，表示投降。\",\n    \"eng\": \"He raised his hand in a gesture of surrender.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他舉起手，表示投降。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5416,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::glimpse::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We only had a ____ of the magnificent mountain range.","expectedAnswer":"glimpse","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We only had a ____ of the magnificent mountain range.","clozeAnswer":"glimpse","exampleTranslation":"我們僅能窺見壯麗的山脈一角。","reference":{"eng":"glimpse","kk":"ɡlɪmps","tense":"n.","ch":"[['一瞥'], ['瞥見'], ['短暫的觀察']]","chEntries":["一瞥","瞥見","短暫的觀察"],"practiceMeaning":"我們僅能窺見壯麗的山脈一角。","analysis":"此字詞源尚不明確，可能與中古英語 \"glim\" (微弱的光) 或 \"glint\" (閃爍) 有關，或是擬聲詞。其核心語意圍繞著「短暫的」、「模糊的」或「不完整的」視覺體驗。構詞上沒有明顯的字首、字根或字尾可拆解，應視為一個整體詞源的發展。原始語義可能與微弱或快速的光線有關，引申為「短暫的看見」或「看到一小部分」的動作或結果。","definition":"a momentary or brief look; a quick sight; a slight suggestion or indication.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I caught a glimpse of her as she left the room.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她離開房間時我瞥見了她一眼。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The documentary offered a glimpse into the lives of the villagers.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這部紀錄片讓我們得以一窺村民的生活。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We only had a glimpse of the magnificent mountain range.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們僅能窺見壯麗的山脈一角。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們僅能窺見壯麗的山脈一角。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4557,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::global::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need a ____ approach to solve this crisis.","expectedAnswer":"global","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need a ____ approach to solve this crisis.","clozeAnswer":"global","exampleTranslation":"我們需要一個整體的辦法來解決這次危機。","reference":{"eng":"global","kk":"/ˈɡloʊbəl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['全球的', '全世界的'], ['整體的', '全面的']]","chEntries":["全球的","全世界的","整體的","全面的"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要一個整體的辦法來解決這次危機。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'globus'，意為 'ball, sphere' (球體)。核心概念是指像球體一樣涵蓋整個地球。\n    1. 全球的、全世界的：指涉及整個地球或全世界範圍的。\n    2. 整體的、全面的：指涵蓋所有部分或方面，不局限於局部。","definition":"1. relating to or affecting the whole world.; 2. encompassing or covering the whole of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Global warming is a serious environmental issue.\",\n    \"ch\": \"全球暖化是一個嚴重的環境問題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company has a global presence.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司業務遍及全球。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need a global approach to solve this crisis.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要一個整體的辦法來解決這次危機。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要一個整體的辦法來解決這次危機。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5787,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::grip::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The pen has a comfortable ____.","expectedAnswer":"grip","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The pen has a comfortable ____.","clozeAnswer":"grip","exampleTranslation":"這支筆有一個舒適的握把。","reference":{"eng":"grip","kk":"ɡrɪp","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"緊握\"  ],  [    \"抓牢\"  ],  [    \"控制\"  ],  [    \"吸引力\"  ],  [    \"握把\"  ]]","chEntries":["緊握","抓牢","控制","吸引力","握把"],"practiceMeaning":"這支筆有一個舒適的握把。","analysis":"此字為名詞，與動詞同源，源自中古英語gripen。核心語義是指「用力抓住或握緊的動作或狀態」，或「被抓住的物體」。引申為「控制」、「掌握」，以及「對人產生的強烈吸引力或影響力」。此外，也可指工具或武器上的「握把」。語意演變上，從「抓握」的動作，發展出「控制」、「吸引力」等抽象意義，以及「握把」這類具體名詞。","definition":"1. a firm hold or grasp; 2. control or power over someone or something; 3. the ability to attract and hold people's attention or interest; 4. the part of the handle of a tool or weapon that is held in the hand.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He lost his grip on the rope and fell.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他鬆開了繩索的抓握，掉了下去。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The book has a strong grip on the imagination.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本書對想像力有很強的吸引力。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The pen has a comfortable grip.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這支筆有一個舒適的握把。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這支筆有一個舒適的握把。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4510,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::have::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ some tea.","expectedAnswer":"Have","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ some tea.","clozeAnswer":"Have","exampleTranslation":"喝點茶。","reference":{"eng":"have","kk":"/hæv/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['有'], ['持有'], ['經歷（事件、情況）'], ['吃、喝'], ['導致'], ['認為']]","chEntries":["有","持有","經歷","吃、喝","導致","認為"],"practiceMeaning":"喝點茶。","analysis":"源自古英語 habban。是一個極其核心且語意廣泛的動詞。常用作助動詞（如構成現在完成時），也獨立表示「擁有」、「持有」、「經歷」等。語意涵蓋物理擁有、抽象擁有、經歷、飲食、原因等。","definition":"1. To possess, own, or hold; 2. To experience (a feeling, state, or injury); 3. To eat, drink, or take; 4. To cause to happen; 5. To consider or regard.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I have a car.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我有一輛車。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We had a great time at the party.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們在派對上度過了愉快的時光。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Have some tea.\",\n    \"ch\": \"喝點茶。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I think he is mistaken.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我認為他弄錯了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"喝點茶。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6077,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::hockey::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The children were playing ____ in the park.","expectedAnswer":"hockey","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The children were playing ____ in the park.","clozeAnswer":"hockey","exampleTranslation":"孩子們正在公園裡玩曲棍球。","reference":{"eng":"hockey","kk":"ˈhɔki","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"曲棍球\"  ]]","chEntries":["曲棍球"],"practiceMeaning":"孩子們正在公園裡玩曲棍球。","analysis":"此字的詞源不確定，可能源自古法語 hoquet（牧羊杖），或與某種詞頭相關，表示「棍棒」。核心語義是指一種使用棍棒擊球的運動。最常見的是指冰球（ice hockey）或草地曲棍球（field hockey）。","definition":"a game played on ice or a grass field between two teams of players who try to score points by hitting a puck or ball into the opponents' goal with a stick.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He plays ice hockey for the local team.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他為當地隊伍打冰球。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Field hockey is a popular sport in many countries.\",\n    \"ch\": \"曲棍球在許多國家是一種受歡迎的運動。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The children were playing hockey in the park.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子們正在公園裡玩曲棍球。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"孩子們正在公園裡玩曲棍球。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6079,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::hormone::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ levels can fluctuate during different life stages.","expectedAnswer":"Hormone","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ levels can fluctuate during different life stages.","clozeAnswer":"Hormone","exampleTranslation":"荷爾蒙水平在不同生命階段可能會波動。","reference":{"eng":"hormone","kk":"ˈhɔrmon","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"荷爾蒙\"  ],  [    \"激素\"  ]]","chEntries":["荷爾蒙","激素"],"practiceMeaning":"荷爾蒙水平在不同生命階段可能會波動。","analysis":"此字源自希臘語 horman，意為「激動，刺激，使……開始」，由 hormē（衝動，推動）演變而來。Hormone 指的是由生物體內的內分泌腺體分泌，並通過血液輸送到身體其他部位，對身體功能產生調節作用的化學物質。核心語義是「引發生理反應的化學信號」。","definition":"a regulatory substance produced in an organism and transported in the blood or other fluid to distant cells or organs to regulate physiology or behavior.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The doctor explained the role of hormones in the body.\",\n    \"ch\": \"醫生解釋了荷爾蒙在人體中的作用。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Adrenaline is a hormone that is released in response to stress.\",\n    \"ch\": \"腎上腺素是一種壓力荷爾蒙。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Hormone levels can fluctuate during different life stages.\",\n    \"ch\": \"荷爾蒙水平在不同生命階段可能會波動。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"荷爾蒙水平在不同生命階段可能會波動。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4620,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::horror::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He's a fan of ____ novels.","expectedAnswer":"horror","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He's a fan of ____ novels.","clozeAnswer":"horror","exampleTranslation":"他是恐怖小說迷。","reference":{"eng":"horror","kk":"/ˈhɔːrər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['恐怖'], ['驚恐'], ['恐懼'], ['（電影、文學作品）恐怖片']]","chEntries":["恐怖","驚恐","恐懼","恐怖片"],"practiceMeaning":"他是恐怖小說迷。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'horrere' (感到恐懼、戰慄)。核心是強烈的恐懼、厭惡或厭惡感，通常是由於看到或想到可怕、令人不安的事物。其名詞形式 'horror' 指這種感覺本身，也指引起這種感覺的事物，如恐怖電影。","definition":"an intense feeling of fear, shock, or disgust; something that causes such a feeling.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The movie was full of horror and suspense.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這部電影充滿了恐怖和懸疑。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She looked at the scene with horror.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她驚恐地看著眼前的景象。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He's a fan of horror novels.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是恐怖小說迷。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他是恐怖小說迷。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6124,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::icon::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The artist became an ____ of the youth movement.","expectedAnswer":"icon","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The artist became an ____ of the youth movement.","clozeAnswer":"icon","exampleTranslation":"這位藝術家成為青年運動的標誌性人物。","reference":{"eng":"icon","kk":"ˈaɪkɑːn","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"圖像\"  ],  [    \"圖標\"  ],  [    \"偶像\"  ]]","chEntries":["圖像","圖標","偶像"],"practiceMeaning":"這位藝術家成為青年運動的標誌性人物。","analysis":"此字源自希臘語 eikōn，意為「圖像；肖像」。在早期，主要指宗教畫像，特別是東方教會中用於崇拜的聖像。在 modern English 中，icon 指電腦螢幕上的小圖形符號（圖標），或比喻某個領域中被廣泛崇拜或模仿的傑出人物（偶像）。其語意演變是從「圖像」到「宗教聖像」，再到「電腦圖標」和「現代偶像」。","definition":"1. a person or thing regarded as a representative symbol or as worthy of veneration; 2. a small graphic image or symbol on a computer screen that represents a program, command, or file.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is an icon of the fashion industry.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是時尚界的偶像。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Click on the folder icon to open it.\",\n    \"ch\": \"點擊文件夾圖標將其打開。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The artist became an icon of the youth movement.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位藝術家成為青年運動的標誌性人物。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這位藝術家成為青年運動的標誌性人物。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5840,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::immune::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company is ____ from prosecution.","expectedAnswer":"immune","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company is ____ from prosecution.","clozeAnswer":"immune","exampleTranslation":"該公司免於起訴。","reference":{"eng":"immune","kk":"ɪˈmjuːn","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"免疫的\"  ],  [    \"不受影響的\"  ],  [    \"免於……的\"  ],  [    \"豁免的\"  ]]","chEntries":["免疫的","不受影響的","免於……的","豁免的"],"practiceMeaning":"該公司免於起訴。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'immūnis'，由 'in-' (not) 和 'mūnus' (duty, service, gift) 構成。'Immūnis' 的字面意思是「不受……負擔的」或「免除……義務的」。最初用於指免稅或免於公共服務的人。在醫學上，'immune' 指身體對某種疾病或病原體產生抵抗力，不再容易受到感染。這也與「不受……侵害」的核心意義相符。引申義則指「不受……影響」或「免於……」。例如，也可指「免除……責任的」。","definition":"1. Protected against a particular disease.; 2. Not affected or influenced by something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Children are often immune to common colds after exposure.\",\n    \"ch\": \"孩子們在接觸後通常對普通感冒產生免疫。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He seems immune to criticism.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他似乎不受批評的影響。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company is immune from prosecution.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司免於起訴。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Diplomats are often immune from local laws.\",\n    \"ch\": \"外交官員通常豁免於當地法律。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該公司免於起訴。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5789,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::incorporate::vt","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They chose to ____ their business as a limited liability company.","expectedAnswer":"incorporate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They chose to ____ their business as a limited liability company.","clozeAnswer":"incorporate","exampleTranslation":"他們選擇將他們的業務註冊為有限責任公司（使公司法人化）。","reference":{"eng":"incorporate","kk":"ɪnˈkɔrpəreɪt","tense":"vt.","ch":"[  [    \"包含\"  ],  [    \"納入\"  ],  [    \"吸收\"  ],  [    \"使公司法人化\"  ]]","chEntries":["包含","納入","吸收","使公司法人化"],"practiceMeaning":"他們選擇將他們的業務註冊為有限責任公司（使公司法人化）。","analysis":"此字為及物動詞，源自拉丁語incorporare，由in-（進入；在……之中）+corpus（身體；身體，來自原始印歐語\\\\*korpus-）組成。corpus是拉丁語。因此，incorporate的核心語義是「將某物納入一個整體中，使其成為整體的一部分」，如同將東西「化為身體」一樣。語意演變上，從「使成一體」的概念，引申出「包含」、「納入」、「吸收」，以及法律上「使一個組織法人化」的特定用法。","definition":"1. to include something as part of a group, system, or plan; 2. to form a company or organization legally so that it becomes a separate legal entity.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The new design incorporates feedback from customers.\",\n    \"ch\": \"新設計納入了客戶的意見。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company decided to incorporate overseas branches into its main structure.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司決定將海外分支機構納入其主體結構。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They chose to incorporate their business as a limited liability company.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們選擇將他們的業務註冊為有限責任公司（使公司法人化）。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們選擇將他們的業務註冊為有限責任公司（使公司法人化）。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5087,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::index::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The presence of these pollutants is an ____ of water quality degradation.","expectedAnswer":"index","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The presence of these pollutants is an ____ of water quality degradation.","clozeAnswer":"index","exampleTranslation":"這些污染物的存在是水質惡化的指標。","reference":{"eng":"index","kk":"ˈɪndeks","tense":"n.","ch":"[['索引'], ['指數'], ['指示器']]","chEntries":["索引","指數","指示器"],"practiceMeaning":"這些污染物的存在是水質惡化的指標。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'index'，意為 '指示者、標記者'，源於 'indicere' (to proclaim, to announce)。'Index' 最初指 '指示牌' 或 '標記'。在書籍中，它發展成為 '索引'，用於標記和指示內容位置。在經濟學或科學中，'index' 則指 '指數'，用於量化某種趨勢或情況的指標，它指示著變化的方向和幅度。","definition":"1. A list of names, subjects, etc. with references to where they occur, typically found at the end of a book.; 2. A figure or number that indicates the level of something, especially in economics or science.; 3. A sign or indication.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"You can find the topic in the index at the back of the book.\",\n    \"ch\": \"你可以在書後的索引中找到這個主題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The stock market index rose today.\",\n    \"ch\": \"股市指數今天上漲了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The presence of these pollutants is an index of water quality degradation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這些污染物的存在是水質惡化的指標。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這些污染物的存在是水質惡化的指標。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3169,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::indicate::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"High blood pressure may ____ underlying health problems.","expectedAnswer":"indicate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"High blood pressure may ____ underlying health problems.","clozeAnswer":"indicate","exampleTranslation":"高血壓可能表明存在潛在的健康問題。","reference":{"eng":"indicate","kk":"/ˈɪndɪkeɪt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['表明；顯示'], ['指示；指向'], ['（醫學）適宜於']]","chEntries":["表明","顯示","指示","指向","適宜於"],"practiceMeaning":"高血壓可能表明存在潛在的健康問題。","analysis":"詞源來自拉丁語 'indicare'，意為「指出，宣告」，由 'in-'（在...上）+ 'dicare'（宣告，指示）組成。'Indicate' 的核心是「指出」或「顯示」。它可以指用語言或行動表明某事，預示某種情況，或用手指、箭頭等指向某個方向。在醫學上，它用於說明某種治療方法是否適合某種疾病。","definition":"1. point out or show; 2. suggest as a desirable or necessary course of action; 3. (of a fact or event) serve as a sign or symptom of.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The survey results indicate a growing trend.\",\n    \"ch\": \"調查結果顯示出一個增長的趨勢。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He indicated the correct way to his students.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他向他的學生們指出了正確的方法。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"High blood pressure may indicate underlying health problems.\",\n    \"ch\": \"高血壓可能表明存在潛在的健康問題。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"高血壓可能表明存在潛在的健康問題。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3168,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::indication::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Fever is a common ____ of infection.","expectedAnswer":"indication","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Fever is a common ____ of infection.","clozeAnswer":"indication","exampleTranslation":"發燒是感染的常見指徵。","reference":{"eng":"indication","kk":"/ˌɪndɪˈkeɪʃn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['表示；表明'], ['指示；跡象；徵兆'], ['（醫學）適應症；指徵']]","chEntries":["表示","表明","指示","跡象","徵兆","適應症","指徵"],"practiceMeaning":"發燒是感染的常見指徵。","analysis":"名詞，源自動詞 'indicate'。'Indication' 指的是某事物顯示、表明或預示的信號或線索。它可以是視覺上的指示（如路標），身體上的症狀（如疾病的跡象），或數據顯示的趨勢。在醫學上，'indication' 指的是某種治療方法適用的情況。","definition":"1. a sign or piece of information that shows something exists or is likely to happen; 2. a sign of a particular situation or condition; 3. (medicine) a sign that a particular treatment or medicine is appropriate for a particular condition.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The dark clouds are an indication of coming rain.\",\n    \"ch\": \"烏雲預示著即將下雨。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was no indication that he was unhappy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"沒有任何跡象表明他感到不開心。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Fever is a common indication of infection.\",\n    \"ch\": \"發燒是感染的常見指徵。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"發燒是感染的常見指徵。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4042,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::inform::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This book will ____ you about the history of Rome.","expectedAnswer":"inform","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This book will ____ you about the history of Rome.","clozeAnswer":"inform","exampleTranslation":"這本書會讓你了解羅馬的歷史。","reference":{"eng":"inform","kk":"/ɪnˈfɔrm/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['通知', '告知'], ['使...有所了解', '給...情報']]","chEntries":["通知","告知","使...有所了解","給...情報"],"practiceMeaning":"這本書會讓你了解羅馬的歷史。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'informare'，由 'in-' (into) + 'formare' (to form, to shape) 構成，原意是「賦予形狀」、「塑造」，引申為「告知」、「使（人）形成概念」。因此，它的核心意義是「傳達信息」，讓人知道某事。","definition":"1. to tell someone about something; 2. to give someone information","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"請通知我們您住址的任何變更。\",\n    \"eng\": \"Please inform us of any changes in your address.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"警方向家屬告知了事故情況。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The police informed the family of the accident.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"這本書會讓你了解羅馬的歷史。\",\n    \"eng\": \"This book will inform you about the history of Rome.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這本書會讓你了解羅馬的歷史。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4536,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::injury::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ occurred during training.","expectedAnswer":"injury","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ occurred during training.","clozeAnswer":"injury","exampleTranslation":"這次受傷發生在訓練期間。","reference":{"eng":"injury","kk":"/ˈɪndʒəri/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['傷害', '損傷'], ['（名譽、感情等的）損害']]","chEntries":["傷害","損傷","損害"],"practiceMeaning":"這次受傷發生在訓練期間。","analysis":"源自古法語 'injurye'，源於拉丁語 'iniuria'，由 'in-' (not) 和 'ius' (law, right - 法律、權利) 組成。原意為 'wrong, injustice' (錯誤、不公)。引申為對身體造成的傷害（physical injury），以及對名譽、感情、權利等的損害（damage to reputation/feelings/rights）。","definition":"1. physical harm or damage to someone's body.; 2. harm or damage caused to someone's reputation or feelings.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He suffered a serious injury to his knee.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的膝蓋受了重傷。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The scandal caused a severe injury to the company's reputation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這樁醜聞嚴重損害了公司的聲譽。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The injury occurred during training.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這次受傷發生在訓練期間。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這次受傷發生在訓練期間。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4164,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::insignificant::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We shouldn't waste time on ____ details.","expectedAnswer":"insignificant","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We shouldn't waste time on ____ details.","clozeAnswer":"insignificant","exampleTranslation":"我們不應該在無關緊要的細節上浪費時間。","reference":{"eng":"insignificant","kk":"/ˌɪnsɪɡˈnɪfɪkənt/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['微不足道的', '無關緊要的']]","chEntries":["微不足道的","無關緊要的"],"practiceMeaning":"我們不應該在無關緊要的細節上浪費時間。","analysis":"由 in-（否定前綴）+ significant（重要的）組成。核心概念是「不重要的」、「缺乏意義」。","definition":"1. too small or unimportant to be worth consideration; 2. not significant; trivial","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His contribution was insignificant.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的貢獻微不足道。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The difference between the two amounts is insignificant.\",\n    \"ch\": \"兩個數額之間的差異微乎其微。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We shouldn't waste time on insignificant details.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們不應該在無關緊要的細節上浪費時間。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們不應該在無關緊要的細節上浪費時間。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3173,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::insult::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The public reaction was seen as an ____ to the nation's heroes.","expectedAnswer":"insult","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The public reaction was seen as an ____ to the nation's heroes.","clozeAnswer":"insult","exampleTranslation":"公眾的反應被視為對國家英雄的侮辱。","reference":{"eng":"insult","kk":"/ˈɪnsʌlt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['侮辱；辱罵；冒犯']]","chEntries":["侮辱","辱罵","冒犯"],"practiceMeaning":"公眾的反應被視為對國家英雄的侮辱。","analysis":"名詞用法，源自動詞 'insult'。指「侮辱」、「辱罵」或「冒犯」的行為或言論，通常是故意用來貶低、傷害或激怒他人。它是一種對他人尊嚴或感情的攻擊。","definition":"1. a disrespectful or scornfully abusive remark or action; 2. an act or statement that shows disrespect or offends.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His comments were a direct insult to her intelligence.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的評論是對她智慧的直接侮辱。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She refused to tolerate such an insult.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她拒絕容忍這樣的侮辱。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The public reaction was seen as an insult to the nation's heroes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公眾的反應被視為對國家英雄的侮辱。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"公眾的反應被視為對國家英雄的侮辱。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3174,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::intuition::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His ____ about the market proved to be correct.","expectedAnswer":"intuition","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His ____ about the market proved to be correct.","clozeAnswer":"intuition","exampleTranslation":"他對市場的直覺被證明是正確的。","reference":{"eng":"intuition","kk":"/ˌɪntuˈɪʃn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['直覺；直覺力']]","chEntries":["直覺","直覺力"],"practiceMeaning":"他對市場的直覺被證明是正確的。","analysis":"詞源來自拉丁語 'intueri'，意為「看，觀察」。'Intuition' 指的是一種直接的、非理性或非邏輯的理解或知識，無需經過明顯的推理過程就能獲得。它是一種內在的感知或「預感」，通常基於潛意識的經驗或感受。","definition":"the ability to understand something immediately, without the need for conscious reasoning.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She had a strong intuition that something was wrong.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她強烈的直覺告訴她，有什麼事情不對勁。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Trust your intuition when making important decisions.\",\n    \"ch\": \"做重要決定時，相信你的直覺。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His intuition about the market proved to be correct.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對市場的直覺被證明是正確的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他對市場的直覺被證明是正確的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3175,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::isolate::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Scientists ____ the active compound from the plant.","expectedAnswer":"isolate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Scientists ____ the active compound from the plant.","clozeAnswer":"isolate","exampleTranslation":"科學家們從植物中分離出活性化合物。","reference":{"eng":"isolate","kk":"/ˈaɪsəleɪt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['孤立；使隔離'], ['（使）隔離，（使）隔絕']]","chEntries":["孤立","使隔離","隔離，隔絕"],"practiceMeaning":"科學家們從植物中分離出活性化合物。","analysis":"詞源來自意大利語 'isola'，意為「島嶼」。'Isolate' 的核心是「使分離」、「使獨處」。它可以指將人或物體從其他群體中分開，使其單獨存在。在醫學上，常用於指隔離病人以防止疾病傳播。也可指將某事物從其周圍環境中分離出來進行研究或分析。","definition":"1. cause (a person or place) to be or remain alone or apart from others; 2. set apart, disconnect, or remove from all others.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government decided to isolate the affected region to prevent the spread of the virus.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府決定隔離受影響地區以防止病毒傳播。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He felt isolated after moving to a new city.\",\n    \"ch\": \"搬到新城市後，他感到孤獨。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Scientists isolate the active compound from the plant.\",\n    \"ch\": \"科學家們從植物中分離出活性化合物。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"科學家們從植物中分離出活性化合物。","sourceName":"字彙王、龍騰課本","unitName":"U40、L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3176,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::isolation::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Quarantine is a form of medical ____.","expectedAnswer":"isolation","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Quarantine is a form of medical ____.","clozeAnswer":"isolation","exampleTranslation":"隔離檢疫是一種醫療隔離形式。","reference":{"eng":"isolation","kk":"/ˌaɪsəˈleɪʃn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['孤立；隔離'], ['（與社會的）隔絕']]","chEntries":["孤立","隔離","隔絕"],"practiceMeaning":"隔離檢疫是一種醫療隔離形式。","analysis":"名詞，源自動詞 'isolate'。指「孤立」、「隔離」或「隔絕」的狀態或過程。它可以指物理上的分離，如將某人或某物與外界隔離開。也可以指心理或社會上的孤立，即與他人缺乏聯繫，感到孤獨。在醫學上，指隔離傳染病患者的措施。","definition":"1. the process or fact of isolating or being isolated; 2. a state of being alone or removed from others.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The fear of isolation prevented her from speaking out.\",\n    \"ch\": \"對孤立的恐懼阻止了她發聲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The isolation of the island made it difficult to access.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個島嶼的地理隔離使得它難以抵達。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Quarantine is a form of medical isolation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"隔離檢疫是一種醫療隔離形式。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"隔離檢疫是一種醫療隔離形式。","sourceName":"字彙王、龍騰課本","unitName":"U40、L5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3313,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::just::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It's ____ the beginning.","expectedAnswer":"just","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It's ____ the beginning.","clozeAnswer":"just","exampleTranslation":"這僅僅是個開始。","reference":{"eng":"just","kk":"/dʒʌst/","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['僅僅；只是'], ['剛才；剛']]","chEntries":["僅僅","只是","剛才","剛"],"practiceMeaning":"這僅僅是個開始。","analysis":"詞源同上，但發展出作為副詞的用法。表示範圍的限定（僅僅）或時間的臨近（剛才）。","definition":"1. only; simply; 2. a very short time ago.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I was just kidding.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我只是在開玩笑。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has just arrived.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他剛才抵達。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's just the beginning.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這僅僅是個開始。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這僅僅是個開始。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4608,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::knight::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Move the ____ two squares forward and one to the side.","expectedAnswer":"knight","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Move the ____ two squares forward and one to the side.","clozeAnswer":"knight","exampleTranslation":"將馬走兩個格子往前，再往旁邊一個。","reference":{"eng":"knight","kk":"/naɪt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['騎士'], ['（棋子）馬']]","chEntries":["騎士","馬"],"practiceMeaning":"將馬走兩個格子往前，再往旁邊一個。","analysis":"源自古英語 'cniht'，意為「男孩、僕人」，後來演變為「戰士」。其詞源與印歐語系 'kno-' (削、磨) 或 'gne-' (認識) 有關，可能指受過訓練或有知識的人。中世紀的騎士是具有特定社會地位和軍事職責的戰士。在西洋棋中，馬的走法獨特，狀似彎曲，因此也稱 'knight'。","definition":"1. a man who has been given a rank of honor by a king or queen; a medieval warrior who served a lord. 2. a piece in chess.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The knight rode his horse into battle.\",\n    \"ch\": \"騎士騎馬進入戰鬥。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was knighted for his bravery.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他因英勇而被封為爵士。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Move the knight two squares forward and one to the side.\",\n    \"ch\": \"將馬走兩個格子往前，再往旁邊一個。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"將馬走兩個格子往前，再往旁邊一個。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3891,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::lately::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The weather has been strange ____.","expectedAnswer":"lately","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The weather has been strange ____.","clozeAnswer":"lately","exampleTranslation":"最近天氣很奇怪。","reference":{"eng":"lately","kk":"/ˈleɪtli/","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['最近', '近來']]","chEntries":["最近","近來"],"practiceMeaning":"最近天氣很奇怪。","analysis":"由 'late' (晚的) 加上副詞後綴 '-ly' 構成。核心是「晚近的」。指在不久的過去，相對於現在的時間點而言。","definition":"recently; in the recent past.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I haven't seen him lately.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我最近沒見到他。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"What have you been doing lately?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你最近在忙什麼？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The weather has been strange lately.\",\n    \"ch\": \"最近天氣很奇怪。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"最近天氣很奇怪。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5843,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::legitimate::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The court ruled the contract ____.","expectedAnswer":"legitimate","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The court ruled the contract ____.","clozeAnswer":"legitimate","exampleTranslation":"法院裁定該合同合法有效。","reference":{"eng":"legitimate","kk":"lɪˈdʒɪtəmət","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"合法的\"  ],  [    \"正當的\"  ],  [    \"合理的\"  ],  [    \"合乎規定的\"  ]]","chEntries":["合法的","正當的","合理的","合乎規定的"],"practiceMeaning":"法院裁定該合同合法有效。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'legitimus'，意為「合法的」、「合乎法律的」，由 'lex' (law) 構成。'-ate' 是常見的形容詞或動詞字尾。'Legitimus' 的核心語意是「符合法律」或「基於法律」。在現代英語中，'legitimate' 指符合法律規定、規則、原則或道德標準。它可以指法律上的「合法性」，也可以指行為、要求或理由的「正當性」或「合理性」。例如，也可指「非婚生子女以外的」，即「婚生子女」。","definition":"1. Complying with the law.; 2. Able to be defended with logic or reason.; 3. Genuine, or one regarded as such.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a legitimate business operation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個合法的商業運營。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her concerns are perfectly legitimate.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的擔憂完全是合理的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The court ruled the contract legitimate.\",\n    \"ch\": \"法院裁定該合同合法有效。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The couple hoped for a legitimate heir to the throne.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這對夫婦希望有一位合法的王位繼承人。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"法院裁定該合同合法有效。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5790,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::likelihood::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ of success is quite low.","expectedAnswer":"likelihood","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ of success is quite low.","clozeAnswer":"likelihood","exampleTranslation":"成功的可能性相當低。","reference":{"eng":"likelihood","kk":"ˈlaɪkliˌhʊd","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"可能性\"  ],  [    \"概率\"  ]]","chEntries":["可能性","概率"],"practiceMeaning":"成功的可能性相當低。","analysis":"此字為名詞，構詞自likely（可能的；很可能的）+ -hood（名詞字尾，表示「狀態；性質」）。likely本身是形容詞，源自古英語līclīc，由līc（相似的；同樣的）+ -lic（形容詞字尾）組成，līc的原始印歐語詞根是\\\\*līk-（形狀）。-hood字尾源自古英語-hād，與原始日耳曼語\\\\*haiduz（樣式；形式）有關。因此，likelihood的核心語義是指「某事物發生的可能性或概率」。語意演變上，由形容詞「可能的」轉化為表示「可能性」的抽象名詞。","definition":"1. the probability or chance that something will happen or be the case.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There is a high likelihood of rain this afternoon.\",\n    \"ch\": \"今天下午很有可能下雨。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"What is the likelihood that the project will be completed on time?\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個項目按時完成的可能性有多大？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The likelihood of success is quite low.\",\n    \"ch\": \"成功的可能性相當低。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"成功的可能性相當低。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3300,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::magnificent::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It was a ____ performance by the orchestra.","expectedAnswer":"magnificent","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It was a ____ performance by the orchestra.","clozeAnswer":"magnificent","exampleTranslation":"這是管弦樂團一次傑出的演出。","reference":{"eng":"magnificent","kk":"/mæɡˈnɪfɪsənt/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['宏偉的；壯麗的'], ['華麗的；令人印象深刻的'], ['極好的；傑出的']]","chEntries":["宏偉的","壯麗的","華麗的","令人印象深刻的","極好的","傑出的"],"practiceMeaning":"這是管弦樂團一次傑出的演出。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'magnificens'，由 'magnus' (偉大的) + 'facere' (製作) 組成。形容事物非常壯觀、宏偉、富麗堂皇，令人肅然起敬，也可用於讚美品質或表現的傑出。","definition":"1. extremely beautiful, elaborate, or impressive; 2. very good or excellent.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The view from the mountaintop was magnificent.\",\n    \"ch\": \"山頂的景色非常壯麗。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The palace was magnificent, with gold and jewels everywhere.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座宮殿金碧輝煌，到處都是金銀珠寶。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was a magnificent performance by the orchestra.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是管弦樂團一次傑出的演出。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是管弦樂團一次傑出的演出。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3897,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::majority::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The decision was made by the ____.","expectedAnswer":"majority","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The decision was made by the ____.","clozeAnswer":"majority","exampleTranslation":"這個決定是由多數人做出的。","reference":{"eng":"majority","kk":"/məˈdʒɑːrəti/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['大多數', '大部分'], ['（選舉）得票最多者']]","chEntries":["大多數","大部分","得票最多者"],"practiceMeaning":"這個決定是由多數人做出的。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'maior' (greater) 的比較級，後演變為名詞 'maioritas'。核心是「更大」、「較多」。指總數中的絕大部分，或在投票中獲得最多票數的一方。","definition":"1. the greater number or part; a number or proportion larger than half the total. 2. the party or side in an election or vote that polls the largest number of votes.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The majority of students passed the exam.\",\n    \"ch\": \"大多數學生通過了考試。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He won the election by a large majority.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他以絕對多數贏得了選舉。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The decision was made by the majority.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個決定是由多數人做出的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個決定是由多數人做出的。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U1、L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3302,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::makeup::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Her natural ____ looked very elegant.","expectedAnswer":"makeup","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Her natural ____ looked very elegant.","clozeAnswer":"makeup","exampleTranslation":"她的自然妝容看起來非常優雅。","reference":{"eng":"makeup","kk":"/ˈmeɪkʌp/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['化妝品'], ['化妝；妝容'], ['組成；構成'], ['（事物的）性質；總體情況'], ['（尤指戲劇、電影中的）化妝，道具']]","chEntries":["化妝品","化妝","妝容","組成","構成","性質","總體情況","化妝，道具"],"practiceMeaning":"她的自然妝容看起來非常優雅。","analysis":"由 'make' (做) + 'up' (組成) 組成。名詞形式有多種意義：指用於修飾容貌的化妝品；化妝這個動作或結果；事物的組成或性質；以及戲劇中的特殊化妝。這些意義都源於「組成」、「構成」的核心概念。","definition":"1. substances such as lipstick, powder, and mascara that are used to make a person's face look more attractive; 2. the act or process of applying cosmetics; 3. the way in which something is put together or arranged; 4. the nature or character of something; 5. the art of applying cosmetics to an actor's face or body.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She buys a lot of makeup.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她買了很多化妝品。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The makeup of the committee was diverse.\",\n    \"ch\": \"委員會的組成很多元化。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her natural makeup looked very elegant.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的自然妝容看起來非常優雅。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The makeup artist worked quickly before the performance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"化妝師在表演前快速地工作。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她的自然妝容看起來非常優雅。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4503,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::man::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She is looking for a good ____ to marry.","expectedAnswer":"man","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She is looking for a good ____ to marry.","clozeAnswer":"man","exampleTranslation":"她在尋找一個好男人結婚。","reference":{"eng":"man","kk":"/mæn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['男人'], ['人類'], ['丈夫'], ['（軍隊或船上的）人員']]","chEntries":["男人","人類","丈夫","人員"],"practiceMeaning":"她在尋找一個好男人結婚。","analysis":"源自古英語 mann，意為「人」、「男性」。核心語意是「成年男性」。廣泛引申為「人」、「人類」整體，以及「丈夫」、「有能力的人」等。","definition":"1. An adult human male; 2. A human being; a person; 3. A husband.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a man of great integrity.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一個品格高尚的人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"All men are created equal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"人人生而平等。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is looking for a good man to marry.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在尋找一個好男人結婚。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她在尋找一個好男人結婚。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6080,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::massage::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"A regular ____ can improve circulation.","expectedAnswer":"massage","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"A regular ____ can improve circulation.","clozeAnswer":"massage","exampleTranslation":"定期的按摩可以改善血液循環。","reference":{"eng":"massage","kk":"məˈsɑʒ","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"按摩\"  ],  [    \"撫摩\"  ]]","chEntries":["按摩","撫摩"],"practiceMeaning":"定期的按摩可以改善血液循環。","analysis":"此字源自法語 massage，本身來自 provencal masa（to knead），追溯至希臘語 massein（to knead）。核心語義是「揉捏」或「按壓」。作為名詞，指一種通過手技（揉、捏、拍打等）來放鬆肌肉、緩解疼痛或促進血液循環的治療或放鬆方法。","definition":"an act of rubbing and kneading the body with the hands, especially to relieve tension or pain.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She found a deep tissue massage very relaxing.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她覺得深層組織按摩非常放鬆。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The sports massage helped relieve his muscle soreness.\",\n    \"ch\": \"運動按摩幫助緩解了他的肌肉痠痛。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A regular massage can improve circulation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"定期的按摩可以改善血液循環。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"定期的按摩可以改善血液循環。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6082,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::meantime::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We are waiting for the results. ____, let's review the previous findings.","expectedAnswer":"Meantime","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We are waiting for the results. ____, let's review the previous findings.","clozeAnswer":"Meantime","exampleTranslation":"我們在等待結果。同時，讓我們複習一下之前的發現。","reference":{"eng":"meantime","kk":"ˈmintˌaɪm","tense":"adv.","ch":"[  [    \"其間\"  ],  [    \"同時\"  ]]","chEntries":["其間","同時"],"practiceMeaning":"我們在等待結果。同時，讓我們複習一下之前的發現。","analysis":"此字為複合詞，由 mean（中間的）和 time（時間）組成。核心語義是「在中間的時間裡」或「在兩件事之間的時間裡」。它用來連接兩個事件或時間段，指在第一個事件發生時或之後，到第二個事件發生前的那段時間。","definition":"during the time between two specified times or events.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The train will be here in ten minutes; in the meantime, you can sit down.\",\n    \"ch\": \"火車十分鐘後就到；在此期間，你可以坐下。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She's studying abroad for a year. In the meantime, her family is taking care of her apartment.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她將在國外學習一年。與此同時，她的家人會幫忙照看她的公寓。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We are waiting for the results. Meantime, let's review the previous findings.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們在等待結果。同時，讓我們複習一下之前的發現。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們在等待結果。同時，讓我們複習一下之前的發現。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5663,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l8::measure::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The music was in 4/4 ____.","expectedAnswer":"measure","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The music was in 4/4 ____.","clozeAnswer":"measure","exampleTranslation":"這音樂是 4/4 拍的。","reference":{"eng":"measure","kk":"ˈmɛʒər","tense":"n.","ch":"[['測量'], ['衡量'], ['尺度'], ['（法律、規定等）措施'], ['節奏（音樂）']]","chEntries":["測量","衡量","尺度","措施","節奏"],"practiceMeaning":"這音樂是 4/4 拍的。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 mesure，來自古法語 mesure，再追溯至拉丁語 mensura（測量），來自 mensus（測量），是 mētiri（測量，to measure）的過去分詞。mētiri 來自原始印歐語 *meh₁-（測量）。核心語義為「測量」的結果或行為。構詞上，mētiri 提供「測量」的核心動作，-ure 是常見的名詞字尾，表示「動作」、「手段」或「結果」。此處為名詞用法，指代「測量」、「尺度」、「措施」或「節奏」。","definition":"a system or standard of measurement; the size, amount, or degree of something; an action taken to achieve a particular purpose; a regular beat or rhythm.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"What is the measure of this room?\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個房間的尺寸是多少？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to take drastic measures.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要採取嚴厲的措施。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The music was in 4/4 measure.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這音樂是 4/4 拍的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這音樂是 4/4 拍的。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6083,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::mechanism::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This is a simple ____ to open the bottle.","expectedAnswer":"mechanism","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This is a simple ____ to open the bottle.","clozeAnswer":"mechanism","exampleTranslation":"這是一個開啟瓶子的簡單裝置。","reference":{"eng":"mechanism","kk":"ˈmɛkəˌnɪzəm","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"機制\"  ],  [    \"機械裝置\"  ],  [    \"構造\"  ],  [    \"原理\"  ]]","chEntries":["機制","機械裝置","構造","原理"],"practiceMeaning":"這是一個開啟瓶子的簡單裝置。","analysis":"此字源自希臘語 mēkhanḗ（machine, device, means），來自 mēkhanos（inventive, clever）。核心語義是「機器」或「裝置」。引申為「機制」，指某事物運作的方式、過程或內部結構，尤其是指一套相互關聯的組成部分如何協同工作以達成某種結果。","definition":"1. a system of parts working together in a machine; 2. a natural or physical process considered in terms of the way in which it operates; 3. a way of achieving something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The mechanism of the clock needs to be repaired.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這台鐘表的機械裝置需要修理。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to understand the mechanism of disease transmission.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要了解疾病傳播的機制。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a simple mechanism to open the bottle.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個開啟瓶子的簡單裝置。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是一個開啟瓶子的簡單裝置。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6126,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::mentor::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He served as a ____ to many aspiring writers.","expectedAnswer":"mentor","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He served as a ____ to many aspiring writers.","clozeAnswer":"mentor","exampleTranslation":"他曾是許多有抱負的作家的人生導師。","reference":{"eng":"mentor","kk":"ˈmɛntɔːr","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"導師\"  ],  [    \"顧問\"  ],  [    \"良師益友\"  ]]","chEntries":["導師","顧問","良師益友"],"practiceMeaning":"他曾是許多有抱負的作家的人生導師。","analysis":"此字源自古希臘神話人物 Mentor，他是奧德修斯的朋友，負責教導和保護奧德修斯的兒子 Telemachus。在 modern English 中，mentor 指經驗豐富、提供建議和指導的顧問或導師。此名詞的語意直接來自於歷史人物名稱。因此，它是一個專有名詞演變而來的普通名詞。","definition":"An experienced and trusted advisor.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She found a great mentor in her professor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在教授身上找到了一位很棒的導師。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The program pairs young entrepreneurs with experienced mentors.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該計畫為年輕企業家配備了經驗豐富的導師。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He served as a mentor to many aspiring writers.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他曾是許多有抱負的作家的人生導師。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他曾是許多有抱負的作家的人生導師。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5554,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::merely::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She is not ____ a singer, but also a talented actress.","expectedAnswer":"merely","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She is not ____ a singer, but also a talented actress.","clozeAnswer":"merely","exampleTranslation":"她不只是個歌手，更是一位才華洋溢的演員。","reference":{"eng":"merely","kk":"ˈmɪrli","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['僅僅'], ['只是'], ['不過是']]","chEntries":["僅僅","只是","不過是"],"practiceMeaning":"她不只是個歌手，更是一位才華洋溢的演員。","analysis":"此字是 \"mere\"（僅僅的）加上副詞字尾 \"-ly\" 構成。\"mere\" 源自古英語 \"mǣre\"，意為 \"boundary, limit, distinguished\"（界線，極限，傑出的），後來語義演變為 \"nothing more than, only\"（僅僅是，不過是），可能與「極小」或「單一」的概念有關。因此，\"merely\" 作為副詞，強調「僅僅」、「只是」的意思，表示所敘述的事物或情況是有限的、微不足道的，或者沒有其他更重要的內容。","definition":"1. Just only; solely; 2. In the smallest degree; only.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was merely trying to help.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他只是想幫忙。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was merely a suggestion, not an order.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這只是一個建議，並非命令。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is not merely a singer, but also a talented actress.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她不只是個歌手，更是一位才華洋溢的演員。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她不只是個歌手，更是一位才華洋溢的演員。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6127,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::merge::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The firm will ____ with its competitor.","expectedAnswer":"merge","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The firm will ____ with its competitor.","clozeAnswer":"merge","exampleTranslation":"這家公司將與其競爭對手合併。","reference":{"eng":"merge","kk":"mɜːrdʒ","tense":"v.","ch":"[  [    \"合併\"  ],  [    \"融合\"  ],  [    \"併入\"  ]]","chEntries":["合併","融合","併入"],"practiceMeaning":"這家公司將與其競爭對手合併。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 mergere，意為「淹沒；沉浸」。構詞上，mergere 的核心語義是「浸入」或「沉入」。此動詞表示兩個或更多個事物結合、合併，形成一個單一的整體。常用於商業、法律或抽象概念。此處使用 v. 詞性，表示及物與不及物皆可。當作及物動詞時，表示「合併」，例如 merge two companies。當作不及物動詞時，表示「合併」，例如 the two companies merge。其語意演變是從「沉浸、淹沒」到「結合、融合」。","definition":"1. to combine or cause to combine to form a single entity; 2. to become absorbed or integrated into something else.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The two companies decided to merge.\",\n    \"ch\": \"兩家公司決定合併。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The small stream merges into the river.\",\n    \"ch\": \"小溪匯入河流。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The firm will merge with its competitor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司將與其競爭對手合併。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這家公司將與其競爭對手合併。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6178,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::milestone::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The signpost marked a ____ of five miles.","expectedAnswer":"milestone","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The signpost marked a ____ of five miles.","clozeAnswer":"milestone","exampleTranslation":"路標標示著五英里的里程碑。","reference":{"eng":"milestone","kk":"ˈmaɪlstəʊn","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"里程碑\"  ],  [    \"轉捩點\"  ],  [    \"重要事件\"  ]]","chEntries":["里程碑","轉捩點","重要事件"],"practiceMeaning":"路標標示著五英里的里程碑。","analysis":"此字由 mile（英里）和 stone（石頭）兩個名詞組成。在古代，里程碑是用來標示道路距離的石頭。此字在現代英語中可視為複合詞，其語義由兩部分組成。作為名詞，其核心語義是「一個重要的事件或階段，標誌著進步或發展」。詞源中的「標示距離的石頭」引申為「標誌重要進展的事件」。","definition":"1. a significant stage or event in the development of something; 2. a stone or post set up beside a road or path to mark the distance to a place.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company celebrated a major milestone in its history.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司慶祝了其歷史上的重要里程碑。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Graduating from college was a significant milestone for her.\",\n    \"ch\": \"大學畢業對她來說是一個重要的轉捩點。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The signpost marked a milestone of five miles.\",\n    \"ch\": \"路標標示著五英里的里程碑。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The birth of their first child was a milestone for the couple.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們第一個孩子的出生對這對夫婦來說是一個重要的里程碑。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"路標標示著五英里的里程碑。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6233,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::mint::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He made a ____ selling software.","expectedAnswer":"mint","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He made a ____ selling software.","clozeAnswer":"mint","exampleTranslation":"他透過銷售軟體賺了一大筆錢。","reference":{"eng":"mint","kk":"mɪnt","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"薄荷\"  ],  [    \"造幣廠\"  ],  [    \"巨額財富\"  ]]","chEntries":["薄荷","造幣廠","巨額財富"],"practiceMeaning":"他透過銷售軟體賺了一大筆錢。","analysis":"此字有多個詞源。作「薄荷」時，源自拉丁語 mentha。作「造幣廠」時，源自拉丁語 moneta（女神名，後指錢幣，鑄幣廠），與 mint（薄荷）的詞源不同，但中古英語時期兩者拼寫合併。作「巨額財富」時，為俚語，來自造幣廠能製造大量金錢的概念。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。名詞義包含植物、製造貨幣的場所，以及引申的「巨額財富」。中文翻譯為「薄荷；造幣廠；巨額財富」。","definition":"1. a type of plant with fragrant leaves that are used to flavor food and in herbal remedies; 2. a place where money is officially made; 3. a very large amount of money (informal).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She put some fresh mint in her tea.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她把一些新鮮薄荷放進茶裡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The new coins were minted at the royal mint.\",\n    \"ch\": \"新硬幣是在皇家造幣廠鑄造的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He made a mint selling software.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他透過銷售軟體賺了一大筆錢。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他透過銷售軟體賺了一大筆錢。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3878,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::mostly::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The weather was ____ sunny.","expectedAnswer":"mostly","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The weather was ____ sunny.","clozeAnswer":"mostly","exampleTranslation":"天氣大部分是晴朗的。","reference":{"eng":"mostly","kk":"/ˈmoʊstli/","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['大部分', '主要'], ['差不多']]","chEntries":["大部分","主要","差不多"],"practiceMeaning":"天氣大部分是晴朗的。","analysis":"由 'most' (最多) 和 '-ly' (副詞後綴) 組成。核心是「最大程度地」或「佔大部分」。表示在絕大多數情況下、主要地、或涵蓋了絕大部分。","definition":"1. for the most part; mainly; chiefly. 2. in most cases.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The audience was mostly women.\",\n    \"ch\": \"觀眾大部分是女性。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He eats mostly vegetables.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他主要吃蔬菜。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The weather was mostly sunny.\",\n    \"ch\": \"天氣大部分是晴朗的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"天氣大部分是晴朗的。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5466,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::multiple::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He suffered ____ injuries in the accident.","expectedAnswer":"multiple","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He suffered ____ injuries in the accident.","clozeAnswer":"multiple","exampleTranslation":"他在事故中受了多處傷。","reference":{"eng":"multiple","kk":"ˈmʌltəpəl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['多個的'], ['多種的'], ['重複的']]","chEntries":["多個的","多種的","重複的"],"practiceMeaning":"他在事故中受了多處傷。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'multiplus'，由 'multus'（許多）和 '-plus'（-倍的）組成。'-plus' 在此類似於「加」或「倍」。'Multus' 意為「多的、許多的」。因此，'multiple' 的核心語意是「由許多部分組成、包含許多事物、或有多個」。它可以用來形容數量、種類或元素的眾多。與 'many' 相比，'multiple' 更強調「由多個獨立部分構成」或「多重性」的概念。","definition":"1. Consisting of, including, or involving more than one individual, element, or part.; 2. Many; numerous.; 3. (Of a number) divisible by another number without a remainder.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The project requires multiple skills.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個專案需要多種技能。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has multiple reasons for her decision.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對她的決定有多重理由。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He suffered multiple injuries in the accident.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在事故中受了多處傷。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他在事故中受了多處傷。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4560,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::multiply::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The problems seem to ____ each day.","expectedAnswer":"multiply","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The problems seem to ____ each day.","clozeAnswer":"multiply","exampleTranslation":"問題似乎一天天增多。","reference":{"eng":"multiply","kk":"/ˈmʌltɪplaɪ/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['乘以', '（數學上）乘'], ['繁殖', '增殖'], ['增加', '增多']]","chEntries":["乘以","乘","繁殖","增殖","增加","增多"],"practiceMeaning":"問題似乎一天天增多。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'multiplicare'，'multus' (many - 許多) 的派生詞。\n    1. 乘以：數學運算，將一個數與另一個數相乘。\n    2. 繁殖、增殖：生物體產生後代，數量增加。\n    3. 增加、增多：泛指數量、規模等的大幅增加。","definition":"1. (of a living organism) reproduce; generate offspring.; 2. increase or cause to increase greatly in number or quantity.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Two multiplied by three equals six.\",\n    \"ch\": \"二乘以三等於六。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Bacteria can multiply rapidly under favorable conditions.\",\n    \"ch\": \"細菌在有利條件下可以迅速繁殖。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The problems seem to multiply each day.\",\n    \"ch\": \"問題似乎一天天增多。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"問題似乎一天天增多。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitNa