/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['上漲', '增加'], ['（太陽、月亮等）升起'], ['起義', '反抗']]","chEntries":["上漲","增加","升起","起義","反抗"],"practiceMeaning":"工人的崛起帶來了重大的變革。","analysis":"源自古英語 rīsan（起來，升起）。核心概念是「向上移動」或「增加」。引申為價格、水平的提高，或反抗的行動。","definition":"1. an increase in amount, level, or strength; 2. the act of getting up; 3. an upward movement","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There has been a steep rise in living costs.\",\n    \"ch\": \"生活成本急劇上漲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We witnessed the rise of the sun.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們目睹了太陽的升起。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The rise of the workers led to significant changes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"工人的崛起帶來了重大的變革。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"工人的崛起帶來了重大的變革。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4172,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::role::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He has the lead ____ in the play.","expectedAnswer":"role","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He has the lead ____ in the play.","clozeAnswer":"role","exampleTranslation":"他在戲劇中擔任主角。","reference":{"eng":"role","kk":"/roʊl/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['角色'], ['作用', '職責']]","chEntries":["角色","作用","職責"],"practiceMeaning":"他在戲劇中擔任主角。","analysis":"源自古法語 rolle（捲軸，列表，記錄），後引申為戲劇中的演員角色，再擴展到任何職責或功能。","definition":"1. the function assumed or part played by a person or thing in a particular situation or activity; 2. a part played by an actor or actress","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She plays a significant role in the company.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在公司中扮演著重要的角色。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The internet plays a vital role in our lives.\",\n    \"ch\": \"網際網路在我們的生活中扮演著至關重要的作用。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has the lead role in the play.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在戲劇中擔任主角。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他在戲劇中擔任主角。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4145,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::salary::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He negotiated a higher ____.","expectedAnswer":"salary","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He negotiated a higher ____.","clozeAnswer":"salary","exampleTranslation":"他談判爭取到了更高的薪水。","reference":{"eng":"salary","kk":"/ˈsæləri/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['薪水', '薪金']]","chEntries":["薪水","薪金"],"practiceMeaning":"他談判爭取到了更高的薪水。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 salarium（羅馬士兵領取的食鹽津貼），後引申為「報酬」。核心概念是「為工作定期支付的固定金錢」。","definition":"a fixed regular payment, typically paid on a monthly or biweekly basis but often expressed as an annual sum, made by an employer to an employee","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her annual salary is $50,000.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的年薪是五萬美元。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company offers a competitive salary.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司提供有競爭力的薪資。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He negotiated a higher salary.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他談判爭取到了更高的薪水。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他談判爭取到了更高的薪水。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U5、L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5487,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::sample::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This is just a ____ of his work.","expectedAnswer":"sample","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This is just a ____ of his work.","clozeAnswer":"sample","exampleTranslation":"這只是他作品的一個範例。","reference":{"eng":"sample","kk":"ˈsæmpəl","tense":"n.","ch":"[['樣本'], ['樣品'], ['範例']]","chEntries":["樣本","樣品","範例"],"practiceMeaning":"這只是他作品的一個範例。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 'essample'，意為「範例、例子」，來自拉丁語 'exemplum'（例子、範本）。'Exemplum' 是由 'ex-'（出）和 'templum'（樣板、模型）構成。在中古英語中，'sample' 是一個非標準形式，後來演變成現代的 'sample'。'Sample' 作名詞，指「為了代表整體而取出的部分」，用於檢驗、展示或研究。核心語意是「代表整體的一部分」。","definition":"1. A small part or quantity intended to show what the whole is like.; 2. A specimen or example.; 3. A representative part or a single item from a larger whole.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Would you like to try a sample of our new cheese?\",\n    \"ch\": \"您想嚐嚐我們的起司樣本嗎？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The scientist took a blood sample for analysis.\",\n    \"ch\": \"科學家抽取了血液樣本進行分析。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is just a sample of his work.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這只是他作品的一個範例。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這只是他作品的一個範例。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5579,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::scheme::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He was involved in a criminal ____.","expectedAnswer":"scheme","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He was involved in a criminal ____.","clozeAnswer":"scheme","exampleTranslation":"他捲入了一個犯罪陰謀。","reference":{"eng":"scheme","kk":"skim","tense":"n.","ch":"[['計畫'], ['方案'], ['陰謀'], ['體系']]","chEntries":["計畫","方案","陰謀","體系"],"practiceMeaning":"他捲入了一個犯罪陰謀。","analysis":"此字源自古希臘語 \"schēma\"（shape, form, appearance, plan，形狀，形式，外觀，計畫），該詞源於 \"echō\"（to have, to hold，擁有，持有）。\"schēma\" 的核心語義是「事物的形式或架構」。在中古英語中，\"scheme\"（原為 \"sceme\"）借用於古法語 \"esqueme\"，繼承了希臘語的「形式、架構」概念。它的語義發展廣泛：指「一個有組織的、事先計畫好的行動藍圖」（a plan or program of action）；指「一個系統或結構」（a system or framework）；也可能帶有負面含義，指「一個秘密的、不誠實的計畫」（a secret plot or conspiracy）。","definition":"1. A plan or program of action; 2. A system of rules, principles, or methods; 3. A secret plan made by a group of people to do something illegal or harmful.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They have a scheme to reduce costs.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們有一個削減成本的計畫。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government introduced a new housing scheme.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府推出了一個新的住房方案。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was involved in a criminal scheme.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他捲入了一個犯罪陰謀。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他捲入了一個犯罪陰謀。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6092,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::scrap::vt","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They had to ____ their holiday plans due to the storm.","expectedAnswer":"scrap","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They had to ____ their holiday plans due to the storm.","clozeAnswer":"scrap","exampleTranslation":"由於風暴，他們不得不取消了假期計畫。","reference":{"eng":"scrap","kk":"skræp","tense":"vt.","ch":"[  [    \"報廢\"  ],  [    \"廢棄\"  ],  [    \"捨棄\"  ],  [    \"（尤指）取消（計畫）\"  ]]","chEntries":["報廢","廢棄","捨棄","取消"],"practiceMeaning":"由於風暴，他們不得不取消了假期計畫。","analysis":"此字源自 scrap 的名詞用法，意為「零碎的、無用的部分」。作為及物動詞，核心語義是「將……視為廢棄物，從而處理掉」。引申為「捨棄」、「廢棄」，或尤其指「取消（計畫、協議）」。","definition":"1. discard or get rid of (something no longer useful or wanted); 2. abandon or cancel (a plan, policy, or agreement).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The old factory was eventually scrapped.\",\n    \"ch\": \"舊工廠最終被廢棄了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government decided to scrap the controversial policy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府決定取消這項有爭議的政策。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They had to scrap their holiday plans due to the storm.\",\n    \"ch\": \"由於風暴，他們不得不取消了假期計畫。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"由於風暴，他們不得不取消了假期計畫。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5860,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::sensation::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The new invention was a ____.","expectedAnswer":"sensation","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The new invention was a ____.","clozeAnswer":"sensation","exampleTranslation":"這項新發明引起了轟動。","reference":{"eng":"sensation","kk":"senˈseɪʃn","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"感覺\"  ],  [    \"知覺\"  ],  [    \"轟動\"  ],  [    \"感動\"  ],  [    \"感覺器官\"  ]]","chEntries":["感覺","知覺","轟動","感動","感覺器官"],"practiceMeaning":"這項新發明引起了轟動。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'sensus' (feeling, sense)，是 'sentire' (to feel) 的名詞形式。'Sensation' 的核心語意是指「通過感官獲得的感覺」或「對刺激的反應」。在更廣泛的語境中，它也可以指「引起強烈興趣或興奮的事件」，即「轟動」或「激動人心的事物」。這種語意轉移是由於強烈的感覺往往伴隨著興奮或情感的波動。例如，也可指「一種感覺器官」。","definition":"1. A physical feeling or perception resulting from a stimulus.; 2. An ability to feel, perceive, or experience objects, quality, and actions through the senses.; 3. An event or situation that causes great public interest and excitement.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The news caused a sensation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這消息引起了轟動。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He lost all sensation in his legs.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他失去雙腿的所有感覺。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The new invention was a sensation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這項新發明引起了轟動。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Touch is one of the five basic sensations.\",\n    \"ch\": \"觸覺是五種基本感覺之一。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這項新發明引起了轟動。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5060,"wordRef":"字彙王::u59::sensitivity::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He reacted with considerable ____ to the criticism.","expectedAnswer":"sensitivity","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He reacted with considerable ____ to the criticism.","clozeAnswer":"sensitivity","exampleTranslation":"他對批評反應相當敏感（不高興）。","reference":{"eng":"sensitivity","kk":"ˌsensəˈtɪvəti","tense":"n.","ch":"[['敏感性'], ['敏感度'], ['體貼'], ['（對批評或指責的）不高興']]","chEntries":["敏感性","敏感度","體貼","不高興"],"practiceMeaning":"他對批評反應相當敏感（不高興）。","analysis":"此字由形容詞 sensitive（敏感的）加上名詞化字尾 -ity（表示狀態或性質）構成。sensitive 源自拉丁語sensibilis，是動詞sentire（感覺）的派生詞。sensitivity 指「容易受到影響、感覺或傷害的性質或程度」，可指生理上（對刺激）、情感上（對他人感受）或智力上（對細微差別）的敏感。OCR 掃描時可能將 's' 誤判為 '5'，或 't' 誤判為 'l'。此處修正為 sensitivity。","definition":"1. the quality or state of being sensitive; 2. the ability to detect or respond to physical stimuli; 3. a quick and sympathetic awareness of the feelings of others.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has great sensitivity to the needs of others.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對他人的需求有很強的敏感性（體貼）。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The data requires careful handling due to its sensitivity.\",\n    \"ch\": \"由於其敏感性，這些數據需要小心處理。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He reacted with considerable sensitivity to the criticism.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對批評反應相當敏感（不高興）。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他對批評反應相當敏感（不高興）。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U59"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6136,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::sentiment::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"What is your ____ on this issue?","expectedAnswer":"sentiment","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"What is your ____ on this issue?","clozeAnswer":"sentiment","exampleTranslation":"你對這個問題有何看法？","reference":{"eng":"sentiment","kk":"ˈsɛntɪmənt","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"情緒\"  ],  [    \"情感\"  ],  [    \"感傷\"  ],  [    \"意見\"  ]]","chEntries":["情緒","情感","感傷","意見"],"practiceMeaning":"你對這個問題有何看法？","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 sentimentum，意為「思想；感覺；意見」，來自 sentire（感覺；感受）。因此，sentiment 的核心語義是「內心的感受」。此名詞指一種情感、感覺或態度，特別是微妙的、傾向於感傷的。也可指一種意見或看法。其語意演變是從「感覺」到「表達的情感」或「所持的意見」。","definition":"1. a feeling or emotion; 2. a view or attitude toward something; an opinion.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He expressed his warm sentiments to his friend.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他向朋友表達了他溫暖的情感。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The speech appealed to the audience's sentiments.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這篇演講打動了聽眾的情感。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"What is your sentiment on this issue?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你對這個問題有何看法？\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"你對這個問題有何看法？","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4046,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::sexy::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The idea of traveling the world is a ____ one.","expectedAnswer":"sexy","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The idea of traveling the world is a ____ one.","clozeAnswer":"sexy","exampleTranslation":"環遊世界的想法很令人興奮。","reference":{"eng":"sexy","kk":"/ˈsɛksi/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['性感的', '色情的'], ['誘人的', '有魅力的'], ['（使人）興奮的', '刺激的']]","chEntries":["性感的","色情的","誘人的","有魅力的","興奮的","刺激的"],"practiceMeaning":"環遊世界的想法很令人興奮。","analysis":"源自 'sex' (性)，加上 '-y' 後綴。直接指與性吸引力有關。引申為「誘人的」、「有魅力的」，不一定僅限於性方面，也可以指事物本身具有吸引力。第三個義項「（使人）興奮的」則強調其能引起強烈興趣或刺激感。","definition":"1. sexually attractive; 2. exciting or interesting; 3. appealing or alluring","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"她穿那件洋裝看起來很性感。\",\n    \"eng\": \"She looked very sexy in that dress.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"那是一輛極具吸引力的新跑車。\",\n    \"eng\": \"That was a sexy new sports car.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"環遊世界的想法很令人興奮。\",\n    \"eng\": \"The idea of traveling the world is a sexy one.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"環遊世界的想法很令人興奮。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6139,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::shareholder::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He is a major ____ in the tech startup.","expectedAnswer":"shareholder","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He is a major ____ in the tech startup.","clozeAnswer":"shareholder","exampleTranslation":"他是這家科技新創公司的主要股東。","reference":{"eng":"shareholder","kk":"ˈʃɛərˌhoʊldər","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"股東\"  ]]","chEntries":["股東"],"practiceMeaning":"他是這家科技新創公司的主要股東。","analysis":"此字為複合詞，由 share（股份；分享）和 holder（持有者）組成。share 源自古英語 scearu（份額；分割），向上可追溯至原始日耳曼語 *skērō。holder 是 hold（持有）加 -er（表示持有者）。因此，shareholder 的核心語義是「持有股份的人」。此名詞指擁有公司一部分所有權（股份）的個人或機構。其語意演變是將「持有」與「股份」結合。","definition":"A person or company that owns shares in a company and therefore part of that company.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Shareholders have the right to vote on company matters.\",\n    \"ch\": \"股東有權對公司事務進行投票。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company announced its annual profits to the shareholders.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司向股東公佈了其年度利潤。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a major shareholder in the tech startup.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是這家科技新創公司的主要股東。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他是這家科技新創公司的主要股東。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6096,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::sheriff::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He was elected ____ for his third term.","expectedAnswer":"sheriff","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He was elected ____ for his third term.","clozeAnswer":"sheriff","exampleTranslation":"他第三次當選為警長。","reference":{"eng":"sheriff","kk":"ˈʃɛrɪf","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"警長\"  ]]","chEntries":["警長"],"practiceMeaning":"他第三次當選為警長。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 scīrgerefa，由 scīr（郡，行政區）和 gerefa（官員）組成。核心語義是「地區官員」，特別是指在英語國家，負責某個郡或縣的執法官員。現代美式英語中，sheriff 通常指由選民選舉產生的、負責一個郡的治安的官員。","definition":"the chief law enforcement officer in a county.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The sheriff's department is responsible for law enforcement in the county.\",\n    \"ch\": \"郡治安官部門負責該縣的執法工作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The sheriff arrived at the scene of the crime.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警長到達了犯罪現場。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was elected sheriff for his third term.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他第三次當選為警長。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他第三次當選為警長。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6191,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::shove::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Don't ____ me!","expectedAnswer":"shove","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Don't ____ me!","clozeAnswer":"shove","exampleTranslation":"別推我！","reference":{"eng":"shove","kk":"ʃʌv","tense":"v.","ch":"[  [    \"推\"  ],  [    \"擠\"  ],  [    \"猛推\"  ]]","chEntries":["推","擠","猛推"],"practiceMeaning":"別推我！","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 shoven，與古英語 scufan「推、刮」同源，可能源自原始日耳曼語 *skūfan。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作為動詞，其核心語義是用力向前或向某方向推動某物或某人。這個動作的語義是其主要構成要素，強調力量和直接性。","definition":"1. push roughly or carelessly; 2. to move or push something with force.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He shoved the door open.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他猛地推開了門。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They had to shove their way through the crowd.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們不得不擠過人群。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Don't shove me!\",\n    \"ch\": \"別推我！\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He shoved the box onto the shelf.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他把箱子塞進了架子。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"別推我！","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6194,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::shrug::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Her ____ conveyed her lack of interest.","expectedAnswer":"shrug","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Her ____ conveyed her lack of interest.","clozeAnswer":"shrug","exampleTranslation":"她的聳肩傳達了她不感興趣。","reference":{"eng":"shrug","kk":"ʃrʌɡ","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"聳肩\"  ]]","chEntries":["聳肩"],"practiceMeaning":"她的聳肩傳達了她不感興趣。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 scrybban。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作為名詞，是動詞 shrug「聳肩」的名詞化。其核心語義是指「聳肩這個動作」，通常用以表達不確定、無知、無所謂或無助。","definition":"1. an act of shrugging the shoulders.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A shrug of indifference was his only reply.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一絲無所謂的聳肩是他的唯一答覆。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He gave a shrug and walked away.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他聳了聳肩就走開了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her shrug conveyed her lack of interest.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的聳肩傳達了她不感興趣。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她的聳肩傳達了她不感興趣。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5433,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::situated::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ancient ruins are ____ near the river.","expectedAnswer":"situated","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ancient ruins are ____ near the river.","clozeAnswer":"situated","exampleTranslation":"古老的廢墟位於河邊附近。","reference":{"eng":"situated","kk":"ˈsɪtʃueɪtɪd","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['位於'], ['坐落於']]","chEntries":["位於","坐落於"],"practiceMeaning":"古老的廢墟位於河邊附近。","analysis":"此字為動詞 \"situate\" 的過去分詞，可作形容詞使用。\"situate\" 源自拉丁語 \"situare\"，意為\"使處於……位置\"，來自 \"situs\" (位置、地點)。構詞上，\"situ-\" 提供了核心的「位置」語意，\"-ate\" 是動詞字尾。 \"Situatd\" 作形容詞，表示某物「被放置在」或「位於」某個特定地點或環境，通常用來描述建築物、城市或地理位置。","definition":"located or positioned in a particular place or position.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The hotel is situated on a hill overlooking the sea.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家酒店坐落於俯瞰大海的山丘上。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The village is situated in a remote valley.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個村莊坐落於一個偏遠的山谷中。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The ancient ruins are situated near the river.\",\n    \"ch\": \"古老的廢墟位於河邊附近。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"古老的廢墟位於河邊附近。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3871,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::situation::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company is in a good financial ____.","expectedAnswer":"situation","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company is in a good financial ____.","clozeAnswer":"situation","exampleTranslation":"公司財務狀況良好。","reference":{"eng":"situation","kk":"/ˌsɪtʃuˈeɪʃən/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['情況', '局勢'], ['處境'], ['地點', '場所']]","chEntries":["情況","局勢","處境","地點","場所"],"practiceMeaning":"公司財務狀況良好。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 ' situs' (site, position)，後經由法語 'situation' 傳入。核心是「位置」或「所處的狀態」。可指一個具體情境的實際狀態、一連串事件的發展，或某人所處的困難/有利的境地。較少見的用法指特定地點。","definition":"1. a set of circumstances or conditions; a state of affairs. 2. a person's position or condition at a particular time. 3. a place or location.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The political situation is very tense.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政治局勢非常緊張。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He found himself in a difficult situation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他發現自己處於一個困難的境地。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company is in a good financial situation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司財務狀況良好。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"公司財務狀況良好。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5806,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::skeleton::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His ____ was found buried in the garden.","expectedAnswer":"skeleton","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His ____ was found buried in the garden.","clozeAnswer":"skeleton","exampleTranslation":"他的骸骨被發現埋在花園裡。","reference":{"eng":"skeleton","kk":"ˈskɛlɪtn","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"骨骼\"  ],  [    \"骨架\"  ],  [    \"骨架（結構）\"  ],  [    \"骨架（人或動物）\"  ]]","chEntries":["骨骼","骨架"],"practiceMeaning":"他的骸骨被發現埋在花園裡。","analysis":"此字為名詞，源自中古英語scoleton，來自現代拉丁語Sceletus，後者又源自古希臘語skeletón（乾燥的；枯乾的），來自skelein（弄乾；枯萎）。核心語義是指「支撐身體的骨頭的總體」，即骨骼或骨架。語意演變上，從「乾燥物」的概念，具體化為支撐生物體的「骨架」，再引申為「結構的基本框架」。","definition":"1. all the bones in a person's or animal's body; 2. the basic structure or framework of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The museum displayed a dinosaur skeleton.\",\n    \"ch\": \"博物館展示了恐龍的骨架。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The skeleton of the building was erected in just a few weeks.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座建築的骨架在短短幾週內就豎立起來了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His skeleton was found buried in the garden.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的骸骨被發現埋在花園裡。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他的骸骨被發現埋在花園裡。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4165,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::society::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Social media has changed ____.","expectedAnswer":"society","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Social media has changed ____.","clozeAnswer":"society","exampleTranslation":"社交媒體改變了社會。","reference":{"eng":"society","kk":"/səˈsaɪəti/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['社會'], ['學會', '協會']]","chEntries":["社會","學會","協會"],"practiceMeaning":"社交媒體改變了社會。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 societas（夥伴關係，聯盟），由 socius（夥伴）而來。核心概念是「一群人共同生活、交往的集合體」。","definition":"1. the aggregate of people living together in a more or less ordered community; 2. an association or group of people with similar interests or aims","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They live in a democratic society.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們生活在一個民主社會。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is a member of the Royal Society.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是皇家學會的會員。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Social media has changed society.\",\n    \"ch\": \"社交媒體改變了社會。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"社交媒體改變了社會。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4128,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::solid::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We have ____ evidence to prove his guilt.","expectedAnswer":"solid","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We have ____ evidence to prove his guilt.","clozeAnswer":"solid","exampleTranslation":"我們有確鑿的證據證明他的罪行。","reference":{"eng":"solid","kk":"/ˈsɒlɪd/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['固體的'], ['結實的', '穩固的'], ['可靠的', '實在的'], ['一致的', '無異議的']]","chEntries":["固體的","結實的","穩固的","可靠的","實在的","一致的","無異議的"],"practiceMeaning":"我們有確鑿的證據證明他的罪行。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 solidus（堅實的，完整的）。核心概念是「穩定」、「不流動」、「堅固」。引申為物理狀態（固體），結構的穩固，證據的確鑿，或意見的一致性。","definition":"1. firmly packed or condensed; 2. (of a substance) having a definite shape and volume; 3. strong and reliable; 4. showing firm agreement or support","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Ice is the solid form of water.\",\n    \"ch\": \"冰是水的固體形態。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The building is made of solid stone.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座建築是用實心石頭建造的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We have solid evidence to prove his guilt.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們有確鑿的證據證明他的罪行。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The team's performance was solid throughout the season.\",\n    \"ch\": \"整個賽季球隊的表現都很穩定。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們有確鑿的證據證明他的罪行。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5436,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::spare::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She managed to ____ a few dollars for charity.","expectedAnswer":"spare","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She managed to ____ a few dollars for charity.","clozeAnswer":"spare","exampleTranslation":"她設法省下了一些錢捐給慈善機構。","reference":{"eng":"spare","kk":"sper","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['備用的'], ['多餘的'], ['節省的'], ['空閒的'], ['無事可做的']]","chEntries":["備用的","多餘的","節省的","空閒的","無事可做的"],"practiceMeaning":"她設法省下了一些錢捐給慈善機構。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 \"spær\"，意為\"節儉的\"、\"稀少的\"。其詞源可能與\"sparse\" (稀疏的) 有聯繫。構詞上沒有明顯的字首、字根或字尾可拆解，應視為一個整體詞源的演變。原始語義是「稀少」、「節省」，引申為「不需要的」、「多餘的」，因此可以用作「備用的」；同時也表示「有空閒的」、「可供支配的」。","definition":"not being used or needed at the moment; kept in reserve for future use; not used or spoken; not strictly necessary; not busy; free.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Do you have a spare tire in your car?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你的車上有備胎嗎？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I have some spare time this afternoon.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我今天下午有些空閒時間。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She managed to spare a few dollars for charity.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她設法省下了一些錢捐給慈善機構。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她設法省下了一些錢捐給慈善機構。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5478,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l4::species::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This is a rare ____ of bird.","expectedAnswer":"species","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This is a rare ____ of bird.","clozeAnswer":"species","exampleTranslation":"這是稀有的鳥類物種。","reference":{"eng":"species","kk":"ˈspishiz","tense":"n.","ch":"[['物種'], ['種類']]","chEntries":["物種","種類"],"practiceMeaning":"這是稀有的鳥類物種。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'species'，原意是「樣貌、外觀、形式、種類」，也指「圖像、模型」。在科學分類中，它被用來表示「一個物種」，即生物分類學中的一個基本單位，指一群能夠相互繁殖並產生可育後代的生物。'Species' 是單數與複數同形。其詞源 'specere'（看）表明了「種類」的概念是基於「外觀」的區分。核心語意是「一個具有共同特徵、能夠繁殖的生物分類單元」。","definition":"1. A group of living organisms consisting of similar individuals capable of exchanging genes or interbreeding.; 2. A class or kind of persons or things.; 3. A particular kind of.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The Amazon rainforest is home to thousands of species of plants and animals.\",\n    \"ch\": \"亞馬遜雨林是數千種動植物的家園。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Scientists are trying to protect endangered species.\",\n    \"ch\": \"科學家正努力保護瀕危物種。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a rare species of bird.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是稀有的鳥類物種。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是稀有的鳥類物種。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3993,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u3::specific::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need more ____ details about the project.","expectedAnswer":"specific","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need more ____ details about the project.","clozeAnswer":"specific","exampleTranslation":"我們需要關於這個計畫更具體的細節。","reference":{"eng":"specific","kk":"/spəˈsɪfɪk/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['特定的', '具體的'], ['明確的', '確切的'], ['（種類）獨特的']]","chEntries":["特定的","具體的","明確的","確切的","獨特的"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要關於這個計畫更具體的細節。","analysis":"詞源：拉丁文 'specificus' (區分的、特定的)，源自 'species' (種類、外觀)。指明確界定、不含糊的，或屬於某一特定類別的。","definition":"1. clearly defined or identified; 2. relating to a particular thing, person, or category; 3. precisely indicated or stated.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Do you have any specific instructions for me?\",\n    \"ch\": \"您有任何具體的指示要給我嗎？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This disease is specific to the region.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種疾病是該地區特有的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need more specific details about the project.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要關於這個計畫更具體的細節。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要關於這個計畫更具體的細節。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3301,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::spectacular::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He made a ____ recovery from his illness.","expectedAnswer":"spectacular","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He made a ____ recovery from his illness.","clozeAnswer":"spectacular","exampleTranslation":"他從疾病中奇蹟般地康復了。","reference":{"eng":"spectacular","kk":"/spɛkˈtækjʊlər/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['壯觀的；引人注目的'], ['精彩的；驚人的']]","chEntries":["壯觀的","引人注目的","精彩的","驚人的"],"practiceMeaning":"他從疾病中奇蹟般地康復了。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'spectaculum' (戲劇表演，景象)，由 'spectare' (觀看) 演變而來。指令人印象深刻、引人注目、極為精彩或壯觀的。","definition":"1. beautiful in a dramatic and eye-catching way; 2. very impressive or remarkable.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The fireworks display was spectacular.\",\n    \"ch\": \"煙火表演非常精彩。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The Grand Canyon offers spectacular views.\",\n    \"ch\": \"大峽谷提供了壯觀的景色。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He made a spectacular recovery from his illness.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他從疾病中奇蹟般地康復了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他從疾病中奇蹟般地康復了。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5103,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::spine::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She found the courage to stand up to her boss, showing real ____.","expectedAnswer":"spine","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She found the courage to stand up to her boss, showing real ____.","clozeAnswer":"spine","exampleTranslation":"她鼓起勇氣反抗老闆，展現了真正的勇氣。","reference":{"eng":"spine","kk":"spaɪn","tense":"n.","ch":"[['脊椎'], ['書脊'], ['勇氣']]","chEntries":["脊椎","書脊","勇氣"],"practiceMeaning":"她鼓起勇氣反抗老闆，展現了真正的勇氣。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'spina'，意為 '刺、荊棘'，後引申為 '脊骨'，可能因為脊椎像一連串的骨刺。其核心語義是指身體後部的骨骼結構，即 '脊椎'。它也延伸指書籍封面連接的邊緣，即 '書脊'。更比喻地，'spine' 可以指一個人 '堅強的意志' 或 '勇氣'，因為脊椎支撐著身體，給人一種挺直、堅定的形象。","definition":"1. The series of bones forming the backbone of a person or animal.; 2. The back edge of a book, where the pages are bound together.; 3. Courage or determination.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A healthy spine is crucial for good posture.\",\n    \"ch\": \"健康的脊椎對保持良好姿態至關重要。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The book has a colorful spine.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本書的書脊色彩鮮豔。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She found the courage to stand up to her boss, showing real spine.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她鼓起勇氣反抗老闆，展現了真正的勇氣。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她鼓起勇氣反抗老闆，展現了真正的勇氣。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4570,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::splash::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Her bold dress made a ____ at the party.","expectedAnswer":"splash","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Her bold dress made a ____ at the party.","clozeAnswer":"splash","exampleTranslation":"她那大膽的洋裝在派對上引起了轟動。","reference":{"eng":"splash","kk":"/splæʃ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['潑濺', '飛濺'], ['（水花）濺起聲'], ['（顏料、墨水等的）一灘', '一抹'], ['（引人注意的）引人注目的事物', '轟動']]","chEntries":["潑濺","飛濺","濺起聲","一灘","一抹","引人注目的事物","轟動"],"practiceMeaning":"她那大膽的洋裝在派對上引起了轟動。","analysis":"擬聲詞，模仿水花濺起的聲音。\n    1. 潑濺、飛濺：指液體被拋灑開來的動作或結果。\n    2. 聲音：指水花濺起時發出的聲音。\n    3. 一灘、一抹：指濺灑後在物體表面留下的痕跡。\n    4. 轟動：引申為引起廣泛關注或轟動的事件。","definition":"1. the action or sound of splashing.; 2. a quantity of liquid suddenly or violently dispersed in droplets.; 3. a vivid or striking effect.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The splash of water woke him up.\",\n    \"ch\": \"水花濺起的聲音把他吵醒了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was a splash of ink on the page.\",\n    \"ch\": \"紙上有一灘墨水。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her bold dress made a splash at the party.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她那大膽的洋裝在派對上引起了轟動。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她那大膽的洋裝在派對上引起了轟動。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3194,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::split::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The party ____ into two factions.","expectedAnswer":"split","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The party ____ into two factions.","clozeAnswer":"split","exampleTranslation":"這個黨派分裂成兩個派系。","reference":{"eng":"split","kk":"/splɪt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['分裂；分開'], ['（使）裂開；破裂'], ['分享；分配（尤指不均）']]","chEntries":["分裂","分開","裂開","破裂","分享","分配"],"practiceMeaning":"這個黨派分裂成兩個派系。","analysis":"詞源來自古諾爾斯語 'splita'，意為「劈開，分裂」。'Split' 的核心是「分離」、「裂開」或「分開」。它可以指物理上的分離，如將物體劈開、裂開，或將一群人分成小組。也可指意見、關係的分歧。在分配財物時，'split' 也常用來表示分享，但有時帶有均勻或不均勻分配的意味。","definition":"1. break or cause to break into pieces; 2. divide into parts or groups; 3. separate from a larger group or body.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The log split easily when I hit it with the axe.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我用斧頭砍下去，木頭很容易就劈開了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The friends decided to split the cost of the meal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"朋友們決定分攤飯錢。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The party split into two factions.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個黨派分裂成兩個派系。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The tree trunk was split by lightning.\",\n    \"ch\": \"樹幹被閃電劈開了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個黨派分裂成兩個派系。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U40"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3953,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::stand-for::phrase","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They ____ equal rights for all.","expectedAnswer":"stand for","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They ____ equal rights for all.","clozeAnswer":"stand for","exampleTranslation":"他們主張所有人的平等權利。","reference":{"eng":"stand for","kk":"None","tense":"phrase","ch":"[['代表', '象徵'], ['贊成', '支持'], ['容忍']]","chEntries":["代表","象徵","贊成","支持","容忍"],"practiceMeaning":"他們主張所有人的平等權利。","analysis":"此為動詞片語。'stand' (動詞，站立) 加上介詞 'for' (為了)。有多種意義：1. 作為某事的代表或象徵；2. 支持某種觀點或行動；3. 容忍某事（通常用於否定句）。","definition":"1. to be a symbol of something; 2. to support or approve of something; 3. to tolerate something (often used in the negative).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The letters 'UN' stand for United Nations.\",\n    \"ch\": \"字母「UN」代表聯合國。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He will not stand for injustice.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他不會容忍不公。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They stand for equal rights for all.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們主張所有人的平等權利。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們主張所有人的平等權利。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4148,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::steep::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The tuition fees are very ____.","expectedAnswer":"steep","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The tuition fees are very ____.","clozeAnswer":"steep","exampleTranslation":"學費非常高昂。","reference":{"eng":"steep","kk":"/stiːp/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['陡峭的', '險峻的'], ['（價格、增長等）急劇的'], ['（要求、期望）過高的'], ['（學習）艱深的']]","chEntries":["陡峭的","險峻的","急劇的","過高的","艱深的"],"practiceMeaning":"學費非常高昂。","analysis":"源自古英語 steap（高聳的，陡峭的）。核心概念是「極度傾斜」或「高度」。引申為物理上的陡峭、數量上的急劇變化、要求過高，或學習曲線的陡峭。","definition":"1. rising or falling sharply; 2. (of a price or amount) very high; 3. (of a task or idea) demanding or difficult","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The path up the mountain was very steep.\",\n    \"ch\": \"上山的路非常陡峭。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There has been a steep rise in inflation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"通貨膨脹急劇上升。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The tuition fees are very steep.\",\n    \"ch\": \"學費非常高昂。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"學費非常高昂。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4705,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u17::stomach::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"I don't have the ____ for this kind of violence.","expectedAnswer":"stomach","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"I don't have the ____ for this kind of violence.","clozeAnswer":"stomach","exampleTranslation":"我受不了這種暴力。","reference":{"eng":"stomach","kk":"/ˈstʌmək/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['胃'], ['腹部'], ['（非正式）消化能力；容忍力']]","chEntries":["胃","腹部","消化能力","容忍力"],"practiceMeaning":"我受不了這種暴力。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 *stomachus*，來自希臘語 *stómakhos*（食道、胃）。核心是指消化食物的器官。引申至身體的腹部區域，以及非正式地指消化食物的能力，或容忍某種情況的能力。","definition":"1. An organ in the digestive tract where food is mixed with digestive juices. 2. The belly or abdomen. 3. (informal) The capacity to digest food or to tolerate something unpleasant.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The food was difficult for his stomach to digest.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種食物對他的胃來說很難消化。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He clutched his stomach in pain.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他痛苦地捂著肚子。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I don't have the stomach for this kind of violence.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我受不了這種暴力。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我受不了這種暴力。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U17"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4324,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::stormy::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"A ____ argument broke out.","expectedAnswer":"stormy","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"A ____ argument broke out.","clozeAnswer":"stormy","exampleTranslation":"一場激烈的爭論爆發了。","reference":{"eng":"stormy","kk":"/ˈstɔːrmi/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['暴風雨的；有風暴的'], ['（天氣）惡劣的'], ['（局勢、關係等）激烈的；動盪的']]","chEntries":["暴風雨的","有風暴的","惡劣的","激烈的","動盪的"],"practiceMeaning":"一場激烈的爭論爆發了。","analysis":"源自 'storm' (風暴)。1. 直接指天氣上有『風暴的』。2. 進一步指天氣『惡劣的』。3. 作為比喻，指情況、氣氛、關係等『激烈的、動盪的、充滿衝突的』，如同風暴一樣不平靜。","definition":"characterized by or like a storm; (of weather) very bad with strong winds and rain; full of strong feelings or arguments","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We had to cancel the picnic due to the stormy weather.\",\n    \"ch\": \"由於天氣惡劣，我們不得不取消野餐。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Their marriage was often stormy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們的婚姻經常處於動盪之中。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A stormy argument broke out.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一場激烈的爭論爆發了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"一場激烈的爭論爆發了。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3927,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::strength::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Her biggest ____ is her determination.","expectedAnswer":"strength","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Her biggest ____ is her determination.","clozeAnswer":"strength","exampleTranslation":"她最大的優勢是她的決心。","reference":{"eng":"strength","kk":"/streŋkθ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['力量', '力氣'], ['強度'], ['優勢'], ['效力']]","chEntries":["力量","力氣","強度","優勢","效力"],"practiceMeaning":"她最大的優勢是她的決心。","analysis":"源自古英語 'strengþu'，由 'streng' (意為「強壯的」) 和 '-þu' (名詞後綴，表示「狀態」) 組成。指物理上的力量、堅固的程度、精神上的毅力、能力或優勢。","definition":"1. the quality or state of being physically strong; 2. the capacity to withstand great force or pressure; 3. the degree to which something is powerful or effective; 4. an advantage or good quality.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has great physical strength.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他擁有強大的體力。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The strength of the fabric is impressive.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這塊布料的強度令人印象深刻。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her biggest strength is her determination.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她最大的優勢是她的決心。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The strength of the argument was undeniable.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個論點的說服力是無可否認的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她最大的優勢是她的決心。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3196,"wordRef":"字彙王::u40::strive::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They will continue to ____ for peace.","expectedAnswer":"strive","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They will continue to ____ for peace.","clozeAnswer":"strive","exampleTranslation":"他們將繼續為和平而奮鬥。","reference":{"eng":"strive","kk":"/straɪv/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['努力；奮鬥；力爭']]","chEntries":["努力","奮鬥","力爭"],"practiceMeaning":"他們將繼續為和平而奮鬥。","analysis":"詞源來自古英語 'strivean'，意為「爭鬥，奮鬥」。'Strive' 指的是付出巨大的努力、奮鬥和堅持，以達到某個目標或實現某種理想。它強調的是一種積極、持續的追求，即使面臨困難或挑戰。","definition":"make great efforts to achieve or obtain something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We must strive for excellence in everything we do.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們必須在我們所做的一切事情上力求卓越。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She strived to overcome her weaknesses.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她努力克服自己的弱點。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They will continue to strive for peace.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們將繼續為和平而奮鬥。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們將繼續為和平而奮鬥。","sourceName":"字彙王、龍騰課本","unitName":"U40、L8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4330,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::substance::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He had a ____ abuse problem.","expectedAnswer":"substance","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He had a ____ abuse problem.","clozeAnswer":"substance","exampleTranslation":"他有藥物濫用問題。","reference":{"eng":"substance","kk":"/ˈsʌbstəns/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['物質；材料'], ['實質；要旨'], ['（論點、計畫等的）重要性；意義'], ['（非法）藥物']]","chEntries":["物質","材料","實質","要旨","重要性","意義","藥物"],"practiceMeaning":"他有藥物濫用問題。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'substantia'，意為 'being, essence, material'，來自 'subsistere' (to stand under, to exist)，由 'sub-' (under) 和 'sistere' (to stand) 構成。核心意為『立足於下』、『存在』。1. 指『物質、材料』，有形的、構成事物的東西。2. 指事物的『實質、要旨』，內在的內容而非形式。3. 指『重要性、意義』，有實質內容，有價值。4. 指具有精神作用的『藥物』，強調其作為一種『物質』對人的影響。","definition":"a type of solid liquid, or gas that is made of a particular combination of atoms and that makes up all matter; the most important part of something; importance or value","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Water is a chemical substance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"水是一種化學物質。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The report lacks substance and is full of vague statements.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這份報告缺乏實質內容，充滿了含糊不清的陳述。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He had a substance abuse problem.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他有藥物濫用問題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His argument has a lot of substance.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的論點很有分量。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他有藥物濫用問題。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5149,"wordRef":"字彙王::u62::subtle::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The wine had a ____ hint of oak.","expectedAnswer":"subtle","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The wine had a ____ hint of oak.","clozeAnswer":"subtle","exampleTranslation":"這款酒帶有一絲淡淡的橡木味。","reference":{"eng":"subtle","kk":"ˈsʌtl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['微妙的'], ['精細的'], ['不易察覺的'], ['狡猾的']]","chEntries":["微妙的","精細的","不易察覺的","狡猾的"],"practiceMeaning":"這款酒帶有一絲淡淡的橡木味。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 sotil，意為「精細、纖細、巧妙」，來自拉丁語 subtilis，由 sub-（在…下面）+ tĭla（紡織品、結構，來自 texere「編織」）組成。原意是「編織得非常細密」。引申為「不易察覺的、微妙的、精細的」。可指氣味、味道、變化、或人的心思。","definition":"so delicate or precise as not to be obvious; slight and gradual; (of a person or their manner) making use of clever indirect methods; artful.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was a subtle change in her attitude.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的態度有了微妙的轉變。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has a subtle sense of humor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他有著一種含蓄的幽默感。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The wine had a subtle hint of oak.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這款酒帶有一絲淡淡的橡木味。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這款酒帶有一絲淡淡的橡木味。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U62"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4576,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::subtract::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ the costs from the revenue to find the profit.","expectedAnswer":"Subtract","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ the costs from the revenue to find the profit.","clozeAnswer":"Subtract","exampleTranslation":"從收入中減去成本來找出利潤。","reference":{"eng":"subtract","kk":"/səbˈtrækt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['減去', '扣除']]","chEntries":["減去","扣除"],"practiceMeaning":"從收入中減去成本來找出利潤。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'subtractum'，'sub-' (under) 和 'trahere' (to draw - 牽引)。核心概念是「從下面抽出」或「從總數中移走」。\n    1. 減去、扣除：在數學上表示從一個數中減去另一個數；在實際應用中，指從總額中扣除一部分。","definition":"1. take away (a number or amount) from another.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"You need to subtract five from ten.\",\n    \"ch\": \"你需要從十中減去五。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Taxes are subtracted from your salary before you receive it.\",\n    \"ch\": \"稅金在你收到薪水前會被扣除。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Subtract the costs from the revenue to find the profit.\",\n    \"ch\": \"從收入中減去成本來找出利潤。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"從收入中減去成本來找出利潤。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5567,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::swift::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need a ____ response to this crisis.","expectedAnswer":"swift","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need a ____ response to this crisis.","clozeAnswer":"swift","exampleTranslation":"我們需要對這場危機作出迅速的應對。","reference":{"eng":"swift","kk":"swɪft","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['快速的'], ['敏捷的'], ['迅速的']]","chEntries":["快速的","敏捷的","迅速的"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要對這場危機作出迅速的應對。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 \"swift\"，與荷蘭語 \"swift\"、德語 \"sch(w)ift\" 同源，最終可追溯至原始印歐語 \\*swep-（to go, to flow，去，流動）。其核心語義是「快速、敏捷」。\"swift\" 形容詞用於描述人、動物、動作或事件，強調其移動或發生的速度極快，沒有延遲。它比 \"fast\" 更強調一種流暢、敏捷的移動感。例如 \"a swift current\"（湍急的水流），\"swift progress\"（快速的進展）。","definition":"1. Happening or moving very quickly; 2. Able to move very quickly; agile.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He made a swift decision.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他做了一個迅速的決定。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The swift movement of the bird caught my eye.\",\n    \"ch\": \"那隻鳥敏捷的動作吸引了我的目光。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need a swift response to this crisis.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要對這場危機作出迅速的應對。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要對這場危機作出迅速的應對。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4504,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::take::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need to ____ action immediately.","expectedAnswer":"take","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need to ____ action immediately.","clozeAnswer":"take","exampleTranslation":"我們必須立即採取行動。","reference":{"eng":"take","kk":"/teɪk/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['拿'], ['取得'], ['接受'], ['花費（時間、金錢）'], ['考慮'], ['採取（行動、措施）']]","chEntries":["拿","取得","接受","花費","考慮","採取"],"practiceMeaning":"我們必須立即採取行動。","analysis":"源自古英語 tacan，意為「抓住」、「獲得」。是一個非常核心且用途廣泛的動詞。其語意極其豐富，涵蓋了從具體的「獲取」、「攜帶」到抽象的「接受」、「考慮」、「採取」等。","definition":"1. To lay hold of (something) with one's hands; 2. To obtain possession of; 3. To accept or receive; 4. To spend or require (time or effort); 5. To consider or regard in a particular way; 6. To carry out or perform (an action or undertaking).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please take this book.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請拿這本書。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It will take an hour to finish.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這需要一個小時才能完成。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to take action immediately.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們必須立即採取行動。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Do you take sugar in your coffee?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你的咖啡加糖嗎？\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們必須立即採取行動。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4492,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::talent::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His ____ for storytelling made him popular.","expectedAnswer":"talent","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His ____ for storytelling made him popular.","clozeAnswer":"talent","exampleTranslation":"他講故事的才能使他很受歡迎。","reference":{"eng":"talent","kk":"/ˈtælənt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['天賦'], ['才能'], ['有才能的人']]","chEntries":["天賦","才能","有才能的人"],"practiceMeaning":"他講故事的才能使他很受歡迎。","analysis":"源自古希臘語 talanton，意為「重量」、「貨幣單位」。在聖經中，talanton 被用來比喻一個人所擁有的能力或恩賜。語意從「貨幣」、「資產」引申為「天生的能力」或「才能」。","definition":"1. Natural aptitude or skill; 2. A person with a talent for something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a natural talent for music.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她有學習音樂的天賦。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The organization is looking for talented individuals.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該組織正在尋找有才能的個人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His talent for storytelling made him popular.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他講故事的才能使他很受歡迎。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他講故事的才能使他很受歡迎。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4125,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::talkative::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ child dominated the conversation.","expectedAnswer":"talkative","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ child dominated the conversation.","clozeAnswer":"talkative","exampleTranslation":"這個愛說話的孩子主導了談話。","reference":{"eng":"talkative","kk":"/ˈtɔːkətɪv/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['健談的', '愛說話的']]","chEntries":["健談的","愛說話的"],"practiceMeaning":"這個愛說話的孩子主導了談話。","analysis":"源自 talk（說話）+ -ative（形容詞後綴，表示傾向或特性）。核心概念是「有說話的傾向或特性」。","definition":"1. fond of or given to talking; 2. (of a machine or device) designed to speak or communicate verbally","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She's a very talkative person.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是一個很健談的人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He became more talkative after a few drinks.\",\n    \"ch\": \"喝了幾杯酒後，他變得更加健談了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The talkative child dominated the conversation.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個愛說話的孩子主導了談話。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個愛說話的孩子主導了談話。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4176,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::tell::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"It's hard to ____ when he's lying.","expectedAnswer":"tell","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"It's hard to ____ when he's lying.","clozeAnswer":"tell","exampleTranslation":"很難辨認他何時在撒謊。","reference":{"eng":"tell","kk":"/tɛl/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['告訴', '講述'], ['分辨', '區分'], ['辨認']]","chEntries":["告訴","講述","分辨","區分","辨認"],"practiceMeaning":"很難辨認他何時在撒謊。","analysis":"源自古英語 tellan（敘述，計算）。核心概念是「傳達信息」或「辨別」。引申為告知、講述、區分或辨認。","definition":"1. communicate information to someone by speaking or writing; 2. distinguish (someone or something) with difficulty by its characteristics; 3. discern or make out","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Can you tell the difference between these two colors?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你能分辨這兩種顏色之間的差異嗎？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He told me a story.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他給我講了一個故事。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's hard to tell when he's lying.\",\n    \"ch\": \"很難辨認他何時在撒謊。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"很難辨認他何時在撒謊。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6100,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::testify::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Witnesses will ____ about what they saw.","expectedAnswer":"testify","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Witnesses will ____ about what they saw.","clozeAnswer":"testify","exampleTranslation":"目擊者將會作證他們所見。","reference":{"eng":"testify","kk":"ˈtɛstəˌfaɪ","tense":"v.","ch":"[  [    \"證明\"  ],  [    \"作證\"  ],  [    \"表明\"  ]]","chEntries":["證明","作證","表明"],"practiceMeaning":"目擊者將會作證他們所見。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 testis（witness）和 facere（to make）。核心語義是「做出見證」或「證明」。在法律上，testify 指「在法庭上作證」。廣義上，testify 可以指「表明」、「證明」某事物的存在或真實性。","definition":"1. give evidence as a witness in a court or legal proceeding; 2. serve as a testimony to; show or confirm.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was called to testify in the trial.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他被傳喚出庭作證。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her actions testify to her sincerity.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的行為證明了她的真誠。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Witnesses will testify about what they saw.\",\n    \"ch\": \"目擊者將會作證他們所見。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"目擊者將會作證他們所見。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6101,"wordRef":"字彙王::u64::theology::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ often involves interpreting religious texts.","expectedAnswer":"Theology","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ often involves interpreting religious texts.","clozeAnswer":"Theology","exampleTranslation":"神學經常涉及解釋宗教文本。","reference":{"eng":"theology","kk":"θiˈɑlədʒi","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"神學\"  ]]","chEntries":["神學"],"practiceMeaning":"神學經常涉及解釋宗教文本。","analysis":"此字源自希臘語 theologia，由 theos（god）和 logia（discourse, study）組成。核心語義是「對神的研究」或「關於神的學說」。","definition":"the study of the nature of God and religious belief.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is studying theology at university.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在大學攻讀神學。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The book explores different aspects of Christian theology.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本書探討了基督教神學的各個方面。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Theology often involves interpreting religious texts.\",\n    \"ch\": \"神學經常涉及解釋宗教文本。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"神學經常涉及解釋宗教文本。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U64"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6144,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::thereby::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She mastered the technique, ____ impressing her instructor.","expectedAnswer":"thereby","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She mastered the technique, ____ impressing her instructor.","clozeAnswer":"thereby","exampleTranslation":"她掌握了這項技術，因此給了她的指導員一個深刻的印象。","reference":{"eng":"thereby","kk":"ˌðɛərˈbaɪ","tense":"adv.","ch":"[  [    \"藉此\"  ],  [    \"因此\"  ],  [    \"從而\"  ]]","chEntries":["藉此","因此","從而"],"practiceMeaning":"她掌握了這項技術，因此給了她的指導員一個深刻的印象。","analysis":"此字為合成詞，由 there（在那裡；因此）和 by（藉著；通過）構成。there 來自古英語 þær（在那裡）。by 來自古英語 bī（在……旁邊；通過）。因此，thereby 的核心語義是「藉著那個」或「因此」。此副詞用於連接兩個子句，表示通過前一個子句的動作或情況，而達到了後一個子句的結果。其語意演變是從「通過那個」到「因此；從而」。","definition":"By that means; as a result of that.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He secured his promotion, thereby earning a higher salary.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他獲得了晉升，從而獲得了更高的薪水。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company increased its investment, thereby boosting its market share.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司增加了投資，藉此提升了其市場份額。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She mastered the technique, thereby impressing her instructor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她掌握了這項技術，因此給了她的指導員一個深刻的印象。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她掌握了這項技術，因此給了她的指導員一個深刻的印象。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5810,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::thigh::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She rested her arm on her ____.","expectedAnswer":"thigh","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She rested her arm on her ____.","clozeAnswer":"thigh","exampleTranslation":"她把手臂放在大腿上。","reference":{"eng":"thigh","kk":"θaɪ","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"大腿\"  ]]","chEntries":["大腿"],"practiceMeaning":"她把手臂放在大腿上。","analysis":"此字為名詞，源自古英語þēoh，詞源不明。核心語義是指人或動物腿部從臀部到膝蓋的部分，即大腿。此字沒有明顯的字首、字根或字尾可透明拆解。","definition":"1. the part of the human leg between the hip and the knee.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He had a deep cut on his thigh.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的大腿上有一個很深的傷口。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The horse galloped, its powerful thighs propelling it forward.\",\n    \"ch\": \"馬匹奔馳，牠強壯的大腿推動牠前進。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She rested her arm on her thigh.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她把手臂放在大腿上。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她把手臂放在大腿上。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6200,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::threshold::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The pain reached a ____ where she could no longer bear it.","expectedAnswer":"threshold","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The pain reached a ____ where she could no longer bear it.","clozeAnswer":"threshold","exampleTranslation":"疼痛達到了她無法忍受的閾值。","reference":{"eng":"threshold","kk":"ˈθreʃhoʊld","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"門檻\"  ],  [    \"入門\"  ],  [    \"閾值\"  ],  [    \"起始點\"  ]]","chEntries":["門檻","入門","閾值","起始點"],"practiceMeaning":"疼痛達到了她無法忍受的閾值。","analysis":"此字是古英語 þrescold 或 þerscold 的演變，由 þres（打穀）和 scold（門檻）組合而成，意為「打穀場的門檻」。此字在現代英語中可視為複合詞，但其詞源的準確性有待考證，通常認為是整體詞源演變。作為名詞，其核心語義是指「進入某個地方的入口處的門檻」，引申為「某事的開始、起始點或進入的關卡」。詞源的「打穀場的門檻」引申出「進入」的物理概念，進而發展出「關鍵的起始點」的抽象概念。","definition":"1. the floor or step at the bottom of a doorway; 2. the point at which something begins; 3. the point at which a stimulus is perceived or a response is initiated; 4. the lower limit of a person's ability to perceive or react to a particular stimulus.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He stepped over the threshold into the house.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他跨過門檻走進屋裡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This event marks a new threshold in our relationship.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個事件標誌著我們關係的新開端。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The pain reached a threshold where she could no longer bear it.\",\n    \"ch\": \"疼痛達到了她無法忍受的閾值。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Crossing the threshold of the ancient temple, they felt a sense of awe.\",\n    \"ch\": \"跨過古老寺廟的門檻，他們感到一陣敬畏。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"疼痛達到了她無法忍受的閾值。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5812,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::thrill::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He experienced the ____ of victory.","expectedAnswer":"thrill","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He experienced the ____ of victory.","clozeAnswer":"thrill","exampleTranslation":"他體驗了勝利的激動。","reference":{"eng":"thrill","kk":"θrɪl","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"興奮\"  ],  [    \"激動\"  ],  [    \"戰慄\"  ],  [    \"驚險刺激\"  ]]","chEntries":["興奮","激動","戰慄","驚險刺激"],"practiceMeaning":"他體驗了勝利的激動。","analysis":"此字為名詞，與動詞同源。核心語義是指「強烈的興奮、激動或恐懼的感覺」。語意演變上，從「顫抖」的生理反應，引申為「強烈的情感衝擊」，包括愉悅的興奮，也包括因恐懼而產生的戰慄。也可用來指「驚險刺激的體驗」。","definition":"1. a sudden feeling of excitement and pleasure; 2. a feeling of fear or excitement; 3. an experience that gives you a strong feeling of excitement.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The ski jump gave her a real thrill.\",\n    \"ch\": \"滑雪跳躍讓她感到真正的興奮。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There's a thrill in exploring the unknown.\",\n    \"ch\": \"探索未知充滿了驚險刺激。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He experienced the thrill of victory.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他體驗了勝利的激動。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他體驗了勝利的激動。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4547,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::toss::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She felt faint and had to ____ her head back.","expectedAnswer":"toss","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She felt faint and had to ____ her head back.","clozeAnswer":"toss","exampleTranslation":"她感到頭暈，不得不仰起頭。","reference":{"eng":"toss","kk":"/tɔːs/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['扔', '拋', '擲'], ['（使）搖晃', '顛簸'], ['（使）昏迷', '失神']]","chEntries":["扔","拋","擲","搖晃","顛簸","昏迷","失神"],"practiceMeaning":"她感到頭暈，不得不仰起頭。","analysis":"源自斯堪地那維亞語系，意為 'to throw' (扔)。\n    1. 扔、拋：指向上或隨機地扔東西，如 'toss a ball' (扔球)。\n    2. 搖晃、顛簸：指物體或人被拋起又落下，或在水中、風中劇烈晃動，如 'the boat was tossed by the waves' (船被海浪顛簸)。\n    3. 昏迷、失神：指因為身體不適或受傷而暫時失去意識，或感覺頭暈，如 'he tossed and turned all night' (他整晚翻來覆去睡不著)。","definition":"1. throw (something) with a quick, light movement of the hand and wrist.; 2. move or cause to move with a sudden jerking motion.; 3. lose consciousness for a short time.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He tossed the coin to decide who should go first.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他拋硬幣決定誰先走。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The ship was tossed about in the storm.\",\n    \"ch\": \"船在風暴中顛簸。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She felt faint and had to toss her head back.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她感到頭暈，不得不仰起頭。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她感到頭暈，不得不仰起頭。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3888,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::tough::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Leather is a ____ material.","expectedAnswer":"tough","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Leather is a ____ material.","clozeAnswer":"tough","exampleTranslation":"皮革是一種堅韌的材料。","reference":{"eng":"tough","kk":"/tʌf/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['困難的', '艱難的'], ['堅強的', '頑固的'], ['嚴厲的'], ['強韌的', '堅韌的']]","chEntries":["困難的","艱難的","堅強的","頑固的","嚴厲的","強韌的","堅韌的"],"practiceMeaning":"皮革是一種堅韌的材料。","analysis":"源自古英語 'tōh'，意為「韌性的」。核心是「難以處理」或「不易被改變」。可指事情的難度、人的堅韌或頑固、物質的堅固或不易破損。","definition":"1. difficult to overcome or deal with. 2. strong and resilient; not easily broken or cut. 3. able to endure hardship or adversity. 4. severe or harsh.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It was a tough decision to make.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個艱難的決定。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He's a tough negotiator.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他是一位強硬的談判者。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Leather is a tough material.\",\n    \"ch\": \"皮革是一種堅韌的材料。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The police were tough on the criminals.\",\n    \"ch\": \"警方對罪犯採取了嚴厲的措施。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"皮革是一種堅韌的材料。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字、龍騰課本","unitName":"C3U1、L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4566,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u11::trail::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The weaker runners began to ____ behind.","expectedAnswer":"trail","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The weaker runners began to ____ behind.","clozeAnswer":"trail","exampleTranslation":"較弱的選手們開始落後了。","reference":{"eng":"trail","kk":"/treɪl/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['跟蹤', '追蹤'], ['（緩慢地）移動', '拖曳'], ['（體力、精神等）衰退', '落後']]","chEntries":["跟蹤","追蹤","移動","拖曳","衰退","落後"],"practiceMeaning":"較弱的選手們開始落後了。","analysis":"動詞用法源自名詞。\n    1. 跟蹤、追蹤：指緊隨其後。\n    2. 移動、拖曳：指物體緩慢地移動，並在後面留下痕跡。\n    3. 衰退、落後：指速度、能力或狀態下降，落後於前面的人。","definition":"1. move in a long, thin line or track.; 2. follow behind (someone or something) at a distance.; 3. fall behind in progress, movement, or development.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The detective trailed the suspect through the city.\",\n    \"ch\": \"偵探在城市裡跟蹤嫌疑人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her long dress trailed on the floor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的長裙拖在地板上。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The weaker runners began to trail behind.\",\n    \"ch\": \"較弱的選手們開始落後了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"較弱的選手們開始落後了。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U11"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5107,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::transmission::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He learned how to change the car's ____.","expectedAnswer":"transmission","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He learned how to change the car's ____.","clozeAnswer":"transmission","exampleTranslation":"他學會了如何更換汽車的變速器。","reference":{"eng":"transmission","kk":"trænzˈmɪʃn","tense":"n.","ch":"[['傳輸'], ['傳播'], ['變速器']]","chEntries":["傳輸","傳播","變速器"],"practiceMeaning":"他學會了如何更換汽車的變速器。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'transmittere'，由 'trans-' (across) + 'mittere' (to send) 構成，原意是 '送過、傳遞'。'Transmission' 的核心語義是 '從一個地方或個體傳遞到另一個地方或個體的過程'。這可以指能量、資訊（如無線電訊號）、疾病（如病毒傳播）、或動力的傳遞（如汽車的變速器）。","definition":"1. The act or process of transmitting something.; 2. The sending of something across places or to people.; 3. (In a vehicle) a system for transmitting mechanical power and torque from the engine to the driven parts.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The transmission of the virus can occur through airborne droplets.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該病毒可通過空氣飛沫傳播。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The radio transmission was clear.\",\n    \"ch\": \"無線電的傳輸很清晰。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He learned how to change the car's transmission.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他學會了如何更換汽車的變速器。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他學會了如何更換汽車的變速器。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5431,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::transport::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This software can ____ data between different systems.","expectedAnswer":"transport","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This software can ____ data between different systems.","clozeAnswer":"transport","exampleTranslation":"該軟體可以在不同系統之間傳輸數據。","reference":{"eng":"transport","kk":"ˈtrænspɔːrt","tense":"v.","ch":"[['運輸'], ['運送'], ['傳輸'], ['使放逐']]","chEntries":["運輸","運送","傳輸","使放逐"],"practiceMeaning":"該軟體可以在不同系統之間傳輸數據。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 \"transportare\"，意為\"搬運\"、\"運送\"。其中 \"trans-\" 是表示\"跨越\"、\"穿越\"的字首，\"portare\" 則是\"攜帶\"、\"運送\"的意思。構詞上，\"trans-\" 提供了移動的「方向」或「跨越」的語意，\"portare\" 提供了核心的「攜帶」動作。因此，\"transport\" 的核心語義是「跨越空間地攜帶」，引申為「運輸」、「運送」。也可指「傳輸」信息或能量，或引申為「使放逐」。","definition":"to carry something or someone from one place to another; to move goods or people from one place to another; to move or convey from one place to another.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company transports goods by sea and air.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司通過海運和空運運輸貨物。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He was transported to a hospital after the accident.\",\n    \"ch\": \"事故發生後，他被送往醫院。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This software can transport data between different systems.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該軟體可以在不同系統之間傳輸數據。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該軟體可以在不同系統之間傳輸數據。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5432,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::transportation::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The country relies heavily on air ____ for international trade.","expectedAnswer":"transportation","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The country relies heavily on air ____ for international trade.","clozeAnswer":"transportation","exampleTranslation":"該國嚴重依賴航空運輸進行國際貿易。","reference":{"eng":"transportation","kk":"ˌtrænspɔːrˈteɪʃn","tense":"n.","ch":"[['運輸'], ['交通'], ['運輸工具'], ['放逐']]","chEntries":["運輸","交通","運輸工具","放逐"],"practiceMeaning":"該國嚴重依賴航空運輸進行國際貿易。","analysis":"此字為派生詞，由動詞 \"transport\" 加上名詞化字尾 \"-ation\" 構成。\"transport\" 源自拉丁語 \"transportare\"，意為\"搬運\"、\"運送\"，由 \"trans-\" (跨越) 和 \"portare\" (攜帶) 組成。構詞上，\"trans-\" 提供了移動的「方向」或「跨越」的語意，\"portare\" 提供了核心的「攜帶」動作。字尾 \"-ation\" 將動詞的「運輸」行為轉化為抽象名詞。因此，\"transportation\" 指的是「運輸」的系統、過程、行業，或是「交通」方式。也可指「運輸工具」或「放逐」的行為。","definition":"the action of transporting someone or something or the process of being transported; the system or means of carrying passengers or goods from place to place.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Public transportation in the city is efficient.\",\n    \"ch\": \"市區的公共交通系統很有效率。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The cost of transportation has increased significantly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"運輸成本已顯著增加。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The country relies heavily on air transportation for international trade.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該國嚴重依賴航空運輸進行國際貿易。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該國嚴重依賴航空運輸進行國際貿易。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3275,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::treasure::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This old book is a real ____.","expectedAnswer":"treasure","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This old book is a real ____.","clozeAnswer":"treasure","exampleTranslation":"這本舊書是真正的珍寶。","reference":{"eng":"treasure","kk":"/ˈtrɛʒər/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['寶藏；財寶'], ['珍寶；極有價值的人或物'], ['（尤指）儲藏的財富']]","chEntries":["寶藏","財寶","珍寶","極有價值的人或物","儲藏的財富"],"practiceMeaning":"這本舊書是真正的珍寶。","analysis":"源自古法語 'tresor'，來自拉丁語 'thesaurus' (寶庫)。指非常珍貴、有價值或被儲存起來的物品，可以是物質的（金銀珠寶）或非物質的（才能、回憶）。","definition":"1. a quantity of valuable things, such as gold, jewels, and coins; 2. a person or thing that is greatly valued or cherished; 3. a collection of valuable objects, especially one that has been carefully collected over a period of time.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Pirates buried their treasure on the island.\",\n    \"ch\": \"海盜們把他們的寶藏埋在了島上。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her children are her greatest treasure.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的孩子是她最大的寶貝。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This old book is a real treasure.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這本舊書是真正的珍寶。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這本舊書是真正的珍寶。","sourceName":"字彙王、龍騰課本","unitName":"U42、L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4525,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::trouble::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She is having ____ sleeping.","expectedAnswer":"trouble","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She is having ____ sleeping.","clozeAnswer":"trouble","exampleTranslation":"她睡眠方面有些困難。","reference":{"eng":"trouble","kk":"/ˈtrʌbl/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['麻煩'], ['困難'], ['憂慮'], ['（健康）病痛']]","chEntries":["麻煩","困難","憂慮","病痛"],"practiceMeaning":"她睡眠方面有些困難。","analysis":"源自古法語 troble，來自拉丁語 turba，意為「混亂」、「人群」。核心語意是「混亂、干擾」。引申為「困難」、「麻煩」、「憂慮」、「疾病」等。","definition":"1. Difficulty or problems; 2. Worry or anxiety; 3. A state of commotion or disturbance.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He got into trouble with the law.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他捲入了法律麻煩。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I don't want to cause you any trouble.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我不想給你帶來任何麻煩。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is having trouble sleeping.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她睡眠方面有些困難。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她睡眠方面有些困難。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6145,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::tumor::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Early detection of the ____ is crucial.","expectedAnswer":"tumor","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Early detection of the ____ is crucial.","clozeAnswer":"tumor","exampleTranslation":"早期發現腫瘤至關重要。","reference":{"eng":"tumor","kk":"ˈtuːmər","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"腫瘤\"  ],  [    \"腫塊\"  ]]","chEntries":["腫瘤","腫塊"],"practiceMeaning":"早期發現腫瘤至關重要。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 tumor，意為「腫脹；鼓起」，來自 tumēre（腫脹）。原始印歐語詞根 *tu- 可能與「鼓起；腫起」有關。此名詞指身體上異常的腫塊，通常是由異常細胞增殖而成。其語意演變是從「腫脹」到「病理性的腫塊」。","definition":"A swelling of a part of the body, generally without pain or fever, caused by an abnormal growth of tissue.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The doctor diagnosed a benign tumor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"醫生診斷出一個良性腫瘤。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Surgery was required to remove the tumor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"手術是為了移除腫瘤。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Early detection of the tumor is crucial.\",\n    \"ch\": \"早期發現腫瘤至關重要。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"早期發現腫瘤至關重要。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3947,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::underlying::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ layer of soil is rich in nutrients.","expectedAnswer":"underlying","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ layer of soil is rich in nutrients.","clozeAnswer":"underlying","exampleTranslation":"下面的土壤層富含營養。","reference":{"eng":"underlying","kk":"/ˌʌndərˈlaɪɪŋ/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['潛在的', '根本的'], ['在下面的']]","chEntries":["潛在的","根本的","在下面的"],"practiceMeaning":"下面的土壤層富含營養。","analysis":"由 'under' (介詞，在…下面) 和 'lying' (動詞 'lie' 的現在分詞) 組成。指位於表面之下，但對事物有重要影響的，即「潛在的、根本的」；也可以指實際位於物理下方的位置。","definition":"1. fundamental; basic; 2. located below.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to address the underlying causes of the problem.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要解決問題的根本原因。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There are underlying tensions in the community.\",\n    \"ch\": \"社區中存在潛在的緊張關係。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The underlying layer of soil is rich in nutrients.\",\n    \"ch\": \"下面的土壤層富含營養。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"下面的土壤層富含營養。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5108,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::undertake::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They will ____ further research.","expectedAnswer":"undertake","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They will ____ further research.","clozeAnswer":"undertake","exampleTranslation":"他們將從事進一步的研究。","reference":{"eng":"undertake","kk":"ˌʌndərˈteɪk","tense":"v.","ch":"[['承擔'], ['從事'], ['保證']]","chEntries":["承擔","從事","保證"],"practiceMeaning":"他們將從事進一步的研究。","analysis":"此字由 'under-' (under) + 'take' (拿、做) 構成。'Under-' 在此表示 '在……之下' 或 '承擔（責任）'。'Undertake' 的核心語義是 '承擔某項任務、責任或工作，通常是重大的、艱鉅的或需要承諾的'。它強調了 '接受並開始執行' 的過程，並隱含著一種責任感。","definition":"1. To commit oneself to and begin or accept (a task or course of action).; 2. To contract to do (work) for another party.; 3. To pledge oneself to do.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company undertook a major construction project.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司承擔了一個大型建築專案。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She undertook to finish the report by Friday.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她保證星期五前完成報告。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They will undertake further research.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們將從事進一步的研究。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們將從事進一步的研究。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3899,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::unique::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She has a ____ talent for music.","expectedAnswer":"unique","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She has a ____ talent for music.","clozeAnswer":"unique","exampleTranslation":"她有著獨特的音樂天賦。","reference":{"eng":"unique","kk":"/juˈniːk/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['獨一無二的', '獨特的'], ['罕見的']]","chEntries":["獨一無二的","獨特的","罕見的"],"practiceMeaning":"她有著獨特的音樂天賦。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'unicus'，'unus' (one) 的衍生詞。核心是「只有一個」。引申為與所有其他事物都不同，因此是獨特的、特別的。","definition":"1. being the only one of its kind; unlike anything else. 2. unusual, special, or rare.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Each snowflake is unique.\",\n    \"ch\": \"每一片雪花都是獨一無二的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a unique opportunity.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個獨特的機會。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a unique talent for music.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她有著獨特的音樂天賦。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她有著獨特的音樂天賦。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3870,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u1::unite::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Let us ____ our efforts to achieve this goal.","expectedAnswer":"unite","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Let us ____ our efforts to achieve this goal.","clozeAnswer":"unite","exampleTranslation":"讓我們團結力量以達成這個目標。","reference":{"eng":"unite","kk":"/juˈnaɪt/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['結合', '統一'], ['連合']]","chEntries":["結合","統一","連合"],"practiceMeaning":"讓我們團結力量以達成這個目標。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'unitus'，'unus' (one) 的過去分詞。核心概念是使之成為一。引申為團結、聯合，或使國家、組織等歸於統一。","definition":"1. to bring together or form into one whole; combine; join: to unite the states. 2. to join in an action, for a common cause, or for mutual benefit: to unite in protest. 3. to combine for a common purpose; merge: The companies united to form a larger corporation.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The people united to demand their rights.\",\n    \"ch\": \"人民團結起來要求他們的權利。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The two small kingdoms united to form a larger empire.\",\n    \"ch\": \"兩個小王國合併成一個大帝國。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Let us unite our efforts to achieve this goal.\",\n    \"ch\": \"讓我們團結力量以達成這個目標。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"讓我們團結力量以達成這個目標。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U1"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6149,"wordRef":"字彙王::u65::unprecedented::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This is an ____ opportunity.","expectedAnswer":"unprecedented","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This is an ____ opportunity.","clozeAnswer":"unprecedented","exampleTranslation":"這是一個前所未有的機會。","reference":{"eng":"unprecedented","kk":"ʌnˈprɛsɪdɛntɪd","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"前所未有的\"  ],  [    \"史無前例的\"  ]]","chEntries":["前所未有的","史無前例的"],"practiceMeaning":"這是一個前所未有的機會。","analysis":"此字由否定字首 un-（不）、precedent（先例）和形容詞後綴 -ed 構成。precedent 源自拉丁語 praecedēns，是 praecedere（先行）的現在分詞，意為「先前的；在前的」。因此，unprecedented 的核心語義是「沒有先例的」。此形容詞表示某事物是第一次發生，沒有先前的例子可循，非常新穎或獨特。其語意演變是從「沒有之前發生的事情」到「史無前例」。","definition":"Never done or known before.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company achieved unprecedented success.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司取得了前所未有的成功。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The pandemic caused unprecedented disruption.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這場大流行病造成了史無前例的擾亂。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is an unprecedented opportunity.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個前所未有的機會。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這是一個前所未有的機會。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U65"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5441,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::urban::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Many people move from rural areas to ____ centers for work.","expectedAnswer":"urban","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Many people move from rural areas to ____ centers for work.","clozeAnswer":"urban","exampleTranslation":"許多人為了工作而從鄉村地區遷往城市中心。","reference":{"eng":"urban","kk":"ˈɜːrbən","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['城市的'], ['都市的']]","chEntries":["城市的","都市的"],"practiceMeaning":"許多人為了工作而從鄉村地區遷往城市中心。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 \"urbanus\"，意為\"城市的\"、\"屬城市居民的\"，來自 \"urbs\" (城市)。構詞上，\"urban-\" 提供了核心的「城市」語意，\"-us\" 是拉丁語的形容詞字尾。 \"Urban\" 形容與城市相關的事物，包括城市本身、城市的特徵、或城市中的生活方式，與\"rural\" (鄉村的) 形成對比。","definition":"relating to, characteristic of, or found in a city or town; relating to cities rather than rural areas.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The city has a vibrant urban culture.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座城市擁有充滿活力的都市文化。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Urban planning is a complex field.\",\n    \"ch\": \"都市規劃是一個複雜的領域。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Many people move from rural areas to urban centers for work.\",\n    \"ch\": \"許多人為了工作而從鄉村地區遷往城市中心。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"許多人為了工作而從鄉村地區遷往城市中心。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5445,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l3::urgent::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Emergency services responded to an ____ call.","expectedAnswer":"urgent","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Emergency services responded to an ____ call.","clozeAnswer":"urgent","exampleTranslation":"緊急服務部門響應了一個緊急呼叫。","reference":{"eng":"urgent","kk":"ˈɜːrdʒənt","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['緊急的'], ['急迫的'], ['緊迫的']]","chEntries":["緊急的","急迫的","緊迫的"],"practiceMeaning":"緊急服務部門響應了一個緊急呼叫。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 \"urgens\"，是動詞 \"urgere\" (催促、驅使、緊迫) 的現在分詞。\"urgere\" 的詞源不明確，但與\"torque\" (扭轉、轉動) 有聯繫，可能表示\"被推動\"或\"被施壓\"。構詞上，\"urg-\" 提供了核心的「催促」、「緊迫」語意，\"-ent\" 是形容詞字尾。 \"Urgent\" 形容某事「需要立即關注或處理」，具有「急迫性」或「緊迫性」。","definition":"requiring immediate action or attention; pressing; demanding prompt action.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We have an urgent deadline to meet.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們有一個緊急的截止日期要遵守。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is an urgent matter that requires your immediate attention.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是需要你立即關注的緊急事項。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Emergency services responded to an urgent call.\",\n    \"ch\": \"緊急服務部門響應了一個緊急呼叫。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"緊急服務部門響應了一個緊急呼叫。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L3"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5866,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::variation::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The orchestra performed a ____ on the theme.","expectedAnswer":"variation","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The orchestra performed a ____ on the theme.","clozeAnswer":"variation","exampleTranslation":"樂團演奏了該主題的變奏曲。","reference":{"eng":"variation","kk":"ˌveəriˈeɪʃn","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"變化\"  ],  [    \"差異\"  ],  [    \"變異\"  ],  [    \"變奏\"  ]]","chEntries":["變化","差異","變異","變奏"],"practiceMeaning":"樂團演奏了該主題的變奏曲。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'variatio'，是 'variare' (to change, alter) 的名詞形式。'Variare' 來自 'varius' (various, diverse)。'-ion' 是常見的名詞字尾，表示「過程」、「狀態」或「結果」。'Variation' 的核心語意是指「改變」、「差異」或「一種與標準不同的形式」。它可以指事物在數量、程度、形式或性質上的不同，也可以指物種的遺傳變異，或音樂中的主題變奏。例如，也可指「一種變奏形式」。","definition":"1. A change or difference between two or more similar things.; 2. The process or result of varying.; 3. A deviation from a standard or norm.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There are noticeable variations in temperature.\",\n    \"ch\": \"溫度存在明顯的差異。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Genetic variation is essential for evolution.\",\n    \"ch\": \"遺傳變異對演化至關重要。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The orchestra performed a variation on the theme.\",\n    \"ch\": \"樂團演奏了該主題的變奏曲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We observed a slight variation in the results.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們觀察到結果有輕微的差異。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"樂團演奏了該主題的變奏曲。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3928,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::various::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The shop sells ____ kinds of tea.","expectedAnswer":"various","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The shop sells ____ kinds of tea.","clozeAnswer":"various","exampleTranslation":"這家店販售各種茶葉。","reference":{"eng":"various","kk":"/ˈveəriəs/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['各種的', '不同的'], ['多樣的']]","chEntries":["各種的","不同的","多樣的"],"practiceMeaning":"這家店販售各種茶葉。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'varius' (意為「多樣的、變化的」)。形容事物有多種不同的種類、形式或情況。","definition":"1. different; of different kinds; 2. many and different.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We offer various courses to suit your needs.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們提供各種課程以滿足您的需求。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There are various reasons why this happened.\",\n    \"ch\": \"發生這種事有各種各樣的原因。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The shop sells various kinds of tea.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家店販售各種茶葉。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這家店販售各種茶葉。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3916,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::vary::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We need to ____ our approach to solve this problem.","expectedAnswer":"vary","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We need to ____ our approach to solve this problem.","clozeAnswer":"vary","exampleTranslation":"我們需要改變我們的策略來解決這個問題。","reference":{"eng":"vary","kk":"/ˈveəri/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['變化', '改變'], ['不同', '相異']]","chEntries":["變化","改變","不同","相異"],"practiceMeaning":"我們需要改變我們的策略來解決這個問題。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'varius' (意為「多樣的、變化的」)。最初的意義是「改變、不同」，引申為「使…有所不同」或「本身有所不同」。","definition":"1. to be different from each other; 2. to change or be different over time; 3. to make something different.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The prices vary depending on the season.\",\n    \"ch\": \"價格會因季節而異。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her mood tends to vary from day to day.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的心情往往每天都有所變化。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to vary our approach to solve this problem.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要改變我們的策略來解決這個問題。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們需要改變我們的策略來解決這個問題。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6251,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::vein::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The marble had a beautiful ____ pattern.","expectedAnswer":"vein","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The marble had a beautiful ____ pattern.","clozeAnswer":"vein","exampleTranslation":"大理石有著美麗的紋路。","reference":{"eng":"vein","kk":"veɪn","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"靜脈\"  ],  [    \"血管\"  ],  [    \"礦脈\"  ],  [    \"紋路\"  ],  [    \"風格\"  ]]","chEntries":["靜脈","血管","礦脈","紋路","風格"],"practiceMeaning":"大理石有著美麗的紋路。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 fēn，向上可追溯至拉丁語 vena，意為「血管，水道」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。名詞義指將血液從身體各部位輸送到心臟的血管，也引申指礦藏所在的「礦脈」，物體表面的「紋路」，或人或事物中某種「風格」或「特質」。中文翻譯為「靜脈；血管；礦脈；紋路；風格」。","definition":"1. one of the tubes that carry blood from the body to the heart; 2. a line of mineral ore within a rock; 3. a pattern of lines in something, such as a leaf or a piece of wood; 4. a particular style or manner.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The nurse drew blood from a vein in his arm.\",\n    \"ch\": \"護士從他手臂的一條靜脈抽了血。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Geologists searched for a vein of gold.\",\n    \"ch\": \"地質學家們在尋找金礦脈。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The marble had a beautiful vein pattern.\",\n    \"ch\": \"大理石有著美麗的紋路。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His writing has a sarcastic vein.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的寫作帶有一種諷刺的風格。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"大理石有著美麗的紋路。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6252,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::venue::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The court is the ____ for the legal proceedings.","expectedAnswer":"venue","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The court is the ____ for the legal proceedings.","clozeAnswer":"venue","exampleTranslation":"法院是法律訴訟的發生地點。","reference":{"eng":"venue","kk":"ˈvɛnju","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"場地\"  ],  [    \"地點\"  ],  [    \"場所\"  ]]","chEntries":["場地","地點","場所"],"practiceMeaning":"法院是法律訴訟的發生地點。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 venue，意為「到來，地點」，向上可追溯至拉丁語 venire，意為「來」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。名詞義指某事將要發生的地點，特別是活動、演出、會議或運動比賽的場所。中文翻譯為「場地；地點；場所」。","definition":"1. the place where an organized event such as a concert, conference, or sporting event takes place; 2. the place where an action or event happens.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The stadium is a popular venue for concerts.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個體育場是舉辦音樂會的熱門場地。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We are looking for a venue for our wedding reception.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們正在為我們的婚禮招待會尋找一個場所。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The court is the venue for the legal proceedings.\",\n    \"ch\": \"法院是法律訴訟的發生地點。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"法院是法律訴訟的發生地點。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4469,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::violence::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The storm caused considerable ____ to the coastline.","expectedAnswer":"violence","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The storm caused considerable ____ to the coastline.","clozeAnswer":"violence","exampleTranslation":"風暴對海岸線造成了相當大的破壞。","reference":{"eng":"violence","kk":"/ˈvaɪələns/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['暴力'], ['猛烈'], ['（行為）不文明']]","chEntries":["暴力","猛烈","不文明"],"practiceMeaning":"風暴對海岸線造成了相當大的破壞。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 violentia，來自 violare，意為「侵犯」、「粗暴對待」。核心語意是「使用武力或力量造成傷害或破壞」。","definition":"1. Behavior involving physical force intended to hurt, damage, or kill someone or something; 2. Intense or uncontrolled force.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The film depicted scenes of extreme violence.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這部電影描繪了極端暴力的場面。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was a sudden outbreak of violence in the city.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這座城市突然爆發了暴力事件。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The storm caused considerable violence to the coastline.\",\n    \"ch\": \"風暴對海岸線造成了相當大的破壞。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"風暴對海岸線造成了相當大的破壞。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3294,"wordRef":"字彙王::u42::virus::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Fear can spread like a ____ through a crowd.","expectedAnswer":"virus","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Fear can spread like a ____ through a crowd.","clozeAnswer":"virus","exampleTranslation":"恐懼會像病毒一樣在人群中傳播。","reference":{"eng":"virus","kk":"/ˈvaɪərəs/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['病毒'], ['（計算機）病毒'], ['（不良思想、情感等的）傳染性因素；毒害']]","chEntries":["病毒","傳染性因素","毒害"],"practiceMeaning":"恐懼會像病毒一樣在人群中傳播。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'virus' (毒液，黏液)。指一種非細胞性的傳染因子，只能在宿主細胞內複製。引申至計算機領域，指惡意代碼。也可用於比喻，指像病毒一樣傳播開來的負面事物。","definition":"1. a submicroscopic infectious agent that replicates only inside the living cells of an organism; 2. a piece of code that is capable of copying itself and spreading from one computer to another, usually causing harm; 3. something that is able to infect and harm others.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The flu is caused by a virus.\",\n    \"ch\": \"流感是由病毒引起的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"My computer was infected by a virus.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我的電腦被病毒感染了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Fear can spread like a virus through a crowd.\",\n    \"ch\": \"恐懼會像病毒一樣在人群中傳播。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"恐懼會像病毒一樣在人群中傳播。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U42"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4201,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::visible::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"His relief was ____.","expectedAnswer":"visible","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"His relief was ____.","clozeAnswer":"visible","exampleTranslation":"他的寬慰顯而易見。","reference":{"eng":"visible","kk":"/ˈvɪzəbl/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['可見的；看得見的'], ['顯著的；明顯的']]","chEntries":["可見的","看得見的","顯著的","明顯的"],"practiceMeaning":"他的寬慰顯而易見。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 visibilis，'videre'（看）+ '-ibilis'（可…的）。字面意思是“可被看見的”。1. “可見的”指客觀上處於可視範圍內。2. “顯著的；明顯的”是抽象意義，指某事物能夠被注意到，其影響或存在是清晰的。","definition":"1. able to be seen; 2. easily seen or noticed; apparent.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The stars are visible tonight.\",\n    \"ch\": \"今晚星星清晰可見。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was a visible increase in their profits.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們的利潤有了顯著的增長。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His relief was visible.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的寬慰顯而易見。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他的寬慰顯而易見。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4048,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u4::vocabulary::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Learning new ____ is essential for language acquisition.","expectedAnswer":"vocabulary","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Learning new ____ is essential for language acquisition.","clozeAnswer":"vocabulary","exampleTranslation":"學習新詞彙是語言習得的關鍵。","reference":{"eng":"vocabulary","kk":"/voʊˈkæbjəlɛri/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['詞彙', '詞彙量'], ['（某領域的）術語']]","chEntries":["詞彙","詞彙量","術語"],"practiceMeaning":"學習新詞彙是語言習得的關鍵。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'vocabularium'，意為「詞的列表」，來自 'vocabulum' (a word)，'vocabulum' 又來自 'vocare' (to call)。核心是「被稱為的詞」。引申為個人所知的詞語總匯（詞彙量），以及特定領域或行業使用的專門術語。","definition":"1. all the words that someone knows or uses; 2. all the words that exist in a language; 3. a set of words used in a particular subject or field","example":"[\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"她的英語詞彙量很大。\",\n    \"eng\": \"She has a large English vocabulary.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"這本書介紹了工程師的技術術語。\",\n    \"eng\": \"This book introduces technical vocabulary for engineers.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"ch\": \"學習新詞彙是語言習得的關鍵。\",\n    \"eng\": \"Learning new vocabulary is essential for language acquisition.\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"學習新詞彙是語言習得的關鍵。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U4"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3941,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u2::weakness::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company acknowledged its ____ in marketing.","expectedAnswer":"weakness","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company acknowledged its ____ in marketing.","clozeAnswer":"weakness","exampleTranslation":"該公司承認其在行銷方面的弱點。","reference":{"eng":"weakness","kk":"/ˈwiːknəs/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['虛弱', '軟弱'], ['弱點', '缺點']]","chEntries":["虛弱","軟弱","弱點","缺點"],"practiceMeaning":"該公司承認其在行銷方面的弱點。","analysis":"源自古英語 'wācnes'，由 'wāc' (意為「軟弱的」) 和 '-nes' (名詞後綴，表示「狀態」) 組成。指身體、精神上的虛弱，或指能力、性格上的不足或缺點。","definition":"1. the state of being weak; 2. a fault or failing.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His greatest weakness is his lack of confidence.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他最大的弱點是缺乏自信。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The old man was overcome by weakness.\",\n    \"ch\": \"老人因虛弱而倒下。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company acknowledged its weakness in marketing.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該公司承認其在行銷方面的弱點。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該公司承認其在行銷方面的弱點。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U2"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5816,"wordRef":"字彙王::u60::whereas::conj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The plan is expensive, ____ the alternative is less effective.","expectedAnswer":"whereas","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The plan is expensive, ____ the alternative is less effective.","clozeAnswer":"whereas","exampleTranslation":"這個計劃很昂貴，而另一種選擇效果較差。","reference":{"eng":"whereas","kk":"ˌwɛərˈæz","tense":"conj.","ch":"[  [    \"然而\"  ],  [    \"比較起來\"  ],  [    \"鑒於\"  ]]","chEntries":["然而","比較起來","鑒於"],"practiceMeaning":"這個計劃很昂貴，而另一種選擇效果較差。","analysis":"此字為連接詞，源自中古英語wheras，由where（在哪裡）+as（如同；和）組成。核心語義是「用來連接兩個對比或比較的子句，表示前者與後者之間的差異」。語意演變上，從「在哪裡……如同……」，演變為表示「對比」或「儘管如此」的連接詞。","definition":"1. in contrast or comparison with; 2. in view of the fact that; because.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Some people like to travel abroad, whereas others prefer to stay home.\",\n    \"ch\": \"有些人喜歡出國旅行，而有些人則偏好待在家裡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is very outgoing, whereas his brother is quite shy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他非常外向，而他的兄弟則相當害羞。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The plan is expensive, whereas the alternative is less effective.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個計劃很昂貴，而另一種選擇效果較差。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這個計劃很昂貴，而另一種選擇效果較差。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U60"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5113,"wordRef":"字彙王::u61::wither::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The old man seemed to ____ with grief.","expectedAnswer":"wither","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The old man seemed to ____ with grief.","clozeAnswer":"wither","exampleTranslation":"老人似乎因悲傷而日漸憔悴。","reference":{"eng":"wither","kk":"ˈwɪðər","tense":"v.","ch":"[['枯萎'], ['凋謝'], ['衰敗']]","chEntries":["枯萎","凋謝","衰敗"],"practiceMeaning":"老人似乎因悲傷而日漸憔悴。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 'wiðerian'，意為 '枯萎、乾枯'。其核心語義是 '由於缺乏水分、養分或活力而變得乾癟、萎縮並失去生命力'。這通常用於植物，但也可比喻形容人、事業或情感的衰退、衰敗或失去活力。","definition":"1. To become weak and dry through lack of water.; 2. To become dry and shriveled.; 3. To lose strength or vigor.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The flowers began to wither in the heat.\",\n    \"ch\": \"花兒在炎熱中開始枯萎。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His enthusiasm for the project withered away.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對這個專案的熱情逐漸消退。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The old man seemed to wither with grief.\",\n    \"ch\": \"老人似乎因悲傷而日漸憔悴。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"老人似乎因悲傷而日漸憔悴。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U61"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5591,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::without-a-doubt::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He will, ____, succeed in his endeavors.","expectedAnswer":"without a doubt","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He will, ____, succeed in his endeavors.","clozeAnswer":"without a doubt","exampleTranslation":"他肯定會在他的事業上取得成功。","reference":{"eng":"without a doubt","kk":"wɪˈðaʊt ə daʊt","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['無疑地'], ['毫無疑問地']]","chEntries":["無疑地","毫無疑問地"],"practiceMeaning":"他肯定會在他的事業上取得成功。","analysis":"此片語由介詞 \"without\"（沒有），不定冠詞 \"a\"，名詞 \"doubt\"（懷疑）組成。\"without\" 表示「缺乏」。\"doubt\" 表示「懷疑、不確定」。\"without a doubt\" 是一個慣用語，字面意思是「沒有任何懷疑」，引申為「確定地、無疑地」。它用來強調說話者對某件事情的絕對確定性。","definition":"1. Certainly; undoubtedly; 2. Beyond any question or suspicion.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is without a doubt the best candidate for the job.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她毫無疑問是這個職位的最佳人選。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is without a doubt the most beautiful sunset I've ever seen.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這毫無疑問是我見過最美的日落。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He will, without a doubt, succeed in his endeavors.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他肯定會在他的事業上取得成功。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他肯定會在他的事業上取得成功。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4517,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::work::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"My car doesn't ____ anymore.","expectedAnswer":"work","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"My car doesn't ____ anymore.","clozeAnswer":"work","exampleTranslation":"我的車不能開了。","reference":{"eng":"work","kk":"/wɜːrk/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['工作'], ['起作用'], ['奏效'], ['（機器）運行']]","chEntries":["工作","起作用","奏效","運行"],"practiceMeaning":"我的車不能開了。","analysis":"源自古英語 weorc，意為「勞動」、「工作」。核心語意是「進行有目的的活動以生產成果」。引申為「機器運行」、「計劃奏效」等。","definition":"1. To perform work or tasks; 2. To function or operate properly; 3. To achieve a desired result.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She works in a hospital.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在一家醫院工作。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The new strategy is starting to work.\",\n    \"ch\": \"新的策略開始奏效了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"My car doesn't work anymore.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我的車不能開了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我的車不能開了。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6151,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::alien::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ species was discovered in the deep ocean.","expectedAnswer":"alien","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ species was discovered in the deep ocean.","clozeAnswer":"alien","exampleTranslation":"這種外星物種是在深海中發現的。","reference":{"eng":"alien","kk":"ˈeɪliən","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"外星人\"  ],  [    \"外籍人士\"  ],  [    \"不受歡迎的人\"  ],  [    \"無關係者\"  ]]","chEntries":["外星人","外籍人士","不受歡迎的人","無關係者"],"practiceMeaning":"這種外星物種是在深海中發現的。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 alienus，意為「別人的、外國的、不相干的」，為 alius「別的、其他的」之衍生詞。它進入中古英語 via 古法語 alien。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，應視為整體詞源演變。作為名詞，主要語義是來自另一個國家、地方或宇宙的人。詞源中的「外國的、不相干的」概念是核心，引申出「外籍人士」和「外星人」。後也用於比喻意義，指一個群體中格格不入或與之無關的人。","definition":"1. a being from outer space; 2. a person who lives in a country but is not a citizen of that country; 3. a person who is completely different from other people and not accepted by them; 4. a person who is not related to you.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The film depicts a terrifying alien invasion.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這部電影描繪了一場可怕的外星人入侵。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is an alien in his own country, treated with suspicion.\",\n    \"ch\": \"在他自己的國家，他被視為外人，受到懷疑。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Her ideas seemed alien to the rest of the group.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她的想法對團體中的其他人來說顯得很陌生。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The alien species was discovered in the deep ocean.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種外星物種是在深海中發現的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這種外星物種是在深海中發現的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6154,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::banner::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The team marched under its ____.","expectedAnswer":"banner","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The team marched under its ____.","clozeAnswer":"banner","exampleTranslation":"隊伍在他們的旗幟下行進。","reference":{"eng":"banner","kk":"ˈbænər","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"旗幟\"  ],  [    \"橫幅\"  ],  [    \"標語\"  ],  [    \"冠軍\"  ],  [    \"領袖\"  ]]","chEntries":["旗幟","橫幅","標語","冠軍","領袖"],"practiceMeaning":"隊伍在他們的旗幟下行進。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 banner、bandiere，意為「旗幟」，其最終詞源可能與日耳曼語系表示「綁帶」的詞根有關，例如古英語 band「綁帶」。在現代英語中，其核心語義是「旗幟」，特別是指用於飄揚、展示或標示的布條。詞源中的「綁帶」概念與旗幟的懸掛方式相關。除了字面上的「旗幟」和「橫幅」，它也引申為「冠軍」的象徵，或用於標示、宣傳的「標語」，以及某個運動或運動的「領袖人物」。","definition":"1. a long strip of cloth bearing a slogan or design, carried in a demonstration or procession or hung in a public place; 2. a large piece of cloth with a name or slogan on it, carried as a symbol; 3. a flag; 4. (often in plural) a person or thing that is a symbol of a particular quality or activity, or that is an outstanding example of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The protestors carried banners calling for peace.\",\n    \"ch\": \"抗議者們舉著呼籲和平的橫幅。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The winning team was awarded a championship banner.\",\n    \"ch\": \"獲勝隊伍被授予了冠軍旗幟。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She was the banner of the feminist movement.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她是女權運動的旗幟人物。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The team marched under its banner.\",\n    \"ch\": \"隊伍在他們的旗幟下行進。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"隊伍在他們的旗幟下行進。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6155,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::beware::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"____ of pickpockets in crowded areas.","expectedAnswer":"Beware","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"____ of pickpockets in crowded areas.","clozeAnswer":"Beware","exampleTranslation":"在擁擠的地區要小心扒手。","reference":{"eng":"beware","kk":"bɪˈwɛr","tense":"v.","ch":"[  [    \"警惕\"  ],  [    \"提防\"  ],  [    \"注意\"  ]]","chEntries":["警惕","提防","注意"],"practiceMeaning":"在擁擠的地區要小心扒手。","analysis":"此字源自中古英語 be+ware，意為「注意、警覺」。ware 本身是古英語 wær 的變體，意為「警覺的」。此字通常作為一個獨立的動詞或感嘆詞使用，其核心語義是「對潛在的危險或困難保持警惕」。它的結構由介詞 be- (表示強調或作為動詞前綴) 和形容詞/過去分詞 ware (警覺的) 組成，暗示著一種主動的、持續的警覺狀態。","definition":"1. be careful of (someone or something), especially by avoiding danger or harm.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Beware of the dog.\",\n    \"ch\": \"小心惡犬。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Drivers should beware of icy roads in winter.\",\n    \"ch\": \"司機在冬天應提防結冰的路面。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Beware! He is known for his deceitful tactics.\",\n    \"ch\": \"小心！他以狡猾的策略聞名。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Beware of pickpockets in crowded areas.\",\n    \"ch\": \"在擁擠的地區要小心扒手。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"在擁擠的地區要小心扒手。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5821,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::biological::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The drug has a strong ____ effect.","expectedAnswer":"biological","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The drug has a strong ____ effect.","clozeAnswer":"biological","exampleTranslation":"這種藥物有強烈的生理效應。","reference":{"eng":"biological","kk":"ˌbaɪəˈlɑːdʒɪkl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"生物的\"  ],  [    \"生物學的\"  ],  [    \"生理的\"  ]]","chEntries":["生物的","生物學的","生理的"],"practiceMeaning":"這種藥物有強烈的生理效應。","analysis":"此字由名詞 'biology' 加上形容詞字尾 '-ical' 構成。'Biology' 本身是一個複合詞，來自希臘語 'bios' (life) 和 '-logia' (study of, discourse)。'-logia' 來自 'logos' (word, speech, reason)。因此，'biology' 的字面意思是「生命的學問」。'-ical' 字尾用於將名詞轉化為形容詞，表示「關於……的」、「屬於……的」、「具有……性質的」。所以 'biological' 的意思就是「關於生物的」或「屬於生物學的」。另外，也可指「與生命體正常機能相關的」，即「生理的」。","definition":"1. Relating to or resulting from the functions of living organisms.; 2. Relating to biology.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The research focuses on biological processes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這項研究聚焦於生物過程。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Genetic engineering has many biological applications.\",\n    \"ch\": \"基因工程有許多生物學上的應用。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to consider the biological impact of the pollution.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要考慮污染的生物影響。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The drug has a strong biological effect.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這種藥物有強烈的生理效應。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這種藥物有強烈的生理效應。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5822,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::blast::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The music hit us with a ____ of sound.","expectedAnswer":"blast","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The music hit us with a ____ of sound.","clozeAnswer":"blast","exampleTranslation":"音樂以震耳欲聾的聲響衝擊著我們。","reference":{"eng":"blast","kk":"blæst","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"爆炸\"  ],  [    \"衝擊波\"  ],  [    \"陣風\"  ],  [    \"巨響\"  ]]","chEntries":["爆炸","衝擊波","陣風","巨響"],"practiceMeaning":"音樂以震耳欲聾的聲響衝擊著我們。","analysis":"此字詞源不明確，可能與原始日耳曼語 *blastaz（氣息、風）或 *blastōną（吹響）有關，與 'blossom'、'blow' 等詞有關聯。早期用於表示「爆炸」或「衝擊」。字義的演變可能與聲音或空氣的突然釋放有關。一個突發的、強烈的聲音或氣流可以被描述為 'blast'。例如，爆炸的衝擊波，或突然而強烈的風。現代語義擴展至形容音樂的「震耳欲聾」或「強烈的氣流」。例如，也可指「吹奏樂器的響亮聲音」。","definition":"1. An explosion or detonation.; 2. A strong gust of wind.; 3. A loud, short blast of a musical instrument or a siren.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The blast of the explosion was heard for miles.\",\n    \"ch\": \"爆炸的巨響遠達數英里。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"A strong blast of wind blew his hat off.\",\n    \"ch\": \"一陣強風吹掉了他的帽子。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The ship's horn gave a loud blast.\",\n    \"ch\": \"船的汽笛發出響亮的鳴響。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The music hit us with a blast of sound.\",\n    \"ch\": \"音樂以震耳欲聾的聲響衝擊著我們。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"音樂以震耳欲聾的聲響衝擊著我們。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5622,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l7::bold::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Please format the headings in ____.","expectedAnswer":"bold","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Please format the headings in ____.","clozeAnswer":"bold","exampleTranslation":"請將標題格式化為粗體。","reference":{"eng":"bold","kk":"boʊld","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['大膽的'], ['勇敢的'], ['魯莽的'], ['醒目的'], ['粗體的']]","chEntries":["大膽的","勇敢的","魯莽的","醒目的","粗體的"],"practiceMeaning":"請將標題格式化為粗體。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 'bāld'，其原始日耳曼語形式為 *balþuz。構詞學上，此字通常被視為一個整體詞，詞源與「強壯」、「大膽」相關。語意核心是「敢於冒險」、「不畏縮」。從「勇敢」、「無畏」引申出「魯莽」的負面含義。在印刷術中，指字體「粗體」，因為這種字體看起來更「醒目」、「強壯」。","definition":"1. Showing an ability to take risks; confident and courageous; 2. (Of a color, design, or shape) having a strong or vivid appearance; 3. (Of print) having the letters thicker and heavier than normal; 4. Showing an impudent lack of respect.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She was bold enough to ask for a raise.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她大膽到足以要求加薪。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The designer used bold colors in the artwork.\",\n    \"ch\": \"設計師在這件藝術品中使用了醒目的顏色。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He made a bold decision to invest in the startup.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他做出了大膽的決定，投資那家初創公司。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please format the headings in bold.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請將標題格式化為粗體。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"請將標題格式化為粗體。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L7"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6158,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::coherent::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"After the accident, he was unable to speak in a ____ manner.","expectedAnswer":"coherent","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"After the accident, he was unable to speak in a ____ manner.","clozeAnswer":"coherent","exampleTranslation":"事故發生後，他無法清晰地表達。","reference":{"eng":"coherent","kk":"koʊˈhɪərənt","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"連貫的\"  ],  [    \"條理清晰的\"  ],  [    \"前後一致的\"  ],  [    \"能理解的\"  ]]","chEntries":["連貫的","條理清晰的","前後一致的","能理解的"],"practiceMeaning":"事故發生後，他無法清晰地表達。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 cohaerēns，是 cohaerēre「緊密結合、一致」的現在分詞。cohaerēre 由 com- (together) + haerēre (to stick, cling) 組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 com-「一起」和 haerēre「黏合」是其核心語意來源。作為形容詞，其核心語義是「緊密結合，能夠清晰地理解」。從「黏合在一起」引申出「條理清晰、前後一致、易於理解」的語義，特別用於描述論點、計劃或思緒。詞源中的「黏合」概念是其連結性和一致性的基礎。","definition":"1. logical and consistent; 2. able to be understood or believed; 3. forming a whole; 4. (of a group of people) united.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His argument was coherent and well-supported.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的論點連貫且有充分的證據支持。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She found it difficult to make a coherent speech.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她發現很難發表一篇條理清晰的演講。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The team needs to present a coherent plan.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個團隊需要提出一個前後一致的計畫。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"After the accident, he was unable to speak in a coherent manner.\",\n    \"ch\": \"事故發生後，他無法清晰地表達。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"事故發生後，他無法清晰地表達。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3072,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::crack::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"That joke was a real ____!","expectedAnswer":"crack","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"That joke was a real ____!","clozeAnswer":"crack","exampleTranslation":"那個笑話真是太妙了！","reference":{"eng":"crack","kk":"/kræk/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['裂縫；縫隙'], ['爆裂聲；巨響'], ['（口語）嘗試；機會'], ['（口語）傑作；妙語']]","chEntries":["裂縫","縫隙","爆裂聲","巨響","嘗試","機會","傑作","妙語"],"practiceMeaning":"那個笑話真是太妙了！","analysis":"源自古英語 'crac' (a loud noise)，或與動詞 'crack' 同源。指「裂開」的狀態或由此產生的結果。\n1. 裂縫；縫隙：指物體表面或結構上出現的細長開口。\n2. 爆裂聲；巨響：指突然發出的、尖銳或響亮的聲音。\n3. （口語）嘗試；機會：指一次試驗或獲得某事的機會，常帶有一點冒險意味。\n4. （口語）傑作；妙語：指非常出色、令人印象深刻的事情或一句話。","definition":"1. a line on the surface of something along which it has split without breaking apart; 2. a sudden loud noise; 3. an attempt to do something; 4. a very good example of something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There is a crack in the wall.\",\n    \"ch\": \"牆上有道裂縫。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The thunder made a loud crack.\",\n    \"ch\": \"雷聲發出巨大的爆裂聲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is your last crack at the problem.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是你解決這個問題的最後一次機會。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"That joke was a real crack!\",\n    \"ch\": \"那個笑話真是太妙了！\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"那個笑話真是太妙了！","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6167,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::denial::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The company issued a ____ of the rumors.","expectedAnswer":"denial","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The company issued a ____ of the rumors.","clozeAnswer":"denial","exampleTranslation":"公司發布聲明否認這些謠言。","reference":{"eng":"denial","kk":"dɪˈnaɪəl","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"否認\"  ],  [    \"否定\"  ],  [    \"拒絕承認\"  ],  [    \"拒絕給予\"  ]]","chEntries":["否認","否定","拒絕承認","拒絕給予"],"practiceMeaning":"公司發布聲明否認這些謠言。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 denegare，意為「否認、拒絕」，由 de- (away, negating) + negare (to deny) 組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 de-「否定」和 negare「否認」是其核心語意來源。作為名詞，其核心語義是由動詞 deny「否認」名詞化而來，指「拒絕承認事實或真實性」，也指「拒絕給予某物」。詞源中的「否定」概念是其核心。此義項由「否認」的動作延伸出「拒絕承認」或「拒絕給予」的結果。","definition":"1. the action of declaring something to be untrue; 2. an act of refusing to acknowledge or accept something; 3. an act of refusing to grant or allow something.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His denial of the allegations was not convincing.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他對這些指控的否認並不可信。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She lived in denial about her illness.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對自己的病情一直處於否認狀態。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The request was met with denial.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個請求被拒絕了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company issued a denial of the rumors.\",\n    \"ch\": \"公司發布聲明否認這些謠言。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"公司發布聲明否認這些謠言。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6221,"wordRef":"字彙王::u67::derive::vt","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"We can ____ the formula from the given principles.","expectedAnswer":"derive","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"We can ____ the formula from the given principles.","clozeAnswer":"derive","exampleTranslation":"我們可以從給定的原理推導出這個公式。","reference":{"eng":"derive","kk":"dɪˈraɪv","tense":"vt.","ch":"[  [    \"獲得\"  ],  [    \"得到\"  ],  [    \"源自\"  ],  [    \"源於\"  ],  [    \"推導出\"  ]]","chEntries":["獲得","得到","源自","源於","推導出"],"practiceMeaning":"我們可以從給定的原理推導出這個公式。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 deriver，由 de-（表示源自，關於）和 river（河流）組成，意為「從…流出」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作及物動詞時，核心語義是從某個來源獲得、得到某物，特別是利益、知識、名稱或從某個源頭演變而來。在數學或邏輯上，也指從已知前提推導出結論。此及物動詞義必須接受詞，例如 derive income、derive pleasure、derive from sth.。中文翻譯為「獲得；得到；源自；源於；推導出」。","definition":"1. to get something, especially an advantage or pleasure, from something; 2. to come from or be descended from a particular person, place, or thing; 3. to reach a conclusion or an answer by reasoning.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Many people derive great pleasure from reading.\",\n    \"ch\": \"許多人從閱讀中獲得極大的樂趣。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This word is derived from Latin.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個詞源自拉丁語。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company derives its revenue from online sales.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司的收入來自於線上銷售。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We can derive the formula from the given principles.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們可以從給定的原理推導出這個公式。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"我們可以從給定的原理推導出這個公式。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U67"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5834,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::destructive::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Negative thinking can be ____.","expectedAnswer":"destructive","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Negative thinking can be ____.","clozeAnswer":"destructive","exampleTranslation":"消極思維可能是有害的。","reference":{"eng":"destructive","kk":"dɪˈstrʌktɪv","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"破壞性的\"  ],  [    \"毀滅性的\"  ],  [    \"有害的\"  ]]","chEntries":["破壞性的","毀滅性的","有害的"],"practiceMeaning":"消極思維可能是有害的。","analysis":"此字由拉丁語 'destructivus' 演變而來，是 'destruere' (to destroy) 的派生詞。'Destruere' 由 'de-' (down) 和 'struere' (to build, to pile up) 構成，字面意思是「拆毀」、「推倒」。'-ive' 是常見的形容詞字尾，表示「具有……性質的」。因此，'destructive' 指「具有破壞性質的」或「傾向於破壞」。它描述的是對事物造成損害、毀滅或瓦解的力量或行為。例如，也可指「對個人身心有害的」。","definition":"1. Causing great damage or destruction.; 2. Tending or likely to destroy.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The hurricane caused destructive winds.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這場颶風帶來了毀滅性的強風。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His criticism was destructive rather than constructive.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的批評具有破壞性而非建設性。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The wildfire had a destructive impact on the forest.\",\n    \"ch\": \"野火對森林造成了毀滅性的影響。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Negative thinking can be destructive.\",\n    \"ch\": \"消極思維可能是有害的。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"消極思維可能是有害的。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4350,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u8::element::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"There was an ____ of truth in his statement.","expectedAnswer":"element","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"There was an ____ of truth in his statement.","clozeAnswer":"element","exampleTranslation":"他的陳述中有一絲真理。","reference":{"eng":"element","kk":"/ˈɛlɪmənt/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['元素（化學）'], ['要素；成分'], ['（惡劣的）天氣；（危險的）環境'], ['（微量的）痕跡']]","chEntries":["元素","要素","成分","天氣","環境","痕跡"],"practiceMeaning":"他的陳述中有一絲真理。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 'elementum'，意為 'first principle, rudiment, element'。1. 指化學上構成物質的『基本元素』。2. 指構成事物的『基本要素、成分』。3. 指『惡劣的環境、條件』，如風雨、寒冷等，強調其粗獷、基礎的性質。4. 指『微量、痕跡』，如『一絲』、『一點』，強調其是某事物最基礎、最簡單的部分。","definition":"a part of something, especially a system or plan; any of the four basic substances: earth, air, fire, and water; a substance that cannot be broken down into simpler substances by chemical means; a small trace of something","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Oxygen is an element.\",\n    \"ch\": \"氧氣是一種元素。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Patience is an important element of success.\",\n    \"ch\": \"耐心是成功的重要要素。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They were exposed to the elements.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們遭受了風雨的侵襲。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There was an element of truth in his statement.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的陳述中有一絲真理。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他的陳述中有一絲真理。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U8"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6168,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::emission::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The car has low ____ levels.","expectedAnswer":"emission","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The car has low ____ levels.","clozeAnswer":"emission","exampleTranslation":"這輛車的排放水平很低。","reference":{"eng":"emission","kk":"iˈmɪʃən","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"排放\"  ],  [    \"散發\"  ],  [    \"發射\"  ],  [    \"排放物\"  ]]","chEntries":["排放","散發","發射","排放物"],"practiceMeaning":"這輛車的排放水平很低。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 emissiōnem，是動詞 emittere「發出、送出」的名詞化。emittere 由 ex- (out) + mittere (to send) 組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 ex-「出」和 mittere「送」是其核心語意來源。作為名詞，其核心語義是由動詞 emit「發出、散發」名詞化而來，指「發出、排放或散發的行為或過程」，也指「被排放出來的物質」。詞源中的「送出」概念是其核心。此義項由「發出」的動作延伸出「排放」的行為與「排放物」的結果。","definition":"1. the act of emitting or sending out; 2. a substance or radiation that is emitted.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The emission of greenhouse gases is a major concern.\",\n    \"ch\": \"溫室氣體的排放是一個主要問題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The factory's emissions were causing pollution.\",\n    \"ch\": \"工廠的排放物造成了污染。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The sun emits heat and light.\",\n    \"ch\": \"太陽散發出熱量和光芒。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The car has low emission levels.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這輛車的排放水平很低。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這輛車的排放水平很低。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6169,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::exploit::vt","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"She knows how to ____ every advantage.","expectedAnswer":"exploit","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"She knows how to ____ every advantage.","clozeAnswer":"exploit","exampleTranslation":"她知道如何利用一切優勢。","reference":{"eng":"exploit","kk":"ɪkˈsplɔɪt","tense":"vt.","ch":"[  [    \"剝削\"  ],  [    \"利用\"  ],  [    \"開發\"  ],  [    \"發揮\"  ]]","chEntries":["剝削","利用","開發","發揮"],"practiceMeaning":"她知道如何利用一切優勢。","analysis":"此字源自法語 exploiter，最終源自拉丁語 explicare「展開、闡明」，後來意義轉變為「利用、發揮」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但其詞源演變是關鍵。作為及物動詞，其核心語義有兩方面：一是指「開發或利用（資源、潛力）」，這部分語義帶有積極或中性的意味；二是指「剝削、不正當地利用（人）」，這部分語義帶有負面含義。詞源的「展開」引申出「發揮」和「利用」的用法，而後者又發展出「剝削」的負面意義。","definition":"1. to make full use of and derive benefit from (a resource); 2. to treat (a person or situation) unfairly in order to benefit from them; 3. to develop or make use of (a resource).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company was accused of exploiting its workers.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司被指控剝削其工人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We need to exploit these new opportunities.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們需要利用這些新的機會。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The region's natural resources are being fully exploited.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該地區的自然資源正在被充分開發。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She knows how to exploit every advantage.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她知道如何利用一切優勢。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"她知道如何利用一切優勢。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6173,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::forum::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They held a town hall ____ on public safety.","expectedAnswer":"forum","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They held a town hall ____ on public safety.","clozeAnswer":"forum","exampleTranslation":"他們就公共安全問題舉行了市政廳論壇。","reference":{"eng":"forum","kk":"ˈfɔrəm","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"論壇\"  ],  [    \"討論會\"  ],  [    \"廣場\"  ],  [    \"（辯論、討論的）場所\"  ]]","chEntries":["論壇","討論會","廣場","場所"],"practiceMeaning":"他們就公共安全問題舉行了市政廳論壇。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 forum，意為「公共場所、市場、廣場」。在古羅馬，它是舉行公共集會、辯論和商業活動的中心。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作為名詞，其核心語義是「一個用於公開討論、辯論或交流意見的場所或場合」。此義項由古羅馬時期的「公共廣場」引申出「討論會」和「論壇」的現代用法。","definition":"1. a place, meeting, or medium where ideas and views on a particular issue can be exchanged; 2. a public meeting or lecture, typically held in a university or college, at which invited speakers debate a topic of current interest.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The internet forum is a popular place for discussion.\",\n    \"ch\": \"網路論壇是一個受歡迎的討論場所。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The forum will focus on environmental issues.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這次討論會將聚焦於環境議題。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's an open forum for all members to express their views.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是個讓所有成員表達意見的公開論壇。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They held a town hall forum on public safety.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們就公共安全問題舉行了市政廳論壇。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們就公共安全問題舉行了市政廳論壇。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4518,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::in::prep","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They are involved ____ the project.","expectedAnswer":"in","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They are involved ____ the project.","clozeAnswer":"in","exampleTranslation":"他們參與了這個項目。","reference":{"eng":"in","kk":"/ɪn/","tense":"prep.","ch":"[['在...裡面'], ['在...之中'], ['在（某個時間、地點、情況）']]","chEntries":["在...裡面","在...之中","在"],"practiceMeaning":"他們參與了這個項目。","analysis":"源自古英語 in。是一個極其基本且用途廣泛的介詞。核心語意是「在一個封閉的空間或區域內」。引申義涵蓋時間、狀態、方法、組成等。","definition":"1. Expressing the situation of being enclosed or surrounded by something; 2. Expressing location or position within a place or area; 3. Expressing the period of time during which an event occurs.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The keys are in the drawer.\",\n    \"ch\": \"鑰匙在抽屜裡。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He lives in London.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他住在倫敦。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She will arrive in an hour.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她將在一小時內到達。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They are involved in the project.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們參與了這個項目。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們參與了這個項目。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6176,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::incentive::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The bonus served as an ____ to work harder.","expectedAnswer":"incentive","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The bonus served as an ____ to work harder.","clozeAnswer":"incentive","exampleTranslation":"獎金起到了激勵更努力工作的誘因作用。","reference":{"eng":"incentive","kk":"ɪnˈsɛntɪv","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"刺激\"  ],  [    \"誘因\"  ],  [    \"動機\"  ]]","chEntries":["刺激","誘因","動機"],"practiceMeaning":"獎金起到了激勵更努力工作的誘因作用。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 incentivum，是動詞 incendere「點燃、激勵」的中性過去分詞，引申為「激勵因素」。incendere 由 in- (in, into) + candēre (to burn, glow) 組成。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 in-「進入」和 candēre「燃燒」是其核心語意來源。作為名詞，其核心語義是「促使某人做某事的東西」，即「刺激」或「誘因」。詞源中的「點燃」概念引申為「激發、促使」的動力。","definition":"1. a thing that motivates or encourages one to do something; 2. a payment or other consideration by which one is influenced.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Higher wages provide a strong incentive for workers.\",\n    \"ch\": \"更高的工資為工人提供了強烈的誘因。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The government offered tax incentives for new businesses.\",\n    \"ch\": \"政府提供了稅收優惠來鼓勵新企業。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"What is your incentive for taking this job?\",\n    \"ch\": \"你從事這份工作的動機是什麼？\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The bonus served as an incentive to work harder.\",\n    \"ch\": \"獎金起到了激勵更努力工作的誘因作用。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"獎金起到了激勵更努力工作的誘因作用。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5571,"wordRef":"龍騰課本::l6::load::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The game's graphics ____ slowly.","expectedAnswer":"load","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The game's graphics ____ slowly.","clozeAnswer":"load","exampleTranslation":"遊戲的畫面載入很慢。","reference":{"eng":"load","kk":"loʊd","tense":"n.","ch":"[['負荷'], ['載重'], ['裝載量'], ['負擔']]","chEntries":["負荷","載重","裝載量","負擔"],"practiceMeaning":"遊戲的畫面載入很慢。","analysis":"此字源自古英語 \"lād\"，意為 \"way, journey, cargo\"（路，旅程，貨物），最終可能源自原始印歐語 \\*leith-（to go, to travel，去，旅行）。\"lād\" 最初指「旅程」或「所載的貨物」。\"load\" 作名詞，核心語義是「被攜帶或承受的重量、數量或負擔」。它可以指物理上的「貨物」（cargo）；「機器或車輛所能承受的最大重量」（carrying capacity）；在工程學上指「作用在結構上的力」（force or stress）；在計算機領域指「載入的數據或程式」（data to be loaded）；引申義指「精神上的負擔」（burden）。","definition":"1. A large quantity of goods or people, especially one that is carried or conveyed; 2. The weight of goods put on a vehicle or in a ship, aircraft, etc.; 3. A quantity of something such as ammunition, that is put into a gun; 4. The amount of work or responsibility that someone has.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The maximum load for this elevator is 1000 kg.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這部電梯的最大負荷是 1000 公斤。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The lorry had a heavy load of timber.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這輛貨車載有大量木材。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is carrying a heavy emotional load.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他承受著沉重的精神負擔。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The game's graphics load slowly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"遊戲的畫面載入很慢。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"遊戲的畫面載入很慢。","sourceName":"龍騰課本","unitName":"L6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":3113,"wordRef":"字彙王::u39::maintain::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The mechanic will ____ the car regularly.","expectedAnswer":"maintain","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The mechanic will ____ the car regularly.","clozeAnswer":"maintain","exampleTranslation":"機械師會定期保養汽車。","reference":{"eng":"maintain","kk":"/meɪnˈteɪn/","tense":"v.","ch":"[['維持；保持'], ['堅持（觀點）；認為'], ['供給；供養'], ['維修；保養']]","chEntries":["維持","保持","堅持","認為","供給","供養","維修","保養"],"practiceMeaning":"機械師會定期保養汽車。","analysis":"源自古法語 'maintenir'，'main-' (hand) + 'tenir' (to hold)。核心意義是「用手拿著」。\n1. 維持；保持：指使事物處於某種狀態，不使其衰退或改變。\n2. 堅持（觀點）；認為：指不斷主張或信奉某種信念或看法。\n3. 供給；供養：指提供生活所需，支持某人或某物。\n4. 維修；保養：指對設備、建築物等進行必要的修繕和保養，使其正常運作。","definition":"1. to keep something in good condition; 2. to continue to have something; 3. to say something strongly and believe it to be true; 4. to provide someone with the money that they need to live.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It is important to maintain a healthy diet.\",\n    \"ch\": \"保持健康的飲食很重要。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He maintained that he was innocent.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他堅持認為自己是無辜的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They struggled to maintain their large family.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們努力維持著大家庭的生活。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The mechanic will maintain the car regularly.\",\n    \"ch\": \"機械師會定期保養汽車。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"機械師會定期保養汽車。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U39"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6179,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::miniature::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He bought a ____ schnauzer puppy.","expectedAnswer":"miniature","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He bought a ____ schnauzer puppy.","clozeAnswer":"miniature","exampleTranslation":"他買了一隻迷你雪納瑞幼犬。","reference":{"eng":"miniature","kk":"ˈmɪniətʃər","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"小型的\"  ],  [    \"微型的\"  ],  [    \"縮小的\"  ]]","chEntries":["小型的","微型的","縮小的"],"practiceMeaning":"他買了一隻迷你雪納瑞幼犬。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 miniatura，與 miniare「塗色」（尤其指手稿中的紅色）有關，可能與 minor「較小的」有關。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，應視為整體詞源演變。作為形容詞，其核心語義是指「非常小的、微小的」。此義項由「小的」概念引申，強調尺寸上的微小。","definition":"1. a thing that is very small in size.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She has a collection of miniature cars.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她收藏了一批微型汽車。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The artist painted a miniature portrait.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位藝術家畫了一幅微型肖像。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a miniature version of the original building.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是這個建築物的一個縮小版。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He bought a miniature schnauzer puppy.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他買了一隻迷你雪納瑞幼犬。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他買了一隻迷你雪納瑞幼犬。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5848,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::parallel::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The artist found a ____ in nature for his design.","expectedAnswer":"parallel","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The artist found a ____ in nature for his design.","clozeAnswer":"parallel","exampleTranslation":"這位藝術家在自然界中找到了他設計的相似之處。","reference":{"eng":"parallel","kk":"ˈpærəlel","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"平行線\"  ],  [    \"平行面\"  ],  [    \"平行事物\"  ],  [    \"對比\"  ],  [    \"相似處\"  ]]","chEntries":["平行線","平行面","平行事物","對比","相似處"],"practiceMeaning":"這位藝術家在自然界中找到了他設計的相似之處。","analysis":"此名詞形式與形容詞形式同源。其核心語意是「平行線」或「與某事物並列、相似、或同時發生的事物」。在幾何學上，指「平行線」。在引申義上，指「類似的事件」、「同時發生的情況」或「可與之對比的事物」。它強調的是一種「並列」、「相似」或「同步」的關係，可以是一種結構上的對稱，也可以是事件發展上的並行。例如，也可指「一種可供比較的事物」。","definition":"1. A line or plane that is parallel to another line or plane.; 2. A person or thing that is similar or analogous to another.; 3. A corresponding aspect or feature.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Draw a parallel line.\",\n    \"ch\": \"畫一條平行線。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"There are striking parallels between the two situations.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這兩種情況之間有驚人的相似之處。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The historian drew parallels between ancient Rome and modern society.\",\n    \"ch\": \"歷史學家將古羅馬與現代社會進行了對比。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The artist found a parallel in nature for his design.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位藝術家在自然界中找到了他設計的相似之處。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這位藝術家在自然界中找到了他設計的相似之處。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4147,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u5::passage::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"They had difficulty in ____ through the mountains.","expectedAnswer":"passage","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"They had difficulty in ____ through the mountains.","clozeAnswer":"passage","exampleTranslation":"他們在穿越山脈時遇到了困難。","reference":{"eng":"passage","kk":"/ˈpæsɪdʒ/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['通道', '走廊'], ['（書籍、文章等的）段落', '樂句'], ['（時間）流逝'], ['通過', '通行']]","chEntries":["通道","走廊","段落","樂句","流逝","通過","通行"],"practiceMeaning":"他們在穿越山脈時遇到了困難。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 passus（步伐），是動詞 pandere（擴展，打開）的過去分詞。核心概念是「前進」或「被打開的路徑」。引申為物理上的通道、時間的流逝、口頭或書面表達的一部分，以及通過的行為。","definition":"1. a narrow area or route that connects one place to another; 2. a portion of a written work or musical composition; 3. the act or process of moving through, under, over, or past something; 4. the continuous passing of time","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The narrow passage led to a hidden room.\",\n    \"ch\": \"狹窄的通道通往一個隱藏的房間。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please read the following passage carefully.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請仔細閱讀以下段落。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"With the passage of time, things will change.\",\n    \"ch\": \"隨著時間的流逝，事情會改變。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"They had difficulty in passage through the mountains.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他們在穿越山脈時遇到了困難。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他們在穿越山脈時遇到了困難。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U5"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6183,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::plural::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He holds ____ positions in the organization.","expectedAnswer":"plural","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He holds ____ positions in the organization.","clozeAnswer":"plural","exampleTranslation":"他在該組織中擔任多個職位。","reference":{"eng":"plural","kk":"ˈplʊrəl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"複數的\"  ],  [    \"多數的\"  ],  [    \"複数\"  ]]","chEntries":["複數的","多數的","複数"],"practiceMeaning":"他在該組織中擔任多個職位。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 plūrālis，是 plus（更多）的衍生形容詞，意為「更多的」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 plus「更多」是其核心語意來源。作為形容詞，其核心語義是指「兩個或兩個以上」或「多於一個」的狀態。詞源中的「更多」概念引申出「多數」和「複數」的用法，特別是在語法上指代兩個以上的名詞、代詞或動詞形式。","definition":"1. (of a word or form) denoting more than one; 2. more than one.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The plural of 'cat' is 'cats'.\",\n    \"ch\": \"「cat」的複數是「cats」。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a plural noun.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個複數名詞。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The company has plural shareholders.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這家公司有多個股東。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He holds plural positions in the organization.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他在該組織中擔任多個職位。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他在該組織中擔任多個職位。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5855,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::radical::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The dentist performed a ____ surgery to remove the tumor.","expectedAnswer":"radical","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The dentist performed a ____ surgery to remove the tumor.","clozeAnswer":"radical","exampleTranslation":"牙醫進行了根除性手術以移除腫瘤。","reference":{"eng":"radical","kk":"ˈrædɪkl","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"激進的\"  ],  [    \"根本的\"  ],  [    \"徹底的\"  ],  [    \"主根的\"  ]]","chEntries":["激進的","根本的","徹底的","主根的"],"practiceMeaning":"牙醫進行了根除性手術以移除腫瘤。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'radicalis'，是 'radix' (root) 的派生詞。'Radix' 指「根」，引申為「基礎」、「起源」。'-al' 是常見的形容詞字尾。'Radical' 的核心語意與「根」相關，指「關於根部的」或「從根源來的」。這引申出「根本的」、「徹底的」意思，表示涉及事物最基本的部分。引申到政治或社會思想，則指追求根本性變革的「激進的」。例如，也可指「極端的」或「全面的」。","definition":"1. Relating to or affecting the fundamental nature of something; far-reaching or thorough.; 2. (of change or action) advocating or based on thorough or complete political or social change.; 3. Relating to the root of a plant or hair follicle.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The proposal calls for radical changes.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這項提議要求進行根本性的改變。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He is known for his radical political views.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他以其激進的政治觀點而聞名。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is a radical solution to the problem.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這是一個解決問題的徹底方案。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The dentist performed a radical surgery to remove the tumor.\",\n    \"ch\": \"牙醫進行了根除性手術以移除腫瘤。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"牙醫進行了根除性手術以移除腫瘤。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5858,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::saint::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He described his neighbor as a ____ for helping him move.","expectedAnswer":"saint","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He described his neighbor as a ____ for helping him move.","clozeAnswer":"saint","exampleTranslation":"他形容他的鄰居像個聖人一樣幫他搬家。","reference":{"eng":"saint","kk":"seɪnt","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"聖人\"  ],  [    \"聖徒\"  ],  [    \"品德高尚的人\"  ],  [    \"極有耐心或善良的人\"  ]]","chEntries":["聖人","聖徒","品德高尚的人","極有耐心或善良的人"],"practiceMeaning":"他形容他的鄰居像個聖人一樣幫他搬家。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'sanctus' (holy, consecrated)，意為「神聖的」。'Sanctus' 是 'sancire' (to make sacred, to hallow) 的過去分詞。'Saint' 在宗教中指被奉為神聖、德行卓著，並常被尊崇崇拜的人，尤其是在基督宗教中。它強調的是「神聖的」、「受人尊敬」和「品德完美」的特質。引申義可用來形容品德極好、行為高尚的人。例如，也可形容「極有耐心或善良的人」。","definition":"1. A person acknowledged as being especially holy or virtuous and as being a representative of God or of a particular religion.; 2. A person of great virtue and goodness.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Saint Peter is one of the apostles.\",\n    \"ch\": \"聖彼得是使徒之一。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is a saint for putting up with all that trouble.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她為了忍受所有那些麻煩真是個聖人。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Many churches are named after saints.\",\n    \"ch\": \"許多教堂都是以聖徒的名字命名的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He described his neighbor as a saint for helping him move.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他形容他的鄰居像個聖人一樣幫他搬家。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他形容他的鄰居像個聖人一樣幫他搬家。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5859,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::salon::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The art ____ exhibited works by local painters.","expectedAnswer":"salon","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The art ____ exhibited works by local painters.","clozeAnswer":"salon","exampleTranslation":"藝術沙龍展出了本地畫家的作品。","reference":{"eng":"salon","kk":"səˈlɑːn","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"沙龍\"  ],  [    \"美容院\"  ],  [    \"客廳\"  ],  [    \"陳列室\"  ]]","chEntries":["沙龍","美容院","客廳","陳列室"],"practiceMeaning":"藝術沙龍展出了本地畫家的作品。","analysis":"此字源自法語 'salon'，原意為「大廳」、「接待室」，由 'salle' (hall) 演變而來，'salle' 源自拉丁語 'sal' (salt)，或有說源自'sala' (room)，表示「主要房間」。'Salon' 在18世紀法國興起，指「名流聚集的客廳」，成為文化交流的場所。現代語義擴展至「美容院」或「髮廊」，指提供美容、美髮服務的專業場所，這些場所也常被設計成舒適、有格調的空間，如同昔日的社交沙龍。例如，也可指「藝術品陳列室」。","definition":"1. A large room in a private house or hotel, especially one used for entertaining guests.; 2. A fashionable beauty salon or hairdressing establishment.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She went to the salon to get her hair done.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她去沙龍做頭髮。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The salon hosted a gathering of artists.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個沙龍舉辦了一場藝術家聚會。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He opened a new beauty salon.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他開了一家新的美容院。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The art salon exhibited works by local painters.\",\n    \"ch\": \"藝術沙龍展出了本地畫家的作品。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"藝術沙龍展出了本地畫家的作品。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6196,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::shuttle::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ service operates between the terminal and the parking lot.","expectedAnswer":"shuttle","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ service operates between the terminal and the parking lot.","clozeAnswer":"shuttle","exampleTranslation":"接駁車服務在航站樓和停車場之間運營。","reference":{"eng":"shuttle","kk":"ˈʃʌtl","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"梭子\"  ],  [    \"接駁車\"  ],  [    \"穿梭班機\"  ]]","chEntries":["梭子","接駁車","穿梭班機"],"practiceMeaning":"接駁車服務在航站樓和停車場之間運營。","analysis":"此字源自古法語 shuttle，原意指紡織機上的「梭子」。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作為名詞，其核心語義是指「用於紡織機上來回移動的梭子」，引申為「短程來回運輸的車輛或飛機」。詞源中的「梭子」象徵著來回移動的特徵。","definition":"1. a large shuttlecock used in badminton; 2. a device for weaving that moves back and forth between the threads of a warp; 3. a bus, train, or aircraft that travels regularly between two places.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The shuttle runs every hour from the hotel to the airport.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這班接駁車每小時一班，從旅館到機場。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She hit the shuttlecock hard in the game.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她在比賽中用力擊打羽毛球。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The airport shuttle was convenient.\",\n    \"ch\": \"機場接駁車很方便。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The shuttle service operates between the terminal and the parking lot.\",\n    \"ch\": \"接駁車服務在航站樓和停車場之間運營。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"接駁車服務在航站樓和停車場之間運營。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":5861,"wordRef":"字彙王::u58::sustain::v","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"Good nutrition can ____ good health.","expectedAnswer":"sustain","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"Good nutrition can ____ good health.","clozeAnswer":"sustain","exampleTranslation":"良好的營養可以滋養健康的身體。","reference":{"eng":"sustain","kk":"səˈsteɪn","tense":"v.","ch":"[  [    \"維持\"  ],  [    \"支撐\"  ],  [    \"承受\"  ],  [    \"供給\"  ],  [    \"滋養\"  ]]","chEntries":["維持","支撐","承受","供給","滋養"],"practiceMeaning":"良好的營養可以滋養健康的身體。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 'sustinere'，由 'sus-' (under, up) 和 'tenere' (to hold) 構成，字面意思是「向上托住」或「從下面支撐」。'Sustain' 的核心語意是「支撐」、「維持」某物的存在、狀態或功能，抵抗其崩潰或衰退。它可以指物理上的支撐（如建築物、身體），也可以指精神上的支持，或使某物在一段時間內保持下去。還可指「承受」困難或痛苦。例如，也可指「滋養」身體或心靈。","definition":"1. To bear all or all of the weight of; to keep from falling or collapsing.; 2. To strengthen or support physically or mentally.; 3. To suffer or undergo (an injury, loss, or affliction).","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The pillars sustain the roof.\",\n    \"ch\": \"柱子支撐著屋頂。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He sustained himself on a meager diet.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他靠著粗茶淡飯維持生計。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She sustained a serious injury.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她受了重傷。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Good nutrition can sustain good health.\",\n    \"ch\": \"良好的營養可以滋養健康的身體。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"良好的營養可以滋養健康的身體。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U58"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6199,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::thesis::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The ____ defended the author's position.","expectedAnswer":"thesis","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The ____ defended the author's position.","clozeAnswer":"thesis","exampleTranslation":"這篇論點為作者的立場辯護。","reference":{"eng":"thesis","kk":"ˈθiːsɪs","tense":"n.","ch":"[  [    \"論文\"  ],  [    \"論點\"  ],  [    \"學說\"  ]]","chEntries":["論文","論點","學說"],"practiceMeaning":"這篇論點為作者的立場辯護。","analysis":"此字源自古希臘語 θέσις (thesis)，意為「放置、安排、主張」，與 θεῖναι (theinai)「放置」同源。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根。作為名詞，其核心語義是指「為學術目的而寫的一篇長篇文章」，通常是大學學位的要求。詞源中的「放置、安排、主張」概念引申為「提出的論點」和「學術性的主張」。","definition":"1. a long essay or dissertation involving personal research, written as part of a course of study for a degree; 2. a statement or theory that is put forward as a premise to be maintained or proved.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She is writing her doctoral thesis on artificial intelligence.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她正在撰寫關於人工智能的博士論文。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His thesis argued for the importance of early childhood education.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的論文主張了早期兒童教育的重要性。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This paper presents a novel thesis.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這篇論文提出了一個新穎的論點。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The thesis defended the author's position.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這篇論點為作者的立場辯護。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這篇論點為作者的立場辯護。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4636,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u16::tight::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The money supply is ____.","expectedAnswer":"tight","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The money supply is ____.","clozeAnswer":"tight","exampleTranslation":"資金供應緊張。","reference":{"eng":"tight","kk":"/taɪt/","tense":"adj.","ch":"[['緊的'], ['牢固的'], ['（空間）狹窄的'], ['（供應）緊張的'], ['（時間）緊迫的']]","chEntries":["緊的","牢固的","狹窄的","緊張的","緊迫的"],"practiceMeaning":"資金供應緊張。","analysis":"源自古英語 'tiht' (緊湊、快速)，與 'tie' (綁) 同源。核心概念是緊密、不易移動或變形。可以是物理上的緊縛，也可以是抽象上的限制，如空間、時間或供應的緊縮。","definition":"fixed firmly in place; not loose; not having much space; limited in supply or time.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The knot was very tight.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這個結打得很緊。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The city streets are very tight and narrow.\",\n    \"ch\": \"市區的街道非常狹窄。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"We have a tight schedule for the project.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我們這個專案的時間表很緊。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The money supply is tight.\",\n    \"ch\": \"資金供應緊張。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"資金供應緊張。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U16"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4516,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::to::prep","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"This is important ____ me.","expectedAnswer":"to","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"This is important ____ me.","clozeAnswer":"to","exampleTranslation":"這對我來說很重要。","reference":{"eng":"to","kk":"/tu/","tense":"prep.","ch":"[['向'], ['到'], ['對於'], ['以便']]","chEntries":["向","到","對於","以便"],"practiceMeaning":"這對我來說很重要。","analysis":"源自古英語 tō。是一個極其常見的介詞，用於表示方向、目的地、目的、範圍、程度、時間等。","definition":"1. Expressing motion in the direction of (a particular location); 2. Expressing the recipient of an action or gift; 3. Up to the point in time or the degree specified; 4. In order to achieve or bring about.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He walked to the store.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他走向商店。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Give it to me.\",\n    \"ch\": \"把它給我。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"I came to help.\",\n    \"ch\": \"我來是為了幫忙。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This is important to me.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這對我來說很重要。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"這對我來說很重要。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4524,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u10::up::adv","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The meeting is all wrapped ____.","expectedAnswer":"up","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The meeting is all wrapped ____.","clozeAnswer":"up","exampleTranslation":"會議已經全部結束了。","reference":{"eng":"up","kk":"/ʌp/","tense":"adv.","ch":"[['向上'], ['起來'], ['在...上面'], ['完成']]","chEntries":["向上","起來","在...上面","完成"],"practiceMeaning":"會議已經全部結束了。","analysis":"源自古英語 up。是一個表示方向、位置、狀態或完成的副詞。核心語意是「朝上」、「向上」。引申義廣泛，包括「停止」、「完成」、「在場」等。","definition":"1. Towards a higher place or position; 2. Completely or entirely; 3. Out of bed; 4. In progress.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Look up!\",\n    \"ch\": \"向上看！\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He got up early.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他早早地起床了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"It's time to clean up.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該打掃了。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The meeting is all wrapped up.\",\n    \"ch\": \"會議已經全部結束了。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"會議已經全部結束了。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U10"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":6203,"wordRef":"字彙王::u66::valid::adj","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"The contract is ____ from today.","expectedAnswer":"valid","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"The contract is ____ from today.","clozeAnswer":"valid","exampleTranslation":"該合同從今天起生效。","reference":{"eng":"valid","kk":"ˈvælɪd","tense":"adj.","ch":"[  [    \"有效的\"  ],  [    \"有法律效力的\"  ],  [    \"合理的\"  ],  [    \"有說服力的\"  ]]","chEntries":["有效的","有法律效力的","合理的","有說服力的"],"practiceMeaning":"該合同從今天起生效。","analysis":"此字源自拉丁語 validus，意為「強壯的、有力的」，與 valēre「強壯、有力」相關。此字在現代英語中不宜硬拆為字首或字根，但 valēre「強壯、有力」是其核心語意來源。作為形容詞，其核心語義是指「有充分證據或理由支持的、為法律或規章所承認的」。詞源中的「強壯、有力」引申為「有說服力的、有效的」。","definition":"1. legally or officially acceptable; 2. based on known facts and sound reasoning; 3. (of a ticket or other document) allowing the holder to travel or gain admission; 4. (of an argument or point) having a sound basis in logic or fact.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"This ticket is valid for one year.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這張票一年內有效。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"His argument is valid.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他的論點是有說服力的。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"Please ensure your passport is valid.\",\n    \"ch\": \"請確保您的護照有效。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The contract is valid from today.\",\n    \"ch\": \"該合同從今天起生效。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"該合同從今天起生效。","sourceName":"字彙王","unitName":"U66"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}},{"wordId":4186,"wordRef":"文華高中-常春藤單字::c3u6::vision::n","mode":"cloze_en","questionType":"typing","prompt":"He described his ____ in vivid detail.","expectedAnswer":"vision","choices":[],"clozeSentence":"He described his ____ in vivid detail.","clozeAnswer":"vision","exampleTranslation":"他生動地描述了他的幻想。","reference":{"eng":"vision","kk":"/ˈvɪʒn/","tense":"n.","ch":"[['視力；視覺'], ['想像；幻想'], ['遠見；洞察力'], ['（對未來的）設想；規劃']]","chEntries":["視力","視覺","想像","幻想","遠見","洞察力","設想","規劃"],"practiceMeaning":"他生動地描述了他的幻想。","analysis":"源自拉丁語 visio，意為“看，看見，景象”。'Visio' 來自 'videre'，意為“看”。核心是“看”的能力和所見的景象。引申至抽象概念：1. 抽象化的“看”即“想像”或“幻想”；2. 預見未來、有遠見的“看”即“遠見”或“洞察力”；3. 具體規劃的“看”即對未來的“設想”或“規劃”。","definition":"1. the ability to see; sight; 2. the ability to imagine or think about the future with imagination or wisdom; 3. a mental image or picture of what the future could be like.","example":"[\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He has poor vision in his left eye.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他左眼的視力很差。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"She had a vision of a better future for her country.\",\n    \"ch\": \"她對國家有了一個更美好未來的設想。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"The entrepreneur's vision revolutionized the industry.\",\n    \"ch\": \"這位企業家的遠見徹底改變了這個行業。\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"eng\": \"He described his vision in vivid detail.\",\n    \"ch\": \"他生動地描述了他的幻想。\"\n  }\n]","exampleTranslation":"他生動地描述了他的幻想。","sourceName":"文華高中-常春藤單字","unitName":"C3U6"},"learningMeta":{"attempts":0,"accuracy":0,"mastered":false}}]}